RECORD	para 245	10 Recommended parameter semantics
RECORD	Renderer parameter Physical analogue Recommended interpretation	Renderer parameter Physical analogue Recommended interpretation
RECORD	AOD 550 Aerosol optical depth Column aerosol extinction at the	AOD 550 Aerosol optical depth Column aerosol extinction at the visible reference wavelength.
RECORD	ANGSTROM ALPHA Angstrom exponent Wavelength slope of aerosol optical	ANGSTROM ALPHA Angstrom exponent Wavelength slope of aerosol optical depth.
RECORD	WET TURBIDITY GAIN f (RH) or a fit parameter for it Hydrated-aerosol scattering	WET TURBIDITY GAIN f (RH) or a fit parameter for it Hydrated-aerosol scattering en- hancement; do not use it to rep- resent cloud opacity.
RECORD	AEROSOL SCALE HEIGHT Ha Converts column AOD into an ap-	AEROSOL SCALE HEIGHT Ha Converts column AOD into an ap- proximate surface extinction pro- file.
WHEN	PREETHAM TURBIDITY T Clear-sky haze/molecular optical-	PREETHAM TURBIDITY T Clear-sky haze/molecular optical- thickness ratio; derived from or cal- ibrated against AOD when possi- ble.
RECORD	WATER PATH REFERENCE M Geometric cloud-water reference Normalization/transition	WATER PATH REFERENCE M Geometric cloud-water reference Normalization/transition length for cloud LWC/LWP logic; not an aerosol scale.
RECORD	CLOUD LWP Liquid water path Integrated cloud liquid water per	CLOUD LWP Liquid water path Integrated cloud liquid water per unit horizontal area.
RECORD	CLOUD REFF Effective droplet radius Controls cloud optical thickness for	CLOUD REFF Effective droplet radius Controls cloud optical thickness for fixed LWP.
RECORD	TWILIGHT CURVE Empirical/engineering illumi-	TWILIGHT CURVE Empirical/engineering illumi- nance curve Ambient intensity transition for so- lar elevation 0 to −6 degrees.
RECORD	para 256	11 Failure modes this separation prevents
DEFINE	para 257	Failure 1: “More cloud” is implemented by raising turbidity. This makes the sky white/hazy rather than volumetrically clouded and breaks the distinction between horizontal haze and vertically
RECORD	para 260	concentrated cloud water.
DEFINE	para 261	Failure 2: AOD is converted directly to visibility with no aerosol profile. The resulting surface extinction is implicitly assuming a scale height even if the code does not state one.
DEFINE	para 262	Failure 3: Wet aerosol is represented by adding cloud LWP. Sub-saturated aerosol water uptake and saturated cloud droplets occupy very different microphysical regimes.
ALLOW	para 263	Failure 4: Preetham is extrapolated far past its fit range. The result may look plausible in one camera direction while failing near the Sun, horizon, or during strong haze/sunset conditions. Hosek-Wilkie is a better upgrade path for those cases. [23]
DEFINE	para 264	Failure 5: Twilight is just a smoothstep on daytime RGB. This misses the measured intensity and spectral changes across the 0 to -6 degree civil-twilight interval. [25, 24]
RECORD	para 266	A physically organized implementation can be tested in this order:
RECORD	para 270	13 Key equations at a glance σext = σsca + σabs,
RECORD	para 272	AODλ = ∫ σext, a(z, λ) dz,
RECORD	para 276	fsca(RH) = σsca(RH) σsca(RHref ) ,
RECORD	para 277	LWC(z) ≈ fadΓad(z − zb),
RECORD	LWP = 1	LWP = 1 2 fadΓadH 2,
RECORD	para 279	τc ≈ 3LWP 2ρwreff ,
