RECORD	Glossy-diffuse base A dielectric interface over a strongly scattering/absorbing	Glossy-diffuse base A dielectric interface over a strongly scattering/absorbing interior, approximated as diffuse-like response. Concrete, cardboard, wall paint.
RECORD	Subsurface base Light penetrates, scatters internally and exits at a displaced	Subsurface base Light penetrates, scatters internally and exits at a displaced location. Skin, wax, marble, fruit, leaves.
RECORD	Translucent base A dielectric interface plus a volume that can absorb and scatte	Translucent base A dielectric interface plus a volume that can absorb and scatter transmitted light. Glass, colored liquids, honey, opalescent media.
RECORD	para 40	Coat An upper dielectric interface, potentially colored/absorbing, with its own roughness and Fresnel behavior. Varnish, clear coat, lacquer.
RECORD	para 41	Fuzz A fiber-like upper response. Peach skin, cloth fibers, fine hair, dust.
RECORD	para 42	A parameter model is not a claim of universal physical uniqueness. A material such as base_metalness = 0.5 is a useful, art-directable mixture in OpenPBR. It should not be mistaken for a literal homogeneous substance that is half metallic at every microscopic point. The shader is a controlled model of appearance.
