RECORD	A surface cannot spend the same incoming energy twice	A surface cannot spend the same incoming energy twice
WHEN	para 56	Emission is a separate source term. A glowing surface can add energy because it is modeled as emitting light. Its emitted radiance does not come from the incident-light budget, although the emitted light still participates in transport when it strikes other surfaces.
