RECORD	para 237	15. Failure diagnosis: symptom to likely cause
RECORD	Symptom Likely explanation Next test	Symptom Likely explanation Next test
RECORD	Material gets darker at high roughness	Material gets darker at high roughness in a white environment. Single-scattering microfacet loss, missing compensation, too few bounces, or prefiltered environment mismatch. White-furnace roughness sweep in linear output.
DEFINE	Coat makes the surface brighter overall	Coat makes the surface brighter overall in every view. Top/base lobes added instead of layered, or coat attenuation is skipped. Compare base-only and coated energy integrals.
RECORD	Diffuse stays equally bright at grazing	Diffuse stays equally bright at grazing angles under a strong dielectric highlight.
DEFINE	Specular/base coupling is missing or using a	Specular/base coupling is missing or using a non-directional shortcut. Rotate an IOR 1.5 dielectric sphere through grazing angles.
RECORD	Glass transmits more energy than the	Glass transmits more energy than the environment provides. Incorrect Fresnel complement, refraction throughput / eta factor, duplicate transmission or path-weight bug. Test an unabsorbing slab; integrate reflected + transmitted energy.
ALLOW	para 244	Metal looks like bright plastic. Metallic and diffuse responses may both be active; conductor Fresnel color/weight mapping may be wrong. Compare metalness endpoints and inspect lobe contributions separately.
RECORD	para 245	Asset appearance changes after import. Different OpenPBR version, color space, roughness remapping, unsupported feature or changed scene scale. Round-trip parameter dump and render a versioned reference asset.
ALLOW	A white furnace sphere is too bright	A white furnace sphere is too bright only with normal mapping. Shading-normal correction or frame handling may break reciprocity/normalization. Disable map; then introduce a fixed, known normal map.
RECORD	Image-based light differs from direct	Image-based light differs from direct light tests. Environment prefilter / integration LUT does not match actual BSDF, or importance sampling is biased. Use a simple directional light plus environment and compare isolated components.
RECORD	Minimal reproducibility record	Minimal reproducibility record
RECORD	OpenPBR version + renderer build + parameter values + scene units + linear envir	OpenPBR version + renderer build + parameter values + scene units + linear environment + transport settings + linear output
REQUIRE	para 250	Save intermediate component renders when possible: base, interface specular, transmission, coat, fuzz and emission. Component renders are diagnostic tools, not necessarily physically meaningful standalone materials. The final combined result must pass the whole-model tests.
RECORD	para 251	Do not “fix” every energy symptom with albedo. A lower base_color can hide excess lobe energy in one view; a higher base_color can hide lost single-scattering energy. Those edits undermine interoperability because the material now compensates for a specific renderer or light setup.
