FORBID	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. In this world, you shall not find any shelter; in the world hereafter, being false, you shall suffer. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 807	Awip sujwxu n BuleI scw vf ikrswxu ] (19-1, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) aap sujaan na bhul-ee sachaa vad kirsaan. The True Lord Himself knows all; He makes no mistakes. He is the Great Farmer of the Universe.
RECORD	para 808	pihlw DrqI swiD kY scu nwmu dy dwxu ] (19-2, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) pahilaa Dhartee saaDh kai sach naam day daan. First, He prepares the ground, and then He plants the Seed of the True Name.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	nau iniD aupjY nwmu eyku krim pvY nIswxu ]2] (19-2, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) na-o niDh upjai naam ayk karam pavai neesaan. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	The nine treasures are produced from Name of the One Lord. By His Grace, we obtain His Banner and Insignia. ||2||
DEFINE	para 810	gur kau jwix n jwxeI ikAw iqsu cju Acwru ] (19-2, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) gur ka-o jaan na jaan-ee ki-aa tis chaj achaar. Some are very knowledgeable, but if they do not know the Guru, then what is the use of their lives?
RECORD	para 811	AMDulY nwmu ivswirAw mnmuiK AMD gubwru ] (19-3, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) anDhulai naam visaari-aa manmukh anDh gubaar. The blind have forgotten the Naam, the Name of the Lord. The self-willed manmukhs are in utter darkness.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Awvxu jwxu n cukeI mir jnmY hoie KuAwru ]3] (19-3, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) aavan jaan na chuk-ee mar janmai ho-ay khu-aar. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Their comings and goings in reincarnation do not end; through death and rebirth, they are wasting away. ||3||
ALLOW	para 813	cMdnu moil AxwieAw kuMgU mWg sMDUru ] (19-4, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) chandan mol anaa-i-aa kungoo maa Ng sanDhoor. The bride may buy sandalwood oil and perfumes, and apply them in great quantities to her hair;
ALLOW	para 814	coAw cMdnu bhu Gxw pwnw nwil kpUru ] (19-4, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) cho-aa chandan baho ghanaa paanaa naal kapoor. she may sweeten her breath with betel leaf and camphor,
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	jy Dn kMiq n BwveI q siB AfMbr kUVu ]4] (19-5, isrIrwgu, mhl 1) jay Dhan kant na bhaav-ee ta sabh adambar koorh. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	but if this bride is not pleasing to her Husband Lord, then all these trappings are false. ||4||
DEFINE	para 816	siB rs Bogx bwid hih siB sIgwr ivkwr ] (19-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabh ras bhogan baad heh sabh seegaar vikaar. Her enjoyment of all pleasures is futile, and all her decorations are corrupt.
RECORD	para 817	jb lgu sbid n BydIAY ikau sohY gurduAwir ] (19-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jab lag sabad na bhaydee-ai ki-o sohai gurdu-aar. Until she has been pierced through with the Shabad, how can she look beautiful at Guru's Gate?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	nwnk DMnu suhwgxI ijn sh nwil ipAwru ]5]13] (19-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak Dhan suhaaganee jin sah naal pi-aar. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	13|| O Nanak, blessed is that fortunate bride, who is in love with her Husband Lord. ||5||13||
DEFINE	para 820	suM\I dyh frwvxI jw jIau ivchu jwie ] (19-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sunjee dayh daraavanee jaa jee-o vichahu jaa-ay. The empty body is dreadful, when the soul goes out from within.
DEFINE	para 821	Bwih blµdI ivJvI DUau n inkisE kwie ] (19-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaahi balandee vijhvee Dhoo-o na niksi-o kaa-ay. The burning fire of life is extinguished, and the smoke of the breath no longer emerges.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	pMcy ruMny duiK Bry ibnsy dUjY Bwie ]1] (19-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) panchay runnay dukh bharay binsay doojai bhaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	The five relatives (the senses) weep and wail painfully, and waste away through the love of duality. ||1||
RECORD	para 823	mUVy rwmu jphu gux swir ] (19-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) moorhay raam japahu gun saar. You fool: chant the Name of the Lord, and preserve your virtue.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	haumY mmqw mohxI sB muTI AhMkwir ]1] rhwau ] (19-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ha-umai mamtaa mohnee sabh muthee ahaNkaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Egotism and possessiveness are very enticing; egotistical pride has plundered everyone. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 825	ijnI nwmu ivswirAw dUjI kwrY lig ] (19-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jinee naam visaari-aa doojee kaarai lag. Those who have forgotten the Naam, the Name of the Lord, are attached to affairs of duality.
DEFINE	para 826	duibDw lwgy pic muey AMqir iqRsnw Aig ] (19-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) dubiDhaa laagay pach mu-ay antar tarisnaa ag. Attached to duality, they putrefy and die; they are filled with the fire of desire within.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	guir rwKy sy aubry hoir muTI DMDY Tig ]2] (19-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur raakhay say ubray hor muthee DhanDhai thag. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Those who are protected by the Guru are saved; all others are cheated and plundered by deceitful worldly affairs. ||2||
RECORD	para 828	mueI prIiq ipAwru gieAw muAw vYru ivroDu ] (19-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mu-ee pareet pi-aar ga-i-aa mu-aa vair viroDh. Love dies, and affection vanishes. Hatred and alienation die.
RECORD	para 829	DMDw Qkw hau mueI mmqw mwieAw k®oDu ] (19-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) DhanDhaa thakaa ha-o mu-ee mamtaa maa-i-aa kroDh. Entanglements end, and egotism dies, along with attachment to Maya, possessiveness and anger.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	krim imlY scu pweIAY gurmuiK sdw inroDu ]3] (19-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) karam milai sach paa-ee-ai gurmukh sadaa niroDh. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Those who receive His Mercy obtain the True One. The Gurmukhs dwell forever in balanced restraint. ||3||
DEFINE	para 831	scI kwrY scu imlY gurmiq plY pwie ] (19-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sachee kaarai sach milai gurmat palai paa-ay. By true actions, the True Lord is met, and the Guru's Teachings are found.
DEFINE	para 832	so nru jMmY nw mrY nw AwvY nw jwie ] (19-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) so nar jammai naa marai naa aavai naa jaa-ay. Then, they are not subject to birth and death; they do not come and go in reincarnation.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	nwnk dir prDwnu so drgih pYDw jwie ]4]14] (19-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak dar parDhaan so dargahi paiDhaa jaa-ay. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	14|| O Nanak, they are respected at the Lord's Gate; they are robed in honor in the Court of the Lord. ||4||14||
DEFINE	para 835	qnu jil bil mwtI BieAw mnu mwieAw moih mnUru ] (19-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tan jal bal maatee bha-i-aa man maa-i-aa mohi manoor. The body is burnt to ashes; by its love of Maya, the mind is rusted through.
RECORD	para 836	Aaugx iPir lwgU Bey kUir vjwvY qUru ] (19-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) a-ugan fir laagoo bha-ay koor vajaavai toor. Demerits become one's enemies, and falsehood blows the bugle of attack.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhl 1 v1	ibnu sbdY BrmweIAY duibDw foby pUru ]1] (19-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin sabdai bharmaa-ee-ai dubiDhaa dobay poor. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhl 1 v1	Without the Word of the Shabad, people wander lost in reincarnation. Through the love of duality, multitudes have been drowned. ||1||
RECORD	para 838	mn ry sbid qrhu icqu lwie ] (19-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man ray sabad tarahu chit laa-ay. O mind, swim across, by focusing your consciousness on the Shabad.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhl 1 v1	ijin gurmuiK nwmu n bUiJAw mir jnmY AwvY jwie ]1] rhwau ] (19-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jin gurmukh naam na boojhi-aa mar janmai aavai jaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhl 1 v1	rahaa-o. Those who do not become Gurmukh do not understand the Naam; they die, and continue coming and going in reincarnation. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 840	qnu sUcw so AwKIAY ijsu mih swcw nwau ] (19-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tan soochaa so aakhee-ai jis meh saachaa naa-o. That body is said to be pure, in which the True Name abides.
DEFINE	para 841	BY sic rwqI dyhurI ijhvw scu suAwau ] (19-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhai sach raatee dayhuree jihvaa sach su-aa-o. One whose body is imbued with the Fear of the True One, and whose tongue savors Truthfulness,
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhl 1 v2	scI ndir inhwlIAY bhuiV n pwvY qwau ]2] (19-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sachee nadar nihaalee-ai bahurh na paavai taa-o. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhl 1 v2	is brought to ecstasy by the True Lord's Glance of Grace. That person does not have to go through the fire of the womb again. ||2||
RECORD	para 843	swcy qy pvnw BieAw pvnY qy jlu hoie ] (19-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saachay tay pavnaa bha-i-aa pavnai tay jal ho-ay. From the True Lord came the air, and from the air came water.
RECORD	para 844	jl qy iqRBvxu swijAw Git Git joiq smoie ] (19-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jal tay taribhavan saaji-aa ghat ghat jot samo-ay. From water, He created the three worlds; in each and every heart He has infused His Light.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhl 1 v3	inrmlu mYlw nw QIAY sbid rqy piq hoie ]3] (19-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nirmal mailaa naa thee-ai sabad ratay pat ho-ay. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhl 1 v3	The Immaculate Lord does not become polluted. Attuned to the Shabad, honor is obtained. ||3||
DEFINE	para 846	iehu mnu swic sMqoiKAw ndir kry iqsu mwih ] (19-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ih man saach santokhi-aa nadar karay tis maahi. One whose mind is contented with Truthfulness, is blessed with the Lord's Glance of Grace.
