DEFINE	para 852	ieik Awvih ieik jwvhI pUir Bry AhMkwir ] (20-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ik aavahi ik jaavhee poor bharay aha Nkaar. Some come, and some go; they are totally filled with egotism.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	mnhiT mqI bUfIAY gurmuiK scu su qwir ]1] (20-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manhath matee boodee-ai gurmukh sach so taar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	Through stubborn-mindedness, the intellect is drowned; one who becomes Gurmukh and truthful is saved. ||1||
RECORD	para 854	gur ibnu ikau qrIAY suKu hoie ] (20-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur bin ki-o taree-ai sukh ho-ay. Without the Guru, how can anyone swim across to find peace?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ijau BwvY iqau rwKu qU mY Avru n dUjw koie ]1] rhwau ] (20-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o bhaavai ti-o raakh too mai avar na doojaa ko-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. As it pleases You, Lord, You save me. There is no other for me at all. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 856	AwgY dyKau fau jlY pwCY hirE AMgUru ] (20-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aagai daykh-a-u da-o jalai paachhai hari-o angoor. In front of me, I see the jungle burning; behind me, I see green plants sprouting.
