DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. The Gurmukh praises the Naam, and the fire of egotism is extinguished. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 874	suix suix gMFxu gMFIAY iliK piV buJih Bwru ] (20-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sun sun gandhan gandhee-ai likh parh bujheh bhaar. Again and again, we hear and tell stories; we read and write and understand loads of knowledge,
RECORD	para 875	iqRsnw Aihinis AglI haumY rogu ivkwru ] (20-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tarisnaa ahinis aglee ha-umai rog vikaar. but still, desires increase day and night, and the disease of egotism fills us with corruption.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Ehu vyprvwhu Aqolvw gurmiq kImiq swru ]2] (20-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) oh vayparvaahu atolvaa gurmat keemat saar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	That Carefree Lord cannot be appraised; His Real Value is known only through the Wisdom of the Guru's Teachings. ||2||
WHEN	para 877	lK isAwxp jy krI lK isau pRIiq imlwpu ] (20-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) lakh si-aanap jay karee lakh si-o pareet milaap. Even if someone has hundreds of thousands of clever mental tricks, and the love and company of hundreds of thousands of people
RECORD	para 878	ibnu sMgiq swD n DRwpIAw ibnu nwvY dUK sMqwpu ] (20-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin sangat saaDh na Dharaapee-aa bin naavai dookh santaap. -still, without the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, he will not feel satisfied. Without the Name, all suffer in sorrow.
