DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	The beautiful, Unstruck Sound of the Shabad is obtained, contemplating the Guru. ||2||
DEFINE	para 893	Anhd bwxI pweIAY qh haumY hoie ibnwsu ] (21-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) anhad banee paa-ee-ai tah ha-umai ho-ay binaas. The Unstruck Melody of Gurbani is obtained, and egotism is eliminated.
RECORD	para 894	sqguru syvy Awpxw hau sd kurbwxY qwsu ] (21-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) satgur sayvay aapnaa ha-o sad kurbaanai taas. I am forever a sacrifice to those who serve their True Guru.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	KiV drgh pYnweIAY muiK hir nwm invwsu ]3] (21-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kharh dargeh painaa-ee-ai mukh har naam nivaas. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	They are dressed in robes of honor in the Court of the Lord; the Name of the Lord is on their lips. ||3||
RECORD	para 896	jh dyKw qh riv rhy isv skqI kw mylu ] (21-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jah daykhaa tah rav rahay siv saktee kaa mayl. Wherever I look, I see the Lord pervading there, in the union of Shiva and Shakti, of consciousness and matter.
RECORD	para 897	iqRhu gux bMDI dyhurI jo AwieAw jig so Kylu ] (21-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tarihu gun banDhee dayhuree jo aa-i-aa jag so khayl. The three qualities hold the body in bondage; whoever comes into the world is subject to their play.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	ivjogI duiK ivCuVy mnmuiK lhih n mylu ]4] (21-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vijogee dukh vichhurhay manmukh laheh na mayl. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Those who separate themselves from the Lord wander lost in misery. The self-willed manmukhs do not attain union with Him. ||4||
WHEN	para 899	mnu bYrwgI Gir vsY sc BY rwqw hoie ] (21-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man bairaagee ghar vasai sach bhai raataa ho-ay. If the mind becomes balanced and detached, and comes to dwell in its own true home, imbued with the Fear of God,
REQUIRE	para 900	igAwn mhwrsu BogvY bwhuiV BUK n hoie ] (21-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gi-aan mahaaras bhogvai baahurh bhookh na ho-ay. then it enjoys the essence of supreme spiritual wisdom; it shall never feel hunger again.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	nwnk iehu mnu mwir imlu BI iPir duKu n hoie ]5]18] (21-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak ih man maar mil bhee fir dukh na ho-ay. ||5||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	18|| O Nanak, conquer and subdue this mind; meet with the Lord, and you shall never again suffer in pain. ||5||18||
DEFINE	para 903	eyhu mno mUrKu loBIAw loBy lgw luoBwnu ] (21-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ayhu mano moorakh lobhee-aa lobhay lagaa lobhaan. This foolish mind is greedy; through greed, it becomes even more attached to greed.
RECORD	para 904	sbid n BIjY swkqw durmiq Awvnu jwnu ] (21-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad na bheejai saaktaa durmat aavan jaan. The evil-minded shaaktas, the faithless cynics, are not attuned to the Shabad; they come and go in reincarnation.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	swDU sqguru jy imlY qw pweIAY guxI inDwnu ]1] (21-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saaDhoo satgur jay milai taa paa-ee-ai gunee niDhaan. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	One who meets with the Holy True Guru finds the Treasure of Excellence. ||1||
WHEN	para 906	mn ry haumY Coif gumwnu ] (21-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man ray ha-umai chhod gumaan. O mind, renounce your egotistical pride.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	hir guru srvru syiv qU pwvih drgh mwnu ]1] rhwau ] (21-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har gur sarvar sayv too paavahi dargeh maan. ||1||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Serve the Lord, the Guru, the Sacred Pool, and you shall be honored in the Court of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 908	rwm nwmu jip idnsu rwiq gurmuiK hir Dnu jwnu ] (21-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) raam naam jap dinas raat gurmukh har Dhan jaan. Chant the Name of the Lord day and night; become Gurmukh, and know the Wealth of the Lord.
UPHOLD	para 909	siB suK hir rs Bogxy sMq sBw imil igAwnu ] (21-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabh sukh har ras bhognay sant sabhaa mil gi-aan. All comforts and peace, and the Essence of the Lord, are enjoyed by acquiring spiritual wisdom in the Society of the Saints.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	iniq Aihinis hir pRBu syivAw sqguir dIAw nwmu ]2] (21-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nit ahinis har parabh sayvi-aa satgur dee-aa naam. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Day and night, continually serve the Lord God; the True Guru has given the Naam. ||2||
REQUIRE	para 911	kUkr kUVu kmweIAY gur inMdw pcY pcwnu ] (21-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kookar koorh kamaa-ee-ai gur nindaa pachai pachaan. Those who practice falsehood are dogs; those who slander the Guru shall burn in their own fire.
REQUIRE	para 912	Brmy BUlw duKu Gxo jmu mwir krY Kulhwnu ] (21-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bharmay bhoolaa dukh ghano jam maar karai khulhaan. They wander lost and confused, deceived by doubt, suffering in terrible pain. The Messenger of Death shall beat them to a pulp.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	mnmuiK suKu n pweIAY gurmuiK suKu suBwnu ]3] (21-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manmukh sukh na paa-ee-ai gurmukh sukh subhaan. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	The self-willed manmukhs find no peace, while the Gurmukhs are wondrously joyful. ||3||
RECORD	para 914	AYQY DMDu iptweIAY scu ilKqu prvwnu ] (21-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aithai DhanDh pitaa-ee-ai sach likhat parvaan. In this world, people are engrossed in false pursuits, but in the world hereafter, only the account of your true actions is accepted.
DEFINE	para 915	hir sjxu guru syvdw gur krxI prDwnu ] (21-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har sajan gur sayvdaa gur karnee parDhaan. The Guru serves the Lord, His Intimate Friend. The Guru's actions are supremely exalted.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	nwnk nwmu n vIsrY krim scY nIswxu ]4]19] (21-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak naam na veesrai karam sachai neesaan. ||4||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	19|| O Nanak, never forget the Naam, the Name of the Lord; the True Lord shall bless you with His Mark of Grace. ||4||19||
DEFINE	para 918	ieku iqlu ipAwrw vIsrY rogu vfw mn mwih ] (21-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ik til pi-aaraa veesrai rog vadaa man maahi. Forgetting the Beloved, even for a moment, the mind is afflicted with terrible diseases.
WHEN	para 919	ikau drgh piq pweIAY jw hir n vsY mn mwih ] (21-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ki-o dargeh pat paa-ee-ai jaa har na vasai man maahi. How can honor be attained in His Court, if the Lord does not dwell in the mind?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	guir imilAY suKu pweIAY Agin mrY gux mwih ]1] (21-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur mili-ai sukh paa-ee-ai agan marai gun maahi. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	Meeting with the Guru, peace is found. The fire is extinguished in His Glorious Praises. ||1||
RECORD	para 921	mn ry Aihinis hir gux swir ] (21-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man ray ahinis har gun saar. O mind, enshrine the Praises of the Lord, day and night.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ijn iKnu plu nwmu n vIsrY qy jn ivrly sMswir ]1] rhwau ] (21-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jin khin pal naam na veesrai tay jan virlay sansaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. One who does not forget the Naam, for a moment or even an instant-how rare is such a person in this world! ||1||Pause||
WHEN	para 923	joqI joiq imlweIAY surqI suriq sMjogu ] (21-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jotee jot milaa-ee-ai surtee surat sanjog. When one's light merges into the Light, and one's intuitive consciousness is joined with the Intuitive Consciousness,
RECORD	para 924	ihMsw haumY gqu gey nwhI shsw sogu ] (21-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) hinsaa ha-umai gat ga-ay naahee sahsaa sog. then one's cruel and violent instincts and egotism depart, and skepticism and sorrow are taken away.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	gurmuiK ijsu hir min vsY iqsu myly guru sMjogu ]2] (21-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh jis har man vasai tis maylay gur sanjog. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	The Lord abides within the mind of the Gurmukh, who merges in the Lord's Union, through the Guru. ||2||
WHEN	para 926	kwieAw kwmix jy krI Bogy Bogxhwru ] (21-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa kaaman jay karee bhogay bhoganhaar. If I surrender my body like a bride, the Enjoyer will enjoy me.
DEFINE	para 927	iqsu isau nyhu n kIjeI jo dIsY clxhwru ] (21-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tis si-o nayhu na keej-ee jo deesai chalanhaar. Do not make love with one who is just a passing show.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	gurmuiK rvih sohwgxI so pRBu syj Bqwru ]3] (21-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh raveh sohaaganee so parabh sayj bhataar. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	The Gurmukh is ravished like the pure and happy bride on the Bed of God, her Husband. ||3||
RECORD	para 930	cwry Agin invwir mru gurmuiK hir jlu pwie ] (22-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) chaaray agan nivaar mar gurmukh har jal paa-ay. The Gurmukh puts out the four fires, with the Water of the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 931	AMqir kmlu pRgwisAw AMimRqu BirAw AGwie ] (22-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) antar kamal pargaasi-aa amrit bhari-aa aghaa-ay. The lotus blossoms deep within the heart, and filled with Ambrosial Nectar, one is satisfied.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	nwnk sqguru mIqu kir scu pwvih drgh jwie ]4]20] (22-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak satgur meet kar sach paavahi dargeh jaa-ay. ||4||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	20|| O Nanak, make the True Guru your friend; going to His Court, you shall obtain the True Lord. ||4||20||
RECORD	para 934	hir hir jphu ipAwirAw gurmiq ly hir boil ] (22-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har har japahu pi-aari-aa gurmat lay har bol. Meditate on the Lord, Har, Har, O my beloved; follow the Guru's Teachings, and speak of the Lord.
WHEN	para 935	mnu sc ksvtI lweIAY qulIAY pUrY qoil ] (22-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man sach kasvatee laa-ee-ai tulee-ai poorai tol. Apply the Touchstone of Truth to your mind, and see if it comes up to its full weight.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	kImiq iknY n pweIAY ird mwxk moil Amoil ]1] (22-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) keemat kinai na paa-ee-ai rid maanak mol amol. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	No one has found the worth of the ruby of the heart; its value cannot be estimated. ||1||
DEFINE	para 937	BweI ry hir hIrw gur mwih ] (22-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaa-ee ray har heeraa gur maahi. O Siblings of Destiny, the Diamond of the Lord is within the Guru.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	sqsMgiq sqguru pweIAY Aihinis sbid slwih ]1] rhwau ] (22-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) satsangat satgur paa-ee-ai ahinis sabad salaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. The True Guru is found in the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation. Day and night, praise the Word of His Shabad. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 939	scu vKru Dnu rwis lY pweIAY gur prgwis ] (22-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sach vakhar Dhan raas lai paa-ee-ai gur pargaas. The True Merchandise, Wealth and Capital are obtained through the Radiant Light of the Guru.
RECORD	para 940	ijau Agin mrY jil pwieAY iqau iqRsnw dwsin dwis ] (22-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o agan marai jal paa-i-ai ti-o tarisnaa daasan daas. Just as fire is extinguished by pouring on water, desire becomes the slave of the Lord's slaves.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	jm jMdwru n lgeI ieau Baujlu qrY qrwis ]2] (22-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jam jandaar na lag-ee i-o bha-ojal tarai taraas. ||2||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	The Messenger of Death will not touch you; in this way, you shall cross over the terrifying world-ocean, carrying others across with you. ||2||
DEFINE	para 942	gurmuiK kUVu n BwveI sic rqy sc Bwie ] (22-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh koorh na bhaav-ee sach ratay sach bhaa-ay. The Gurmukhs do not like falsehood. They are imbued with Truth; they love only Truth.
DEFINE	para 943	swkq scu n BwveI kUVY kUVI pWie ] (22-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saakat sach na bhaav-ee koorhai koorhee paaN-ay. The shaaktas, the faithless cynics, do not like the Truth; false are the foundations of the false.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	sic rqy guir myilAY scy sic smwie ]3] (22-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sach ratay gur mayli-ai sachay sach samaa-ay. ||3||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Imbued with Truth, you shall meet the Guru. The true ones are absorbed into the True Lord. ||3||
DEFINE	para 945	mn mih mwxku lwlu nwmu rqnu pdwrQu hIru ] (22-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man meh maanak laal naam ratan padaarath heer. Within the mind are emeralds and rubies, the Jewel of the Naam, treasures and diamonds.
RECORD	para 946	scu vKru Dnu nwmu hY Git Git gihr gMBIru ] (22-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sach vakhar Dhan naam hai ghat ghat gahir gambheer. The Naam is the True Merchandise and Wealth; in each and every heart, His Presence is deep and profound.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	nwnk gurmuiK pweIAY dieAw kry hir hIru ]4]21] (22-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh paa-ee-ai da-i-aa karay har heer. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	21|| O Nanak, the Gurmukh finds the Diamond of the Lord, by His Kindness and Compassion. ||4||21||
ALLOW	para 949	Brmy Bwih n ivJvY jy BvY idsMqr dysu ] (22-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bharmay bhaahi na vijhvai jay bhavai disantar days. The fire of doubt is not extinguished, even by wandering through foreign lands and countries.
DEFINE	para 950	AMqir mYlu n auqrY iDRgu jIvxu iDRgu vysu ] (22-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) antar mail na utrai Dharig jeevan Dharig vays. If inner filth is not removed, one's life is cursed, and one's clothes are cursed.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	horu ikqY Bgiq n hoveI ibnu siqgur ky aupdys ]1] (22-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) hor kitai bhagat na hova-ee bin satgur kay updays. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	There is no other way to perform devotional worship, except through the Teachings of the True Guru. ||1||
RECORD	para 952	mn ry gurmuiK Agin invwir ] (22-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man ray gurmukh agan nivaar. O mind, become Gurmukh, and extinguish the fire within.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	gur kw kihAw min vsY haumY iqRsnw mwir ]1] rhwau ] (22-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur kaa kahi-aa man vasai ha-umai tarisnaa maar. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Let the Words of the Guru abide within your mind; let egotism and desires die. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 954	mnu mwxku inrmolu hY rwm nwim piq pwie ] (22-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man maanak nirmol hai raam naam pat paa-ay. The jewel of the mind is priceless; through the Name of the Lord, honor is obtained.
RECORD	para 955	imil sqsMgiq hir pweIAY gurmuiK hir ilv lwie ] (22-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mil satsangat har paa-ee-ai gurmukh har liv laa-ay. Join the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation, and find the Lord. The Gurmukh embraces love for the Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Awpu gieAw suKu pwieAw imil sllY sll smwie ]2] (22-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aap ga-i-aa sukh paa-i-aa mil sallai salal samaa-ay. ||2||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Give up your selfishness, and you shall find peace; like water mingling with water, you shall merge in absorption. ||2||
RECORD	para 957	ijin hir hir nwmu n cyiqE su Aauguix AwvY jwie ] (22-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jin har har naam na chayti-o so a-ogun aavai jaa-ay. Those who have not contemplated the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, are unworthy; they come and go in reincarnation.
RECORD	para 958	ijsu sqguru purKu n ByitE su Baujil pcY pcwie ] (22-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jis satgur purakh na bhayti-o so bha-ojal pachai pachaa-ay. One who has not met with the True Guru, the Primal Being, is bothered and bewildered in the terrifying world-ocean.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	iehu mwxku jIau inrmolu hY ieau kaufI bdlY jwie ]3] (22-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ih maanak jee-o nirmol hai i-o ka-udee badlai jaa-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	This jewel of the soul is priceless, and yet it is being squandered like this, in exchange for a mere shell. ||3||
DEFINE	para 960	ijMnw sqguru ris imlY sy pUry purK sujwx ] (22-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jinna satgur ras milai say pooray purakh sujaan. Those who joyfully meet with the True Guru are perfectly fulfilled and wise.
RECORD	para 961	gur imil Baujlu lµGIAY drgh piq prvwxu ] (22-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur mil bha-ojal langhee-ai dargeh pat parvaan. Meeting with the Guru, they cross over the terrifying world-ocean. In the Court of the Lord, they are honored and approved.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	nwnk qy muK aujly Duin aupjY sbdu nIswxu ]4]22] (22-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak tay mukh ujlay Dhun upjai sabad neesaan. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	22|| O Nanak, their faces are radiant; the Music of the Shabad, the Word of God, wells up within them. ||4||22||
RECORD	para 964	vxju krhu vxjwirho vKru lyhu smwil ] (22-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vanaj karahu vanjaariho vakhar layho samaal. Make your deals, dealers, and take care of your merchandise.
RECORD	para 965	qYsI vsqu ivswhIAY jYsI inbhY nwil ] (22-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) taisee vasat visaahee-ai jaisee nibhai naal. Buy that object which will go along with you.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	AgY swhu sujwxu hY lYsI vsqu smwil ]1] (22-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) agai saahu sujaan hai laisee vasat samaal. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	In the next world, the All-knowing Merchant will take this object and care for it. ||1||
RECORD	para 967	BweI ry rwmu khhu icqu lwie ] (22-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaa-ee ray raam kahhu chit laa-ay. O Siblings of Destiny, chant the Lord's Name, and focus your consciousness on Him.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	hir jsu vKru lY clhu shu dyKY pqIAwie ]1] rhwau ] (22-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har jas vakhar lai chalhu saho daykhai patee-aa-ay. ||1||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Take the Merchandise of the Lord's Praises with you. Your Husband Lord shall see this and approve. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 970	ijnw rwis n scu hY ikau iqnw suKu hoie ] (23-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jinaa raas na sach hai ki-o tinaa sukh ho-ay. Those who do not have the Assets of Truth-how can they find peace?
RECORD	para 971	KotY vxij vxMijAY mnu qnu Kotw hoie ] (23-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khotai vanaj vananji-ai man tan khotaa ho-ay. By dealing their deals of falsehood, their minds and bodies become false.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	PwhI PwQy imrg ijau dUKu Gxo inq roie ]2] (23-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) faahee faathay mirag ji-o dookh ghano nit ro-ay. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Like the deer caught in the trap, they suffer in terrible agony; they continually cry out in pain. ||2||
UPHOLD	para 973	Koty poqY nw pvih iqn hir gur drsu n hoie ] (23-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khotay potai naa paveh tin har gur daras na ho-ay. The counterfeit coins are not put into the Treasury; they do not obtain the Blessed Vision of the Lord-Guru.
RECORD	para 974	Koty jwiq n piq hY Koit n sIJis koie ] (23-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khotay jaat na pat hai khot na seejhas ko-ay. The false ones have no social status or honor. No one succeeds through falsehood.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Koty Kotu kmwvxw Awie gieAw piq Koie ]3] (23-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khotay khot kamaavanaa aa-ay ga-i-aa pat kho-ay. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Practicing falsehood again and again, people come and go in reincarnation, and forfeit their honor. ||3||
RECORD	para 976	nwnk mnu smJweIAY gur kY sbid swlwh ] (23-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak man samjaa-ee-ai gur kai sabad saalaah. O Nanak, instruct your mind through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, and praise the Lord.
DEFINE	para 977	rwm nwm rMig riqAw Bwru n Brmu iqnwh ] (23-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) raam naam rang rati-aa bhaar na bharam tinaah. Those who are imbued with the love of the Name of the Lord are not loaded down by doubt.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	hir jip lwhw Aglw inrBau hir mn mwh ]4]23] (23-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har jap laahaa aglaa nirbha-o har man maah. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	23|| Those who chant the Name of the Lord earn great profits; the Fearless Lord abides within their minds. ||4||23||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 2	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 2 ] (23-5)
RECORD	para 979	sireeraag mehlaa 1 ghar 2. Siree Raag, First Mehl, Second House:
DEFINE	para 980	Dnu jobnu Aru PulVw nwTIAVy idn cwir ] (23-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) Dhan joban ar fulrhaa naathee-arhay din chaar. Wealth, the beauty of youth and flowers are guests for only a few days.
