RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v4	O Nanak, meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord, the Support of all beings. ||4||
RECORD	para 1246	sareeraag mehlaa 3. Siree Raag, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 1247	mnmuKu moih ivAwipAw bYrwgu audwsI n hoie ] (29-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh mohi vi-aapi-aa bairaag udaasee na ho-ay. The self-willed manmukhs are engrossed in emotional attachment; they are not balanced or detached.
RECORD	para 1248	sbdu n cInY sdw duKu hir drgih piq Koie ] (29-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabad na cheenai sadaa dukh har dargahi pat kho-ay. They do not comprehend the Word of the Shabad. They suffer in pain forever, and lose their honor in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	haumY gurmuiK KoeIAY nwim rqy suKu hoie ]1] (29-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ha-umai gurmukh kho-ee-ai naam ratay sukh ho-ay. ||1||
RECORD	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	The Gurmukhs shed their ego; attuned to the Naam, they find peace. ||1||
DEFINE	para 1250	myry mn Aihinis pUir rhI inq Awsw ] (29-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) mayray man ahinis poor rahee nit aasaa. O my mind, day and night, you are always full of wishful hopes.
RECORD	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	sqguru syiv mohu prjlY Gr hI mwih audwsw ]1] rhwau ] (29-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur sayv moh parjalai ghar hee maahi udaasaa. ||1||
REQUIRE	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Serve the True Guru, and your emotional attachment shall be totally burnt away; remain detached within the home of your heart. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 1252	gurmuiK krm kmwvY ibgsY hir bYrwgu Anµdu ] (29-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmukh karam kamaavai bigsai har bairaag anand. The Gurmukhs do good deeds and blossom forth; balanced and detached in the Lord, they are in ecstasy.
RECORD	para 1253	Aihinis Bgiq kry idnu rwqI haumY mwir incMdu ] (29-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ahinis bhagat karay din raatee ha-umai maar nichand. Night and day, they perform devotional worship, day and night; subduing their ego, they are carefree.
RECORD	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v2	vfY Bwig sqsMgiq pweI hir pwieAw shij Anµdu ]2] (29-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) vadai bhaag satsangat paa-ee har paa-i-aa sahj anand. ||2||
RECORD	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v2	By great good fortune, I found the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation; I have found the Lord, with intuitive ease and ecstasy. ||2||
DEFINE	para 1255	so swDU bYrwgI soeI ihrdY nwmu vswey ] (29-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) so saaDhoo bairaagee so-ee hirdai naam vasaa-ay. That person is a Holy Saadhu, and a renouncer of the world, whose heart is filled with the Naam.
RECORD	para 1256	AMqir lwig n qwmsu mUly ivchu Awpu gvwey ] (29-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) antar laag na taamas moolay vichahu aap gavaa-ay. His inner being is not touched by anger or dark energies at all; he has lost his selfishness and conceit.
RECORD	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v3	nwmu inDwnu sqgurU idKwilAw hir rsu pIAw AGwey ]3] (29-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naam niDhaan satguroo dikhaali-aa har ras pee-aa aghaa-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v3	The True Guru has revealed to him the Treasure of the Naam, the Name of the Lord; he drinks in the Sublime Essence of the Lord, and is satisfied. ||3||
RECORD	para 1258	ijin iknY pwieAw swDsMgqI pUrY Bwig bYrwig ] (29-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jin kinai paa-i-aa saaDhsangtee poorai bhaag bairaag. Whoever has found it, has done so in the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy. Through perfect good fortune, such balanced detachment is attained.
RECORD	para 1259	mnmuK iPrih n jwxih sqguru haumY AMdir lwig ] (29-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh fireh na jaaneh satgur ha-umai andar laag. The self-willed manmukhs wander around lost, but they do not know the True Guru. They are inwardly attached to egotism.
RECORD	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v4	nwnk sbid rqy hir nwim rMgwey ibnu BY kyhI lwig ]4]8]41] (29-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak sabad ratay har naam rangaa-ay bin bhai kayhee laag. ||4||
DEFINE	sRIrwgu mhlw 3 v4	O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Shabad are dyed in the Color of the Lord's Name. Without the Fear of God, how can they retain this Color? ||4||
DEFINE	para 1262	Gr hI saudw pweIAY AMqir sB vQu hoie ] (29-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ghar hee sa-udaa paa-ee-ai antar sabh vath ho-ay. Within the home of your own inner being, the merchandise is obtained. All commodities are within.
RECORD	para 1263	iKnu iKnu nwmu smwlIAY gurmuiK pwvY koie ] (29-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) khin khin naam samaalee-ai gurmukh paavai ko-ay. Each and every moment, dwell on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; the Gurmukhs obtain it.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	nwmu inDwnu AKutu hY vfBwig prwpiq hoie ]1] (29-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naam niDhaan akhut hai vadbhaag paraapat ho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	The Treasure of the Naam is inexhaustible. By great good fortune, it is obtained. ||1||
RECORD	para 1265	myry mn qij inMdw haumY AhMkwru ] (29-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) mayray man taj nindaa ha-umai aha Nkaar. O my mind, give up slander, egotism and arrogance.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	hir jIau sdw iDAwie qU gurmuiK eykMkwru ]1] rhwau ] (30-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har jee-o sadaa Dhi-aa-ay too gurmukh aykankaar. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Become Gurmukh, and meditate forever on the Dear Lord, the One and Only Creator. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 1268	gurmuKw ky muK aujly gur sbdI bIcwir ] (30-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmukhaa kay mukh ujlay gur sabdee beechaar. The faces of the Gurmukhs are radiant and bright; they reflect on the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
