RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v2	They enjoy their Husband Lord forever, and their life-night passes in the most blissful peace. ||2||
UPHOLD	para 1597	igAwn ivhUxI ipr muqIAw iprmu n pwieAw jwie ] (38-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gi-aan vihoonee pir mutee-aa piram na paa-i-aa jaa-ay. She is utterly lacking in spiritual wisdom; she is abandoned by her Husband Lord. She cannot obtain His Love.
RECORD	para 1598	AigAwn mqI AMDyru hY ibnu ipr dyKy BuK n jwie ] (38-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) agi-aan matee anDhayr hai bin pir daykhay bhukh na jaa-ay. In the darkness of intellectual ignorance, she cannot see her Husband, and her hunger does not depart.
RECORD	para 1599	Awvhu imlhu shylIho mY ipru dyhu imlwie ] (38-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aavhu milhu sahayleeho mai pir dayh milaa-ay. Come and meet with me, my sister soul-brides, and unite me with my Husband.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v3	pUrY Bwig siqguru imlY ipru pwieAw sic smwie ]3] (38-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) poorai bhaag satgur milai pir paa-i-aa sach samaa-ay. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v3	She who meets the True Guru, by perfect good fortune, finds her Husband; she is absorbed in the True One. ||3||
RECORD	para 1601	sy shIAw sohwgxI ijn kau ndir kryie ] (38-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) say sahee-aa sohaaganee jin ka-o nadar karay-i. Those upon whom He casts His Glance of Grace become His happy soul-brides.
RECORD	para 1602	Ksmu pCwxih Awpxw qnu mnu AwgY dyie ] (38-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) khasam pachhaaneh aapnaa tan man aagai day-ay. One who recognizes her Lord and Master places her body and mind in offering before Him.
DEFINE	para 1603	Gir vru pwieAw Awpxw haumY dUir kryie ] (38-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ghar var paa-i-aa aapnaa ha-umai door karay-i. Within her own home, she finds her Husband Lord; her egotism is dispelled.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v4	nwnk soBwvMqIAw sohwgxI Anidnu Bgiq kryie ]4]28]61] (38-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak sobhaavantee-aa sohaaganee an-din bhagat karay-i. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v4	O Nanak, the happy soul-brides are embellished and exalted; night and day they are absorbed in devotional worship. ||4||
RECORD	para 1606	ieik ipru rwvih Awpxw hau kY dir pUCau jwie ] (38-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ik pir raaveh aapnaa ha-o kai dar poochha-o jaa-ay. Some enjoy their Husband Lord; unto whose door should I go to ask for Him?
ALLOW	para 1607	siqguru syvI Bwau kir mY ipru dyhu imlwie ] (38-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur sayvee bhaa-o kar mai pir dayh milaa-ay. I serve my True Guru with love, that He may lead me to Union with my Husband Lord.
DEFINE	para 1608	sBu aupwey Awpy vyKY iksu nyVY iksu dUir ] (38-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabh upaa-ay aapay vaykhai kis nayrhai kis door. He created all, and He Himself watches over us. Some are close to Him, and some are far away.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	ijin ipru sMgy jwixAw ipru rwvy sdw hdUir ]1] (38-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jin pir sangay jaani-aa pir raavay sadaa hadoor. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	She who knows her Husband Lord to be always with her, enjoys His Constant Presence. ||1||
REQUIRE	para 1610	muMDy qU clu gur kY Bwie ] (38-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) munDhay too chal gur kai bhaa-ay. O woman, you must walk in harmony with the Guru's Will.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	Anidnu rwvih ipru Awpxw shjy sic smwie ]1] rhwau ] (38-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) an-din raaveh pir aapnaa sehjay sach samaa-ay. ||1||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Night and day, you shall enjoy your Husband, and you shall intuitively merge into the True One. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 1612	sbid rqIAw sohwgxI scY sbid sIgwir ] (38-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabad ratee-aa sohaaganee sachai sabad seegaar. Attuned to the Shabad, the happy soul-brides are adorned with the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 1613	hir vru pwiein Gir AwpxY gur kY hyiq ipAwir ] (38-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har var paa-in ghar aapnai gur kai hayt pi-aar. Within their own home, they obtain the Lord as their Husband, with love for the Guru.
RECORD	para 1614	syj suhwvI hir rMig rvY Bgiq Bry BMfwr ] (38-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sayj suhaavee har rang ravai bhagat bharay bhandaar. Upon her beautiful and cozy bed, she enjoys the Love of her Lord. She is overflowing with the treasure of devotion.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v2	so pRBu pRIqmu min vsY ij sBsY dyie ADwru ]2] (38-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) so parabh pareetam man vasai je sabhsai day-ay aDhaar. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v2	That Beloved God abides in her mind; He gives His Support to all. ||2||
RECORD	para 1616	ipru swlwhin Awpxw iqn kY hau sd bilhwrY jwau ] (38-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) pir saalaahan aapnaa tin kai ha-o sad balihaarai jaa-o. I am forever a sacrifice to those who praise their Husband Lord.
RECORD	para 1617	mnu qnu ArpI isru dyeI iqn kY lwgw pwie ] (38-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) man tan arpee sir day-ee tin kai laagaa paa-ay. I dedicate my mind and body to them, and give my head as well; I fall at their feet.
RECORD	para 1618	ijnI ieku pCwixAw dUjw Bwau cukwie ] (38-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jinee ik pachhaani-aa doojaa bhaa-o chukaa-ay. Those who recognize the One renounce the love of duality.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v3	gurmuiK nwmu pCwxIAY nwnk sic smwie ]3]29]62] (38-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmukh naam pachhaanee-ai naanak sach samaa-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v3	The Gurmukh recognizes the Naam, O Nanak, and is absorbed into the True One. ||3||
DEFINE	para 1621	hir jI scw scu qU sBu ikCu qyrY cIrY ] (38-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har jee sachaa sach too sabh kichh tayrai cheerai. O Dear Lord, You are the Truest of the True. All things are in Your Power.
RECORD	para 1622	lK caurwsIh qrsdy iPry ibnu gur Byty pIrY ] (38-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) lakh cha-oraaseeh tarasday firay bin gur bhaytay peerai. The 8.4 million species of beings wander around searching for You, but without the Guru, they do not find You.
WHEN	para 1623	hir jIau bKsy bKis ley sUK sdw srIrY ] (38-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har jee-o bakhsay bakhas la-ay sookh sadaa sareerai. When the Dear Lord grants His Forgiveness, this human body finds lasting peace.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	gur prswdI syv krI scu gihr gMBIrY ]1] (38-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee sayv karee sach gahir gambheerai. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	By Guru's Grace, I serve the True One, who is Immeasurably Deep and Profound. ||1||
REQUIRE	para 1625	mn myry nwim rqy suKu hoie ] (38-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) man mayray naam ratay sukh ho-ay. O my mind, attuned to the Naam, you shall find peace.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	gurmqI nwmu slwhIAY dUjw Avru n koie ]1] rhwau ] (38-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmatee naam salaahee-ai doojaa avar na ko-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Follow the Guru's Teachings, and praise the Naam; there is no other at all. ||1||Pause||
UPHOLD	para 1627	Drm rwie no hukmu hY bih scw Drmu bIcwir ] (38-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) Dharam raa-ay no hukam hai bahi sachaa Dharam beechaar. The Righteous Judge of Dharma, by the Hukam of God's Command, sits and administers True Justice.
DEFINE	para 1628	dUjY Bwie dustu Awqmw Ehu qyrI srkwr ] (38-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay dusat aatmaa oh tayree sarkaar. Those evil souls, ensnared by the love of duality, are subject to Your Command.
RECORD	para 1629	AiDAwqmI hir gux qwsu min jpih eyku murwir ] (38-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aDhi-aatmee har gun taas man jaapeh ayk muraar. The souls on their spiritual journey chant and meditate within their minds on the One Lord, the Treasure of Excellence.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v2	iqn kI syvw Drm rwie krY DMnu svwrxhwru ]2] (39-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) tin kee sayvaa Dharam raa-ay karai Dhan savaaranhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 3 v2	The Righteous Judge of Dharma serves them; blessed is the Lord who adorns them. ||2||
