UPHOLD	para 1696	mnu rMghu vfBwgIho guru quTw kry pswau ] (40-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) man rangahu vadbhaageeho gur tuthaa karay pasaa-o. Let your minds be imbued with His Love, O blessed and fortunate ones. By His Pleasure, the Guru bestows His Gifts.
RECORD	para 1697	guru nwmu idRVwey rMg isau hau siqgur kY bil jwau ] (40-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) gur naam drirh-aa-ay rang si-o ha-o satgur kai bal jaa-o. The Guru has lovingly implanted the Naam, the Name of the Lord, within me; I am a sacrifice to the True Guru.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 4 v2	ibnu siqgur hir nwmu n lBeI lK kotI krm kmwau ]2] (40-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) bin satgur har naam na labh-ee lakh kotee karam kamaa-o. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 4 v2	Without the True Guru, the Name of the Lord is not found, even though people may perform hundreds of thousands, even millions of rituals. ||2||
RECORD	para 1699	ibnu Bwgw siqguru nw imlY Gir bYiTAw inkit inq pwis ] (40-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) bin bhaagaa satgur naa milai ghar baithi-aa nikat nit paas. Without destiny, the True Guru is not found, even though He sits within the home of our own inner being, always near and close at hand.
DEFINE	para 1700	AMqir AigAwn duKu Brmu hY ivic pVdw dUir peIAwis ] (40-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) antar agi-aan dukh bharam hai vich parh-daa door pa-ee-aas. There is ignorance within, and the pain of doubt, like a separating screen.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 4 v3	ibnu siqgur Byty kMcnu nw QIAY mnmuKu lohu bUfw byVI pwis ]3] (40-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) bin satgur bhaytay kanchan naa thee-ai manmukh lohu boodaa bayrhee paas. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 4 v3	Without meeting with the True Guru, no one is transformed into gold. The self-willed manmukh sinks like iron, while the boat is very close. ||3||
DEFINE	para 1702	siqguru boihQu hir nwv hY ikqu ibiD ciVAw jwie ] (40-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) satgur bohith har naav hai kit biDh charhi-aa jaa-ay. The Boat of the True Guru is the Name of the Lord. How can we climb on board?
RECORD	para 1703	siqgur kY BwxY jo clY ivic boihQ bYTw Awie ] (40-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) satgur kai bhaanai jo chalai vich bohith baithaa aa-ay. One who walks in harmony with the True Guru's Will comes to sit in this Boat.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 4 v4	DMnu DMnu vfBwgI nwnkw ijnw siqguru ley imlwie ]4]3]67] (40-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 4) Dhan Dhan vadbhaagee naankaa jinaa satgur la-ay milaa-ay. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 4 v4	Blessed, blessed are those very fortunate ones, O Nanak, who are united with the Lord through the True Guru. ||4||
