RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 5 v4	Nanak seeks the Sanctuary of the Guru, who does not die, or come and go in reincarnation. ||4||
RECORD	para 2209	<> siqgur pRswid ] (53-7) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw ] (53-8)
RECORD	para 2210	sireeraag mehlaa 1 ghar 1 asatpadee-aa. Siree Raag, First Mehl, First House, Ashtapadees:
RECORD	para 2211	AwiK AwiK mnu vwvxw ijau ijau jwpY vwie ] (53-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aakh aakh man vaavnaa ji-o ji-o jaapai vaa-ay. I speak and chant His Praises, vibrating the instrument of my mind. The more I know Him, the more I vibrate it.
DEFINE	para 2212	ijs no vwie suxweIAY so kyvfu ikqu Qwie ] (53-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jis no vaa-ay sunaa-ee-ai so kayvad kit thaa-ay. The One, unto whom we vibrate and sing-how great is He, and where is His Place?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v1	AwKx vwly jyqVy siB AwiK rhy ilv lwie ]1] (53-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aakhan vaalay jayt-rhay sabh aakh rahay liv laa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v1	Those who speak of Him and praise Him-they all continue speaking of Him with love. ||1||
DEFINE	para 2214	bwbw Alhu Agm Apwru ] (53-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) baabaa alhu agam apaar. O Baba, the Lord Allah is Inaccessible and Infinite.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v1	pwkI nweI pwk Qwie scw prvidgwru ]1] rhwau ] (53-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) paakee naa-ee paak thaa-ay sachaa paravdigaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v1	rahaa-o. Sacred is His Name, and Sacred is His Place. He is the True Cherisher. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 2216	qyrw hukmu n jwpI kyqVw iliK n jwxY koie ] (53-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tayraa hukam na jaapee kayt-rhaa likh na jaanai ko-ay. The extent of Your Command cannot be seen; no one knows how to write it.
WHEN	para 2217	jy sau swier mylIAih iqlu n pujwvih roie ] (53-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jay sa-o saa-ir maylee-ah til na pujaaveh ro-ay. Even if a hundred poets met together, they could not describe even a tiny bit of it.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v2	kImiq iknY n pweIAw siB suix suix AwKih soie ]2] (53-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) keemat kinai na paa-ee-aa sabh sun sun aakhahi so-ay. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v2	No one has found Your Value; they all merely write what they have heard again and again. ||2||
RECORD	para 2219	pIr pYkwmr swlk swdk suhdy Aauru shId ] (53-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) peer paikaamar saalak saadak suhday a-or saheed. The Pirs, the Prophets, the spiritual teachers, the faithful, the innocents and the martyrs,
RECORD	para 2220	syK mswiek kwjI mulw dir drvys rsId ] (53-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saykh masaa-ik kaajee mulaa dar darvays raseed. the Shaikhs, the mystics, the Qazis, the Mullahs and the Dervishes at His Door
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v3	brkiq iqn kau AglI pVdy rhin drUd ]3] (53-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) barkat tin ka-o aglee parh-day rahan darood. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v3	-they are blessed all the more as they continue reading their prayers in praise to Him. ||3||
WHEN	para 2222	puiC n swjy puiC n Fwhy puiC n dyvY lyie ] (53-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) puchh na saajay puchh na dhaahay puchh na dayvai lay-ay. He seeks no advice when He builds; He seeks no advice when He destroys. He seeks no advice while giving or taking.
RECORD	para 2223	AwpxI kudriq Awpy jwxY Awpy krxu kryie ] (53-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapnee kudrat aapay jaanai aapay karan karay-i. He alone knows His Creative Power; He Himself does all deeds.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v4	sBnw vyKY ndir kir jY BwvY qY dyie ]4] (53-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabhnaa vaykhai nadar kar jai bhaavai tai day-ay. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v4	He beholds all in His Vision. He gives to those with whom He is pleased. ||4||
DEFINE	para 2225	Qwvw nwv n jwxIAih nwvw kyvfu nwau ] (53-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) thaavaa naav na jaanee-ahi naavaa kayvad naa-o. His Place and His Name are not known, no one knows how great is His Name.
DEFINE	para 2226	ijQY vsY myrw pwiqswhu so kyvfu hY Qwau ] (53-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jithai vasai mayraa paatisaahu so kayvad hai thaa-o. How great is that place where my Sovereign Lord dwells?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v5	AMbiV koie n skeI hau iks no puCix jwau ]5] (53-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ambarh ko-ay na sak-ee ha-o kis no puchhan jaa-o. ||5||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v5	No one can reach it; whom shall I go and ask? ||5||
WHEN	para 2228	vrnw vrn n BwvnI jy iksY vfw kryie ] (53-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) varnaa varan na bhaavnee jay kisai vadaa karay-i. One class of people does not like the other, when one has been made great.
DEFINE	para 2229	vfy hiQ vifAweIAw jY BwvY qY dyie ] (53-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vaday hath vadi-aa-ee-aa jai bhaavai tai day-ay. Greatness is only in His Great Hands; He gives to those with whom He is pleased.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v6	hukim svwry AwpxY csw n iFl kryie ]6] (53-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) hukam savaaray aapnai chasaa na dhil karay-i. ||6||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v6	By the Hukam of His Command, He Himself regenerates, without a moment's delay. ||6||
RECORD	para 2231	sBu ko AwKY bhuqu bhuqu lYxY kY vIcwir ] (53-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabh ko aakhai bahut bahut lainai kai veechaar. Everyone cries out, "More! More!", with the idea of receiving.
DEFINE	para 2232	kyvfu dwqw AwKIAY dy kY rihAw sumwir ] (53-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kayvad daataa aakhee-ai day kai rahi-aa sumaar. How great should we call the Giver? His Gifts are beyond estimation.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v7	nwnk qoit n AwveI qyry jugh jugh BMfwr ]7]1] (53-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak tot na aavee tayray jugah jugah bhandaar. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v7	1|| O Nanak, there is no deficiency; Your Storehouses are filled to overflowing, age after age. ||7||1||
RECORD	para 2234	mhlw 1 ] (53-19) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 2235	sBy kMq mhylIAw sglIAw krih sIgwru ] (53-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabhay kant mahaylee-aa saglee-aa karahi seegaar. All are brides of the Husband Lord; all decorate themselves for Him.
DEFINE	para 2237	gxq gxwvix AweIAw sUhw vysu ivkwru ] (54-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ganat ganaavan aa-ee-aa soohaa vays vikaar. But when the time comes to settle their accounts, their red robes are corrupt.
WHEN	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v1	pwKMif pRymu n pweIAY Kotw pwju KuAwru ]1] (54-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pakhand paraym na paa-ee-ai khotaa paaj khu-aar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v1	His Love is not obtained through hypocrisy. Her false coverings bring only ruin. ||1||
RECORD	para 2239	hir jIau ieau ipru rwvY nwir ] (54-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har jee-o i-o pir raavai naar. In this way, the Dear Husband Lord ravishes and enjoys His bride.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v1	quDu Bwvin sohwgxI ApxI ikrpw lYih svwir ]1] rhwau ] (54-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tuDh bhaavan sohaaganee apnee kirpaa laihi savaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v1	rahaa-o. The happy soul-bride is pleasing to You, Lord; by Your Grace, You adorn her. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 2241	gur sbdI sIgwrIAw qnu mnu ipr kY pwis ] (54-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur sabdee seegaaree-aa tan man pir kai paas. She is decorated with the Word of the Guru's Shabad; her mind and body belong to her Husband Lord.
RECORD	para 2242	duie kr joiV KVI qkY scu khY Ardwis ] (54-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) du-ay kar jorh kharhee takai sach kahai ardaas. With her palms pressed together, she stands, waiting on Him, and offers her True prayers to Him.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v2	lwil rqI sc BY vsI Bwie rqI rMig rwis ]2] (54-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) laal ratee sach bhai vasee bhaa-ay ratee rang raas. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v2	Dyed in the deep crimson of the Love of her Darling Lord, she dwells in the Fear of the True One. Imbued with His Love, she is dyed in the color of His Love. ||2||
DEFINE	para 2244	ipRA kI cyrI kWFIAY lwlI mwnY nwau ] (54-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pari-a kee chayree kaaNdhee-ai laalee maanai naa-o. She is said to be the hand-maiden of her Beloved Lord; His sweetheart surrenders to His Name.
DEFINE	para 2245	swcI pRIiq n quteI swcy myil imlwau ] (54-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saachee pareet na tut-ee saachay mayl milaa-o. True Love is never broken; she is united in Union with the True One.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v3	sbid rqI mnu vyiDAw hau sd bilhwrY jwau ]3] (54-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad ratee man vayDhi-aa ha-o sad balihaarai jaa-o. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v3	Attuned to the Word of the Shabad, her mind is pierced through. I am forever a sacrifice to Him. ||3||
REQUIRE	para 2247	sw Dn rMf n bYseI jy siqgur mwih smwie ] (54-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saa Dhan rand na bais-ee jay satgur maahi samaa-ay. That bride, who is absorbed into the True Guru, shall never become a widow.
FORBID	para 2248	ipru rIswlU nauqno swcau mrY n jwie ] (54-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pir reesaaloo na-otano saacha-o marai na jaa-ay. Her Husband Lord is Beautiful; His Body is forever fresh and new. The True One does not die, and shall not go.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v4	inq rvY sohwgxI swcI ndir rjwie ]4] (54-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nit ravai sohaaganee saachee nadar rajaa-ay. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v4	He continually enjoys His happy soul-bride; He casts His Gracious Glance of Truth upon her, and she abides in His Will. ||4||
DEFINE	para 2250	swcu DVI Dn mwfIAY kwpVu pRym sIgwru ] (54-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saach Dharhee Dhan maadee-ai kaaparh paraym seegaar. The bride braids her hair with Truth; her clothes are decorated with His Love.
DEFINE	para 2251	cMdnu cIiq vswieAw mMdru dsvw duAwru ] (54-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) chandan cheet vasaa-i-aa mandar dasvaa du-aar. Like the essence of sandalwood, He permeates her consciousness, and the Temple of the Tenth Gate is opened.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v5	dIpku sbid ivgwisAw rwm nwmu aur hwru ]5] (54-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) deepak sabad vigaasi-aa raam naam ur haar. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v5	The lamp of the Shabad is lit, and the Name of the Lord is her necklace. ||5||
DEFINE	para 2253	nwrI AMdir sohxI msqik mxI ipAwru ] (54-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naaree andar sohnee mastak manee pi-aar. She is the most beautiful among women; upon her forehead she wears the Jewel of the Lord's Love.
DEFINE	para 2254	soBw suriq suhwvxI swcY pRyim Apwr ] (54-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sobhaa surat suhaavanee saachai paraym apaar. Her glory and her wisdom are magnificent; her love for the Infinite Lord is True.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v6	ibnu ipr purKu n jwxeI swcy gur kY hyiq ipAwir ]6] (54-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin pir purakh na jaan-ee saachay gur kai hayt pi-aar. ||6||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v6	Other than her Beloved Lord, she knows no man. She enshrines love for the True Guru. ||6||
REQUIRE	para 2256	inis AMiDAwrI suqIey ikau ipr ibnu rYix ivhwie ] (54-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nis anDhi-aaree sutee-ay ki-o pir bin rain vihaa-ay. Asleep in the darkness of the night, how shall she pass her life-night without her Husband?
REQUIRE	para 2257	AMku jlau qnu jwlIAau mnu Dnu jil bil jwie ] (54-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ank jala-o tan jaalee-a-o man Dhan jal bal jaa-ay. Her limbs shall burn, her body shall burn, and her mind and wealth shall burn as well.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v7	jw Dn kMiq n rwvIAw qw ibrQw jobnu jwie ]7] (54-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jaa Dhan kant na raavee-aa taa birthaa joban jaa-ay. ||7||
WHEN	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v7	When the Husband does not enjoy His bride, then her youth passes away in vain. ||7||
DEFINE	para 2259	syjY kMq mhylVI sUqI bUJ n pwie ] (54-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sayjai kant mahaylrhee sootee boojh na paa-ay. The Husband is on the Bed, but the bride is asleep, and so she does not come to know Him.
DEFINE	para 2260	hau suqI ipru jwgxw iks kau pUCau jwie ] (54-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ha-o sutee pir jaagnaa kis ka-o poochha-o jaa-ay. While I am asleep, my Husband Lord is awake. Where can I go for advice?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v8	siqguir mylI BY vsI nwnk pRymu sKwie ]8]2] (54-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) satgur maylee bhai vasee naanak paraym sakhaa-ay. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 Gru 1 AstpdIAw v8	2|| The True Guru has led me to meet Him, and now I dwell in the Fear of God. O Nanak, His Love is always with me. ||8||2||
DEFINE	para 2263	Awpy gux Awpy kQY Awpy suix vIcwru ] (54-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay gun aapay kathai aapay sun veechaar. O Lord, You are Your Own Glorious Praise. You Yourself speak it; You Yourself hear it and contemplate it.
DEFINE	para 2264	Awpy rqnu priK qUM Awpy molu Apwru ] (54-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay ratan parakh tooN aapay mol apaar. You Yourself are the Jewel, and You are the Appraiser. You Yourself are of Infinite Value.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	swcau mwnu mhqu qUM Awpy dyvxhwru ]1] (54-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saacha-o maan mahat tooN aapay dayvanhaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	O True Lord, You are Honor and Glory; You Yourself are the Giver. ||1||
DEFINE	para 2266	hir jIau qUM krqw krqwru ] (54-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har jee-o tooN kartaa kartaar. O Dear Lord, You are the Creator and the Cause.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ijau BwvY iqau rwKu qUM hir nwmu imlY Awcwru ]1] rhwau ] (54-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o bhaavai ti-o raakh tooN har naam milai aachaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. If it is Your Will, please save and protect me; please bless me with the lifestyle of the Lord's Name. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 2268	Awpy hIrw inrmlw Awpy rMgu mjIT ] (54-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay heeraa nirmalaa aapay rang majeeth. You Yourself are the flawless diamond; You Yourself are the deep crimson color.
DEFINE	para 2269	Awpy moqI aUjlo Awpy Bgq bsITu ] (54-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay motee oojlo aapay bhagat baseeth. You Yourself are the perfect pearl; You Yourself are the devotee and the priest.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	gur kY sbid slwhxw Git Git fITu AfITu ]2] (54-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur kai sabad salaahnaa ghat ghat deeth adeeth. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, You are praised. In each and every heart, the Unseen is seen. ||2||
DEFINE	para 2271	Awpy swgru boihQw Awpy pwru Apwru ] (54-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay saagar bohithaa aapay paar apaar. You Yourself are the ocean and the boat. You Yourself are this shore, and the one beyond.
DEFINE	para 2272	swcI vwt sujwxu qUM sbid lGwvxhwru ] (54-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saachee vaat sujaan tooN sabad laghaavanhaar. O All-knowing Lord, You are the True Way. The Shabad is the Navigator to ferry us across.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	infirAw fru jwxIAY bwJu gurU gubwru ]3] (54-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nidri-aa dar jaanee-ai baajh guroo gubaar. ||3||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	One who does not fear God shall live in fear; without the Guru, there is only pitch darkness. ||3||
DEFINE	para 2274	AsiQru krqw dyKIAY horu kyqI AwvY jwie ] (54-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) asthir kartaa daykhee-ai hor kaytee aavai jaa-ay. The Creator alone is seen to be Eternal; all others come and go.
DEFINE	para 2275	Awpy inrmlu eyku qUM hor bMDI DMDY pwie ] (54-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay nirmal ayk too N hor banDhee DhanDhai paa-ay. Only You, Lord, are Immaculate and Pure. All others are bound up in worldly pursuits.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	guir rwKy sy aubry swcy isau ilv lwie ]4] (54-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur raakhay say ubray saachay si-o liv laa-ay. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Those who are protected by the Guru are saved. They are lovingly attuned to the True Lord. ||4||
RECORD	para 2278	hir jIau sbid pCwxIAY swic rqy gur vwik ] (55-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har jee-o sabad pachhaanee-ai saach ratay gur vaak. Through the Shabad, they recognize the Dear Lord; through the Guru's Word, they are attuned to Truth.
RECORD	para 2279	iqqu qin mYlu n lgeI sc Gir ijsu Eqwku ] (55-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tit tan mail na lag-ee sach ghar jis otaak. Filth does not stick to the body of one who has secured a dwelling in his True Home.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	ndir kry scu pweIAY ibnu nwvY ikAw swku ]5] (55-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nadar karay sach paa-ee-ai bin naavai ki-aa saak. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	When the Lord bestows His Glance of Grace, we obtain the True Name. Without the Name, who are our relatives? ||5||
DEFINE	para 2281	ijnI scu pCwixAw sy suKIey jug cwir ] (55-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jinee sach pachhaani-aa say sukhee-ay jug chaar. Those who have realized the Truth are at peace throughout the four ages.
RECORD	para 2282	haumY iqRsnw mwir kY scu riKAw aur Dwir ] (55-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ha-umai tarisnaa maar kai sach rakhi-aa ur Dhaar. Subduing their egotism and desires, they keep the True Name enshrined in their hearts.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	jg mih lwhw eyku nwmu pweIAY gur vIcwir ]6] (55-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jag meh laahaa ayk naam paa-ee-ai gur veechaar. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	In this world, the only real profit is the Name of the One Lord; it is earned by contemplating the Guru. ||6||
REQUIRE	para 2284	swcau vKru lwdIAY lwBu sdw scu rwis ] (55-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saacha-o vakhar laadee-ai laabh sadaa sach raas. Loading the Merchandise of the True Name, you shall gather in your profits forever with the Capital of Truth.
REQUIRE	para 2285	swcI drgh bYseI Bgiq scI Ardwis ] (55-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saachee dargeh bais-ee bhagat sachee ardaas. In the Court of the True One, you shall sit in truthful devotion and prayer.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	piq isau lyKw inbVY rwm nwmu prgwis ]7] (55-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pat si-o laykhaa nibrhai raam naam pargaas. ||7||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Your account shall be settled with honor, in the Radiant Light of the Name of the Lord. ||7||
DEFINE	para 2287	aUcw aUcau AwKIAY khau n dyiKAw jwie ] (55-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) oochaa oocha-o aakhee-ai kaha-o na daykhi-aa jaa-ay. The Lord is said to be the Highest of the High; no one can perceive Him.
RECORD	para 2288	jh dyKw qh eyku qUM siqguir dIAw idKwie ] (55-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jah daykhaa tah ayk tooN satgur dee-aa dikhaa-ay. Wherever I look, I see only You. The True Guru has inspired me to see You.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	joiq inrMqir jwxIAY nwnk shij suBwie ]8]3] (55-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jot nirantar jaanee-ai naanak sahj subhaa-ay. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	3|| The Divine Light within is revealed, O Nanak, through this intuitive understanding. ||8||3||
RECORD	para 2291	mCulI jwlu n jwixAw sru Kwrw Asgwhu ] (55-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) machhulee jaal na jaani-aa sar khaaraa asgaahu. The fish did not notice the net in the deep and salty sea.
RECORD	para 2292	Aiq isAwxI sohxI ikau kIqo vyswhu ] (55-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) at si-aanee sohnee ki-o keeto vaysaahu. It was so clever and beautiful, but why was it so confident?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	kIqy kwrix pwkVI kwlu n tlY isrwhu ]1] (55-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) keetay kaaran paakrhee kaal na talai siraahu. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	By its actions it was caught, and now death cannot be turned away from its head. ||1||
RECORD	para 2294	BweI ry ieau isir jwxhu kwlu ] (55-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaa-ee ray i-o sir jaanhu kaal. O Siblings of Destiny, just like this, see death hovering over your own heads!
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ijau mCI iqau mwxsw pvY AicMqw jwlu ]1] rhwau ] (55-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o machhee ti-o maansaa pavai achintaa jaal. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. People are just like this fish; unaware, the noose of death descends upon them. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 2296	sBu jgu bwDo kwl ko ibnu gur kwlu APwru ] (55-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabh jag baaDho kaal ko bin gur kaal afaar. The whole world is bound by death; without the Guru, death cannot be avoided.
DEFINE	para 2297	sic rqy sy aubry duibDw Coif ivkwr ] (55-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sach ratay say ubray dubiDhaa chhod vikaar. Those who are attuned to Truth are saved; they renounce duality and corruption.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	hau iqn kY bilhwrxY dir scY sicAwr ]2] (55-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ha-o tin kai balihaarnai dar sachai sachiaar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	I am a sacrifice to those who are found to be Truthful in the True Court. ||2||
RECORD	para 2299	sIcwny ijau pMKIAw jwlI biDk hwiQ ] (55-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) seechaanay ji-o pankhee-aa jaalee baDhik haath. Think of the hawk preying on the birds, and the net in the hands of the hunter.
DEFINE	para 2300	guir rwKy sy aubry hoir PwQy cogY swiQ ] (55-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur raakhay say ubray hor faathay chogai saath. Those who are protected by the Guru are saved; the others are caught by the bait.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	ibnu nwvY cuix sutIAih koie n sMgI swiQ ]3] (55-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin naavai chun sutee-ah ko-ay na sangee saath. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Without the Name, they are picked up and thrown away; they have no friends or companions. ||3||
DEFINE	para 2302	sco scw AwKIAY scy scw Qwnu ] (55-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sacho sachaa aakhee-ai sachay sachaa thaan. God is said to be the Truest of the True; His Place is the Truest of the True.
RECORD	para 2303	ijnI scw mMinAw iqn min scu iDAwnu ] (55-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jinee sachaa mani-aa tin man sach Dhi-aan. Those who obey the True One-their minds abide in true meditation.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	min muiK sUcy jwxIAih gurmuiK ijnw igAwnu ]4] (55-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man mukh soochay jaanee-ahi gurmukh jinaa gi-aan. ||4||
UPHOLD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Those who become Gurmukh, and obtain spiritual wisdom-their minds and mouths are known to be pure. ||4||
ALLOW	para 2305	siqgur AgY Ardwis kir swjnu dyie imlwie ] (55-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) satgur agai ardaas kar saajan day-ay milaa-ay. Offer your most sincere prayers to the True Guru, so that He may unite you with your Best Friend.
REQUIRE	para 2306	swjin imilAY suKu pwieAw jmdUq muey ibKu Kwie ] (55-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saajan mili-ai sukh paa-i-aa jamdoot mu-ay bikh khaa-ay. Meeting your Best Friend, you shall find peace; the Messenger of Death shall take poison and die.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	nwvY AMdir hau vsW nwau vsY min Awie ]5] (55-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naavai andar ha-o vasaa N naa-o vasai man aa-ay. ||5||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	I dwell deep within the Name; the Name has come to dwell within my mind. ||5||
DEFINE	para 2308	bwJu gurU gubwru hY ibnu sbdY bUJ n pwie ] (55-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) baajh guroo gubaar hai bin sabdai boojh na paa-ay. Without the Guru, there is only pitch darkness; without the Shabad, understanding is not obtained.
REQUIRE	para 2309	gurmqI prgwsu hoie sic rhY ilv lwie ] (55-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmatee pargaas ho-ay sach rahai liv laa-ay. Through the Guru's Teachings, you shall be enlightened; remain absorbed in the Love of the True Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	iqQY kwlu n sMcrY joqI joiq smwie ]6] (55-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tithai kaal na sanchrai jotee jot samaa-ay. ||6||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	Death does not go there; your light shall merge with the Light. ||6||
DEFINE	para 2311	qUMhY swjnu qUM sujwxu qUM Awpy mylxhwru ] (55-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tooNhai saajan tooN sujaan tooN aapay maylanhaar. You are my Best Friend; You are All-knowing. You are the One who unites us with Yourself.
RECORD	para 2312	gur sbdI swlwhIAY AMqu n pwrwvwru ] (55-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur sabdee salaahee-ai ant na paaraavaar. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, we praise You; You have no end or limitation.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	iqQY kwlu n ApVY ijQY gur kw sbdu Apwru ]7] (55-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tithai kaal na aprhai jithai gur kaa sabad apaar. ||7||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Death does not reach that place, where the Infinite Word of the Guru's Shabad resounds. ||7||
DEFINE	para 2314	hukmI sBy aUpjih hukmI kwr kmwih ] (55-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) hukmee sabhay oopjahi hukmee kaar kamaahi. By the Hukam of His Command, all are created. By His Command, actions are performed.
DEFINE	para 2315	hukmI kwlY vis hY hukmI swic smwih ] (55-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) hukmee kaalai vas hai hukmee saach samaahi. By His Command, all are subject to death; by His Command, they merge in Truth.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk jo iqsu BwvY so QIAY ienw jMqw vis ikCu nwih ]8]4] (55-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak jo tis bhaavai so thee-ai inaa jantaa vas kichh naahi. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	4|| O Nanak, whatever pleases His Will comes to pass. Nothing is in the hands of these beings. ||8||4||
DEFINE	para 2318	min jUTY qin jUiT hY ijhvw jUTI hoie ] (55-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man joothai tan jooth hai jihvaa joothee ho-ay. If the mind is polluted, then the body is polluted, and the tongue is polluted as well.
RECORD	para 2320	muiK JUTY JUTu bolxw ikau kir sUcw hoie ] (56-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mukh jhoothai jhooth bolnaa ki-o kar soochaa ho-ay. With false mouths, people speak falsehood. How can they be made pure?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ibnu AB sbd n mWjIAY swcy qy scu hoie ]1] (56-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin abh sabad na maa Njee-ai saachay tay sach ho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	Without the Holy Water of the Shabad, they are not cleansed. From the True One alone comes Truth. ||1||
RECORD	para 2322	muMDy guxhIxI suKu kyih ] (56-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) munDhay gunheenee sukh kayhi. O soul-bride, without virtue, what happiness can there be?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ipru rlIAw ris mwxsI swic sbid suKu nyih ]1] rhwau ] (56-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pir ralee-aa ras maansee saach sabad sukh nayhi. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. The Husband Lord enjoys her with pleasure and delight; she is at peace in the love of the True Word of the Shabad. ||1||Pause||
WHEN	para 2324	ipru prdysI jy QIAY Dn vWFI JUryie ] (56-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pir pardaysee jay thee-ai Dhan vaa Ndhee jooray-ay. When the Husband goes away, the bride suffers in the pain of separation,
RECORD	para 2325	ijau jil QoVY mCulI krx plwv kryie ] (56-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o jal thorhai machhulee karan palaav karay-i. like the fish in shallow water, crying for mercy.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	ipr BwvY suKu pweIAY jw Awpy ndir kryie ]2] (56-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pir bhaavai sukh paa-ee-ai jaa aapay nadar karay-i. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	As it pleases the Will of the Husband Lord, peace is obtained, when He Himself casts His Glance of Grace. ||2||
RECORD	para 2327	ipru swlwhI Awpxw sKI shylI nwil ] (56-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pir saalaahee aapnaa sakhee sahaylee naal. Praise your Husband Lord, together with your bridesmaids and friends.
DEFINE	para 2328	qin sohY mnu moihAw rqI rMig inhwil ] (56-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tan sohai man mohi-aa ratee rang nihaal. The body is beautified, and the mind is fascinated. Imbued with His Love, we are enraptured.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	sbid svwrI sohxI ipru rwvy gux nwil ]3] (56-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad savaaree sohnee pir raavay gun naal. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Adorned with the Shabad, the beautiful bride enjoys her Husband with virtue. ||3||
DEFINE	para 2330	kwmix kwim n AwveI KotI AvgixAwir ] (56-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kaaman kaam na aavee khotee avgani-aar. The soul-bride is of no use at all, if she is evil and without virtue.
RECORD	para 2331	nw suKu pyeIAY swhurY JUiT jlI vykwir ] (56-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naa sukh pay-ee-ai saahurai jhooth jalee vaykaar. She does not find peace in this world or the next; she burns in falsehood and corruption.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Awvxu vM\xu fwKVo CofI kMiq ivswir ]4] (56-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aavan vanjan daakh-rho chhodee kant visaar. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Coming and going are very difficult for that bride who is abandoned and forgotten by her Husband Lord. ||4||
RECORD	para 2333	ipr kI nwir suhwvxI muqI so ikqu swid ] (56-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pir kee naar suhaavanee mutee so kit saad. The beautiful soul-bride of the Husband Lord-by what sensual pleasures has she been doomed?
DEFINE	para 2334	ipr kY kwim n AwveI boly Pwidlu bwid ] (56-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pir kai kaam na aavee bolay faadil baad. She is of no use to her Husband if she babbles in useless arguments.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	dir Gir FoeI nw lhY CUtI dUjY swid ]5] (56-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) dar ghar dho-ee naa lahai chhootee doojai saad. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	At the Door of His Home, she finds no shelter; she is discarded for seeking other pleasures. ||5||
RECORD	para 2336	pMifq vwcih poQIAw nw bUJih vIcwru ] (56-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pandit vaacheh pothee-aa naa boojheh veechaar. The Pandits, the religious scholars, read their books, but they do not understand the real meaning.
RECORD	para 2337	An kau mqI dy clih mwieAw kw vwpwru ] (56-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) an ka-o matee day chaleh maa-i-aa kaa vaapaar. They give instructions to others, and then walk away, but they deal in Maya themselves.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	kQnI JUTI jgu BvY rhxI sbdu su swru ]6] (56-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kathnee jhoothee jag bhavai rahnee sabad so saar. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	Speaking falsehood, they wander around the world, while those who remain true to the Shabad are excellent and exalted. ||6||
DEFINE	para 2339	kyqy pMifq joqkI bydw krih bIcwru ] (56-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kaytay pandit jotkee baydaa karahi beechaar. There are so many Pandits and astrologers who ponder over the Vedas.
RECORD	para 2340	vwid ivroiD slwhxy vwdy Awvxu jwxu ] (56-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vaad viroDh salaahnay vaaday aavan jaan. They glorify their disputes and arguments, and in these controversies they continue coming and going.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	ibnu gur krm n CutsI kih suix AwiK vKwxu ]7] (56-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin gur karam na chhutsee kahi sun aakh vakhaan. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Without the Guru, they are not released from their karma, although they speak and listen and preach and explain. ||7||
RECORD	para 2342	siB guxvMqI AwKIAih mY guxu nwhI koie ] (56-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabh gunvantee aakhee-ahi mai gun naahee ko-ay. They all call themselves virtuous, but I have no virtue at all.
DEFINE	para 2343	hir vru nwir suhwvxI mY BwvY pRBu soie ] (56-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har var naar suhaavanee mai bhaavai parabh so-ay. With the Lord as her Husband, the soul-bride is happy; I, too, love that God.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk sbid imlwvVw nw vyCoVw hoie ]8]5] (56-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak sabad milaavrhaa naa vaychhorhaa ho-ay. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	5|| O Nanak, through the Shabad, union is obtained; there is no more separation. ||8||5||
ALLOW	para 2346	jpu qpu sMjmu swDIAY qIriQ kIcY vwsu ] (56-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jap tap sanjam saaDhee-ai tirath keechai vaas. You may chant and meditate, practice austerities and self-restraint, and dwell at sacred shrines of pilgrimage;
ALLOW	para 2347	puMn dwn cMigAweIAw ibnu swcy ikAw qwsu ] (56-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) punn daan chang-aa-ee-aa bin saachay ki-aa taas. you may give donations to charity, and perform good deeds, but without the True One, what is the use of it all?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	jyhw rwDy qyhw luxY ibnu gux jnmu ivxwsu ]1] (56-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jayhaa raaDhay tayhaa lunai bin gun janam vinaas. ||1||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	As you plant, so shall you harvest. Without virtue, this human life passes away in vain. ||1||
REQUIRE	para 2349	muMDy gux dwsI suKu hoie ] (56-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) munDhay gun daasee sukh ho-ay. O young bride, be a slave to virtue, and you shall find peace.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	Avgx iqAwig smweIAY gurmiq pUrw soie ]1] rhwau ] (56-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) avgan ti-aag samaa-ee-ai gurmat pooraa so-ay. ||1||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Renouncing wrongful actions, following the Guru's Teachings, you shall be absorbed into the Perfect One. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 2351	ivxu rwsI vwpwrIAw qky kuMfw cwir ] (56-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vin raasee vapaaree-aa takay kundaa chaar. Without capital, the trader looks around in all four directions.
RECORD	para 2352	mUlu n buJY Awpxw vsqu rhI Gr bwir ] (56-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mool na bujhai aapnaa vasat rahee ghar baar. He does not understand his own origins; the merchandise remains within the door of his own house.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	ivxu vKr duKu Aglw kUiV muTI kUiVAwir ]2] (56-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vin vakhar dukh aglaa koorh muthee koorhi-aar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Without this commodity, there is great pain. The false are ruined by falsehood. ||2||
RECORD	para 2354	lwhw Aihinis nauqnw prKy rqnu vIcwir ] (56-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) laahaa ahinis na-otanaa parkhay ratan veechaar. One who contemplates and appraises this Jewel day and night reaps new profits.
RECORD	para 2355	vsqu lhY Gir AwpxY clY kwrju swir ] (56-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vasat lahai ghar aapnai chalai kaaraj saar. He finds the merchandise within his own home, and departs after arranging his affairs.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	vxjwirAw isau vxju kir gurmuiK bRhmu bIcwir ]3] (56-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vanjaari-aa si-o vanaj kar gurmukh barahm beechaar. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	So trade with the true traders, and as Gurmukh, contemplate God. ||3||
DEFINE	para 2357	sMqW sMgiq pweIAY jy myly mylxhwru ] (56-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jantaaN sangat paa-ee-ai jay maylay maylanhaar. In the Society of the Saints, He is found, if the Uniter unites us.
REQUIRE	para 2358	imilAw hoie n ivCuVY ijsu AMqir joiq Apwr ] (56-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mili-aa ho-ay na vichhurhai jis antar jot apaar. One whose heart is filled with His Infinite Light meets with Him, and shall never again be separated from Him.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	scY Awsix sic rhY scY pRym ipAwr ]4] (56-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sachai aasan sach rahai sachai paraym pi-aar. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	True is his position; he abides in Truth, with love and affection for the True One. ||4||
RECORD	para 2360	ijnI Awpu pCwixAw Gr mih mhlu suQwie ] (56-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jinee aap pachhaani-aa ghar meh mahal suthaa-ay. One who understands himself finds the Mansion of the Lord's Presence within his own home.
DEFINE	para 2361	scy syqI riqAw sco plY pwie ] (56-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sachay saytee rati-aa sacho palai paa-ay. Imbued with the True Lord, Truth is gathered in.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	iqRBvix so pRBu jwxIAY swco swcY nwie ]5] (57-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) taribhavan so parabh jaanee-ai saacho saachai naa-ay. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	God is known throughout the three worlds. True is the Name of the True One. ||5||
DEFINE	para 2364	sw Dn KrI suhwvxI ijin ipru jwqw sMig ] (57-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saa Dhan kharee suhaavanee jin pir jaataa sang. The wife who knows that her Husband Lord is always with her is very beautiful.
DEFINE	para 2365	mhlI mhil bulweIAY so ipru rwvy rMig ] (57-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mahlee mahal bulaa-ee-ai so pir raavay rang. The soul-bride is called to the Mansion of the His Presence, and her Husband Lord ravishes her with love.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	sic suhwgix sw BlI ipir mohI gux sMig ]6] (57-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sach suhaagan saa bhalee pir mohee gun sang. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	The happy soul-bride is true and good; she is fascinated by the Glories of her Husband Lord. ||6||
RECORD	para 2367	BUlI BUlI Qil cVw Qil ciV fUgir jwau ] (57-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhoolee bhoolee thal charhaa thal charh doogar jaa-o. Wandering around and making mistakes, I climb the plateau; having climbed the plateau, I go up the mountain.
RECORD	para 2368	bn mih BUlI jy iPrw ibnu gur bUJ n pwau ] (57-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ban meh bhoolee jay firaa bin gur boojh na paa-o. But now I have lost my way, and I am wandering around in the forest; without the Guru, I do not understand.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	nwvhu BUlI jy iPrw iPir iPir Awvau jwau ]7] (57-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naavhu bhoolee jay firaa fir fir aava-o jaa-o. ||7||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	If I wander around forgetting God's Name, I shall continue coming and going in reincarnation, over and over again. ||7||
RECORD	para 2370	puChu jwie pDwaUAw cly cwkr hoie ] (57-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) puchhahu jaa-ay paDhaa-oo-aa chalay chaakar ho-ay. Go and ask the travellers, how to walk on the Path as His slave.
DEFINE	para 2371	rwjnu jwxih Awpxw dir Gir Twk n hoie ] (57-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) raajan jaaneh aapnaa dar ghar thaak na ho-ay. They know the Lord to be their King, and at the Door to His Home, their way is not blocked.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk eyko riv rihAw dUjw Avru n koie ]8]6] (57-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak ayko rav rahi-aa doojaa avar na ko-ay. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	6|| O Nanak, the One is pervading everywhere; there is no other at all. ||8||6||
DEFINE	para 2374	gur qy inrmlu jwxIAY inrml dyh srIru ] (57-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur tay nirmal jaanee-ai nirmal dayh sareer. Through the Guru, the Pure One is known, and the human body becomes pure as well.
RECORD	para 2375	inrmlu swco min vsY so jwxY AB pIr ] (57-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nirmal saacho man vasai so jaanai abh peer. The Pure, True Lord abides within the mind; He knows the pain of our hearts.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	shjY qy suKu Aglo nw lwgY jm qIru ]1] (57-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sahjai tay sukh aglo naa laagai jam teer. ||1||
FORBID	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	With intuitive ease, a great peace is found, and the arrow of death shall not strike you. ||1||
DEFINE	para 2377	BweI ry mYlu nwhI inrml jil nwie ] (57-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaa-ee ray mail naahee nirmal jal naa-ay. O Siblings of Destiny, filth is washed away by bathing in the Pure Water of the Name.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	inrmlu swcw eyku qU horu mYlu BrI sB jwie ]1] rhwau ] (57-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nirmal saachaa ayk too hor mail bharee sabh jaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. You alone are Perfectly Pure, O True Lord; all other places are filled with filth. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 2379	hir kw mMdru sohxw kIAw krxYhwir ] (57-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har kaa mandar sohnaa kee-aa karnaihaar. The Temple of the Lord is beautiful; it was made by the Creator Lord.
RECORD	para 2380	riv sis dIp AnUp joiq iqRBvix joiq Apwr ] (57-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) rav sas deep anoop jot taribhavan jot apaar. The sun and the moon are lamps of incomparably beautiful light. Throughout the three worlds, the Infinite Light is pervading.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	hwt ptx gV koTVI scu saudw vwpwr ]2] (57-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) haat patan garh koth-rhee sach sa-udaa vaapaar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	In the shops of the city of the body, in the fortresses and in the huts, the True Merchandise is traded. ||2||
DEFINE	para 2382	igAwn AMjnu BY BMjnw dyKu inrMjn Bwie ] (57-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gi-aan anjan bhai bhanjnaa daykh niranjan bhaa-ay. The ointment of spiritual wisdom is the destroyer of fear; through love, the Pure One is seen.
DEFINE	para 2383	gupqu pRgtu sB jwxIAY jy mnu rwKY Twie ] (57-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gupat pargat sabh jaanee-ai jay man raakhai thaa-ay. The mysteries of the seen and the unseen are all known, if the mind is kept centered and balanced.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	AYsw siqguru jy imlY qw shjy ley imlwie ]3] (57-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aisaa satgur jay milai taa sehjay la-ay milaa-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	If one finds such a True Guru, the Lord is met with intuitive ease. ||3||
RECORD	para 2385	kis ksvtI lweIAY prKy ihqu icqu lwie ] (57-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kas kasvatee laa-ee-ai parkhay hit chit laa-ay. He draws us to His Touchstone, to test our love and consciousness.
DEFINE	para 2386	Koty Taur n pwienI Kry KjwnY pwie ] (57-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khotay tha-ur na paa-inee kharay khajaanai paa-ay. The counterfeit have no place there, but the genuine are placed in His Treasury.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Aws AMdysw dUir kir ieau mlu jwie smwie ]4] (57-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aas andaysaa door kar i-o mal jaa-ay samaa-ay. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Let your hopes and anxieties depart; thus pollution is washed away. ||4||
RECORD	para 2388	suK kau mwgY sBu ko duKu n mwgY koie ] (57-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sukh ka-o maagai sabh ko dukh na maagai ko-ay. Everyone begs for happiness; no one asks for suffering.
RECORD	para 2389	suKY kau duKu Aglw mnmuiK bUJ n hoie ] (57-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sukhai ka-o dukh aglaa manmukh boojh na ho-ay. But in the wake of happiness, there comes great suffering. The self-willed manmukhs do not understand this.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	suK duK sm kir jwxIAih sbid Byid suKu hoie ]5] (57-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sukh dukh sam kar jaanee-ahi sabad bhayd sukh ho-ay. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	Those who see pain and pleasure as one and the same find peace; they are pierced through by the Shabad. ||5||
RECORD	para 2391	bydu pukwry vwcIAY bwxI bRhm ibAwsu ] (57-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bayd pukaaray vaachee-ai banee barahm bi-aas. The Vedas proclaim, and the words of Vyaasa tell us,
RECORD	para 2392	muin jn syvk swiDkw nwim rqy guxqwsu ] (57-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mun jan sayvak saaDhikaa naam ratay guntaas. that the silent sages, the servants of the Lord, and those who practice a life of spiritual discipline are attuned to the Naam, the Treasure of Excellence.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	sic rqy sy ijix gey hau sd bilhwrY jwsu ]6] (57-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sach ratay say jin ga-ay ha-o sad balihaarai jaas. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	Those who are attuned to the True Name win the game of life; I am forever a sacrifice to them. ||6||
RECORD	para 2394	chu juig mYly mlu Bry ijn muiK nwmu n hoie ] (57-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) chahu jug mailay mal bharay jin mukh naam na ho-ay. Those who do not have the Naam in their mouths are filled with pollution; they are filthy throughout the four ages.
DEFINE	para 2395	BgqI Bwie ivhUixAw muhu kwlw piq Koie ] (57-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhagtee bhaa-ay vihooni-aa muhu kaalaa pat kho-ay. Without loving devotion to God, their faces are blackened, and their honor is lost.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	ijnI nwmu ivswirAw Avgx muTI roie ]7] (57-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jinee naam visaari-aa avgan muthee ro-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Those who have forgotten the Naam are plundered by evil; they weep and wail in dismay. ||7||
RECORD	para 2397	Kojq Kojq pwieAw fru kir imlY imlwie ] (57-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khojat khojat paa-i-aa dar kar milai milaa-ay. I searched and searched, and found God. In the Fear of God, I have been united in His Union.
RECORD	para 2398	Awpu pCwxY Gir vsY haumY iqRsnw jwie ] (57-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aap pachhaanai ghar vasai ha-umai tarisnaa jaa-ay. Through self-realization, people dwell within the home of their inner being; egotism and desire depart.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk inrml aUjly jo rwqy hir nwie ]8]7] (57-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak nirmal oojlay jo raatay har naa-ay. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	7|| O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Name of the Lord are immaculate and radiant. ||8||7||
RECORD	para 2401	suix mn BUly bwvry gur kI crxI lwgu ] (57-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sun man bhoolay baavray gur kee charnee laag. Listen, O deluded and demented mind: hold tight to the Guru's Feet.
REQUIRE	para 2402	hir jip nwmu iDAwie qU jmu frpY duK Bwgu ] (57-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har jap naam Dhi-aa-ay too jam darpai dukh bhaag. Chant and meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; death will be afraid of you, and suffering shall depart.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	dUKu Gxo dohwgxI ikau iQru rhY suhwgu ]1] (57-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) dookh ghano duhaaganee ki-o thir rahai suhaag. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	The deserted wife suffers terrible pain. How can her Husband Lord remain with her forever? ||1||
RECORD	para 2405	BweI ry Avru nwhI mY Qwau ] (58-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaa-ee ray avar naahee mai thaa-o. O Siblings of Destiny, I have no other place to go.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	mY Dnu nwmu inDwnu hY guir dIAw bil jwau ]1] rhwau ] (58-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mai Dhan naam niDhaan hai gur dee-aa bal jaa-o. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. The Guru has given me the Treasure of the Wealth of the Naam; I am a sacrifice to Him. ||1||Pause||
ALLOW	para 2407	gurmiq piq swbwis iqsu iqs kY sMig imlwau ] (58-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmat pat saabaas tis tis kai sang milaa-o. The Guru's Teachings bring honor. Blessed is He-may I meet and be with Him!
RECORD	para 2408	iqsu ibnu GVI n jIvaU ibnu nwvY mir jwau ] (58-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tis bin gharhee na jeev-oo bin naavai mar jaa-o. Without Him, I cannot live, even for a moment. Without His Name, I die.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	mY AMDuly nwmu n vIsrY tyk itkI Gir jwau ]2] (58-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mai anDhulay naam na veesrai tayk tikee ghar jaa-o. ||2||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	I am blind-may I never forget the Naam! Under His Protection, I shall reach my true home. ||2||
FORBID	para 2410	gurU ijnw kw AMDulw cyly nwhI Twau ] (58-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) guroo jinaa kaa anDhulaa chaylay naahee thaa-o. Those chaylaas, those devotees, whose spiritual teacher is blind, shall not find their place of rest.
RECORD	para 2411	ibnu siqgur nwau n pweIAY ibnu nwvY ikAw suAwau ] (58-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin satgur naa-o na paa-ee-ai bin naavai ki-aa su-aa-o. Without the True Guru, the Name is not obtained. Without the Name, what is the use of it all?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Awie gieAw pCuqwvxw ijau suM\Y Gir kwau ]3] (58-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aa-ay ga-i-aa pachhutaavnaa ji-o sunjai ghar kaa-o. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	People come and go, regretting and repenting, like crows in a deserted house. ||3||
RECORD	para 2413	ibnu nwvY duKu dyhurI ijau klr kI BIiq ] (58-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin naavai dukh dayhuree ji-o kalar kee bheet. Without the Name, the body suffers in pain; it crumbles like a wall of sand.
RECORD	para 2414	qb lgu mhlu n pweIAY jb lgu swcu n cIiq ] (58-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tab lag mahal na paa-ee-ai jab lag saach na cheet. As long as Truth does not enter into the consciousness, the Mansion of the Lord's Presence is not found.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	sbid rpY Gru pweIAY inrbwxI pdu nIiq ]4] (58-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad rapai ghar paa-ee-ai nirbaanee pad neet. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Attuned to the Shabad, we enter our home, and obtain the Eternal State of Nirvaanaa. ||4||
RECORD	para 2416	hau gur pUCau Awpxy gur puiC kwr kmwau ] (58-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ha-o gur poochha-o aapnay gur puchh kaar kamaa-o. I ask my Guru for His Advice, and I follow the Guru's Advice.
DEFINE	para 2417	sbid slwhI min vsY haumY duKu jil jwau ] (58-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad salaahee man vasai ha-umai dukh jal jaa-o. With the Shabads of Praise abiding in the mind, the pain of egotism is burnt away.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	shjy hoie imlwvVw swcy swic imlwau ]5] (58-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sehjay ho-ay milaavrhaa saachay saach milaa-o. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	We are intuitively united with Him, and we meet the Truest of the True. ||5||
RECORD	para 2419	sbid rqy sy inrmly qij kwm k®oDu AhMkwru ] (58-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad ratay say nirmalay taj kaam kroDh aha Nkaar. Those who are attuned to the Shabad are spotless and pure; they renounce sexual desire, anger, selfishness and conceit.
RECORD	para 2420	nwmu slwhin sd sdw hir rwKih aur Dwir ] (58-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naam salaahan sad sadaa har raakhahi ur Dhaar. They sing the Praises of the Naam, forever and ever; they keep the Lord enshrined within their hearts.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	so ikau mnhu ivswrIAY sB jIAw kw AwDwru ]6] (58-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) so ki-o manhu visaaree-ai sabh jee-aa kaa aaDhaar. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	How could we ever forget Him from our minds? He is the Support of all beings. ||6||
REQUIRE	para 2422	sbid mrY so mir rhY iPir mrY n dUjI vwr ] (58-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad marai so mar rahai fir marai na doojee vaar. One who dies in the Shabad is beyond death, and shall never die again.
ALLOW	para 2423	sbdY hI qy pweIAY hir nwmy lgY ipAwru ] (58-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabdai hee tay paa-ee-ai har naamay lagai pi-aar. Through the Shabad, we find Him, and embrace love for the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	ibnu sbdY jgu BUlw iPrY mir jnmY vwro vwr ]7] (58-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin sabdai jag bhoolaa firai mar janmai vaaro vaar. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Without the Shabad, the world is deceived; it dies and is reborn, over and over again. ||7||
RECORD	para 2425	sB swlwhY Awp kau vfhu vfyrI hoie ] (58-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabh salaahai aap ka-o vadahu vadayree ho-ay. All praise themselves, and call themselves the greatest of the great.
RECORD	para 2426	gur ibnu Awpu n cInIAY khy suxy ikAw hoie ] (58-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur bin aap na cheenee-ai kahay sunay ki-aa ho-ay. Without the Guru, one's self cannot be known. By merely speaking and listening, what is accomplished?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk sbid pCwxIAY haumY krY n koie ]8]8] (58-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak sabad pachhaanee-ai ha-umai karai na ko-ay. ||8||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	8|| O Nanak, one who realizes the Shabad does not act in egotism. ||8||8||
DEFINE	para 2429	ibnu ipr Dn sIgwrIAY jobnu bwid KuAwru ] (58-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin pir Dhan seegaaree-ai joban baad khu-aar. Without her Husband, the soul-bride's youth and ornaments are useless and wretched.
RECORD	para 2430	nw mwxy suiK syjVI ibnu ipr bwid sIgwru ] (58-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naa maanay sukh sayjrhee bin pir baad seegaar. She does not enjoy the pleasure of His Bed; without her Husband, her ornaments are absurd.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	dUKu Gxo dohwgxI nw Gir syj Bqwru ]1] (58-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) dookh ghano duhaaganee naa ghar sayj bhataar. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	The discarded bride suffers terrible pain; her Husband does not come to the bed of her home. ||1||
RECORD	para 2432	mn ry rwm jphu suKu hoie ] (58-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man ray raam japahu sukh ho-ay. O mind, meditate on the Lord, and find peace.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ibnu gur pRymu n pweIAY sbid imlY rMgu hoie ]1] rhwau ] (58-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin gur paraym na paa-ee-ai sabad milai rang ho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Without the Guru, love is not found. United with the Shabad, happiness is found. ||1||Pause||
UPHOLD	para 2434	gur syvw suKu pweIAY hir vru shij sIgwru ] (58-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur sayvaa sukh paa-ee-ai har var sahj seegaar. Serving the Guru, she finds peace, and her Husband Lord adorns her with intuitive wisdom.
RECORD	para 2435	sic mwxy ipr syjVI gUVw hyqu ipAwru ] (58-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sach maanay pir sayjrhee goorhaa hayt pi-aar. Truly, she enjoys the Bed of her Husband, through her deep love and affection.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	gurmuiK jwix is\wxIAY guir mylI gux cwru ]2] (58-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh jaan sinjaanee-ai gur maylee gun chaar. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	As Gurmukh, she comes to know Him. Meeting with the Guru, she maintains a virtuous lifestyle. ||2||
RECORD	para 2437	sic imlhu vr kwmxI ipir mohI rMgu lwie ] (58-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sach milhu var kaamnee pir mohee rang laa-ay. Through Truth, meet your Husband Lord, O soul-bride. Enchanted by your Husband, enshrine love for Him.
REQUIRE	para 2438	mnu qnu swic ivgisAw kImiq khxu n jwie ] (58-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man tan saach vigsi-aa keemat kahan na jaa-ay. Your mind and body shall blossom forth in Truth. The value of this cannot be described.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	hir vru Gir sohwgxI inrml swcY nwie ]3] (58-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har var ghar sohaaganee nirmal saachai naa-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	The soul-bride finds her Husband Lord in the home of her own being; she is purified by the True Name. ||3||
WHEN	para 2440	mn mih mnUAw jy mrY qw ipru rwvY nwir ] (58-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man meh manoo-aa jay marai taa pir raavai naar. If the mind within the mind dies, then the Husband ravishes and enjoys His bride.
DEFINE	para 2441	iekqu qwgY ril imlY gil moqIAn kw hwru ] (58-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ikat taagai ral milai gal motee-an kaa haar. They are woven into one texture, like pearls on a necklace around the neck.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	sMq sBw suKu aUpjY gurmuiK nwm ADwru ]4] (58-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sant sabhaa sukh oopjai gurmukh naam aDhaar. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	In the Society of the Saints, peace wells up; the Gurmukhs take the Support of the Naam. ||4||
RECORD	para 2443	iKn mih aupjY iKin KpY iKnu AwvY iKnu jwie ] (58-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khin meh upjai khin khapai khin aavai khin jaa-ay. In an instant, one is born, and in an instant, one dies. In an instant one comes, and in an instant one goes.
DEFINE	para 2444	sbdu pCwxY riv rhY nw iqsu kwlu sMqwie ] (58-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad pachhaanai rav rahai naa tis kaal santaa-ay. One who recognizes the Shabad merges into it, and is not afflicted by death.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	swihbu Aqulu n qolIAY kQin n pwieAw jwie ]5] (59-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saahib atul na tolee-ai kathan na paa-i-aa jaa-ay. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	Our Lord and Master is Unweighable; He cannot be weighed. He cannot be found merely by talking. ||5||
DEFINE	para 2447	vwpwrI vxjwirAw Awey vjhu ilKwie ] (59-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vaapaaree vanjaari-aa aa-ay vajahu likhaa-ay. The merchants and the traders have come; their profits are pre-ordained.
RECORD	para 2448	kwr kmwvih sc kI lwhw imlY rjwie ] (59-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kaar kamaaveh sach kee laahaa milai rajaa-ay. Those who practice Truth reap the profits, abiding in the Will of God.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	pUMjI swcI guru imlY nw iqsu iqlu n qmwie ]6] (59-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) poonjee saachee gur milai naa tis til na tamaa-ay. ||6||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	With the Merchandise of Truth, they meet the Guru, who does not have a trace of greed. ||6||
DEFINE	para 2450	gurmuiK qoil quolwiesI scu qrwjI qolu ] (59-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh tol tolaa-isee sach taraajee tol. As Gurmukh, they are weighed and measured, in the balance and the scales of Truth.
DEFINE	para 2451	Awsw mnsw mohxI guir TwkI scu bolu ] (59-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aasaa mansaa mohnee gur thaakee sach bol. The enticements of hope and desire are quieted by the Guru, whose Word is True.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Awip qulwey qolsI pUry pUrw qolu ]7] (59-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aap tulaa-ay tolsee pooray pooraa tol. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	He Himself weighs with the scale; perfect is the weighing of the Perfect One. ||7||
DEFINE	para 2453	kQnY khix n CutIAY nw piV pusqk Bwr ] (59-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kathnai kahan na chhutee-ai naa parh pustak bhaar. No one is saved by mere talk and speech, nor by reading loads of books.
RECORD	para 2454	kwieAw soc n pweIAY ibnu hir Bgiq ipAwr ] (59-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa soch na paa-ee-ai bin har bhagat pi-aar. The body does not obtain purity without loving devotion to the Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk nwmu n vIsrY myly guru krqwr ]8]9] (59-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak naam na veesrai maylay gur kartaar. ||8||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	9|| O Nanak, never forget the Naam; the Guru shall unite us with the Creator. ||8||9||
RECORD	para 2457	siqguru pUrw jy imlY pweIAY rqnu bIcwru ] (59-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) satgur pooraa jay milai paa-ee-ai ratan beechaar. Meeting the Perfect True Guru, we find the jewel of meditative reflection.
RECORD	para 2458	mnu dIjY gur Awpxy pweIAY srb ipAwru ] (59-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man deejai gur aapnay paa-ee-ai sarab pi-aar. Surrendering our minds to our Guru, we find universal love.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	mukiq pdwrQu pweIAY Avgx mytxhwru ]1] (59-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mukat padaarath paa-ee-ai avgan maytanhaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	We find the wealth of liberation, and our demerits are erased. ||1||
DEFINE	para 2460	BweI ry gur ibnu igAwnu n hoie ] (59-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaa-ee ray gur bin gi-aan na ho-ay. O Siblings of Destiny, without the Guru, there is no spiritual wisdom.
ALLOW	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	pUChu bRhmy nwrdY byd ibAwsY koie ]1] rhwau ] (59-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) poochhahu barahmay naardai bayd bi-aasai ko-ay. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Go and ask Brahma, Naarad and Vyaas, the writer of the Vedas. ||1||Pause||
UPHOLD	para 2462	igAwnu iDAwnu Duin jwxIAY AkQu khwvY soie ] (59-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gi-aan Dhi-aan Dhun jaanee-ai akath kahaavai so-ay. Know that from the vibration of the Word, we obtain spiritual wisdom and meditation. Through it, we speak the Unspoken.
DEFINE	para 2463	sPilE ibrKu hrIAwvlw Cwv GxyrI hoie ] (59-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) safli-o birakh haree-aavlaa chhaav ghanayree ho-ay. He is the fruit-bearing Tree, luxuriantly green with abundant shade.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	lwl jvyhr mwxkI gur BMfwrY soie ]2] (59-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) laal javayhar maankee gur bhandaarai so-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	The rubies, jewels and emeralds are in the Guru's Treasury. ||2||
RECORD	para 2465	gur BMfwrY pweIAY inrml nwm ipAwru ] (59-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur bhandaarai paa-ee-ai nirmal naam pi-aar. From the Guru's Treasury, we receive the Love of the Immaculate Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 2466	swco vKru sMcIAY pUrY krim Apwru ] (59-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saacho vakhar sanchee-ai poorai karam apaar. We gather in the True Merchandise, through the Perfect Grace of the Infinite.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	suKdwqw duK mytxo siqguru Asur sMGwru ]3] (59-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sukh-daata dukh maytno satgur asur sanghaar. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	The True Guru is the Giver of peace, the Dispeller of pain, the Destroyer of demons. ||3||
DEFINE	para 2468	Bvjlu ibKmu frwvxo nw kMDI nw pwru ] (59-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhavjal bikham daraavno naa kanDhee naa paar. The terrifying world-ocean is difficult and dreadful; there is no shore on this side or the one beyond.
DEFINE	para 2469	nw byVI nw qulhVw nw iqsu vMJu mlwru ] (59-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naa bayrhee naa tulharhaa naa tis vanjh malaar. There is no boat, no raft, no oars and no boatman.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	siqguru BY kw boihQw ndrI pwir auqwru ]4] (59-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) satgur bhai kaa bohithaa nadree paar utaar. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	The True Guru is the only boat on this terrifying ocean. His Glance of Grace carries us across. ||4||
WHEN	para 2471	ieku iqlu ipAwrw ivsrY duKu lwgY suKu jwie ] (59-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ik til pi-aaraa visrai dukh laagai sukh jaa-ay. If I forget my Beloved, even for an instant, suffering overtakes me and peace departs.
RECORD	para 2472	ijhvw jlau jlwvxI nwmu n jpY rswie ] (59-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jihvaa jala-o jalaavanee naam na japai rasaa-ay. Let that tongue be burnt in flames, which does not chant the Naam with love.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	Gtu ibnsY duKu Aglo jmu pkVY pCuqwie ]5] (59-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ghat binsai dukh aglo jam pakrhai pachhutaa-ay. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	When the pitcher of the body bursts, there is terrible pain; those who are caught by the Minister of Death regret and repent. ||5||
RECORD	para 2474	myrI myrI kir gey qnu Dnu klqu n swiQ ] (59-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mayree mayree kar ga-ay tan Dhan kalat na saath. Crying out, "Mine! Mine!", they have departed, but their bodies, their wealth, and their wives did not go with them.
DEFINE	para 2475	ibnu nwvY Dnu bwid hY BUlo mwrig AwiQ ] (59-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin naavai Dhan baad hai bhoolo maarag aath. Without the Name, wealth is useless; deceived by wealth, they have lost their way.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	swcau swihbu syvIAY gurmuiK AkQo kwiQ ]6] (59-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saacha-o saahib sayvee-ai gurmukh aktho kaath. ||6||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	So serve the True Lord; become Gurmukh, and speak the Unspoken. ||6||
RECORD	para 2477	AwvY jwie BvweIAY pieAY ikriq kmwie ] (59-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aavai jaa-ay bhavaa-ee-ai pa-i-ai kirat kamaa-ay. Coming and going, people wander through reincarnation; they act according to their past actions.
RECORD	para 2478	pUrib iliKAw ikau mytIAY iliKAw lyKu rjwie ] (59-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) poorab likhi-aa ki-o maytee-ai likhi-aa laykh rajaa-ay. How can one's pre-ordained destiny be erased? It is written in accordance with the Lord's Will.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	ibnu hir nwm n CutIAY gurmiq imlY imlwie ]7] (59-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin har naam na chhutee-ai gurmat milai milaa-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Without the Name of the Lord, no one can be saved. Through the Guru's Teachings, we are united in His Union. ||7||
RECORD	para 2480	iqsu ibnu myrw ko nhI ijs kw jIau prwnu ] (59-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tis bin mayraa ko nahee jis kaa jee-o paraan. Without Him, I have no one to call my own. My soul and my breath of life belong to Him.
ALLOW	para 2481	haumY mmqw jil blau loBu jlau AiBmwnu ] (59-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ha-umai mamtaa jal bala-o lobh jala-o abhimaan. May my egotism and possessiveness be burnt to ashes, and my greed and egotistical pride consigned to the fire.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk sbdu vIcwrIAY pweIAY guxI inDwnu ]8]10] (59-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak sabad veechaaree-ai paa-ee-ai gunee niDhaan. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	10|| O Nanak, contemplating the Shabad, the Treasure of Excellence is obtained. ||8||10||
RECORD	para 2484	ry mn AYsI hir isau pRIiq kir jYsI jl kmlyih ] (59-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ray man aisee har si-o pareet kar jaisee jal kamlayhi. O mind, love the Lord, as the lotus loves the water.
RECORD	para 2485	lhrI nwil pCwVIAY BI ivgsY Asnyih ] (59-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) lahree naal pachhaarhee-ai bhee vigsai asnayhi. Tossed about by the waves, it still blossoms with love.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	jl mih jIA aupwie kY ibnu jl mrxu iqnyih ]1] (59-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jal meh jee-a upaa-ay kai bin jal maran tinayhi. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	In the water, the creatures are created; outside of the water they die. ||1||
RECORD	para 2488	mn ry ikau CUtih ibnu ipAwr ] (60-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man ray ki-o chhooteh bin pi-aar. O mind, how can you be saved without love?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	gurmuiK AMqir riv rihAw bKsy Bgiq BMfwr ]1] rhwau ] (60-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh antar rav rahi-aa bakhsay bhagat bhandaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. God permeates the inner beings of the Gurmukhs. They are blessed with the treasure of devotion. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 2490	ry mn AYsI hir isau pRIiq kir jYsI mCulI nIr ] (60-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ray man aisee har si-o pareet kar jaisee machhulee neer. O mind, love the Lord, as the fish loves the water.
RECORD	para 2491	ijau AiDkau iqau suKu Gxo min qin sWiq srIr ] (60-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o aDhika-o ti-o sukh ghano man tan saa Nt sareer. The more the water, the more the happiness, and the greater the peace of mind and body.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	ibnu jl GVI n jIveI pRBu jwxY AB pIr ]2] (60-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin jal gharhee na jeev-ee parabh jaanai abh peer. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Without water, she cannot live, even for an instant. God knows the suffering of her mind. ||2||
RECORD	para 2493	ry mn AYsI hir isau pRIiq kir jYsI cwiqRk myh ] (60-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ray man aisee har si-o pareet kar jaisee chaatrik mayh. O mind, love the Lord, as the song-bird loves the rain.
WHEN	para 2494	sr Bir Ql hrIAwvly iek bUMd n pveI kyh ] (60-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sar bhar thal haree-aavlay ik boond na pav-ee kayh. The pools are overflowing with water, and the land is luxuriantly green, but what are they to her, if that single drop of rain does not fall into her mouth?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	krim imlY so pweIAY ikrqu pieAw isir dyh ]3] (60-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) karam milai so paa-ee-ai kirat pa-i-aa sir dayh. ||3||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	By His Grace, she receives it; otherwise, because of her past actions, she gives her head. ||3||
RECORD	para 2496	ry mn AYsI hir isau pRIiq kir jYsI jl duD hoie ] (60-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ray man aisee har si-o pareet kar jaisee jal duDh ho-ay. O mind, love the Lord, as the water loves the milk.
RECORD	para 2497	Awvtxu Awpy KvY duD kau Kpix n dyie ] (60-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aavtan aapay khavai duDh ka-o khapan na day-ay. The water, added to the milk, itself bears the heat, and prevents the milk from burning.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Awpy myil ivCuMinAw sic vifAweI dyie ]4] (60-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay mayl vichhunni-aa sach vadi-aa-ee day-ay. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	God unites the separated ones with Himself again, and blesses them with true greatness. ||4||
RECORD	para 2499	ry mn AYsI hir isau pRIiq kir jYsI ckvI sUr ] (60-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ray man aisee har si-o pareet kar jaisee chakvee soor. O mind, love the Lord, as the chakvee duck loves the sun.
DEFINE	para 2500	iKnu plu nId n soveI jwxY dUir hjUir ] (60-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khin pal need na sov-ee jaanai door hajoor. She does not sleep, for an instant or a moment; the sun is so far away, but she thinks that it is near.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	mnmuiK soJI nw pvY gurmuiK sdw hjUir ]5] (60-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manmukh sojhee naa pavai gurmukh sadaa hajoor. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	Understanding does not come to the self-willed manmukh. But to the Gurmukh, the Lord is always close. ||5||
RECORD	para 2502	mnmuiK gxq gxwvxI krqw kry su hoie ] (60-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manmukh ganat ganaavanee kartaa karay so ho-ay. The self-willed manmukhs make their calculations and plans, but only the actions of the Creator come to pass.
ALLOW	para 2503	qw kI kImiq nw pvY jy locY sBu koie ] (60-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) taa kee keemat naa pavai jay lochai sabh ko-ay. His Value cannot be estimated, even though everyone may wish to do so.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	gurmiq hoie q pweIAY sic imlY suKu hoie ]6] (60-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmat ho-ay ta paa-ee-ai sach milai sukh ho-ay. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	Through the Guru's Teachings, it is revealed. Meeting with the True One, peace is found. ||6||
FORBID	para 2505	scw nyhu n quteI jy siqguru BytY soie ] (60-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sachaa nayhu na tut-ee jay satgur bhaytai so-ay. True love shall not be broken, if the True Guru is met.
UPHOLD	para 2506	igAwn pdwrQu pweIAY iqRBvx soJI hoie ] (60-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gi-aan padaarath paa-ee-ai taribhavan sojhee ho-ay. Obtaining the wealth of spiritual wisdom, the understanding of the three worlds is acquired.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	inrmlu nwmu n vIsrY jy gux kw gwhku hoie ]7] (60-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) nirmal naam na veesrai jay gun kaa gaahak ho-ay. ||7||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	So become a customer of merit, and do not forget the Immaculate Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||7||
RECORD	para 2508	Kyil gey sy pMKxUM jo cugdy sr qil ] (60-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) khayl ga-ay say pa Nkh-nooN jo chugday sar tal. Those birds which peck at the shore of the pool have played and have departed.
REQUIRE	para 2509	GVI ik muhiq ik clxw Kylxu Aju ik kil ] (60-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gharhee ke muhat ke chalnaa khaylan aj ke kal. In a moment, in an instant, we too must depart. Our play is only for today or tomorrow.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	ijsu qUM mylih so imlY jwie scw ipVu mil ]8] (60-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jis tooN mayleh so milai jaa-ay sachaa pirh mal. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	But those whom You unite, Lord, are united with You; they obtain a seat in the Arena of Truth. ||8||
RECORD	para 2511	ibnu gur pRIiq n aUpjY haumY mYlu n jwie ] (60-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin gur pareet na oopjai ha-umai mail na jaa-ay. Without the Guru, love does not well up, and the filth of egotism does not depart.
RECORD	para 2512	sohM Awpu pCwxIAY sbid Byid pqIAwie ] (60-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sohaN aap pachhaanee-ai sabad bhayd patee-aa-ay. One who recognizes within himself that, "He is me", and who is pierced through by the Shabad, is satisfied.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v9	gurmuiK Awpu pCwxIAY Avr ik kry krwie ]9] (60-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh aap pachhaanee-ai avar ke karay karaa-ay. ||9||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v9	When one becomes Gurmukh and realizes his own self, what more is there left to do or have done? ||9||
RECORD	para 2514	imilAw kw ikAw mylIAY sbid imly pqIAwie ] (60-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mili-aa kaa ki-aa maylee-ai sabad milay patee-aa-ay. Why speak of union to those who are already united with the Lord? Receiving the Shabad, they are satisfied.
RECORD	para 2515	mnmuiK soJI nw pvY vICuiV cotw Kwie ] (60-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manmukh sojhee naa pavai veechhurh chotaa khaa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs do not understand; separated from Him, they endure beatings.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v10	nwnk dru Gru eyku hY Avru n dUjI jwie ]10]11] (60-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak dar ghar ayk hai avar na doojee jaa-ay. ||10||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v10	11|| O Nanak, there is only the one door to His Home; there is no other place at all. ||10||11||
RECORD	para 2518	mnmuiK BulY BulweIAY BUlI Taur n kwie ] (60-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manmukh bhulai bhulaa-ee-ai bhoolee tha-ur na kaa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs wander around, deluded and deceived. They find no place of rest.
DEFINE	para 2519	gur ibnu ko n idKwveI AMDI AwvY jwie ] (60-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur bin ko na dikhaava-ee anDhee aavai jaa-ay. Without the Guru, no one is shown the Way. Like the blind, they continue coming and going.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	igAwn pdwrQu KoieAw TigAw muTw jwie ]1] (60-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gi-aan padaarath kho-i-aa thagi-aa muthaa jaa-ay. ||1||
UPHOLD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	Having lost the treasure of spiritual wisdom, they depart, defrauded and plundered. ||1||
RECORD	para 2521	bwbw mwieAw Brim Bulwie ] (60-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) baabaa maa-i-aa bharam bhulaa-ay. O Baba, Maya deceives with its illusion.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	Brim BulI fohwgxI nw ipr AMik smwie ]1] rhwau ] (60-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bharam bhulee dohaaganee naa pir ank samaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Deceived by doubt, the discarded bride is not received into the Lap of her Beloved. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 2523	BUlI iPrY idsMqrI BUlI igRhu qij jwie ] (60-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhoolee firai disantree bhoolee garihu taj jaa-ay. The deceived bride wanders around in foreign lands; she leaves, and abandons her own home.
RECORD	para 2524	BUlI fUMgir Qil cVY BrmY mnu folwie ] (60-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhoolee doongar thal charhai bharmai man dolaa-ay. Deceived, she climbs the plateaus and mountains; her mind wavers in doubt.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Durhu ivCuMnI ikau imlY grib muTI ibllwie ]2] (60-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) Dharahu vichhunnee ki-o milai garab muthee billaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Separated from the Primal Being, how can she meet with Him again? Plundered by pride, she cries out and bewails. ||2||
RECORD	para 2526	ivCuiVAw guru mylsI hir ris nwm ipAwir ] (60-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vichhurhi-aa gur maylsee har ras naam pi-aar. The Guru unites the separated ones with the Lord again, through the love of the Delicious Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 2528	swic shij soBw GxI hir gux nwm ADwir ] (61-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saach sahj sobhaa ghanee har gun naam aDhaar. Through truth and intuitive poise, great honor is obtained, with the Support of the Naam and the Glory of the Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	ijau BwvY iqau rKu qUM mY quJ ibnu kvnu Bqwru ]3] (61-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o bhaavai ti-o rakh tooN mai tujh bin kavan bhataar. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	As it pleases You, Lord, please save and protect me. Without You, O my Husband Lord, who else is there for me? ||3||
RECORD	para 2530	AKr piV piV BulIAY ByKI bhuqu AiBmwnu ] (61-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) akhar parh parh bhulee-ai bhaykhee bahut abhimaan. Reading their books over and over again, people continue making mistakes; they are so proud of their religious robes.
WHEN	para 2531	qIrQ nwqw ikAw kry mn mih mYlu gumwnu ] (61-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tirath naataa ki-aa karay man meh mail gumaan. But what is the use of bathing at sacred shrines of pilgrimage, when the filth of stubborn pride is within the mind?
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	gur ibnu ikin smJweIAY mnu rwjw sulqwnu ]4] (61-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur bin kin samjaa-ee-ai man raajaa sultaan. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Other than the Guru, who can explain that within the mind is the Lord, the King, the Emperor? ||4||
DEFINE	para 2533	pRym pdwrQu pweIAY gurmuiK qqu vIcwru ] (61-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) paraym padaarath paa-ee-ai gurmukh tat veechaar. The Treasure of the Lord's Love is obtained by the Gurmukh, who contemplates the essence of reality.
RECORD	para 2534	sw Dn Awpu gvwieAw gur kY sbid sIgwru ] (61-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saa Dhan aap gavaa-i-aa gur kai sabad seegaar. The bride eradicates her selfishness, and adorns herself with the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	Gr hI so ipru pwieAw gur kY hyiq Apwru ]5] (61-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ghar hee so pir paa-i-aa gur kai hayt apaar. ||5||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	Within her own home, she finds her Husband, through infinite love for the Guru. ||5||
DEFINE	para 2536	gur kI syvw cwkrI mnu inrmlu suKu hoie ] (61-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur kee sayvaa chaakree man nirmal sukh ho-ay. Applying oneself to the service of the Guru, the mind is purified, and peace is obtained.
DEFINE	para 2537	gur kw sbdu min visAw haumY ivchu Koie ] (61-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur kaa sabad man vasi-aa ha-umai vichahu kho-ay. The Word of the Guru's Shabad abides within the mind, and egotism is eliminated from within.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	nwmu pdwrQu pwieAw lwBu sdw min hoie ]6] (61-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naam padaarath paa-i-aa laabh sadaa man ho-ay. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	The Treasure of the Naam is acquired, and the mind reaps the lasting profit. ||6||
WHEN	para 2539	krim imlY qw pweIAY Awip n lieAw jwie ] (61-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) karam milai taa paa-ee-ai aap na la-i-aa jaa-ay. If He grants His Grace, then we obtain it. We cannot find it by our own efforts.
RECORD	para 2540	gur kI crxI lig rhu ivchu Awpu gvwie ] (61-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur kee charnee lag rahu vichahu aap gavaa-ay. Remain attached to the Feet of the Guru, and eradicate selfishness from within.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	scy syqI riqAw sco plY pwie ]7] (61-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sachay saytee rati-aa sacho palai paa-ay. ||7||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Attuned to Truth, you shall obtain the True One. ||7||
DEFINE	para 2542	Bulx AMdir sBu ko ABulu gurU krqwru ] (61-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhulan andar sabh ko abhul guroo kartaar. Everyone makes mistakes; only the Guru and the Creator are infallible.
RECORD	para 2543	gurmiq mnu smJwieAw lwgw iqsY ipAwru ] (61-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmat man samjhaa-i-aa laagaa tisai pi-aar. One who instructs his mind with the Guru's Teachings comes to embrace love for the Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk swcu n vIsrY myly sbdu Apwru ]8]12] (61-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak saach na veesrai maylay sabad apaar. ||8||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	12|| O Nanak, do not forget the Truth; you shall receive the Infinite Word of the Shabad. ||8||12||
RECORD	para 2546	iqRsnw mwieAw mohxI suq bMDp Gr nwir ] (61-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tarisnaa maa-i-aa mohnee sut banDhap ghar naar. The enticing desire for Maya leads people to become emotionally attached to their children, relatives, households and spouses.
DEFINE	para 2547	Din jobin jgu TigAw lib loiB AhMkwir ] (61-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) Dhan joban jag thagi-aa lab lobh aha Nkaar. The world is deceived and plundered by riches, youth, greed and egotism.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	moh TgaulI hau mueI sw vrqY sMswir ]1] (61-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) moh thag-ulee ha-o mu-ee saa vartai sansaar. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	The drug of emotional attachment has destroyed me, as it has destroyed the whole world. ||1||
RECORD	para 2549	myry pRIqmw mY quJ ibnu Avru n koie ] (61-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mayray pareetamaa mai tujh bin avar na ko-ay. O my Beloved, I have no one except You.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	mY quJ ibnu Avru n BwveI qUM Bwvih suKu hoie ]1] rhwau ] (61-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) mai tujh bin avar na bhaav-ee tooN bhaaveh sukh ho-ay. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Without You, nothing else pleases me. Loving You, I am at peace. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 2551	nwmu swlwhI rMg isau gur kY sbid sMqoKu ] (61-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naam saalaahee rang si-o gur kai sabad santokh. I sing the Praises of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, with love; I am content with the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
REQUIRE	para 2552	jo dIsY so clsI kUVw mohu n vyKu ] (61-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jo deesai so chalsee koorhaa moh na vaykh. Whatever is seen shall pass away. So do not be attached to this false show.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	vwt vtwaU AwieAw inq cldw swQu dyKu ]2] (61-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vaat vataa-oo aa-i-aa nit chaldaa saath daykh. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Like a traveller in his travels, you have come. Behold the caravan leaving each day. ||2||
DEFINE	para 2554	AwKix AwKih kyqVy gur ibnu bUJ n hoie ] (61-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aakhan aakhahi kayt-rhay gur bin boojh na ho-ay. Many preach sermons, but without the Guru, understanding is not obtained.
DEFINE	para 2555	nwmu vfweI jy imlY sic rpY piq hoie ] (61-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naam vadaa-ee jay milai sach rapai pat ho-ay. If someone receives the Glory of the Naam, he is attuned to truth and blessed with honor.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	jo quDu Bwvih sy Bly Kotw Krw n koie ]3] (61-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jo tuDh bhaaveh say bhalay khotaa kharaa na ko-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	Those who are pleasing to You are good; no one is counterfeit or genuine. ||3||
DEFINE	para 2557	gur srxweI CutIAY mnmuK KotI rwis ] (61-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur sarnaa-ee chhutee-ai manmukh khotee raas. In the Guru's Sanctuary we are saved. The assets of the self-willed manmukhs are false.
DEFINE	para 2558	Ast Dwqu pwiqswh kI GVIAY sbid ivgwis ] (61-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) asat Dhaat paatisaah kee gharhee-ai sabad vigaas. The eight metals of the King are made into coins by the Word of His Shabad.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	Awpy prKy pwrKU pvY KjwnY rwis ]4] (61-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay parkhay paarkhoo pavai khajaanai raas. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	The Assayer Himself assays them, and He places the genuine ones in His Treasury. ||4||
RECORD	para 2560	qyrI kImiq nw pvY sB ifTI Toik vjwie ] (61-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tayree keemat naa pavai sabh dithee thok vajaa-ay. Your Value cannot be appraised; I have seen and tested everything.
DEFINE	para 2561	khxY hwQ n lBeI sic itkY piq pwie ] (61-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kahnai haath na labh-ee sach tikai pat paa-ay. By speaking, His Depth cannot be found. Abiding in truth, honor is obtained.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	gurmiq qUM swlwhxw horu kImiq khxu n jwie ]5] (61-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmat tooN salaahnaa hor keemat kahan na jaa-ay. ||5||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	Through the Guru's Teachings, I praise You; otherwise, I cannot describe Your Value. ||5||
DEFINE	para 2563	ijqu qin nwmu n BwveI iqqu qin haumY vwdu ] (61-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jit tan naam na bhaav-ee tit tan ha-umai vaad. That body which does not appreciate the Naam-that body is infested with egotism and conflict.
DEFINE	para 2564	gur ibnu igAwnu n pweIAY ibiKAw dUjw swdu ] (61-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gur bin gi-aan na paa-ee-ai bikhi-aa doojaa saad. Without the Guru, spiritual wisdom is not obtained; other tastes are poison.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	ibnu gux kwim n AwveI mwieAw PIkw swdu ]6] (61-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin gun kaam na aavee maa-i-aa feekaa saad. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	Without virtue, nothing is of any use. The taste of Maya is bland and insipid. ||6||
DEFINE	para 2566	Awsw AMdir jMimAw Awsw rs ks Kwie ] (61-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aasaa andar jammi-aa aasaa ras kas khaa-ay. Through desire, people are cast into the womb and reborn. Through desire, they taste the sweet and sour flavors.
DEFINE	para 2567	Awsw bMiD clweIAY muhy muih cotw Kwie ] (61-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aasaa banDh chalaa-ee-ai muhay muhi chotaa khaa-ay. Bound by desire, they are led on, beaten and struck on their faces and mouths.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Avgix bDw mwrIAY CUtY gurmiq nwie ]7] (61-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) avgan baDhaa maaree-ai chhootai gurmat naa-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Bound and gagged and assaulted by evil, they are released only through the Name, through the Guru's Teachings. ||7||
DEFINE	para 2570	srby QweI eyku qUM ijau BwvY iqau rwKu ] (62-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sarbay thaa-ee ayk tooN ji-o bhaavai ti-o raakh. In all places, You are the One and Only. As it pleases You, Lord, please save and protect me!
RECORD	para 2571	gurmiq swcw min vsY nwmu Blo piq swKu ] (62-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmat saachaa man vasai naam bhalo pat saakh. Through the Guru's Teachings, the True One abides within the mind. The Companionship of the Naam brings the most excellent honor.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	haumY rogu gvweIAY sbid scY scu BwKu ]8] (62-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ha-umai rog gavaa-ee-ai sabad sachai sach bhaakh. ||8||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	Eradicate the disease of egotism, and chant the True Shabad, the Word of the True Lord. ||8||
DEFINE	para 2573	AwkwsI pwqwil qUM iqRBvix rihAw smwie ] (62-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aakaasee paataal tooN taribhavan rahi-aa samaa-ay. You are pervading throughout the Akaashic Ethers, the nether regions and the three worlds.
DEFINE	para 2574	Awpy BgqI Bwau qUM Awpy imlih imlwie ] (62-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aapay bhagtee bhaa-o tooN aapay mileh milaa-ay. You Yourself are bhakti, loving devotional worship. You Yourself unite us in Union with Yourself.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v9	nwnk nwmu n vIsrY ijau BwvY iqvY rjwie ]9]13] (62-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak naam na veesrai ji-o bhaavai tivai rajaa-ay. ||9||
ALLOW	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v9	13|| O Nanak, may I never forget the Naam! As is Your Pleasure, so is Your Will. ||9||13||
DEFINE	para 2577	rwm nwim mnu byiDAw Avru ik krI vIcwru ] (62-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) raam naam man bayDhi-aa avar ke karee veechaar. My mind is pierced through by the Name of the Lord. What else should I contemplate?
RECORD	para 2578	sbd suriq suKu aUpjY pRB rwqau suK swru ] (62-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabad surat sukh oopjai parabh raata-o sukh saar. Focusing your awareness on the Shabad, happiness wells up. Attuned to God, the most excellent peace is found.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ijau BwvY iqau rwKu qUM mY hir nwmu ADwru ]1] (62-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o bhaavai ti-o raakh tooN mai har naam aDhaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	As it pleases You, please save me, Lord. The Name of the Lord is my Support. ||1||
DEFINE	para 2580	mn ry swcI Ksm rjwie ] (62-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) man ray saachee khasam rajaa-ay. O mind, the Will of our Lord and Master is true.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	ijin qnu mnu swij sIgwirAw iqsu syqI ilv lwie ]1] rhwau ] (62-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jin tan man saaj seegaari-aa tis saytee liv laa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Focus your love upon the One who created and adorned your body and mind. ||1||Pause||
WHEN	para 2582	qnu bYsMqir homIAY iek rqI qoil ktwie ] (62-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tan baisantar homee-ai ik ratee tol kataa-ay. If I cut my body into pieces, and burn them in the fire,
WHEN	para 2583	qnu mnu smDw jy krI Anidnu Agin jlwie ] (62-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tan man samDhaa jay karee an-din agan jalaa-ay. and if I make my body and mind into firewood, and night and day burn them in the fire,
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	hir nwmY quil n pujeI jy lK kotI krm kmwie ]2] (62-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har naamai tul na puj-ee jay lakh kotee karam kamaa-ay. ||2||
WHEN	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	and if I perform hundreds of thousands and millions of religious rituals-still, all these are not equal to the Name of the Lord. ||2||
WHEN	para 2585	ArD srIru ktweIAY isir krvqu Drwie ] (62-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) araDh sareer kataa-ee-ai sir karvat Dharaa-ay. If my body were cut in half, if a saw was put to my head,
WHEN	para 2586	qnu hYmMcil gwlIAY BI mn qy rogu n jwie ] (62-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tan haimanchal gaalee-ai bhee man tay rog na jaa-ay. and if my body were frozen in the Himalayas-even then, my mind would not be free of disease.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	hir nwmY quil n pujeI sB ifTI Toik vjwie ]3] (62-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har naamai tul na puj-ee sabh dithee thok vajaa-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	None of these are equal to the Name of the Lord. I have seen and tried and tested them all. ||3||
WHEN	para 2588	kMcn ky kot dqu krI bhu hYvr gYvr dwnu ] (62-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kanchan kay kot dat karee baho haivar gaivar daan. If I made a donation of castles of gold, and gave lots of fine horses and wondrous elephants in charity,
WHEN	para 2589	BUim dwnu gaUAw GxI BI AMqir grbu gumwnu ] (62-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhoom daan ga-oo-aa ghanee bhee antar garab gumaan. and if I made donations of land and cows-even then, pride and ego would still be within me.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	rwm nwim mnu byiDAw guir dIAw scu dwnu ]4] (62-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) raam naam man bayDhi-aa gur dee-aa sach daan. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	The Name of the Lord has pierced my mind; the Guru has given me this true gift. ||4||
DEFINE	para 2591	mnhT buDI kyqIAw kyqy byd bIcwr ] (62-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manhath buDhee kaytee-aa kaytay bayd beechaar. There are so many stubborn-minded intelligent people, and so many who contemplate the Vedas.
DEFINE	para 2592	kyqy bMDn jIA ky gurmuiK moK duAwr ] (62-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kaytay banDhan jee-a kay gurmukh mokh du-aar. There are so many entanglements for the soul. Only as Gurmukh do we find the Gate of Liberation.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	schu ErY sBu ko aupir scu Awcwru ]5] (62-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sachahu orai sabh ko upar sach aachaar. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	Truth is higher than everything; but higher still is truthful living. ||5||
RECORD	para 2594	sBu ko aUcw AwKIAY nIcu n dIsY koie ] (62-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabh ko oochaa aakhee-ai neech na deesai ko-ay. Call everyone exalted; no one seems lowly.
RECORD	para 2595	ieknY BWfy swijAY ieku cwnxu iqhu loie ] (62-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) iknai bhaa Nday saaji-ai ik chaanan tihu lo-ay. The One Lord has fashioned the vessels, and His One Light pervades the three worlds.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	krim imlY scu pweIAY Duir bKs n mytY koie ]6] (62-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) karam milai sach paa-ee-ai Dhur bakhas na maytai ko-ay. ||6||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	Receiving His Grace, we obtain Truth. No one can erase His Primal Blessing. ||6||
WHEN	para 2597	swDu imlY swDU jnY sMqoKu vsY gur Bwie ] (62-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saaDh milai saaDhoo janai santokh vasai gur bhaa-ay. When one Holy person meets another Holy person, they abide in contentment, through the Love of the Guru.
RECORD	para 2598	AkQ kQw vIcwrIAY jy siqgur mwih smwie ] (62-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) akath kathaa veechaaree-ai jay satgur maahi samaa-ay. They contemplate the Unspoken Speech, merging in absorption in the True Guru.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	pI AMimRqu sMqoiKAw drgih pYDw jwie ]7] (62-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pee amrit santokhi-aa dargahi paiDhaa jaa-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Drinking in the Ambrosial Nectar, they are contented; they go to the Court of the Lord in robes of honor. ||7||
RECORD	para 2600	Git Git vwjY ikMgurI Anidnu sbid suBwie ] (62-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ghat ghat vaajai kinguree an-din sabad subhaa-ay. In each and every heart the Music of the Lord's Flute vibrates, night and day, with sublime love for the Shabad.
RECORD	para 2601	ivrly kau soJI peI gurmuiK mnu smJwie ] (62-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) virlay ka-o sojhee pa-ee gurmukh man samjhaa-ay. Only those few who become Gurmukh understand this by instructing their minds.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk nwmu n vIsrY CUtY sbdu kmwie ]8]14] (62-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak naam na veesrai chhootai sabad kamaa-ay. ||8||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	14|| O Nanak, do not forget the Naam. Practicing the Shabad you shall be saved. ||8||14||
DEFINE	para 2604	icqy idsih Daulhr bgy bMk duAwr ] (62-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) chitay diseh Dha-ulhar bagay bank du-aar. There are painted mansions to behold, white-washed, with beautiful doors;
DEFINE	para 2605	kir mn KusI auswirAw dUjY hyiq ipAwir ] (62-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kar man khusee usaari-aa doojai hayt pi-aar. they were constructed to give pleasure to the mind, but this is only for the sake of the love of duality.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	AMdru KwlI pRym ibnu Fih FyrI qnu Cwru ]1] (62-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) andar khaalee paraym bin dheh dhayree tan chhaar. ||1||
REQUIRE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	The inner being is empty without love. The body shall crumble into a heap of ashes. ||1||
FORBID	para 2607	BweI ry qnu Dnu swiQ n hoie ] (62-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaa-ee ray tan Dhan saath na ho-ay. O Siblings of Destiny, this body and wealth shall not go along with you.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rwm nwmu Dnu inrmlo guru dwiq kry pRBu soie ]1] rhwau ] (62-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) raam naam Dhan nirmalo gur daat karay parabh so-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. The Lord's Name is the pure wealth; through the Guru, God bestows this gift. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 2609	rwm nwmu Dnu inrmlo jy dyvY dyvxhwru ] (62-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) raam naam Dhan nirmalo jay dayvai dayvanhaar. The Lord's Name is the pure wealth; it is given only by the Giver.
FORBID	para 2610	AwgY pUC n hoveI ijsu bylI guru krqwru ] (62-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aagai poochh na hova-ee jis baylee gur kartaar. One who has the Guru, the Creator, as his Friend, shall not be questioned hereafter.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	Awip Cfwey CutIAY Awpy bKsxhwru ]2] (62-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aap chhadaa-ay chhutee-ai aapay bakhsanhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v2	He Himself delivers those who are delivered. He Himself is the Forgiver. ||2||
RECORD	para 2613	mnmuKu jwxY Awpxy DIAw pUq sMjogu ] (63-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manmukh jaanai aapnay Dhee-aa poot sanjog. The self-willed manmukh looks upon his daughters, sons and relatives as his own.
DEFINE	para 2614	nwrI dyiK ivgwsIAih nwly hrKu su sogu ] (63-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naaree daykh vigaasee-ah naalay harakh so sog. Gazing upon his wife, he is pleased. But along with happiness, they bring grief.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	gurmuiK sbid rMgwvly Aihinis hir rsu Bogu ]3] (63-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh sabad rangaavlay ahinis har ras bhog. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v3	The Gurmukhs are attuned to the Word of the Shabad. Day and night, they enjoy the Sublime Essence of the Lord. ||3||
RECORD	para 2616	icqu clY ivqu jwvxo swkq foil folwie ] (63-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) chit chalai vit jaavno saakat dol dolaa-ay. The consciousness of the wicked, faithless cynics wanders around in search of transitory wealth, unstable and distracted.
WHEN	para 2617	bwhir FUMiF ivgucIAY Gr mih vsqu suQwie ] (63-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) baahar dhoondh viguchee-ai ghar meh vasat suthaa-ay. Searching outside of themselves, they are ruined; the object of their search is in that sacred place within the home of the heart.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	mnmuiK haumY kir musI gurmuiK plY pwie ]4] (63-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manmukh ha-umai kar musee gurmukh palai paa-ay. ||4||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v4	The self-willed manmukhs, in their ego, miss it; the Gurmukhs receive it in their laps. ||4||
RECORD	para 2619	swkq inrguixAwirAw Awpxw mUlu pCwxu ] (63-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) saakat nirguni-aari-aa aapnaa mool pachhaan. You worthless, faithless cynic-recognize your own origin!
REQUIRE	para 2620	rkqu ibMdu kw iehu qno AgnI pwis iprwxu ] (63-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) rakat bind kaa ih tano agnee paas piraan. This body is made of blood and semen. It shall be consigned to the fire in the end.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	pvxY kY vis dyhurI msqik scu nIswxu ]5] (63-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pavnai kai vas dayhuree mastak sach neesaan. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v5	The body is under the power of the breath, according to the True Sign inscribed upon your forehead. ||5||
RECORD	para 2622	bhuqw jIvxu mMgIAY muAw n loVY koie ] (63-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bahutaa jeevan mangee-ai mu-aa na lorhai ko-ay. Everyone begs for a long life-no one wishes to die.
RECORD	para 2623	suK jIvxu iqsu AwKIAY ijsu gurmuiK visAw soie ] (63-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sukh jeevan tis aakhee-ai jis gurmukh vasi-aa so-ay. A life of peace and comfort comes to that Gurmukh, within whom God dwells.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	nwm ivhUxy ikAw gxI ijsu hir gur drsu n hoie ]6] (63-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naam vihoonay ki-aa ganee jis har gur daras na ho-ay. ||6||
UPHOLD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v6	Without the Naam, what good those who do not have the Blessed Vision, the Darshan of the Lord and Guru? ||6||
RECORD	para 2625	ijau supnY inis BulIAY jb lig indRw hoie ] (63-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) ji-o supnai nis bhulee-ai jab lag nidraa ho-ay. In their dreams at night, people wander around as long as they sleep;
RECORD	para 2626	ieau srpin kY vis jIAVw AMqir haumY doie ] (63-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) i-o sarpan kai vas jee-arhaa antar ha-umai do-ay. just so, they are under the power of the snake Maya, as long as their hearts are filled with ego and duality.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	gurmiq hoie vIcwrIAY supnw iehu jgu loie ]7] (63-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmat ho-ay veechaaree-ai supnaa ih jag lo-ay. ||7||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v7	Through the Guru's Teachings, they come to understand and see that this world is just a dream. ||7||
DEFINE	para 2628	Agin mrY jlu pweIAY ijau bwirk dUDY mwie ] (63-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) agan marai jal paa-ee-ai ji-o baarik dooDhai maa-ay. As thirst is quenched with water, and the baby is satisfied with mother's milk,
RECORD	para 2629	ibnu jl kml su nw QIAY ibnu jl mInu mrwie ] (63-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin jal kamal so naa thee-ai bin jal meen maraa-ay. and as the lotus does not exist without water, and as the fish dies without water
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	nwnk gurmuiK hir ris imlY jIvw hir gux gwie ]8]15] (63-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh har ras milai jeevaa har gun gaa-ay. ||8||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v8	15|| -O Nanak, so does the Gurmukh live, receiving the Sublime Essence of the Lord, and singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||8||15||
RECORD	para 2632	fUMgru dyiK frwvxo pyeIAVY frIAwsu ] (63-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) doongar daykh daraavno pay-ee-arhai daree-aas. Beholding the terrifying mountain in this world of my father's home, I am terrified.
DEFINE	para 2633	aUcau prbqu gwKVo nw pauVI iqqu qwsu ] (63-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) oocha-o parbat gaakh-rho naa pa-orhee tit taas. It is so difficult to climb this high mountain; there is no ladder which reaches up there.
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	gurmuiK AMqir jwixAw guir mylI qrIAwsu ]1] (63-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) gurmukh antar jaani-aa gur maylee taree-aas. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	But as Gurmukh, I know that it is within my self; the Guru has brought me to Union, and so I cross over. ||1||
DEFINE	para 2635	BweI ry Bvjlu ibKmu frWau ] (63-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bhaa-ee ray bhavjal bikham daraa N-o. O Siblings of Destiny, the terrifying world-ocean is so difficult to cross-I am terrified!
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	pUrw siqguru ris imlY guru qwry hir nwau ]1] rhwau ] (63-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) pooraa satgur ras milai gur taaray har naa-o. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwgu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. The Perfect True Guru, in His Pleasure, has met with me; the Guru has saved me, through the Name of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
REQUIRE	para 2637	clw clw jy krI jwxw clxhwru ] (63-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) chalaa chalaa jay karee jaanaa chalanhaar. I may say, "I am going, I am going", but I know that, in the end, I must really go.
REQUIRE	para 2638	jo AwieAw so clsI Amru su guru krqwru ] (63-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jo aa-i-aa so chalsee amar so gur kartaar. Whoever comes must also go. Only the Guru and the Creator are Eternal.
