RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	They obtain the Perfect Vision of the Lord, while those who gossip find no place of rest. ||2||
RECORD	para 3407	pauVI ] (83-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3408	sB Awpy quDu aupwie kY Awip kwrY lweI ] (83-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabh aapay tuDh upaa-ay kai aap kaarai laa-ee. You Yourself created all; You Yourself delegate the tasks.
DEFINE	para 3409	qUM Awpy vyiK ivgsdw AwpxI vifAweI ] (83-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tooN aapay vaykh vigsadaa aapnee vadi-aa-ee. You Yourself are pleased, beholding Your Own Glorious Greatness.
DEFINE	para 3410	hir quDhu bwhir ikCu nwhI qUM scw sweI ] (83-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har tuDhhu baahar kichh naahee tooN sachaa saa-ee. O Lord, there is nothing at all beyond You. You are the True Lord.
DEFINE	para 3411	qUM Awpy Awip vrqdw sBnI hI QweI ] (83-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tooN aapay aap varatdaa sabhnee hee thaa-ee. You Yourself are contained in all places.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	hir iqsY iDAwvhu sMq jnhu jo ley CfweI ]2] (83-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har tisai Dhi-aavahu sant janhu jo la-ay chhadaa-ee. ||2||
REQUIRE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	Meditate on that Lord, O Saints; He shall rescue and save you. ||2||
RECORD	para 3413	slok mÚ 1 ] (83-13) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3414	PkV jwqI PkVu nwau ] (83-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) fakarh jaatee fakarh naa-o. Pride in social status is empty; pride in personal glory is useless.
RECORD	para 3415	sBnw jIAw iekw Cwau ] (83-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sabhnaa jee-aa ikaa chhaa-o. The One Lord gives shade to all beings.
ALLOW	para 3416	Awphu jy ko Blw khwey ] (83-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) aaphu jay ko bhalaa kahaa-ay. You may call yourself good;
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk qw pru jwpY jw piq lyKY pwey ]1] (83-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak taa par jaapai jaa pat laykhai paa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, this will only be known when your honor is approved in God's Account. ||1||
RECORD	para 3418	mÚ 2 ] (83-15) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 3419	ijsu ipAwry isau nyhu iqsu AwgY mir clIAY ] (83-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) jis pi-aaray si-o nayhu tis aagai mar chalee-ai. Die before the one whom you love;
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	iDRgu jIvxu sMswir qw kY pwCY jIvxw ]2] (83-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) Dharig jeevan sansaar taa kai paachhai jeevnaa. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	to live after he dies is to live a worthless life in this world. ||2||
RECORD	para 3421	pauVI ] (83-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3422	quDu Awpy DrqI swjIAY cMdu sUrju duie dIvy ] (83-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) tuDh aapay Dhartee saajee-ai chand sooraj du-ay deevay. You Yourself created the earth, and the two lamps of the sun and the moon.
DEFINE	para 3423	ds cwir ht quDu swijAw vwpwru krIvy ] (83-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) das chaar hat tuDh saaji-aa vaapaar kareevay. You created the fourteen world-shops, in which Your Business is transacted.
RECORD	para 3424	ieknw no hir lwBu dyie jo gurmuiK QIvy ] (83-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) iknaa no har laabh day-ay jo gurmukh theevay. The Lord bestows His Profits on those who become Gurmukh.
RECORD	para 3425	iqn jmkwlu n ivAwpeI ijn scu AMimRqu pIvy ] (83-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) tin jamkaal na vi-aapa-ee jin sach amrit peevay. The Messenger of Death does not touch those who drink in the True Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v3	Eie Awip Cuty prvwr isau iqn ipCY sBu jgqu CutIvy ]3] (83-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) o-ay aap chhutay parvaar si-o tin pichhai sabh jagat chhuteevay. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v3	They themselves are saved, along with their family, and all those who follow them are saved as well. ||3||
RECORD	para 3427	slok mÚ 1 ] (83-18) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 3428	kudriq kir kY visAw soie ] (83-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kudrat kar kai vasi-aa so-ay. He created the Creative Power of the Universe, within which He dwells.
RECORD	para 3430	vKqu vIcwry su bMdw hoie ] (84-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) vakhat veechaaray so bandaa ho-ay. One who reflects upon his allotted span of life, becomes the slave of God.
RECORD	para 3431	kudriq hY kImiq nhI pwie ] (84-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) kudrat hai keemat nahee paa-ay. The value of the Creative Power of the Universe cannot be known.
WHEN	para 3432	jw kImiq pwie q khI n jwie ] (84-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jaa keemat paa-ay ta kahee na jaa-ay. Even if its value were known, it could not be described.
RECORD	para 3433	srY srIAiq krih bIcwru ] (84-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sarai saree-at karahi beechaar. Some think about religious rituals and regulations,
RECORD	para 3434	ibnu bUJy kYsy pwvih pwru ] (84-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) bin boojhay kaisay paavahi paar. but without understanding, how can they cross over to the other side?
RECORD	para 3435	isdku kir isjdw mnu kir mKsUdu ] (84-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) sidak kar sijdaa man kar makhsood. Let sincere faith be your bowing in prayer, and let the conquest of your mind be your objective in life.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	ijh iDir dyKw iqh iDir maujUdu ]1] (84-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) jih Dhir daykhaa tih Dhir ma-ujood. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	Wherever I look, there I see God's Presence. ||1||
RECORD	para 3437	mÚ 3 ] (84-3) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3438	gur sBw eyv n pweIAY nw nyVY nw dUir ] (84-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur sabhaa ayv na paa-ee-ai naa nayrhai naa door. The Society of the Guru is not obtained like this, by trying to be near or far away.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk siqguru qW imlY jw mnu rhY hdUir ]2] (84-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak satgur taaN milai jaa man rahai hadoor. ||2||
REQUIRE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, you shall meet the True Guru, if your mind remains in His Presence. ||2||
RECORD	para 3440	pauVI ] (84-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3441	spq dIp spq swgrw nv KMf cwir vyd ds Ast purwxw ] (84-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sapat deep sapat saagraa nav khand chaar vayd das asat puraanaa. The seven islands, seven seas, nine continents, four Vedas and eighteen Puraanas
RECORD	para 3442	hir sBnw ivic qUM vrqdw hir sBnw Bwxw ] (84-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har sabhnaa vich tooN varatdaa har sabhnaa bhaanaa. -O Lord, You pervade and permeate all. Lord, everyone loves You.
RECORD	para 3443	siB quJY iDAwvih jIA jMq hir swrg pwxw ] (84-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabh tujhai Dhi-aavahi jee-a jant har saarag paanaa. All beings and creatures meditate on You, Lord. You hold the earth in Your Hands.
RECORD	para 3444	jo gurmuiK hir AwrwDdy iqn hau kurbwxw ] (84-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jo gurmukh har aaraaDhaday tin ha-o kurbaanaa. I am a sacrifice to those Gurmukhs who worship and adore the Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v4	qUM Awpy Awip vrqdw kir coj ivfwxw ]4] (84-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) tooN aapay aap varatdaa kar choj vidaanaa. ||4||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v4	You Yourself are All-pervading; You stage this wondrous drama! ||4||
RECORD	para 3446	slok mÚ 3 ] (84-7) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3447	klau mswjnI ikAw sdweIAY ihrdY hI iliK lyhu ] (84-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) kala-o masaajnee ki-aa sadaa-ee-ai hirdai hee likh layho. Why ask for a pen, and why ask for ink? Write within your heart.
REQUIRE	para 3448	sdw swihb kY rMig rhY kbhUM n qUtis nyhu ] (84-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sadaa saahib kai rang rahai kabahoo N na tootas nayhu. Remain immersed forever in the Love of your Lord and Master, and your love for Him shall never break.
REQUIRE	para 3449	klau mswjnI jwiesI iliKAw BI nwly jwie ] (84-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) kala-o masaajnee jaa-isee likhi-aa bhee naalay jaa-ay. Pen and ink shall pass away, along with what has been written.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk sh pRIiq n jwiesI jo Duir CofI scY pwie ]1] (84-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak sah pareet na jaa-isee jo Dhur chhodee sachai paa-ay. ||1||
REQUIRE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, the Love of your Husband Lord shall never perish. The True Lord has bestowed it, as it was pre-ordained. ||1||
RECORD	para 3451	mÚ 3 ] (84-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
FORBID	para 3452	ndrI Awvdw nwil n cleI vyKhu ko ivaupwie ] (84-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) nadree aavdaa naal na chal-ee vaykhhu ko vi-upaa-ay. That which is seen, shall not go along with you. What does it take to make you see this?
RECORD	para 3453	siqguir scu idRVwieAw sic rhhu ilv lwie ] (84-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur sach drirh-aa-i-aa sach rahhu liv laa-ay. The True Guru has implanted the True Name within; remain lovingly absorbed in the True One.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk sbdI scu hY krmI plY pwie ]2] (84-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak sabdee sach hai karmee palai paa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, the Word of His Shabad is True. By His Grace, it is obtained. ||2||
RECORD	para 3455	pauVI ] (84-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 3456	hir AMdir bwhir ieku qUM qUM jwxih Byqu ] (84-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har andar baahar ik tooN tooN jaaneh bhayt. O Lord, You are inside and outside as well. You are the Knower of secrets.
RECORD	para 3457	jo kIcY so hir jwxdw myry mn hir cyqu ] (84-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jo keechai so har jaandaa mayray man har chayt. Whatever anyone does, the Lord knows. O my mind, think of the Lord.
UPHOLD	para 3458	so frY ij pwp kmwvdw DrmI ivgsyqu ] (84-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) so darai je paap kamaavdaa Dharmee vigsayt. The one who commits sins lives in fear, while the one who lives righteously rejoices.
DEFINE	para 3459	qUM scw Awip inAwau scu qw frIAY kyqu ] (84-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) tooN sachaa aap ni-aa-o sach taa daree-ai kayt. O Lord, You Yourself are True, and True is Your Justice. Why should anyone be afraid?
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v5	ijnw nwnk scu pCwixAw sy sic rlyqu ]5] (84-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jinaa naanak sach pachhaani-aa say sach ralayt. ||5||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v5	O Nanak, those who recognize the True Lord are blended with the True One. ||5||
RECORD	para 3461	slok mÚ 3 ] (84-13) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3462	klm jlau sxu msvwxIAY kwgdu BI jil jwau ] (84-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) kalam jala-o san masvaanee-ai kaagad bhee jal jaa-o. Burn the pen, and burn the ink; burn the paper as well.
RECORD	para 3463	ilKx vwlw jil blau ijin iliKAw dUjw Bwau ] (84-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) likhan vaalaa jal bala-o jin likhi-aa doojaa bhaa-o. Burn the writer who writes in the love of duality.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk pUrib iliKAw kmwvxw Avru n krxw jwie ]1] (84-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak poorab likhi-aa kamaavanaa avar na karnaa jaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, people do what is pre-ordained; they cannot do anything else. ||1||
RECORD	para 3465	mÚ 3 ] (84-15) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3466	horu kUVu pVxw kUVu bolxw mwieAw nwil ipAwru ] (84-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) hor koorh parh-naa koorh bolnaa maa-i-aa naal pi-aar. False is other reading, and false is other speaking, in the love of Maya.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk ivxu nwvY ko iQru nhI piV piV hoie KuAwru ]2] (84-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak vin naavai ko thir nahee parh parh ho-ay khu-aar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, without the Name, nothing is permanent; those who read and read are ruined. ||2||
RECORD	para 3468	pauVI ] (84-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 3469	hir kI vifAweI vfI hY hir kIrqnu hir kw ] (84-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kee vadi-aa-ee vadee hai har keertan har kaa. Great is the Greatness of the Lord, and the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises.
DEFINE	para 3470	hir kI vifAweI vfI hY jw inAwau hY Drm kw ] (84-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kee vadi-aa-ee vadee hai jaa ni-aa-o hai Dharam kaa. Great is the Greatness of the Lord; His Justice is totally Righteous.
DEFINE	para 3471	hir kI vifAweI vfI hY jw Plu hY jIA kw ] (84-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kee vadi-aa-ee vadee hai jaa fal hai jee-a kaa. Great is the Greatness of the Lord; people receive the fruits of the soul.
RECORD	para 3472	hir kI vifAweI vfI hY jw n suxeI kihAw cugl kw ] (84-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kee vadi-aa-ee vadee hai jaa na sun-ee kahi-aa chugal kaa. Great is the Greatness of the Lord; He does not hear the words of the back-biters.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v6	hir kI vifAweI vfI hY ApuiCAw dwnu dyvkw ]6] (84-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kee vadi-aa-ee vadee hai apuchhi-aa daan dayvkaa. ||6||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v6	Great is the Greatness of the Lord; He gives His Gifts without being asked. ||6||
RECORD	para 3474	slok mÚ 3 ] (84-19) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
FORBID	para 3475	hau hau krqI sB mueI sMpau iksY n nwil ] (84-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ha-o ha-o kartee sabh mu-ee sampa-o kisai na naal. Those who act in ego shall all die. Their worldly possessions shall not go along with them.
RECORD	para 3476	dUjY Bwie duKu pwieAw sB johI jmkwil ] (84-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay dukh paa-i-aa sabh johee jamkaal. Because of their love of duality, they suffer in pain. The Messenger of Death is watching all.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk gurmuiK aubry swcw nwmu smwil ]1] (85-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh ubray saachaa naam samaal. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are saved, by contemplating the True Name. ||1||
RECORD	para 3479	mÚ 1 ] (85-1) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3480	glˆØI AsI cMgIAw AwcwrI burIAwh ] (85-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) galee N asee changee-aa aachaaree buree-aah. We are good at talking, but our actions are bad.
DEFINE	para 3481	mnhu kusuDw kwlIAw bwhir ictvIAwh ] (85-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) manhu kusuDhaa kaalee-aa baahar chitvee-aah. Mentally, we are impure and black, but outwardly, we appear white.
RECORD	para 3482	rIsw kirh iqnwVIAw jo syvih dru KVIAwh ] (85-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) reesaa karih tinaarhee-aa jo sayveh dar kharhee-aah. We imitate those who stand and serve at the Lord's Door.
DEFINE	para 3483	nwil KsmY rqIAw mwxih suiK rlIAwh ] (85-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naal khasmai ratee-aa maaneh sukh ralee-aah. They are attuned to the Love of their Husband Lord, and they experience the pleasure of His Love.
RECORD	para 3484	hodY qwix inqwxIAw rhih inmwnxIAwh ] (85-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) hodai taan nitaanee-aa raheh nimaannee-aah. They remain powerless, even while they have power; they remain humble and meek.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk jnmu skwrQw jy iqn kY sMig imlwh ]2] (85-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) naanak janam sakaarthaa jay tin kai sang milaah. ||2||
WHEN	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, our lives become profitable if we associate with them. ||2||
RECORD	para 3486	pauVI ] (85-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 3487	qUM Awpy jlu mInw hY Awpy Awpy hI Awip jwlu ] (85-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tooN aapay jal meenaa hai aapay aapay hee aap jaal. You Yourself are the water, You Yourself are the fish, and You Yourself are the net.
DEFINE	para 3488	qUM Awpy jwlu vqwiedw Awpy ivic sybwlu ] (85-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tooN aapay jaal vataa-idaa aapay vich saybaal. You Yourself cast the net, and You Yourself are the bait.
DEFINE	para 3489	qUM Awpy kmlu Ailpqu hY sY hQw ivic gulwlu ] (85-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tooN aapay kamal alipat hai sai hathaa vich gulaal. You Yourself are the lotus, unaffected and still brightly-colored in hundreds of feet of water.
RECORD	para 3490	qUM Awpy mukiq krwiedw iek inmK GVI kir iKAwlu ] (85-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) tooN aapay mukat karaa-idaa ik nimakh gharhee kar khi-aal. You Yourself liberate those who think of You for even an instant.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v7	hir quDhu bwhir ikCu nhI gur sbdI vyiK inhwlu ]7] (85-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 1) har tuDhhu baahar kichh nahee gur sabdee vaykh nihaal. ||7||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v7	O Lord, nothing is beyond You. I am delighted to behold You, through the Word of the Guru's Shabad. ||7||
RECORD	para 3492	slok mÚ 3 ] (85-7) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3493	hukmu n jwxY bhuqw rovY ] (85-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) hukam na jaanai bahutaa rovai. One who does not know the Hukam of the Lord's Command cries out in terrible pain.
DEFINE	para 3494	AMdir DoKw nId n sovY ] (85-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) andar Dhokhaa need na sovai. She is filled with deception, and she cannot sleep in peace.
REQUIRE	para 3495	jy Dn KsmY clY rjweI ] dir Gir soBw mhil bulweI ] (85-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jay Dhan khasmai chalai rajaa-ee. dar ghar sobhaa mahal bulaa-ee. But if the soul-bride follows the Will of her Lord and Master, she shall be honored in her own home, and called to the Mansion of His Presence.
DEFINE	para 3496	nwnk krmI ieh miq pweI ] (85-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak karmee ih mat paa-ee. O Nanak, by His Mercy, this understanding is obtained.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	gur prswdI sic smweI ]1] (85-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee sach samaa-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	By Guru's Grace, she is absorbed into the True One. ||1||
RECORD	para 3498	mÚ 3 ] (85-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3499	mnmuK nwm ivhUixAw rMgu ksuMBw dyiK n Bulu ] (85-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh naam vihooni-aa rang kasumbhaa daykh na bhul. O self-willed manmukh, devoid of the Naam, do not be misled upon beholding the color of the safflower.
DEFINE	para 3500	ies kw rMgu idn QoiVAw CoCw ies dw mulu ] (85-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) is kaa rang din thorhi-aa chhochhaa is daa mul. Its color lasts for only a few days-it is worthless!
RECORD	para 3501	dUjY lgy pic muey mUrK AMD gvwr ] (85-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) doojai lagay pach mu-ay moorakh anDh gavaar. Attached to duality, the foolish, blind and stupid people waste away and die.
RECORD	para 3502	ibstw AMdir kIt sy pie pcih vwro vwr ] (85-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) bistaa andar keet say pa-i pacheh vaaro vaar. Like worms, they live in manure, and in it, they die over and over again.
RECORD	para 3503	nwnk nwm rqy sy rMguly gur kY shij suBwie ] (85-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay say rangulay gur kai sahj subhaa-ay. O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam are dyed in the color of truth; they take on the intuitive peace and poise of the Guru.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	BgqI rMgu n auqrY shjy rhY smwie ]2] (85-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) bhagtee rang na utrai sehjay rahai samaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	The color of devotional worship does not fade away; they remain intuitively absorbed in the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 3505	pauVI ] (85-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3506	issit aupweI sB quDu Awpy irjku sMbwihAw ] (85-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sisat upaa-ee sabh tuDh aapay rijak sambaahi-aa. You created the entire universe, and You Yourself bring sustenance to it.
RECORD	para 3507	ieik vlu Clu kir kY Kwvdy muhhu kUVu kusqu iqnI FwihAw ] (85-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ik val chhal kar kai khaavday muhhu koorh kusat tinee dhaahi-aa. Some eat and survive by practicing fraud and deceit; from their mouths they drop falsehood and lies.
RECORD	para 3508	quDu Awpy BwvY so krih quDu EqY kMim Eie lwieAw ] (85-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) tuDh aapay bhaavai so karahi tuDh otai kamm o-ay laa-i-aa. As it pleases You, You assign them their tasks.
DEFINE	para 3509	ieknw scu buJwieEnu iqnw Aqut BMfwr dyvwieAw ] (85-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) iknaa sach bujhaa-i-on tinaa atut bhandaar dayvaa-i-aa. Some understand Truthfulness; they are given the inexhaustible treasure.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v8	hir cyiq Kwih iqnw sPlu hY Acyqw hQ qfwieAw ]8] (85-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har chayt khaahi tinaa safal hai achaytaa hath tadaa-i-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v8	Those who eat by remembering the Lord are prosperous, while those who do not remember Him stretch out their hands in need. ||8||
RECORD	para 3511	slok mÚ 3 ] (85-15) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3512	piV piV pMifq byd vKwxih mwieAw moh suAwie ] (85-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) parh parh pandit bayd vakaaneh maa-i-aa moh su-aa-ay. The Pandits, the religious scholars, constantly read and recite the Vedas, for the sake of the love of Maya.
RECORD	para 3513	dUjY Bwie hir nwmu ivswirAw mn mUrK imlY sjwie ] (85-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay har naam visaari-aa man moorakh milai sajaa-ay. In the love of duality, the foolish people have forgotten the Lord's Name; they shall receive their punishment.
RECORD	para 3514	ijin jIau ipMfu idqw iqsu kbhUM n cyqY jo dyNdw irjku sMbwih ] (85-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jin jee-o pind ditaa tis kabahoo N na chaytai jo day Ndaa rijak sambaahi. They never think of the One who gave them body and soul, who provides sustenance to all.
FORBID	para 3515	jm kw Pwhw glhu n ktIAY iPir iPir AwvY jwie ] (85-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jam kaa faahaa galhu na katee-ai fir fir aavai jaa-ay. The noose of death shall not be cut away from their necks; they shall come and go in reincarnation over and over again.
RECORD	para 3516	mnmuiK ikCU n sUJY AMDuly pUrib iliKAw kmwie ] (85-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh kichhoo na soojhai anDhulay poorab likhi-aa kamaa-ay. The blind, self-willed manmukhs do not understand anything. They do what they are pre-ordained to do.
RECORD	para 3517	pUrY Bwig siqguru imlY suKdwqw nwmu vsY min Awie ] (85-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) poorai bhaag satgur milai sukh-daata naam vasai man aa-ay. Through perfect destiny, they meet the True Guru, the Giver of peace, and the Naam comes to abide in the mind.
RECORD	para 3518	suKu mwxih suKu pYnxw suKy suiK ivhwie ] (85-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sukh maaneh sukh painnaa sukhay sukh vihaa-ay. They enjoy peace, they wear peace, and they pass their lives in the peace of peace.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk so nwau mnhu n ivswrIAY ijqu dir scY soBw pwie ]1] (85-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak so naa-o manhu na visaaree-ai jit dar sachai sobhaa paa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, they do not forget the Naam from the mind; they are honored in the Court of the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 3520	mÚ 3 ] (85-19) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3521	siqguru syiv suKu pwieAw scu nwmu guxqwsu ] (85-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur sayv sukh paa-i-aa sach naam guntaas. Serving the True Guru, peace is obtained. The True Name is the Treasure of Excellence.
REQUIRE	para 3523	gurmqI Awpu pCwixAw rwm nwm prgwsu ] (86-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmatee aap pachhaani-aa raam naam pargaas. Follow the Guru's Teachings, and recognize your own self; the Divine Light of the Lord's Name shall shine within.
RECORD	para 3524	sco scu kmwvxw vifAweI vfy pwis ] (86-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sacho sach kamaavanaa vadi-aa-ee vaday paas. The true ones practice Truth; greatness rests in the Great Lord.
RECORD	para 3525	jIau ipMfu sBu iqs kw isPiq kry Ardwis ] (86-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jee-o pind sabh tis kaa sifat karay ardaas. Body, soul and all things belong to the Lord-praise Him, and offer your prayers to Him.
REQUIRE	para 3526	scY sbid swlwhxw suKy suiK invwsu ] (86-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sachai sabad salaahnaa sukhay sukh nivaas. Sing the Praises of the True Lord through the Word of His Shabad, and you shall abide in the peace of peace.
ALLOW	para 3527	jpu qpu sMjmu mnY mwih ibnu nwvY iDRgu jIvwsu ] (86-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jap tap sanjam manai maahi bin naavai Dharig jeevaas. You may practice chanting, penance and austere self-discipline within your mind, but without the Name, life is useless.
RECORD	para 3528	gurmqI nwau pweIAY mnmuK moih ivxwsu ] (86-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmatee naa-o paa-ee-ai manmukh mohi vinaas. Through the Guru's Teachings, the Name is obtained, while the self-willed manmukh wastes away in emotional attachment.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	ijau BwvY iqau rwKu qUM nwnku qyrw dwsu ]2] (86-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ji-o bhaavai ti-o raakh tooN naanak tayraa daas. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	Please protect me, by the Pleasure of Your Will. Nanak is Your slave. ||2||
RECORD	para 3530	pauVI ] (86-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 3531	sBu ko qyrw qUM sBsu dw qUM sBnw rwis ] (86-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabh ko tayraa tooN sabhas daa tooN sabhnaa raas. All are Yours, and You belong to all. You are the wealth of all.
RECORD	para 3532	siB quDY pwshu mMgdy inq kir Ardwis ] (86-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabh tuDhai paashu mangday nit kar ardaas. Everyone begs from You, and all offer prayers to You each day.
RECORD	para 3533	ijsu qUM dyih iqsu sBu ikCu imlY ieknw dUir hY pwis ] (86-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jis tooN deh tis sabh kichh milai iknaa door hai paas. Those, unto whom You give, receive everything. You are far away from some, and You are close to others.
RECORD	para 3534	quDu bwJhu Qwau ko nwhI ijsu pwshu mMgIAY min vyKhu ko inrjwis ] (86-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) tuDh baajhahu thaa-o ko naahee jis paashu mangee-ai man vaykhhu ko nirjaas. Without You, there is not even a place to stand begging. See this yourself and verify it in your mind.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v9	siB quDY no swlwhdy dir gurmuKw no prgwis ]9] (86-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabh tuDhai no salaahday dar gurmukhaa no pargaas. ||9||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v9	All praise You, O Lord; at Your Door, the Gurmukhs are enlightened. ||9||
RECORD	para 3536	slok mÚ 3 ] (86-7) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3537	pMifqu piV piV aucw kUkdw mwieAw moih ipAwru ] (86-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) pandit parh parh uchaa kookdaa maa-i-aa mohi pi-aar. The Pandits, the religious scholars, read and read, and shout out loud, but they are attached to the love of Maya.
DEFINE	para 3538	AMqir bRhmu n cIneI min mUrKu gwvwru ] (86-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) antar barahm na cheen-ee man moorakh gaavaar. They do not recognize God within themselves-they are so foolish and ignorant!
RECORD	para 3539	dUjY Bwie jgqu prboDdw nw bUJY bIcwru ] (86-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay jagat parboDhadaa naa boojhai beechaar. In the love of duality, they try to teach the world, but they do not understand meditative contemplation.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	ibrQw jnmu gvwieAw mir jMmY vwro vwr ]1] (86-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) birthaa janam gavaa-i-aa mar jammai vaaro vaar. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	They lose their lives uselessly; they die, only to be re-born, over and over again. ||1||
RECORD	para 3541	mÚ 3 ] (86-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3542	ijnI siqguru syivAw iqnI nwau pwieAw bUJhu kir bIcwru ] (86-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jinee satgur sayvi-aa tinee naa-o paa-i-aa boojhhu kar beechaar. Those who serve the True Guru obtain the Name. Reflect on this and understand.
RECORD	para 3543	sdw sWiq suKu min vsY cUkY kUk pukwr ] (86-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sadaa saa Nt sukh man vasai chookai kook pukaar. Eternal peace and joy abide in their minds; they abandon their cries and complaints.
RECORD	para 3544	AwpY no Awpu Kwie mnu inrmlu hovY gur sbdI vIcwru ] (86-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aapai no aap khaa-ay man nirmal hovai gur sabdee veechaar. Their identity consumes their identical identity, and their minds become pure by contemplating the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk sbid rqy sy mukqu hY hir jIau hyiq ipAwru ]2] (86-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak sabad ratay say mukat hai har jee-o hayt pi-aar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, attuned to the Shabad, they are liberated. They love their Beloved Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 3546	pauVI ] (86-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 3547	hir kI syvw sPl hY gurmuiK pwvY Qwie ] (86-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kee sayvaa safal hai gurmukh paavai thaa-ay. Service to the Lord is fruitful; through it, the Gurmukh is honored and approved.
RECORD	para 3548	ijsu hir BwvY iqsu guru imlY so hir nwmu iDAwie ] (86-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jis har bhaavai tis gur milai so har naam Dhi-aa-ay. That person, with whom the Lord is pleased, meets with the Guru, and meditates on the Name of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 3549	gur sbdI hir pweIAY hir pwir lGwie ] (86-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur sabdee har paa-ee-ai har paar laghaa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Lord is found. The Lord carries us across.
RECORD	para 3550	mnhiT iknY n pwieE puChu vydw jwie ] (86-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manhath kinai na paa-i-o puchhahu vaydaa jaa-ay. Through stubborn-mindedness, none have found Him; go and consult the Vedas on this.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v10	nwnk hir kI syvw so kry ijsu ley hir lwie ]10] (86-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak har kee sayvaa so karay jis la-ay har laa-ay. ||10||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v10	O Nanak, he alone serves the Lord, whom the Lord attaches to Himself. ||10||
RECORD	para 3552	slok mÚ 3 ] (86-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3553	nwnk so sUrw vrIAwmu ijin ivchu dustu AhMkrxu mwirAw ] (86-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak so sooraa varee-aam jin vichahu dusat ahankaran maari-aa. O Nanak, he is a brave warrior, who conquers and subdues his vicious inner ego.
RECORD	para 3554	gurmuiK nwmu swlwih jnmu svwirAw ] (86-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmukh naam saalaahi janam savaari-aa. Praising the Naam, the Name of the Lord, the Gurmukhs redeem their lives.
DEFINE	para 3555	Awip hoAw sdw mukqu sBu kulu insqwirAw ] (86-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aap ho-aa sadaa mukat sabh kul nistaari-aa. They themselves are liberated forever, and they save all their ancestors.
RECORD	para 3556	sohin sic duAwir nwmu ipAwirAw ] (86-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sohan sach du-aar naam pi-aari-aa. Those who love the Naam look beauteous at the Gate of Truth.
DEFINE	para 3557	mnmuK mrih AhMkwir mrxu ivgwiVAw ] (86-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh mareh aha Nkaar maran vigaarhi-aa. The self-willed manmukhs die in egotism-even their death is painfully ugly.
RECORD	para 3558	sBo vrqY hukmu ikAw krih ivcwirAw ] (86-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabho vartai hukam ki-aa karahi vichaari-aa. Everything happens according to the Lord's Will; what can the poor people do?
RECORD	para 3559	Awphu dUjY lig Ksmu ivswirAw ] (86-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aaphu doojai lag khasam visaari-aa. Attached to self-conceit and duality, they have forgotten their Lord and Master.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk ibnu nwvY sBu duKu suKu ivswirAw ]1] (86-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak bin naavai sabh dukh sukh visaari-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, without the Name, everything is painful, and happiness is forgotten. ||1||
RECORD	para 3561	mÚ 3 ] (86-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3562	guir pUrY hir nwmu idVwieAw iqin ivchu Brmu cukwieAw ] (86-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur poorai har naam dirhaa-i-aa tin vichahu bharam chukaa-i-aa. The Perfect Guru has implanted the Name of the Lord within me. It has dispelled my doubts from within.
RECORD	para 3563	rwm nwmu hir kIriq gweI kir cwnxu mgu idKwieAw ] (86-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) raam naam har keerat gaa-ee kar chaanan mag dikhaa-i-aa. I sing the Lord's Name and the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises; the Divine Light shines, and now I see the Way.
RECORD	para 3564	haumY mwir eyk ilv lwgI AMqir nwmu vswieAw ] (86-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) ha-umai maar ayk liv laagee antar naam vasaa-i-aa. Conquering my ego, I am lovingly focused on the One Lord; the Naam has come to dwell within me.
RECORD	para 3566	gurmqI jmu joih n swkY swcY nwim smwieAw ] (87-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmatee jam johi na saakai saachai naam samaa-i-aa. Following the Guru's Teachings, I cannot be touched by the Messenger of Death. I am absorbed in the True Name.
RECORD	para 3567	sBu Awpy Awip vrqY krqw jo BwvY so nwie lwieAw ] (87-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabh aapay aap vartai kartaa jo bhaavai so naa-ay laa-i-aa. The Creator Himself is All-pervading everywhere; He links those with whom He is pleased to His Name.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	jn nwnku nwmu ley qw jIvY ibnu nwvY iKnu mir jwieAw ]2] (87-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jan naanak naam la-ay taa jeevai bin naavai khin mar jaa-i-aa. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	Servant Nanak chants the Naam, and so he lives. Without the Name, he would die in an instant. ||2||
RECORD	para 3569	pauVI ] (87-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
REQUIRE	para 3570	jo imilAw hir dIbwx isau so sBnI dIbwxI imilAw ] (87-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jo mili-aa har deebaan si-o so sabhnee deebaanee mili-aa. One who is accepted at the Court of the Lord shall be accepted in courts everywhere.
RECORD	para 3571	ijQY Ehu jwie iqQY Ehu surKrU aus kY muih ifTY sB pwpI qirAw ] (87-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jithai oh jaa-ay tithai oh surkharoo us kai muhi dithai sabh paapee tari-aa. Wherever he goes, he is recognized as honorable. Seeing his face, all sinners are saved.
DEFINE	para 3572	Esu AMqir nwmu inDwnu hY nwmo prvirAw ] (87-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) os antar naam niDhaan hai naamo parvaari-aa. Within him is the Treasure of the Naam, the Name of the Lord. Through the Naam, he is exalted.
RECORD	para 3573	nwau pUjIAY nwau mMnIAY nwie iklivK sB ihirAw ] (87-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naa-o poojee-ai naa-o mannee-ai naa-ay kilvikh sabh hiri-aa. He worships the Name, and believes in the Name; the Name erases all his sinful mistakes.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v11	ijnI nwmu iDAwieAw iek min iek iciq sy AsiQru jig rihAw ]11] (87-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jinee naam Dhi-aa-i-aa ik man ik chit say asthir jag rahi-aa. ||11||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v11	Those who meditate on the Name, with one-pointed mind and focused consciousness, remain forever stable in the world. ||11||
RECORD	para 3575	slok mÚ 3 ] (87-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3576	Awqmw dyau pUjIAY gur kY shij suBwie ] (87-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aatmaa day-o poojee-ai gur kai sahj subhaa-ay. Worship the Divine, Supreme Soul, with the intuitive peace and poise of the Guru.
REQUIRE	para 3577	Awqmy no Awqmy dI pRqIiq hoie qw Gr hI prcw pwie ] (87-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aatmay no aatmay dee parteet ho-ay taa ghar hee parchaa paa-ay. If the individual soul has faith in the Supreme Soul, then it shall obtain realization within its own home.
RECORD	para 3578	Awqmw Afolu n foleI gur kY Bwie suBwie ] (87-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aatmaa adol na dol-ee gur kai bhaa-ay subhaa-ay. The soul becomes steady, and does not waver, by the natural inclination of the Guru's Loving Will.
UPHOLD	para 3579	gur ivxu shju n AwveI loBu mYlu n ivchu jwie ] (87-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur vin sahj na aavee lobh mail na vichahu jaa-ay. Without the Guru, intuitive wisdom does not come, and the filth of greed does not depart from within.
WHEN	para 3580	iKnu plu hir nwmu min vsY sB ATsiT qIrQ nwie ] (87-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) khin pal har naam man vasai sabh athsath tirath naa-ay. If the Lord's Name abides within the mind, for a moment, even for an instant, it is like bathing at all the sixty-eight sacred shrines of pilgrimage.
DEFINE	para 3581	scy mYlu n lgeI mlu lwgY dUjY Bwie ] (87-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sachay mail na lag-ee mal laagai doojai bhaa-ay. Filth does not stick to those who are true, but filth attaches itself to those who love duality.
RECORD	para 3582	DoqI mUil n auqrY jy ATsiT qIrQ nwie ] (87-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) Dhotee mool na utrai jay athsath tirath naa-ay. This filth cannot be washed off, even by bathing at the sixty-eight sacred shrines of pilgrimage.
RECORD	para 3583	mnmuK krm kry AhMkwrI sBu duKo duKu kmwie ] (87-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh karam karay aha Nkaaree sabh dukho dukh kamaa-ay. The self-willed manmukh does deeds in egotism; he earns only pain and more pain.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk mYlw aUjlu qw QIAY jw siqgur mwih smwie ]1] (87-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak mailaa oojal taa thee-ai jaa satgur maahi samaa-ay. ||1||
WHEN	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, the filthy ones become clean only when they meet and surrender to the True Guru. ||1||
RECORD	para 3585	mÚ 3 ] (87-10) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
ALLOW	para 3586	mnmuKu loku smJweIAY kdhu smJwieAw jwie ] (87-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh lok samjaa-ee-ai kadahu samjhaa-i-aa jaa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs may be taught, but how can they really be taught?
RECORD	para 3587	mnmuKu rlwieAw nw rlY pieAY ikriq iPrwie ] (87-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh ralaa-i-aa naa ralai pa-i-ai kirat firaa-ay. The manmukhs do not fit in at all. Because of their past actions, they are condemned to the cycle of reincarnation.
RECORD	para 3588	ilv Dwqu duie rwh hY hukmI kwr kmwie ] (87-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) liv Dhaat du-ay raah hai hukmee kaar kamaa-ay. Loving attention to the Lord and attachment to Maya are the two separate ways; all act according to the Hukam of the Lord's Command.
RECORD	para 3589	gurmuiK Awpxw mnu mwirAw sbid ksvtI lwie ] (87-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmukh aapnaa man maari-aa sabad kasvatee laa-ay. The Gurmukh has conquered his own mind, by applying the Touchstone of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 3590	mn hI nwil JgVw mn hI nwil sQ mn hI mMiJ smwie ] (87-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) man hee naal jhagrhaa man hee naal sath man hee manjh samaa-ay. He fights with his mind, he settles with his mind, and he is at peace with his mind.
RECORD	para 3591	mnu jo ieCy so lhY scY sbid suBwie ] (87-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) man jo ichhay so lahai sachai sabad subhaa-ay. All obtain the desires of their minds, through the Love of the True Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 3592	AMimRq nwmu sd BuMcIAY gurmuiK kwr kmwie ] (87-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) amrit naam sad bhunchee-ai gurmukh kaar kamaa-ay. They drink in the Ambrosial Nectar of the Naam forever; this is how the Gurmukhs act.
REQUIRE	para 3593	ivxu mnY ij horI nwil luJxw jwsI jnmu gvwie ] (87-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) vin manai je horee naal lujh-naa jaasee janam gavaa-ay. Those who struggle with something other than their own mind, shall depart having wasted their lives.
RECORD	para 3594	mnmuKI mnhiT hwirAw kUVu kusqu kmwie ] (87-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukhee manhath haari-aa koorh kusat kamaa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs, through stubborn-mindedness and the practice of falsehood, lose the game of life.
RECORD	para 3595	gur prswdI mnu ijxY hir syqI ilv lwie ] (87-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee man jinai har saytee liv laa-ay. Those who conquer their own mind, by Guru's Grace, lovingly focus their attention on the Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk gurmuiK scu kmwvY mnmuiK AwvY jwie ]2] (87-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh sach kamaavai manmukh aavai jaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs practice Truth, while the self-willed manmukhs continue coming and going in reincarnation. ||2||
RECORD	para 3597	pauVI ] (87-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3598	hir ky sMq suxhu jn BweI hir siqgur kI iek swKI ] (87-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kay sant sunhu jan bhaa-ee har satgur kee ik saakhee. O Saints of the Lord, O Siblings of Destiny, listen, and hear the Lord's Teachings, through the True Guru.
RECORD	para 3599	ijsu Duir Bwgu hovY muiK msqik iqin jin lY ihrdY rwKI ] (87-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jis Dhur bhaag hovai mukh mastak tin jan lai hirdai raakhee. Those who have good destiny pre-ordained and inscribed on their foreheads, grasp it and keep it enshrined in the heart.
RECORD	para 3600	hir AMimRq kQw sryst aUqm gur bcnI shjy cwKI ] (87-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har amrit kathaa saraysat ootam gur bachnee sehjay chaakhee. Through the Guru's Teachings, they intuitively taste the sublime, exquisite and ambrosial sermon of the Lord.
RECORD	para 3601	qh BieAw pRgwsu imitAw AMiDAwrw ijau sUrj rYix ikrwKI ] (87-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) tah bha-i-aa pargaas miti-aa anDhi-aaraa ji-o sooraj rain kiraakhee. The Divine Light shines in their hearts, and like the sun which removes the darkness of night, it dispels the darkness of ignorance.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v12	Aidstu Agocru AlKu inrMjnu so dyiKAw gurmuiK AwKI ]12] (87-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) adisat agochar alakh niranjan so daykhi-aa gurmukh aakhee. ||12||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v12	As Gurmukh, they behold with their eyes the Unseen, Imperceptible, Unknowable, Immaculate Lord. ||12||
RECORD	para 3603	sloku mÚ 3 ] (87-19) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3605	siqguru syvy Awpxw so isru lyKY lwie ] (88-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay aapnaa so sir laykhai laa-ay. Those who serve their True Guru are certified and accepted.
RECORD	para 3606	ivchu Awpu gvwie kY rhin sic ilv lwie ] (88-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) vichahu aap gavaa-ay kai rahan sach liv laa-ay. They eradicate selfishness and conceit from within; they remain lovingly absorbed in the True One.
RECORD	para 3607	siqguru ijnI n syivE iqnw ibrQw jnmu gvwie ] (88-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur jinee na sayvi-o tinaa birthaa janam gavaa-ay. Those who do not serve the True Guru waste away their lives in vain.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk jo iqsu BwvY so kry khxw ikCU n jwie ]1] (88-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak jo tis bhaavai so karay kahnaa kichhoo na jaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, the Lord does just as He pleases. No one has any say in this. ||1||
RECORD	para 3609	mÚ 3 ] (88-3) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3610	mnu vykwrI vyiVAw vykwrw krm kmwie ] (88-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) man vaykaaree vayrhi-aa vaykaaraa karam kamaa-ay. With the mind encircled by wickedness and evil, people do evil deeds.
REQUIRE	para 3611	dUjY Bwie AigAwnI pUjdy drgh imlY sjwie ] (88-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay agi-aanee poojday dargeh milai sajaa-ay. The ignorant worship the love of duality; in the Lord's Court they shall be punished.
RECORD	para 3612	Awqm dyau pUjIAY ibnu siqgur bUJ n pwie ] (88-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aatam day-o poojee-ai bin satgur boojh na paa-ay. So worship the Lord, the Light of the soul; without the True Guru, understanding is not obtained.
RECORD	para 3613	jpu qpu sMjmu Bwxw siqgurU kw krmI plY pwie ] (88-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jap tap sanjam bhaanaa satguroo kaa karmee palai paa-ay. Meditation, penance and austere self-discipline are found by surrendering to the True Guru's Will. By His Grace this is received.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk syvw suriq kmwvxI jo hir BwvY so Qwie pwie ]2] (88-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak sayvaa surat kamaavnee jo har bhaavai so thaa-ay paa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, serve with this intuitive awareness; only that which is pleasing to the Lord is approved. ||2||
RECORD	para 3615	pauVI ] (88-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3616	hir hir nwmu jphu mn myry ijqu sdw suKu hovY idnu rwqI ] (88-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har har naam japahu man mayray jit sadaa sukh hovai din raatee. Chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, O my mind; it will bring you eternal peace, day and night.
REQUIRE	para 3617	hir hir nwmu jphu mn myry ijqu ismrq siB iklivK pwp lhwqI ] (88-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har har naam japahu man mayray jit simrat sabh kilvikh paap lahaatee. Chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, O my mind; meditating on it, all sins and misdeeds shall be erased.
REQUIRE	para 3618	hir hir nwmu jphu mn myry ijqu dwldu duK BuK sB lih jwqI ] (88-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har har naam japahu man mayray jit daalad dukh bhukh sabh leh jaatee. Chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, O my mind; through it, all poverty, pain and hunger shall be removed.
RECORD	para 3619	hir hir nwmu jphu mn myry muiK gurmuiK pRIiq lgwqI ] (88-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har har naam japahu man mayray mukh gurmukh pareet lagaatee. Chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, O my mind; as Gurmukh, declare your love.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v13	ijqu muiK Bwgu iliKAw Duir swcY hir iqqu muiK nwmu jpwqI ]13] (88-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jit mukh bhaag likhi-aa Dhur saachai har tit mukh naam japaatee. ||13||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v13	One who has such pre-ordained destiny inscribed upon his forehead by the True Lord, chants the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||13||
RECORD	para 3621	slok mÚ 3 ] (88-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3622	siqguru ijnI n syivE sbid n kIqo vIcwru ] (88-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur jinee na sayvi-o sabad na keeto veechaar. Those who do not serve the True Guru, and who do not contemplate the Word of the Shabad
DEFINE	para 3623	AMqir igAwnu n AwieE imrqku hY sMswir ] (88-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) antar gi-aan na aa-i-o mirtak hai sansaar. -spiritual wisdom does not enter into their hearts; they are like dead bodies in the world.
RECORD	para 3624	lK caurwsIh Pyru pieAw mir jMmY hoie KuAwru ] (88-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) lakh cha-oraaseeh fayr pa-i-aa mar jammai ho-ay khu-aar. They go through the cycle of 8.4 million reincarnations, and they are ruined through death and rebirth.
RECORD	para 3625	siqgur kI syvw so kry ijs no Awip krwey soie ] (88-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur kee sayvaa so karay jis no aap karaa-ay so-ay. He alone serves the True Guru, whom the Lord Himself inspires to do so.
DEFINE	para 3626	siqgur ivic nwmu inDwnu hY krim prwpiq hoie ] (88-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur vich naam niDhaan hai karam paraapat ho-ay. The Treasure of the Naam is within the True Guru; by His Grace, it is obtained.
DEFINE	para 3627	sic rqy gur sbd isau iqn scI sdw ilv hoie ] (88-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sach ratay gur sabad si-o tin sachee sadaa liv ho-ay. Those who are truly attuned to the Word of the Guru's Shabad-their love is forever True.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk ijs no myly n ivCuVY shij smwvY soie ]1] (88-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak jis no maylay na vichhurhai sahj samaavai so-ay. ||1||
FORBID	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, those who are united with Him shall not be separated again. They merge imperceptibly into God. ||1||
RECORD	para 3629	mÚ 3 ] (88-13) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3630	so BgauqI juo BgvMqY jwxY ] (88-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) so bhag-utee jo bhagvantai jaanai. One who knows the Benevolent Lord God is the true devotee of Bhagaautee.
DEFINE	para 3631	gur prswdI Awpu pCwxY ] (88-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee aap pachhaanai. By Guru's Grace, he is self-realized.
RECORD	para 3632	Dwvqu rwKY iekqu Gir AwxY ] (88-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) Dhaavat raakhai ikat ghar aanai. He restrains his wandering mind, and brings it back to its own home within the self.
RECORD	para 3633	jIvqu mrY hir nwmu vKwxY ] (88-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jeevat marai har naam vakhaanai. He remains dead while yet alive, and he chants the Name of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 3634	AYsw BgauqI auqmu hoie ] (88-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) aisaa bhag-utee utam ho-ay. Such a Bhagaautee is most exalted.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk sic smwvY soie ]2] (88-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak sach samaavai so-ay. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, he merges into the True One. ||2||
RECORD	para 3636	mÚ 3 ] (88-15) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3637	AMqir kptu BgauqI khwey ] (88-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) antar kapat bhag-utee kahaa-ay. He is full of deceit, and yet he calls himself a devotee of Bhagaautee.
REQUIRE	para 3638	pwKMif pwrbRhmu kdy n pwey ] (88-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) pakhand paarbarahm kaday na paa-ay. Through hypocrisy, he shall never attain the Supreme Lord God.
RECORD	para 3639	pr inMdw kry AMqir mlu lwey ] (88-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) par nindaa karay antar mal laa-ay. He slanders others, and pollutes himself with his own filth.
RECORD	para 3640	bwhir mlu DovY mn kI jUiT n jwey ] (88-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) baahar mal Dhovai man kee jooth na jaa-ay. Outwardly, he washes off the filth, but the impurity of his mind does not go away.
RECORD	para 3641	sqsMgiq isau bwdu rcwey ] (88-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satsangat si-o baad rachaa-ay. He argues with the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation.
RECORD	para 3642	Anidnu duKIAw dUjY Bwie rcwey ] (88-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) an-din dukhee-aa doojai bhaa-ay rachaa-ay. Night and day, he suffers, engrossed in the love of duality.
RECORD	para 3643	hir nwmu n cyqY bhu krm kmwey ] (88-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har naam na chaytai baho karam kamaa-ay. He does not remember the Name of the Lord, but still, he performs all sorts of empty rituals.
DEFINE	para 3644	pUrb iliKAw su mytxw n jwey ] (88-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) poorab likhi-aa so maytnaa na jaa-ay. That which is pre-ordained cannot be erased.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v3	nwnk ibnu siqgur syvy moKu n pwey ]3] (88-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak bin satgur sayvay mokh na paa-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v3	O Nanak, without serving the True Guru, liberation is not obtained. ||3||
RECORD	para 3646	pauVI ] (88-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
FORBID	para 3647	siqguru ijnI iDAwieAw sy kiV n svwhI ] (88-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur jinee Dhi-aa-i-aa say karh na savaahee. Those who meditate on the True Guru shall not be burnt to ashes.
DEFINE	para 3648	siqguru ijnI iDAwieAw sy iqRpiq AGwhI ] (88-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur jinee Dhi-aa-i-aa say taripat aghaahee. Those who meditate on the True Guru are satisfied and fulfilled.
DEFINE	para 3649	siqguru ijnI iDAwieAw iqn jm fru nwhI ] (88-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur jinee Dhi-aa-i-aa tin jam dar naahee. Those who meditate on the True Guru are not afraid of the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	para 3651	ijn kau hoAw ik®pwlu hir sy siqgur pYrI pwhI ] (89-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jin ka-o ho-aa kirpaal har say satgur pairee paahee. Those upon whom the Lord showers His Mercy, fall at the Feet of the True Guru.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v14	iqn AYQY EQY muK aujly hir drgh pYDy jwhI ]14] (89-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) tin aithai othai mukh ujlay har dargeh paiDhay jaahee. ||14||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v14	Here and hereafter, their faces are radiant; they go to the Lord's Court in robes of honor. ||14||
RECORD	para 3653	slok mÚ 2 ] (89-2) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 3654	jo isru sWeI nw invY so isru dIjY fwir ] (89-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) jo sir saaN-ee naa nivai so sir deejai daar. Chop off that head which does not bow to the Lord.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk ijsu ipMjr mih ibrhw nhI so ipMjru lY jwir ]1] (89-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 2) naanak jis pinjar meh birhaa nahee so pinjar lai jaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, that human body, in which there is no pain of separation from the Lord-take that body and burn it. ||1||
RECORD	para 3656	mÚ 5 ] (89-3) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3657	muMFhu BulI nwnkw iPir iPir jnim mueIAwsu ] (89-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 5) mundhhu bhulee naankaa fir fir janam mu-ee-aas. Forgetting the Primal Lord, O Nanak, people are born and die, over and over again.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	ksqUrI kY BolVY gMdy fuMim peIAwsu ]2] (89-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 5) kastooree kai bholrhai gunday dumm pa-ee-aas. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	Mistaking it for musk, they have fallen into the stinking pit of filth. ||2||
RECORD	para 3659	pauVI ] (89-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3660	so AYsw hir nwmu iDAweIAY mn myry jo sBnw aupir hukmu clwey ] (89-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 5) so aisaa har naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai man mayray jo sabhnaa upar hukam chalaa-ay. Meditate on that Name of the Lord, O my mind, whose Command rules over all.
RECORD	para 3661	so AYsw hir nwmu jpIAY mn myry jo AMqI Aausir ley Cfwey ] (89-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 5) so aisaa har naam japee-ai man mayray jo antee a-osar la-ay chhadaa-ay. Chant that Name of the Lord, O my mind, which will save you at the very last moment.
REQUIRE	para 3662	so AYsw hir nwmu jpIAY mn myry ju mn kI iqRsnw sB BuK gvwey ] (89-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 5) so aisaa har naam japee-ai man mayray jo man kee tarisnaa sabh bhukh gavaa-ay. Chant that Name of the Lord, O my mind, which shall drive out all hunger and desire from your mind.
REQUIRE	para 3663	so gurmuiK nwmu jipAw vfBwgI iqn inMdk dust siB pYrI pwey ] (89-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 5) so gurmukh naam japi-aa vadbhaagee tin nindak dusat sabh pairee paa-ay. Very fortunate and blessed is that Gurmukh who chants the Naam; it shall bring all slanderers and wicked enemies to fall at his feet.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v15	nwnk nwmu ArwiD sBnw qy vfw siB nwvY AgY Awix invwey ]15] (89-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 5) naanak naam araaDh sabhnaa tay vadaa sabh naavai agai aan nivaa-ay. ||15||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v15	O Nanak, worship and adore the Naam, the Greatest Name of all, before which all come and bow. ||15||
RECORD	para 3665	slok mÚ 3 ] (89-8) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
ALLOW	para 3666	vys kry kurUip kulKxI min KotY kUiVAwir ] (89-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) vays karay kuroop kulkhanee man khotai koorhi-aar. She may wear good clothes, but the bride is ugly and rude; her mind is false and impure.
RECORD	para 3667	ipr kY BwxY nw clY hukmu kry gwvwir ] (89-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) pir kai bhaanai naa chalai hukam karay gaavaar. She does not walk in harmony with the Will of her Husband Lord. Instead, she foolishly gives Him orders.
REQUIRE	para 3668	gur kY BwxY jo clY siB duK invwrxhwir ] (89-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur kai bhaanai jo chalai sabh dukh nivaaranhaar. But she who walks in harmony with the Guru's Will, shall be spared all pain and suffering.
RECORD	para 3669	iliKAw myit n skIAY jo Duir iliKAw krqwir ] (89-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) likhi-aa mayt na sakee-ai jo Dhur likhi-aa kartaar. That destiny which was pre-ordained by the Creator cannot be erased.
REQUIRE	para 3670	mnu qnu saupy kMq kau sbdy Dry ipAwru ] (89-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) man tan sa-upay kant ka-o sabday Dharay pi-aar. She must dedicate her mind and body to her Husband Lord, and enshrine love for the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 3671	ibnu nwvY iknY n pwieAw dyKhu irdY bIcwir ] (89-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) bin naavai kinai na paa-i-aa daykhhu ridai beechaar. Without His Name, no one has found Him; see this and reflect upon it in your heart.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk sw suAwilE sulKxI ij rwvI isrjnhwir ]1] (89-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak saa su-aali-o sulakh-nee je raavee sirjanhaar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, she is beautiful and graceful; the Creator Lord ravishes and enjoys her. ||1||
RECORD	para 3673	mÚ 3 ] (89-12) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3674	mwieAw mohu gubwru hY iqs dw n idsY aurvwru n pwru ] (89-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh gubaar hai tis daa na disai urvaar na paar. Attachment to Maya is an ocean of darkness; neither this shore nor the one beyond can be seen.
RECORD	para 3675	mnmuK AigAwnI mhw duKu pwiedy fuby hir nwmu ivswir ] (89-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh agi-aanee mahaa dukh paa-iday dubay har naam visaar. The ignorant, self-willed manmukhs suffer in terrible pain; they forget the Lord's Name and drown.
RECORD	para 3676	Blky auiT bhu krm kmwvih dUjY Bwie ipAwru ] (89-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) bhalkay uth baho karam kamaaveh doojai bhaa-ay pi-aar. They arise in the morning and perform all sorts of rituals, but they are caught in the love of duality.
RECORD	para 3677	siqguru syvih Awpxw Baujlu auqry pwir ] (89-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur sayveh aapnaa bha-ojal utray paar. Those who serve the True Guru cross over the terrifying world-ocean.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk gurmuiK sic smwvih scu nwmu aur Dwir ]2] (89-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh sach samaaveh sach naam ur Dhaar. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs keep the True Name enshrined in their hearts; they are absorbed into the True One. ||2||
RECORD	para 3679	pauVI ] (89-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 3680	hir jil Qil mhIAil BrpUir dUjw nwih koie ] (89-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har jal thal mahee-al bharpoor doojaa naahi ko-ay. The Lord pervades and permeates the water, the land and the sky; there is no other at all.
RECORD	para 3681	hir Awip bih kry inAwau kUiVAwr sB mwir kFoie ] (89-15, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har aap bahi karay ni-aa-o koorhi-aar sabh maar kadho-ay. The Lord Himself sits upon His Throne and administers justice. He beats and drives out the false-hearted.
UPHOLD	para 3682	sicAwrw dyie vifAweI hir Drm inAwau kIEie ] (89-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sachi-aaraa day-ay vadi-aa-ee har Dharam ni-aa-o kee-o-ay. The Lord bestows glorious greatness upon those who are truthful. He administers righteous justice.
RECORD	para 3683	sB hir kI krhu ausqiq ijin grIb AnwQ rwiK lIEie ] (89-16, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabh har kee karahu ustat jin gareeb anaath raakh lee-o-i. So praise the Lord, everybody; He protects the poor and the lost souls.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v16	jYkwru kIE DrmIAw kw pwpI kau fMfu dIEie ]16] (89-17, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) jaikaar kee-o dharmee-aa kaa paapee ka-o dand dee-o-i. ||16||
UPHOLD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v16	He honors the righteous and punishes the sinners. ||16||
RECORD	para 3685	slok mÚ 3 ] (89-18) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3686	mnmuK mYlI kwmxI kulKxI kunwir ] (89-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh mailee kaamnee kulkhanee kunaar. The self-willed manmukh, the foolish bride, is a filthy, rude and evil wife.
RECORD	para 3687	ipru CoifAw Gir Awpxw pr purKY nwil ipAwru ] (89-18, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) pir chhodi-aa ghar aapnaa par purkhai naal pi-aar. Forsaking her Husband Lord and leaving her own home, she gives her love to another.
DEFINE	para 3688	iqRsnw kdy n cukeI jldI kry pUkwr ] (89-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) tarisnaa kaday na chuk-ee jaldee karay pookaar. Her desires are never satisfied, and she burns and cries out in pain.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk ibnu nwvY kurUip kusohxI prhir CofI Bqwir ]1] (89-19, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak bin naavai kuroop kusohanee parhar chhodee bhataar. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, without the Name, she is ugly and ungraceful. She is abandoned and left behind by her Husband Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 3691	mÚ 3 ] (90-1) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 3692	sbid rqI sohwgxI siqgur kY Bwie ipAwir ] (90-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabad ratee sohaaganee satgur kai bhaa-ay pi-aar. The happy soul-bride is attuned to the Word of the Shabad; she is in love with the True Guru.
RECORD	para 3693	sdw rwvy ipru Awpxw scY pRyim ipAwir ] (90-1, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sadaa raavay pir aapnaa sachai paraym pi-aar. She continually enjoys and ravishes her Beloved, with true love and affection.
DEFINE	para 3694	Aiq suAwilau suMdrI soBwvMqI nwir ] (90-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) at su-aali-o sundree sobhaavantee naar. She is such a loveable, beautiful and noble woman.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	nwnk nwim sohwgxI mylI mylxhwir ]2] (90-2, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak naam sohaaganee maylee maylanhaar. ||2||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	O Nanak, through the Naam, the happy soul-bride unites with the Lord of Union. ||2||
RECORD	para 3696	pauVI ] (90-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3697	hir qyrI sB krih ausqiq ijin PwQy kwiFAw ] (90-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har tayree sabh karahi ustat jin faathay kaadhi-aa. Lord, everyone sings Your Praises. You have freed us from bondage.
RECORD	para 3698	hir quDno krih sB nmskwru ijin pwpY qy rwiKAw ] (90-3, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har tuDhno karahi sabh namaskaar jin paapai tay raakhi-aa. Lord, everyone bows in reverence to You. You have saved us from our sinful ways.
DEFINE	para 3699	hir inmwixAw qUM mwxu hir fwFI hUM qUM fwiFAw ] (90-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har nimaani-aa tooN maan har daadhee hooN tooN daadhi-aa. Lord, You are the Honor of the dishonored. Lord, You are the Strongest of the strong.
RECORD	para 3700	hir AhMkwrIAw mwir invwey mnmuK mUV swiDAw ] (90-4, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har ahaNkaaree-aa maar nivaa-ay manmukh moorh saaDhi-aa. The Lord beats down the egocentrics and corrects the foolish, self-willed manmukhs.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v17	hir Bgqw dyie vifAweI grIb AnwiQAw ]17] (90-5, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har bhagtaa day-ay vadi-aa-ee gareeb anaathi-aa. ||17||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v17	The Lord bestows glorious greatness on His devotees, the poor, and the lost souls. ||17||
RECORD	para 3702	slok mÚ 3 ] (90-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3703	siqgur kY BwxY jo clY iqsu vifAweI vfI hoie ] (90-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) satgur kai bhaanai jo chalai tis vadi-aa-ee vadee ho-ay. One who walks in harmony with the Will of the True Guru, obtains the greatest glory.
RECORD	para 3704	hir kw nwmu auqmu min vsY myit n skY koie ] (90-6, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kaa naam utam man vasai mayt na sakai ko-ay. The Exalted Name of the Lord abides in his mind, and no one can take it away.
RECORD	para 3705	ikrpw kry ijsu AwpxI iqsu krim prwpiq hoie ] (90-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) kirpaa karay jis aapnee tis karam paraapat ho-ay. That person, upon whom the Lord bestows His Grace, receives His Mercy.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	nwnk kwrxu krqy vis hY gurmuiK bUJY koie ]1] (90-7, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak kaaran kartay vas hai gurmukh boojhai ko-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v1	O Nanak, creativity is under the control of the Creator; how rare are those who, as Gurmukh, realize this! ||1||
RECORD	para 3707	mÚ 3 ] (90-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 3708	nwnk hir nwmu ijnI AwrwiDAw Anidnu hir ilv qwr ] (90-8, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) naanak har naam jinee aaraaDhi-aa an-din har liv taar. O Nanak, those who worship and adore the Lord's Name night and day, vibrate the String of the Lord's Love.
RECORD	para 3709	mwieAw bMdI Ksm kI iqn AgY kmwvY kwr ] (90-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa bandee khasam kee tin agai kamaavai kaar. Maya, the maid-servant of our Lord and Master, serves them.
RECORD	para 3710	pUrY pUrw kir CoifAw hukim svwrxhwr ] (90-9, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) poorai pooraa kar chhodi-aa hukam savaaranhaar. The Perfect One has made them perfect; by the Hukam of His Command, they are embellished.
RECORD	para 3711	gur prswdI ijin buiJAw iqin pwieAw moK duAwru ] (90-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee jin bujhi-aa tin paa-i-aa mokh du-aar. By Guru's Grace, they understand Him, and they find the gate of salvation.
RECORD	para 3712	mnmuK hukmu n jwxnI iqn mwry jm jMdwru ] (90-10, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) manmukh hukam na jaannee tin maaray jam jandaar. The self-willed manmukhs do not know the Lord's Command; they are beaten down by the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	para 3713	gurmuiK ijnI ArwiDAw iqnI qirAw Baujlu sMswru ] (90-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) gurmukh jinee araaDhi-aa tinee tari-aa bha-ojal sansaar. But the Gurmukhs, who worship and adore the Lord, cross over the terrifying world- ocean.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	siB Aaugx guxI imtwieAw guru Awpy bKsxhwru ]2] (90-11, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sabh a-ugan gunee mitaa-i-aa gur aapay bakhsanhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v2	All their demerits are erased, and replaced with merits. The Guru Himself is their Forgiver. ||2||
RECORD	para 3715	pauVI ] (90-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 3716	hir kI Bgqw prqIiq hir sB ikCu jwxdw ] (90-12, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har kee bhagtaa parteet har sabh kichh jaandaa. The Lord's devotees have faith in Him. The Lord knows everything.
DEFINE	para 3717	hir jyvfu nwhI koeI jwxu hir Drmu bIcwrdw ] (90-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) har jayvad naahee ko-ee jaan har Dharam beechaardaa. No one is as great a Knower as the Lord; the Lord administers righteous justice.
RECORD	para 3718	kwVw AMdysw ikau kIjY jw nwhI ADrim mwrdw ] (90-13, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) kaarhaa andaysaa ki-o keejai jaa naahee aDhram maardaa. Why should we feel any burning anxiety, since the Lord does not punish without just cause?
DEFINE	para 3719	scw swihbu scu inAwau pwpI nru hwrdw ] (90-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) sachaa saahib sach ni-aa-o paapee nar haardaa. True is the Master, and True is His Justice; only the sinners are defeated.
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v18	swlwihhu Bgqhu kr joiV hir Bgq jn qwrdw ]18] (90-14, isrIrwgu, mÚ 3) saalaahihu bhagtahu kar jorh har bhagat jan taardaa. ||18||
RECORD	isrIrwg kI vwr mhlw 4 slokw nwil v18	O devotees, praise the Lord with your palms pressed together; the Lord saves His humble devotees. ||18||
RECORD	para 3721	slok mÚ 3 ] (90-15) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
