DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	They serve the True Guru, the Giver of eternal peace, and all their desires are fulfilled. ||5||
RECORD	para 4608	hir jIau qyrI sdw srxweI ] (111-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) har jee-o tayree sadaa sarnaa-ee. O Dear Lord, I seek Your Sanctuary forever.
RECORD	para 4609	Awpy bKisih dy vifAweI ] (111-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay bakhsihi day vadi-aa-ee. You Yourself forgive us, and bless us with Glorious Greatness.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	jmkwlu iqsu nyiV n AwvY jo hir hir nwmu iDAwvixAw ]6] (111-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) jamkaal tis nayrh na aavai jo har har naam Dhi-aavani-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	The Messenger of Death does not draw near those who meditate on the Name of the Lord, Har, Har. ||6||
DEFINE	para 4611	Anidnu rwqy jo hir Bwey ] (111-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din raatay jo har bhaa-ay. Night and day, they are attuned to His Love; they are pleasing to the Lord.
RECORD	para 4612	myrY pRiB myly myil imlwey ] (111-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) mayrai parabh maylay mayl milaa-ay. My God merges with them, and unites them in Union.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	sdw sdw scy qyrI srxweI qUM Awpy scu buJwvixAw ]7] (111-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa sachay tayree sarnaa-ee tooN aapay sach bujhaavani-aa. ||7||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Forever and ever, O True Lord, I seek the Protection of Your Sanctuary; You Yourself inspire us to understand the Truth. ||7||
DEFINE	para 4614	ijn scu jwqw sy sic smwxy ] (111-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) jin sach jaataa say sach samaanay. Those who know the Truth are absorbed in Truth.
RECORD	para 4615	hir gux gwvih scu vKwxy ] (111-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) har gun gaavahi sach vakhaanay. They sing the Lord's Glorious Praises, and speak the Truth.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwim rqy bYrwgI inj Gir qwVI lwvixAw ]8]3]4] (111-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay bairaagee nij ghar taarhee laavani-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam remain unattached and balanced; in the home of the inner self, they are absorbed in the primal trance of deep meditation. ||8||
DEFINE	para 4618	sbid mrY su muAw jwpY ] (111-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabad marai so mu-aa jaapai. One who dies in the Word of the Shabad is truly dead.
RECORD	para 4619	kwlu n cwpY duKu n sMqwpY ] (111-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) kaal na chaapai dukh na santaapai. Death does not crush him, and pain does not afflict him.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	joqI ivic imil joiq smwxI suix mn sic smwvixAw ]1] (111-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) jotee vich mil jot samaanee sun man sach samaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	His light merges and is absorbed into the Light, when he hears and merges in the Truth. ||1||
DEFINE	para 4621	hau vwrI jIau vwrI hir kY nwie soBw pwvixAw ] (111-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree har kai naa-ay sobhaa paavni-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to the Lord's Name, which brings us to glory.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	siqguru syiv sic icqu lwieAw gurmqI shij smwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (111-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayv sach chit laa-i-aa gurmatee sahj samaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. One who serves the True Guru, and focuses his consciousness on Truth, following the Guru's Teachings, is absorbed in intuitive peace and poise. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 4623	kwieAw kcI kcw cIru hMFwey ] (111-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kachee kachaa cheer handhaa-ay. This human body is transitory, and transitory are the garments it wears.
RECORD	para 4624	dUjY lwgI mhlu n pwey ] (111-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) doojai laagee mahal na paa-ay. Attached to duality, no one attains the Mansion of the Lord's Presence.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	Anidnu jldI iPrY idnu rwqI ibnu ipr bhu duKu pwvixAw ]2] (112-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din jaldee firai din raatee bin pir baho dukh paavni-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	Night and day, day and night, they burn. Without her Husband Lord, the soul-bride suffers in terrible pain. ||2||
