REQUIRE	para 4628	ijQY lyKw mMgIAY iqQY CutY scu kmwey ] (112-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) jithai laykhaa mangee-ai tithai chhutai sach kamaa-ay. Where she is called to answer for her account, there, she shall be emancipated only by true actions.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	siqguru syvin sy DnvMqy AYQY EQY nwim smwvixAw ]3] (112-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvan say Dhanvantay aithai othai naam samaavani-aa. ||3||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Those who serve the True Guru shall prosper; here and hereafter, they are absorbed in the Naam. ||3||
RECORD	para 4630	BY Bwie sIgwru bxwey ] (112-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) bhai bhaa-ay seegaar banaa-ay. She who adorns herself with the Love and the Fear of God,
RECORD	para 4631	gur prswdI mhlu Gru pwey ] (112-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee mahal ghar paa-ay. by Guru's Grace, obtains the Mansion of the Lord's Presence as her home.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	Anidnu sdw rvY idnu rwqI mjITY rMgu bxwvixAw ]4] (112-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din sadaa ravai din raatee majeethai rang banaavani-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	Night and day, day and night, she constantly ravishes and enjoys her Beloved. She is dyed in the permanent color of His Love. ||4||
RECORD	para 4633	sBnw ipru vsY sdw nwly ] (112-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabhnaa pir vasai sadaa naalay. The Husband Lord abides with everyone, always;
DEFINE	para 4634	gur prswdI ko ndir inhwly ] (112-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee ko nadar nihaalay. but how rare are those few who, by Guru's Grace, obtain His Glance of Grace.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	myrw pRBu Aiq aUco aUcw kir ikrpw Awip imlwvixAw ]5] (112-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) mayraa parabh at oocho oochaa kar kirpaa aap milaavani-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	My God is the Highest of the High; granting His Grace, He merges us into Himself. ||5||
DEFINE	para 4636	mwieAw moih iehu jgu suqw ] (112-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi ih jag sutaa. This world is asleep in emotional attachment to Maya.
RECORD	para 4637	nwmu ivswir AMiq ivguqw ] (112-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) naam visaar ant vigutaa. Forgetting the Naam, the Name of the Lord, it ultimately comes to ruin.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	ijs qy suqw so jwgwey gurmiq soJI pwvixAw ]6] (112-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) jis tay sutaa so jaagaa-ay gurmat sojhee paavni-aa. ||6||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	The One who put it to sleep shall also awaken it. Through the Guru's Teachings, understanding dawns. ||6||
REQUIRE	para 4639	Aipau pIAY so Brmu gvwey ] (112-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) api-o pee-ai so bharam gavaa-ay. One who drinks in this Nectar, shall have his delusions dispelled.
DEFINE	para 4640	gur prswid mukiq giq pwey ] (112-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaad mukat gat paa-ay. By Guru's Grace, the state of liberation is attained.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	BgqI rqw sdw bYrwgI Awpu mwir imlwvixAw ]7] (112-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) bhagtee rataa sadaa bairaagee aap maar milaavani-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	One who is imbued with devotion to the Lord, remains always balanced and detached. Subduing selfishness and conceit, he is united with the Lord. ||7||
RECORD	para 4642	Awip aupwey DMDY lwey ] (112-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) aap upaa-ay DhanDhai laa-ay. He Himself creates, and He Himself assigns us to our tasks.
RECORD	para 4643	lK caurwsI irjku Awip ApVwey ] (112-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) lakh cha-uraasee rijak aap aprhaa-ay. He Himself gives sustenance to the 8.4 million species of beings.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwmu iDAwie sic rwqy jo iqsu BwvY su kwr krwvixAw ]8]4]5] (112-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam Dhi-aa-ay sach raatay jo tis bhaavai so kaar karaavani-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, those who meditate on the Naam are atuned to Truth. They do that which is pleasing to His Will. ||8||
DEFINE	para 4646	AMdir hIrw lwlu bxwieAw ] (112-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) andar heeraa laal banaa-i-aa. Diamonds and rubies are produced deep within the self.
DEFINE	para 4647	gur kY sbid priK prKwieAw ] (112-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad parakh parkhaa-i-aa. They are assayed and valued tthrough the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	ijn scu plY scu vKwxih scu ksvtI lwvixAw ]1] (112-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) jin sach palai sach vakaaneh sach kasvatee laavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Those who have gathered Truth, speak Truth; they apply the Touch-stone of Truth. ||1||
RECORD	para 4649	hau vwrI jIau vwrI gur kI bwxI mMin vswvixAw ] (112-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree gur kee banee man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who enshrine the Word of the Guru's Bani within their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	AMjn mwih inrMjnu pwieAw joqI joiq imlwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (112-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) anjan maahi niranjan paa-i-aa jotee jot milaavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. In the midst of the darkness of the world, they obtain the Immaculate One, and their light merges into the Light. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 4651	iesu kwieAw AMdir bhuqu pswrw ] (112-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) is kaa-i-aa andar bahut pasaaraa. Within this body are countless vast vistas;
DEFINE	para 4652	nwmu inrMjnu Aiq Agm Apwrw ] (112-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) naam niranjan at agam apaaraa. the Immaculate Naam is totally Inaccessible and Infinite.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	gurmuiK hovY soeI pwey Awpy bKis imlwvixAw ]2] (112-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so-ee paa-ay aapay bakhas milaavani-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	He alone becomes Gurmukh and obtains it, whom the Lord forgives, and unites with Himself. ||2||
RECORD	para 4654	myrw Twkuru scu idRVwey ] (112-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) mayraa thaakur sach drirh-aa-ay. My Lord and Master implants the Truth.
DEFINE	para 4655	gur prswdI sic icqu lwey ] (112-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee sach chit laa-ay. By Guru's Grace, one's consciousness is attached to the Truth.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	sco scu vrqY sBnI QweI scy sic smwvixAw ]3] (112-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) sacho sach vartai sabhnee thaa-ee sachay sach samaavani-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	The Truest of the True is pervading everywhere; the true ones merge in Truth. ||3||
DEFINE	para 4657	vyprvwhu scu myrw ipAwrw ] (112-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) vayparvaahu sach mayraa pi-aaraa. The True Carefree Lord is my Beloved.
RECORD	para 4658	iklivK Avgx kwtxhwrw ] (112-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) kilvikh avgan kaatanhaaraa. He cuts out our sinful mistakes and evil actions;
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	pRym pRIiq sdw iDAweIAY BY Bwie Bgiq idRVwvixAw ]4] (112-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) paraym pareet sadaa Dhi-aa-ee-ai bhai bhaa-ay bhagat darirhaavni-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	with love and affection, meditate forever on Him. He implants the Fear of God and loving devotional worship within us. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4660	qyrI Bgiq scI jy scy BwvY ] (112-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) tayree bhagat sachee jay sachay bhaavai. Devotional worship is True, if it pleases the True Lord.
RECORD	para 4661	Awpy dyie n pCoqwvY ] (112-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay day-ay na pachhotaavai. He Himself bestows it; He does not regret it later.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	sBnw jIAw kw eyko dwqw sbdy mwir jIvwvixAw ]5] (112-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabhnaa jee-aa kaa ayko daataa sabday maar jeevaavni-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	He alone is the Giver of all beings. The Lord kills with the Word of His Shabad, and then revives. ||5||
DEFINE	para 4663	hir quDu bwJhu mY koeI nwhI ] (112-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) har tuDh baajhahu mai ko-ee naahee. Other than You, Lord, nothing is mine.
RECORD	para 4664	hir quDY syvI qY quDu swlwhI ] (112-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) har tuDhai sayvee tai tuDh saalaahee. I serve You, Lord, and I praise You.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Awpy myil lYhu pRB swcy pUrY krim qUM pwvixAw ]6] (112-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay mayl laihu parabh saachay poorai karam tooN paavni-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	You unite me with Yourself, O True God. Through perfect good karma You are obtained. ||6||
DEFINE	para 4666	mY horu n koeI quDY jyhw ] (112-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) mai hor na ko-ee tuDhai jayhaa. For me, there is no other like You.
DEFINE	para 4667	qyrI ndrI sIJis dyhw ] (112-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) tayree nadree seejhas dayhaa. By Your Glance of Grace, my body is blessed and sanctified.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Anidnu swir smwil hir rwKih gurmuiK shij smwvixAw ]7] (112-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din saar samaal har raakhahi gurmukh sahj samaavani-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Night and day, the Lord takes care of us and protects us. The Gurmukhs are absorbed in intuitive peace and poise. ||7||
DEFINE	para 4669	quDu jyvfu mY horu n koeI ] (112-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) tuDh jayvad mai hor na ko-ee. For me, there is no other as Great as You.
RECORD	para 4670	quDu Awpy isrjI Awpy goeI ] (112-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) tuDh aapay sirjee aapay go-ee. You Yourself create, and You Yourself destroy.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	qUM Awpy hI GiV BMin svwrih nwnk nwim suhwvixAw ]8]5]6] (113-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) tooN aapay hee gharh bhann savaareh naanak naam suhaavani-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	You Yourself create, destroy and adorn. O Nanak, we are adorned and embellished with the Naam. ||8||
DEFINE	para 4674	sB Gt Awpy Bogxhwrw ] (113-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabh ghat aapay bhoganhaaraa. He is the Enjoyer of all hearts.
DEFINE	para 4675	AlKu vrqY Agm Apwrw ] (113-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) alakh vartai agam apaaraa. The Invisible, Inaccessible and Infinite is pervading everywhere.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	gur kY sbid myrw hir pRBu iDAweIAY shjy sic smwvixAw ]1] (113-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad mayraa har parabh Dhi-aa-ee-ai sehjay sach samaavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Meditating on my Lord God, through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, I am intuitively absorbed in the Truth. ||1||
RECORD	para 4677	hau vwrI jIau vwrI gur sbdu mMin vswvixAw ] (113-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree gur sabad man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who implant the Word of the Guru's Shabad in their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	sbdu sUJY qw mn isau lUJY mnsw mwir smwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (113-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabad soojhai taa man si-o loojhai mansaa maar samaavani-aa. ||1||
WHEN	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. When someone understands the Shabad, then he wrestles with his own mind; subduing his desires, he merges with the Lord. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 4679	pMc dUq muhih sMswrw ] (113-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) panch doot muheh sansaaraa. The five enemies are plundering the world.
RECORD	para 4680	mnmuK AMDy suiD n swrw ] (113-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh anDhay suDh na saaraa. The blind, self-willed manmukhs do not understand or appreciate this.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	gurmuiK hovY su Apxw Gru rwKY pMc dUq sbid pcwvixAw ]2] (113-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so apnaa ghar raakhai panch doot sabad pachaavani-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	Those who become Gurmukh-their houses are protected. The five enemies are destroyed by the Shabad. ||2||
DEFINE	para 4682	ieik gurmuiK sdw scY rMig rwqy ] (113-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) ik gurmukh sadaa sachai rang raatay. The Gurmukhs are forever imbued with love for the True One.
DEFINE	para 4683	shjy pRBu syvih Anidnu mwqy ] (113-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) sehjay parabh sayveh an-din maatay. They serve God with intuitive ease. Night and day, they are intoxicated with His Love.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	imil pRIqm scy gux gwvih hir dir soBw pwvixAw ]3] (113-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) mil pareetam sachay gun gaavahi har dar sobhaa paavni-aa. ||3||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Meeting with their Beloved, they sing the Glorious Praises of the True one; they are honored in the Court of the Lord. ||3||
RECORD	para 4685	eykm eykY Awpu aupwieAw ] (113-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) aykam aykai aap upaa-i-aa. First, the One created Himself;
RECORD	para 4686	duibDw dUjw iqRibiD mwieAw ] (113-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) dubiDhaa doojaa taribaDh maa-i-aa. second, the sense of duality; third, the three-phased Maya.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	cauQI pauVI gurmuiK aUcI sco scu kmwvixAw ]4] (113-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) cha-uthee pa-orhee gurmukh oochee sacho sach kamaavani-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	The fourth state, the highest, is obtained by the Gurmukh, who practices Truth, and only Truth. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4688	sBu hY scw jy scy BwvY ] (113-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabh hai sachaa jay sachay bhaavai. Everything which is pleasing to the True Lord is true.
RECORD	para 4689	ijin scu jwqw so shij smwvY ] (113-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) jin sach jaataa so sahj samaavai. Those who know the Truth merge in intuitive peace and poise.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	gurmuiK krxI scy syvih swcy jwie smwvixAw ]5] (113-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh karnee sachay sayveh saachay jaa-ay samaavani-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	The life-style of the Gurmukh is to serve the True Lord. He goes and blends with the True Lord. ||5||
DEFINE	para 4691	scy bwJhu ko Avru n dUAw ] (113-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachay baajhahu ko avar na doo-aa. Without the True One, there is no other at all.
DEFINE	para 4692	dUjY lwig jgu Kip Kip mUAw ] (113-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) doojai laag jag khap khap moo-aa. Attached to duality, the world is distracted and distressed to death.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	gurmuiK hovY su eyko jwxY eyko syiv suKu pwvixAw ]6] (113-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so ayko jaanai ayko sayv sukh paavni-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	One who becomes Gurmukh knows only the One. Serving the One, peace is obtained. ||6||
DEFINE	para 4694	jIA jMq siB srix qumwrI ] (113-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) jee-a jant sabh saran tumaaree. All beings and creatures are in the Protection of Your Sanctuary.
RECORD	para 4695	Awpy Dir dyKih kcI pkI swrI ] (113-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay Dhar daykheh kachee pakee saaree. You place the chessmen on the board; You see the imperfect and the perfect as well.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Anidnu Awpy kwr krwey Awpy myil imlwvixAw ]7] (113-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din aapay kaar karaa-ay aapay mayl milaavani-aa. ||7||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Night and day, You cause people to act; You unite them in Union with Yourself. ||7||
RECORD	para 4697	qUM Awpy mylih vyKih hdUir ] (113-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) tooN aapay mayleh vaykheh hadoor. You Yourself unite, and You see Yourself close at hand.
DEFINE	para 4698	sB mih Awip rihAw BrpUir ] (113-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabh meh aap rahi-aa bharpoor. You Yourself are totally pervading amongst all.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk Awpy Awip vrqY gurmuiK soJI pwvixAw ]8]6]7] (113-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak aapay aap vartai gurmukh sojhee paavni-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, God Himself is pervading and permeating everywhere; only the Gurmukhs understand this. ||8||
DEFINE	para 4701	AMimRq bwxI gur kI mITI ] (113-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit banee gur kee meethee. The Nectar of the Guru's Bani is very sweet.
DEFINE	para 4702	gurmuiK ivrlY iknY ciK fITI ] (113-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlai kinai chakh deethee. Rare are the Gurmukhs who see and taste it.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	AMqir prgwsu mhw rsu pIvY dir scY sbdu vjwvixAw ]1] (113-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) antar pargaas mahaa ras peevai dar sachai sabad vajaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	The Divine Light dawns within, and the supreme essence is found. In the True Court, the Word of the Shabad vibrates. ||1||
DEFINE	para 4704	hau vwrI jIau vwrI gur crxI icqu lwvixAw ] (113-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree gur charnee chit laavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who focus their consciousness on the Guru's Feet.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	siqguru hY AMimRq sru swcw mnu nwvY mYlu cukwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (113-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur hai amrit sar saachaa man naavai mail chukaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The True Guru is the True Pool of Nectar; bathing in it, the mind is washed clean of all filth. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 4706	qyrw scy iknY AMqu n pwieAw ] (113-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) tayraa sachay kinai ant na paa-i-aa. Your limits, O True Lord, are not known to anyone.
DEFINE	para 4707	gur prswid iknY ivrlY icqu lwieAw ] (113-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaad kinai virlai chit laa-i-aa. Rare are those who, by Guru's Grace, focus their consciousness on You.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	quDu swlwih n rjw kbhUM scy nwvY kI BuK lwvixAw ]2] (113-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) tuDh saalaahi na rajaa kabahoo N sachay naavai kee bhukh laavani-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	Praising You, I am never satisfied; such is the hunger I feel for the True Name. ||2||
RECORD	para 4709	eyko vyKw Avru n bIAw ] (113-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) ayko vaykhaa avar na bee-aa. I see only the One, and no other.
RECORD	para 4710	gur prswdI AMimRqu pIAw ] (113-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee amrit pee-aa. By Guru's Grace, I drink in the Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	gur kY sbid iqKw invwrI shjy sUiK smwvixAw ]3] (113-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad tikhaa nivaaree sehjay sookh samaavani-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	My thirst is quenched by the Word of the Guru's Shabad; I am absorbed in intuitive peace and poise. ||3||
DEFINE	para 4712	rqnu pdwrQu plir iqAwgY ] (113-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) ratan padaarath palar ti-aagai. The Priceless Jewel is discarded like straw;
DEFINE	para 4713	mnmuKu AMDw dUjY Bwie lwgY ] (113-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh anDhaa doojai bhaa-ay laagai. the blind self-willed manmukhs are attached to the love of duality.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	jo bIjY soeI Plu pwey supnY suKu n pwvixAw ]4] (113-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) jo beejai so-ee fal paa-ay supnai sukh na paavni-aa. ||4||
FORBID	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	As they plant, so do they harvest. They shall not obtain peace, even in their dreams. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4715	ApnI ikrpw kry soeI jnu pwey ] (113-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) apnee kirpaa karay so-ee jan paa-ay. Those who are blessed with His Mercy find the Lord.
RECORD	para 4716	gur kw sbdu mMin vswey ] (113-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kaa sabad man vasaa-ay. The Word of the Guru's Shabad abides in the mind.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Anidnu sdw rhY BY AMdir BY mwir Brmu cukwvixAw ]5] (114-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din sadaa rahai bhai andar bhai maar bharam chukaavani-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Night and day, they remain in the Fear of God; conquering their fears, their doubts are dispelled. ||5||
RECORD	para 4719	Brmu cukwieAw sdw suKu pwieAw ] (114-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) bharam chukaa-i-aa sadaa sukh paa-i-aa. Dispelling their doubts, they find a lasting peace.
DEFINE	para 4720	gur prswid prm pdu pwieAw ] (114-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaad param pad paa-i-aa. By Guru's Grace, the supreme status is attained.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	AMqru inrmlu inrml bwxI hir gux shjy gwvixAw ]6] (114-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) antar nirmal nirmal banee har gun sehjay gaavani-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Deep within, they are pure, and their words are pure as well; intuitively, they sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||6||
RECORD	para 4722	isimRiq swsq byd vKwxY ] (114-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) simrit saasat bayd vakhaanai. They recite the Simritees, the Shaastras and the Vedas,
ALLOW	para 4723	Brmy BUlw qqu n jwxY ] (114-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) bharmay bhoolaa tat na jaanai. but deluded by doubt, they do not understand the essence of reality.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	ibnu siqgur syvy suKu n pwey duKo duKu kmwvixAw ]7] (114-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay sukh na paa-ay dukho dukh kamaavani-aa. ||7||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Without serving the True Guru, they find no peace; they earn only pain and misery. ||7||
RECORD	para 4725	Awip kry iksu AwKY koeI ] (114-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) aap karay kis aakhai ko-ee. The Lord Himself acts; unto whom should we complain?
RECORD	para 4726	AwKix jweIAY jy BUlw hoeI ] (114-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) aakhan jaa-ee-ai jay bhoolaa ho-ee. How can anyone complain that the Lord has made a mistake?
ALLOW	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk Awpy kry krwey nwmy nwim smwvixAw ]8]7]8] (114-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak aapay karay karaa-ay naamay naam samaavani-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, the Lord Himself does, and causes things to be done; chanting the Naam, we are absorbed in the Naam. ||8||
RECORD	para 4729	Awpy rMgy shij suBwey ] (114-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay rangay sahj subhaa-ay. He Himself imbues us with His Love, with effortless ease.
DEFINE	para 4730	gur kY sbid hir rMgu cVwey ] (114-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad har rang charhaa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, we are dyed in the color of the Lord's Love.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	mnu qnu rqw rsnw rMig clUlI BY Bwie rMgu cVwvixAw ]1] (114-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) man tan rataa rasnaa rang chaloolee bhai bhaa-ay rang charhaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	This mind and body are so imbued, and this tongue is dyed in the deep crimson color of the poppy. Through the Love and the Fear of God, we are dyed in this color. ||1||
DEFINE	para 4732	hau vwrI jIau vwrI inrBau mMin vswvixAw ] (114-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree nirbha-o man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who enshrine the Fearless Lord within their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	gur ikrpw qy hir inrBau iDAwieAw ibKu Baujlu sbid qrwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (114-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kirpaa tay har nirbha-o Dhi-aa-i-aa bikh bha-ojal sabad taraavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa- o. By Guru's Grace, I meditate on the Fearless Lord; the Shabad has carried me across the poisonous world-ocean. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 4734	mnmuK mugD krih cqurweI ] (114-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh mugaDh karahi chaturaa-ee. The idiotic self-willed manmukhs try to be clever,
FORBID	para 4735	nwqw Doqw Qwie n pweI ] (114-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) naataa Dhotaa thaa-ay na paa-ee. but in spite of their bathing and washing, they shall not be acceptable.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	jyhw AwieAw qyhw jwsI kir Avgx pCoqwvixAw ]2] (114-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) jayhaa aa-i-aa tayhaa jaasee kar avgan pachhotaavani-aa. ||2||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	As they came, so shall they go, regretting the mistakes they made. ||2||
RECORD	para 4737	mnmuK AMDy ikCU n sUJY ] (114-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh anDhay kichhoo na soojhai. The blind, self-willed manmukhs do not understand anything;
WHEN	para 4738	mrxu ilKwie Awey nhI bUJY ] (114-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) maran likhaa-ay aa-ay nahee boojhai. death was pre-ordained for them when they came into the world, but they do not understand.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	mnmuK krm kry nhI pwey ibnu nwvY jnmu gvwvixAw ]3] (114-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh karam karay nahee paa-ay bin naavai janam gavaavni-aa. ||3||
ALLOW	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	The self-willed manmukhs may practice religious rituals, but they do not obtain the Name; without the Name, they lose this life in vain. ||3||
DEFINE	para 4740	scu krxI sbdu hY swru ] (114-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach karnee sabad hai saar. The practice of Truth is the essence of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 4741	pUrY guir pweIAY moK duAwru ] (114-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) poorai gur paa-ee-ai mokh du-aar. Through the Perfect Guru, the gate of salvation is found.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	Anidnu bwxI sbid suxwey sic rwqy rMig rMgwvixAw ]4] (114-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din banee sabad sunaa-ay sach raatay rang rangaavin-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	So, night and day, listen to the Word of the Guru's Bani, and the Shabad. Let yourself be colored by this love. ||4||
RECORD	para 4743	rsnw hir ris rwqI rMgu lwey ] (114-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) rasnaa har ras raatee rang laa-ay. The tongue, imbued with the Lord's Essence, delights in His Love.
DEFINE	para 4744	mnu qnu moihAw shij suBwey ] (114-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) man tan mohi-aa sahj subhaa-ay. My mind and body are enticed by the Lord's Sublime Love.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	shjy pRIqmu ipAwrw pwieAw shjy shij imlwvixAw ]5] (114-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) sehjay pareetam pi-aaraa paa-i-aa sehjay sahj milaavani-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	I have easily obtained my Darling Beloved; I am intuitively absorbed in celestial peace. ||5||
RECORD	para 4746	ijsu AMdir rMgu soeI gux gwvY ] (114-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) jis andar rang so-ee gun gaavai. Those who have the Lord's Love within, sing His Glorious Praises;
DEFINE	para 4747	gur kY sbid shjy suiK smwvY ] (114-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad sehjay sukh samaavai. through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, they are intuitively absorbed in celestial peace.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	hau bilhwrI sdw iqn ivthu gur syvw icqu lwvixAw ]6] (114-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o balihaaree sadaa tin vitahu gur sayvaa chit laavani-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	I am forever a sacrifice to those who dedicate their consciousness to the Guru's Service. ||6||
DEFINE	para 4749	scw sco sic pqIjY ] (114-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachaa sacho sach pateejai. The True Lord is pleased with Truth, and only Truth.
DEFINE	para 4750	gur prswdI AMdru BIjY ] (114-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee andar bheejai. By Guru's Grace, one's inner being is deeply imbued with His Love.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	bYis suQwin hir gux gwvih Awpy kir siq mnwvixAw ]7] (114-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) bais suthaan har gun gaavahi aapay kar sat manaavni-aa. ||7||
UPHOLD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Sitting in that blessed place, sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, who Himself inspires us to accept His Truth. ||7||
RECORD	para 4752	ijs no ndir kry so pwey ] (114-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) jis no nadar karay so paa-ay. That one, upon whom the Lord casts His Glance of Grace, obtains it.
RECORD	para 4753	gur prswdI haumY jwey ] (114-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee ha-umai jaa-ay. By Guru's Grace, egotism departs.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwmu vsY mn AMqir dir scY soBw pwvixAw ]8]8]9] (114-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam vasai man antar dar sachai sobhaa paavni-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, that one, within whose mind the Name dwells, is honored in the True Court. ||8||
RECORD	para 4755	maajh mehlaa 3. Maajh Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 4756	siqguru syivAY vfI vifAweI ] (114-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvi-ai vadee vadi-aa-ee. Serving the True Guru is the greatest greatness.
RECORD	para 4757	hir jI AicMqu vsY min AweI ] (114-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) har jee achint vasai man aa-ee. The Dear Lord automatically comes to dwell in the mind.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	hir jIau sPilE ibrKu hY AMimRqu ijin pIqw iqsu iqKw lhwvixAw ]1] (114-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) har jee-o safli-o birakh hai amrit jin peetaa tis tikhaa lahaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	The Dear Lord is the fruit-bearing tree; drinking in the Ambrosial Nectar, thirst is quenched. ||1||
RECORD	para 4759	hau vwrI jIau vwrI scu sMgiq myil imlwvixAw ] (114-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree sach sangat mayl milaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to the one who leads me to join the True Congregation.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	hir sqsMgiq Awpy mylY gur sbdI hir gux gwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (114-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) har satsangat aapay maylai gur sabdee har gun gaavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The Lord Himself unites me with the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, I sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 4762	siqguru syvI sbid suhwieAw ] (115-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvee sabad suhaa-i-aa. I serve the True Guru; the Word of His Shabad is beautiful.
RECORD	para 4763	ijin hir kw nwmu mMin vswieAw ] (115-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) jin har kaa naam man vasaa-i-aa. Through it, the Name of the Lord comes to dwell within the mind.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	hir inrmlu haumY mYlu gvwey dir scY soBw pwvixAw ]2] (115-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) har nirmal ha-umai mail gavaa-ay dar sachai sobhaa paavni-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	The Pure Lord removes the filth of egotism, and we are honored in the True Court. ||2||
RECORD	para 4765	ibnu gur nwmu n pwieAw jwie ] (115-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin gur naam na paa-i-aa jaa-ay. Without the Guru, the Naam cannot be obtained.
RECORD	para 4766	isD swiDk rhy ibllwie ] (115-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) siDh saaDhik rahay billaa-ay. The Siddhas and the seekers lack it; they weep and wail.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	ibnu gur syvy suKu n hovI pUrY Bwig guru pwvixAw ]3] (115-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin gur sayvay sukh na hovee poorai bhaag gur paavni-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Without serving the True Guru, peace is not obtained; through perfect destiny, the Guru is found. ||3||
DEFINE	para 4768	iehu mnu AwrsI koeI gurmuiK vyKY ] (115-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) ih man aarsee ko-ee gurmukh vaykhai. This mind is a mirror; how rare are those who, as Gurmukh, see themselves in it.
RECORD	para 4769	morcw n lwgY jw haumY soKY ] (115-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) morchaa na laagai jaa ha-umai sokhai. Rust does not stick to those who burn their ego.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	Anhq bwxI inrml sbdu vjwey gur sbdI sic smwvixAw ]4] (115-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) anhat banee nirmal sabad vajaa-ay gur sabdee sach samaavani-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	The Unstruck Melody of the Bani resounds through the Pure Word of the Shabad; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, we are absorbed into the True One. ||4||
RECORD	para 4771	ibnu siqgur ikhu n dyiKAw jwie ] (115-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin satgur kihu na daykhi-aa jaa-ay. Without the True Guru, the Lord cannot be seen.
RECORD	para 4772	guir ikrpw kir Awpu idqw idKwie ] (115-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kirpaa kar aap ditaa dikhaa-ay. Granting His Grace, He Himself has allowed me to see Him.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Awpy Awip Awip imil rihAw shjy shij smwvixAw ]5] (115-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay aap aap mil rahi-aa sehjay sahj samaavani-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	All by Himself, He Himself is permeating and pervading; He is intuitively absorbed in celestial peace. ||5||
RECORD	para 4774	gurmuiK hovY su ieksu isau ilv lwey ] (115-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so ikas si-o liv laa-ay. One who becomes Gurmukh embraces love for the One.
DEFINE	para 4775	dUjw Brmu gur sbid jlwey ] (115-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) doojaa bharam gur sabad jalaa-ay. Doubt and duality are burned away by the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	kwieAw AMdir vxju kry vwpwrw nwmu inDwnu scu pwvixAw ]6] (115-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa andar vanaj karay vaapaaraa naam niDhaan sach paavni-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Within his body, he deals and trades, and obtains the Treasure of the True Name. ||6||
DEFINE	para 4777	gurmuiK krxI hir kIriq swru ] (115-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh karnee har keerat saar. The life-style of the Gurmukh is sublime; he sings the Praises of the Lord.
RECORD	para 4778	gurmuiK pwey moK duAwru ] (115-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh paa-ay mokh du-aar. The Gurmukh finds the gate of salvation.
