DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Truth, contentment and intuitive peace and poise are obtained from the Bani, the Word of the Perfect Guru. ||3||
RECORD	para 4795	siqguru n syvih mUrK AMD gvwrw ] (115-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur na sayveh moorakh anDh gavaaraa. The blind and ignorant fools do not serve the True Guru;
RECORD	para 4796	iPir Eie ikQhu pwiein moK duAwrw ] (115-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) fir o-ay kithhu paa-in mokh du-aaraa. how will they find the gate of salvation?
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	mir mir jMmih iPir iPir Awvih jm dir cotw KwvixAw ]4] (115-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) mar mar jameh fir fir aavahi jam dar chotaa khaavani-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	They die and die, over and over again, only to be reborn, over and over again. They are struck down at Death's Door. ||4||
RECORD	para 4798	sbdY swdu jwxih qw Awpu pCwxih ] (115-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabdai saad jaaneh taa aap pachhaaneh. Those who know the essence of the Shabad, understand their own selves.
DEFINE	para 4799	inrml bwxI sbid vKwxih ] (115-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal banee sabad vakaaneh. Immaculate is the speech of those who chant the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	scy syiv sdw suKu pwiein nau iniD nwmu mMin vswvixAw ]5] (115-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachay sayv sadaa sukh paa-in na-o niDh naam man vasaavani-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Serving the True One, they find a lasting peace; they enshrine the nine treasures of the Naam within their minds. ||5||
DEFINE	para 4801	so Qwnu suhwieAw jo hir min BwieAw ] (115-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) so thaan suhaa-i-aa jo har man bhaa-i-aa. Beautiful is that place, which is pleasing to the Lord's Mind.
DEFINE	para 4802	sqsMgiq bih hir gux gwieAw ] (115-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) satsangat bahi har gun gaa-i-aa. There, sitting in the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation, the Glorious Praises of the Lord are sung.
