DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Night and day, the True One is praised; the Immaculate Sound-current of the Naad resounds there. ||6||
DEFINE	para 4805	mnmuK KotI rwis Kotw pwswrw ] (116-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh khotee raas khotaa paasaaraa. The wealth of the self-willed manmukhs is false, and false is their ostentatious display.
RECORD	para 4806	kUVu kmwvin duKu lwgY Bwrw ] (116-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) koorh kamaavan dukh laagai bhaaraa. They practice falsehood, and suffer terrible pain.
ALLOW	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Brmy BUly iPrin idn rwqI mir jnmih jnmu gvwvixAw ]7] (116-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) bharmay bhoolay firan din raatee mar janmeh janam gavaavni-aa. ||7||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Deluded by doubt, they wander day and night; through birth and death, they lose their lives. ||7||
DEFINE	para 4808	scw swihbu mY Aiq ipAwrw ] (116-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachaa saahib mai at pi-aaraa. My True Lord and Master is very dear to me.
DEFINE	para 4809	pUry gur kY sbid ADwrw ] (116-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) pooray gur kai sabad aDhaaraa. The Shabad of the Perfect Guru is my Support.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwim imlY vifAweI duKu suKu sm kir jwnixAw ]8]10]11] (116-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam milai vadi-aa-ee dukh sukh sam kar jaanni-aa. ||8||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, one who obtains the Greatness of the Naam, looks upon pain and pleasure as one and the same. ||8||
DEFINE	para 4812	qyrIAw KwxI qyrIAw bwxI ] (116-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) tayree-aa khaanee tayree-aa banee. The four sources of creation are Yours; the spoken word is Yours.
DEFINE	para 4813	ibnu nwvY sB Brim BulwxI ] (116-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin naavai sabh bharam bhulaanee. Without the Name, all are deluded by doubt.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	gur syvw qy hir nwmu pwieAw ibnu siqgur koie n pwvixAw ]1] (116-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur sayvaa tay har naam paa-i-aa bin satgur ko-ay na paavni-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Serving the Guru, the Lord's Name is obtained. Without the True Guru, no one can receive it. ||1||
DEFINE	para 4815	hau vwrI jIau vwrI hir syqI icqu lwvixAw ] (116-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree har saytee chit laavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who focus their consciousness on the Lord.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	hir scw gur BgqI pweIAY shjy mMin vswvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (116-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) har sachaa gur bhagtee paa-ee-ai sehjay man vasaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Through devotion to the Guru, the True One is found; He comes to abide in the mind, with intuitive ease. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 4817	siqguru syvy qw sB ikCu pwey ] (116-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay taa sabh kichh paa-ay. Serving the True Guru, all things are obtained.
DEFINE	para 4818	jyhI mnsw kir lwgY qyhw Plu pwey ] (116-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) jayhee mansaa kar laagai tayhaa fal paa-ay. As are the desires one harbors, so are the rewards one receives.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	siqguru dwqw sBnw vQU kw pUrY Bwig imlwvixAw ]2] (116-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur daataa sabhnaa vathoo kaa poorai bhaag milaavani-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	The True Guru is the Giver of all things; through perfect destiny, He is met. ||2||
DEFINE	para 4820	iehu mnu mYlw ieku n iDAwey ] (116-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) ih man mailaa ik na Dhi-aa-ay. This mind is filthy and polluted; it does not meditate on the One.
DEFINE	para 4821	AMqir mYlu lwgI bhu dUjY Bwey ] (116-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) antar mail laagee baho doojai bhaa-ay. Deep within, it is soiled and stained by the love of duality.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	qit qIriQ idsMqir BvY AhMkwrI horu vDyrY haumY mlu lwvixAw ]3] (116-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) tat tirath disantar bhavai aha Nkaaree hor vaDhayrai ha-umai mal laavani-aa. ||3||
ALLOW	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	The egotists may go on pilgrimages to holy rivers, sacred shrines and foreign lands, but they only gather more of the dirt of egotism. ||3||
DEFINE	para 4823	siqguru syvy qw mlu jwey ] (116-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay taa mal jaa-ay. Serving the True Guru, filth and pollution are removed.
RECORD	para 4824	jIvqu mrY hir isau icqu lwey ] (116-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) jeevat marai har si-o chit laa-ay. Those who focus their consciousness on the Lord remain dead while yet alive.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	hir inrmlu scu mYlu n lwgY sic lwgY mYlu gvwvixAw ]4] (116-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) har nirmal sach mail na laagai sach laagai mail gavaavni-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	The True Lord is Pure; no filth sticks to Him. Those who are attached to the True One have their filth washed away. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4826	bwJu gurU hY AMD gubwrw ] (116-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) baajh guroo hai anDh gubaaraa. Without the Guru, there is only pitch darkness.
DEFINE	para 4827	AigAwnI AMDw AMDu AMDwrw ] (116-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) agi-aanee anDhaa anDh anDhaaraa. The ignorant ones are blind-there is only utter darkness for them.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	ibstw ky kIVy ibstw kmwvih iPir ibstw mwih pcwvixAw ]5] (116-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) bistaa kay keerhay bistaa kamaaveh fir bistaa maahi pachaavani-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	The maggots in manure do filthy deeds, and in filth they rot and putrefy. ||5||
DEFINE	para 4829	mukqy syvy mukqw hovY ] (116-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) muktay sayvay muktaa hovai. Serving the Lord of Liberation, liberation is achieved.
RECORD	para 4830	haumY mmqw sbdy KovY ] (116-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-umai mamtaa sabday khovai. The Word of the Shabad eradicates egotism and possessiveness.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Anidnu hir jIau scw syvI pUrY Bwig guru pwvixAw ]6] (116-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din har jee-o sachaa sayvee poorai bhaag gur paavni-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	So serve the Dear True Lord, night and day. By perfect good destiny, the Guru is found. ||6||
RECORD	para 4832	Awpy bKsy myil imlwey ] (116-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay bakhsay mayl milaa-ay. He Himself forgives and unites in His Union.
DEFINE	para 4833	pUry gur qy nwmu iniD pwey ] (116-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) pooray gur tay naam niDh paa-ay. From the Perfect Guru, the Treasure of the Naam is obtained.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	scY nwim sdw mnu scw scu syvy duKu gvwvixAw ]7] (116-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachai naam sadaa man sachaa sach sayvay dukh gavaavni-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	By the True Name, the mind is made true forever. Serving the True Lord, sorrow is driven out. ||7||
DEFINE	para 4835	sdw hjUir dUir n jwxhu ] (116-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) sadaa hajoor door na jaanhu. He is always close at hand-do not think that He is far away.
RECORD	para 4836	gur sbdI hir AMqir pCwxhu ] (116-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur sabdee har antar pachhaanhu. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, recognize the Lord deep within your own being.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwim imlY vifAweI pUry gur qy pwvixAw ]8]11]12] (116-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam milai vadi-aa-ee pooray gur tay paavni-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, through the Naam, glorious greatness is received. Through the Perfect Guru, the Naam is obtained. ||8||
DEFINE	para 4839	AYQY swcy su AwgY swcy ] (116-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) aithai saachay so aagai saachay. Those who are True here, are True hereafter as well.
DEFINE	para 4840	mnu scw scY sbid rwcy ] (116-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) man sachaa sachai sabad raachay. That mind is true, which is attuned to the True Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	scw syvih scu kmwvih sco scu kmwvixAw ]1] (116-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachaa sayveh sach kamaaveh sacho sach kamaavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	They serve the True One, and practice Truth; they earn Truth, and only Truth. ||1||
DEFINE	para 4842	hau vwrI jIau vwrI scw nwmu mMin vswvixAw ] (116-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree sachaa naam man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those whose minds are filled with the True Name.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	scy syvih sic smwvih scy ky gux gwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (116-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachay sayveh sach samaaveh sachay kay gun gaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. They serve the True One, and are absorbed into the True One, singing the Glorious Praises of the True One. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 4844	pMifq pVih swdu n pwvih ] (116-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) pandit parheh saad na paavahi. The Pandits, the religious scholars read, but they do not taste the essence.
RECORD	para 4845	dUjY Bwie mwieAw mnu Brmwvih ] (116-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay maa-i-aa man bharmaaveh. In love with duality and Maya, their minds wander, unfocused.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	mwieAw moih sB suiD gvweI kir Avgx pCoqwvixAw ]2] (116-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi sabh suDh gavaa-ee kar avgan pachhotaavani-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	The love of Maya has displaced all their understanding; making mistakes, they live in regret. ||2||
WHEN	para 4847	siqguru imlY qw qqu pwey ] (116-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur milai taa tat paa-ay. But if they should meet the True Guru, then they obtain the essence of reality;
RECORD	para 4848	hir kw nwmu mMin vswey ] (116-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) har kaa naam man vasaa-ay. the Name of the Lord comes to dwell in their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	sbid mrY mnu mwrY Apunw mukqI kw dru pwvixAw ]3] (117-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabad marai man maarai apunaa muktee kaa dar paavni-aa. ||3||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Those who die in the Shabad and subdue their own minds, obtain the door of liberation. ||3||
RECORD	para 4851	iklivK kwtY k®oDu invwry ] (117-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) kilvikh kaatai kroDh nivaaray. They erase their sins, and eliminate their anger;
RECORD	para 4852	gur kw sbdu rKY aur Dwry ] (117-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kaa sabad rakhai ur Dhaaray. they keep the Guru's Shabad clasped tightly to their hearts.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	sic rqy sdw bYrwgI haumY mwir imlwvixAw ]4] (117-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach ratay sadaa bairaagee ha-umai maar milaavani-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	Those who are attuned to Truth, remain balanced and detached forever. Subduing their egotism, they are united with the Lord. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4854	AMqir rqnu imlY imlwieAw ] (117-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) antar ratan milai milaa-i-aa. Deep within the nucleus of the self is the jewel; we receive it only if the Lord inspires us to receive it.
DEFINE	para 4855	iqRibiD mnsw iqRibiD mwieAw ] (117-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) taribaDh mansaa taribaDh maa-i-aa. The mind is bound by the three dispositions-the three modes of Maya.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	piV piV pMifq monI Qky cauQy pd kI swr n pwvixAw ]5] (117-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) parh parh pandit monee thakay cha-uthay pad kee saar na paavni-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Reading and reciting, the Pandits, the religious scholars, and the silent sages have grown weary, but they have not found the supreme essence of the fourth state. ||5||
RECORD	para 4857	Awpy rMgy rMgu cVwey ] (117-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay rangay rang charhaa-ay. The Lord Himself dyes us in the color of His Love.
DEFINE	para 4858	sy jn rwqy gur sbid rMgwey ] (117-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) say jan raatay gur sabad rangaa-ay. Only those who are steeped in the Word of the Guru's Shabad are so imbued with His Love.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	hir rMgu ciVAw Aiq Apwrw hir ris ris gux gwvixAw ]6] (117-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) har rang charhi-aa at apaaraa har ras ras gun gaavani-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Imbued with the most beautiful color of the Lord's Love, they sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, with great pleasure and joy. ||6||
DEFINE	para 4860	gurmuiK iriD isiD scu sMjmu soeI ] (117-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh riDh siDh sach sanjam so-ee. To the Gurmukh, the True Lord is wealth, miraculous spiritual powers and strict self- discipline.
UPHOLD	para 4861	gurmuiK igAwnu nwim mukiq hoeI ] (117-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh gi-aan naam mukat ho-ee. Through the spiritual wisdom of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, the Gurmukh is liberated.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	gurmuiK kwr scu kmwvih scy sic smwvixAw ]7] (117-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh kaar sach kamaaveh sachay sach samaavani-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	The Gurmukh practices Truth, and is absorbed in the Truest of the True. ||7||
RECORD	para 4863	gurmuiK Qwpy Qwip auQwpy ] (117-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh thaapay thaap uthaapay. The Gurmukh realizes that the Lord alone creates, and having created, He destroys.
DEFINE	para 4864	gurmuiK jwiq piq sBu Awpy ] (117-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh jaat pat sabh aapay. To the Gurmukh, the Lord Himself is social class, status and all honor.
ALLOW	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk gurmuiK nwmu iDAwey nwmy nwim smwvixAw ]8]12]13] (117-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh naam Dhi-aa-ay naamay naam samaavani-aa. ||8||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs meditate on the Naam; through the Naam, they merge in the Naam. ||8||
RECORD	para 4867	auqpiq prlau sbdy hovY ] (117-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) utpat parla-o sabday hovai. Creation and destruction happen through the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 4868	sbdy hI iPir Epiq hovY ] (117-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabday hee fir opat hovai. Through the Shabad, creation happens again.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	gurmuiK vrqY sBu Awpy scw gurmuiK aupwie smwvixAw ]1] (117-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh vartai sabh aapay sachaa gurmukh upaa-ay samaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	The Gurmukh knows that the True Lord is all-pervading. The Gurmukh understands creation and merger. ||1||
RECORD	para 4870	hau vwrI jIau vwrI guru pUrw mMin vswvixAw ] (117-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree gur pooraa man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who enshrine the Perfect Guru within their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	gur qy swiq Bgiq kry idnu rwqI gux kih guxI smwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (117-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur tay saat bhagat karay din raatee gun kahi gunee samaavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. From the Guru comes peace and tranquility; worship Him with devotion, day and night. Chanting His Glorious Praises, merge into the Glorious Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 4872	gurmuiK DrqI gurmuiK pwxI ] (117-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh Dhartee gurmukh paanee. The Gurmukh sees the Lord on the earth, and the Gurmukh sees Him in the water.
DEFINE	para 4873	gurmuiK pvxu bYsMqru KylY ivfwxI ] (117-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh pavan baisantar khaylai vidaanee. The Gurmukh sees Him in wind and fire; such is the wonder of His Play.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	so ingurw jo mir mir jMmY ingury Awvx jwvixAw ]2] (117-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) so niguraa jo mar mar jammai niguray aavan jaavani-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	One who has no Guru, dies over and over again, only to be re-born. One who has no Guru continues coming and going in reincarnation. ||2||
RECORD	para 4875	iqin krqY ieku Kylu rcwieAw ] (117-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) tin kartai ik khayl rachaa-i-aa. The One Creator has set this play in motion.
RECORD	para 4876	kwieAw srIrY ivic sBu ikCu pwieAw ] (117-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa sareerai vich sabh kichh paa-i-aa. In the frame of the human body, He has placed all things.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	sbid Byid koeI mhlu pwey mhly mhil bulwvixAw ]3] (117-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabad bhayd ko-ee mahal paa-ay mahlay mahal bulaavani-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Those few who are pierced through by the Word of the Shabad, obtain the Mansion of the Lord's Presence. He calls them into His Wondrous Palace. ||3||
DEFINE	para 4878	scw swhu scy vxjwry ] (117-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachaa saahu sachay vanjaaray. True is the Banker, and true are His traders.
RECORD	para 4879	scu vxMjih gur hyiq Apwry ] (117-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach vana Njahi gur hayt apaaray. They purchase Truth, with infinite love for the Guru.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	scu ivhwJih scu kmwvih sco scu kmwvixAw ]4] (117-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach vihaajheh sach kamaaveh sacho sach kamaavani-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	They deal in Truth, and they practice Truth. They earn Truth, and only Truth. ||4||
RECORD	para 4881	ibnu rwsI ko vQu ikau pwey ] (117-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin raasee ko vath ki-o paa-ay. Without investment capital, how can anyone acquire merchandise?
RECORD	para 4882	mnmuK BUly lok sbwey ] (117-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh bhoolay lok sabaa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs have all gone astray.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	ibnu rwsI sB KwlI cly KwlI jwie duKu pwvixAw ]5] (117-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin raasee sabh khaalee chalay khaalee jaa-ay dukh paavni-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Without true wealth, everyone goes empty-handed; going empty-handed, they suffer in pain. ||5||
RECORD	para 4884	ieik scu vxMjih gur sbid ipAwry ] (117-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) ik sach vana Njahi gur sabad pi-aaray. Some deal in Truth, through love of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 4885	Awip qrih sgly kul qwry ] (117-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) aap tareh saglay kul taaray. They save themselves, and save all their ancestors as well.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Awey sy prvwxu hoey imil pRIqm suKu pwvixAw ]6] (117-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) aa-ay say parvaan ho-ay mil pareetam sukh paavni-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Very auspicious is the coming of those who meet their Beloved and find peace. ||6||
DEFINE	para 4887	AMqir vsqu mUVw bwhru Bwly ] (117-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) antar vasat moorhaa baahar bhaalay. Deep within the self is the secret, but the fool looks for it outside.
RECORD	para 4888	mnmuK AMDy iPrih byqwly ] (117-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh anDhay fireh baytaalay. The blind self-willed manmukhs wander around like demons;
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	ijQY vQu hovY iqQhu koie n pwvY mnmuK Brim BulwvixAw ]7] (117-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) jithai vath hovai tithhu ko-ay na paavai manmukh bharam bhulaavani-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	but where the secret is, there, they do not find it. The manmukhs are deluded by doubt. ||7||
RECORD	para 4890	Awpy dyvY sbid bulwey ] (117-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay dayvai sabad bulaa-ay. He Himself calls us, and bestows the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 4891	mhlI mhil shj suKu pwey ] (117-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) mahlee mahal sahj sukh paa-ay. The soul-bride finds intuitive peace and poise in the Mansion of the Lord's Presence.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwim imlY vifAweI Awpy suix suix iDAwvixAw ]8]13]14] (117-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam milai vadi-aa-ee aapay sun sun Dhi-aavani-aa. ||8||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, she obtains the glorious greatness of the Naam; she hears it again and again, and she meditates on it. ||8||
RECORD	para 4894	siqgur swcI isK suxweI ] (117-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur saachee sikh sunaa-ee. The True Guru has imparted the True Teachings.
REQUIRE	para 4896	hir cyqhu AMiq hoie sKweI ] (118-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) har chaytahu ant ho-ay sakhaa-ee. Think of the Lord, who shall be your Help and Support in the end.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	hir Agmu Agocru AnwQu AjonI siqgur kY Bwie pwvixAw ]1] (118-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) har agam agochar anaath ajonee satgur kai bhaa-ay paavni-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	The Lord is Inaccessible and Incomprehensible. He has no master, and He is not born. He is obtained through love of the True Guru. ||1||
DEFINE	para 4898	hau vwrI jIau vwrI Awpu invwrixAw ] (118-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree aap nivaarni-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who eliminate selfishness and conceit.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Awpu gvwey qw hir pwey hir isau shij smwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (118-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) aap gavaa-ay taa har paa-ay har si-o sahj samaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. They eradicate selfishness and conceit, and then find the Lord; they are intuitively immersed in the Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 4900	pUrib iliKAw su krmu kmwieAw ] (118-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) poorab likhi-aa so karam kamaa-i-aa. According to their pre-ordained destiny, they act out their karma.
DEFINE	para 4901	siqguru syiv sdw suKu pwieAw ] (118-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayv sadaa sukh paa-i-aa. Serving the True Guru, a lasting peace is found.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	ibnu Bwgw guru pweIAY nwhI sbdY myil imlwvixAw ]2] (118-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin bhaagaa gur paa-ee-ai naahee sabdai mayl milaavani-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	Without good fortune, the Guru is not found. Through the Word of the Shabad, they are united in the Lord's Union. ||2||
RECORD	para 4903	gurmuiK Ailpqu rhY sMswry ] (118-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh alipat rahai sansaaray. The Gurmukhs remain unaffected in the midst of the world.
DEFINE	para 4904	gur kY qkIAY nwim ADwry ] (118-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai takee-ai naam aDhaaray. The Guru is their cushion, and the Naam, the Name of the Lord, is their Support.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	gurmuiK joru kry ikAw iqs no Awpy Kip duKu pwvixAw ]3] (118-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh jor karay ki-aa tis no aapay khap dukh paavni-aa. ||3||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Who can oppress the Gurmukh? One who tries shall perish, writhing in pain. ||3||
RECORD	para 4906	mnmuiK AMDy suiD n kweI ] (118-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh anDhay suDh na kaa-ee. The blind self-willed manmukhs have no understanding at all.
DEFINE	para 4907	Awqm GwqI hY jgq ksweI ] (118-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) aatam ghaatee hai jagat kasaa-ee. They are the assassins of the self, and the butchers of the world.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	inMdw kir kir bhu Bwru auTwvY ibnu mjUrI Bwru phucwvixAw ]4] (118-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) nindaa kar kar baho bhaar uthaavai bin majooree bhaar pahuchaavani-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	By continually slandering others, they carry a terrible load, and they carry the loads of others for nothing. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4909	iehu jgu vwVI myrw pRBu mwlI ] (118-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) ih jag vaarhee mayraa parabh maalee. This world is a garden, and my Lord God is the Gardener.
DEFINE	para 4910	sdw smwly ko nwhI KwlI ] (118-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) sadaa samaalay ko naahee khaalee. He always takes care of it-nothing is exempt from His Care.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	jyhI vwsnw pwey qyhI vrqY vwsU vwsu jxwvixAw ]5] (118-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) jayhee vaasnaa paa-ay tayhee vartai vaasoo vaas janaavani-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	As is the fragrance which He bestows, so is the fragrant flower known. ||5||
DEFINE	para 4912	mnmuKu rogI hY sMswrw ] (118-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh rogee hai sansaaraa. The self-willed manmukhs are sick and diseased in the world.
RECORD	para 4913	suKdwqw ivsirAw Agm Apwrw ] (118-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) sukh-daata visri-aa agam apaaraa. They have forgotten the Giver of peace, the Unfathomable, the Infinite.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	duKIey iniq iPrih ibllwdy ibnu gur sWiq n pwvixAw ]6] (118-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) dukhee-ay nit fireh billaaday bin gur saa Nt na paavni-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	These miserable people wander endlessly, crying out in pain; without the Guru, they find no peace. ||6||
RECORD	para 4915	ijin kIqy soeI ibiD jwxY ] (118-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) jin keetay so-ee biDh jaanai. The One who created them, knows their condition.
WHEN	para 4916	Awip kry qw hukim pCwxY ] (118-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) aap karay taa hukam pachhaanai. And if He inspires them, then they realize the Hukam of His Command.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	jyhw AMdir pwey qyhw vrqY Awpy bwhir pwvixAw ]7] (118-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) jayhaa andar paa-ay tayhaa vartai aapay baahar paavni-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Whatever He places within them, that is what prevails, and so they outwardly appear. ||7||
RECORD	para 4918	iqsu bwJhu scy mY horu n koeI ] (118-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) tis baajhahu sachay mai hor na ko-ee. I know of no other except the True One.
RECORD	para 4919	ijsu lwie ley so inrmlu hoeI ] (118-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) jis laa-ay la-ay so nirmal ho-ee. Those, whom the Lord attaches to Himself, become pure.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwmu vsY Gt AMqir ijsu dyvY so pwvixAw ]8]14]15] (118-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam vasai ghat antar jis dayvai so paavni-aa. ||8||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, the Naam, the Name of the Lord, abides deep within the heart of those, unto whom He has given it. ||8||
RECORD	para 4922	AMimRq nwmu mMin vswey ] (118-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit naam man vasaa-ay. Enshrining the Ambrosial Naam, the Name of the Lord, in the mind,
DEFINE	para 4923	haumY myrw sBu duKu gvwey ] (118-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-umai mayraa sabh dukh gavaa-ay. all the pains of egotism, selfishness and conceit are eliminated.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	AMimRq bwxI sdw slwhy AMimRiq AMimRqu pwvixAw ]1] (118-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit banee sadaa salaahay amrit amrit paavni-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	By continually praising the Ambrosial Bani of the Word, I obtain the Amrit, the Ambrosial Nectar. ||1||
RECORD	para 4925	hau vwrI jIau vwrI AMimRq bwxI mMin vswvixAw ] (118-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree amrit banee man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who enshrine the Ambrosial Bani of the Word within their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	AMimRq bwxI mMin vswey AMimRqu nwmu iDAwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (118-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit banee man vasaa-ay amrit naam Dhi-aavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Enshrining the Ambrosial Bani in their minds, they meditate on the Ambrosial Naam. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 4927	AMimRqu bolY sdw muiK vYxI ] AMimRqu vyKY prKY sdw nYxI ] (118-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit bolai sadaa mukh vainee. amrit vaykhai parkhai sadaa nainee. Those who continually chant the Ambrosial Words of Nectar see and behold this Amrit everywhere with their eyes.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	AMimRq kQw khY sdw idnu rwqI Avrw AwiK sunwvixAw ]2] (118-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit kathaa kahai sadaa din raatee avraa aakh sunaavni-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	They continually chant the Ambrosial Sermon day and night; chanting it, they cause others to hear it. ||2||
RECORD	para 4929	AMimRq rMig rqw ilv lwey ] (118-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit rang rataa liv laa-ay. Imbued with the Ambrosial Love of the Lord, they lovingly focus their attention on Him.
RECORD	para 4930	AMimRqu gur prswdI pwey ] (118-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit gur parsaadee paa-ay. By Guru's Grace, they receive this Amrit.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	AMimRqu rsnw bolY idnu rwqI min qin AMimRqu pIAwvixAw ]3] (118-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit rasnaa bolai din raatee man tan amrit pee-aavni-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	They chant the Ambrosial Name with their tongues day and night; their minds and bodies are satisfied by this Amrit. ||3||
DEFINE	para 4932	so ikCu krY ju iciq n hoeI ] (118-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) so kichh karai jo chit na ho-ee. That which God does is beyond anyone's consciousness;
RECORD	para 4933	iqs dw hukmu myit n skY koeI ] (118-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) tis daa hukam mayt na sakai ko-ee. no one can erase the Hukam of His Command.
ALLOW	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	hukmy vrqY AMimRq bwxI hukmy AMimRqu pIAwvixAw ]4] (118-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) hukmay vartai amrit banee hukmay amrit pee-aavni-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	By His Command, the Ambrosial Bani of the Word prevails, and by His Command, we drink in the Amrit. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4935	Ajb kMm krqy hir kyry ] (118-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) ajab kamm kartay har kayray. The actions of the Creator Lord are marvellous and wonderful.
DEFINE	para 4936	iehu mnu BUlw jWdw Pyry ] (118-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) ih man bhoolaa jaa Ndaa fayray. This mind is deluded, and goes around the wheel of reincarnation.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	AMimRq bwxI isau icqu lwey AMimRq sbid vjwvixAw ]5] (118-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit banee si-o chit laa-ay amrit sabad vajaavani-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Those who focus their consciousness on the Ambrosial Bani of the Word, hear the vibrations of the Ambrosial Word of the Shabad. ||5||
RECORD	para 4939	Koty Kry quDu Awip aupwey ] (119-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) khotay kharay tuDh aap upaa-ay. You Yourself created the counterfeit and the genuine.
RECORD	para 4940	quDu Awpy prKy lok sbwey ] (119-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) tuDh aapay parkhay lok sabaa-ay. You Yourself appraise all people.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Kry priK KjwnY pwieih Koty Brim BulwvixAw ]6] (119-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) kharay parakh khajaanai paa-ihi khotay bharam bhulaavani-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	You appraise the true, and place them in Your Treasury; You consign the false to wander in delusion. ||6||
RECORD	para 4942	ikau kir vyKw ikau swlwhI ] (119-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) ki-o kar vaykhaa ki-o saalaahee. How can I behold You? How can I praise You?
RECORD	para 4943	gur prswdI sbid slwhI ] (119-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee sabad salaahee. By Guru's Grace, I praise You through the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	qyry Bwxy ivic AMimRqu vsY qUM BwxY AMimRqu pIAwvixAw ]7] (119-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) tayray bhaanay vich amrit vasai tooN bhaanai amrit pee-aavni-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	In Your Sweet Will, the Amrit is found; by Your Will, You inspire us to drink in this Amrit. ||7||
DEFINE	para 4945	AMimRq sbdu AMimRq hir bwxI ] (119-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit sabad amrit har banee. The Shabad is Amrit; the Lord's Bani is Amrit.
RECORD	para 4946	siqguir syivAY irdY smwxI ] (119-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvi-ai ridai samaanee. Serving the True Guru, it permeates the heart.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk AMimRq nwmu sdw suKdwqw pI AMimRqu sB BuK lih jwvixAw ]8]15]16] (119-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak amrit naam sadaa sukh-daata pee amrit sabh bhukh leh jaavani-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, the Ambrosial Naam is forever the Giver of peace; drinking in this Amrit, all hunger is satisfied. ||8||
RECORD	para 4949	AMimRqu vrsY shij suBwey ] (119-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit varsai sahj subhaa-ay. The Ambrosial Nectar rains down, softly and gently.
DEFINE	para 4950	gurmuiK ivrlw koeI jnu pwey ] (119-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlaa ko-ee jan paa-ay. How rare are those Gurmukhs who find it.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	AMimRqu pI sdw iqRpqwsy kir ikrpw iqRsnw buJwvixAw ]1] (119-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit pee sadaa tariptaasay kar kirpaa tarisnaa bujhaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Those who drink it in are satisfied forever. Showering His Mercy upon them, the Lord quenches their thirst. ||1||
DEFINE	para 4952	hau vwrI jIau vwrI gurmuiK AMimRqu pIAwvixAw ] (119-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree gurmukh amrit pee-aavni-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those Gurmukhs who drink in this Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rsnw rsu cwiK sdw rhY rMig rwqI shjy hir gux gwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (119-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) rasnaa ras chaakh sadaa rahai rang raatee sehjay har gun gaavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The tongue tastes the essence, and remains forever imbued with the Lord's Love, intuitively singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 4954	gur prswdI shju ko pwey ] (119-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee sahj ko paa-ay. By Guru's Grace, intuitive understanding is obtained;
DEFINE	para 4955	duibDw mwry ieksu isau ilv lwey ] (119-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) dubiDhaa maaray ikas si-o liv laa-ay. subduing the sense of duality, they are in love with the One.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	ndir kry qw hir gux gwvY ndrI sic smwvixAw ]2] (119-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) nadar karay taa har gun gaavai nadree sach samaavani-aa. ||2||
WHEN	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	When He bestows His Glance of Grace, then they sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord; by His Grace, they merge in Truth. ||2||
DEFINE	para 4957	sBnw aupir ndir pRB qyrI ] (119-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabhnaa upar nadar parabh tayree. Above all is Your Glance of Grace, O God.
DEFINE	para 4958	iksY QoVI iksY hY GxyrI ] (119-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) kisai thorhee kisai hai ghanayree. Upon some it is bestowed less, and upon others it is bestowed more.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	quJ qy bwhir ikCu n hovY gurmuiK soJI pwvixAw ]3] (119-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) tujh tay baahar kichh na hovai gurmukh sojhee paavni-aa. ||3||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Without You, nothing happens at all; the Gurmukhs understand this. ||3||
RECORD	para 4960	gurmuiK qqu hY bIcwrw ] (119-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh tat hai beechaaraa. The Gurmukhs contemplate the essence of reality;
DEFINE	para 4961	AMimRiq Bry qyry BMfwrw ] (119-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit bharay tayray bhandaaraa. Your Treasures are overflowing with Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	ibnu siqgur syvy koeI n pwvY gur ikrpw qy pwvixAw ]4] (119-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay ko-ee na paavai gur kirpaa tay paavni-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	Without serving the True Guru, no one obtains it. It is obtained only by Guru's Grace. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4963	siqguru syvY so jnu sohY ] (119-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvai so jan sohai. Those who serve the True Guru are beautiful.
RECORD	para 4964	AMimRq nwim AMqru mnu mohY ] (119-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit naam antar man mohai. The Ambrosial Naam, the Name of the Lord, entices their inner minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	AMimRiq mnu qnu bwxI rqw AMimRqu shij suxwvixAw ]5] (119-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit man tan banee rataa amrit sahj sunaavni-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Their minds and bodies are attuned to the Ambrosial Bani of the Word; this Ambrosial Nectar is intuitively heard. ||5||
DEFINE	para 4966	mnmuKu BUlw dUjY Bwie KuAwey ] (119-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh bhoolaa doojai bhaa-ay khu-aa-ay. The deluded, self-willed manmukhs are ruined through the love of duality.
RECORD	para 4967	nwmu n lyvY mrY ibKu Kwey ] (119-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) naam na layvai marai bikh khaa-ay. They do not chant the Naam, and they die, eating poison.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Anidnu sdw ivstw mih vwsw ibnu syvw jnmu gvwvixAw ]6] (119-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din sadaa vistaa meh vaasaa bin sayvaa janam gavaavni-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Night and day, they continually sit in manure. Without selfless service, their lives are wasted away. ||6||
RECORD	para 4969	AMimRqu pIvY ijs no Awip pIAwey ] (119-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) amrit peevai jis no aap pee-aa-ay. They alone drink in this Amrit, whom the Lord Himself inspires to do so.
RECORD	para 4970	gur prswdI shij ilv lwey ] (119-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee sahj liv laa-ay. By Guru's Grace, they intuitively enshrine love for the Lord.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	pUrn pUir rihAw sB Awpy gurmiq ndrI AwvixAw ]7] (119-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) pooran poor rahi-aa sabh aapay gurmat nadree aavani-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	The Perfect Lord is Himself perfectly pervading everywhere; through the Guru's Teachings, He is perceived. ||7||
DEFINE	para 4972	Awpy Awip inrMjnu soeI ] (119-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay aap niranjan so-ee. He Himself is the Immaculate Lord.
REQUIRE	para 4973	ijin isrjI iqin Awpy goeI ] (119-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) jin sirjee tin aapay go-ee. He who has created, shall Himself destroy.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwmu smwil sdw qUM shjy sic smwvixAw ]8]16]17] (119-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam samaal sadaa tooN sehjay sach samaavani-aa. ||8||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, remember the Naam forever, and you shall merge into the True One with intuitive ease. ||8||
DEFINE	para 4976	sy sic lwgy jo quDu Bwey ] (119-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) say sach laagay jo tuDh bhaa-ay. Those who please You are linked to the Truth.
RECORD	para 4977	sdw scu syvih shj suBwey ] (119-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) sadaa sach sayveh sahj subhaa-ay. They serve the True One forever, with intuitive ease.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	scY sbid scw swlwhI scY myil imlwvixAw ]1] (119-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachai sabad sachaa saalaahee sachai mayl milaavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Through the True Word of the Shabad, they praise the True One, and they merge in the merging of Truth. ||1||
DEFINE	para 4979	hau vwrI jIau vwrI scu swlwhixAw ] (119-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree sach salaahni-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who praise the True One.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	scu iDAwiein sy sic rwqy scy sic smwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (119-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach Dhi-aa-in say sach raatay sachay sach samaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Those who meditate on the True One are attuned to Truth; they are absorbed into the Truest of the True. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 4981	jh dyKw scu sBnI QweI ] (119-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) jah daykhaa sach sabhnee thaa-ee. The True One is everywhere, wherever I look.
RECORD	para 4982	gur prswdI mMin vsweI ] (119-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee man vasaa-ee. By Guru's Grace, I enshrine Him in my mind.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	qnu scw rsnw sic rwqI scu suix AwiK vKwnixAw ]2] (119-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) tan sachaa rasnaa sach raatee sach sun aakh vakhaanni-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	True are the bodies of those whose tongues are attuned to Truth. They hear the Truth, and speak it with their mouths. ||2||
RECORD	para 4985	mnsw mwir sic smwxI ] (120-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) mansaa maar sach samaanee. Subduing their desires, they merge with the True One;
RECORD	para 4986	iein min fITI sB Awvx jwxI ] (120-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) in man deethee sabh aavan jaanee. they see in their minds that everyone comes and goes in reincarnation.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	siqguru syvy sdw mnu inhclu inj Gir vwsw pwvixAw ]3] (120-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay sadaa man nihchal nij ghar vaasaa paavni-aa. ||3||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Serving the True Guru, they become stable forever, and they obtain their dwelling in the home of the self. ||3||
DEFINE	para 4988	gur kY sbid irdY idKwieAw ] (120-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad ridai dikhaa-i-aa. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Lord is seen within one's own heart.
RECORD	para 4989	mwieAw mohu sbid jlwieAw ] (120-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh sabad jalaa-i-aa. Through the Shabad, I have burned my emotional attachment to Maya.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	sco scw vyiK swlwhI gur sbdI scu pwvixAw ]4] (120-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) sacho sachaa vaykh saalaahee gur sabdee sach paavni-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	I gaze upon the Truest of the True, and I praise Him. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, I obtain the True One. ||4||
DEFINE	para 4991	jo sic rwqy iqn scI ilv lwgI ] (120-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) jo sach raatay tin sachee liv laagee. Those who are attuned to Truth are blessed with the Love of the True One.
DEFINE	para 4992	hir nwmu smwlih sy vfBwgI ] (120-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) har naam samaaleh say vadbhaagee. Those who praise the Lord's Name are very fortunate.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	scY sbid Awip imlwey sqsMgiq scu gux gwvixAw ]5] (120-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachai sabad aap milaa-ay satsangat sach gun gaavani-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Through the Word of His Shabad, the True One blends with Himself, those who join the True Congregation and sing the Glorious Praises of the True One. ||5||
WHEN	para 4994	lyKw pVIAY jy lyKy ivic hovY ] (120-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) laykhaa parhee-ai jay laykhay vich hovai. We could read the account of the Lord, if He were in any account.
DEFINE	para 4995	Ehu Agmu Agocru sbid suiD hovY ] (120-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) oh agam agochar sabad suDh hovai. He is Inaccessible and Incomprehensible; through the Shabad, understanding is obtained.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Anidnu sc sbid swlwhI horu koie n kImiq pwvixAw ]6] (120-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din sach sabad saalaahee hor ko-ay na keemat paavni-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	Night and day, praise the True Word of the Shabad. There is no other way to know His Worth. ||6||
RECORD	para 4997	piV piV Qwky sWiq n AweI ] (120-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) parh parh thaakay saa Nt na aa-ee. People read and recite until they grow weary, but they do not find peace.
RECORD	para 4998	iqRsnw jwly suiD n kweI ] (120-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) tarisnaa jaalay suDh na kaa-ee. Consumed by desire, they have no understanding at all.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	ibKu ibhwJih ibKu moh ipAwsy kUVu boil ibKu KwvixAw ]7] (120-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) bikh bihaajheh bikh moh pi-aasay koorh bol bikh khaavani-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	They purchase poison, and they are thirsty with their fascination for poison. Telling lies, they eat poison. ||7||
RECORD	para 5000	gur prswdI eyko jwxw ] (120-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee ayko jaanaa. By Guru's Grace, I know the One.
DEFINE	para 5001	dUjw mwir mnu sic smwxw ] (120-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) doojaa maar man sach samaanaa. Subduing my sense of duality, my mind is absorbed into the True One.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk eyko nwmu vrqY mn AMqir gur prswdI pwvixAw ]8]17]18] (120-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak ayko naam vartai man antar gur parsaadee paavni-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, the One Name is pervading deep within my mind; by Guru's Grace, I receive it. ||8||
DEFINE	para 5004	vrn rUp vrqih sB qyry ] (120-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) varan roop varteh sabh tayray. In all colors and forms, You are pervading.
DEFINE	para 5005	mir mir jMmih Pyr pvih Gxyry ] (120-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) mar mar jameh fayr paveh ghanayray. People die over and over again; they are re-born, and make their rounds on the wheel of reincarnation.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	qUM eyko inhclu Agm Apwrw gurmqI bUJ buJwvixAw ]1] (120-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) tooN ayko nihchal agam apaaraa gurmatee boojh bujhaavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	You alone are Eternal and Unchanging, Inaccessible and Infinite. Through the Guru's Teachings, understanding is imparted. ||1||
DEFINE	para 5007	hau vwrI jIau vwrI rwm nwmu mMin vswvixAw ] (120-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree raam naam man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who enshrine the Lord's Name in their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	iqsu rUpu n ryiKAw vrnu n koeI gurmqI Awip buJwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (120-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) tis roop na raykh-i-aa varan na ko-ee gurmatee aap bujhaavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The Lord has no form, features or color. Through the Guru's Teachings, He inspires us to understand Him. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 5009	sB eykw joiq jwxY jy koeI ] (120-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabh aykaa jot jaanai jay ko-ee. The One Light is all-pervading; only a few know this.
DEFINE	para 5010	siqguru syivAY prgtu hoeI ] (120-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvi-ai pargat ho-ee. Serving the True Guru, this is revealed.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	gupqu prgtu vrqY sB QweI joqI joiq imlwvixAw ]2] (120-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) gupat pargat vartai sabh thaa-ee jotee jot milaavani-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	In the hidden and in the obvious, He is pervading all places. Our light merges into the Light. ||2||
DEFINE	para 5012	iqsnw Agin jlY sMswrw ] (120-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) tisnaa agan jalai sansaaraa. The world is burning in the fire of desire,
RECORD	para 5013	loBu AiBmwnu bhuqu AhMkwrw ] (120-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) lobh abhimaan bahut aha Nkaaraa. in greed, arrogance and excessive ego.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	mir mir jnmY piq gvwey ApxI ibrQw jnmu gvwvixAw ]3] (120-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) mar mar janmai pat gavaa-ay apnee birthaa janam gavaavni-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	People die over and over again; they are re-born, and lose their honor. They waste away their lives in vain. ||3||
DEFINE	para 5015	gur kw sbdu ko ivrlw bUJY ] (120-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kaa sabad ko virlaa boojhai. Those who understand the Word of the Guru's Shabad are very rare.
RECORD	para 5016	Awpu mwry qw iqRBvxu sUJY ] (120-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) aap maaray taa taribhavan soojhai. Those who subdue their egotism, come to know the three worlds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	iPir Ehu mrY n mrxw hovY shjy sic smwvixAw ]4] (120-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) fir oh marai na marnaa hovai sehjay sach samaavani-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	Then, they die, never to die again. They are intuitively absorbed in the True One. ||4||
RECORD	para 5018	mwieAw mih iPir icqu n lwey ] (120-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa meh fir chit na laa-ay. They do not focus their consciousness on Maya again.
RECORD	para 5019	gur kY sbid sd rhY smwey ] (120-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad sad rahai samaa-ay. They remain absorbed forever in the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	scu slwhy sB Gt AMqir sco scu suhwvixAw ]5] (120-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach salaahay sabh ghat antar sacho sach suhaavani-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	They praise the True One, who is contained deep within all hearts. They are blessed and exalted by the Truest of the True. ||5||
DEFINE	para 5021	scu swlwhI sdw hjUry ] (120-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach saalaahee sadaa hajooray. Praise the True One, who is Ever-present.
DEFINE	para 5022	gur kY sbid rihAw BrpUry ] (120-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad rahi-aa bharpooray. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, He is pervading everywhere.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	gur prswdI scu ndrI AwvY scy hI suKu pwvixAw ]6] (120-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee sach nadree aavai sachay hee sukh paavni-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	By Guru's Grace, we come to behold the True One; from the True One, peace is obtained. ||6||
RECORD	para 5024	scu mn AMdir rihAw smwie ] (120-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach man andar rahi-aa samaa-ay. The True One permeates and pervades the mind within.
DEFINE	para 5025	sdw scu inhclu AwvY n jwie ] (120-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) sadaa sach nihchal aavai na jaa-ay. The True One is Eternal and Unchanging; He does not come and go in reincarnation.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	scy lwgY so mnu inrmlu gurmqI sic smwvixAw ]7] (120-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) sachay laagai so man nirmal gurmatee sach samaavani-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	Those who are attached to the True One are immaculate and pure. Through the Guru's Teachings, they merge in the True One. ||7||
RECORD	para 5027	scu swlwhI Avru n koeI ] (120-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach saalaahee avar na ko-ee. Praise the True One, and no other.
DEFINE	para 5028	ijqu syivAY sdw suKu hoeI ] (120-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) jit sayvi-ai sadaa sukh ho-ee. Serving Him, eternal peace is obtained.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwim rqy vIcwrI sco scu kmwvixAw ]8]18]19] (121-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay veechaaree sacho sach kamaavani-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam, reflect deeply on the Truth; they practice only Truth. ||8||
DEFINE	para 5032	inrml sbdu inrml hY bwxI ] (121-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal sabad nirmal hai banee. The Word of the Shabad is Immaculate and Pure; the Bani of the Word is Pure.
DEFINE	para 5033	inrml joiq sB mwih smwxI ] (121-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal jot sabh maahi samaanee. The Light which is pervading among all is Immaculate.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	inrml bwxI hir swlwhI jip hir inrmlu mYlu gvwvixAw ]1] (121-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal banee har saalaahee jap har nirmal mail gavaavni-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	So praise the Immaculate Word of the Lord's Bani; chanting the Immaculate Name of the Lord, all filth is washed away. ||1||
RECORD	para 5035	hau vwrI jIau vwrI suKdwqw mMin vswvixAw ] (121-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree sukh-daata man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who enshrine the Giver of peace within their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	hir inrmlu gur sbid slwhI sbdo suix iqsw imtwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (121-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) har nirmal gur sabad salaahee sabdo sun tisaa mitaavni-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Praise the Immaculate Lord, through the Word of the Guru's Shabad. Listen to the Shabad, and quench your thirst. ||1||Pause||
WHEN	para 5037	inrml nwmu visAw min Awey ] (121-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal naam vasi-aa man aa-ay. When the Immaculate Naam comes to dwell in the mind,
RECORD	para 5038	mnu qnu inrmlu mwieAw mohu gvwey ] (121-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) man tan nirmal maa-i-aa moh gavaa-ay. the mind and body become Immaculate, and emotional attachment to Maya departs.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	inrml gux gwvY inq swcy ky inrml nwdu vjwvixAw ]2] (121-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal gun gaavai nit saachay kay nirmal naad vajaavani-aa. ||2||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	Sing the Glorious Praises of the Immaculate True Lord forever, and the Immaculate Sound-current of the Naad shall vibrate within. ||2||
DEFINE	para 5040	inrml AMimRqu gur qy pwieAw ] (121-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal amrit gur tay paa-i-aa. The Immaculate Ambrosial Nectar is obtained from the Guru.
DEFINE	para 5041	ivchu Awpu muAw iqQY mohu n mwieAw ] (121-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) vichahu aap mu-aa tithai moh na maa-i-aa. When selfishness and conceit are eradicated from within, then there is no attachment to Maya.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	inrml igAwnu iDAwnu Aiq inrmlu inrml bwxI mMin vswvixAw ]3] (121-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal gi-aan Dhi-aan at nirmal nirmal banee man vasaavani-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Immaculate is the spiritual wisdom, and utterly immaculate is the meditation, of those whose minds are filled with the Immaculate Bani of the Word. ||3||
RECORD	para 5043	jo inrmlu syvy su inrmlu hovY ] (121-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) jo nirmal sayvay so nirmal hovai. One who serves the Immaculate Lord becomes immaculate.
DEFINE	para 5044	haumY mYlu gur sbdy DovY ] (121-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-umai mail gur sabday Dhovai. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the filth of egotism is washed away.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	inrml vwjY Anhd Duin bwxI dir scY soBw pwvixAw ]4] (121-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal vaajai anhad Dhun banee dar sachai sobhaa paavni-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	The Immaculate Bani and the Unstruck Melody of the Sound-current vibrate, and in the True Court, honor is obtained. ||4||
RECORD	para 5046	inrml qy sB inrml hovY ] (121-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal tay sabh nirmal hovai. Through the Immaculate Lord, all become immaculate.
DEFINE	para 5047	inrmlu mnUAw hir sbid provY ] (121-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal manoo-aa har sabad parovai. Immaculate is the mind which weaves the Word of the Lord's Shabad into itself.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	inrml nwim lgy bfBwgI inrmlu nwim suhwvixAw ]5] (121-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal naam lagay badbhaagee nirmal naam suhaavani-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Blessed and very fortunate are those who are committed to the Immaculate Name; through the Immaculate Name, they are blessed and beautified. ||5||
DEFINE	para 5049	so inrmlu jo sbdy sohY ] (121-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) so nirmal jo sabday sohai. Immaculate is the one who is adorned with the Shabad.
RECORD	para 5050	inrml nwim mnu qnu mohY ] (121-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal naam man tan mohai. The Immaculate Naam, the Name of the Lord, entices the mind and body.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	sic nwim mlu kdy n lwgY muKu aUjlu scu krwvixAw ]6] (121-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) sach naam mal kaday na laagai mukh oojal sach karaavani-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	No filth ever attaches itself to the True Name; one's face is made radiant by the True One. ||6||
DEFINE	para 5052	mnu mYlw hY dUjY Bwie ] (121-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) man mailaa hai doojai bhaa-ay. The mind is polluted by the love of duality.
DEFINE	para 5053	mYlw caukw mYlY Qwie ] (121-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) mailaa cha-ukaa mailai thaa-ay. Filthy is that kitchen, and filthy is that dwelling;
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	mYlw Kwie iPir mYlu vDwey mnmuK mYlu duKu pwvixAw ]7] (121-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) mailaa khaa-ay fir mail vaDhaa-ay manmukh mail dukh paavni-aa. ||7||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	eating filth, the self-willed manmukhs become even more filthy. Because of their filth, they suffer in pain. ||7||
DEFINE	para 5055	mYly inrml siB hukim sbwey ] (121-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) mailay nirmal sabh hukam sabaa-ay. The filthy, and the immaculate as well, are all subject to the Hukam of God's Command.
DEFINE	para 5056	sy inrml jo hir swcy Bwey ] (121-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) say nirmal jo har saachay bhaa-ay. They alone are immaculate, who are pleasing to the True Lord.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwmu vsY mn AMqir gurmuiK mYlu cukwvixAw ]8]19]20] (121-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam vasai man antar gurmukh mail chukaavani-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, the Naam abides deep within the minds of the Gurmukhs, who are cleansed of all their filth. ||8||
DEFINE	para 5059	goivMdu aUjlu aUjl hMsw ] (121-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) govind oojal oojal hansaa. The Lord of the Universe is radiant, and radiant are His soul-swans.
DEFINE	para 5060	mnu bwxI inrml myrI mnsw ] (121-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) man banee nirmal mayree mansaa. Their minds and their speech are immaculate; they are my hope and ideal.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	min aUjl sdw muK sohih Aiq aUjl nwmu iDAwvixAw ]1] (121-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) man oojal sadaa mukh soheh at oojal naam Dhi-aavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Their minds are radiant, and their faces are always beautiful; they meditate on the most radiant Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||1||
DEFINE	para 5062	hau vwrI jIau vwrI goibMd gux gwvixAw ] (121-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree gobind gun gaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord of the Universe.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	goibdu goibdu khY idn rwqI goibd gux sbid suxwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (121-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) gobid gobid kahai din raatee gobid gun sabad sunaavni-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. So chant Gobind, Gobind, the Lord of the Universe, day and night; sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord Gobind, through the Word of His Shabad. ||1||Pause||
