RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, one who receives the greatness of the Naam night and day, constantly sings His Glorious Praises. ||8||
DEFINE	para 5306	aUqm jnmu suQwin hY vwsw ] (127-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) ootam janam suthaan hai vaasaa. Sublime is their birth, and the place where they dwell.
RECORD	para 5307	siqguru syvih Gr mwih audwsw ] (127-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayveh ghar maahi udaasaa. Those who serve the True Guru remain detached in the home of their own being.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	hir rMig rhih sdw rMig rwqy hir ris mnu iqRpqwvixAw ]1] (127-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) har rang raheh sadaa rang raatay har ras man tariptaavni-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	They abide in the Lord's Love, and constantly imbued with His Love, their minds are satisfied and fulfilled with the Lord's Essence. ||1||
RECORD	para 5309	hau vwrI jIau vwrI piV buiJ mMin vswvixAw ] (127-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree parh bujh man vasaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who read of the Lord, who understand and enshrine Him within their minds.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	gurmuiK pVih hir nwmu slwhih dir scY soBw pwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (127-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh parheh har naam salaaheh dar sachai sobhaa paavni-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The Gurmukhs read and praise the Lord's Name; they are honored in the True Court. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 5311	AlK AByau hir rihAw smwey ] (127-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) alakh abhay-o har rahi-aa samaa-ay. The Unseen and Inscrutable Lord is permeating and pervading everywhere.
RECORD	para 5312	aupwie n ikqI pwieAw jwey ] (127-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) upaa-ay na kitee paa-i-aa jaa-ay. He cannot be obtained by any effort.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	ikrpw kry qw siqguru BytY ndrI myil imlwvixAw ]2] (127-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) kirpaa karay taa satgur bhaytai nadree mayl milaavani-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	If the Lord grants His Grace, then we come to meet the True Guru. By His Kindness, we are united in His Union. ||2||
RECORD	para 5314	dUjY Bwie pVY nhI bUJY ] (127-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay parhai nahee boojhai. One who reads, while attached to duality, does not understand.
RECORD	para 5315	iqRibiD mwieAw kwrix lUJY ] (127-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) taribaDh maa-i-aa kaaran loojhai. He yearns for the three-phased Maya.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	iqRibiD bMDn qUtih gur sbdI gur sbdI mukiq krwvixAw ]3] (127-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) taribaDh banDhan tooteh gur sabdee gur sabdee mukat karaavani-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	The bonds of the three-phased Maya are broken by the Word of the Guru's Shabad. Through the Guru's Shabad, liberation is achieved. ||3||
RECORD	para 5317	iehu mnu cMclu vis n AwvY ] (127-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) ih man chanchal vas na aavai. This unstable mind cannot be held steady.
RECORD	para 5318	duibDw lwgY dh idis DwvY ] (127-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) dubiDhaa laagai dah dis Dhaavai. Attached to duality, it wanders in the ten directions.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	ibKu kw kIVw ibKu mih rwqw ibKu hI mwih pcwvixAw ]4] (127-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) bikh kaa keerhaa bikh meh raataa bikh hee maahi pachaavani-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	It is a poisonous worm, drenched with poison, and in poison it rots away. ||4||
RECORD	para 5320	hau hau kry qY Awpu jxwey ] (127-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o ha-o karay tai aap janaa-ay. Practicing egotism and selfishness, they try to impress others by showing off.
RECORD	para 5321	bhu krm krY ikCu Qwie n pwey ] (127-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) baho karam karai kichh thaa-ay na paa-ay. They perform all sorts of rituals, but they gain no acceptance.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	quJ qy bwhir ikCU n hovY bKsy sbid suhwvixAw ]5] (127-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) tujh tay baahar kichhoo na hovai bakhsay sabad suhaavani-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Without You, Lord, nothing happens at all. You forgive those who are adorned with the Word of Your Shabad. ||5||
DEFINE	para 5323	aupjY pcY hir bUJY nwhI ] (127-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) upjai pachai har boojhai naahee. They are born, and they die, but they do not understand the Lord.
RECORD	para 5324	Anidnu dUjY Bwie iPrwhI ] (127-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din doojai bhaa-ay firaa-ee. Night and day, they wander, in love with duality.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	mnmuK jnmu gieAw hY ibrQw AMiq gieAw pCuqwvixAw ]6] (127-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh janam ga-i-aa hai birthaa ant ga-i-aa pachhutaavani-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	The lives of the self-willed manmukhs are useless; in the end, they die, regretting and repenting. ||6||
DEFINE	para 5326	ipru prdyis isgwru bxwey ] (127-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) pir pardays sigaar banaa-ay. The Husband is away, and the wife is getting dressed up.
DEFINE	para 5327	mnmuK AMDu AYsy krm kmwey ] (127-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh anDh aisay karam kamaa-ay. This is what the blind, self-willed manmukhs are doing.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	hliq n soBw pliq n FoeI ibrQw jnmu gvwvixAw ]7] (127-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) halat na sobhaa palat na dho-ee birthaa janam gavaavni-aa. ||7||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	They are not honored in this world, and they shall find no shelter in the world hereafter. They are wasting their lives in vain. ||7||
DEFINE	para 5329	hir kw nwmu iknY ivrlY jwqw ] (127-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) har kaa naam kinai virlai jaataa. How rare are those who know the Name of the Lord!
DEFINE	para 5330	pUry gur kY sbid pCwqw ] (127-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) pooray gur kai sabad pachhaataa. Through the Shabad, the Word of the Perfect Guru, the Lord is realized.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	Anidnu Bgiq kry idnu rwqI shjy hI suKu pwvixAw ]8] (127-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) an-din bhagat karay din raatee sehjay hee sukh paavni-aa. ||8||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	Night and day, they perform the Lord's devotional service; day and night, they find intuitive peace. ||8||
DEFINE	para 5332	sB mih vrqY eyko soeI ] (127-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) sabh meh vartai ayko so-ee. That One Lord is pervading in all.
RECORD	para 5333	gurmuiK ivrlw bUJY koeI ] (127-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlaa boojhai ko-ee. Only a few, as Gurmukh, understand this.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v9	nwnk nwim rqy jn sohih kir ikrpw Awip imlwvixAw ]9]29]30] (127-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay jan soheh kar kirpaa aap milaavani-aa. ||9||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v9	O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam are beautiful. Granting His Grace, God unites them with Himself. ||9||
DEFINE	para 5337	mnmuK pVih pMifq khwvih ] (128-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh parheh pandit kahaaveh. The self-willed manmukhs read and recite; they are called Pandits-spiritual scholars.
DEFINE	para 5338	dUjY Bwie mhw duKu pwvih ] (128-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay mahaa dukh paavahi. But they are in love with duality, and they suffer in terrible pain.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	ibiKAw mwqy ikCu sUJY nwhI iPir iPir jUnI AwvixAw ]1] (128-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) bikhi-aa maatay kichh soojhai naahee fir fir joonee aavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Intoxicated with vice, they understand nothing at all. They are reincarnated, over and over again. ||1||
DEFINE	para 5340	hau vwrI jIau vwrI haumY mwir imlwvixAw ] (128-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree ha-umai maar milaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who subdue their ego, and unite with the Lord.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	gur syvw qy hir min visAw hir rsu shij pIAwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (128-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur sayvaa tay har man vasi-aa har ras sahj pee-aavni-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. They serve the Guru, and the Lord dwells within their minds; they intuitively drink in the sublime essence of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 5342	vydu pVih hir rsu nhI AwieAw ] (128-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) vayd parheh har ras nahee aa-i-aa. The Pandits read the Vedas, but they do not obtain the Lord's essence.
RECORD	para 5343	vwdu vKwxih mohy mwieAw ] (128-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) vaad vakaaneh mohay maa-i-aa. Intoxicated with Maya, they argue and debate.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	AigAwnmqI sdw AMiDAwrw gurmuiK bUiJ hir gwvixAw ]2] (128-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) agi-aanmatee sadaa anDhi-aaraa gurmukh boojh har gaavani-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	The foolish intellectuals are forever in spiritual darkness. The Gurmukhs understand, and sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||2||
DEFINE	para 5345	AkQo kQIAY sbid suhwvY ] (128-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) aktho kathee-ai sabad suhaavai. The Indescribable is described only through the beauteous Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 5346	gurmqI min sco BwvY ] (128-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmatee man sacho bhaavai. Through the Guru's Teachings, the Truth becomes pleasing to the mind.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	sco scu rvih idnu rwqI iehu mnu sic rMgwvixAw ]3] (128-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) sacho sach raveh din raatee ih man sach rangaavin-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Those who speak of the truest of the true, day and night-their minds are imbued with the Truth. ||3||
DEFINE	para 5348	jo sic rqy iqn sco BwvY ] (128-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) jo sach ratay tin sacho bhaavai. Those who are attuned to Truth, love the Truth.
FORBID	para 5349	Awpy dyie n pCoqwvY ] (128-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) aapay day-ay na pachhotaavai. The Lord Himself bestows this gift; He shall not take it back.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	gur kY sbid sdw scu jwqw imil scy suKu pwvixAw ]4] (128-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad sadaa sach jaataa mil sachay sukh paavni-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the True Lord is known forever; meeting the True One, peace is found. ||4||
RECORD	para 5351	kUVu kusqu iqnw mYlu n lwgY ] gur prswdI Anidnu jwgY ] (128-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) koorh kusat tinaa mail na laagai. gur parsaadee an-din jaagai. The filth of fraud and falsehood does not stick to those who, by Guru's Grace, remain awake and aware, night and day.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	inrml nwmu vsY Gt BIqir joqI joiq imlwvixAw ]5] (128-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal naam vasai ghat bheetar jotee jot milaavani-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	The Immaculate Naam, the Name of the Lord, abides deep within their hearts; their light merges into the Light. ||5||
RECORD	para 5353	qRY gux pVih hir qqu n jwxih ] (128-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) tarai gun parheh har tat na jaaneh. They read about the three qualities, but they do not know the essential reality of the Lord.
RECORD	para 5354	mUlhu Buly gur sbdu n pCwxih ] (128-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) moolhu bhulay gur sabad na pachhaaneh. They forget the Primal Lord, the Source of all, and they do not recognize the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	moh ibAwpy ikCu sUJY nwhI gur sbdI hir pwvixAw ]6] (128-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) moh bi-aapay kichh soojhai naahee gur sabdee har paavni-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	They are engrossed in emotional attachment; they do not understand anything at all. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Lord is found. ||6||
DEFINE	para 5356	vydu pukwrY iqRibiD mwieAw ] (128-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) vayd pukaarai taribaDh maa-i-aa. The Vedas proclaim that Maya is of three qualities.
RECORD	para 5357	mnmuK n bUJih dUjY BwieAw ] (128-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh na boojheh doojai bhaa-i-aa. The self-willed manmukhs, in love with duality, do not understand.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	qRY gux pVih hir eyku n jwxih ibnu bUJy duKu pwvixAw ]7] (128-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) tarai gun parheh har ayk na jaaneh bin boojhay dukh paavni-aa. ||7||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	They read of the three qualities, but they do not know the One Lord. Without understanding, they obtain only pain and suffering. ||7||
WHEN	para 5359	jw iqsu BwvY qw Awip imlwey ] (128-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) jaa tis bhaavai taa aap milaa-ay. When it pleases the Lord, He unites us with Himself.
DEFINE	para 5360	gur sbdI shsw dUKu cukwey ] (128-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur sabdee sahsaa dookh chukaa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, skepticism and suffering are dispelled.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwvY kI scI vifAweI nwmo mMin suKu pwvixAw ]8]30]31] (128-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naavai kee sachee vadi-aa-ee naamo man sukh paavni-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, True is the Greatness of the Name. Believing in the Name, peace is obtained. ||8||
DEFINE	para 5363	inrguxu srguxu Awpy soeI ] (128-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirgun sargun aapay so-ee. The Lord Himself is Unmanifest and Unrelated; He is Manifest and Related as well.
DEFINE	para 5364	qqu pCwxY so pMifqu hoeI ] (128-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) tat pachhaanai so pandit ho-ee. Those who recognize this essential reality are the true Pandits, the spiritual scholars.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	Awip qrY sgly kul qwrY hir nwmu mMin vswvixAw ]1] (128-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) aap tarai saglay kul taarai har naam man vasaavani-aa. ||1||
WHEN	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	They save themselves, and save all their families and ancestors as well, when they enshrine the Lord's Name in the mind. ||1||
RECORD	para 5366	hau vwrI jIau vwrI hir rsu ciK swdu pwvixAw ] (128-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree har ras chakh saad paavni-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who taste the essence of the Lord, and savor its taste.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	hir rsu cwKih sy jn inrml inrml nwmu iDAwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (128-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) har ras chaakhahi say jan nirmal nirmal naam Dhi-aavani-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Those who taste this essence of the Lord are the pure, immaculate beings. They meditate on the Immaculate Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 5368	so inhkrmI jo sbdu bIcwry ] (128-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) so nihkarmee jo sabad beechaaray. Those who reflect upon the Shabad are beyond karma.
UPHOLD	para 5369	AMqir qqu igAwin haumY mwry ] (128-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) antar tat gi-aan ha-umai maaray. They subdue their ego, and find the essence of wisdom, deep within their being.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	nwmu pdwrQu nau iniD pwey qRY gux myit smwvixAw ]2] (128-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) naam padaarath na-o niDh paa-ay tarai gun mayt samaavani-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	They obtain the nine treasures of the wealth of the Naam. Rising above the three qualities, they merge into the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 5371	haumY krY inhkrmI n hovY ] (128-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-umai karai nihkarmee na hovai. Those who act in ego do not go beyond karma.
DEFINE	para 5372	gur prswdI haumY KovY ] (128-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee ha-umai khovai. It is only by Guru's Grace that one is rid of ego.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	AMqir ibbyku sdw Awpu vIcwry gur sbdI gux gwvixAw ]3] (128-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) antar bibayk sadaa aap veechaaray gur sabdee gun gaavani-aa. ||3||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v3	Those who have discriminating minds, continually examine their own selves. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, they sing the Lord's Glorious Praises. ||3||
RECORD	para 5374	hir sru swgru inrmlu soeI ] sMq cugih inq gurmuiK hoeI ] (128-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) har sar saagar nirmal so-ee. sant chugeh nit gurmukh ho-ee. The Lord is the most pure and sublime Ocean. The Saintly Gurmukhs continually peck at the Naam, like swans pecking at pearls in the ocean.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	iesnwnu krih sdw idnu rwqI haumY mYlu cukwvixAw ]4] (128-18, mwJ, mÚ 3) isnaan karahi sadaa din raatee ha-umai mail chukaavani-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v4	They bathe in it continually, day and night, and the filth of ego is washed away. ||4||
RECORD	para 5376	inrml hMsw pRym ipAwir ] hir sir vsY haumY mwir ] (128-19, mwJ, mÚ 3) nirmal hansaa paraym pi-aar. har sar vasai ha-umai maar. The pure swans, with love and affection, dwell in the Ocean of the Lord, and subdue their ego.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Aihinis pRIiq sbid swcY hir sir vwsw pwvixAw ]5] (129-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) ahinis pareet sabad saachai har sar vaasaa paavni-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v5	Day and night, they are in love with the True Word of the Shabad. They obtain their home in the Ocean of the Lord. ||5||
REQUIRE	para 5379	mnmuKu sdw bgu mYlw haumY mlu lweI ] (129-1, mwJ, mÚ 3) manmukh sadaa bag mailaa ha-umai mal laa-ee. The self-willed manmukhs shall always be filthy cranes, smeared with the filth of ego.
ALLOW	para 5380	iesnwnu krY pru mYlu n jweI ] (129-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) isnaan karai par mail na jaa-ee. They may bathe, but their filth is not removed.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	jIvqu mrY gur sbdu bIcwrY haumY mYlu cukwvixAw ]6] (129-2, mwJ, mÚ 3) jeevat marai gur sabad beechaarai ha-umai mail chukaavani-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v6	One who dies while yet alive, and contemplates the Word of the Guru's Shabad, is rid of this filth of ego. ||6||
DEFINE	para 5382	rqnu pdwrQu Gr qy pwieAw ] (129-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) ratan padaarath ghar tay paa-i-aa. The Priceless Jewel is found, in the home of one's own being,
WHEN	para 5383	pUrY siqguir sbdu suxwieAw ] (129-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) poorai satgur sabad sunaa-i-aa. when one listens to the Shabad, the Word of the Perfect True Guru.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	gur prswid imitAw AMiDAwrw Git cwnxu Awpu pCwnixAw ]7] (129-3, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaad miti-aa anDhi-aaraa ghat chaanan aap pachhaanni-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v7	By Guru's Grace, the darkness of spiritual ignorance is dispelled; I have come to recognize the Divine Light within my own heart. ||7||
RECORD	para 5385	Awip aupwey qY Awpy vyKY ] (129-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) aap upaa-ay tai aapay vaykhai. The Lord Himself creates, and He Himself beholds.
RECORD	para 5386	siqguru syvY so jnu lyKY ] (129-4, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur sayvai so jan laykhai. Serving the True Guru, one becomes acceptable.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	nwnk nwmu vsY Gt AMqir gur ikrpw qy pwvixAw ]8]31]32] (129-5, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak naam vasai ghat antar gur kirpaa tay paavni-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v8	O Nanak, the Naam dwells deep within the heart; by Guru's Grace, it is obtained. ||8||
DEFINE	para 5389	mwieAw mohu jgqu sbwieAw ] (129-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh jagat sabaa-i-aa. The whole world is engrossed in emotional attachment to Maya.
DEFINE	para 5390	qRY gux dIsih mohy mwieAw ] (129-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) tarai gun deeseh mohay maa-i-aa. Those who are controlled by the three qualities are attached to Maya.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	gur prswdI ko ivrlw bUJY cauQY pid ilv lwvixAw ]1] (129-6, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee ko virlaa boojhai cha-uthai pad liv laavani-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	By Guru's Grace, a few come to understand; they center their consciousness in the fourth state. ||1||
RECORD	para 5392	hau vwrI jIau vwrI mwieAw mohu sbid jlwvixAw ] (129-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) ha-o vaaree jee-o vaaree maa-i-aa moh sabad jalaavani-aa. I am a sacrifice, my soul is a sacrifice, to those who burn away their emotional attachment to Maya, through the Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	mwieAw mohu jlwey so hir isau icqu lwey hir dir mhlI soBw pwvixAw ]1] rhwau ] (129-7, mwJ, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh jalaa-ay so har si-o chit laa-ay har dar mahlee sobhaa paavni-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Those who burn away this attachment to Maya, and focus their consciousness on the Lord are honored in the True Court, and the Mansion of the Lord's Presence. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 5394	dyvI dyvw mUlu hY mwieAw ] (129-8, mwJ, mÚ 3) dayvee dayvaa mool hai maa-i-aa. The source, the root, of the gods and goddesses is Maya.
RECORD	para 5395	isMimRiq swsq ijMin aupwieAw ] (129-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) simrit saasat jinn upaa-i-aa. For them, the Simritees and the Shaastras were composed.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	kwmu k®oDu psirAw sMswry Awie jwie duKu pwvixAw ]2] (129-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) kaam kroDh pasri-aa sansaaray aa-ay jaa-ay dukh paavni-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 3 v2	Sexual desire and anger are diffused throughout the universe. Coming and going, people suffer in pain. ||2||
UPHOLD	para 5397	iqsu ivic igAwn rqnu ieku pwieAw ] (129-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) tis vich gi-aan ratan ik paa-i-aa. The jewel of spiritual wisdom was placed within the universe.
DEFINE	para 5398	gur prswdI mMin vswieAw ] (129-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee man vasaa-i-aa. By Guru's Grace, it is enshrined within the mind.
