RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 v1	kauxu su igrhI kauxu audwsI kauxu su kImiq pwey jIau ]1] (131-3, mwJ, mÚ 5) ka-un so girhee ka-un udaasee ka-un so keemat paa-ay jee-o. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 v1	Who is a house-holder, and who is a renunciate? Who can estimate the Lord's Value? ||1||
DEFINE	para 5474	ikin ibiD bwDw ikin ibiD CUtw ] (131-4, mwJ, mÚ 5) kin biDh baaDhaa kin biDh chhootaa. How is one bound, and how is one freed of his bonds?
RECORD	para 5475	ikin ibiD Awvxu jwvxu qUtw ] (131-4, mwJ, mÚ 5) kin biDh aavan jaavan tootaa. How can one escape from the cycle of coming and going in reincarnation?
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 v2	kaux krm kaux inhkrmw kauxu su khY khwey jIau ]2] (131-4, mwJ, mÚ 5) ka-un karam ka-un nihkarmaa ka-un so kahai kahaa-ay jee-o. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 v2	Who is subject to karma, and who is beyond karma? Who chants the Name, and inspires others to chant it? ||2||
DEFINE	para 5477	kauxu su suKIAw kauxu su duKIAw ] (131-5, mwJ, mÚ 5) ka-un so sukhee-aa ka-un so dukhee-aa. Who is happy, and who is sad?
RECORD	para 5478	kauxu su snmuKu kauxu vymuKIAw ] (131-5, mwJ, mÚ 5) ka-un so sanmukh ka-un vaymukhee-aa. Who, as sunmukh, turns toward the Guru, and who, as vaymukh, turns away from the Guru?
