RECORD	para 5775	AKI dyKY ijhvw bolY kMnI suriq smwie ] (138-9, mwJ, mÚ 1) akhee daykhai jihvaa bolai kannee surat samaa-ay. With their eyes, they see, and with their tongues, they speak; with their ears, they bring the mind to awareness.
DEFINE	para 5776	pYrI clY hQI krxw idqw pYnY Kwie ] (138-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) pairee chalai hathee karnaa ditaa painai khaa-ay. With their feet, they walk, and with their hands, they work; they wear and eat whatever is given.
RECORD	para 5777	ijin ric ricAw iqsih n jwxY AMDw AMDu kmwie ] (138-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) jin rach rachi-aa tiseh na jaanai anDhaa anDh kamaa-ay. They do not know the One who created the Creation. The blind fools do their dark deeds.
WHEN	para 5778	jw BjY qw TIkru hovY GwVq GVI n jwie ] (138-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa bhajai taa theekar hovai ghaarhat gharhee na jaa-ay. When the pitcher of the body breaks and shatters into pieces, it cannot be re-created again.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nwnk gur ibnu nwih piq piq ivxu pwir n pwie ]1] (138-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak gur bin naahi pat pat vin paar na paa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	O Nanak, without the Guru, there is no honor; without honor, no one is carried across. ||1||
RECORD	para 5780	mÚ 2 ] (138-12) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 5781	dyNdy Qwvhu idqw cMgw mnmuiK AYsw jwxIAY ] (138-12, mwJ, mÚ 2) day Nday thaavhu ditaa changa manmukh aisaa jaanee-ai. They prefer the gift, instead of the Giver; such is the way of the self-willed manmukhs.
RECORD	para 5782	suriq miq cqurweI qw kI ikAw kir AwiK vKwxIAY ] (138-12, mwJ, mÚ 2) surat mat chaturaa-ee taa kee ki-aa kar aakh vakhaanee-ai. What can anyone say about their intelligence, their understanding or their cleverness?
RECORD	para 5783	AMqir bih kY krm kmwvY so chu kuMfI jwxIAY ] (138-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) antar bahi kai karam kamaavai so chahu kundee jaanee-ai. The deeds which one commits, while sitting in one's own home, are known far and wide, in the four directions.
UPHOLD	para 5784	jo Drmu kmwvY iqsu Drm nwau hovY pwip kmwxY pwpI jwxIAY ] (138-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) jo Dharam kamaavai tis Dharam naa-o hovai paap kamaanai paapee jaanee-ai. One who lives righteously is known as righteous; one who commits sins is known as a sinner.
RECORD	para 5785	qUM Awpy Kyl krih siB krqy ikAw dUjw AwiK vKwxIAY ] (138-14, mwJ, mÚ 2) tooN aapay khayl karahi sabh kartay ki-aa doojaa aakh vakhaanee-ai. You Yourself enact the entire play, O Creator. Why should we speak of any other?
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwnk gurmuiK ndrI AwieAw hir ieko suGVu sujwxIAY ]2] (138-15, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak gurmukh nadree aa-i-aa har iko sugharh sujaanee-ai. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	O Nanak, the Lord alone is Perfect and All-knowing; He is revealed to the Gurmukh. ||2||
RECORD	para 5788	pauVI ] (138-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 5789	quDu Awpy jgqu aupwie kY quDu Awpy DMDY lwieAw ] (138-16, mwJ, mÚ 2) tuDh aapay jagat upaa-ay kai tuDh aapay DhanDhai laa-i-aa. You Yourself created the world, and You Yourself put it to work.
RECORD	para 5790	moh TgaulI pwie kY quDu Awphu jgqu KuAwieAw ] (138-17, mwJ, mÚ 2) moh thag-ulee paa-ay kai tuDh aaphu jagat khu-aa-i-aa. Administering the drug of emotional attachment, You Yourself have led the world astray.
DEFINE	para 5791	iqsnw AMdir Agin hY nh iqpqY BuKw iqhwieAw ] (138-17, mwJ, mÚ 2) tisnaa andar agan hai nah tiptai bhukhaa tihaa-i-aa. The fire of desire is deep within; unsatisfied, people remain hungry and thirsty.
DEFINE	para 5792	shsw iehu sMswru hY mir jMmY AwieAw jwieAw ] (138-18, mwJ, mÚ 2) sahsaa ih sansaar hai mar jammai aa-i-aa jaa-i-aa. This world is an illusion; it dies and it is re-born-it comes and it goes in reincarnation.
RECORD	para 5793	ibnu siqgur mohu n quteI siB Qky krm kmwieAw ] (138-18, mwJ, mÚ 2) bin satgur moh na tut-ee sabh thakay karam kamaa-i-aa. Without the True Guru, emotional attachment is not broken. All have grown weary of performing empty rituals.
RECORD	para 5794	gurmqI nwmu iDAweIAY suiK rjw jw quDu BwieAw ] (138-19, mwJ, mÚ 2) gurmatee naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai sukh rajaa jaa tuDh bhaa-i-aa. Those who follow the Guru's Teachings meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord. Filled with a joyful peace, they surrender to Your Will.
DEFINE	para 5795	kulu auDwry Awpxw DMnu jxydI mwieAw ] (138-19, mwJ, mÚ 2) kul uDhaaray aapnaa Dhan janaydee maa-i-aa. They save their families and ancestors; blessed are the mothers who gave birth to them.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	soBw suriq suhwvxI ijin hir syqI icqu lwieAw ]2] (139-1, mwJ, mÚ 2) sobhaa surat suhaavanee jin har saytee chit laa-i-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	Beautiful and sublime is the glory and the understanding of those who focus their consciousness on the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 5798	sloku mÚ 2 ] (139-2) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 5799	AKI bwJhu vyKxw ivxu kMnw sunxw ] (139-2, mwJ, mÚ 2) akhee baajhahu vaykh-naa vin kanna sunnaa. To see without eyes; to hear without ears;
RECORD	para 5800	pYrw bwJhu clxw ivxu hQw krxw ] (139-2, mwJ, mÚ 2) pairaa baajhahu chalnaa vin hathaa karnaa. to walk without feet; to work without hands;
RECORD	para 5801	jIBY bwJhu bolxw ieau jIvq mrxw ] (139-2, mwJ, mÚ 2) jeebhai baajhahu bolnaa i-o jeevat marnaa. to speak without a tongue-like this, one remains dead while yet alive.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nwnk hukmu pCwix kY qau KsmY imlxw ]1] (139-3, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak hukam pachhaan kai ta-o khasmai milnaa. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	O Nanak, recognize the Hukam of the Lord's Command, and merge with your Lord and Master. ||1||
RECORD	para 5803	mÚ 2 ] (139-3) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 5804	idsY suxIAY jwxIAY swau n pwieAw jwie ] (139-3, mwJ, mÚ 2) disai sunee-ai jaanee-ai saa-o na paa-i-aa jaa-ay. He is seen, heard and known, but His subtle essence is not obtained.
RECORD	para 5805	ruhlw tuMfw AMDulw ikau gil lgY Dwie ] (139-4, mwJ, mÚ 2) ruhlaa tundaa anDhulaa ki-o gal lagai Dhaa-ay. How can the lame, armless and blind person run to embrace the Lord?
RECORD	para 5806	BY ky crx kr Bwv ky loiex suriq kryie ] (139-4, mwJ, mÚ 2) bhai kay charan kar bhaav kay lo-in surat karay-i. Let the Fear of God be your feet, and let His Love be your hands; let His Understanding be your eyes.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwnku khY isAwxIey iev kMq imlwvw hoie ]2] (139-5, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak kahai si-aanee-ay iv kant milaavaa ho-ay. ||2||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	Says Nanak, in this way, O wise soul-bride, you shall be united with your Husband Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 5808	pauVI ] (139-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 5809	sdw sdw qUM eyku hY quDu dUjw Kylu rcwieAw ] (139-5, mwJ, mÚ 2) sadaa sadaa tooN ayk hai tuDh doojaa khayl rachaa-i-aa. Forever and ever, You are the only One; You set the play of duality in motion.
RECORD	para 5810	haumY grbu aupwie kY loBu AMqir jMqw pwieAw ] (139-6, mwJ, mÚ 2) ha-umai garab upaa-ay kai lobh antar jantaa paa-i-aa. You created egotism and arrogant pride, and You placed greed within our beings.
RECORD	para 5811	ijau BwvY iqau rKu qU sB kry qyrw krwieAw ] (139-6, mwJ, mÚ 2) ji-o bhaavai ti-o rakh too sabh karay tayraa karaa-i-aa. Keep me as it pleases Your Will; everyone acts as You cause them to act.
DEFINE	para 5812	ieknw bKsih myil lYih gurmqI quDY lwieAw ] (139-7, mwJ, mÚ 2) iknaa bakhsahi mayl laihi gurmatee tuDhai laa-i-aa. Some are forgiven, and merge with You; through the Guru's Teachings, we are joined to You.
RECORD	para 5813	ieik KVy krih qyrI cwkrI ivxu nwvY horu n BwieAw ] (139-7, mwJ, mÚ 2) ik kharhay karahi tayree chaakree vin naavai hor na bhaa-i-aa. Some stand and serve You; without the Name, nothing else pleases them.
RECORD	para 5814	horu kwr vykwr hY ieik scI kwrY lwieAw ] (139-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) hor kaar vaykaar hai ik sachee kaarai laa-i-aa. Any other task would be worthless to them-You have enjoined them to Your True Service.
RECORD	para 5815	puqu klqu kutMbu hY ieik Ailpqu rhy jo quDu BwieAw ] (139-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) put kalat kutamb hai ik alipat rahay jo tuDh bhaa-i-aa. In the midst of children, spouse and relations, some still remain detached; they are pleasing to Your Will.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v3	Eih AMdrhu bwhrhu inrmly scY nwie smwieAw ]3] (139-9, mwJ, mÚ 2) ohi andrahu baahrahu nirmalay sachai naa-ay samaa-i-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v3	Inwardly and outwardly, they are pure, and they are absorbed in the True Name. ||3||
RECORD	para 5817	sloku mÚ 1 ] (139-10) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
