ALLOW	para 5819	kY ivic DrqI kY AwkwsI auriD rhw isir Bwir ] (139-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) kai vich Dhartee kai aakaasee uraDh rahaa sir bhaar. I may remain standing on my head, upside-down, on the earth or up in the sky;
ALLOW	para 5820	puru kir kwieAw kpVu pihrw Dovw sdw kwir ] (139-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) pur kar kaa-i-aa kaparh pahiraa Dhovaa sadaa kaar. I may totally cover my body with clothes, and wash them continually;
ALLOW	para 5821	bgw rqw pIAlw kwlw bydw krI pukwr ] (139-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) bagaa rataa pee-alaa kaalaa baydaa karee pukaar. I may shout out loud, the white, red, yellow and black Vedas;
ALLOW	para 5822	hoie kucIlu rhw mlu DwrI durmiq miq ivkwr ] (139-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) ho-ay kucheel rahaa mal Dhaaree durmat mat vikaar. I may even live in dirt and filth. And yet, all this is just a product of evil-mindedness, and intellectual corruption.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nw hau nw mY nw hau hovw nwnk sbdu vIcwir ]1] (139-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) naa ha-o naa mai naa ha-o hovaa naanak sabad veechaar. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	I was not, I am not, and I will never be anything at all! O Nanak, I dwell only on the Word of the Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	para 5824	mÚ 1 ] (139-13) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 5825	vsqR pKwil pKwly kwieAw Awpy sMjim hovY ] (139-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) vastar pakhaal pakhaalay kaa-i-aa aapay sanjam hovai. They wash their clothes, and scrub their bodies, and try to practice self-discipline.
RECORD	para 5826	AMqir mYlu lgI nhI jwxY bwhrhu mil mil DovY ] (139-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) antar mail lagee nahee jaanai baahrahu mal mal Dhovai. But they are not aware of the filth staining their inner being, while they try and try to wash off the outer dirt.
RECORD	para 5827	AMDw BUil pieAw jm jwly ] (139-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) anDhaa bhool pa-i-aa jam jaalay. The blind go astray, caught by the noose of Death.
RECORD	para 5828	vsqu prweI ApunI kir jwnY haumY ivic duKu Gwly ] (139-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) vasat paraa-ee apunee kar jaanai ha-umai vich dukh ghaalay. They see other people's property as their own, and in egotism, they suffer in pain.
RECORD	para 5829	nwnk gurmuiK haumY qutY qw hir hir nwmu iDAwvY ] (139-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh ha-umai tutai taa har har naam Dhi-aavai. O Nanak, the egotism of the Gurmukhs is broken, and then, they meditate on the Name of the Lord, Har, Har.
ALLOW	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwmu jpy nwmo AwrwDy nwmy suiK smwvY ]2] (139-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) naam japay naamo aaraaDhay naamay sukh samaavai. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	They chant the Naam, meditate on the Naam, and through the Naam, they are absorbed in peace. ||2||
RECORD	para 5831	pvVI ] (139-16) pavrhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 5832	kwieAw hMis sMjogu myil imlwieAw ] (139-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa hans sanjog mayl milaa-i-aa. Destiny has brought together and united the body and the soul-swan.
RECORD	para 5833	iqn hI kIAw ivjogu ijin aupwieAw ] (139-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) tin hee kee-aa vijog jin upaa-i-aa. He who created them, also separates them.
REQUIRE	para 5834	mUrKu Bogy Bogu duK sbwieAw ] (139-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) moorakh bhogay bhog dukh sabaa-i-aa. The fools enjoy their pleasures; they must also endure all their pains.
RECORD	para 5835	suKhu auTy rog pwp kmwieAw ] (139-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) sukhhu uthay rog paap kamaa-i-aa. From pleasures, arise diseases and the commission of sins.
RECORD	para 5836	hrKhu sogu ivjogu aupwie KpwieAw ] (139-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) harkhahu sog vijog upaa-ay khapaa-i-aa. From sinful pleasures come sorrow, separation, birth and death.
RECORD	para 5837	mUrK gxq gxwie JgVw pwieAw ] (139-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) moorakh ganat ganaa-ay jhagrhaa paa-i-aa. The fools try to account for their misdeeds, and argue uselessly.
DEFINE	para 5838	siqgur hiQ inbyVu JgVu cukwieAw ] (139-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) satgur hath nibayrh jhagarh chukaa-i-aa. The judgement is in the Hands of the True Guru, who puts an end to the argument.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v4	krqw kry su hogu n clY clwieAw ]4] (139-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) kartaa karay so hog na chalai chalaa-i-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v4	Whatever the Creator does, comes to pass. It cannot be changed by anyone's efforts. ||4||
RECORD	para 5840	sloku mÚ 1 ] (139-19) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 5841	kUVu boil murdwru Kwie ] (139-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) koorh bol murdaar khaa-ay. Telling lies, they eat dead bodies.
RECORD	para 5843	AvrI no smJwvix jwie ] (140-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) avree no samjhaavan jaa-ay. And yet, they go out to teach others.
DEFINE	para 5844	muTw Awip muhwey swQY ] (140-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) muthaa aap muhaa-ay saathai. They are deceived, and they deceive their companions.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nwnk AYsw AwgU jwpY ]1] (140-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak aisaa aagoo jaapai. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	O Nanak, such are the leaders of men. ||1||
RECORD	para 5846	mhlw 4 ] (140-1) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 5847	ijs dY AMdir scu hY so scw nwmu muiK scu Alwey ] (140-2, mwJ, mÚ 4) jis dai andar sach hai so sachaa naam mukh sach alaa-ay. Those, within whom the Truth dwells, obtain the True Name; they speak only the Truth.
RECORD	para 5848	Ehu hir mwrig Awip cldw hornw no hir mwrig pwey ] (140-2, mwJ, mÚ 4) oh har maarag aap chaldaa hornaa no har maarag paa-ay. They walk on the Lord's Path, and inspire others to walk on the Lord's Path as well.
RECORD	para 5849	jy AgY qIrQu hoie qw mlu lhY CpiV nwqY sgvI mlu lwey ] (140-3, mwJ, mÚ 4) jay agai tirath ho-ay taa mal lahai chhaparh naatai sagvee mal laa-ay. Bathing in a pool of holy water, they are washed clean of filth. But, by bathing in a stagnant pond, they are contaminated with even more filth.
RECORD	para 5850	qIrQu pUrw siqgurU jo Anidnu hir hir nwmu iDAwey ] (140-3, mwJ, mÚ 4) tirath pooraa satguroo jo an-din har har naam Dhi-aa-ay. The True Guru is the Perfect Pool of Holy Water. Night and day, He meditates on the Name of the Lord, Har, Har.
RECORD	para 5851	Ehu Awip Cutw kutMb isau dy hir hir nwmu sB isRsit Cfwey ] (140-4, mwJ, mÚ 4) oh aap chhutaa kutamb si-o day har har naam sabh sarisat chhadaa-ay. He is saved, along with his family; bestowing the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, He saves the whole world.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	jn nwnk iqsu bilhwrxY jo Awip jpY Avrw nwmu jpwey ]2] (140-5, mwJ, mÚ 4) jan naanak tis balihaarnai jo aap japai avraa naam japaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	Servant Nanak is a sacrifice to one who himself chants the Naam, and inspires others to chant it as well. ||2||
RECORD	para 5853	pauVI ] (140-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
WHEN	para 5854	ieik kMd mUlu cuix Kwih vx KMif vwsw ] (140-5, mwJ, mÚ 4) ik kand mool chun khaahi van khand vaasaa. Some pick and eat fruits and roots, and live in the wilderness.
RECORD	para 5855	ieik Bgvw vysu kir iPrih jogI sMinAwsw ] (140-6, mwJ, mÚ 4) ik bhagvaa vays kar fireh jogee saniaasaa. Some wander around wearing saffron robes, as Yogis and Sanyaasees.
DEFINE	para 5856	AMdir iqRsnw bhuqu Cwdn Bojn kI Awsw ] (140-6, mwJ, mÚ 4) andar tarisnaa bahut chhaadan bhojan kee aasaa. But there is still so much desire within them-they still yearn for clothes and food.
DEFINE	para 5857	ibrQw jnmu gvwie n igrhI n audwsw ] (140-7, mwJ, mÚ 4) birthaa janam gavaa-ay na girhee na udaasaa. They waste their lives uselessly; they are neither householders nor renunciates.
RECORD	para 5858	jmkwlu isrhu n auqrY iqRibiD mnsw ] (140-7, mwJ, mÚ 4) jamkaal sirahu na utrai taribaDh mansaa. The Messenger of Death hangs over their heads, and they cannot escape the three- phased desire.
RECORD	para 5859	gurmqI kwlu n AwvY nyVY jw hovY dwsin dwsw ] (140-8, mwJ, mÚ 4) gurmatee kaal na aavai nayrhai jaa hovai daasan daasaa. Death does not even approach those who follow the Guru's Teachings, and become the slaves of the Lord's slaves.
RECORD	para 5860	scw sbdu scu min Gr hI mwih audwsw ] (140-8, mwJ, mÚ 4) sachaa sabad sach man ghar hee maahi udaasaa. The True Word of the Shabad abides in their true minds; within the home of their own inner beings, they remain detached.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v5	nwnk siqguru syvin Awpxw sy Awsw qy inrwsw ]5] (140-8, mwJ, mÚ 4) naanak satgur sayvan aapnaa say aasaa tay niraasaa. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v5	O Nanak, those who serve their True Guru, rise from desire to desirelessness. ||5||
RECORD	para 5862	sloku mÚ 1 ] (140-9) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 5863	jy rqu lgY kpVY jwmw hoie plIqu ] (140-9, mwJ, mÚ 1) jay rat lagai kaprhai jaamaa ho-ay paleet. If one's clothes are stained with blood, the garment becomes polluted.
RECORD	para 5864	jo rqu pIvih mwxsw iqn ikau inrmlu cIqu ] (140-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) jo rat peeveh maansaa tin ki-o nirmal cheet. Those who suck the blood of human beings-how can their consciousness be pure?
RECORD	para 5865	nwnk nwau Kudwie kw idil hCY muiK lyhu ] (140-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak naa-o khudaa-ay kaa dil hachhai mukh layho. O Nanak, chant the Name of God, with heart-felt devotion.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	Avir idvwjy dunI ky JUTy Aml kryhu ]1] (140-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) avar divaajay dunee kay jhoothay amal karayhu. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	Everything else is just a pompous worldly show, and the practice of false deeds. ||1||
RECORD	para 5867	mÚ 1 ] (140-11) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 5868	jw hau nwhI qw ikAw AwKw ikhu nwhI ikAw hovw ] (140-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa ha-o naahee taa ki-aa aakhaa kihu naahee ki-aa hovaa. Since I am no one, what can I say? Since I am nothing, what can I be?
WHEN	para 5869	kIqw krxw kihAw kQnw BirAw Bir Bir DovW ] (140-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) keetaa karnaa kahi-aa kathnaa bhari-aa bhar bhar DhovaaN. As He created me, so I act. As He causes me to speak, so I speak. I am full and overflowing with sins-if only I could wash them away!
DEFINE	para 5870	Awip n buJw lok buJweI AYsw AwgU hovW ] (140-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) aap na bujhaa lok bujhaa-ee aisaa aagoo hovaa N. I do not understand myself, and yet I try to teach others. Such is the guide I am!
DEFINE	para 5871	nwnk AMDw hoie kY dsy rwhY sBsu muhwey swQY ] (140-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak anDhaa ho-ay kai dasay raahai sabhas muhaa-ay saathai. O Nanak, the one who is blind shows others the way, and misleads all his companions.
