DEFINE	para 5972	scy kI isrkwr jugu jugu jwxIAY ] (142-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachay kee sirkaar jug jug jaanee-ai. The True Lord's Sovereign Rule is known throughout the ages.
DEFINE	para 5973	hukmu mMny isrdwru dir dIbwxIAY ] (142-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) hukam mannay sirdaar dar deebaanee-ai. One who respects the Hukam of the Lord's Command is honored and respected in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	para 5974	PurmwnI hY kwr Ksim pTwieAw ] (142-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) furmaanee hai kaar khasam pathaa-i-aa. By the Order of our Lord and Master, we have been brought into this world.
RECORD	para 5975	qblbwj bIcwr sbid suxwieAw ] (142-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) tabalbaaj beechaar sabad sunaa-i-aa. The Drummer, the Guru, has announced the Lord's meditation, through the Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 5976	ieik hoey Asvwr ieknw swKqI ] (142-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) ik ho-ay asvaar iknaa saakh-tee. Some have mounted their horses in response, and others are saddling up.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v10	ieknI bDy Bwr ieknw qwKqI ]10] (142-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) iknee baDhay bhaar iknaa taakh-tee. ||10||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v10	Some have tied up their bridles, and others have already ridden off. ||10||
RECORD	para 5978	sloku mÚ 1 ] (142-17) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 5979	jw pkw qw kitAw rhI su plir vwiV ] (142-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa pakaa taa kati-aa rahee so palar vaarh. When the crop is ripe, then it is cut down; only the stalks are left standing.
DEFINE	para 5980	sxu kIswrw iciQAw kxu lieAw qnu JwiV ] (142-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) san keesaaraa chithi-aa kan la-i-aa tan jhaarh. The corn on the cob is put into the thresher, and the kernels are separated from the cobs.
RECORD	para 5981	duie puV ckI joiV kY pIsx Awie bihTu ] (142-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) du-ay purh chakee jorh kai peesan aa-ay bahith. Placing the kernels between the two mill-stones, people sit and grind the corn.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	jo dir rhy su aubry nwnk Ajbu ifTu ]1] (142-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) jo dar rahay so ubray naanak ajab dith. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	Those kernels which stick to the central axle are spared-Nanak has seen this wonderful vision! ||1||
RECORD	para 5983	mÚ 1 ] (142-19) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 5984	vyKu ij imTw kitAw kit kuit bDw pwie ] (142-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) vaykh je mithaa kati-aa kat kut baDhaa paa-ay. Look, and see how the sugar-cane is cut down. After cutting away its branches, its feet are bound together into bundles,
DEFINE	para 5986	KuMFw AMdir riK kY dyin su ml sjwie ] (143-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) khundhaa andar rakh kai dayn so mal sajaa-ay. and then, it is placed between the wooden rollers and crushed.
RECORD	para 5987	rsu ksu ttir pweIAY qpY qY ivllwie ] (143-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) ras kas tatar paa-ee-ai tapai tai villaa-ay. What punishment is inflicted upon it! Its juice is extracted and placed in the cauldron; as it is heated, it groans and cries out.
DEFINE	para 5988	BI so Pogu smwlIAY idcY Aig jwlwie ] (143-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) bhee so fog samaalee-ai dichai ag jaalaa-ay. And then, the crushed cane is collected and burnt in the fire below.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwnk imTY pqrIAY vyKhu lokw Awie ]2] (143-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak mithai patree-ai vaykhhu lokaa aa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	Nanak: come, people, and see how the sweet sugar-cane is treated! ||2||
RECORD	para 5990	pvVI ] (143-3) pavrhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 5991	ieknw mrxu n iciq Aws GxyirAw ] (143-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) iknaa maran na chit aas ghanayri-aa. Some do not think of death; they entertain great hopes.
DEFINE	para 5992	mir mir jMmih inq iksY n kyirAw ] (143-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) mar mar jameh nit kisai na kayri-aa. They die, and are re-born, and die, over and over again. They are of no use at all!
RECORD	para 5993	AwpnVY min iciq khin cMgyirAw ] (143-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) aapnarhai man chit kahan changayri-aa. In their conscious minds, they call themselves good.
RECORD	para 5994	jmrwjY inq inq mnmuK hyirAw ] (143-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) jamraajai nit nit manmukh hayri-aa. The King of the Angels of Death hunts down those self-willed manmukhs, over and over again.
DEFINE	para 5995	mnmuK lUx hwrwm ikAw n jwixAw ] (143-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) manmukh loon haaraam ki-aa na jaani-aa. The manmukhs are false to their own selves; they feel no gratitude for what they have been given.
DEFINE	para 5996	bDy krin slwm Ksm n BwixAw ] (143-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) baDhay karan salaam khasam na bhaani-aa. Those who merely perform rituals of worship are not pleasing to their Lord and Master.
DEFINE	para 5997	scu imlY muiK nwmu swihb BwvsI ] (143-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) sach milai mukh naam saahib bhaavsee. Those who attain the True Lord and chant His Name are pleasing to the Lord.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v11	krsin qKiq slwmu iliKAw pwvsI ]11] (143-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) karsan takhat salaam likhi-aa paavsee. ||11||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v11	They worship the Lord and bow at His Throne. They fulfill their pre-ordained destiny. ||11||
RECORD	para 5999	mÚ 1 sloku ] (143-6) mehlaa 1 salok. First Mehl, Shalok:
RECORD	para 6000	mCI qwrU ikAw kry pMKI ikAw Awkwsu ] (143-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) machhee taaroo ki-aa karay pankhee ki-aa aakaas. What can deep water do to a fish? What can the vast sky do to a bird?
DEFINE	para 6001	pQr pwlw ikAw kry Kusry ikAw Gr vwsu ] (143-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) pathar paalaa ki-aa karay khusray ki-aa ghar vaas. What can cold do to a stone? What is married life to a eunuch?
ALLOW	para 6002	kuqy cMdnu lweIAY BI so kuqI Dwqu ] (143-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) kutay chandan laa-ee-ai bhee so kutee Dhaat. You may apply sandalwood oil to a dog, but he will still be a dog.
ALLOW	para 6003	bolw jy smJweIAY pVIAih isMimRiq pwT ] (143-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) bolaa jay samjaa-ee-ai parhee-ah simrit paath. You may try to teach a deaf person by reading the Simritees to him, but how will he learn?
ALLOW	para 6004	AMDw cwnix rKIAY dIvy blih pcws ] (143-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) anDhaa chaanan rakhee-ai deevay baleh pachaas. You may place a light before a blind man and burn fifty lamps, but how will he see?
ALLOW	para 6005	cauxy suienw pweIAY cuix cuix KwvY Gwsu ] (143-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) cha-unay su-inaa paa-ee-ai chun chun khaavai ghaas. You may place gold before a herd of cattle, but they will pick out the grass to eat.
ALLOW	para 6006	lohw mwrix pweIAY FhY n hoie kpws ] (143-9, mwJ, mÚ 1) lohaa maaran paa-ee-ai dhahai na ho-ay kapaas. You may add flux to iron and melt it, but it will not become soft like cotton.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nwnk mUrK eyih gux boly sdw ivxwsu ]1] (143-9, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak moorakh ayhi gun bolay sadaa vinaas. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	O Nanak, this is the nature of a fool-everything he speaks is useless and wasted. ||1||
RECORD	para 6008	mÚ 1 ] (143-10) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
WHEN	para 6009	kYhw kMcnu qutY swru ] (143-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) kaihaa kanchan tutai saar. When pieces of bronze or gold or iron break,
DEFINE	para 6010	AgnI gMFu pwey lohwru ] (143-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) agnee gandh paa-ay lohaar. the metal-smith welds them together again in the fire, and the bond is established.
WHEN	para 6011	gorI syqI qutY Bqwru ] (143-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) goree saytee tutai bhataar. If a husband leaves his wife,
ALLOW	para 6012	puqˆØI gMFu pvY sMswir ] (143-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) putee N gandh pavai sansaar. their children may bring them back together in the world, and the bond is established.
DEFINE	para 6013	rwjw mMgY idqY gMFu pwie ] (143-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) raajaa mangai ditai gandh paa-ay. When the king makes a demand, and it is met, the bond is established.
DEFINE	para 6014	BuiKAw gMFu pvY jw Kwie ] (143-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) bhukhi-aa gandh pavai jaa khaa-ay. When the hungry man eats, he is satisfied, and the bond is established.
DEFINE	para 6015	kwlw gMFu ndIAw mIh Jol ] (143-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) kaalaa gandh nadee-aa meeh jhol. In the famine, the rain fills the streams to overflowing, and the bond is established.
DEFINE	para 6016	gMFu prIqI imTy bol ] (143-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) gandh pareetee mithay bol. There is a bond between love and words of sweetness.
DEFINE	para 6017	bydw gMFu boly scu koie ] (143-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) baydaa gandh bolay sach ko-ay. When one speaks the Truth, a bond is established with the Holy Scriptures.
RECORD	para 6018	muieAw gMFu nykI squ hoie ] (143-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) mu-i-aa gandh naykee sat ho-ay. Through goodness and truth, the dead establish a bond with the living.
DEFINE	para 6019	eyqu gMiF vrqY sMswru ] (143-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayt gandh vartai sansaar. Such are the bonds which prevail in the world.
DEFINE	para 6020	mUrK gMFu pvY muih mwr ] (143-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) moorakh gandh pavai muhi maar. The fool establishes his bonds only when he is slapped in the face.
RECORD	para 6021	nwnku AwKY eyhu bIcwru ] (143-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak aakhai ayhu beechaar. Nanak says this after deep reflection:
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	isPqI gMFu pvY drbwir ]2] (143-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) siftee gandh pavai darbaar. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	through the Lord's Praise, we establish a bond with His Court. ||2||
RECORD	para 6023	pauVI ] (143-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 6024	Awpy kudriq swij kY Awpy kry bIcwru ] (143-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) aapay kudrat saaj kai aapay karay beechaar. He Himself created and adorned the Universe, and He Himself contemplates it.
DEFINE	para 6025	ieik Koty ieik Kry Awpy prKxhwru ] (143-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) ik khotay ik kharay aapay parkhanhaar. Some are counterfeit, and some are genuine. He Himself is the Appraiser.
DEFINE	para 6026	Kry KjwnY pweIAih Koty stIAih bwhr vwir ] (143-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) kharay khajaanai paa-ee-ah khotay satee-ah baahar vaar. The genuine are placed in His Treasury, while the counterfeit are thrown away.
DEFINE	para 6027	Koty scI drgh sutIAih iksu AwgY krih pukwr ] (143-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) khotay sachee dargeh sutee-ah kis aagai karahi pukaar. The counterfeit are thrown out of the True Court-unto whom should they complain?
DEFINE	para 6028	siqgur ipCY Bij pvih eyhw krxI swru ] (143-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) satgur pichhai bhaj paveh ayhaa karnee saar. They should worship and follow the True Guru-this is the lifestyle of excellence.
RECORD	para 6029	siqguru KoitAhu Kry kry sbid svwrxhwru ] (143-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) satgur khoti-ahu kharay karay sabad savaaranhaar. The True Guru converts the counterfeit into genuine; through the Word of the Shabad, He embellishes and exalts us.
DEFINE	para 6030	scI drgh mMnIAin gur kY pRym ipAwir ] (143-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachee dargeh mannee-an gur kai paraym pi-aar. Those who have enshrined love and affection for the Guru, are honored in the True Court.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v12	gxq iqnw dI ko ikAw kry jo Awip bKsy krqwir ]12] (143-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) ganat tinaa dee ko ki-aa karay jo aap bakhsay kartaar. ||12||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v12	Who can estimate the value of those who have been forgiven by the Creator Lord Himself? ||12||
RECORD	para 6032	sloku mÚ 1 ] (143-18) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 6033	hm jyr ijmI dunIAw pIrw mswiekw rwieAw ] (143-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) ham jayr jimee dunee-aa peeraa masaa-ikaa raa-i-aa. All the spiritual teachers, their disciples and the rulers of the world shall be buried under the ground.
REQUIRE	para 6034	my rvid bwidswhw APjU Kudwie ] (143-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) may ravad baadisaahaa afjoo khudaa-ay. The emperors shall also pass away; God alone is Eternal.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	eyk qUhI eyk quhI ]1] (143-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayk toohee ayk tuhee. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	You alone, Lord, You alone. ||1||
RECORD	para 6036	mÚ 1 ] (143-19) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 6037	n dyv dwnvw nrw ] n isD swiDkw Drw ] (143-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) na dayv daanvaa naraa. na siDh saaDhikaa Dharaa. Neither the angels, nor the demons, nor human beings, nor the Siddhas, nor the seekers shall remain on the earth.
DEFINE	para 6038	Asiq eyk idgir kueI ] (143-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) asat ayk digar ku-ee. Who else is there?
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	eyk queI eyk queI ]2] (144-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayk tu-ee ayk tu-ee. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	You alone, Lord, You alone. ||2||
RECORD	para 6041	mÚ 1 ] (144-1) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 6042	n dwdy idhMd AwdmI ] n spq jyr ijmI ] (144-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) na daaday dihand aadmee. na sapat jayr jimee. Neither the just, nor the generous, nor any humans at all, nor the seven realms beneath the earth, shall remain.
DEFINE	para 6043	Asiq eyk idgir kueI ] (144-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) asat ayk digar ku-ee. The One Lord alone exists. Who else is there?
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v3	eyk queI eyk queI ]3] (144-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayk tu-ee ayk tu-ee. ||3||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v3	You alone, Lord, You alone. ||3||
RECORD	para 6045	mÚ 1 ] (144-2) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 6046	n sUr sis mMflo ] n spq dIp nh jlo ] AMn paux iQru n kueI ] (144-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) na soor sas mandlo. na sapat deep nah jalo. ann pa-un thir na ku-ee. Neither the sun, nor the moon, nor the planets, nor the seven continents, nor the oceans, nor food, nor the wind-nothing is permanent.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v4	eyku queI eyku queI ]4] (144-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayk tu-ee ayk tu-ee. ||4||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v4	You alone, Lord, You alone. ||4||
RECORD	para 6048	mÚ 1 ] (144-3) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6049	n irjku dsq Aw ksy ] (144-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) na rijak dasat aa kasay. Our sustenance is not in the hands of any person.
RECORD	para 6050	hmw rw eyku Aws vsy ] (144-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) hamaa raa ayk aas vasay. The hopes of all rest in the One Lord.
DEFINE	para 6051	Asiq eyku idgr kueI ] (144-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) asat ayk digar ku-ee. The One Lord alone exists-who else is there?
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v5	eyk queI eyku queI ]5] (144-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayk tu-ee ayk tu-ee. ||5||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v5	You alone, Lord, You alone. ||5||
RECORD	para 6053	mÚ 1 ] (144-4) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 6054	prMdey n igrwh jr ] (144-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) paranday na giraah jar. The birds have no money in their pockets.
RECORD	para 6055	drKq Awb Aws kr ] (144-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) darkhat aab aas kar. They place their hopes on trees and water.
DEFINE	para 6056	idhMd sueI ] (144-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) dihand su-ee. He alone is the Giver.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v6	eyk queI eyk queI ]6] (144-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayk tu-ee ayk tu-ee. ||6||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v6	You alone, Lord, You alone. ||6||
RECORD	para 6058	mÚ 1 ] (144-5) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6059	nwnk illwir iliKAw soie ] (144-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak lilaar likhi-aa so-ay. O Nanak, that destiny which is pre-ordained and written on one's forehead
RECORD	para 6060	myit n swkY koie ] (144-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) mayt na saakai ko-ay. -no one can erase it.
RECORD	para 6061	klw DrY ihrY sueI ] (144-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) kalaa Dharai hirai su-ee. The Lord infuses strength, and He takes it away again.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v7	eyku queI eyku queI ]7] (144-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayk tu-ee ayk tu-ee. ||7||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v7	You alone, O Lord, You alone. ||7||
RECORD	para 6063	pauVI ] (144-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 6064	scw qyrw hukmu gurmuiK jwixAw ] (144-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachaa tayraa hukam gurmukh jaani-aa. True is the Hukam of Your Command. To the Gurmukh, it is known.
DEFINE	para 6065	gurmqI Awpu gvwie scu pCwixAw ] (144-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) gurmatee aap gavaa-ay sach pachhaani-aa. Through the Guru's Teachings, selfishness and conceit are eradicated, and the Truth is realized.
DEFINE	para 6066	scu qyrw drbwru sbdu nIswixAw ] (144-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) sach tayraa darbaar sabad neesaani-aa. True is Your Court. It is proclaimed and revealed through the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 6067	scw sbdu vIcwir sic smwixAw ] (144-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachaa sabad veechaar sach samaani-aa. Meditating deeply on the True Word of the Shabad, I have merged into the Truth.
DEFINE	para 6068	mnmuK sdw kUiVAwr Brim BulwixAw ] (144-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) manmukh sadaa koorhi-aar bharam bhoolaani-aa. The self-willed manmukhs are always false; they are deluded by doubt.
RECORD	para 6069	ivstw AMdir vwsu swdu n jwixAw ] (144-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) vistaa andar vaas saad na jaani-aa. They dwell in manure, and they do not know the taste of the Name.
RECORD	para 6070	ivxu nwvY duKu pwie Awvx jwixAw ] (144-9, mwJ, mÚ 1) vin naavai dukh paa-ay aavan jaani-aa. Without the Name, they suffer the agonies of coming and going.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v13	nwnk pwrKu Awip ijin Kotw Krw pCwixAw ]13] (144-9, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak paarakh aap jin khotaa kharaa pachhaani-aa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v13	O Nanak, the Lord Himself is the Appraiser, who distinguishes the counterfeit from the genuine. ||13||
RECORD	para 6072	sloku mÚ 1 ] (144-10) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 6073	sIhw bwjw crgw kuhIAw eynw Kvwly Gwh ] (144-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) seehaa baajaa chargaa kuhee-aa aynaa khavaalay ghaah. Tigers, hawks, falcons and eagles-the Lord could make them eat grass.
RECORD	para 6074	Gwhu Kwin iqnw mwsu Kvwly eyih clwey rwh ] (144-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) ghaahu khaan tinaa maas khavaalay ayhi chalaa-ay raah. And those animals which eat grass-He could make them eat meat. He could make them follow this way of life.
RECORD	para 6075	ndIAw ivic itby dyKwly QlI kry Asgwh ] (144-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) nadee-aa vich tibay daykhaalay thalee karay asgaah. He could raise dry land from the rivers, and turn the deserts into bottomless oceans.
RECORD	para 6076	kIVw Qwip dyie pwiqswhI lskr kry suAwh ] (144-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) keerhaa thaap day-ay paatisaahee laskar karay su-aah. He could appoint a worm as king, and reduce an army to ashes.
RECORD	para 6077	jyqy jIA jIvih lY swhw jIvwly qw ik Aswh ] (144-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaytay jee-a jeeveh lai saahaa jeevaalay taa ke asaah. All beings and creatures live by breathing, but He could keep us alive, even without the breath.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nwnk ijau ijau scy BwvY iqau iqau dyie igrwh ]1] (144-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak ji-o ji-o sachay bhaavai ti-o ti-o day-ay giraah. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	O Nanak, as it pleases the True Lord, He gives us sustenance. ||1||
RECORD	para 6079	mÚ 1 ] (144-13) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 6080	ieik mwshwrI ieik iqRxu Kwih ] (144-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) ik maashaaree ik tarin khaahi. Some eat meat, while others eat grass.
RECORD	para 6081	ieknw CqIh AMimRq pwih ] (144-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) iknaa chhateeh amrit paahi. Some have all the thirty-six varieties of delicacies,
RECORD	para 6082	ieik imtIAw mih imtIAw Kwih ] (144-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) ik mitee-aa meh mitee-aa khaahi. while others live in the dirt and eat mud.
RECORD	para 6083	ieik paux sumwrI paux sumwir ] (144-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) ik pa-un sumaaree pa-un sumaar. Some control the breath, and regulate their breathing.
RECORD	para 6084	ieik inrMkwrI nwm AwDwir ] (144-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) ik nirankaaree naam aaDhaar. Some live by the Support of the Naam, the Name of the Formless Lord.
RECORD	para 6085	jIvY dwqw mrY n koie ] (144-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) jeevai daataa marai na ko-ay. The Great Giver lives; no one dies.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwnk muTy jwih nwhI min soie ]2] (144-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak muthay jaahi naahee man so-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	O Nanak, those who do not enshrine the Lord within their minds are deluded. ||2||
RECORD	para 6087	pauVI ] (144-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 6088	pUry gur kI kwr krim kmweIAY ] (144-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) pooray gur kee kaar karam kamaa-ee-ai. By the karma of good actions, some come to serve the Perfect Guru.
RECORD	para 6089	gurmqI Awpu gvwie nwmu iDAweIAY ] (144-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) gurmatee aap gavaa-ay naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai. Through the Guru's Teachings, some eliminate selfishness and conceit, and meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 6090	dUjI kwrY lig jnmu gvweIAY ] (144-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) doojee kaarai lag janam gavaa-ee-ai. Undertaking any other task, they waste their lives in vain.
DEFINE	para 6091	ivxu nwvY sB ivsu pYJY KweIAY ] (144-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) vin naavai sabh vis paijhai khaa-ee-ai. Without the Name, all that they wear and eat is poison.
RECORD	para 6092	scw sbdu swlwih sic smweIAY ] (144-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachaa sabad saalaahi sach samaa-ee-ai. Praising the True Word of the Shabad, they merge with the True Lord.
RECORD	para 6093	ivxu siqguru syvy nwhI suiK invwsu iPir iPir AweIAY ] (144-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) vin satgur sayvay naahee sukh nivaas fir fir aa-ee-ai. Without serving the True Guru, they do not obtain the home of peace; they are consigned to reincarnation, over and over again.
RECORD	para 6094	dunIAw KotI rwis kUVu kmweIAY ] (144-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) dunee-aa khotee raas koorh kamaa-ee-ai. Investing counterfeit capital, they earn only falsehood in the world.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v14	nwnk scu Krw swlwih piq isau jweIAY ]14] (144-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak sach kharaa saalaahi pat si-o jaa-ee-ai. ||14||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v14	O Nanak, singing the Praises of the Pure, True Lord, they depart with honor. ||14||
RECORD	para 6096	sloku mÚ 1 ] (144-19) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
WHEN	para 6097	quDu BwvY qw vwvih gwvih quDu BwvY jil nwvih ] (144-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) tuDh bhaavai taa vaaveh gaavahi tuDh bhaavai jal naaveh. When it pleases You, we play music and sing; when it pleases You, we bathe in water.
WHEN	para 6099	jw quDu Bwvih qw krih ibBUqw isM|I nwdu vjwvih ] (145-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa tuDh bhaaveh taa karahi bibhootaa sinyee naad vajaavah. When it pleases You, we smear our bodies with ashes, and blow the horn and the conch shell.
DEFINE	para 6100	jw quDu BwvY qw pVih kqybw mulw syK khwvih ] (145-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa tuDh bhaavai taa parheh kataybaa mulaa saykh kahaaveh. When it pleases You, we read the Islamic Scriptures, and are acclaimed as Mullahs and Shaykhs.
WHEN	para 6101	jw quDu BwvY qw hovih rwjy rs ks bhuqu kmwvih ] (145-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa tuDh bhaavai taa hoveh raajay ras kas bahut kamaaveh. When it pleases You, we become kings, and enjoy all sorts of tastes and pleasures.
WHEN	para 6102	jw quDu BwvY qyg vgwvih isr muMfI kit jwvih ] (145-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa tuDh bhaavai tayg vagaaveh sir mundee kat jaaveh. When it pleases You, we wield the sword, and cut off the heads of our enemies.
WHEN	para 6103	jw quDu BwvY jwih idsMqir suix glw Gir Awvih ] (145-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa tuDh bhaavai jaahi disantar sun galaa ghar aavahi. When it pleases You, we go out to foreign lands; hearing news of home, we come back again.
WHEN	para 6104	jw quDu BwvY nwie rcwvih quDu Bwxy qUM Bwvih ] (145-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa tuDh bhaavai naa-ay rachaaveh tuDh bhaanay tooN bhaaveh. When it pleases You, we are attuned to the Name, and when it pleases You, we become pleasing to You.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nwnku eyk khY bynµqI hoir sgly kUVu kmwvih ]1] (145-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak ayk kahai baynantee hor saglay koorh kamaaveh. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	Nanak utters this one prayer; everything else is just the practice of falsehood. ||1||
RECORD	para 6106	mÚ 1 ] (145-4) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6107	jw qUM vfw siB vifAWeIAw cMgY cMgw hoeI ] (145-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa tooN vadaa sabh vadi-aa N-ee-aa changai changa ho-ee. You are so Great-all Greatness flows from You. You are So Good-Goodness radiates from You.
DEFINE	para 6108	jw qUM scw qw sBu ko scw kUVw koie n koeI ] (145-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) jaa tooN sachaa taa sabh ko sachaa koorhaa ko-ay na ko-ee. You are True-all that flows from You is True. Nothing at all is false.
DEFINE	para 6109	AwKxu vyKxu bolxu clxu jIvxu mrxw Dwqu ] (145-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) aakhan vaykhan bolan chalan jeevan marnaa Dhaat. Talking, seeing, speaking, walking, living and dying-all these are transitory.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	hukmu swij hukmY ivic rKY nwnk scw Awip ]2] (145-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) hukam saaj hukmai vich rakhai naanak sachaa aap. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	By the Hukam of His Command, He creates, and in His Command, He keeps us. O Nanak, He Himself is True. ||2||
RECORD	para 6111	pauVI ] (145-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
REQUIRE	para 6112	siqguru syiv insMgu Brmu cukweIAY ] (145-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) satgur sayv nisang bharam chukhaa-ee-ai. Serve the True Guru fearlessly, and your doubt shall be dispelled.
RECORD	para 6113	siqguru AwKY kwr su kwr kmweIAY ] (145-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) satgur aakhai kaar so kaar kamaa-ee-ai. Do that work which the True Guru asks you to do.
WHEN	para 6114	siqguru hoie dieAwlu q nwmu iDAweIAY ] (145-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal ta naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai. When the True Guru becomes merciful, we meditate on the Naam.
DEFINE	para 6115	lwhw Bgiq su swru gurmuiK pweIAY ] (145-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) laahaa bhagat so saar gurmukh paa-ee-ai. The profit of devotional worship is excellent. It is obtained by the Gurmukh.
DEFINE	para 6116	mnmuiK kUVu gubwru kUVu kmweIAY ] (145-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) manmukh koorh gubaar koorh kamaa-ee-ai. The self-willed manmukhs are trapped in the darkness of falsehood; they practice nothing but falsehood.
RECORD	para 6117	scy dY dir jwie scu cvWeIAY ] (145-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachay dai dar jaa-ay sach chavaa N-ee-ai. Go to the Gate of Truth, and speak the Truth.
RECORD	para 6118	scY AMdir mhil sic bulweIAY ] (145-9, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachai andar mahal sach bulaa-ee-ai. The True Lord calls the true ones to the Mansion of His Presence.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v15	nwnk scu sdw sicAwru sic smweIAY ]15] (145-9, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak sach sadaa sachiaar sach samaa-ee-ai. ||15||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v15	O Nanak, the true ones are forever true; they are absorbed in the True Lord. ||15||
RECORD	para 6120	sloku mÚ 1 ] (145-10) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
UPHOLD	para 6121	kil kwqI rwjy kwsweI Drmu pMK kir aufirAw ] (145-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) kal kaatee raajay kaasaa-ee Dharam pankh kar udri-aa. The Dark Age of Kali Yuga is the knife, and the kings are butchers; righteousness has sprouted wings and flown away.
DEFINE	para 6122	kUVu Amwvs scu cMdRmw dIsY nwhI kh ciVAw ] (145-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) koorh amaavas sach chandarmaa deesai naahee kah charhi-aa. In this dark night of falsehood, the moon of Truth is not visible anywhere.
RECORD	para 6123	hau Bwil ivkuMnI hoeI ] AwDyrY rwhu n koeI ] (145-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) ha-o bhaal vikunnee ho-ee. aaDhaarai raahu na ko-ee. I have searched in vain, and I am so confused; in this darkness, I cannot find the path.
RECORD	para 6124	ivic haumY kir duKu roeI ] (145-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) vich ha-umai kar dukh ro-ee. In egotism, they cry out in pain.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	khu nwnk ikin ibiD giq hoeI ]1] (145-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) kaho naanak kin biDh gat ho-ee. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	Says Nanak, how will they be saved? ||1||
RECORD	para 6126	mÚ 3 ] (145-12) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 6127	kil kIriq prgtu cwnxu sMswir ] (145-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) kal keerat pargat chaanan sansaar. In this Dark Age of Kali Yuga, the Kirtan of the Lord's Praise has appeared as a Light in the world.
DEFINE	para 6128	gurmuiK koeI auqrY pwir ] (145-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) gurmukh ko-ee utrai paar. How rare are those few Gurmukhs who swim across to the other side!
