RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwnk gurmuiK rqnu so lyvY ]2] (145-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh ratan so layvai. ||2||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukh receives the jewel. ||2||
RECORD	para 6131	pauVI ] (145-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 6132	Bgqw qY sYswrIAw joVu kdy n AwieAw ] (145-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) bhagtaa tai saisaaree-aa jorh kaday na aa-i-aa. Between the Lord's devotees and the people of the world, there can never be any true alliance.
DEFINE	para 6133	krqw Awip ABulu hY n BulY iksY dw BulwieAw ] (145-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) kartaa aap abhul hai na bhulai kisai daa bhulaa-i-aa. The Creator Himself is infallible. He cannot be fooled; no one can fool Him.
RECORD	para 6134	Bgq Awpy myilAnu ijnI sco scu kmwieAw ] (145-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) bhagat aapay mayli-an jinee sacho sach kamaa-i-aa. He blends His devotees with Himself; they practice Truth, and only Truth.
RECORD	para 6135	sYswrI Awip KuAwieAnu ijnI kUVu boil boil ibKu KwieAw ] (145-15, mwJ, mÚ 3) saisaaree aap khu-aa-i-an jinee koorh bol bol bikh khaa-i-aa. The Lord Himself leads the people of the world astray; they tell lies, and by telling lies, they eat poison.
