RECORD	para 6137	Bgq krin hir cwkrI ijnI Anidnu nwmu iDAwieAw ] (145-16, mwJ, mÚ 3) bhagat karan har chaakree jinee an-din naam Dhi-aa-i-aa. The devotees serve the Lord; night and day, they meditate on the Naam.
RECORD	para 6138	dwsin dws hoie kY ijnI ivchu Awpu gvwieAw ] (145-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) daasan daas ho-ay kai jinee vichahu aap gavaa-i-aa. Becoming the slaves of the Lord's slaves, they eradicate selfishness and conceit from within.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v16	Enw KsmY kY dir muK aujly scY sbid suhwieAw ]16] (145-17, mwJ, mÚ 3) onaa khasmai kai dar mukh ujlay sachai sabad suhaa-i-aa. ||16||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v16	In the Court of their Lord and Master, their faces are radiant; they are embellished and exalted with the True Word of the Shabad. ||16||
RECORD	para 6140	sloku mÚ 1 ] (145-18) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 6141	sbwhI swlwh ijnI iDAwieAw iek min ] (145-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) sabaahee saalaah jinee Dhi-aa-i-aa ik man. Those who praise the Lord in the early hours of the morning and meditate on Him single-mindedly,
RECORD	para 6142	syeI pUry swh vKqY aupir liV muey ] (145-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) say-ee pooray saah vakh-tai upar larh mu-ay. are the perfect kings; at the right time, they die fighting.
