RECORD	para 6171	cauQY phir sbwh kY suriqAw aupjY cwau ] (146-10, mwJ, mÚ 2) cha-uthai pahar sabaah kai surti-aa upjai chaa-o. In the fourth watch of the early morning hours, a longing arises in their higher consciousness.
DEFINE	para 6172	iqnw drIAwvw isau dosqI min muiK scw nwau ] (146-11, mwJ, mÚ 2) tinaa daree-aavaa si-o dostee man mukh sachaa naa-o. They are attuned to the river of life; the True Name is in their minds and on their lips.
DEFINE	para 6173	EQY AMimRqu vMfIAY krmI hoie pswau ] (146-11, mwJ, mÚ 2) othai amrit vandee-ai karmee ho-ay pasaa-o. The Ambrosial Nectar is distributed, and those with good karma receive this gift.
RECORD	para 6174	kMcn kwieAw ksIAY vMnI cVY cVwau ] (146-11, mwJ, mÚ 2) kanchan kaa-i-aa kasee-ai vannee charhai charhaa-o. Their bodies become golden, and take on the color of spirituality.
DEFINE	para 6175	jy hovY ndir srwP kI bhuiV n pweI qwau ] (146-12, mwJ, mÚ 2) jay hovai nadar saraaf kee bahurh na paa-ee taa-o. If the Jeweller casts His Glance of Grace, they are not placed in the fire again.
DEFINE	para 6176	sqI phrI squ Blw bhIAY piVAw pwis ] (146-12, mwJ, mÚ 2) satee pahree sat bhalaa bahee-ai parhi-aa paas. Throughout the other seven watches of the day, it is good to speak the Truth, and sit with the spiritually wise.
DEFINE	para 6177	EQY pwpu puMnu bIcwrIAY kUVY GtY rwis ] (146-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) othai paap punn beechaaree-ai koorhai ghatai raas. There, vice and virtue are distinguished, and the capital of falsehood is decreased.
DEFINE	para 6178	EQY Koty stIAih Kry kIcih swbwis ] (146-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) othai khotay satee-ah kharay keecheh saabaas. There, the counterfeit are cast aside, and the genuine are cheered.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	bolxu Pwdlu nwnkw duKu suKu KsmY pwis ]1] (146-14, mwJ, mÚ 2) bolan faadal naankaa dukh sukh khasmai paas. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	Speech is vain and useless. O Nanak, pain and pleasure are in the power of our Lord and Master. ||1||
RECORD	para 6180	mÚ 2 ] (146-14) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6181	pauxu gurU pwxI ipqw mwqw Driq mhqu ] (146-14, mwJ, mÚ 2) pa-un guroo paanee pitaa maataa Dharat mahat. Air is the Guru, Water is the Father, and Earth is the Great Mother of all.
DEFINE	para 6182	idnsu rwiq duie dweI dwieAw KylY sgl jgqu ] (146-15, mwJ, mÚ 2) dinas raat du-ay daa-ee daa-i-aa khaylai sagal jagat. Day and night are the two nurses, in whose lap all the world is at play.
DEFINE	para 6183	cMigAweIAw buirAweIAw vwcy Drmu hdUir ] (146-15, mwJ, mÚ 2) chang-aa-ee-aa buri-aa-ee-aa vaachay Dharam hadoor. Good deeds and bad deeds-the record is read out in the Presence of the Lord of Dharma.
DEFINE	para 6184	krmI Awpo AwpxI ky nyVY ky dUir ] (146-16, mwJ, mÚ 2) karmee aapo aapnee kay nayrhai kay door. According to their own actions, some are drawn closer, and some are driven farther away.
RECORD	para 6185	ijnI nwmu iDAwieAw gey mskiq Gwil ] (146-16, mwJ, mÚ 2) jinee naam Dhi-aa-i-aa ga-ay maskat ghaal. Those who have meditated on the Naam, the Name of the Lord, and departed after having worked by the sweat of their brow
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwnk qy muK aujly hor kyqI CutI nwil ]2] (146-17, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak tay mukh ujlay hor kaytee chhutee naal. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	-O Nanak, their faces are radiant in the Court of the Lord, and many others are saved along with them! ||2||
RECORD	para 6187	pauVI ] (146-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 6188	scw Bojnu Bwau siqguir disAw ] (146-17, mwJ, mÚ 2) sachaa bhojan bhaa-o satgur dasi-aa. The True Food is the Love of the Lord; the True Guru has spoken.
RECORD	para 6189	scy hI pqIAwie sic ivgisAw ] (146-18, mwJ, mÚ 2) sachay hee patee-aa-ay sach vigsi-aa. With this True Food, I am satisfied, and with the Truth, I am delighted.
DEFINE	para 6190	scY koit igrWie inj Gir visAw ] (146-18, mwJ, mÚ 2) sachai kot giraa N-ay nij ghar vasi-aa. True are the cities and the villages, where one abides in the True Home of the self.
DEFINE	para 6191	siqguir quTY nwau pRyim rhisAw ] (146-18, mwJ, mÚ 2) satgur tuthai naa-o paraym rehsi-aa. When the True Guru is pleased, one receives the Lord's Name, and blossoms forth in His Love.
RECORD	para 6192	scY dY dIbwix kUiV n jweIAY ] (146-19, mwJ, mÚ 2) sachai dai deebaan koorh na jaa-ee-ai. No one enters the Court of the True Lord through falsehood.
DEFINE	para 6193	JUTo JUTu vKwix su mhlu KuAweIAY ] (146-19, mwJ, mÚ 2) jhootho jhooth vakhaan so mahal khu-aa-ee-ai. By uttering falsehood and only falsehood, the Mansion of the Lord's Presence is lost.
DEFINE	para 6195	scY sbid nIswix Twk n pweIAY ] (147-1, mwJ, mÚ 2) sachai sabad neesaan thaak na paa-ee-ai. No one blocks the way of those who are blessed with the Banner of the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v18	scu suix buiJ vKwix mhil bulweIAY ]18] (147-1, mwJ, mÚ 2) sach sun bujh vakhaan mahal bulaa-ee-ai. ||18||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v18	Hearing, understanding and speaking Truth, one is called to the Mansion of the Lord's Presence. ||18||
RECORD	para 6197	sloku mÚ 1 ] (147-1) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
WHEN	para 6198	pihrw Agin ihvY Gru bwDw Bojnu swru krweI ] (147-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) pahiraa agan hivai ghar baaDhaa bhojan saar karaa-ee. If I dressed myself in fire, and built my house of snow, and made iron my food;
WHEN	para 6199	sgly dUK pwxI kir pIvw DrqI hwk clweI ] (147-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) saglay dookh paanee kar peevaa Dhartee haak chalaa-ee. and if I were to drink in all pain like water, and drive the entire earth before me;
WHEN	para 6200	Dir qwrwjI AMbru qolI ipCY tMku cVweI ] (147-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) Dhar taaraajee ambar tolee pichhai tank charhaa-ee. and if I were to place the earth upon a scale and balance it with a single copper coin;
WHEN	para 6201	eyvfu vDw mwvw nwhI sBsY niQ clweI ] (147-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) ayvad vaDhaa maavaa naahee sabhsai nath chalaa-ee. and if I were to become so great that I could not be contained, and if I were to control and lead all;
WHEN	para 6202	eyqw qwxu hovY mn AMdir krI iB AwiK krweI ] (147-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) aytaa taan hovai man andar karee bhe aakh karaa-ee. and if I were to possess so much power within my mind that I could cause others to do my bidding-so what?
DEFINE	para 6203	jyvfu swihbu qyvf dwqI dy dy kry rjweI ] (147-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) jayvad saahib tayvad daatee day day karay rajaa-ee. As Great as our Lord and Master is, so great are His gifts. He bestows them according to His Will.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nwnk ndir kry ijsu aupir sic nwim vifAweI ]1] (147-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak nadar karay jis upar sach naam vadi-aa-ee. ||1||
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	O Nanak, those upon whom the Lord casts His Glance of Grace, obtain the glorious greatness of the True Name. ||1||
RECORD	para 6205	mÚ 2 ] (147-5) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6206	AwKxu AwiK n rijAw sunix n rjy kMn ] (147-5, mwJ, mÚ 2) aakhan aakh na raji-aa sunan na rajay kann. The mouth is not satisfied by speaking, and the ears are not satisfied by hearing.
DEFINE	para 6207	AKI dyiK n rjIAw gux gwhk iek vMn ] (147-5, mwJ, mÚ 2) akhee daykh na rajee-aa gun gaahak ik vann. The eyes are not satisfied by seeing-each organ seeks out one sensory quality.
DEFINE	para 6208	BuiKAw BuK n auqrY glI BuK n jwie ] (147-6, mwJ, mÚ 2) bhukhi-aa bhukh na utrai galee bhukh na jaa-ay. The hunger of the hungry is not appeased; by mere words, hunger is not relieved.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwnk BuKw qw rjY jw gux kih guxI smwie ]2] (147-6, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak bhukhaa taa rajai jaa gun kahi gunee samaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	O Nanak, hunger is relieved only when one utters the Glorious Praises of the Praiseworthy Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 6210	pauVI ] (147-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 6211	ivxu scy sBu kUVu kUVu kmweIAY ] (147-7, mwJ, mÚ 2) vin sachay sabh koorh koorh kamaa-ee-ai. Without the True One, all are false, and all practice falsehood.
DEFINE	para 6212	ivxu scy kUiVAwru bMin clweIAY ] (147-7, mwJ, mÚ 2) vin sachay koorhi-aar bann chalaa-ee-ai. Without the True One, the false ones are bound and gagged and driven off.
DEFINE	para 6213	ivxu scy qnu Cwru Cwru rlweIAY ] (147-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) vin sachay tan chhaar chhaar ralaa-ee-ai. Without the True One, the body is just ashes, and it mingles again with ashes.
DEFINE	para 6214	ivxu scy sB BuK ij pYJY KweIAY ] (147-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) vin sachay sabh bhukh je paijhai khaa-ee-ai. Without the True Ome, all food and clothes are unsatisfying.
RECORD	para 6215	ivxu scy drbwru kUiV n pweIAY ] (147-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) vin sachay darbaar koorh na paa-ee-ai. Without the True One, the false ones do not attain the Lord's Court.
DEFINE	para 6216	kUVY lwlic lig mhlu KuAweIAY ] (147-9, mwJ, mÚ 2) koorhai laalach lag mahal khu-aa-ee-ai. Attached to false attachments, the Mansion of the Lord's Presence is lost.
DEFINE	para 6217	sBu jgu TigE Tig AweIAY jweIAY ] (147-9, mwJ, mÚ 2) sabh jag thagi-o thag aa-ee-ai jaa-ee-ai. The whole world is deceived by deception, coming and going in reincarnation.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v19	qn mih iqRsnw Aig sbid buJweIAY ]19] (147-9, mwJ, mÚ 2) tan meh tarisnaa ag sabad bujhaa-ee-ai. ||19||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v19	Within the body is the fire of desire; through the Word of the Shabad, it is quenched. ||19||
RECORD	para 6219	slok mÚ 1 ] (147-10) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6220	nwnk guru sMqoKu ruKu Drmu Pulu Pl igAwnu ] (147-10, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak gur santokh rukh Dharam ful fal gi-aan. O Nanak, the Guru is the tree of contentment, with flowers of faith, and fruits of spiritual wisdom.
RECORD	para 6221	ris risAw hirAw sdw pkY krim iDAwin ] (147-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) ras rasi-aa hari-aa sadaa pakai karam Dhi-aan. Watered with the Lord's Love, it remains forever green; through the karma of good deeds and meditation, it ripens.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	piq ky swd Kwdw lhY dwnw kY isir dwnu ]1] (147-11, mwJ, mÚ 1) pat kay saad khaadaa lahai daanaa kai sir daan. ||1||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	Honor is obtained by eating this tasty dish; of all gifts, this is the greatest gift. ||1||
RECORD	para 6223	mÚ 1 ] (147-12) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6224	suieny kw ibrKu pq prvwlw Pul jvyhr lwl ] (147-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) su-inay kaa birakh pat parvaalaa ful javayhar laal. The Guru is the tree of gold, with leaves of coral, and blossoms of jewels and rubies.
DEFINE	para 6225	iqqu Pl rqn lgih muiK BwiKq ihrdY irdY inhwlu ] (147-12, mwJ, mÚ 1) tit fal ratan lageh mukh bhaakhit hirdai ridai nihaal. The Words from His Mouth are fruits of jewels. Within His Heart, He beholds the Lord.
RECORD	para 6226	nwnk krmu hovY muiK msqik iliKAw hovY lyKu ] (147-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak karam hovai mukh mastak likhi-aa hovai laykh. O Nanak, He is obtained by those, upon whose faces and foreheads such pre-recorded destiny is written.
RECORD	para 6227	AiTsiT qIrQ gur kI crxI pUjY sdw ivsyKu ] (147-13, mwJ, mÚ 1) athisath tirath gur kee charnee poojai sadaa visaykh. The sixty-eight sacred shrines of pilgrimage are contained in the constant worship of the feet of the Exalted Guru.
DEFINE	para 6228	hMsu hyqu loBu kopu cwry ndIAw Aig ] (147-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) hans hayt lobh kop chaaray nadee-aa ag. Cruelty, material attachment, greed and anger are the four rivers of fire.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	pvih dJih nwnkw qrIAY krmI lig ]2] (147-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) paveh dajheh naankaa taree-ai karmee lag. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	Falling into them, one is burned, O Nanak! One is saved only by holding tight to good deeds. ||2||
RECORD	para 6230	pauVI ] (147-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
REQUIRE	para 6231	jIvidAw mru mwir n pCoqweIAY ] (147-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) jeevdi-aa mar maar na pachhotaa-ee-ai. While you are alive, conquer death, and you shall have no regrets in the end.
DEFINE	para 6232	JUTw iehu sMswru ikin smJweIAY ] (147-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) jhoothaa ih sansaar kin samjaa-ee-ai. This world is false, but only a few understand this.
RECORD	para 6233	sic n Dry ipAwru DMDY DweIAY ] (147-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) sach na Dharay pi-aar DhanDhai Dhaa-ee-ai. People do not enshrine love for the Truth; they chase after worldly affairs instead.
RECORD	para 6234	kwlu burw KY kwlu isir dunIAweIAY ] (147-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) kaal buraa khai kaal sir dunee-aa-ee-ai. The terrible time of death and annihilation hovers over the heads of the world.
RECORD	para 6235	hukmI isir jMdwru mwry dweIAY ] (147-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) hukmee sir jandaar maaray daa-ee-ai. By the Hukam of the Lord's Command, the Messenger of Death smashes his club over their heads.
RECORD	para 6236	Awpy dyie ipAwru mMin vsweIAY ] (147-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) aapay day-ay pi-aar man vasaa-ee-ai. The Lord Himself gives His Love, and enshrines it within their minds.
ALLOW	para 6237	muhqu n csw ivlµmu BrIAY pweIAY ] (147-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) muhat na chasaa vilamm bharee-ai paa-ee-ai. Not a moment or an instant's delay is permitted, when one's measure of life is full.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v20	gur prswdI buiJ sic smweIAY ]20] (147-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee bujh sach samaa-ee-ai. ||20||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v20	By Guru's Grace, one comes to know the True One, and is absorbed into Him. ||20||
RECORD	para 6239	sloku mÚ 1 ] (147-18) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 6240	qumI qumw ivsu Aku DqUrw inmu Plu ] (147-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) tumee tumaa vis ak Dhatooraa nim fal. Bitter melon, swallow-wort, thorn-apple and nim fruit
RECORD	para 6241	min muiK vsih iqsu ijsu qUM iciq n AwvhI ] (147-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) man mukh vaseh tis jis tooN chit na aavhee. -these bitter poisons lodge in the minds and mouths of those who do not remember You.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	nwnk khIAY iksu hMFin krmw bwhry ]1] (147-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak kahee-ai kis handhan karmaa baahray. ||1||
REQUIRE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v1	O Nanak, how shall I tell them this? Without the karma of good deeds, they are only destroying themselves. ||1||
RECORD	para 6243	mÚ 1 ] (147-19) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6244	miq pMKyrU ikrqu swiQ kb auqm kb nIc ] (147-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) mat pankhayroo kirat saath kab utam kab neech. The intellect is a bird; on account of its actions, it is sometimes high, and sometimes low.
RECORD	para 6246	kb cMdin kb Aik fwil kb aucI prIiq ] (148-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) kab chandan kab ak daal kab uchee pareet. Sometimes it is perched on the sandalwood tree, and sometimes it is on the branch of the poisonous swallow-wort. Sometimes, it soars through the heavens.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	nwnk hukim clweIAY swihb lgI rIiq ]2] (148-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak hukam chalaa-ee-ai saahib lagee reet. ||2||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v2	O Nanak, our Lord and Master leads us on, according to the Hukam of His Command; such is His Way. ||2||
RECORD	para 6248	pauVI ] (148-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 6249	kyqy khih vKwx kih kih jwvxw ] (148-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) kaytay kaheh vakhaan kahi kahi jaavnaa. Some speak and expound, and while speaking and lecturing, they pass away.
RECORD	para 6250	vyd khih viKAwx AMqu n pwvxw ] (148-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) vayd kaheh vakhi-aan ant na paavnaa. The Vedas speak and expound on the Lord, but they do not know His limits.
DEFINE	para 6251	piVAY nwhI Bydu buiJAY pwvxw ] (148-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) parhi-ai naahee bhayd bujhi-ai paavnaa. Not by studying, but through understanding, is the Lord's Mystery revealed.
DEFINE	para 6252	Ktu drsn kY ByiK iksY sic smwvxw ] (148-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) khat darsan kai bhaykh kisai sach samaavnaa. There are six pathways in the Shaastras, but how rare are those who merge in the True Lord through them.
DEFINE	para 6253	scw purKu AlKu sbid suhwvxw ] (148-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachaa purakh alakh sabad suhaavanaa. The True Lord is Unknowable; through the Word of His Shabad, we are embellished.
RECORD	para 6254	mMny nwau ibsMK drgh pwvxw ] (148-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) mannay naa-o bisankh dargeh paavnaa. One who believes in the Name of the Infinite Lord, attains the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	para 6255	Kwlk kau Awdysu FwFI gwvxw ] (148-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) khaalak ka-o aadays dhaadhee gaavnaa. I humbly bow to the Creator Lord; I am a minstrel singing His Praises.
RECORD	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v21	nwnk jugu jugu eyku mMin vswvxw ]21] (148-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak jug jug ayk man vasaavnaa. ||21||
DEFINE	mwJ mhlw 5 idn rYix v21	Nanak enshrines the Lord within his mind. He is the One, throughout the ages. ||21||
RECORD	para 6257	salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 6258	mMqRI hoie ATUihAw nwgI lgY jwie ] Awpx hQI AwpxY dy kUcw Awpy lwie ] (148-5, mwJ, mÚ 2) mantree ho-ay athoohi-aa naagee lagai jaa-ay. aapan hathee aapnai day koochaa aapay laa-ay. Those who charm scorpions and handle snakes only brand themselves with their own hands.
DEFINE	para 6259	hukmu pieAw Duir Ksm kw AqI hU Dkw Kwie ] (148-6, mwJ, mÚ 2) hukam pa-i-aa Dhur khasam kaa atee hoo Dhakaa khaa-ay. By the pre-ordained Order of our Lord and Master, they are beaten badly, and struck down.
DEFINE	para 6260	gurmuK isau mnmuKu AVY fubY hik inAwie ] (148-6, mwJ, mÚ 2) gurmukh si-o manmukh arhai dubai hak ni-aa-ay. If the self-willed manmukhs fight with the Gurmukh, they are condemned by the Lord, the True Judge.
DEFINE	para 6261	duhw isirAw Awpy Ksmu vyKY kir ivaupwie ] (148-7, mwJ, mÚ 2) duhaa siri-aa aapay khasam vaykhai kar vi-upaa-ay. He Himself is the Lord and Master of both worlds. He beholds all and makes the exact determination.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v1	nwnk eyvY jwxIAY sB ikCu iqsih rjwie ]1] (148-7, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak ayvai jaanee-ai sabh kichh tiseh rajaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, know this well: everything is in accordance with His Will. ||1||
RECORD	para 6263	mhlw 2 ] (148-8) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6264	nwnk prKy Awp kau qw pwrKu jwxu ] (148-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak parkhay aap ka-o taa paarakh jaan. O Nanak, if someone judges himself, only then is he known as a real judge.
DEFINE	para 6265	rogu dwrU dovY buJY qw vYdu sujwxu ] (148-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) rog daaroo dovai bujhai taa vaid sujaan. If someone understands both the disease and the medicine, only then is he a wise physician.
DEFINE	para 6266	vwt n kreI mwmlw jwxY imhmwxu ] (148-9, mwJ, mÚ 2) vaat na kar-ee maamlaa jaanai mihmaan. Do not involve yourself in idle business on the way; remember that you are only a guest here.
RECORD	para 6267	mUlu jwix glw kry hwix lwey hwxu ] (148-9, mwJ, mÚ 2) mool jaan galaa karay haan laa-ay haan. Speak with those who know the Primal Lord, and renounce your evil ways.
RECORD	para 6268	lib n cleI sic rhY so ivstu prvwxu ] (148-10, mwJ, mÚ 2) lab na chal-ee sach rahai so visat parvaan. That virtuous person who does not walk in the way of greed, and who abides in Truth, is accepted and famous.
DEFINE	para 6269	sru sMDy Awgws kau ikau phucY bwxu ] (148-10, mwJ, mÚ 2) sar sanDhay aagaas ka-o ki-o pahuchai baan. If an arrow is shot at the sky, how can it reach there?
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v2	AgY Ehu AgMmu hY vwhydVu jwxu ]2] (148-10, mwJ, mÚ 2) agai oh agamm hai vaahaydarh jaan. ||2||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v2	The sky above is unreachable-know this well, O archer! ||2||
RECORD	para 6271	pauVI ] (148-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 6272	nwrI purK ipAwru pRyim sIgwrIAw ] (148-11, mwJ, mÚ 2) naaree purakh pi-aar paraym seegaaree-aa. The soul-bride loves her Husband Lord; she is embellished with His Love.
RECORD	para 6273	krin Bgiq idnu rwiq n rhnI vwrIAw ] (148-11, mwJ, mÚ 2) karan bhagat din raat na rahnee vaaree-aa. She worships Him day and night; she cannot be restrained from doing so.
DEFINE	para 6274	mhlw mMiJ invwsu sbid svwrIAw ] (148-12, mwJ, mÚ 2) mehlaa manjh nivaas sabad savaaree-aa. In the Mansion of the Lord's Presence, she has made her home; she is adorned with the Word of His Shabad.
DEFINE	para 6275	scu khin Ardwis sy vycwrIAw ] (148-12, mwJ, mÚ 2) sach kahan ardaas say vaychaaree-aa. She is humble, and she offers her true and sincere prayer.
DEFINE	para 6276	sohin KsmY pwis hukim isDwrIAw ] (148-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) sohan khasmai paas hukam siDhaaree-aa. She is beautiful in the Company of her Lord and Master; she walks in the Way of His Will.
RECORD	para 6277	sKI khin Ardwis mnhu ipAwrIAw ] (148-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) sakhee kahan ardaas manhu pi-aaree-aa. With her dear friends, she offers her heart-felt prayers to her Beloved.
DEFINE	para 6278	ibnu nwvY iDRgu vwsu iPtu su jIivAw ] (148-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) bin naavai Dharig vaas fit so jeevi-aa. Cursed is that home, and shameful is that life, which is without the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v22	sbid svwrIAwsu AMimRqu pIivAw ]22] (148-14, mwJ, mÚ 2) sabad savaaree-aas amrit peevi-aa. ||22||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v22	But she who is adorned with the Word of His Shabad, drinks in the Amrit of His Nectar. ||22||
RECORD	para 6280	sloku mÚ 1 ] (148-14) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6281	mwrU mIih n iqRpiqAw AgI lhY n BuK ] (148-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) maaroo meehi na taripti-aa agee lahai na bhukh. The desert is not satisfied by rain, and the fire is not quenched by desire.
DEFINE	para 6282	rwjw rwij n iqRpiqAw swier Bry iksuk ] (148-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) raajaa raaj na taripti-aa saa-ir bharay kisuk. The king is not satisfied with his kingdom, and the oceans are full, but still they thirst for more.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v1	nwnk scy nwm kI kyqI puCw puC ]1] (148-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak sachay naam kee kaytee puchhaa puchh. ||1||
REQUIRE	sloku mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, how many times must I seek and ask for the True Name? ||1||
RECORD	para 6284	mhlw 2 ] (148-16) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6285	inhPlµ qis jnmis jwvqu bRhm n ibMdqy ] (148-16, mwJ, mÚ 2) nihfala N tas janmas jaavat barahm na bindtay. Life is useless, as long as one does not know the Lord God.
RECORD	para 6286	swgrM sMswris gur prswdI qrih ky ] (148-16, mwJ, mÚ 2) saagraN sansaaras gur parsaadee tareh kay. Only a few cross over the world-ocean, by Guru's Grace.
DEFINE	para 6287	krx kwrx smrQu hY khu nwnk bIcwir ] (148-17, mwJ, mÚ 2) karan kaaran samrath hai kaho naanak beechaar. The Lord is the All-powerful Cause of causes, says Nanak after deep deliberation.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v2	kwrxu krqy vis hY ijin kl rKI Dwir ]2] (148-17, mwJ, mÚ 2) kaaran kartay vas hai jin kal rakhee Dhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v2	The creation is subject to the Creator, who sustains it by His Almighty Power. ||2||
RECORD	para 6289	pauVI ] (148-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 6290	KsmY kY drbwir FwFI visAw ] (148-18, mwJ, mÚ 2) khasmai kai darbaar dhaadhee vasi-aa. In the Court of the Lord and Master, His minstrels dwell.
RECORD	para 6291	scw Ksmu klwix kmlu ivgisAw ] (148-18, mwJ, mÚ 2) sachaa khasam kalaan kamal vigsi-aa. Singing the Praises of their True Lord and Master, the lotuses of their hearts have blossomed forth.
DEFINE	para 6292	Ksmhu pUrw pwie mnhu rhisAw ] (148-19, mwJ, mÚ 2) khasmahu pooraa paa-ay manhu rehsi-aa. Obtaining their Perfect Lord and Master, their minds are transfixed with ecstasy.
DEFINE	para 6293	dusmn kFy mwir sjx srisAw ] (148-19, mwJ, mÚ 2) dusman kadhay maar sajan sarsi-aa. Their enemies have been driven out and subdued, and their friends are very pleased.
DEFINE	para 6294	scw siqguru syvin scw mwrgu disAw ] (148-19, mwJ, mÚ 2) sachaa satgur sayvan sachaa maarag dasi-aa. Those who serve the Truthful True Guru are shown the True Path.
DEFINE	para 6296	scw sbdu bIcwir kwlu ivDauisAw ] (149-1, mwJ, mÚ 2) sachaa sabad beechaar kaal viDh-usi-aa. Reflecting on the True Word of the Shabad, death is overcome.
DEFINE	para 6297	FwFI kQy AkQu sbid svwirAw ] (149-1, mwJ, mÚ 2) dhaadhee kathay akath sabad savaari-aa. Speaking the Unspoken Speech of the Lord, one is adorned with the Word of His Shabad.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v23	nwnk gux gih rwis hir jIau imly ipAwirAw ]23] (149-1, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak gun geh raas har jee-o milay pi-aari-aa. ||23||
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v23	Nanak holds tight to the Treasure of Virtue, and meets with the Dear, Beloved Lord. ||23||
RECORD	para 6299	sloku mÚ 1 ] (149-2) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
ALLOW	para 6300	KiqAhu jMmy Kqy krin q KiqAw ivic pwih ] (149-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) khati-ahu jammay khatay karan ta khati-aa vich paahi. Born because of the karma of their past mistakes, they make more mistakes, and fall into mistakes.
ALLOW	para 6301	Doqy mUil n auqrih jy sau Dovx pwih ] (149-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) Dhotay mool na utreh jay sa-o Dhovan paahi. By washing, their pollution is not removed, even though they may wash hundreds of times.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v1	nwnk bKsy bKsIAih nwih q pwhI pwih ]1] (149-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak bakhsay bakhsee-ahi naahi ta paahee paahi. ||1||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, if God forgives, they are forgiven; otherwise, they are kicked and beaten. ||1||
RECORD	para 6303	mÚ 1 ] (149-4) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6304	nwnk bolxu JKxw duK Cif mMgIAih suK ] (149-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak bolan jhakh-naa dukh chhad mangee-ah sukh. O Nanak, it is absurd to ask to be spared from pain by begging for comfort.
DEFINE	para 6305	suKu duKu duie dir kpVy pihrih jwie mnuK ] (149-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) sukh dukh du-ay dar kaprhay pahirahi jaa-ay manukh. Pleasure and pain are the two garments given, to be worn in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v2	ijQY bolix hwrIAY iqQY cMgI cup ]2] (149-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) jithai bolan haaree-ai tithai changee chup. ||2||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v2	Where you are bound to lose by speaking, there, you ought to remain silent. ||2||
RECORD	para 6307	pauVI ] (149-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 6308	cwry kuMfw dyiK AMdru BwilAw ] (149-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) chaaray kundaa daykh andar bhaali-aa. After looking around in the four directions, I looked within my own self.
RECORD	para 6309	scY puriK AliK isrij inhwilAw ] (149-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachai purakh alakh siraj nihaali-aa. There, I saw the True, Invisible Lord Creator.
RECORD	para 6310	auJiV Buly rwh guir vyKwilAw ] (149-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) ujharh bhulay raah gur vaykhaali-aa. I was wandering in the wilderness, but now the Guru has shown me the Way.
RECORD	para 6311	siqgur scy vwhu scu smwilAw ] (149-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) satgur sachay vaahu sach samaali-aa. Hail to the True, True Guru, through whom we merge in the Truth.
RECORD	para 6312	pwieAw rqnu Grwhu dIvw bwilAw ] (149-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) paa-i-aa ratan gharaahu deevaa baali-aa. I have found the jewel within the home of my own self; the lamp within has been lit.
RECORD	para 6313	scY sbid slwih suKIey sc vwilAw ] (149-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachai sabad salaahi sukhee-ay sach vaali-aa. Those who praise the True Word of the Shabad, abide in the peace of Truth.
DEFINE	para 6314	infirAw fru lig grib is gwilAw ] (149-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) nidri-aa dar lag garab se gaali-aa. But those who do not have the Fear of God, are overtaken by fear. They are destroyed by their own pride.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v24	nwvhu Bulw jgu iPrY byqwilAw ]24] (149-8, mwJ, mÚ 1) naavhu bhulaa jag firai baytaali-aa. ||24||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v24	Having forgotten the Name, the world is roaming around like a wild demon. ||24||
RECORD	para 6316	sloku mÚ 3 ] (149-8) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 6317	BY ivic jMmY BY mrY BI Bau mn mih hoie ] (149-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) bhai vich jammai bhai marai bhee bha-o man meh ho-ay. In fear we are born, and in fear we die. Fear is always present in the mind.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v1	nwnk BY ivic jy mrY sihlw AwieAw soie ]1] (149-9, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak bhai vich jay marai sahilaa aa-i-aa so-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, if one dies in the fear of God, his coming into the world is blessed and approved. ||1||
RECORD	para 6319	mÚ 3 ] (149-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
ALLOW	para 6320	BY ivxu jIvY bhuqu bhuqu KusIAw KusI kmwie ] (149-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) bhai vin jeevai bahut bahut khusee-aa khusee kamaa-ay. Without the fear of God, you may live very, very long, and savor the most enjoyable pleasures.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v2	nwnk BY ivxu jy mrY muih kwlY auiT jwie ]2] (149-10, mwJ, mÚ 3) naanak bhai vin jay marai muhi kaalai uth jaa-ay. ||2||
WHEN	sloku mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, if you die without the fear of God, you will arise and depart with a blackened face. ||2||
RECORD	para 6322	pauVI ] (149-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 6323	siqguru hoie dieAwlu q srDw pUrIAY ] (149-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal ta sarDhaa pooree-ai. When the True Guru is merciful, then your desires will be fulfilled.
DEFINE	para 6324	siqguru hoie dieAwlu n kbhUM JUrIAY ] (149-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal na kabahoo N jhooree-ai. When the True Guru is merciful, you will never grieve.
DEFINE	para 6325	siqguru hoie dieAwlu qw duKu n jwxIAY ] (149-11, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal taa dukh na jaanee-ai. When the True Guru is merciful, you will know no pain.
DEFINE	para 6326	siqguru hoie dieAwlu qw hir rMgu mwxIAY ] (149-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal taa har rang maanee-ai. When the True Guru is merciful, you will enjoy the Lord's Love.
DEFINE	para 6327	siqguru hoie dieAwlu qw jm kw fru kyhw ] (149-12, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal taa jam kaa dar kayhaa. When the True Guru is merciful, then why should you fear death?
DEFINE	para 6328	siqguru hoie dieAwlu qw sd hI suKu dyhw ] (149-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal taa sad hee sukh dayhaa. When the True Guru is merciful, the body is always at peace.
DEFINE	para 6329	siqguru hoie dieAwlu qw nv iniD pweIAY ] (149-13, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal taa nav niDh paa-ee-ai. When the True Guru is merciful, the nine treasures are obtained.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v25	siqguru hoie dieAwlu q sic smweIAY ]25] (149-14, mwJ, mÚ 3) satgur ho-ay da-i-aal ta sach samaa-ee-ai. ||25||
REQUIRE	sloku mhlw 2 v25	When the True Guru is merciful, you shall be absorbed in the True Lord. ||25||
RECORD	para 6331	sloku mÚ 1 ] (149-14) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 6332	isru Kohwie pIAih mlvwxI jUTw mMig mMig KwhI ] (149-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) sir khohaa-ay pee-ah malvaanee joothaa mang mang khaahee. They pluck the hair out of their heads, and drink in filthy water; they beg endlessly and eat the garbage which others have thrown away.
DEFINE	para 6333	Poil PdIhiq muih lYin BVwsw pwxI dyiK sgwhI ] (149-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) fol fadeehat muhi lain bharhaasaa paanee daykh sagaahee. They spread manure, they suck in rotting smells, and they are afraid of clean water.
DEFINE	para 6334	Byfw vwgI isru Kohwiein BrIAin hQ suAwhI ] (149-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) bhaydaa vaagee sir khohaa-in bharee-an hath su-aahee. Their hands are smeared with ashes, and the hair on their heads is plucked out-they are like sheep!
RECORD	para 6335	mwaU pIaU ikrqu gvwiein tbr rovin DwhI ] (149-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) maa-oo pee-oo kirat gavaa-in tabar rovan Dhaahee. They have renounced the lifestyle of their mothers and fathers, and their families and relatives cry out in distress.
RECORD	para 6336	Enw ipMfu n pqil ikirAw n dIvw muey ikQwaU pwhI ] (149-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) onaa pind na patal kiri-aa na deevaa mu-ay kithaa-oo paahee. No one offers the rice dishes at their last rites, and no one lights the lamps for them. After their death, where will they be sent?
RECORD	para 6337	ATsiT qIrQ dyin n FoeI bRhmx AMnu n KwhI ] (149-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) athsath tirath dayn na dho-ee barahman ann na khaahee. The sixty-eight sacred shrines of pilgrimage give them no place of protection, and no Brahmin will eat their food.
RECORD	para 6338	sdw kucIl rhih idnu rwqI mQY itky nwhI ] (149-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) sadaa kucheel raheh din raatee mathai tikay naahee. They remain polluted forever, day and night; they do not apply the ceremonial tilak mark to their foreheads.
WHEN	para 6339	JuMfI pwie bhin iniq mrxY diV dIbwix n jwhI ] (149-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) jhundee paa-ay bahan nit marnai darh deebaan na jaahee. They sit together in silence, as if in mourning; they do not go to the Lord's Court.
RECORD	para 6340	lkI kwsy hQI PuMmx Ago ipCI jwhI ] (149-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) lakee kaasay hathee fumman ago pichhee jaahee. With their begging bowls hanging from their waists, and their fly-brushes in their hands, they walk along in single file.
DEFINE	para 6341	nw Eie jogI nw Eie jMgm nw Eie kwjI muMlw ] (149-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) naa o-ay jogee naa o-ay jangam naa o-ay kaajee mu Nlaa. They are not Yogis, and they are not Jangams, followers of Shiva. They are not Qazis or Mullahs.
RECORD	para 6343	diX ivgoey iPrih ivguqy iPtw vqY glw ] (150-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) da-yi vigo-ay fireh vigutay fitaa vatai galaa. Ruined by the Merciful Lord, they wander around in disgrace, and their entire troop is contaminated.
RECORD	para 6344	jIAw mwir jIvwly soeI Avru n koeI rKY ] (150-1, mwJ, mÚ 1) jee-aa maar jeevaalay so-ee avar na ko-ee rakhai. The Lord alone kills and restores to life; no one else can protect anyone from Him.
RECORD	para 6345	dwnhu qY iesnwnhu vMjy Bsu peI isir KuQY ] (150-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) daanhu tai isnaanhu vanjay bhas pa-ee sir khuthai. They go without giving alms or any cleansing baths; their shaven heads become covered with dust.
WHEN	para 6346	pwxI ivchu rqn aupMny myru kIAw mwDwxI ] (150-2, mwJ, mÚ 1) paanee vichahu ratan upannay mayr kee-aa maaDhaanee. The jewel emerged from the water, when the mountain of gold was used to churn it.
RECORD	para 6347	ATsiT qIrQ dyvI Qwpy purbI lgY bwxI ] (150-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) athsath tirath dayvee thaapay purbee lagai banee. The gods established the sixty-eight sacred shrines of pilgrimage, where the festivals are celebrated and hymns are chanted.
RECORD	para 6348	nwie invwjw nwqY pUjw nwvin sdw sujwxI ] (150-3, mwJ, mÚ 1) naa-ay nivaajaa naatai poojaa naavan sadaa sujaanee. After bathing, the Muslims recite their prayers, and after bathing, the Hindus perform their worship services. The wise always take cleansing baths.
WHEN	para 6349	muieAw jIvidAw giq hovY jW isir pweIAY pwxI ] (150-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) mu-i-aa jeevdi-aa gat hovai jaa N sir paa-ee-ai paanee. At the time of death, and at the time of birth, they are purified, when water is poured on their heads.
DEFINE	para 6350	nwnk isrKuQy sYqwnI eynw gl n BwxI ] (150-4, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak sirkhutay saitaanee aynaa gal na bhaanee. O Nanak, the shaven-headed ones are devils. They are not pleased to hear these words.
DEFINE	para 6351	vuTY hoieAY hoie iblwvlu jIAw jugiq smwxI ] (150-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) vuthai ho-i-ai ho-ay bilaaval jee-aa jugat samaanee. When it rains, there is happiness. Water is the key to all life.
WHEN	para 6352	vuTY AMnu kmwdu kpwhw sBsY pVdw hovY ] (150-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) vuthai ann kamaad kapaahaa sabhsai parh-daa hovai. When it rains, the corn grows, and the sugar cane, and the cotton, which provides clothing for all.
WHEN	para 6353	vuTY Gwhu crih iniq surhI sw Dn dhI ivlovY ] (150-5, mwJ, mÚ 1) vuthai ghaahu chareh nit surhee saa Dhan dahee vilovai. When it rains, the cows always have grass to graze upon, and housewives can churn the milk into butter.
DEFINE	para 6354	iqqu iGie hom jg sd pUjw pieAY kwrju sohY ] (150-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) tit ghi-ay hom jag sad poojaa pa-i-ai kaaraj sohai. With that ghee, sacred feasts and worship services are performed; all these efforts are blessed.
RECORD	para 6355	gurU smuMdu ndI siB isKI nwqY ijqu vifAweI ] (150-6, mwJ, mÚ 1) guroo samund nadee sabh sikhee naatai jit vadi-aa-ee. The Guru is the ocean, and all His Teachings are the river. Bathing within it, glorious greatness is obtained.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v1	nwnk jy isrKuQy nwvin nwhI qw sq cty isir CweI ]1] (150-7, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak jay sirkhutay naavan naahee taa sat chatay sir chhaa-ee. ||1||
WHEN	sloku mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, if the shaven-headed ones do not bathe, then seven handfuls of ashes are upon their heads. ||1||
RECORD	para 6357	mÚ 2 ] (150-8) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 6358	AgI pwlw ik kry sUrj kyhI rwiq ] (150-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) agee paalaa ke karay sooraj kayhee raat. What can the cold do to the fire? How can the night affect the sun?
RECORD	para 6359	cMd Anyrw ik kry paux pwxI ikAw jwiq ] (150-8, mwJ, mÚ 2) chand anayraa ke karay pa-un paanee ki-aa jaat. What can the darkness do to the moon? What can social status do to air and water?
DEFINE	para 6360	DrqI cIjI ik kry ijsu ivic sBu ikCu hoie ] (150-9, mwJ, mÚ 2) Dhartee cheejee ke karay jis vich sabh kichh ho-ay. What are personal possessions to the earth, from which all things are produced?
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v2	nwnk qw piq jwxIAY jw piq rKY soie ]2] (150-9, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak taa pat jaanee-ai jaa pat rakhai so-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, he alone is known as honorable, whose honor the Lord preserves. ||2||
RECORD	para 6362	pauVI ] (150-9) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 6363	quDu scy subhwnu sdw klwixAw ] (150-10, mwJ, mÚ 2) tuDh sachay sub-haan sadaa kalaani-aa. It is of You, O my True and Wondrous Lord, that I sing forever.
DEFINE	para 6364	qUM scw dIbwxu hoir Awvx jwixAw ] (150-10, mwJ, mÚ 2) tooN sachaa deebaan hor aavan jaani-aa. Yours is the True Court. All others are subject to coming and going.
DEFINE	para 6365	scu ij mMgih dwnu is quDY jyihAw ] (150-10, mwJ, mÚ 2) sach je mangeh daan se tuDhai jayhi-aa. Those who ask for the gift of the True Name are like You.
DEFINE	para 6366	scu qyrw Purmwnu sbdy soihAw ] (150-11, mwJ, mÚ 2) sach tayraa furmaan sabday sohi-aa. Your Command is True; we are adorned with the Word of Your Shabad.
UPHOLD	para 6367	mMinAY igAwnu iDAwnu quDY qy pwieAw ] (150-11, mwJ, mÚ 2) mani-ai gi-aan Dhi-aan tuDhai tay paa-i-aa. Through faith and trust, we receive spiritual wisdom and meditation from You.
DEFINE	para 6368	krim pvY nIswnu n clY clwieAw ] (150-11, mwJ, mÚ 2) karam pavai neesaan na chalai chalaa-i-aa. By Your Grace, the banner of honor is obtained. It cannot be taken away or lost.
DEFINE	para 6369	qUM scw dwqwru inq dyvih cVih svwieAw ] (150-12, mwJ, mÚ 2) tooN sachaa daataar nit dayveh charheh savaa-i-aa. You are the True Giver; You give continually. Your Gifts continue to increase.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v26	nwnku mMgY dwnu jo quDu BwieAw ]26] (150-12, mwJ, mÚ 2) naanak mangai daan jo tuDh bhaa-i-aa. ||26||
DEFINE	sloku mhlw 2 v26	Nanak begs for that gift which is pleasing to You. ||26||
RECORD	para 6371	sloku mÚ 2 ] (150-13) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 6372	dIiKAw AwiK buJwieAw isPqI sic smyau ] (150-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) deekhi-aa aakh bujhaa-i-aa siftee sach samay-o. Those who have accepted the Guru's Teachings, and who have found the path, remain absorbed in the Praises of the True Lord.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v1	iqn kau ikAw aupdysIAY ijn guru nwnk dyau ]1] (150-13, mwJ, mÚ 2) tin ka-o ki-aa updaysee-ai jin gur naanak day-o. ||1||
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v1	What teachings can be imparted to those who have the Divine Guru Nanak as their Guru? ||1||
RECORD	para 6374	mÚ 1 ] (150-14) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
WHEN	para 6375	Awip buJwey soeI bUJY ] (150-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) aap bujhaa-ay so-ee boojhai. We understand the Lord only when He Himself inspires us to understand Him.
RECORD	para 6376	ijsu Awip suJwey iqsu sBu ikCu sUJY ] (150-14, mwJ, mÚ 1) jis aap sujhaa-ay tis sabh kichh soojhai. He alone knows everything, unto whom the Lord Himself gives knowledge.
ALLOW	para 6377	kih kih kQnw mwieAw lUJY ] (150-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) kahi kahi kathnaa maa-i-aa loojhai. One may talk and preach and give sermons but still yearn after Maya.
RECORD	para 6378	hukmI sgl kry Awkwr ] (150-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) hukmee sagal karay aakaar. The Lord, by the Hukam of His Command, has created the entire creation.
RECORD	para 6379	Awpy jwxY srb vIcwr ] (150-15, mwJ, mÚ 1) aapay jaanai sarab veechaar. He Himself knows the inner nature of all.
RECORD	para 6380	AKr nwnk AiKE Awip ] (150-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) akhar naanak akhi-o aap. O Nanak, He Himself uttered the Word.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v2	lhY Brwiq hovY ijsu dwiq ]2] (150-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) lahai bharaat hovai jis daat. ||2||
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v2	Doubt departs from one who receives this gift. ||2||
RECORD	para 6382	pauVI ] (150-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
WHEN	para 6383	hau FwFI vykwru kwrY lwieAw ] (150-16, mwJ, mÚ 1) ha-o dhaadhee vaykaar kaarai laa-i-aa. I was a minstrel, out of work, when the Lord took me into His service.
RECORD	para 6384	rwiq idhY kY vwr Durhu PurmwieAw ] (150-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) raat dihai kai vaar Dharahu furmaa-i-aa. To sing His Praises day and night, He gave me His Order, right from the start.
RECORD	para 6385	FwFI scY mhil Ksim bulwieAw ] (150-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) dhaadhee sachai mahal khasam bulaa-i-aa. My Lord and Master has summoned me, His minstrel, to the True Mansion of His Presence.
RECORD	para 6386	scI isPiq swlwh kpVw pwieAw ] (150-17, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachee sifat saalaah kaprhaa paa-i-aa. He has dressed me in the robes of His True Praise and Glory.
RECORD	para 6387	scw AMimRq nwmu Bojnu AwieAw ] (150-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) sachaa amrit naam bhojan aa-i-aa. The Ambrosial Nectar of the True Name has become my food.
DEFINE	para 6388	gurmqI KwDw rij iqin suKu pwieAw ] (150-18, mwJ, mÚ 1) gurmatee khaaDhaa raj tin sukh paa-i-aa. Those who follow the Guru's Teachings, who eat this food and are satisfied, find peace.
RECORD	para 6389	FwFI kry pswau sbdu vjwieAw ] (150-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) dhaadhee karay pasaa-o sabad vajaa-i-aa. His minstrel spreads His Glory, singing and vibrating the Word of His Shabad.
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v27	nwnk scu swlwih pUrw pwieAw ]27] suDu (150-19, mwJ, mÚ 1) naanak sach saalaahi pooraa paa-i-aa. ||27||
RECORD	sloku mhlw 2 v27	suDhu O Nanak, praising the True Lord, I have obtained His Perfection. ||27||Sudh||
RECORD	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy (151-1)
RECORD	para 6392	raag ga-orhee gu-aarayree mehlaa 1 cha-upday dupday Raag Gauree Gwaarayree, First Mehl, Chau-Padas & Du-Padas:
RECORD	para 6393	<> siq nwmu krqw purKu inrBau inrvYru Akwl mUriq AjUnI sYBM gur pRswid ] (151-2) ik-oNkaar sat naam kartaa purakh nirbha-o nirvair akaal moorat ajoonee saibhaN gur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. Truth Is The Name. Creative Being Personified. No Fear. No Hatred. Image Of The Undying. Beyond Birth. Self-Existent. By Guru's Grace:
DEFINE	para 6394	Bau mucu Bwrw vfw qolu ] (151-3, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) bha-o much bhaaraa vadaa tol. The Fear of God is overpowering, and so very heavy,
DEFINE	para 6395	mn miq haulI boly bolu ] (151-3, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) man mat ha-ulee bolay bol. while the intellect is lightweight, as is the speech one speaks.
RECORD	para 6396	isir Dir clIAY shIAY Bwru ] (151-3, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) sir Dhar chalee-ai sahee-ai bhaar. So place the Fear of God upon your head, and bear that weight;
RECORD	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy v1	ndrI krmI gur bIcwru ]1] (151-3, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) nadree karmee gur beechaar. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy v1	by the Grace of the Merciful Lord, contemplate the Guru. ||1||
RECORD	para 6398	BY ibnu koie n lµGis pwir ] (151-4, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) bhai bin ko-ay na langhas paar. Without the Fear of God, no one crosses over the world-ocean.
RECORD	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy v1	BY Bau rwiKAw Bwie svwir ]1] rhwau ] (151-4, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) bhai bha-o raakhi-aa bhaa-ay savaar. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy v1	rahaa-o. This Fear of God adorns the Love of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 6400	BY qin Agin BKY BY nwil ] (151-4, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) bhai tan agan bhakhai bhai naal. The fire of fear within the body is burnt away by the Fear of God.
DEFINE	para 6401	BY Bau GVIAY sbid svwir ] (151-5, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) bhai bha-o gharhee-ai sabad savaar. Through this Fear of God, we are adorned with the Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 6402	BY ibnu GwVq kcu inkc ] (151-5, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) bhai bin ghaarhat kach nikach. Without the Fear of God, all that is fashioned is false.
RECORD	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy v2	AMDw scw AMDI st ]2] (151-5, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) anDhaa sachaa anDhee sat. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy v2	Useless is the mold, and useless are the hammer-strokes on the mold. ||2||
RECORD	para 6404	buDI bwjI aupjY cwau ] (151-6, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) buDhee baajee upjai chaa-o. The desire for the worldly drama arises in the intellect,
RECORD	para 6405	shs isAwxp pvY n qwau ] (151-6, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) sahas si-aanap pavai na taa-o. but even with thousands of clever mental tricks, the heat of the Fear of God does not come into play.
DEFINE	para 6406	nwnk mnmuiK bolxu vwau ] (151-6, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) naanak manmukh bolan vaa-o. O Nanak, the speech of the self-willed manmukh is just wind.
RECORD	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy v3	AMDw AKru vwau duAwau ]3]1] (151-7, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 1) anDhaa akhar vaa-o du-aa-o. ||3||
DEFINE	rwgu gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 1 caupdy dupdy v3	1|| His words are worthless and empty, like the wind. ||3||1||
RECORD	para 6408	ga-orhee mehlaa 1. Gauree, First Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 6409	fir Gru Gir fru fir fru jwie ] (151-7, gauVI, mÚ 1) dar ghar ghar dar dar dar jaa-ay. Place the Fear of God within the home of your heart; with this Fear of God in your heart, all other fears shall be frightened away.
DEFINE	para 6410	so fru kyhw ijqu fir fru pwie ] (151-7, gauVI, mÚ 1) so dar kayhaa jit dar dar paa-ay. What sort of fear is that, which frightens other fears?
RECORD	para 6411	quDu ibnu dUjI nwhI jwie ] (151-8, gauVI, mÚ 1) tuDh bin doojee naahee jaa-ay. Without You, I have other place of rest at all.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	jo ikCu vrqY sB qyrI rjwie ]1] (151-8, gauVI, mÚ 1) jo kichh vartai sabh tayree rajaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	Whatever happens is all according to Your Will. ||1||
WHEN	para 6413	frIAY jy fru hovY horu ] (151-9, gauVI, mÚ 1) daree-ai jay dar hovai hor. Be afraid, if you have any fear, other than the Fear of God.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	fir fir frxw mn kw soru ]1] rhwau ] (151-9, gauVI, mÚ 1) dar dar darnaa man kaa sor. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Afraid of fear, and living in fear, the mind is held in tumult. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 6415	nw jIau mrY n fUbY qrY ] (151-9, gauVI, mÚ 1) naa jee-o marai na doobai tarai. The soul does not die; it does not drown, and it does not swim across.
RECORD	para 6416	ijin ikCu kIAw so ikCu krY ] (151-10, gauVI, mÚ 1) jin kichh kee-aa so kichh karai. The One who created everything does everything.
ALLOW	para 6417	hukmy AwvY hukmy jwie ] (151-10, gauVI, mÚ 1) hukmay aavai hukmay jaa-ay. By the Hukam of His Command we come, and by the Hukam of His Command we go.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	AwgY pwCY hukim smwie ]2] (151-10, gauVI, mÚ 1) aagai paachhai hukam samaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	Before and after, His Command is pervading. ||2||
RECORD	para 6419	hMsu hyqu Awsw Asmwnu ] (151-10, gauVI, mÚ 1) hans hayt aasaa asmaan. Cruelty, attachment, desire and egotism
DEFINE	para 6420	iqsu ivic BUK bhuqu nY swnu ] (151-11, gauVI, mÚ 1) tis vich bhookh bahut nai saan. - there is great hunger in these, like the raging torrent of a wild stream.
RECORD	para 6421	Bau Kwxw pIxw AwDwru ] (151-11, gauVI, mÚ 1) bha-o khaanaa peenaa aaDhaar. Let the Fear of God be your food, drink and support.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v3	ivxu KwDy mir hoih gvwr ]3] (151-11, gauVI, mÚ 1) vin khaaDhay mar hohi gavaar. ||3||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v3	Without doing this, the fools simply die. ||3||
DEFINE	para 6423	ijs kw koie koeI koie koie ] (151-12, gauVI, mÚ 1) jis kaa ko-ay ko-ee ko-ay ko-ay. If anyone really has anyone else - how rare is that person!
DEFINE	para 6424	sBu ko qyrw qUM sBnw kw soie ] (151-12, gauVI, mÚ 1) sabh ko tayraa tooN sabhnaa kaa so-ay. All are Yours - You are the Lord of all.
RECORD	para 6425	jw ky jIA jMq Dnu mwlu ] (151-12, gauVI, mÚ 1) jaa kay jee-a jant Dhan maal. All beings and creatures, wealth and property belong to Him.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v4	nwnk AwKxu ibKmu bIcwru ]4]2] (151-13, gauVI, mÚ 1) naanak aakhan bikham beechaar. ||4||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v4	2|| O Nanak, it is so difficult to describe and contemplate Him. ||4||2||
UPHOLD	para 6428	mwqw miq ipqw sMqoKu ] (151-13, gauVI, mÚ 1) maataa mat pitaa santokh. Let wisdom be your mother, and contentment your father.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	squ BweI kir eyhu ivsyKu ]1] (151-14, gauVI, mÚ 1) sat bhaa-ee kar ayhu visaykh. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	Let Truth be your brother - these are your best relatives. ||1||
RECORD	para 6430	khxw hY ikCu khxu n jwie ] (151-14, gauVI, mÚ 1) kahnaa hai kichh kahan na jaa-ay. He has been described, but He cannot be described at all.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	qau kudriq kImiq nhI pwie ]1] rhwau ] (151-14, gauVI, mÚ 1) ta-o kudrat keemat nahee paa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Your All-pervading creative nature cannot be estimated. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 6433	srm suriq duie ssur Bey ] (152-1, gauVI, mÚ 1) saram surat du-ay sasur bha-ay. Modesty, humility and intuitive understanding are my mother-in-law and father-in-law;
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	krxI kwmix kir mn ley ]2] (152-1, gauVI, mÚ 1) karnee kaaman kar man la-ay. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	I have made good deeds my spouse. ||2||
DEFINE	para 6435	swhw sMjogu vIAwhu ivjogu ] (152-1, gauVI, mÚ 1) saahaa sanjog vee-aahu vijog. Union with the Holy is my wedding date, and separation from the world is my marriage.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v3	scu sMqiq khu nwnk jogu ]3]3] (152-2, gauVI, mÚ 1) sach santat kaho naanak jog. ||3||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v3	3|| Says Nanak, Truth is the child born of this Union. ||3||3||
RECORD	para 6438	pauxY pwxI AgnI kw mylu ] (152-2, gauVI, mÚ 1) pa-unai paanee agnee kaa mayl. The union of air, water and fire
DEFINE	para 6439	cMcl cpl buiD kw Kylu ] (152-3, gauVI, mÚ 1) chanchal chapal buDh kaa khayl. - the body is the play-thing of the fickle and unsteady intellect.
DEFINE	para 6440	nau drvwjy dsvw duAwru ] (152-3, gauVI, mÚ 1) na-o darvaajay dasvaa du-aar. It has nine doors, and then there is the Tenth Gate.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	buJu ry igAwnI eyhu bIcwru ]1] (152-3, gauVI, mÚ 1) bujh ray gi-aanee ayhu beechaar. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	Reflect upon this and understand it, O wise one. ||1||
DEFINE	para 6442	kQqw bkqw sunqw soeI ] (152-4, gauVI, mÚ 1) kathtaa baktaa suntaa so-ee. The Lord is the One who speaks, teaches and listens.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	Awpu bIcwry su igAwnI hoeI ]1] rhwau ] (152-4, gauVI, mÚ 1) aap beechaaray so gi-aanee ho-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. One who contemplates his own self is truly wise. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 6444	dyhI mwtI bolY pauxu ] (152-4, gauVI, mÚ 1) dayhee maatee bolai pa-un. The body is dust; the wind speaks through it.
RECORD	para 6445	buJu ry igAwnI mUAw hY kauxu ] (152-5, gauVI, mÚ 1) bujh ray gi-aanee moo-aa hai ka-un. Understand, O wise one, who has died.
RECORD	para 6446	mUeI suriq bwdu AhMkwru ] (152-5, gauVI, mÚ 1) moo-ee surat baad aha Nkaar. Awareness, conflict and ego have died,
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	Ehu n mUAw jo dyKxhwru ]2] (152-5, gauVI, mÚ 1) oh na moo-aa jo daykhanhaar. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	but the One who sees does not die. ||2||
RECORD	para 6448	jY kwrix qit qIrQ jwhI ] (152-5, gauVI, mÚ 1) jai kaaran tat tirath jaahee. For the sake of it, you journey to sacred shrines and holy rivers;
DEFINE	para 6449	rqn pdwrQ Gt hI mwhI ] (152-6, gauVI, mÚ 1) ratan padaarath ghat hee maahee. but this priceless jewel is within your own heart.
RECORD	para 6450	piV piV pMifqu bwdu vKwxY ] (152-6, gauVI, mÚ 1) parh parh pandit baad vakhaanai. The Pandits, the religious scholars, read and read endlessly; they stir up arguments and controversies,
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v3	BIqir hodI vsqu n jwxY ]3] (152-6, gauVI, mÚ 1) bheetar hodee vasat na jaanai. ||3||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v3	but they do not know the secret deep within. ||3||
RECORD	para 6452	hau n mUAw myrI mueI blwie ] (152-7, gauVI, mÚ 1) ha-o na moo-aa mayree mu-ee balaa-ay. I have not died - that evil nature within me has died.
DEFINE	para 6453	Ehu n mUAw jo rihAw smwie ] (152-7, gauVI, mÚ 1) oh na moo-aa jo rahi-aa samaa-ay. The One who is pervading everywhere does not die.
RECORD	para 6454	khu nwnk guir bRhmu idKwieAw ] (152-7, gauVI, mÚ 1) kaho naanak gur barahm dikhaa-i-aa. Says Nanak, the Guru has revealed God to me,
