DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v4	4|| and now I see that there is no such thing as birth or death. ||4||4||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI ] (152-8)
RECORD	para 6456	ga-orhee mehlaa 1 dakh-nee. Gauree, First Mehl, Dakhanee:
RECORD	para 6457	suix suix bUJY mwnY nwau ] qw kY sd bilhwrY jwau ] (152-9, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) sun sun boojhai maanai naa-o. taa kai sad balihaarai jaa-o. I am forever a sacrifice to the one who listens and hears, who understands and believes in the Name.
DEFINE	para 6458	Awip Bulwey Taur n Twau ] (152-9, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) aap bhulaa-ay tha-ur na thaa-o. When the Lord Himself leads us astray, there is no other place of rest for us to find.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v1	qUM smJwvih myil imlwau ]1] (152-9, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) tooN samjhaavahi mayl milaa-o. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v1	You impart understanding, and You unite us in Your Union. ||1||
REQUIRE	para 6460	nwmu imlY clY mY nwil ] (152-10, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) naam milai chalai mai naal. I obtain the Naam, which shall go along with me in the end.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v1	ibnu nwvY bwDI sB kwil ]1] rhwau ] (152-10, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) bin naavai baaDhee sabh kaal. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v1	rahaa-o. Without the Name, all are held in the grip of Death. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 6462	KyqI vxju nwvY kI Et ] (152-11, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) khaytee vanaj naavai kee ot. My farming and my trading are by the Support of the Name.
DEFINE	para 6463	pwpu puMnu bIj kI pot ] (152-11, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) paap punn beej kee pot. The seeds of sin and virtue are bound together.
DEFINE	para 6464	kwmu k®oDu jIA mih cot ] (152-11, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) kaam kroDh jee-a meh chot. Sexual desire and anger are the wounds of the soul.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v2	nwmu ivswir cly min Kot ]2] (152-11, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) naam visaar chalay man khot. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v2	The evil-minded ones forget the Naam, and then depart. ||2||
DEFINE	para 6466	swcy gur kI swcI sIK ] (152-12, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) saachay gur kee saachee seekh. True are the Teachings of the True Guru.
DEFINE	para 6467	qnu mnu sIqlu swcu prIK ] (152-12, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) tan man seetal saach pareekh. The body and mind are cooled and soothed, by the touchstone of Truth.
DEFINE	para 6468	jl purwiein rs kml prIK ] (152-12, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) jal puraa-in ras kamal pareekh. This is the true mark of wisdom: that one remains detached, like the water-lily, or the lotus upon the water.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v3	sbid rqy mITy rs eIK ]3] (152-13, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) sabad ratay meethay ras eekh. ||3||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v3	Attuned to the Word of the Shabad, one becomes sweet, like the juice of the sugar cane. ||3||
RECORD	para 6470	hukim sMjogI giV ds duAwr ] (152-13, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) hukam sanjogee garh das du-aar. By the Hukam of the Lord's Command, the castle of the body has ten gates.
RECORD	para 6471	pMc vsih imil joiq Apwr ] (152-13, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) panch vaseh mil jot apaar. The five passions dwell there, together with the Divine Light of the Infinite.
DEFINE	para 6472	Awip qulY Awpy vxjwr ] (152-14, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) aap tulai aapay vanjaar. The Lord Himself is the merchandise, and He Himself is the trader.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v4	nwnk nwim svwrxhwr ]4]5] (152-14, gauVI dKxI, mÚ 1) naanak naam savaaranhaar. ||4||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 dKxI v4	5|| O Nanak, through the Naam, the Name of the Lord, we are adorned and rejuvenated. ||4||5||
RECORD	para 6475	jwqo jwie khw qy AwvY ] (152-15, gauVI, mÚ 1) jaato jaa-ay kahaa tay aavai. How can we know where we came from?
RECORD	para 6476	kh aupjY kh jwie smwvY ] (152-15, gauVI, mÚ 1) kah upjai kah jaa-ay samaavai. Where did we originate, and where will we go and merge?
DEFINE	para 6477	ikau bwiDE ikau mukqI pwvY ] (152-15, gauVI, mÚ 1) ki-o baaDhi-o ki-o muktee paavai. How are we bound, and how do we obtain liberation?
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	ikau AibnwsI shij smwvY ]1] (152-16, gauVI, mÚ 1) ki-o abhinaasee sahj samaavai. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	How do we merge with intuitive ease into the Eternal, Imperishable Lord? ||1||
RECORD	para 6479	nwmu irdY AMimRqu muiK nwmu ] (152-16, gauVI, mÚ 1) naam ridai amrit mukh naam. With the Naam in the heart and the Ambrosial Naam on our lips,
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	nrhr nwmu nrhr inhkwmu ]1] rhwau ] (152-16, gauVI, mÚ 1) narhar naam narhar nihkaam. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. through the Name of the Lord, we rise above desire, like the Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 6481	shjy AwvY shjy jwie ] (152-17, gauVI, mÚ 1) sehjay aavai sehjay jaa-ay. With intuitive ease we come, and with intuitive ease we depart.
DEFINE	para 6482	mn qy aupjY mn mwih smwie ] (152-17, gauVI, mÚ 1) man tay upjai man maahi samaa-ay. From the mind we originate, and into the mind we are absorbed.
DEFINE	para 6483	gurmuiK mukqo bMDu n pwie ] (152-18, gauVI, mÚ 1) gurmukh mukto banDh na paa-ay. As Gurmukh, we are liberated, and are not bound.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	sbdu bIcwir CutY hir nwie ]2] (152-18, gauVI, mÚ 1) sabad beechaar chhutai har naa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	Contemplating the Word of the Shabad, we are emancipated through the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 6485	qrvr pMKI bhu inis bwsu ] (152-18, gauVI, mÚ 1) tarvar pankhee baho nis baas. At night, lots of birds settle on the tree.
DEFINE	para 6486	suK duKIAw min moh ivxwsu ] (152-19, gauVI, mÚ 1) sukh dukhee-aa man moh vinaas. Some are happy, and some are sad. Caught in the desires of the mind, they perish.
WHEN	para 6487	swJ ibhwg qkih Awgwsu ] (152-19, gauVI, mÚ 1) saajh bihaag takeh aagaas. And when the life-night comes to its end, then they look to the sky.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v3	dh idis Dwvih krim iliKAwsu ]3] (152-19, gauVI, mÚ 1) dah dis Dhaaveh karam likhi-aas. ||3||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v3	They fly away in all ten directions, according to their pre-ordained destiny. ||3||
DEFINE	para 6490	nwm sMjogI goieil Qwtu ] (153-1, gauVI, mÚ 1) naam sanjogee go-il thaat. Those who are committed to the Naam, see the world as merely a temporary pasture.
DEFINE	para 6491	kwm k®oD PUtY ibKu mwtu ] (153-1, gauVI, mÚ 1) kaam kroDh footai bikh maat. Sexual desire and anger are broken, like a jar of poison.
DEFINE	para 6492	ibnu vKr sUno Gru hwtu ] (153-1, gauVI, mÚ 1) bin vakhar soono ghar haat. Without the merchandise of the Name, the house of the body and the store of the mind are empty.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v4	gur imil Koly bjr kpwt ]4] (153-2, gauVI, mÚ 1) gur mil kholay bajar kapaat. ||4||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v4	Meeting the Guru, the hard and heavy doors are opened. ||4||
RECORD	para 6494	swDu imlY pUrb sMjog ] (153-2, gauVI, mÚ 1) saaDh milai poorab sanjog. One meets the Holy Saint only through perfect destiny.
RECORD	para 6495	sic rhsy pUry hir log ] (153-2, gauVI, mÚ 1) sach rahsay pooray har log. The Lord's perfect people rejoice in the Truth.
RECORD	para 6496	mnu qnu dy lY shij suBwie ] (153-2, gauVI, mÚ 1) man tan day lai sahj subhaa-ay. Surrendering their minds and bodies, they find the Lord with intuitive ease.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v5	nwnk iqn kY lwgau pwie ]5]6] (153-3, gauVI, mÚ 1) naanak tin kai laaga-o paa-ay. ||5||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v5	6|| Nanak falls at their feet. ||5||6||
DEFINE	para 6499	kwmu k®oDu mwieAw mih cIqu ] (153-3, gauVI, mÚ 1) kaam kroDh maa-i-aa meh cheet. The conscious mind is engrossed in sexual desire, anger and Maya.
DEFINE	para 6500	JUT ivkwir jwgY ihq cIqu ] (153-4, gauVI, mÚ 1) jhooth vikaar jaagai hit cheet. The conscious mind is awake only to falsehood, corruption and attachment.
RECORD	para 6501	pUMjI pwp loB kI kIqu ] (153-4, gauVI, mÚ 1) poonjee paap lobh kee keet. It gathers in the assets of sin and greed.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	qru qwrI min nwmu sucIqu ]1] (153-4, gauVI, mÚ 1) tar taaree man naam sucheet. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	So swim across the river of life, O my mind, with the Sacred Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||1||
DEFINE	para 6503	vwhu vwhu swcy mY qyrI tyk ] (153-4, gauVI, mÚ 1) vaahu vaahu saachay mai tayree tayk. Waaho! Waaho! - Great! Great is my True Lord! I seek Your All-powerful Support.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	hau pwpI qUM inrmlu eyk ]1] rhwau ] (153-5, gauVI, mÚ 1) ha-o paapee tooN nirmal ayk. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. I am a sinner - You alone are pure. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 6505	Agin pwxI bolY BVvwau ] (153-5, gauVI, mÚ 1) agan paanee bolai bharhvaa-o. Fire and water join together, and the breath roars in its fury!
RECORD	para 6506	ijhvw ieMdRI eyku suAwau ] (153-5, gauVI, mÚ 1) jihvaa indree ayk su-aa-o. The tongue and the sex organs each seek to taste.
RECORD	para 6507	idsit ivkwrI nwhI Bau Bwau ] (153-6, gauVI, mÚ 1) disat vikaaree naahee bha-o bhaa-o. The eyes which look upon corruption do not know the Love and the Fear of God.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	Awpu mwry qw pwey nwau ]2] (153-6, gauVI, mÚ 1) aap maaray taa paa-ay naa-o. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 1 v2	Conquering self-conceit, one obtains the Name. ||2||
