DEFINE	gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 3 v1	Occupied with their own affairs, their nights and days are passing away. ||1||
RECORD	para 6810	ihrdY rwmu rmhu myry BweI ] (159-12, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) hirdai raam ramhu mayray bhaa-ee. Meditate on the Lord in your hearts, O my Siblings of Destiny.
RECORD	gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 3 v1	gurmuiK rsnw hir rsn rsweI ]1] rhwau ] (159-12, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) gurmukh rasnaa har rasan rasaa-ee. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The Gurmukh's tongue savors the sublime essence of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 6812	gurmuiK ihrdY ijin rwmu pCwqw ] (159-13, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) gurmukh hirdai jin raam pachhaataa. The Gurmukhs recognize the Lord in their own hearts;
DEFINE	para 6813	jgjIvnu syiv jug cwry jwqw ] (159-13, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) jagjeevan sayv jug chaaray jaataa. they serve the Lord, the Life of the World. They are famous throughout the four ages.
RECORD	para 6814	haumY mwir gur sbid pCwqw ] (159-13, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) ha-umai maar gur sabad pachhaataa. They subdue egotism, and realize the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 3 v2	ik®pw kry pRB krm ibDwqw ]2] (159-14, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) kirpaa karay parabh karam biDhaataa. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI guAwryrI mhlw 3 v2	God, the Architect of Destiny, showers His Mercy upon them. ||2||
DEFINE	para 6816	sy jn scy jo gur sbid imlwey ] (159-14, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) say jan sachay jo gur sabad milaa-ay. True are those who merge into the Word of the Guru's Shabad;
RECORD	para 6817	Dwvq vrjy Twik rhwey ] (159-14, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) Dhaavat varjay thaak rahaa-ay. they restrain their wandering mind and keep it steady.
DEFINE	para 6818	nwmu nv iniD gur qy pwey ] (159-15, gauVI guAwryrI, mÚ 3) naam nav niDh gur tay paa-ay. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is the nine treasures. It is obtained from the Guru.
