RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	gur prswdI mYlu auqwru ]1] rhwau ] (230-9, gauVI, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee mail utaar. ||1||
REQUIRE	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. By Guru's Grace, your filth shall be washed away. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 10198	vwid ivroiD n pwieAw jwie ] (230-10, gauVI, mÚ 3) vaad viroDh na paa-i-aa jaa-ay. Through argument and debate, He cannot be found.
DEFINE	para 10199	mnu qnu PIkw dUjY Bwie ] (230-10, gauVI, mÚ 3) man tan feekaa doojai bhaa-ay. The mind and body are made insipid through the love of duality.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v2	gur kY sbid sic ilv lwie ]2] (230-10, gauVI, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad sach liv laa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v2	Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, lovingly attune yourself to the True Lord. ||2||
DEFINE	para 10201	haumY mYlw iehu sMswrw ] (230-11, gauVI, mÚ 3) ha-umai mailaa ih sansaaraa. This world is polluted with egotism.
DEFINE	para 10202	inq qIriQ nwvY n jwie AhMkwrw ] (230-11, gauVI, mÚ 3) nit tirath naavai na jaa-ay aha Nkaaraa. By taking cleansing baths daily at sacred shrines of pilgrimage, egotism is not eliminated.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v3	ibnu gur Byty jmu kry KuAwrw ]3] (230-11, gauVI, mÚ 3) bin gur bhaytay jam karay khu-aaraa. ||3||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 3 v3	Without meeting the Guru, they are tortured by Death. ||3||
DEFINE	para 10204	so jnu swcw ij haumY mwrY ] (230-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) so jan saachaa je ha-umai maarai. Those humble beings are true, who conquer their ego.
RECORD	para 10205	gur kY sbid pMc sMGwrY ] (230-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad panch sanghaarai. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, they conquer the five thieves.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v4	Awip qrY sgly kul qwrY ]4] (230-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) aap tarai saglay kul taarai. ||4||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v4	They save themselves, and save all their generations as well. ||4||
RECORD	para 10207	mwieAw moih nit bwjI pweI ] (230-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi nat baajee paa-ee. The Actor has staged the drama of emotional attachment to Maya.
RECORD	para 10208	mnmuK AMD rhy lptweI ] (230-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) manmukh anDh rahay laptaa-ee. The self-willed manmukhs cling blindly to it.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v5	gurmuiK Ailpq rhy ilv lweI ]5] (230-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) gurmukh alipat rahay liv laa-ee. ||5||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v5	The Gurmukhs remain detached, and lovingly attune themselves to the Lord. ||5||
RECORD	para 10210	bhuqy ByK krY ByKDwrI ] (230-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) bahutay bhaykh karai bhaykh-Dhaaree. The disguisers put on their various disguises.
RECORD	para 10211	AMqir iqsnw iPrY AhMkwrI ] (230-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) antar tisnaa firai aha Nkaaree. Desire rages within them, and they carry on egotistically.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v6	Awpu n cInY bwjI hwrI ]6] (230-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) aap na cheenai baajee haaree. ||6||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v6	They do not understand themselves, and they lose the game of life. ||6||
RECORD	para 10213	kwpV pihir kry cqurweI ] (230-15, gauVI, mÚ 3) kaaparh pahir karay chaturaa-ee. Putting on religious robes, they act so clever,
DEFINE	para 10214	mwieAw moih Aiq Brim BulweI ] (230-15, gauVI, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi at bharam bhulaa-ee. but they are totally deluded by doubt and emotional attachment to Maya.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v7	ibnu gur syvy bhuqu duKu pweI ]7] (230-15, gauVI, mÚ 3) bin gur sayvay bahut dukh paa-ee. ||7||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v7	Without serving the Guru, they suffer in terrible pain. ||7||
DEFINE	para 10216	nwim rqy sdw bYrwgI ] (230-16, gauVI, mÚ 3) naam ratay sadaa bairaagee. Those who are attuned to the Naam, the Name of the Lord, remain detached forever.
RECORD	para 10217	igRhI AMqir swic ilv lwgI ] (230-16, gauVI, mÚ 3) garihee antar saach liv laagee. Even as householders, they lovingly attune themselves to the True Lord.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v8	nwnk siqguru syvih sy vfBwgI ]8]3] (230-16, gauVI, mÚ 3) naanak satgur sayveh say vadbhaagee. ||8||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 3 v8	3|| O Nanak, those who serve the True Guru are blessed and very fortunate. ||8||3||
DEFINE	para 10220	bRhmw mUlu vyd AiBAwsw ] (230-17, gauVI, mÚ 3) barahmaa mool vayd abhi-aasaa. Brahma is the founder of the study of the Vedas.
RECORD	para 10221	iqs qy aupjy dyv moh ipAwsw ] (230-17, gauVI, mÚ 3) tis tay upjay dayv moh pi-aasaa. From him emanated the gods, enticed by desire.
ALLOW	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	qRY gux Brmy nwhI inj Gir vwsw ]1] (230-18, gauVI, mÚ 3) tarai gun bharmay naahee nij ghar vaasaa. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	They wander in the three qualities, and they do not dwell within their own home. ||1||
RECORD	para 10223	hm hir rwKy siqgurU imlwieAw ] (230-18, gauVI, mÚ 3) ham har raakhay satguroo milaa-i-aa. The Lord has saved me; I have met the True Guru.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	Anidnu Bgiq hir nwmu idRVwieAw ]1] rhwau ] (230-19, gauVI, mÚ 3) an-din bhagat har naam drirh-aa-i-aa. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. He has implanted devotional worship of the Lord's Name, night and day. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 10225	qRY gux bwxI bRhm jMjwlw ] (230-19, gauVI, mÚ 3) tarai gun banee barahm janjaalaa. The songs of Brahma entangle people in the three qualities.
DEFINE	para 10226	piV vwdu vKwxih isir mwry jmkwlw ] (230-19, gauVI, mÚ 3) parh vaad vakaaneh sir maaray jamkaalaa. Reading about the debates and disputes, they are hit over the head by the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v2	qqu n cInih bMnih pMf prwlw ]2] (231-1, gauVI, mÚ 3) tat na cheeneh baneh pand paraalaa. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v2	They do not understand the essence of reality, and they gather their worthless bundles of straw. ||2||
RECORD	para 10229	mnmuK AigAwin kumwrig pwey ] (231-1, gauVI, mÚ 3) manmukh agi-aan kumaarag paa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs, in ignorance, take the path of evil.
RECORD	para 10230	hir nwmu ibswirAw bhu krm idRVwey ] (231-2, gauVI, mÚ 3) har naam bisaari-aa baho karam drirh-aa-ay. They forget the Lord's Name, and in its place, they establish all sorts of rituals.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v3	Bvjil fUby dUjY Bwey ]3] (231-2, gauVI, mÚ 3) bhavjal doobay doojai bhaa-ay. ||3||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v3	They drown in the terrifying world-ocean, in the love of duality. ||3||
RECORD	para 10232	mwieAw kw muhqwju pMifqu khwvY ] (231-2, gauVI, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa kaa muhtaaj pandit kahaavai. Driven crazy, infatuated by Maya, they call themselves Pandits - religious scholars;
RECORD	para 10233	ibiKAw rwqw bhuqu duKu pwvY ] (231-3, gauVI, mÚ 3) bikhi-aa raataa bahut dukh paavai. stained with corruption, they suffer terrible pain.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v4	jm kw gil jyvVw inq kwlu sMqwvY ]4] (231-3, gauVI, mÚ 3) jam kaa gal jayvrhaa nit kaal santaavai. ||4||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 3 v4	The noose of the Messenger of Death is around their necks; they are constantly tormented by death. ||4||
RECORD	para 10235	gurmuiK jmkwlu nyiV n AwvY ] (231-3, gauVI, mÚ 3) gurmukh jamkaal nayrh na aavai. The Messenger of Death does not even approach the Gurmukhs.
RECORD	para 10236	haumY dUjw sbid jlwvY ] (231-4, gauVI, mÚ 3) ha-umai doojaa sabad jalaavai. Through the Word of the Shabad, they burn away their ego and duality.
ALLOW	gauVI mhlw 3 v5	nwmy rwqy hir gux gwvY ]5] (231-4, gauVI, mÚ 3) naamay raatay har gun gaavai. ||5||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v5	Attuned to the Name, they sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||5||
DEFINE	para 10238	mwieAw dwsI Bgqw kI kwr kmwvY ] (231-4, gauVI, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa daasee bhagtaa kee kaar kamaavai. Maya is the slave of the Lord's devotees; it works for them.
RECORD	para 10239	crxI lwgY qw mhlu pwvY ] (231-5, gauVI, mÚ 3) charnee laagai taa mahal paavai. One who falls at their feet attains the Mansion of the Lord's Presence.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v6	sd hI inrmlu shij smwvY ]6] (231-5, gauVI, mÚ 3) sad hee nirmal sahj samaavai. ||6||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 3 v6	He is forever immaculate; he is absorbed in intuitive peace. ||6||
DEFINE	para 10241	hir kQw suxih sy DnvMq idsih jug mwhI ] (231-5, gauVI, mÚ 3) har kathaa suneh say Dhanvant diseh jug maahee. Those who listen to the Lord's Sermon are seen to be the wealthy people in this world.
RECORD	para 10242	iqn kau siB invih Anidnu pUj krwhI ] (231-6, gauVI, mÚ 3) tin ka-o sabh niveh an-din pooj karaahee. Everyone bows down to them, and adores them, night and day.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v7	shjy gux rvih swcy mn mwhI ]7] (231-6, gauVI, mÚ 3) sehjay gun raveh saachay man maahee. ||7||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v7	They intuitively savor the Glories of the True Lord within their minds. ||7||
RECORD	para 10244	pUrY siqguir sbdu suxwieAw ] (231-7, gauVI, mÚ 3) poorai satgur sabad sunaa-i-aa. The Perfect True Guru has revealed the Shabad;
RECORD	para 10245	qRY gux myty cauQY icqu lwieAw ] (231-7, gauVI, mÚ 3) tarai gun maytay cha-uthai chit laa-i-aa. it eradicates the three qualities, and attunes the consciousness to the fourth state.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v8	nwnk haumY mwir bRhm imlwieAw ]8]4] (231-7, gauVI, mÚ 3) naanak ha-umai maar barahm milaa-i-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 3 v8	4|| O Nanak, subduing egotism, one is absorbed into God. ||8||4||
RECORD	para 10248	bRhmw vydu pVY vwdu vKwxY ] (231-8, gauVI, mÚ 3) barahmaa vayd parhai vaad vakhaanai. Brahma studied the Vedas, but these lead only to debates and disputes.
DEFINE	para 10249	AMqir qwmsu Awpu n pCwxY ] (231-8, gauVI, mÚ 3) antar taamas aap na pachhaanai. He is filled with darkness; he does not understand himself.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	qw pRBu pwey gur sbdu vKwxY ]1] (231-9, gauVI, mÚ 3) taa parabh paa-ay gur sabad vakhaanai. ||1||
WHEN	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	And yet, if he chants the Word of the Guru's Shabad, he finds God. ||1||
FORBID	para 10251	gur syvw krau iPir kwlu n Kwie ] (231-9, gauVI, mÚ 3) gur sayvaa kara-o fir kaal na khaa-ay. So serve the Guru, and you shall not be consumed by death.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	mnmuK KwDy dUjY Bwie ]1] rhwau ] (231-9, gauVI, mÚ 3) manmukh khaaDhay doojai bhaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The self-willed manmukhs have been consumed by the love of duality. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 10253	gurmuiK pRwxI AprwDI sIDy ] (231-10, gauVI, mÚ 3) gurmukh paraanee apraaDhee seeDhay. Becoming Gurmukh, the sinful mortals are purified.
RECORD	para 10254	gur kY sbid AMqir shij rIDy ] (231-10, gauVI, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad antar sahj reeDhay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, they find intuitive peace and poise deep within.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v2	myrw pRBu pwieAw gur kY sbid sIDy ]2] (231-10, gauVI, mÚ 3) mayraa parabh paa-i-aa gur kai sabad seeDhay. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v2	I have found my God, through the Guru's Shabad, and I have been reformed. ||2||
RECORD	para 10256	siqguir myly pRiB Awip imlwey ] (231-11, gauVI, mÚ 3) satgur maylay parabh aap milaa-ay. God Himself unites us in Union with the True Guru,
WHEN	para 10257	myry pRB swcy kY min Bwey ] (231-11, gauVI, mÚ 3) mayray parabh saachay kai man bhaa-ay. when we become pleasing to the Mind of my True God.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v3	hir gux gwvih shij suBwey ]3] (231-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) har gun gaavahi sahj subhaa-ay. ||3||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v3	They sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, in the poise of celestial peace. ||3||
DEFINE	para 10259	ibnu gur swcy Brim Bulwey ] (231-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) bin gur saachay bharam bhulaa-ay. Without the True Guru, they are deluded by doubt.
RECORD	para 10260	mnmuK AMDy sdw ibKu Kwey ] (231-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) manmukh anDhay sadaa bikh khaa-ay. The blind, self-willed manmukhs constantly eat poison.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v4	jm fMfu shih sdw duKu pwey ]4] (231-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) jam dand saheh sadaa dukh paa-ay. ||4||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 3 v4	They are beaten by the Messenger of Death with his rod, and they suffer in constant pain. ||4||
RECORD	para 10262	jmUAw n johY hir kI srxweI ] (231-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) jamoo-aa na johai har kee sarnaa-ee. The Messenger of Death does not catch sight of those who enter the Sanctuary of the Lord.
RECORD	para 10263	haumY mwir sic ilv lweI ] (231-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) ha-umai maar sach liv laa-ee. Subduing egotism, they lovingly center their consciousness on the True Lord.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v5	sdw rhY hir nwim ilv lweI ]5] (231-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) sadaa rahai har naam liv laa-ee. ||5||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v5	They keep their consciousness constantly focused on the Lord's Name. ||5||
DEFINE	para 10265	siqguru syvih sy jn inrml pivqw ] (231-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) satgur sayveh say jan nirmal pavitaa. Those humble beings who serve the True Guru are pure and immaculate.
RECORD	para 10266	mn isau mnu imlwie sBu jgu jIqw ] (231-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) man si-o man milaa-ay sabh jag jeetaa. Merging their minds into the Mind, they conquer the entire world.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 3 v6	ien ibiD kuslu qyrY myry mIqw ]6] (231-15, gauVI, mÚ 3) in biDh kusal tayrai mayray meetaa. ||6||
REQUIRE	gauVI mhlw 3 v6	In this way, you too shall find happiness, O my friend. ||6||
DEFINE	para 10268	siqgurU syvy so Plu pwey ] (231-15, gauVI, mÚ 3) satguroo sayvay so fal paa-ay. Those who serve the True Guru are blessed with fruitful rewards.
RECORD	para 10269	ihrdY nwmu ivchu Awpu gvwey ] (231-15, gauVI, mÚ 3) hirdai naam vichahu aap gavaa-ay. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, abides in their hearts; selfishness and conceit depart from within them.
