RECORD	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v5	Return to your own home, and find the palace of love; meet the Guru, and meet the Lord. ||5||
DEFINE	para 10399	mn krhlw qUM mIqu myrw pwKMfu loBu qjwie ] (234-10, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa too N meet mayraa pakhand lobh tajaa-ay. O camel-like mind, you are my friend; abandon hypocrisy and greed.
WHEN	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v6	pwKMif loBI mwrIAY jm fMfu dyie sjwie ]6] (234-10, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) pakhand lobhee maaree-ai jam dand day-ay sajaa-ay. ||6||
DEFINE	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v6	The hypocritical and the greedy are struck down; the Messenger of Death punishes them with his club. ||6||
RECORD	para 10401	mn krhlw myry pRwn qUM mYlu pwKMfu Brmu gvwie ] (234-10, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa mayray paraan too N mail pakhand bharam gavaa-ay. O camel-like mind, you are my breath of life; rid yourself of the pollution of hypocrisy and doubt.
RECORD	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v7	hir AMimRq sru guir pUirAw imil sMgqI mlu lih jwie ]7] (234-11, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) har amrit sar gur poori-aa mil sangtee mal leh jaa-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v7	The Perfect Guru is the Ambrosial Pool of the Lord's Nectar; join the Holy Congregation, and wash away this pollution. ||7||
RECORD	para 10403	mn krhlw myry ipAwirAw iek gur kI isK suxwie ] (234-12, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa mayray pi-aari-aa ik gur kee sikh sunaa-ay. O my dear beloved camel-like mind, listen only to the Teachings of the Guru.
RECORD	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v8	iehu mohu mwieAw psirAw AMiq swiQ n koeI jwie ]8] (234-12, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) ih moh maa-i-aa pasri-aa ant saath na ko-ee jaa-ay. ||8||
REQUIRE	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v8	This emotional attachment to Maya is so pervasive. Ultimately, nothing shall go along with anyone. ||8||
RECORD	para 10405	mn krhlw myry swjnw hir Krcu lIAw piq pwie ] (234-13, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa mayray saajnaa har kharach lee-aa pat paa-ay. O camel-like mind, my good friend, take the supplies of the Lord's Name, and obtain honor.
RECORD	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v9	hir drgh pYnwieAw hir Awip lieAw gil lwie ]9] (234-13, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) har dargeh painaa-i-aa har aap la-i-aa gal laa-ay. ||9||
REQUIRE	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v9	In the Court of the Lord, you shall be robed with honor, and the Lord Himself shall embrace you. ||9||
RECORD	para 10407	mn krhlw guir mMinAw gurmuiK kwr kmwie ] (234-14, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa gur mani-aa gurmukh kaar kamaa-ay. O camel-like mind, one who surrenders to the Guru becomes Gurmukh, and works for the Lord.
RECORD	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v10	gur AwgY kir jodVI jn nwnk hir mylwie ]10]1] (234-15, gauVI pUrbI, mÚ 4) gur aagai kar jod-rhee jan naanak har maylaa-ay. ||10||
REQUIRE	rwgu gauVI pUrbI mhlw 4 krhly v10	1|| Offer your prayers to the Guru; O servant Nanak, He shall unite you with the Lord. ||10||1||
RECORD	para 10409	ga-orhee mehlaa 4. Gauree, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 10410	mn krhlw vIcwrIAw vIcwir dyKu smwil ] (234-15, gauVI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa veechaaree-aa veechaar daykh samaal. O contemplative camel-like mind, contemplate and look carefully.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v1	bn iPir Qky bn vwsIAw ipru gurmiq irdY inhwil ]1] (234-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) ban fir thakay ban vaasee-aa pir gurmat ridai nihaal. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v1	The forest-dwellers have grown weary of wandering in the forests; following the Guru's Teachings, see your Husband Lord within your heart. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v1	mn krhlw gur goivMdu smwil ]1] rhwau ] (234-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa gur govind samaal. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v1	rahaa-o. O camel-like mind, dwell upon the Guru and the Lord of the Universe. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 10413	mn krhlw vIcwrIAw mnmuK PwiQAw mhw jwil ] (234-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa veechaaree-aa manmukh faathi-aa mahaa jaal. O camel-like contemplative mind, the self-willed manmukhs are caught in the great net.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v2	gurmuiK pRwxI mukqu hY hir hir nwmu smwil ]2] (234-18, gauVI, mÚ 4) gurmukh paraanee mukat hai har har naam samaal. ||2||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 4 v2	The mortal who becomes Gurmukh is liberated, dwelling upon the Name of the Lord, Har, Har. ||2||
RECORD	para 10415	mn krhlw myry ipAwirAw sqsMgiq siqguru Bwil ] (234-18, gauVI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa mayray pi-aari-aa satsangat satgur bhaal. O my dear beloved camel-like mind, seek the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation, and the True Guru.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v3	sqsMgiq lig hir iDAweIAY hir hir clY qyrY nwil ]3] (234-19, gauVI, mÚ 4) satsangat lag har Dhi-aa-ee-ai har har chalai tayrai naal. ||3||
REQUIRE	gauVI mhlw 4 v3	Joining the Sat Sangat, meditate on the Lord, and the Lord, Har, Har, shall go along with you. ||3||
RECORD	para 10417	mn krhlw vfBwgIAw hir eyk ndir inhwil ] (234-19, gauVI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa vadbhaagee-aa har ayk nadar nihaal. O very fortunate camel-like mind, with one Glance of Grace from the Lord, you shall be enraptured.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v4	Awip Cfwey CutIAY siqgur crx smwil ]4] (235-1, gauVI, mÚ 4) aap chhadaa-ay chhutee-ai satgur charan samaal. ||4||
REQUIRE	gauVI mhlw 4 v4	If the Lord Himself saves you, then you shall be saved. Dwell upon the Feet of the True Guru. ||4||
RECORD	para 10420	mn krhlw myry ipAwirAw ivic dyhI joiq smwil ] (235-1, gauVI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa mayray pi-aari-aa vich dayhee jot samaal. O my dear beloved camel-like mind, dwell upon the Divine Light within the body.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v5	guir nau iniD nwmu ivKwilAw hir dwiq krI dieAwil ]5] (235-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) gur na-o niDh naam vikhaali-aa har daat karee da-i-aal. ||5||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v5	The Guru has shown me the nine treasures of the Naam. The Merciful Lord has bestowed this gift. ||5||
DEFINE	para 10422	mn krhlw qUM cMclw cqurweI Cif ivkrwil ] (235-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa too N chanchlaa chaturaa-ee chhad vikraal. O camel-like mind, you are so fickle; give up your cleverness and corruption.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v6	hir hir nwmu smwil qUM hir mukiq kry AMq kwil ]6] (235-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) har har naam samaal too N har mukat karay ant kaal. ||6||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v6	Dwell upon the Name of the Lord, Har, Har; at the very last moment, the Lord shall liberate you. ||6||
DEFINE	para 10424	mn krhlw vfBwgIAw qUM igAwnu rqnu smwil ] (235-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) man karhalaa vadbhaagee-aa tooN gi-aan ratan samaal. O camel-like mind, you are so very fortunate; dwell upon the jewel of spiritual wisdom.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v7	gur igAwnu KVgu hiQ DwirAw jmu mwirAVw jmkwil ]7] (235-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) gur gi-aan kharhag hath Dhaari-aa jam maari-arhaa jamkaal. ||7||
UPHOLD	gauVI mhlw 4 v7	You hold in your hands the sword of the Guru's spiritual wisdom; with this destroyer of death, kill the Messenger of Death. ||7||
RECORD	para 10426	AMqir inDwnu mn krhly BRim Bvih bwhir Bwil ] (235-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) antar niDhaan man karhalay bharam bhaveh baahar bhaal. The treasure is deep within, O camel-like mind, but you wander around outside in doubt, searching for it.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v8	guru purKu pUrw ByitAw hir sjxu lDVw nwil ]8] (235-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) gur purakh pooraa bhayti-aa har sajan laDh-rhaa naal. ||8||
REQUIRE	gauVI mhlw 4 v8	Meeting the Perfect Guru, the Primal Being, you shall discover that the Lord, your Best Friend, is with you. ||8||
DEFINE	para 10428	rMig rqVy mn krhly hir rMgu sdw smwil ] (235-6, gauVI, mÚ 4) rang rat-rhay man karhalay har rang sadaa samaal. You are engrossed in pleasures, O camel-like mind; dwell upon the Lord's lasting love instead!
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v9	hir rMgu kdy n auqrY gur syvw sbdu smwil ]9] (235-6, gauVI, mÚ 4) har rang kaday na utrai gur sayvaa sabad samaal. ||9||
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v9	The color of the Lord's Love never fades away; serve the Guru, and dwell upon the Word of the Shabad. ||9||
DEFINE	para 10430	hm pMKI mn krhly hir qrvru purKu Akwil ] (235-7, gauVI, mÚ 4) ham pankhee man karhalay har tarvar purakh akaal. We are birds, O camel-like mind; the Lord, the Immortal Primal Being, is the tree.
RECORD	gauVI mhlw 4 v10	vfBwgI gurmuiK pwieAw jn nwnk nwmu smwil ]10]2] (235-7, gauVI, mÚ 4) vadbhaagee gurmukh paa-i-aa jan naanak naam samaal. ||10||
DEFINE	gauVI mhlw 4 v10	2|| The Gurmukhs are very fortunate - they find it. O servant Nanak, dwell upon the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||10||2||
