RECORD	gauVI bwvn AKrI mhlw 5 v1	xw hau xw qUM xh Cutih inkit n jweIAhu dUq ]1] (256-13, gauVI, mÚ 5) naa ha-o naa tooN nah chhuteh nikat na jaa-ee-ahu doot. ||1||
REQUIRE	gauVI bwvn AKrI mhlw 5 v1	- the Righteous Judge says, "Do not approach that place, O Messenger of Death, or else neither you nor I shall escape!"||1||
RECORD	para 11458	pauVI ] (256-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 11459	xwxw rx qy sIJIAY Awqm jIqY koie ] (256-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanaa ran tay seejhee-ai aatam jeetai ko-ay. NANNA: One who conquers his own soul, wins the battle of life.
RECORD	para 11460	haumY An isau lir mrY so soBw dU hoie ] (256-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) ha-umai an si-o lar marai so sobhaa doo ho-ay. One who dies, while fighting against egotism and alienation, becomes sublime and beautiful.
RECORD	para 11461	mxI imtwie jIvq mrY gur pUry aupdys ] (256-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) manee mitaa-ay jeevat marai gur pooray updays. One who eradicates his ego, remains dead while yet alive, through the Teachings of the Perfect Guru.
DEFINE	para 11462	mnUAw jIqY hir imlY iqh sUrqx vys ] (256-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) manoo-aa jeetai har milai tih soortan vays. He conquers his mind, and meets the Lord; he is dressed in robes of honor.
DEFINE	para 11463	xw ko jwxY Awpxo eykih tyk ADwr ] (256-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) naa ko jaanai aapno aykeh tayk aDhaar. He does not claim anything as his own; the One Lord is his Anchor and Support.
RECORD	para 11464	rYix idxsu ismrq rhY so pRBu purKu Apwr ] (256-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) rain dinas simrat rahai so parabh purakh apaar. Night and day, he continually contemplates the Almighty, Infinite Lord God.
DEFINE	para 11465	ryx sgl ieAw mnu krY eyaU krm kmwie ] (256-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) rayn sagal i-aa man karai ay-oo karam kamaa-ay. He makes his mind the dust of all; such is the karma of the deeds he does.
