DEFINE	para 14016	pwrbRhmu prmysro sB ibiD jwnxhwr ] (300-7, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) paarbarahm parmaysaro sabh biDh jaananhaar. The Supreme Lord God, the Transcendent Lord, is the Knower of all ways and means.
RECORD	para 14017	sMq shweI srin jogu AwT phr nmskwr ] (300-7, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) sant sahaa-ee saran jog aath pahar namaskaar. He is the Support of His Saints, with the Power to give Sanctuary. Twenty-four hours a day, I bow in reverence to Him.
RECORD	para 14018	AkQ kQw nh bUJIAY ismrhu hir ky crn ] (300-8, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) akath kathaa nah boojhee-ai simrahu har kay charan. His Unspoken Speech cannot be understood; I meditate on the Feet of the Lord.
RECORD	iQqI gauVI mhlw 5 v16	piqq auDwrn AnwQ nwQ nwnk pRB kI srn ]16] (300-8, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) patit uDhaaran anaath naath naanak parabh kee saran. ||16||
DEFINE	iQqI gauVI mhlw 5 v16	He is the Saving Grace of sinners, the Master of the masterless; Nanak has entered God's Sanctuary. ||16||
RECORD	para 14020	sloku ] (300-9) salok. Shalok:
DEFINE	para 14021	duK ibnsy shsw gieE srin ghI hir rwie ] (300-9, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) dukh binsay sahsaa ga-i-o saran gahee har raa-ay. My pain is gone, and my sorrows have departed, since I took to the Sanctuary of the Lord, my King.
RECORD	iQqI gauVI mhlw 5 v17	min icMdy Pl pwieAw nwnk hir gun gwie ]17] (300-10, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) man chinday fal paa-i-aa naanak har gun gaa-ay. ||17||
RECORD	iQqI gauVI mhlw 5 v17	I have obtained the fruits of my mind's desires, O Nanak, singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||17||
RECORD	para 14023	pauVI ] (300-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14024	koeI gwvY ko suxY koeI krY bIcwru ] (300-10, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) ko-ee gaavai ko sunai ko-ee karai beechaar. Some sing, some listen, and some contemplate;
DEFINE	para 14025	ko aupdysY ko idRVY iqs kw hoie auDwru ] (300-11, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) ko updaysai ko darirhai tis kaa ho-ay uDhaar. some preach, and some implant the Name within; this is how they are saved.
RECORD	para 14026	iklibK kwtY hoie inrmlw jnm jnm mlu jwie ] (300-11, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) kilbikh kaatai ho-ay nirmalaa janam janam mal jaa-ay. Their sinful mistakes are erased, and they become pure; the filth of countless incarnations is washed away.
FORBID	para 14027	hliq pliq muKu aUjlw nh pohY iqsu mwie ] (300-12, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) halat palat mukh oojlaa nah pohai tis maa-ay. In this world and the next, their faces shall be radiant; they shall not be touched by Maya.
RECORD	para 14028	so surqw so bYsno so igAwnI DnvMqu ] (300-12, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) so surtaa so baisno so gi-aanee Dhanvant. They are intuitively wise, and they are Vaishnaavs, worshippers of Vishnu; they are spiritually wise, wealthy and prosperous.
DEFINE	para 14029	so sUrw kulvMqu soie ijin BijAw BgvMqu ] (300-12, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) so sooraa kulvant so-ay jin bhaji-aa bhagvant. They are spiritual heros, of noble birth, who vibrate upon the Lord God.
RECORD	para 14030	KqRI bRwhmxu sUdu bYsu auDrY ismir cMfwl ] (300-13, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) khatree baraahman sood bais uDhrai simar chandaal. The Kh'shatriyas, the Brahmins, the low-caste Soodras, the Vaisha workers and the outcast pariahs are all saved,
RECORD	iQqI gauVI mhlw 5 v17	ijin jwinE pRBu Awpnw nwnk iqsih rvwl ]17] (300-13, iQqI gauVI, mÚ 5) jin jaani-o parabh aapnaa naanak tiseh ravaal. ||17||
DEFINE	iQqI gauVI mhlw 5 v17	meditating on the Lord. Nanak is the dust of the feet of those who know his God. ||17||
