RECORD	para 14033	<> siqgur pRswid ] (300-15) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	para 14034	slok mÚ 4 ] (300-16) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14035	siqguru purKu dieAwlu hY ijs no smqu sBu koie ] (300-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) satgur purakh da-i-aal hai jis no samat sabh ko-ay. The True Guru, the Primal Being, is kind and compassionate; all are alike to Him.
DEFINE	para 14036	eyk idRsit kir dyKdw mn BwvnI qy isiD hoie ] (300-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) ayk darisat kar daykh-daa man bhaavnee tay siDh ho-ay. He looks upon all impartially; with pure faith in the mind, He is obtained.
DEFINE	para 14037	siqgur ivic AMimRqu hY hir auqmu hir pdu soie ] (300-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) satgur vich amrit hai har utam har pad so-ay. The Ambrosial Nectar is within the True Guru; He is exalted and sublime, of Godly status.
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk ikrpw qy hir iDAweIAY gurmuiK pwvY koie ]1] (300-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) naanak kirpaa tay har Dhi-aa-ee-ai gurmukh paavai ko-ay. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, by His Grace, one meditates on the Lord; the Gurmukhs obtain Him. ||1||
RECORD	para 14039	mÚ 4 ] (300-18) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14040	haumY mwieAw sB ibKu hY inq jig qotw sMswir ] (300-18, gauVI, mÚ 4) ha-umai maa-i-aa sabh bikh hai nit jag totaa sansaar. Egotism and Maya are total poison; in these, people continually suffer loss in this world.
RECORD	para 14041	lwhw hir Dnu KitAw gurmuiK sbdu vIcwir ] (300-18, gauVI, mÚ 4) laahaa har Dhan khati-aa gurmukh sabad veechaar. The Gurmukh earns the profit of the wealth of the Lord's Name, contemplating the Word of the Shabad.
WHEN	para 14042	haumY mYlu ibKu auqrY hir AMimRqu hir aur Dwir ] (300-19, gauVI, mÚ 4) ha-umai mail bikh utrai har amrit har ur Dhaar. The poisonous filth of egotism is removed, when one enshrines the Ambrosial Name of the Lord within the heart.
RECORD	para 14044	siB kwrj iqn ky isiD hih ijn gurmuiK ikrpw Dwir ] (301-1, gauVI, mÚ 4) sabh kaaraj tin kay siDh heh jin gurmukh kirpaa Dhaar. All the Gurmukh's affairs are brought to perfect completion; the Lord has showered him with His Mercy.
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk jo Duir imly sy imil rhy hir myly isrjxhwir ]2] (301-1, gauVI, mÚ 4) naanak jo Dhur milay say mil rahay har maylay sirjanhaar. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, one who meets the Primal Lord remains blended with the Lord, the Creator Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 14046	pauVI ] (301-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14047	qU scw swihbu scu hY scu scw gosweI ] (301-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) too sachaa saahib sach hai sach sachaa gosaa-ee. You are True, O True Lord and Master. You are the Truest of the True, O Lord of the World.
RECORD	para 14048	quDuno sB iDAwiedI sB lgY qyrI pweI ] (301-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) tuDhuno sabh Dhi-aa-idee sabh lagai tayree paa-ee. Everyone meditates on You; everyone falls at Your Feet.
DEFINE	para 14049	qyrI isPiq suAwilau srUp hY ijin kIqI iqsu pwir lGweI ] (301-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) tayree sifat su-aali-o saroop hai jin keetee tis paar laghaa-ee. Your Praises are graceful and beautiful; You save those who speak them.
DEFINE	para 14050	gurmuKw no Plu pwiedw sic nwim smweI ] (301-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) gurmukhaa no fal paa-idaa sach naam samaa-ee. You reward the Gurmukhs, who are absorbed in the True Name.
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	vfy myry swihbw vfI qyrI vifAweI ]1] (301-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) vaday mayray saahibaa vadee tayree vadi-aa-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O my Great Lord and Master, great is Your glorious greatness. ||1||
RECORD	para 14052	slok mÚ 4 ] (301-4) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14053	ivxu nwvY horu slwhxw sBu bolxu iPkw swdu ] (301-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) vin naavai hor salaahnaa sabh bolan fikaa saad. Without the Name, all other praise and speech is insipid and tasteless.
RECORD	para 14054	mnmuK AhMkwru slwhdy haumY mmqw vwdu ] (301-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) manmukh aha Nkaar salaahday ha-umai mamtaa vaad. The self-willed manmukhs praise their own egos; their attachment to egotism is useless.
RECORD	para 14055	ijn swlwhin sy mrih Kip jwvY sBu Apvwdu ] (301-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) jin saalaahan say mareh khap jaavai sabh apvaad. Those whom they praise, die; they all waste away in conflict.
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	jn nwnk gurmuiK aubry jip hir hir prmwnwdu ]1] (301-6, gauVI, mÚ 4) jan naanak gurmukh ubray jap har har parmaanaad. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O servant Nanak, the Gurmukhs are saved, chanting the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, the Embodiment of Supreme Bliss. ||1||
RECORD	para 14057	mÚ 4 ] (301-7) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
