DEFINE	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O servant Nanak, meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; chanting the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, peace is obtained. ||1||
RECORD	para 14375	mÚ 4 ] (309-16) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14376	vfBwgIAw sohwgxI ijnw gurmuiK imilAw hir rwie ] (309-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) vadbhaagee-aa sohaaganee jinaa gurmukh mili-aa har raa-ay. Very fortunate is the soul-bride, who, as Gurmukh, meets the Lord, her King.
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	AMqr joiq pRgwsIAw nwnk nwim smwie ]2] (309-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) antar jot pargaasee-aa naanak naam samaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	Her inner being is illiminated with His Divine Light; O Nanak, she is absorbed in His Name. ||2||
RECORD	para 14378	pauVI ] (309-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14379	iehu srIru sBu Drmu hY ijsu AMdir scy kI ivic joiq ] (309-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) ih sareer sabh Dharam hai jis andar sachay kee vich jot. This body is the home of Dharma; the Divine Light of the True Lord is within it.
RECORD	para 14380	guhj rqn ivic luik rhy koeI gurmuiK syvku kFY Koiq ] (309-18, gauVI, mÚ 4) guhaj ratan vich luk rahay ko-ee gurmukh sayvak kadhai khot. Hidden within it are the jewels of mystery; how rare is that Gurmukh, that selfless servant, who digs them out.
