RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v18	The Perfect Guru serves the Lord God; His vibration vibrates and resounds in the mind. ||18||
RECORD	para 14426	slok mÚ 4 ] (311-2) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14427	ijnw AMdir aumrQl syeI jwxin sUlIAw ] (311-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) jinaa andar umarthal say-ee jaanan soolee-aa. Those who have a festering boil within - they alone know its pain.
RECORD	para 14428	hir jwxih syeI ibrhu hau iqn ivthu sd Guim GolIAw ] (311-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) har jaaneh say-ee birahu ha-o tin vitahu sad ghum gholee-aa. Those who know the pain of separation from the Lord - I am forever a sacrifice, a sacrifice to them.
RECORD	para 14429	hir mylhu sjxu purKu myrw isru iqn ivthu ql rolIAw ] (311-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) har maylhu sajan purakh mayraa sir tin vitahu tal rolee-aa. O Lord, please lead me to meet the Guru, the Primal Being, my Friend; my head shall roll in the dust under His feet.
RECORD	para 14430	jo isK gur kwr kmwvih hau gulmu iqnw kw golIAw ] (311-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) jo sikh gur kaar kamaaveh ha-o gulam tinaa kaa golee-aa. I am the slave of the slaves of those GurSikhs who serve Him.
RECORD	para 14431	hir rMig clUlY jo rqy iqn iBnI hir rMig colIAw ] (311-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) har rang chaloolai jo ratay tin bhinee har rang cholee-aa. Those who are imbued with the deep crimson color of the Lord's Love - their robes are drenched in the Love of the Lord.
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	kir ikrpw nwnk myil gur pih isru vyicAw molIAw ]1] (311-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) kar kirpaa naanak mayl gur peh sir vaychi-aa molee-aa. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	Grant Your Grace, and lead Nanak to meet the Guru; I have sold my head to Him. ||1||
RECORD	para 14433	mÚ 4 ] (311-6) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14434	AaugxI BirAw srIru hY ikau sMqhu inrmlu hoie ] (311-6, gauVI, mÚ 4) a-uganee bhari-aa sareer hai ki-o santahu nirmal ho-ay. The body is full of mistakes and misdeeds; how can it become pure, O Saints?
RECORD	para 14435	gurmuiK gux vyhwJIAih mlu haumY kFY Doie ] (311-7, gauVI, mÚ 4) gurmukh gun vayhaajhee-ah mal ha-umai kadhai Dho-ay. The Gurmukh purchases virtues, which wash off the sin of egotism.
DEFINE	para 14436	scu vxMjih rMg isau scu saudw hoie ] (311-7, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach vana Njahi rang si-o sach sa-udaa ho-ay. True is the trade which purchases the True Lord with love.
RECORD	para 14437	qotw mUil n AwveI lwhw hir BwvY soie ] (311-8, gauVI, mÚ 4) totaa mool na aavee laahaa har bhaavai so-ay. No loss will come from this, and the profit comes by the Lord's Will.
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk iqn scu vxMijAw ijnw Duir iliKAw prwpiq hoie ]2] (311-8, gauVI, mÚ 4) naanak tin sach vananji-aa jinaa Dhur likhi-aa paraapat ho-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, they alone purchase the Truth, who are blessed with such pre-ordained destiny. ||2||
RECORD	para 14439	pauVI ] (311-9) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14440	swlwhI scu swlwhxw scu scw purKu inrwly ] (311-9, gauVI, mÚ 4) saalaahee sach salaahnaa sach sachaa purakh niraalay. I praise the True One, who alone is worthy of praise. The True Primal Being is True - this is His unique quality.
RECORD	para 14441	scu syvI scu min vsY scu scw hir rKvwly ] (311-9, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach sayvee sach man vasai sach sachaa har rakhvaalay. Serving the True Lord, the Truth comes to dwell in the mind. The Lord, the Truest of the True, is my Protector.
REQUIRE	para 14442	scu scw ijnI ArwiDAw sy jwie rly sc nwly ] (311-10, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach sachaa jinee araaDhi-aa say jaa-ay ralay sach naalay. Those who worship and adore the Truest of the True, shall go and merge with the True Lord.
RECORD	para 14443	scu scw ijnI n syivAw sy mnmuK mUV byqwly ] (311-10, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach sachaa jinee na sayvi-aa say manmukh moorh baytaalay. Those who do not serve the Truest of the True - those self-willed manmukhs are foolish demons.
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v19	Eh Awlu pqwlu muhhu boldy ijau pIqY mid mqvwly ]19] (311-11, gauVI, mÚ 4) oh aal pataal muhhu bolday ji-o peetai mad matvaalay. ||19||
RECORD	gauVI kI vwr mhlw 4 v19	With their mouths, they babble on about this and that, like the drunkard who has drunk his wine. ||19||
RECORD	para 14445	salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14446	gauVI rwig sulKxI jy KsmY iciq kryie ] (311-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) ga-orhee raag sulakh-nee jay khasmai chit karay-i. Gauree Raga is auspicious, if, through it, one comes to think of his Lord and Master.
RECORD	para 14447	BwxY clY siqgurU kY AYsw sIgwru kryie ] (311-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) bhaanai chalai satguroo kai aisaa seegaar karay-i. He should walk in harmony with the Will of the True Guru; this should be his decoration.
DEFINE	para 14448	scw sbdu Bqwru hY sdw sdw rwvyie ] (311-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) sachaa sabad bhataar hai sadaa sadaa raavay-ay. The True Word of the Shabad is our spouse; ravish and enjoy it, forever and ever.
REQUIRE	para 14449	ijau aublI mjITY rMgu ghghw iqau scy no jIau dyie ] (311-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) ji-o ublee majeethai rang gahgahaa ti-o sachay no jee-o day-ay. Like the deep crimson color of the madder plant - such is the dye which shall color you, when you dedicate your soul to the True One.
RECORD	para 14450	rMig clUlY Aiq rqI scy isau lgw nyhu ] (311-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) rang chaloolai at ratee sachay si-o lagaa nayhu. One who loves the True Lord is totally imbued with the Lord's Love, like the deep crimson color of the poppy.
ALLOW	para 14451	kUVu TgI guJI nw rhY kUVu mulµmw plyit Dryhu ] (311-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) koorh thagee gujhee naa rahai koorh mulammaa palayt Dharayhu. Falsehood and deception may be covered with false coatings, but they cannot remain hidden.
DEFINE	para 14452	kUVI krin vfweIAw kUVy isau lgw nyhu ] (311-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) koorhee karan vadaa-ee-aa koorhay si-o lagaa nayhu. False is the uttering of praises, by those who love falsehood.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk scw Awip hY Awpy ndir kryie ]1] (311-15, gauVI, mÚ 3) naanak sachaa aap hai aapay nadar karay-i. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, He alone is True; He Himself casts His Glance of Grace. ||1||
RECORD	para 14454	mÚ 4 ] (311-15) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14455	sqsMgiq mih hir ausqiq hY sMig swDU imly ipAwirAw ] (311-15, gauVI, mÚ 4) satsangat meh har ustat hai sang saaDhoo milay pi-aari-aa. In the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation, the Lord's Praises are sung. In the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, the Beloved Lord is met.
UPHOLD	para 14456	Eie purK pRwxI DMin jn hih aupdysu krih praupkwirAw ] (311-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) o-ay purakh paraanee Dhan jan heh updays karahi par-upkaari-aa. Blessed is that mortal being, who shares the Teachings for the good of others.
ALLOW	para 14457	hir nwmu idRVwvih hir nwmu suxwvih hir nwmy jgu insqwirAw ] (311-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) har naam darirhaaveh har naam sunaaveh har naamay jag nistaari-aa. He implants the Name of the Lord, and he preaches the Name of the Lord; through the Name of the Lord, the world is saved.
RECORD	para 14458	gur vyKx kau sBu koeI locY nv KMf jgiq nmskwirAw ] (311-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) gur vaykhan ka-o sabh ko-ee lochai nav khand jagat namaskaari-aa. Everyone longs to see the Guru; the world, and the nine continents, bow down to Him.
RECORD	para 14459	quDu Awpy Awpu riKAw siqgur ivic guru Awpy quDu svwirAw ] (311-18, gauVI, mÚ 4) tuDh aapay aap rakhi-aa satgur vich gur aapay tuDh savaari-aa. You Yourself have established the True Guru; You Yourself have adorned the Guru.
RECORD	para 14460	qU Awpy pUjih pUj krwvih siqgur kau isrjxhwirAw ] (311-19, gauVI, mÚ 4) too aapay poojeh pooj karaaveh satgur ka-o sirjanhaari-aa. You Yourself worship and adore the True Guru; You inspire others to worship Him as well, O Creator Lord.
WHEN	para 14461	koeI ivCuiV jwie siqgurU pwshu iqsu kwlw muhu jim mwirAw ] (311-19, gauVI, mÚ 4) ko-ee vichhurh jaa-ay satguroo paashu tis kaalaa muhu jam maari-aa. If someone separates himself from the True Guru, his face is blackened, and he is destroyed by the Messenger of Death.
REQUIRE	para 14463	iqsu AgY ipCY FoeI nwhI gurisKI min vIcwirAw ] (312-1, gauVI, mÚ 4) tis agai pichhai dho-ee naahee gursikhee man veechaari-aa. He shall find no shelter, here or hereafter; the GurSikhs have realized this in their minds.
RECORD	para 14464	siqgurU no imly syeI jn aubry ijn ihrdY nwmu smwirAw ] (312-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) satguroo no milay say-ee jan ubray jin hirdai naam samaari-aa. That humble being who meets the True Guru is saved; he cherishes the Naam, the Name of the Lord, in his heart.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	jn nwnk ky gurisK puqhhu hir jipAhu hir insqwirAw ]2] (312-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) jan naanak kay gursikh puthahu har japi-ahu har nistaari-aa. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	Servant Nanak says: O GurSikhs, O my sons, meditate on the Lord; only the Lord shall save you. ||2||
RECORD	para 14466	mhlw 3 ] (312-3) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 14467	haumY jgqu BulwieAw durmiq ibiKAw ibkwr ] (312-3, gauVI, mÚ 3) ha-umai jagat bhulaa-i-aa durmat bikhi-aa bikaar. Egotism has led the world astray, along with evil-mindedness and the poison of corruption.
UPHOLD	para 14468	siqguru imlY q ndir hoie mnmuK AMD AMiDAwr ] (312-3, gauVI, mÚ 3) satgur milai ta nadar ho-ay manmukh anDh anDhi-aar. Meeting with the True Guru, we are blessed by the Lord's Glance of Grace, while the self-willed manmukh gropes around in the darkness.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v3	nwnk Awpy myil ley ijs no sbid lwey ipAwru ]3] (312-4, gauVI, mÚ 3) naanak aapay mayl la-ay jis no sabad laa-ay pi-aar. ||3||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v3	O Nanak, the Lord absorbs into Himself those whom He inspires to love the Word of His Shabad. ||3||
RECORD	para 14470	pauVI ] (312-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14471	scu scy kI isPiq slwh hY so kry ijsu AMdru iBjY ] (312-5, gauVI, mÚ 3) sach sachay kee sifat salaah hai so karay jis andar bhijai. True are the Praises and the Glories of the True One; he alone speaks them, whose mind is softened within.
RECORD	para 14472	ijnI iek min ieku ArwiDAw iqn kw kMDu n kbhU iCjY ] (312-5, gauVI, mÚ 3) jinee ik man ik araaDhi-aa tin kaa kanDh na kabhoo chhijai. Those who worship the One Lord with single-minded devotion - their bodies shall never perish.
UPHOLD	para 14473	Dnu Dnu purK swbwis hY ijn scu rsnw AMimRqu ipjY ] (312-6, gauVI, mÚ 3) Dhan Dhan purakh saabaas hai jin sach rasnaa amrit pijai. Blessed, blessed and acclaimed is that person, who tastes with his tongue the Ambrosial Nectar of the True Name.
DEFINE	para 14474	scu scw ijn min Bwvdw sy min scI drgh iljY ] (312-6, gauVI, mÚ 3) sach sachaa jin man bhaavdaa say man sachee dargeh lijai. One whose mind is pleased with the Truest of the True is accepted in the True Court.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v20	Dnu DMnu jnmu sicAwrIAw muK aujl scu kirjY ]20] (312-7, gauVI, mÚ 3) Dhan Dhan janam sachi-aaree-aa mukh ujal sach karijai. ||20||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v20	Blessed, blessed is the birth of those true beings; the True Lord brightens their faces. ||20||
RECORD	para 14476	slok mÚ 4 ] (312-8) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14477	swkq jwie invih gur AwgY min Koty kUiV kUiVAwry ] (312-8, gauVI, mÚ 4) saakat jaa-ay niveh gur aagai man khotay koorh koorhi-aaray. The faithless cynics go and bow before the Guru, but their minds are corrupt and false, totally false.
WHEN	para 14478	jw guru khY auThu myry BweI bih jwih Gusir bgulwry ] (312-8, gauVI, mÚ 4) jaa gur kahai uthahu mayray bhaa-ee bahi jaahi ghusar bagulaaray. When the Guru says, "Rise up, my Siblings of Destiny", they sit down, crowded in like cranes.
RECORD	para 14479	gurisKw AMdir siqguru vrqY cuix kFy lDovwry ] (312-9, gauVI, mÚ 4) gursikhaa andar satgur vartai chun kadhay laDhovaaray. The True Guru prevails among His GurSikhs; they pick out and expel the wanderers.
RECORD	para 14480	Eie AgY ipCY bih muhu Cpwiein n rlnI KotyAwry ] (312-9, gauVI, mÚ 4) o-ay agai pichhai bahi muhu chhapaa-in na ralnee khotay-aaray. Sitting here and there, they hide their faces; being counterfeit, they cannot mix with the genuine.
DEFINE	para 14481	Enw dw BKu su EQY nwhI jwie kUVu lhin Byfwry ] (312-10, gauVI, mÚ 4) onaa daa bhakh so othai naahee jaa-ay koorh lahan bhaydaaray. There is no food for them there; the false go into the filth like sheep.
WHEN	para 14482	jy swkqu nru KwvweIAY locIAY ibKu kFY muiK auglwry ] (312-10, gauVI, mÚ 4) jay saakat nar khaavaa-ee-ai lochee-ai bikh kadhai mukh uglaaray. If you try to feed the faithless cynic, he will spit out poison from his mouth.
UPHOLD	para 14483	hir swkq syqI sMgu n krIAhu Eie mwry isrjxhwry ] (312-11, gauVI, mÚ 4) har saakat saytee sang na karee-ahu o-ay maaray sirjanhaaray. O Lord, let me not be in the company of the faithless cynic, who is cursed by the Creator Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	ijs kw iehu Kylu soeI kir vyKY jn nwnk nwmu smwry ]1] (312-12, gauVI, mÚ 4) jis kaa ih khayl so-ee kar vaykhai jan naanak naam samaaray. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	This drama belongs to the Lord; He performs it, and He watches over it. Servant Nanak cherishes the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 14485	mÚ 4 ] (312-12) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14486	siqguru purKu AgMmu hY ijsu AMdir hir auir DwirAw ] (312-12, gauVI, mÚ 4) satgur purakh agamm hai jis andar har ur Dhaari-aa. The True Guru, the Primal Being, is inaccessible; He has enshrined the Lord's Name within His heart.
DEFINE	para 14487	siqgurU no ApiV koie n skeI ijsu vil isrjxhwirAw ] (312-13, gauVI, mÚ 4) satguroo no aparh ko-ay na sak-ee jis val sirjanhaari-aa. No one can equal the True Guru; the Creator Lord is on His side.
RECORD	para 14488	siqgurU kw KVgu sMjoau hir Bgiq hY ijqu kwlu kMtku mwir ivfwirAw ] (312-13, gauVI, mÚ 4) satguroo kaa kharhag sanjo-o har bhagat hai jit kaal kantak maar vidaari-aa. Devotional worship of the Lord is the sword and armor of the True Guru; He has killed and cast out Death, the torturer.
RECORD	para 14489	siqgurU kw rKxhwrw hir Awip hY siqgurU kY ipCY hir siB aubwirAw ] (312-14, gauVI, mÚ 4) satguroo kaa rakhanhaaraa har aap hai satguroo kai pichhai har sabh ubaari-aa. The Lord Himself is the Protector of the True Guru. The Lord saves all those who follow in the footsteps of the True Guru.
RECORD	para 14490	jo mMdw icqvY pUry siqgurU kw so Awip aupwvxhwrY mwirAw ] (312-15, gauVI, mÚ 4) jo mandaa chitvai pooray satguroo kaa so aap upaavanhaarai maari-aa. One who thinks evil of the Perfect True Guru - the Creator Lord Himself destroys him.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	eyh gl hovY hir drgh scy kI jn nwnk Agmu vIcwirAw ]2] (312-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) ayh gal hovai har dargeh sachay kee jan naanak agam veechaari-aa. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	These words will be confirmed as true in the Court of the Lord; servant Nanak reveals this mystery. ||2||
RECORD	para 14492	pauVI ] (312-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
WHEN	para 14493	scu suiqAw ijnI ArwiDAw jw auTy qw scu cvy ] (312-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach suti-aa jinee araaDhi-aa jaa uthay taa sach chavay. Those who dwell upon the True Lord while asleep, utter the True Name when they are awake.
DEFINE	para 14494	sy ivrly jug mih jwxIAih jo gurmuiK scu rvy ] (312-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) say virlay jug meh jaanee-ahi jo gurmukh sach ravay. How rare in the world are those Gurmukhs who dwell upon the True Lord.
RECORD	para 14495	hau bilhwrI iqn kau ij Anidnu scu lvy ] (312-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) ha-o balihaaree tin ka-o je an-din sach lavay. I am a sacrifice to those who chant the True Name, night and day.
DEFINE	para 14496	ijn min qin scw Bwvdw sy scI drgh gvy ] (312-18, gauVI, mÚ 4) jin man tan sachaa bhaavdaa say sachee dargeh gavay. The True Lord is pleasing to their minds and bodies; they go to the Court of the True Lord.
