DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v21	Servant Nanak chants the True Name; truly, the True Lord is forever brand new. ||21||
RECORD	para 14498	sloku mÚ 4 ] (312-19) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14499	ikAw svxw ikAw jwgxw gurmuiK qy prvwxu ] (312-19, gauVI, mÚ 4) ki-aa savnaa ki-aa jaagnaa gurmukh tay parvaan. Who is asleep, and who is awake? Those who are Gurmukh are approved.
RECORD	para 14501	ijnw swis igrwis n ivsrY sy pUry purK prDwn ] (313-1, gauVI, mÚ 4) jinaa saas giraas na visrai say pooray purakh parDhaan. Those who do not forget the Lord, with each and every breath and morsel of food, are the perfect and famous persons.
RECORD	para 14502	krmI siqguru pweIAY Anidnu lgY iDAwnu ] (313-1, gauVI, mÚ 4) karmee satgur paa-ee-ai an-din lagai Dhi-aan. By His Grace they find the True Guru; night and day, they meditate.
RECORD	para 14503	iqn kI sMgiq imil rhw drgh pweI mwnu ] (313-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) tin kee sangat mil rahaa dargeh paa-ee maan. I join the society of those persons, and in so doing, I am honored in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	para 14504	saudy vwhu vwhu aucrih auTdy BI vwhu kryin ] (313-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) sa-uday vaahu vaahu uchrahi uth-day bhee vaahu karayn. While asleep, they chant, "Waaho! Waaho!", and while awake, they chant, "Waaho!" as well.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk qy muK aujly ij inq auiT sMmwlyin ]1] (313-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) naanak tay mukh ujlay je nit uth samaalayn. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, radiant are the faces of those, who rise up early each day, and dwell upon the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 14506	mÚ 4 ] (313-3) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14507	siqguru syvIAY Awpxw pweIAY nwmu Apwru ] (313-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) satgur sayvee-ai aapnaa paa-ee-ai naam apaar. Serving his True Guru, one obtains the Naam, the Name of the Infinite Lord.
