DEFINE	para 14509	DMnu DMnu sy swh hY ij nwim krih vwpwru ] (313-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) Dhan Dhan say saah hai je naam karahi vaapaar. Blessed, blessed are those bankers who trade the Naam.
DEFINE	para 14510	vxjwry isK Awvdy sbid lGwvxhwru ] (313-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) vanjaaray sikh aavday sabad laghaavanhaar. The Sikhs, the traders come, and through the Word of His Shabad, they are carried across.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	jn nwnk ijn kau ik®pw BeI iqn syivAw isrjxhwru ]2] (313-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) jan naanak jin ka-o kirpaa bha-ee tin sayvi-aa sirjanhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	O servant Nanak, they alone serve the Creator Lord, who are blessed by His Grace. ||2||
RECORD	para 14512	pauVI ] (313-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14513	scu scy ky jn Bgq hih scu scw ijnI ArwiDAw ] (313-6, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach sachay kay jan bhagat heh sach sachaa jinee araaDhi-aa. Those who truly worship and adore the True Lord, are truly the humble devotees of the True Lord.
RECORD	para 14514	ijn gurmuiK Koij FMFoilAw iqn AMdrhu hI scu lwiDAw ] (313-6, gauVI, mÚ 4) jin gurmukh khoj dhandholi-aa tin andrahu hee sach laaDhi-aa. Those Gurmukhs who search and seek, find the True One within themselves.
RECORD	para 14515	scu swihbu scu ijnI syivAw kwlu kMtku mwir iqnI swiDAw ] (313-7, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach saahib sach jinee sayvi-aa kaal kantak maar tinee saaDhi-aa. Those who truly serve their True Lord and Master, overwhelm and conquer Death, the torturer.
RECORD	para 14516	scu scw sB dU vfw hY scu syvin sy sic rlwiDAw ] (313-8, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach sachaa sabh doo vadaa hai sach sayvan say sach ralaaDhi-aa. The True One is truly the greatest of all; those who serve the True One are blended with the True One.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v22	scu scy no swbwis hY scu scw syiv PlwiDAw ]22] (313-8, gauVI, mÚ 4) sach sachay no saabaas hai sach sachaa sayv falaaDhi-aa. ||22||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v22	Blessed and acclaimed is the Truest of the True; serving the Truest of the True, one blossoms forth in fruition. ||22||
RECORD	para 14518	slok mÚ 4 ] (313-9) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14519	mnmuKu pRwxI mugDu hY nwmhIx Brmwie ] (313-9, gauVI, mÚ 4) manmukh paraanee mugaDh hai naamheen bharmaa-ay. The self-willed manmukh is foolish; he wanders around without the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 14520	ibnu gur mnUAw nw itkY iPir iPir jUnI pwie ] (313-9, gauVI, mÚ 4) bin gur manoo-aa naa tikai fir fir joonee paa-ay. Without the Guru, his mind is not held steady, and he is reincarnated, over and over again.
WHEN	para 14521	hir pRBu Awip dieAwl hoih qW siqguru imilAw Awie ] (313-10, gauVI, mÚ 4) har parabh aap da-i-aal hohi taaN satgur mili-aa aa-ay. But when the Lord God Himself becomes merciful to him, then the True Guru comes to meet him.
