DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v25	This is the unique and distinct life-style of the Gurmukhs: listening to the Guru's Teachings, their minds blossom forth. ||25||
RECORD	para 14567	sloku mÚ 3 ] (314-11) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 14568	ijin guru goipAw Awpxw iqsu Taur n Twau ] (314-11, gauVI, mÚ 3) jin gur gopi-aa aapnaa tis tha-ur na thaa-o. Those who do not affirm their Guru shall have no home or place of rest.
RECORD	para 14569	hlqu plqu dovY gey drgh nwhI Qwau ] (314-11, gauVI, mÚ 3) halat palat dovai ga-ay dargeh naahee thaa-o. They lose both this world and the next; they have no place in the Court of the Lord.
REQUIRE	para 14570	Eh vylw hiQ n AwveI iPir siqgur lgih pwie ] (314-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) oh vaylaa hath na aavee fir satgur lageh paa-ay. This opportunity to bow at the Feet of the True Guru shall never come again.
REQUIRE	para 14571	siqgur kI gxqY GusIAY duKy duiK ivhwie ] (314-12, gauVI, mÚ 3) satgur kee gantai ghusee-ai dukhay dukh vihaa-ay. If they miss out on being counted by the True Guru, they shall pass their lives in pain and misery.
RECORD	para 14572	siqguru purKu inrvYru hY Awpy ley ijsu lwie ] (314-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) satgur purakh nirvair hai aapay la-ay jis laa-ay. The True Guru, the Primal Being, has no hatred or vengeance; He unites with Himself those with whom He is pleased.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk drsnu ijnw vyKwilEnu iqnw drgh ley Cfwie ]1] (314-13, gauVI, mÚ 3) naanak darsan jinaa vaykhaali-on tinaa dargeh la-ay chhadaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, those who behold the Blessed Vision of His Darshan, are emancipated in the Court of the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 14574	mÚ 3 ] (314-14) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14575	mnmuKu AigAwnu durmiq AhMkwrI ] (314-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) manmukh agi-aan durmat aha Nkaaree. The self-willed manmukh is ignorant, evil-minded and egotistical.
DEFINE	para 14576	AMqir k®oDu jUAY miq hwrI ] (314-14, gauVI, mÚ 3) antar kroDh joo-ai mat haaree. He is filled with anger within, and he loses his mind in the gamble.
