DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v29	The Guru has blessed Nanak with forgiveness; he is united with the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||29||
RECORD	para 14626	slok mÚ 4 ] (315-14) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14627	qpw n hovY AMdRhu loBI inq mwieAw no iPrY jjmwilAw ] (315-14, gauVI, mÚ 4) tapaa na hovai andarahu lobhee nit maa-i-aa no firai jajmaali-aa. He is not a penitent, who is greedy within his heart, and who constantly chases after Maya like a leper.
RECORD	para 14629	pMc log siB hsx lgy qpw loiB lhir hY gwilAw ] (315-15, gauVI, mÚ 4) panch log sabh hasan lagay tapaa lobh lahar hai gaali-aa. The village elders all laughed, saying that the waves of greed have destroyed this penitent.
WHEN	para 14630	ijQY QoVw Dnu vyKY iqQY qpw iBtY nwhI Din bhuqY ifTY qpY Drmu hwirAw ] (315-16, gauVI, mÚ 4) jithai thorhaa Dhan vaykhai tithai tapaa bhitai naahee Dhan bahutai dithai tapai Dharam haari-aa. If he sees only a little wealth, he does not bother to go there; but when he sees a lot of wealth, the penitent forsakes his vows.
RECORD	para 14631	BweI eyhu qpw n hovI bgulw hY bih swD jnw vIcwirAw ] (315-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) bhaa-ee ayhu tapaa na hovee bagulaa hai bahi saaDh janaa veechaari-aa. O Siblings of Destiny, he is not a penitent - he is only a stork. Sitting together, the Holy Congregation has so decided.
UPHOLD	para 14632	sq purK kI qpw inMdw krY sMswrY kI ausqqI ivic hovY eyqu doKY qpw diX mwirAw ] (315-17, gauVI, mÚ 4) sat purakh kee tapaa nindaa karai sansaarai kee ustatee vich hovai ayt dokhai tapaa da-yi maari-aa. The penitent slanders the True Primal Being, and sings the praises of the material world. For this sin, he is cursed by the Lord.
RECORD	para 14633	mhw purKW kI inMdw kw vyKu ij qpy no Plu lgw sBu gieAw qpy kw GwilAw ] (315-18, gauVI, mÚ 4) mahaa purkhaa N kee nindaa kaa vaykh je tapay no fal lagaa sabh ga-i-aa tapay kaa ghaali-aa. Behold the fruit the penitent gathers, for slandering the Great Primal Being; all his labors have gone in vain.
DEFINE	para 14634	bwhir bhY pMcw ivic qpw sdwey ] (315-19, gauVI, mÚ 4) baahar bahai panchaa vich tapaa sadaa-ay. When he sits outside among the elders, he is called a penitent;
WHEN	para 14635	AMdir bhY qpw pwp kmwey ] (315-19, gauVI, mÚ 4) andar bahai tapaa paap kamaa-ay. but when he sits within the congregation, the penitent commits sin.
RECORD	para 14637	hir AMdrlw pwpu pMcw no auGw kir vyKwilAw ] (316-1, gauVI, mÚ 4) har andarlaa paap panchaa no ughaa kar vaykhaali-aa. The Lord has exposed the penitent's secret sin to the elders.
RECORD	para 14638	Drm rwie jmkMkrw no AwiK CifAw eysu qpy no iqQY KiV pwiehu ijQY mhw mhW hiqAwirAw ] (316-
UPHOLD	para 14639	1, gauVI, mÚ 4) Dharam raa-ay jamkankraa no aakh chhadi-aa ays tapay no tithai kharh paa-ihu jithai mahaa mahaa N hati-aari-aa. The Righteous Judge of Dharma said to the Messenger of Death, "Take this penitent and put him with the worst of the worst murderers."
UPHOLD	para 14640	iPir eysu qpy dY muih koeI lghu nwhI eyhu siqguir hY iPtkwirAw ] (316-2, gauVI, mÚ 4) fir ays tapay dai muhi ko-ee lagahu naahee ayhu satgur hai fitkaari-aa. No one is to look at the face of this penitent again. He has been cursed by the True Guru.
RECORD	para 14641	hir kY dir vriqAw su nwnik AwiK suxwieAw ] (316-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) har kai dar varti-aa so naanak aakh sunaa-i-aa. Nanak speaks and reveals what has taken place in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	so bUJY ju diX svwirAw ]1] (316-3, gauVI, mÚ 4) so boojhai jo da-yi savaari-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	He alone understands, who is blessed and adorned by the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 14643	mÚ 4 ] (316-4) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14644	hir BgqW hir AwrwiDAw hir kI vifAweI ] (316-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) har bhagtaaN har aaraaDhi-aa har kee vadi-aa-ee. The devotees of the Lord worship and adore the Lord, and the glorious greatness of the Lord.
RECORD	para 14645	hir kIrqnu Bgq inq gWvdy hir nwmu suKdweI ] (316-4, gauVI, mÚ 4) har keertan bhagat nit gaa Nvday har naam sukh-daa-ee. The Lord's devotees continually sing the Kirtan of His Praises; the Name of the Lord is the Giver of peace.
RECORD	para 14646	hir BgqW no inq nwvY dI vifAweI bKsIAnu inq cVY svweI ] (316-5, gauVI, mÚ 4) har bhagtaaN no nit naavai dee vadi-aa-ee bakhsee-an nit charhai savaa-ee. The Lord ever bestows upon His devotees the glorious greatness of His Name, which increases day by day.
RECORD	para 14647	hir BgqW no iQru GrI bhwilAnu ApxI pYj rKweI ] (316-6, gauVI, mÚ 4) har bhagtaaN no thir gharee bahaali-an apnee paij rakhaa-ee. The Lord inspires His devotees to sit, steady and stable, in the home of their inner being. He preserves their honor.
RECORD	para 14648	inMdkW pwshu hir lyKw mMgsI bhu dyie sjweI ] (316-6, gauVI, mÚ 4) nindkaa N paashu har laykhaa mangsee baho day-ay sajaa-ee. The Lord summons the slanderers to answer for their accounts, and He punishes them severely.
DEFINE	para 14649	jyhw inMdk ApxY jIie kmwvdy qyho Plu pweI ] (316-7, gauVI, mÚ 4) jayhaa nindak apnai jee-ay kamaavday tayho fal paa-ee. As the slanderers think of acting, so are the fruits they obtain.
WHEN	para 14650	AMdir kmwxw srpr auGVY BwvY koeI bih DrqI ivic kmweI ] (316-7, gauVI, mÚ 4) andar kamaanaa sarpar ugh-rhai bhaavai ko-ee bahi Dhartee vich kamaa-ee. Actions done in secrecy are sure to come to light, even if one does it underground.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	jn nwnku dyiK ivgisAw hir kI vifAweI ]2] (316-8, gauVI, mÚ 4) jan naanak daykh vigsi-aa har kee vadi-aa-ee. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	Servant Nanak blossoms forth in joy, beholding the glorious greatness of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 14652	pauVI mÚ 5 ] (316-8) pa-orhee mehlaa 5. Pauree, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14653	Bgq jnW kw rwKw hir Awip hY ikAw pwpI krIAY ] (316-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) bhagat janaa N kaa raakhaa har aap hai ki-aa paapee karee-ai. The Lord Himself is the Protector of His devotees; what can the sinner do to them?
RECORD	para 14654	gumwnu krih mUV gumwnIAw ivsu KwDI mrIAY ] (316-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) gumaan karahi moorh gumaanee-aa vis khaaDhee maree-ai. The proud fool acts in pride, and eating his own poison, he dies.
