DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v30	Glorious and great is the Lord and Master of servant Nanak; He is the Master of all. ||30||
RECORD	para 14658	slok mÚ 4 ] (316-11) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14659	mnmuK mUlhu BuilAw ivic lbu loBu AhMkwru ] (316-11, gauVI, mÚ 4) manmukh moolhu bhuli-aa vich lab lobh aha Nkaar. The self-willed manmukhs forget the Primal Lord, the Source of all; they are caught in greed and egotism.
RECORD	para 14660	JgVw kridAw Anidnu gudrY sbid n krih vIcwru ] (316-12, gauVI, mÚ 4) jhagrhaa kardi-aa an-din gudrai sabad na karahi veechaar. They pass their nights and days in conflict and struggle; they do not contemplate the Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 14661	suiD miq krqY sB ihir leI bolin sBu ivkwru ] (316-12, gauVI, mÚ 4) suDh mat kartai sabh hir la-ee bolan sabh vikaar. The Creator has taken away all their understanding and purity; all their speech is evil and corrupt.
RECORD	para 14662	idqY ikqY n sMqoKIAih AMqir iqsnw bhu AigAwnu AMD´wru ] (316-13, gauVI, mÚ 4) ditai kitai na santokhee-ah antar tisnaa baho agi-aan anDh-yaar. No matter what they are given, they are not satisfied; within their hearts there is great desire, ignorance and darkness.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk mnmuKw nwlo qutI BlI ijn mwieAw moh ipAwru ]1] (316-13, gauVI, mÚ 4) naanak manmukhaa naalo tutee bhalee jin maa-i-aa moh pi-aar. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, it is good to break away from the self-willed manmukhs, who have love and attachment to Maya. ||1||
RECORD	para 14664	mÚ 4 ] (316-14) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14665	ijnw AMdir dUjw Bwau hY iqn@w gurmuiK pRIiq n hoie ] (316-14, gauVI, mÚ 4) jinaa andar doojaa bhaa-o hai tin Haa gurmukh pareet na ho-ay. Those whose hearts are filled with the love of duality, do not love the Gurmukhs.
RECORD	para 14666	Euhu AwvY jwie BvweIAY supnY suKu n koie ] (316-15, gauVI, mÚ 4) ohu aavai jaa-ay bhavaa-ee-ai supnai sukh na ko-ay. They come and go, and wander in reincarnation; even in their dreams, they find no peace.
