DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	Cursed is that day, no matter how pleasant the season, when the Supreme Lord God is forgotten. ||1||
RECORD	para 14757	mÚ 5 ] (318-15) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14758	nwnk imqRweI iqsu isau sB ikCu ijs kY hwiQ ] (318-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak mitraa-ee tis si-o sabh kichh jis kai haath. O Nanak, become friends with the One, who holds everything in His hands.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	kuimqRw syeI kWFIAih iek ivK n clih swiQ ]2] (318-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) kumitraa say-ee kaaNdhee-ah ik vikh na chaleh saath. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	They are accounted as false friends, who do not go with you, for even one step. ||2||
RECORD	para 14760	pauVI ] (318-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14761	AMimRqu nwmu inDwnu hY imil pIvhu BweI ] (318-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) amrit naam niDhaan hai mil peevhu bhaa-ee. The treasure of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, is Ambrosial Nectar; meet together and drink it in, O Siblings of Destiny.
DEFINE	para 14762	ijsu ismrq suKu pweIAY sB iqKw buJweI ] (318-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) jis simrat sukh paa-ee-ai sabh tikhaa bujhaa-ee. Remembering Him in meditation, peace is found, and all thirst is quenched.
REQUIRE	para 14763	kir syvw pwrbRhm gur BuK rhY n kweI ] (318-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) kar sayvaa paarbarahm gur bhukh rahai na kaa-ee. So serve the Supreme Lord God and the Guru, and you shall never be hungry again.
REQUIRE	para 14764	sgl mnorQ puMinAw Amrw pdu pweI ] (318-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) sagal manorath punni-aa amraa pad paa-ee. All your desires shall be fulfilled, and you shall obtain the status of immortality.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v3	quDu jyvfu qUhY pwrbRhm nwnk srxweI ]3] (318-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) tuDh jayvad toohai paarbarahm naanak sarnaa-ee. ||3||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v3	You alone are as great as Yourself, O Supreme Lord God; Nanak seeks Your Sanctuary. ||3||
RECORD	para 14766	slok mÚ 5 ] (318-19) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14767	ifTVo hB Twie aUx n kweI jwie ] (318-19, gauVI, mÚ 5) dith-rho habh thaa-ay oon na kaa-ee jaa-ay. I have seen all places; there is no place without Him.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk lDw iqn suAwau ijnw siqguru ByitAw ]1] (318-19, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak laDhaa tin su-aa-o jinaa satgur bhayti-aa. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, those who meet with the True Guru find the object of life. ||1||
RECORD	para 14770	mÚ 5 ] (319-1) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14771	dwmnI cmqkwr iqau vrqwrw jg Ky ] (319-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) daamnee chamatkaar ti-o vartaaraa jag khay. Like the flash of lightning, worldly affairs last only for a moment.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	vQu suhwvI swie nwnk nwau jpMdo iqsu DxI ]2] (319-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) vath suhaavee saa-ay naanak naa-o japando tis Dhanee. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	The only thing which is pleasing, O Nanak, is that which inspires one to meditate on the Name of the Master. ||2||
RECORD	para 14773	pauVI ] (319-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14774	isimRiq swsqR soiD siB iknY kIm n jwxI ] (319-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) simrit saastar soDh sabh kinai keem na jaanee. People have searched all the Simritees and Shaastras, but no one knows the Lord's value.
RECORD	para 14775	jo jnu BytY swDsMig so hir rMgu mwxI ] (319-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) jo jan bhaytai saaDhsang so har rang maanee. That being, who joins the Saadh Sangat enjoys the Love of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 14776	scu nwmu krqw purKu eyh rqnw KwxI ] (319-3, gauVI, mÚ 5) sach naam kartaa purakh ayh ratnaa khaanee. True is the Naam, the Name of the Creator, the Primal Being. It is the mine of precious jewels.
RECORD	para 14777	msqik hovY iliKAw hir ismir prwxI ] (319-3, gauVI, mÚ 5) mastak hovai likhi-aa har simar paraanee. That mortal, who has such pre-ordained destiny inscribed upon his forehead, meditates in remembrance on the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v4	qosw idcY scu nwmu nwnk imhmwxI ]4] (319-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) tosaa dichai sach naam naanak mihmaanee. ||4||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v4	O Lord, please bless Nanak, Your humble guest, with the supplies of the True Name. ||4||
RECORD	para 14779	slok mÚ 5 ] (319-4) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14780	AMqir icMqw nYxI suKI mUil n auqrY BuK ] (319-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) antar chintaa nainee sukhee mool na utrai bhukh. He harbors anxiety within himself, but to the eyes, he appears to be happy; his hunger never departs.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk scy nwm ibnu iksY n lQo duKu ]1] (319-5, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak sachay naam bin kisai na latho dukh. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, without the True Name, no one's sorrows have ever departed. ||1||
RECORD	para 14782	mÚ 5 ] (319-5) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14783	muTVy syeI swQ ijnI scu n lidAw ] (319-5, gauVI, mÚ 5) muth-rhay say-ee saath jinee sach na ladi-aa. Those caravans which did not load the Truth have been plundered.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk sy swbwis ijnI gur imil ieku pCwixAw ]2] (319-6, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak say saabaas jinee gur mil ik pachhaani-aa. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, those who meet the True Guru, and acknowledge the One Lord, are congratulated. ||2||
RECORD	para 14785	pauVI ] (319-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14786	ijQY bYsin swD jn so Qwnu suhMdw ] (319-6, gauVI, mÚ 5) jithai baisan saaDh jan so thaan suhandaa. Beautiful is that place, where the Holy people dwell.
RECORD	para 14787	Eie syvin sMimRQu Awpxw ibnsY sBu mMdw ] (319-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) o-ay sayvan sammrith aapnaa binsai sabh mandaa. They serve their All-powerful Lord, and they give up all their evil ways.
DEFINE	para 14788	piqq auDwrx pwrbRhm sMq bydu khMdw ] (319-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) patit uDhaaran paarbarahm sant bayd kahandaa. The Saints and the Vedas proclaim, that the Supreme Lord God is the Saving Grace of sinners.
DEFINE	para 14789	Bgiq vClu qyrw ibrdu hY juig juig vrqMdw ] (319-8, gauVI, mÚ 5) bhagat vachhal tayraa birad hai jug jug vartandaa. You are the Lover of Your devotees - this is Your natural way, in each and every age.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v5	nwnku jwcY eyku nwmu min qin BwvMdw ]5] (319-8, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak jaachai ayk naam man tan bhaavandaa. ||5||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v5	Nanak asks for the One Name, which is pleasing to his mind and body. ||5||
RECORD	para 14791	slok mÚ 5 ] (319-9) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14792	icVI cuhkI phu PutI vgin bhuqu qrMg ] (319-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) chirhee chuhkee pahu futee vagan bahut tarang. The sparrows are chirping, and dawn has come; the wind stirs up the waves.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	Acrj rUp sMqn rcy nwnk nwmih rMg ]1] (319-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) achraj roop santan rachay naanak naameh rang. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	Such a wondrous thing the Saints have fashioned, O Nanak, in the Love of the Naam. ||1||
RECORD	para 14794	mÚ 5 ] (319-10) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14795	Gr mMdr KusIAw qhI jh qU Awvih iciq ] (319-10, gauVI, mÚ 5) ghar mandar khusee-aa tahee jah too aavahi chit. Homes, palaces and pleasures are there, where You, O Lord, come to mind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	dunIAw kIAw vifAweIAw nwnk siB kuimq ]2] (319-10, gauVI, mÚ 5) dunee-aa kee-aa vadi-aa-ee-aa naanak sabh kumit. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	All worldly grandeur, O Nanak, is like false and evil friends. ||2||
RECORD	para 14797	pauVI ] (319-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14798	hir Dnu scI rwis hY iknY ivrlY jwqw ] (319-11, gauVI, mÚ 5) har Dhan sachee raas hai kinai virlai jaataa. The wealth of the Lord is the true capital; how rare are those who understand this.
RECORD	para 14799	iqsY prwpiq Bwierhu ijsu dyie ibDwqw ] (319-11, gauVI, mÚ 5) tisai paraapat bhaa-irahu jis day-ay biDhaataa. He alone receives it, O Siblings of Destiny, unto whom the Architect of Destiny gives it.
DEFINE	para 14800	mn qn BIqir mauilAw hir rMig jnu rwqw ] (319-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) man tan bheetar ma-oli-aa har rang jan raataa. His servant is imbued with the Love of the Lord; his body and mind blossom forth.
RECORD	para 14801	swDsMig gux gwieAw siB doKh Kwqw ] (319-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) saaDhsang gun gaa-i-aa sabh dokhah khaataa. In the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, he sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and all of his sufferings are removed.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v6	nwnk soeI jIivAw ijin ieku pCwqw ]6] (319-13, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak so-ee jeevi-aa jin ik pachhaataa. ||6||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v6	O Nanak, he alone lives, who acknowledges the One Lord. ||6||
RECORD	para 14803	slok mÚ 5 ] (319-13) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14804	KKVIAw suhwvIAw lgVIAw Ak kMiT ] (319-13, gauVI, mÚ 5) khakh-rhee-aa suhaavee-aa lagrhee-aa ak kanth. The fruit of the swallow-wort plant looks beautiful, attached to the branch of the tree;
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	ibrh ivCoVw DxI isau nwnk shsY gMiT ]1] (319-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) birah vichhorhaa Dhanee si-o naanak sahsai ganth. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	but when it is separated from the stem of its Master, O Nanak, it breaks apart into thousands of fragments. ||1||
RECORD	para 14806	mÚ 5 ] (319-14) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14807	ivswrydy mir gey mir iB n skih mUil ] (319-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) visaarayday mar ga-ay mar bhe na sakahi mool. Those who forget the Lord die, but they cannot die a complete death.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	vymuK hoey rwm qy ijau qskr aupir sUil ]2] (319-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) vaimukh ho-ay raam tay ji-o taskar upar sool. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	Those who turn their backs on the Lord suffer, like the thief impaled on the gallows. ||2||
RECORD	para 14809	pauVI ] (319-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14810	suK inDwnu pRBu eyku hY AibnwsI suixAw ] (319-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) sukh niDhaan parabh ayk hai abhinaasee suni-aa. The One God is the treasure of peace; I have heard that He is eternal and imperishable.
RECORD	para 14811	jil Qil mhIAil pUirAw Git Git hir BixAw ] (319-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) jal thal mahee-al poori-aa ghat ghat har bhani-aa. He is totally pervading the water, the land and the sky; the Lord is said to be permeating each and every heart.
RECORD	para 14812	aUc nIc sB iek smwin kIt hsqI bixAw ] (319-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) ooch neech sabh ik samaan keet hastee bani-aa. He looks alike upon the high and the low, the ant and the elephant.
DEFINE	para 14813	mIq sKw suq bMiDpo siB iqs dy jixAw ] (319-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) meet sakhaa sut banDhipo sabh tis day jani-aa. Friends, companions, children and relatives are all created by Him.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v7	quis nwnku dyvY ijsu nwmu iqin hir rMgu mixAw ]7] (319-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) tus naanak dayvai jis naam tin har rang mani-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v7	O Nanak, one who is blessed with the Naam, enjoys the Lord's love and affection. ||7||
RECORD	para 14815	slok mÚ 5 ] (319-18) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14816	ijnw swis igrwis n ivsrY hir nwmW min mMqu ] (319-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) jinaa saas giraas na visrai har naamaa N man mant. Those who do not forget the Lord, with each breath and morsel of food, whose minds are filled with the Mantra of the Lord's Name
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	DMnu is syeI nwnkw pUrnu soeI sMqu ]1] (319-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) Dhan se say-ee naankaa pooran so-ee sant. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	- they alone are blessed; O Nanak, they are the perfect Saints. ||1||
RECORD	para 14818	mÚ 5 ] (319-19) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14819	ATy phr Baudw iPrY Kwvx sMdVY sUil ] (319-19, gauVI, mÚ 5) athay pahar bha-udaa firai khaavan sand-rhai sool. Twenty-four hours a day, he wanders around, driven by his hunger for food.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	dojik paudw ikau rhY jw iciq n hoie rsUil ]2] (319-19, gauVI, mÚ 5) dojak pa-udaa ki-o rahai jaa chit na ho-ay rasool. ||2||
WHEN	slok mhlw 3 v2	How can he escape from falling into hell, when he does not remember the Prophet? ||2||
RECORD	para 14822	pauVI ] (320-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14823	iqsY sryvhu pRwxIho ijs dY nwau plY ] (320-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) tisai sarayvhu paraaneeho jis dai naa-o palai. Serve Him, O mortals, who has the Lord's Name in His lap.
REQUIRE	para 14824	AYQY rhhu suhyilAw AgY nwil clY ] (320-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) aithai rahhu suhayli-aa agai naal chalai. You shall dwell in peace and ease in this world; in the world hereafter, it shall go with you.
WHEN	para 14825	Gru bMDhu sc Drm kw gif QMmu AhlY ] (320-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) ghar banDhhu sach Dharam kaa gad thamm ahlai. So build your home of true righteousness, with the unshakable pillars of Dharma.
RECORD	para 14826	Et lYhu nwrwiexY dIn dunIAw JlY ] (320-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) ot laihu naaraa-inai deen dunee-aa jhalai. Take the Support of the Lord, who gives support in the spiritual and material worlds.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v8	nwnk pkVy crx hir iqsu drgh mlY ]8] (320-3, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak pakrhay charan har tis dargeh malai. ||8||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v8	Nanak grasps the Lotus Feet of the Lord; he humbly bows in His Court. ||8||
RECORD	para 14828	slok mÚ 5 ] (320-3) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14829	jwcku mMgY dwnu dyih ipAwirAw ] (320-3, gauVI, mÚ 5) jaachak mangai daan deh pi-aari-aa. The beggar begs for charity: give to me, O my Beloved!
DEFINE	para 14830	dyvxhwru dwqwru mY inq icqwirAw ] (320-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) dayvanhaar daataar mai nit chitaari-aa. O Great Giver, O Giving Lord, my consciousness is continually centered on You.
RECORD	para 14831	inKuit n jweI mUil Aqul BMfwirAw ] (320-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) nikhut na jaa-ee mool atul bhandaari-aa. The immeasurable warehouses of the Lord can never be emptied out.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk sbdu Apwru iqin sBu ikCu swirAw ]1] (320-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak sabad apaar tin sabh kichh saari-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, the Word of the Shabad is infinite; it has arranged everything perfectly. ||1||
RECORD	para 14833	mÚ 5 ] (320-5) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14834	isKhu sbdu ipAwirho jnm mrn kI tyk ] (320-5, gauVI, mÚ 5) sikhahu sabad pi-aariho janam maran kee tayk. O Sikhs, love the Word of the Shabad; in life and death, it is our only support.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	muK aUjl sdw suKI nwnk ismrq eyk ]2] (320-5, gauVI, mÚ 5) mukh oojal sadaa sukhee naanak simrat ayk. ||2||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 3 v2	Your face shall be radiant, and you shall find a lasting peace, O Nanak, remembering the One Lord in meditation. ||2||
RECORD	para 14836	pauVI ] (320-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14837	EQY AMimRqu vMfIAY suKIAw hir krxy ] (320-6, gauVI, mÚ 5) othai amrit vandee-ai sukhee-aa har karnay. There, the Ambrosial Nectar is distributed; the Lord is the Bringer of peace.
FORBID	para 14838	jm kY pMiQ n pweIAih iPir nwhI mrxy ] (320-6, gauVI, mÚ 5) jam kai panth na paa-ee-ah fir naahee marnay. They are not placed upon the path of Death, and they shall not have to die again.
RECORD	para 14839	ijs no AwieAw pRym rsu iqsY hI jrxy ] (320-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) jis no aa-i-aa paraym ras tisai hee jarnay. One who comes to savor the Lord's Love experiences it.
RECORD	para 14840	bwxI aucrih swD jn Aimau clih Jrxy ] (320-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) banee uchrahi saaDh jan ami-o chaleh jharnay. The Holy beings chant the Bani of the Word, like nectar flowing from a spring.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v9	pyiK drsnu nwnku jIivAw mn AMdir Drxy ]9] (320-8, gauVI, mÚ 5) paykh darsan naanak jeevi-aa man andar Dharnay. ||9||
UPHOLD	slok mhlw 3 v9	Nanak lives by beholding the Blessed Vision of the Darshan of those who have implanted the Lord's Name within their minds. ||9||
RECORD	para 14842	slok mÚ 5 ] (320-8) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14843	siqguir pUrY syivAY dUKw kw hoie nwsu ] (320-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) satgur poorai sayvi-ai dookhaa kaa ho-ay naas. Serving the Perfect True Guru, suffering ends.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk nwim ArwiDAY kwrju AwvY rwis ]1] (320-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak naam araaDhi-ai kaaraj aavai raas. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, worshipping the Naam in adoration, one's affairs come to be resolved. ||1||
RECORD	para 14845	mÚ 5 ] (320-9) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14846	ijsu ismrq sMkt Cutih And mMgl ibsRwm ] (320-10, gauVI, mÚ 5) jis simrat sankat chhuteh anad mangal bisraam. Remembering Him in meditation, misfortune departs, and one comes to abide in peace and bliss.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk jpIAY sdw hir inmK n ibsrau nwmu ]2] (320-10, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak japee-ai sadaa har nimakh na bisara-o naam. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, meditate forever on the Lord - do not forget Him, even for an instant. ||2||
RECORD	para 14848	pauVI ] (320-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14849	iqn kI soBw ikAw gxI ijnI hir hir lDw ] (320-11, gauVI, mÚ 5) tin kee sobhaa ki-aa ganee jinee har har laDhaa. How can I estimate the glory of those, who have found the Lord, Har, Har?
DEFINE	para 14850	swDw srxI jo pvY su CutY bDw ] (320-11, gauVI, mÚ 5) saaDhaa sarnee jo pavai so chhutai baDhaa. One who seeks the Sanctuary of the Holy is released from bondage.
RECORD	para 14851	gux gwvY AibnwsIAY join griB n dDw ] (320-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) gun gaavai abinaasee-ai jon garabh na daDhaa. One who sings the Glorious Praises of the Imperishable Lord does not burn in the womb of reincarnation.
RECORD	para 14852	guru ByitAw pwrbRhmu hir piV buiJ smDw ] (320-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) gur bhayti-aa paarbarahm har parh bujh samDhaa. One who meets the Guru and the Supreme Lord God, who reads and understands, enters the state of Samaadhi.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v10	nwnk pwieAw so DxI hir Agm AgDw ]10] (320-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak paa-i-aa so Dhanee har agam agDhaa. ||10||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v10	Nanak has obtained that Lord Master, who is inaccessible and unfathomable. ||10||
RECORD	para 14854	slok mÚ 5 ] (320-13) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14855	kwmu n krhI Awpxw iPrih Avqw loie ] (320-13, gauVI, mÚ 5) kaam na karhee aapnaa fireh avtaa lo-ay. People do not perform their duties, but instead, they wander around aimlessly.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk nwie ivswirAY suKu iknyhw hoie ]1] (320-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak naa-ay visaari-ai sukh kinayhaa ho-ay. ||1||
WHEN	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, if they forget the Name, how can they ever find peace? ||1||
RECORD	para 14857	mÚ 5 ] (320-14) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14858	ibKY kauVqix sgl mwih jgiq rhI lptwie ] (320-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) bikhai ka-urh-tan sagal maahi jagat rahee laptaa-ay. The bitter poison of corruption is everywhere; it clings to the substance of the world.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk jin vIcwirAw mITw hir kw nwau ]2] (320-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak jan veechaari-aa meethaa har kaa naa-o. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, the humble being has realized that the Name of the Lord alone is sweet. ||2||
RECORD	para 14860	pauVI ] (320-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14861	ieh nIswxI swD kI ijsu Bytq qrIAY ] (320-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) ih neesaanee saaDh kee jis bhaytat taree-ai. This is the distinguishing sign of the Holy Saint, that by meeting with him, one is saved.
RECORD	para 14862	jmkMkru nyiV n AwveI iPir bhuiV n mrIAY ] (320-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) jamkankar nayrh na aavee fir bahurh na maree-ai. The Messenger of Death does not come near him; he never has to die again.
RECORD	para 14863	Bv swgru sMswru ibKu so pwir auqrIAY ] (320-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) bhav saagar sansaar bikh so paar utree-ai. He crosses over the terrifying, poisonous world-ocean.
REQUIRE	para 14864	hir gux guMPhu min mwl hir sB mlu prhrIAY ] (320-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) har gun gufhu man maal har sabh mal parharee-ai. So weave the garland of the Lord's Glorious Praises into your mind, and all your filth shall be washed away.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v11	nwnk pRIqm imil rhy pwrbRhm nrhrIAY ]11] (320-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak pareetam mil rahay paarbarahm narharee-ai. ||11||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v11	Nanak remains blended with his Beloved, the Supreme Lord God. ||11||
RECORD	para 14866	slok mÚ 5 ] (320-18) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14867	nwnk Awey sy prvwxu hY ijn hir vuTw iciq ] (320-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak aa-ay say parvaan hai jin har vuthaa chit. O Nanak, approved is the birth of those, within whose consciousness the Lord abides.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	gwl@I Al plwlIAw kMim n Awvih imq ]1] (320-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) gaalHee al palaalee-aa kamm na aavahi mit. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	Useless talk and babbling is useless, my friend. ||1||
RECORD	para 14869	mÚ 5 ] (320-19) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14870	pwrbRhmu pRBu idRstI AwieAw pUrn Agm ibsmwd ] (320-19, gauVI, mÚ 5) paarbarahm parabh daristee aa-i-aa pooran agam bismaad. I have come to see the Supreme Lord God, the Perfect, Inaccessible, Wonderful Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk rwm nwmu Dnu kIqw pUry gur prswid ]2] (321-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak raam naam Dhan keetaa pooray gur parsaad. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	Nanak has made the Lord's Name his wealth, by the Grace of the Perfect Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 14873	pauVI ] (321-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14874	Dohu n clI Ksm nwil lib moih ivguqy ] (321-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) Dhohu na chalee khasam naal lab mohi vigutay. Deception does not work with our Lord and Master; through their greed and emotional attachment, people are ruined.
RECORD	para 14875	krqb krin BlyirAw mid mwieAw suqy ] (321-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) kartab karan bhalayri-aa mad maa-i-aa sutay. They do their evil deeds, and sleep in the intoxication of Maya.
DEFINE	para 14876	iPir iPir jUin BvweIAin jm mwrig muqy ] (321-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) fir fir joon bhavaa-ee-an jam maarag mutay. Time and time again, they are consigned to reincarnation, and abandoned on the path of Death.
DEFINE	para 14877	kIqw pwiein Awpxw duK syqI juqy ] (321-3, gauVI, mÚ 5) keetaa paa-in aapnaa dukh saytee jutay. They receive the consequences of their own actions, and are yoked to their pain.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v12	nwnk nwie ivswirAY sB mMdI ruqy ]12] (321-3, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak naa-ay visaari-ai sabh mandee rutay. ||12||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v12	O Nanak, if one forgets the Name, all the seasons are evil. ||12||
RECORD	para 14879	slok mÚ 5 ] (321-3) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14880	auTMidAw bhMidAw svMidAw suKu soie ] (321-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) uthandi-aa bahandi-aa suvandiaa sukh so-ay. While standing up, sitting down and sleeping, be at peace;
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk nwim slwihAY mnu qnu sIqlu hoie ]1] (321-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak naam salaahi-ai man tan seetal ho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, praising the Naam, the Name of the Lord, the mind and body are cooled and soothed. ||1||
RECORD	para 14882	mÚ 5 ] (321-4) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14883	lwlic AitAw inq iPrY suAwrQu kry n koie ] (321-5, gauVI, mÚ 5) laalach ati-aa nit firai su-aarath karay na ko-ay. Filled with greed, he constantly wanders around; he does not do any good deeds.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	ijsu guru BytY nwnkw iqsu min visAw soie ]2] (321-5, gauVI, mÚ 5) jis gur bhaytai naankaa tis man vasi-aa so-ay. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, the Lord abides within the mind of one who meets with the Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 14885	pauVI ] (321-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14886	sBy vsqU kauVIAw scy nwau imTw ] (321-6, gauVI, mÚ 5) sabhay vastoo ka-urhee-aa sachay naa-o mithaa. All material things are bitter; the True Name alone is sweet.
RECORD	para 14887	swdu AwieAw iqn hir jnW ciK swDI ifTw ] (321-6, gauVI, mÚ 5) saad aa-i-aa tin har janaa N chakh saaDhee dithaa. Those humble servants of the Lord who taste it, come to savor its flavor.
DEFINE	para 14888	pwrbRhim ijsu iliKAw min iqsY vuTw ] (321-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) paarbarahm jis likhi-aa man tisai vuthaa. It comes to dwell within the mind of those who are so pre-destined by the Supreme Lord God.
DEFINE	para 14889	ieku inrMjnu riv rihAw Bwau duXw kuTw ] (321-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) ik niranjan rav rahi-aa bhaa-o duyaa kuthaa. The One Immaculate Lord is pervading everywhere; He destroys the love of duality.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v13	hir nwnku mMgY joiV kr pRBu dyvY quTw ]13] (321-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) har naanak mangai jorh kar parabh dayvai tuthaa. ||13||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v13	Nanak begs for the Lord's Name, with his palms pressed together; by His Pleasure, God has granted it. ||13||
RECORD	para 14891	slok mÚ 5 ] (321-8) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14892	jwcVI sw swru jo jwcMdI hykVo ] (321-8, gauVI, mÚ 5) jaachrhee saa saar jo jaachandee haykrho. The most excellent begging is begging for the One Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	gwl@I ibAw ivkwr nwnk DxI ivhUxIAw ]1] (321-8, gauVI, mÚ 5) gaalHee bi-aa vikaar naanak Dhanee vihoonee-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	Other talk is corrupt, O Nanak, except that of the Lord Master. ||1||
RECORD	para 14894	mÚ 5 ] (321-9) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14895	nIih ij ivDw mMnu pCwxU ivrlo iQE ] (321-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) neehi je viDhaa man pachhaanoo virlo thi-o. One who recognizes the Lord is very rare; his mind is pierced through with the Love of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	joVxhwrw sMqu nwnk pwDru pDro ]2] (321-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) jorhanhaaraa sant naanak paaDhar paDhro. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	Such a Saint is the Uniter, O Nanak - he straightens out the path. ||2||
RECORD	para 14897	pauVI ] (321-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14898	soeI syivhu jIAVy dwqw bKisMdu ] (321-10, gauVI, mÚ 5) so-ee sayvihu jee-arhay daataa bakhsind. Serve Him, O my soul, who is the Giver and the Forgiver.
DEFINE	para 14899	iklivK siB ibnwsu hoin ismrq goivMdu ] (321-10, gauVI, mÚ 5) kilvikh sabh binaas hon simrat govind. All sinful mistakes are erased, by meditating in remembrance on the Lord of the Universe.
RECORD	para 14900	hir mwrgu swDU disAw jpIAY gurmMqu ] (321-11, gauVI, mÚ 5) har maarag saaDhoo dasi-aa japee-ai gurmant. The Holy Saint has shown me the Way to the Lord; I chant the GurMantra.
DEFINE	para 14901	mwieAw suAwd siB iPikAw hir min BwvMdu ] (321-11, gauVI, mÚ 5) maa-i-aa su-aad sabh fiki-aa har man bhaavand. The taste of Maya is totally bland and insipid; the Lord alone is pleasing to my mind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v14	iDAwie nwnk prmysrY ijin idqI ijMdu ]14] (321-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) Dhi-aa-ay naanak parmaysrai jin ditee jind. ||14||
UPHOLD	slok mhlw 3 v14	Meditate, O Nanak, on the Transcendent Lord, who has blessed you with your soul and your life. ||14||
RECORD	para 14903	slok mÚ 5 ] (321-12) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 14904	vq lgI scy nwm kI jo bIjy so Kwie ] (321-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) vat lagee sachay naam kee jo beejay so khaa-ay. The time has come to plant the seed of the Lord's Name; one who plants it, shall eat its fruit.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	iqsih prwpiq nwnkw ijs no iliKAw Awie ]1] (321-13, gauVI, mÚ 5) tiseh paraapat naankaa jis no likhi-aa aa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	He alone receives it, O Nanak, whose destiny is so pre-ordained. ||1||
RECORD	para 14906	mÚ 5 ] (321-13) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14907	mMgxw q scu ieku ijsu quis dyvY Awip ] (321-13, gauVI, mÚ 5) mangnaa ta sach ik jis tus dayvai aap. If one begs, then he should beg for the Name of the True One, which is given only by His Pleasure.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	ijqu KwDY mnu iqRpqIAY nwnk swihb dwiq ]2] (321-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) jit khaaDhai man taripat-ee-ai naanak saahib daat. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	Eating this gift from the Lord and Master, O Nanak, the mind is satisfied. ||2||
RECORD	para 14909	pauVI ] (321-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14910	lwhw jg mih sy Ktih ijn hir Dnu rwis ] (321-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) laahaa jag meh say khateh jin har Dhan raas. They alone earn profit in this world, who have the wealth of the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 14911	duqIAw Bwau n jwxnI scy dI Aws ] (321-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) dutee-aa bhaa-o na jaannee sachay dee aas. They do not know the love of duality; they place their hopes in the True Lord.
RECORD	para 14912	inhclu eyku sryivAw horu sB ivxwsu ] (321-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) nihchal ayk sarayvi-aa hor sabh vinaas. They serve the One Eternal Lord, and give up everything else.
DEFINE	para 14913	pwrbRhmu ijsu ivsrY iqsu ibrQw swsu ] (321-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) paarbarahm jis visrai tis birthaa saas. One who forgets the Supreme Lord God - useless is his breath.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v15	kMiT lwie jn riKAw nwnk bil jwsu ]15] (321-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) kanth laa-ay jan rakhi-aa naanak bal jaas. ||15||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v15	God draws His humble servant close in His loving embrace and protects him - Nanak is a sacrifice to Him. ||15||
RECORD	para 14915	slok mÚ 5 ] (321-17) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14916	pwrbRhim PurmwieAw mIhu vuTw shij suBwie ] (321-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) paarbarahm furmaa-i-aa meehu vuthaa sahj subhaa-ay. The Supreme Lord God gave the Order, and the rain automatically began to fall.
RECORD	para 14917	AMnu DMnu bhuqu aupijAw ipRQmI rjI iqpiq AGwie ] (321-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) ann Dhan bahut upji-aa parithmee rajee tipat aghaa-ay. Grain and wealth were produced in abundance; the earth was totally satisfied and satiated.
RECORD	para 14918	sdw sdw gux aucrY duKu dwldu gieAw iblwie ] (321-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) sadaa sadaa gun uchrai dukh daalad ga-i-aa bilaa-ay. Forever and ever, chant the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and pain and poverty shall run away.
DEFINE	para 14919	pUrib iliKAw pwieAw imilAw iqsY rjwie ] (321-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) poorab likhi-aa paa-i-aa mili-aa tisai rajaa-ay. People obtain that which they are pre-ordained to receive, according to the Will of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	prmysir jIvwilAw nwnk iqsY iDAwie ]1] (321-19, gauVI, mÚ 5) parmaysar jeevaali-aa naanak tisai Dhi-aa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	The Transcendent Lord keeps you alive; O Nanak, meditate on Him. ||1||
RECORD	para 14921	mÚ 5 ] (321-19) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14923	jIvn pdu inrbwxu ieko ismrIAY ] (322-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) jeevan pad nirbaan iko simree-ai. To obtain the state of life of Nirvaanaa, meditate in remembrance on the One Lord.
DEFINE	para 14924	dUjI nwhI jwie ikin ibiD DIrIAY ] (322-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) doojee naahee jaa-ay kin biDh Dheeree-ai. There is no other place; how else can we be comforted?
DEFINE	para 14925	ifTw sBu sMswru suKu n nwm ibnu ] (322-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) dithaa sabh sansaar sukh na naam bin. I have seen the whole world - without the Lord's Name, there is no peace at all.
REQUIRE	para 14926	qnu Dnu hosI Cwru jwxY koie jnu ] (322-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) tan Dhan hosee chhaar jaanai ko-ay jan. Body and wealth shall return to dust - hardly anyone realizes this.
DEFINE	para 14927	rMg rUp rs bwid ik krih prwxIAw ] (322-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) rang roop ras baad ke karahi paraanee-aa. Pleasure, beauty and delicious tastes are useless; what are you doing, O mortal?
RECORD	para 14928	ijsu Bulwey Awip iqsu kl nhI jwxIAw ] (322-2, gauVI, mÚ 5) jis bhulaa-ay aap tis kal nahee jaanee-aa. One whom the Lord Himself misleads, does not understand His awesome power.
DEFINE	para 14929	rMig rqy inrbwxu scw gwvhI ] (322-3, gauVI, mÚ 5) rang ratay nirbaan sachaa gaavhee. Those who are imbued with the Love of the Lord attain Nirvaanaa, singing the Praises of the True One.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk srix duAwir jy quDu BwvhI ]2] (322-3, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak saran du-aar jay tuDh bhaavhee. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	Nanak: those who are pleasing to Your Will, O Lord, seek Sanctuary at Your Door. ||2||
RECORD	para 14931	pauVI ] (322-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14932	jMmxu mrxu n iqn@ kau jo hir liV lwgy ] (322-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) jaman maran na tin H ka-o jo har larh laagay. Those who are attached to the hem of the Lord's robe, do not suffer birth and death.
DEFINE	para 14933	jIvq sy prvwxu hoey hir kIrqin jwgy ] (322-4, gauVI, mÚ 5) jeevat say parvaan ho-ay har keertan jaagay. Those who remain awake to the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises - their lives are approved.
DEFINE	para 14934	swDsMgu ijn pwieAw syeI vfBwgy ] (322-5, gauVI, mÚ 5) saaDhsang jin paa-i-aa say-ee vadbhaagay. Those who attain the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, are very fortunate.
DEFINE	para 14935	nwie ivsirAY iDRgu jIvxw qUty kc Dwgy ] (322-5, gauVI, mÚ 5) naa-ay visri-ai Dharig jeevnaa tootay kach Dhaagay. But those who forget the Name - their lives are cursed, and broken like thin strands of thread.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v16	nwnk DUiV punIq swD lK koit iprwgy ]16] (322-6, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak Dhoorh puneet saaDh lakh kot piraagay. ||16||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v16	O Nanak, the dust of the feet of the Holy is more sacred than hundreds of thousands, even millions of cleansing baths at sacred shrines. ||16||
RECORD	para 14937	sloku mÚ 5 ] (322-6) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14938	Drix suvMnI KV rqn jVwvI hir pRym purKu min vuTw ] (322-6, gauVI, mÚ 5) Dharan suvannee kharh ratan jarhaavee har paraym purakh man vuthaa. Like the beautiful earth, adorned with jewels of grass - such is the mind, within which the Love of the Lord abides.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	sBy kwj suhylVy QIey guru nwnku siqguru quTw ]1] (322-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) sabhay kaaj suhaylrhay thee-ay gur naanak satgur tuthaa. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	All one's affairs are easily resolved, O Nanak, when the Guru, the True Guru, is pleased. ||1||
RECORD	para 14940	mÚ 5 ] (322-7) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 14941	iPrdI iPrdI dh idsw jl prbq bnrwie ] (322-7, gauVI, mÚ 5) firdee firdee dah disaa jal parbat banraa-ay. Roaming and wandering in the ten directions, over water, mountains and forests
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	ijQY ifTw imrqko iel bihTI Awie ]2] (322-8, gauVI, mÚ 5) jithai dithaa mirtako il bahithee aa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	- wherever the vulture sees a dead body, he flies down and lands. ||2||
RECORD	para 14943	pauVI ] (322-8) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14944	ijsu srb suKw Pl loVIAih so scu kmwvau ] (322-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) jis sarab sukhaa fal lorhee-ah so sach kamaava-o. One who longs for all comforts and rewards should practice Truth.
RECORD	para 14945	nyVY dyKau pwrbRhmu ieku nwmu iDAwvau ] (322-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) nayrhai daykh-a-u paarbarahm ik naam Dhi-aava-o. Behold the Supreme Lord God near you, and meditate on the Naam, the Name of the One Lord.
RECORD	para 14946	hoie sgl kI ryxukw hir sMig smwvau ] (322-9, gauVI, mÚ 5) ho-ay sagal kee raynukaa har sang samaava-o. Become the dust of all men's feet, and so merge with the Lord.
REQUIRE	para 14947	dUKu n dyeI iksY jIA piq isau Gir jwvau ] (322-10, gauVI, mÚ 5) dookh na day-ee kisai jee-a pat si-o ghar jaava-o. Do not cause any being to suffer, and you shall go to your true home with honor.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v17	piqq punIq krqw purKu nwnk suxwvau ]17] (322-10, gauVI, mÚ 5) patit puneet kartaa purakh naanak sunaava-o. ||17||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v17	Nanak speaks of the Purifier of sinners, the Creator, the Primal Being. ||17||
RECORD	para 14949	slok dohw mÚ 5 ] (322-11) salok dohaa mehlaa 5. Shalok, Dohaa, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14950	eyku ij swjnu mY kIAw srb klw smrQu ] (322-11, gauVI, mÚ 5) ayk je saajan mai kee-aa sarab kalaa samrath. I have made the One Lord my Friend; He is All-powerful to do everything.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	jIau hmwrw KMnIAY hir mn qn sMdVI vQu ]1] (322-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) jee-o hamaaraa khannee-ai har man tan sand-rhee vath. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	My soul is a sacrifice to Him; the Lord is the treasure of my mind and body. ||1||
RECORD	para 14952	mÚ 5 ] (322-12) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 14953	jy kru ghih ipAwrVy quDu n Cofw mUil ] (322-12, gauVI, mÚ 5) jay kar gaheh pi-aarrhay tuDh na chhodaa mool. Take my hand, O my Beloved; I shall never forsake You.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	hir Cofin sy durjnw pVih dojk kY sUil ]2] (322-13, gauVI, mÚ 5) har chhodan say durjanaa parheh dojak kai sool. ||2||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 3 v2	Those who forsake the Lord, are the most evil people; they shall fall into the horrible pit of hell. ||2||
RECORD	para 14955	pauVI ] (322-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 14956	siB inDwn Gir ijs dY hir kry su hovY ] (322-13, gauVI, mÚ 5) sabh niDhaan ghar jis dai har karay so hovai. All treasures are in His Home; whatever the Lord does, comes to pass.
RECORD	para 14957	jip jip jIvih sMq jn pwpw mlu DovY ] (322-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) jap jap jeeveh sant jan paapaa mal Dhovai. The Saints live by chanting and meditating on the Lord, washing off the filth of their sins.
DEFINE	para 14958	crn kml ihrdY vsih sMkt siB KovY ] (322-14, gauVI, mÚ 5) charan kamal hirdai vaseh sankat sabh khovai. With the Lotus Feet of the Lord dwelling within the heart, all misfortune is taken away.
FORBID	para 14959	guru pUrw ijsu BytIAY mir jnim n rovY ] (322-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) gur pooraa jis bhaytee-ai mar janam na rovai. One who meets the Perfect Guru, shall not have to suffer through birth and death.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v18	pRB drs ipAws nwnk GxI ikrpw kir dyvY ]18] (322-15, gauVI, mÚ 5) parabh daras pi-aas naanak ghanee kirpaa kar dayvai. ||18||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v18	Nanak is thirsty for the Blessed Vision of God's Darshan; by His Grace, He has bestowed it. ||18||
RECORD	para 14961	slok fKxw mÚ 5 ] (322-16) salok dakh-naa mehlaa 5. Shalok, Dakhanaa, Fifth Mehl:
WHEN	para 14962	BorI Brmu v\wie iprI muhbiq ihku qU ] (322-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) bhoree bharam vanjaa-ay piree muhabat hik too. If you can dispel your doubts, even for an instant, and love your only Beloved,
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	ijQhu vM\Y jwie iqQwaU maujUdu soie ]1] (322-16, gauVI, mÚ 5) jithahu vanjai jaa-ay tithaa-oo ma-ujood so-ay. ||1||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 3 v1	then wherever you go, there you shall find Him. ||1||
RECORD	para 14964	mÚ 5 ] (322-17) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14965	ciV kY GoVVY kuMdy pkVih KUMfI dI KyfwrI ] (322-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) charh kai ghorh-rhai kunday pakrheh khoondee dee khaydaaree. Can they mount horses and handle guns, if all they know is the game of polo?
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	hMsw syqI icqu aulwsih kukV dI EfwrI ]2] (322-17, gauVI, mÚ 5) hansaa saytee chit ulaaseh kukarh dee odaaree. ||2||
WHEN	slok mhlw 3 v2	Can they be swans, and fulfill their conscious desires, if they can only fly like chickens? ||2||
RECORD	para 14967	pauVI ] (322-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 14968	rsnw aucrY hir sRvxI suxY so auDrY imqw ] (322-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) rasnaa uchrai har sarvanee sunai so uDhrai mitaa. Those who chant the Lord's Name with their tongues and hear it with their ears are saved, O my friend.
DEFINE	para 14969	hir jsu ilKih lwie BwvnI sy hsq pivqw ] (322-18, gauVI, mÚ 5) har jas likheh laa-ay bhaavnee say hasat pavitaa. Those hands which lovingly write the Praises of the Lord are pure.
DEFINE	para 14970	ATsiT qIrQ mjnw siB puMn iqin ikqw ] (322-19, gauVI, mÚ 5) athsath tirath majnaa sabh punn tin kitaa. It is like performing all sorts of virtuous deeds, and bathing at the sixty-eight sacred shrines of pilgrimage.
RECORD	para 14971	sMswr swgr qy auDry ibiKAw gVu ijqw ] (322-19, gauVI, mÚ 5) sansaar saagar tay uDhray bikhi-aa garh jitaa. They cross over the world-ocean, and conquer the fortress of corruption.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v19	nwnk liV lwie auDwirAnu dXu syiv Aimqw ]19] (323-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) naanak larh laa-ay uDhaari-an da-yu sayv amitaa. ||19||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v19	O Nanak, serve the Infinite Lord; grasp the hem of His robe, and He will save you. ||19||
RECORD	para 14974	slok mÚ 5 ] (323-1) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 14975	DMDVy kulwh iciq n AwvY hykVo ] (323-1, gauVI, mÚ 5) DhanDh-rhay kulaah chit na aavai haykrho. Worldly affairs are unprofitable, if the One Lord does not come to mind.
