DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	No life or death, no pain or pleasure is felt there. There is only the Primal Trance of Samaadhi, and no duality. ||1||
DEFINE	para 15517	shj kI AkQ kQw hY inrwrI ] (333-9, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) sahj kee akath kathaa hai niraaree. The description of the state of intuitive poise is indescribable and sublime.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	quil nhI cFY jwie n mukwqI hlukI lgY n BwrI ]1] rhwau ] (333-9, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) tul nahee chadhai jaa-ay na mukaatee halukee lagai na bhaaree. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	rahaa-o. It is not measured, and it is not exhausted. It is neither light nor heavy. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 15519	ArD aurD doaU qh nwhI rwiq idnsu qh nwhI ] (333-10, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) araDh uraDh do-oo tah naahee raat dinas tah naahee. Neither lower nor upper worlds are there; neither day nor night are there.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v2	jlu nhI pvnu pwvku Puin nwhI siqgur qhw smwhI ]2] (333-11, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) jal nahee pavan paavak fun naahee satgur tahaa samaahee. ||2||
DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v2	There is no water, wind or fire; there, the True Guru is contained. ||2||
RECORD	para 15521	Agm Agocru rhY inrMqir gur ikrpw qy lhIAY ] (333-11, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) agam agochar rahai nirantar gur kirpaa tay lahee-ai. The Inaccessible and Unfathomable Lord dwells there within Himself; by Guru's Grace, He is found.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v3	khu kbIr bil jwau gur Apuny sqsMgiq imil rhIAY ]3]4]48] (333-12, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) kaho kabeer bal jaa-o gur apunay satsangat mil rahee-ai. ||3||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v3	Says Kabeer, I am a sacrifice to my Guru; I remain in the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy. ||3||
RECORD	para 15523	gauVI ] (333-13) ga-orhee. Gauree:
RECORD	para 15524	pwpu puMnu duie bYl ibswhy pvnu pUjI prgwisE ] (333-13, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) paap punn du-ay bail bisaahay pavan poojee pargaasi-o. With both sin and virtue, the ox of the body is purchased; the air of the breath is the capital which has appeared.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	iqRsnw gUix BrI Gt BIqir ien ibiD tWf ibswihE ]1] (333-13, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) tarisnaa goon bharee ghat bheetar in biDh taaNd bisaahi-o. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	The bag on its back is filled with desire; this is how we purchase the herd. ||1||
DEFINE	para 15526	AYsw nwieku rwmu hmwrw ] (333-14, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) aisaa naa-ik raam hamaaraa. My Lord is such a wealthy merchant!
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	sgl sMswru kIE bnjwrw ]1] rhwau ] (333-14, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) sagal sansaar kee-o banjaaraa. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	rahaa-o. He has made the whole world his peddler. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 15528	kwmu k®oDu duie Bey jgwqI mn qrMg btvwrw ] (333-15, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) kaam kroDh du-ay bha-ay jagaatee man tarang batvaaraa. Sexual desire and anger are the tax-collectors, and the waves of the mind are the highway robbers.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v2	pMc qqu imil dwnu inbyrih tWfw auqirE pwrw ]2] (333-15, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) panch tat mil daan nibayreh taa Ndaa utri-o paaraa. ||2||
DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v2	The five elements join together and divide up their loot. This is how our herd is disposed of! ||2||
DEFINE	para 15530	khq kbIru sunhu ry sMqhu Ab AYsI bin AweI ] (333-16, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) kahat kabeer sunhu ray santahu ab aisee ban aa-ee. Says Kabeer, listen, O Saints: This is the state of affairs now!
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v3	GwtI cFq bYlu ieku Qwkw clo goin iCtkweI ]3]5]49] (333-16, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) ghaatee chadhat bail ik thaakaa chalo gon chhitkaa-ee. ||3||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v3	Going uphill, the ox has grown weary; throwing off his load, he continues on his journey. ||3||
RECORD	para 15532	gauVI pMcpdw ] (333-17) ga-orhee panchpadaa. Gauree, Panch-Padas:
REQUIRE	para 15533	pyvkVY idn cwir hY swhurVY jwxw ] (333-17, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) payvkarhai din chaar hai saahurrhai jaanaa. For a few short days, the soul-bride stays in her parent's house; then, she must go to her in-laws.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	AMDw loku n jwxeI mUrKu eyAwxw ]1] (333-17, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) anDhaa lok na jaan-ee moorakh ay-aanaa. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	The blind, foolish and ignorant people do not know this. ||1||
DEFINE	para 15535	khu ffIAw bwDY Dn KVI ] (333-18, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) kaho dadee-aa baaDhai Dhan kharhee. Tell me, why is the bride wearing her ordinary clothes?
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	pwhU Gir Awey muklwaU Awey ]1] rhwau ] (333-18, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) paahoo ghar aa-ay muklaa-oo aa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	rahaa-o. The guests have arrived at her home, and her Husband has come to take her away. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 15537	Eh ij idsY KUhVI kaun lwju vhwrI ] (333-18, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) oh je disai khoohrhee ka-un laaj vahaaree. Who has lowered the rope of the breath down, into the well of the world which we see?
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v2	lwju GVI isau qUit pVI auiT clI pinhwrI ]2] (333-19, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) laaj gharhee si-o toot parhee uth chalee panihaaree. ||2||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v2	The rope of the breath breaks away from the pitcher of the body, and the water- carrier gets up and departs. ||2||
WHEN	para 15539	swihbu hoie dieAwlu ik®pw kry Apunw kwrju svwry ] (333-19, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) saahib ho-ay da-i-aal kirpaa karay apunaa kaaraj savaaray. When the Lord and Master is kind and grants His Grace, then her affairs are all resolved.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v3	qw sohwgix jwxIAY gur sbdu bIcwry ]3] (334-1, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) taa sohagan jaanee-ai gur sabad beechaaray. ||3||
DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v3	Then she is known as the happy soul-bride, if she contemplates the Word of the Guru's Shabad. ||3||
RECORD	para 15542	ikrq kI bWDI sB iPrY dyKhu bIcwrI ] (334-1, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) kirat kee baa NDhee sabh firai daykhhu beechaaree. Bound by the actions she has committed, she wanders around - see this and understand.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v4	eys no ikAw AwKIAY ikAw kry ivcwrI ]4] (334-2, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) ays no ki-aa aakhee-ai ki-aa karay vichaaree. ||4||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v4	What can we say to her? What can the poor soul-bride do? ||4||
RECORD	para 15544	BeI inrwsI auiT clI icq bMiD n DIrw ] (334-2, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) bha-ee niraasee uth chalee chit banDh na Dheeraa. Disappointed and hopeless, she gets up and departs. There is no support or encouragement in her consciousness.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v5	hir kI crxI lwig rhu Bju srix kbIrw ]5]6]50] (334-3, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) har kee charnee laag rahu bhaj saran kabeeraa. ||5||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v5	So remain attached to the Lord's Lotus Feet, and hurry to His Sanctuary, Kabeer! ||5||
RECORD	para 15546	gauVI ] (334-3) ga-orhee. Gauree :
DEFINE	para 15547	jogI khih jogu Bl mITw Avru n dUjw BweI ] (334-3, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) jogee kaheh jog bhal meethaa avar na doojaa bhaa-ee. The Yogi says that Yoga is good and sweet, and nothing else is, O Siblings of Destiny.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	ruMifq muMifq eykY sbdI eyie khih isiD pweI ]1] (334-4, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) rundit mundit aykai sabdee ay-ay kaheh siDh paa-ee. ||1||
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	Those who shave their heads, and those who amputate their limbs, and those who utter only a single word, all say that they have attained the spiritual perfection of the Siddhas. ||1||
DEFINE	para 15549	hir ibnu Brim Bulwny AMDw ] (334-5, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) har bin bharam bhulaanay anDhaa. Without the Lord, the blind ones are deluded by doubt.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	jw pih jwau Awpu Cutkwvin qy bwDy bhu PMDw ]1] rhwau ] (334-5, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) jaa peh jaa-o aap chhutkaavan tay baaDhay baho fanDhaa. ||1||
DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v1	rahaa-o. And those, to whom I go to find release - they themselves are bound by all sorts of chains. ||1||Pause||
WHEN	para 15551	jh qy aupjI qhI smwnI ieh ibiD ibsrI qb hI ] (334-5, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) jah tay upjee tahee samaanee ih biDh bisree tab hee. The soul is re-absorbed into that from which it originated, when one leaves this path of errors.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v2	pMifq guxI sUr hm dwqy eyih khih bf hm hI ]2] (334-6, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) pandit gunee soor ham daatay ayhi kaheh bad ham hee. ||2||
DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v2	The scholarly Pandits, the virtuous, the brave and the generous, all assert that they alone are great. ||2||
RECORD	para 15553	ijsih buJwey soeI bUJY ibnu bUJy ikau rhIAY ] (334-7, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) jisahi bujhaa-ay so-ee boojhai bin boojhay ki-o rahee-ai. He alone understands, whom the Lord inspires to understand. Without understanding, what can anyone do?
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v3	siqguru imlY AMDyrw cUkY ien ibiD mwxku lhIAY ]3] (334-7, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) satgur milai anDhayraa chookai in biDh maanak lahee-ai. ||3||
DEFINE	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v3	Meeting the True Guru, the darkness is dispelled, and in this way, the jewel is obtained. ||3||
RECORD	para 15555	qij bwvy dwhny ibkwrw hir pdu idRVu kir rhIAY ] (334-8, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) taj baavay daahnay bikaaraa har pad darirh kar rahee-ai. Give up the evil actions of your left and right hands, and grasp hold of the Feet of the Lord.
RECORD	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v4	khu kbIr gUMgY guVu KwieAw pUCy qy ikAw khIAY ]4]7]51] (334-8, gauVI, Bgq kbIr jI) kaho kabeer goo Ngai gurh khaa-i-aa poochhay tay ki-aa kahee-ai. ||4||
WHEN	gauVI kbIr jI kI nwil rlwie iliKAw mhlw 5 v4	Says Kabeer, the mute has tasted the molasses, but what can he say about it if he is asked? ||4||
RECORD	para 15557	rwgu gauVI pUrbI kbIr jI ] (334-10) raag ga-orhee poorbee kabeer jee. Raag Gauree Poorbee, Kabeer Jee:
RECORD	para 15558	<> siqgur pRswid ] (334-10) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
