DEFINE	para 21606	rwm nwmu dyvw mih sUru ] (470-5, Awsw, mÚ 1) raam naam dayvaa meh soor. among the deities, the Lord's Name is the most exalted.
RECORD	para 21607	nwie lieAY prwCq jwih ] (470-5, Awsw, mÚ 1) naa-ay la-i-ai paraachhat jaahi. Chanting the Name, sins depart;
RECORD	para 21608	nwnk qau moKMqru pwih ] (470-5, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak ta-o mokhantar paahi. O Nanak, then, one obtains salvation.
RECORD	para 21609	juj mih joir ClI cMdRwvil kwn@ ik®snu jwdmu BieAw ] (470-6, Awsw, mÚ 1) juj meh jor chhalee chandraaval kaan H krisan jaadam bha-i-aa. In the Jujar Veda, Kaan Krishna of the Yaadva tribe seduced Chandraavali by force.
RECORD	para 21610	pwrjwqu gopI lY AwieAw ibMdRwbn mih rMgu kIAw ] (470-6, Awsw, mÚ 1) paarjaat gopee lai aa-i-aa bindraaban meh rang kee-aa. He brought the Elysian Tree for his milk-maid, and revelled in Brindaaban.
RECORD	para 21611	kil mih bydu AQrbxu hUAw nwau KudweI Alhu BieAw ] (470-7, Awsw, mÚ 1) kal meh bayd atharban hoo-aa naa-o khudaa-ee alhu bha-i-aa. In the Dark Age of Kali Yuga, the Atharva Veda became prominent; Allah became the Name of God.
RECORD	para 21612	nIl bsqR ly kpVy pihry qurk pTwxI Amlu kIAw ] (470-7, Awsw, mÚ 1) neel bastar lay kaprhay pahiray turak pathaanee amal kee-aa. Men began to wear blue robes and garments; Turks and Pat'haans assumed power.
