RECORD	para 21696	kUVu boil krih Awhwru ] (471-18, Awsw, mÚ 1) koorh bol karahi aahaar. Speaking falsehood, they take their food.
DEFINE	para 21697	srm Drm kw fyrw dUir ] (471-18, Awsw, mÚ 1) saram Dharam kaa dayraa door. The home of modesty and Dharma is far from them.
DEFINE	para 21698	nwnk kUVu rihAw BrpUir ] (471-19, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak koorh rahi-aa bharpoor. O Nanak, they are totally permeated with falsehood.
DEFINE	para 21699	mQY itkw qyiV DoqI kKweI ] (471-19, Awsw, mÚ 1) mathai tikaa tayrh Dhotee kakhaa-ee. The sacred marks are on their foreheads, and the saffron loin-cloths are around their waists;
DEFINE	para 21700	hiQ CurI jgq kwsweI ] (471-19, Awsw, mÚ 1) hath chhuree jagat kaasaa-ee. in their hands they hold the knives - they are the butchers of the world!
RECORD	para 21702	nIl vsqR pihir hovih prvwxu ] (472-1, Awsw, mÚ 1) neel vastar pahir hoveh parvaan. Wearing blue robes, they seek the approval of the Muslim rulers.
RECORD	para 21703	mlyC Dwnu ly pUjih purwxu ] (472-1, Awsw, mÚ 1) malaychh Dhaan lay poojeh puraan. Accepting bread from the Muslim rulers, they still worship the Puraanas.
DEFINE	para 21704	ABwiKAw kw kuTw bkrw Kwxw ] (472-1, Awsw, mÚ 1) abhaakhi-aa kaa kuthaa bakraa khaanaa. They eat the meat of the goats, killed after the Muslim prayers are read over them,
RECORD	para 21705	cauky aupir iksY n jwxw ] (472-2, Awsw, mÚ 1) cha-ukay upar kisai na jaanaa. but they do not allow anyone else to enter their kitchen areas.
RECORD	para 21706	dy kY caukw kFI kwr ] (472-2, Awsw, mÚ 1) day kai cha-ukaa kadhee kaar. They draw lines around them, plastering the ground with cow-dung.
RECORD	para 21707	aupir Awie bYTy kUiVAwr ] (472-2, Awsw, mÚ 1) upar aa-ay baithay koorhi-aar. The false come and sit within them.
RECORD	para 21708	mqu iBtY vy mqu iBtY ] iehu AMnu Aswfw iPtY ] (472-3, Awsw, mÚ 1) mat bhitai vay mat bhitai. ih ann asaadaa fitai. They cry out, "Do not touch our food, or it will be polluted!"
RECORD	para 21709	qin iPtY PyV kryin ] (472-3, Awsw, mÚ 1) tan fitai fayrh karayn. But with their polluted bodies, they commit evil deeds.
RECORD	para 21710	min jUTY culI Bryin ] (472-3, Awsw, mÚ 1) man joothai chulee bharayn. With filthy minds, they try to cleanse their mouths.
RECORD	para 21711	khu nwnk scu iDAweIAY ] (472-3, Awsw, mÚ 1) kaho naanak sach Dhi-aa-ee-ai. Says Nanak, meditate on the True Lord.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	suic hovY qw scu pweIAY ]2] (472-4, Awsw, mÚ 1) such hovai taa sach paa-ee-ai. ||2||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	If you are pure, you will obtain the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 21713	pauVI ] (472-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 21714	icqY AMdir sBu ko vyiK ndrI hyiT clwiedw ] (472-4, Awsw, mÚ 1) chitai andar sabh ko vaykh nadree hayth chalaa-idaa. All are within Your mind; You see and move them under Your Glance of Grace, O Lord.
RECORD	para 21715	Awpy dy vifAweIAw Awpy hI krm krwiedw ] (472-5, Awsw, mÚ 1) aapay day vadi-aa-ee-aa aapay hee karam karaa-idaa. You Yourself grant them glory, and You Yourself cause them to act.
DEFINE	para 21716	vfhu vfw vf mydnI isry isir DMDY lwiedw ] (472-5, Awsw, mÚ 1) vadahu vadaa vad maydnee siray sir DhanDhai laa-idaa. The Lord is the greatest of the great; great is His world. He enjoins all to their tasks.
WHEN	para 21717	ndir aupTI jy kry sulqwnw Gwhu krwiedw ] (472-6, Awsw, mÚ 1) nadar upthee jay karay sultaanaa ghaahu karaa-idaa. If he should cast an angry glance, He can transform kings into blades of grass.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v16	dir mMgin iBK n pwiedw ]16] (472-6, Awsw, mÚ 1) dar mangan bhikh na paa-idaa. ||16||
ALLOW	Awsw mhlw 1 v16	Even though they may beg from door to door, no one will give them charity. ||16||
RECORD	para 21719	sloku mÚ 1 ] (472-7) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 21720	jy mohwkw Gru muhY Gru muih ipqrI dyie ] (472-7, Awsw, mÚ 1) jay mohaakaa ghar muhai ghar muhi pitree day-ay. The thief robs a house, and offers the stolen goods to his ancestors.
DEFINE	para 21721	AgY vsqu is\wxIAY ipqrI cor kryie ] (472-7, Awsw, mÚ 1) agai vasat sinjaanee-ai pitree chor karay-i. In the world hereafter, this is recognized, and his ancestors are considered thieves as well.
DEFINE	para 21722	vFIAih hQ dlwl ky musPI eyh kryie ] (472-8, Awsw, mÚ 1) vadhee-ah hath dalaal kay musfee ayh karay-i. The hands of the go-between are cut off; this is the Lord's justice.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v1	nwnk AgY so imlY ij Kty Gwly dyie ]1] (472-8, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak agai so milai je khatay ghaalay day-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, in the world hereafter, that alone is received, which one gives to the needy from his own earnings and labor. ||1||
RECORD	para 21724	mÚ 1 ] (472-8) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 21725	ijau jorU isrnwvxI AwvY vwro vwr ] (472-9, Awsw, mÚ 1) ji-o joroo sirnaavanee aavai vaaro vaar. As a woman has her periods, month after month,
RECORD	para 21726	jUTy jUTw muiK vsY inq inq hoie KuAwru ] (472-9, Awsw, mÚ 1) joothay joothaa mukh vasai nit nit ho-ay khu-aar. so does falsehood dwell in the mouth of the false; they suffer forever, again and again.
DEFINE	para 21727	sUcy eyih n AwKIAih bhin ij ipMfw Doie ] (472-9, Awsw, mÚ 1) soochay ayhi na aakhee-ahi bahan je pindaa Dho-ay. They are not called pure, who sit down after merely washing their bodies.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	sUcy syeI nwnkw ijn min visAw soie ]2] (472-10, Awsw, mÚ 1) soochay say-ee naankaa jin man vasi-aa so-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	Only they are pure, O Nanak, within whose minds the Lord abides. ||2||
RECORD	para 21729	pauVI ] (472-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 21730	qury plwxy paux vyg hr rMgI hrm svwirAw ] (472-10, Awsw, mÚ 1) turay palaanay pa-un vayg har rangee haram savaari-aa. With saddled horses, as fast as the wind, and harems decorated in every way;
RECORD	para 21731	koTy mMfp mwVIAw lwie bYTy kir pwswirAw ] (472-11, Awsw, mÚ 1) kothay mandap maarhee-aa laa-ay baithay kar paasaari-aa. in houses and pavilions and lofty mansions, they dwell, making ostentatious shows.
RECORD	para 21732	cIj krin min Bwvdy hir buJin nwhI hwirAw ] (472-12, Awsw, mÚ 1) cheej karan man bhaavday har bujhan naahee haari-aa. They act out their minds' desires, but they do not understand the Lord, and so they are ruined.
RECORD	para 21733	kir Purmwieis KwieAw vyiK mhliq mrxu ivswirAw ] (472-12, Awsw, mÚ 1) kar furmaa-is khaa-i-aa vaykh mahlat maran visaari-aa. Asserting their authority, they eat, and beholding their mansions, they forget about death.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v17	jru AweI jobin hwirAw ]17] (472-13, Awsw, mÚ 1) jar aa-ee joban haari-aa. ||17||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v17	But old age comes, and youth is lost. ||17||
RECORD	para 21735	sloku mÚ 1 ] (472-13) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 21736	jy kir sUqku mMnIAY sB qY sUqku hoie ] (472-13, Awsw, mÚ 1) jay kar sootak mannee-ai sabh tai sootak ho-ay. If one accepts the concept of impurity, then there is impurity everywhere.
DEFINE	para 21737	gohy AqY lkVI AMdir kIVw hoie ] (472-14, Awsw, mÚ 1) gohay atai lakrhee andar keerhaa ho-ay. In cow-dung and wood there are worms.
DEFINE	para 21738	jyqy dwxy AMn ky jIAw bwJu n koie ] (472-14, Awsw, mÚ 1) jaytay daanay ann kay jee-aa baajh na ko-ay. As many as are the grains of corn, none is without life.
DEFINE	para 21739	pihlw pwxI jIau hY ijqu hirAw sBu koie ] (472-14, Awsw, mÚ 1) pahilaa paanee jee-o hai jit hari-aa sabh ko-ay. First, there is life in the water, by which everything else is made green.
RECORD	para 21740	sUqku ikau kir rKIAY sUqku pvY rsoie ] (472-15, Awsw, mÚ 1) sootak ki-o kar rakhee-ai sootak pavai raso-ay. How can it be protected from impurity? It touches our own kitchen.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v1	nwnk sUqku eyv n auqrY igAwnu auqwry Doie ]1] (472-15, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak sootak ayv na utrai gi-aan utaaray Dho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, impurity cannot be removed in this way; it is washed away only by spiritual wisdom. ||1||
RECORD	para 21742	mÚ 1 ] (472-16) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 21743	mn kw sUqku loBu hY ijhvw sUqku kUVu ] (472-16, Awsw, mÚ 1) man kaa sootak lobh hai jihvaa sootak koorh. The impurity of the mind is greed, and the impurity of the tongue is falsehood.
DEFINE	para 21744	AKI sUqku vyKxw pr iqRA pr Dn rUpu ] (472-16, Awsw, mÚ 1) akhee sootak vaykh-naa par tari-a par Dhan roop. The impurity of the eyes is to gaze upon the beauty of another man's wife, and his wealth.
DEFINE	para 21745	kMnI sUqku kMin pY lwieqbwrI Kwih ] (472-17, Awsw, mÚ 1) kannee sootak kann pai laa-itbaaree khaahi. The impurity of the ears is to listen to the slander of others.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	nwnk hMsw AwdmI bDy jm puir jwih ]2] (472-17, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak hansaa aadmee baDhay jam pur jaahi. ||2||
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, the mortal's soul goes, bound and gagged to the city of Death. ||2||
RECORD	para 21747	mÚ 1 ] (472-18) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 21748	sBo sUqku Brmu hY dUjY lgY jwie ] (472-18, Awsw, mÚ 1) sabho sootak bharam hai doojai lagai jaa-ay. All impurity comes from doubt and attachment to duality.
DEFINE	para 21749	jMmxu mrxw hukmu hY BwxY AwvY jwie ] (472-18, Awsw, mÚ 1) jaman marnaa hukam hai bhaanai aavai jaa-ay. Birth and death are subject to the Command of the Lord's Will; through His Will we come and go.
DEFINE	para 21750	Kwxw pIxw pivqRü hY idqonu irjku sMbwih ] (472-19, Awsw, mÚ 1) khaanaa peenaa pavitar hai diton rijak sambaahi. Eating and drinking are pure, since the Lord gives nourishment to all.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v3	nwnk ijn@I gurmuiK buiJAw iqn@w sUqku nwih ]3] (472-19, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak jin Hee gurmukh bujhi-aa tin Haa sootak naahi. ||3||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v3	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs, who understand the Lord, are not stained by impurity. ||3||
RECORD	para 21753	pauVI ] (473-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 21754	siqguru vfw kir swlwhIAY ijsu ivic vfIAw vifAweIAw ] (473-1, Awsw, mÚ 1) satgur vadaa kar salaahee-ai jis vich vadee-aa vadi-aa-ee-aa. Praise the Great True Guru; within Him is the greatest greatness.
WHEN	para 21755	sih myly qw ndrI AweIAw ] (473-1, Awsw, mÚ 1) seh maylay taa nadree aa-ee-aa. When the Lord causes us to meet the Guru, then we come to see them.
WHEN	para 21756	jw iqsu Bwxw qw min vsweIAw ] (473-2, Awsw, mÚ 1) jaa tis bhaanaa taa man vasaa-ee-aa. When it pleases Him, they come to dwell in our minds.
WHEN	para 21757	kir hukmu msqik hQu Dir ivchu mwir kFIAw buirAweIAw ] (473-2, Awsw, mÚ 1) kar hukam mastak hath Dhar vichahu maar kadhee-aa buri-aa-ee-aa. By His Command, when He places His hand on our foreheads, wickedness departs from within.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v18	sih quTY nau iniD pweIAw ]18] (473-3, Awsw, mÚ 1) seh tuthai na-o niDh paa-ee-aa. ||18||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v18	When the Lord is thoroughly pleased, the nine treasures are obtained. ||18||
RECORD	para 21759	sloku mÚ 1 ] (473-3) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 21760	pihlw sucw Awip hoie sucY bYTw Awie ] (473-3, Awsw, mÚ 1) pahilaa suchaa aap ho-ay suchai baithaa aa-ay. First, purifying himself, the Brahmin comes and sits in his purified enclosure.
DEFINE	para 21761	sucy AgY riKEnu koie n iBitE jwie ] (473-4, Awsw, mÚ 1) suchay agai rakhi-on ko-ay na bhiti-o jaa-ay. The pure foods, which no one else has touched, are placed before him.
RECORD	para 21762	sucw hoie kY jyivAw lgw pVix sloku ] (473-4, Awsw, mÚ 1) suchaa ho-ay kai jayvi-aa lagaa parhan salok. Being purified, he takes his food, and begins to read his sacred verses.
DEFINE	para 21763	kuhQI jweI sitAw iksu eyhu lgw doKu ] (473-5, Awsw, mÚ 1) kuhthee jaa-ee sati-aa kis ayhu lagaa dokh. But it is then thrown into a filthy place - whose fault is this?
WHEN	para 21764	AMnu dyvqw pwxI dyvqw bYsMqru dyvqw lUxu pMjvw pwieAw iGrqu ] (473-5, Awsw, mÚ 1) ann dayvtaa paanee dayvtaa baisantar dayvtaa loon panjvaa paa-i-aa ghirat. The corn is sacred, the water is sacred; the fire and salt are sacred as well; when the fifth thing, the ghee, is added,
RECORD	para 21765	qw hoAw pwku pivqu ] (473-6, Awsw, mÚ 1) taa ho-aa paak pavit. then the food becomes pure and sanctified.
RECORD	para 21766	pwpI isau qnu gifAw Qukw peIAw iqqu ] (473-6, Awsw, mÚ 1) paapee si-o tan gadi-aa thukaa pa-ee-aa tit. Coming into contact with the sinful human body, the food becomes so impure that is is spat upon.
RECORD	para 21767	ijqu muiK nwmu n aUcrih ibnu nwvY rs Kwih ] (473-6, Awsw, mÚ 1) jit mukh naam na oochrahi bin naavai ras khaahi. That mouth which does not chant the Naam, and without the Name eats tasty foods
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v1	nwnk eyvY jwxIAY iqqu muiK Qukw pwih ]1] (473-7, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak ayvai jaanee-ai tit mukh thukaa paahi. ||1||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v1	- O Nanak, know this: such a mouth is to be spat upon. ||1||
RECORD	para 21769	mÚ 1 ] (473-7) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 21770	BMif jMmIAY BMif inMmIAY BMif mMgxu vIAwhu ] (473-8, Awsw, mÚ 1) bhand jammee-ai bhand nimmee-ai bhand mangan vee-aahu. From woman, man is born; within woman, man is conceived; to woman he is engaged and married.
RECORD	para 21771	BMfhu hovY dosqI BMfhu clY rwhu ] (473-8, Awsw, mÚ 1) bhandahu hovai dostee bhandahu chalai raahu. Woman becomes his friend; through woman, the future generations come.
DEFINE	para 21772	BMfu muAw BMfu BwlIAY BMif hovY bMDwnu ] (473-8, Awsw, mÚ 1) bhand mu-aa bhand bhaalee-ai bhand hovai banDhaan. When his woman dies, he seeks another woman; to woman he is bound.
DEFINE	para 21773	so ikau mMdw AwKIAY ijqu jMmih rwjwn ] (473-9, Awsw, mÚ 1) so ki-o mandaa aakhee-ai jit jameh raajaan. So why call her bad? From her, kings are born.
DEFINE	para 21774	BMfhu hI BMfu aUpjY BMfY bwJu n koie ] (473-9, Awsw, mÚ 1) bhandahu hee bhand oopjai bhandai baajh na ko-ay. From woman, woman is born; without woman, there would be no one at all.
DEFINE	para 21775	nwnk BMfY bwhrw eyko scw soie ] (473-10, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak bhandai baahraa ayko sachaa so-ay. O Nanak, only the True Lord is without a woman.
DEFINE	para 21776	ijqu muiK sdw swlwhIAY Bwgw rqI cwir ] (473-10, Awsw, mÚ 1) jit mukh sadaa salaahee-ai bhaagaa ratee chaar. That mouth which praises the Lord continually is blessed and beautiful.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	nwnk qy muK aUjly iqqu scY drbwir ]2] (473-10, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak tay mukh oojlay tit sachai darbaar. ||2||
REQUIRE	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, those faces shall be radiant in the Court of the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 21778	pauVI ] (473-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 21779	sBu ko AwKY Awpxw ijsu nwhI so cuix kFIAY ] (473-11, Awsw, mÚ 1) sabh ko aakhai aapnaa jis naahee so chun kadhee-ai. All call You their own, Lord; one who does not own You, is picked up and thrown away.
DEFINE	para 21780	kIqw Awpo Awpxw Awpy hI lyKw sMFIAY ] (473-12, Awsw, mÚ 1) keetaa aapo aapnaa aapay hee laykhaa sandhee-ai. Everyone receives the rewards of his own actions; his account is adjusted accordingly.
RECORD	para 21781	jw rhxw nwhI AYqu jig qw kwiequ gwrib hMFIAY ] (473-12, Awsw, mÚ 1) jaa rahnaa naahee ait jag taa kaa-it gaarab handhee-ai. Since one is not destined to remain in this world anyway, why should he ruin himself in pride?
RECORD	para 21782	mMdw iksY n AwKIAY piV AKru eyho buJIAY ] (473-13, Awsw, mÚ 1) mandaa kisai na aakhee-ai parh akhar ayho bujhee-ai. Do not call anyone bad; read these words, and understand.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v19	mUrKY nwil n luJIAY ]19] (473-13, Awsw, mÚ 1) moorkhai naal na lujhee-ai. ||19||
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v19	Don't argue with fools. ||19||
RECORD	para 21784	sloku mÚ 1 ] (473-13) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 21785	nwnk iPkY boilAY qnu mnu iPkw hoie ] (473-14, Awsw, mÚ 1) naanak fikai boli-ai tan man fikaa ho-ay. O Nanak, speaking insipid words, the body and mind become insipid.
DEFINE	para 21786	iPko iPkw sdIAY iPky iPkI soie ] (473-14, Awsw, mÚ 1) fiko fikaa sadee-ai fikay fikee so-ay. He is called the most insipid of the insipid; the most insipid of the insipid is his reputation.
DEFINE	para 21787	iPkw drgh stIAY muih Qukw iPky pwie ] (473-14, Awsw, mÚ 1) fikaa dargeh satee-ai muhi thukaa fikay paa-ay. The insipid person is discarded in the Court of the Lord, and the insipid one's face is spat upon.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v1	iPkw mUrKu AwKIAY pwxw lhY sjwie ]1] (473-15, Awsw, mÚ 1) fikaa moorakh aakhee-ai paanaa lahai sajaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v1	The insipid one is called a fool; he is beaten with shoes in punishment. ||1||
RECORD	para 21789	mÚ 1 ] (473-15) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 21790	AMdrhu JUTy pYj bwhir dunIAw AMdir PYlu ] (473-15, Awsw, mÚ 1) andrahu jhoothay paij baahar dunee-aa andar fail. Those who are false within, and honorable on the outside, are very common in this world.
ALLOW	para 21791	ATsiT qIrQ jy nwvih auqrY nwhI mYlu ] (473-16, Awsw, mÚ 1) athsath tirath jay naaveh utrai naahee mail. Even though they may bathe at the sixty-eight sacred shrines of pilgrimage, still, their filth does not depart.
DEFINE	para 21792	ijn@ ptu AMdir bwhir gudVu qy Bly sMswir ] (473-16, Awsw, mÚ 1) jin H pat andar baahar gudarh tay bhalay sansaar. Those who have silk on the inside and rags on the outside, are the good ones in this world.
RECORD	para 21793	iqn@ nyhu lgw rb syqI dyKn@y vIcwir ] (473-17, Awsw, mÚ 1) tin H nayhu lagaa rab saytee daykhn Hay veechaar. They embrace love for the Lord, and contemplate beholding Him.
RECORD	para 21794	rMig hsih rMig rovih cup BI kir jwih ] (473-17, Awsw, mÚ 1) rang haseh rang roveh chup bhee kar jaahi. In the Lord's Love, they laugh, and in the Lord's Love, they weep, and also keep silent.
RECORD	para 21795	prvwh nwhI iksY kyrI bwJu scy nwh ] (473-18, Awsw, mÚ 1) parvaah naahee kisai kayree baajh sachay naah. They do not care for anything else, except their True Husband Lord.
WHEN	para 21796	dir vwt aupir Krcu mMgw jbY dyie q Kwih ] (473-18, Awsw, mÚ 1) dar vaat upar kharach mangaa jabai day-ay ta khaahi. Sitting, waiting at the Lord's Door, they beg for food, and when He gives to them, they eat.
DEFINE	para 21797	dIbwnu eyko klm eykw hmw qum@w mylu ] (473-19, Awsw, mÚ 1) deebaan ayko kalam aykaa hamaa tum Haa mayl. There is only One Court of the Lord, and He has only one pen; there, you and I shall meet.
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	dir ley lyKw pIiV CutY nwnkw ijau qylu ]2] (473-19, Awsw, mÚ 1) dar la-ay laykhaa peerh chhutai naankaa ji-o tayl. ||2||
DEFINE	Awsw mhlw 1 v2	In the Court of the Lord, the accounts are examined; O Nanak, the sinners are crushed, like oil seeds in the press. ||2||
RECORD	para 21800	pauVI ] (474-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 21801	Awpy hI krxw kIE kl Awpy hI qY DwrIAY ] (474-1, Awsw, mÚ 1) aapay hee karnaa kee-o kal aapay hee tai Dhaaree-ai. You Yourself created the creation; You Yourself infused Your power into it.
RECORD	para 21802	dyKih kIqw Awpxw Dir kcI pkI swrIAY ] (474-1, Awsw, mÚ 1) daykheh keetaa aapnaa Dhar kachee pakee saaree-ai. You behold Your creation, like the losing and winning dice of the earth.
REQUIRE	para 21803	jo AwieAw so clsI sBu koeI AweI vwrIAY ] (474-2, Awsw, mÚ 1) jo aa-i-aa so chalsee sabh ko-ee aa-ee vaaree-ai. Whoever has come, shall depart; all shall have their turn.
RECORD	para 21804	ijs ky jIA prwx hih ikau swihbu mnhu ivswrIAY ] (474-2, Awsw, mÚ 1) jis kay jee-a paraan heh ki-o saahib manhu visaaree-ai. He who owns our soul, and our very breath of life - why should we forget that Lord and Master from our minds?
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v20	Awpx hQI Awpxw Awpy hI kwju svwrIAY ]20] (474-3, Awsw, mÚ 1) aapan hathee aapnaa aapay hee kaaj savaaree-ai. ||20||
RECORD	Awsw mhlw 1 v20	With our own hands, let us resolve our own affairs. ||20||
DEFINE	para 21807	eyh iknyhI AwskI dUjY lgY jwie ] (474-3, Awsw, mÚ 2) ayh kinayhee aaskee doojai lagai jaa-ay. What sort of love is this, which clings to duality?
DEFINE	para 21808	nwnk Awsku kWFIAY sd hI rhY smwie ] (474-4, Awsw, mÚ 2) naanak aasak kaa Ndhee-ai sad hee rahai samaa-ay. O Nanak, he alone is called a lover, who remains forever immersed in absorption.
