DEFINE	para 23164	sdw sdw so syvIAY jo sB mih rhY smwie ] (509-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa so sayvee-ai jo sabh meh rahai samaa-ay. So serve Him, forever and ever; He is contained in all.
DEFINE	para 23165	Avru dUjw ikau syvIAY jMmY qY mir jwie ] (509-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) avar doojaa ki-o sayvee-ai jammai tai mar jaa-ay. Why serve another who is born, and then dies?
RECORD	para 23166	inhPlu iqn kw jIivAw ij Ksmu n jwxih Awpxw AvrI kau icqu lwie ] (509-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) nihfal tin kaa jeevi-aa je khasam na jaaneh aapnaa avree ka-o chit laa-ay. Fruitless is the life of those who do not know their Lord and Master, and who center their consciousness on others.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk eyv n jwpeI krqw kyqI dyie sjwie ]1] (509-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak ayv na jaap-ee kartaa kaytee day-ay sajaa-ay. ||1||
REQUIRE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, it cannot be known, how much punishment the Creator shall inflict on them. ||1||
RECORD	para 23168	mÚ 3 ] (509-7) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23169	scw nwmu iDAweIAY sBo vrqY scu ] (509-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sachaa naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai sabho vartai sach. Meditate on the True Name; the True Lord is pervading everywhere.
RECORD	para 23170	nwnk hukmu buiJ prvwxu hoie qw Plu pwvY scu ] (509-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak hukam bujh parvaan ho-ay taa fal paavai sach. O Nanak, by understanding the Hukam of the Lord's Command, one becomes acceptable, and then obtains the fruit of Truth.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	kQnI bdnI krqw iPrY hukmY mUil n buJeI AMDw kcu inkcu ]2] (509-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) kathnee badnee kartaa firai hukmai mool na bujh-ee anDhaa kach nikach. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	He wanders around babbling and speaking, but he does not understand the Lord's Command at all. He is blind, the falsest of the false. ||2||
RECORD	para 23172	pauVI ] (509-9) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 23173	sMjogu ivjogu aupwieEnu isRstI kw mUlu rcwieAw ] (509-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sanjog vijog upaa-i-on saristee kaa mool rachaa-i-aa. Creating union and separation, He laid the foundations of the Universe.
RECORD	para 23174	hukmI isRsit swjIAnu joqI joiq imlwieAw ] (509-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) hukmee sarisat saajee-an jotee jot milaa-i-aa. By His Command, the Lord of Light fashioned the Universe, and infused His Divine Light into it.
RECORD	para 23175	joqI hUM sBu cwnxw siqguir sbdu suxwieAw ] (509-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jotee hooN sabh chaannaa satgur sabad sunaa-i-aa. From the Lord of Light, all light originates. The True Guru proclaims the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 23176	bRhmw ibsnu mhysu qRY gux isir DMDY lwieAw ] (509-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) barahmaa bisan mahays tarai gun sir DhanDhai laa-i-aa. Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva, under the influence of the three dispositions, were put to their tasks.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	mwieAw kw mUlu rcwieEnu qurIAw suKu pwieAw ]2] (509-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa kaa mool rachaa-i-on turee-aa sukh paa-i-aa. ||2||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	He created the root of Maya, and the peace obtained in the fourth state of consciousness. ||2||
RECORD	para 23178	sloku mÚ 3 ] (509-12) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23179	so jpu so qpu ij siqgur BwvY ] (509-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) so jap so tap je satgur bhaavai. That alone is chanting, and that alone is deep meditation, which is pleasing to the True Guru.
DEFINE	para 23180	siqgur kY BwxY vifAweI pwvY ] (509-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur kai bhaanai vadi-aa-ee paavai. Pleasing the True Guru, glorious greatness is obtained.
WHEN	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk Awpu Coif gur mwih smwvY ]1] (509-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak aap chhod gur maahi samaavai. ||1||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, renouncing self-conceit, one merges into the Guru. ||1||
RECORD	para 23182	mÚ 3 ] (509-13) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23183	gur kI isK ko ivrlw lyvY ] (509-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gur kee sikh ko virlaa layvai. How rare are those who receive the Guru's Teachings.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk ijsu Awip vifAweI dyvY ]2] (509-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak jis aap vadi-aa-ee dayvai. ||2||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, he alone receives it, whom the Lord Himself blesses with glorious greatness. ||2||
RECORD	para 23185	pauVI ] (509-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 23186	mwieAw mohu AigAwnu hY ibKmu Aiq BwrI ] (509-14, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh agi-aan hai bikham at bhaaree. Emotional attachment to Maya is spiritual darkness; it is very difficult and such a heavy load.
RECORD	para 23187	pQr pwp bhu lidAw ikau qrIAY qwrI ] (509-14, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) pathar paap baho ladi-aa ki-o taree-ai taaree. Loaded with so very many stones of sin, how can the boat cross over?
DEFINE	para 23188	Anidnu BgqI riqAw hir pwir auqwrI ] (509-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) an-din bhagtee rati-aa har paar utaaree. Those who are attuned to the Lord's devotional worship night and day are carried across.
WHEN	para 23189	gur sbdI mnu inrmlw haumY Cif ivkwrI ] (509-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gur sabdee man nirmalaa ha-umai chhad vikaaree. Under the Instruction of the Guru's Shabad, one sheds egotism and corruption, and the mind becomes immaculate.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v3	hir hir nwmu iDAweIAY hir hir insqwrI ]3] (509-16, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har har naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai har har nistaaree. ||3||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v3	Meditate on the Name of the Lord, Har, Har; the Lord, Har, Har, is our Saving Grace. ||3||
RECORD	para 23191	sloku ] (509-16) salok. Shalok:
DEFINE	para 23192	kbIr mukiq duAwrw sMkuVw rweI dsvY Bwie ] (509-16, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) kabeer mukat du-aaraa sankurhaa raa-ee dasvai bhaa-ay. O Kabeer, the gate of liberation is narrow, less than one-tenth of a mustard seed.
RECORD	para 23193	mnu qau mYglu hoie rhw inkisAw ikau kir jwie ] (509-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) man ta-o maigal ho-ay rahaa niksi-aa ki-o kar jaa-ay. The mind has become as big as an elephant; how can it pass through this gate?
WHEN	para 23194	AYsw siqguru jy imlY quTw kry pswau ] (509-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aisaa satgur jay milai tuthaa karay pasaa-o. If one meets such a True Guru, by His Pleasure, He shows His Mercy.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	mukiq duAwrw moklw shjy Awvau jwau ]1] (509-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) mukat du-aaraa moklaa sehjay aava-o jaa-o. ||1||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	Then, the gate of liberation becomes wide open, and the soul easily passes through. ||1||
RECORD	para 23196	mÚ 3 ] (509-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23197	nwnk mukiq duAwrw Aiq nIkw nwn@w hoie su jwie ] (509-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak mukat du-aaraa at neekaa naan Haa ho-ay so jaa-ay. O Nanak, the gate of liberation is very narrow; only the very tiny can pass through.
RECORD	para 23198	haumY mnu AsQUlu hY ikau kir ivcu dy jwie ] (509-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) ha-umai man asthool hai ki-o kar vich day jaa-ay. Through egotism, the mind has become bloated. How can it pass through?
DEFINE	para 23199	siqgur imilAY haumY geI joiq rhI sB Awie ] (509-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur mili-ai ha-umai ga-ee jot rahee sabh aa-ay. Meeting the True Guru, egotism departs, and one is filled with the Divine Light.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	iehu jIau sdw mukqu hY shjy rihAw smwie ]2] (510-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) ih jee-o sadaa mukat hai sehjay rahi-aa samaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	Then, this soul is liberated forever, and it remains absorbed in celestial bliss. ||2||
RECORD	para 23202	pauVI ] (510-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 23203	pRiB sMswru aupwie kY vis AwpxY kIqw ] (510-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) parabh sansaar upaa-ay kai vas aapnai keetaa. God created the Universe, and He keeps it under His power.
RECORD	para 23204	gxqY pRBU n pweIAY dUjY BrmIqw ] (510-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gantai parabhoo na paa-ee-ai doojai bharmeetaa. God cannot be obtained by counting; the mortal wanders in doubt.
RECORD	para 23205	siqgur imilAY jIvqu mrY buiJ sic smIqw ] (510-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur mili-ai jeevat marai bujh sach sameetaa. Meeting the True Guru, one remains dead while yet alive; understanding Him, he is absorbed in the Truth.
DEFINE	para 23206	sbdy haumY KoeIAY hir myil imlIqw ] (510-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sabday ha-umai kho-ee-ai har mayl mileetaa. Through the Word of the Shabad, egotism is eradicated, and one is united in the Lord's Union.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v4	sB ikCu jwxY kry Awip Awpy ivgsIqw ]4] (510-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sabh kichh jaanai karay aap aapay vigseetaa. ||4||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v4	He knows everything, and Himself does everything; beholding His Creation, He rejoices. ||4||
RECORD	para 23208	sloku mÚ 3 ] (510-4) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23209	siqgur isau icqu n lwieE nwmu n visE min Awie ] (510-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur si-o chit na laa-i-o naam na vasi-o man aa-ay. One who has not focused his consciousness on the True Guru, and into whose mind the Naam does not come
DEFINE	para 23210	iDRgu ievyhw jIivAw ikAw jug mih pwieAw Awie ] (510-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) Dharig ivayhaa jeevi-aa ki-aa jug meh paa-i-aa aa-ay. - cursed is such a life. What has he gained by coming into the world?
DEFINE	para 23211	mwieAw KotI rwis hY eyk csy mih pwju lih jwie ] (510-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa khotee raas hai ayk chasay meh paaj leh jaa-ay. Maya is false capital; in an instant, its false covering falls off.
WHEN	para 23212	hQhu CuVkI qnu isAwhu hoie bdnu jwie kumlwie ] (510-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) hathahu chhurhkee tan si-aahu ho-ay badan jaa-ay kumlaa-ay. When it slips from his hand, his body turns black, and his face withers away.
RECORD	para 23213	ijn siqgur isau icqu lwieAw iqn@ suKu visAw min Awie ] (510-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jin satgur si-o chit laa-i-aa tin H sukh vasi-aa man aa-ay. Those who focus their consciousness on the True Guru - peace comes to abide in their minds.
RECORD	para 23214	hir nwmu iDAwvih rMg isau hir nwim rhy ilv lwie ] (510-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har naam Dhi-aavahi rang si-o har naam rahay liv laa-ay. They meditate on the Name of the Lord with love; they are lovingly attuned to the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 23215	nwnk siqgur so Dnu sauipAw ij jIA mih rihAw smwie ] (510-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak satgur so Dhan sa-upi-aa je jee-a meh rahi-aa samaa-ay. O Nanak, the True Guru has bestowed upon them the wealth, which remains contained within their hearts.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	rMgu iqsY kau Aglw vMnI cVY cVwie ]1] (510-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) rang tisai ka-o aglaa vannee charhai charhaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	They are imbued with supreme love; its color increases day by day. ||1||
RECORD	para 23217	mÚ 3 ] (510-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23218	mwieAw hoeI nwgnI jgiq rhI lptwie ] (510-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa ho-ee naagnee jagat rahee laptaa-ay. Maya is a serpent, clinging to the world.
RECORD	para 23219	ies kI syvw jo kry iqs hI kau iPir Kwie ] (510-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) is kee sayvaa jo karay tis hee ka-o fir khaa-ay. Whoever serves her, she ultimately devours.
RECORD	para 23220	gurmuiK koeI gwrVU iqin mil dil lweI pwie ] (510-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gurmukh ko-ee gaarrhoo tin mal dal laa-ee paa-ay. The Gurmukh is a snake-charmer; he has trampled her and thrown her down, and crushed her underfoot.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk syeI aubry ij sic rhy ilv lwie ]2] (510-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak say-ee ubray je sach rahay liv laa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, they alone are saved, who remain lovingly absorbed in the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 23222	pauVI ] (510-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 23223	FwFI kry pukwr pRBU suxwiesI ] (510-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) dhaadhee karay pukaar parabhoo sunaa-isee. The minstrel cries out, and God hears him.
DEFINE	para 23224	AMdir DIrk hoie pUrw pwiesI ] (510-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) andar Dheerak ho-ay pooraa paa-isee. He is comforted within his mind, and he obtains the Perfect Lord.
DEFINE	para 23225	jo Duir iliKAw lyKu sy krm kmwiesI ] (510-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jo Dhur likhi-aa laykh say karam kamaa-isee. Whatever destiny is pre-ordained by the Lord, those are the deeds he does.
WHEN	para 23226	jw hovY Ksmu dieAwlu qw mhlu Gru pwiesI ] (510-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jaa hovai khasam da-i-aal taa mahal ghar paa-isee. When the Lord and Master becomes Merciful, then one obtains the Mansion of the Lord's Presence as his home.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v5	so pRBu myrw Aiq vfw gurmuiK mylwiesI ]5] (510-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) so parabh mayraa at vadaa gurmukh maylaa-isee. ||5||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v5	That God of mine is so very great; as Gurmukh, I have met Him. ||5||
RECORD	para 23228	slok mÚ 3 ] (510-13) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23229	sBnw kw shu eyku hY sd hI rhY hjUir ] (510-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sabhnaa kaa saho ayk hai sad hee rahai hajoor. There is One Lord God of all; He remains ever-present.
WHEN	para 23230	nwnk hukmu n mMneI qw Gr hI AMdir dUir ] (510-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak hukam na mann-ee taa ghar hee andar door. O Nanak, if one does not obey the Hukam of the Lord's Command, then within one's own home, the Lord seems far away.
RECORD	para 23231	hukmu BI iqn@w mnwiesI ijn@ kau ndir kryie ] (510-14, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) hukam bhee tin Haa manaa-isee jin H ka-o nadar karay-i. They alone obey the Lord's Command, upon whom He casts His Glance of Grace.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	hukmu mMin suKu pwieAw pRym suhwgix hoie ]1] (510-14, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) hukam man sukh paa-i-aa paraym suhaagan ho-ay. ||1||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	Obeying His Command, one obtains peace, and becomes the happy, loving soul-bride. ||1||
RECORD	para 23233	mÚ 3 ] (510-15) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23234	rYix sbweI jil mueI kMq n lwieE Bwau ] (510-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) rain sabaa-ee jal mu-ee kant na laa-i-o bhaa-o. She who does not love her Husband Lord, burns and wastes away all through the night of her life.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk suiK vsin suohwgxI ijn@ ipAwrw purKu hir rwau ]2] (510-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak sukh vasan sohaaganee jin H pi-aaraa purakh har raa-o. ||2||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, the soul-brides dwell in peace; they have the Lord, their King, as their Husband. ||2||
RECORD	para 23236	pauVI ] (510-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 23237	sBu jgu iPir mY dyiKAw hir ieko dwqw ] (510-16, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sabh jag fir mai daykhi-aa har iko daataa. Roaming over the entire world, I have seen that the Lord is the only Giver.
DEFINE	para 23238	aupwie ikqY n pweIAY hir krm ibDwqw ] (510-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) upaa-ay kitai na paa-ee-ai har karam biDhaataa. The Lord cannot be obtained by any device at all; He is the Architect of Karma.
RECORD	para 23239	gur sbdI hir min vsY hir shjy jwqw ] (510-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gur sabdee har man vasai har sehjay jaataa. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Lord comes to dwell in the mind, and the Lord is easily revealed within.
RECORD	para 23240	AMdrhu iqRsnw Agin buJI hir AMimRq sir nwqw ] (510-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) andrahu tarisnaa agan bujhee har amrit sar naataa. The fire of desire within is quenched, and one bathes in the Lord's Pool of Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v6	vfI vifAweI vfy kI gurmuiK bolwqw ]6] (510-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vadee vadi-aa-ee vaday kee gurmukh bolaataa. ||6||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v6	The great greatness of the great Lord God - the Gurmukh speaks of this. ||6||
RECORD	para 23242	sloku mÚ 3 ] (510-19) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23243	kwieAw hMs ikAw pRIiq hY ij pieAw hI Cif jwie ] (510-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa hans ki-aa pareet hai je pa-i-aa hee chhad jaa-ay. What love is this between the body and soul, which ends when the body falls?
WHEN	para 23244	eys no kUVu boil ik KvwlIAY ij clidAw nwil n jwie ] (510-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) ays no koorh bol ke khavaalee-ai je chaldi-aa naal na jaa-ay. Why feed it by telling lies? When you leave, it does not go with you.
DEFINE	para 23246	kwieAw imtI AMDu hY pauxY puChu jwie ] (511-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa mitee anDh hai pa-unai puchhahu jaa-ay. The body is merely blind dust; go, and ask the soul.
RECORD	para 23247	hau qw mwieAw moihAw iPir iPir Awvw jwie ] (511-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) ha-o taa maa-i-aa mohi-aa fir fir aavaa jaa-ay. The soul answers, "I am enticed by Maya, and so I come and go, again and again."
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk hukmu n jwqo Ksm kw ij rhw sic smwie ]1] (511-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak hukam na jaato khasam kaa je rahaa sach samaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, I do not know my Lord and Master's Command, by which I would merge in the Truth. ||1||
RECORD	para 23249	mÚ 3 ] (511-3) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23250	eyko inhcl nwm Dnu horu Dnu AwvY jwie ] (511-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) ayko nihchal naam Dhan hor Dhan aavai jaa-ay. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is the only permanent wealth; all other wealth comes and goes.
RECORD	para 23251	iesu Dn kau qskru joih n skeI nw Eckw lY jwie ] (511-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) is Dhan ka-o taskar johi na sak-ee naa ochkaa lai jaa-ay. Thieves cannot steal this wealth, nor can robbers take it away.
REQUIRE	para 23252	iehu hir Dnu jIAY syqI riv rihAw jIAY nwly jwie ] (511-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) ih har Dhan jee-ai saytee rav rahi-aa jee-ai naalay jaa-ay. This wealth of the Lord is embedded in the soul, and with the soul, it shall depart.
DEFINE	para 23253	pUry gur qy pweIAY mnmuiK plY n pwie ] (511-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) pooray gur tay paa-ee-ai manmukh palai na paa-ay. It is obtained from the Perfect Guru; the self-willed manmukhs do not receive it.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	Dnu vwpwrI nwnkw ijn@w nwm Dnu KitAw Awie ]2] (511-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) Dhan vaapaaree naankaa jin Haa naam Dhan khati-aa aa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	Blessed are the traders, O Nanak, who have come to earn the wealth of the Naam. ||2||
RECORD	para 23255	pauVI ] (511-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 23256	myrw swihbu Aiq vfw scu gihr gMBIrw ] (511-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) mayraa saahib at vadaa sach gahir gambheeraa. My Master is so very great, true, profound and unfathomable.
DEFINE	para 23257	sBu jgu iqs kY vis hY sBu iqs kw cIrw ] (511-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sabh jag tis kai vas hai sabh tis kaa cheeraa. The whole world is under His power; everything is the projection of Him.
DEFINE	para 23258	gur prswdI pweIAY inhclu Dnu DIrw ] (511-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee paa-ee-ai nihchal Dhan Dheeraa. By Guru's Grace, the eternal wealth is obtained, bringing peace and patience to the mind.
RECORD	para 23259	ikrpw qy hir min vsY BytY guru sUrw ] (511-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) kirpaa tay har man vasai bhaytai gur sooraa. By His Grace, the Lord dwells in the mind, and one meets the Brave Guru.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v7	guxvMqI swlwihAw sdw iQru inhclu hir pUrw ]7] (511-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gunvantee salaahi-aa sadaa thir nihchal har pooraa. ||7||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v7	The virtuous praise the ever-stable, permanent, perfect Lord. ||7||
RECORD	para 23261	sloku mÚ 3 ] (511-8) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23263	mnmuK AigAwnI mwieAw moih ivAwpy iqn@ bUJ n kweI pwie ] (511-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) manmukh agi-aanee maa-i-aa mohi vi-aapay tin H boojh na kaa-ee paa-ay. The ignorant self-willed manmukhs are engrossed in the love of Maya; they have no understanding at all.
RECORD	para 23264	hliq pliq Eie suKu n pwvih AMiq gey pCuqwie ] (511-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) halat palat o-ay sukh na paavahi ant ga-ay pachhutaa-ay. In this world and in the world beyond, they do not find peace; in the end, they depart regretting and repenting.
ALLOW	para 23265	gur prswdI ko nwmu iDAwey iqsu haumY ivchu jwie ] (511-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee ko naam Dhi-aa-ay tis ha-umai vichahu jaa-ay. By Guru's Grace, one may meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord, and egotism departs from within him.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk ijsu pUrib hovY iliKAw so gur crxI Awie pwie ]1] (511-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak jis poorab hovai likhi-aa so gur charnee aa-ay paa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, one who has such pre-ordained destiny, comes and falls at the Guru's Feet. ||1||
RECORD	para 23267	mÚ 3 ] (511-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23268	mnmuKu aUDw kaulu hY nw iqsu Bgiq n nwau ] (511-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) manmukh ooDhaa ka-ul hai naa tis bhagat na naa-o. The self-willed manmukh is like the inverted lotus; he has neither devotional worship, nor the Lord's Name.
DEFINE	para 23269	skqI AMdir vrqdw kUVu iqs kw hY aupwau ] (511-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) saktee andar varatdaa koorh tis kaa hai upaa-o. He remains engrossed in material wealth, and his efforts are false.
DEFINE	para 23270	iqs kw AMdru icqu n iBjeI muiK PIkw Awlwau ] (511-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) tis kaa andar chit na bhij-ee mukh feekaa aalaa-o. His consciousness is not softened within, and the words from his mouth are insipid.
DEFINE	para 23271	Eie Drim rlwey nw rlin@ Enw AMdir kUVu suAwau ] (511-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) o-ay Dharam ralaa-ay naa ralni H onaa andar koorh su-aa-o. He does not mingle with the righteous; within him are falsehood and selfishness.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk krqY bxq bxweI mnmuK kUVu boil boil fuby gurmuiK qry jip hir nwau ]2] (511-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak kartai banat banaa-ee manmukh koorh bol bol dubay gurmukh taray jap har naa-o. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, the Creator Lord has arranged things, so that the self-willed manmukhs are drowned by telling lies, while the Gurmukhs are saved by chanting the Lord's Name. ||2||
RECORD	para 23273	pauVI ] (511-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
REQUIRE	para 23274	ibnu bUJy vfw Pyru pieAw iPir AwvY jweI ] (511-14, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) bin boojhay vadaa fayr pa-i-aa fir aavai jaa-ee. Without understanding, one must wander around the cycle of reincarnation, and continue coming and going.
REQUIRE	para 23275	siqgur kI syvw n kIqIAw AMiq gieAw pCuqweI ] (511-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur kee sayvaa na keetee-aa ant ga-i-aa pachhutaa-ee. One who has not served the True Guru, shall depart regretting and repenting in the end.
DEFINE	para 23276	AwpxI ikrpw kry guru pweIAY ivchu Awpu gvweI ] (511-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aapnee kirpaa karay gur paa-ee-ai vichahu aap gavaa-ee. But if the Lord shows His Mercy, one finds the Guru, and ego is banished from within.
RECORD	para 23277	iqRsnw BuK ivchu auqrY suKu vsY min AweI ] (511-16, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) tarisnaa bhukh vichahu utrai sukh vasai man aa-ee. Hunger and thirst depart from within, and peace comes to dwell in the mind.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v8	sdw sdw swlwhIAY ihrdY ilv lweI ]8] (511-16, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa salaahee-ai hirdai liv laa-ee. ||8||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v8	Forever and ever, praise Him with love in your heart. ||8||
RECORD	para 23279	sloku mÚ 3 ] (511-17) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23280	ij siqguru syvy Awpxw iqs no pUjy sBu koie ] (511-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) je satgur sayvay aapnaa tis no poojay sabh ko-ay. One who serves his True Guru, is worshipped by everyone.
DEFINE	para 23281	sBnw aupwvw isir aupwau hY hir nwmu prwpiq hoie ] (511-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sabhnaa upaavaa sir upaa-o hai har naam paraapat ho-ay. Of all efforts, the supreme effort is the attainment of the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 23282	AMqir sIql swiq vsY jip ihrdY sdw suKu hoie ] (511-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) antar seetal saat vasai jap hirdai sadaa sukh ho-ay. Peace and tranquility come to dwell within the mind; meditating within the heart, there comes a lasting peace.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	AMimRqu Kwxw AMimRqu pYnxw nwnk nwmu vfweI hoie ]1] (511-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) amrit khaanaa amrit painnaa naanak naam vadaa-ee ho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	The Ambrosial Amrit is his food, and the Ambrosial Amrit is his clothes; O Nanak, through the Naam, the Name of the Lord, greatness is obtained. ||1||
RECORD	para 23284	mÚ 3 ] (511-19) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 23285	ey mn gur kI isK suix hir pwvih guxI inDwnu ] (511-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) ay man gur kee sikh sun har paavahi gunee niDhaan. O mind, listen to the Guru's Teachings, and you shall obtain the treasure of virtue.
REQUIRE	para 23287	hir suKdwqw min vsY haumY jwie gumwnu ] (512-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har sukh-daata man vasai ha-umai jaa-ay gumaan. The Lord, the Giver of peace, shall dwell in your mind, and your egotism and pride shall depart.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk ndrI pweIAY qw Anidnu lwgY iDAwnu ]2] (512-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak nadree paa-ee-ai taa an-din laagai Dhi-aan. ||2||
WHEN	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, when the Lord bestows His Glance of Grace, then, night and day, one centers his meditation on the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 23289	pauVI ] (512-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 23290	squ sMqoKu sBu scu hY gurmuiK pivqw ] (512-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sat santokh sabh sach hai gurmukh pavitaa. The Gurmukh is totally truthful, content and pure.
RECORD	para 23291	AMdrhu kptu ivkwru gieAw mnu shjy ijqw ] (512-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) andrahu kapat vikaar ga-i-aa man sehjay jitaa. Deception and wickedness have departed from within him, and he easily conquers his mind.
DEFINE	para 23292	qh joiq pRgwsu Anµd rsu AigAwnu givqw ] (512-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) tah jot pargaas anand ras agi-aan gavitaa. There, the Divine Light and the essence of bliss are manifest, and ignorance is eliminated.
RECORD	para 23293	Anidnu hir ky gux rvY gux prgtu ikqw ] (512-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) an-din har kay gun ravai gun pargat kitaa. Night and day, he sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and manifests the excellence of the Lord.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v9	sBnw dwqw eyku hY ieko hir imqw ]9] (512-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sabhnaa daataa ayk hai iko har mitaa. ||9||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v9	The One Lord is the Giver of all; the Lord alone is our friend. ||9||
RECORD	para 23295	sloku mÚ 3 ] (512-4) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23296	bRhmu ibMdy so bRwhmxu khIAY ij Anidnu hir ilv lwey ] (512-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) barahm binday so baraahman kahee-ai je an-din har liv laa-ay. One who understands God, who lovingly centers his mind on the Lord night and day, is called a Brahmin.
RECORD	para 23297	siqgur puCY scu sMjmu kmwvY haumY rogu iqsu jwey ] (512-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur puchhai sach sanjam kamaavai ha-umai rog tis jaa-ay. Consulting the True Guru, he practices Truth and self-restraint, and he is rid of the disease of ego.
RECORD	para 23298	hir gux gwvY gux sMgRhY joqI joiq imlwey ] (512-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har gun gaavai gun sangrahai jotee jot milaa-ay. He sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and gathers in His Praises; his light is blended with the Light.
RECORD	para 23299	iesu jug mih ko ivrlw bRhm igAwnI ij haumY myit smwey ] (512-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) is jug meh ko virlaa barahm gi-aanee je ha-umai mayt samaa-ay. In this world, one who knows God is very rare; eradicating ego, he is absorbed in God.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk iqs no imilAw sdw suKu pweIAY ij Anidnu hir nwmu iDAwey ]1] (512-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak tis no mili-aa sadaa sukh paa-ee-ai je an-din har naam Dhi-aa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, meeting him, peace is obtained; night and day, he meditates on the Lord's Name. ||1||
RECORD	para 23301	mÚ 3 ] (512-7) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23302	AMqir kptu mnmuK AigAwnI rsnw JUTu bolwie ] (512-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) antar kapat manmukh agi-aanee rasnaa jhooth bolaa-ay. Within the ignorant self-willed manmukh is deception; with his tongue, he speaks lies.
RECORD	para 23303	kpit kIqY hir purKu n BIjY inq vyKY suxY suBwie ] (512-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) kapat keetai har purakh na bheejai nit vaykhai sunai subhaa-ay. Practicing deception, he does not please the Lord God, who always sees and hears with natural ease.
RECORD	para 23304	dUjY Bwie jwie jgu prboDY ibKu mwieAw moh suAwie ] (512-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay jaa-ay jag parboDhai bikh maa-i-aa moh su-aa-ay. In the love of duality, he goes to instruct the world, but he is engrossed in the poison of Maya and attachment to pleasure.
RECORD	para 23305	iequ kmwxY sdw duKu pwvY jMmY mrY iPir AwvY jwie ] (512-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) it kamaanai sadaa dukh paavai jammai marai fir aavai jaa-ay. By doing so, he suffers in constant pain; he is born and then dies, and comes and goes again and again.
RECORD	para 23306	shsw mUil n cukeI ivic ivstw pcY pcwie ] (512-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sahsaa mool na chuk-ee vich vistaa pachai pachaa-ay. His doubts do not leave him at all, and he rots away in manure.
RECORD	para 23307	ijs no ik®pw kry myrw suAwmI iqsu gur kI isK suxwie ] (512-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jis no kirpaa karay mayraa su-aamee tis gur kee sikh sunaa-ay. One, unto whom my Lord Master shows His Mercy, listens to the Guru's Teachings.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	hir nwmu iDAwvY hir nwmo gwvY hir nwmo AMiq Cfwie ]2] (512-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har naam Dhi-aavai har naamo gaavai har naamo ant chhadaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	He meditates on the Lord's Name, and sings the Lord's Name; in the end, the Lord's Name will deliver him. ||2||
RECORD	para 23309	pauVI ] (512-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 23310	ijnw hukmu mnwieEnu qy pUry sMswir ] (512-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jinaa hukam manaa-i-on tay pooray sansaar. Those who obey the Hukam of the Lord's Command, are the perfect persons in the world.
RECORD	para 23311	swihbu syvin@ Awpxw pUrY sbid vIcwir ] (512-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) saahib sayvni H aapnaa poorai sabad veechaar. They serve their Lord Master, and reflect upon the Perfect Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 23312	hir kI syvw cwkrI scY sbid ipAwir ] (512-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har kee sayvaa chaakree sachai sabad pi-aar. They serve the Lord, and love the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 23313	hir kw mhlu iqn@I pwieAw ijn@ haumY ivchu mwir ] (512-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har kaa mahal tin Hee paa-i-aa jin H ha-umai vichahu maar. They attain the Mansion of the Lord's Presence, as they eradicate egotism from within.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v10	nwnk gurmuiK imil rhy jip hir nwmw aur Dwir ]10] (512-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh mil rahay jap har naamaa ur Dhaar. ||10||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v10	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs remain united with Him, chanting the Name of the Lord, and enshrining it within their hearts. ||10||
RECORD	para 23315	sloku mÚ 3 ] (512-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23316	gurmuiK iDAwn shj Duin aupjY sic nwim icqu lwieAw ] (512-14, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gurmukh Dhi-aan sahj Dhun upjai sach naam chit laa-i-aa. The Gurmukh meditates on the Lord; the celestial sound-current resounds within him, and he focuses his consciousness on the True Name.
RECORD	para 23317	gurmuiK Anidnu rhY rMig rwqw hir kw nwmu min BwieAw ] (512-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gurmukh an-din rahai rang raataa har kaa naam man bhaa-i-aa. The Gurmukh remains imbued with the Lord's Love, night and day; his mind is pleased with the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 23318	gurmuiK hir vyKih gurmuiK hir bolih gurmuiK hir shij rMgu lwieAw ] (512-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gurmukh har vaykheh gurmukh har boleh gurmukh har sahj rang laa-i-aa. The Gurmukh beholds the Lord, the Gurmukh speaks of the Lord, and the Gurmukh naturally loves the Lord.
UPHOLD	para 23319	nwnk gurmuiK igAwnu prwpiq hovY iqmr AigAwnu ADyru cukwieAw ] (512-16, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh gi-aan paraapat hovai timar agi-aan aDhayr chukaa-i-aa. O Nanak, the Gurmukh attains spiritual wisdom, and the pitch-black darkness of ignorance is dispelled.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	ijs no krmu hovY Duir pUrw iqin gurmuiK hir nwmu iDAwieAw ]1] (512-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jis no karam hovai Dhur pooraa tin gurmukh har naam Dhi-aa-i-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	One who is blessed by the Perfect Lord's Grace - as Gurmukh, he meditates on the Lord's Name. ||1||
RECORD	para 23321	mÚ 3 ] (512-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23322	siqguru ijnw n syivE sbid n lgo ipAwru ] (512-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur jinaa na sayvi-o sabad na lago pi-aar. Those who do not serve the True Guru do not embrace love for the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 23323	shjy nwmu n iDAwieAw ikqu AwieAw sMswir ] (512-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sehjay naam na Dhi-aa-i-aa kit aa-i-aa sansaar. They do not meditate on the Celestial Naam, the Name of the Lord - why did they even bother to come into the world?
DEFINE	para 23324	iPir iPir jUnI pweIAY ivstw sdw KuAwru ] (512-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) fir fir joonee paa-ee-ai vistaa sadaa khu-aar. Time and time again, they are reincarnated, and they rot away forever in manure.
DEFINE	para 23325	kUVY lwlic ligAw nw aurvwru n pwru ] (512-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) koorhai laalach lagi-aa naa urvaar na paar. They are attached to false greed; they are not on this shore, nor on the one beyond.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk gurmuiK aubry ij Awip myly krqwir ]2] (513-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh ubray je aap maylay kartaar. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are saved; the Creator Lord unites them with Himself. ||2||
RECORD	para 23328	pauVI ] (513-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 23329	Bgq scY dir sohdy scY sbid rhwey ] (513-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) bhagat sachai dar sohday sachai sabad rahaa-ay. The devotees look beauteous in the True Court of the Lord; they abide in the True Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 23330	hir kI pRIiq iqn aUpjI hir pRym kswey ] (513-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har kee pareet tin oopjee har paraym kasaa-ay. The Lord's Love wells up in them; they are attracted by the Lord's Love.
RECORD	para 23331	hir rMig rhih sdw rMig rwqy rsnw hir rsu ipAwey ] (513-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har rang raheh sadaa rang raatay rasnaa har ras pi-aa-ay. They abide in the Lord's Love, they remain imbued with the Lord's Love forever, and with their tongues, they drink in the sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	para 23332	sPlu jnmu ijn@I gurmuiK jwqw hir jIau irdY vswey ] (513-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) safal janam jin Hee gurmukh jaataa har jee-o ridai vasaa-ay. Fruitful are the lives of those Gurmukhs who recognize the Lord and enshrine Him in their hearts.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v11	bwJu gurU iPrY ibllwdI dUjY Bwie KuAwey ]11] (513-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) baajh guroo firai billaadee doojai bhaa-ay khu-aa-ay. ||11||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v11	Without the Guru, they wander around crying out in misery; in the love of duality, they are ruined. ||11||
RECORD	para 23334	sloku mÚ 3 ] (513-4) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23335	kiljug mih nwmu inDwnu BgqI KitAw hir auqm pdu pwieAw ] (513-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) kalijug meh naam niDhaan bhagtee khati-aa har utam pad paa-i-aa. In the Dark Age of Kali Yuga, the devotees earn the treasure of the Naam, the Name of the Lord; they obtain the supreme status of the Lord.
RECORD	para 23336	siqgur syiv hir nwmu min vswieAw Anidnu nwmu iDAwieAw ] (513-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur sayv har naam man vasaa-i-aa an-din naam Dhi-aa-i-aa. Serving the True Guru, they enshrine the Lord's Name in their minds, and they meditate on the Naam, night and day.
RECORD	para 23337	ivcy igRh gur bcin audwsI haumY mohu jlwieAw ] (513-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vichay garih gur bachan udaasee ha-umai moh jalaa-i-aa. Within the home of their own selves, they remain unattached, through the Guru's Teachings; they burn away egotism and emotional attachment.
UPHOLD	para 23338	Awip qirAw kul jgqu qrwieAw DMnu jxydI mwieAw ] (513-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aap tari-aa kul jagat taraa-i-aa Dhan janaydee maa-i-aa. They save themselves, and they save the whole world. Blessed are the mothers who gave birth to them.
RECORD	para 23339	AYsw siqguru soeI pwey ijsu Duir msqik hir iliK pwieAw ] (513-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aisaa satgur so-ee paa-ay jis Dhur mastak har likh paa-i-aa. He alone finds such a True Guru, upon whose forehead the Lord inscribed such pre- ordained destiny.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	jn nwnk bilhwrI gur Awpxy ivthu ijin BRim Bulw mwrig pwieAw ]1] (513-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jan naanak balihaaree gur aapnay vitahu jin bharam bhulaa maarag paa-i-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	Servant Nanak is a sacrifice to his Guru; when he was wandering in doubt, He placed him on the Path. ||1||
RECORD	para 23341	mÚ 3 ] (513-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23342	qRY gux mwieAw vyiK Buly ijau dyiK dIpik pqMg pcwieAw ] (513-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) tarai gun maa-i-aa vaykh bhulay ji-o daykh deepak patang pachaa-i-aa. Beholding Maya with her three dispositions, he goes astray; he is like the moth, which sees the flame, and is consumed.
RECORD	para 23343	pMifq Buil Buil mwieAw vyKih idKw iknY ikhu Awix cVwieAw ] (513-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) pandit bhul bhul maa-i-aa vaykheh dikhaa kinai kihu aan charhaa-i-aa. The mistaken, deluded Pandits gaze upon Maya, and watch to see whether anyone has offered them something.
RECORD	para 23344	dUjY Bwie pVih inq ibiKAw nwvhu diX KuAwieAw ] (513-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay parheh nit bikhi-aa naavhu da-yi khu-aa-i-aa. In the love of duality, they read continually about sin, while the Lord has withheld His Name from them.
