RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, those who chant Waaho! Waaho! - unto them I dedicate my body and mind. ||1||
RECORD	para 23433	mÚ 3 ] (515-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23434	vwhu vwhu swihbu scu hY AMimRqu jw kw nwau ] (515-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu saahib sach hai amrit jaa kaa naa-o. Waaho! Waaho! is the True Lord Master; His Name is Ambrosial Nectar.
DEFINE	para 23435	ijin syivAw iqin Plu pwieAw hau iqn bilhwrY jwau ] (515-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jin sayvi-aa tin fal paa-i-aa ha-o tin balihaarai jaa-o. Those who serve the Lord are blessed with the fruit; I am a sacrifice to them.
DEFINE	para 23436	vwhu vwhu guxI inDwnu hY ijs no dyie su Kwie ] (515-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu gunee niDhaan hai jis no day-ay so khaa-ay. Waaho! Waaho! is the treasure of virtue; he alone tastes it, who is so blessed.
RECORD	para 23437	vwhu vwhu jil Qil BrpUru hY gurmuiK pwieAw jwie ] (515-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu jal thal bharpoor hai gurmukh paa-i-aa jaa-ay. Waaho! Waaho! The Lord is pervading and permeating the oceans and the land; the Gurmukh attains Him.
RECORD	para 23438	vwhu vwhu gurisK inq sB krhu gur pUry vwhu vwhu BwvY ] (515-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu gursikh nit sabh karahu gur pooray vaahu vaahu bhaavai. Waaho! Waaho! Let all the Gursikhs continually praise Him. Waaho! Waaho! The Perfect Guru is pleased with His Praises.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk vwhu vwhu jo min iciq kry iqsu jmkMkru nyiV n AwvY ]2] (515-14, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak vaahu vaahu jo man chit karay tis jamkankar nayrh na aavai. ||2||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, one who chants Waaho! Waaho! with his heart and mind - the Messenger of Death does not approach him. ||2||
RECORD	para 23440	pauVI ] (515-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 23441	hir jIau scw scu hY scI gurbwxI ] (515-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) har jee-o sachaa sach hai sachee gurbaanee. The Dear Lord is the Truest of the True; True is the Word of the Guru's Bani.
DEFINE	para 23442	siqgur qy scu pCwxIAY sic shij smwxI ] (515-15, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) satgur tay sach pachhaanee-ai sach sahj samaanee. Through the True Guru, the Truth is realized, and one is easily absorbed in the True Lord.
RECORD	para 23443	Anidnu jwgih nw svih jwgq rYix ivhwxI ] (515-16, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) an-din jaageh naa saveh jaagat rain vihaanee. Night and day, they remain awake, and do not sleep; in wakefulness, the night of their lives passes.
RECORD	para 23444	gurmqI hir rsu cwiKAw sy puMn prwxI ] (515-16, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gurmatee har ras chaakhi-aa say punn paraanee. Those who taste the sublime essence of the Lord, through the Guru's Teachings, are the most worthy persons.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v17	ibnu gur iknY n pwieE pic muey AjwxI ]17] (515-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) bin gur kinai na paa-i-o pach mu-ay ajaanee. ||17||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v17	Without the Guru, no one has obtained the Lord; the ignorant rot away and die. ||17||
RECORD	para 23446	sloku mÚ 3 ] (515-17) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23447	vwhu vwhu bwxI inrMkwr hY iqsu jyvfu Avru n koie ] (515-17, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu banee nirankaar hai tis jayvad avar na ko-ay. Waaho! Waaho! is the Bani, the Word, of the Formless Lord. There is no other as great as He is.
RECORD	para 23448	vwhu vwhu Agm AQwhu hY vwhu vwhu scw soie ] (515-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu agam athaahu hai vaahu vaahu sachaa so-ay. Waaho! Waaho! The Lord is unfathomable and inaccessible. Waaho! Waaho! He is the True One.
RECORD	para 23449	vwhu vwhu vyprvwhu hY vwhu vwhu kry su hoie ] (515-18, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu vayparvaahu hai vaahu vaahu karay so ho-ay. Waaho! Waaho! He is the self-existent Lord. Waaho! Waaho! As He wills, so it comes to pass.
RECORD	para 23450	vwhu vwhu AMimRq nwmu hY gurmuiK pwvY koie ] (515-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu amrit naam hai gurmukh paavai ko-ay. Waaho! Waaho! is the Ambrosial Nectar of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, obtained by the Gurmukh.
DEFINE	para 23451	vwhu vwhu krmI pweIAY Awip dieAw kir dyie ] (515-19, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu karmee paa-ee-ai aap da-i-aa kar day-ay. Waaho! Waaho! This is realized by His Grace, as He Himself grants His Grace.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk vwhu vwhu gurmuiK pweIAY Anidnu nwmu leyie ]1] (516-1, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak vaahu vaahu gurmukh paa-ee-ai an-din naam la-ay-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, Waaho! Waaho! This is obtained by the Gurmukhs, who hold tight to the Naam, night and day. ||1||
RECORD	para 23454	mÚ 3 ] (516-1) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23455	ibnu siqgur syvy swiq n AwveI dUjI nwhI jwie ] (516-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay saat na aavee doojee naahee jaa-ay. Without serving the True Guru, peace is not obtained, and the sense of duality does not depart.
ALLOW	para 23456	jy bhuqyrw locIAY ivxu krmY n pwieAw jwie ] (516-2, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jay bahutayraa lochee-ai vin karmai na paa-i-aa jaa-ay. No matter how much one may wish, without the Lord's Grace, He is not found.
DEFINE	para 23457	ijn@w AMqir loB ivkwru hY dUjY Bwie KuAwie ] (516-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jin Haa antar lobh vikaar hai doojai bhaa-ay khu-aa-ay. Those who are filled with greed and corruption are ruined by the love of duality.
RECORD	para 23458	jMmxu mrxu n cukeI haumY ivic duKu pwie ] (516-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jaman maran na chuk-ee ha-umai vich dukh paa-ay. They cannot escape birth and death, and with egotism within them, they suffer in misery.
RECORD	para 23459	ijn@w siqgur isau icqu lwieAw su KwlI koeI nwih ] (516-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jin Haa satgur si-o chit laa-i-aa so khaalee ko-ee naahi. Those who center their consciousness on the True Guru, never go empty-handed.
DEFINE	para 23460	iqn jm kI qlb n hoveI nw Eie duK shwih ] (516-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) tin jam kee talab na hova-ee naa o-ay dukh sahaahi. They are not summoned by the Messenger of Death, and they do not suffer in pain.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk gurmuiK aubry scY sbid smwih ]2] (516-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh ubray sachai sabad samaahi. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are saved; they merge in the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 23462	pauVI ] (516-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 23463	FwFI iqs no AwKIAY ij KsmY Dry ipAwru ] (516-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) dhaadhee tis no aakhee-ai je khasmai Dharay pi-aar. He alone is called a minstrel, who enshrines love for his Lord and Master.
RECORD	para 23464	dir KVw syvw kry gur sbdI vIcwru ] (516-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) dar kharhaa sayvaa karay gur sabdee veechaar. Standing at the Lord's Door, he serves the Lord, and reflects upon the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 23465	FwFI dru Gru pwiesI scu rKY aur Dwir ] (516-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) dhaadhee dar ghar paa-isee sach rakhai ur Dhaar. The minstrel attains the Lord's Gate and Mansion, and he keeps the True Lord clasped to his heart.
DEFINE	para 23466	FwFI kw mhlu Aglw hir kY nwie ipAwir ] (516-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) dhaadhee kaa mahal aglaa har kai naa-ay pi-aar. The status of the minstrel is exalted; he loves the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v18	FwFI kI syvw cwkrI hir jip hir insqwir ]18] (516-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) dhaadhee kee sayvaa chaakree har jap har nistaar. ||18||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v18	The service of the minstrel is to meditate on the Lord; he is emancipated by the Lord. ||18||
RECORD	para 23468	sloku mÚ 3 ] (516-8) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23469	gUjrI jwiq gvwir jw shu pwey Awpxw ] (516-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) goojree jaat gavaar jaa saho paa-ay aapnaa. The milkmaid's status is very low, but she attains her Husband Lord
WHEN	para 23470	gur kY sbid vIcwir Anidnu hir jpu jwpxw ] (516-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad veechaar an-din har jap jaapnaa. when she reflects upon the Word of the Guru's Shabad, and chants the Lord's Name, night and day.
DEFINE	para 23471	ijsu siqguru imlY iqsu Bau pvY sw kulvMqI nwir ] (516-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jis satgur milai tis bha-o pavai saa kulvantee naar. She who meets the True Guru, lives in the Fear of God; she is a woman of noble birth.
UPHOLD	para 23472	sw hukmu pCwxY kMq kw ijs no ik®pw kIqI krqwir ] (516-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) saa hukam pachhaanai kant kaa jis no kirpaa keetee kartaar. She alone realizes the Hukam of her Husband Lord's Command, who is blessed by the Creator Lord's Mercy.
DEFINE	para 23473	Eh kucjI kulKxI prhir CofI Bqwir ] (516-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) oh kuchjee kulkhanee parhar chhodee bhataar. She who is of little merit and ill-mannered, is discarded and forsaken by her Husband Lord.
DEFINE	para 23474	BY pieAY mlu ktIAY inrml hovY srIru ] (516-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) bhai pa-i-ai mal katee-ai nirmal hovai sareer. By the Fear of God, filth is washed off, and the body becomes immaculately pure.
RECORD	para 23475	AMqir prgwsu miq aUqm hovY hir jip guxI ghIru ] (516-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) antar pargaas mat ootam hovai har jap gunee gaheer. The soul is enlightened, and the intellect is exalted, meditating on the Lord, the ocean of excellence.
RECORD	para 23476	BY ivic bYsY BY rhY BY ivic kmwvY kwr ] (516-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) bhai vich baisai bhai rahai bhai vich kamaavai kaar. One who dwells in the Fear of God, lives in the Fear of God, and acts in the Fear of God.
RECORD	para 23477	AYQY suKu vifAweIAw drgh moK duAwr ] (516-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aithai sukh vadi-aa-ee-aa dargeh mokh du-aar. He obtains peace and glorious greatness here, in the Lord's Court, and at the Gate of Salvation.
RECORD	para 23478	BY qy inrBau pweIAY imil joqI joiq Apwr ] (516-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) bhai tay nirbha-o paa-ee-ai mil jotee jot apaar. Through the Fear of God, the Fearless Lord is obtained, and one's light merges in the Infinite Light.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk KsmY BwvY sw BlI ijs no Awpy bKsy krqwru ]1] (516-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak khasmai bhaavai saa bhalee jis no aapay bakhsay kartaar. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, that bride alone is good, who is pleasing to her Lord and Master, and whom the Creator Lord Himself forgives. ||1||
RECORD	para 23480	mÚ 3 ] (516-13) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23481	sdw sdw swlwhIAY scy kau bil jwau ] (516-13, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa salaahee-ai sachay ka-o bal jaa-o. Praise the Lord, forever and ever, and make yourself a sacrifice to the True Lord.
WHEN	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk eyku Coif dUjY lgY sw ijhvw jil jwau ]2] (516-14, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak ayk chhod doojai lagai saa jihvaa jal jaa-o. ||2||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, let that tongue be burnt, which renounces the One Lord, and attaches itself to another. ||2||
RECORD	para 23483	pauVI ] (516-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
