DEFINE	para 23505	mhl BgqI Gir srY sjx pwhuixAau ] (517-3, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) mahal bhagtee ghar sarai sajan paahuni-a-o. When devotion comes to the mind of the soul-bride, she is visited by the friendly guest.
DEFINE	para 23506	brsnw q brsu Gnw bhuiV brsih kwih ] (517-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) barsanaa ta baras ghanaa bahurh barseh kaahi. O clouds, if you are going to rain, then go ahead and rain; why rain after the season has passed?
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk iqn@ bilhwrxY ijn@ gurmuiK pwieAw mn mwih ]1] (517-4, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak tin H balihaarnai jin H gurmukh paa-i-aa man maahi. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	Nanak is a sacrifice to those Gurmukhs who obtain the Lord in their minds. ||1||
RECORD	para 23508	mÚ 3 ] (517-5) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 23509	imTw so jo Bwvdw sjxu so ij rwis ] (517-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) mithaa so jo bhaavdaa sajan so je raas. That which is pleasing is sweet, and one who is sincere is a friend.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk gurmuiK jwxIAY jw kau Awip kry prgwsu ]2] (517-5, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh jaanee-ai jaa ka-o aap karay pargaas. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, he is known as a Gurmukh, whom the Lord Himself enlightens. ||2||
RECORD	para 23511	pauVI ] (517-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 23512	pRB pwis jn kI Ardwis qU scw sWeI ] (517-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) parabh paas jan kee ardaas too sachaa saa N-ee. O God, Your humble servant offers his prayer to You; You are my True Master.
DEFINE	para 23513	qU rKvwlw sdw sdw hau quDu iDAweI ] (517-6, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) too rakhvaalaa sadaa sadaa ha-o tuDh Dhi-aa-ee. You are my Protector, forever and ever; I meditate on You.
DEFINE	para 23514	jIA jMq siB qyirAw qU rihAw smweI ] (517-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jee-a jant sabh tayri-aa too rahi-aa samaa-ee. All the beings and creatures are Yours; You are pervading and permeating in them.
DEFINE	para 23515	jo dws qyry kI inMdw kry iqsu mwir pcweI ] (517-7, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) jo daas tayray kee nindaa karay tis maar pachaa-ee. One who slanders Your slave is crushed and destroyed.
WHEN	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v21	icMqw Cif AicMqu rhu nwnk lig pweI ]21] (517-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) chintaa chhad achint rahu naanak lag paa-ee. ||21||
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v21	Falling at Your Feet, Nanak has renounced his cares, and has become care-free. ||21||
RECORD	para 23517	slok mÚ 3 ] (517-8) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 23518	Awsw krqw jgu muAw Awsw mrY n jwie ] (517-8, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aasaa kartaa jag mu-aa aasaa marai na jaa-ay. Building up its hopes, the world dies, but its hopes do not die or depart.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	nwnk Awsw pUrIAw scy isau icqu lwie ]1] (517-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak aasaa pooree-aa sachay si-o chit laa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v1	O Nanak, hopes are fulfilled only by attaching one's consciousness to the True Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 23520	mÚ 3 ] (517-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 23521	Awsw mnsw mir jwiesI ijin kIqI so lY jwie ] (517-9, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aasaa mansaa mar jaa-isee jin keetee so lai jaa-ay. Hopes and desires shall die only when He, who created them, takes them away.
RECORD	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	nwnk inhclu ko nhI bwJhu hir kY nwie ]2] (517-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) naanak nihchal ko nahee baajhahu har kai naa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	gUjrI mhlw 5 Gru 4 v2	O Nanak, nothing is permanent, except the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 23523	pauVI ] (517-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 23524	Awpy jgqu aupwieEnu kir pUrw Qwtu ] (517-10, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aapay jagat upaa-i-on kar pooraa thaat. He Himself created the world, with His perfect workmanship.
DEFINE	para 23525	Awpy swhu Awpy vxjwrw Awpy hI hir hwtu ] (517-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aapay saahu aapay vanjaaraa aapay hee har haat. He Himself is the true banker, He Himself is the merchant, and He Himself is the store.
DEFINE	para 23526	Awpy swgru Awpy boihQw Awpy hI Kyvwtu ] (517-11, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aapay saagar aapay bohithaa aapay hee khayvaat. He Himself is the ocean, He Himself is the boat, and He Himself is the boatman.
DEFINE	para 23527	Awpy guru cylw hY Awpy Awpy dsy Gwtu ] (517-12, gUjrI kI vwr, mÚ 3) aapay gur chaylaa hai aapay aapay dasay ghaat. He Himself is the Guru, He Himself is the disciple, and He Himself shows the destination.
