DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	Your wondrous play is pervading everywhere. I place my pain and pleasure before You. ||2||
RECORD	para 24737	slok mÚ 3 ] (549-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24738	gurmuiK scY Bwvdy dir scY sicAwr ] (549-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gurmukh sachai bhaavday dar sachai sachiaar. The Gurmukhs are pleasing to the True Lord; they are judged to be true in the True Court.
DEFINE	para 24739	swjn min Awnµdu hY gur kw sbdu vIcwr ] (549-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) saajan man aanand hai gur kaa sabad veechaar. The minds of such friends are filled with bliss, as they reflect upon the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 24740	AMqir sbdu vswieAw duKu kitAw cwnxu kIAw krqwir ] (549-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) antar sabad vasaa-i-aa dukh kati-aa chaanan kee-aa kartaar. They enshrine the Shabad within their hearts; their pain is dispelled, and the Creator blesses them with the Divine Light.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk rKxhwrw rKsI AwpxI ikrpw Dwir ]1] (549-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak rakhanhaaraa rakhsee aapnee kirpaa Dhaar. ||1||
REQUIRE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, the Savior Lord shall save them, and shower them with His Mercy. ||1||
RECORD	para 24742	mÚ 3 ] (549-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24743	gur kI syvw cwkrI BY ric kwr kmwie ] (549-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur kee sayvaa chaakree bhai rach kaar kamaa-ay. Serve the Guru, and wait upon Him; as you work, maintain the Fear of God.
RECORD	para 24744	jyhw syvY qyho hovY jy clY iqsY rjwie ] (549-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jayhaa sayvai tayho hovai jay chalai tisai rajaa-ay. As you serve Him, you will become like Him, as you walk according to His Will.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk sBu ikCu Awip hY Avru n dUjI jwie ]2] (549-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak sabh kichh aap hai avar na doojee jaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, He Himself is everything; there is no other place to go. ||2||
RECORD	para 24746	pauVI ] (549-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 24747	qyrI vifAweI qUhY jwxdw quDu jyvfu Avru n koeI ] (549-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) tayree vadi-aa-ee toohai jaandaa tuDh jayvad avar na ko-ee. You alone know Your greatness - no one else is as great as You.
WHEN	para 24748	quDu jyvfu horu srIku hovY qw AwKIAY quDu jyvfu qUhY hoeI ] (549-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) tuDh jayvad hor sareek hovai taa aakhee-ai tuDh jayvad toohai ho-ee. If there were some other rival as great as You, then I would speak of him. You alone are as great as You are.
RECORD	para 24749	ijin qU syivAw iqin suKu pwieAw horu iqs dI rIs kry ikAw koeI ] (549-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jin too sayvi-aa tin sukh paa-i-aa hor tis dee rees karay ki-aa ko-ee. One who serves You obtains peace; who else can compare to You?
RECORD	para 24750	qU BMnx GVx smrQu dwqwru hih quDu AgY mMgx no hQ joiV KlI sB hoeI ] (549-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) too bhannan gharhan samrath daataar heh tuDh agai mangan no hath jorh khalee sabh ho-ee. You are all-powerful to destroy and create, O Great Giver; with palms pressed together, all stand begging before You.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v3	quDu jyvfu dwqwru mY koeI ndir n AwveI quDu sBsY no dwnu idqw KMfI vrBMfI pwqwlI pureI sB loeI ]3] (549-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) tuDh jayvad daataar mai ko-ee nadar na aavee tuDh sabhsai no daan ditaa khandee varbhandee paataalee pur-ee sabh lo-ee. ||3||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v3	I see none as great as You, O Great Giver; You give in charity to the beings of all the continents, worlds, solar systems, nether regions and universes. ||3||
RECORD	para 24752	slok mÚ 3 ] (549-16) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24753	min prqIiq n AweIAw shij n lgo Bwau ] (549-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) man parteet na aa-ee-aa sahj na lago bhaa-o. O mind, you have no faith, and you have not embraced love for the Celestial Lord;
RECORD	para 24754	sbdY swdu n pwieE mnhiT ikAw gux gwie ] (549-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sabdai saad na paa-i-o manhath ki-aa gun gaa-ay. you do not enjoy the sublime taste of the Word of the Shabad - what Praises of the Lord will you stubborn-mindedly sing?
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk AwieAw so prvwxu hY ij gurmuiK sic smwie ]1] (549-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak aa-i-aa so parvaan hai je gurmukh sach samaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, his coming alone is approved, who, as Gurmukh, merges into the True Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 24756	mÚ 3 ] (549-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24757	Awpxw Awpu n pCwxY mUVw Avrw AwiK duKwey ] (549-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapnaa aap na pachhaanai moorhaa avraa aakh dukhaa-ay. The fool does not understand his own self; he annoys others with his speech.
RECORD	para 24758	muMFY dI Ksliq n geIAw AMDy ivCuiV cotw Kwey ] (549-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) mundhai dee khaslat na ga-ee-aa anDhay vichhurh chotaa khaa-ay. His underlying nature does not leave him; separated from the Lord, he suffers cruel blows.
RECORD	para 24759	siqgur kY BY BMin n GiVE rhY AMik smwey ] (549-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) satgur kai bhai bhann na gharhi-o rahai ank samaa-ay. Through the fear of the True Guru, he has not changed and reformed himself, so that he might merge in the lap of God.
RECORD	para 24761	Anidnu shsw kdy n cUkY ibnu sbdY duKu pwey ] (550-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) an-din sahsaa kaday na chookai bin sabdai dukh paa-ay. Night and day, his doubts never stop; without the Word of the Shabad, he suffers in pain.
RECORD	para 24762	kwmu k®oDu loBu AMqir sblw inq DMDw krq ivhwey ] (550-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) kaam kroDh lobh antar sablaa nit DhanDhaa karat vihaa-ay. Sexual desire, anger and greed are so powerful within him; he passes his life constantly entangled in worldly affairs.
DEFINE	para 24763	crx kr dyKq suix Qky idh muky nyVY Awey ] (550-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) charan kar daykhat sun thakay dih mukay nayrhai aa-ay. His feet, hands, eyes and ears are exhausted; his days are numbered, and his death is immanent.
RECORD	para 24764	scw nwmu n lgo mITw ijqu nwim nv iniD pwey ] (550-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sachaa naam na lago meethaa jit naam nav niDh paa-ay. The True Name does not seem sweet to him - the Name by which the nine treasures are obtained.
WHEN	para 24765	jIvqu mrY mrY Puin jIvY qW moKMqru pwey ] (550-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jeevat marai marai fun jeevai taaN mokhantar paa-ay. But if he remains dead while yet alive, then by so dying, he truly lives; thus, he attains liberation.
WHEN	para 24766	Duir krmu n pwieE prwxI ivxu krmw ikAw pwey ] (550-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) Dhur karam na paa-i-o paraanee vin karmaa ki-aa paa-ay. But if he is not blessed with such pre-ordained karma, then without this karma, what can he obtain?
REQUIRE	para 24767	gur kw sbdu smwil qU mUVy giq miq sbdy pwey ] (550-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur kaa sabad samaal too moorhay gat mat sabday paa-ay. Meditate in remembrance on the Word of the Guru's Shabad, you fool; through the Shabad, you shall obtain salvation and wisdom.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk siqguru qd hI pwey jW ivchu Awpu gvwey ]2] (550-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak satgur tad hee paa-ay jaa N vichahu aap gavaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, he alone finds the True Guru, who eliminates self-conceit from within. ||2||
RECORD	para 24769	pauVI ] (550-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24770	ijs dY iciq visAw myrw suAwmI iqs no ikau AMdysw iksY glY dw loVIAY ] (550-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jis dai chit vasi-aa mayraa su-aamee tis no ki-o andaysaa kisai galai daa lorhee-ai. One whose consciousness is filled with my Lord Master - why should he feel anxious about anything?
RECORD	para 24773	siB duK BuK rog gey hir syvk ky siB jn ky bMDn qoVIAY ] (550-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sabh dukh bhukh rog ga-ay har sayvak kay sabh jan kay banDhan torhee-ai. All the pain, hunger, and disease of the Lord's servant are eradicated; the bonds of the humble beings are torn away.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v4	hir ikrpw qy hoAw hir Bgqu hir Bgq jnw kY muih ifTY jgqu qirAw sBu loVIAY ]4] (550-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har kirpaa tay ho-aa har bhagat har bhagat janaa kai muhi dithai jagat tari-aa sabh lorhee-ai. ||4||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v4	By the Lord's Grace, one becomes the Lord's devotee; beholding the face of the Lord's humble devotee, the whole world is saved and carried across. ||4||
RECORD	para 24775	slok mÚ 3 ] (550-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24776	sw rsnw jil jwau ijin hir kw suAwau n pwieAw ] (550-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) saa rasnaa jal jaa-o jin har kaa su-aa-o na paa-i-aa. Let that tongue, which has not tasted the Name of the Lord, be burnt.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk rsnw sbid rswie ijin hir hir mMin vswieAw ]1] (550-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak rasnaa sabad rasaa-ay jin har har man vasaa-i-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, one whose mind is filled with the Name of the Lord, Har, Har - his tongue savors the Word of the Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	para 24778	mÚ 3 ] (550-10) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24779	sw rsnw jil jwau ijin hir kw nwau ivswirAw ] (550-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) saa rasnaa jal jaa-o jin har kaa naa-o visaari-aa. Let that tongue, which has forgotten the Name of the Lord, be burnt.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk gurmuiK rsnw hir jpY hir kY nwie ipAwirAw ]2] (550-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh rasnaa har japai har kai naa-ay pi-aari-aa. ||2||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, the tongue of the Gurmukh chants the Lord's Name, and loves the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 24781	pauVI ] (550-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24782	hir Awpy Twkuru syvku Bgqu hir Awpy kry krwey ] (550-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har aapay thaakur sayvak bhagat har aapay karay karaa-ay. The Lord Himself is the Master, the servant and the devotee; the Lord Himself is the Cause of causes.
RECORD	para 24783	hir Awpy vyKY ivgsY Awpy ijqu BwvY iqqu lwey ] (550-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har aapay vaykhai vigsai aapay jit bhaavai tit laa-ay. The Lord Himself beholds, and He Himself rejoices. As He wills, so does He enjoin us.
RECORD	para 24784	hir ieknw mwrig pwey Awpy hir ieknw auJiV pwey ] (550-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har iknaa maarag paa-ay aapay har iknaa ujharh paa-ay. The Lord places some on the Path, and the Lord leads others into the wilderness.
RECORD	para 24785	hir scw swihbu scu qpwvsu kir vyKY clq sbwey ] (550-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har sachaa saahib sach tapaavas kar vaykhai chalat sabaa-ay. The Lord is the True Master; True is His justice. He arranges and beholds all His plays.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v5	gur prswid khY jnu nwnku hir scy ky gux gwey ]5] (550-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur parsaad kahai jan naanak har sachay kay gun gaa-ay. ||5||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v5	By Guru's Grace, servant Nanak speaks and sings the Glorious Praises of the True Lord. ||5||
RECORD	para 24787	slok mÚ 3 ] (550-15) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24788	drvysI ko jwxsI ivrlw ko drvysu ] (550-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) darvaysee ko jaansee virlaa ko darvays. How rare is the dervish, the Saintly renunciate, who understands renunciation.
UPHOLD	para 24789	jy Gir Gir hMFY mMgdw iDgu jIvxu iDgu vysu ] (550-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jay ghar ghar handhai mangdaa Dhig jeevan Dhig vays. Cursed is the life, and cursed are the clothes, of one who wanders around, begging from door to door.
WHEN	para 24790	jy Awsw AMdysw qij rhY gurmuiK iBiKAw nwau ] (550-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jay aasaa andaysaa taj rahai gurmukh bhikhi-aa naa-o. But, if he abandons hope and anxiety, and as Gurmukh receives the Name as his charity,
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	iqs ky crn pKwlIAih nwnk hau bilhwrY jwau ]1] (550-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) tis kay charan pakhaalee-ah naanak ha-o balihaarai jaa-o. ||1||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	then Nanak washes his feet, and is a sacrifice to him. ||1||
RECORD	para 24792	mÚ 3 ] (550-17) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24793	nwnk qrvru eyku Plu duie pMKyrU Awih ] (550-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak tarvar ayk fal du-ay pankhayroo aahi. O Nanak, the tree has one fruit, but two birds are perched upon it.
DEFINE	para 24794	Awvq jwq n dIshI nw pr pMKI qwih ] (550-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aavat jaat na deeshee naa par pankhee taahi. They are not seen coming or going; these birds have no wings.
RECORD	para 24795	bhu rMgI rs BoigAw sbid rhY inrbwxu ] (550-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) baho rangee ras bhogi-aa sabad rahai nirbaan. One enjoys so many pleasures, while the other, through the Word of the Shabad, remains in Nirvaanaa.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	hir ris Pil rwqy nwnkw krim scw nIswxu ]2] (550-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har ras fal raatay naankaa karam sachaa neesaan. ||2||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	Imbued with the subtle essence of the fruit of the Lord's Name, O Nanak, the soul bears the True Insignia of God's Grace. ||2||
RECORD	para 24797	pauVI ] (550-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 24798	Awpy DrqI Awpy hY rwhku Awip jMmwie pIswvY ] (550-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay Dhartee aapay hai raahak aap jammaa-ay peesaavai. He Himself is the field, and He Himself is the farmer. He Himself grows and grinds the corn.
RECORD	para 24799	Awip pkwvY Awip BWfy dyie prosY Awpy hI bih KwvY ] (550-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aap pakaavai aap bhaa Nday day-ay parosai aapay hee bahi khaavai. He Himself cooks it, He Himself puts the food in the dishes, and He Himself sits down to eat.
DEFINE	para 24801	Awpy jlu Awpy dy iCMgw Awpy culI BrwvY ] (551-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay jal aapay day chhingaa aapay chulee bharaavai. He Himself is the water, He Himself gives the tooth-pick, and He Himself offers the mouthwash.
RECORD	para 24802	Awpy sMgiq sid bhwlY Awpy ivdw krwvY ] (551-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay sangat sad bahaalai aapay vidaa karaavai. He Himself calls and seats the congregation, and He Himself bids them goodbye.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v6	ijs no ikrpwlu hovY hir Awpy iqs no hukmu mnwvY ]6] (551-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jis no kirpaal hovai har aapay tis no hukam manaavai. ||6||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v6	One whom the Lord Himself blesses with His Mercy - the Lord causes him to walk according to His Will. ||6||
RECORD	para 24804	slok mÚ 3 ] (551-2) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24805	krm Drm siB bMDnw pwp puMn snbMDu ] (551-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) karam Dharam sabh banDhnaa paap punn san-banDh. Rituals and religions are all just entanglements; bad and good are bound up with them.
RECORD	para 24806	mmqw mohu su bMDnw puqR klqR su DMDu ] (551-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) mamtaa moh so banDhnaa putar kaltar so DhanDh. Those things done for the sake of children and spouse, in ego and attachment, are just more bonds.
RECORD	para 24807	jh dyKw qh jyvrI mwieAw kw snbMDu ] (551-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jah daykhaa tah jayvree maa-i-aa kaa san-banDh. Wherever I look, there I see the noose of attachment to Maya.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk scy nwm ibnu vrqix vrqY AMDu ]1] (551-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak sachay naam bin vartan vartai anDh. ||1||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, without the True Name, the world is engrossed in blind entanglements. ||1||
RECORD	para 24809	mÚ 4 ] (551-4) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
WHEN	para 24810	AMDy cwnxu qw QIAY jw siqguru imlY rjwie ] (551-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) anDhay chaanan taa thee-ai jaa satgur milai rajaa-ay. The blind receive the Divine Light, when they merge with the Will of the True Guru.
DEFINE	para 24811	bMDn qoVY sic vsY AigAwnu ADyrw jwie ] (551-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) banDhan torhai sach vasai agi-aan aDhayraa jaa-ay. They break their bonds, and dwell in Truth, and the darkness of ignorance is dispelled.
RECORD	para 24812	sBu ikCu dyKY iqsY kw ijin kIAw qnu swij ] (551-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) sabh kichh daykhai tisai kaa jin kee-aa tan saaj. They see that everything belongs to the One who created and fashioned the body.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk srix krqwr kI krqw rwKY lwj ]2] (551-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) naanak saran kartaar kee kartaa raakhai laaj. ||2||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	Nanak seeks the Sanctuary of the Creator - the Creator preserves his honor. ||2||
RECORD	para 24814	pauVI ] (551-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
WHEN	para 24815	jdhu Awpy Qwtu kIAw bih krqY qdhu puiC n syvku bIAw ] (551-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) jadahu aapay thaat kee-aa bahi kartai tadahu puchh na sayvak bee-aa. When the Creator, sitting all by Himself, created the Universe, he did not consult with any of His servants;
WHEN	para 24816	qdhu ikAw ko lyvY ikAw ko dyvY jW Avru n dUjw kIAw ] (551-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) tadahu ki-aa ko layvai ki-aa ko dayvai jaa N avar na doojaa kee-aa. so what can anyone take, and what can anyone give, when He did not create any other like Himself?
UPHOLD	para 24817	iPir Awpy jgqu aupwieAw krqY dwnu sBnw kau dIAw ] (551-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) fir aapay jagat upaa-i-aa kartai daan sabhnaa ka-o dee-aa. Then, after fashioning the world, the Creator blessed all with His blessings.
RECORD	para 24818	Awpy syv bxweIAnu gurmuiK Awpy AMimRqu pIAw ] (551-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) aapay sayv banaa-ee-an gurmukh aapay amrit pee-aa. He Himself instructs us in His service, and as Gurmukh, we drink in His Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v7	Awip inrMkwr Awkwru hY Awpy Awpy krY su QIAw ]7] (551-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) aap nirankaar aakaar hai aapay aapay karai so thee-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v7	He Himself is formless, and He Himself is formed; whatever He Himself does, comes to pass. ||7||
RECORD	para 24820	slok mÚ 3 ] (551-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24821	gurmuiK pRBu syvih sd swcw Anidnu shij ipAwir ] (551-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gurmukh parabh sayveh sad saachaa an-din sahj pi-aar. The Gurmukhs serve God forever; night and day, they are steeped in the Love of the True Lord.
RECORD	para 24822	sdw Anµid gwvih gux swcy AriD auriD auir Dwir ] (551-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sadaa anand gaavahi gun saachay araDh uraDh ur Dhaar. They are in bliss forever, singing the Glorious Praises of the True Lord; in this world and in the next, they keep Him clasped to their hearts.
RECORD	para 24823	AMqir pRIqmu visAw Duir krmu iliKAw krqwir ] (551-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) antar pareetam vasi-aa Dhur karam likhi-aa kartaar. Their Beloved dwells deep within; the Creator pre-ordained this destiny.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk Awip imlwieAnu Awpy ikrpw Dwir ]1] (551-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak aap milaa-i-an aapay kirpaa Dhaar. ||1||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, He blends them into Himself; He Himself showers His Mercy upon them. ||1||
RECORD	para 24825	mÚ 3 ] (551-12) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24826	kihAY kiQAY n pweIAY Anidnu rhY sdw gux gwie ] (551-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) kahi-ai kathi-ai na paa-ee-ai an-din rahai sadaa gun gaa-ay. By merely talking and speaking, He is not found. Night and day, sing His Glorious Praises continually.
RECORD	para 24827	ivxu krmY iknY n pwieE Bauik muey ibllwie ] (551-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) vin karmai kinai na paa-i-o bha-uk mu-ay billaa-ay. Without His Merciful Grace, no one finds Him; many have died barking and bewailing.
WHEN	para 24828	gur kY sbid mnu qnu iBjY Awip vsY min Awie ] (551-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad man tan bhijai aap vasai man aa-ay. When the mind and body are saturated with the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Lord Himself comes to dwell in his mind.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk ndrI pweIAY Awpy ley imlwie ]2] (551-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak nadree paa-ee-ai aapay la-ay milaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, by His Grace, He is found; He unites us in His Union. ||2||
RECORD	para 24830	pauVI ] (551-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24831	Awpy vyd purwx siB swsq Awip kQY Awip BIjY ] (551-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay vayd puraan sabh saasat aap kathai aap bheejai. He Himself is the Vedas, the Puraanas and all the Shaastras; He Himself chants them, and He Himself is pleased.
RECORD	para 24832	Awpy hI bih pUjy krqw Awip prpMcu krIjY ] (551-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay hee bahi poojay kartaa aap parpanch kareejai. He Himself sits down to worship, and He Himself creates the world.
DEFINE	para 24833	Awip privriq Awip inrivrqI Awpy AkQu kQIjY ] (551-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aap parvirat aap nirvirtee aapay akath katheejai. He Himself is a householder, and He Himself is a renunciate; He Himself utters the Unutterable.
DEFINE	para 24834	Awpy puMnu sBu Awip krwey Awip Ailpqu vrqIjY ] (551-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay punn sabh aap karaa-ay aap alipat varteejai. He Himself is all goodness, and He Himself causes us to act; He Himself remains detached.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v8	Awpy suKu duKu dyvY krqw Awpy bKs krIjY ]8] (551-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay sukh dukh dayvai kartaa aapay bakhas kareejai. ||8||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v8	He Himself grants pleasure and pain; the Creator Himself bestows His gifts. ||8||
RECORD	para 24836	slok mÚ 3 ] (551-17) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
WHEN	para 24837	syKw AMdrhu joru Cif qU Bau kir Jlu gvwie ] (551-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) saykhaa andrahu jor chhad too bha-o kar jhal gavaa-ay. O Shaykh, abandon your cruel nature; live in the Fear of God and give up your madness.
RECORD	para 24838	gur kY BY kyqy insqry BY ivic inrBau pwie ] (551-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur kai bhai kaytay nistaray bhai vich nirbha-o paa-ay. Through the Fear of the Guru, many have been saved; in this fear, find the Fearless Lord.
RECORD	para 24839	mnu kToru sbid Byid qUM sWiq vsY min Awie ] (551-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) man kathor sabad bhayd tooN saa Nt vasai man aa-ay. Pierce your stone heart with the Word of the Shabad; let peace and tranquility come to abide in your mind.
DEFINE	para 24840	sWqI ivic kwr kmwvxI sw Ksmu pwey Qwie ] (551-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) saaNtee vich kaar kamaavnee saa khasam paa-ay thaa-ay. If good deeds are done in this state of peace, they are approved by the Lord and Master.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk kwim k®oiD iknY n pwieE puChu igAwnI jwie ]1] (551-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak kaam kroDh kinai na paa-i-o puchhahu gi-aanee jaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, through sexual desire and anger, no one has ever found God - go, and ask any wise man. ||1||
RECORD	para 24842	mÚ 3 ] (551-19) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24844	mnmuK mwieAw mohu hY nwim n lgo ipAwru ] (552-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) manmukh maa-i-aa moh hai naam na lago pi-aar. The self-willed manmukh is emotionally attached to Maya - he has no love for the Naam.
RECORD	para 24845	kUVu kmwvY kUVu sMgRhY kUVu kry Awhwru ] (552-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) koorh kamaavai koorh sangrahai koorh karay aahaar. He practices falsehood, gathers in falsehood, and makes falsehood his sustenance.
RECORD	para 24846	ibKu mwieAw Dnu sMic mrih AMqy hoie sBu Cwru ] (552-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) bikh maa-i-aa Dhan sanch mareh antay ho-ay sabh chhaar. He collects the poisonous wealth of Maya, and then dies; in the end, it is all reduced to ashes.
RECORD	para 24847	krm Drm suc sMjm krih AMqir loBu ivkwru ] (552-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) karam Dharam such sanjam karahi antar lobh vikaar. He practices religious rituals, purity and austere self-discipline, but within, there is greed and corruption.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk ij mnmuKu kmwvY su Qwie nw pvY drgih hoie KuAwru ]2] (552-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak je manmukh kamaavai so thaa-ay naa pavai dargahi ho-ay khu-aar. ||2||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, whatever the self-willed manmukh does, is not acceptable; in the Court of the Lord, he is dishonored. ||2||
RECORD	para 24849	pauVI ] (552-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24850	Awpy KwxI Awpy bwxI Awpy KMf vrBMf kry ] (552-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay khaanee aapay banee aapay khand varbhand karay. He Himself created the four sources of creation, and He Himself fashioned speech; He Himself formed the worlds and solar systems.
DEFINE	para 24851	Awip smuMdu Awip hY swgru Awpy hI ivic rqn Dry ] (552-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aap samund aap hai saagar aapay hee vich ratan Dharay. He Himself is the ocean, and He Himself is the sea; He Himself puts the pearls in it.
RECORD	para 24852	Awip lhwey kry ijsu ikrpw ijs no gurmuiK kry hry ] (552-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aap lahaa-ay karay jis kirpaa jis no gurmukh karay haray. By His Grace, the Lord enables the Gurmukh to find these pearls.
RECORD	para 24853	Awpy Baujlu Awip hY boihQw Awpy Kyvtu Awip qry ] (552-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay bha-ojal aap hai bohithaa aapay khayvat aap taray. He Himself is the terrifying world-ocean, and He Himself is the boat; He Himself is the boatman, and He Himself ferries us across.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v9	Awpy kry krwey krqw Avru n dUjw quJY sry ]9] (552-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay karay karaa-ay kartaa avar na doojaa tujhai saray. ||9||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v9	The Creator Himself acts, and causes us to act; no one else can equal You, Lord. ||9||
RECORD	para 24855	slok mÚ 3 ] (552-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24856	siqgur kI syvw sPl hY jy ko kry icqu lwie ] (552-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) satgur kee sayvaa safal hai jay ko karay chit laa-ay. Fruitful is service to the True Guru, if one does so with a sincere mind.
DEFINE	para 24857	nwmu pdwrQu pweIAY AicMqu vsY min Awie ] (552-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naam padaarath paa-ee-ai achint vasai man aa-ay. The treasure of the Naam, is obtained, and the mind comes to be free of anxiety.
DEFINE	para 24858	jnm mrn duKu ktIAY haumY mmqw jwie ] (552-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) janam maran dukh katee-ai ha-umai mamtaa jaa-ay. The pains of birth and death are eradicated, and the mind is rid of egotism and self- conceit.
RECORD	para 24859	auqm pdvI pweIAY scy rhY smwie ] (552-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) utam padvee paa-ee-ai sachay rahai samaa-ay. One achieves the ultimate state, and remains absorbed in the True Lord.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk pUrib ijn kau iliKAw iqnw siqguru imilAw Awie ]1] (552-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak poorab jin ka-o likhi-aa tinaa satgur mili-aa aa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, the True Guru comes and meets those who have such pre-ordained destiny. ||1||
RECORD	para 24861	mÚ 3 ] (552-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24862	nwim rqw siqgurU hY kiljug boihQu hoie ] (552-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naam rataa satguroo hai kalijug bohith ho-ay. The True Guru is imbued with the Naam, the Name of the Lord; He is the boat in this Dark Age of Kali Yuga.
RECORD	para 24863	gurmuiK hovY su pwir pvY ijnw AMdir scw soie ] (552-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so paar pavai jinaa andar sachaa so-ay. One who becomes Gurmukh crosses over; the True Lord dwells within him.
ALLOW	para 24864	nwmu sm@wly nwmu sMgRhY nwmy hI piq hoie ] (552-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naam sam Haalay naam sangrahai naamay hee pat ho-ay. He remembers the Naam, he gathers in the Naam, and he obtains honor through the Naam.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk siqguru pwieAw krim prwpiq hoie ]2] (552-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak satgur paa-i-aa karam paraapat ho-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	Nanak has found the True Guru; by His Grace, the Name is obtained. ||2||
RECORD	para 24866	pauVI ] (552-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24867	Awpy pwrsu Awip Dwqu hY Awip kIqonu kMcnu ] (552-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay paaras aap Dhaat hai aap keeton kanchan. He Himself is the Philosopher's Stone, He Himself is the metal, and He Himself is transformed into gold.
RECORD	para 24868	Awpy Twkuru syvku Awpy Awpy hI pwp KMfnu ] (552-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay thaakur sayvak aapay aapay hee paap khandan. He Himself is the Lord and Master, He Himself is the servant, and He Himself is the Destroyer of sins.
DEFINE	para 24869	Awpy siB Gt BogvY suAwmI Awpy hI sBu AMjnu ] (552-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay sabh ghat bhogvai su-aamee aapay hee sabh anjan. He Himself enjoys every heart; the Lord Master Himself is the basis of all illusion.
RECORD	para 24870	Awip ibbyku Awip sBu byqw Awpy gurmuiK BMjnu ] (552-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aap bibayk aap sabh baytaa aapay gurmukh bhanjan. He Himself is the discerning one, and He Himself is the Knower of all; He Himself breaks the bonds of the Gurmukhs.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v10	jnu nwnku swlwih n rjY quDu krqy qU hir suKdwqw vfnu ]10] (552-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jan naanak saalaahi na rajai tuDh kartay too har sukh-daata vadan. ||10||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v10	Servant Nanak is not satisfied by merely praising You, O Creator Lord; You are the Great Giver of peace. ||10||
RECORD	para 24872	sloku mÚ 4 ] (552-14) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 24873	ibnu siqgur syvy jIA ky bMDnw jyqy krm kmwih ] (552-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) bin satgur sayvay jee-a kay banDhnaa jaytay karam kamaahi. Without serving the True Guru, the deeds which are done are only chains binding the soul.
RECORD	para 24874	ibnu siqgur syvy Tvr n pwvhI mir jMmih Awvih jwih ] (552-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) bin satgur sayvay thavar na paavhee mar jameh aavahi jaahi. Without serving the True Guru, they find no place of rest. They die, only to be born again - they continue coming and going.
RECORD	para 24875	ibnu siqgur syvy iPkw bolxw nwmu n vsY min Awie ] (552-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) bin satgur sayvay fikaa bolnaa naam na vasai man aa-ay. Without serving the True Guru, their speech is insipid. They do not enshrine the Naam, the Name of the Lord, in the mind.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk ibnu siqgur syvy jm puir bDy mwrIAih muih kwlY auiT jwih ]1] (552-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 4) naanak bin satgur sayvay jam pur baDhay maaree-ah muhi kaalai uth jaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, without serving the True Guru, they are bound and gagged, and beaten in the City of Death; they depart with blackened faces. ||1||
RECORD	para 24877	mÚ 3 ] (552-16) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
ALLOW	para 24878	ieik siqgur kI syvw krih cwkrI hir nwmy lgY ipAwru ] (552-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ik satgur kee sayvaa karahi chaakree har naamay lagai pi-aar. Some wait upon and serve the True Guru; they embrace love for the Lord's Name.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk jnmu svwrin Awpxw kul kw krin auDwru ]2] (552-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak janam savaaran aapnaa kul kaa karan uDhaar. ||2||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, they reform their lives, and redeem their generations as well. ||2||
RECORD	para 24880	pauVI ] (552-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24881	Awpy cwtswl Awip hY pwDw Awpy cwtVy pVx kau Awxy ] (552-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay chaatsaal aap hai paaDhaa aapay chaatrhay parhan ka-o aanay. He Himself is the school, He Himself is the teacher, and He Himself brings the students to be taught.
RECORD	para 24882	Awpy ipqw mwqw hY Awpy Awpy bwlk kry isAwxy ] (552-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay pitaa maataa hai aapay aapay baalak karay si-aanay. He Himself is the father, He Himself is the mother, and He Himself makes the children wise.
RECORD	para 24883	iek QY piV buJY sBu Awpy iek QY Awpy kry ieAwxy ] (552-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ik thai parh bujhai sabh aapay ik thai aapay karay i-aanay. In one place, He teaches them to read and understand everything, while in another place, He Himself makes them ignorant.
WHEN	para 24884	ieknw AMdir mhil bulwey jw Awip qyrY min scy Bwxy ] (552-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) iknaa andar mahal bulaa-ay jaa aap tayrai man sachay bhaanay. Some, You summon to the Mansion of Your Presence within, when they are pleasing to Your Mind, O True Lord.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v11	ijnw Awpy gurmuiK dy vifAweI sy jn scI drgih jwxy ]11] (553-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jinaa aapay gurmukh day vadi-aa-ee say jan sachee dargahi jaanay. ||11||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v11	That Gurmukh, whom You have blessed with greatness - that humble being is known in Your True Court. ||11||
RECORD	para 24887	sloku mrdwnw 1 ] (553-2) salok mardaanaa 1. Shalok, Mardaanaa:
DEFINE	para 24888	kil klvwlI kwmu mdu mnUAw pIvxhwru ] (553-2, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) kal kalvaalee kaam mad manoo-aa peevanhaar. The Dark Age of Kali Yuga is the vessel, filled with the wine of sexual desire; the mind is the drunkard.
DEFINE	para 24889	k®oD ktorI moih BrI pIlwvw AhMkwru ] (553-2, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) kroDh katoree mohi bharee peelaavaa ahaNkaar. Anger is the cup, filled with emotional attachment, and egotism is the server.
DEFINE	para 24890	mjls kUVy lb kI pI pI hoie KuAwru ] (553-3, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) majlas koorhay lab kee pee pee ho-ay khu-aar. Drinking too much in the company of falsehood and greed, one is ruined.
RECORD	para 24891	krxI lwhix squ guVu scu srw kir swru ] (553-3, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) karnee laahan sat gurh sach saraa kar saar. So let good deeds be your distillery, and Truth your molasses; in this way, make the most excellent wine of Truth.
RECORD	para 24892	gux mMfy kir sIlu iGau srmu mwsu Awhwru ] (553-4, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) gun manday kar seel ghi-o saram maas aahaar. Make virtue your bread, good conduct the ghee, and modesty the meat to eat.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	gurmuiK pweIAY nwnkw KwDY jwih ibkwr ]1] (553-4, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) gurmukh paa-ee-ai naankaa khaaDhai jaahi bikaar. ||1||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	As Gurmukh, these are obtained, O Nanak; partaking of them, one's sins depart. ||1||
RECORD	para 24894	mrdwnw 1 ] (553-5) mardaanaa 1. Mardaanaa:
DEFINE	para 24895	kwieAw lwhix Awpu mdu mjls iqRsnw Dwqu ] (553-5, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) kaa-i-aa laahan aap mad majlas tarisnaa Dhaat. The human body is the vat, self-conceit is the wine, and desire is the company of drinking buddies.
DEFINE	para 24896	mnsw ktorI kUiV BrI pIlwey jmkwlu ] (553-5, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) mansaa katoree koorh bharee peelaa-ay jamkaal. The cup of the mind's longing is overflowing with falsehood, and the Messenger of Death is the cup-bearer.
RECORD	para 24897	iequ mid pIqY nwnkw bhuqy KtIAih ibkwr ] (553-6, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) it mad peetai naankaa bahutay khatee-ah bikaar. Drinking in this wine, O Nanak, one takes on countless sins and corruptions.
UPHOLD	para 24898	igAwnu guVu swlwh mMfy Bau mwsu Awhwru ] (553-6, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) gi-aan gurh saalaah manday bha-o maas aahaar. So make spiritual wisdom your molasses, the Praise of God your bread, and the Fear of God the meat you eat.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk iehu Bojnu scu hY scu nwmu AwDwru ]2] (553-7, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) naanak ih bhojan sach hai sach naam aaDhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, this is the true food; let the True Name be your only Support. ||2||
WHEN	para 24900	kWXW lwhix Awpu mdu AMimRq iqs kI Dwr ] (553-7, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) kaaNyaaN laahan aap mad amrit tis kee Dhaar. If the human body is the vat, and self-realization is the wine, then a stream of Ambrosial Nectar is produced.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v3	sqsMgiq isau mylwpu hoie ilv ktorI AMimRq BrI pI pI ktih ibkwr ]3] (553-8, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) satsangat si-o maylaap ho-ay liv katoree amrit bharee pee pee kateh bikaar. ||3||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v3	Meeting with the Society of the Saints, the cup of the Lord's Love is filled with this Ambrosial Nectar; drinking it in, one's corruptions and sins are wiped away. ||3||
RECORD	para 24902	pauVI ] (553-9) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24903	Awpy suir nr gx gMDrbw Awpy Kt drsn kI bwxI ] (553-9, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) aapay sur nar gan ganDharbaa aapay khat darsan kee banee. He Himself is the angelic being, the heavenly herald, and the celestial singer. He Himself is the one who explains the six schools of philosophy.
RECORD	para 24904	Awpy isv sMkr mhysw Awpy gurmuiK AkQ khwxI ] (553-9, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) aapay siv sankar mahaysaa aapay gurmukh akath kahaanee. He Himself is Shiva, Shankara and Mahaysh; He Himself is the Gurmukh, who speaks the Unspoken Speech.
RECORD	para 24905	Awpy jogI Awpy BogI Awpy sMinAwsI iPrY ibbwxI ] (553-10, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) aapay jogee aapay bhogee aapay sani-aasee firai bibaanee. He Himself is the Yogi, He Himself is the Sensual Enjoyer, and He Himself is the Sannyaasee, wandering through the wilderness.
RECORD	para 24906	AwpY nwil gosit Awip aupdysY Awpy suGVu srUpu isAwxI ] (553-10, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) aapai naal gosat aap updaysai aapay sugharh saroop si-aanee. He discusses with Himself, and He teaches Himself; He Himself is discrete, graceful and wise.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v12	Awpxw coju kir vyKY Awpy Awpy sBnw jIAw kw hY jwxI ]12] (553-11, ibhwgVw, mrdwnw) aapnaa choj kar vaykhai aapay aapay sabhnaa jee-aa kaa hai jaanee. ||12||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v12	Staging His own play, He Himself watches it; He Himself is the Knower of all beings. ||12||
RECORD	para 24908	sloku mÚ 3 ] (553-12) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24909	eyhw sMiDAw prvwxu hY ijqu hir pRBu myrw iciq AwvY ] (553-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ayhaa sanDhi-aa parvaan hai jit har parabh mayraa chit aavai. That evening prayer alone is acceptable, which brings the Lord God to my consciousness.
DEFINE	para 24910	hir isau pRIiq aUpjY mwieAw mohu jlwvY ] (553-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har si-o pareet oopjai maa-i-aa moh jalaavai. Love for the Lord wells up within me, and my attachment to Maya is burnt away.
RECORD	para 24911	gur prswdI duibDw mrY mnUAw AsiQru sMiDAw kry vIcwru ] (553-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee dubiDhaa marai manoo-aa asthir sanDhi-aa karay veechaar. By Guru's Grace, duality is conquered, and the mind becomes stable; I have made contemplative meditation my evening prayer.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk sMiDAw krY mnmuKI jIau n itkY mir jMmY hoie KuAwru ]1] (553-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak sanDhi-aa karai manmukhee jee-o na tikai mar jammai ho-ay khu-aar. ||1||
ALLOW	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, the self-willed manmukh may recite his evening prayers, but his mind is not centered on it; through birth and death, he is ruined. ||1||
RECORD	para 24913	mÚ 3 ] (553-14) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24914	ipRau ipRau krqI sBu jgu iPrI myrI ipAws n jwie ] (553-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) pari-o pari-o kartee sabh jag firee mayree pi-aas na jaa-ay. I wandered over the whole world, crying out, "Love, O Love!", but my thirst was not quenched.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk siqguir imilAY myrI ipAws geI ipru pwieAw Gir Awie ]2] (553-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak satgur mili-ai mayree pi-aas ga-ee pir paa-i-aa ghar aa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, meeting the True Guru, my desires are satisfied; I found my Beloved, when I returned to my own home. ||2||
RECORD	para 24916	pauVI ] (553-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24917	Awpy qMqu prm qMqu sBu Awpy Awpy Twkuru dwsu BieAw ] (553-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay tant param tant sabh aapay aapay thaakur daas bha-i-aa. He Himself is the supreme essence, He Himself is the essence of all. He Himself is the Lord and Master, and He Himself is the servant.
RECORD	para 24918	Awpy ds AT vrn aupwieAnu Awip bRhmu Awip rwju lieAw ] (553-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay das ath varan upaa-i-an aap barahm aap raaj la-i-aa. He Himself created the people of the eighteen castes; God Himself acquired His domain.
RECORD	para 24919	Awpy mwry Awpy CofY Awpy bKsy kry dieAw ] (553-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay maaray aapay chhodai aapay bakhsay karay da-i-aa. He Himself kills, and He Himself redeems; He Himself, in His Kindness, forgives us. He is infallible
DEFINE	para 24920	Awip ABulu n BulY kb hI sBu scu qpwvsu scu iQAw ] (553-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aap abhul na bhulai kab hee sabh sach tapaavas sach thi-aa. - He never errs; the justice of the True Lord is totally True.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v13	Awpy ijnw buJwey gurmuiK iqn AMdrhu dUjw Brmu gieAw ]13] (553-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay jinaa bujhaa-ay gurmukh tin andrahu doojaa bharam ga-i-aa. ||13||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v13	Those whom the Lord Himself instructs as Gurmukh - duality and doubt depart from within them. ||13||
RECORD	para 24922	sloku mÚ 5 ] (553-19) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 24923	hir nwmu n ismrih swDsMig qY qin aufY Kyh ] (553-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) har naam na simrahi saaDhsang tai tan udai khayh. That body, which does not remember the Lord's Name in meditation in the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, shall be reduced to dust.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	ijin kIqI iqsY n jwxeI nwnk iPtu AlUxI dyh ]1] (553-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) jin keetee tisai na jaan-ee naanak fit aloonee dayh. ||1||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	Cursed and insipid is that body, O Nanak, which does not know the One who created it. ||1||
RECORD	para 24926	mÚ 5 ] (554-1) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 24927	Git vsih crxwribMd rsnw jpY gupwl ] (554-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) ghat vaseh charnaarbind rasnaa japai gupaal. Let the Lotus Feet of the Lord abide within your heart, and with your tongue, chant God's Name.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk so pRBu ismrIAY iqsu dyhI kau pwil ]2] (554-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) naanak so parabh simree-ai tis dayhee ka-o paal. ||2||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, meditate in remembrance on God, and nurture this body. ||2||
RECORD	para 24929	pauVI ] (554-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24930	Awpy ATsiT qIrQ krqw Awip kry iesnwnu ] (554-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) aapay athsath tirath kartaa aap karay isnaan. The Creator Himself is the sixty-eight sacred places of pilgrimage; He Himself takes the cleansing bath in them.
RECORD	para 24931	Awpy sMjim vrqY sÍwmI Awip jpwieih nwmu ] (554-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) aapay sanjam vartai savaamee aap japaa-ihi naam. He Himself practices austere self-discipline; the Lord Master Himself causes us to chant His Name.
RECORD	para 24932	Awip dieAwlu hoie Bau KMfnu Awip krY sBu dwnu ] (554-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) aap da-i-aal ho-ay bha-o khandan aap karai sabh daan. He Himself becomes merciful to us; the Destroyer of fear Himself gives in charity to all.
RECORD	para 24933	ijs no gurmuiK Awip buJwey so sd hI drgih pwey mwnu ] (554-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) jis no gurmukh aap bujhaa-ay so sad hee dargahi paa-ay maan. One whom He has enlightened and made Gurmukh, ever obtains honor in His Court.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v14	ijs dI pYj rKY hir suAwmI so scw hir jwnu ]14] (554-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 5) jis dee paij rakhai har su-aamee so sachaa har jaan. ||14||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v14	One whose honor the Lord Master has preserved, comes to know the True Lord. ||14||
RECORD	para 24935	sloku mÚ 3 ] (554-5) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24936	nwnk ibnu siqgur Byty jgu AMDu hY AMDy krm kmwie ] (554-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak bin satgur bhaytay jag anDh hai anDhay karam kamaa-ay. O Nanak, without meeting the True Guru, the world is blind, and it does blind deeds.
RECORD	para 24937	sbdY isau icqu n lwveI ijqu suKu vsY min Awie ] (554-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sabdai si-o chit na laav-ee jit sukh vasai man aa-ay. It does not focus its consciousness on the Word of the Shabad, which would bring peace to abide in the mind.
RECORD	para 24938	qwmis lgw sdw iPrY Aihinis jlqu ibhwie ] (554-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) taamas lagaa sadaa firai ahinis jalat bihaa-ay. Always afflicted with the dark passions of low energy, it wanders around, passing its days and nights burning.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	jo iqsu BwvY so QIAY khxw ikCU n jwie ]1] (554-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jo tis bhaavai so thee-ai kahnaa kichhoo na jaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	Whatever pleases Him, comes to pass; no one has any say in this. ||1||
RECORD	para 24940	mÚ 3 ] (554-7) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24941	siqgurU PurmwieAw kwrI eyh kryhu ] (554-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) satguroo furmaa-i-aa kaaree ayh karayhu. The True Guru has commanded us to do this:
RECORD	para 24942	gurU duAwrY hoie kY swihbu sMmwlyhu ] (554-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) guroo du-aarai ho-ay kai saahib sammaalayhu. through the Guru's Gate, meditate on the Lord Master.
RECORD	para 24943	swihbu sdw hjUir hY BrmY ky CauV kit kY AMqir joiq Dryhu ] (554-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) saahib sadaa hajoor hai bharmai kay chha-urh kat kai antar jot Dharayhu. The Lord Master is ever-present. He tears away the veil of doubt, and installs His Light within the mind.
DEFINE	para 24944	hir kw nwmu AMimRqu hY dwrU eyhu lweyhu ] (554-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har kaa naam amrit hai daaroo ayhu laa-ayhu. The Name of the Lord is Ambrosial Nectar - take this healing medicine!
RECORD	para 24945	siqgur kw Bwxw iciq rKhu sMjmu scw nyhu ] (554-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) satgur kaa bhaanaa chit rakhahu sanjam sachaa nayhu. Enshrine the Will of the True Guru in your consciousness, and make the True Lord's Love your self-discipline.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk AYQY suKY AMdir rKsI AgY hir isau kyl kryhu ]2] (554-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak aithai sukhai andar rakhsee agai har si-o kayl karayhu. ||2||
REQUIRE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, you shall be kept in peace here, and hereafter, you shall celebrate with the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 24947	pauVI ] (554-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 24948	Awpy Bwr ATwrh bxspiq Awpy hI Pl lwey ] (554-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay bhaar athaarah banaspat aapay hee fal laa-ay. He Himself is the vast variety of Nature, and He Himself makes it bear fruit.
RECORD	para 24949	Awpy mwlI Awip sBu isMcY Awpy hI muih pwey ] (554-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay maalee aap sabh sinchai aapay hee muhi paa-ay. He Himself is the Gardener, He Himself irrigates all the plants, and He Himself puts them in His mouth.
DEFINE	para 24950	Awpy krqw Awpy Bugqw Awpy dyie idvwey ] (554-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay kartaa aapay bhugtaa aapay day-ay divaa-ay. He Himself is the Creator, and He Himself is the Enjoyer; He Himself gives, and causes others to give.
RECORD	para 24951	Awpy swihbu Awpy hY rwKw Awpy rihAw smwey ] (554-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay saahib aapay hai raakhaa aapay rahi-aa samaa-ay. He Himself is the Lord and Master, and He Himself is the Protector; He Himself is permeating and pervading everywhere.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v15	jnu nwnk vifAweI AwKY hir krqy kI ijs no iqlu n qmwey ]15] (554-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jan naanak vadi-aa-ee aakhai har kartay kee jis no til na tamaa-ay. ||15||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v15	Servant Nanak speaks of the greatness of the Lord, the Creator, who has no greed at all. ||15||
RECORD	para 24953	slok mÚ 3 ] (554-13) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24954	mwxsu BirAw AwixAw mwxsu BirAw Awie ] (554-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) maanas bhari-aa aani-aa maanas bhari-aa aa-ay. One person brings a full bottle, and another fills his cup.
RECORD	para 24955	ijqu pIqY miq dUir hoie brlu pvY ivic Awie ] (554-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jit peetai mat door ho-ay baral pavai vich aa-ay. Drinking the wine, his intelligence departs, and madness enters his mind;
DEFINE	para 24956	Awpxw prwieAw n pCwxeI Ksmhu Dky Kwie ] (554-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapnaa paraa-i-aa na pachhaan-ee khasmahu Dhakay khaa-ay. he cannot distinguish between his own and others, and he is struck down by his Lord and Master.
DEFINE	para 24957	ijqu pIqY Ksmu ivsrY drgh imlY sjwie ] (554-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jit peetai khasam visrai dargeh milai sajaa-ay. Drinking it, he forgets his Lord and Master, and he is punished in the Court of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 24958	JUTw mdu mUil n pIceI jy kw pwir vswie ] (554-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jhoothaa mad mool na peech-ee jay kaa paar vasaa-ay. Do not drink the false wine at all, if it is in your power.
RECORD	para 24959	nwnk ndrI scu mdu pweIAY siqguru imlY ijsu Awie ] (554-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak nadree sach mad paa-ee-ai satgur milai jis aa-ay. O Nanak, the True Guru comes and meets the mortal; by His Grace, one obtains the True Wine.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	sdw swihb kY rMig rhY mhlI pwvY Qwau ]1] (554-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sadaa saahib kai rang rahai mahlee paavai thaa-o. ||1||
REQUIRE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	He shall dwell forever in the Love of the Lord Master, and obtain a seat in the Mansion of His Presence. ||1||
RECORD	para 24961	mÚ 3 ] (554-17) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24962	iehu jgqu jIvqu mrY jw ies no soJI hoie ] (554-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ih jagat jeevat marai jaa is no sojhee ho-ay. When this world comes to understand, it remains dead while yet alive.
WHEN	para 24963	jw iqin@ svwilAw qW siv rihAw jgwey qW suiD hoie ] (554-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jaa tiniH savaali-aa taaN sav rahi-aa jagaa-ay taaN suDh ho-ay. When the Lord puts him to sleep, he remains asleep; when He wakes him up, he regains consciousness.
WHEN	para 24964	nwnk ndir kry jy AwpxI siqguru mylY soie ] (554-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak nadar karay jay aapnee satgur maylai so-ay. O Nanak, when the Lord casts His Glance of Grace, He causes him to meet the True Guru.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	gur pRswid jIvqu mrY qw iPir mrxu n hoie ]2] (554-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur parsaad jeevat marai taa fir maran na ho-ay. ||2||
FORBID	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	By Guru's Grace, remain dead while yet alive, and you shall not have to die again. ||2||
RECORD	para 24966	pauVI ] (554-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 24967	ijs dw kIqw sBu ikCu hovY iqs no prvwh nwhI iksY kyrI ] (554-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jis daa keetaa sabh kichh hovai tis no parvaah naahee kisai kayree. By His doing, everything happens; what does He care for anyone else?
RECORD	para 24968	hir jIau qyrw idqw sBu ko KwvY sB muhqwjI kFY qyrI ] (554-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) har jee-o tayraa ditaa sabh ko khaavai sabh muhtaajee kadhai tayree. O Dear Lord, everyone eats whatever You give - all are subservient to You.
RECORD	para 24970	ij quD no swlwhy su sBu ikCu pwvY ijs no ikrpw inrMjn kyrI ] (555-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) je tuDh no saalaahay so sabh kichh paavai jis no kirpaa niranjan kayree. One who praises You obtains everything; You bestow Your Mercy upon him, O Immaculate Lord.
RECORD	para 24971	soeI swhu scw vxjwrw ijin vKru lidAw hir nwmu Dnu qyrI ] (555-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) so-ee saahu sachaa vanjaaraa jin vakhar ladi-aa har naam Dhan tayree. He alone is a true banker and trader, who loads the merchandise of the wealth of the Your Name, O Lord.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v16	siB iqsY no swlwihhu sMqhu ijin dUjy Bwv kI mwir ivfwrI FyrI ]16] (555-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sabh tisai no saalaahihu santahu jin doojay bhaav kee maar vidaaree dhayree. ||16||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v16	O Saints, let everyone praise the Lord, who has destroyed the pile of the love of duality. ||16||
RECORD	para 24973	slok ] (555-3) salok. Shalok:
DEFINE	para 24974	kbIrw mrqw mrqw jgu muAw mir iB n jwnY koie ] (555-3, ibhwgVw, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeeraa martaa martaa jag mu-aa mar bhe na jaanai ko-ay. Kabeer, the world is dying - dying to death, but no one knows how to truly die.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	AYsI mrnI jo mrY bhuir n mrnw hoie ]1] (555-4, ibhwgVw, Bgq kbIr jI) aisee marnee jo marai bahur na marnaa ho-ay. ||1||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	Whoever dies, let him die such a death, that he does not have to die again. ||1||
RECORD	para 24976	mÚ 3 ] (555-4) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24977	ikAw jwxw ikv mrhgy kYsw mrxw hoie ] (555-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ki-aa jaanaa kiv marhagay kaisaa marnaa ho-ay. What do I know? How will I die? What sort of death will it be?
WHEN	para 24978	jy kir swihbu mnhu n vIsrY qw sihlw mrxw hoie ] (555-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jay kar saahib manhu na veesrai taa sahilaa marnaa ho-ay. If I do not forget the Lord Master from my mind, then my death will be easy.
DEFINE	para 24979	mrxY qy jgqu frY jIivAw loVY sBu koie ] (555-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) marnai tay jagat darai jeevi-aa lorhai sabh ko-ay. The world is terrified of death; everyone longs to live.
RECORD	para 24980	gur prswdI jIvqu mrY hukmY bUJY soie ] (555-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee jeevat marai hukmai boojhai so-ay. By Guru's Grace, one who dies while yet alive, understands the Lord's Will.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk AYsI mrnI jo mrY qw sd jIvxu hoie ]2] (555-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak aisee marnee jo marai taa sad jeevan ho-ay. ||2||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, one who dies such a death, lives forever. ||2||
RECORD	para 24982	pauVI ] (555-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
WHEN	para 24983	jw Awip ik®pwlu hovY hir suAwmI qw AwpxW nwau hir Awip jpwvY ] (555-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jaa aap kirpaal hovai har su-aamee taa aapnaaN naa-o har aap japaavai. When the Lord Master Himself becomes merciful, the Lord Himself causes His Name to be chanted.
RECORD	para 24984	Awpy siqguru myil suKu dyvY AwpxW syvku Awip hir BwvY ] (555-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay satgur mayl sukh dayvai aapnaaN sayvak aap har bhaavai. He Himself causes us to meet the True Guru, and blesses us with peace. His servant is pleasing to the Lord.
RECORD	para 24985	AwpixAw syvkw kI Awip pYj rKY AwpixAw Bgqw kI pYrI pwvY ] (555-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapni-aa sayvkaa kee aap paij rakhai aapni-aa bhagtaa kee pairee paavai. He Himself preserves the honor of His servants; He causes others to fall at the feet of His devotees.
UPHOLD	para 24986	Drm rwie hY hir kw kIAw hir jn syvk nyiV n AwvY ] (555-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) Dharam raa-ay hai har kaa kee-aa har jan sayvak nayrh na aavai. The Righteous Judge of Dharma is a creation of the Lord; he does not approach the humble servant of the Lord.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v17	jo hir kw ipAwrw so sBnw kw ipAwrw hor kyqI JiK JiK AwvY jwvY ]17] (555-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jo har kaa pi-aaraa so sabhnaa kaa pi-aaraa hor kaytee jhakh jhakh aavai jaavai. ||17||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v17	One who is dear to the Lord, is dear to all; so many others come and go in vain. ||17||
RECORD	para 24988	slok mÚ 3 ] (555-10) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 24989	rwmu rwmu krqw sBu jgu iPrY rwmu n pwieAw jwie ] (555-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) raam raam kartaa sabh jag firai raam na paa-i-aa jaa-ay. The entire world roams around, chanting, "Raam, Raam, Lord, Lord", but the Lord cannot be obtained like this.
DEFINE	para 24990	Agmu Agocru Aiq vfw Aqulu n quilAw jwie ] (555-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) agam agochar at vadaa atul na tuli-aa jaa-ay. He is inaccessible, unfathomable and so very great; He is unweighable, and cannot be weighed.
RECORD	para 24991	kImiq iknY n pweIAw ikqY n lieAw jwie ] (555-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) keemat kinai na paa-ee-aa kitai na la-i-aa jaa-ay. No one can evaluate Him; He cannot be purchased at any price.
RECORD	para 24992	gur kY sbid ByidAw ien ibiD visAw min Awie ] (555-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad bhaydi-aa in biDh vasi-aa man aa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, His mystery is known; in this way, He comes to dwell in the mind.
RECORD	para 24993	nwnk Awip Amyau hY gur ikrpw qy rihAw smwie ] (555-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak aap amay-o hai gur kirpaa tay rahi-aa samaa-ay. O Nanak, He Himself is infinite; by Guru's Grace, He is known to be permeating and pervading everywhere.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	Awpy imilAw imil rihAw Awpy imilAw Awie ]1] (555-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay mili-aa mil rahi-aa aapay mili-aa aa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	He Himself comes to blend, and having blended, remains blended. ||1||
RECORD	para 24995	mÚ 3 ] (555-14) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 24996	ey mn iehu Dnu nwmu hY ijqu sdw sdw suKu hoie ] (555-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ay man ih Dhan naam hai jit sadaa sadaa sukh ho-ay. O my soul, this is the wealth of the Naam; through it, comes peace, forever and ever.
RECORD	para 24997	qotw mUil n AwveI lwhw sd hI hoie ] (555-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) totaa mool na aavee laahaa sad hee ho-ay. It never brings any loss; through it, one earns profits forever.
RECORD	para 24998	KwDY KricAY qoit n AwveI sdw sdw Ehu dyie ] (555-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) khaaDhai kharchi-ai tot na aavee sadaa sadaa oh day-ay. Eating and spending it, it never decreases; He continues to give, forever and ever.
RECORD	para 24999	shsw mUil n hoveI hwxq kdy n hoie ] (555-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sahsaa mool na hova-ee haanat kaday na ho-ay. One who has no skepticism at all never suffers humiliation.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk gurmuiK pweIAY jw kau ndir kryie ]2] (555-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh paa-ee-ai jaa ka-o nadar karay-i. ||2||
WHEN	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukh obtains the Name of the Lord, when the Lord bestows His Glance of Grace. ||2||
RECORD	para 25001	pauVI ] (555-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 25002	Awpy sB Gt AMdry Awpy hI bwhir ] (555-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay sabh ghat andray aapay hee baahar. He Himself is deep within all hearts, and He Himself is outside them.
DEFINE	para 25003	Awpy gupqu vrqdw Awpy hI jwhir ] (555-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay gupat varatdaa aapay hee jaahar. He Himself is prevailing unmanifest, and He Himself is manifest.
RECORD	para 25004	jug CqIh gubwru kir vriqAw suMnwhir ] (555-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jug chhateeh gubaar kar varti-aa sunnaahar. For thirty-six ages, He created the darkness, abiding in the void.
RECORD	para 25005	EQY vyd purwn n swsqw Awpy hir nrhir ] (555-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) othai vayd puraan na saastaa aapay har narhar. There were no Vedas, Puraanas or Shaastras there; only the Lord Himself existed.
RECORD	para 25006	bYTw qwVI lwie Awip sB dU hI bwhir ] (555-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) baithaa taarhee laa-ay aap sabh doo hee baahar. He Himself sat in the absolute trance, withdrawn from everything.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v18	AwpxI imiq Awip jwxdw Awpy hI gauhru ]18] (555-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapnee mit aap jaandaa aapay hee ga-uhar. ||18||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v18	Only He Himself knows His state; He Himself is the unfathomable ocean. ||18||
RECORD	para 25008	slok mÚ 3 ] (555-19) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 25009	haumY ivic jgqu muAw mrdo mrdw jwie ] (555-19, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ha-umai vich jagat mu-aa mardo mardaa jaa-ay. In egotism, the world is dead; it dies and dies, again and again.
RECORD	para 25011	ijcru ivic dMmu hY iqcru n cyqeI ik krygu AgY jwie ] (556-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jichar vich damm hai tichar na chayt-ee ke karayg agai jaa-ay. As long as there is breath in the body, he does not remember the Lord; what will he do in the world hereafter?
DEFINE	para 25012	igAwnI hoie su cyqMnu hoie AigAwnI AMDu kmwie ] (556-1, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) gi-aanee ho-ay so chaytann ho-ay agi-aanee anDh kamaa-ay. One who remembers the Lord is a spiritual teacher; the ignorant one acts blindly.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk eyQY kmwvY so imlY AgY pwey jwie ]1] (556-2, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak aythai kamaavai so milai agai paa-ay jaa-ay. ||1||
REQUIRE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, whatever one does in this world, determines what he shall receive in the world hereafter. ||1||
RECORD	para 25014	mÚ 3 ] (556-2) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 25015	Duir KsmY kw hukmu pieAw ivxu siqgur cyiqAw n jwie ] (556-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) Dhur khasmai kaa hukam pa-i-aa vin satgur chayti-aa na jaa-ay. From the very beginning, it has been the Will of the Lord Master, that He cannot be remembered without the True Guru.
RECORD	para 25016	siqguir imilAY AMqir riv rihAw sdw rihAw ilv lwie ] (556-3, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) satgur mili-ai antar rav rahi-aa sadaa rahi-aa liv laa-ay. Meeting the True Guru, he realizes that the Lord is permeating and pervading deep within him; he remains forever absorbed in the Lord's Love.
RECORD	para 25017	dim dim sdw smwldw dMmu n ibrQw jwie ] (556-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) dam dam sadaa samaaldaa damm na birthaa jaa-ay. With each and every breath, he constantly remembers the Lord in meditation; not a single breath passes in vain.
RECORD	para 25018	jnm mrn kw Bau gieAw jIvn pdvI pwie ] (556-4, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) janam maran kaa bha-o ga-i-aa jeevan padvee paa-ay. His fears of birth and death depart, and he obtains the honored state of eternal life.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk iehu mrqbw iqs no dyie ijs no ikrpw kry rjwie ]2] (556-5, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak ih martabaa tis no day-ay jis no kirpaa karay rajaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, He bestows this rank upon that mortal, upon whom He showers His Mercy. ||2||
RECORD	para 25020	pauVI ] (556-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 25021	Awpy dwnW bIinAw Awpy prDwnW ] (556-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay daanaa N beeni-aa aapay parDhaanaa N. He Himself is all-wise and all-knowing; He Himself is supreme.
RECORD	para 25022	Awpy rUp idKwldw Awpy lwie iDAwnW ] (556-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay roop dikhaaldaa aapay laa-ay Dhi-aanaa N. He Himself reveals His form, and He Himself enjoins us to His meditation.
UPHOLD	para 25023	Awpy monI vrqdw Awpy kQY igAwnW ] (556-6, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay monee varatdaa aapay kathai gi-aanaa N. He Himself poses as a silent sage, and He Himself speaks spiritual wisdom.
DEFINE	para 25024	kauVw iksY n lgeI sBnw hI Bwnw ] (556-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ka-urhaa kisai na lag-ee sabhnaa hee bhaanaa. He does not seem bitter to anyone; He is pleasing to all.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v19	ausqiq brin n skIAY sd sd kurbwnw ]19] (556-7, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) ustat baran na sakee-ai sad sad kurbaanaa. ||19||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v19	His Praises cannot be described; forever and ever, I am a sacrifice to Him. ||19||
RECORD	para 25026	slok mÚ 1 ] (556-8) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 25027	klI AMdir nwnkw ijMnW dw Aauqwru ] (556-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) kalee andar naankaa jinnaa N daa a-utaar. In this Dark Age of Kali Yuga, O Nanak, the demons have taken birth.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	puqu ijnUrw DIA ijMnUrI jorU ijMnw dw iskdwru ]1] (556-8, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) put jinooraa Dhee-a jinnooree joroo jinna daa sikdaar. ||1||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	The son is a demon, and the daughter is a demon; the wife is the chief of the demons. ||1||
RECORD	para 25029	mÚ 1 ] (556-9) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 25030	ihMdU mUly BUly AKutI jWhI ] (556-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) hindoo moolay bhoolay akhutee jaaNhee. The Hindus have forgotten the Primal Lord; they are going the wrong way.
RECORD	para 25031	nwrid kihAw is pUj krWhI ] AMDy guMgy AMD AMDwru ] (556-9, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) naarad kahi-aa se pooj karaa Nhee. anDhay gungay anDh anDhaar. As Naarad instructed them, they are worshipping idols. They are blind and mute, the blindest of the blind.
RECORD	para 25032	pwQru ly pUjih mugD gvwr ] (556-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) paathar lay poojeh mugaDh gavaar. The ignorant fools pick up stones and worship them.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	Eih jw Awip fuby qum khw qrxhwru ]2] (556-10, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) ohi jaa aap dubay tum kahaa taranhaar. ||2||
WHEN	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	But when those stones themselves sink, who will carry you across? ||2||
RECORD	para 25034	pauVI ] (556-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 25035	sBu ikhu qyrY vis hY qU scw swhu ] (556-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) sabh kihu tayrai vas hai too sachaa saahu. Everything is in Your power; You are the True King.
DEFINE	para 25036	Bgq rqy rMig eyk kY pUrw vyswhu ] (556-11, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) bhagat ratay rang ayk kai pooraa vaysaahu. The devotees are imbued with the Love of the One Lord; they have perfect faith in Him.
DEFINE	para 25037	AMimRqu Bojnu nwmu hir rij rij jn Kwhu ] (556-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) amrit bhojan naam har raj raj jan khaahu. The Name of the Lord is the ambrosial food; His humble servants eat their fill.
DEFINE	para 25038	siB pdwrQ pweIAin ismrxu scu lwhu ] (556-12, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) sabh padaarath paa-ee-an simran sach laahu. All treasures are obtained - meditative remembrance on the Lord is the true profit.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v20	sMq ipAwry pwrbRhm nwnk hir Agm Agwhu ]20] (556-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 1) sant pi-aaray paarbarahm naanak har agam agaahu. ||20||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v20	The Saints are very dear to the Supreme Lord God, O Nanak; the Lord is unapproachable and unfathomable. ||20||
RECORD	para 25040	slok mÚ 3 ] (556-13) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
ALLOW	para 25041	sBu ikCu hukmy Awvdw sBu ikCu hukmy jwie ] (556-13, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) sabh kichh hukmay aavdaa sabh kichh hukmay jaa-ay. Everything comes by the Lord's Will, and everything goes by the Lord's Will.
DEFINE	para 25042	jy ko mUrKu Awphu jwxY AMDw AMDu kmwie ] (556-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) jay ko moorakh aaphu jaanai anDhaa anDh kamaa-ay. If some fool believes that he is the creator, he is blind, and acts in blindness.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk hukmu ko gurmuiK buJY ijs no ikrpw kry rjwie ]1] (556-14, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak hukam ko gurmukh bujhai jis no kirpaa karay rajaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukh understands the Hukam of the Lord's Command; the Lord showers His Mercy upon him. ||1||
RECORD	para 25044	mÚ 3 ] (556-15) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 25045	so jogI jugiq so pwey ijs no gurmuiK nwmu prwpiq hoie ] (556-15, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) so jogee jugat so paa-ay jis no gurmukh naam paraapat ho-ay. He alone is a Yogi, and he alone finds the Way, who, as Gurmukh, obtains the Naam.
RECORD	para 25046	iqsu jogI kI ngrI sBu ko vsY ByKI jogu n hoie ] (556-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) tis jogee kee nagree sabh ko vasai bhaykhee jog na ho-ay. In the body-village of that Yogi are all blessings; this Yoga is not obtained by outward show.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk AYsw ivrlw ko jogI ijsu Git prgtu hoie ]2] (556-16, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak aisaa virlaa ko jogee jis ghat pargat ho-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, such a Yogi is very rare; the Lord is manifest in his heart. ||2||
RECORD	para 25048	pauVI ] (556-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 25049	Awpy jMq aupwieAnu Awpy AwDwru ] (556-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay jant upaa-i-an aapay aaDhaar. He Himself created the creatures, and He Himself supports them.
DEFINE	para 25050	Awpy sUKmu BwlIAY Awpy pwswru ] (556-17, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aapay sookham bhaalee-ai aapay paasaar. He Himself is seen to be subtle, and He Himself is obvious.
RECORD	para 25051	Awip iekwqI hoie rhY Awpy vf prvwru ] (556-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) aap ikaatee ho-ay rahai aapay vad parvaar. He Himself remains a solitary recluse, and He Himself has a huge family.
RECORD	para 25052	nwnku mMgY dwnu hir sMqw rynwru ] (556-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) naanak mangai daan har santaa raynaar. Nanak asks for the gift of the dust of the feet of the Saints of the Lord.
RECORD	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v21	horu dwqwru n suJeI qU dyvxhwru ]21]1] suDu ] (556-18, ibhwgVw, mÚ 3) hor daataar na sujh-ee too dayvanhaar. ||21||
DEFINE	ibhwgVy kI vwr mhlw 4 v21	1|| suDh. I cannot see any other Giver; You alone are the Giver, O Lord. ||21||1|| Sudh||
RECORD	para 25055	<> siq nwmu krqw purKu inrBau inrvYru Akwl mUriq AjUnI sYBM gur pRswid ] (557-1) ik-oNkaar sat naam kartaa purakh nirbha-o nirvair akaal moorat ajoonee saibhaN gur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. Truth Is The Name. Creative Being Personified. No Fear. No Hatred. Image Of The Undying. Beyond Birth. Self-Existent. By Guru's Grace:
RECORD	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 ] (557-3)
RECORD	para 25056	raag vad-hans mehlaa 1 ghar 1. Raag Wadahans, First Mehl, First House:
DEFINE	para 25057	AmlI Amlu n AMbVY mCI nIru n hoie ] (557-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) amlee amal na ambrhai machhee neer na ho-ay. To the addict, there is nothing like the drug; to the fish, there is nothing else like water.
RECORD	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v1	jo rqy sih AwpxY iqn BwvY sBu koie ]1] (557-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) jo ratay seh aapnai tin bhaavai sabh ko-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v1	Those who are attuned to their Lord - everyone is pleasing to them. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v1	hau vwrI vM\w KMnIAY vM\w qau swihb ky nwvY ]1] rhwau ] (557-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) ha-o vaaree vanjaa khannee-ai vanjaa ta-o saahib kay naavai. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v1	rahaa-o. I am a sacrifice, cut apart into pieces, a sacrifice to Your Name, O Lord Master. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 25060	swihbu sPilE ruKVw AMimRqu jw kw nwau ] (557-5, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) saahib safli-o rukh-rhaa amrit jaa kaa naa-o. The Lord is the fruitful tree; His Name is ambrosial nectar.
RECORD	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v2	ijn pIAw qy iqRpq Bey hau iqn bilhwrY jwau ]2] (557-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) jin pee-aa tay taripat bha-ay ha-o tin balihaarai jaa-o. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v2	Those who drink it in are satisfied; I am a sacrifice to them. ||2||
DEFINE	para 25062	mY kI ndir n AwvhI vsih hBIAW nwil ] (557-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) mai kee nadar na aavhee vaseh habhee-aaN naal. You are not visible to me, although You dwell with everyone.
RECORD	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v3	iqKw iqhwieAw ikau lhY jw sr BIqir pwil ]3] (557-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) tikhaa tihaa-i-aa ki-o lahai jaa sar bheetar paal. ||3||
RECORD	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v3	How can the thirst of the thirsty be quenched, with that wall between me and the pond? ||3||
DEFINE	para 25064	nwnku qyrw bwxIAw qU swihbu mY rwis ] (557-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) naanak tayraa baanee-aa too saahib mai raas. Nanak is Your merchant; You, O Lord Master, are my merchandise.
RECORD	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v4	mn qy DoKw qw lhY jw isPiq krI Ardwis ]4]1] (557-8, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) man tay Dhokhaa taa lahai jaa sifat karee ardaas. ||4||
DEFINE	rwgu vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 1 v4	1|| My mind is cleansed of doubt, only when I praise You, and pray to You. ||4||1||
RECORD	para 25066	vad-hans mehlaa 1. Wadahans, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 25067	guxvMqI shu rwivAw inrguix kUky kwie ] (557-8, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) gunvantee saho raavi-aa nirgun kookay kaa-ay. The virtuous bride enjoys her Husband Lord; why does the unworthy one cry out?
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v1	jy guxvMqI QI rhY qw BI shu rwvx jwie ]1] (557-9, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) jay gunvantee thee rahai taa bhee saho raavan jaa-ay. ||1||
WHEN	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v1	If she were to become virtuous, then she too could enjoy her Husband Lord. ||1||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v1	myrw kMqu rIswlU kI Dn Avrw rwvy jI ]1] rhwau ] (557-9, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) mayraa kant reesaaloo kee Dhan avraa raavay jee. ||1||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. My Husband Lord is loving and playful; why should the soul-bride enjoy anyone else? ||1||Pause||
WHEN	para 25070	krxI kwmx jy QIAY jy mnu Dwgw hoie ] (557-10, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) karnee kaaman jay thee-ai jay man Dhaagaa ho-ay. If the soul-bride does good deeds, and strings them on the thread of her mind,
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v2	mwxku muil n pweIAY lIjY iciq proie ]2] (557-10, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) maanak mul na paa-ee-ai leejai chit paro-ay. ||2||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v2	she obtains the jewel, which cannot be purchased for any price, strung upon the thread of her consciousness. ||2||
RECORD	para 25072	rwhu dsweI n julW AwKW AMmVIAwsu ] (557-11, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) raahu dasaa-ee na julaa N aakhaaN ambrhee-aas. I ask, but do not follow the way shown to me; still, I claim to have reached my destination.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v3	qY sh nwil AkUAxw ikau QIvY Gr vwsu ]3] (557-11, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) tai sah naal akoo-anaa ki-o theevai ghar vaas. ||3||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v3	I do not speak with You, O my Husband Lord; how then can I come to have a place in Your home? ||3||
DEFINE	para 25074	nwnk eykI bwhrw dUjw nwhI koie ] (557-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) naanak aykee baahraa doojaa naahee ko-ay. O Nanak, without the One Lord, there is no other at all.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v4	qY sh lgI jy rhY BI shu rwvY soie ]4]2] (557-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) tai sah lagee jay rahai bhee saho raavai so-ay. ||4||
REQUIRE	vfhMsu mhlw 1 v4	2|| If the soul-bride remains attached to You, then she shall enjoy her Husband Lord. ||4||2||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 2	vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 2 ] (557-13)
RECORD	para 25076	vad-hans mehlaa 1 ghar 2. Wadahans, First Mehl, Second House:
DEFINE	para 25077	morI rux Jux lwieAw BYxy swvxu AwieAw ] (557-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) moree run jhun laa-i-aa bhainay saavan aa-i-aa. The peacocks are singing so sweetly, O sister; the rainy season of Saawan has come.
RECORD	para 25078	qyry muMD ktwry jyvfw iqin loBI loB luBwieAw ] (557-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) tayray munDh kataaray jayvdaa tin lobhee lobh lubhaa-i-aa. Your beauteous eyes are like a string of charms, fascinating and enticing the soul- bride.
UPHOLD	para 25079	qyry drsn ivthu KMnIAY vM\w qyry nwm ivthu kurbwxo ] (557-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) tayray darsan vitahu khannee-ai vanjaa tayray naam vitahu kurbaano. I would cut myself into pieces for the Blessed Vision of Your Darshan; I am a sacrifice to Your Name.
RECORD	para 25080	jw qU qw mY mwxu kIAw hY quDu ibnu kyhw myrw mwxo ] (557-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) jaa too taa mai maan kee-aa hai tuDh bin kayhaa mayraa maano. I take pride in You; without You, what could I be proud of?
RECORD	para 25081	cUVw BMnu plµG isau muMDy sxu bwhI sxu bwhw ] (557-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) choorhaa bhann palangh si-o munDhay san baahee san baahaa. So smash your bracelets along with your bed, O soul-bride, and break your arms, along with the arms of your couch.
RECORD	para 25082	eyqy vys krydIey muMDy shu rwqo Avrwhw ] (557-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) aytay vays karaydee-ay munDhay saho raato avraahaa. In spite of all the decorations which you have made, O soul-bride, your Husband Lord is enjoying someone else.
RECORD	para 25084	nw mnIAwru n cUVIAw nw sy vMguVIAwhw ] (558-1, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) naa manee-aar na choorhee-aa naa say vangoorhee-aahaa. You don't have the bracelets of gold, nor the good crystal jewelry; you haven't dealt with the true jeweller.
DEFINE	para 25085	jo sh kMiT n lgIAw jlnu is bwhVIAwhw ] (558-1, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) jo sah kanth na lagee-aa jalan se bahrhee-aahaa. Those arms, which do not embrace the neck of the Husband Lord, burn in anguish.
RECORD	para 25086	siB shIAw shu rwvix geIAw hau dwDI kY dir jwvw ] (558-2, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) sabh sahee-aa saho raavan ga-ee-aa ha-o daaDhee kai dar jaavaa. All my companions have gone to enjoy their Husband Lord; which door should I, the wretched one, go to?
ALLOW	para 25087	AMmwlI hau KrI sucjI qY sh eyik n Bwvw ] (558-2, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) ammaalee ha-o kharee suchjee tai sah ayk na bhaavaa. O friend, I may look very attractive, but I am not pleasing to my Husband Lord at all.
RECORD	para 25088	mwiT guMdweˆØI ptIAw BrIAY mwg sMDUry ] (558-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) maath gu Ndaa-eeN patee-aa bharee-ai maag sanDhooray. I have woven my hair into lovely braids, and saturated their partings with vermillion;
WHEN	para 25089	AgY geI n mMnIAw mrau ivsUir ivsUry ] (558-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) agai ga-ee na mannee-aa mara-o visoor visooray. but when I go before Him, I am not accepted, and I die, suffering in anguish.
RECORD	para 25090	mY rovMdI sBu jgu runw ruMnVy vxhu pMKyrU ] (558-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) mai rovandee sabh jag runaa runnrhay vanhu pankhayroo. I weep; the whole world weeps; even the birds of the forest weep with me.
RECORD	para 25091	ieku n runw myry qn kw ibrhw ijin hau iprhu ivCoVI ] (558-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) ik na runaa mayray tan kaa birhaa jin ha-o pirahu vichhorhee. The only thing which doesn't weep is my body's sense of separateness, which has separated me from my Lord.
RECORD	para 25092	supnY AwieAw BI gieAw mY jlu BirAw roie ] (558-5, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) supnai aa-i-aa bhee ga-i-aa mai jal bhari-aa ro-ay. In a dream, He came, and went away again; I cried so many tears.
RECORD	para 25093	Awie n skw quJ kin ipAwry Byij n skw koie ] (558-5, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) aa-ay na sakaa tujh kan pi-aaray bhayj na sakaa ko-ay. I can't come to You, O my Beloved, and I can't send anyone to You.
UPHOLD	para 25094	Awau sBwgI nIdVIey mqu shu dyKw soie ] (558-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) aa-o sabhaagee need-rhee-ay mat saho daykhaa so-ay. Come to me, O blessed sleep - perhaps I will see my Husband Lord again.
REQUIRE	para 25095	qY swihb kI bwq ij AwKY khu nwnk ikAw dIjY ] (558-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) tai saahib kee baat je aakhai kaho naanak ki-aa deejai. One who brings me a message from my Lord and Master - says Nanak, what shall I give to Him?
REQUIRE	para 25096	sIsu vFy kir bYsxu dIjY ivxu isr syv krIjY ] (558-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) sees vadhay kar baisan deejai vin sir sayv kareejai. Cutting off my head, I give it to Him to sit upon; without my head, I shall still serve Him.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 2 v1	ikau n mrIjY jIAVw n dIjY jw shu BieAw ivfwxw ]1]3] (558-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) ki-o na mareejai jee-arhaa na deejai jaa saho bha-i-aa vidaanaa. ||1||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 1 Gru 2 v1	3|| Why haven't I died? Why hasn't my life just ended? My Husband Lord has become a stranger to me. ||1||3||
