DEFINE	para 26267	guir rwKy sy aubry mnmuKw dyie sjwie ] (588-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gur raakhay say ubray manmukhaa day-ay sajaa-ay. Those who are protected by the Guru are saved, while the self-willed manmukhs receive their punishment.
RECORD	para 26268	jmkwlY vis jgu bWiDAw iqs dw PrU n koie ] (588-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jamkaalai vas jag baa NDhi-aa tis daa faroo na ko-ay. The world is under the control, and in the bondage of the Messenger of Death; no one can hold him back.
REQUIRE	para 26269	ijin jmu kIqw so syvIAY gurmuiK duKu n hoie ] (588-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jin jam keetaa so sayvee-ai gurmukh dukh na ho-ay. So serve the One who created Death; as Gurmukh, no pain shall touch you.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	nwnk gurmuiK jmu syvw kry ijn min scw hoie ]1] (588-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh jam sayvaa karay jin man sachaa ho-ay. ||1||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, Death serves the Gurmukhs; the True Lord abides in their minds. ||1||
RECORD	para 26271	mÚ 3 ] (588-15) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
