RECORD	para 26285	gux inDwnu min pwieAw eyko scw soie ] (589-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gun niDhaan man paa-i-aa ayko sachaa so-ay. They obtain the treasure of virtue, the One True Lord, within their minds.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	nwnk gurmuiK imil rhy iPir ivCoVw kdy n hoie ]1] (589-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh mil rahay fir vichhorhaa kaday na ho-ay. ||1||
REQUIRE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs remain united with the Lord; they shall never be separated again. ||1||
RECORD	para 26287	mÚ 3 ] (589-4) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26288	siqgur kI syv n kInIAw ikAw Ehu kry vIcwru ] (589-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) satgur kee sayv na keenee-aa ki-aa oh karay veechaar. He does not serve the True Guru; how can he reflect upon the Lord?
RECORD	para 26289	sbdY swr n jwxeI ibKu BUlw gwvwru ] (589-5, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) sabdai saar na jaan-ee bikh bhoolaa gaavaar. He does not appreciate the value of the Shabad; the fool wanders in corruption and sin.
RECORD	para 26290	AigAwnI AMDu bhu krm kmwvY dUjY Bwie ipAwru ] (589-5, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) agi-aanee anDh baho karam kamaavai doojai bhaa-ay pi-aar. The blind and ignorant perform all sorts of ritualistic actions; they are in love with duality.
RECORD	para 26291	Axhodw Awpu gxwiedy jmu mwir kry iqn KuAwru ] (589-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) anhodaa aap ganaa-iday jam maar karay tin khu-aar. Those who take unjustified pride in themselves, are punished and humiliated by the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnk iks no AwKIAY jw Awpy bKsxhwru ]2] (589-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak kis no aakhee-ai jaa aapay bakhsanhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, who else is there to ask? The Lord Himself is the Forgiver. ||2||
RECORD	para 26293	pauVI ] (589-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 26294	qU krqw sBu ikCu jwxdw siB jIA qumwry ] (589-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) too kartaa sabh kichh jaandaa sabh jee-a tumaaray. You, O Creator, know all things; all beings belong to You.
DEFINE	para 26295	ijsu qU BwvY iqsu qU myil lYih ikAw jMq ivcwry ] (589-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jis too bhaavai tis too mayl laihi ki-aa jant vichaaray. Those who are pleasing to You, You unite with Yourself; what can the poor creatures do?
DEFINE	para 26296	qU krx kwrx smrQu hY scu isrjxhwry ] (589-8, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) too karan kaaran samrath hai sach sirjanhaaray. You are all-powerful, the Cause of causes, the True Creator Lord.
RECORD	para 26297	ijsu qU mylih ipAwirAw so quDu imlY gurmuiK vIcwry ] (589-8, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jis too mayleh pi-aari-aa so tuDh milai gurmukh veechaaray. Only those unite with you, Beloved Lord, whom you approve and who meditate on Guru's Word.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v8	hau bilhwrI siqgur Awpxy ijin myrw hir AlKu lKwry ]8] (589-9, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) ha-o balihaaree satgur aapnay jin mayraa har alakh lakhaaray. ||8||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v8	I am a sacrifice to my True Guru, who has allowed me to see my unseen Lord. ||8||
RECORD	para 26299	slok mÚ 3 ] (589-10) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 26300	rqnw pwrKu jo hovY su rqnw kry vIcwru ] (589-10, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) ratnaa paarakh jo hovai so ratnaa karay veechaar. He is the Assayer of jewels; He contemplates the jewel.
DEFINE	para 26301	rqnw swr n jwxeI AigAwnI AMDu AMDwru ] (589-10, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) ratnaa saar na jaan-ee agi-aanee anDh anDhaar. He is ignorant and totally blind - he does not appreciate the value of the jewel.
DEFINE	para 26302	rqnu gurU kw sbdu hY bUJY bUJxhwru ] (589-11, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) ratan guroo kaa sabad hai boojhai boojhanhaar. The Jewel is the Word of the Guru's Shabad; the Knower alone knows it.
DEFINE	para 26303	mUrK Awpu gxwiedy mir jMmih hoie KuAwru ] (589-11, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) moorakh aap ganaa-iday mar jameh ho-ay khu-aar. The fools take pride in themselves, and are ruined in birth and death.
RECORD	para 26304	nwnk rqnw so lhY ijsu gurmuiK lgY ipAwru ] (589-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak ratnaa so lahai jis gurmukh lagai pi-aar. O Nanak, he alone obtains the jewel, who, as Gurmukh, enshrines love for it.
RECORD	para 26305	sdw sdw nwmu aucrY hir nwmo inq ibauhwru ] (589-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa naam uchrai har naamo nit bi-uhaar. Chanting the Naam, the Name of the Lord, forever and ever, make the Name of the Lord your daily occupation.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	ik®pw kry jy AwpxI qw hir rKw aur Dwir ]1] (589-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) kirpaa karay jay aapnee taa har rakhaa ur Dhaar. ||1||
WHEN	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	If the Lord shows His Mercy, then I keep Him enshrined within my heart. ||1||
RECORD	para 26307	mÚ 3 ] (589-13) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26308	siqgur kI syv n kInIAw hir nwim n lgo ipAwru ] (589-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) satgur kee sayv na keenee-aa har naam na lago pi-aar. They do not serve the True Guru, and they do not embrace love for the Lord's Name.
DEFINE	para 26309	mq qum jwxhu Eie jIvdy Eie Awip mwry krqwir ] (589-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) mat tum jaanhu o-ay jeevday o-ay aap maaray kartaar. Do not even think that they are alive - the Creator Lord Himself has killed them.
DEFINE	para 26310	haumY vfw rogu hY Bwie dUjY krm kmwie ] (589-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) ha-umai vadaa rog hai bhaa-ay doojai karam kamaa-ay. Egotism is such a terrible disease; in the love of duality, they do their deeds.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnk mnmuiK jIvidAw muey hir ivsirAw duKu pwie ]2] (589-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak manmukh jeevdi-aa mu-ay har visri-aa dukh paa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, the self-willed manmukhs are in a living death; forgetting the Lord, they suffer in pain. ||2||
RECORD	para 26312	pauVI ] (589-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 26313	ijsu AMqru ihrdw suDu hY iqsu jn kau siB nmskwrI ] (589-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jis antar hirdaa suDh hai tis jan ka-o sabh namaskaaree. Let all bow in reverence, to that humble being whose heart is pure within.
RECORD	para 26314	ijsu AMdir nwmu inDwnu hY iqsu jn kau hau bilhwrI ] (589-16, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jis andar naam niDhaan hai tis jan ka-o ha-o balihaaree. I am a sacrifice to that humble being whose mind is filled with the treasure of the Naam.
RECORD	para 26315	ijsu AMdir buiD ibbyku hY hir nwmu murwrI ] (589-17, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jis andar buDh bibayk hai har naam muraaree. He has a discriminating intellect; he meditates on the Name of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 26316	so siqguru sBnw kw imqu hY sB iqsih ipAwrI ] (589-17, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) so satgur sabhnaa kaa mit hai sabh tiseh pi-aaree. That True Guru is a friend to all; everyone is dear to Him.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v9	sBu Awqm rwmu pswirAw gur buiD bIcwrI ]9] (589-18, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) sabh aatam raam pasaari-aa gur buDh beechaaree. ||9||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v9	The Lord, the Supreme Soul, is pervading everywhere; reflect upon the wisdom of the Guru's Teachings. ||9||
RECORD	para 26318	slok mÚ 3 ] (589-18) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26319	ibnu siqgur syvy jIA ky bMDnw ivic haumY krm kmwih ] (589-18, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay jee-a kay banDhnaa vich ha-umai karam kamaahi. Without serving the True Guru, the soul is in the bondage of deeds done in ego.
RECORD	para 26320	ibnu siqgur syvy Taur n pwvhI mir jMmih Awvih jwih ] (589-19, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay tha-ur na paavhee mar jameh aavahi jaahi. Without serving the True Guru, one finds no place of rest; he dies, and is reincarnated, and continues coming and going.
RECORD	para 26321	ibnu siqgur syvy iPkw bolxw nwmu n vsY mn mwih ] (589-19, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay fikaa bolnaa naam na vasai man maahi. Without serving the True Guru, one's speech is vapid and insipid; the Naam, the Name of the Lord, does not abide in his mind.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	nwnk ibnu siqgur syvy jm puir bDy mwrIAin muih kwlY auiT jwih ]1] (590-1, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak bin satgur sayvay jam pur baDhay maaree-an muhi kaalai uth jaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, without serving the True Guru, they are bound and beaten in the City of Death; they arise and depart with blackened faces. ||1||
RECORD	para 26324	mhlw 1 ] (590-2) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 26325	jwlau AYsI rIiq ijqu mY ipAwrw vIsrY ] (590-2, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) jaala-o aisee reet jit mai pi-aaraa veesrai. Burn away those rituals which lead you to forget the Beloved Lord.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnk sweI BlI prIiq ijqu swihb syqI piq rhY ]2] (590-2, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) naanak saa-ee bhalee pareet jit saahib saytee pat rahai. ||2||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, sublime is that love, which preserves my honor with my Lord Master. ||2||
RECORD	para 26327	pauVI ] (590-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 26328	hir ieko dwqw syvIAY hir ieku iDAweIAY ] (590-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) har iko daataa sayvee-ai har ik Dhi-aa-ee-ai. Serve the One Lord, the Great Giver; meditate on the One Lord.
REQUIRE	para 26329	hir ieko dwqw mMgIAY mn icMidAw pweIAY ] (590-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) har iko daataa mangee-ai man chindi-aa paa-ee-ai. Beg from the One Lord, the Great Giver, and you shall obtain your heart's desires.
REQUIRE	para 26330	jy dUjy pwshu mMgIAY qw lwj mrweIAY ] (590-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) jay doojay paashu mangee-ai taa laaj maraa-ee-ai. But if you beg from another, then you shall be shamed and destroyed.
RECORD	para 26331	ijin syivAw iqin Plu pwieAw iqsu jn kI sB BuK gvweIAY ] (590-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) jin sayvi-aa tin fal paa-i-aa tis jan kee sabh bhukh gavaa-ee-ai. One who serves the Lord obtains the fruits of his rewards; all of his hunger is satisfied.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v10	nwnku iqn ivthu vwirAw ijn Anidnu ihrdY hir nwmu iDAweIAY ]10] (590-5, vfhMsu, mÚ 1) naanak tin vitahu vaari-aa jin an-din hirdai har naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai. ||10||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v10	Nanak is a sacrifice to those, who night and day, meditate within their hearts on the Name of the Lord. ||10||
RECORD	para 26333	sloku mÚ 3 ] (590-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26334	Bgq jnw kMau Awip quTw myrw ipAwrw Awpy lieAnu jn lwie ] (590-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) bhagat janaa ka N-u aap tuthaa mayraa pi-aaraa aapay la-i-an jan laa-ay. He Himself is pleased with His humble devotees; my Beloved Lord attaches them to Himself.
RECORD	para 26335	pwiqswhI Bgq jnw kau idqIAnu isir Cqu scw hir bxwie ] (590-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) paatisaahee bhagat janaa ka-o ditee-an sir chhat sachaa har banaa-ay. The Lord blesses His humble devotees with royalty; He fashions the true crown upon their heads.
DEFINE	para 26336	sdw suKIey inrmly siqgur kI kwr kmwie ] (590-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) sadaa sukhee-ay nirmalay satgur kee kaar kamaa-ay. They are always at peace, and immaculately pure; they perform service for the True Guru.
RECORD	para 26337	rwjy Eie n AwKIAih iBiV mrih iPir jUnI pwih ] (590-8, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) raajay o-ay na aakhee-ahi bhirh mareh fir joonee paahi. They are not said to be kings, who die in conflict, and then enter again the cycle of reincarnation.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	nwnk ivxu nwvY nkˆØI vFˆØI iPrih soBw mUil n pwih ]1] (590-9, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak vin naavai nakee N vadhee N fireh sobhaa mool na paahi. ||1||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, without the Name of the Lord, they wander about with their noses cut off in disgrace; they get no respect at all. ||1||
RECORD	para 26339	mÚ 3 ] (590-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26340	suix isiKAY swdu n AwieE ijcru gurmuiK sbid n lwgY ] (590-9, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) sun sikhi-ai saad na aa-i-o jichar gurmukh sabad na laagai. Hearing the teachings, he does not appreciate them, as long as he is not Gurmukh, attached to the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 26341	siqguir syivAY nwmu min vsY ivchu BRmu Bau BwgY ] (590-10, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) satgur sayvi-ai naam man vasai vichahu bharam bha-o bhaagai. Serving the True Guru, the Naam comes to abide in the mind, and doubts and fears run away.
RECORD	para 26342	jyhw siqgur no jwxY qyho hovY qw sic nwim ilv lwgY ] (590-10, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jayhaa satgur no jaanai tayho hovai taa sach naam liv laagai. As he knows the True Guru, so he is transformed, and then, he lovingly focuses his consciousness on the Naam.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnk nwim imlY vifAweI hir dir sohin AwgY ]2] (590-11, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak naam milai vadi-aa-ee har dar sohan aagai. ||2||
REQUIRE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, through the Naam, the Name of the Lord, greatness is obtained; he shall be resplendent in the Court of the Lord hereafter. ||2||
RECORD	para 26344	pauVI ] (590-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 26345	gurisKW min hir pRIiq hY guru pUjx Awvih ] (590-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gursikhaa N man har pareet hai gur poojan aavahi. The minds of the Gursikhs are filled with the love of the Lord; they come and worship the Guru.
RECORD	para 26346	hir nwmu vxMjih rMg isau lwhw hir nwmu lY jwvih ] (590-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) har naam vana Njahi rang si-o laahaa har naam lai jaaveh. They trade lovingly in the Lord's Name, and depart after earning the profit of the Lord's Name.
DEFINE	para 26347	gurisKw ky muK aujly hir drgh Bwvih ] (590-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gursikhaa kay mukh ujlay har dargeh bhaaveh. The faces of the Gursikhs are radiant; in the Court of the Lord, they are approved.
RECORD	para 26348	guru siqguru bohlu hir nwm kw vfBwgI isK gux sWJ krwvih ] (590-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gur satgur bohal har naam kaa vadbhaagee sikh gun saa Njh karaaveh. The Guru, the True Guru, is the treasure of the Lord's Name; how very fortunate are the Sikhs who share in this treasure of virtue.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v11	iqnw gurisKw kMau hau vwirAw jo bhidAw auTidAw hir nwmu iDAwvih ]11] (590-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) tinaa gursikhaa ka N-u ha-o vaari-aa jo bahdi-aa uth-di-aa har naam Dhi-aavahi. ||11||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v11	I am a sacrifice to those Gursikhs who, sitting and standing, meditate on the Lord's Name. ||11||
RECORD	para 26350	slok mÚ 3 ] (590-15) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 26351	nwnk nwmu inDwnu hY gurmuiK pwieAw jwie ] (590-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak naam niDhaan hai gurmukh paa-i-aa jaa-ay. O Nanak, the Naam, the Name of the Lord, is the treasure, which the Gurmukhs obtain.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	mnmuK Gir hodI vQu n jwxnI AMDy Bauik muey ibllwie ]1] (590-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) manmukh ghar hodee vath na jaannee anDhay bha-uk mu-ay billaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	The self-willed manmukhs are blind; they do not realize that it is within their own home. They die barking and crying. ||1||
RECORD	para 26353	mÚ 3 ] (590-16) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 26354	kMcn kwieAw inrmlI jo sic nwim sic lwgI ] (590-16, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) kanchan kaa-i-aa nirmalee jo sach naam sach laagee. That body is golden and immaculate, which is attached to the True Name of the True Lord.
RECORD	para 26355	inrml joiq inrMjnu pwieAw gurmuiK BRmu Bau BwgI ] (590-17, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) nirmal jot niranjan paa-i-aa gurmukh bharam bha-o bhaagee. The Gurmukh obtains the Pure Light of the Luminous Lord, and his doubts and fears run away.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnk gurmuiK sdw suKu pwvih Anidnu hir bYrwgI ]2] (590-17, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh sadaa sukh paavahi an-din har bairaagee. ||2||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs find lasting peace; night and day, they remain detached, while in the Love of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 26357	pauVI ] (590-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
UPHOLD	para 26358	sy gurisK Dnu DMnu hY ijnI gur aupdysu suixAw hir kMnI ] (590-18, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) say gursikh Dhan Dhan hai jinee gur updays suni-aa har kannee. Blessed, blessed are those Gursikhs, who, with their ears, listen to the Guru's Teachings about the Lord.
RECORD	para 26359	guir siqguir nwmu idRVwieAw iqin hMaumY duibDw BMnI ] (590-19, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gur satgur naam drirh-aa-i-aa tin ha N-umai dubiDhaa bhannee. The Guru, the True Guru, implants the Naam within them, and their egotism and duality are silenced.
RECORD	para 26360	ibnu hir nwvY ko imqRü nwhI vIcwir ifTw hir jMnI ] (590-19, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) bin har naavai ko mitar naahee veechaar dithaa har jannee. There is no friend, other than the Name of the Lord; the Lord's humble servants reflect upon this and see.
RECORD	para 26362	ijnw gurisKw kau hir sMqustu hY iqnI siqgur kI gl mMnI ] (591-1, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jinaa gursikhaa ka-o har santusat hai tinee satgur kee gal mannee. Those Gursikhs, with whom the Lord is pleased, accept the Word of the True Guru.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v12	jo gurmuiK nwmu iDAwiedy iqnI cVI cvgix vMnI ]12] (591-1, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jo gurmukh naam Dhi-aa-iday tinee charhee chavgan vannee. ||12||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v12	Those Gurmukhs who meditate on the Naam are imbued with the four-fold color of the Lord's Love. ||12||
RECORD	para 26364	slok mÚ 3 ] (591-2) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26365	mnmuKu kwieru krUpu hY ibnu nwvY nku nwih ] (591-2, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) manmukh kaa-ir karoop hai bin naavai nak naahi. The self-willed manmukh is cowardly and ugly; lacking the Name of the Lord, his nose is cut off in disgrace.
DEFINE	para 26366	Anidnu DMDY ivAwipAw supnY BI suKu nwih ] (591-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) an-din DhanDhai vi-aapi-aa supnai bhee sukh naahi. Night and day, he is engrossed in worldly affairs, and even in his dreams, he finds no peace.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	nwnk gurmuiK hovih qw aubrih nwih q bDy duK shwih ]1] (591-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh hoveh taa ubrahi naahi ta baDhay dukh sahaahi. ||1||
REQUIRE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, if he becomes Gurmukh, then he shall be saved; otherwise, he is held in bondage, and suffers in pain. ||1||
RECORD	para 26368	mÚ 3 ] (591-4) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26369	gurmuiK sdw dir sohxy gur kw sbdu kmwih ] (591-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gurmukh sadaa dar sohnay gur kaa sabad kamaahi. The Gurmukhs always look beautiful in the Court of the Lord; they practice the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
DEFINE	para 26370	AMqir sWiq sdw suKu dir scY soBw pwih ] (591-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) antar saaNt sadaa sukh dar sachai sobhaa paahi. There is a lasting peace and happiness deep within them; at the Court of the True Lord, they receive honor.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnk gurmuiK hir nwmu pwieAw shjy sic smwih ]2] (591-5, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh har naam paa-i-aa sehjay sach samaahi. ||2||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are blessed with the Name of the Lord; they merge imperceptibly into the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 26372	pauVI ] (591-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 26373	gurmuiK pRihlwid jip hir giq pweI ] (591-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gurmukh par-hilaad jap har gat paa-ee. As Gurmukh, Prahlaad meditated on the Lord, and was saved.
RECORD	para 26374	gurmuiK jnik hir nwim ilv lweI ] (591-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gurmukh janak har naam liv laa-ee. As Gurmukh, Janak lovingly centered his consciousness on the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 26375	gurmuiK bissit hir aupdysu suxweI ] (591-6, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gurmukh basist har updays sunaa-ee. As Gurmukh, Vashisht taught the Teachings of the Lord.
RECORD	para 26376	ibnu gur hir nwmu n iknY pwieAw myry BweI ] (591-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) bin gur har naam na kinai paa-i-aa mayray bhaa-ee. Without the Guru, no one has found the Lord's Name, O my Siblings of Destiny.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v13	gurmuiK hir Bgiq hir Awip lhweI ]13] (591-7, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) gurmukh har bhagat har aap lahaa-ee. ||13||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v13	The Lord blesses the Gurmukh with devotion. ||13||
RECORD	para 26378	sloku mÚ 3 ] (591-8) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26379	siqgur kI prqIiq n AweIAw sbid n lwgo Bwau ] (591-8, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) satgur kee parteet na aa-ee-aa sabad na laago bhaa-o. One who has no faith in the True Guru, and who does not love the Word of the Shabad,
REQUIRE	para 26380	Es no suKu n aupjY BwvY sau gyVw Awvau jwau ] (591-9, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) os no sukh na upjai bhaavai sa-o gayrhaa aava-o jaa-o. shall find no peace, even though he may come and go hundreds of times.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	nwnk gurmuiK shij imlY scy isau ilv lwau ]1] (591-9, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh sahj milai sachay si-o liv laa-o. ||1||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukh meets the True Lord with natural ease; he is in love with the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 26382	mÚ 3 ] (591-10) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26383	ey mn AYsw siqguru Koij lhu ijqu syivAY jnm mrx duKu jwie ] (591-10, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) ay man aisaa satgur khoj lahu jit sayvi-ai janam maran dukh jaa-ay. O mind, search for such a True Guru, by serving whom the pains of birth and death are dispelled.
REQUIRE	para 26384	shsw mUil n hoveI haumY sbid jlwie ] (591-10, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) sahsaa mool na hova-ee ha-umai sabad jalaa-ay. Doubt shall never afflict you, and your ego shall be burnt away through the Word of the Shabad.
REQUIRE	para 26385	kUVY kI pwil ivchu inklY scu vsY min Awie ] (591-11, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) koorhai kee paal vichahu niklai sach vasai man aa-ay. The veil of falsehood shall be torn down from within you, and Truth shall come to dwell in the mind.
REQUIRE	para 26386	AMqir sWiq min suKu hoie sc sMjim kwr kmwie ] (591-11, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) antar saaNt man sukh ho-ay sach sanjam kaar kamaa-ay. Peace and happiness shall fill your mind deep within, if you act according to truth and self-discipline.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnk pUrY krim siqguru imlY hir jIau ikrpw kry rjwie ]2] (591-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak poorai karam satgur milai har jee-o kirpaa karay rajaa-ay. ||2||
REQUIRE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, by perfect good karma, you shall meet the True Guru, and then the Dear Lord, by His Sweet Will, shall bless you with His Mercy. ||2||
RECORD	para 26388	pauVI ] (591-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 26389	ijs kY Gir dIbwnu hir hovY iqs kI muTI ivic jgqu sBu AwieAw ] (591-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jis kai ghar deebaan har hovai tis kee muthee vich jagat sabh aa-i-aa. The whole world comes under the control of one whose home is filled with the Lord, the King.
RECORD	para 26390	iqs kau qlkI iksY dI nwhI hir dIbwin siB Awix pYrI pwieAw ] (591-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) tis ka-o talkee kisai dee naahee har deebaan sabh aan pairee paa-i-aa. He is subject to no one else's rule, and the Lord, the King, causes everyone to fall at his feet.
ALLOW	para 26391	mwxsw ikAhu dIbwxhu koeI nis Bij inklY hir dIbwxhu koeI ikQY jwieAw ] (591-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) maansaa ki-ahu deebaanahu ko-ee nas bhaj niklai har deebaanahu ko-ee kithai jaa-i- aa. One may run away from the courts of other men, but where can one go to escape the Lord's Kingdom?
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v14	hir nwvY kI vifAweI krim prwpiq hovY gurmuiK ivrlY iknY iDAwieAw ]14] (591-16, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) har naavai kee vadi-aa-ee karam paraapat hovai gurmukh virlai kinai Dhi-aa-i-aa. ||14||
DEFINE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v14	The glorious greatness of the Lord's Name is obtained only by His Grace; how few are the Gurmukhs who meditate on Him. ||14||
RECORD	para 26394	sloku mÚ 3 ] (591-17) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26395	ibnu siqgur syvy jgqu muAw ibrQw jnmu gvwie ] (591-17, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay jagat mu-aa birthaa janam gavaa-ay. Without serving the True Guru, the people of the world are dead; they waste their lives away in vain.
RECORD	para 26396	dUjY Bwie Aiq duKu lgw mir jMmY AwvY jwie ] (591-17, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay at dukh lagaa mar jammai aavai jaa-ay. In love with duality, they suffer terrible pain; they die, and are reincarnated, and continue coming and going.
DEFINE	para 26397	ivstw AMdir vwsu hY iPir iPir jUnI pwie ] (591-18, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) vistaa andar vaas hai fir fir joonee paa-ay. They live in manure, and are reincarnated again and again.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	nwnk ibnu nwvY jmu mwrsI AMiq gieAw pCuqwie ]1] (591-18, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak bin naavai jam maarsee ant ga-i-aa pachhutaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, without the Name, the Messenger of Death punishes them; in the end, they depart regretting and repenting. ||1||
RECORD	para 26399	mÚ 3 ] (591-19) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 26400	iesu jg mih purKu eyku hY hor sglI nwir sbweI ] (591-19, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) is jag meh purakh ayk hai hor saglee naar sabaa-ee. In this world, there is one Husband Lord; all other beings are His brides.
DEFINE	para 26402	siB Gt BogvY Ailpqu rhY AlKu n lKxw jweI ] (592-1, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) sabh ghat bhogvai alipat rahai alakh na lakh-naa jaa-ee. He enjoys the hearts of all, and yet He remains detached; He is unseen; He cannot be described.
RECORD	para 26403	pUrY guir vyKwilAw sbdy soJI pweI ] (592-1, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) poorai gur vaykhaali-aa sabday sojhee paa-ee. The Perfect Guru reveals Him, and through the Word of His Shabad, we come to understand Him.
RECORD	para 26404	purKY syvih sy purK hovih ijnI haumY sbid jlweI ] (592-2, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) purkhai sayveh say purakh hoveh jinee ha-umai sabad jalaa-ee. Those who serve their Husband Lord, become like Him; their egos are burnt away by His Shabad.
RECORD	para 26405	iqs kw srIku ko nhI nw ko kMtku vYrweI ] (592-2, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) tis kaa sareek ko nahee naa ko kantak vairaa-ee. He has no rival, no attacker, no enemy.
DEFINE	para 26406	inhcl rwju hY sdw iqsu kyrw nw AwvY nw jweI ] (592-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) nihchal raaj hai sadaa tis kayraa naa aavai naa jaa-ee. His rule is unchanging and eternal; He does not come or go.
RECORD	para 26407	Anidnu syvku syvw kry hir scy ky gux gweI ] (592-3, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) an-din sayvak sayvaa karay har sachay kay gun gaa-ee. Night and day, His servant serves Him, singing the Glorious Praises of the True Lord.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnku vyiK ivgisAw hir scy kI vifAweI ]2] (592-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak vaykh vigsi-aa har sachay kee vadi-aa-ee. ||2||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	Beholding the Glorious Greatness of the True Lord, Nanak blossoms forth. ||2||
RECORD	para 26409	pauVI ] (592-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 26410	ijn kY hir nwmu visAw sd ihrdY hir nwmo iqn kMau rKxhwrw ] (592-4, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jin kai har naam vasi-aa sad hirdai har naamo tin ka N-u rakhanhaaraa. Those whose hearts are forever filled with the Name of the Lord, have the Name of the Lord as their Protector.
RECORD	para 26411	hir nwmu ipqw hir nwmo mwqw hir nwmu sKweI imqRü hmwrw ] (592-5, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) har naam pitaa har naamo maataa har naam sakhaa-ee mitar hamaaraa. The Lord's Name is my father, the Lord's Name is my mother; the Lord's Name is my helper and friend.
