DEFINE	para 26500	ifTY mukiq n hoveI ijcru sbid n kry vIcwru ] (594-11, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) dithai mukat na hova-ee jichar sabad na karay veechaar. One is not liberated by merely seeing Him, unless one contemplates the Word of His Shabad.
DEFINE	para 26501	haumY mYlu n cukeI nwim n lgY ipAwru ] (594-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) ha-umai mail na chuk-ee naam na lagai pi-aar. The filth of ego is not removed, and he does not enshrine love for the Naam.
RECORD	para 26502	ieik Awpy bKis imlwieAnu duibDw qij ivkwr ] (594-12, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) ik aapay bakhas milaa-i-an dubiDhaa taj vikaar. The Lord forgives some, and unites them with Himself; they forsake their duality and sinful ways.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	nwnk ieik drsnu dyiK mir imly siqgur hyiq ipAwir ]1] (594-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak ik darsan daykh mar milay satgur hayt pi-aar. ||1||
UPHOLD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, some behold the Blessed Vision of the True Guru's Darshan, with love and affection; conquering their ego, they meet with the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 26504	mÚ 3 ] (594-13) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 26505	siqgurU n syivE mUrK AMD gvwir ] (594-13, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) satguroo na sayvi-o moorakh anDh gavaar. The foolish, blind clown does not serve the True Guru.
RECORD	para 26506	dUjY Bwie bhuqu duKu lwgw jlqw kry pukwr ] (594-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay bahut dukh laagaa jaltaa karay pukaar. In love with duality, he endures terrible suffering, and burning, he cries out in pain.
RECORD	para 26507	ijn kwrix gurU ivswirAw sy n aupkry AMqI vwr ] (594-14, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) jin kaaran guroo visaari-aa say na upkaray antee vaar. He forgets the Guru, for the sake of mere objects, but they will not come to his rescue in the end.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	nwnk gurmqI suKu pwieAw bKsy bKsxhwr ]2] (594-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmatee sukh paa-i-aa bakhsay bakhsanhaar. ||2||
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v2	Through the Guru's Instructions, Nanak has found peace; the Forgiving Lord has forgiven him. ||2||
RECORD	para 26509	pauVI ] (594-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
WHEN	para 26510	qU Awpy Awip Awip sBu krqw koeI dUjw hoie su Avro khIAY ] (594-15, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) too aapay aap aap sabh kartaa ko-ee doojaa ho-ay so avro kahee-ai. You Yourself, all by Yourself, are the Creator of all. If there were any other, then I would speak of another.
RECORD	para 26511	hir Awpy bolY Awip bulwvY hir Awpy jil Qil riv rhIAY ] (594-16, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) har aapay bolai aap bulaavai har aapay jal thal rav rahee-ai. The Lord Himself speaks, and causes us to speak; He Himself is pervading the water and the land.
RECORD	para 26512	hir Awpy mwrY hir Awpy CofY mn hir srxI piV rhIAY ] (594-17, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) har aapay maarai har aapay chhodai man har sarnee parh rahee-ai. The Lord Himself destroys, and the Lord Himself saves. O mind, seek and remain in the Lord's Sanctuary.
RECORD	para 26513	hir ibnu koeI mwir jIvwil n skY mn hoie inicMd inslu hoie rhIAY ] (594-17, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) har bin ko-ee maar jeevaal na sakai man ho-ay nichind nisal ho-ay rahee-ai. Other than the Lord, no one can kill or rejuvenate. O mind, do not be anxious - remain fearless.
RECORD	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v21	auTidAw bhidAw suiqAw sdw sdw hir nwmu iDAweIAY jn nwnk gurmuiK hir lhIAY ]21]1] suDu (594-18, vfhMsu, mÚ 3) uth-di-aa bahdi-aa suti-aa sadaa sadaa har naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai jan naanak gurmukh har lahee-ai. ||21||
REQUIRE	vfhMsu mhlw 3 v21	1|| suDhu While standing, sitting, and sleeping, forever and ever, meditate on the Lord's Name; O servant Nanak, as Gurmukh, you shall attain the Lord. ||21||1||Sudh||
RECORD	para 26516	<> siq nwmu krqw purKu inrBau inrvYru Akwl mUriq AjUnI sYBM gur pRswid ] (595-1) ik-oNkaar sat naam kartaa purakh nirbha-o nirvair akaal moorat ajoonee saibhaN gur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. Truth Is The Name. Creative Being Personified. No Fear. No Hatred. Image Of The Undying. Beyond Birth. Self-Existent. By Guru's Grace:
