RECORD	soriT mhlw 1 v3	bjr kpwt mukqy gurmqI inrBY qwVI lweI ]3] (597-8, soriT, mÚ 1) bajar kapaat muktay gurmatee nirbhai taarhee laa-ee. ||3||
DEFINE	soriT mhlw 1 v3	The heavy doors are opened by Guru's Instructions; one becomes fearless, in the trance of deep meditation. ||3||
RECORD	para 26599	jMq aupwie kwlu isir jMqw vsgiq jugiq sbweI ] (597-8, soriT, mÚ 1) jant upaa-ay kaal sir jantaa vasgat jugat sabaa-ee. The Lord created all beings, and placed death over the heads of all; all the world is under His Power.
RECORD	soriT mhlw 1 v4	siqguru syiv pdwrQu pwvih CUtih sbdu kmweI ]4] (597-9, soriT, mÚ 1) satgur sayv padaarath paavahi chhooteh sabad kamaa-ee. ||4||
DEFINE	soriT mhlw 1 v4	Serving the True Guru, the treasure is obtained; living the Word of the Shabad, one is emancipated. ||4||
DEFINE	para 26601	sUcY BwfY swcu smwvY ivrly sUcwcwrI ] (597-9, soriT, mÚ 1) soochai bhaadai saach samaavai virlay soochaachaaree. In the pure vessel, the True Name is contained; how few are those who practice true conduct.
