WHEN	para 26642	Awvq kau hrK jwq kau rovih iehu duKu suKu nwly lwgw ] (598-13, soriT, mÚ 1) aavat ka-o harakh jaat ka-o roveh ih dukh sukh naalay laagaa. When things come, he is pleased, but when they go, he weeps and wails; this pain and pleasure remains attached to him.
RECORD	soriT mhlw 1 pMcpdy v2	Awpy duK suK Boig BogwvY gurmuiK so Anrwgw ]2] (598-13, soriT, mÚ 1) aapay dukh sukh bhog bhogaavai gurmukh so anraagaa. ||2||
RECORD	soriT mhlw 1 pMcpdy v2	The Lord Himself causes him to enjoy pleasure and endure pain; the Gurmukh, however, remains unaffected. ||2||
