RECORD	soriT mhlw 1 pMcpdy v4	jy qU dyih q hir rsu gweI mnu iqRpqY hir ilv lwgw ]4] (598-16, soriT, mÚ 1) jay too deh ta har ras gaa-ee man tariptai har liv laagaa. ||4||
DEFINE	soriT mhlw 1 pMcpdy v4	If You so bless us, Lord, then we sing Your Praises; the mind is satisfied and fulfilled, lovingly attached to the Lord. ||4||
RECORD	para 26648	swDsMgiq mih hir rsu pweIAY guir imilAY jm Bau Bwgw ] (598-16, soriT, mÚ 1) saaDhsangat meh har ras paa-ee-ai gur mili-ai jam bha-o bhaagaa. In the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, the subtle essence of the Lord is obtained; meeting the Guru, the fear of death departs.
RECORD	soriT mhlw 1 pMcpdy v5	nwnk rwm nwmu jip gurmuiK hir pwey msqik Bwgw ]5]10] (598-17, soriT, mÚ 1) naanak raam naam jap gurmukh har paa-ay mastak bhaagaa. ||5||
REQUIRE	soriT mhlw 1 pMcpdy v5	10|| O Nanak, chant the Name of the Lord, as Gurmukh; you shall obtain the Lord, and realize your pre-ordained destiny. ||5||10||
