RECORD	soriT mhlw 1 v1	Awip AlyKu kudriq kir dyKY hukim clwey soeI jIau ]1] (598-18, soriT, mÚ 1) aap alaykh kudrat kar daykhai hukam chalaa-ay so-ee jee-o. ||1||
DEFINE	soriT mhlw 1 v1	Only He Himself is beyond destiny; creating the creation by His creative power, He beholds it, and causes His Command to be followed. ||1||
RECORD	para 26653	mn ry rwm jphu suKu hoeI ] (598-19, soriT, mÚ 1) man ray raam japahu sukh ho-ee. O mind, chant the Name of the Lord, and be at peace.
RECORD	para 26654	Aihinis gur ky crn sryvhu hir dwqw Bugqw soeI ] rhwau ] (598-19, soriT, mÚ 1) ahinis gur kay charan sarayvhu har daataa bhugtaa so-ee. rahaa-o. Day and night, serve at the Guru's feet; the Lord is the Giver, and the Enjoyer. ||Pause||
DEFINE	para 26656	jo AMqir so bwhir dyKhu Avru n dUjw koeI jIau ] (599-1, soriT, mÚ 1) jo antar so baahar daykhhu avar na doojaa ko-ee jee-o. He is within - see Him outside as well; there is no one, other than Him.
RECORD	soriT mhlw 1 v2	gurmuiK eyk idRsit kir dyKhu Git Git joiq smoeI jIau ]2] (599-2, soriT, mÚ 1) gurmukh ayk darisat kar daykhhu ghat ghat jot samo-ee jee-o. ||2||
DEFINE	soriT mhlw 1 v2	As Gurmukh, look upon all with the single eye of equality; in each and every heart, the Divine Light is contained. ||2||
