RECORD	soriT mhlw 5 Gru 2 AstpdIAw v6	vfI Awrjw iPir iPir jnmY hir isau sMgu n gihAw ]6] (642-5, soriT, mÚ 5) vadee aarjaa fir fir janmai har si-o sang na gahi-aa. ||6||
DEFINE	soriT mhlw 5 Gru 2 AstpdIAw v6	He lives a long life, but is reincarnated again and again; he has not met with the Lord. ||6||
ALLOW	para 28422	rwj lIlw rwjn kI rcnw kirAw hukmu APwrw ] (642-6, soriT, mÚ 5) raaj leelaa raajan kee rachnaa kari-aa hukam afaaraa. He may enjoy princely pleasures, and regal pomp and ceremony, and issue unchallenged commands.
RECORD	soriT mhlw 5 Gru 2 AstpdIAw v7	syj sohnI cMdnu coAw nrk Gor kw duAwrw ]7] (642-6, soriT, mÚ 5) sayj sohnee chandan cho-aa narak ghor kaa du-aaraa. ||7||
ALLOW	soriT mhlw 5 Gru 2 AstpdIAw v7	He may lie on beautiful beds, perfumed with sandalwood oil, but this will led him only to the gates of the most horrible hell. ||7||
RECORD	para 28424	hir kIriq swDsMgiq hY isir krmn kY krmw ] (642-7, soriT, mÚ 5) har keerat saaDhsangat hai sir karman kai karmaa. Singing the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises in the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, is the highest of all actions.
RECORD	soriT mhlw 5 Gru 2 AstpdIAw v8	khu nwnk iqsu BieE prwpiq ijsu purb ilKy kw lhnw ]8] (642-7, soriT, mÚ 5) kaho naanak tis bha-i-o paraapat jis purab likhay kaa lahnaa. ||8||
DEFINE	soriT mhlw 5 Gru 2 AstpdIAw v8	Says Nanak, he alone obtains it, who is pre-destined to receive it. ||8||
DEFINE	para 28426	qyro syvku ieh rMig mwqw ] (642-8, soriT, mÚ 5) tayro sayvak ih rang maataa. Your slave is intoxicated with this Love of Yours.
RECORD	soriT mhlw 5 Gru 2 AstpdIAw v1	BieE ik®pwlu dIn duK BMjnu hir hir kIrqin iehu mnu rwqw ] rhwau dUjw ]1]3] (642-8, soriT, mÚ 5) bha-i-o kirpaal deen dukh bhanjan har har keertan ih man raataa. rahaa-o doojaa. ||1||
RECORD	soriT mhlw 5 Gru 2 AstpdIAw v1	3|| The Destroyer of the pains of the poor has become merciful to me, and this mind is imbued with the Praises of the Lord, Har, Har. ||Second Pause||1||3||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI (642-10)
RECORD	para 28428	raag sorath vaar mahlay 4 kee Vaar Of Raag Sorat'h, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 28429	<> siqgur pRswid ] (642-10) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	para 28430	sloku mÚ 1 ] (642-11) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28431	soriT sdw suhwvxI jy scw min hoie ] (642-11, soriT, mÚ 1) sorath sadaa suhaavanee jay sachaa man ho-ay. Sorat'h is always beautiful, if it brings the True Lord to dwell in the mind of the soul- bride.
DEFINE	para 28432	dMdI mYlu n kqu min jIBY scw soie ] (642-11, soriT, mÚ 1) dandee mail na kat man jeebhai sachaa so-ay. Her teeth are clean and her mind is not split by duality; the Name of the True Lord is on her tongue.
RECORD	para 28433	ssurY pyeIAY BY vsI siqguru syiv insMg ] (642-12, soriT, mÚ 1) sasurai pay-ee-ai bhai vasee satgur sayv nisang. Here and hereafter, she abides in the Fear of God, and serves the True Guru without hesitation.
RECORD	para 28434	prhir kpVu jy ipr imlY KusI rwvY ipru sMig ] (642-12, soriT, mÚ 1) parhar kaparh jay pir milai khusee raavai pir sang. Discarding worldly adornments, she meets her Husband Lord, and she celebrates joyfully with Him.
DEFINE	para 28435	sdw sIgwrI nwau min kdy n mYlu pqMgu ] (642-12, soriT, mÚ 1) sadaa seegaaree naa-o man kaday na mail patang. She is adorned forever with the Name in her mind, and she does not have even an iota of filth.
RECORD	para 28436	dyvr jyT muey duiK ssU kw fru iksu ] (642-13, soriT, mÚ 1) dayvar jayth mu-ay dukh sasoo kaa dar kis. Her husband's younger and elder brothers, the corrupt desires, have died, suffering in pain; and now, who fears Maya, the mother-in-law?
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	jy ipr BwvY nwnkw krm mxI sBu scu ]1] (642-13, soriT, mÚ 1) jay pir bhaavai naankaa karam manee sabh sach. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	If she becomes pleasing to her Husband Lord, O Nanak, she bears the jewel of good karma upon her forehead, and everything is Truth to her. ||1||
RECORD	para 28438	mÚ 4 ] (642-14) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28439	soriT qwim suhwvxI jw hir nwmu FMFoly ] (642-14, soriT, mÚ 4) sorath taam suhaavanee jaa har naam dhandholay. Sorat'h is beautiful only when it leads the soul-bride to seek the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 28440	gur purKu mnwvY Awpxw gurmqI hir hir boly ] (642-14, soriT, mÚ 4) gur purakh manaavai aapnaa gurmatee har har bolay. She pleases her Guru and God; under Guru's Instruction, she speaks the Name of the Lord, Har, Har.
RECORD	para 28441	hir pRyim ksweI idnsu rwiq hir rqI hir rMig coly ] (642-15, soriT, mÚ 4) har paraym kasaa-ee dinas raat har ratee har rang cholay. She is attracted to the Lord's Name, day and night, and her body is drenched in the color of the Love of the Lord, Har, Har.
RECORD	para 28442	hir jYsw purKu n lBeI sBu dyiKAw jgqu mY toly ] (642-15, soriT, mÚ 4) har jaisaa purakh na labh-ee sabh daykhi-aa jagat mai tolay. No other being like the Lord God can be found; I have looked and searched over the whole world.
RECORD	para 28443	guir siqguir nwmu idRVwieAw mnu Anq n kwhU foly ] (642-16, soriT, mÚ 4) gur satgur naam drirh-aa-i-aa man anat na kaahoo dolay. The Guru, the True Guru, has implanted the Naam within me; my mind does not waver any more.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	jnu nwnku hir kw dwsu hY gur siqgur ky gol goly ]2] (642-17, soriT, mÚ 4) jan naanak har kaa daas hai gur satgur kay gol golay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	Servant Nanak is the Lord's slave, the slave of the slaves of the Guru, the True Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 28445	pauVI ] (642-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28446	qU Awpy issit krqw isrjxhwirAw ] (642-17, soriT, mÚ 4) too aapay sisat kartaa sirjanhaari-aa. You Yourself are the Creator, the Fashioner of the world.
RECORD	para 28447	quDu Awpy Kylu rcwie quDu Awip svwirAw ] (642-18, soriT, mÚ 4) tuDh aapay khayl rachaa-ay tuDh aap savaari-aa. You Yourself have arranged the play, and You Yourself arrange it.
DEFINE	para 28448	dwqw krqw Awip Awip BogxhwirAw ] (642-18, soriT, mÚ 4) daataa kartaa aap aap bhoganhaari-aa. You Yourself are the Giver and the Creator; You Yourself are the Enjoyer.
DEFINE	para 28449	sBu qyrw sbdu vrqY aupwvxhwirAw ] (642-19, soriT, mÚ 4) sabh tayraa sabad vartai upaavanhaari-aa. The Word of Your Shabad is pervading everywhere, O Creator Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	hau gurmuiK sdw slwhI gur kau vwirAw ]1] (642-19, soriT, mÚ 4) ha-o gurmukh sadaa salaahee gur ka-o vaari-aa. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	As Gurmukh, I ever praise the Lord; I am a sacrifice to the Guru. ||1||
RECORD	para 28452	sloku mÚ 3 ] (643-1) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28453	haumY jlqy jil muey BRim Awey dUjY Bwie ] (643-1, soriT, mÚ 3) ha-umai jaltay jal mu-ay bharam aa-ay doojai bhaa-ay. In the flames of egotism, he is burnt to death; he wanders in doubt and the love of duality.
RECORD	para 28454	pUrY siqguir rwiK lIey AwpxY pMnY pwie ] (643-1, soriT, mÚ 3) poorai satgur raakh lee-ay aapnai pannai paa-ay. The Perfect True Guru saves him, making him His own.
DEFINE	para 28455	iehu jgu jlqw ndrI AwieAw gur kY sbid suBwie ] (643-2, soriT, mÚ 3) ih jag jaltaa nadree aa-i-aa gur kai sabad subhaa-ay. This world is burning; through the Sublime Word of the Guru's Shabad, this comes to be seen.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	sbid rqy sy sIql Bey nwnk scu kmwie ]1] (643-2, soriT, mÚ 3) sabad ratay say seetal bha-ay naanak sach kamaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	Those who are attuned to the Shabad are cooled and soothed; O Nanak, they practice Truth. ||1||
RECORD	para 28457	mÚ 3 ] (643-3) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28458	sPilE siqguru syivAw DMnu jnmu prvwxu ] (643-3, soriT, mÚ 3) safli-o satgur sayvi-aa Dhan janam parvaan. Service to the True Guru is fruitful and rewarding; blessed and acceptable is such a life.
RECORD	para 28459	ijnw siqguru jIvidAw muieAw n ivsrY syeI purK sujwx ] (643-3, soriT, mÚ 3) jinaa satgur jeevdi-aa mu-i-aa na visrai say-ee purakh sujaan. Those who do not forget the True Guru, in life and in death, are truly wise people.
DEFINE	para 28460	kulu auDwry Awpxw so jnu hovY prvwxu ] (643-4, soriT, mÚ 3) kul uDhaaray aapnaa so jan hovai parvaan. Their families are saved, and they are approved by the Lord.
RECORD	para 28461	gurmuiK muey jIvdy prvwxu hih mnmuK jnim mrwih ] (643-4, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh mu-ay jeevday parvaan heh manmukh janam maraahi. The Gurmukhs are approved in death as in life, while the self-willed manmukhs continue the cycle of birth and death.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk muey n AwKIAih ij gur kY sbid smwih ]2] (643-5, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak mu-ay na aakhee-ahi je gur kai sabad samaahi. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, they are not described as dead, who are absorbed in the Word of the Guru's Shabad. ||2||
RECORD	para 28463	pauVI ] (643-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28464	hir purKu inrMjnu syiv hir nwmu iDAweIAY ] (643-6, soriT, mÚ 3) har purakh niranjan sayv har naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai. Serve the Immaculate Lord God, and meditate on the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 28465	sqsMgiq swDU lig hir nwim smweIAY ] (643-6, soriT, mÚ 3) satsangat saaDhoo lag har naam samaa-ee-ai. Join the Society of the Holy Saints, and be absorbed in the Lord's Name.
DEFINE	para 28466	hir qyrI vfI kwr mY mUrK lweIAY ] (643-6, soriT, mÚ 3) har tayree vadee kaar mai moorakh laa-ee-ai. O Lord, glorious and great is service to You; I am so foolish
RECORD	para 28467	hau golw lwlw quDu mY hukmu PurmweIAY ] (643-7, soriT, mÚ 3) ha-o golaa laalaa tuDh mai hukam furmaa-ee-ai. - please, commit me to it. I am Your servant and slave; command me, according to Your Will.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	hau gurmuiK kwr kmwvw ij guir smJweIAY ]2] (643-7, soriT, mÚ 3) ha-o gurmukh kaar kamaavaa je gur samjaa-ee-ai. ||2||
REQUIRE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	As Gurmukh, I shall serve You, as Guru has instructed me. ||2||
RECORD	para 28469	sloku mÚ 3 ] (643-8) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28470	pUrib iliKAw kmwvxw ij krqY Awip iliKAwsu ] (643-8, soriT, mÚ 3) poorab likhi-aa kamaavanaa je kartai aap likhi-aas. He acts according to pre-ordained destiny, written by the Creator Himself.
RECORD	para 28471	moh TgaulI pweIAnu ivsirAw guxqwsu ] (643-9, soriT, mÚ 3) moh thag-ulee paa-ee-an visri-aa guntaas. Emotional attachment has drugged him, and he has forgotten the Lord, the treasure of virtue.
DEFINE	para 28472	mqu jwxhu jgu jIvdw dUjY Bwie muieAwsu ] (643-9, soriT, mÚ 3) mat jaanhu jag jeevdaa doojai bhaa-ay mu-i-aas. Don't think that he is alive in the world - he is dead, through the love of duality.
ALLOW	para 28473	ijnI gurmuiK nwmu n cyiqE sy bhix n imlnI pwis ] (643-9, soriT, mÚ 3) jinee gurmukh naam na chayti-o say bahan na milnee paas. Those who do not meditate on the Lord, as Gurmukh, are not permitted to sit near the Lord.
RECORD	para 28474	duKu lwgw bhu Aiq Gxw puqu klqu n swiQ koeI jwis ] (643-10, soriT, mÚ 3) dukh laagaa baho at ghanaa put kalat na saath ko-ee jaas. They suffer the most horrible pain and suffering, and neither their sons nor their wives go along with them.
DEFINE	para 28475	lokw ivic muhu kwlw hoAw AMdir auBy sws ] (643-11, soriT, mÚ 3) lokaa vich muhu kaalaa ho-aa andar ubhay saas. Their faces are blackened among men, and they sigh in deep regret.
DEFINE	para 28476	mnmuKw no ko n ivshI cuik gieAw vyswsu ] (643-11, soriT, mÚ 3) manmukhaa no ko na vishee chuk ga-i-aa vaysaas. No one places any reliance in the self-willed manmukhs; trust in them is lost.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk gurmuKw no suKu Aglw ijnw AMqir nwm invwsu ]1] (643-12, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukhaa no sukh aglaa jinaa antar naam nivaas. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs live in absolute peace; the Naam, the Name of the Lord, abides within them. ||1||
RECORD	para 28478	mÚ 3 ] (643-12) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28479	sy sYx sy sjxw ij gurmuiK imlih suBwie ] (643-12, soriT, mÚ 3) say sain say sajnaa je gurmukh mileh subhaa-ay. They alone are relatives, and they alone are friends, who, as Gurmukh, join together in love.
RECORD	para 28480	siqgur kw Bwxw Anidnu krih sy sic rhy smwie ] (643-13, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur kaa bhaanaa an-din karahi say sach rahay samaa-ay. Night and day, they act according to the True Guru's Will; they remain absorbed in the True Name.
RECORD	para 28481	dUjY Bwie lgy sjx n AwKIAih ij AiBmwnu krih vykwr ] (643-13, soriT, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay lagay sajan na aakhee-ahi je abhimaan karahi vaykaar. Those who are attached to the love of duality are not called friends; they practice egotism and corruption.
DEFINE	para 28482	mnmuK Awp suAwrQI kwrju n skih svwir ] (643-14, soriT, mÚ 3) manmukh aap su-aarthee kaaraj na sakahi savaar. The self-willed manmukhs are selfish; they cannot resolve anyone's affairs.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk pUrib iliKAw kmwvxw koie n mytxhwru ]2] (643-15, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak poorab likhi-aa kamaavanaa ko-ay na maytanhaar. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, they act according to their pre-ordained destiny; no one can erase it. ||2||
RECORD	para 28484	pauVI ] (643-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28485	quDu Awpy jgqu aupwie kY Awip Kylu rcwieAw ] (643-15, soriT, mÚ 3) tuDh aapay jagat upaa-ay kai aap khayl rachaa-i-aa. You Yourself created the world, and You Yourself arranged the play of it.
RECORD	para 28486	qRY gux Awip isrijAw mwieAw mohu vDwieAw ] (643-16, soriT, mÚ 3) tarai gun aap sirji-aa maa-i-aa moh vaDhaa-i-aa. You Yourself created the three qualities, and fostered emotional attachment to Maya.
DEFINE	para 28487	ivic haumY lyKw mMgIAY iPir AwvY jwieAw ] (643-16, soriT, mÚ 3) vich ha-umai laykhaa mangee-ai fir aavai jaa-i-aa. He is called to account for his deeds done in egotism; he continues coming and going in reincarnation.
RECORD	para 28488	ijnw hir Awip ik®pw kry sy guir smJwieAw ] (643-17, soriT, mÚ 3) jinaa har aap kirpaa karay say gur samjhaa-i-aa. The Guru instructs those whom the Lord Himself blesses with Grace.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v3	bilhwrI gur Awpxy sdw sdw GumwieAw ]3] (643-17, soriT, mÚ 3) balihaaree gur aapnay sadaa sadaa ghumaa-i-aa. ||3||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v3	I am a sacrifice to my Guru; forever and ever, I am a sacrifice to Him. ||3||
RECORD	para 28490	sloku mÚ 3 ] (643-18) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28491	mwieAw mmqw mohxI ijin ivxu dMqw jgu KwieAw ] (643-18, soriT, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mamtaa mohnee jin vin dantaa jag khaa-i-aa. The love of Maya is enticing; without teeth, it has eaten up the world.
RECORD	para 28492	mnmuK KwDy gurmuiK aubry ijnI sic nwim icqu lwieAw ] (643-18, soriT, mÚ 3) manmukh khaaDhay gurmukh ubray jinee sach naam chit laa-i-aa. The self-willed manmukhs are eaten away, while the Gurmukhs are saved; they focus their consciousness on the True Name.
RECORD	para 28493	ibnu nwvY jgu kmlw iPrY gurmuiK ndrI AwieAw ] (643-19, soriT, mÚ 3) bin naavai jag kamlaa firai gurmukh nadree aa-i-aa. Without the Name, the world wanders around insane; the Gurmukhs come to see this.
RECORD	para 28495	DMDw kriqAw inhPlu jnmu gvwieAw suKdwqw min n vswieAw ] (644-1, soriT, mÚ 3) DhanDhaa karti-aa nihfal janam gavaa-i-aa sukh-daata man na vasaa-i-aa. Involved in worldly affairs, he wastes his life in vain; the peace-giving Lord does not come to abide in his mind.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk nwmu iqnw kau imilAw ijn kau Duir iliK pwieAw ]1] (644-1, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak naam tinaa ka-o mili-aa jin ka-o Dhur likh paa-i-aa. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, they alone obtain the Name, who have such pre-ordained destiny. ||1||
RECORD	para 28497	mÚ 3 ] (644-2) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28498	Gr hI mih AMimRqu BrpUru hY mnmuKw swdu n pwieAw ] (644-2, soriT, mÚ 3) ghar hee meh amrit bharpoor hai manmukhaa saad na paa-i-aa. The home within is filled with Ambrosial Nectar, but the self-willed manmukh does not get to taste it.
RECORD	para 28499	ijau ksqUrI imrgu n jwxY BRmdw Brim BulwieAw ] (644-3, soriT, mÚ 3) ji-o kastooree mirag na jaanai bharmadaa bharam bhulaa-i-aa. He is like the deer, who does not recognize its own musk-scent; it wanders around, deluded by doubt.
RECORD	para 28500	AMimRqu qij ibKu sMgRhY krqY Awip KuAwieAw ] (644-3, soriT, mÚ 3) amrit taj bikh sangrahai kartai aap khu-aa-i-aa. The manmukh forsakes the Ambrosial Nectar, and instead gathers poison; the Creator Himself has fooled him.
RECORD	para 28501	gurmuiK ivrly soJI peI iqnw AMdir bRhmu idKwieAw ] (644-4, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlay sojhee pa-ee tinaa andar barahm dikhaa-i-aa. How rare are the Gurmukhs, who obtain this understanding; they behold the Lord God within themselves.
DEFINE	para 28502	qnu mnu sIqlu hoieAw rsnw hir swdu AwieAw ] (644-4, soriT, mÚ 3) tan man seetal ho-i-aa rasnaa har saad aa-i-aa. Their minds and bodies are cooled and soothed, and their tongues enjoy the sublime taste of the Lord.
RECORD	para 28503	sbdy hI nwau aUpjY sbdy myil imlwieAw ] (644-5, soriT, mÚ 3) sabday hee naa-o oopjai sabday mayl milaa-i-aa. Through the Word of the Shabad, the Name wells up; through the Shabad, we are united in the Lord's Union.
DEFINE	para 28504	ibnu sbdY sBu jgu baurwnw ibrQw jnmu gvwieAw ] (644-5, soriT, mÚ 3) bin sabdai sabh jag ba-uraanaa birthaa janam gavaa-i-aa. Without the Shabad, the whole world is insane, and it loses its life in vain.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	AMimRqu eyko sbdu hY nwnk gurmuiK pwieAw ]2] (644-6, soriT, mÚ 3) amrit ayko sabad hai naanak gurmukh paa-i-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	The Shabad alone is Ambrosial Nectar; O Nanak, the Gurmukhs obtain it. ||2||
RECORD	para 28506	pauVI ] (644-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28507	so hir purKu AgMmu hY khu ikqu ibiD pweIAY ] (644-7, soriT, mÚ 3) so har purakh agamm hai kaho kit biDh paa-ee-ai. The Lord God is inaccessible; tell me, how can we find Him?
RECORD	para 28508	iqsu rUpu n ryK AidRstu khu jn ikau iDAweIAY ] (644-7, soriT, mÚ 3) tis roop na raykh adrist kaho jan ki-o Dhi-aa-ee-ai. He has no form or feature, and He cannot be seen; tell me, how can we meditate on Him?
RECORD	para 28509	inrMkwru inrMjnu hir Agmu ikAw kih gux gweIAY ] (644-8, soriT, mÚ 3) nirankaar niranjan har agam ki-aa kahi gun gaa-ee-ai. The Lord is formless, immaculate and inaccessible; which of His Virtues should we speak of and sing?
RECORD	para 28510	ijsu Awip buJwey Awip su hir mwrig pweIAY ] (644-8, soriT, mÚ 3) jis aap bujhaa-ay aap so har maarag paa-ee-ai. They alone walk on the Lord's Path, whom the Lord Himself instructs.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v4	guir pUrY vyKwilAw gur syvw pweIAY ]4] (644-9, soriT, mÚ 3) gur poorai vaykhaali-aa gur sayvaa paa-ee-ai. ||4||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v4	The Perfect Guru has revealed Him to me; serving the Guru, He is found. ||4||
RECORD	para 28512	sloku mÚ 3 ] (644-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28513	ijau qnu kolU pIVIAY rqu n BorI fyih ] (644-9, soriT, mÚ 3) ji-o tan koloo peerhee-ai rat na bhoree dayhi. It is as if my body has been crushed in the oil-press, without yielding even a drop of blood;
DEFINE	para 28514	jIau vM\Y cau KMnIAY scy sMdVY nyih ] (644-10, soriT, mÚ 3) jee-o vanjai cha-o khannee-ai sachay sand-rhai nayhi. it is as if my soul has been cut apart into pieces for the sake of the Love of the True Lord;
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk mylu n cukeI rwqI AqY fyh ]1] (644-10, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak mayl na chuk-ee raatee atai dayh. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, still, night and day, my Union with the Lord is not broken. ||1||
RECORD	para 28516	mÚ 3 ] (644-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28517	sjxu mYfw rMgulw rMgu lwey mnu lyie ] (644-11, soriT, mÚ 3) sajan maidaa rangulaa rang laa-ay man lay-ay. My Friend is so full of joy and love; He colors my mind with the color of His Love,
DEFINE	para 28518	ijau mwjITY kpVy rMgy BI pwhyih ] (644-11, soriT, mÚ 3) ji-o maajeethai kaprhay rangay bhee paahayhi. like the fabric which is treated to retain the color of the dye.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk rMgu n auqrY ibAw n lgY kyh ]2] (644-11, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak rang na utrai bi-aa na lagai kayh. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, this color does not depart, and no other color can be imparted to this fabric. ||2||
RECORD	para 28520	pauVI ] (644-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28521	hir Awip vrqY Awip hir Awip bulwiedw ] (644-12, soriT, mÚ 3) har aap vartai aap har aap bulaa-idaa. The Lord Himself is pervading everywhere; the Lord Himself causes us to chant His Name.
RECORD	para 28522	hir Awpy isRsit svwir isir DMDY lwiedw ] (644-12, soriT, mÚ 3) har aapay sarisat savaar sir DhanDhai laa-idaa. The Lord Himself created the creation; He commits all to their tasks.
RECORD	para 28523	ieknw BgqI lwie ieik Awip KuAwiedw ] (644-13, soriT, mÚ 3) iknaa bhagtee laa-ay ik aap khu-aa-idaa. He engages some in devotional worship, and others, He causes to stray.
RECORD	para 28524	ieknw mwrig pwie ieik auJiV pwiedw ] (644-13, soriT, mÚ 3) iknaa maarag paa-ay ik ujharh paa-idaa. He places some on the Path, while He leads others into the wilderness.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v5	jnu nwnku nwmu iDAwey gurmuiK gux gwiedw ]5] (644-14, soriT, mÚ 3) jan naanak naam Dhi-aa-ay gurmukh gun gaa-idaa. ||5||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v5	Servant Nanak meditates on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; as Gurmukh, he sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||5||
RECORD	para 28526	sloku mÚ 3 ] (644-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
WHEN	para 28527	siqgur kI syvw sPlu hY jy ko kry icqu lwie ] (644-15, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur kee sayvaa safal hai jay ko karay chit laa-ay. Service to the True Guru is fruitful and rewarding, if one performs it with his mind focused on it.
DEFINE	para 28528	min icMidAw Plu pwvxw haumY ivchu jwie ] (644-15, soriT, mÚ 3) man chindi-aa fal paavnaa ha-umai vichahu jaa-ay. The fruits of the mind's desires are obtained, and egotism departs from within.
DEFINE	para 28529	bMDn qoVY mukiq hoie scy rhY smwie ] (644-16, soriT, mÚ 3) banDhan torhai mukat ho-ay sachay rahai samaa-ay. His bonds are broken, and he is liberated; he remains absorbed in the True Lord.
RECORD	para 28530	iesu jg mih nwmu AlBu hY gurmuiK vsY min Awie ] (644-16, soriT, mÚ 3) is jag meh naam alabh hai gurmukh vasai man aa-ay. It is so difficult to obtain the Naam in this world; it comes to dwell in the mind of the Gurmukh.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk jo guru syvih Awpxw hau iqn bilhwrY jwau ]1] (644-17, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak jo gur sayveh aapnaa ha-o tin balihaarai jaa-o. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, I am a sacrifice to one who serves his True Guru. ||1||
RECORD	para 28532	mÚ 3 ] (644-17) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28533	mnmuK mMnu Aijqu hY dUjY lgY jwie ] (644-17, soriT, mÚ 3) manmukh man ajit hai doojai lagai jaa-ay. The mind of the self-willed manmukh is so very stubborn; it is stuck in the love of duality.
RECORD	para 28534	iqs no suKu supnY nhI duKy duiK ivhwie ] (644-18, soriT, mÚ 3) tis no sukh supnai nahee dukhay dukh vihaa-ay. He does not find peace, even in dreams; he passes his life in misery and suffering.
RECORD	para 28535	Gir Gir piV piV pMifq Qky isD smwiD lgwie ] (644-18, soriT, mÚ 3) ghar ghar parh parh pandit thakay siDh samaaDh lagaa-ay. The Pandits have grown weary of going door to door, reading and reciting their scriptures; the Siddhas have gone into their trances of Samaadhi.
DEFINE	para 28536	iehu mnu vis n AwveI Qky krm kmwie ] (644-19, soriT, mÚ 3) ih man vas na aavee thakay karam kamaa-ay. This mind cannot be controlled; they are tired of performing religious rituals.
RECORD	para 28537	ByKDwrI ByK kir Qky AiTsiT qIrQ nwie ] (644-19, soriT, mÚ 3) bhaykh-Dhaaree bhaykh kar thakay athisath tirath naa-ay. The impersonators have grown weary of wearing false costumes, and bathing at the sixty-eight sacred shrines.
DEFINE	para 28539	mn kI swr n jwxnI haumY Brim Bulwie ] (645-1, soriT, mÚ 3) man kee saar na jaannee ha-umai bharam bhulaa-ay. They do not know the state of their own minds; they are deluded by doubt and egotism.
RECORD	para 28540	gur prswdI Bau pieAw vfBwig visAw min Awie ] (645-1, soriT, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee bha-o pa-i-aa vadbhaag vasi-aa man aa-ay. By Guru's Grace, the Fear of God is obtained; by great good fortune, the Lord comes to abide in the mind.
WHEN	para 28541	BY pieAY mnu vis hoAw haumY sbid jlwie ] (645-2, soriT, mÚ 3) bhai pa-i-ai man vas ho-aa ha-umai sabad jalaa-ay. When the Fear of God comes, the mind is restrained, and through the Word of the Shabad, the ego is burnt away.
DEFINE	para 28542	sic rqy sy inrmly joqI joiq imlwie ] (645-2, soriT, mÚ 3) sach ratay say nirmalay jotee jot milaa-ay. Those who are imbued with Truth are immaculate; their light merges in the Light.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	siqguir imilAY nwau pwieAw nwnk suiK smwie ]2] (645-3, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur mili-ai naa-o paa-i-aa naanak sukh samaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	Meeting the True Guru, one obtains the Name; O Nanak, he is absorbed in peace. ||2||
RECORD	para 28544	pauVI ] (645-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28545	eyh BUpiq rwxy rMg idn cwir suhwvxw ] (645-3, soriT, mÚ 3) ayh bhoopat raanay rang din chaar suhaavanaa. The pleasures of kings and emperors are pleasing, but they last for only a few days.
DEFINE	para 28546	eyhu mwieAw rMgu ksuMB iKn mih lih jwvxw ] (645-4, soriT, mÚ 3) ayhu maa-i-aa rang kasumbh khin meh leh jaavnaa. These pleasures of Maya are like the color of the safflower, which wears off in a moment.
WHEN	para 28547	clidAw nwil n clY isir pwp lY jwvxw ] (645-4, soriT, mÚ 3) chaldi-aa naal na chalai sir paap lai jaavnaa. They do not go with him when he departs; instead, he carries the load of sins upon his head.
WHEN	para 28548	jW pkiV clwieAw kwil qW Krw frwvxw ] (645-5, soriT, mÚ 3) jaa N pakarh chalaa-i-aa kaal taaN kharaa daraavanaa. When death seizes him, and marches him away, then he looks absolutely hideous.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v6	Eh vylw hiQ n AwvY iPir pCuqwvxw ]6] (645-5, soriT, mÚ 3) oh vaylaa hath na aavai fir pachhutaavnaa. ||6||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v6	That lost opportunity will not come into his hands again, and in the end, he regrets and repents. ||6||
RECORD	para 28550	sloku mÚ 3 ] (645-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28551	siqgur qy jo muh iPry sy bDy duK shwih ] (645-6, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur tay jo muh firay say baDhay dukh sahaahi. Those who turn their faces away from the True Guru, suffer in sorrow and bondage.
DEFINE	para 28552	iPir iPir imlxu n pwienI jMmih qY mir jwih ] (645-6, soriT, mÚ 3) fir fir milan na paa-inee jameh tai mar jaahi. Again and again, they are born only to die; they cannot meet their Lord.
RECORD	para 28553	shsw rogu n CofeI duK hI mih duK pwih ] (645-7, soriT, mÚ 3) sahsaa rog na chhod-ee dukh hee meh dukh paahi. The disease of doubt does not depart, and they find only pain and more pain.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk ndrI bKis lyih sbdy myil imlwih ]1] (645-7, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak nadree bakhas layhi sabday mayl milaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, if the Gracious Lord forgives, then one is united in Union with the Word of the Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	para 28555	mÚ 3 ] (645-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 28556	jo siqgur qy muh iPry iqnw Taur n Twau ] (645-8, soriT, mÚ 3) jo satgur tay muh firay tinaa tha-ur na thaa-o. Those who turn their faces away from the True Guru, shall find no place of rest or shelter.
RECORD	para 28557	ijau CutiV Gir Gir iPrY duhcwrix bdnwau ] (645-8, soriT, mÚ 3) ji-o chhutarh ghar ghar firai duhchaaran badnaa-o. They wander around from door to door, like a woman forsaken, with a bad character and a bad reputation.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk gurmuiK bKsIAih sy siqgur myil imlwau ]2] (645-9, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh bakhsee-ah say satgur mayl milaa-o. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are forgiven, and united in Union with the True Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 28559	pauVI ] (645-9) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28560	jo syvih siq murwir sy Bvjl qir gieAw ] (645-9, soriT, mÚ 3) jo sayveh sat muraar say bhavjal tar ga-i-aa. Those who serve the True Lord, the Destroyer of ego, cross over the terrifying world- ocean.
DEFINE	para 28561	jo bolih hir hir nwau iqn jmu Cif gieAw ] (645-10, soriT, mÚ 3) jo boleh har har naa-o tin jam chhad ga-i-aa. Those who chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, are passed over by the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	para 28562	sy drgh pYDy jwih ijnw hir jip lieAw ] (645-10, soriT, mÚ 3) say dargeh paiDhay jaahi jinaa har jap la-i-aa. Those who meditate on the Lord, go to His Court in robes of honor.
RECORD	para 28563	hir syvih syeI purK ijnw hir quDu mieAw ] (645-11, soriT, mÚ 3) har sayveh say-ee purakh jinaa har tuDh ma-i-aa. They alone serve You, O Lord, whom You bless with Grace.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v7	gux gwvw ipAwry inq gurmuiK BRm Bau gieAw ]7] (645-11, soriT, mÚ 3) gun gaavaa pi-aaray nit gurmukh bharam bha-o ga-i-aa. ||7||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v7	I sing continually Your Glorious Praises, O Beloved; as Gurmukh, my doubts and fears have been dispelled. ||7||
RECORD	para 28565	sloku mÚ 3 ] (645-12) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28566	QwlY ivic qY vsqU peIE hir Bojnu AMimRqu swru ] (645-12, soriT, mÚ 3) thaalai vich tai vastoo pa-ee-o har bhojan amrit saar. Upon the plate, three things have been placed; this is the sublime, ambrosial food of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 28567	ijqu KwDY mnu iqRpqIAY pweIAY moK duAwru ] (645-13, soriT, mÚ 3) jit khaaDhai man taripat-ee-ai paa-ee-ai mokh du-aar. Eating this, the mind is satisfied, and the Door of Salvation is found.
DEFINE	para 28568	iehu Bojnu AlBu hY sMqhu lBY gur vIcwir ] (645-13, soriT, mÚ 3) ih bhojan alabh hai santahu labhai gur veechaar. It is so difficult to obtain this food, O Saints; it is obtained only by contemplating the Guru.
RECORD	para 28569	eyh mudwvxI ikau ivchu kFIAY sdw rKIAY auir Dwir ] (645-14, soriT, mÚ 3) ayh mudaavanee ki-o vichahu kadhee-ai sadaa rakhee-ai ur Dhaar. Why should we cast this riddle out of our minds? We should keep it ever enshrined in our hearts.
RECORD	para 28570	eyh mudwvxI siqgurU pweI gurisKw lDI Bwil ] (645-14, soriT, mÚ 3) ayh mudaavanee satguroo paa-ee gursikhaa laDhee bhaal. The True Guru has posed this riddle. The Guru's Sikhs have found its solution.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk ijsu buJwey su buJsI hir pwieAw gurmuiK Gwil ]1] (645-15, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak jis bujhaa-ay so bujhsee har paa-i-aa gurmukh ghaal. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, he alone understands this, whom the Lord inspires to understand. The Gurmukhs work hard, and find the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 28572	mÚ 3 ] (645-15) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28573	jo Duir myly sy imil rhy siqgur isau icqu lwie ] (645-15, soriT, mÚ 3) jo Dhur maylay say mil rahay satgur si-o chit laa-ay. Those whom the Primal Lord unites, remain in Union with Him; they focus their consciousness on the True Guru.
RECORD	para 28574	Awip ivCoVynu sy ivCuVy dUjY Bwie KuAwie ] (645-16, soriT, mÚ 3) aap vichhorhayn say vichhurhay doojai bhaa-ay khu-aa-ay. Those whom the Lord Himself separates, remain separated; in the love of duality, they are ruined.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk ivxu krmw ikAw pweIAY pUrib iliKAw kmwie ]2] (645-16, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak vin karmaa ki-aa paa-ee-ai poorab likhi-aa kamaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, without good karma, what can anyone obtain? He earns what he is pre- destined to receive. ||2||
RECORD	para 28576	pauVI ] (645-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28577	bih sKIAw jsu gwvih gwvxhwrIAw ] (645-17, soriT, mÚ 3) bahi sakhee-aa jas gaavahi gavanhaaree-aa. Sitting together, the companions sing the Songs of the Lord's Praises.
DEFINE	para 28578	hir nwmu slwihhu inq hir kau bilhwrIAw ] (645-18, soriT, mÚ 3) har naam salaahihu nit har ka-o balihaaree-aa. They praise the Lord's Name continually; they are a sacrifice to the Lord.
RECORD	para 28579	ijnI suix mMinAw hir nwau iqnw hau vwrIAw ] (645-18, soriT, mÚ 3) jinee sun mani-aa har naa-o tinaa ha-o vaaree-aa. Those who hear, and believe in the Lord's Name, to them I am a sacrifice.
DEFINE	para 28580	gurmuKIAw hir mylu imlwvxhwrIAw ] (645-19, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukhee-aa har mayl milaavanhaaree-aa. O Lord, let me unite with the Gurmukhs, who are united with You.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v8	hau bil jwvw idnu rwiq gur dyKxhwrIAw ]8] (645-19, soriT, mÚ 3) ha-o bal jaavaa din raat gur daikhanhaaree-aa. ||8||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v8	I am a sacrifice to those who, day and night, behold their Guru. ||8||
RECORD	para 28582	sloku mÚ 3 ] (645-19) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28584	ivxu nwvY siB Brmdy inq jig qotw sYswir ] (646-1, soriT, mÚ 3) vin naavai sabh bharamday nit jag totaa saisaar. Without the Name of the Lord, everyone wanders around the world, losing.
RECORD	para 28585	mnmuiK krm kmwvxy haumY AMDu gubwru ] (646-1, soriT, mÚ 3) manmukh karam kamaavnay ha-umai anDh gubaar. The self-willed manmukhs do their deeds in the pitch black darkness of egotism.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	gurmuiK AMimRqu pIvxw nwnk sbdu vIcwir ]1] (646-2, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh amrit peevnaa naanak sabad veechaar. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	The Gurmukhs drink in the Ambrosial Nectar, O Nanak, contemplating the Word of the Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	para 28587	mÚ 3 ] (646-2) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28588	shjy jwgY shjy sovY ] (646-2, soriT, mÚ 3) sehjay jaagai sehjay sovai. He wakes in peace, and he sleeps in peace.
RECORD	para 28589	gurmuiK Anidnu ausqiq hovY ] (646-2, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh an-din ustat hovai. The Gurmukh praises the Lord night and day.
RECORD	para 28590	mnmuK BrmY shsw hovY ] (646-3, soriT, mÚ 3) manmukh bharmai sahsaa hovai. The self-willed manmukh remains deluded by his doubts.
DEFINE	para 28591	AMqir icMqw nId n sovY ] (646-3, soriT, mÚ 3) antar chintaa need na sovai. He is filled with anxiety, and he cannot even sleep.
RECORD	para 28592	igAwnI jwgih svih suBwie ] (646-3, soriT, mÚ 3) gi-aanee jaageh saveh subhaa-ay. The spiritually wise wake and sleep in peace.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk nwim riqAw bil jwau ]2] (646-4, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak naam rati-aa bal jaa-o. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	Nanak is a sacrifice to those who are imbued with the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 28594	pauVI ] (646-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28595	sy hir nwmu iDAwvih jo hir riqAw ] (646-4, soriT, mÚ 3) say har naam Dhi-aavahi jo har rati-aa. They alone meditate on the Lord's Name, who are imbued with the Lord.
DEFINE	para 28596	hir ieku iDAwvih ieku ieko hir siqAw ] (646-4, soriT, mÚ 3) har ik Dhi-aavahi ik iko har sati-aa. They meditate on the One Lord; the One and Only Lord is True.
DEFINE	para 28597	hir ieko vrqY ieku ieko auqpiqAw ] (646-5, soriT, mÚ 3) har iko vartai ik iko utpati-aa. The One Lord is pervading everywhere; the One Lord created the Universe.
RECORD	para 28598	jo hir nwmu iDAwvih iqn fru sit GiqAw ] (646-5, soriT, mÚ 3) jo har naam Dhi-aavahi tin dar sat ghati-aa. Those who meditate on the Lord's Name, cast out their fears.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v9	gurmqI dyvY Awip gurmuiK hir jipAw ]9] (646-6, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmatee dayvai aap gurmukh har japi-aa. ||9||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v9	The Lord Himself blesses them with Guru's Instruction; the Gurmukh meditates on the Lord. ||9||
RECORD	para 28600	slok mÚ 3 ] (646-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
UPHOLD	para 28601	AMqir igAwnu n AwieE ijqu ikCu soJI pwie ] (646-6, soriT, mÚ 3) antar gi-aan na aa-i-o jit kichh sojhee paa-ay. Spiritual wisdom, which would bring understanding, does not enter into his mind.
RECORD	para 28602	ivxu ifTw ikAw swlwhIAY AMDw AMDu kmwie ] (646-7, soriT, mÚ 3) vin dithaa ki-aa salaahee-ai anDhaa anDh kamaa-ay. Without seeing, how can he praise the Lord? The blind act in blindness.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk sbdu pCwxIAY nwmu vsY min Awie ]1] (646-7, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak sabad pachhaanee-ai naam vasai man aa-ay. ||1||
WHEN	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, when one realizes the Word of the Shabad, then the Naam comes to abide in the mind. ||1||
RECORD	para 28604	mÚ 3 ] (646-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28605	iekw bwxI ieku guru ieko sbdu vIcwir ] (646-8, soriT, mÚ 3) ikaa banee ik gur iko sabad veechaar. There is One Bani; there is One Guru; there is one Shabad to contemplate.
DEFINE	para 28606	scw saudw htu scu rqnI Bry BMfwr ] (646-8, soriT, mÚ 3) sachaa sa-udaa hat sach ratnee bharay bhandaar. True is the merchandise, and true is the shop; the warehouses are overflowing with jewels.
DEFINE	para 28607	gur ikrpw qy pweIAin jy dyvY dyvxhwru ] (646-9, soriT, mÚ 3) gur kirpaa tay paa-ee-an jay dayvai dayvanhaar. By Guru's Grace, they are obtained, if the Great Giver gives them.
RECORD	para 28608	scw saudw lwBu sdw KitAw nwmu Apwru ] (646-9, soriT, mÚ 3) sachaa sa-udaa laabh sadaa khati-aa naam apaar. Dealing in this true merchandise, one earns the profit of the incomparable Naam.
DEFINE	para 28609	ivKu ivic AMimRqu pRgitAw krim pIAwvxhwru ] (646-10, soriT, mÚ 3) vikh vich amrit pargati-aa karam pee-aavanhaar. In the midst of poison, the Ambrosial Nectar is revealed; by His Mercy, one drinks it in.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk scu slwhIAY DMnu svwrxhwru ]2] (646-10, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak sach salaahee-ai Dhan savaaranhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, praise the True Lord; blessed is the Creator, the Embellisher. ||2||
RECORD	para 28611	pauVI ] (646-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28612	ijnw AMdir kUVu vrqY scu n BwveI ] (646-11, soriT, mÚ 3) jinaa andar koorh vartai sach na bhaav-ee. Those who are permeated by falsehood, do not love the Truth.
DEFINE	para 28613	jy ko bolY scu kUVw jil jwveI ] (646-11, soriT, mÚ 3) jay ko bolai sach koorhaa jal jaav-ee. If someone speaks the Truth, falsehood is burnt away.
DEFINE	para 28614	kUiVAwrI rjY kUiV ijau ivstw kwgu KwveI ] (646-12, soriT, mÚ 3) khoorhi-aaree rajai koorh ji-o vistaa kaag khaav-ee. The false are satisfied by falsehood, like the crows who eat manure.
WHEN	para 28615	ijsu hir hoie ik®pwlu so nwmu iDAwveI ] (646-12, soriT, mÚ 3) jis har ho-ay kirpaal so naam Dhi-aava-ee. When the Lord grants His Grace, then one meditates on the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v10	hir gurmuiK nwmu ArwiD kUVu pwpu lih jwveI ]10] (646-13, soriT, mÚ 3) har gurmukh naam araaDh koorh paap leh jaav-ee. ||10||
REQUIRE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v10	As Gurmukh, worship the Lord's Name in adoration; fraud and sin shall disappear. ||10||
RECORD	para 28617	sloku mÚ 3 ] (646-13) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28618	syKw caucikAw cauvwieAw eyhu mnu iekqu Gir Awix ] (646-13, soriT, mÚ 3) saykhaa cha-uchaki-aa cha-uvaa-i-aa ayhu man ikat ghar aan. O Shaykh, you wander in the four directions, blown by the four winds; bring your mind back to the home of the One Lord.
WHEN	para 28619	eyhV qyhV Cif qU gur kw sbdu pCwxu ] (646-14, soriT, mÚ 3) ayharh tayharh chhad too gur kaa sabad pachhaan. Renounce your petty arguments, and realize the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
DEFINE	para 28620	siqgur AgY Fih pau sBu ikCu jwxY jwxu ] (646-14, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur agai dheh pa-o sabh kichh jaanai jaan. Bow in humble respect before the True Guru; He is the Knower who knows everything.
RECORD	para 28621	Awsw mnsw jlwie qU hoie rhu imhmwxu ] (646-15, soriT, mÚ 3) aasaa mansaa jalaa-ay too ho-ay rahu mihmaan. Burn away your hopes and desires, and live like a guest in this world.
REQUIRE	para 28622	siqgur kY BwxY BI clih qw drgh pwvih mwxu ] (646-15, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur kai bhaanai bhee chaleh taa dargeh paavahi maan. If you walk in harmony with the True Guru's Will, then you shall be honored in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk ij nwmu n cyqnI iqn iDgu pYnxu iDgu Kwxu ]1] (646-16, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak je naam na chaytnee tin Dhig painan Dhig khaan. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, those who do not contemplate the Naam, the Name of the Lord - cursed are their clothes, and cursed is their food. ||1||
RECORD	para 28624	mÚ 3 ] (646-16) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28625	hir gux qoit n AwveI kImiq khxu n jwie ] (646-16, soriT, mÚ 3) har gun tot na aavee keemat kahan na jaa-ay. There is no end to the Lord's Glorious Praises; His worth cannot be described.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk gurmuiK hir gux rvih gux mih rhY smwie ]2] (646-17, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh har gun raveh gun meh rahai samaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs chant the Glorious Praises of the Lord; they are absorbed in His Glorious Virtues. ||2||
RECORD	para 28627	pauVI ] (646-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
WHEN	para 28628	hir colI dyh svwrI kiF pYDI Bgiq kir ] (646-18, soriT, mÚ 3) har cholee dayh savaaree kadh paiDhee bhagat kar. The Lord has adorned the coat of the body; He has embroidered it with devotional worship.
RECORD	para 28629	hir pwtu lgw AiDkweI bhu bhu ibiD Bwiq kir ] (646-18, soriT, mÚ 3) har paat lagaa aDhikaa-ee baho baho biDh bhaat kar. The Lord has woven His silk into it, in so many ways and fashions.
DEFINE	para 28630	koeI bUJY bUJxhwrw AMqir ibbyku kir ] (646-19, soriT, mÚ 3) ko-ee boojhai boojhanhaaraa antar bibayk kar. How rare is that man of understanding, who understands, and deliberates within.
RECORD	para 28631	so bUJY eyhu ibbyku ijsu buJwey Awip hir ] (646-19, soriT, mÚ 3) so boojhai ayhu bibayk jis bujhaa-ay aap har. He alone understands these deliberations, whom the Lord Himself inspires to understand.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v11	jnu nwnku khY ivcwrw gurmuiK hir siq hir ]11] (646-19, soriT, mÚ 3) jan naanak kahai vichaaraa gurmukh har sat har. ||11||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v11	Poor servant Nanak speaks: the Gurmukhs know the Lord, the Lord is True. ||11||
RECORD	para 28634	sloku mÚ 3 ] (647-1) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28635	prQwie swKI mhw purK boldy swJI sgl jhwnY ] (647-1, soriT, mÚ 3) parthaa-ay saakhee mahaa purakh bolday saajhee sagal jahaanai. Great men speak the teachings by relating them to individual situations, but the whole world shares in them.
RECORD	para 28636	gurmuiK hoie su Bau kry Awpxw Awpu pCwxY ] (647-2, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh ho-ay so bha-o karay aapnaa aap pachhaanai. One who becomes Gurmukh knows the Fear of God, and realizes his own self.
RECORD	para 28637	gur prswdI jIvqu mrY qw mn hI qy mnu mwnY ] (647-2, soriT, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee jeevat marai taa man hee tay man maanai. If, by Guru's Grace, one remains dead while yet alive, the mind becomes content in itself.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	ijn kau mn kI prqIiq nwhI nwnk sy ikAw kQih igAwnY ]1] (647-3, soriT, mÚ 3) jin ka-o man kee parteet naahee naanak say ki-aa katheh gi-aanai. ||1||
UPHOLD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	Those who have no faith in their own minds, O Nanak - how can they speak of spiritual wisdom? ||1||
RECORD	para 28639	mÚ 3 ] (647-3) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28640	gurmuiK icqu n lwieE AMiq duKu phuqw Awie ] (647-3, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh chit na laa-i-o ant dukh pahutaa aa-ay. Those who do not focus their consciousness on the Lord, as Gurmukh, suffer pain and grief in the end.
DEFINE	para 28641	AMdrhu bwhrhu AMiDAW suiD n kweI pwie ] (647-4, soriT, mÚ 3) andrahu baahrahu anDhi-aaN suDh na kaa-ee paa-ay. They are blind, inwardly and outwardly, and they do not understand anything.
RECORD	para 28642	pMifq iqn kI brkqI sBu jgqu Kwie jo rqy hir nwie ] (647-4, soriT, mÚ 3) pandit tin kee barkatee sabh jagat khaa-ay jo ratay har naa-ay. O Pandit, O religious scholar, the whole world is fed for the sake of those who are attuned to the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 28643	ijn gur kY sbid slwihAw hir isau rhy smwie ] (647-5, soriT, mÚ 3) jin gur kai sabad sahaali-aa har si-o rahay samaa-ay. Those who praise the Word of the Guru's Shabad, remain blended with the Lord.
RECORD	para 28644	pMifq dUjY Bwie brkiq n hoveI nw Dnu plY pwie ] (647-6, soriT, mÚ 3) pandit doojai bhaa-ay barkat na hova-ee naa Dhan palai paa-ay. O Pandit, O religious scholar, no one is satisfied, and no one finds true wealth through the love of duality.
RECORD	para 28645	piV Qky sMqoKu n AwieE Anidnu jlq ivhwie ] (647-6, soriT, mÚ 3) parh thakay santokh na aa-i-o an-din jalat vihaa-ay. They have grown weary of reading scriptures, but still, they do not find contentment, and they pass their lives burning, night and day.
RECORD	para 28646	kUk pUkwr n cukeI nw sMsw ivchu jwie ] (647-7, soriT, mÚ 3) kook pookaar na chuk-ee naa sansaa vichahu jaa-ay. Their cries and complaints never end, and doubt does not depart from within them.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk nwm ivhUixAw muih kwlY auiT jwie ]2] (647-7, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak naam vihooni-aa muhi kaalai uth jaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, without the Naam, the Name of the Lord, they rise up and depart with blackened faces. ||2||
RECORD	para 28648	pauVI ] (647-8) pa-orhee. Pauree:
REQUIRE	para 28649	hir sjx myil ipAwry imil pMQu dsweI ] (647-8, soriT, mÚ 3) har sajan mayl pi-aaray mil panth dasaa-ee. O Beloved, lead me to meet my True Friend; meeting with Him, I shall ask Him to show me the Path.
RECORD	para 28650	jo hir dsy imqu iqsu hau bil jweI ] (647-8, soriT, mÚ 3) jo har dasay mit tis ha-o bal jaa-ee. I am a sacrifice to that Friend, who shows it to me.
RECORD	para 28651	gux swJI iqn isau krI hir nwmu iDAweI ] (647-9, soriT, mÚ 3) gun saajhee tin si-o karee har naam Dhi-aa-ee. I share His Virtues with Him, and meditate on the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 28652	hir syvI ipAwrw inq syiv hir suKu pweI ] (647-9, soriT, mÚ 3) har sayvee pi-aaraa nit sayv har sukh paa-ee. I serve my Beloved Lord forever; serving the Lord, I have found peace.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v12	bilhwrI siqgur iqsu ijin soJI pweI ]12] (647-9, soriT, mÚ 3) balihaaree satgur tis jin sojhee paa-ee. ||12||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v12	I am a sacrifice to the True Guru, who has imparted this understanding to me. ||12||
RECORD	para 28654	sloku mÚ 3 ] (647-10) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
FORBID	para 28655	pMifq mYlu n cukeI jy vyd pVY jug cwir ] (647-10, soriT, mÚ 3) pandit mail na chuk-ee jay vayd parhai jug chaar. O Pandit, O religious scholar, your filth shall not be erased, even if you read the Vedas for four ages.
RECORD	para 28656	qRY gux mwieAw mUlu hY ivic haumY nwmu ivswir ] (647-11, soriT, mÚ 3) tarai gun maa-i-aa mool hai vich ha-umai naam visaar. The three qualities are the roots of Maya; in egotism, one forgets the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 28657	pMifq BUly dUjY lwgy mwieAw kY vwpwir ] (647-11, soriT, mÚ 3) pandit bhoolay doojai laagay maa-i-aa kai vaapaar. The Pandits are deluded, attached to duality, and they deal only in Maya.
DEFINE	para 28658	AMqir iqRsnw BuK hY mUrK BuiKAw muey gvwr ] (647-11, soriT, mÚ 3) antar tarisnaa bhukh hai moorakh bhukhi-aa mu-ay gavaar. They are filled with thirst and hunger; the ignorant fools starve to death.
DEFINE	para 28659	siqguir syivAY suKu pwieAw scY sbid vIcwir ] (647-12, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur sayvi-ai sukh paa-i-aa sachai sabad veechaar. Serving the True Guru, peace is obtained, contemplating the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 28660	AMdrhu iqRsnw BuK geI scY nwie ipAwir ] (647-12, soriT, mÚ 3) andrahu tarisnaa bhukh ga-ee sachai naa-ay pi-aar. Hunger and thirst have departed from within me; I am in love with the True Name.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk nwim rqy shjy rjy ijnw hir riKAw auir Dwir ]1] (647-13, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay sehjay rajay jinaa har rakhi-aa ur Dhaar. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, those who are imbued with the Naam, who keep the Lord clasped tightly to their hearts, are automatically satisfied. ||1||
RECORD	para 28662	mÚ 3 ] (647-14) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28663	mnmuK hir nwmu n syivAw duKu lgw bhuqw Awie ] (647-14, soriT, mÚ 3) manmukh har naam na sayvi-aa dukh lagaa bahutaa aa-ay. The self-willed manmukh does not serve the Lord's Name, and so he suffers in horrible pain.
DEFINE	para 28664	AMqir AigAwnu AMDyru hY suiD n kweI pwie ] (647-14, soriT, mÚ 3) antar agi-aan anDhayr hai suDh na kaa-ee paa-ay. He is filled with the darkness of ignorance, and he does not understand anything.
RECORD	para 28665	mnhiT shij n bIijE BuKw ik AgY Kwie ] (647-15, soriT, mÚ 3) manhath sahj na beeji-o bhukhaa ke agai khaa-ay. Because of his stubborn mind, he does not plant the seeds of intuitive peace; what will he eat in the world hereafter, to satisfy his hunger?
DEFINE	para 28666	nwmu inDwnu ivswirAw dUjY lgw jwie ] (647-15, soriT, mÚ 3) naam niDhaan visaari-aa doojai lagaa jaa-ay. He has forgotten the treasure of the Naam; he is caught in the love of duality.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk gurmuiK imlih vifAweIAw jy Awpy myil imlwie ]2] (647-16, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh mileh vadi-aa-ee-aa jay aapay mayl milaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are honored with glory, when the Lord Himself unites them in His Union. ||2||
RECORD	para 28668	pauVI ] (647-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28669	hir rsnw hir jsu gwvY KrI suhwvxI ] (647-16, soriT, mÚ 3) har rasnaa har jas gaavai kharee suhaavanee. The tongue which sings the Lord's Praises, is so very beautiful.
DEFINE	para 28670	jo min qin muiK hir bolY sw hir BwvxI ] (647-17, soriT, mÚ 3) jo man tan mukh har bolai saa har bhaavnee. One who speaks the Lord's Name, with mind, body and mouth, is pleasing to the Lord.
DEFINE	para 28671	jo gurmuiK cKY swdu sw iqRpqwvxI ] (647-17, soriT, mÚ 3) jo gurmukh chakhai saad saa tariptaavnee. That Gurmukh tastes the the sublime taste of the Lord, and is satisfied.
RECORD	para 28672	gux gwvY ipAwry inq gux gwie guxI smJwvxI ] (647-18, soriT, mÚ 3) gun gaavai pi-aaray nit gun gaa-ay gunee samjhaavanee. She sings continually the Glorious Praises of her Beloved; singing His Glorious Praises, she is uplifted.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v13	ijsu hovY Awip dieAwlu sw siqgurU gurU bulwvxI ]13] (647-18, soriT, mÚ 3) jis hovai aap da-i-aal saa satguroo guroo bulaavanee. ||13||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v13	She is blessed with the Lord's Mercy, and she chants the Words of the Guru, the True Guru. ||13||
RECORD	para 28674	sloku mÚ 3 ] (647-19) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28675	hsqI isir ijau AMksu hY Ahrix ijau isru dyie ] (647-19, soriT, mÚ 3) hastee sir ji-o ankas hai ahran ji-o sir day-ay. The elephant offers its head to the reins, and the anvil offers itself to the hammer;
RECORD	para 28676	mnu qnu AwgY rwiK kY aUBI syv kryie ] (647-19, soriT, mÚ 3) man tan aagai raakh kai oobhee sayv karay-i. just so, we offer our minds and bodies to our Guru; we stand before Him, and serve Him.
RECORD	para 28678	ieau gurmuiK Awpu invwrIAY sBu rwju isRsit kw lyie ] (648-1, soriT, mÚ 3) i-o gurmukh aap nivaaree-ai sabh raaj sarisat kaa lay-ay. This is how the Gurmukhs eliminate their self-conceit, and come to rule the whole world.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk gurmuiK buJIAY jw Awpy ndir kryie ]1] (648-1, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh bujhee-ai jaa aapay nadar karay-i. ||1||
WHEN	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukh understands, when the Lord casts His Glance of Grace. ||1||
RECORD	para 28680	mÚ 3 ] (648-2) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
UPHOLD	para 28681	ijn gurmuiK nwmu iDAwieAw Awey qy prvwxu ] (648-2, soriT, mÚ 3) jin gurmukh naam Dhi-aa-i-aa aa-ay tay parvaan. Blessed and approved is the coming into the world, of those Gurmukhs who meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk kul auDwrih Awpxw drgh pwvih mwxu ]2] (648-3, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak kul uDhaareh aapnaa dargeh paavahi maan. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, they save their families, and they are honored in the Court of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 28683	pauVI ] (648-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28684	gurmuiK sKIAw isK gurU mylweIAw ] (648-3, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh sakhee-aa sikh guroo maylaa-ee-aa. The Guru unites His Sikhs, the Gurmukhs, with the Lord.
RECORD	para 28685	ieik syvk gur pwis ieik guir kwrY lweIAw ] (648-4, soriT, mÚ 3) ik sayvak gur paas ik gur kaarai laa-ee-aa. The Guru keeps some of them with Himself, and engages others in His Service.
RECORD	para 28686	ijnw guru ipAwrw min iciq iqnw Bwau gurU dyvweIAw ] (648-4, soriT, mÚ 3) jinaa gur pi-aaraa man chit tinaa bhaa-o guroo dayvaa-ee-aa. Those who cherish their Beloved in their conscious minds, the Guru blesses them with His Love.
RECORD	para 28687	gur isKw ieko ipAwru gur imqw puqw BweIAw ] (648-5, soriT, mÚ 3) gur sikhaa iko pi-aar gur mitaa putaa bhaa-ee-aa. The Guru loves all of His Gursikhs equally well, like friends, children and siblings.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v14	guru siqguru bolhu siB guru AwiK gurU jIvweIAw ]14] (648-5, soriT, mÚ 3) gur satgur bolhu sabh gur aakh guroo jeevaa-ee-aa. ||14||
REQUIRE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v14	So chant the Name of the Guru, the True Guru, everyone! Chanting the Name of the Guru, Guru, you shall be rejuvenated. ||14||
RECORD	para 28689	sloku mÚ 3 ] (648-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28690	nwnk nwmu n cyqnI AigAwnI AMDuly Avry krm kmwih ] (648-6, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak naam na chaytnee agi-aanee anDhulay avray karam kamaahi. O Nanak, the blind, ignorant fools do not remember the Naam, the Name of the Lord; they involve themselves in other activities.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	jm dir bDy mwrIAih iPir ivstw mwih pcwih ]1] (648-7, soriT, mÚ 3) jam dar baDhay maaree-ah fir vistaa maahi pachaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	They are bound and gagged at the door of the Messenger of Death; they are punished, and in the end, they rot away in manure. ||1||
RECORD	para 28692	mÚ 3 ] (648-7) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28693	nwnk siqguru syvih Awpxw sy jn scy prvwxu ] (648-7, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak satgur sayveh aapnaa say jan sachay parvaan. O Nanak, those humble beings are true and approved, who serve their True Guru.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	hir kY nwie smwie rhy cUkw Awvxu jwxu ]2] (648-8, soriT, mÚ 3) har kai naa-ay samaa-ay rahay chookaa aavan jaan. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	They remain absorbed in the Name of the Lord, and their comings and goings cease. ||2||
RECORD	para 28695	pauVI ] (648-8) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28696	Dnu sMpY mwieAw sMcIAY AMqy duKdweI ] (648-8, soriT, mÚ 3) Dhan sampai maa-i-aa sanchee-ai antay dukh-daa-ee. Gathering the wealth and property of Maya, brings only pain in the end.
RECORD	para 28697	Gr mMdr mhl svwrIAih ikCu swiQ n jweI ] (648-9, soriT, mÚ 3) ghar mandar mahal savaaree-ah kichh saath na jaa-ee. Homes, mansions and adorned palaces will not go with anyone.
ALLOW	para 28698	hr rMgI qury inq pwlIAih ikqY kwim n AweI ] (648-9, soriT, mÚ 3) har rangee turay nit paalee-ah kitai kaam na aa-ee. He may breed horses of various colors, but these will not be of any use to him.
REQUIRE	para 28699	jn lwvhu icqu hir nwm isau AMiq hoie sKweI ] (648-10, soriT, mÚ 3) jan laavhu chit har naam si-o ant ho-ay sakhaa-ee. O human, link your consciousness to the Lord's Name, and in the end, it shall be your companion and helper.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v15	jn nwnk nwmu iDAwieAw gurmuiK suKu pweI ]15] (648-10, soriT, mÚ 3) jan naanak naam Dhi-aa-i-aa gurmukh sukh paa-ee. ||15||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v15	Servant Nanak meditates on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; the Gurmukh is blessed with peace. ||15||
RECORD	para 28701	sloku mÚ 3 ] (648-11) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28702	ibnu krmY nwau n pweIAY pUrY krim pwieAw jwie ] (648-11, soriT, mÚ 3) bin karmai naa-o na paa-ee-ai poorai karam paa-i-aa jaa-ay. Without the karma of good actions, the Name is not obtained; it can be obtained only by perfect good karma.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk ndir kry jy AwpxI qw gurmiq myil imlwie ]1] (648-12, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak nadar karay jay aapnee taa gurmat mayl milaa-ay. ||1||
WHEN	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, if the Lord casts His Glance of Grace, then under Guru's Instruction, one is united in His Union. ||1||
RECORD	para 28704	mÚ 1 ] (648-12) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28705	iek dJih iek dbIAih ieknw kuqy Kwih ] (648-12, soriT, mÚ 1) ik dajheh ik dabee-ah iknaa kutay khaahi. Some are cremated, and some are buried; some are eaten by dogs.
DEFINE	para 28706	ieik pwxI ivic austIAih ieik BI iPir hsix pwih ] (648-13, soriT, mÚ 1) ik paanee vich ustee-ah ik bhee fir hasan paahi. Some are thrown into water, while others are thrown into wells.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk eyv n jwpeI ikQY jwie smwih ]2] (648-14, soriT, mÚ 1) naanak ayv na jaap-ee kithai jaa-ay samaahi. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, it is not known, where they go and into what they merge. ||2||
RECORD	para 28708	pauVI ] (648-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28709	iqn kw KwDw pYDw mwieAw sBu pivqu hY jo nwim hir rwqy ] (648-14, soriT, mÚ 1) tin kaa khaaDhaa paiDhaa maa-i-aa sabh pavit hai jo naam har raatay. The food and clothes, and all the worldly possessions of those who are attuned to the Lord's Name are sacred.
RECORD	para 28711	iqn ky qury jIn KurgIr siB pivqu hih ijnI gurmuiK isK swD sMq ciV jwqy ] (648-16, soriT, mÚ 1) tin kay turay jeen khurgeer sabh pavit heh jinee gurmukh sikh saaDh sant charh jaatay. All the horses, saddles and horse blankets are sacred, upon which the Gurmukhs, the Sikhs, the Holy and the Saints, mount and ride.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v16	ijn kY poqY puMnu hY sy gurmuiK isK gurU pih jwqy ]16] (648-18, soriT, mÚ 1) jin kai potai punn hai say gurmukh sikh guroo peh jaatay. ||16||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v16	Those Gurmukhs, those Sikhs, who have purity as their treasure, go to their Guru. ||16||
RECORD	para 28714	sloku mÚ 3 ] (648-18) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28715	nwnk nwvhu GuiQAw hlqu plqu sBu jwie ] (648-18, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak naavhu ghuthi-aa halat palat sabh jaa-ay. O Nanak, forsaking the Name, he loses everything, in this world and the next.
RECORD	para 28716	jpu qpu sMjmu sBu ihir lieAw muTI dUjY Bwie ] (648-19, soriT, mÚ 3) jap tap sanjam sabh hir la-i-aa muthee doojai bhaa-ay. Chanting, deep meditation and austere self-disciplined practices are all wasted; he is deceived by the love of duality.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	jm dir bDy mwrIAih bhuqI imlY sjwie ]1] (648-19, soriT, mÚ 3) jam dar baDhay maaree-ah bahutee milai sajaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	He is bound and gagged at the door of the Messenger of Death. He is beaten, and receives terrible punishment. ||1||
RECORD	para 28719	mÚ 3 ] (649-1) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28720	sMqw nwil vYru kmwvdy dustw nwil mohu ipAwru ] (649-1, soriT, mÚ 3) santaa naal vair kamaavday dustaa naal moh pi-aar. They inflict their hatred upon the Saints, and they love the wicked sinners.
DEFINE	para 28721	AgY ipCY suKu nhI mir jMmih vwro vwr ] (649-1, soriT, mÚ 3) agai pichhai sukh nahee mar jameh vaaro vaar. They find no peace in either this world or the next; they are born only to die, again and again.
DEFINE	para 28722	iqRsnw kdy n buJeI duibDw hoie KuAwru ] (649-2, soriT, mÚ 3) tarisnaa kaday na bujh-ee dubiDhaa ho-ay khu-aar. Their hunger is never satisfied, and they are ruined by duality.
DEFINE	para 28723	muh kwly iqnw inMdkw iqqu scY drbwir ] (649-2, soriT, mÚ 3) muh kaalay tinaa nindkaa tit sachai darbaar. The faces of these slanderers are blackened in the Court of the True Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk nwm ivhUixAw nw aurvwir n pwir ]2] (649-3, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak naam vihooni-aa naa urvaar na paar. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, without the Naam, they find no shelter on either this shore, or the one beyond. ||2||
RECORD	para 28725	pauVI ] (649-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28726	jo hir nwmu iDAwiedy sy hir hir nwim rqy mn mwhI ] (649-3, soriT, mÚ 3) jo har naam Dhi-aa-iday say har har naam ratay man maahee. Those who meditate on the Lord's Name, are imbued with the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, in their minds.
RECORD	para 28727	ijnw min iciq ieku ArwiDAw iqnw ieks ibnu dUjw ko nwhI ] (649-4, soriT, mÚ 3) jinaa man chit ik araaDhi-aa tinaa ikas bin doojaa ko naahee. For those who worship the One Lord in their conscious minds, there is no other than the One Lord.
RECORD	para 28728	syeI purK hir syvdy ijn Duir msqik lyKu ilKwhI ] (649-5, soriT, mÚ 3) say-ee purakh har sayvday jin Dhur mastak laykh likhaahee. They alone serve the Lord, upon whose foreheads such pre-ordained destiny is written.
RECORD	para 28729	hir ky gux inq gwvdy hir gux gwie guxI smJwhI ] (649-5, soriT, mÚ 3) har kay gun nit gaavday har gun gaa-ay gunee samjhaahee. They continually sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and singing the Glories of the Glorious Lord, they are uplifted.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v17	vifAweI vfI gurmuKw gur pUrY hir nwim smwhI ]17] (649-6, soriT, mÚ 3) vadi-aa-ee vadee gurmukhaa gur poorai har naam samaahee. ||17||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v17	Great is the greatness of the Gurmukhs, who, through the Perfect Guru, remain absorbed in the Lord's Name. ||17||
RECORD	para 28731	sloku mÚ 3 ] (649-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28732	siqgur kI syvw gwKVI isru dIjY Awpu gvwie ] (649-6, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur kee sayvaa gaakh-rhee sir deejai aap gavaa-ay. It is very difficult to serve the True Guru; offer your head, and eradicate self-conceit.
REQUIRE	para 28733	sbid mrih iPir nw mrih qw syvw pvY sB Qwie ] (649-7, soriT, mÚ 3) sabad mareh fir naa mareh taa sayvaa pavai sabh thaa-ay. One who dies in the Word of the Shabad shall never have to die again; his service is totally approved.
RECORD	para 28734	pwrs prisAY pwrsu hovY sic rhY ilv lwie ] (649-8, soriT, mÚ 3) paaras parsi-ai paaras hovai sach rahai liv laa-ay. Touching the philosopher's stone, one becomes the philosopher's stone, which transforms lead into gold; remain lovingly attached to the True Lord.
RECORD	para 28735	ijsu pUrib hovY iliKAw iqsu siqguru imlY pRBu Awie ] (649-8, soriT, mÚ 3) jis poorab hovai likhi-aa tis satgur milai parabh aa-ay. One who has such pre-ordained destiny, comes to meet the True Guru and God.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk gxqY syvku nw imlY ijsu bKsy so pvY Qwie ]1] (649-9, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gantai sayvak naa milai jis bakhsay so pavai thaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, the Lord's servant does not meet Him because of his own account; he alone is acceptable, whom the Lord forgives. ||1||
RECORD	para 28737	mÚ 3 ] (649-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28738	mhlu kumhlu n jwxnI mUrK ApxY suAwie ] (649-9, soriT, mÚ 3) mahal kumhal na jaannee moorakh apnai su-aa-ay. The fools do not know the difference between good and bad; they are deceived by their self-interests.
WHEN	para 28739	sbdu cInih qw mhlu lhih joqI joiq smwie ] (649-10, soriT, mÚ 3) sabad cheeneh taa mahal laheh jotee jot samaa-ay. But if they contemplate the Word of the Shabad, they obtain the Mansion of the Lord's Presence, and their light merges in the Light.
DEFINE	para 28740	sdw scy kw Bau min vsY qw sBw soJI pwie ] (649-10, soriT, mÚ 3) sadaa sachay kaa bha-o man vasai taa sabhaa sojhee paa-ay. The Fear of God is always on their minds, and so they come to understand everything.
DEFINE	para 28741	siqguru ApxY Gir vrqdw Awpy ley imlwie ] (649-11, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur apnai ghar varatdaa aapay la-ay milaa-ay. The True Guru is pervading the homes within; He Himself blends them with the Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk siqguir imilAY sB pUrI peI ijs no ikrpw kry rjwie ]2] (649-11, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak satgur mili-ai sabh pooree pa-ee jis no kirpaa karay rajaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, they meet the True Guru, and all their desires are fulfilled, if the Lord grants His Grace and so wills. ||2||
RECORD	para 28743	pauVI ] (649-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
UPHOLD	para 28744	DMnu Dnu Bwg iqnw Bgq jnw jo hir nwmw hir muiK khiqAw ] (649-12, soriT, mÚ 3) Dhan Dhan bhaag tinaa bhagat janaa jo har naamaa har mukh kehti-aa. Blessed, blessed is the good fortune of those devotees, who, with their mouths, utter the Name of the Lord.
UPHOLD	para 28745	Dnu Dnu Bwg iqnw sMq jnw jo hir jsu sRvxI suxiqAw ] (649-13, soriT, mÚ 3) Dhan Dhan bhaag tinaa sant janaa jo har jas sarvanee sunti-aa. Blessed, blessed is the good fortune of those Saints, who, with their ears, listen to the Lord's Praises.
UPHOLD	para 28746	Dnu Dnu Bwg iqnw swD jnw hir kIrqnu gwie guxI jn bxiqAw ] (649-13, soriT, mÚ 3) Dhan Dhan bhaag tinaa saaDh janaa har keertan gaa-ay gunee jan banti-aa. Blessed, blessed is the good fortune of those holy people, who sing the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises, and so become virtuous.
UPHOLD	para 28747	Dnu Dnu Bwg iqnw gurmuKw jo gurisK lY mnu ijxiqAw ] (649-14, soriT, mÚ 3) Dhan Dhan bhaag tinaa gurmukhaa jo gursikh lai man jinti-aa. Blessed, blessed is the good fortune of those Gurmukhs, who live as Gursikhs, and conquer their minds.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v18	sB dU vfy Bwg gurisKw ky jo gur crxI isK pViqAw ]18] (649-15, soriT, mÚ 3) sabh doo vaday bhaag gursikhaa kay jo gur charnee sikh parh-ti-aa. ||18||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v18	But the greatest good fortune of all, is that of the Guru's Sikhs, who fall at the Guru's feet. ||18||
RECORD	para 28749	sloku mÚ 3 ] (649-15) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28750	bRhmu ibMdY iqs dw bRhmqu rhY eyk sbid ilv lwie ] (649-15, soriT, mÚ 3) barahm bindai tis daa barahmat rahai ayk sabad liv laa-ay. One who knows God, and who lovingly focuses his attention on the One Word of the Shabad, keeps his spirituality intact.
RECORD	para 28751	nv inDI ATwrh isDI ipCY lgIAw iPrih jo hir ihrdY sdw vswie ] (649-16, soriT, mÚ 3) nav niDhee athaarah siDhee pichhai lagee-aa fireh jo har hirdai sadaa vasaa-ay. The nine treasures and the eighteen spiritual powers of the Siddhas follow him, who keeps the Lord enshrined in his heart.
DEFINE	para 28752	ibnu siqgur nwau n pweIAY buJhu kir vIcwru ] (649-17, soriT, mÚ 3) bin satgur naa-o na paa-ee-ai bujhahu kar veechaar. Without the True Guru, the Name is not found; understand this, and reflect upon it.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk pUrY Bwig siqguru imlY suKu pwey jug cwir ]1] (649-17, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak poorai bhaag satgur milai sukh paa-ay jug chaar. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, through perfect good destiny, one meets the True Guru, and finds peace, throughout the four ages. ||1||
RECORD	para 28754	mÚ 3 ] (649-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28755	ikAw gBrU ikAw ibriD hY mnmuK iqRsnw BuK n jwie ] (649-18, soriT, mÚ 3) ki-aa gabhroo ki-aa biraDh hai manmukh tarisnaa bhukh na jaa-ay. Whether he is young or old, the self-willed manmukh cannot escape hunger and thirst.
RECORD	para 28756	gurmuiK sbdy riqAw sIqlu hoey Awpu gvwie ] (649-19, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh sabday rati-aa seetal ho-ay aap gavaa-ay. The Gurmukhs are imbued with the Word of the Shabad; they are at peace, having lost their self-conceit.
DEFINE	para 28757	AMdru iqRpiq sMqoiKAw iPir BuK n lgY Awie ] (649-19, soriT, mÚ 3) andar taripat santokhi-aa fir bhukh na lagai aa-ay. They are satisfied and satiated within; they never feel hungry again.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk ij gurmuiK krih so prvwxu hY jo nwim rhy ilv lwie ]2] (650-1, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak je gurmukh karahi so parvaan hai jo naam rahay liv laa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, whatever the Gurmukhs do is acceptable; they remain lovingly absorbed in the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 28760	pauVI ] (650-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28761	hau bilhwrI iqMn kMau jo gurmuiK isKw ] (650-1, soriT, mÚ 3) ha-o balihaaree tinn ka N-u jo gurmukh sikhaa. I am a sacrifice to those Sikhs who are Gurmukhs.
UPHOLD	para 28762	jo hir nwmu iDAwiedy iqn drsnu ipKw ] (650-2, soriT, mÚ 3) jo har naam Dhi-aa-iday tin darsan pikhaa. I behold the Blessed Vision, the Darshan of those who meditate on the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 28763	suix kIrqnu hir gux rvw hir jsu min ilKw ] (650-2, soriT, mÚ 3) sun keertan har gun ravaa har jas man likhaa. Listening to the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises, I contemplate His virtues; I write His Praises on the fabric of my mind.
RECORD	para 28764	hir nwmu slwhI rMg isau siB iklivK ik®Kw ] (650-3, soriT, mÚ 3) har naam salaahee rang si-o sabh kilvikh krikhaa. I praise the Lord's Name with love, and eradicate all my sins.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v19	Dnu DMnu suhwvw so srIru Qwnu hY ijQY myrw guru Dry ivKw ]19] (650-3, soriT, mÚ 3) Dhan Dhan suhaavaa so sareer thaan hai jithai mayraa gur Dharay vikhaa. ||19||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v19	Blessed, blessed and beauteous is that body and place, where my Guru places His feet. ||19||
RECORD	para 28766	sloku mÚ 3 ] (650-4) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28767	gur ibnu igAwnu n hoveI nw suKu vsY min Awie ] (650-4, soriT, mÚ 3) gur bin gi-aan na hova-ee naa sukh vasai man aa-ay. Without the Guru, spiritual wisdom is not obtained, and peace does not come to abide in the mind.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk nwm ivhUxy mnmuKI jwsin jnmu gvwie ]1] (650-5, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak naam vihoonay manmukhee jaasan janam gavaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, without the Naam, the Name of the Lord, the self-willed manmukhs depart, after having wasted their lives. ||1||
RECORD	para 28769	mÚ 3 ] (650-5) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28770	isD swiDk nwvY no siB Kojdy Qik rhy ilv lwie ] (650-5, soriT, mÚ 3) siDh saaDhik naavai no sabh khojday thak rahay liv laa-ay. All the Siddhas, spiritual masters and seekers search for the Name; they have grown weary of concentrating and focusing their attention.
RECORD	para 28771	ibnu siqgur iknY n pwieE gurmuiK imlY imlwie ] (650-6, soriT, mÚ 3) bin satgur kinai na paa-i-o gurmukh milai milaa-ay. Without the True Guru, no one finds the Name; the Gurmukhs unite in Union with the Lord.
UPHOLD	para 28772	ibnu nwvY pYnxu Kwxu sBu bwid hY iDgu isDI iDgu krmwiq ] (650-6, soriT, mÚ 3) bin naavai painan khaan sabh baad hai Dhig siDhee Dhig karmaat. Without the Name, all food and clothes are worthless; cursed is such spirituality, and cursed are such miraculous powers.
RECORD	para 28773	sw isiD sw krmwiq hY AicMqu kry ijsu dwiq ] (650-7, soriT, mÚ 3) saa siDh saa karmaat hai achint karay jis daat. That alone is spirituality, and that alone is miraculous power, which the Carefree Lord spontaneously bestows.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk gurmuiK hir nwmu min vsY eyhw isiD eyhw krmwiq ]2] (650-7, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh har naam man vasai ayhaa siDh ayhaa karmaat. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, the Lord's Name abides in the mind of the Gurmukh; this is spirituality, and this is miraculous power. ||2||
RECORD	para 28775	pauVI ] (650-8) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28776	hm FwFI hir pRB Ksm ky inq gwvh hir gux CMqw ] (650-8, soriT, mÚ 3) ham dhaadhee har parabh khasam kay nit gaavah har gun chhantaa. I am a minstrel of God, my Lord and Master; every day, I sing the songs of the Lord's Glorious Praises.
RECORD	para 28777	hir kIrqnu krh hir jsu suxh iqsu kvlw kMqw ] (650-9, soriT, mÚ 3) har keertan karah har jas sunah tis kavlaa kantaa. I sing the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises, and I listen to the Praises of the Lord, the Master of wealth and Maya.
DEFINE	para 28778	hir dwqw sBu jgqu iBKwrIAw mMgq jn jMqw ] (650-9, soriT, mÚ 3) har daataa sabh jagat bhikhaaree-aa mangat jan jantaa. The Lord is the Great Giver; all the world is begging; all beings and creatures are beggars.
RECORD	para 28779	hir dyvhu dwnu dieAwl hoie ivic pwQr ik®m jMqw ] (650-10, soriT, mÚ 3) har dayvhu daan da-i-aal ho-ay vich paathar kiram jantaa. O Lord, You are kind and compassionate; You give Your gifts to even worms and insects among the rocks.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v20	jn nwnk nwmu iDAwieAw gurmuiK DnvMqw ]20] (650-10, soriT, mÚ 3) jan naanak naam Dhi-aa-i-aa gurmukh Dhanvantaa. ||20||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v20	Servant Nanak meditates on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; as Gurmukh, he has become truly wealthy. ||20||
RECORD	para 28781	sloku mÚ 3 ] (650-11) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
WHEN	para 28782	pVxw guVxw sMswr kI kwr hY AMdir iqRsnw ivkwru ] (650-11, soriT, mÚ 3) parh-naa gurh-naa sansaar kee kaar hai andar tarisnaa vikaar. Reading and studying are just worldly pursuits, if there is thirst and corruption within.
RECORD	para 28783	haumY ivic siB piV Qky dUjY Bwie KuAwru ] (650-12, soriT, mÚ 3) ha-umai vich sabh parh thakay doojai bhaa-ay khu-aar. Reading in egotism, all have grown weary; through the love of duality, they are ruined.
RECORD	para 28784	so piVAw so pMifqu bInw gur sbid kry vIcwru ] (650-12, soriT, mÚ 3) so parhi-aa so pandit beenaa gur sabad karay veechaar. He alone is educated, and he alone is a wise Pandit, who contemplates the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 28785	AMdru KojY qqu lhY pwey moK duAwru ] (650-13, soriT, mÚ 3) andar khojai tat lahai paa-ay mokh du-aar. He searches within himself, and finds the true essence; he finds the Door of Salvation.
RECORD	para 28786	gux inDwnu hir pwieAw shij kry vIcwru ] (650-13, soriT, mÚ 3) gun niDhaan har paa-i-aa sahj karay veechaar. He finds the Lord, the treasure of excellence, and peacefully contemplates Him.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	DMnu vwpwrI nwnkw ijsu gurmuiK nwmu ADwru ]1] (650-14, soriT, mÚ 3) Dhan vaapaaree naankaa jis gurmukh naam aDhaar. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	Blessed is the trader, O Nanak, who, as Gurmukh, takes the Name as his only Support. ||1||
RECORD	para 28788	mÚ 3 ] (650-14) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28789	ivxu mnu mwry koie n isJeI vyKhu ko ilv lwie ] (650-14, soriT, mÚ 3) vin man maaray ko-ay na sijh-ee vaykhhu ko liv laa-ay. Without conquering his mind, no one can be successful. See this, and concentrate on it.
RECORD	para 28790	ByKDwrI qIrQI Biv Qky nw eyhu mnu mwirAw jwie ] (650-15, soriT, mÚ 3) bhaykh-Dhaaree teerthee bhav thakay naa ayhu man maari-aa jaa-ay. The wandering holy men are tired of of making pilgrimages to sacred shrines; they have not been able to conquer their minds.
RECORD	para 28791	gurmuiK eyhu mnu jIvqu mrY sic rhY ilv lwie ] (650-15, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh ayhu man jeevat marai sach rahai liv laa-ay. The Gurmukh has conquered his mind, and he remains lovingly absorbed in the True Lord.
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk iesu mn kI mlu ieau auqrY haumY sbid jlwie ]2] (650-16, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak is man kee mal i-o utrai ha-umai sabad jalaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, this is how the filth of the mind is removed; the Word of the Shabad burns away the ego. ||2||
RECORD	para 28793	pauVI ] (650-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28794	hir hir sMq imlhu myry BweI hir nwmu idRVwvhu iek iknkw ] (650-17, soriT, mÚ 3) har har sant milhu mayray bhaa-ee har naam darirhaavahu ik kinkaa. O Saints of the Lord, O my Siblings of Destiny, please meet with me, and implant the Name of the One Lord within me.
RECORD	para 28795	hir hir sIgwru bnwvhu hir jn hir kwpVu pihrhu iKm kw ] (650-17, soriT, mÚ 3) har har seegaar banaavahu har jan har kaaparh pahirahu khim kaa. O humble servants of the Lord, adorn me with the decorations of the Lord, Har, Har; let me wear the robes of the Lord's forgiveness.
DEFINE	para 28796	AYsw sIgwru myry pRB BwvY hir lwgY ipAwrw ipRm kw ] (650-18, soriT, mÚ 3) aisaa seegaar mayray parabh bhaavai har laagai pi-aaraa parim kaa. Such decorations are pleasing to my God; such love is dear to the Lord.
RECORD	para 28797	hir hir nwmu bolhu idnu rwqI siB iklibK kwtY iek plkw ] (650-18, soriT, mÚ 3) har har naam bolhu din raatee sabh kilbikh kaatai ik palkaa. I chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, day and night; in an instant, all sins are eradicated.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v21	hir hir dieAwlu hovY ijsu aupir so gurmuiK hir jip ijxkw ]21] (650-19, soriT, mÚ 3) har har da-i-aal hovai jis upar so gurmukh har jap jinkaa. ||21||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v21	That Gurmukh, unto whom the Lord becomes merciful, chants the Lord's Name, and wins the game of life. ||21||
RECORD	para 28800	sloku mÚ 3 ] (651-1) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28801	jnm jnm kI iesu mn kau mlu lwgI kwlw hoAw isAwhu ] (651-1, soriT, mÚ 3) janam janam kee is man ka-o mal laagee kaalaa ho-aa si-aahu. The filth of countless incarnations sticks to this mind; it has become pitch black.
DEFINE	para 28802	KMnlI DoqI aujlI n hoveI jy sau Dovix pwhu ] (651-2, soriT, mÚ 3) khanlee Dhotee ujlee na hova-ee jay sa-o Dhovan paahu. The oily rag cannot be cleaned by merely washing it, even if it is washed a hundred times.
RECORD	para 28803	gur prswdI jIvqu mrY aultI hovY miq bdlwhu ] (651-2, soriT, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee jeevat marai ultee hovai mat badlaahu. By Guru's Grace, one remains dead while yet alive; his intellect is transformed, and he becomes detached from the world.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk mYlu n lgeI nw iPir jonI pwhu ]1] (651-3, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak mail na lag-ee naa fir jonee paahu. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, no filth sticks to him, and he does not fall into the womb again. ||1||
RECORD	para 28805	mÚ 3 ] (651-3) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28806	chu jugI kil kwlI kWFI iek auqm pdvI iesu jug mwih ] (651-3, soriT, mÚ 3) chahu jugee kal kaalee kaa Ndhee ik utam padvee is jug maahi. Kali Yuga is called the Dark Age, but the most sublime state is attained in this age.
RECORD	para 28807	gurmuiK hir kIriq Plu pweIAY ijn kau hir iliK pwih ] (651-4, soriT, mÚ 3) gurmukh har keerat fal paa-ee-ai jin ka-o har likh paahi. The Gurmukh obtains the fruit, the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises; this is his destiny, ordained by the Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk gur prswdI Anidnu Bgiq hir aucrih hir BgqI mwih smwih ]2] (651-4, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gur parsaadee an-din bhagat har uchrahi har bhagtee maahi samaahi. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, by Guru's Grace, he worships the Lord night and day; he chants the Lord's Name, and remains absorbed in the Lord's devotional worship. ||2||
RECORD	para 28809	pauVI ] (651-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
ALLOW	para 28810	hir hir myil swD jn sMgiq muiK bolI hir hir BlI bwix ] (651-5, soriT, mÚ 3) har har mayl saaDh jan sangat mukh bolee har har bhalee baan. O Lord, unite me with the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, so that with my mouth, I may speak the sublime Word of the Guru's Bani.
RECORD	para 28811	hir gux gwvw hir inq cvw gurmqI hir rMgu sdw mwix ] (651-6, soriT, mÚ 3) har gun gaavaa har nit chavaa gurmatee har rang sadaa maan. I sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and constantly chant the Lord's Name; through the Guru's Teachings, I enjoy the Lord's Love constantly.
RECORD	para 28812	hir jip jip AauKD KwiDAw siB rog gvwqy duKw Gwix ] (651-7, soriT, mÚ 3) har jap jap a-ukhaDh khaaDhi-aa sabh rog gavaatay dukhaa ghaan. I take the medicine of meditation on the Lord's Name, which has cured all diseases and multitudes of sufferings.
RECORD	para 28813	ijnw swis igrwis n ivsrY sy hir jn pUry shI jwix ] (651-7, soriT, mÚ 3) jinaa saas giraas na visrai say har jan pooray sahee jaan. Those who do not forget the Lord, while breathing or eating - know them to be the perfect servants of the Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v22	jo gurmuiK hir AwrwDdy iqn cUkI jm kI jgq kwix ]22] (651-8, soriT, mÚ 3) jo gurmukh har aaraaDhaday tin chookee jam kee jagat kaan. ||22||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v22	Those Gurmukhs who worship the Lord in adoration end their subservience to the Messenger of Death, and to the world. ||22||
RECORD	para 28815	sloku mÚ 3 ] (651-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 28816	ry jn auQwrY dibEhu suiqAw geI ivhwie ] (651-9, soriT, mÚ 3) ray jan uthaarai dabi-ohu suti-aa ga-ee vihaa-ay. O man, you have been tormented by a nightmare, and you have passed your life in sleep.
RECORD	para 28817	siqgur kw sbdu suix n jwigE AMqir n aupijE cwau ] (651-9, soriT, mÚ 3) satgur kaa sabad sun na jaagi-o antar na upji-o chaa-o. You did not wake to hear the Word of the True Guru's Shabad; you have no inspiration within yourself.
RECORD	para 28818	srIru jlau gux bwhrw jo gur kwr n kmwie ] (651-10, soriT, mÚ 3) sareer jala-o gun baahraa jo gur kaar na kamaa-ay. That body burns, which has no virtue, and which does not serve the Guru.
DEFINE	para 28819	jgqu jlµdw ifTu mY haumY dUjY Bwie ] (651-10, soriT, mÚ 3) jagat jalandaa dith mai ha-umai doojai bhaa-ay. I have seen that the world is burning, in egotism and the love of duality.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk gur srxweI aubry scu min sbid iDAwie ]1] (651-11, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak gur sarnaa-ee ubray sach man sabad Dhi-aa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, those who seek the Guru's Sanctuary are saved; within their minds, they meditate on the True Word of the Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	para 28821	mÚ 3 ] (651-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28822	sbid rqy haumY geI soBwvMqI nwir ] (651-11, soriT, mÚ 3) sabad ratay ha-umai ga-ee sobhaavantee naar. Attuned to the Word of the Shabad, the soul-bride is rid of egotism, and she is glorified.
DEFINE	para 28823	ipr kY BwxY sdw clY qw binAw sIgwru ] (651-12, soriT, mÚ 3) pir kai bhaanai sadaa chalai taa bani-aa seegaar. If she walks steadily in the way of His Will, then she is adorned with decorations.
RECORD	para 28824	syj suhwvI sdw ipru rwvY hir vru pwieAw nwir ] (651-12, soriT, mÚ 3) sayj suhaavee sadaa pir raavai har var paa-i-aa naar. Her couch becomes beautiful, and she constantly enjoys her Husband Lord; she obtains the Lord as her Husband.
DEFINE	para 28825	nw hir mrY n kdy duKu lwgY sdw suhwgix nwir ] (651-13, soriT, mÚ 3) naa har marai na kaday dukh laagai sadaa suhaagan naar. The Lord does not die, and she never suffers pain; she is a happy soul-bride forever.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk hir pRB myil leI gur kY hyiq ipAwir ]2] (651-13, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak har parabh mayl la-ee gur kai hayt pi-aar. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, the Lord God unites her with Himself; she enshrines love and affection for the Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 28827	pauVI ] (651-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28828	ijnw guru goipAw Awpxw qy nr buirAwrI ] (651-14, soriT, mÚ 3) jinaa gur gopi-aa aapnaa tay nar buri-aaree. Those who conceal and deny their Guru, are the most evil people.
DEFINE	para 28829	hir jIau iqn kw drsnu nw krhu pwipst hiqAwrI ] (651-14, soriT, mÚ 3) har jee-o tin kaa darsan naa karahu paapisat hati-aaree. O Dear Lord, let me not even see them; they are the worst sinners and murderers.
RECORD	para 28830	Eih Gir Gir iPrih kusuD min ijau Drkt nwrI ] (651-15, soriT, mÚ 3) ohi ghar ghar fireh kusuDh man ji-o Dharkat naaree. They wander from house to house, with impure minds, like wicked, forsaken women.
ALLOW	para 28831	vfBwgI sMgiq imly gurmuiK svwrI ] (651-16, soriT, mÚ 3) vadbhaagee sangat milay gurmukh savaaree. But by great good fortune, they may meet the Company of the Holy; as Gurmukhs, they are reformed.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v23	hir mylhu siqgur dieAw kir gur kau bilhwrI ]23] (651-16, soriT, mÚ 3) har maylhu satgur da-i-aa kar gur ka-o balihaaree. ||23||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v23	O Lord, please be kind and let me meet the True Guru; I am a sacrifice to the Guru. ||23||
RECORD	para 28833	sloku mÚ 3 ] (651-17) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28834	gur syvw qy suKu aUpjY iPir duKu n lgY Awie ] (651-17, soriT, mÚ 3) gur sayvaa tay sukh oopjai fir dukh na lagai aa-ay. Serving the Guru, peace is produced, and then, one does not suffer in pain.
DEFINE	para 28835	jMmxu mrxw imit gieAw kwlY kw ikCu n bswie ] (651-17, soriT, mÚ 3) jaman marnaa mit ga-i-aa kaalai kaa kichh na basaa-ay. The cycle of birth and death is brought to an end, and death has no power over at all.
DEFINE	para 28836	hir syqI mnu riv rihAw scy rihAw smwie ] (651-18, soriT, mÚ 3) har saytee man rav rahi-aa sachay rahi-aa samaa-ay. His mind is imbued with the Lord, and he remains merged in the True Lord.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	nwnk hau bilhwrI iqMn kau jo clin siqgur Bwie ]1] (651-18, soriT, mÚ 3) naanak ha-o balihaaree tinn ka-o jo chalan satgur bhaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	O Nanak, I am a sacrifice to those who walk in the Way of the True Guru's Will. ||1||
RECORD	para 28838	mÚ 3 ] (651-19) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
ALLOW	para 28839	ibnu sbdY suDu n hoveI jy Anyk krY sIgwr ] (651-19, soriT, mÚ 3) bin sabdai suDh na hova-ee jay anayk karai seegaar. Without the Word of the Shabad, purity is not obtained, even though the soul-bride may adorn herself with all sorts of decorations.
DEFINE	para 28841	ipr kI swr n jwxeI dUjY Bwie ipAwru ] (652-1, soriT, mÚ 3) pir kee saar na jaan-ee doojai bhaa-ay pi-aar. She does not know the value of her Husband Lord; she is attached to the love of duality.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	sw kusuD sw kulKxI nwnk nwrI ivic kunwir ]2] (652-1, soriT, mÚ 3) saa kusuDh saa kulkhanee naanak naaree vich kunaar. ||2||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	She is impure, and ill-mannered, O Nanak; among women, she is the most evil woman. ||2||
RECORD	para 28843	pauVI ] (652-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28844	hir hir ApxI dieAw kir hir bolI bYxI ] (652-2, soriT, mÚ 3) har har apnee da-i-aa kar har bolee bainee. Be kind to me, Lord, that I might chant the Word of Your Bani.
ALLOW	para 28845	hir nwmu iDAweI hir aucrw hir lwhw lYxI ] (652-2, soriT, mÚ 3) har naam Dhi-aa-ee har uchraa har laahaa lainee. May I meditate on the Lord's Name, chant the Lord's Name, and obtain the profit of the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 28846	jo jpdy hir hir idnsu rwiq iqn hau kurbYxI ] (652-3, soriT, mÚ 3) jo japday har har dinas raat tin ha-o kurbainee. I am a sacrifice to those who chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, day and night.
ALLOW	para 28847	ijnw siqguru myrw ipAwrw ArwiDAw iqn jn dyKw nYxI ] (652-3, soriT, mÚ 3) jinaa satgur mayraa pi-aaraa araaDhi-aa tin jan daykhaa nainee. May I behold with my eyes those who worship and adore my Beloved True Guru.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v24	hau vwirAw Apxy gurU kau ijin myrw hir sjxu myilAw sYxI ]24] (652-4, soriT, mÚ 3) ha-o vaari-aa apnay guroo ka-o jin mayraa har sajan mayli-aa sainee. ||24||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v24	I am a sacrifice to my Guru, who has united me with my Lord, my friend, my very best friend. ||24||
RECORD	para 28849	sloku mÚ 4 ] (652-5) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 28850	hir dwsn isau pRIiq hY hir dwsn ko imqu ] (652-5, soriT, mÚ 4) har daasan si-o pareet hai har daasan ko mit. The Lord loves His slaves; the Lord is the friend of His slaves.
RECORD	para 28851	hir dwsn kY vis hY ijau jMqI kY vis jMqu ] (652-5, soriT, mÚ 4) har daasan kai vas hai ji-o jantee kai vas jant. The Lord is under the control of His slaves, like the musical instrument under the control of the musician.
RECORD	para 28852	hir ky dws hir iDAwiedy kir pRIqm isau nyhu ] (652-6, soriT, mÚ 4) har kay daas har Dhi-aa-iday kar pareetam si-o nayhu. The Lord's slaves meditate on the Lord; they love their Beloved.
RECORD	para 28853	ikrpw kir kY sunhu pRB sB jg mih vrsY myhu ] (652-6, soriT, mÚ 4) kirpaa kar kai sunhu parabh sabh jag meh varsai mayhu. Please, hear me, O God - let Your Grace rain over the whole world.
DEFINE	para 28854	jo hir dwsn kI ausqiq hY sw hir kI vifAweI ] (652-7, soriT, mÚ 4) jo har daasan kee ustat hai saa har kee vadi-aa-ee. The praise of the Lord's slaves is the Glory of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 28855	hir AwpxI vifAweI BwvdI jn kw jYkwru krweI ] (652-7, soriT, mÚ 4) har aapnee vadi-aa-ee bhaavdee jan kaa jaikaar karaa-ee. The Lord loves His Own Glory, and so His humble servant is celebrated and hailed.
RECORD	para 28856	so hir jnu nwmu iDAwiedw hir hir jnu iek smwin ] (652-8, soriT, mÚ 4) so har jan naam Dhi-aa-idaa har har jan ik samaan. That humble servant of the Lord meditates on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; the Lord, and the Lord's humble servant, are one and the same.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	jnu nwnku hir kw dwsu hY hir pYj rKhu Bgvwn ]1] (652-8, soriT, mÚ 4) jan naanak har kaa daas hai har paij rakhahu bhagvaan. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	Servant Nanak is the slave of the Lord; O Lord, O God, please, preserve his honor. ||1||
RECORD	para 28858	mÚ 4 ] (652-9) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 28859	nwnk pRIiq lweI iqin swcY iqsu ibnu rhxu n jweI ] (652-9, soriT, mÚ 4) naanak pareet laa-ee tin saachai tis bin rahan na jaa-ee. Nanak loves the True Lord; without Him, he cannot even survive.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	siqguru imlY q pUrw pweIAY hir ris rsn rsweI ]2] (652-10, soriT, mÚ 4) satgur milai ta pooraa paa-ee-ai har ras rasan rasaa-ee. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	Meeting the True Guru, one finds the Perfect Lord, and the tongue enjoys the sublime essence of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 28861	pauVI ] (652-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 28862	rYix idnsu prBwiq qUhY hI gwvxw ] (652-10, soriT, mÚ 4) rain dinas parbhaat toohai hee gaavnaa. Night and day, morning and night, I sing to You, Lord.
RECORD	para 28863	jIA jMq srbq nwau qyrw iDAwvxw ] (652-11, soriT, mÚ 4) jee-a jant sarbat naa-o tayraa Dhi-aavanaa. All beings and creatures meditate on Your Name.
DEFINE	para 28864	qU dwqw dwqwru qyrw idqw Kwvxw ] (652-11, soriT, mÚ 4) too daataa daataar tayraa ditaa khaavnaa. You are the Giver, the Great Giver; we eat whatever You give us.
DEFINE	para 28865	Bgq jnw kY sMig pwp gvwvxw ] (652-11, soriT, mÚ 4) bhagat janaa kai sang paap gavaavnaa. In the congregation of the devotees, sins are eradicated.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v25	jn nwnk sd bilhwrY bil bil jwvxw ]25] (652-12, soriT, mÚ 4) jan naanak sad balihaarai bal bal jaavnaa. ||25||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v25	Servant Nanak is forever a sacrifice, a sacrifice, a sacrifice, O Lord. ||25||
RECORD	para 28867	sloku mÚ 4 ] (652-12) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 28868	AMqir AigAwnu BeI miq miDm siqgur kI prqIiq nwhI ] (652-12, soriT, mÚ 4) antar agi-aan bha-ee mat maDhim satgur kee parteet naahee. He has spiritual ignorance within, and his intellect is dull and dim; he does not place his faith in the True Guru.
RECORD	para 28869	AMdir kptu sBu kpto kir jwxY kpty Kpih KpwhI ] (652-13, soriT, mÚ 4) andar kapat sabh kapto kar jaanai kaptay khapeh khapaahee. He has deceit within himself, and so he sees deception in all others; through his deceptions, he is totally ruined.
RECORD	para 28870	siqgur kw Bwxw iciq n AwvY AwpxY suAwie iPrwhI ] (652-14, soriT, mÚ 4) satgur kaa bhaanaa chit na aavai aapnai su-aa-ay firaa-ee. The True Guru's Will does not enter into his consciousness, and so he wanders around, pursuing his own interests.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	ikrpw kry jy AwpxI qw nwnk sbid smwhI ]1] (652-14, soriT, mÚ 4) kirpaa karay jay aapnee taa naanak sabad samaahee. ||1||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v1	If He grants His Grace, then Nanak is absorbed into the Word of the Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	para 28872	mÚ 4 ] (652-15) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 28873	mnmuK mwieAw moih ivAwpy dUjY Bwie mnUAw iQru nwih ] (652-15, soriT, mÚ 4) manmukh maa-i-aa mohi vi-aapay doojai bhaa-ay manoo-aa thir naahi. The self-willed manmukhs are engrossed in emotional attachment to Maya; in the love of duality, their minds are unsteady.
DEFINE	para 28874	Anidnu jlq rhih idnu rwqI haumY Kpih Kpwih ] (652-16, soriT, mÚ 4) an-din jalat raheh din raatee ha-umai khapeh khapaahi. Night and day, they are burning; day and night, they are totally ruined by their egotism.
DEFINE	para 28875	AMqir loBu mhw gubwrw iqn kY inkit n koeI jwih ] (652-16, soriT, mÚ 4) antar lobh mahaa gubaaraa tin kai nikat na ko-ee jaahi. Within them, is the total pitch darkness of greed, and no one even approaches them.
RECORD	para 28876	Eie Awip duKI suKu kbhU n pwvih jnim mrih mir jwih ] (652-17, soriT, mÚ 4) o-ay aap dukhee sukh kabhoo na paavahi janam mareh mar jaahi. They themselves are miserable, and they never find peace; they are born, only to die, and die again.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	nwnk bKis ley pRBu swcw ij gur crnI icqu lwih ]2] (652-17, soriT, mÚ 4) naanak bakhas la-ay parabh saachaa je gur charnee chit laahi. ||2||
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v2	O Nanak, the True Lord God forgives those, who focus their consciousness on the Guru's feet. ||2||
RECORD	para 28878	pauVI ] (652-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 28879	sMq Bgq prvwxu jo pRiB BwieAw ] (652-18, soriT, mÚ 4) sant bhagat parvaan jo parabh bhaa-i-aa. That Saint, that devotee, is acceptable, who is loved by God.
DEFINE	para 28880	syeI ibcKx jMq ijnI hir iDAwieAw ] (652-18, soriT, mÚ 4) say-ee bichkhan jant jinee har Dhi-aa-i-aa. Those beings are wise, who meditate on the Lord.
RECORD	para 28881	AMimRqu nwmu inDwnu Bojnu KwieAw ] (652-19, soriT, mÚ 4) amrit naam niDhaan bhojan khaa-i-aa. They eat the food, the treasure of the Ambrosial Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 28882	sMq jnw kI DUir msqik lwieAw ] (652-19, soriT, mÚ 4) sant janaa kee Dhoor mastak laa-i-aa. They apply the dust of the feet of the Saints to their foreheads.
RECORD	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v26	nwnk Bey punIq hir qIriQ nwieAw ]26] (653-1, soriT, mÚ 4) naanak bha-ay puneet har tirath naa-i-aa. ||26||
DEFINE	rwgu soriT vwr mhly 4 kI v26	O Nanak, they are purified, bathing in the sacred shrine of the Lord. ||26||
RECORD	para 28885	sloku mÚ 4 ] (653-1) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 28886	gurmuiK AMqir sWiq hY min qin nwim smwie ] (653-1, soriT, mÚ 4) gurmukh antar saa Nt hai man tan naam samaa-ay. Within the Gurmukh is peace and tranquility; his mind and body are absorbed in the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 28887	nwmo icqvY nwmu pVY nwim rhY ilv lwie ] (653-2, soriT, mÚ 4) naamo chitvai naam parhai naam rahai liv laa-ay. He contemplates the Naam, he studies the Naam, and he remains lovingly absorbed in the Naam.
DEFINE	para 28888	nwmu pdwrQu pwieAw icMqw geI iblwie ] (653-2, soriT, mÚ 4) naam padaarath paa-i-aa chintaa ga-ee bilaa-ay. He obtains the treasure of the Naam, and his anxiety is dispelled.
DEFINE	para 28889	siqguir imilAY nwmu aUpjY iqsnw BuK sB jwie ] (653-3, soriT, mÚ 4) satgur mili-ai naam oopjai tisnaa bhukh sabh jaa-ay. Meeting with the Guru, the Naam wells up, and his thirst and hunger are completely relieved.
