DEFINE	para 33019	kwieAw AMdir rqn pdwrQ Bgiq Bry BMfwrw ] (754-11, sUhI, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa andar ratan padaarath bhagat bharay bhandaaraa. Within the body there are jewels and precious treasures, the over-flowing treasure of devotion.
DEFINE	para 33020	iesu kwieAw AMdir nauKMf ipRQmI hwt ptx bwjwrw ] (754-11, sUhI, mÚ 3) is kaa-i-aa andar na-ukhand parithmee haat patan baajaaraa. Within this body are the nine continents of the earth, its markets, cities and streets.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v4	iesu kwieAw AMdir nwmu nau iniD pweIAY gur kY sbid vIcwrw ]4] (754-12, sUhI, mÚ 3) is kaa-i-aa andar naam na-o niDh paa-ee-ai gur kai sabad veechaaraa. ||4||
DEFINE	sUhI mhlw 3 v4	Within this body are the nine treasures of the Naam; contemplating the Word of the Guru's Shabad, it is obtained. ||4||
DEFINE	para 33022	kwieAw AMdir qoil qulwvY Awpy qolxhwrw ] (754-13, sUhI, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa andar tol tulaavai aapay tolanhaaraa. Within the body, the Lord estimates the weight; He Himself is the weigher.
DEFINE	para 33023	iehu mnu rqnu jvwhr mwxku iqs kw molu APwrw ] (754-13, sUhI, mÚ 3) ih man ratan javaahar maanak tis kaa mol afaaraa. This mind is the jewel, the gem, the diamond; it is absolutely priceless.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v5	moil ikq hI nwmu pweIAY nwhI nwmu pweIAY gur bIcwrw ]5] (754-14, sUhI, mÚ 3) mol kit hee naam paa-ee-ai naahee naam paa-ee-ai gur beechaaraa. ||5||
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v5	The Naam, the Name of the Lord, cannot be purchased at any price; the Naam is obtained by contemplating the Guru. ||5||
RECORD	para 33025	gurmuiK hovY su kwieAw KojY hor sB Brim BulweI ] (754-14, sUhI, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so kaa-i-aa khojai hor sabh bharam bhulaa-ee. One who becomes Gurmukh searches this body; all others just wander around in confusion.
RECORD	para 33026	ijs no dyie soeI jnu pwvY hor ikAw ko kry cqurweI ] (754-15, sUhI, mÚ 3) jis no day-ay so-ee jan paavai hor ki-aa ko karay chaturaa-ee. That humble being alone obtains it, unto whom the Lord bestows it. What other clever tricks can anyone try?
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v6	kwieAw AMdir Bau Bwau vsY gur prswdI pweI ]6] (754-15, sUhI, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa andar bha-o bhaa-o vasai gur parsaadee paa-ee. ||6||
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v6	Within the body, the Fear of God and Love for Him abides; by Guru's Grace, they are obtained. ||6||
RECORD	para 33028	kwieAw AMdir bRhmw ibsnu mhysw sB Epiq ijqu sMswrw ] (754-16, sUhI, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa andar barahmaa bisan mahaysaa sabh opat jit sansaaraa. Within the body, are Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva, from whom the whole world emanated.
RECORD	para 33029	scY Awpxw Kylu rcwieAw Awvw gauxu pwswrw ] (754-17, sUhI, mÚ 3) sachai aapnaa khayl rachaa-i-aa aavaa ga-on paasaaraa. The True Lord has staged and contrived His own play; the expanse of the Universe comes and goes.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v7	pUrY siqguir Awip idKwieAw sic nwim insqwrw ]7] (754-17, sUhI, mÚ 3) poorai satgur aap dikhaa-i-aa sach naam nistaaraa. ||7||
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v7	The Perfect True Guru Himself has made it clear, that emancipation comes through the True Name. ||7||
DEFINE	para 33031	sw kwieAw jo siqguru syvY scY Awip svwrI ] (754-18, sUhI, mÚ 3) saa kaa-i-aa jo satgur sayvai sachai aap savaaree. That body, which serves the True Guru, is embellished by the True Lord Himself.
RECORD	para 33032	ivxu nwvY dir FoeI nwhI qw jmu kry KuAwrI ] (754-18, sUhI, mÚ 3) vin naavai dar dho-ee naahee taa jam karay khu-aaree. Without the Name, the mortal finds no place of rest in the Court of the Lord; he shall be tortured by the Messenger of Death.
