RECORD	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v29	iehu jgqu moih dUjY ivAwipAw gurmqI scu iDAwie ]29] (756-12, sUhI, mÚ 3) ih jagat mohi doojai vi-aapi-aa gurmatee sach Dhi-aa-ay. ||29||
DEFINE	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v29	This world is engrossed in the love of duality; follow the Guru's Teachings, and meditate on the True Lord. ||29||
RECORD	para 33098	hir kI kImiq n pvY hir jsu ilKxu n jwie ] (756-13, sUhI, mÚ 3) har kee keemat na pavai har jas likhan na jaa-ay. The Lord's value cannot be estimated; the Lord's Praises cannot be written down.
RECORD	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v30	gur kY sbid mnu qnu rpY hir isau rhY smwie ]30] (756-13, sUhI, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad man tan rapai har si-o rahai samaa-ay. ||30||
DEFINE	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v30	When one's mind and body are attuned to the Word of the Guru's Shabad, one remains merged in the Lord. ||30||
DEFINE	para 33100	so shu myrw rMgulw rMgy shij suBwie ] (756-14, sUhI, mÚ 3) so saho mayraa rangulaa rangay sahj subhaa-ay. My Husband Lord is playful; He has imbued me with His Love, with natural ease.
RECORD	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v31	kwmix rMgu qw cVY jw ipr kY AMik smwie ]31] (756-14, sUhI, mÚ 3) kaaman rang taa charhai jaa pir kai ank samaa-ay. ||31||
DEFINE	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v31	The soul-bride is imbued with His Love, when her Husband Lord merges her into His Being. ||31||
DEFINE	para 33102	icrI ivCuMny BI imlin jo siqguru syvMin ] (756-15, sUhI, mÚ 3) chiree vichhunay bhee milan jo satgur sayvann. Even those who have been separated for so very long, are reunited with Him, when they serve the True Guru.
RECORD	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v32	AMqir nv iniD nwmu hY Kwin Krcin n inKuteI hir gux shij rvMin ]32] (756-15, sUhI, mÚ 3) antar nav niDh naam hai khaan kharchan na nikhuta-ee har gun sahj ravann. ||32||
DEFINE	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v32	The nine treasures of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, are deep within the nucleus of the self; consuming them, they are still never exhausted. Chant the Glorious Praises of the Lord, with natural ease. ||32||
DEFINE	para 33104	nw Eie jnmih nw mrih nw Eie duK shMin ] (756-16, sUhI, mÚ 3) naa o-ay janmeh naa mareh naa o-ay dukh sahann. They are not born, and they do not die; they do not suffer in pain.
RECORD	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v33	guir rwKy sy aubry hir isau kyl krMin ]33] (756-16, sUhI, mÚ 3) gur raakhay say ubray har si-o kayl karann. ||33||
DEFINE	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v33	Those who are protected by the Guru are saved. They celebrate with the Lord. ||33||
RECORD	para 33106	sjx imly n ivCuVih ij Anidnu imly rhMin ] (756-17, sUhI, mÚ 3) sajan milay na vichhurheh je an-din milay rahann. Those who are united with the Lord, the True Friend, are not separated again; night and day, they remain blended with Him.
RECORD	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v34	iesu jg mih ivrly jwxIAih nwnk scu lhMin ]34]1]3] (756-17, sUhI, mÚ 3) is jag meh virlay jaanee-ahi naanak sach lahann. ||34||
DEFINE	rwgu sUhI mhlw 3 Gru 10 v34	In this world, only a rare few are known, O Nanak, to have obtained the True Lord. ||34||
DEFINE	para 33109	hir jI sUKmu Agmu hY ikqu ibiD imilAw jwie ] (756-18, sUhI, mÚ 3) har jee sookham agam hai kit biDh mili-aa jaa-ay. The Dear Lord is subtle and inaccessible; how can we ever meet Him?
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v1	gur kY sbid BRmu ktIAY AicMqu vsY min Awie ]1] (756-19, sUhI, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad bharam katee-ai achint vasai man aa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	sUhI mhlw 3 v1	Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, doubt is dispelled, and the Carefree Lord comes to abide in the mind. ||1||
RECORD	para 33111	gurmuiK hir hir nwmu jpMin ] (756-19, sUhI, mÚ 3) gurmukh har har naam japann. The Gurmukhs chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v1	hau iqn kY bilhwrxY min hir gux sdw rvMin ]1] rhwau ] (757-1, sUhI, mÚ 3) ha-o tin kai balihaarnai man har gun sadaa ravann. ||1||
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. I am a sacrifice to those who chant the Glorious Praises of the Lord in their minds forever. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 33114	guru srvru mwn srovru hY vfBwgI purK lhMin@ ] (757-1, sUhI, mÚ 3) gur sarvar maan sarovar hai vadbhaagee purakh laha NniH. The Guru is like the Mansarovar Lake; only the very fortunate beings find Him.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v2	syvk gurmuiK KoijAw sy hMsuly nwmu lhMin ]2] (757-2, sUhI, mÚ 3) sayvak gurmukh khoji-aa say hansulay naam lahann. ||2||
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v2	The Gurmukhs, the selfless servants, seek out the Guru; the swan-souls feed there on the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 33116	nwmu iDAwiein@ rMg isau gurmuiK nwim lgMin@ ] (757-2, sUhI, mÚ 3) naam Dhi-aa-eeniH rang si-o gurmukh naam laga NniH. The Gurmukhs meditate on the Naam, and remain linked to the Naam.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v3	Duir pUrib hovY iliKAw gur Bwxw mMin leyin@ ]3] (757-3, sUhI, mÚ 3) Dhur poorab hovai likhi-aa gur bhaanaa man la-ayni H. ||3||
DEFINE	sUhI mhlw 3 v3	Whatever is pre-ordained, accept it as the Will of the Guru. ||3||
RECORD	para 33118	vfBwgI Gru KoijAw pwieAw nwmu inDwnu ] (757-3, sUhI, mÚ 3) vadbhaagee ghar khoji-aa paa-i-aa naam niDhaan. By great good fortune, I searched my home, and found the treasure of the Naam.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v4	guir pUrY vyKwilAw pRBu Awqm rwmu pCwnu ]4] (757-4, sUhI, mÚ 3) gur poorai vaykhaali-aa parabh aatam raam pachhaan. ||4||
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v4	The Perfect Guru has shown God to me; I have realized the Lord, the Supreme Soul. ||4||
DEFINE	para 33120	sBnw kw pRBu eyku hY dUjw Avru n koie ] (757-4, sUhI, mÚ 3) sabhnaa kaa parabh ayk hai doojaa avar na ko-ay. There is One God of all; there is no other at all.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v5	gur prswdI min vsY iqqu Git prgtu hoie ]5] (757-5, sUhI, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee man vasai tit ghat pargat ho-ay. ||5||
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v5	By Guru's Grace, the Lord comes to abide in the mind; in the heart of such a one, He is revealed. ||5||
DEFINE	para 33122	sBu AMqrjwmI bRhmu hY bRhmu vsY sB Qwie ] (757-5, sUhI, mÚ 3) sabh antarjaamee barahm hai barahm vasai sabh thaa-ay. God is the Inner-knower of all hearts; God dwells in every place.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v6	mMdw iks no AwKIAY sbid vyKhu ilv lwie ]6] (757-6, sUhI, mÚ 3) mandaa kis no aakhee-ai sabad vaykhhu liv laa-ay. ||6||
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v6	So who should we call evil? Behold the Word of the Shabad, and lovingly dwell upon it. ||6||
DEFINE	para 33124	burw Blw iqcru AwKdw ijcru hY duhu mwih ] (757-6, sUhI, mÚ 3) buraa bhalaa tichar aakh-daa jichar hai duhu maahi. He calls others bad and good, as long as he is in duality.
RECORD	sUhI mhlw 3 v7	gurmuiK eyko buiJAw eyksu mwih smwie ]7] (757-7, sUhI, mÚ 3) gurmukh ayko bujhi-aa aykas maahi samaa-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	sUhI mhlw 3 v7	The Gurmukh understands the One and Only Lord; He is absorbed in the One Lord. ||7||
