RECORD	para 34210	pauVI ] (787-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 34211	mohu kUVu kutMbu hY mnmuKu mugDu rqw ] (787-6, sUhI, mÚ 3) moh koorh kutamb hai manmukh mugaDh rataa. The foolish, self-willed manmukh is engrossed in false attachment to family.
RECORD	para 34212	haumY myrw kir muey ikCu swiQ n ilqw ] (787-6, sUhI, mÚ 3) ha-umai mayraa kar mu-ay kichh saath na litaa. Practicing egotism and self-conceit, he dies and departs, taking nothing along with him.
DEFINE	para 34213	isr aupir jmkwlu n suJeI dUjY Brimqw ] (787-6, sUhI, mÚ 3) sir upar jamkaal na sujh-ee doojai bharmitaa. He does not understand that the Messenger of Death is hovering over his head; he is deluded by duality.
RECORD	para 34214	iPir vylw hiQ n AwveI jmkwil vis ikqw ] (787-7, sUhI, mÚ 3) fir vaylaa hath na aavee jamkaal vas kitaa. This opportunity will not come into his hands again; the Messenger of Death will seize him.
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v5	jyhw Duir iliK pwieEnu sy krm kimqw ]5] (787-7, sUhI, mÚ 3) jayhaa Dhur likh paa-i-on say karam kamitaa. ||5||
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v5	He acts according to his pre-ordained destiny. ||5||
RECORD	para 34216	sloku mÚ 3 ] (787-8) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 34217	sqIAw eyih n AwKIAin jo miVAw lig jlµin@ ] (787-8, sUhI, mÚ 3) satee-aa ayhi na aakhee-an jo marhi-aa lag jala NniH. Do not call them 'satee', who burn themselves along with their husbands' corpses.
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v1	nwnk sqIAw jwxIAin@ ij ibrhy cot mrMin@ ]1] (787-9, sUhI, mÚ 3) naanak satee-aa jaanee-aniH je birhay chot mara NniH. ||1||
DEFINE	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, they alone are known as 'satee', who die from the shock of separation. ||1||
RECORD	para 34219	mÚ 3 ] (787-9) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34220	BI so sqIAw jwxIAin sIl sMqoiK rhMin@ ] (787-9, sUhI, mÚ 3) bhee so satee-aa jaanee-an seel santokh raha NniH. They are also known as 'satee', who abide in modesty and contentment.
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v2	syvin sweI Awpxw inq auiT sMm@wlµin@ ]2] (787-10, sUhI, mÚ 3) sayvan saa-ee aapnaa nit uth sam Haala NniH. ||2||
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v2	They serve their Lord, and rise in the early hours to contemplate Him. ||2||
RECORD	para 34222	mÚ 3 ] (787-10) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 34223	kMqw nwil mhylIAw syqI Aig jlwih ] (787-10, sUhI, mÚ 3) kantaa naal mahaylee-aa saytee ag jalaahi. The widows burn themselves in the fire, along with their husbands' corpses.
WHEN	para 34224	jy jwxih ipru Awpxw qw qin duK shwih ] (787-11, sUhI, mÚ 3) jay jaaneh pir aapnaa taa tan dukh sahaahi. If they truly knew their husbands, then they suffer terrible bodily pain.
WHEN	para 34225	nwnk kMq n jwxnI sy ikau Aig jlwih ] (787-11, sUhI, mÚ 3) naanak kant na jaannee say ki-o ag jalaahi. O Nanak, if they did not truly know their husbands, why should they burn themselves in the fire?
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v3	BwvY jIvau kY mrau dUrhu hI Bij jwih ]3] (787-12, sUhI, mÚ 3) bhaavai jeeva-o kai mara-o Dhoorahu hee bhaj jaahi. ||3||
DEFINE	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v3	Whether their husbands are alive or dead, those wives remain far away from them. ||3||
RECORD	para 34227	pauVI ] (787-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 34228	quDu duKu suKu nwil aupwieAw lyKu krqY iliKAw ] (787-12, sUhI, mÚ 3) tuDh dukh sukh naal upaa-i-aa laykh kartai likhi-aa. You created pain along with pleasure; O Creator, such is the writ You have written.
DEFINE	para 34229	nwvY jyvf hor dwiq nwhI iqsu rUpu n iriKAw ] (787-13, sUhI, mÚ 3) naavai jayvad hor daat naahee tis roop na rikhi-aa. There is no other gift as great as the Name; it has no form or sign.
DEFINE	para 34230	nwmu AKutu inDwnu hY gurmuiK min visAw ] (787-13, sUhI, mÚ 3) naam akhut niDhaan hai gurmukh man vasi-aa. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is an inexhaustible treasure; it abides in the mind of the Gurmukh.
RECORD	para 34231	kir ikrpw nwmu dyvsI iPir lyKu n iliKAw ] (787-14, sUhI, mÚ 3) kar kirpaa naam dayvsee fir laykh na likhi-aa. In His Mercy, He blesses us with the Naam, and then, the writ of pain and pleasure is not written.
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v6	syvk Bwie sy jn imly ijn hir jpu jipAw ]6] (787-14, sUhI, mÚ 3) sayvak bhaa-ay say jan milay jin har jap japi-aa. ||6||
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v6	Those humble servants who serve with love, meet the Lord, chanting the Chant of the Lord. ||6||
RECORD	para 34233	sloku mÚ 2 ] (787-15) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 34234	ijnI clxu jwixAw sy ikau krih ivQwr ] (787-15, sUhI, mÚ 2) jinee chalan jaani-aa say ki-o karahi vithaar. They know that they will have to depart, so why do they make such ostentatious displays?
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v1	clx swr n jwxnI kwj svwrxhwr ]1] (787-15, sUhI, mÚ 2) chalan saar na jaannee kaaj savaaranhaar. ||1||
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v1	Those who do not know that they will have to depart, continue to arrange their affairs. ||1||
RECORD	para 34236	mÚ 2 ] (787-16) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 34237	rwiq kwrix Dnu sMcIAY Blky clxu hoie ] (787-16, sUhI, mÚ 2) raat kaaran Dhan sanchee-ai bhalkay chalan ho-ay. He accumulates wealth during the night of his life, but in the morning, he must depart.
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v2	nwnk nwil n cleI iPir pCuqwvw hoie ]2] (787-16, sUhI, mÚ 2) naanak naal na chal-ee fir pachhutaavaa ho-ay. ||2||
FORBID	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, it shall not go along with him, and so he regrets. ||2||
RECORD	para 34239	mÚ 2 ] (787-17) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 34240	bDw ctI jo Bry nw guxu nw aupkwru ] (787-17, sUhI, mÚ 2) baDhaa chatee jo bharay naa gun naa upkaar. Paying a fine under pressure, does not bring either merit or goodness.
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v3	syqI KusI svwrIAY nwnk kwrju swru ]3] (787-17, sUhI, mÚ 2) saytee khusee savaaree-ai naanak kaaraj saar. ||3||
DEFINE	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v3	That alone is a good deed, O Nanak, which is done by one's own free will. ||3||
RECORD	para 34242	mÚ 2 ] (787-18) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 34243	mnhiT qrP n ijpeI jy bhuqw Gwly ] (787-18, sUhI, mÚ 2) manhath taraf na jip-ee jay bahutaa ghaalay. Stubborn-mindedness will not win the Lord to one's side, no matter how much it is tried.
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v4	qrP ijxY sq Bwau dy jn nwnk sbdu vIcwry ]4] (787-18, sUhI, mÚ 2) taraf jinai sat bhaa-o day jan naanak sabad veechaaray. ||4||
DEFINE	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v4	The Lord is won over to your side, by offering Him your true love, O servant Nanak, and contemplating the Word of the Shabad. ||4||
RECORD	para 34245	pauVI ] (787-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 34246	krqY kwrxu ijin kIAw so jwxY soeI ] (787-19, sUhI, mÚ 2) kartai kaaran jin kee-aa so jaanai so-ee. The Creator created the world; He alone understands it.
REQUIRE	para 34247	Awpy isRsit aupweIAnu Awpy Puin goeI ] (787-19, sUhI, mÚ 2) aapay sarisat upaa-ee-an aapay fun go-ee. He Himself created the Universe, and He Himself shall destroy it afterwards.
RECORD	para 34249	jug cwry sB Biv QkI ikin kImiq hoeI ] (788-1, sUhI, mÚ 2) jug chaaray sabh bhav thakee kin keemat ho-ee. All have grown weary of wandering throughout the four ages, but none know the Lord's worth.
DEFINE	para 34250	siqguir eyku ivKwilAw min qin suKu hoeI ] (788-1, sUhI, mÚ 2) satgur ayk vikhaali-aa man tan sukh ho-ee. The True Guru has shown me the One Lord, and my mind and body are at peace.
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v7	gurmuiK sdw slwhIAY krqw kry su hoeI ]7] (788-2, sUhI, mÚ 2) gurmukh sadaa salaahee-ai kartaa karay so ho-ee. ||7||
RECORD	vwr sUhI kI slokw nwil mhlw 3 v7	The Gurmukh praises the Lord forever; that alone happens, which the Creator Lord does. ||7||
RECORD	para 34253	ijnw Bau iqn@ nwih Bau mucu Bau inBivAwh ] (788-2, sUhI, mÚ 2) jinaa bha-o tin H naahi bha-o much bha-o nibhvi-aah. Those who have the Fear of God, have no other fears; those who do not have the Fear of God, are very afraid.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	nwnk eyhu ptMqrw iqqu dIbwix gieAwh ]1] (788-3, sUhI, mÚ 2) naanak ayhu patantaraa tit deebaan ga-i-aah. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, this mystery is revealed at the Court of the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 34255	mÚ 2 ] (788-3) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 34256	qurdy kau qurdw imlY aufqy kau aufqw ] (788-3, sUhI, mÚ 2) turday ka-o turdaa milai udtay ka-o udtaa. That which flows, mingles with that which flows; that which blows, mingles with that which blows.
RECORD	para 34257	jIvqy kau jIvqw imlY mUey kau mUAw ] (788-4, sUhI, mÚ 2) jeevtay ka-o jeevtaa milai moo-ay ka-o moo-aa. The living mingle with the living, and the dead mingle with the dead.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	nwnk so swlwhIAY ijin kwrxu kIAw ]2] (788-4, sUhI, mÚ 2) naanak so salaahee-ai jin kaaran kee-aa. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, praise the One who created the creation. ||2||
RECORD	para 34259	pauVI ] (788-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 34260	scu iDAwiein sy scy gur sbid vIcwrI ] (788-5, sUhI, mÚ 2) sach Dhi-aa-in say sachay gur sabad veechaaree. Those who meditate on the True Lord are true; they contemplate the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 34261	haumY mwir mnu inrmlw hir nwmu auir DwrI ] (788-5, sUhI, mÚ 2) ha-umai maar man nirmalaa har naam ur Dhaaree. They subdue their ego, purify their minds, and enshrine the Lord's Name within their hearts.
DEFINE	para 34262	koTy mMfp mwVIAw lig pey gwvwrI ] (788-6, sUhI, mÚ 2) kothay mandap maarhee-aa lag pa-ay gaavaaree. The fools are attached to their homes, mansions and balconies.
DEFINE	para 34263	ijin@ kIey iqsih n jwxnI mnmuiK gubwrI ] (788-6, sUhI, mÚ 2) jiniH kee-ay tiseh na jaannee manmukh gubaaree. The self-willed manmukhs are caught in darkness; they do not know the One who created them.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v8	ijsu buJwieih so buJsI sicAw ikAw jMq ivcwrI ]8] (788-7, sUhI, mÚ 2) jis bujhaa-ihi so bujhsee sachi-aa ki-aa jant vichaaree. ||8||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v8	He alone understands, whom the True Lord causes to understand; what can the helpless creatures do? ||8||
RECORD	para 34265	slok mÚ 3 ] (788-7) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 34266	kwmix qau sIgwru kir jw pihlW kMqu mnwie ] (788-7, sUhI, mÚ 3) kaaman ta-o seegaar kar jaa pahilaa N kant manaa-ay. O bride, decorate yourself, after you surrender and accept your Husband Lord.
RECORD	para 34267	mqu syjY kMqu n AwveI eyvY ibrQw jwie ] (788-8, sUhI, mÚ 3) mat sayjai kant na aavee ayvai birthaa jaa-ay. Otherwise, your Husband Lord will not come to your bed, and your ornaments will be useless.
WHEN	para 34268	kwmix ipr mnu mwinAw qau bixAw sIgwru ] (788-8, sUhI, mÚ 3) kaaman pir man maani-aa ta-o bani-aa seegaar. O bride, your decorations will adorn you, only when your Husband Lord's Mind is pleased.
WHEN	para 34269	kIAw qau prvwxu hY jw shu Dry ipAwru ] (788-9, sUhI, mÚ 3) kee-aa ta-o parvaan hai jaa saho Dharay pi-aar. Your ornaments will be acceptable and approved, only when your Husband Lord loves you.
RECORD	para 34270	Bau sIgwru qbol rsu Bojnu Bwau kryie ] (788-9, sUhI, mÚ 3) bha-o seegaar tabol ras bhojan bhaa-o karay-i. So make the Fear of God your ornaments, joy your betel nuts to chew, and love your food.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	qnu mnu saupy kMq kau qau nwnk Bogu kryie ]1] (788-10, sUhI, mÚ 3) tan man sa-upay kant ka-o ta-o naanak bhog karay-i. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	Surrender your body and mind to your Husband Lord, and then, O Nanak, He will enjoy you. ||1||
RECORD	para 34272	mÚ 3 ] (788-10) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 34273	kwjl PUl qMbol rsu ly Dn kIAw sIgwru ] (788-10, sUhI, mÚ 3) kaajal fool tambol ras lay Dhan kee-aa seegaar. The wife takes flowers, and fragrance of betel, and decorates herself.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	syjY kMqu n AwieE eyvY BieAw ivkwru ]2] (788-11, sUhI, mÚ 3) sayjai kant na aa-i-o ayvai bha-i-aa vikaar. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	But her Husband Lord does not come to her bed, and so these efforts are useless. ||2||
RECORD	para 34275	mÚ 3 ] (788-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34276	Dn ipru eyih n AwKIAin bhin iekTy hoie ] (788-11, sUhI, mÚ 3) Dhan pir ayhi na aakhee-an bahan ikthay ho-ay. They are not said to be husband and wife, who merely sit together.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v3	eyk joiq duie mUrqI Dn ipru khIAY soie ]3] (788-12, sUhI, mÚ 3) ayk jot du-ay moortee Dhan pir kahee-ai so-ay. ||3||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v3	They alone are called husband and wife, who have one light in two bodies. ||3||
RECORD	para 34278	pauVI ] (788-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 34279	BY ibnu Bgiq n hoveI nwim n lgY ipAwru ] (788-13, sUhI, mÚ 3) bhai bin bhagat na hova-ee naam na lagai pi-aar. Without the Fear of God, there is no devotional worship, and no love for the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 34280	siqguir imilAY Bau aUpjY BY Bwie rMgu svwir ] (788-13, sUhI, mÚ 3) satgur mili-ai bha-o oopjai bhai bhaa-ay rang savaar. Meeting with the True Guru, the Fear of God wells up, and one is embellished with the Fear and the Love of God.
DEFINE	para 34281	qnu mnu rqw rMg isau haumY iqRsnw mwir ] (788-14, sUhI, mÚ 3) tan man rataa rang si-o ha-umai tarisnaa maar. When the body and mind are imbued with the Lord's Love, egotism and desire are conquered and subdued.
WHEN	para 34282	mnu qnu inrmlu Aiq sohxw ByitAw ik®sn murwir ] (788-14, sUhI, mÚ 3) man tan nirmal at sohnaa bhayti-aa krisan muraar. The mind and body become immaculately pure and very beautiful, when one meets the Lord, the Destroyer of ego.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v9	Bau Bwau sBu iqs dw so scu vrqY sMswir ]9] (788-15, sUhI, mÚ 3) bha-o bhaa-o sabh tis daa so sach vartai sansaar. ||9||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v9	Fear and love all belong to Him; He is the True Lord, permeating and pervading the Universe. ||9||
RECORD	para 34284	slok mÚ 1 ] (788-15) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34285	vwhu Ksm qU vwhu ijin ric rcnw hm kIey ] (788-15, sUhI, mÚ 1) vaahu khasam too vaahu jin rach rachnaa ham kee-ay. Waaho! Waaho! You are wonderful and great, O Lord and Master; You created the creation, and made us.
RECORD	para 34286	swgr lhir smuMd sr vyil vrs vrwhu ] (788-16, sUhI, mÚ 1) saagar lahar samund sar vayl varas varaahu. You made the waters, waves, oceans, pools, plants, clouds and mountains.
RECORD	para 34287	Awip KVovih Awip kir AwpIxY Awpwhu ] (788-16, sUhI, mÚ 1) aap kharhoveh aap kar aapeenai aapaahu. You Yourself stand in the midst of what You Yourself created.
DEFINE	para 34288	gurmuiK syvw Qwie pvY aunmin qqu kmwhu ] (788-17, sUhI, mÚ 1) gurmukh sayvaa thaa-ay pavai unman tat kamaahu. The selfless service of the Gurmukhs is approved; in celestial peace, they live the essence of reality.
RECORD	para 34289	mskiq lhhu mjUrIAw mMig mMig Ksm drwhu ] (788-17, sUhI, mÚ 1) maskat lahhu majooree-aa mang mang khasam daraahu. They receive the wages of their labor, begging at the Door of their Lord and Master.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	nwnk pur dr vyprvwh qau dir aUxw nwih ko scw vyprvwhu ]1] (788-18, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak pur dar vayparvaah ta-o dar oonaa naahi ko sachaa vayparvaahu. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, the Court of the Lord is overflowing and carefree; O my True Carefree Lord, no one returns empty-handed from Your Court. ||1||
RECORD	para 34291	mhlw 1 ] (788-19) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34292	aujl moqI sohxy rqnw nwil juVMin ] (788-19, sUhI, mÚ 1) ujal motee sohnay ratnaa naal jurhann. The teeth are like brilliant, beautiful pearls, and the eyes are like sparkling jewels.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	iqn jru vYrI nwnkw ij buFy QIie mrMin ]2] (788-19, sUhI, mÚ 1) tin jar vairee naankaa je budhay thee-ay marann. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	Old age is their enemy, O Nanak; when they grow old, they waste away. ||2||
RECORD	para 34295	pauVI ] (789-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 34296	hir swlwhI sdw sdw qnu mnu sauip srIru ] (789-1, sUhI, mÚ 1) har saalaahee sadaa sadaa tan man sa-up sareer. Praise the Lord, forever and ever; dedicate your body and mind to Him.
RECORD	para 34297	gur sbdI scu pwieAw scw gihr gMBIru ] (789-1, sUhI, mÚ 1) gur sabdee sach paa-i-aa sachaa gahir gambheer. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, I have found the True, Profound and Unfathomable Lord.
DEFINE	para 34298	min qin ihrdY riv rihAw hir hIrw hIru ] (789-2, sUhI, mÚ 1) man tan hirdai rav rahi-aa har heeraa heer. The Lord, the jewel of jewels, is permeating my mind, body and heart.
REQUIRE	para 34299	jnm mrx kw duKu gieAw iPir pvY n PIru ] (789-2, sUhI, mÚ 1) janam maran kaa dukh ga-i-aa fir pavai na feer. The pains of birth and death are gone, and I shall never again be consigned to the cycle of reincarnation.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v10	nwnk nwmu slwih qU hir guxI ghIru ]10] (789-3, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak naam salaahi too har gunee gaheer. ||10||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v10	O Nanak, praise the Naam, the Name of the Lord, the ocean of excellence. ||10||
RECORD	para 34301	slok mÚ 1 ] (789-3) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 34302	nwnk iehu qnu jwil ijin jilAY nwmu ivswirAw ] (789-3, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak ih tan jaal jin jali-ai naam visaari-aa. O Nanak, burn this body; this burnt body has forgotten the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	paudI jwie prwil ipCY hQu n AMbVY iqqu invMDY qwil ]1] (789-4, sUhI, mÚ 1) pa-udee jaa-ay paraal pichhai hath na ambrhai tit nivanDhai taal. ||1||
FORBID	slok mhlw 2 v1	The dirt is piling up, and in the world hereafter, your hand shall not be able to reach down into this stagnant pond to clean it out. ||1||
RECORD	para 34304	mÚ 1 ] (789-4) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34305	nwnk mn ky kMm iPitAw gxq n AwvhI ] (789-5, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak man kay kamm fiti-aa ganat na aavhee. O Nanak, wicked are the uncountable actions of the mind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	ikqI lhw shMm jw bKsy qw Dkw nhI ]2] (789-5, sUhI, mÚ 1) kitee lahaa sahamm jaa bakhsay taa Dhakaa nahee. ||2||
WHEN	slok mhlw 2 v2	They bring terrible and painful retributions, but if the Lord forgives me, then I will be spared this punishment. ||2||
RECORD	para 34307	pauVI ] (789-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 34308	scw Amru clwieEnu kir scu Purmwxu ] (789-6, sUhI, mÚ 1) sachaa amar chalaa-i-on kar sach furmaan. True is the Command He sends forth, and True are the Orders He issues.
DEFINE	para 34309	sdw inhclu riv rihAw so purKu sujwxu ] (789-6, sUhI, mÚ 1) sadaa nihchal rav rahi-aa so purakh sujaan. Forever unmoving and unchanging, permeating and pervading everywhere, He is the All-knowing Primal Lord.
RECORD	para 34310	gur prswdI syvIAY scu sbid nIswxu ] (789-6, sUhI, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee sayvee-ai sach sabad neesaan. By Guru's Grace, serve Him, through the True Insignia of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 34311	pUrw Qwtu bxwieAw rMgu gurmiq mwxu ] (789-7, sUhI, mÚ 1) pooraa thaat banaa-i-aa rang gurmat maan. That which He makes is perfect; through the Guru's Teachings, enjoy His Love.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v11	Agm Agocru AlKu hY gurmuiK hir jwxu ]11] (789-7, sUhI, mÚ 1) agam agochar alakh hai gurmukh har jaan. ||11||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v11	He is inaccessible, unfathomable and unseen; as Gurmukh, know the Lord. ||11||
RECORD	para 34313	slok mÚ 1 ] (789-8) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34314	nwnk bdrw mwl kw BIqir DirAw Awix ] (789-8, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak badraa maal kaa bheetar Dhari-aa aan. O Nanak, the bags of coins are brought in
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	Koty Kry prKIAin swihb kY dIbwix ]1] (789-8, sUhI, mÚ 1) khotay kharay parkhee-an saahib kai deebaan. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v1	and placed in the Court of our Lord and Master, and there, the genuine and the counterfeit are separated. ||1||
RECORD	para 34316	mÚ 1 ] (789-9) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34317	nwvx cly qIrQI min KotY qin cor ] (789-9, sUhI, mÚ 1) naavan chalay teerthee man khotai tan chor. They go and bathe at sacred shrines of pilgrimage, but their minds are still evil, and their bodies are thieves.
DEFINE	para 34318	ieku Bwau lQI nwiqAw duie Bw cVIAsu hor ] (789-9, sUhI, mÚ 1) ik bhaa-o lathee naati-aa du-ay bhaa charhee-as hor. Some of their filth is washed off by these baths, but they only accumulate twice as much.
ALLOW	para 34319	bwhir DoqI qUmVI AMdir ivsu inkor ] (789-10, sUhI, mÚ 1) baahar Dhotee toomrhee andar vis nikor. Like a gourd, they may be washed off on the outside, but on the inside, they are still filled with poison.
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	swD Bly AxnwiqAw cor is corw cor ]2] (789-10, sUhI, mÚ 1) saaDh bhalay annaati-aa chor se choraa chor. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	The holy man is blessed, even without such bathing, while a thief is a thief, no matter how much he bathes. ||2||
RECORD	para 34321	pauVI ] (789-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 34322	Awpy hukmu clwiedw jgu DMDY lwieAw ] (789-11, sUhI, mÚ 1) aapay hukam chalaa-idaa jag DhanDhai laa-i-aa. He Himself issues His Commands, and links the people of the world to their tasks.
RECORD	para 34323	ieik Awpy hI Awip lwieAnu gur qy suKu pwieAw ] (789-11, sUhI, mÚ 1) ik aapay hee aap laa-i-an gur tay sukh paa-i-aa. He Himself joins some to Himself, and through the Guru, they find peace.
RECORD	para 34324	dh ids iehu mnu Dwvdw guir Twik rhwieAw ] (789-12, sUhI, mÚ 1) dah dis ih man Dhaavdaa gur thaak rahaa-i-aa. The mind runs around in the ten directions; the Guru holds it still.
DEFINE	para 34325	nwvY no sB locdI gurmqI pwieAw ] (789-12, sUhI, mÚ 1) naavai no sabh lochdee gurmatee paa-i-aa. Everyone longs for the Name, but it is only found through the Guru's Teachings.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v12	Duir iliKAw myit n skIAY jo hir iliK pwieAw ]12] (789-13, sUhI, mÚ 1) Dhur likhi-aa mayt na sakee-ai jo har likh paa-i-aa. ||12||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v12	Your pre-ordained destiny, written by the Lord in the very beginning, cannot be erased. ||12||
RECORD	para 34327	slok mÚ 1 ] (789-13) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 34328	duie dIvy caudh htnwly ] (789-13, sUhI, mÚ 1) du-ay deevay cha-odah hatnaalay. The two lamps light the fourteen markets.
DEFINE	para 34329	jyqy jIA qyqy vxjwry ] (789-14, sUhI, mÚ 1) jaytay jee-a taytay vanjaaray. There are just as many traders as there are living beings.
DEFINE	para 34330	Kul@y ht hoAw vwpwru ] (789-14, sUhI, mÚ 1) khulHay hat ho-aa vaapaar. The shops are open, and trading is going on;
DEFINE	para 34331	jo phucY so clxhwru ] (789-14, sUhI, mÚ 1) jo pahuchai so chalanhaar. whoever comes there, is bound to depart.
DEFINE	para 34332	Drmu dlwlu pwey nIswxu ] (789-14, sUhI, mÚ 1) Dharam dalaal paa-ay neesaan. The Righteous Judge of Dharma is the broker, who gives his sign of approval.
DEFINE	para 34333	nwnk nwmu lwhw prvwxu ] (789-15, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak naam laahaa parvaan. O Nanak, those who earn the profit of the Naam are accepted and approved.
DEFINE	para 34334	Gir Awey vjI vwDweI ] (789-15, sUhI, mÚ 1) ghar aa-ay vajee vaaDhaa-ee. And when they return home, they are greeted with cheers;
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	sc nwm kI imlI vifAweI ]1] (789-15, sUhI, mÚ 1) sach naam kee milee vadi-aa-ee. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	they obtain the glorious greatness of the True Name. ||1||
RECORD	para 34336	mÚ 1 ] (789-16) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34337	rwqI hovin kwlIAw supydw sy vMn ] (789-16, sUhI, mÚ 1) raatee hovan kaalee-aa supaydaa say vann. Even when the night is dark, whatever is white retains its white color.
DEFINE	para 34338	idhu bgw qpY Gxw kwilAw kwly vMn ] (789-16, sUhI, mÚ 1) dihu bagaa tapai ghanaa kaali-aa kaalay vann. And even when the light of day is dazzlingly bright, whatever is black retains its black color.
DEFINE	para 34339	AMDy AklI bwhry mUrK AMD igAwnu ] (789-16, sUhI, mÚ 1) anDhay aklee baahray moorakh anDh gi-aan. The blind fools have no wisdom at all; their understanding is blind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	nwnk ndrI bwhry kbih n pwvih mwnu ]2] (789-17, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak nadree baahray kabeh na paavahi maan. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, without the Lord's Grace, they will never receive honor. ||2||
RECORD	para 34341	pauVI ] (789-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 34342	kwieAw kotu rcwieAw hir scY Awpy ] (789-17, sUhI, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa kot rachaa-i-aa har sachai aapay. The True Lord Himself created the body-fortress.
DEFINE	para 34343	ieik dUjY Bwie KuAwieAnu haumY ivic ivAwpy ] (789-18, sUhI, mÚ 1) ik doojai bhaa-ay khu-aa-i-an ha-umai vich vi-aapay. Some are ruined through the love of duality, engrossed in egotism.
DEFINE	para 34344	iehu mwns jnmu dulµBu sw mnmuK sMqwpy ] (789-18, sUhI, mÚ 1) ih maanas janam dulambh saa manmukh santaapay. This human body is so difficult to obtain; the self-willed manmukhs suffer in pain.
DEFINE	para 34345	ijsu Awip buJwey so buJsI ijsu siqguru Qwpy ] (789-19, sUhI, mÚ 1) jis aap bujhaa-ay so bujhsee jis satgur thaapay. He alone understands, whom the Lord Himself causes to understand; he is blessed by the True Guru.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v13	sBu jgu Kylu rcwieEnu sB vrqY Awpy ]13] (789-19, sUhI, mÚ 1) sabh jag khayl rachaa-i-on sabh vartai aapay. ||13||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v13	He created the entire world for His play; He is pervading amongst all. ||13||
RECORD	para 34348	slok mÚ 1 ] (790-1) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
UPHOLD	para 34349	corw jwrw rMfIAw kutxIAw dIbwxu ] vydInw kI dosqI vydInw kw Kwxu ] (790-1, sUhI, mÚ 1) choraa jaaraa randee-aa kutnee-aa deebaan. vaydeenaa kee dostee vaydeenaa kaa khaan. Thieves, adulterers, prostitutes and pimps, make friendships with the unrighteous, and eat with the unrighteous.
DEFINE	para 34350	isPqI swr n jwxnI sdw vsY sYqwnu ] (790-2, sUhI, mÚ 1) siftee saar na jaannee sadaa vasai saitaan. They do not know the value of the Lord's Praises, and Satan is always with them.
DEFINE	para 34351	gdhu cMdin KaulIAY BI swhU isau pwxu ] (790-2, sUhI, mÚ 1) gadahu chandan kha-ulee-ai bhee saahoo si-o paan. If a donkey is anointed with sandalwood paste, he still loves to roll in the dirt.
DEFINE	para 34352	nwnk kUVY kiqAY kUVw qxIAY qwxu ] (790-3, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak koorhai kati-ai koorhaa tanee-ai taan. O Nanak, by spinning falsehood, a fabric of falsehood is woven.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	kUVw kpVu kCIAY kUVw pYnxu mwxu ]1] (790-3, sUhI, mÚ 1) koorhaa kaparh kachhee-ai koorhaa painan maan. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v1	False is the cloth and its measurement, and false is pride in such a garment. ||1||
RECORD	para 34354	mÚ 1 ] (790-4) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 34355	bWgw burgU isM|IAw nwly imlI klwx ] (790-4, sUhI, mÚ 1) baa Ngaa burgoo sinyee-aa naalay milee kalaan. The callers to prayer, the flute-players, the horn-blowers, and also the singers
DEFINE	para 34356	ieik dwqy ieik mMgqy nwmu qyrw prvwxu ] (790-4, sUhI, mÚ 1) ik daatay ik mangtay naam tayraa parvaan. - some are givers, and some are beggars; they become acceptable only through Your Name, Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	nwnk ijn@I suix kY mMinAw hau iqnw ivthu kurbwxu ]2] (790-5, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak jin Hee sun kai mani-aa ha-o tinaa vitahu kurbaan. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, I am a sacrifice to those who hear and accept the Name. ||2||
RECORD	para 34358	pauVI ] (790-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 34359	mwieAw mohu sBu kUVu hY kUVo hoie gieAw ] (790-5, sUhI, mÚ 1) maa-i-aa moh sabh koorh hai koorho ho-ay ga-i-aa. Attachment to Maya is totally false, and false are those who go that way.
DEFINE	para 34360	haumY JgVw pwieEnu JgVY jgu muieAw ] (790-6, sUhI, mÚ 1) ha-umai jhagrhaa paa-i-on jhagrhai jag mu-i-aa. Through egotism, the world is caught in conflict and strife, and it dies.
DEFINE	para 34361	gurmuiK JgVu cukwieEnu ieko riv rihAw ] (790-6, sUhI, mÚ 1) gurmukh jhagarh chukaa-i-on iko rav rahi-aa. The Gurmukh is free of conflict and strife, and sees the One Lord, pervading everywhere.
DEFINE	para 34362	sBu Awqm rwmu pCwixAw Baujlu qir gieAw ] (790-7, sUhI, mÚ 1) sabh aatam raam pachhaani-aa bha-ojal tar ga-i-aa. Recognizing that the Supreme Soul is everywhere, he crosses over the terrifying world-ocean.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v14	joiq smwxI joiq ivic hir nwim smieAw ]14] (790-7, sUhI, mÚ 1) jot samaanee jot vich har naam sam-i-aa. ||14||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v14	His light merges into the Light, and he is absorbed into the Lord's Name. ||14||
RECORD	para 34364	slok mÚ 1 ] (790-8) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok: First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34365	siqgur BIiKAw dyih mY qUM sMmRQu dwqwru ] (790-8, sUhI, mÚ 1) satgur bheekhi-aa deh mai tooN samrath daataar. O True Guru, bless me with Your charity; You are the All-powerful Giver.
ALLOW	para 34366	haumY grbu invwrIAY kwmu k®oDu AhMkwru ] (790-8, sUhI, mÚ 1) ha-umai garab nivaaree-ai kaam kroDh aha Nkaar. May I subdue and quiet my egotism, pride, sexual desire, anger and self-conceit.
RECORD	para 34367	lbu loBu prjwlIAY nwmu imlY AwDwru ] (790-9, sUhI, mÚ 1) lab lobh parjaalee-ai naam milai aaDhaar. Burn away all my greed, and give me the Support of the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 34368	Aihinis nvqn inrmlw mYlw kbhUM n hoie ] (790-9, sUhI, mÚ 1) ahinis navtan nirmalaa mailaa kabahoo N na ho-ay. Day and night, keep me ever-fresh and new, spotless and pure; let me never be soiled by sin.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	nwnk ieh ibiD CutIAY ndir qyrI suKu hoie ]1] (790-10, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak ih biDh chhutee-ai nadar tayree sukh ho-ay. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, in this way I am saved; by Your Grace, I have found peace. ||1||
RECORD	para 34370	mÚ 1 ] (790-10) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34371	ieko kMqu sbweIAw ijqI dir KVIAwh ] (790-10, sUhI, mÚ 1) iko kant sabaa-ee-aa jitee dar kharhee-aah. There is only the one Husband Lord, for all who stand at His Door.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	nwnk kMqY rqIAw puCih bwqVIAwh ]2] (790-11, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak kantai ratee-aa puchheh baat-rhee-aah. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, they ask for news of their Husband Lord, from those who are imbued with His Love. ||2||
RECORD	para 34373	mÚ 1 ] (790-11) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34374	sBy kMqY rqIAw mY dohwgix ikqu ] (790-11, sUhI, mÚ 1) sabhay kantai ratee-aa mai dohaagan kit. All are imbued with love for their Husband Lord; I am a discarded bride - what good am I?
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v3	mY qin Avgx eyqVy Ksmu n Pyry icqu ]3] (790-12, sUhI, mÚ 1) mai tan avgan -ayt-rhay khasam na fayray chit. ||3||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v3	My body is filled with so many faults; my Lord and Master does not even turn His thoughts to me. ||3||
RECORD	para 34376	mÚ 1 ] (790-12) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 34377	hau bilhwrI iqn kau isPiq ijnw dY vwiq ] (790-12, sUhI, mÚ 1) ha-o balihaaree tin ka-o sifat jinaa dai vaat. I am a sacrifice to those who praise the Lord with their mouths.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v4	siB rwqI sohwgxI iek mY dohwgix rwiq ]4] (790-13, sUhI, mÚ 1) sabh raatee sohaaganee ik mai dohaagan raat. ||4||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v4	All the nights are for the happy soul-brides; I am a discarded bride - if only I could have even one night with Him! ||4||
RECORD	para 34379	pauVI ] (790-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 34380	dir mMgqu jwcY dwnu hir dIjY ik®pw kir ] (790-13, sUhI, mÚ 1) dar mangat jaachai daan har deejai kirpaa kar. I am a beggar at Your Door, begging for charity; O Lord, please grant me Your Mercy, and give to me.
ALLOW	para 34381	gurmuiK lyhu imlwie jnu pwvY nwmu hir ] (790-14, sUhI, mÚ 1) gurmukh layho milaa-ay jan paavai naam har. As Gurmukh, unite me, your humble servant, with You, that I may receive Your Name.
RECORD	para 34382	Anhd sbdu vjwie joqI joiq Dir ] (790-14, sUhI, mÚ 1) anhad sabad vajaa-ay jotee jot Dhar. Then, the unstruck melody of the Shabad will vibrate and resound, and my light will blend with the Light.
RECORD	para 34383	ihrdY hir gux gwie jY jY sbdu hir ] (790-15, sUhI, mÚ 1) hirdai har gun gaa-ay jai jai sabad har. Within my heart, I sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and celebrate the Word of the Lord's Shabad.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v15	jg mih vrqY Awip hir syqI pRIiq kir ]15] (790-15, sUhI, mÚ 1) jag meh vartai aap har saytee pareet kar. ||15||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v15	The Lord Himself is pervading and permeating the world; so fall in love with Him! ||15||
RECORD	para 34385	slok mÚ 1 ] (790-16) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 34386	ijnI n pwieE pRym rsu kMq n pwieE swau ] (790-16, sUhI, mÚ 1) jinee na paa-i-o paraym ras kant na paa-i-o saa-o. Those who do not obtain the sublime essence, the love and delight of their Husband Lord,
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	suM\y Gr kw pwhuxw ijau AwieAw iqau jwau ]1] (790-16, sUhI, mÚ 1) sunjay ghar kaa paahunaa ji-o aa-i-aa ti-o jaa-o. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	are like guests in a deserted house; they leave just as they have come, empty- handed. ||1||
RECORD	para 34388	mÚ 1 ] (790-17) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 34389	sau Elwm@y idnY ky rwqI imlin@ shMs ] (790-17, sUhI, mÚ 1) sa-o olaam Hay dinai kay raatee milniH saha Ns. He receives hundreds and thousands of reprimands, day and night;
WHEN	para 34390	isPiq slwhxu Cif kY krMgI lgw hMsu ] (790-17, sUhI, mÚ 1) sifat salaahan chhad kai karangee lagaa hans. the swan-soul has renounced the Lord's Praises, and attached itself to a rotting carcass.
DEFINE	para 34391	iPtu ievyhw jIivAw ijqu Kwie vDwieAw pytu ] (790-18, sUhI, mÚ 1) fit ivayhaa jeevi-aa jit khaa-ay vaDhaa-i-aa payt. Cursed is that life, in which one only eats to fill his belly.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	nwnk scy nwm ivxu sBo dusmnu hyqu ]2] (790-18, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak sachay naam vin sabho dusman hayt. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, without the True Name, all one's friends turn to enemies. ||2||
RECORD	para 34393	pauVI ] (790-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 34394	FwFI gux gwvY inq jnmu svwirAw ] (790-19, sUhI, mÚ 1) dhaadhee gun gaavai nit janam savaari-aa. The minstrel continually sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord, to embellish his life.
RECORD	para 34395	gurmuiK syiv slwih scw aur DwirAw ] (790-19, sUhI, mÚ 1) gurmukh sayv salaahi sachaa ur Dhaari-aa. The Gurmukh serves and praises the True Lord, enshrining Him within his heart.
RECORD	para 34397	Gru dru pwvY mhlu nwmu ipAwirAw ] (791-1, sUhI, mÚ 1) ghar dar paavai mahal naam pi-aari-aa. He obtains his own home and mansion, by loving the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 34398	gurmuiK pwieAw nwmu hau gur kau vwirAw ] (791-1, sUhI, mÚ 1) gurmukh paa-i-aa naam ha-o gur ka-o vaari-aa. As Gurmukh, I have obtained the Naam; I am a sacrifice to the Guru.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v16	qU Awip svwrih Awip isrjnhwirAw ]16] (791-2, sUhI, mÚ 1) too aap savaareh aap sirjanhaari-aa. ||16||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v16	You Yourself embellish and adorn us, O Creator Lord. ||16||
RECORD	para 34400	slok mÚ 1 ] (791-2) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 34401	dIvw blY AMDyrw jwie ] (791-2, sUhI, mÚ 1) deevaa balai anDhayraa jaa-ay. When the lamp is lit, the darkness is dispelled;
DEFINE	para 34402	byd pwT miq pwpw Kwie ] (791-3, sUhI, mÚ 1) bayd paath mat paapaa khaa-ay. reading the Vedas, sinful intellect is destroyed.
DEFINE	para 34403	augvY sUru n jwpY cMdu ] (791-3, sUhI, mÚ 1) ugvai soor na jaapai chand. When the sun rises, the moon is not visible.
DEFINE	para 34404	jh igAwn pRgwsu AigAwnu imtMqu ] (791-3, sUhI, mÚ 1) jah gi-aan pargaas agi-aan mitant. Wherever spiritual wisdom appears, ignorance is dispelled.
DEFINE	para 34405	byd pwT sMswr kI kwr ] (791-3, sUhI, mÚ 1) bayd paath sansaar kee kaar. Reading the Vedas is the world's occupation;
RECORD	para 34406	piV@ piV@ pMifq krih bIcwr ] (791-4, sUhI, mÚ 1) parhH parh H pandit karahi beechaar. the Pandits read them, study them and contemplate them.
DEFINE	para 34407	ibnu bUJy sB hoie KuAwr ] (791-4, sUhI, mÚ 1) bin boojhay sabh ho-ay khu-aar. Without understanding, all are ruined.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	nwnk gurmuiK auqris pwir ]1] (791-4, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh utras paar. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukh is carried across. ||1||
RECORD	para 34409	mÚ 1 ] (791-5) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 34410	sbdY swdu n AwieE nwim n lgo ipAwru ] (791-5, sUhI, mÚ 1) sabdai saad na aa-i-o naam na lago pi-aar. Those who do not savor the Word of the Shabad, do not love the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 34411	rsnw iPkw bolxw inq inq hoie KuAwru ] (791-5, sUhI, mÚ 1) rasnaa fikaa bolnaa nit nit ho-ay khu-aar. They speak insipidly with their tongues, and are continually disgraced.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	nwnk pieAY ikriq kmwvxw koie n mytxhwru ]2] (791-6, sUhI, mÚ 1) naanak pa-i-ai kirat kamaavanaa ko-ay na maytanhaar. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, they act according to the karma of their past actions, which no one can erase. ||2||
RECORD	para 34413	pauVI ] (791-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 34414	ij pRBu swlwhy Awpxw so soBw pwey ] (791-6, sUhI, mÚ 1) je parabh saalaahay aapnaa so sobhaa paa-ay. One who praises his God, receives honor.
RECORD	para 34415	haumY ivchu dUir kir scu mMin vswey ] (791-7, sUhI, mÚ 1) ha-umai vichahu door kar sach man vasaa-ay. He drives out egotism from within himself, and enshrines the True Name within his mind.
RECORD	para 34416	scu bwxI gux aucrY scw suKu pwey ] (791-7, sUhI, mÚ 1) sach banee gun uchrai sachaa sukh paa-ay. Through the True Word of the Guru's Bani, he chants the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and finds true peace.
RECORD	para 34417	mylu BieAw icrI ivCuMinAw gur puriK imlwey ] (791-8, sUhI, mÚ 1) mayl bha-i-aa chiree vichhunni-aa gur purakh milaa-ay. He is united with the Lord, after being separated for so long; the Guru, the Primal Being, unites him with the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v17	mnu mYlw iev suDu hY hir nwmu iDAwey ]17] (791-8, sUhI, mÚ 1) man mailaa iv suDh hai har naam Dhi-aa-ay. ||17||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v17	In this way, his filthy mind is cleansed and purified, and he meditates on the Name of the Lord. ||17||
RECORD	para 34419	slok mÚ 1 ] (791-9) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 34420	kwieAw kUml Pul gux nwnk gupis mwl ] (791-9, sUhI, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa koomal ful gun naanak gupas maal. With the fresh leaves of the body, and the flowers of virtue, Nanak has weaved his garland.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	eynI PulI rau kry Avr ik cuxIAih fwl ]1] (791-9, sUhI, mÚ 1) aynee fulee ra-o karay avar ke chunee-ah daal. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v1	The Lord is pleased with such garlands, so why pick any other flowers? ||1||
RECORD	para 34422	mhlw 2 ] (791-10) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
