RECORD	iblwvlu mhlw 5 v2	igRih swkq CqIh pRkwr qy ibKU smwn ]2] (811-16, iblwvlu, mÚ 5) garihi saakat chhateeh parkaar tay bikhoo samaan. ||2||
DEFINE	iblwvlu mhlw 5 v2	The thirty-six tasty dishes of the faithless cynic, are just like poison. ||2||
DEFINE	para 35324	Bgq jnw kw lUgrw EiF ngn n hoeI ] (811-17, iblwvlu, mÚ 5) bhagat janaa kaa loograa odh nagan na ho-ee. Wearing the old blankets of the humble devotees, one is not naked.
RECORD	iblwvlu mhlw 5 v3	swkq isrpwau rysmI pihrq piq KoeI ]3] (811-17, iblwvlu, mÚ 5) saakat sirpaa-o raysmee pahirat pat kho-ee. ||3||
RECORD	iblwvlu mhlw 5 v3	But by putting on the silk clothes of the faithless cynic, one loses one's honor. ||3||
RECORD	para 35326	swkq isau muiK joirAY AD vIchu tUtY ] (811-18, iblwvlu, mÚ 5) saakat si-o mukh jori-ai aDh veechahu tootai. Friendship with the faithless cynic breaks down mid-way.
RECORD	iblwvlu mhlw 5 v4	hir jn kI syvw jo kry ieq aUqih CUtY ]4] (811-18, iblwvlu, mÚ 5) har jan kee sayvaa jo karay it ooteh chhootai. ||4||
DEFINE	iblwvlu mhlw 5 v4	But whoever serves the humble servants of the Lord, is emancipated here and hereafter. ||4||
RECORD	para 35328	sB ikCu qum@ hI qy hoAw Awip bxq bxweI ] (811-19, iblwvlu, mÚ 5) sabh kichh tum H hee tay ho-aa aap banat banaa-ee. Everything comes from You, O Lord; You Yourself created the creation.
RECORD	iblwvlu mhlw 5 v5	drsnu Bytq swD kw nwnk gux gweI ]5]14]44] (811-19, iblwvlu, mÚ 5) darsan bhaytat saaDh kaa naanak gun gaa-ee. ||5||
UPHOLD	iblwvlu mhlw 5 v5	Blessed with the Blessed Vision of the Darshan of the Holy, Nanak sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||5||
