DEFINE	para 36918	gurmuiK jnmu sPlu hY ijs no Awpy ley imlwie ] (850-5, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gurmukh janam safal hai jis no aapay la-ay milaa-ay. The birth of the Gurmukh is fruitful and auspicious. The Lord unites him with Himself.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk ndrI ndir kry qw nwm Dnu plY pwie ]2] (850-6, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak nadree nadar karay taa naam Dhan palai paa-ay. ||2||
WHEN	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, when the Merciful Lord grants His Mercy, one obtains the wealth of the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 36920	pauVI ] (850-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 36921	sB vifAweIAw hir nwm ivic hir gurmuiK iDAweIAY ] (850-6, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) sabh vadi-aa-ee-aa har naam vich har gurmukh Dhi-aa-ee-ai. All glorious greatness is in the Name of the Lord; as Gurmukh, meditate on the Lord.
WHEN	para 36922	ij vsqu mMgIAY sweI pweIAY jy nwim icqu lweIAY ] (850-7, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) je vasat mangee-ai saa-ee paa-ee-ai jay naam chit laa-ee-ai. One obtains all that he asks for, if he keeps his consciousness focused on the Lord.
WHEN	para 36923	guhj gl jIA kI kIcY siqgurU pwis qw srb suKu pweIAY ] (850-8, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) guhaj gal jee-a kee keechai satguroo paas taa sarab sukh paa-ee-ai. If he tells the secrets of his soul to the True Guru, then he finds absolute peace.
WHEN	para 36924	guru pUrw hir aupdysu dyie sB BuK lih jweIAY ] (850-8, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gur pooraa har updays day-ay sabh bhukh leh jaa-ee-ai. When the Perfect Guru bestows the Lord's Teachings, then all hunger departs.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v3	ijsu pUrib hovY iliKAw so hir gux gweIAY ]3] (850-9, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jis poorab hovai likhi-aa so har gun gaa-ee-ai. ||3||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v3	One who is blessed with such pre-ordained destiny, sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||3||
RECORD	para 36926	slok mÚ 3 ] (850-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 36927	siqgur qy KwlI ko nhI myrY pRiB myil imlwey ] (850-9, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) satgur tay khaalee ko nahee mayrai parabh mayl milaa-ay. No one goes away empty-handed from the True Guru; He unites me in Union with my God.
UPHOLD	para 36928	siqgur kw drsnu sPlu hY jyhw ko ieCy qyhw Plu pwey ] (850-10, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) satgur kaa darsan safal hai jayhaa ko ichhay tayhaa fal paa-ay. Fruitful is the Blessed Vision of the Darshan of the True Guru; through it, one obtains whatever fruitful rewards he desires.
DEFINE	para 36929	gur kw sbdu AMimRqu hY sB iqRsnw BuK gvwey ] (850-10, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gur kaa sabad amrit hai sabh tarisnaa bhukh gavaa-ay. The Word of the Guru's Shabad is Ambrosial Nectar. It banishes all hunger and thirst.
RECORD	para 36930	hir rsu pI sMqoKu hoAw scu visAw min Awey ] (850-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) har ras pee santokh ho-aa sach vasi-aa man aa-ay. Drinking in the sublime essence of the Lord brings contentment; the True Lord comes to dwell in the mind.
RECORD	para 36931	scu iDAwie Amrw pdu pwieAw Anhd sbd vjwey ] (850-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) sach Dhi-aa-ay amraa pad paa-i-aa anhad sabad vajaa-ay. Meditating on the True Lord, the status of immortality is obtained; the Unstruck Word of the Shabad vibrates and resounds.
DEFINE	para 36932	sco dh idis psirAw gur kY shij suBwey ] (850-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) sacho dah dis pasri-aa gur kai sahj subhaa-ay. The True Lord is pervading in the ten directions; through the Guru, this is intuitively known.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk ijn AMdir scu hY sy jn Cpih n iksY dy Cpwey ]1] (850-13, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak jin andar sach hai say jan chhapeh na kisai day chhapaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, those humble beings who have the Truth deep within, are never hidden, even if others try to hide them. ||1||
RECORD	para 36934	mÚ 3 ] (850-13) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
WHEN	para 36935	gur syvw qy hir pweIAY jw kau ndir kryie ] (850-13, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gur sayvaa tay har paa-ee-ai jaa ka-o nadar karay-i. Serving the Guru, one finds the Lord, when the Lord blesses him with His Glance of Grace.
WHEN	para 36936	mwns qy dyvqy Bey scI Bgiq ijsu dyie ] (850-14, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) maanas tay dayvtay bha-ay sachee bhagat jis day-ay. Human beings become angels, when the Lord blesses them with true devotional worship.
RECORD	para 36937	haumY mwir imlwieAnu gur kY sbid sucyie ] (850-14, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) ha-umai maar milaa-i-an gur kai sabad suchay-ay. Conquering egotism, they are blended with the Lord; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, they are purified.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk shjy imil rhy nwmu vifAweI dyie ]2] (850-15, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak sehjay mil rahay naam vadi-aa-ee day-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, they remain merged with the Lord; they are blessed with the glorious greatness of the Naam. ||2||
RECORD	para 36939	pauVI ] (850-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 36940	gur siqgur ivic nwvY kI vfI vifAweI hir krqY Awip vDweI ] (850-15, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gur satgur vich naavai kee vadee vadi-aa-ee har kartai aap vaDhaa-ee. Within the Guru, the True Guru, is the glorious greatness of the Name. The Creator Lord Himself has magnified it.
RECORD	para 36941	syvk isK siB vyiK vyiK jIvin@ En@w AMdir ihrdY BweI ] (850-16, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) sayvak sikh sabh vaykh vaykh jeevni H on Haa andar hirdai bhaa-ee. All His servants and Sikhs live by gazing, gazing upon it. It is pleasing to their hearts deep within.
RECORD	para 36942	inMdk dust vifAweI vyiK n skin En@w prwieAw Blw n suKweI ] (850-17, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) nindak dusat vadi-aa-ee vaykh na sakan on Haa paraa-i-aa bhalaa na sukhaa-ee. The slanderers and evil-doers cannot see this glorious greatness; they do not appreciate the goodness of others.
RECORD	para 36943	ikAw hovY iks hI kI JK mwrI jw scy isau bix AweI ] (850-17, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) ki-aa hovai kis hee kee jhakh maaree jaa sachay si-o ban aa-ee. What can be achieved by anyone babbling? The Guru is in love with the True Lord.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v4	ij gl krqy BwvY sw inq inq cVY svweI sB JiK JiK mrY lokweI ]4] (850-18, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) je gal kartay bhaavai saa nit nit charhai savaa-ee sabh jhakh jhakh marai lokaa-ee. ||4||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v4	That which is pleasing to the Creator Lord, increases day by day, while all the people babble uselessly. ||4||
RECORD	para 36945	slok mÚ 3 ] (850-19) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
UPHOLD	para 36946	iDRgu eyh Awsw dUjy Bwv kI jo moih mwieAw icqu lwey ] (850-19, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) Dharig ayh aasaa doojay bhaav kee jo mohi maa-i-aa chit laa-ay. Cursed are the hopes in the love of duality; they tie the consciousness to love and attachment to Maya.
RECORD	para 36947	hir suKu pl@ir iqAwigAw nwmu ivswir duKu pwey ] (850-19, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) har sukh pal Har ti-aagi-aa naam visaar dukh paa-ay. One who forsakes the peace of the Lord in exchange for straw, and forgets the Naam, suffers in pain.
RECORD	para 36949	mnmuK AigAwnI AMDuly jnim mrih iPir AwvY jwey ] (851-1, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) manmukh agi-aanee anDhulay janam mareh fir aavai jaa-ay. The ignorant self-willed manmukhs are blind. They are born, only to die again, and continue coming and going.
DEFINE	para 36950	kwrj isiD n hovnI AMiq gieAw pCuqwey ] (851-2, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) kaaraj siDh na hovnee ant ga-i-aa pachhutaa-ay. Their affairs are not resolved, and in the end, they depart, regretting and repenting.
