REQUIRE	para 36972	suKdwqw qyrY min vsY haumY jwie AiBmwnu ] (851-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) sukh-daata tayrai man vasai ha-umai jaa-ay abhimaan. The Giver of peace shall dwell in your mind; you shall be rid of egotism and pride.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk ndrI pweIAY AMimRqu guxI inDwnu ]2] (851-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak nadree paa-ee-ai amrit gunee niDhaan. ||2||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, by His Grace, one is blessed with the Ambrosial Nectar of the treasure of virtue. ||2||
RECORD	para 36974	pauVI ] (851-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 36975	ijqny pwiqswh swh rwjy Kwn aumrwv iskdwr hih iqqny siB hir ky kIey ] (851-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jitnay paatisaah saah raajay khaan umraav sikdaar heh titnay sabh har kay kee-ay. The kings, emperors, rulers, lords, nobles and chiefs, are all created by the Lord.
RECORD	para 36976	jo ikCu hir krwvY su Eie krih siB hir ky ArQIey ] (851-13, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jo kichh har karaavai so o-ay karahi sabh har kay arthee-ay. Whatever the Lord causes them to do, they do; they are all beggars, dependent on the Lord.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v6	hir hir ikrpwlu hoAw Bgq jnw aupir hir AwpxI ikrpw kir hir Awip riK lIey ]6] (851-16, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) har har kirpaal ho-aa bhagat janaa upar har aapnee kirpaa kar har aap rakh lee-ay. ||6||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v6	The Lord, Har, Har, is Merciful to His humble devotees; granting His Grace, the Lord Himself protects and preserves them. ||6||
RECORD	para 36980	slok mÚ 3 ] (851-17) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 36981	AMdir kptu sdw duKu hY mnmuK iDAwnu n lwgY ] (851-17, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) andar kapat sadaa dukh hai manmukh Dhi-aan na laagai. Fraud and hypocrisy within bring constant pain; the self-willed manmukh does not practice meditation.
REQUIRE	para 36982	duK ivic kwr kmwvxI duKu vrqY duKu AwgY ] (851-18, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) dukh vich kaar kamaavnee dukh vartai dukh aagai. Suffering in pain, he does his deeds; he is immersed in pain, and he shall suffer in pain hereafter.
DEFINE	para 36983	krmI siqguru BytIAY qw sic nwim ilv lwgY ] (851-18, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) karmee satgur bhaytee-ai taa sach naam liv laagai. By his karma, he meets the True Guru, and then, he is lovingly attuned to the True Name.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk shjy suKu hoie AMdrhu BRmu Bau BwgY ]1] (851-19, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak sehjay sukh ho-ay andrahu bharam bha-o bhaagai. ||1||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, he is naturally at peace; doubt and fear run away and leave him. ||1||
RECORD	para 36985	mÚ 3 ] (851-19) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 36986	gurmuiK sdw hir rMgu hY hir kw nwau min BwieAw ] (851-19, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gurmukh sadaa har rang hai har kaa naa-o man bhaa-i-aa. The Gurmukh is in love with the Lord forever. The Name of the Lord is pleasing to his mind.
RECORD	para 36988	gurmuiK vyKxu bolxw nwmu jpq suKu pwieAw ] (852-1, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gurmukh vaykhan bolnaa naam japat sukh paa-i-aa. The Gurmukh beholds and speaks the Naam, the Name of the Lord; chanting the Naam, he finds peace.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk gurmuiK igAwnu pRgwisAw iqmr AigAwnu AMDyru cukwieAw ]2] (852-1, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh gi-aan pargaasi-aa timar agi-aan anDhayr chukaa-i-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, the spiritual wisdom of the Gurmukh shines forth; the black darkness of ignorance is dispelled. ||2||
RECORD	para 36990	mÚ 3 ] (852-2) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 36991	mnmuK mYly mrih gvwr ] (852-2, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) manmukh mailay mareh gavaar. The filthy, foolish, self-willed manmukhs die.
DEFINE	para 36992	gurmuiK inrml hir rwiKAw aur Dwir ] (852-3, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gurmukh nirmal har raakhi-aa ur Dhaar. The Gurmukhs are immaculate and pure; they keep the Lord enshrined within their hearts.
RECORD	para 36993	Bniq nwnku suxhu jn BweI ] (852-3, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) bhanat naanak sunhu jan bhaa-ee. Prays Nanak, listen, O Siblings of Destiny!
REQUIRE	para 36994	siqguru syivhu haumY mlu jweI ] (852-3, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) satgur sayvihu ha-umai mal jaa-ee. Serve the True Guru, and the filth of your ego shall be gone.
RECORD	para 36995	AMdir sMsw dUKu ivAwpy isir DMDw inq mwr ] (852-4, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) andar sansaa dookh vi-aapay sir DhanDhaa nit maar. Deep within, the pain of skepticism afflicts them; their heads are constantly assaulted by worldly entanglements.
RECORD	para 36996	dUjY Bwie sUqy kbhu n jwgih mwieAw moh ipAwr ] (852-4, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay sootay kabahu na jaageh maa-i-aa moh pi-aar. Asleep in the love of duality, they never wake up; they are attached to the love of Maya.
RECORD	para 36997	nwmu n cyqih sbdu n vIcwrih iehu mnmuK kw bIcwr ] (852-5, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naam na cheeteh sabad na vichaareh ih manmukh kaa beechaar. They do not remember the Name, and they do not contemplate the Word of the Shabad; this is the view of the self-willed manmukhs.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v3	hir nwmu n BwieAw ibrQw jnmu gvwieAw nwnk jmu mwir kry KuAwr ]3] (852-5, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) har naam na bhaa-i-aa birthaa janam gavaa-i-aa naanak jam maar karay khu-aar. ||3||
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v3	They do not love the Lord's Name, and they lose their life uselessly. O Nanak, the Messenger of Death attacks them, and humiliates them. ||3||
RECORD	para 36999	pauVI ] (852-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 37000	ijs no hir Bgiq scu bKsIAnu so scw swhu ] (852-6, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jis no har bhagat sach bakhsee-an so sachaa saahu. He alone is a true king, whom the Lord blesses with true devotion.
RECORD	para 37001	iqs kI muhqwjI loku kFdw horqu hit n vQu n vyswhu ] (852-7, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) tis kee muhtaajee lok kadh-daa horat hat na vath na vaysaahu. People pledge their allegiance to him; no other store stocks this merchandise, nor deals in this trade.
RECORD	para 37002	Bgq jnw kau snmuKu hovY su hir rwis ley vymuK Bsu pwhu ] (852-7, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) bhagat janaa ka-o sanmukh hovai so har raas la-ay vaimukh bhas paahu. That humble devotee who turns his face towards the Guru and becomes sunmukh, receives the Lord's wealth; the faithless baymukh, who turns his face away from the Guru, gathers only ashes.
RECORD	para 37003	hir ky nwm ky vwpwrI hir Bgq hih jmu jwgwqI iqnw nyiV n jwhu ] (852-8, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) har kay naam kay vaapaaree har bhagat heh jam jaagaatee tinaa nayrh na jaahu. The Lord's devotees are dealers in the Name of the Lord. The Messenger of Death, the tax-collector, does not even approach them.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v7	jn nwnik hir nwm Dnu lidAw sdw vyprvwhu ]7] (852-9, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jan naanak har naam Dhan ladi-aa sadaa vayparvaahu. ||7||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v7	Servant Nanak has loaded the wealth of the Name of the Lord, who is forever independent and care-free. ||7||
RECORD	para 37005	slok mÚ 3 ] (852-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 37006	iesu jug mih BgqI hir Dnu KitAw horu sBu jgqu Brim BulwieAw ] (852-9, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) is jug meh bhagtee har Dhan khati-aa hor sabh jagat bharam bhulaa-i-aa. In this age, the devotee earns the wealth of the Lord; all the rest of the world wanders deluded in doubt.
RECORD	para 37007	gur prswdI nwmu min visAw Anidnu nwmu iDAwieAw ] (852-10, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee naam man vasi-aa an-din naam Dhi-aa-i-aa. By Guru's Grace, the Naam, the Name of the Lord, comes to dwell in his mind; night and day, he meditates on the Naam.
RECORD	para 37008	ibiKAw mwih audws hY haumY sbid jlwieAw ] (852-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) bikhi-aa maahi udaas hai ha-umai sabad jalaa-i-aa. In the midst of corruption, he remains detached; through the Word of the Shabad, he burns away his ego.
DEFINE	para 37009	Awip qirAw kul auDry DMnu jxydI mwieAw ] (852-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) aap tari-aa kul uDhray Dhan janaydee maa-i-aa. He crosses over, and saves his relatives as well; blessed is the mother who gave birth to him.
RECORD	para 37010	sdw shju suKu min visAw scy isau ilv lwieAw ] (852-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) sadaa sahj sukh man vasi-aa sachay si-o liv laa-i-aa. Peace and poise fill his mind forever, and he embraces love for the True Lord.
RECORD	para 37011	bRhmw ibsnu mhwdyau qRY gux Buly haumY mohu vDwieAw ] (852-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) barahmaa bisan mahaaday-o tarai gun bhulay ha-umai moh vaDhaa-i-aa. Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva wander in the three qualities, while their egotism and desire increase.
RECORD	para 37012	pMifq piV piV monI Buly dUjY Bwie icqu lwieAw ] (852-13, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) pandit parh parh monee bhulay doojai bhaa-ay chit laa-i-aa. The Pandits, the religious scholars and the silent sages read and debate in confusion; their consciousness is centered on the love of duality.
RECORD	para 37013	jogI jMgm sMinAwsI Buly ivxu gur qqu n pwieAw ] (852-14, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jogee jangam sani-aasee bhulay vin gur tat na paa-i-aa. The Yogis, wandering pilgrims and Sanyaasees are deluded; without the Guru, they do not find the essence of reality.
RECORD	para 37014	mnmuK duKIey sdw BRim Buly iqn@I ibrQw jnmu gvwieAw ] (852-14, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) manmukh dukhee-ay sadaa bharam bhulay tin Hee birthaa janam gavaa-i-aa. The miserable self-willed manmukhs are forever deluded by doubt; they waste away their lives uselessly.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk nwim rqy syeI jn smDy ij Awpy bKis imlwieAw ]1] (852-15, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay say-ee jan samDhay je aapay bakhas milaa-i-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, those who are imbued with the Naam are balanced and poised; forgiving them, the Lord blends them with Himself. ||1||
RECORD	para 37016	mÚ 3 ] (852-15) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 37017	nwnk so swlwhIAY ijsu vis sBu ikCu hoie ] (852-15, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak so salaahee-ai jis vas sabh kichh ho-ay. O Nanak, praise Him, who has control over everything.
DEFINE	para 37018	iqsih sryvhu pRwxIho iqsu ibnu Avru n koie ] (852-16, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) tiseh sarayvhu paraaneeho tis bin avar na ko-ay. Remember Him, O mortals - without Him, there is no other at all.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	gurmuiK AMqir min vsY sdw sdw suKu hoie ]2] (852-16, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gurmukh antar man vasai sadaa sadaa sukh ho-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	He dwells deep within those who are Gurmukh; forever and ever, they are at peace. ||2||
RECORD	para 37020	pauVI ] (852-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 37021	ijnI gurmuiK hir nwm Dnu n KitE sy dyvwlIey jug mwih ] (852-17, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jinee gurmukh har naam Dhan na khati-o say dayvaalee-ay jug maahi. Those who do not become Gurmukh and earn the wealth of the Lord's Name, are bankrupt in this age.
RECORD	para 37022	Eie mMgdy iPrih sB jgq mih koeI muih Quk n iqn kau pwih ] (852-18, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) o-ay mangday fireh sabh jagat meh ko-ee muhi thuk na tin ka-o paahi. They wander around begging all over the world, but no one even spits in their faces.
RECORD	para 37023	prweI bKIlI krih AwpxI prqIiq Kovin sgvw BI Awpu lKwih ] (852-18, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) paraa-ee bakheelee karahi aapnee parteet khovan sagvaa bhee aap lakhaahi. They gossip about others, and lose their credit, and expose themselves as well.
RECORD	para 37024	ijsu Dn kwrix cuglI krih so Dnu cuglI hiQ n AwvY Eie BwvY iqQY jwih ] (852-19, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jis Dhan kaaran chuglee karahi so Dhan chuglee hath na aavai o-ay bhaavai tithai jaahi. That wealth, for which they slander others, does not come into their hands, no matter where they go.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v8	gurmuiK syvk Bwie hir Dnu imlY iqQhu krmhIx lY n skih hor QY dys idsMqir hir Dnu nwih ]8] (853-1, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gurmukh sayvak bhaa-ay har Dhan milai tithhu karamheen lai na sakahi hor thai days disantar har Dhan naahi. ||8||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v8	Through loving service, the Gurmukhs receive the wealth of the Naam, but the unfortunate ones cannot receive it. This wealth is not found anywhere else, in this country or in any other. ||8||
RECORD	para 37027	slok mÚ 3 ] (853-2) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 37028	gurmuiK sMsw mUil n hoveI icMqw ivchu jwie ] (853-2, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gurmukh sansaa mool na hova-ee chintaa vichahu jaa-ay. The Gurmukh does not have an iota of skepticism or doubt; worries depart from within him.
RECORD	para 37029	jo ikCu hoie su shjy hoie khxw ikCU n jwie ] (853-3, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jo kichh ho-ay so sehjay ho-ay kahnaa kichhoo na jaa-ay. Whatever he does, he does with grace and poise. Nothing else can be said about him.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk iqn kw AwiKAw Awip suxy ij lieAnu pMnY pwie ]1] (853-3, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak tin kaa aakhi-aa aap sunay je la-i-an pannai paa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, the Lord Himself hears the speech of those whom He makes His own. ||1||
RECORD	para 37031	mÚ 3 ] (853-4) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 37032	kwlu mwir mnsw mnih smwxI AMqir inrmlu nwau ] (853-4, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) kaal maar mansaa maneh samaanee antar nirmal naa-o. He conquers death, and subdues the desires of his mind; the Immaculate Name abides deep within him.
RECORD	para 37033	Anidnu jwgY kdy n sovY shjy AMimRqu ipAwau ] (853-5, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) an-din jaagai kaday na sovai sehjay amrit pi-aa-o. Night and day, he remains awake and aware; he never sleeps, and he intuitively drinks in the Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	para 37034	mITw boly AMimRq bwxI Anidnu hir gux gwau ] (853-5, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) meethaa bolay amrit banee an-din har gun gaa-o. His speech is sweet, and his words are nectar; night and day, he sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	inj Gir vwsw sdw sohdy nwnk iqn imilAw suKu pwau ]2] (853-6, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) nij ghar vaasaa sadaa sohday naanak tin mili-aa sukh paa-o. ||2||
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	He dwells in the home of his own self, and appears beautiful forever; meeting him, Nanak finds peace. ||2||
RECORD	para 37036	pauVI ] (853-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 37037	hir Dnu rqn jvyhrI so guir hir Dnu hir pwshu dyvwieAw ] (853-6, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) har Dhan ratan javayharee so gur har Dhan har paashu dayvaa-i-aa. The wealth of the Lord is a jewel, a gem; the Guru has caused the Lord to grant that wealth of the Lord.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v9	hir ky idqy nwil iksY joru bKIlI n cleI idhu idhu inq inq cVY svwieAw ]9] (853-10, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) har kay ditay naal kisai jor bakheelee na chal-ee dihu dihu nit nit charhai savaa-i-aa. ||9||
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v9	No one's power or slander can prevail against the gifts of the Lord; day by day they continually, continuously increase. ||9||
RECORD	para 37042	slok mÚ 3 ] (853-11) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 37043	jgqu jlµdw riK lY AwpxI ikrpw Dwir ] (853-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jagat jalandaa rakh lai aapnee kirpaa Dhaar. The world is going up in flames - shower it with Your Mercy, and save it!
RECORD	para 37044	ijqu duAwrY aubrY iqqY lYhu aubwir ] (853-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jit du-aarai ubrai titai laihu ubaar. Save it, and deliver it, by whatever method it takes.
RECORD	para 37045	siqguir suKu vyKwilAw scw sbdu bIcwir ] (853-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) satgur sukh vaykhaali-aa sachaa sabad beechaar. The True Guru has shown the way to peace, contemplating the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk Avru n suJeI hir ibnu bKsxhwru ]1] (853-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak avar na sujh-ee har bin bakhsanhaar. ||1||
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	Nanak knows no other than the Lord, the Forgiving Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 37047	mÚ 3 ] (853-13) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 37048	haumY mwieAw mohxI dUjY lgY jwie ] (853-13, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) ha-umai maa-i-aa mohnee doojai lagai jaa-ay. Through egotism, fascination with Maya has trapped them in duality.
RECORD	para 37049	nw ieh mwrI n mrY nw ieh hit ivkwie ] (853-13, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naa ih maaree na marai naa ih hat vikaa-ay. It cannot be killed, it does not die, and it cannot be sold in a store.
DEFINE	para 37050	gur kY sbid prjwlIAY qw ieh ivchu jwie ] (853-14, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad parjaalee-ai taa ih vichahu jaa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, it is burnt away, and then it departs from within.
RECORD	para 37051	qnu mnu hovY aujlw nwmu vsY min Awie ] (853-14, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) tan man hovai ujlaa naam vasai man aa-ay. The body and mind become pure, and the Naam, the Name of the Lord, comes to dwell within the mind.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk mwieAw kw mwrxu sbdu hY gurmuiK pwieAw jwie ]2] (853-15, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak maa-i-aa kaa maaran sabad hai gurmukh paa-i-aa jaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, the Shabad is the killer of Maya; the Gurmukh obtains it. ||2||
RECORD	para 37053	pauVI ] (853-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 37054	siqgur kI vifAweI siqguir idqI Durhu hukmu buiJ nIswxu ] (853-16, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) satgur kee vadi-aa-ee satgur ditee Dharahu hukam bujh neesaan. The glorious greatness of the True Guru was bestowed by the True Guru; He understood this as the Insignia, the Mark of the Primal Lord's Will.
RECORD	para 37055	puqI BwqIeI jwvweI skI Aghu ipChu toil ifTw lwihEnu sBnw kw AiBmwnu ] (853-16, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) putee bhaatee-ee jaavaa-ee sakee agahu pichhahu tol dithaa laahi-on sabhnaa kaa abhimaan. He tested His sons, nephews, sons-in-law and relatives, and subdued the egotistical pride of them all.
UPHOLD	para 37056	ijQY ko vyKY iqQY myrw siqgurU hir bKisEsu sBu jhwnu ] (853-17, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jithai ko vaykhai tithai mayraa satguroo har bakhsi-os sabh jahaan. Wherever anyone looks, my True Guru is there; the Lord blessed Him with the whole world.
RECORD	para 37059	jn nwnk kY vil hoAw myrw suAwmI hir sjx purKu sujwnu ] (854-1, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jan naanak kai val ho-aa mayraa su-aamee har sajan purakh sujaan. My Lord and Master is on the side of servant Nanak. The All-powerful and All-knowing Lord God is my Best Friend.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v10	paudI iBiq dyiK kY siB Awie pey siqgur kI pYrI lwihEnu sBnw ikAhu mnhu gumwnu ]10] (854- 1, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) pa-udee bhit daykh kai sabh aa-ay pa-ay satgur kee pairee laahi-on sabhnaa ki-ahu manhu gumaan. ||10||
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v10	Seeing the food being distributed, everyone came and fell at the feet of the True Guru, who cleansed the minds of all of their egotistical pride. ||10||
RECORD	para 37061	slok mÚ 1 ] (854-2) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 37062	koeI vwhy ko luxY ko pwey Kilhwin ] (854-2, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) ko-ee vaahay ko lunai ko paa-ay khalihaan. One plants the seed, another harvests the crop, and still another beats the grain from the chaff.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	nwnk eyv n jwpeI koeI Kwie indwin ]1] (854-3, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) naanak ayv na jaap-ee ko-ee khaa-ay nidaan. ||1||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	O Nanak, it is not known, who will ultimately eat the grain. ||1||
RECORD	para 37064	mÚ 1 ] (854-3) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 37065	ijsu min visAw qirAw soie ] (854-3, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) jis man vasi-aa tari-aa so-ay. He alone is carried across, within whose mind the Lord abides.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	nwnk jo BwvY so hoie ]2] (854-4, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) naanak jo bhaavai so ho-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	O Nanak, that alone happens, which is pleasing to His Will. ||2||
RECORD	para 37067	pauVI ] (854-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 37068	pwrbRhim dieAwil swgru qwirAw ] (854-4, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) paarbarahm da-i-aal saagar taari-aa. The Merciful Supreme Lord God has carried me across the world-ocean.
RECORD	para 37069	guir pUrY imhrvwin Brmu Bau mwirAw ] (854-4, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) gur poorai miharvaan bharam bha-o maari-aa. The compassionate perfect Guru has eradicated my doubts and fears.
RECORD	para 37070	kwm k®oDu ibkrwlu dUq siB hwirAw ] (854-5, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) kaam kroDh bikraal doot sabh haari-aa. Unsatisfied sexual desire and unresolved anger, the horrible demons, have been totally destroyed.
RECORD	para 37071	AMimRq nwmu inDwnu kMiT auir DwirAw ] (854-5, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) amrit naam niDhaan kanth ur Dhaari-aa. I have enshrined the treasure of the Ambrosial Naam within my throat and heart.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v11	nwnk swDU sMig jnmu mrxu svwirAw ]11] (854-6, iblwvlu, mÚ 1) naanak saaDhoo sang janam maran savaari-aa. ||11||
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v11	O Nanak, in the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, my birth and death have been adorned and redeemed. ||11||
RECORD	para 37073	slok mÚ 3 ] (854-6) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 37074	ijn@I nwmu ivswirAw kUVy khx khMin@ ] (854-6, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jin Hee naam visaari-aa koorhay kahan kaha NniH. Those who forget the Naam, the Name of the Lord, are said to be false.
RECORD	para 37075	pMc cor iqnw Gru muhin@ haumY AMdir sMin@ ] (854-7, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) panch chor tinaa ghar muhni H ha-umai andar sa NniH. The five thieves plunder their homes, and egotism breaks in.
RECORD	para 37076	swkq muTy durmqI hir rsu n jwxMin@ ] (854-7, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) saakat muthay durmatee har ras na jaanaNniH. The faithless cynics are defrauded by their own evil-mindedness; they do not know the sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	para 37077	ijn@I AMimRqu Brim lutwieAw ibKu isau rcih rcMin@ ] (854-8, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jin Hee amrit bharam lutaa-i-aa bikh si-o racheh racha NniH. Those who lose the Ambrosial Nectar through doubt, remain engrossed and entangled in corruption.
RECORD	para 37078	dustw syqI iprhVI jn isau vwdu krMin@ ] (854-8, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) dustaa saytee pirharhee jan si-o vaad kara NniH. They make friends with the wicked, and argue with the humble servants of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 37079	nwnk swkq nrk mih jim bDy duK shMin@ ] (854-9, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak saakat narak meh jam baDhay dukh saha NniH. O Nanak, the faithless cynics are bound and gagged by the Messenger of Death, and suffer agony in hell.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	pieAY ikriq kmwvdy ijv rwKih iqvY rhMin@ ]1] (854-9, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) pa-i-ai kirat kamaavday jiv raakhahi tivai raha NniH. ||1||
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v1	They act according to the karma of the actions they committed before; as the Lord keeps them, so do they live. ||1||
RECORD	para 37081	mÚ 3 ] (854-10) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 37082	ijn@I siqguru syivAw qwxu inqwxy iqsu ] (854-10, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jin Hee satgur sayvi-aa taan nitaanay tis. Those who serve the True Guru, are transformed from powerless into powerful.
RECORD	para 37083	swis igrwis sdw min vsY jmu joih n skY iqsu ] (854-10, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) saas giraas sadaa man vasai jam johi na sakai tis. With every breath and morsel of food, the Lord abides in their minds forever, and the Messenger of Death cannot even see them.
DEFINE	para 37084	ihrdY hir hir nwm rsu kvlw syvik iqsu ] (854-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) hirdai har har naam ras kavlaa sayvak tis. The Name of the Lord, Har, Har, fills their hearts, and Maya is their servant.
RECORD	para 37085	hir dwsw kw dwsu hoie prm pdwrQu iqsu ] (854-11, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) har daasaa kaa daas ho-ay param padaarath tis. One who becomes the slave of the Lord's slaves, obtains the greatest treasure.
RECORD	para 37086	nwnk min qin ijsu pRBu vsY hau sd kurbwxY iqsu ] (854-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) naanak man tan jis parabh vasai ha-o sad kurbaanai tis. O Nanak, I am forever a sacrifice to that one, within whose mind and body God dwells.
RECORD	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	ijn@ kau pUrib iliKAw rsu sMq jnw isau iqsu ]2] (854-12, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jin H ka-o poorab likhi-aa ras sant janaa si-o tis. ||2||
DEFINE	iblwvlu kI vwr mhlw 4 v2	One who has such pre-ordained destiny, he alone is in love with the humble Saints. ||2||
RECORD	para 37088	pauVI ] (854-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 37089	jo boly pUrw siqgurU so prmysir suixAw ] (854-13, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) jo bolay pooraa satguroo so parmaysar suni-aa. Whatever the Perfect True Guru says, the Transcendent Lord hears.
DEFINE	para 37090	soeI vriqAw jgq mih Git Git muiK BixAw ] (854-13, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) so-ee varti-aa jagat meh ghat ghat mukh bhani-aa. It pervades and permeates the whole world, and it is on the mouth of each and every being.
DEFINE	para 37091	bhuqu vifAweIAw swihbY nh jwhI gxIAw ] (854-14, iblwvlu, mÚ 3) bahut vadi-aa-ee-aa saahibai nah jaahee ganee-aa. So numerous are the great glories of the Lord, they cannot even be counted.
