DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	You are not a renunciate, nor a man of the world. ||1||
RECORD	para 39475	jogI bYis rhhu duibDw duKu BwgY ] (903-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jogee bais rahhu dubiDhaa dukh bhaagai. Yogi, remain seated, and the pain of duality will run away from you.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	Gir Gir mwgq lwj n lwgY ]1] rhwau ] (903-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghar ghar maagat laaj na laagai. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. You beg from door to door, and you don't feel ashamed. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 39477	gwvih gIq n cInih Awpu ] (903-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gaavahi geet na cheeneh aap. You sing the songs, but you do not understand your own self.
RECORD	para 39478	ikau lwgI invrY prqwpu ] (903-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o laagee nivrai partaap. How will the burning pain within be relieved?
RECORD	para 39479	gur kY sbid rcY mn Bwie ] (903-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur kai sabad rachai man bhaa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, let your mind be absorbed in the Lord's Love,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	iBiKAw shj vIcwrI Kwie ]2] (903-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bhikhi-aa sahj veechaaree khaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	and you will intuitively experience the charity of contemplation. ||2||
RECORD	para 39481	Bsm cVwie krih pwKMfu ] (903-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bhasam charhaa-ay karahi pakhand. You apply ashes to your body, while acting in hypocrisy.
RECORD	para 39482	mwieAw moih shih jm fMfu ] (903-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) maa-i-aa mohi saheh jam dand. Attached to Maya, you will be beaten by Death's heavy club.
DEFINE	para 39483	PUtY Kwpru BIK n Bwie ] (903-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) footai khaapar bheekh na bhaa-ay. Your begging bowl is broken; it will not hold the charity of the Lord's Love.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	bMDin bwiDAw AwvY jwie ]3] (903-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) banDhan baaDhi-aa aavai jaa-ay. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	Bound in bondage, you come and go. ||3||
RECORD	para 39485	ibMdu n rwKih jqI khwvih ] (903-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bind na raakhahi jatee kahaaveh. You do not control your seed and semen, and yet you claim to practice abstinence.
RECORD	para 39486	mweI mwgq qRY loBwvih ] (903-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) maa-ee maagat tarai lobhaaveh. You beg from Maya, lured by the three qualities.
RECORD	para 39487	inrdieAw nhI joiq aujwlw ] (903-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) nirda-i-aa nahee jot ujaalaa. You have no compassion; the Lord's Light does not shine in you.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	bUfq bUfy srb jMjwlw ]4] (903-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) boodat booday sarab janjaalaa. ||4||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	You are drowned, drowned in worldly entanglements. ||4||
RECORD	para 39489	ByK krih iKMQw bhu QtUAw ] (903-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bhaykh karahi khinthaa baho thatoo-aa. You wear religious robes, and your patched coat assumes many disguises.
RECORD	para 39490	JUTo Kylu KylY bhu ntUAw ] (903-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jhootho khayl khaylai baho natoo-aa. You play all sorts of false tricks, like a juggler.
RECORD	para 39491	AMqir Agin icMqw bhu jwry ] (903-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar agan chintaa baho jaaray. The fire of anxiety burns brightly within you.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	ivxu krmw kYsy auqris pwry ]5] (903-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) vin karmaa kaisay utras paaray. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	Without the karma of good actions, how can you cross over? ||5||
RECORD	para 39493	muMdRw Ptk bnweI kwin ] (903-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mundraa fatak banaa-ee kaan. You make ear-rings of glass to wear in your ears.
RECORD	para 39494	mukiq nhI ibidAw ibigAwin ] (903-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mukat nahee bidi-aa bigi-aan. But liberation does not come from learning without understanding.
DEFINE	para 39495	ijhvw ieMdRI swid luoBwnw ] (903-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jihvaa indree saad lobhaanaa. You are lured by the tastes of the tongue and sex organs.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	psU Bey nhI imtY nIswnw ]6] (903-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) pasoo bha-ay nahee mitai neesaanaa. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	You have become a beast; this sign cannot be erased. ||6||
DEFINE	para 39497	iqRibiD logw iqRibiD jogw ] (903-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) taribaDh logaa taribaDh jogaa. The people of the world are entangled in the three modes; the Yogis are entangled in the three modes.
DEFINE	para 39498	sbdu vIcwrY cUkis sogw ] (903-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad veechaarai chookas sogaa. Contemplating the Word of the Shabad, sorrows are dispelled.
RECORD	para 39499	aUjlu swcu su sbdu hoie ] (903-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) oojal saach so sabad ho-ay. Through the Shabad, one becomes radiant, pure and truthful.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	jogI jugiq vIcwry soie ]7] (903-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jogee jugat veechaaray so-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	One who contemplates the true lifestyle is a Yogi. ||7||
DEFINE	para 39501	quJ pih nau iniD qU krxY jogu ] (903-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tujh peh na-o niDh too karnai jog. The nine treasures are with You, Lord; You are potent, the Cause of causes.
RECORD	para 39502	Qwip auQwpy kry su hogu ] (903-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) thaap uthaapay karay so hog. You establish and disestablish; whatever You do, happens.
RECORD	para 39503	jqu squ sMjmu scu sucIqu ] (903-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jat sat sanjam sach sucheet. One who practices celibacy, chastity, self-control, truth and pure consciousness
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	nwnk jogI iqRBvx mIqu ]8]2] (903-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak jogee taribhavan meet. ||8||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	2|| - O Nanak, that Yogi is the friend of the three worlds. ||8||2||
RECORD	para 39506	Ktu mtu dyhI mnu bYrwgI ] (903-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) khat mat dayhee man bairaagee. Above the six chakras of the body dwells the detached mind.
RECORD	para 39507	suriq sbdu Duin AMqir jwgI ] (903-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) surat sabad Dhun antar jaagee. Awareness of the vibration of the Word of the Shabad has been awakened deep within.
RECORD	para 39508	vwjY Anhdu myrw mnu lIxw ] (903-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) vaajai anhad mayraa man leenaa. The unstruck melody of the sound current resonates and resounds within; my mind is attuned to it.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	gur bcnI sic nwim pqIxw ]1] (903-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur bachnee sach naam pateenaa. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	Through the Guru's Teachings, my faith is confirmed in the True Name. ||1||
DEFINE	para 39510	pRwxI rwm Bgiq suKu pweIAY ] (903-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) paraanee raam bhagat sukh paa-ee-ai. O mortal, through devotion to the Lord, peace is obtained.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	gurmuiK hir hir mITw lwgY hir hir nwim smweIAY ]1] rhwau ] (903-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh har har meethaa laagai har har naam samaa-ee-ai. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. The Lord, Har, Har, seems sweet to the Gurmukh, who merges in the Name of the Lord, Har, Har. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 39513	mwieAw mohu ibvrij smwey ] (904-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) maa-i-aa moh bivaraj samaa-ay. Eradicating attachment to Maya, one merges into the Lord.
RECORD	para 39514	siqguru BytY myil imlwey ] (904-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satgur bhaytai mayl milaa-ay. Meeting with the True Guru, we unite in His Union.
DEFINE	para 39515	nwmu rqnu inrmolku hIrw ] (904-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naam ratan nirmolak heeraa. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is a priceless jewel, a diamond.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	iqqu rwqw myrw mnu DIrw ]2] (904-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tit raataa mayraa man Dheeraa. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	Attuned to it, the mind is comforted and encouraged. ||2||
RECORD	para 39517	haumY mmqw rogu n lwgY ] (904-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ha-umai mamtaa rog na laagai. The diseases of egotism and possessiveness do not afflict
RECORD	para 39518	rwm Bgiq jm kw Bau BwgY ] (904-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) raam bhagat jam kaa bha-o bhaagai. one who worships the Lord. Fear of the Messenger of Death runs away.
RECORD	para 39519	jmu jMdwru n lwgY moih ] (904-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jam jandaar na laagai mohi. The Messenger of Death, the enemy of the soul, does not touch me at all.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	inrml nwmu irdY hir soih ]3] (904-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) nirmal naam ridai har sohi. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	The Immaculate Name of the Lord illuminates my heart. ||3||
RECORD	para 39521	sbdu bIcwir Bey inrMkwrI ] (904-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad beechaar bha-ay nirankaaree. Contemplating the Shabad, we become Nirankaari - we come to belong to the Formless Lord God.
DEFINE	para 39522	gurmiq jwgy durmiq prhwrI ] (904-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmat jaagay durmat parhaaree. Awakening to the Guru's Teachings, evil-mindedness is taken away.
RECORD	para 39523	Anidnu jwig rhy ilv lweI ] (904-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) an-din jaag rahay liv laa-ee. Remaining awake and aware night and day, lovingly focused on the Lord,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	jIvn mukiq giq AMqir pweI ]4] (904-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jeevan mukat gat antar paa-ee. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	one becomes Jivan Mukta - liberated while yet alive. He finds this state deep within himself. ||4||
RECORD	para 39525	Ailpq guPw mih rhih inrwry ] (904-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) alipat gufaa meh raheh niraaray. In the secluded cave, I remain unattached.
RECORD	para 39526	qskr pMc sbid sMGwry ] (904-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) taskar panch sabad sanghaaray. With the Word of the Shabad, I have killed the five thieves.
RECORD	para 39527	pr Gr jwie n mnu folwey ] (904-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) par ghar jaa-ay na man dolaa-ay. My mind does not waver or go to the home of any other.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	shj inrMqir rhau smwey ]5] (904-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sahj nirantar raha-o samaa-ay. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	I remain intuitively absorbed deep within. ||5||
RECORD	para 39529	gurmuiK jwig rhy AauDUqw ] (904-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh jaag rahay a-uDhootaa. As Gurmukh, I remain awake and aware, unattached.
RECORD	para 39530	sd bYrwgI qqu proqw ] (904-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sad bairaagee tat parotaa. Forever detached, I am woven into the essence of reality.
DEFINE	para 39531	jgu sUqw mir AwvY jwie ] (904-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jag sootaa mar aavai jaa-ay. The world is asleep; it dies, and comes and goes in reincarnation.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	ibnu gur sbd n soJI pwie ]6] (904-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin gur sabad na sojhee paa-ay. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	Without the Word of the Guru's Shabad, it does not understand. ||6||
RECORD	para 39533	Anhd sbdu vjY idnu rwqI ] (904-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) anhad sabad vajai din raatee. The unstruck sound current of the Shabad vibrates day and night.
RECORD	para 39534	Aivgq kI giq gurmuiK jwqI ] (904-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) avigat kee gat gurmukh jaatee. The Gurmukh knows the state of the eternal, unchanging Lord God.
WHEN	para 39535	qau jwnI jw sbid pCwnI ] (904-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ta-o jaanee jaa sabad pachhaanee. When someone realizes the Shabad, then he truly knows.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	eyko riv rihAw inrbwnI ]7] (904-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ayko rav rahi-aa nirbaanee. ||7||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	The One Lord is permeating and pervading everywhere in Nirvaanaa. ||7||
DEFINE	para 39537	suMn smwiD shij mnu rwqw ] (904-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sunn samaaDh sahj man raataa. My mind is intuitively absorbed in the state of deepest Samaadhi;
RECORD	para 39538	qij hau loBw eyko jwqw ] (904-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) taj ha-o lobhaa ayko jaataa. renouncing egotism and greed, I have come to know the One Lord.
WHEN	para 39539	gur cyly Apnw mnu mwinAw ] (904-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur chaylay apnaa man maani-aa. When the disciple's mind accepts the Guru,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	nwnk dUjw myit smwinAw ]8]3] (904-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak doojaa mayt samaani-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	3|| O Nanak, duality is eradicated, and he merges in the Lord. ||8||3||
RECORD	para 39542	swhw gxih n krih bIcwru ] (904-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saahaa ganeh na karahi beechaar. You calculate the auspicious days, but you do not understand
DEFINE	para 39543	swhy aUpir eykMkwru ] (904-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saahay oopar aykankaar. that the One Creator Lord is above these auspicious days.
RECORD	para 39544	ijsu guru imlY soeI ibiD jwxY ] (904-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jis gur milai so-ee biDh jaanai. He alone knows the way, who meets the Guru.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	gurmiq hoie q hukmu pCwxY ]1] (904-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmat ho-ay ta hukam pachhaanai. ||1||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	When one follows the Guru's Teachings, then he realizes the Hukam of God's Command. ||1||
RECORD	para 39546	JUTu n boil pwfy scu khIAY ] (904-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jhooth na bol paaday sach kahee-ai. Do not tell lies, O Pandit; O religious scholar, speak the Truth.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	haumY jwie sbid Gru lhIAY ]1] rhwau ] (904-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ha-umai jaa-ay sabad ghar lahee-ai. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. When egotism is eradicated through the Word of the Shabad, then one finds His home. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 39548	gix gix joqku kWfI kInI ] (904-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gan gan jotak kaa Ndee keenee. Calculating and counting, the astrologer draws the horoscope.
RECORD	para 39549	pVY suxwvY qqu n cInI ] (904-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) parhai sunaavai tat na cheenee. He studies it and announces it, but he does not understand reality.
DEFINE	para 39550	sBsY aUpir gur sbdu bIcwru ] (904-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabhsai oopar gur sabad beechaar. Understand, that the Word of the Guru's Shabad is above all.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	hor kQnI bdau n sglI Cwru ]2] (904-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hor kathnee bada-o na saglee chhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	Do not speak of anything else; it is all just ashes. ||2||
RECORD	para 39552	nwvih Dovih pUjih sYlw ] (904-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naaveh Dhoveh poojeh sailaa. You bathe, wash, and worship stones.
DEFINE	para 39553	ibnu hir rwqy mYlo mYlw ] (904-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin har raatay mailo mailaa. But without being imbued with the Lord, you are the filthiest of the filthy.
REQUIRE	para 39554	grbu invwir imlY pRBu swriQ ] (904-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) garab nivaar milai parabh saarath. Subduing your pride, you shall receive the supreme wealth of God.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	mukiq pRwn jip hir ikrqwriQ ]3] (904-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mukat paraan jap har kirtaarath. ||3||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	The mortal is liberated and emancipated, meditating on the Lord. ||3||
RECORD	para 39556	vwcY vwdu n bydu bIcwrY ] (904-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) vaachai vaad na bayd beechaarai. You study the arguments, but do not contemplate the Vedas.
RECORD	para 39557	Awip fubY ikau ipqrw qwrY ] (904-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aap dubai ki-o pitraa taarai. You drown yourself - how will you save your ancestors?
DEFINE	para 39558	Git Git bRhmu cInY jnu koie ] (904-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghat ghat barahm cheenai jan ko-ay. How rare is that person who realizes that God is in each and every heart.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	siqguru imlY q soJI hoie ]4] (904-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satgur milai ta sojhee ho-ay. ||4||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	When one meets the True Guru, then he understands. ||4||
RECORD	para 39560	gxq gxIAY shsw duKu jIAY ] (904-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ganat ganee-ai sahsaa dukh jee-ai. Making his calculations, cynicism and suffering afflict his soul.
DEFINE	para 39561	gur kI srix pvY suKu QIAY ] (904-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur kee saran pavai sukh thee-ai. Seeking the Sanctuary of the Guru, peace is found.
RECORD	para 39562	kir AprwD srix hm AwieAw ] (904-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kar apraaDh saran ham aa-i-aa. I sinned and made mistakes, but now I seek Your Sanctuary.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	gur hir Byty purib kmwieAw ]5] (904-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur har bhaytay purab kamaa-i-aa. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	The Guru led me to meet the Lord, according to my past actions. ||5||
WHEN	para 39564	gur srix n AweIAY bRhmu n pweIAY ] (904-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur saran na aa-ee-ai barahm na paa-ee-ai. If one does not enter the Guru's Sanctuary, God cannot be found.
DEFINE	para 39565	Brim BulweIAY jnim mir AweIAY ] (904-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bharam bhulaa-ee-ai janam mar aa-ee-ai. Deluded by doubt, one is born, only to die, and come back again.
DEFINE	para 39566	jm dir bwDau mrY ibkwru ] (904-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jam dar baaDha-o marai bikaar. Dying in corruption, he is bound and gagged at Death's door.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	nw irdY nwmu n sbdu Acwru ]6] (904-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naa ridai naam na sabad achaar. ||6||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is not in his heart, and he does not act according to the Shabad. ||6||
RECORD	para 39568	ieik pwDy pMifq imsr khwvih ] (904-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ik paaDhay pandit misar kahaaveh. Some call themselves Pandits, religious scholars and spiritual teachers.
RECORD	para 39569	duibDw rwqy mhlu n pwvih ] (904-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) dubiDhaa raatay mahal na paavahi. Tinged with double-mindedness, they do not find the Mansion of the Lord's Presence.
RECORD	para 39571	ijsu gur prswdI nwmu ADwru ] (905-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jis gur parsaadee naam aDhaar. One who takes the Support of the Naam, by Guru's Grace,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	koit mDy ko jnu Awpwru ]7] (905-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kot maDhay ko jan aapaar. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	is a rare person, one among millions, incomparable. ||7||
DEFINE	para 39573	eyku burw Blw scu eykY ] (905-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ayk buraa bhalaa sach aykai. One is bad, and another good, but the One True Lord is contained in all.
RECORD	para 39574	bUJu igAwnI sqgur kI tykY ] (905-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) boojh gi-aanee satgur kee taykai. Understand this, O spiritual teacher, through the support of the True Guru:
DEFINE	para 39575	gurmuiK ivrlI eyko jwixAw ] (905-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh virlee ayko jaani-aa. rare indeed is that Gurmukh, who realizes the One Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	Awvxu jwxw myit smwixAw ]8] (905-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aavan jaanaa mayt samaani-aa. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	His comings and goings cease, and he merges in the Lord. ||8||
RECORD	para 39577	ijn kY ihrdY eykMkwru ] (905-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jin kai hirdai aykankaar. Those who have the One Universal Creator Lord within their hearts,
RECORD	para 39578	srb guxI swcw bIcwru ] (905-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sarab gunee saachaa beechaar. possess all virtues; they contemplate the True Lord.
RECORD	para 39579	gur kY BwxY krm kmwvY ] (905-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur kai bhaanai karam kamaavai. One who acts in harmony with the Guru's Will,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v9	nwnk swcy swic smwvY ]9]4] (905-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak saachay saach samaavai. ||9||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v9	4|| O Nanak, is absorbed in the Truest of the True. ||9||4||
RECORD	para 39582	hTu ingRhu kir kwieAw CIjY ] (905-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hath nigarahu kar kaa-i-aa chheejai. Practicing restraint by Hatha Yoga, the body wears away.
DEFINE	para 39583	vrqu qpnu kir mnu nhI BIjY ] (905-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) varat tapan kar man nahee bheejai. The mind is not softened by fasting or austerities.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	rwm nwm sir Avru n pUjY ]1] (905-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) raam naam sar avar na poojai. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	Nothing else is equal to worship of the Lord's Name. ||1||
RECORD	para 39585	guru syiv mnw hir jn sMgu kIjY ] (905-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur sayv manaa har jan sang keejai. Serve the Guru, O mind, and associate with the humble servants of the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	jmu jMdwru joih nhI swkY srpin fis n skY hir kw rsu pIjY ]1] rhwau ] (905-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jam jandaar johi nahee saakai sarpan das na sakai har kaa ras peejai. ||1||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. The tyrannical Messenger of Death cannot touch you, and the serpent of Maya cannot sting you, when you drink in the sublime essence of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 39587	vwdu pVY rwgI jgu BIjY ] (905-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) vaad parhai raagee jag bheejai. The world reads the arguments, and is softened only by music.
DEFINE	para 39588	qRY gux ibiKAw jnim mrIjY ] (905-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tarai gun bikhi-aa janam mareejai. In the three modes and corruption, they are born and die.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	rwm nwm ibnu dUKu shIjY ]2] (905-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) raam naam bin dookh saheejai. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	Without the Lord's Name, they endure suffering and pain. ||2||
RECORD	para 39590	cwVis pvnu isMGwsnu BIjY ] (905-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) chaarhas pavan singhaasan bheejai. The Yogi draws the breath upwards, and opens the Tenth Gate.
RECORD	para 39591	inaulI krm Ktu krm krIjY ] (905-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ni-ulee karam khat karam kareejai. He practices inner cleansing and the six rituals of purification.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	rwm nwm ibnu ibrQw swsu lIjY ]3] (905-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) raam naam bin birthaa saas leejai. ||3||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	But without the Lord's Name, the breath he draws is useless. ||3||
RECORD	para 39593	AMqir pMc Agin ikau DIrju DIjY ] (905-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar panch agan ki-o Dheeraj Dheejai. The fire of the five passions burns within him; how can he be calm?
DEFINE	para 39594	AMqir coru ikau swdu lhIjY ] (905-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar chor ki-o saad laheejai. The thief is within him; how can he taste the taste?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	gurmuiK hoie kwieAw gVu lIjY ]4] (905-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh ho-ay kaa-i-aa garh leejai. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	One who becomes Gurmukh conquers the body-fortress. ||4||
RECORD	para 39596	AMqir mYlu qIrQ BrmIjY ] (905-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar mail tirath bharmeejai. With filth within, he wanders around at places of pilgrimage.
DEFINE	para 39597	mnu nhI sUcw ikAw soc krIjY ] (905-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) man nahee soochaa ki-aa soch kareejai. His mind is not pure, so what is the use of performing ritual cleansings?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	ikrqu pieAw dosu kw kau dIjY ]5] (905-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kirat pa-i-aa dos kaa ka-o deejai. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	He carries the karma of his own past actions; who else can he blame? ||5||
RECORD	para 39599	AMnu n Kwih dyhI duKu dIjY ] (905-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ann na khaahi dayhee dukh deejai. He does not eat food; he tortures his body.
DEFINE	para 39600	ibnu gur igAwn iqRpiq nhI QIjY ] (905-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin gur gi-aan taripat nahee theejai. Without the Guru's wisdom, he is not satisfied.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	mnmuiK jnmY jnim mrIjY ]6] (905-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manmukh janmai janam mareejai. ||6||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	The self-willed manmukh is born only to die, and be born again. ||6||
RECORD	para 39602	siqgur pUiC sMgiq jn kIjY ] (905-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satgur poochh sangat jan keejai. Go, and ask the True Guru, and associate with the Lord's humble servants.
FORBID	para 39603	mnu hir rwcY nhI jnim mrIjY ] (905-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) man har raachai nahee janam mareejai. Your mind shall merge into the Lord, and you shall not be reincarnated to die again.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	rwm nwm ibnu ikAw krmu kIjY ]7] (905-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) raam naam bin ki-aa karam keejai. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	Without the Lord's Name, what can anyone do? ||7||
RECORD	para 39605	aUNdr dUMdr pwis DrIjY ] (905-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ooNdar dooNdar paas Dhareejai. Silence the mouse scurrying around within you.
RECORD	para 39606	Dur kI syvw rwmu rvIjY ] (905-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) Dhur kee sayvaa raam raveejai. Serve the Primal Lord, by chanting the Lord's Name.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	nwnk nwmu imlY ikrpw pRB kIjY ]8]5] (905-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak naam milai kirpaa parabh keejai. ||8||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	5|| O Nanak, God blesses us with His Name, when He grants His Grace. ||8||5||
DEFINE	para 39609	AMqir auqBuju Avru n koeI ] (905-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar ut-bhuj avar na ko-ee. The created Universe emanated from within You; there is no other at all.
DEFINE	para 39610	jo khIAY so pRB qy hoeI ] (905-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jo kahee-ai so parabh tay ho-ee. Whatever is said to be, is from You, O God.
DEFINE	para 39611	jugh jugMqir swihbu scu soeI ] (905-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jugah jugantar saahib sach so-ee. He is the True Lord and Master, throughout the ages.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	auqpiq prlau Avru n koeI ]1] (905-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) utpat parla-o avar na ko-ee. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	Creation and destruction do not come from anyone else. ||1||
DEFINE	para 39613	AYsw myrw Twkuru gihr gMBIru ] (905-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aisaa mayraa thaakur gahir gambheer. Such is my Lord and Master, profound and unfathomable.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	ijin jipAw iqn hI suKu pwieAw hir kY nwim n lgY jm qIru ]1] rhwau ] (905-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jin japi-aa tin hee sukh paa-i-aa har kai naam na lagai jam teer. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Whoever meditates on Him, finds peace. The arrow of the Messenger of Death does not strike one who has the Name of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 39615	nwmu rqnu hIrw inrmolu ] (905-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naam ratan heeraa nirmol. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is a priceless jewel, a diamond.
DEFINE	para 39616	swcw swihbu Amru Aqolu ] (905-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saachaa saahib amar atol. The True Lord Master is immortal and immeasurable.
DEFINE	para 39617	ijhvw sUcI swcw bolu ] (905-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jihvaa soochee saachaa bol. That tongue which chants the True Name is pure.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	Gir dir swcw nwhI rolu ]2] (905-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghar dar saachaa naahee rol. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	The True Lord is in the home of the self; there is no doubt about it. ||2||
RECORD	para 39619	ieik bn mih bYsih fUgir AsQwnu ] (905-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ik ban meh baiseh doogar asthaan. Some sit in the forests, and some make their home in the mountains.
RECORD	para 39620	nwmu ibswir pcih AiBmwnu ] (905-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naam bisaar pacheh abhimaan. Forgetting the Naam, they rot away in egotistical pride.
DEFINE	para 39621	nwm ibnw ikAw igAwn iDAwnu ] (905-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naam binaa ki-aa gi-aan Dhi-aan. Without the Naam, what is the use of spiritual wisdom and meditation?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	gurmuiK pwvih drgih mwnu ]3] (905-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh paavahi dargahi maan. ||3||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	The Gurmukhs are honored in the Court of the Lord. ||3||
RECORD	para 39623	hTu AhMkwru krY nhI pwvY ] (905-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hath aha Nkaar karai nahee paavai. Acting stubbornly in egotism, one does not find the Lord.
RECORD	para 39624	pwT pVY ly lok suxwvY ] (905-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) paath parhai lay lok sunaavai. Studying the scriptures, reading them to other people,
DEFINE	para 39626	qIriQ Brmis ibAwiD n jwvY ] (906-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tirath bharmas bi-aaDh na jaavai. and wandering around at places of pilgrimage, the disease is not taken away.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	nwm ibnw kYsy suKu pwvY ]4] (906-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naam binaa kaisay sukh paavai. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	Without the Naam, how can one find peace? ||4||
RECORD	para 39628	jqn krY ibMdu ikvY n rhweI ] (906-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jatan karai bind kivai na rahaa-ee. No matter how much he tries, he cannot control his semen and seed.
RECORD	para 39629	mnUAw folY nrky pweI ] (906-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manoo-aa dolai narkay paa-ee. His mind wavers, and he falls into hell.
DEFINE	para 39630	jm puir bwDo lhY sjweI ] (906-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jam pur baaDho lahai sajaa-ee. Bound and gagged in the City of Death, he is tortured.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	ibnu nwvY jIau jil bil jweI ]5] (906-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin naavai jee-o jal bal jaa-ee. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	Without the Name, his soul cries out in agony. ||5||
RECORD	para 39632	isD swiDk kyqy muin dyvw ] (906-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) siDh saaDhik kaytay mun dayvaa. The many Siddhas and seekers, silent sages and demi-gods
RECORD	para 39633	hiT ingRih n iqRpqwvih Byvw ] (906-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hath nigrahi na tariptaaveh bhayvaa. cannot satisfy themselves by practicing restraint through Hatha Yoga.
RECORD	para 39634	sbdu vIcwir ghih gur syvw ] (906-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad veechaar gaheh gur sayvaa. One who contemplates the Word of the Shabad, and serves the Guru
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	min qin inrml AiBmwn AByvw ]6] (906-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) man tan nirmal abhimaan abhayvaa. ||6||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	- his mind and body become immaculate, and his egotistical pride is obliterated. ||6||
UPHOLD	para 39636	krim imlY pwvY scu nwau ] (906-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) karam milai paavai sach naa-o. Blessed with Your Grace, I obtain the True Name.
RECORD	para 39637	qum srxwgiq rhau suBwau ] (906-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tum sarnaagat raha-o subhaa-o. I remain in Your Sanctuary, in loving devotion.
RECORD	para 39638	qum qy aupijE BgqI Bwau ] (906-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tum tay upji-o bhagtee bhaa-o. Love for Your devotional worship has welled up within me.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	jpu jwpau gurmuiK hir nwau ]7] (906-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jap jaapa-o gurmukh har naa-o. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	As Gurmukh, I chant and meditate on the Lord's Name. ||7||
DEFINE	para 39640	haumY grbu jwie mn BInY ] (906-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ha-umai garab jaa-ay man bheenai. When one is rid of egotism and pride, his mind is drenched in the Lord's Love.
WHEN	para 39641	JUiT n pwvis pwKMif kInY ] (906-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jhooth na paavas pakhand keenai. Practicing fraud and hypocrisy, he does not find God.
RECORD	para 39642	ibnu gur sbd nhI Gru bwru ] (906-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin gur sabad nahee ghar baar. Without the Word of the Guru's Shabad, he cannot find the Lord's Door.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	nwnk gurmuiK qqu bIcwru ]8]6] (906-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh tat beechaar. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	6|| O Nanak, the Gurmukh contemplates the essence of reality. ||8||6||
ALLOW	para 39645	ijau AwieAw iqau jwvih baury ijau jnmy iqau mrxu BieAw ] (906-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ji-o aa-i-aa ti-o jaaveh ba-uray ji-o janmay ti-o maran bha-i-aa. As you come, so will you leave, you fool; as you were born, so will you die.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	ijau rs Bog kIey qyqw duKu lwgY nwmu ivswir Bvjil pieAw ]1] (906-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ji-o ras bhog kee-ay taytaa dukh laagai naam visaar bhavjal pa-i-aa. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	As you enjoy pleasures, so will you suffer pain. Forgetting the Naam, the Name of the Lord, you will fall into the terrifying world-ocean. ||1||
DEFINE	para 39647	qnu Dnu dyKq grib gieAw ] (906-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tan Dhan daykhat garab ga-i-aa. Gazing upon your body and wealth, you are so proud.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	kink kwmnI isau hyqu vDwieih kI nwmu ivswrih Brim gieAw ]1] rhwau ] (906-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kanik kaamnee si-o hayt vaDhaa-ihi kee naam visaareh bharam ga-i-aa. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Your love for gold and sexual pleasures increases; why have you forgotten the Naam, and why do you wander in doubt? ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 39649	jqu squ sMjmu sIlu n rwiKAw pRyq ipMjr mih kwstu BieAw ] (906-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jat sat sanjam seel na raakhi-aa parayt pinjar meh kaasat bha-i-aa. You do not practice truth, abstinence, self-discipline or humility; the ghost within your skeleton has turned to dry wood.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	puMnu dwnu iesnwnu n sMjmu swDsMgiq ibnu bwid jieAw ]2] (906-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) punn daan isnaan na sanjam saaDhsangat bin baad ja-i-aa. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	You have not practiced charity, donations, cleansing baths or austerities. Without the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, your life has gone in vain. ||2||
RECORD	para 39651	lwlic lwgY nwmu ibswirE Awvq jwvq jnmu gieAw ] (906-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) laalach laagai naam bisaari-o aavat jaavat janam ga-i-aa. Attached to greed, you have forgotten the Naam. Coming and going, your life has been ruined.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	jw jmu Dwie kys gih mwrY suriq nhI muiK kwl gieAw ]3] (906-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jaa jam Dhaa-ay kays geh maarai surat nahee mukh kaal ga-i-aa. ||3||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	When the Messenger of Death grabs you by your hair, you will be punished. You are unconscious, and have fallen into Death's mouth. ||3||
RECORD	para 39653	Aihinis inMdw qwiq prweI ihrdY nwmu n srb dieAw ] (906-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ahinis nindaa taat paraa-ee hirdai naam na sarab da-i-aa. Day and night, you jealously slander others; in your heart, you have neither the Naam, nor compassion for all.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	ibnu gur sbd n giq piq pwvih rwm nwm ibnu nrik gieAw ]4] (906-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin gur sabad na gat pat paavahi raam naam bin narak ga-i-aa. ||4||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	Without the Word of the Guru's Shabad, you will not find salvation or honor. Without the Lord's Name, you shall go to hell. ||4||
RECORD	para 39655	iKn mih vys krih ntUAw ijau moh pwp mih glqu gieAw ] (906-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) khin meh vays karahi natoo-aa ji-o moh paap meh galat ga-i-aa. In an instant, you change into various costumes, like a juggler; you are entangled in emotional attachment and sin.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	ieq auq mwieAw dyiK pswrI moh mwieAw kY mgnu BieAw ]5] (906-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) it ut maa-i-aa daykh pasaaree moh maa-i-aa kai magan bha-i-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	You gaze here and there upon the expanse of Maya; you are intoxicated with attachment to Maya. ||5||
RECORD	para 39657	krih ibkwr ivQwr Gnyry suriq sbd ibnu Brim pieAw ] (906-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) karahi bikaar vithaar ghanayray surat sabad bin bharam pa-i-aa. You act in corruption, and put on ostentatious shows, but without awareness of the Shabad, you have fallen into confusion.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	haumY rogu mhw duKu lwgw gurmiq lyvhu rogu gieAw ]6] (906-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ha-umai rog mahaa dukh laagaa gurmat layvhu rog ga-i-aa. ||6||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	You suffer great pain from the disease of egotism. Following the Guru's Teachings, you shall be rid of this disease. ||6||
RECORD	para 39659	suK sMpiq kau Awvq dyKY swkq min AiBmwnu BieAw ] (906-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sukh sampat ka-o aavat daykhai saakat man abhimaan bha-i-aa. Seeing peace and wealth come to him, the faithless cynic become proud in his mind.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	ijs kw iehu qnu Dnu so iPir lyvY AMqir shsw dUKu pieAw ]7] (906-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jis kaa ih tan Dhan so fir layvai antar sahsaa dookh pa-i-aa. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	But He who owns this body and wealth, takes them back again, and then the mortal feels anxiety and pain deep within. ||7||
RECORD	para 39661	AMiq kwil ikCu swiQ n cwlY jo dIsY sBu iqsih mieAw ] (906-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ant kaal kichh saath na chaalai jo deesai sabh tiseh ma-i-aa. At the very last instant, nothing goes along with you; all is visible only by His Mercy.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	Awid purKu AprMpru so pRBu hir nwmu irdY lY pwir pieAw ]8] (906-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aad purakh aprampar so parabh har naam ridai lai paar pa-i-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	God is our Primal and Infinite Lord; enshrining the Lord's Name in the heart, one crosses over. ||8||
RECORD	para 39663	mUey kau rovih iksih suxwvih BY swgr Asrwil pieAw ] (906-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) moo-ay ka-o roveh kiseh sunaaveh bhai saagar asraal pa-i-aa. You weep for the dead, but who hears you weeping? The dead have fallen to the serpent in the terrifying world-ocean.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v9	dyiK kutMbu mwieAw igRh mMdru swkqu jMjwil prwil pieAw ]9] (906-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) daykh kutamb maa-i-aa garih mandar saakat janjaal paraal pa-i-aa. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v9	Gazing upon his family, wealth, household and mansions, the faithless cynic is entangled in worthless worldly affairs. ||9||
WHEN	para 39666	jw Awey qw iqnih pTwey cwly iqnY bulwie lieAw ] (907-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jaa aa-ay taa tineh pathaa-ay chaalay tinai bulaa-ay la-i-aa. He comes when the Lord sends him; when the Lord calls him back, he goes.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v10	jo ikCu krxw so kir rihAw bKsxhwrY bKis lieAw ]10] (907-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jo kichh karnaa so kar rahi-aa bakhsanhaarai bakhas la-i-aa. ||10||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v10	Whatever he does, the Lord is doing. The Forgiving Lord forgives him. ||10||
RECORD	para 39668	ijin eyhu cwiKAw rwm rswiexu iqn kI sMgiq Koju BieAw ] (907-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jin ayhu chaakhi-aa raam rasaa-in tin kee sangat khoj bha-i-aa. I seek to be with those who have tasted this sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v11	iriD isiD buiD igAwnu gurU qy pwieAw mukiq pdwrQu srix pieAw ]11] (907-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) riDh siDh buDh gi-aan guroo tay paa-i-aa mukat padaarath saran pa-i-aa. ||11||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v11	Wealth, miraculous spiritual powers, wisdom and spiritual knowledge, are obtained from the Guru. The treasure of liberation is obtained in His Sanctuary. ||11||
RECORD	para 39670	duKu suKu gurmuiK sm kir jwxw hrK sog qy ibrkqu BieAw ] (907-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) dukh sukh gurmukh sam kar jaanaa harakh sog tay birkat bha-i-aa. The Gurmukh looks upon pain and pleasure as one and the same; he remains untouched by joy and sorrow.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v12	Awpu mwir gurmuiK hir pwey nwnk shij smwie lieAw ]12]7] (907-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aap maar gurmukh har paa-ay naanak sahj samaa-ay la-i-aa. ||12||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v12	7|| Conquering his self-conceit, the Gurmukh finds the Lord; O Nanak, he intuitively merges into the Lord. ||12||7||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 ] (907-5)
RECORD	para 39672	raamkalee dakh-nee mehlaa 1. Raamkalee, Dakhanee, First Mehl:
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v1	jqu squ sMjmu swcu idRVwieAw swc sbid ris lIxw ]1] (907-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) jat sat sanjam saach drirh-aa-i-aa saach sabad ras leenaa. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v1	Abstinence, chastity, self-control and truthfulness have been implanted within me; I am imbued with the sublime essence of the True Word of the Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	para 39674	myrw guru dieAwlu sdw rMig lIxw ] (907-6, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) mayraa gur da-i-aal sadaa rang leenaa. My Merciful Guru remains forever imbued with the Lord's Love.
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v1	Aihinis rhY eyk ilv lwgI swcy dyiK pqIxw ]1] rhwau ] (907-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ahinis rahai ayk liv laagee saachay daykh pateenaa. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Day and night, He remains lovingly focused on the One Lord; gazing upon the True Lord, He is pleased. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v2	rhY ggn puir idRsit smYsir Anhq sbid rMgIxw ]2] (907-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) rahai gagan pur darisat samaisar anhat sabad rangeenaa. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v2	He abides in the Tenth Gate, and looks equally upon all; He is imbued with the unstruck sound current of the Shabad. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v3	squ bMiD kupIn Birpuir lIxw ijhvw rMig rsIxw ]3] (907-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sat banDh kupeen bharipur leenaa jihvaa rang raseenaa. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v3	Wearing the loin-cloth of chastity, He remains absorbed in the all-pervading Lord; His tongue enjoys the taste of God's Love. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v4	imlY gur swcy ijin rcu rwcy ikrqu vIcwir pqIxw ]4] (907-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) milai gur saachay jin rach raachay kirat veechaar pateenaa. ||4||
DEFINE	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v4	The One who created the creation has met the True Guru; contemplating the Guru's lifestyle, He is pleased. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v5	eyk mih srb srb mih eykw eyh siqguir dyiK idKweI ]5] (907-9, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ayk meh sarab sarab meh aykaa ayh satgur daykh dikhaa-ee. ||5||
DEFINE	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v5	All are in the One, and the One is in all. This is what the True Guru has shown me. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v6	ijin kIey KMf mMfl bRhmMfw so pRBu lKnu n jweI ]6] (907-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) jin kee-ay khand mandal barahmandaa so parabh lakhan na jaa-ee. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v6	He who created the worlds, solar systems and galaxies - that God cannot be known. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v7	dIpk qy dIpku prgwisAw iqRBvx joiq idKweI ]7] (907-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) deepak tay deepak pargaasi-aa taribhavan jot dikhaa-ee. ||7||
DEFINE	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v7	From the lamp of God, the lamp within is lit; the Divine Light illuminates the three worlds. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v8	scY qKiq sc mhlI bYTy inrBau qwVI lweI ]8] (907-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sachai takhat sach mahlee baithay nirbha-o taarhee laa-ee. ||8||
DEFINE	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v8	The Guru sits on the true throne in the true mansion; He is attuned, absorbed in the Fearless Lord. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v9	moih gieAw bYrwgI jogI Git Git ikMgurI vweI ]9] (907-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) mohi ga-i-aa bairaagee jogee ghat ghat kinguree vaa-ee. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v9	The Guru, the detached Yogi, has enticed the hearts of all; He plays His harp in each and every heart. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v10	nwnk srix pRBU kI CUty siqgur scu sKweI ]10]8] (907-12, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naanak saran parabhoo kee chhootay satgur sach sakhaa-ee. ||10||
DEFINE	rwmklI dKxI mhlw 1 v10	8|| O Nanak, in God's Sanctuary, one is emancipated; the True Guru becomes our true help and support. ||10||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	AauhiT hsq mVI Gru CwieAw Drix ggn kl DwrI ]1] (907-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) a-uhath hasat marhee ghar chhaa-i-aa Dharan gagan kal Dhaaree. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	He has made His home in the monastery of the heart; He has infused His power into the earth and the sky. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	gurmuiK kyqI sbid auDwrI sMqhu ]1] rhwau ] (907-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh kaytee sabad uDhaaree santahu. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Through the Word of the Shabad, the Gurmukhs have saved so very many, O Saints. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	mmqw mwir haumY soKY iqRBvix joiq qumwrI ]2] (907-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mamtaa maar ha-umai sokhai taribhavan jot tumaaree. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v2	He conquers attachment, and eradicates egotism, and sees Your Divine Light pervading the three worlds, Lord. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	mnsw mwir mnY mih rwKY siqgur sbid vIcwrI ]3] (907-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mansaa maar manai meh raakhai satgur sabad veechaaree. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v3	He conquers desire, and enshrines the Lord within his mind; he contemplates the Word of the True Guru's Shabad. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	isM|I suriq Anwhid vwjY Git Git joiq qumwrI ]4] (907-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sinyee surat anaahad vaajai ghat ghat jot tumaaree. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v4	The horn of consciousness vibrates the unstruck sound current; Your Light illuminates each and every heart, Lord. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	prpMc byxu qhI mnu rwiKAw bRhm Agin prjwrI ]5] (907-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) parpanch bayn tahee man raakhi-aa barahm agan parjaaree. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v5	He plays the flute of the universe in his mind, and lights the fire of God. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	pMc qqu imil Aihinis dIpku inrml joiq ApwrI ]6] (907-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) panch tat mil ahinis deepak nirmal jot apaaree. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v6	Bringing together the five elements, day and night, the Lord's lamp shines with the Immaculate Light of the Infinite. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	riv sis lauky iehu qnu ikMgurI vwjY sbdu inrwrI ]7] (907-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) rav sas la-ukay ih tan kinguree vaajai sabad niraaree. ||7||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v7	The right and left nostrils, the sun and the moon channels, are the strings of the body-harp; they vibrate the wondrous melody of the Shabad. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	isv ngrI mih Awsxu AauDU AlKu AgMmu ApwrI ]8] (907-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) siv nagree meh aasan a-oDhoo alakh agamm apaaree. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v8	The true hermit obtains a seat in the City of God, the invisible, inaccessible, infinite. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v9	kwieAw ngrI iehu mnu rwjw pMc vsih vIcwrI ]9] (907-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa nagree ih man raajaa panch vaseh veechaaree. ||9||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v9	The mind is the king of the city of the body; the five sources of knowledge dwell within it. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v10	sbid rvY Awsix Gir rwjw Adlu kry guxkwrI ]10] (907-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad ravai aasan ghar raajaa adal karay gunkaaree. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v10	Seated in his home, this king chants the Shabad; he administers justice and virtue. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v11	kwlu ibkwlu khy kih bpury jIvq mUAw mnu mwrI ]11] (907-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaal bikaal kahay kahi bapuray jeevat moo-aa man maaree. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v11	What can poor death or birth say to him? Conquering his mind, he remains dead while yet alive. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v12	bRhmw ibsnu mhys iek mUriq Awpy krqw kwrI ]12] (908-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) barahmaa bisan mahays ik moorat aapay kartaa kaaree. ||12||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v12	Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva are manifestations of the One God. He Himself is the Doer of deeds. ||12||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v13	kwieAw soiD qrY Bv swgru Awqm qqu vIcwrI ]13] (908-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa soDh tarai bhav saagar aatam tat veechaaree. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v13	One who purifies his body, crosses over the terrifying world-ocean; he contemplates the essence of his own soul. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v14	gur syvw qy sdw suKu pwieAw AMqir sbdu rivAw guxkwrI ]14] (908-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur sayvaa tay sadaa sukh paa-i-aa antar sabad ravi-aa gunkaaree. ||14||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v14	Serving the Guru, he finds everlasting peace; deep within, the Shabad permeates him, coloring him with virtue. ||14||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v15	Awpy myil ley guxdwqw haumY iqRsnw mwrI ]15] (908-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay mayl la-ay gundaataa ha-umai tarisnaa maaree. ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v15	The Giver of virtue unites with Himself, one who conquers egotism and desire. ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v16	qRY gux myty cauQY vrqY eyhw Bgiq inrwrI ]16] (908-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tarai gun maytay cha-uthai vartai ayhaa bhagat niraaree. ||16||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v16	Eradicating the three qualities, dwell in the fourth state. This is the unparalleled devotional worship. ||16||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v17	gurmuiK jog sbid Awqmu cInY ihrdY eyku murwrI ]17] (908-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh jog sabad aatam cheenai hirdai ayk muraaree. ||17||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v17	This is the Yoga of the Gurmukh: Through the Shabad, he understands his own soul, and he enshrines within his heart the One Lord. ||17||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v18	mnUAw AsiQru sbdy rwqw eyhw krxI swrI ]18] (908-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manoo-aa asthir sabday raataa ayhaa karnee saaree. ||18||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v18	Imbued with the Shabad, his mind becomes steady and stable; this is the most excellent action. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v19	bydu bwdu n pwKMfu AauDU gurmuiK sbid bIcwrI ]19] (908-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bayd baad na pakhand a-oDhoo gurmukh sabad beechaaree. ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v19	This true hermit does not enter into religious debates or hypocrisy; the Gurmukh contemplates the Shabad. ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v20	gurmuiK jogu kmwvY AauDU jqu squ sbid vIcwrI ]20] (908-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh jog kamaavai a-oDhoo jat sat sabad veechaaree. ||20||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v20	The Gurmukh practices Yoga - he is the true hermit; he practices abstinence and truth, and contemplates the Shabad. ||20||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v21	sbid mrY mnu mwry AauDU jog jugiq vIcwrI ]21] (908-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad marai man maaray a-oDhoo jog jugat veechaaree. ||21||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v21	One who dies in the Shabad and conquers his mind is the true hermit; he understands the Way of Yoga. ||21||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v22	mwieAw mohu Bvjlu hY AvDU sbid qrY kul qwrI ]22] (908-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) maa-i-aa moh bhavjal hai avDhoo sabad tarai kul taaree. ||22||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v22	Attachment to Maya is the terrifying world-ocean; through the Shabad, the true hermit saves himself, and his ancestors as well. ||22||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v23	sbid sUr jug cwry AauDU bwxI Bgiq vIcwrI ]23] (908-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad soor jug chaaray a-oDhoo banee bhagat veechaaree. ||23||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v23	Contemplating the Shabad, you shall be a hero throughout the four ages, O hermit; contemplate the Word of the Guru's Bani in devotion. ||23||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v24	eyhu mnu mwieAw moihAw AauDU inksY sbid vIcwrI ]24] (908-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ayhu man maa-i-aa mohi-aa a-oDhoo niksai sabad veechaaree. ||24||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 1 v24	This mind is enticed by Maya, O hermit; contemplating the Shabad, you shall find release. ||24||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v25	Awpy bKsy myil imlwey nwnk srix qumwrI ]25]9] (908-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay bakhsay mayl milaa-ay naanak saran tumaaree. ||25||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 v25	9|| He Himself forgives, and unites in His Union; Nanak seeks Your Sanctuary, Lord. ||25||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw (908-10)
RECORD	para 39713	raamkalee mehlaa 3 asatpadee-aa Raamkalee, Third Mehl, Ashtapadees:
RECORD	para 39714	<> siqgur pRswid ] (908-10) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	para 39715	srmY dIAw muMdRw kMnI pwie jogI iKMQw kir qU dieAw ] (908-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sarmai dee-aa mundraa kannee paa-ay jogee khinthaa kar too da-i-aa. Make humility your ear-rings, Yogi, and compassion your patched coat.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v1	Awvxu jwxu ibBUiq lwie jogI qw qIin Bvx ijix lieAw ]1] (908-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aavan jaan bibhoot laa-ay jogee taa teen bhavan jin la-i-aa. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v1	Let coming and going be the ashes you apply to your body, Yogi, and then you shall conquer the three worlds. ||1||
RECORD	para 39717	AYsI ikMgurI vjwie jogI ] (908-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aisee kinguree vajaa-ay jogee. Play that harp, Yogi,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v1	ijqu ikMgurI Anhdu vwjY hir isau rhY ilv lwie ]1] rhwau ] (908-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jit kinguree anhad vaajai har si-o rahai liv laa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v1	rahaa-o. which vibrates the unstruck sound current, and remain lovingly absorbed in the Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 39719	squ sMqoKu pqu kir JolI jogI AMimRq nwmu Bugiq pweI ] (908-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sat santokh pat kar jholee jogee amrit naam bhugat paa-ee. Make truth and contentment your plate and pouch, Yogi; take the Ambrosial Naam as your food.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v2	iDAwn kw kir fMfw jogI isM|I suriq vjweI ]2] (908-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) Dhi-aan kaa kar dandaa jogee sinyee surat vajaa-ee. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v2	Make meditation your walking stick, Yogi, and make higher consciousness the horn you blow. ||2||
REQUIRE	para 39721	mnu idRVu kir Awsix bYsu jogI qw qyrI klpxw jweI ] (908-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) man darirh kar aasan bais jogee taa tayree kalpanaa jaa-ee. Make your stable mind the Yogic posture you sit in, Yogi, and then you shall be rid of your tormenting desires.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v3	kwieAw ngrI mih mMgix cVih jogI qw nwmu plY pweI ]3] (908-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa nagree meh mangan charheh jogee taa naam palai paa-ee. ||3||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v3	Go begging in the village of the body, Yogi, and then, you shall obtain the Naam in your lap. ||3||
RECORD	para 39723	iequ ikMgurI iDAwnu n lwgY jogI nw scu plY pwie ] (908-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) it kinguree Dhi-aan na laagai jogee naa sach palai paa-ay. This harp does not center you in meditation, Yogi, nor does it bring the True Name into your lap.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v4	iequ ikMgurI sWiq n AwvY jogI AiBmwnu n ivchu jwie ]4] (908-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) it kinguree saa Nt na aavai jogee abhimaan na vichahu jaa-ay. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v4	This harp does not bring you peace, Yogi, nor eliminate egotism from within you. ||4||
RECORD	para 39725	Bau Bwau duie pq lwie jogI iehu srIru kir fMfI ] (908-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bha-o bhaa-o du-ay pat laa-ay jogee ih sareer kar dandee. Make the Fear of God, and the Love of God, the two gourds of your lute, Yogi, and make this body its neck.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v5	gurmuiK hovih qw qMqI vwjY ien ibiD iqRsnw KMfI ]5] (908-17, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gurmukh hoveh taa tantee vaajai in biDh tarisnaa khandee. ||5||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v5	Become Gurmukh, and then vibrate the strings; in this way, your desires shall depart. ||5||
RECORD	para 39727	hukmu buJY so jogI khIAY eyks isau icqu lwey ] (908-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) hukam bujhai so jogee kahee-ai aykas si-o chit laa-ay. One who understands the Hukam of the Lord's Command is called a Yogi; he links his consciousness to the One Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v6	shsw qUtY inrmlu hovY jog jugiq iev pwey ]6] (908-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sahsaa tootai nirmal hovai jog jugat iv paa-ay. ||6||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v6	His cynicism is dispelled, and he becomes immaculately pure; this is how he finds the Way of Yoga. ||6||
REQUIRE	para 39729	ndrI Awvdw sBu ikCu ibnsY hir syqI icqu lwie ] (908-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) nadree aavdaa sabh kichh binsai har saytee chit laa-ay. Everything that comes into view shall be destroyed; focus your consciousness on the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v7	siqgur nwil qyrI BwvnI lwgY qw ieh soJI pwie ]7] (908-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satgur naal tayree bhaavnee laagai taa ih sojhee paa-ay. ||7||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v7	Enshrine love for the True Guru, and then you shall obtain this understanding. ||7||
DEFINE	para 39732	eyhu jogu n hovY jogI ij kutMbu Coif prBvxu krih ] (909-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ayhu jog na hovai jogee je kutamb chhod parbhavan karahi. This is not Yoga, O Yogi, to abandon your family and wander around.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v8	igRh srIr mih hir hir nwmu gur prswdI Apxw hir pRBu lhih ]8] (909-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) garih sareer meh har har naam gur parsaadee apnaa har parabh laheh. ||8||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v8	The Name of the Lord, Har, Har, is within the household of the body. By Guru's Grace, you shall find your Lord God. ||8||
RECORD	para 39734	iehu jgqu imtI kw puqlw jogI iesu mih rogu vfw iqRsnw mwieAw ] (909-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ih jagat mitee kaa putlaa jogee is meh rog vadaa tarisnaa maa-i-aa. This world is a puppet of clay, Yogi; the terrible disease, the desire for Maya is in it.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v9	Anyk jqn ByK kry jogI rogu n jwie gvwieAw ]9] (909-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) anayk jatan bhaykh karay jogee rog na jaa-ay gavaa-i-aa. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v9	Making all sorts of efforts, and wearing religious robes, Yogi, this disease cannot be cured. ||9||
DEFINE	para 39736	hir kw nwmu AauKDu hY jogI ijs no mMin vswey ] (909-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) har kaa naam a-ukhaDh hai jogee jis no man vasaa-ay. The Name of the Lord is the medicine, Yogi; the Lord enshrines it in the mind.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v10	gurmuiK hovY soeI bUJY jog jugiq so pwey ]10] (909-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so-ee boojhai jog jugat so paa-ay. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v10	One who becomes Gurmukh understands this; he alone finds the Way of Yoga. ||10||
RECORD	para 39738	jogY kw mwrgu ibKmu hY jogI ijs no ndir kry so pwey ] (909-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jogai kaa maarag bikham hai jogee jis no nadar karay so paa-ay. The Path of Yoga is very difficult, Yogi; he alone finds it, whom God blesses with His Grace.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v11	AMqir bwhir eyko vyKY ivchu Brmu cukwey ]11] (909-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) antar baahar ayko vaykhai vichahu bharam chukaa-ay. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v11	Inside and outside, he sees the One Lord; he eliminates doubt from within himself. ||11||
RECORD	para 39740	ivxu vjweI ikMgurI vwjY jogI sw ikMgurI vjwie ] (909-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) vin vajaa-ee kinguree vaajai jogee saa kinguree vajaa-ay. So play the harp which vibrates without being played, Yogi.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v12	khY nwnku mukiq hovih jogI swcy rhih smwie ]12]1]10] (909-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) kahai naanak mukat hoveh jogee saachay raheh samaa-ay. ||12||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 3 AstpdIAw v12	Says Nanak, thus you shall be liberated, Yogi, and remain merged in the True Lord. ||12||
RECORD	para 39742	raamkalee mehlaa 3. Raamkalee, Third Mehl:
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	Bgiq Kjwnw gurmuiK jwqw siqguir bUiJ buJweI ]1] (909-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bhagat khajaanaa gurmukh jaataa satgur boojh bujhaa-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	The treasure of devotional worship is revealed to the Gurmukh; the True Guru has inspired me to understand this understanding. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	sMqhu gurmuiK dyie vifAweI ]1] rhwau ] (909-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) santahu gurmukh day-ay vadi-aa-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. O Saints, the Gurmukh is blessed with glorious greatness. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v2	sic rhhu sdw shju suKu aupjY kwmu k®oDu ivchu jweI ]2] (909-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sach rahhu sadaa sahj sukh upjai kaam kroDh vichahu jaa-ee. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v2	Dwelling always in Truth, celestial peace wells up; sexual desire and anger are eliminated from within. ||2||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 3 v3	Awpu Coif nwm ilv lwgI mmqw sbid jlweI ]3] (909-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aap chhod naam liv laagee mamtaa sabad jalaa-ee. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v3	Eradicating self-conceit, remain lovingly focused on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; through the Word of the Shabad, burn away possessiveness. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v4	ijs qy aupjY iqs qy ibnsY AMqy nwmu sKweI ]4] (909-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jis tay upjai tis tay binsai antay naam sakhaa-ee. ||4||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v4	By Him we are created, and by Him we are destroyed; in the end, the Naam will be our only help and support. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v5	sdw hjUir dUir nh dyKhu rcnw ijin rcweI ]5] (909-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sadaa hajoor door nah daykhhu rachnaa jin rachaa-ee. ||5||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v5	He is ever-present; don't think that He is far away. He created the creation. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v6	scw sbdu rvY Gt AMqir scy isau ilv lweI ]6] (909-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sachaa sabad ravai ghat antar sachay si-o liv laa-ee. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v6	Deep within your heart, chant the True Word of the Shabad; remain lovingly absorbed in the True Lord. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v7	sqsMgiq mih nwmu inrmolku vfY Bwig pwieAw jweI ]7] (909-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satsangat meh naam nirmolak vadai bhaag paa-i-aa jaa-ee. ||7||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v7	The Priceless Naam is in the Society of the Saints; by great good fortune, it is obtained. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v8	Brim n BUlhu siqguru syvhu mnu rwKhu iek TweI ]8] (909-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bharam na bhoolahu satgur sayvhu man raakho ik thaa-ee. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v8	Do not be deluded by doubt; serve the True Guru, and keep your mind steady in one place. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v9	ibnu nwvY sB BUlI iPrdI ibrQw jnmu gvweI ]9] (909-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bin naavai sabh bhoolee firdee birthaa janam gavaa-ee. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v9	Without the Name, everyone wanders around in confusion; they waste away their lives in vain. ||9||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 3 v10	jogI jugiq gvweI hMFY pwKMif jogu n pweI ]10] (909-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jogee jugat gavaa-ee handhai pakhand jog na paa-ee. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v10	Yogi, you have lost the Way; you wander around confused. Through hypocrisy, Yoga is not attained. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v11	isv ngrI mih Awsix bYsY gur sbdI jogu pweI ]11] (909-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) siv nagree meh aasan baisai gur sabdee jog paa-ee. ||11||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v11	Sitting in Yogic postures in the City of God, through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, you shall find Yoga. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v12	Dwqur bwjI sbid invwry nwmu vsY min AweI ]12] (909-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) Dhaatur baajee sabad nivaaray naam vasai man aa-ee. ||12||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v12	Restrain your restless wanderings through the Shabad, and the Naam will come to dwell in your mind. ||12||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v13	eyhu srIru srvru hY sMqhu iesnwnu kry ilv lweI ]13] (909-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ayhu sareer sarvar hai santahu isnaan karay liv laa-ee. ||13||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v13	This body is a pool, O Saints; bathe in it, and enshrine love for the Lord. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v14	nwim iesnwnu krih sy jn inrml sbdy mYlu gvweI ]14] (909-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naam isnaan karahi say jan nirmal sabday mail gavaa-ee. ||14||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v14	Those who cleanse themselves through the Naam, are the most immaculate people; through the Shabad, they wash off their filth. ||14||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v15	qRY gux Acyq nwmu cyqih nwhI ibnu nwvY ibnis jweI ]15] (909-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tarai gun achayt naam cheeteh naahee bin naavai binas jaa-ee. ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v15	Trapped by the three qualities, the unconscious person does not think of the Naam; without the Name, he wastes away. ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v16	bRhmw ibsnu mhysu qRY mUriq iqRguix Brim BulweI ]16] (909-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) barahmaa bisan mahays tarai moorat tarigun bharam bhulaa-ee. ||16||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v16	The three forms of Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva are trapped in the three qualities, lost in confusion. ||16||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v17	gur prswdI iqRkutI CUtY cauQY pid ilv lweI ]17] (909-17, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee tarikutee chhootai cha-uthai pad liv laa-ee. ||17||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v17	By Guru's Grace, this triad is eradicated, and one is lovingly absorbed in the fourth state. ||17||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v18	pMifq pVih piV vwdu vKwxih iqMnw bUJ n pweI ]18] (909-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) pandit parheh parh vaad vakaaneh tinnaa boojh na paa-ee. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v18	The Pandits, the religious scholars, read, study and discuss the arguments; they do not understand. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v19	ibiKAw mwqy Brim Bulwey aupdysu khih iksu BweI ]19] (909-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bikhi-aa maatay bharam bhulaa-ay updays kaheh kis bhaa-ee. ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v19	Engrossed in corruption, they wander in confusion; who can they possibly instruct, O Siblings of Destiny? ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v20	Bgq jnw kI aUqm bwxI juig juig rhI smweI ]20] (909-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bhagat janaa kee ootam banee jug jug rahee samaa-ee. ||20||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v20	The Bani, the Word of the humble devotee is the most sublime and exalted; it prevails throughout the ages. ||20||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v21	bwxI lwgY so giq pwey sbdy sic smweI ]21] (909-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) banee laagai so gat paa-ay sabday sach samaa-ee. ||21||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v21	One who is committed to this Bani is emancipated, and through the Shabad, merges in Truth. ||21||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v22	kwieAw ngrI sbdy Kojy nwmu nvM iniD pweI ]22] (910-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa nagree sabday khojay naam nava N niDh paa-ee. ||22||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v22	One who searches the village of the body, through the Shabad, obtains the nine treasures of the Naam. ||22||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v23	mnsw mwir mnu shij smwxw ibnu rsnw ausqiq krweI ]23] (910-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) mansaa maar man sahj samaanaa bin rasnaa ustat karaa-ee. ||23||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v23	Conquering desire, the mind is absorbed in intuitive ease, and then one chants the Lord's Praises without speaking. ||23||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v24	loiex dyiK rhy ibsmwdI icqu Aidsit lgweI ]24] (910-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) lo-in daykh rahay bismaadee chit adisat lagaa-ee. ||24||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v24	Let your eyes gaze upon the Wondrous Lord; let your consciousness be attached to the Unseen Lord. ||24||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v25	Aidstu sdw rhY inrwlmu joqI joiq imlweI ]25] (910-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) adisat sadaa rahai niraalam jotee jot milaa-ee. ||25||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v25	The Unseen Lord is forever absolute and immaculate; one's light merges into the Light. ||25||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v26	hau guru swlwhI sdw Awpxw ijin swcI bUJ buJweI ]26] (910-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ha-o gur saalaahee sadaa aapnaa jin saachee boojh bujhaa-ee. ||26||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v26	I praise my Guru forever, who has inspired me to understand this true understanding. ||26||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v27	nwnku eyk khY bynµqI nwvhu giq piq pweI ]27]2]11] (910-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak ayk kahai baynantee naavhu gat pat paa-ee. ||27||
ALLOW	rwmklI mhlw 3 v27	Nanak offers this one prayer: through the Name, may I find salvation and honor. ||27||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	hir kI pUjw dulµB hY sMqhu khxw kCU n jweI ]1] (910-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) har kee poojaa dulambh hai santahu kahnaa kachhoo na jaa-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	It is so hard to obtain that devotional worship of the Lord, O Saints. It cannot be described at all. ||1||
RECORD	para 39774	sMqhu gurmuiK pUrw pweI ] (910-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) santahu gurmukh pooraa paa-ee. O Saints, as Gurmukh, find the Perfect Lord,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	nwmo pUj krweI ]1] rhwau ] (910-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naamo pooj karaa-ee. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. and worship the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v2	hir ibnu sBu ikCu mYlw sMqhu ikAw hau pUj cVweI ]2] (910-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) har bin sabh kichh mailaa santahu ki-aa ha-o pooj charhaa-ee. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v2	Without the Lord, everything is filthy, O Saints; what offering should I place before Him? ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v3	hir swcy BwvY sw pUjw hovY Bwxw min vsweI ]3] (910-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) har saachay bhaavai saa poojaa hovai bhaanaa man vasaa-ee. ||3||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v3	Whatever pleases the True Lord is devotional worship; His Will abides in the mind. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v4	pUjw krY sBu loku sMqhu mnmuiK Qwie n pweI ]4] (910-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) poojaa karai sabh lok santahu manmukh thaa-ay na paa-ee. ||4||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v4	Everyone worships Him, O Saints, but the self-willed manmukh is not accepted or approved. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v5	sbid mrY mnu inrmlu sMqhu eyh pUjw Qwie pweI ]5] (910-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabad marai man nirmal santahu ayh poojaa thaa-ay paa-ee. ||5||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v5	If someone dies in the Word of the Shabad, his mind become immaculate, O Saints; such worship is accepted and approved. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v6	pivq pwvn sy jn swcy eyk sbid ilv lweI ]6] (910-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) pavit paavan say jan saachay ayk sabad liv laa-ee. ||6||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v6	Sanctified and pure are those true beings, who enshrine love for the Shabad. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v7	ibnu nwvY hor pUj n hovI Brim BulI lokweI ]7] (910-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bin naavai hor pooj na hovee bharam bhulee lokaa-ee. ||7||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v7	There is no worship of the Lord, other than the Name; the world wanders, deluded by doubt. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v8	gurmuiK Awpu pCwxY sMqhu rwm nwim ilv lweI ]8] (910-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gurmukh aap pachhaanai santahu raam naam liv laa-ee. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v8	The Gurmukh understands his own self, O Saints; he lolvingly centers his mind on the Lord's Name. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v9	Awpy inrmlu pUj krwey gur sbdI Qwie pweI ]9] (910-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay nirmal pooj karaa-ay gur sabdee thaa-ay paa-ee. ||9||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v9	The Immaculate Lord Himself inspires worship of Him; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, it is accepted and approved. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v10	pUjw krih pru ibiD nhI jwxih dUjY Bwie mlu lweI ]10] (910-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) poojaa karahi par biDh nahee jaaneh doojai bhaa-ay mal laa-ee. ||10||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v10	Those who worship Him, but do not know the Way, are polluted with the love of duality. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v11	gurmuiK hovY su pUjw jwxY Bwxw min vsweI ]11] (910-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so poojaa jaanai bhaanaa man vasaa-ee. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v11	One who becomes Gurmukh, knows what worship is; the Lord's Will abides within his mind. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v12	Bwxy qy siB suK pwvY sMqhu AMqy nwmu sKweI ]12] (910-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bhaanay tay sabh sukh paavai santahu antay naam sakhaa-ee. ||12||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v12	One who accepts the Lord's Will obtains total peace, O Saints; in the end, the Naam will be our help and support. ||12||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v13	Apxw Awpu n pCwxih sMqhu kUiV krih vifAweI ]13] (910-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) apnaa aap na pachhaaneh santahu koorh karahi vadi-aa-ee. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v13	One who does not understand his own self, O Saints, falsely flatters himself. ||13||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 3 v14	pwKMif kInY jmu nhI CofY lY jwsI piq gvweI ]14] (910-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) pakhand keenai jam nahee chhodai lai jaasee pat gavaa-ee. ||14||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v14	The Messenger of Death does not give up on those who practices hypocrisy; they are dragged away in disgrace. ||14||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v15	ijn AMqir sbdu Awpu pCwxih giq imiq iqn hI pweI ]15] (910-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jin antar sabad aap pachhaaneh gat mit tin hee paa-ee. ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v15	Those who have the Shabad deep within, understand themselves; they find the way of salvation. ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v16	eyhu mnUAw suMn smwiD lgwvY joqI joiq imlweI ]16] (910-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ayhu manoo-aa sunn samaaDh lagaavai jotee jot milaa-ee. ||16||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v16	Their minds enter into the deepest state of Samaadhi, and their light is absorbed into the Light. ||16||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v17	suix suix gurmuiK nwmu vKwxih sqsMgiq mylweI ]17] (910-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sun sun gurmukh naam vakaaneh satsangat maylaa-ee. ||17||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v17	The Gurmukhs listen constantly to the Naam, and chant it in the True Congregation. ||17||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v18	gurmuiK gwvY Awpu gvwvY dir swcY soBw pweI ]18] (910-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gurmukh gaavai aap gavaavai dar saachai sobhaa paa-ee. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v18	The Gurmukhs sing the Lord's Praises, and erase self-conceit; they obtain true honor in the Court of the Lord. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v19	swcI bwxI scu vKwxY sic nwim ilv lweI ]19] (910-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) saachee banee sach vakhaanai sach naam liv laa-ee. ||19||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v19	True are their words; they speak only the Truth; they lovingly focus on the True Name. ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v20	BY BMjnu Aiq pwp inKMjnu myrw pRBu AMiq sKweI ]20] (910-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bhai bhanjan at paap nikhanjan mayraa parabh ant sakhaa-ee. ||20||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v20	My God is the Destroyer of fear, the Destroyer of sin; in the end, He is our only help and support. ||20||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v21	sBu ikCu Awpy Awip vrqY nwnk nwim vifAweI ]21]3]12] (910-17, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabh kichh aapay aap vartai naanak naam vadi-aa-ee. ||21||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v21	He Himself pervades and permeates everything; O Nanak, glorious greatness is obtained through the Naam. ||21||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	hm kucl kucIl Aiq AiBmwnI imil sbdy mYlu auqwrI ]1] (910-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ham kuchal kucheel at abhimaanee mil sabday mail utaaree. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	I am filthy and polluted, proud and egotistical; receiving the Word of the Shabad, my filth is taken away. ||1||
DEFINE	para 39798	sMqhu gurmuiK nwim insqwrI ] (910-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) santahu gurmukh naam nistaaree. O Saints, the Gurmukhs are saved through the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	scw nwmu visAw Gt AMqir krqY Awip svwrI ]1] rhwau ] (910-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sachaa naam vasi-aa ghat antar kartai aap savaaree. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The True Name abides deep within their hearts. The Creator Himself embellishes them. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v2	pwrs prsy iPir pwrsu hoey hir jIau ApxI ikrpw DwrI ]2] (911-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) paaras parsay fir paaras ho-ay har jee-o apnee kirpaa Dhaaree. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v2	Touching the philosopher's stone, they themselves become the philosopher's stone; the Dear Lord Himself blesses them with His Mercy. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v3	ieik ByK krih iPrih AiBmwnI iqn jUAY bwjI hwrI ]3] (911-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ik bhaykh karahi fireh abhimaanee tin joo-ai baajee haaree. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v3	Some wear religious robes, and wander around in pride; they lose their life in the gamble. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v4	ieik Anidnu Bgiq krih idnu rwqI rwm nwmu auir DwrI ]4] (911-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ik an-din bhagat karahi din raatee raam naam ur Dhaaree. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v4	Some worship the Lord in devotion, night and day; day and night, they keep the Lord's Name enshrined in their hearts. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v5	Anidnu rwqy shjy mwqy shjy haumY mwrI ]5] (911-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) an-din raatay sehjay maatay sehjay ha-umai maaree. ||5||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v5	Those who are imbued with Him night and day, are spontaneously intoxicated with Him; they intuitively conquer their ego. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v6	BY ibnu Bgiq n hoeI kb hI BY Bwie Bgiq svwrI ]6] (911-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bhai bin bhagat na ho-ee kab hee bhai bhaa-ay bhagat savaaree. ||6||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v6	Without the Fear of God, devotional worship is never performed; through the Love and the Fear of God, devotional worship is embellished. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v7	mwieAw mohu sbid jlwieAw igAwin qiq bIcwrI ]7] (911-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh sabad jalaa-i-aa gi-aan tat beechaaree. ||7||
UPHOLD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v7	The Shabad burns away emotional attachment to Maya, and then one contemplates the essence of spiritual wisdom. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v8	Awpy Awip krwey krqw Awpy bKis BMfwrI ]8] (911-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay aap karaa-ay kartaa aapay bakhas bhandaaree. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v8	The Creator Himself inspires us to act; He Himself blesses us with His treasure. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v9	iqs ikAw guxw kw AMqu n pwieAw hau gwvw sbid vIcwrI ]9] (911-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tis ki-aa gunaa kaa ant na paa-i-aa ha-o gaavaa sabad veechaaree. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v9	The limits of His virtues cannot be found; I sing His Praises and contemplate the Word of the Shabad. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v10	hir jIau jpI hir jIau swlwhI ivchu Awpu invwrI ]10] (911-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) har jee-o japee har jee-o saalaahee vichahu aap nivaaree. ||10||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v10	I chant the Lord's Name, and praise my Dear Lord; egotism is eradicated from within me. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v11	nwmu pdwrQu gur qy pwieAw AKut scy BMfwrI ]11] (911-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naam padaarath gur tay paa-i-aa akhut sachay bhandaaree. ||11||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v11	The treasure of the Naam is obtained from the Guru; the treasures of the True Lord are inexhaustible. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v12	ApixAw Bgqw no Awpy quTw ApxI ikrpw kir kl DwrI ]12] (911-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) apni-aa bhagtaa no aapay tuthaa apnee kirpaa kar kal Dhaaree. ||12||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v12	He Himself is pleased with His devotees; by His Grace, He infuses His strength within them. ||12||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v13	iqn swcy nwm kI sdw BuK lwgI gwvin sbid vIcwrI ]13] (911-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tin saachay naam kee sadaa bhukh laagee gaavan sabad veechaaree. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v13	They always feel hunger for the True Name; they sing and contemplate the Shabad. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v14	jIau ipMfu sBu ikCu hY iqs kw AwKxu ibKmu bIcwrI ]14] (911-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jee-o pind sabh kichh hai tis kaa aakhan bikham beechaaree. ||14||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v14	Soul, body and everything are His; it is so difficult to speak of, and contemplate Him. ||14||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v15	sbid lgy syeI jn insqry Baujlu pwir auqwrI ]15] (911-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabad lagay say-ee jan nistaray bha-ojal paar utaaree. ||15||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v15	Those humble beings who are attached to the Shabad are saved; they cross over the terrifying world-ocean. ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v16	ibnu hir swcy ko pwir n pwvY bUJY ko vIcwrI ]16] (911-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bin har saachay ko paar na paavai boojhai ko veechaaree. ||16||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v16	Without the True Lord, no one can cross over; how rare are those who contemplate and understand this. ||16||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v17	jo Duir iliKAw soeI pwieAw imil hir sbid svwrI ]17] (911-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jo Dhur likhi-aa so-ee paa-i-aa mil har sabad savaaree. ||17||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v17	We obtain only that which is pre-ordained; receiving the Lord's Shabad, we are embellished. ||17||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v18	kwieAw kMcnu sbdy rwqI swcY nwie ipAwrI ]18] (911-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kanchan sabday raatee saachai naa-ay pi-aaree. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v18	Imbued with the Shabad, the body becomes golden, and loves only the True Name. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v19	kwieAw AMimRiq rhI BrpUry pweIAY sbid vIcwrI ]19] (911-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa amrit rahee bharpooray paa-ee-ai sabad veechaaree. ||19||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v19	The body is then filled to overflowing with Ambrosial Nectar, obtained by contemplating the Shabad. ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v20	jo pRBu Kojih syeI pwvih hoir PUit mUey AhMkwrI ]20] (911-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jo parabh khojeh say-ee paavahi hor foot moo-ay aha Nkaaree. ||20||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v20	Those who seek God, find Him; others burst and die from their own egotism. ||20||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v21	bwdI ibnsih syvk syvih gur kY hyiq ipAwrI ]21] (911-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) baadee binsahi sayvak sayveh gur kai hayt pi-aaree. ||21||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v21	The debaters waste away, while the servants serve, with love and affection for the Guru. ||21||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v22	so jogI qqu igAwnu bIcwry haumY iqRsnw mwrI ]22] (911-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) so jogee tat gi-aan beechaaray ha-umai tarisnaa maaree. ||22||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v22	He alone is a Yogi, who contemplates the essence of spiritual wisdom, and conquers egotism and thirsty desire. ||22||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v23	siqguru dwqw iqnY pCwqw ijs no ik®pw qumwrI ]23] (911-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satgur daataa tinai pachhaataa jis no kirpaa tumaaree. ||23||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v23	The True Guru, the Great Giver, is revealed to those upon whom You bestow Your Grace, O Lord. ||23||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v24	siqguru n syvih mwieAw lwgy fUib mUey AhMkwrI ]24] (911-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satgur na sayveh maa-i-aa laagay doob moo-ay aha Nkaaree. ||24||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v24	Those who do not serve the True Guru, and who are attached to Maya, are drowned; they die in their own egotism. ||24||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v25	ijcru AMdir swsu iqcru syvw kIcY jwie imlIAY rwm murwrI ]25] (911-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jichar andar saas tichar sayvaa keechai jaa-ay milee-ai raam muraaree. ||25||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v25	As long as there is breath within you, so long you should serve the Lord; then, you will go and meet the Lord. ||25||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v26	Anidnu jwgq rhY idnu rwqI Apny ipRA pRIiq ipAwrI ]26] (911-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) an-din jaagat rahai din raatee apnay pari-a pareet pi-aaree. ||26||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v26	Night and day, she remains awake and aware, day and night; she is the darling bride of her Beloved Husband Lord. ||26||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v27	qnu mnu vwrI vwir GumweI Apny gur ivthu bilhwrI ]27] (911-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tan man vaaree vaar ghumaa-ee apnay gur vitahu balihaaree. ||27||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v27	I offer my body and mind in sacrifice to my Guru; I am a sacrifice to Him. ||27||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v28	mwieAw mohu ibnis jwiegw aubry sbid vIcwrI ]28] (911-17, rwmklI, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh binas jaa-igaa ubray sabad veechaaree. ||28||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v28	Attachment to Maya will end and go away; only by contemplating the Shabad will you be saved. ||28||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v29	Awip jgwey syeI jwgy gur kY sbid vIcwrI ]29] (911-17, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aap jagaa-ay say-ee jaagay gur kai sabad veechaaree. ||29||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v29	They are awake and aware, whom the Lord Himself awakens; so contemplate the Word of the Guru's Shabad. ||29||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v30	nwnk syeI mUey ij nwmu n cyqih Bgq jIvy vIcwrI ]30]4]13] (911-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak say-ee moo-ay je naam na cheeteh bhagat jeevay veechaaree. ||30||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v30	O Nanak, those who do not remember the Naam are dead. The devotees live in contemplative meditation. ||30||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	nwmu Kjwnw gur qy pwieAw iqRpiq rhy AwGweI ]1] (911-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naam khajaanaa gur tay paa-i-aa taripat rahay aaghaa-ee. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	Receiving the treasure of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, from the Guru, I remain satisfied and fulfilled. ||1||
RECORD	para 39832	sMqhu gurmuiK mukiq giq pweI ] (911-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) santahu gurmukh mukat gat paa-ee. O Saints, the Gurmukhs attain the state of liberation.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	eyku nwmu visAw Gt AMqir pUry kI vifAweI ]1] rhwau ] (912-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ayk naam vasi-aa ghat antar pooray kee vadi-aa-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. The One Name abides deep within my heart; such is the glorious greatness of the Perfect Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v2	Awpy krqw Awpy Bugqw dydw irjku sbweI ]2] (912-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay kartaa aapay bhugtaa daydaa rijak sabaa-ee. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v2	He Himself is the Creator, and He Himself is the Enjoyer. He Himself gives sustenance to all. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v3	jo ikCu krxw so kir rihAw Avru n krxw jweI ]3] (912-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jo kichh karnaa so kar rahi-aa avar na karnaa jaa-ee. ||3||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v3	Whatever He wants to do, He is doing; no one else can do anything. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v4	Awpy swjy isRsit aupwey isir isir DMDY lweI ]4] (912-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay saajay sarisat upaa-ay sir sir DhanDhai laa-ee. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v4	He Himself fashions and creates the creation; He links each and every person to their task. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v5	iqsih sryvhu qw suKu pwvhu siqguir myil imlweI ]5] (912-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tiseh sarayvhu taa sukh paavhu satgur mayl milaa-ee. ||5||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 3 v5	If you serve Him, then you will find peace; the True Guru will unite you in His Union. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v6	Awpxw Awpu Awip aupwey AlKu n lKxw jweI ]6] (912-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapnaa aap aap upaa-ay alakh na lakh-naa jaa-ee. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v6	The Lord Himself creates Himself; the Unseen Lord cannot be seen. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v7	Awpy mwir jIvwly Awpy iqs no iqlu n qmweI ]7] (912-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay maar jeevaalay aapay tis no til na tamaa-ee. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v7	He Himself kills, and brings back to life; He does not have even an iota of greed. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v8	ieik dwqy ieik mMgqy kIqy Awpy Bgiq krweI ]8] (912-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ik daatay ik mangtay keetay aapay bhagat karaa-ee. ||8||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v8	Some are made givers, and some are made beggars; He Himself inspires us to devotional worship. ||8||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v9	sy vfBwgI ijnI eyko jwqw scy rhy smweI ]9] (912-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) say vadbhaagee jinee ayko jaataa sachay rahay samaa-ee. ||9||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v9	Those who know the One Lord are very fortunate; they remain absorbed in the True Lord. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v10	Awip srUpu isAwxw Awpy kImiq khxu n jweI ]10] (912-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aap saroop si-aanaa aapay keemat kahan na jaa-ee. ||10||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v10	He Himself is beautiful, He Himself is wise and clever; His worth cannot be expressed. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v11	Awpy duKu suKu pwey AMqir Awpy Brim BulweI ]11] (912-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay dukh sukh paa-ay antar aapay bharam bhulaa-ee. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v11	He Himself infuses pain and pleasure; He Himself makes them wander around in doubt. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v12	vfw dwqw gurmuiK jwqw ingurI AMD iPrY lokweI ]12] (912-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) vadaa daataa gurmukh jaataa niguree anDh firai lokaa-ee. ||12||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v12	The Great Giver is revealed to the Gurmukh; without the Guru, the world wanders in darkness. ||12||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v13	ijnI cwiKAw iqnw swdu AwieAw siqguir bUJ buJweI ]13] (912-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jinee chaakhi-aa tinaa saad aa-i-aa satgur boojh bujhaa-ee. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v13	Those who taste, enjoy the flavor; the True Guru imparts this understanding. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v14	ieknw nwvhu Awip Bulwey ieknw gurmuiK dyie buJweI ]14] (912-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) iknaa naavhu aap bhulaa-ay iknaa gurmukh day-ay bujhaa-ee. ||14||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v14	Some, the Lord causes to forget and lose the Name; others become Gurmukh, and are granted this understanding. ||14||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v15	sdw sdw swlwihhu sMqhu iqs dI vfI vifAweI ]15] (912-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa saalaahihu santahu tis dee vadee vadi-aa-ee. ||15||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v15	Forever and ever, praise the Lord, O Saints; how glorious is His greatness! ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v16	iqsu ibnu Avru n koeI rwjw kir qpwvsu bxq bxweI ]16] (912-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tis bin avar na ko-ee raajaa kar tapaavas banat banaa-ee. ||16||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v16	There is no other King except Him; He administers justice, as He has made it. ||16||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v17	inAwau iqsY kw hY sd swcw ivrly hukmu mnweI ]17] (912-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ni-aa-o tisai kaa hai sad saachaa virlay hukam manaa-ee. ||17||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v17	His justice is always True; how rare are those who accept His Command. ||17||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v18	iqs no pRwxI sdw iDAwvhu ijin gurmuiK bxq bxweI ]18] (912-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tis no paraanee sadaa Dhi-aavahu jin gurmukh banat banaa-ee. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v18	O mortal, meditate forever on the Lord, who has made the Gurmukh in His making. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v19	siqgur BytY so jnu sIJY ijsu ihrdY nwmu vsweI ]19] (912-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satgur bhaytai so jan seejhai jis hirdai naam vasaa-ee. ||19||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v19	That humble being who meets with the True Guru is fulfilled; the Naam abides in his heart. ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v20	scw Awip sdw hY swcw bwxI sbid suxweI ]20] (912-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sachaa aap sadaa hai saachaa banee sabad sunaa-ee. ||20||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v20	The True Lord is Himself forever True; He announces His Bani, the Word of His Shabad. ||20||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 3 v21	nwnk suix vyiK rihAw ivsmwdu myrw pRBu rivAw sRb QweI ]21]5]14] (912-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak sun vaykh rahi-aa vismaad mayraa parabh ravi-aa sarab thaa-ee. ||21||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 3 v21	Nanak is wonderstruck, hearing and seeing His Lord; my God is all-pervading, everywhere. ||21||
