RECORD	para 40799	mnu dIjY isru saupIAY BI krqy kI tyk ] (934-16, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) man deejai sir sa-upee-ai bhee kartay kee tayk. Dedicate your mind, and surrender your head; seek only the Support of the Creator Lord.
DEFINE	para 40800	DMDw Dwvq rih gey mn mih sbdu Anµdu ] (934-17, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) DhanDhaa Dhaavat reh ga-ay man meh sabad anand. Worldly affairs and wanderings cease, when the mind is filled with the bliss of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 40801	durjn qy swjn Bey Byty gur goivMd ] (934-17, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) durjan tay saajan bha-ay bhaytay gur govind. Even one's enemies become friends, meeting with the Guru, the Lord of the Universe.
RECORD	para 40802	bnu bnu iPrqI FUFqI bsqu rhI Gir bwir ] (934-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ban ban firtee dhoodh-tee basat rahee ghar baar. Wandering from forest to forest searching, you will find that those things are within the home of your own heart.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v36	siqguir mylI imil rhI jnm mrx duKu invwir ]36] (934-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) satgur maylee mil rahee janam maran dukh nivaar. ||36||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v36	United by the True Guru, you shall remain united, and the pains of birth and death will be ended. ||36||
RECORD	para 40804	nwnw krq n CUtIAY ivxu gux jm puir jwih ] (934-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naanaa karat na chhootee-ai vin gun jam pur jaahi. Through various rituals, one does not find release. Without virtue, one is sent to the City of Death.
RECORD	para 40805	nw iqsu eyhu n Ehu hY Avguix iPir pCuqwih ] (934-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naa tis ayhu na oh hai avgun fir pachhutaahi. One will not have this world or the next; committing sinful mistakes, one comes to regret and repent in the end.
UPHOLD	para 40807	nw iqsu igAwnu n iDAwnu hY nw iqsu Drmu iDAwnu ] (935-1, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naa tis gi-aan na Dhi-aan hai naa tis Dharam Dhi-aan. He has neither spiritual wisdom or meditation; neither Dharmic faith mor meditation.
RECORD	para 40808	ivxu nwvY inrBau khw ikAw jwxw AiBmwnu ] (935-1, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) vin naavai nirbha-o kahaa ki-aa jaanaa abhimaan. Without the Name, how can one be fearless? How can he understand egotistical pride?
RECORD	para 40809	Qwik rhI ikv ApVw hwQ nhI nw pwru ] (935-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) thaak rahee kiv aprhaa haath nahee naa paar. I am so tired - how can I get there? This ocean has no bottom or end.
RECORD	para 40810	nw swjn sy rMguly iksu pih krI pukwr ] (935-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naa saajan say rangulay kis peh karee pukaar. I have no loving companions, whom I can ask for help.
DEFINE	para 40811	nwnk ipRau ipRau jy krI myly mylxhwru ] (935-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naanak pari-o pari-o jay karee maylay maylanhaar. O Nanak, crying out, "Beloved, Beloved", we are united with the Uniter.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v37	ijin ivCoVI so mylsI gur kY hyiq Apwir ]37] (935-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) jin vichhorhee so maylsee gur kai hayt apaar. ||37||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v37	He who separated me, unites me again; my love for the Guru is infinite. ||37||
DEFINE	para 40813	pwpu burw pwpI kau ipAwrw ] (935-4, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) paap buraa paapee ka-o pi-aaraa. Sin is bad, but it is dear to the sinner.
RECORD	para 40814	pwip ldy pwpy pwswrw ] (935-4, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) paap laday paapay paasaaraa. He loads himself with sin, and expands his world through sin.
DEFINE	para 40815	prhir pwpu pCwxY Awpu ] (935-4, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) parhar paap pachhaanai aap. Sin is far away from one who understands himself.
DEFINE	para 40816	nw iqsu sogu ivjogu sMqwpu ] (935-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naa tis sog vijog santaap. He is not afflicted by sorrow or separation.
RECORD	para 40817	nrik pVMqau ikau rhY ikau bMcY jmkwlu ] (935-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) narak parha Nta-o ki-o rahai ki-o banchai jamkaal. How can one avoid falling into hell? How can he cheat the Messenger of Death?
DEFINE	para 40818	ikau Awvx jwxw vIsrY JUTu burw KY kwlu ] (935-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ki-o aavan jaanaa veesrai jhooth buraa khai kaal. How can coming and going be forgotten? Falsehood is bad, and death is cruel.
DEFINE	para 40819	mnu jMjwlI vyiVAw BI jMjwlw mwih ] (935-6, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) man janjaalee vayrhi-aa bhee janjaalaa maahi. The mind is enveloped by entanglements, and into entanglements it falls.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v38	ivxu nwvY ikau CUtIAY pwpy pcih pcwih ]38] (935-6, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) vin naavai ki-o chhootee-ai paapay pacheh pachaahi. ||38||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v38	Without the Name, how can anyone be saved? They rot away in sin. ||38||
RECORD	para 40821	iPir iPir PwhI PwsY kaUAw ] (935-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) fir fir faahee faasai ka-oo-aa. Again and again, the crow falls into the trap.
RECORD	para 40822	iPir pCuqwnw Ab ikAw hUAw ] (935-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) fir pachhutaanaa ab ki-aa hoo-aa. Then he regrets it, but what can he do now?
DEFINE	para 40823	PwQw cog cugY nhI bUJY ] (935-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) faathaa chog chugai nahee boojhai. Even though he is trapped, he pecks at the food; he does not understand.
WHEN	para 40824	sqguru imlY q AwKI sUJY ] (935-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) satgur milai ta aakhee soojhai. If he meets the True Guru, then he sees with his eyes.
DEFINE	para 40825	ijau mCulI PwQI jm jwil ] (935-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ji-o machhulee faathee jam jaal. Like a fish, he is caught in the noose of death.
RECORD	para 40826	ivxu gur dwqy mukiq n Bwil ] (935-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) vin gur daatay mukat na bhaal. Do not seek liberation from anyone else, except the Guru, the Great Giver.
RECORD	para 40827	iPir iPir AwvY iPir iPir jwie ] (935-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) fir fir aavai fir fir jaa-ay. Over and over again, he comes; over and over again, he goes.
RECORD	para 40828	iek rMig rcY rhY ilv lwie ] (935-9, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ik rang rachai rahai liv laa-ay. Be absorbed in love for the One Lord, and remain lovingly focused on Him.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v39	iev CUtY iPir Pws n pwie ]39] (935-9, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) iv chhootai fir faas na paa-ay. ||39||
FORBID	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v39	In this way you shall be saved, and you shall not fall into the trap again. ||39||
RECORD	para 40830	bIrw bIrw kir rhI bIr Bey bYrwie ] (935-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) beeraa beeraa kar rahee beer bha-ay bairaa-ay. She calls out, "Brother, O brother - stay, O brother!" But he becomes a stranger.
RECORD	para 40831	bIr cly Gir AwpxY bihx ibrih jil jwie ] (935-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) beer chalay ghar aapnai bahin bireh jal jaa-ay. Her brother departs for his own home, and his sister burns with the pain of separation.
RECORD	para 40832	bwbul kY Gir bytVI bwlI bwlY nyih ] (935-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) baabul kai ghar baytrhee baalee baalai nayhi. In this world, her father's home, the daughter, the innocent soul bride, loves her Young Husband Lord.
WHEN	para 40833	jy loVih vru kwmxI siqguru syvih qyih ] (935-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) jay lorheh var kaamnee satgur sayveh tayhi. If you long for your Husband Lord, O soul bride, then serve the True Guru with love.
DEFINE	para 40834	ibrlo igAwnI bUJxau siqguru swic imlyie ] (935-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) birlo gi-aanee boojh-na-o satgur saach milay-ay. How rare are the spiritually wise, who meet the True Guru, and truly understand.
WHEN	para 40835	Twkur hwiQ vfweIAw jY BwvY qY dyie ] (935-12, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) thaakur haath vadaa-ee-aa jai bhaavai tai day-ay. All glorious greatness rests in the Lord and Master's Hands. He grants them, when He is pleased.
DEFINE	para 40836	bwxI ibrlau bIcwrsI jy ko gurmuiK hoie ] (935-12, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) banee birla-o beechaarsee jay ko gurmukh ho-ay. How rare are those who contemplate the Word of the Guru's Bani; they become Gurmukh.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v40	ieh bwxI mhw purK kI inj Gir vwsw hoie ]40] (935-13, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ih banee mahaa purakh kee nij ghar vaasaa ho-ay. ||40||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v40	This is the Bani of the Supreme Being; through it, one dwells within the home of his inner being. ||40||
RECORD	para 40838	Bin Bin GVIAY GiV GiV BjY Fwih auswrY ausry FwhY ] (935-13, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) bhan bhan gharhee-ai gharh gharh bhajai dhaahi usaarai usray dhaahai. Shattering and breaking apart, He creates and re-creates; creating, He shatters again. He builds up what He has demolished, and demolishes what He has built.
RECORD	para 40839	sr Bir soKY BI Bir poKY smrQ vyprvwhY ] (935-14, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sar bhar sokhai bhee bhar pokhai samrath vayparvaahai. He dries up the pools which are full, and fills the dried tanks again. He is all-powerful and independent.
RECORD	para 40840	Brim Bulwny Bey idvwny ivxu Bwgw ikAw pweIAY ] (935-14, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) bharam bhulaanay bha-ay divaanay vin bhaagaa ki-aa paa-ee-ai. Deluded by doubt, they have gone insane; without destiny, what do they obtain?
REQUIRE	para 40841	gurmuiK igAwnu forI pRiB pkVI ijn iKMcY iqn jweIAY ] (935-15, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) gurmukh gi-aan doree parabh pakrhee jin khinchai tin jaa-ee-ai. The Gurmukhs know that God holds the string; wherever He pulls it, they must go.
RECORD	para 40842	hir gux gwie sdw rMig rwqy bhuiV n pCoqweIAY ] (935-16, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) har gun gaa-ay sadaa rang raatay bahurh na pachhotaa-ee-ai. Those who sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, are forever imbued with His Love; they never again feel regret.
WHEN	para 40843	BBY Bwlih gurmuiK bUJih qw inj Gir vwsw pweIAY ] (935-16, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) bhabhai bhaaleh gurmukh boojheh taa nij ghar vaasaa paa-ee-ai. Bhabha: If someone seeks, and then becomes Gurmukh, then he comes to dwell in the home of his own heart.
REQUIRE	para 40844	BBY Baujlu mwrgu ivKVw Aws inrwsw qrIAY ] (935-17, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) bhabhai bha-ojal maarag vikh-rhaa aas niraasaa taree-ai. Bhabha: The way of the terrifying world-ocean is treacherous. Remain free of hope, in the midst of hope, and you shall cross over.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v41	gur prswdI Awpo cIn@Y jIviqAw iev mrIAY ]41] (935-17, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee aapo cheenHai jeevti-aa iv maree-ai. ||41||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v41	By Guru's Grace, one comes to understand himself; in this way, he remains dead while yet alive. ||41||
RECORD	para 40846	mwieAw mwieAw kir muey mwieAw iksY n swiQ ] (935-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) maa-i-aa maa-i-aa kar mu-ay maa-i-aa kisai na saath. Crying out for the wealth and riches of Maya, they die; but Maya does not go along with them.
RECORD	para 40847	hMsu clY auiT fumxo mwieAw BUlI AwiQ ] (935-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) hans chalai uth dumno maa-i-aa bhoolee aath. The soul-swan arises and departs, sad and depressed, leaving its wealth behind.
DEFINE	para 40848	mnu JUTw jim joihAw Avgux clih nwil ] (935-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) man jhoothaa jam johi-aa avgun chaleh naal. The false mind is hunted by the Messenger of Death; it carries its faults along when it goes.
DEFINE	para 40849	mn mih mnu aulto mrY jy gux hovih nwil ] (935-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) man meh man ulto marai jay gun hoveh naal. The mind turns inward, and merges with mind, when it is with virtue.
RECORD	para 40851	myrI myrI kir muey ivxu nwvY duKu Bwil ] (936-1, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) mayree mayree kar mu-ay vin naavai dukh bhaal. Crying out, "Mine, mine!", they have died, but without the Name, they find only pain.
DEFINE	para 40852	gV mMdr mhlw khw ijau bwjI dIbwxu ] (936-1, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) garh mandar mehlaa kahaa ji-o baajee deebaan. So where are their forts, mansions, palaces and courts? They are like a short story.
RECORD	para 40853	nwnk scy nwm ivxu JUTw Awvx jwxu ] (936-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naanak sachay naam vin jhoothaa aavan jaan. O Nanak, without the True Name, the false just come and go.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v42	Awpy cquru srUpu hY Awpy jwxu sujwxu ]42] (936-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) aapay chatur saroop hai aapay jaan sujaan. ||42||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v42	He Himself is clever and so very beautiful; He Himself is wise and all-knowing. ||42||
REQUIRE	para 40855	jo Awvih sy jwih Puin Awie gey pCuqwih ] (936-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) jo aavahi say jaahi fun aa-ay ga-ay pachhutaahi. Those who come, must go in the end; they come and go, regretting and repenting.
RECORD	para 40856	lK caurwsIh mydnI GtY n vDY auqwih ] (936-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) lakh cha-oraaseeh maydnee ghatai na vaDhai utaahi. They will pass through 8.4 millions species; this number does not decrease or rise.
DEFINE	para 40857	sy jn aubry ijn hir BwieAw ] (936-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) say jan ubray jin har bhaa-i-aa. They alone are saved, who love the Lord.
DEFINE	para 40858	DMDw muAw ivgUqI mwieAw ] (936-4, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) DhanDhaa mu-aa vigootee maa-i-aa. Their worldly entanglements are ended, and Maya is conquered.
REQUIRE	para 40859	jo dIsY so cwlsI iks kau mIqu kryau ] (936-4, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) jo deesai so chaalsee kis ka-o meet karay-o. Whoever is seen, shall depart; who should I make my friend?
RECORD	para 40860	jIau smpau Awpxw qnu mnu AwgY dyau ] (936-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) jee-o sampa-o aapnaa tan man aagai day-o. I dedicate my soul, and place my body and mind in offering before Him.
DEFINE	para 40861	AsiQru krqw qU DxI iqs hI kI mY Et ] (936-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) asthir kartaa too Dhanee tis hee kee mai ot. You are eternally stable, O Creator, Lord and Master; I lean on Your Support.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v43	gux kI mwrI hau mueI sbid rqI min cot ]43] (936-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) gun kee maaree ha-o mu-ee sabad ratee man chot. ||43||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v43	Conquered by virtue, egotism is killed; imbued with the Word of the Shabad, the mind rejects the world. ||43||
RECORD	para 40863	rwxw rwau n ko rhY rMgu n quMgu PkIru ] (936-6, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) raanaa raa-o na ko rahai rang na tung fakeer. Neither the kings nor the nobles will remain; neither the rich nor the poor will remain.
WHEN	para 40864	vwrI Awpo AwpxI koie n bMDY DIr ] (936-6, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) vaaree aapo aapnee ko-ay na banDhai Dheer. When one's turn comes, no one can stay here.
DEFINE	para 40865	rwhu burw BIhwvlw sr fUgr Asgwh ] (936-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) raahu buraa bheehaavalaa sar doogar asgaah. The path is difficult and treacherous; the pools and mountains are impassable.
DEFINE	para 40866	mY qin Avgx Juir mueI ivxu gux ikau Gir jwh ] (936-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) mai tan avgan jhur mu-ee vin gun ki-o ghar jaah. My body is filled with faults; I am dying of grief. Without virtue, how can I enter my home?
RECORD	para 40867	guxIAw gux ly pRB imly ikau iqn imlau ipAwir ] (936-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) gunee-aa gun lay parabh milay ki-o tin mila-o pi-aar. The virtuous take virtue, and meet God; how can I meet them with love?
WHEN	para 40868	iqn hI jYsI QI rhW jip jip irdY murwir ] (936-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) tin hee jaisee thee rahaaN jap jap ridai muraar. If ony I could be like them, chanting and meditating within my heart on the Lord.
DEFINE	para 40869	AvguxI BrpUr hY gux BI vsih nwil ] (936-9, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) avgunee bharpoor hai gun bhee vaseh naal. He is overflowing with faults and demerits, but virtue dwells within him as well.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v44	ivxu sqgur gux n jwpnI ijcru sbid n kry bIcwru ]44] (936-9, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) vin satgur gun na jaapnee jichar sabad na karay beechaar. ||44||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v44	Without the True Guru, he does not see God's Virtues; he does not chant the Glorious Virtues of God. ||44||
DEFINE	para 40871	lskrIAw Gr sMmly Awey vjhu ilKwie ] (936-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) laskaree-aa ghar sammlay aa-ay vajahu likhaa-ay. God's soldiers take care of their homes; their pay is pre-ordained, before they come into the world.
RECORD	para 40872	kwr kmwvih isir DxI lwhw plY pwie ] (936-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) kaar kamaaveh sir Dhanee laahaa palai paa-ay. They serve their Supreme Lord and Master, and obtain the profit.
RECORD	para 40873	lbu loBu buirAweIAw Cofy mnhu ivswir ] (936-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) lab lobh buri-aa-ee-aa chhoday manhu visaar. They renounce greed, avarice and evil, and forget them from their minds.
RECORD	para 40874	giV dohI pwiqswh kI kdy n AwvY hwir ] (936-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) garh dohee paatisaah kee kaday na aavai haar. In the fortress of the body, they announce the victory of their Supreme King; they are never ever vanquished.
RECORD	para 40875	cwkru khIAY Ksm kw sauhy auqr dyie ] (936-12, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) chaakar kahee-ai khasam kaa sa-uhay utar day-ay. One who calls himself a servant of his Lord and Master, and yet speaks defiantly to Him,
REQUIRE	para 40876	vjhu gvwey Awpxw qKiq n bYsih syie ] (936-12, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) vajahu gavaa-ay aapnaa takhat na baiseh say-ay. shall forfeit his pay, and not be seated upon the throne.
RECORD	para 40877	pRIqm hiQ vifAweIAw jY BwvY qY dyie ] (936-13, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) pareetam hath vadi-aa-ee-aa jai bhaavai tai day-ay. Glorious greatness rests in the hands of my Beloved; He gives, according to the Pleasure of His Will.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v45	Awip kry iksu AwKIAY Avru n koie kryie ]45] (936-13, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) aap karay kis aakhee-ai avar na ko-ay karay-i. ||45||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v45	He Himself does everything; who else should we address? No one else does anything. ||45||
RECORD	para 40879	bIjau sUJY ko nhI bhY dulIcw pwie ] (936-14, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) beeja-o soojhai ko nahee bahai duleechaa paa-ay. I cannot conceive of any other, who could be seated upon the royal cushions.
DEFINE	para 40880	nrk invwrxu nrh nru swcau swcY nwie ] (936-14, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) narak nivaaran narah nar saacha-o saachai naa-ay. The Supreme Man of men eradicates hell; He is True, and True is His Name.
RECORD	para 40881	vxu iqRxu FUFq iPir rhI mn mih krau bIcwru ] (936-14, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) van tarin dhoodhat fir rahee man meh kara-o beechaar. I wandered around searching for Him in the forests and meadows; I contemplate Him within my mind.
DEFINE	para 40882	lwl rqn bhu mwxkI siqgur hwiQ BMfwru ] (936-15, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) laal ratan baho maankee satgur haath bhandaar. The treasures of myriads of pearls, jewels and emeralds are in the hands of the True Guru.
RECORD	para 40883	aUqmu hovw pRBu imlY iek min eykY Bwie ] (936-15, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ootam hovaa parabh milai ik man aykai bhaa-ay. Meeting with God, I am exalted and elevated; I love the One Lord single-mindedly.
RECORD	para 40884	nwnk pRIqm ris imly lwhw lY prQwie ] (936-16, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naanak pareetam ras milay laahaa lai parthaa-ay. O Nanak, one who lovingly meets with his Beloved, earns profit in the world hereafter.
RECORD	para 40885	rcnw rwic ijin rcI ijin isirAw Awkwru ] (936-16, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) rachnaa raach jin rachee jin siri-aa aakaar. He who created and formed the creation, made your form as well.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v46	gurmuiK byAMqu iDAweIAY AMqu n pwrwvwru ]46] (936-17, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) gurmukh bay-ant Dhi-aa-ee-ai ant na paaraavaar. ||46||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v46	As Gurmukh, meditate on the Infinite Lord, who has no end or limitation. ||46||
DEFINE	para 40887	VwVY rUVw hir jIau soeI ] (936-17, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) rhaarhai roorhaa har jee-o so-ee. Rharha: The Dear Lord is beautiful;
DEFINE	para 40888	iqsu ibnu rwjw Avru n koeI ] (936-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) tis bin raajaa avar na ko-ee. There is no other king, except Him.
RECORD	para 40889	VwVY gwruVu qum suxhu hir vsY mn mwih ] (936-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) rhaarhai gaarurh tum sunhu har vasai man maahi. Rharha: Listen to the spell, and the Lord will come to dwell in your mind.
RECORD	para 40890	gur prswdI hir pweIAY mqu ko Brim Bulwih ] (936-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee har paa-ee-ai mat ko bharam bhulaahi. By Guru's Grace, one finds the Lord; do not be deluded by doubt.
DEFINE	para 40891	so swhu swcw ijsu hir Dnu rwis ] (936-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) so saahu saachaa jis har Dhan raas. He alone is the true banker, who has the capital of the wealth of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 40892	gurmuiK pUrw iqsu swbwis ] (936-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) gurmukh pooraa tis saabaas. The Gurmukh is perfect - applaud him!
RECORD	para 40893	rUVI bwxI hir pwieAw gur sbdI bIcwir ] (936-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) roorhee banee har paa-i-aa gur sabdee beechaar. Through the beautiful Word of the Guru's Bani, the Lord is obtained; contemplate the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v47	Awpu gieAw duKu kitAw hir vru pwieAw nwir ]47] (937-1, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) aap ga-i-aa dukh kati-aa har var paa-i-aa naar. ||47||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v47	Self-conceit is eliminated, and pain is eradicated; the soul bride obtains her Husband Lord. ||47||
DEFINE	para 40896	suienw rupw sMcIAY Dnu kwcw ibKu Cwru ] (937-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) su-inaa rupaa sanchee-ai Dhan kaachaa bikh chhaar. He hoards gold and silver, but this wealth is false and poisonous, nothing more than ashes.
DEFINE	para 40897	swhu sdwey sMic Dnu duibDw hoie KuAwru ] (937-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) saahu sadaa-ay sanch Dhan dubiDhaa ho-ay khu-aar. He calls himself a banker, gathering wealth, but he is ruined by his dual-mindedness.
DEFINE	para 40898	sicAwrI scu sMicAw swcau nwmu Amolu ] (937-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sachi-aaree sach sanchi-aa saacha-o naam amol. The truthful ones gather Truth; the True Name is priceless.
DEFINE	para 40899	hir inrmwielu aUjlo piq swcI scu bolu ] (937-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) har nirmaa-il oojlo pat saachee sach bol. The Lord is immaculate and pure; through Him, their honor is true, and their speech is true.
DEFINE	para 40900	swjnu mIqu sujwxu qU qU srvru qU hMsu ] (937-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) saajan meet sujaan too too sarvar too hans. You are my friend and companion, all-knowing Lord; You are the lake, and You are the swan.
DEFINE	para 40901	swcau Twkuru min vsY hau bilhwrI iqsu ] (937-4, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) saacha-o thaakur man vasai ha-o balihaaree tis. I am a sacrifice to that being, whose mind is filled with the True Lord and Master.
RECORD	para 40902	mwieAw mmqw mohxI ijin kIqI so jwxu ] (937-4, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) maa-i-aa mamtaa mohnee jin keetee so jaan. Know the One who created love and attachment to Maya, the Enticer.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v48	ibiKAw AMimRqu eyku hY bUJY purKu sujwxu ]48] (937-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) bikhi-aa amrit ayk hai boojhai purakh sujaan. ||48||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v48	One who realizes the all-knowing Primal Lord, looks alike upon poison and nectar. ||48||
RECORD	para 40904	iKmw ivhUxy Kip gey KUhix lK AsMK ] (937-5, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) khimaa vihoonay khap ga-ay khoohan lakh asa Nkh. Without patience and forgiveness, countless hundreds of thousands have perished.
RECORD	para 40905	gxq n AwvY ikau gxI Kip Kip muey ibsMK ] (937-6, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ganat na aavai ki-o ganee khap khap mu-ay bisankh. Their numbers cannot be counted; how could I count them? Bothered and bewildered, uncounted numbers have died.
DEFINE	para 40906	Ksmu pCwxY Awpxw KUlY bMDu n pwie ] (937-6, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) khasam pachhaanai aapnaa khoolai banDh na paa-ay. One who realizes his Lord and Master is set free, and not bound by chains.
UPHOLD	para 40907	sbid mhlI Krw qU iKmw scu suK Bwie ] (937-6, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sabad mahlee kharaa too khimaa sach sukh bhaa-ay. Through the Word of the Shabad, enter the Mansion of the Lord's Presence; you shall be blessed with patience, forgiveness, truth and peace.
REQUIRE	para 40908	Krcu Krw Dnu iDAwnu qU Awpy vsih srIir ] (937-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) kharach kharaa Dhan Dhi-aan too aapay vaseh sareer. Partake of the true wealth of meditation, and the Lord Himself shall abide within your body.
REQUIRE	para 40909	min qin muiK jwpY sdw gux AMqir min DIr ] (937-7, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) man tan mukh jaapai sadaa gun antar man Dheer. With mind, body and mouth, chant His Glorious Virtues forever; courage and composure shall enter deep within your mind.
DEFINE	para 40910	haumY KpY KpwiesI bIjau vQu ivkwru ] (937-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ha-umai khapai khapaa-isee beeja-o vath vikaar. Through egotism, one is distracted and ruined; other than the Lord, all things are corrupt.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v49	jMq aupwie ivic pwieAnu krqw Algu Apwru ]49] (937-8, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) jant upaa-ay vich paa-i-an kartaa alag apaar. ||49||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v49	Forming His creatures, He placed Himself within them; the Creator is unattached and infinite. ||49||
RECORD	para 40912	isRsty Byau n jwxY koie ] (937-9, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) saristay bhay-o na jaanai ko-ay. No one knows the mystery of the Creator of the World.
DEFINE	para 40913	isRstw krY su inhcau hoie ] (937-9, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) saristaa karai so nihcha-o ho-ay. Whatever the Creator of the World does, is certain to occur.
RECORD	para 40914	sMpY kau eIsru iDAweIAY ] (937-9, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sampai ka-o eesar Dhi-aa-ee-ai. For wealth, some meditate on the Lord.
DEFINE	para 40915	sMpY purib ilKy kI pweIAY ] (937-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sampai purab likhay kee paa-ee-ai. By pre-ordained destiny, wealth is obtained.
RECORD	para 40916	sMpY kwrix cwkr cor ] (937-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sampai kaaran chaakar chor. For the sake of wealth, some become servants or thieves.
WHEN	para 40917	sMpY swiQ n cwlY hor ] (937-10, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sampai saath na chaalai hor. Wealth does not go along with them when they die; it passes into the hands of others.
DEFINE	para 40918	ibnu swcy nhI drgh mwnu ] (937-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) bin saachay nahee dargeh maan. Without Truth, honor is not obtained in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v50	hir rsu pIvY CutY indwin ]50] (937-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) har ras peevai chhutai nidaan. ||50||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v50	Drinking in the subtle essence of the Lord, one is emancipated in the end. ||50||
RECORD	para 40920	hyrq hyrq hy sKI hoie rhI hYrwnu ] (937-11, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) hayrat hayrat hay sakhee ho-ay rahee hairaan. Seeing and perceiving, O my companions, I am wonder-struck and amazed.
UPHOLD	para 40921	hau hau krqI mY mueI sbid rvY min igAwnu ] (937-12, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) ha-o ha-o kartee mai mu-ee sabad ravai man gi-aan. My egotism, which proclaimed itself in possessiveness and self-conceit, is dead. My mind chants the Word of the Shabad, and attains spiritual wisdom.
RECORD	para 40922	hwr for kMkn Gxy kir QwkI sIgwru ] (937-12, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) haar dor kankan ghanay kar thaakee seegaar. I am so tired of wearing all these necklaces, hair-ties and bracelets, and decorating myself.
RECORD	para 40923	imil pRIqm suKu pwieAw sgl guxw gil hwru ] (937-13, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) mil pareetam sukh paa-i-aa sagal gunaa gal haar. Meeting with my Beloved, I have found peace; now, I wear the necklace of total virtue.
RECORD	para 40924	nwnk gurmuiK pweIAY hir isau pRIiq ipAwru ] (937-13, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh paa-ee-ai har si-o pareet pi-aar. O Nanak, the Gurmukh attains the Lord, with love and affection.
RECORD	para 40925	hir ibnu ikin suKu pwieAw dyKhu min bIcwir ] (937-14, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) har bin kin sukh paa-i-aa daykhhu man beechaar. Without the Lord, who has found peace? Reflect upon this in your mind, and see.
RECORD	para 40926	hir pVxw hir buJxw hir isau rKhu ipAwru ] (937-14, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) har parh-naa har bujh-naa har si-o rakhahu pi-aar. Read about the Lord, understand the Lord, and enshrine love for the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v51	hir jpIAY hir iDAweIAY hir kw nwmu ADwru ]51] (937-15, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) har japee-ai har Dhi-aa-ee-ai har kaa naam aDhaar. ||51||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v51	Chant the Lord's Name, and meditate on the Lord; hold tight to the Support of the Name of the Lord. ||51||
RECORD	para 40928	lyKu n imteI hy sKI jo iliKAw krqwir ] (937-15, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) laykh na mit-ee hay sakhee jo likhi-aa kartaar. The inscription inscribed by the Creator Lord cannot be erased, O my companions.
RECORD	para 40929	Awpy kwrxu ijin kIAw kir ikrpw pgu Dwir ] (937-16, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) aapay kaaran jin kee-aa kar kirpaa pag Dhaar. He who created the universe, in His Mercy, installs His Feet within us.
RECORD	para 40930	krqy hiQ vifAweIAw bUJhu gur bIcwir ] (937-16, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) kartay hath vadi-aa-ee-aa boojhhu gur beechaar. Glorious greatness rests in the Hands of the Creator; reflect upon the Guru, and understand this.
RECORD	para 40931	iliKAw Pyir n skIAY ijau BwvI iqau swir ] (937-17, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) likhi-aa fayr na sakee-ai ji-o bhaavee ti-o saar. This inscription cannot be challenged. As it pleases You, You care for me.
RECORD	para 40932	ndir qyrI suKu pwieAw nwnk sbdu vIcwir ] (937-17, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) nadar tayree sukh paa-i-aa naanak sabad veechaar. By Your Glance of Grace, I have found peace; O Nanak, reflect upon the Shabad.
RECORD	para 40933	mnmuK BUly pic muey aubry gur bIcwir ] (937-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) manmukh bhoolay pach mu-ay ubray gur beechaar. The self-willed manmukhs are confused; they rot away and die. Only by reflecting upon the Guru can they be saved.
RECORD	para 40934	ij purKu ndir n AwveI iqs kw ikAw kir kihAw jwie ] (937-18, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) je purakh nadar na aavee tis kaa ki-aa kar kahi-aa jaa-ay. What can anyone say, about that Primal Lord, who cannot be seen?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v52	bilhwrI gur Awpxy ijin ihrdY idqw idKwie ]52] (937-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) balihaaree gur aapnay jin hirdai ditaa dikhaa-ay. ||52||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v52	I am a sacrifice to my Guru, who has revealed Him to me, within my own heart. ||52||
WHEN	para 40936	pwDw piVAw AwKIAY ibidAw ibcrY shij suBwie ] (937-19, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) paaDhaa parhi-aa aakhee-ai bidi-aa bichrai sahj subhaa-ay. That Pandit, that religious scholar, is said to be well-educated, if he contemplates knowledge with intuitive ease.
RECORD	para 40938	ibidAw soDY qqu lhY rwm nwm ilv lwie ] (938-1, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) bidi-aa soDhai tat lahai raam naam liv laa-ay. Considering his knowledge, he finds the essence of reality, and lovingly focuses his attention on the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 40939	mnmuKu ibidAw ibk®dw ibKu Kty ibKu Kwie ] (938-1, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) manmukh bidi-aa bikardaa bikh khatay bikh khaa-ay. The self-willed manmukh sells his knowledge; he earns poison, and eats poison.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v53	mUrKu sbdu n cIneI sUJ bUJ nh kwie ]53] (938-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) moorakh sabad na cheen-ee soojh boojh nah kaa-ay. ||53||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v53	The fool does not think of the Word of the Shabad. He has no understanding, no comprehension. ||53||
DEFINE	para 40941	pwDw gurmuiK AwKIAY cwtiVAw miq dyie ] (938-2, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) paaDhaa gurmukh aakhee-ai chaatrhi-aa mat day-ay. That Pandit is called Gurmukh, who imparts understanding to his students.
RECORD	para 40942	nwmu smwlhu nwmu sMgrhu lwhw jg mih lyie ] (938-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naam samaalahu naam sangrahu laahaa jag meh lay-ay. Contemplate the Naam, the Name of the Lord; gather in the Naam, and earn the true profit in this world.
RECORD	para 40943	scI ptI scu min pVIAY sbdu su swru ] (938-3, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) sachee patee sach man parhee-ai sabad so saar. With the true notebook of the true mind, study the most sublime Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v54	nwnk so piVAw so pMifqu bInw ijsu rwm nwmu gil hwru ]54]1] (938-4, rwmklI dKxI, mÚ 1) naanak so parhi-aa so pandit beenaa jis raam naam gal haar. ||54||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 dKxI EAMkwru v54	1|| O Nanak, he alone is learned, and he alone is a wise Pandit, who wears the necklace of the Lord's Name. ||54||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit (938-5)
RECORD	para 40945	raamkalee mehlaa 1 siDh gosat Raamkalee, First Mehl, Sidh Gosht ~ Conversations With The Siddhas:
RECORD	para 40946	<> siqgur pRswid ] (938-5) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	para 40947	isD sBw kir Awsix bYTy sMq sBw jYkwro ] (938-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) siDh sabhaa kar aasan baithay sant sabhaa jaikaaro. The Siddhas formed an assembly; sitting in their Yogic postures, they shouted, "Salute this gathering of Saints."
DEFINE	para 40948	iqsu AwgY rhrwis hmwrI swcw Apr Apwro ] (938-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tis aagai rahraas hamaaree saachaa apar apaaro. I offer my salutation to the One who is true, infinite and incomparably beautiful.
RECORD	para 40949	msqku kwit DrI iqsu AwgY qnu mnu AwgY dyau ] (938-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mastak kaat Dharee tis aagai tan man aagai day-o. I cut off my head, and offer it to Him; I dedicate my body and mind to Him.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v1	nwnk sMqu imlY scu pweIAY shj Bwie jsu lyau ]1] (938-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak sant milai sach paa-ee-ai sahj bhaa-ay jas lay-o. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v1	O Nanak, meeting with the Saints, Truth is obtained, and one is spontaneously blessed with distinction. ||1||
DEFINE	para 40951	ikAw BvIAY sic sUcw hoie ] (938-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-aa bhavee-ai sach soochaa ho-ay. What is the use of wandering around? Purity comes only through Truth.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v1	swc sbd ibnu mukiq n koie ]1] rhwau ] (938-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saach sabad bin mukat na ko-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v1	rahaa-o. Without the True Word of the Shabad, no one finds liberation. ||1||Pause||
