DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit · what is #1	What is your name?
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit · what is #2	What is your way?
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit · what is #3	What is your goal?
DEFINE	para 40954	swcu khau Ardwis hmwrI hau sMq jnw bil jwE ] (938-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saach kaha-o ardaas hamaaree ha-o sant janaa bal jaa-o. We pray that you will answer us truthfully; we are a sacrifice to the humble Saints.
DEFINE	para 40955	kh bYshu kh rhIAY bwly kh Awvhu kh jwho ] (938-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kah baishu kah rahee-ai baalay kah aavhu kah jaaho. Where is your seat? Where do you live, boy? Where did you come from, and where are you going?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v2	nwnku bolY suix bYrwgI ikAw qumwrw rwho ]2] (938-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak bolai sun bairaagee ki-aa tumaaraa raaho. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v2	Tell us, Nanak - the detached Siddhas wait to hear your reply. What is your path?"||2||
RECORD	para 40957	Git Git bYis inrMqir rhIAY cwlih siqgur Bwey ] (938-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghat ghat bais nirantar rahee-ai chaaleh satgur bhaa-ay. He dwells deep within the nucleus of each and every heart. This is my seat and my home. I walk in harmony with the Will of the True Guru.
RECORD	para 40958	shjy Awey hukim isDwey nwnk sdw rjwey ] (938-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sehjay aa-ay hukam siDhaa-ay naanak sadaa rajaa-ay. I came from the Celestial Lord God; I go wherever He orders me to go. I am Nanak, forever under the Command of His Will.
RECORD	para 40959	Awsix bYsix iQru nwrwiexu AYsI gurmiq pwey ] (938-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aasan baisan thir naaraa-in aisee gurmat paa-ay. I sit in the posture of the eternal, imperishable Lord. These are the Teachings I have received from the Guru.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v3	gurmuiK bUJY Awpu pCwxY scy sic smwey ]3] (938-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh boojhai aap pachhaanai sachay sach samaa-ay. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v3	As Gurmukh, I have come to understand and realize myself; I merge in the Truest of the True. ||3||
DEFINE	para 40961	dunIAw swgru duqru khIAY ikau kir pweIAY pwro ] (938-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) dunee-aa saagar dutar kahee-ai ki-o kar paa-ee-ai paaro. "The world-ocean is treacherous and impassable; how can one cross over?
RECORD	para 40962	crptu bolY AauDU nwnk dyhu scw bIcwro ] (938-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) charpat bolai a-oDhoo naanak dayh sachaa beechaaro. Charpat the Yogi says, O Nanak, think it over, and give us your true reply."
RECORD	para 40963	Awpy AwKY Awpy smJY iqsu ikAw auqru dIjY ] (938-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay aakhai aapay samjhai tis ki-aa utar deejai. What answer can I give to someone, who claims to understand himself?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v4	swcu khhu qum pwrgrwmI quJu ikAw bYsxu dIjY ]4] (938-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saach kahhu tum paargaraamee tujh ki-aa baisan deejai. ||4||
WHEN	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v4	I speak the Truth; if you have already crossed over, how can I argue with you? ||4||
RECORD	para 40965	jYsy jl mih kmlu inrwlmu murgweI nY swxy ] (938-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jaisay jal meh kamal niraalam murgaa-ee nai saanay. The lotus flower floats untouched upon the surface of the water, and the duck swims through the stream;
RECORD	para 40966	suriq sbid Bv swgru qrIAY nwnk nwmu vKwxy ] (938-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) surat sabad bhav saagar taree-ai naanak naam vakhaanay. with one's consciousness focused on the Word of the Shabad, one crosses over the terrifying world-ocean. O Nanak, chant the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 40967	rhih iekWiq eyko min visAw Awsw mwih inrwso ] (938-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) raheh ikaa Nt ayko man vasi-aa aasaa maahi niraaso. One who lives alone, as a hermit, enshrining the One Lord in his mind, remaining unaffected by hope in the midst of hope,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v5	Agmu Agocru dyiK idKwey nwnku qw kw dwso ]5] (938-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) agam agochar daykh dikhaa-ay naanak taa kaa daaso. ||5||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v5	sees and inspires others to see the inaccessible, unfathomable Lord. Nanak is his slave. ||5||
RECORD	para 40969	suix suAwmI Ardwis hmwrI pUCau swcu bIcwro ] (938-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sun su-aamee ardaas hamaaree poochha-o saach beechaaro. "Listen, Lord, to our prayer. We seek your true opinion.
RECORD	para 40970	rosu n kIjY auqru dIjY ikau pweIAY gur duAwro ] (938-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ros na keejai utar deejai ki-o paa-ee-ai gur du-aaro. Don't be angry with us - please tell us: How can we find the Guru's Door?"
RECORD	para 40971	iehu mnu clqau sc Gir bYsY nwnk nwmu ADwro ] (938-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ih man chalta-o sach ghar baisai naanak naam aDhaaro. This fickle mind sits in its true home, O Nanak, through the Support of the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v6	Awpy myil imlwey krqw lwgY swic ipAwro ]6] (938-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay mayl milaa-ay kartaa laagai saach pi-aaro. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v6	The Creator Himself unites us in Union, and inspires us to love the Truth. ||6||
RECORD	para 40973	hwtI bwtI rhih inrwly rUiK ibriK auidAwny ] (938-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) haatee baatee raheh niraalay rookh birakh udi-aanay. "Away from stores and highways, we live in the woods, among plants and trees.
DEFINE	para 40974	kMd mUlu Ahwro KweIAY AauDU bolY igAwny ] (938-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kand mool ahaaro khaa-ee-ai a-oDhoo bolai gi-aanay. For food, we take fruits and roots. This is the spiritual wisdom spoken by the renunciates.
RECORD	para 40976	qIriQ nweIAY suKu Plu pweIAY mYlu n lwgY kweI ] (939-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tirath naa-ee-ai sukh fal paa-ee-ai mail na laagai kaa-ee. We bathe at sacred shrines of pilgrimage, and obtain the fruits of peace; not even an iota of filth sticks to us.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v7	gorK pUqu lohwrIpw bolY jog jugiq ibiD sweI ]7] (939-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gorakh poot lohaareepaa bolai jog jugat biDh saa-ee. ||7||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v7	Luhaareepaa, the disciple of Gorakh says, this is the Way of Yoga."||7||
RECORD	para 40978	hwtI bwtI nId n AwvY pr Gir icqu n fuolweI ] (939-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) haatee baatee need na aavai par ghar chit na dolaa-ee. In the stores and on the road, do not sleep; do not let your consciousness covet anyone else's home.
RECORD	para 40979	ibnu nwvY mnu tyk n itkeI nwnk BUK n jweI ] (939-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin naavai man tayk na tik-ee naanak bhookh na jaa-ee. Without the Name, the mind has no firm support; O Nanak, this hunger never departs.
RECORD	para 40980	hwtu ptxu Gru gurU idKwieAw shjy scu vwpwro ] (939-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) haat patan ghar guroo dikhaa-i-aa sehjay sach vaapaaro. The Guru has revealed the stores and the city within the home of my own heart, where I intuitively carry on the true trade.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v8	KMifq indRw Alp AhwrM nwnk qqu bIcwro ]8] (939-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) khandit nidraa alap ahaara N naanak tat beechaaro. ||8||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v8	Sleep little, and eat little; O Nanak, this is the essence of wisdom. ||8||
RECORD	para 40982	drsnu ByK krhu joigMdRw muMdRw JolI iKMQw ] (939-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) darsan bhaykh karahu jogindaraa mundraa jholee khinthaa. "Wear the robes of the sect of Yogis who follow Gorakh; put on the ear-rings, begging wallet and patched coat.
RECORD	para 40983	bwrh AMqir eyku sryvhu Ktu drsn iek pMQw ] (939-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) baarah antar ayk sarayvhu khat darsan ik panthaa. Among the twelve schools of Yoga, ours is the highest; among the six schools of philosophy, ours is the best path.
DEFINE	para 40984	ien ibiD mnu smJweIAY purKw bwhuiV cot n KweIAY ] (939-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) in biDh man samjaa-ee-ai purkhaa baahurh chot na khaa-ee-ai. This is the way to instruct the mind, so you will never suffer beatings again."
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v9	nwnku bolY gurmuiK bUJY jog jugiq iev pweIAY ]9] (939-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak bolai gurmukh boojhai jog jugat iv paa-ee-ai. ||9||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v9	Nanak speaks: the Gurmukh understands; this is the way that Yoga is attained. ||9||
RECORD	para 40986	AMqir sbdu inrMqir mudRw haumY mmqw dUir krI ] (939-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar sabad nirantar mudraa ha-umai mamtaa door karee. Let constant absorption in the Word of the Shabad deep within be your ear-rings; eradicate egotism and attachment.
RECORD	para 40987	kwmu k®oDu AhMkwru invwrY gur kY sbid su smJ prI ] (939-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaam kroDh aha Nkaar nivaarai gur kai sabad so samajh paree. Discard sexual desire, anger and egotism, and through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, attain true understanding.
RECORD	para 40988	iKMQw JolI Birpuir rihAw nwnk qwrY eyku hrI ] (939-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) khinthaa jholee bharipur rahi-aa naanak taarai ayk haree. For your patched coat and begging bowl, see the Lord God pervading and permeating everywhere; O Nanak, the One Lord will carry you across.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v10	swcw swihbu swcI nweI prKY gur kI bwq KrI ]10] (939-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saachaa saahib saachee naa-ee parkhai gur kee baat kharee. ||10||
REQUIRE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v10	True is our Lord and Master, and True is His Name. Analyze it, and you shall find the Word of the Guru to be True. ||10||
RECORD	para 40990	aUNDau Kpru pMc BU topI ] (939-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ooNDha-o khapar panch bhoo topee. Let your mind turn away in detachment from the world, and let this be your begging bowl. Let the lessons of the five elements be your cap.
RECORD	para 40991	kWieAw kVwsxu mnu jwgotI ] (939-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaaN-i-aa karhaasan man jaagotee. Let the body be your meditation mat, and the mind your loin cloth.
RECORD	para 40992	squ sMqoKu sMjmu hY nwil ] (939-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sat santokh sanjam hai naal. Let truth, contentment and self-discipline be your companions.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v11	nwnk gurmuiK nwmu smwil ]11] (939-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh naam samaal. ||11||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v11	O Nanak, the Gurmukh dwells on the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||11||
DEFINE	para 40994	kvnu su gupqw kvnu su mukqw ] (939-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan so guptaa kavan so muktaa. "Who is hidden? Who is liberated?
DEFINE	para 40995	kvnu su AMqir bwhir jugqw ] (939-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan so antar baahar jugtaa. Who is united, inwardly and outwardly?
RECORD	para 40996	kvnu su AwvY kvnu su jwie ] (939-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan so aavai kavan so jaa-ay. Who comes, and who goes?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v12	kvnu su iqRBvix rihAw smwie ]12] (939-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan so taribhavan rahi-aa samaa-ay. ||12||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v12	Who is permeating and pervading the three worlds?"||12||
DEFINE	para 40998	Git Git gupqw gurmuiK mukqw ] (939-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghat ghat guptaa gurmukh muktaa. He is hidden within each and every heart. The Gurmukh is liberated.
DEFINE	para 40999	AMqir bwhir sbid su jugqw ] (939-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar baahar sabad so jugtaa. Through the Word of the Shabad, one is united, inwardly and outwardly.
RECORD	para 41000	mnmuiK ibnsY AwvY jwie ] (939-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manmukh binsai aavai jaa-ay. The self-willed manmukh perishes, and comes and goes.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v13	nwnk gurmuiK swic smwie ]13] (939-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh saach samaa-ay. ||13||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v13	O Nanak, the Gurmukh merges in Truth. ||13||
DEFINE	para 41002	ikau kir bwDw srpin KwDw ] (939-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o kar baaDhaa sarpan khaaDhaa. "How is one placed in bondage, and consumed by the serpent of Maya?
RECORD	para 41003	ikau kir KoieAw ikau kir lwDw ] (939-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o kar kho-i-aa ki-o kar laaDhaa. How does one lose, and how does one gain?
DEFINE	para 41004	ikau kir inrmlu ikau kir AMiDAwrw ] (939-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o kar nirmal ki-o kar anDhi-aaraa. How does one become immaculate and pure? How is the darkness of ignorance removed?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v14	iehu qqu bIcwrY su gurU hmwrw ]14] (939-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ih tat beechaarai so guroo hamaaraa. ||14||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v14	One who understands this essence of reality is our Guru."||14||
DEFINE	para 41006	durmiq bwDw srpin KwDw ] (939-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) durmat baaDhaa sarpan khaaDhaa. Man is bound by evil-mindedness, and consumed by Maya, the serpent.
RECORD	para 41007	mnmuiK KoieAw gurmuiK lwDw ] (939-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manmukh kho-i-aa gurmukh laaDhaa. The self-willed manmukh loses, and the Gurmukh gains.
DEFINE	para 41008	siqguru imlY AMDyrw jwie ] (939-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satgur milai anDhayraa jaa-ay. Meeting the True Guru, darkness is dispelled.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v15	nwnk haumY myit smwie ]15] (939-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak ha-umai mayt samaa-ay. ||15||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v15	O Nanak, eradicating egotism, one merges in the Lord. ||15||
RECORD	para 41010	suMn inrMqir dIjY bMDu ] (939-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sunn nirantar deejai banDh. Focused deep within, in perfect absorption,
RECORD	para 41011	aufY n hMsw pVY n kMDu ] (939-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) udai na hansaa parhai na kanDh. the soul-swan does not fly away, and the body-wall does not collapse.
DEFINE	para 41012	shj guPw Gru jwxY swcw ] (939-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sahj gufaa ghar jaanai saachaa. Then, one knows that his true home is in the cave of intuitive poise.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v16	nwnk swcy BwvY swcw ]16] (939-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak saachay bhaavai saachaa. ||16||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v16	O Nanak, the True Lord loves those who are truthful. ||16||
RECORD	para 41014	iksu kwrix igRhu qijE audwsI ] (939-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kis kaaran garihu taji-o udaasee. "Why have you left your house and become a wandering Udaasee?
RECORD	para 41015	iksu kwrix iehu ByKu invwsI ] (939-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kis kaaran ih bhaykh nivaasee. Why have you adopted these religious robes?
RECORD	para 41016	iksu vKr ky qum vxjwry ] (939-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kis vakhar kay tum vanjaaray. What merchandise do you trade?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v17	ikau kir swQu lµGwvhu pwry ]17] (939-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o kar saath langhaavahu paaray. ||17||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v17	How will you carry others across with you?"||17||
RECORD	para 41018	gurmuiK Kojq Bey audwsI ] (939-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh khojat bha-ay udaasee. I became a wandering Udaasee, searching for the Gurmukhs.
UPHOLD	para 41019	drsn kY qweI ByK invwsI ] (939-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) darsan kai taa-ee bhaykh nivaasee. I have adopted these robes seeking the Blessed Vision of the Lord's Darshan.
RECORD	para 41020	swc vKr ky hm vxjwry ] (939-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saach vakhar kay ham vanjaaray. I trade in the merchandise of Truth.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v18	nwnk gurmuiK auqris pwry ]18] (939-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh utras paaray. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v18	O Nanak, as Gurmukh, I carry others across. ||18||
RECORD	para 41022	ikqu ibiD purKw jnmu vtwieAw ] (939-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kit biDh purkhaa janam vataa-i-aa. "How have you changed the course of your life?
RECORD	para 41023	kwhy kau quJu iehu mnu lwieAw ] (939-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaahay ka-o tujh ih man laa-i-aa. With what have you linked your mind?
RECORD	para 41025	ikqu ibiD Awsw mnsw KweI ] (940-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kit biDh aasaa mansaa khaa-ee. How have you subdued your hopes and desires?
RECORD	para 41026	ikqu ibiD joiq inrMqir pweI ] (940-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kit biDh jot nirantar paa-ee. How have you found the Light deep within your nucleus?
RECORD	para 41027	ibnu dMqw ikau KweIAY swru ] (940-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin dantaa ki-o khaa-ee-ai saar. Without teeth, how can you eat iron?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v19	nwnk swcw krhu bIcwru ]19] (940-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak saachaa karahu beechaar. ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v19	Give us your true opinion, Nanak."||19||
ALLOW	para 41029	siqgur kY jnmy gvnu imtwieAw ] (940-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satgur kai janmay gavan mitaa-i-aa. Born into the House of the True Guru, my wandering in reincarnation ended.
DEFINE	para 41030	Anhiq rwqy iehu mnu lwieAw ] (940-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) anhat raatay ih man laa-i-aa. My mind is attached and attuned to the unstruck sound current.
RECORD	para 41031	mnsw Awsw sbid jlweI ] (940-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mansaa aasaa sabad jalaa-ee. Through the Word of the Shabad, my hopes and desires have been burnt away.
RECORD	para 41032	gurmuiK joiq inrMqir pweI ] (940-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh jot nirantar paa-ee. As Gurmukh, I found the Light deep within the nucleus of my self.
RECORD	para 41033	qRY gux myty KweIAY swru ] (940-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tarai gun maytay khaa-ee-ai saar. Eradicating the three qualities, one eats iron.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v20	nwnk qwry qwrxhwru ]20] (940-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak taaray taaranhaar. ||20||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v20	O Nanak, the Emancipator emancipates. ||20||
RECORD	para 41035	Awid kau kvnu bIcwru kQIAly suMn khw Gr vwso ] (940-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aad ka-o kavan beechaar kathee-alay sunn kahaa ghar vaaso. "What can you tell us about the beginning? In what home did the absolute dwell then?
DEFINE	para 41036	igAwn kI mudRw kvn kQIAly Git Git kvn invwso ] (940-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gi-aan kee mudraa kavan kathee-alay ghat ghat kavan nivaaso. What are the ear-rings of spiritual wisdom? Who dwells in each and every heart?
RECORD	para 41037	kwl kw TIgw ikau jlweIAly ikau inrBau Gir jweIAY ] (940-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaal kaa theegaa ki-o jalaa-ee-alay ki-o nirbha-o ghar jaa-ee-ai. How can one avoid the attack of death? How can one enter the home of fearlessness?
RECORD	para 41038	shj sMqoK kw Awsxu jwxY ikau Cydy bYrweIAY ] (940-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sahj santokh kaa aasan jaanai ki-o chhayday bairaa-ee-ai. How can one know the posture of intuition and contentment, and overcome one's adversaries?"
RECORD	para 41039	gur kY sbid haumY ibKu mwrY qw inj Gir hovY vwso ] (940-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur kai sabad ha-umai bikh maarai taa nij ghar hovai vaaso. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, egotism and corruption are conquered, and then one comes to dwell in the home of the self within.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v21	ijin ric ricAw iqsu sbid pCwxY nwnku qw kw dwso ]21] (940-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jin rach rachi-aa tis sabad pachhaanai naanak taa kaa daaso. ||21||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v21	One who realizes the Shabad of the One who created the creation - Nanak is his slave. ||21||
DEFINE	para 41041	khw qy AwvY khw iehu jwvY khw iehu rhY smweI ] (940-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kahaa tay aavai kahaa ih jaavai kahaa ih rahai samaa-ee. "Where did we come from? Where are we going? Where will we be absorbed?
DEFINE	para 41042	eysu sbd kau jo ArQwvY iqsu gur iqlu n qmweI ] (940-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ays sabad ka-o jo arthaavai tis gur til na tamaa-ee. One who reveals the meaning of this Shabad is the Guru, who has no greed at all.
RECORD	para 41043	ikau qqY AivgqY pwvY gurmuiK lgY ipAwro ] (940-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o tatai avigatai paavai gurmukh lagai pi-aaro. How can one find the essence of the unmanifest reality? How does one become Gurmukh, and enshrine love for the Lord?
DEFINE	para 41044	Awpy surqw Awpy krqw khu nwnk bIcwro ] (940-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay surtaa aapay kartaa kaho naanak beechaaro. He Himself is consciousness, He Himself is the Creator; share with us, Nanak, your wisdom."
ALLOW	para 41045	hukmy AwvY hukmy jwvY hukmy rhY smweI ] (940-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hukmay aavai hukmay jaavai hukmay rahai samaa-ee. By His Command we come, and by His Command we go; by His Command, we merge in absorption.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v22	pUry gur qy swcu kmwvY giq imiq sbdy pweI ]22] (940-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) pooray gur tay saach kamaavai gat mit sabday paa-ee. ||22||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v22	Through the Perfect Guru, live the Truth; through the Word of the Shabad, the state of dignity is attained. ||22||
RECORD	para 41047	Awid kau ibsmwdu bIcwru kQIAly suMn inrMqir vwsu lIAw ] (940-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aad ka-o bismaad beechaar kathee-alay sunn nirantar vaas lee-aa. We can only express a sense of wonder about the beginning. The absolute abided endlessly deep within Himself then.
UPHOLD	para 41048	Aklpq mudRw gur igAwnu bIcwrIAly Git Git swcw srb jIAw ] (940-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) akalpat mudraa gur gi-aan beechaaree-alay ghat ghat saachaa sarab jee-aa. Consider freedom from desire to be the ear-rings of the Guru's spiritual wisdom. The True Lord, the Soul of all, dwells within each and every heart.
RECORD	para 41049	gur bcnI Aivgiq smweIAY qqu inrMjnu shij lhY ] (940-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur bachnee avigat samaa-ee-ai tat niranjan sahj lahai. Through the Guru's Word, one merges in the absolute, and intuitively receives the immaculate essence.
RECORD	para 41050	nwnk dUjI kwr n krxI syvY isKu su Koij lhY ] (940-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak doojee kaar na karnee sayvai sikh so khoj lahai. O Nanak, that Sikh who seeks and finds the Way does not serve any other.
RECORD	para 41051	hukmu ibsmwdu hukim pCwxY jIA jugiq scu jwxY soeI ] (940-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hukam bismaad hukam pachhaanai jee-a jugat sach jaanai so-ee. Wonderful and amazing is His Command; He alone realizes His Command and knows the true way of life of His creatures.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v23	Awpu myit inrwlmu hovY AMqir swcu jogI khIAY soeI ]23] (940-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aap mayt niraalam hovai antar saach jogee kahee-ai so-ee. ||23||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v23	One who eradicates his self-conceit becomes free of desire; he alone is a Yogi, who enshrines the True Lord deep within. ||23||
RECORD	para 41053	Aivgqo inrmwielu aupjy inrgux qy srguxu QIAw ] (940-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) avigato nirmaa-il upjay nirgun tay sargun thee-aa. From His state of absolute existence, He assumed the immaculate form; from formless, He assumed the supreme form.
RECORD	para 41054	siqgur prcY prm pdu pweIAY swcY sbid smwie lIAw ] (940-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satgur parchai param pad paa-ee-ai saachai sabad samaa-ay lee-aa. By pleasing the True Guru, the supreme status is obtained, and one is absorbed in the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 41055	eyky kau scu eykw jwxY haumY dUjw dUir kIAw ] (940-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aykay ka-o sach aykaa jaanai ha-umai doojaa door kee-aa. He knows the True Lord as the One and only; he sends his egotism and duality far away.
RECORD	para 41056	so jogI gur sbdu pCwxY AMqir kmlu pRgwsu QIAw ] (940-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so jogee gur sabad pachhaanai antar kamal pargaas thee-aa. He alone is a Yogi, who realizes the Word of the Guru's Shabad; the lotus of the heart blossoms forth within.
WHEN	para 41057	jIvqu mrY qw sBu ikCu sUJY AMqir jwxY srb dieAw ] (940-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jeevat marai taa sabh kichh soojhai antar jaanai sarab da-i-aa. If one remains dead while yet alive, then he understands everything; he knows the Lord deep within himself, who is kind and compassionate to all.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v24	nwnk qw kau imlY vfweI Awpu pCwxY srb jIAw ]24] (940-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak taa ka-o milai vadaa-ee aap pachhaanai sarab jee-aa. ||24||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v24	O Nanak, he is blessed with glorious greatness; he realizes himself in all beings. ||24||
RECORD	para 41059	swcO aupjY swic smwvY swcy sUcy eyk mieAw ] (940-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saachou upjai saach samaavai saachay soochay ayk ma-i-aa. We emerge from Truth, and merge into Truth again. The pure being merges into the One True Lord.
RECORD	para 41060	JUTy Awvih Tvr n pwvih dUjY Awvw gauxu BieAw ] (940-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jhoothay aavahi thavar na paavahi doojai aavaa ga-on bha-i-aa. The false come, and find no place of rest; in duality, they come and go.
RECORD	para 41061	Awvw gauxu imtY gur sbdI Awpy prKY bKis lieAw ] (940-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aavaa ga-on mitai gur sabdee aapay parkhai bakhas la-i-aa. This coming and going in reincarnation is ended through the Word of the Guru's Shabad; the Lord Himself analyzes and grants His forgiveness.
RECORD	para 41062	eykw bydn dUjY ibAwpI nwmu rswiexu vIsirAw ] (940-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aykaa baydan doojai bi-aapee naam rasaa-in veesri-aa. One who suffers from the disease of duality, forgets the Naam, the source of nectar.
RECORD	para 41064	so bUJY ijsu Awip buJwey gur kY sbid su mukqu BieAw ] (941-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so boojhai jis aap bujhaa-ay gur kai sabad so mukat bha-i-aa. He alone understands, whom the Lord inspires to understand. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, one is liberated.
