DEFINE	para 41169	kvx mUlu kvx miq vylw ] (942-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan mool kavan mat vaylaa. "What is the root, the source of all? What teachings hold for these times?
DEFINE	para 41170	qyrw kvxu gurU ijs kw qU cylw ] (942-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tayraa kavan guroo jis kaa too chaylaa. Who is your guru? Whose disciple are you?
DEFINE	para 41171	kvx kQw ly rhhu inrwly ] (942-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan kathaa lay rahhu niraalay. What is that speech, by which you remain unattached?
RECORD	para 41172	bolY nwnku suxhu qum bwly ] (942-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai naanak sunhu tum baalay. Listen to what we say, O Nanak, you little boy.
RECORD	para 41173	eysu kQw kw dyie bIcwru ] (942-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ays kathaa kaa day-ay beechaar. Give us your opinion on what we have said.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v43	Bvjlu sbid lµGwvxhwru ]43] (942-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bhavjal sabad langhaavanhaar. ||43||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v43	How can the Shabad carry us across the terrifying world-ocean?"||43||
DEFINE	para 41176	pvn ArMBu siqgur miq vylw ] (943-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) pavan arambh satgur mat vaylaa. From the air came the beginning. This is the age of the True Guru's Teachings.
DEFINE	para 41177	sbdu gurU suriq Duin cylw ] (943-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad guroo surat Dhun chaylaa. The Shabad is the Guru, upon whom I lovingly focus my consciousness; I am the chaylaa, the disciple.
RECORD	para 41178	AkQ kQw ly rhau inrwlw ] (943-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) akath kathaa lay raha-o niraalaa. Speaking the Unspoken Speech, I remain unattached.
DEFINE	para 41179	nwnk juig juig gur gopwlw ] (943-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak jug jug gur gopaalaa. O Nanak, throughout the ages, the Lord of the World is my Guru.
RECORD	para 41180	eyku sbdu ijqu kQw vIcwrI ] (943-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ayk sabad jit kathaa veechaaree. I contemplate the sermon of the Shabad, the Word of the One God.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v44	gurmuiK haumY Agin invwrI ]44] (943-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh ha-umai agan nivaaree. ||44||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v44	The Gurmukh puts out the fire of egotism. ||44||
RECORD	para 41182	mYx ky dMq ikau KweIAY swru ] (943-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) main kay dant ki-o khaa-ee-ai saar. "With teeth of wax, how can one chew iron?
DEFINE	para 41183	ijqu grbu jwie su kvxu Awhwru ] (943-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jit garab jaa-ay so kavan aahaar. What is that food, which takes away pride?
RECORD	para 41184	ihvY kw Gru mMdru Agin iprwhnu ] (943-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hivai kaa ghar mandar agan piraahan. How can one live in the palace, the home of snow, wearing robes of fire?
ALLOW	para 41185	kvn guPw ijqu rhY Avwhnu ] (943-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan gufaa jit rahai avaahan. Where is that cave, within which one may remain unshaken?
RECORD	para 41186	ieq auq iks kau jwix smwvY ] (943-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) it ut kis ka-o jaan samaavai. Who should we know to be pervading here and there?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v45	kvn iDAwnu mnu mnih smwvY ]45] (943-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan Dhi-aan man maneh samaavai. ||45||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v45	What is that meditation, which leads the mind to be absorbed in itself?"||45||
RECORD	para 41188	hau hau mY mY ivchu KovY ] (943-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ha-o ha-o mai mai vichahu khovai. Eradicating egotism and individualism from within,
RECORD	para 41189	dUjw mytY eyko hovY ] (943-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) doojaa maytai ayko hovai. and erasing duality, the mortal becomes one with God.
DEFINE	para 41190	jgu krVw mnmuKu gwvwru ] (943-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jag karrhaa manmukh gaavaar. The world is difficult for the foolish, self-willed manmukh;
RECORD	para 41191	sbdu kmweIAY KweIAY swru ] (943-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad kamaa-ee-ai khaa-ee-ai saar. practicing the Shabad, one chews iron.
RECORD	para 41192	AMqir bwhir eyko jwxY ] (943-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar baahar ayko jaanai. Know the One Lord, inside and out.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v46	nwnk Agin mrY siqgur kY BwxY ]46] (943-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak agan marai satgur kai bhaanai. ||46||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v46	O Nanak, the fire is quenched, through the Pleasure of the True Guru's Will. ||46||
DEFINE	para 41194	sc BY rwqw grbu invwrY ] (943-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sach bhai raataa garab nivaarai. Imbued with the True Fear of God, pride is taken away;
DEFINE	para 41195	eyko jwqw sbdu vIcwrY ] (943-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ayko jaataa sabad veechaarai. realize that He is One, and contemplate the Shabad.
RECORD	para 41196	sbdu vsY scu AMqir hIAw ] (943-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad vasai sach antar hee-aa. With the True Shabad abiding deep within the heart,
DEFINE	para 41197	qnu mnu sIqlu rMig rMgIAw ] (943-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tan man seetal rang rangee-aa. the body and mind are cooled and soothed, and colored with the Lord's Love.
DEFINE	para 41198	kwmu k®oDu ibKu Agin invwry ] (943-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaam kroDh bikh agan nivaaray. The fire of sexual desire, anger and corruption is quenched.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v47	nwnk ndrI ndir ipAwry ]47] (943-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak nadree nadar pi-aaray. ||47||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v47	O Nanak, the Beloved bestows His Glance of Grace. ||47||
DEFINE	para 41200	kvn muiK cMdu ihvY Gru CwieAw ] (943-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan mukh chand hivai ghar chhaa-i-aa. "The moon of the mind is cool and dark; how is it enlightened?
RECORD	para 41201	kvn muiK sUrju qpY qpwieAw ] (943-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan mukh sooraj tapai tapaa-i-aa. How does the sun blaze so brilliantly?
RECORD	para 41202	kvn muiK kwlu johq inq rhY ] (943-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan mukh kaal johat nit rahai. How can the constant watchful gaze of Death be turned away?
DEFINE	para 41203	kvn buiD gurmuiK piq rhY ] (943-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan buDh gurmukh pat rahai. By what understanding is the honor of the Gurmukh preserved?
DEFINE	para 41204	kvnu joDu jo kwlu sMGwrY ] (943-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan joDh jo kaal sanghaarai. Who is the warrior, who conquers Death?
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v48	bolY bwxI nwnku bIcwrY ]48] (943-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai banee naanak beechaarai. ||48||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v48	Give us your thoughtful reply, O Nanak."||48||
DEFINE	para 41206	sbdu BwKq sis joiq Apwrw ] (943-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad bhaakhat sas jot apaaraa. Giving voice to the Shabad, the moon of the mind is illuminated with infinity.
DEFINE	para 41207	sis Gir sUru vsY imtY AMiDAwrw ] (943-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sas ghar soor vasai mitai anDhi-aaraa. When the sun dwells in the house of the moon, the darkness is dispelled.
DEFINE	para 41208	suKu duKu sm kir nwmu ADwrw ] (943-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sukh dukh sam kar naam aDhaaraa. Pleasure and pain are just the same, when one takes the Support of the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 41209	Awpy pwir auqwrxhwrw ] (943-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay paar utaaranhaaraa. He Himself saves, and carries us across.
RECORD	para 41210	gur prcY mnu swic smwie ] (943-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur parchai man saach samaa-ay. With faith in the Guru, the mind merges in Truth,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v49	pRxviq nwnku kwlu n Kwie ]49] (943-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) paranvat naanak kaal na khaa-ay. ||49||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v49	and then, prays Nanak, one is not consumed by Death. ||49||
DEFINE	para 41212	nwm qqu sB hI isir jwpY ] (943-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naam tat sabh hee sir jaapai. The essence of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, is known to be the most exalted and excellent of all.
DEFINE	para 41213	ibnu nwvY duKu kwlu sMqwpY ] (943-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin naavai dukh kaal santaapai. Without the Name, one is afflicted by pain and death.
DEFINE	para 41214	qqo qqu imlY mnu mwnY ] (943-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tato tat milai man maanai. When one's essence merges into the essence, the mind is satisfied and fulfilled.
DEFINE	para 41215	dUjw jwie iekqu Gir AwnY ] (943-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) doojaa jaa-ay ikat ghar aanai. Duality is gone, and one enters into the home of the One Lord.
RECORD	para 41216	bolY pvnw ggnu grjY ] (943-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai pavnaa gagan garjai. The breath blows across the sky of the Tenth Gate and vibrates.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v50	nwnk inhclu imlxu shjY ]50] (943-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak nihchal milan sahjai. ||50||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v50	O Nanak, the mortal then intuitively meets the eternal, unchanging Lord. ||50||
RECORD	para 41218	AMqir suMnµ bwhir suMnµ iqRBvx suMn msuMnµ ] (943-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar sunaN baahar suna N taribhavan sunn masu Nna N. The absolute Lord is deep within; the absolute Lord is outside us as well. The absolute Lord totally fills the three worlds.
DEFINE	para 41219	cauQy suMnY jo nru jwxY qw kau pwpu n puMnµ ] (943-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) cha-uthay sunnai jo nar jaanai taa ka-o paap na pu Nna N. One who knows the Lord in the fourth state, is not subject to virtue or vice.
RECORD	para 41220	Git Git suMn kw jwxY Byau ] Awid purKu inrMjn dyau ] (943-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghat ghat sunn kaa jaanai bhay-o. aad purakh niranjan day-o. One who knows the mystery of God the Absolute, who pervades each and every heart, knows the Primal Being, the Immaculate Divine Lord.
DEFINE	para 41221	jo jnu nwm inrMjn rwqw ] (943-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jo jan naam niranjan raataa. That humble being who is imbued with the Immaculate Naam,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v51	nwnk soeI purKu ibDwqw ]51] (943-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak so-ee purakh biDhaataa. ||51||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v51	O Nanak, is himself the Primal Lord, the Architect of Destiny. ||51||
RECORD	para 41223	suMno suMnu khY sBu koeI ] (943-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sunno sunn kahai sabh ko-ee. "Everyone speaks of the Absolute Lord, the unmanifest void.
RECORD	para 41224	Anhq suMnu khw qy hoeI ] (943-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) anhat sunn kahaa tay ho-ee. How can one find this absolute void?
DEFINE	para 41225	Anhq suMin rqy sy kYsy ] (943-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) anhat sunn ratay say kaisay. Who are they, who are attuned to this absolute void?"
DEFINE	para 41226	ijs qy aupjy iqs hI jYsy ] (943-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jis tay upjay tis hee jaisay. They are like the Lord, from whom they originated.
DEFINE	para 41227	Eie jnim n mrih n Awvih jwih ] (943-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) o-ay janam na mareh na aavahi jaahi. They are not born, they do not die; they do not come and go.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v52	nwnk gurmuiK mnu smJwih ]52] (943-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh man samjhaahi. ||52||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v52	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs instruct their minds. ||52||
RECORD	para 41229	nau sr suBr dsvY pUry ] (943-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) na-o sar subhar dasvai pooray. By practicing control over the nine gates, one attains perfect control over the Tenth Gate.
RECORD	para 41230	qh Anhq suMn vjwvih qUry ] (943-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tah anhat sunn vajaavah tooray. There, the unstruck sound current of the absolute Lord vibrates and resounds.
RECORD	para 41231	swcY rwcy dyiK hjUry ] (943-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saachai raachay daykh hajooray. Behold the True Lord ever-present, and merge with Him.
DEFINE	para 41232	Git Git swcu rihAw BrpUry ] (943-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghat ghat saach rahi-aa bharpooray. The True Lord is pervading and permeating each and every heart.
DEFINE	para 41234	gupqI bwxI prgtu hoie ] (944-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) guptee banee pargat ho-ay. The hidden Bani of the Word is revealed.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v53	nwnk priK ley scu soie ]53] (944-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak parakh la-ay sach so-ay. ||53||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v53	O Nanak, the True Lord is revealed and known. ||53||
DEFINE	para 41236	shj Bwie imlIAY suKu hovY ] (944-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sahj bhaa-ay milee-ai sukh hovai. Meeting with the Lord through intuition and love, peace is found.
RECORD	para 41237	gurmuiK jwgY nId n sovY ] (944-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh jaagai need na sovai. The Gurmukh remains awake and aware; he does not fall sleep.
RECORD	para 41238	suMn sbdu AprMpir DwrY ] (944-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sunn sabad aprampar Dhaarai. He enshrines the unlimited, absolute Shabad deep within.
DEFINE	para 41239	khqy mukqu sbid insqwrY ] (944-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kahtay mukat sabad nistaarai. Chanting the Shabad, he is liberated, and saves others as well.
DEFINE	para 41240	gur kI dIiKAw sy sic rwqy ] (944-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur kee deekhi-aa say sach raatay. Those who practice the Guru's Teachings are attuned to the Truth.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v54	nwnk Awpu gvwie imlx nhI BRwqy ]54] (944-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak aap gavaa-ay milan nahee bharaatay. ||54||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v54	O Nanak, those who eradicate their self-conceit meet with the Lord; they do not remain separated by doubt. ||54||
DEFINE	para 41242	kubuiD cvwvY so ikqu Twie ] (944-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kubuDh chavaavai so kit thaa-ay. "Where is that place, where evil thoughts are destroyed?
REQUIRE	para 41243	ikau qqu n bUJY cotw Kwie ] (944-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o tat na boojhai chotaa khaa-ay. The mortal does not understand the essence of reality; why must he suffer in pain?"
DEFINE	para 41244	jm dir bwDy koie n rwKY ] (944-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jam dar baaDhay ko-ay na raakhai. No one can save one who is tied up at Death's door.
RECORD	para 41245	ibnu sbdY nwhI piq swKY ] (944-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin sabdai naahee pat saakhai. Without the Shabad, no one has any credit or honor.
RECORD	para 41246	ikau kir bUJY pwvY pwru ] (944-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o kar boojhai paavai paar. "How can one obtain understanding and cross over?"
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v55	nwnk mnmuiK n buJY gvwru ]55] (944-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak manmukh na bujhai gavaar. ||55||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v55	O Nanak, the foolish self-willed manmukh does not understand. ||55||
DEFINE	para 41248	kubuiD imtY gur sbdu bIcwir ] (944-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kubuDh mitai gur sabad beechaar. Evil thoughts are erased, contemplating the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
DEFINE	para 41249	siqguru BytY moK duAwr ] (944-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satgur bhaytai mokh du-aar. Meeting with the True Guru, the door of liberation is found.
DEFINE	para 41250	qqu n cInY mnmuKu jil jwie ] (944-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tat na cheenai manmukh jal jaa-ay. The self-willed manmukh does not understand the essence of reality, and is burnt to ashes.
RECORD	para 41251	durmiq ivCuiV cotw Kwie ] (944-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) durmat vichhurh chotaa khaa-ay. His evil-mindedness separates him from the Lord, and he suffers.
DEFINE	para 41252	mwnY hukmu sBy gux igAwn ] (944-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) maanai hukam sabhay gun gi-aan. Accepting the Hukam of the Lord's Command, he is blessed with all virtues and spiritual wisdom.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v56	nwnk drgh pwvY mwnu ]56] (944-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak dargeh paavai maan. ||56||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v56	O Nanak, he is honored in the Court of the Lord. ||56||
RECORD	para 41254	swcu vKru Dnu plY hoie ] (944-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saach vakhar Dhan palai ho-ay. One who possesses the merchandise, the wealth of the True Name,
RECORD	para 41255	Awip qrY qwry BI soie ] (944-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aap tarai taaray bhee so-ay. crosses over, and carries others across with him as well.
DEFINE	para 41256	shij rqw bUJY piq hoie ] (944-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sahj rataa boojhai pat ho-ay. One who intuitively understands, and is attuned to the Lord, is honored.
RECORD	para 41257	qw kI kImiq krY n koie ] (944-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) taa kee keemat karai na ko-ay. No one can estimate his worth.
RECORD	para 41258	jh dyKw qh rihAw smwie ] (944-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jah daykhaa tah rahi-aa samaa-ay. Wherever I look, I see the Lord permeating and pervading.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v57	nwnk pwir prY sc Bwie ]57] (944-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak paar parai sach bhaa-ay. ||57||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v57	O Nanak, through the Love of the True Lord, one crosses over. ||57||
RECORD	para 41260	su sbd kw khw vwsu kQIAly ijqu qrIAY Bvjlu sMswro ] (944-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so sabad kaa kahaa vaas kathee-alay jit taree-ai bhavjal sansaaro. "Where is the Shabad said to dwell? What will carry us across the terrifying world- ocean?
DEFINE	para 41261	qRY sq AMgul vweI khIAY iqsu khu kvnu ADwro ] (944-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tarai sat angul vaa-ee kahee-ai tis kaho kavan aDhaaro. The breath, when exhaled, extends out ten finger lengths; what is the support of the breath?
RECORD	para 41262	bolY KylY AsiQru hovY ikau kir AlKu lKwey ] (944-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai khaylai asthir hovai ki-o kar alakh lakhaa-ay. Speaking and playing, how can one be stable and steady? How can the unseen be seen?"
RECORD	para 41263	suix suAwmI scu nwnku pRxvY Apxy mn smJwey ] (944-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sun su-aamee sach naanak paranvai apnay man samjhaa-ay. Listen, O master; Nanak prays truly. Instruct your own mind.
RECORD	para 41264	gurmuiK sbdy sic ilv lwgY kir ndrI myil imlwey ] (944-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh sabday sach liv laagai kar nadree mayl milaa-ay. The Gurmukh is lovingly attuned to the True Shabad. Bestowing His Glance of Grace, He unites us in His Union.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v58	Awpy dwnw Awpy bInw pUrY Bwig smwey ]58] (944-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay daanaa aapay beenaa poorai bhaag samaa-ay. ||58||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v58	He Himself is all-knowing and all-seeing. By perfect destiny, we merge in Him. ||58||
RECORD	para 41266	su sbd kau inrMqir vwsu AlKM jh dyKw qh soeI ] (944-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so sabad ka-o nirantar vaas alkhaN jah daykhaa tah so-ee. That Shabad dwells deep within the nucleus of all beings. God is invisible; wherever I look, there I see Him.
DEFINE	para 41267	pvn kw vwsw suMn invwsw Akl klw Dr soeI ] (944-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) pavan kaa vaasaa sunn nivaasaa akal kalaa Dhar so-ee. The air is the dwelling place of the absolute Lord. He has no qualities; He has all qualities.
WHEN	para 41268	ndir kry sbdu Gt mih vsY ivchu Brmu gvwey ] (944-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) nadar karay sabad ghat meh vasai vichahu bharam gavaa-ay. When He bestows His Glance of Grace, the Shabad comes to abide within the heart, and doubt is eradicated from within.
RECORD	para 41269	qnu mnu inrmlu inrml bwxI nwmuo mMin vswey ] (944-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tan man nirmal nirmal banee naamo man vasaa-ay. The body and mind become immaculate, through the Immaculate Word of His Bani. Let His Name be enshrined in your mind.
RECORD	para 41270	sbid gurU Bvswgru qrIAY ieq auq eyko jwxY ] (944-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad guroo bhavsaagar taree-ai it ut ayko jaanai. The Shabad is the Guru, to carry you across the terrifying world-ocean. Know the One Lord alone, here and hereafter.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v59	ichnu vrnu nhI CwieAw mwieAw nwnk sbdu pCwxY ]59] (944-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) chihan varan nahee chhaa-i-aa maa-i-aa naanak sabad pachhaanai. ||59||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v59	He has no form or color, shadow or illusion; O Nanak, realize the Shabad. ||59||
RECORD	para 41272	qRY sq AMgul vweI AauDU suMn scu Awhwro ] (944-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tarai sat angul vaa-ee a-oDhoo sunn sach aahaaro. O reclusive hermit, the True, Absolute Lord is the support of the exhaled breath, which extends out ten finger lengths.
RECORD	para 41273	gurmuiK bolY qqu ibrolY cInY AlK Apwro ] (944-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh bolai tat birolai cheenai alakh apaaro. The Gurmukh speaks and churns the essence of reality, and realizes the unseen, infinite Lord.
RECORD	para 41274	qRY gux mytY sbdu vswey qw min cUkY AhMkwro ] (944-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tarai gun maytai sabad vasaa-ay taa man chookai ahankaaro. Eradicating the three qualities, he enshrines the Shabad within, and then, his mind is rid of egotism.
DEFINE	para 41275	AMqir bwhir eyko jwxY qw hir nwim lgY ipAwro ] (944-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar baahar ayko jaanai taa har naam lagai pi-aaro. Inside and out, he knows the One Lord alone; he is in love with the Name of the Lord.
WHEN	para 41276	suKmnw ieVw ipMgulw bUJY jw Awpy AlKu lKwey ] (944-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sukhmanaa irhaa pingulaa boojhai jaa aapay alakh lakhaa-ay. He understands the Sushmana, Ida and Pingala, when the unseen Lord reveals Himself.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v60	nwnk iqhu qy aUpir swcw siqgur sbid smwey ]60] (944-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak tihu tay oopar saachaa satgur sabad samaa-ay. ||60||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v60	O Nanak, the True Lord is above these three energy channels. Through the Word, the Shabad of the True Guru, one merges with Him. ||60||
DEFINE	para 41278	mn kw jIau pvnu kQIAly pvnu khw rsu KweI ] (944-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) man kaa jee-o pavan kathee-alay pavan kahaa ras khaa-ee. "The air is said to be the soul of the mind. But what does the air feed on?
RECORD	para 41279	igAwn kI mudRw kvn AauDU isD kI kvn kmweI ] (944-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gi-aan kee mudraa kavan a-oDhoo siDh kee kavan kamaa-ee. What is the way of the spiritual teacher, and the reclusive hermit? What is the occupation of the Siddha?"
RECORD	para 41281	ibnu sbdY rsu n AwvY AauDU haumY ipAws n jweI ] (945-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin sabdai ras na aavai a-oDhoo ha-umai pi-aas na jaa-ee. Without the Shabad, the essence does not come, O hermit, and the thirst of egotism does not depart.
RECORD	para 41282	sbid rqy AMimRq rsu pwieAw swcy rhy AGweI ] (945-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabad ratay amrit ras paa-i-aa saachay rahay aghaa-ee. Imbued with the Shabad, one finds the ambrosial essence, and remains fulfilled with the True Name.
UPHOLD	para 41283	kvn buiD ijqu AsiQru rhIAY ikqu Bojin iqRpqwsY ] (945-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kavan buDh jit asthir rahee-ai kit bhojan tariptaasai. "What is that wisdom, by which one remains steady and stable? What food brings satisfaction?"
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v61	nwnk duKu suKu sm kir jwpY siqgur qy kwlu n gRwsY ]61] (945-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak dukh sukh sam kar jaapai satgur tay kaal na garaasai. ||61||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v61	O Nanak, when one looks upon pain and pleasure alike, through the True Guru, then he is not consumed by Death. ||61||
DEFINE	para 41285	rMig n rwqw ris nhI mwqw ] (945-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) rang na raataa ras nahee maataa. If one is not imbued with the Lord's Love, nor intoxicated with His subtle essence,
DEFINE	para 41286	ibnu gur sbdY jil bil qwqw ] (945-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin gur sabdai jal bal taataa. without the Word of the Guru's Shabad, he is frustrated, and consumed by his own inner fire.
RECORD	para 41287	ibMdu n rwiKAw sbdu n BwiKAw ] (945-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bind na raakhi-aa sabad na bhaakhi-aa. He does not preserve his semen and seed, and does not chant the Shabad.
RECORD	para 41288	pvnu n swiDAw scu n ArwiDAw ] (945-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) pavan na saaDhi-aa sach na araaDhi-aa. He does not control his breath; he does not worship and adore the True Lord.
RECORD	para 41289	AkQ kQw ly sm kir rhY ] (945-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) akath kathaa lay sam kar rahai. But one who speaks the Unspoken Speech, and remains balanced,
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v62	qau nwnk Awqm rwm kau lhY ]62] (945-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ta-o naanak aatam raam ka-o lahai. ||62||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v62	O Nanak, attains the Lord, the Supreme Soul. ||62||
DEFINE	para 41291	gur prswdI rMgy rwqw ] (945-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee rangay raataa. By Guru's Grace, one is attuned to the Lord's Love.
DEFINE	para 41292	AMimRqu pIAw swcy mwqw ] (945-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) amrit pee-aa saachay maataa. Drinking in the Ambrosial Nectar, he is intoxicated with the Truth.
DEFINE	para 41293	gur vIcwrI Agin invwrI ] (945-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur veechaaree agan nivaaree. Contemplating the Guru, the fire within is put out.
RECORD	para 41294	Aipau pIE Awqm suKu DwrI ] (945-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) api-o pee-o aatam sukh Dhaaree. Drinking in the Ambrosial Nectar, the soul settles in peace.
RECORD	para 41295	scu ArwiDAw gurmuiK qru qwrI ] (945-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sach araaDhi-aa gurmukh tar taaree. Worshipping the True Lord in adoration, the Gurmukh crosses over the river of life.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v63	nwnk bUJY ko vIcwrI ]63] (945-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak boojhai ko veechaaree. ||63||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v63	O Nanak, after deep contemplation, this is understood. ||63||
RECORD	para 41297	iehu mnu mYglu khw bsIAly khw bsY iehu pvnw ] (945-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ih man maigal kahaa basee-alay kahaa basai ih pavnaa. "Where does this mind-elephant live? Where does the breath reside?
ALLOW	para 41298	khw bsY su sbdu AauDU qw kau cUkY mn kw Bvnw ] (945-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kahaa basai so sabad a-oDhoo taa ka-o chookai man kaa bhavnaa. Where should the Shabad reside, so that the wanderings of the mind may cease?"
WHEN	para 41299	ndir kry qw siqguru myly qw inj Gir vwsw iehu mnu pwey ] (945-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) nadar karay taa satgur maylay taa nij ghar vaasaa ih man paa-ay. When the Lord blesses one with His Glance of Grace, he leads him to the True Guru. Then, this mind dwells in its own home within.
WHEN	para 41300	AwpY Awpu Kwie qw inrmlu hovY Dwvqu vrij rhwey ] (945-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapai aap khaa-ay taa nirmal hovai Dhaavat varaj rahaa-ay. When the individual consumes his egotism, he becomes immaculate, and his wandering mind is restrained.
RECORD	para 41301	ikau mUlu pCwxY Awqmu jwxY ikau sis Gir sUru smwvY ] (945-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o mool pachhaanai aatam jaanai ki-o sas ghar soor samaavai. "How can the root, the source of all be realized? How can the soul know itself? How can the sun enter into the house of the moon?"
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v64	gurmuiK haumY ivchu KovY qau nwnk shij smwvY ]64] (945-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh ha-umai vichahu khovai ta-o naanak sahj samaavai. ||64||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v64	The Gurmukh eliminates egotism from within; then, O Nanak, the sun naturally enters into the home of the moon. ||64||
WHEN	para 41303	iehu mnu inhclu ihrdY vsIAly gurmuiK mUlu pCwix rhY ] (945-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ih man nihchal hirdai vasee-alay gurmukh mool pachhaan rahai. When the mind becomes steady and stable, it abides in the heart, and then the Gurmukh realizes the root, the source of all.
RECORD	para 41304	nwiB pvnu Gir Awsix bYsY gurmuiK Kojq qqu lhY ] (945-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naabh pavan ghar aasan baisai gurmukh khojat tat lahai. The breath is seated in the home of the navel; the Gurmukh searches, and finds the essence of reality.
RECORD	para 41305	su sbdu inrMqir inj Gir AwCY iqRBvx joiq su sbid lhY ] (945-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so sabad nirantar nij ghar aachhai taribhavan jot so sabad lahai. This Shabad permeates the nucleus of the self, deep within, in its own home; the Light of this Shabad pervades the three worlds.
REQUIRE	para 41306	KwvY dUK BUK swcy kI swcy hI iqRpqwis rhY ] (945-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) khaavai dookh bhookh saachay kee saachay hee tariptaas rahai. Hunger for the True Lord shall consume your pain, and through the True Lord, you shall be satisfied.
DEFINE	para 41307	Anhd bwxI gurmuiK jwxI ibrlo ko ArQwvY ] (945-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) anhad banee gurmukh jaanee birlo ko arthaavai. The Gurmukh knows the unstruck sound current of the Bani; how rare are those who understand.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v65	nwnku AwKY scu suBwKY sic rpY rMgu kbhU n jwvY ]65] (945-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak aakhai sach subhaakhai sach rapai rang kabhoo na jaavai. ||65||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v65	Says Nanak, one who speaks the Truth is dyed in the color of Truth, which will never fade away. ||65||
WHEN	para 41309	jw iehu ihrdw dyh n hoqI qau mnu kYTY rhqw ] (945-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jaa ih hirdaa dayh na hotee ta-o man kaithai rahtaa. "When this heart and body did not exist, where did the mind reside?
WHEN	para 41310	nwiB kml AsQMBu n hoqo qw pvnu kvn Gir shqw ] (945-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naabh kamal asthambh na hoto taa pavan kavan ghar sahtaa. When there was no support of the navel lotus, then in which home did the breath reside?
WHEN	para 41311	rUpu n hoqo ryK n kweI qw sbid khw ilv lweI ] (945-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) roop na hoto raykh na kaa-ee taa sabad kahaa liv laa-ee. When there was no form or shape, then how could anyone lovingly focus on the Shabad?
WHEN	para 41312	rkqu ibMdu kI mVI n hoqI imiq kImiq nhI pweI ] (945-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) rakat bind kee marhee na hotee mit keemat nahee paa-ee. When there was no dungeon formed from egg and sperm, who could measure the Lord's value and extent?
WHEN	para 41313	vrnu ByKu AsrUpu n jwpI ikau kir jwpis swcw ] (945-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) varan bhaykh asroop na jaapee ki-o kar jaapas saachaa. When color, dress and form could not be seen, how could the True Lord be known?"
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v66	nwnk nwim rqy bYrwgI ieb qb swco swcw ]66] (945-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak naam ratay bairaagee ib tab saacho saachaa. ||66||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v66	O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam, the Name of the Lord, are detached. Then and now, they see the Truest of the True. ||66||
WHEN	para 41315	ihrdw dyh n hoqI AauDU qau mnu suMin rhY bYrwgI ] (945-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hirdaa dayh na hotee a-oDhoo ta-o man sunn rahai bairaagee. When the heart and the body did not exist, O hermit, then the mind resided in the absolute, detached Lord.
WHEN	para 41316	nwiB kmlu AsQMBu n hoqo qw inj Gir bsqau pvnu AnrwgI ] (945-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naabh kamal asthambh na hoto taa nij ghar basta-o pavan anraagee. When there was no support of the lotus of the navel, the breath remained in its own home, attuned to the Lord's Love.
WHEN	para 41317	rUpu n ryiKAw jwiq n hoqI qau AkulIix rhqau sbdu su swru ] (945-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) roop na raykh-i-aa jaat na hotee ta-o akuleen rahta-o sabad so saar. When there was no form or shape or social class, then the Shabad, in its essence, resided in the unmanifest Lord.
WHEN	para 41318	gaunu ggnu jb qbih n hoqau iqRBvx joiq Awpy inrMkwru ] (945-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ga-un gagan jab tabeh na hota-o taribhavan jot aapay nirankaar. When the world and the sky did not even exist, the Light of the Formless Lord filled the three worlds.
RECORD	para 41320	vrnu ByKu AsrUpu su eyko eyko sbdu ivfwxI ] (946-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) varan bhaykh asroop so ayko ayko sabad vidaanee. Color, dress and form were contained in the One Lord; the Shabad was contained in the One, Wondrous Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v67	swc ibnw sUcw ko nwhI nwnk AkQ khwxI ]67] (946-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saach binaa soochaa ko naahee naanak akath kahaanee. ||67||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v67	Without the True Name, no one can become pure; O Nanak, this is the Unspoken Speech. ||67||
RECORD	para 41322	ikqu ikqu ibiD jgu aupjY purKw ikqu ikqu duiK ibnis jweI ] (946-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kit kit biDh jag upjai purkhaa kit kit dukh binas jaa-ee. "How, in what way, was the world formed, O man? And what disaster will end it?"
RECORD	para 41323	haumY ivic jgu aupjY purKw nwim ivsirAY duKu pweI ] (946-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ha-umai vich jag upjai purkhaa naam visri-ai dukh paa-ee. In egotism, the world was formed, O man; forgetting the Naam, it suffers and dies.
UPHOLD	para 41324	gurmuiK hovY su igAwnu qqu bIcwrY haumY sbid jlwey ] (946-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh hovai so gi-aan tat beechaarai ha-umai sabad jalaa-ay. One who becomes Gurmukh contemplates the essence of spiritual wisdom; through the Shabad, he burns away his egotism.
RECORD	para 41325	qnu mnu inrmlu inrml bwxI swcY rhY smwey ] (946-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tan man nirmal nirmal banee saachai rahai samaa-ay. His body and mind become immaculate, through the Immaculate Bani of the Word. He remains absorbed in Truth.
ALLOW	para 41326	nwmy nwim rhY bYrwgI swcu riKAw auir Dwry ] (946-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naamay naam rahai bairaagee saach rakhi-aa ur Dhaaray. Through the Naam, the Name of the Lord, he remains detached; he enshrines the True Name in his heart.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v68	nwnk ibnu nwvY jogu kdy n hovY dyKhu irdY bIcwry ]68] (946-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak bin naavai jog kaday na hovai daykhhu ridai beechaaray. ||68||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v68	O Nanak, without the Name, Yoga is never attained; reflect upon this in your heart, and see. ||68||
DEFINE	para 41328	gurmuiK swcu sbdu bIcwrY koie ] (946-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh saach sabad beechaarai ko-ay. The Gurmukh is one who reflects upon the True Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 41329	gurmuiK scu bwxI prgtu hoie ] (946-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh sach banee pargat ho-ay. The True Bani is revealed to the Gurmukh.
DEFINE	para 41330	gurmuiK mnu BIjY ivrlw bUJY koie ] (946-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh man bheejai virlaa boojhai ko-ay. The mind of the Gurmukh is drenched with the Lord's Love, but how rare are those who understand this.
RECORD	para 41331	gurmuiK inj Gir vwsw hoie ] (946-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh nij ghar vaasaa ho-ay. The Gurmukh dwells in the home of the self, deep within.
RECORD	para 41332	gurmuiK jogI jugiq pCwxY ] (946-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh jogee jugat pachhaanai. The Gurmukh realizes the Way of Yoga.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v69	gurmuiK nwnk eyko jwxY ]69] (946-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh naanak ayko jaanai. ||69||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v69	O Nanak, the Gurmukh knows the One Lord alone. ||69||
DEFINE	para 41334	ibnu siqgur syvy jogu n hoeI ] (946-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin satgur sayvay jog na ho-ee. Without serving the True Guru, Yoga is not attained;
DEFINE	para 41335	ibnu siqgur Byty mukiq n koeI ] (946-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin satgur bhaytay mukat na ko-ee. without meeting the True Guru, no one is liberated.
RECORD	para 41336	ibnu siqgur Byty nwmu pwieAw n jwie ] (946-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin satgur bhaytay naam paa-i-aa na jaa-ay. Without meeting the True Guru, the Naam cannot be found.
RECORD	para 41337	ibnu siqgur Byty mhw duKu pwie ] (946-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin satgur bhaytay mahaa dukh paa-ay. Without meeting the True Guru, one suffers in terrible pain.
DEFINE	para 41338	ibnu siqgur Byty mhw grib gubwir ] (946-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin satgur bhaytay mahaa garab gubaar. Without meeting the True Guru, there is only the deep darkness of egotistical pride.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v70	nwnk ibnu gur muAw jnmu hwir ]70] (946-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak bin gur mu-aa janam haar. ||70||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v70	O Nanak, without the True Guru, one dies, having lost the opportunity of this life. ||70||
RECORD	para 41340	gurmuiK mnu jIqw haumY mwir ] (946-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh man jeetaa ha-umai maar. The Gurmukh conquers his mind by subduing his ego.
RECORD	para 41341	gurmuiK swcu riKAw aur Dwir ] (946-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh saach rakhi-aa ur Dhaar. The Gurmukh enshrines Truth in his heart.
RECORD	para 41342	gurmuiK jgu jIqw jmkwlu mwir ibdwir ] (946-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh jag jeetaa jamkaal maar bidaar. The Gurmukh conquers the world; he knocks down the Messenger of Death, and kills it.
RECORD	para 41343	gurmuiK drgh n AwvY hwir ] (946-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh dargeh na aavai haar. The Gurmukh does not lose in the Court of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 41344	gurmuiK myil imlwey suo jwxY ] (946-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh mayl milaa-ay so jaanai. The Gurmukh is united in God's Union; he alone knows.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v71	nwnk gurmuiK sbid pCwxY ]71] (946-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh sabad pachhaanai. ||71||
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v71	O Nanak, the Gurmukh realizes the Word of the Shabad. ||71||
RECORD	para 41346	sbdY kw inbyVw suix qU AauDU ibnu nwvY jogu n hoeI ] (946-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabdai kaa nibayrhaa sun too a-oDhoo bin naavai jog na ho-ee. This is the essence of the Shabad - listen, you hermits and Yogis. Without the Name, there is no Yoga.
ALLOW	para 41347	nwmy rwqy Anidnu mwqy nwmY qy suKu hoeI ] (946-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naamay raatay an-din maatay naamai tay sukh ho-ee. Those who are attuned to the Name, remain intoxicated night and day; through the Name, they find peace.
ALLOW	para 41348	nwmY hI qy sBu prgtu hovY nwmy soJI pweI ] (946-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naamai hee tay sabh pargat hovai naamay sojhee paa-ee. Through the Name, everything is revealed; through the Name, understanding is obtained.
RECORD	para 41349	ibnu nwvY ByK krih bhuqyry scY Awip KuAweI ] (946-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bin naavai bhaykh karahi bahutayray sachai aap khu-aa-ee. Without the Name, people wear all sorts of religious robes; the True Lord Himself has confused them.
DEFINE	para 41350	siqgur qy nwmu pweIAY AauDU jog jugiq qw hoeI ] (946-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satgur tay naam paa-ee-ai a-oDhoo jog jugat taa ho-ee. The Name is obtained only from the True Guru, O hermit, and then, the Way of Yoga is found.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v72	kir bIcwru min dyKhu nwnk ibnu nwvY mukiq n hoeI ]72] (946-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kar beechaar man daykhhu naanak bin naavai mukat na ho-ee. ||72||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v72	Reflect upon this in your mind, and see; O Nanak, without the Name, there is no liberation. ||72||
RECORD	para 41352	qyrI giq imiq qUhY jwxih ikAw ko AwiK vKwxY ] (946-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tayree gat mit toohai jaaneh ki-aa ko aakh vakhaanai. You alone know Your state and extent, Lord; What can anyone say about it?
DEFINE	para 41353	qU Awpy gupqw Awpy prgtu Awpy siB rMg mwxY ] (946-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) too aapay guptaa aapay pargat aapay sabh rang maanai. You Yourself are hidden, and You Yourself are revealed. You Yourself enjoy all pleasures.
RECORD	para 41354	swiDk isD gurU bhu cyly Kojq iPrih PurmwxY ] (946-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saaDhik siDh guroo baho chaylay khojat fireh furmaanai. The seekers, the Siddhas, the many gurus and disciples wander around searching for You, according to Your Will.
UPHOLD	para 41355	mwgih nwmu pwie ieh iBiKAw qyry drsn kau kurbwxY ] (946-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) maageh naam paa-ay ih bhikhi-aa tayray darsan ka-o kurbaanai. They beg for Your Name, and You bless them with this charity. I am a sacrifice to the Blessed Vision of Your Darshan.
RECORD	para 41356	AibnwsI pRiB Kylu rcwieAw gurmuiK soJI hoeI ] (946-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) abhinaasee parabh khayl rachaa-i-aa gurmukh sojhee ho-ee. The eternal imperishable Lord God has staged this play; the Gurmukh understands it.
RECORD	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v73	nwnk siB jug Awpy vrqY dUjw Avru n koeI ]73]1] (946-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak sabh jug aapay vartai doojaa avar na ko-ee. ||73||
DEFINE	rwmklI mhlw 1 isD gosit v73	1|| O Nanak, He extends Himself throughout the ages; there is no other than Him. ||73||1||
