DEFINE	para 41365	haumY eyho bIju hY shsw gieAw ivlwie ] (947-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ha-umai ayho beej hai sahsaa ga-i-aa vilaa-ay. But this egotism is the seed of skepticism; it has been uprooted.
DEFINE	para 41366	nw ikCu bIjy n augvY jo bKsy so Kwie ] (947-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naa kichh beejay na ugvai jo bakhsay so khaa-ay. It is not planted there, and it does not sprout; whatever God grants us, we eat.
WHEN	para 41367	AMBY syqI AMBu rilAw bhuiV n inkisAw jwie ] (947-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ambhai saytee ambh rali-aa bahurh na niksi-aa jaa-ay. When water mixes with water, it cannot be separated again.
DEFINE	para 41368	nwnk gurmuiK clqu hY vyKhu lokw Awie ] (947-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh chalat hai vaykhhu lokaa aa-ay. O Nanak, the Gurmukh is wonderful; come, poeple, and see!
RECORD	para 41369	loku ik vyKY bpuVw ijs no soJI nwih ] (947-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) lok ke vaykhai bapurhaa jis no sojhee naahi. But what can the poor people see? They do not understand.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	ijsu vyKwly so vyKY ijsu visAw mn mwih ]1] (947-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jis vaykhaalay so vaykhai jis vasi-aa man maahi. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	He alone sees, whom the Lord causes to see; the Lord comes to dwell in his mind. ||1||
RECORD	para 41371	mÚ 3 ] (947-6) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41372	mnmuKu duK kw Kyqu hY duKu bIjy duKu Kwie ] (947-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) manmukh dukh kaa khayt hai dukh beejay dukh khaa-ay. The self-willed manmukh is the field of sorrow and suffering. He plains sorrow, and eats sorrow.
DEFINE	para 41373	duK ivic jMmY duiK mrY haumY krq ivhwie ] (947-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) dukh vich jammai dukh marai ha-umai karat vihaa-ay. In sorrow he is born, and in sorrow he dies. Acting in egotism, his life passes away.
RECORD	para 41374	Awvxu jwxu n suJeI AMDw AMDu kmwie ] (947-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aavan jaan na sujh-ee anDhaa anDh kamaa-ay. He does not understand the coming and going of reincarnation; the blind man acts in blindness.
DEFINE	para 41375	jo dyvY iqsY n jwxeI idqy kau lptwie ] (947-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jo dayvai tisai na jaan-ee ditay ka-o laptaa-ay. He does not know the One who gives, but he is attached to what is given.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk pUrib iliKAw kmwvxw Avru n krxw jwie ]2] (947-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak poorab likhi-aa kamaavanaa avar na karnaa jaa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, he acts according to his pre-ordained destiny. He cannot do anything else. ||2||
RECORD	para 41377	mÚ 3 ] (947-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41378	siqguir imilAY sdw suKu ijs no Awpy myly soie ] (947-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satgur mili-ai sadaa sukh jis no aapay maylay so-ay. Meeting the True Guru, everlasting peace is obtained. He Himself leads us to meet Him.
DEFINE	para 41379	suKY eyhu ibbyku hY AMqru inrmlu hoie ] (947-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sukhai ayhu bibayk hai antar nirmal ho-ay. This is the true meaning of peace, that one becomes immaculate within oneself.
DEFINE	para 41380	AigAwn kw BRmu ktIAY igAwnu prwpiq hoie ] (947-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) agi-aan kaa bharam katee-ai gi-aan paraapat ho-ay. The doubt of ignorance is eradicated, and spiritual wisdom is obtained.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	nwnk eyko ndrI AwieAw jh dyKw qh soie ]3] (947-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak ayko nadree aa-i-aa jah daykhaa tah so-ay. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	Nanak comes to gaze upon the One Lord alone; wherever he looks, there He is. ||3||
RECORD	para 41382	pauVI ] (947-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 41383	scY qKqu rcwieAw bYsx kau jWeI ] (947-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sachai takhat rachaa-i-aa baisan ka-o jaa N-ee. The True Lord created His throne, upon which He sits.
DEFINE	para 41384	sBu ikCu Awpy Awip hY gur sbid suxweI ] (947-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabh kichh aapay aap hai gur sabad sunaa-ee. He Himself is everything; this is what the Word of the Guru's Shabad says.
RECORD	para 41385	Awpy kudriq swjIAnu kir mhl srweI ] (947-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay kudrat saajee-an kar mahal saraa-ee. Through His almighty creative power, He created and fashioned the mansions and hotels.
RECORD	para 41386	cMdu sUrju duie cwnxy pUrI bxq bxweI ] (947-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) chand sooraj du-ay chaannay pooree banat banaa-ee. He made the two lamps, the sun and the moon; He formed the perfect form.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	Awpy vyKY suxy Awip gur sbid iDAweI ]1] (947-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay vaykhai sunay aap gur sabad Dhi-aa-ee. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	He Himself sees, and He Himself hears; meditate on the Word of the Guru's Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	vwhu vwhu scy pwiqswh qU scI nweI ]1] rhwau ] (947-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) vaahu vaahu sachay paatisaah too sachee naa-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	rahaa-o. Waaho! Waaho! Hail, hail, O True King! True is Your Name. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 41389	sloku ] (947-13) salok. Shalok:
RECORD	para 41390	kbIr mihdI kir kY GwilAw Awpu pIswie pIswie ] (947-13, rwmklI, kbIr) kabeer mahidee kar kai ghaali-aa aap peesaa-ay peesaa-ay. Kabeer, I have ground myself into henna paste.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	qY sh bwq n puCIAw kbhU n lweI pwie ]1] (947-14, rwmklI, kbIr) tai sah baat na puchhee-aa kabhoo na laa-ee paa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O my Husband Lord, You took no notice of me; You never applied me to Your feet. ||1||
RECORD	para 41392	mÚ 3 ] (947-14) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
