RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, such a man of disciplined meditation attains liberation. ||1||
RECORD	para 41447	mÚ 3 ] (948-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41448	so qpw ij iehu qpu Gwly ] (948-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) so tapaa je ih tap ghaalay. He alone is a man of disciplined meditation, who practices this self-discipline.
RECORD	para 41449	siqgur no imlY sbdu smwly ] (948-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satgur no milai sabad samaalay. Meeting with the True Guru, he contemplates the Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 41450	siqgur kI syvw iehu qpu prvwxu ] (948-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satgur kee sayvaa ih tap parvaan. Serving the True Guru - this is the only acceptable disciplined meditation.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk so qpw drgih pwvY mwxu ]2] (948-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak so tapaa dargahi paavai maan. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, such a man of disciplined meditation is honored in the Court of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 41452	pauVI ] (948-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 41453	rwiq idnsu aupwieAnu sMswr kI vrqix ] (948-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) raat dinas upaa-i-an sansaar kee vartan. He created the night and the day, for the activities of the world.
DEFINE	para 41455	gurmqI Git cwnxw Awnyru ibnwsix ] (949-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gurmatee ghat chaannaa aanayr binaasan. Following the Guru's Teachings, one's heart is illumined, and the darkness is dispelled.
ALLOW	para 41456	hukmy hI sB swjIAnu rivAw sB vix iqRix ] (949-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) hukmay hee sabh saajee-an ravi-aa sabh van tarin. By the Hukam of His Command, He creates everything; He pervades and permeates all the woods and meadows.
DEFINE	para 41457	sBu ikCu Awpy Awip hY gurmuiK sdw hir Bix ] (949-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabh kichh aapay aap hai gurmukh sadaa har bhan. He Himself is everything; the Gurmukh constantly chants the Lord's Name.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v5	sbdy hI soJI peI scY Awip buJweI ]5] (949-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabday hee sojhee pa-ee sachai aap bujhaa-ee. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v5	Through the Shabad, understanding comes; the True Lord Himself inspires us to understand. ||5||
RECORD	para 41459	slok mÚ 3 ] (949-3) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41460	AiBAwgq eyih n AwKIAin ijn ky icq mih Brmu ] (949-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) abhi-aagat ayhi na aakhee-an jin kay chit meh bharam. He is not called a renunciate, whose consciousness is filled with doubt.
RECORD	para 41461	iqs dY idqY nwnkw qyho jyhw Drmu ] (949-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tis dai ditai naankaa tayho jayhaa Dharam. Donations to him bring proportionate rewards.
RECORD	para 41462	ABY inrMjnu prm pdu qw kw BUKw hoie ] (949-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) abhai niranjan param pad taa kaa bhookhaa ho-ay. He hungers for the supreme status of the Fearless, Immaculate Lord;
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	iqs kw Bojnu nwnkw ivrlw pwey koie ]1] (949-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tis kaa bhojan naankaa virlaa paa-ay ko-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, how rare are those who offer him this food. ||1||
RECORD	para 41464	mÚ 3 ] (949-5) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41465	AiBAwgq eyih n AwKIAin ij pr Gir Bojnu kryin ] (949-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) abhi-aagat ayhi na aakhee-an je par ghar bhojan karayn. They are not called renunciates, who take food in the homes of others.
RECORD	para 41466	audrY kwrix Awpxy bhly ByiK kryin ] (949-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) udrai kaaran aapnay bahlay bhaykh karayn. For the sake of their bellies, they wear various religious robes.
DEFINE	para 41467	AiBAwgq syeI nwnkw ij Awqm gauxu kryin ] (949-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) abhi-aagat say-ee naankaa je aatam ga-on karayn. They alone are renunciates, O Nanak, who enter into their own souls.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	Bwil lhin shu Awpxw inj Gir rhxu kryin ]2] (949-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bhaal lahan saho aapnaa nij ghar rahan karayn. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	They seek and find their Husband Lord; they dwell within the home of their own inner self. ||2||
RECORD	para 41469	pauVI ] (949-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41470	AMbru Driq ivCoiVAnu ivic scw Asrwau ] (949-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ambar Dharat vichhorhi-an vich sachaa asraa-o. They sky and the earth are separate, but the True Lord supports them from within.
DEFINE	para 41471	Gru dru sBo scu hY ijsu ivic scw nwau ] (949-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ghar dar sabho sach hai jis vich sachaa naa-o. True are all those homes and gates, within which the True Name is enshrined.
DEFINE	para 41472	sBu scw hukmu vrqdw gurmuiK sic smwau ] (949-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabh sachaa hukam varatdaa gurmukh sach samaa-o. The Hukam of the True Lord's Command is effective everywhere. The Gurmukh merges in the True Lord.
DEFINE	para 41473	scw Awip qKqu scw bih scw kry inAwau ] (949-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sachaa aap takhat sachaa bahi sachaa karay ni-aa-o. He Himself is True, and True is His throne. Seated upon it, He administers true justice.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v6	sBu sco scu vrqdw gurmuiK AlKu lKweI ]6] (949-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabh sacho sach varatdaa gurmukh alakh lakhaa-ee. ||6||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v6	The Truest of the True is all-pervading everywhere; the Gurmukh sees the unseen. ||6||
RECORD	para 41475	sloku mÚ 3 ] (949-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 41476	rYxwier mwih Anµqu hY kUVI AwvY jwie ] (949-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) rainaa-ir maahi anant hai koorhee aavai jaa-ay. In the world-ocean, the Infinite Lord abides. The false come and go in reincarnation.
RECORD	para 41477	BwxY clY AwpxY bhuqI lhY sjwie ] (949-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bhaanai chalai aapnai bahutee lahai sajaa-ay. One who walks according to his own will, suffers terrible punishment.
DEFINE	para 41478	rYxwier mih sBu ikCu hY krmI plY pwie ] (949-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) rainaa-ir meh sabh kichh hai karmee palai paa-ay. All things are in the world-ocean, but they are obtained only by the karma of good actions.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk nau iniD pweIAY jy clY iqsY rjwie ]1] (949-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak na-o niDh paa-ee-ai jay chalai tisai rajaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, he alone obtains the nine treasures, who walks in the Will of the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 41480	mÚ 3 ] (949-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 41481	shjy siqguru n syivE ivic haumY jnim ibnwsu ] (949-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sehjay satgur na sayvi-o vich ha-umai janam binaas. One who intuitively serves the True Guru, loses his life in egotism.
RECORD	para 41482	rsnw hir rsu n ciKE kmlu n hoieE prgwsu ] (949-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) rasnaa har ras na chakhi-o kamal na ho-i-o pargaas. His tongue does not taste the sublime essence of the Lord, and his heart-lotus does not blossom forth.
DEFINE	para 41483	ibKu KwDI mnmuKu muAw mwieAw moih ivxwsu ] (949-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bikh khaaDhee manmukh mu-aa maa-i-aa mohi vinaas. The self-willed manmukh eats poison and dies; he is ruined by love and attachment to Maya.
DEFINE	para 41484	ieksu hir ky nwm ivxu iDRgu jIvxu iDRgu vwsu ] (949-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ikas har kay naam vin Dharig jeevan Dharig vaas. Without the Name of the One Lord, his life is cursed, and his home is cursed as well.
WHEN	para 41485	jw Awpy ndir kry pRBu scw qw hovY dwsin dwsu ] (949-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jaa aapay nadar karay parabh sachaa taa hovai daasan daas. When God Himself bestows His Glance of Grace, then one becomes the slave of His slaves.
RECORD	para 41486	qw Anidnu syvw kry siqgurU kI kbih n CofY pwsu ] (949-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) taa an-din sayvaa karay satguroo kee kabeh na chhodai paas. And then, night and day, he serves the True Guru, and never leaves His side.
RECORD	para 41487	ijau jl mih kmlu Ailpqo vrqY iqau ivcy igrh audwsu ] (949-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ji-o jal meh kamal alipato vartai ti-o vichay girah udaas. As the lotus flower floats unaffected in the water, so does he remain detached in his own household.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	jn nwnk kry krwieAw sBu ko ijau BwvY iqv hir guxqwsu ]2] (949-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jan naanak karay karaa-i-aa sabh ko ji-o bhaavai tiv har guntaas. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O servant Nanak, the Lord acts, and inspires everyone to act, according to the Pleasure of His Will. He is the treasure of virtue. ||2||
RECORD	para 41489	pauVI ] (949-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 41490	CqIh jug gubwru sw Awpy gxq kInI ] (949-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) chhateeh jug gubaar saa aapay ganat keenee. For thirty-six ages, there was utter darkness. Then, the Lord revealed Himself.
UPHOLD	para 41491	Awpy isRsit sB swjIAnu Awip miq dInI ] (949-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aapay sarisat sabh saajee-an aap mat deenee. He Himself created the entire universe. He Himself blessed it with understanding.
RECORD	para 41492	isimRiq swsq swijAnu pwp puMn gxq gxInI ] (949-17, rwmklI, mÚ 3) simrit saasat saaji-an paap punn ganat ganeenee. He created the Simritees and the Shaastras; He calculates the accounts of virtue and vice.
RECORD	para 41493	ijsu buJwey so buJsI scY sbid pqInI ] (949-17, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jis bujhaa-ay so bujhsee sachai sabad pateenee. He alone understands, whom the Lord inspires to understand and to be pleased with the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v7	sBu Awpy Awip vrqdw Awpy bKis imlweI ]7] (949-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabh aapay aap varatdaa aapay bakhas milaa-ee. ||7||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v7	He Himself is all-pervading; He Himself forgives, and unites with Himself. ||7||
RECORD	para 41495	slok mÚ 3 ] (949-18) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41496	iehu qnu sBo rqu hY rqu ibnu qMnu n hoie ] (949-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ih tan sabho rat hai rat bin tann na ho-ay. This body is all blood; without blood, the body cannot exist.
DEFINE	para 41497	jo sih rqy AwpxY iqn qin loB rqu n hoie ] (949-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jo seh ratay aapnai tin tan lobh rat na ho-ay. Those who are attuned to their Lord - their bodies are not filled with the blood of greed.
RECORD	para 41498	BY pieAY qnu KIxu hoie loB rqu ivchu jwie ] (949-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bhai pa-i-ai tan kheen ho-ay lobh rat vichahu jaa-ay. In the Fear of God, the body becomes thin, and the blood of greed passes out of the body.
RECORD	para 41500	ijau bYsMqir Dwqu suDu hoie iqau hir kw Bau durmiq mYlu gvwie ] (950-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ji-o baisantar Dhaat suDh ho-ay ti-o har kaa bha-o durmat mail gavaa-ay. As fire purifies metal, so does the Fear of the Lord eradicate the filth of evil- mindedness.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk qy jn sohxy jo rqy hir rMgu lwie ]1] (950-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak tay jan sohnay jo ratay har rang laa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, beautiful are those humble beings, who are imbued with the Lord's Love. ||1||
RECORD	para 41502	mÚ 3 ] (950-2) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 41503	rwmklI rwmu min visAw qw binAw sIgwru ] (950-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) raamkalee raam man vasi-aa taa bani-aa seegaar. In Raamkalee, I have enshrined the Lord in my mind; thus I have been embellished.
UPHOLD	para 41504	gur kY sbid kmlu ibgisAw qw sauipAw Bgiq BMfwru ] (950-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad kamal bigsi-aa taa sa-upi-aa bhagat bhandaar. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, my heart-lotus has blossomed forth; the Lord blessed me with the treasure of devotional worship.
RECORD	para 41505	Brmu gieAw qw jwigAw cUkw AigAwn AMDwru ] (950-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bharam ga-i-aa taa jaagi-aa chookaa agi-aan anDhaar. My doubt was dispelled, and I woke up; the darkness of ignorance was dispelled.
DEFINE	para 41506	iqs no rUpu Aiq Aglw ijsu hir nwil ipAwru ] (950-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tis no roop at aglaa jis har naal pi-aar. She who is in love with her Lord, is the most infinitely beautiful.
RECORD	para 41507	sdw rvY ipru Awpxw soBwvMqI nwir ] (950-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sadaa ravai pir aapnaa sobhaavantee naar. Such a beautiful, happy soul-bride enjoys her Husband Lord forever.
RECORD	para 41508	mnmuiK sIgwru n jwxnI jwsin jnmu sBu hwir ] (950-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) manmukh seegaar na jaannee jaasan janam sabh haar. The self-willed manmukhs do not know how to decorate themselves; wasting their whole lives, they depart.
RECORD	para 41509	ibnu hir BgqI sIgwru krih inq jMmih hoie KuAwru ] (950-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bin har bhagtee seegaar karahi nit jameh ho-ay khu-aar. Those who decorate themselves without devotional worship to the Lord, are continually reincarnated to suffer.
RECORD	para 41510	sYswrY ivic soB n pwienI AgY ij kry su jwxY krqwru ] (950-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) saisaarai vich sobh na paa-inee agai je karay so jaanai kartaar. They do not obtain respect in this world; the Creator Lord alone knows what will happen to them in the world hereafter.
DEFINE	para 41511	nwnk scw eyku hY duhu ivic hY sMswru ] (950-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak sachaa ayk hai duhu vich hai sansaar. O Nanak, the True Lord is the One and only; duality exists only in the world.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	cMgY mMdY Awip lwieAnu so krin ij Awip krwey krqwru ]2] (950-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) changai mandai aap laa-i-an so karan je aap karaa-ay kartaar. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	He Himself enjoins them to good and bad; they do only that which the Creator Lord causes them to do. ||2||
RECORD	para 41513	mÚ 3 ] (950-7) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 41514	ibnu siqgur syvy sWiq n AwveI dUjI nwhI jwie ] (950-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay saa Nt na aavee doojee naahee jaa-ay. Without serving the True Guru, tranquility is not obtained. It cannot be found anywhere else.
ALLOW	para 41515	jy bhuqyrw locIAY ivxu krmw pwieAw n jwie ] (950-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jay bahutayraa lochee-ai vin karmaa paa-i-aa na jaa-ay. No matter how much one may long for it, without the karma of good actions, it cannot be found.
DEFINE	para 41516	AMqir loBu ivkwru hY dUjY Bwie KuAwie ] (950-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) antar lobh vikaar hai doojai bhaa-ay khu-aa-ay. Those whose inner beings are filled with greed and corruption, are ruined through the love of duality.
DEFINE	para 41517	iqn jMmxu mrxu n cukeI haumY ivic duKu pwie ] (950-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tin jaman maran na chuk-ee ha-umai vich dukh paa-ay. The cycle of birth and death is not ended, and filled with egotism, they suffer in pain.
RECORD	para 41518	ijnI siqgur isau icqu lwieAw so KwlI koeI nwih ] (950-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jinee satgur si-o chit laa-i-aa so khaalee ko-ee naahi. Those who focus their consciousness on the True Guru, do not remain unfulfilled.
DEFINE	para 41519	iqn jm kI qlb n hoveI nw Eie duK shwih ] (950-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tin jam kee talab na hova-ee naa o-ay dukh sahaahi. They are not summoned by the Messenger of Death, and they do not suffer in pain.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	nwnk gurmuiK aubry scY sbid smwih ]3] (950-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh ubray sachai sabad samaahi. ||3||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	O Nanak, the Gurmukh is saved, merging in the True Word of the Shabad. ||3||
RECORD	para 41521	pauVI ] (950-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 41522	Awip Ailpqu sdw rhY hoir DMDY siB Dwvih ] (950-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aap alipat sadaa rahai hor DhanDhai sabh Dhaaveh. He Himself remains unattached forever; all others run after worldly affairs.
DEFINE	para 41523	Awip inhclu Aclu hY hoir Awvih jwvih ] (950-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aap nihchal achal hai hor aavahi jaaveh. He Himself is eternal, unchanging and unmoving; the others continue coming and going in reincarnation.
RECORD	para 41524	sdw sdw hir iDAweIAY gurmuiK suKu pwvih ] (950-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa har Dhi-aa-ee-ai gurmukh sukh paavahi. Meditating on the Lord forever and ever, the Gurmukh finds peace.
RECORD	para 41525	inj Gir vwsw pweIAY sic isPiq smwvih ] (950-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) nij ghar vaasaa paa-ee-ai sach sifat samaaveh. He dwells in the home of his own inner being, absorbed in the Praise of the True Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v8	scw gihr gMBIru hY gur sbid buJweI ]8] (950-13, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sachaa gahir gambheer hai gur sabad bujhaa-ee. ||8||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v8	The True Lord is profound and unfathomable; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, He is understood. ||8||
RECORD	para 41527	slok mÚ 3 ] (950-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41528	scw nwmu iDAwie qU sBo vrqY scu ] (950-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sachaa naam Dhi-aa-ay too sabho vartai sach. Meditate on the True Name; the True Lord is all-pervading.
RECORD	para 41529	nwnk hukmY jo buJY so Plu pwey scu ] (950-14, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak hukmai jo bujhai so fal paa-ay sach. O Nanak, one who realizes the Hukam of the Lord's Command, obtains the fruit of Truth.
RECORD	para 41530	kQnI bdnI krqw iPrY hukmu n bUJY scu ] (950-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) kathnee badnee kartaa firai hukam na boojhai sach. One who merely mouths the words, does not understand the Hukam of the True Lord's Command.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk hir kw Bwxw mMny so Bgqu hoie ivxu mMny kcu inkcu ]1] (950-15, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak har kaa bhaanaa mannay so bhagat ho-ay vin mannay kach nikach. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, one who accepts the Will of the Lord is His devotee. Without accepting it, he is the falsest of the false. ||1||
RECORD	para 41532	mÚ 3 ] (950-16) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 41533	mnmuK boil n jwxnI Enw AMdir kwmu k®oDu AhMkwru ] (950-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) manmukh bol na jaannee onaa andar kaam kroDh aha Nkaar. The self-willed manmukhs do not know what they are saying. They are filled with sexual desire, anger and egotism.
RECORD	para 41534	Eie Qwau kuQwau n jwxnI aun AMqir loBu ivkwru ] (950-16, rwmklI, mÚ 3) o-ay thaa-o kuthaa-o na jaannee un antar lobh vikaar. They do not understand right places and wrong places; they are filled with greed and corruption.
RECORD	para 41535	Eie AwpxY suAwie Awie bih glw krih Enw mwry jmu jMdwru ] (950-17, rwmklI, mÚ 3) o-ay aapnai su-aa-ay aa-ay bahi galaa karahi onaa maaray jam jandaar. They come, and sit and talk for their own purposes. The Messenger of Death strikes them down.
RECORD	para 41536	AgY drgh lyKY mMigAY mwir KuAwru kIcih kUiVAwr ] (950-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) agai dargeh laykhai mangi-ai maar khu-aar keecheh koorhi-aar. Hereafter, they are called to account in the Court of the Lord; the false ones are struck down and humiliated.
RECORD	para 41537	eyh kUVY kI mlu ikau auqrY koeI kFhu iehu vIcwru ] (950-18, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ayh koorhai kee mal ki-o utrai ko-ee kadhahu ih veechaar. How can this filth of falsehood be washed off? Can anyone think about this, and find the way?
WHEN	para 41538	siqguru imlY qw nwmu idVwey siB iklivK ktxhwru ] (950-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) satgur milai taa naam dirhaa-ay sabh kilvikh katanhaar. If one meets with the True Guru, He implants the Naam, the Name of the Lord within; all his sins are destroyed.
RECORD	para 41539	nwmu jpy nwmo AwrwDy iqsu jn kau krhu siB nmskwru ] (950-19, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naam japay naamo aaraaDhay tis jan ka-o karahu sabh namaskaar. Let all bow in humility to that humble being who chants the Naam, and worships the Naam in adoration.
RECORD	para 41541	mlu kUVI nwim auqwrIAnu jip nwmu hoAw sicAwru ] (951-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) mal koorhee naam utaaree-an jap naam ho-aa sachiaar. The Naam washes off the filth of falsehood; chanting the Naam, one becomes truthful.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	jn nwnk ijs dy eyih clq hih so jIvau dyvxhwru ]2] (951-1, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jan naanak jis day ayhi chalat heh so jeeva-o dayvanhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O servant Nanak, wondrous are the plays of the Lord, the Giver of life. ||2||
RECORD	para 41543	pauVI ] (951-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41544	quDu jyvfu dwqw nwih iksu AwiK suxweIAY ] (951-2, rwmklI, mÚ 3) tuDh jayvad daataa naahi kis aakh sunaa-ee-ai. You are the Great Giver; no other is as great as You. Unto whom should I speak and talk?
RECORD	para 41545	gur prswdI pwie ijQhu haumY jweIAY ] (951-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee paa-ay jithahu ha-umai jaa-ee-ai. By Guru's Grace, I find You; You eradicate egotism from within.
DEFINE	para 41546	rs ks swdw bwhrw scI vifAweIAY ] (951-3, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ras kas saadaa baahraa sachee vadi-aa-ee-ai. You are beyond sweet and salty flavors; True is Your glorious greatness.
RECORD	para 41547	ijs no bKsy iqsu dyie Awip ley imlweIAY ] (951-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jis no bakhsay tis day-ay aap la-ay milaa-ee-ai. You bless those whom You forgive, and unite them with Yourself.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v9	Gt AMqir AMimRqu riKEnu gurmuiK iksY ipAweI ]9] (951-4, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ghat antar amrit rakhi-on gurmukh kisai pi-aa-ee. ||9||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v9	You have placed the Ambrosial Nectar deep within the heart; the Gurmukh drinks it in. ||9||
RECORD	para 41549	slok mÚ 3 ] (951-5) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 41550	bwbwxIAw khwxIAw puq spuq kryin ] (951-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) baabaanee-aa kahaanee-aa put saput karayn. The stories of one's ancestors make the children good children.
DEFINE	para 41551	ij siqgur BwvY su mMin lYin syeI krm kryin ] (951-5, rwmklI, mÚ 3) je satgur bhaavai so man lain say-ee karam karayn. They accept what is pleasing to the Will of the True Guru, and act accordingly.
RECORD	para 41552	jwie puChu isimRiq swsq ibAws suk nwrd bcn sB isRsit kryin ] (951-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jaa-ay puchhahu simrit saasat bi-aas suk naarad bachan sabh sarisat karayn. Go and consult the Simritees, the Shaastras, the writings of Vyaas, Suk Dayv, Naarad, and all those who preach to the world.
DEFINE	para 41553	scY lwey sic lgy sdw scu smwlyin ] (951-6, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sachai laa-ay sach lagay sadaa sach samaalayn. Those, whom the True Lord attaches, are attached to the Truth; they contemplate the True Name forever.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk Awey sy prvwxu Bey ij sgly kul qwryin ]1] (951-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak aa-ay say parvaan bha-ay je saglay kul taarayn. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, their coming into the world is approved; they redeem all their ancestors. ||1||
RECORD	para 41555	mÚ 3 ] (951-7) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41556	gurU ijnw kw AMDulw isK BI AMDy krm kryin ] (951-7, rwmklI, mÚ 3) guroo jinaa kaa anDhulaa sikh bhee anDhay karam karayn. The disciples whose teacher is blind, act blindly as well.
RECORD	para 41557	Eie BwxY clin AwpxY inq JUTo JUTu bolyin ] (951-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) o-ay bhaanai chalan aapnai nit jhootho jhooth bolayn. They walk according to their own wills, and continually speak falsehood and lies.
RECORD	para 41558	kUVu kusqu kmwvdy pr inMdw sdw kryin ] (951-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) koorh kusat kamaavday par nindaa sadaa karayn. They practice falsehood and deception, and endlessly slander others.
RECORD	para 41559	Eie Awip fuby pr inMdkw sgly kul fobyin ] (951-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) o-ay aap dubay par nindkaa saglay kul dobayn. Slandering others, they drown themselves, and drown all their generations as well.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk ijqu Eie lwey iqqu lgy auie bpuVy ikAw kryin ]2] (951-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak jit o-ay laa-ay tit lagay u-ay bapurhay ki-aa karayn. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, whatever the Lord links them to, to that they are linked; what can the poor creatures do? ||2||
RECORD	para 41561	pauVI ] (951-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 41562	sB ndrI AMdir rKdw jyqI issit sB kIqI ] (951-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) sabh nadree andar rakh-daa jaytee sisat sabh keetee. He keeps all under His Gaze; He created the entire Universe.
RECORD	para 41563	ieik kUiV kusiq lwieAnu mnmuK ivgUqI ] (951-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ik koorh kusat laa-i-an manmukh vigootee. He has linked some to falsehood and deception; these self-willed manmukhs are plundered.
DEFINE	para 41564	gurmuiK sdw iDAweIAY AMdir hir pRIqI ] (951-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gurmukh sadaa Dhi-aa-ee-ai andar har pareetee. The Gurmukhs meditate on the Lord forever; their inner beings are filled with love.
RECORD	para 41565	ijn kau poqY puMnu hY iqn@ vwiq ispIqI ] (951-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) jin ka-o potai punn hai tin H vaat sipeetee. Those who have the treasure of virtue, chant the Praises of the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v10	nwnk nwmu iDAweIAY scu isPiq snweI ]10] (951-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai sach sifat sanaa-ee. ||10||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v10	O Nanak, meditate on the Naam, and the Glorious Praises of the True Lord. ||10||
RECORD	para 41567	sloku mÚ 1 ] (951-13) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41568	sqI pwpu kir squ kmwih ] (951-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) satee paap kar sat kamaahi. Men of charity gather wealth by committing sins, and then give it away in donations to charity.
RECORD	para 41569	gur dIiKAw Gir dyvx jwih ] (951-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur deekhi-aa ghar dayvan jaahi. Their spiritual teachers go to their homes to instruct them.
RECORD	para 41570	iesqrI purKY KitAY Bwau ] (951-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) istaree purkhai khati-ai bhaa-o. The woman loves the man only for his wealth;
RECORD	para 41571	BwvY Awvau BwvY jwau ] (951-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bhaavai aava-o bhaavai jaa-o. they come and go as they please.
RECORD	para 41572	swsqu bydu n mwnY koie ] (951-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saasat bayd na maanai ko-ay. No one obeys the Shaastras or the Vedas.
RECORD	para 41573	Awpo AwpY pUjw hoie ] (951-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapo aapai poojaa ho-ay. Everyone worships himself.
RECORD	para 41574	kwjI hoie kY bhY inAwie ] (951-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaajee ho-ay kai bahai ni-aa-ay. Becoming judges, they sit and administer justice.
RECORD	para 41575	Pyry qsbI kry Kudwie ] (951-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) fayray tasbee karay khudaa-ay. They chant on their malas, and call upon God.
RECORD	para 41576	vFI lY kY hku gvwey ] (951-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) vadhee lai kai hak gavaa-ay. They accept bribes, and block justice.
WHEN	para 41577	jy ko puCY qw piV suxwey ] (951-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jay ko puchhai taa parh sunaa-ay. If someone asks them, they read quotations from their books.
DEFINE	para 41578	qurk mMqRü kin irdY smwih ] (951-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) turak mantar kan ridai samaahi. The Muslim scriptures are in their ears and in their hearts.
RECORD	para 41579	lok muhwvih cwVI Kwih ] (951-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) lok muhaaveh chaarhee khaahi. They plunder the people, and engage in gossip and flattery.
RECORD	para 41580	caukw dy kY sucw hoie ] (951-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) cha-ukaa day kai suchaa ho-ay. They anoint their kitchens to try to become pure.
DEFINE	para 41581	AYsw ihMdU vyKhu koie ] (951-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aisaa hindoo vaykhhu ko-ay. Behold, such is the Hindu.
RECORD	para 41582	jogI igrhI jtw ibBUq ] (951-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jogee girhee jataa bibhoot. The Yogi, with matted hair and ashes on his body, has become a householder.
RECORD	para 41583	AwgY pwCY rovih pUq ] (951-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aagai paachhai roveh poot. The children weep in front of him and behind him.
RECORD	para 41584	jogu n pwieAw jugiq gvweI ] (951-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jog na paa-i-aa jugat gavaa-ee. He does not attain Yoga - he has lost his way.
RECORD	para 41585	ikqu kwrix isir CweI pweI ] (951-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kit kaaran sir chhaa-ee paa-ee. Why does he apply ashes to his forehead?
DEFINE	para 41586	nwnk kil kw eyhu prvwxu ] (951-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak kal kaa ayhu parvaan. O Nanak, this is the sign of the Dark Age of Kali Yuga;
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	Awpy AwKxu Awpy jwxu ]1] (951-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay aakhan aapay jaan. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	everyone says that he himself knows. ||1||
RECORD	para 41588	mÚ 1 ] (951-18) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41589	ihMdU kY Gir ihMdU AwvY ] (951-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hindoo kai ghar hindoo aavai. The Hindu comes to the house of a Hindu.
RECORD	para 41590	sUqu jnyaU piV gil pwvY ] (951-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) soot janay-oo parh gal paavai. He puts the sacred thread around his neck and reads the scriptures.
RECORD	para 41591	sUqu pwie kry buirAweI ] (951-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) soot paa-ay karay buri-aa-ee. He puts on the thread, but does evil deeds.
RECORD	para 41592	nwqw Doqw Qwie n pweI ] (951-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naataa Dhotaa thaa-ay na paa-ee. His cleansings and washings will not be approved.
RECORD	para 41593	muslmwnu kry vifAweI ] (951-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) musalmaan karay vadi-aa-ee. The Muslim glorifies his own faith.
DEFINE	para 41595	ivxu gur pIrY ko Qwie n pweI ] (952-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) vin gur peerai ko thaa-ay na paa-ee. Without the Guru or a spiritual teacher, no one is accepted.
ALLOW	para 41596	rwhu dswie EQY ko jwie ] (952-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) raahu dasaa-ay othai ko jaa-ay. They may be shown the way, but only a few go there.
DEFINE	para 41597	krxI bwJhu iBsiq n pwie ] (952-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) karnee baajhahu bhisat na paa-ay. Without the karma of good actions, heaven is not attained.
DEFINE	para 41598	jogI kY Gir jugiq dsweI ] (952-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jogee kai ghar jugat dasaa-ee. The Way of Yoga is demonstrated in the Yogi's monastery.
RECORD	para 41599	iqqu kwrix kin muMdRw pweI ] (952-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tit kaaran kan mundraa paa-ee. They wear ear-rings to show the way.
RECORD	para 41600	muMdRw pwie iPrY sMswir ] (952-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mundraa paa-ay firai sansaar. Wearing ear-rings, they wander around the world.
DEFINE	para 41601	ijQY ikQY isrjxhwru ] (952-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jithai kithai sirjanhaar. The Creator Lord is everywhere.
DEFINE	para 41602	jyqy jIA qyqy vwtwaU ] (952-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jaytay jee-a taytay vaataa-oo. There are as many travellers as there are beings.
DEFINE	para 41603	cIrI AweI iFl n kwaU ] (952-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) cheeree aa-ee dhil na kaa-oo. When one's death warrant is issued, there is no delay.
RECORD	para 41604	eyQY jwxY su jwie is\wxY ] (952-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aythai jaanai so jaa-ay sinjaanai. One who knows the Lord here, realizes Him there as well.
DEFINE	para 41605	horu PkVu ihMdU muslmwxY ] (952-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hor fakarh hindoo musalmaanai. Others, whether Hindu or Muslim, are just babbling.
DEFINE	para 41606	sBnw kw dir lyKw hoie ] (952-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabhnaa kaa dar laykhaa ho-ay. Everyone's account is read in the Court of the Lord;
RECORD	para 41607	krxI bwJhu qrY n koie ] (952-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) karnee baajhahu tarai na ko-ay. without the karma of good actions, no one crosses over.
RECORD	para 41608	sco scu vKwxY koie ] (952-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sacho sach vakhaanai ko-ay. One who speaks the True Name of the True Lord,
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk AgY puC n hoie ]2] (952-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak agai puchh na ho-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, is not called to account hereafter. ||2||
RECORD	para 41610	pauVI ] (952-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41611	hir kw mMdru AwKIAY kwieAw kotu gVu ] (952-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) har kaa mandar aakhee-ai kaa-i-aa kot garh. The fortress of the body is called the Mansion of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 41612	AMdir lwl jvyhrI gurmuiK hir nwmu pVu ] (952-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) andar laal javayharee gurmukh har naam parh. The rubies and gems are found within it; the Gurmukh chants the Name of the Lord.
WHEN	para 41613	hir kw mMdru srIru Aiq sohxw hir hir nwmu idVu ] (952-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) har kaa mandar sareer at sohnaa har har naam dirh. The body, the Mansion of the Lord, is very beautiful, when the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, is implanted deep within.
RECORD	para 41614	mnmuK Awip KuAwieAnu mwieAw moh inq kVu ] (952-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manmukh aap khu-aa-i-an maa-i-aa moh nit karh. The self-willed manmukhs ruin themselves; they boil continuously in attachment to Maya.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v11	sBnw swihbu eyku hY pUrY Bwig pwieAw jweI ]11] (952-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabhnaa saahib ayk hai poorai bhaag paa-i-aa jaa-ee. ||11||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v11	The One Lord is the Master of all. He is found only by perfect destiny. ||11||
RECORD	para 41616	slok mÚ 1 ] (952-8) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41617	nw siq duKIAw nw siq suKIAw nw siq pwxI jMq iPrih ] (952-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naa sat dukhee-aa naa sat sukhee-aa naa sat paanee jant fireh. There is no Truth in suffering, there is no Truth in comfort. There is no Truth in wandering like animals through the water.
RECORD	para 41618	nw siq mUMf mufweI kysI nw siq piVAw dys iPrih ] (952-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naa sat moond mudaa-ee kaysee naa sat parhi-aa days fireh. There is no Truth in shaving one's head; there is no Truth is studying the scriptures or wandering in foreign lands.
DEFINE	para 41619	nw siq ruKI ibrKI pQr Awpu qCwvih duK shih ] (952-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naa sat rukhee birkhee pathar aap tachhaaveh dukh saheh. There is no Truth in trees, plants or stones, in mutilating oneself or suffering in pain.
DEFINE	para 41620	nw siq hsqI bDy sMgl nw siq gweI Gwhu crih ] (952-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naa sat hastee baDhay sangal naa sat gaa-ee ghaahu chareh. There is no Truth in binding elephants in chains; there is no Truth in grazing cows.
RECORD	para 41621	ijsu hiQ isiD dyvY jy soeI ijs no dyie iqsu Awie imlY ] (952-10, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jis hath siDh dayvai jay so-ee jis no day-ay tis aa-ay milai. He alone grants it, whose hands hold spritual perfection; he alone receives it, unto whom it is given.
UPHOLD	para 41622	nwnk qw kau imlY vfweI ijsu Gt BIqir sbdu rvY ] (952-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak taa ka-o milai vadaa-ee jis ghat bheetar sabad ravai. O Nanak, he alone is blessed with glorious greatness, whose heart is filled with the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 41623	siB Gt myry hau sBnw AMdir ijsih KuAweI iqsu kauxu khY ] (952-11, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabh ghat mayray ha-o sabhnaa andar jisahi khu-aa-ee tis ka-un kahai. God says, all hearts are mine, and I am in all hearts. Who can explain this to one who is confused?
RECORD	para 41624	ijsih idKwlw vwtVI iqsih BulwvY kauxu ] (952-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jisahi dikhaalaa vaatrhee tiseh bhulaavai ka-un. Who can confuse that being, unto whom I have shown the Way?
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	ijsih BulweI pMD isir iqsih idKwvY kauxu ]1] (952-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jisahi bhulaa-ee panDh sir tiseh dikhaavai ka-un. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	And who can show the Path to that being whom I have confused since the beginning of time? ||1||
RECORD	para 41626	mÚ 1 ] (952-13) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41627	so igrhI jo ingRhu krY ] (952-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so girhee jo nigarahu karai. He alone is a householder, who restrains his passions
RECORD	para 41628	jpu qpu sMjmu BIiKAw krY ] (952-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jap tap sanjam bheekhi-aa karai. and begs for meditation, austerity and self-discipline.
RECORD	para 41629	puMn dwn kw kry srIru ] (952-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) punn daan kaa karay sareer. He gives donations to charity with his body;
DEFINE	para 41630	so igrhI gMgw kw nIru ] (952-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so girhee gangaa kaa neer. such a householder is as pure as the water of the Ganges.
DEFINE	para 41631	bolY eIsru siq srUpu ] (952-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai eesar sat saroop. Says Eeshar, the Lord is the embodiment of Truth.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	prm qMq mih ryK n rUpu ]2] (952-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) param tant meh raykh na roop. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	The supreme essence of reality has no shape or form. ||2||
RECORD	para 41633	mÚ 1 ] (952-15) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41634	so AauDUqI jo DUpY Awpu ] (952-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so a-uDhootee jo Dhoopai aap. He alone is a detached hermit, who burns away his self-conceit.
RECORD	para 41635	iBiKAw Bojnu krY sMqwpu ] (952-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bhikhi-aa bhojan karai santaap. He begs for suffering as his food.
RECORD	para 41636	AauhT ptx mih BIiKAw krY ] (952-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) a-uhath patan meh bheekhi-aa karai. In the city of the heart, he begs for charity.
RECORD	para 41637	so AauDUqI isv puir cVY ] (952-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so a-uDhootee siv pur charhai. Such a renunciate ascends to the City of God.
DEFINE	para 41638	bolY gorKu siq srUpu ] (952-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai gorakh sat saroop. Says Gorakh, God is the embodiment of Truth;
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	prm qMq mih ryK n rUpu ]3] (952-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) param tant meh raykh na roop. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	the supreme essence of reality has no shape or form. ||3||
RECORD	para 41640	mÚ 1 ] (952-17) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41641	so audwsI ij pwly audwsu ] (952-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so udaasee je paalay udaas. He alone is an Udasi, a shaven-headed renunciate, who embraces renunciation.
RECORD	para 41642	ArD aurD kry inrMjn vwsu ] (952-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) araDh uraDh karay niranjan vaas. He sees the Immaculate Lord dwelling in both the upper and lower regions.
WHEN	para 41643	cMd sUrj kI pwey gMiF ] (952-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) chand sooraj kee paa-ay gandh. He balances the sun and the moon energies.
RECORD	para 41644	iqsu audwsI kw pVY n kMDu ] (952-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tis udaasee kaa parhai na kanDh. The body-wall of such an Udasi does not collapse.
DEFINE	para 41645	bolY gopI cMdu siq srUpu ] (952-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai gopee chand sat saroop. Says Gopi Chand, God is the embodiment of Truth;
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v4	prm qMq mih ryK n rUpu ]4] (952-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) param tant meh raykh na roop. ||4||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v4	the supreme essence of reality has no shape or form. ||4||
RECORD	para 41647	mÚ 1 ] (952-19) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41648	so pwKMfI ij kwieAw pKwly ] (952-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so paakhandee je kaa-i-aa pakhaalay. He alone is a Paakhandi, who cleanses his body of filth.
RECORD	para 41649	kwieAw kI Agin bRhmu prjwly ] (952-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa kee agan barahm parjaalay. The fire of his body illuminates God within.
RECORD	para 41650	supnY ibMdu n dyeI Jrxw ] (952-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) supnai bind na day-ee jharnaa. He does not waste his energy in wet dreams.
RECORD	para 41652	iqsu pwKMfI jrw n mrxw ] (953-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tis paakhandee jaraa na marnaa. Such a Paakhandi does not grow old or die.
DEFINE	para 41653	bolY crptu siq srUpu ] (953-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai charpat sat saroop. Says Charpat, God is the embodiment of Truth;
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v5	prm qMq mih ryK n rUpu ]5] (953-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) param tant meh raykh na roop. ||5||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v5	the supreme essence of reality has no shape or form. ||5||
RECORD	para 41655	mÚ 1 ] (953-2) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41656	so bYrwgI ij aulty bRhmu ] (953-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so bairaagee je ultay barahm. He alone is a Bairaagi, who turns himself toward God.
RECORD	para 41657	ggn mMfl mih ropY QMmu ] (953-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gagan mandal meh ropai thamm. In the Tenth Gate, the sky of the mind, he erects his pillar.
RECORD	para 41658	Aihinis AMqir rhY iDAwin ] (953-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ahinis antar rahai Dhi-aan. Night and day, he remains in deep inner meditation.
DEFINE	para 41659	qy bYrwgI sq smwin ] (953-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tay bairaagee sat samaan. Such a Bairaagi is just like the True Lord.
DEFINE	para 41660	bolY BrQir siq srUpu ] (953-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bolai bharthar sat saroop. Says Bhart'har, God is the embodiment of Truth;
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v6	prm qMq mih ryK n rUpu ]6] (953-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) param tant meh raykh na roop. ||6||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v6	the supreme essence of reality has no shape or form. ||6||
RECORD	para 41662	mÚ 1 ] (953-3) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41663	ikau mrY mMdw ikau jIvY jugiq ] (953-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ki-o marai mandaa ki-o jeevai jugat. How is evil eradicated? How can the true way of life be found?
DEFINE	para 41664	kMn pVwie ikAw KwjY Bugiq ] (953-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kann parhaa-ay ki-aa khaajai bhugat. What is the use of piercing the ears, or begging for food?
DEFINE	para 41665	Awsiq nwsiq eyko nwau ] (953-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aasat naasat ayko naa-o. Throughout existence and non-existence, there is only the Name of the One Lord.
DEFINE	para 41666	kauxu su AKru ijqu rhY ihAwau ] (953-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ka-un so akhar jit rahai hi-aa-o. What is that Word, which holds the heart in its place?
WHEN	para 41667	DUp Cwv jy sm kir shY ] (953-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) Dhoop chhaav jay sam kar sahai. When you look alike upon sunshine and shade,
RECORD	para 41668	qw nwnku AwKY guru ko khY ] (953-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) taa naanak aakhai gur ko kahai. says Nanak, then the Guru will speak to you.
RECORD	para 41669	iCA vrqwry vrqih pUq ] (953-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) chhi-a vartaaray varteh poot. The students follow the six systems.
DEFINE	para 41670	nw sMswrI nw AauDUq ] (953-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naa sansaaree naa a-uDhoot. They are neither worldly people, nor detached renunciates.
RECORD	para 41671	inrMkwir jo rhY smwie ] (953-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) nirankaar jo rahai samaa-ay. One who remains absorbed in the Formless Lord
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v7	kwhy BIiKAw mMgix jwie ]7] (953-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kaahay bheekhi-aa mangan jaa-ay. ||7||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v7	- why should he go out begging? ||7||
RECORD	para 41673	pauVI ] (953-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41674	hir mMdru soeI AwKIAY ijQhu hir jwqw ] (953-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) har mandar so-ee aakhee-ai jithahu har jaataa. That alone is said to be the Lord's temple, where the Lord is known.
WHEN	para 41675	mwns dyh gur bcnI pwieAw sBu Awqm rwmu pCwqw ] (953-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) maanas dayh gur bachnee paa-i-aa sabh aatam raam pachhaataa. In the human body, the Guru's Word is found, when one understands that the Lord, the Supreme Soul, is in all.
RECORD	para 41676	bwhir mUil n KojIAY Gr mwih ibDwqw ] (953-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) baahar mool na khojee-ai ghar maahi biDhaataa. Don't look for Him outside your self. The Creator, the Architect of Destiny, is within the home of your own heart.
RECORD	para 41677	mnmuK hir mMdr kI swr n jwxnI iqnI jnmu gvwqw ] (953-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manmukh har mandar kee saar na jaannee tinee janam gavaataa. The self-willed manmukh does not appreciate the value of the Lord's temple; they waste away and lose their lives.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v12	sB mih ieku vrqdw gur sbdI pwieAw jweI ]12] (953-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabh meh ik varatdaa gur sabdee paa-i-aa jaa-ee. ||12||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v12	The One Lord is pervading in all; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, He can be found. ||12||
RECORD	para 41679	slok mÚ 3 ] (953-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 41680	mUrKu hovY so suxY mUrK kw khxw ] (953-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) moorakh hovai so sunai moorakh kaa kahnaa. Only a fool listens to the words of the fool.
DEFINE	para 41681	mUrK ky ikAw lKx hY ikAw mUrK kw krxw ] (953-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) moorakh kay ki-aa lakhan hai ki-aa moorakh kaa karnaa. What are the signs of the fool? What does the fool do?
DEFINE	para 41682	mUrKu Ehu ij mugDu hY AhMkwry mrxw ] (953-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) moorakh oh je mugaDh hai aha Nkaaray marnaa. A fool is stupid; he dies of egotism.
RECORD	para 41683	eyqu kmwxY sdw duKu duK hI mih rhxw ] (953-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ayt kamaanai sadaa dukh dukh hee meh rahnaa. His actions always bring him pain; he lives in pain.
WHEN	para 41684	Aiq ipAwrw pvY KUih ikhu sMjmu krxw ] (953-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) at pi-aaraa pavai khoohi kihu sanjam karnaa. If someone's beloved friend falls into the pit, what can be used to pull him out?
RECORD	para 41685	gurmuiK hoie su kry vIcwru Esu Ailpqo rhxw ] (953-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) gurmukh ho-ay so karay veechaar os alipato rahnaa. One who becomes Gurmukh contemplates the Lord, and remains detached.
RECORD	para 41686	hir nwmu jpY Awip auDrY Esu ipCY fubdy BI qrxw ] (953-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) har naam japai aap uDhrai os pichhai dubday bhee tarnaa. Chanting the Lord's Name, he saves himself, and he carries across those who are drowning as well.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk jo iqsu BwvY so kry jo dyie su shxw ]1] (953-12, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak jo tis bhaavai so karay jo day-ay so sahnaa. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, he acts in accordance with the Will of God; he endures whatever he is given. ||1||
RECORD	para 41688	mÚ 1 ] (953-13) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41689	nwnku AwKY ry mnw suxIAY isK shI ] (953-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak aakhai ray manaa sunee-ai sikh sahee. Says Nanak, listen, O mind, to the True Teachings.
WHEN	para 41690	lyKw rbu mMgysIAw bYTw kiF vhI ] (953-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) laykhaa rab mangaysee-aa baithaa kadh vahee. Opening His ledger, God will call you to account.
REQUIRE	para 41691	qlbw pausin AwkIAw bwkI ijnw rhI ] (953-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) talbaa pa-usan aakee-aa baakee jinaa rahee. Those rebels who have unpaid accounts shall be called out.
REQUIRE	para 41692	AjrweIlu Prysqw hosI Awie qeI ] (953-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ajraa-eel faraystaa hosee aa-ay ta-ee. Azraa-eel, the Angel of Death, shall be appointed to punish them.
DEFINE	para 41693	Awvxu jwxu n suJeI BIVI glI PhI ] (953-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aavan jaan na sujh-ee bheerhee galee fahee. They will find no way to escape coming and going in reincarnation; they are trapped in the narrow path.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	kUV inKuty nwnkw EVik sic rhI ]2] (953-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) koorh nikhutay naankaa orhak sach rahee. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	Falsehood will come to an end, O Nanak, and Truth will prevail in the end. ||2||
RECORD	para 41695	pauVI ] (953-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41696	hir kw sBu srIru hY hir riv rihAw sBu AwpY ] (953-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) har kaa sabh sareer hai har rav rahi-aa sabh aapai. The body and everything belongs to the Lord; the Lord Himself is all-pervading.
RECORD	para 41697	hir kI kImiq n pvY ikCu khxu n jwpY ] (953-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) har kee keemat na pavai kichh kahan na jaapai. The Lord's value cannot be estimated; nothing can be said about it.
RECORD	para 41698	gur prswdI swlwhIAY hir BgqI rwpY ] (953-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee salaahee-ai har bhagtee raapai. By Guru's Grace, one praises the Lord, imbued with feelings of devotion.
DEFINE	para 41699	sBu mnu qnu hirAw hoieAw AhMkwru gvwpY ] (953-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabh man tan hari-aa ho-i-aa aha Nkaar gavaapai. The mind and body are totally rejuvenated, and egotism is eradicated.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v13	sBu ikCu hir kw Kylu hY gurmuiK iksY buJweI ]13] (953-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabh kichh har kaa khayl hai gurmukh kisai bujhaa-ee. ||13||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v13	Everything is the play of the Lord. The Gurmukh understands this. ||13||
RECORD	para 41701	sloku mÚ 1 ] (953-18) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41702	shMsr dwn dy ieMdRü roAwieAw ] (953-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sahaNsar daan day indar ro-aa-i-aa. Branded with a thousand marks of disgrace, Indra cried in shame.
RECORD	para 41703	prs rwmu rovY Gir AwieAw ] (953-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) paras raam rovai ghar aa-i-aa. Paras Raam returned home crying.
WHEN	para 41704	AjY su rovY BIiKAw Kwie ] (953-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ajai so rovai bheekhi-aa khaa-ay. Ajai cried and wept, when he was made to eat the manure he had given, pretending it was charity.
DEFINE	para 41705	AYsI drgh imlY sjwie ] (953-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aisee dargeh milai sajaa-ay. Such is the punishment received in the Court of the Lord.
WHEN	para 41706	rovY rwmu inkwlw BieAw ] (953-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) rovai raam nikaalaa bha-i-aa. Rama wept when he was sent into exile,
RECORD	para 41708	sIqw lKmxu ivCuiV gieAw ] (954-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) seetaa lakhman vichhurh ga-i-aa. and separated from Sita and Lakhshman.
WHEN	para 41709	rovY dhisru lµk gvwie ] ijin sIqw AwdI faurU vwie ] (954-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) rovai dehsir lank gavaa-ay. jin seetaa aadee da-uroo vaa-ay. The ten-headed Raawan, who stole away Sita with the beat of his tambourine, wept when he lost Sri Lanka.
RECORD	para 41710	rovih pWfv Bey mjUr ] ijn kY suAwmI rhq hdUir ] (954-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) roveh paa Ndav bha-ay majoor. jin kai su-aamee rahat hadoor. The Paandavas once lived in the Presence of the Lord; they were made slaves, and wept.
RECORD	para 41711	rovY jnmyjw Kuie gieAw ] (954-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) rovai janmayjaa khu-ay ga-i-aa. Janmayjaa wept, that he had lost his way.
RECORD	para 41712	eykI kwrix pwpI BieAw ] (954-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aykee kaaran paapee bha-i-aa. One mistake, and he became a sinner.
RECORD	para 41713	rovih syK mswiek pIr ] (954-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) roveh saykh masaa-ik peer. The Shaykhs, Pirs and spiritual teachers weep;
RECORD	para 41714	AMiq kwil mqu lwgY BIV ] (954-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ant kaal mat laagai bheerh. at the very last instant, they suffer in agony.
DEFINE	para 41715	rovih rwjy kMn pVwie ] (954-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) roveh raajay kann parhaa-ay. The kings weep - their ears are cut;
RECORD	para 41716	Gir Gir mwgih BIiKAw jwie ] (954-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghar ghar maageh bheekhi-aa jaa-ay. they go begging from house to house.
RECORD	para 41717	rovih ikrpn sMcih Dnu jwie ] (954-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) roveh kirpan sa Ncheh Dhan jaa-ay. The miser weeps; he has to leave behind the wealth he has gathered.
DEFINE	para 41718	pMifq rovih igAwnu gvwie ] (954-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) pandit roveh gi-aan gavaa-ay. The Pandit, the religious scholar, weeps when his learning is gone.
RECORD	para 41719	bwlI rovY nwih Bqwru ] (954-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) baalee rovai naahi bhataar. The young woman weeps because she has no husband.
DEFINE	para 41720	nwnk duKIAw sBu sMswru ] (954-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak dukhee-aa sabh sansaar. O Nanak, the whole world is suffering.
DEFINE	para 41721	mMny nwau soeI ijix jwie ] (954-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) mannay naa-o so-ee jin jaa-ay. He alone is victorious, who believes in the Lord's Name.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	AaurI krm n lyKY lwie ]1] (954-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) a-uree karam na laykhai laa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	No other action is of any account. ||1||
RECORD	para 41723	mÚ 2 ] (954-6) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 41724	jpu qpu sBu ikCu mMinAY Avir kwrw siB bwid ] (954-6, rwmklI, mÚ 2) jap tap sabh kichh mani-ai avar kaaraa sabh baad. Meditation, austerity and everything come through belief in the Lord's Name. All other actions are useless.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk mMinAw mMnIAY buJIAY gur prswid ]2] (954-6, rwmklI, mÚ 2) naanak mani-aa mannee-ai bujhee-ai gur parsaad. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, believe in the One who is worth believing in. By Guru's Grace, he is realized. ||2||
RECORD	para 41726	pauVI ] (954-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 41727	kwieAw hMs Duir mylu krqY iliK pwieAw ] (954-7, rwmklI, mÚ 2) kaa-i-aa hans Dhur mayl kartai likh paa-i-aa. The union of the body and the soul-swan was pre-ordained by the Creator Lord.
DEFINE	para 41728	sB mih gupqu vrqdw gurmuiK pRgtwieAw ] (954-8, rwmklI, mÚ 2) sabh meh gupat varatdaa gurmukh paragtaa-i-aa. He is hidden, and yet pervading all. He is revealed to the Gurmukh.
RECORD	para 41729	gux gwvY gux aucrY gux mwih smwieAw ] (954-8, rwmklI, mÚ 2) gun gaavai gun uchrai gun maahi samaa-i-aa. Singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and chanting His Praises, one merges in His Glories.
DEFINE	para 41730	scI bwxI scu hY scu myil imlwieAw ] (954-8, rwmklI, mÚ 2) sachee banee sach hai sach mayl milaa-i-aa. True is the True Word of the Guru's Bani. One unites in Union with the True Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v14	sBu ikCu Awpy Awip hY Awpy dyie vifAweI ]14] (954-9, rwmklI, mÚ 2) sabh kichh aapay aap hai aapay day-ay vadi-aa-ee. ||14||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v14	He Himself is everything; He Himself grants glorious greatness. ||14||
RECORD	para 41732	slok mÚ 2 ] (954-9) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
ALLOW	para 41733	nwnk AMDw hoie kY rqnw prKx jwie ] (954-10, rwmklI, mÚ 2) naanak anDhaa ho-ay kai ratnaa parkhan jaa-ay. O Nanak, the blind man may go to appraise the jewels,
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	rqnw swr n jwxeI AwvY Awpu lKwie ]1] (954-10, rwmklI, mÚ 2) ratnaa saar na jaan-ee aavai aap lakhaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	but he will not know their value; he will return home after exposing his ignorance. ||1||
RECORD	para 41735	mÚ 2 ] (954-11) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 41736	rqnw kyrI guQlI rqnI KolI Awie ] (954-11, rwmklI, mÚ 2) ratnaa kayree guthlee ratnee kholee aa-ay. The Jeweller has come, and opened up the bag of jewels.
DEFINE	para 41737	vKr qY vxjwirAw duhw rhI smwie ] (954-11, rwmklI, mÚ 2) vakhar tai vanjaari-aa duhaa rahee samaa-ay. The merchandise and the merchant are merged together.
RECORD	para 41738	ijn guxu plY nwnkw mwxk vxjih syie ] (954-11, rwmklI, mÚ 2) jin gun palai naankaa maanak vanjahi say-ay. They alone purchase the gem, O Nanak, who have virtue in their purse.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	rqnw swr n jwxnI AMDy vqih loie ]2] (954-12, rwmklI, mÚ 2) ratnaa saar na jaannee anDhay vateh lo-ay. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	Those who do not appreciate the value of the jewels, wander like blind men in the world. ||2||
RECORD	para 41740	pauVI ] (954-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41741	nau drvwjy kwieAw kotu hY dsvY gupqu rKIjY ] (954-12, rwmklI, mÚ 2) na-o darvaajay kaa-i-aa kot hai dasvai gupat rakheejai. The fortress of the body has nine gates; the tenth gate is kept hidden.
DEFINE	para 41742	bjr kpwt n KulnI gur sbid KulIjY ] (954-13, rwmklI, mÚ 2) bajar kapaat na khulnee gur sabad khuleejai. The rigid door is not open; only through the Word of the Guru's Shabad can it be opened.
DEFINE	para 41743	Anhd vwjy Duin vjdy gur sbid suxIjY ] (954-13, rwmklI, mÚ 2) anhad vaajay Dhun vajday gur sabad suneejai. The unstruck sound current resounds and vibrates there. The Word of the Guru's Shabad is heard.
RECORD	para 41744	iqqu Gt AMqir cwnxw kir Bgiq imlIjY ] (954-14, rwmklI, mÚ 2) tit ghat antar chaannaa kar bhagat mileejai. Deep within the nucleus of the heart, the Divine Light shines forth. Through devotional worship, one meets the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v15	sB mih eyku vrqdw ijin Awpy rcn rcweI ]15] (954-14, rwmklI, mÚ 2) sabh meh ayk varatdaa jin aapay rachan rachaa-ee. ||15||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v15	The One Lord is pervading and permeating all. He Himself created the creation. ||15||
RECORD	para 41746	slok mÚ 2 ] (954-15) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41747	AMDy kY rwih disAY AMDw hoie su jwie ] (954-15, rwmklI, mÚ 2) anDhay kai raahi dasi-ai anDhaa ho-ay so jaa-ay. He is truly blind, who follows the way shown by the blind man.
RECORD	para 41748	hoie sujwKw nwnkw so ikau auJiV pwie ] (954-16, rwmklI, mÚ 2) ho-ay sujaakhaa naankaa so ki-o ujharh paa-ay. O Nanak, why should the one who can see, get lost?
RECORD	para 41749	AMDy eyih n AwKIAin ijn muiK loiex nwih ] (954-16, rwmklI, mÚ 2) anDhay ayhi na aakhee-an jin mukh lo-in naahi. Do not call them blind, who have no eyes in their face.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	AMDy syeI nwnkw Ksmhu GuQy jwih ]1] (954-16, rwmklI, mÚ 2) anDhay say-ee naankaa khasmahu ghuthay jaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	They alone are blind, O Nanak, who wander away from their Lord and Master. ||1||
RECORD	para 41751	mÚ 2 ] (954-17) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 41752	swihib AMDw jo kIAw kry sujwKw hoie ] (954-17, rwmklI, mÚ 2) saahib anDhaa jo kee-aa karay sujaakhaa ho-ay. One whom the Lord has made blind - the Lord can make him see again.
ALLOW	para 41753	jyhw jwxY qyho vrqY jy sau AwKY koie ] (954-17, rwmklI, mÚ 2) jayhaa jaanai tayho vartai jay sa-o aakhai ko-ay. He acts only as he knows, although he may be spoken to a hundred times.
DEFINE	para 41754	ijQY su vsqu n jwpeI Awpy vrqau jwix ] (954-18, rwmklI, mÚ 2) jithai so vasat na jaap-ee aapay varta-o jaan. Where the real thing is not seen, self-conceit prevails there - know this well.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk gwhku ikau ley skY n vsqu pCwix ]2] (954-18, rwmklI, mÚ 2) naanak gaahak ki-o la-ay sakai na vasat pachhaan. ||2||
WHEN	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, how can the purshaser purchase the real thing, if he cannot recognize it? ||2||
RECORD	para 41756	mÚ 2 ] (954-19) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
WHEN	para 41757	so ikau AMDw AwKIAY ij hukmhu AMDw hoie ] (954-19, rwmklI, mÚ 2) so ki-o anDhaa aakhee-ai je hukmahu anDhaa ho-ay. How can someone be called blind, if he was made blind by the Lord's Command?
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	nwnk hukmu n buJeI AMDw khIAY soie ]3] (954-19, rwmklI, mÚ 2) naanak hukam na bujh-ee anDhaa kahee-ai so-ay. ||3||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	O Nanak, one who does not understand the Hukam of the Lord's Command should be called blind. ||3||
RECORD	para 41760	pauVI ] (955-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41761	kwieAw AMdir gVu kotu hY siB idsMqr dysw ] (955-1, rwmklI, mÚ 2) kaa-i-aa andar garh kot hai sabh disantar daysaa. Deep within the body is the fortress of the Lord, and all lands and countries.
DEFINE	para 41762	Awpy qwVI lweIAnu sB mih prvysw ] (955-1, rwmklI, mÚ 2) aapay taarhee laa-ee-an sabh meh parvaysaa. He Himself sits in primal, profound Samaadhi; He Himself is all-pervading.
RECORD	para 41763	Awpy isRsit swjIAnu Awip gupqu rKysw ] (955-2, rwmklI, mÚ 2) aapay sarisat saajee-an aap gupat rakhaysaa. He Himself created the Universe, and He Himself remains hidden within it.
DEFINE	para 41764	gur syvw qy jwixAw scu prgtIeysw ] (955-2, rwmklI, mÚ 2) gur sayvaa tay jaani-aa sach pargatee-aysaa. Serving the Guru, the Lord is known, and the Truth is revealed.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v16	sBu ikCu sco scu hY guir soJI pweI ]16] (955-3, rwmklI, mÚ 2) sabh kichh sacho sach hai gur sojhee paa-ee. ||16||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v16	He is True, the Truest of the True; the Guru has imparted this understanding. ||16||
RECORD	para 41766	slok mÚ 1 ] (955-3) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41767	swvxu rwiq AhwVu idhu kwmu k®oDu duie Kyq ] (955-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saavan raat ahaarh dihu kaam kroDh du-ay khayt. Night is the summer season, and day is the winter season; sexual desire and anger are the two fields planted.
DEFINE	para 41768	lbu vqR drogu bIau hwlI rwhku hyq ] (955-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) lab vatar darog bee-o haalee raahak hayt. Greed prepares the soil, and the seed of falsehood is planted; attachment and love are the farmer and hired hand.
RECORD	para 41769	hlu bIcwru ivkwr mx hukmI Kty Kwie ] (955-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hal beechaar vikaar man hukmee khatay khaa-ay. Contemplation is the plow, and corruption is the harvest; this is what one earns and eats, according to the Hukam of the Lord's Command.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk lyKY mMigAY Aauqu jxydw jwie ]1] (955-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak laykhai mangi-ai a-ut janaydaa jaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, when one is called to give his account, he will be barren and infertile. ||1||
RECORD	para 41771	mÚ 1 ] (955-5) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41772	Bau Buie pivqu pwxI squ sMqoKu blyd ] (955-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bha-o bhu-ay pavit paanee sat santokh balayd. Make the Fear of God the farm, purity the water, truth and contentment the cows and bulls,
RECORD	para 41773	hlu hlymI hwlI icqu cyqw vqR vKq sMjogu ] (955-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) hal halaymee haalee chit chaytaa vatar vakhat sanjog. humility the plow, consciousness the plowman, remembrance the preparation of the soil, and union with the Lord the planting time.
RECORD	para 41774	nwau bIju bKsIs bohl dunIAw sgl drog ] (955-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naa-o beej bakhsees bohal dunee-aa sagal darog. Let the Lord's Name be the seed, and His Forgiving Grace the harvest. Do this, and the whole world will seem false.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk ndrI krmu hoie jwvih sgl ivjog ]2] (955-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak nadree karam ho-ay jaaveh sagal vijog. ||2||
WHEN	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, if He bestows His Merciful Glance of Grace, then all your separation will be ended. ||2||
RECORD	para 41776	pauVI ] (955-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41777	mnmuiK mohu gubwru hY dUjY Bwie bolY ] (955-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manmukh moh gubaar hai doojai bhaa-ay bolai. The self-willed manmukh is trapped in the darkness of emotional attachment; in the love of duality he speaks.
RECORD	para 41778	dUjY Bwie sdw duKu hY inq nIru ivrolY ] (955-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) doojai bhaa-ay sadaa dukh hai nit neer virolai. The love of duality brings pain forever; he churns the water endlessly.
RECORD	para 41779	gurmuiK nwmu iDAweIAY miQ qqu kFolY ] (955-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai math tat kadholai. The Gurmukh meditates on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; he churns, and obtains the essence of reality.
RECORD	para 41780	AMqir prgwsu Git cwnxw hir lDw tolY ] (955-8, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar pargaas ghat chaannaa har laDhaa tolai. The Divine Light illuminates his heart deep within; he seeks the Lord, and obtains Him.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v17	Awpy Brim Bulwiedw ikCu khxu n jweI ]17] (955-9, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay bharam bhulaa-idaa kichh kahan na jaa-ee. ||17||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v17	He Himself deludes in doubt; no one can comment on this. ||17||
RECORD	para 41782	slok mÚ 2 ] (955-9) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 41783	nwnk icMqw miq krhu icMqw iqs hI hyie ] (955-10, rwmklI, mÚ 2) naanak chintaa mat karahu chintaa tis hee hay-ay. O Nanak, don't be anxious; the Lord will take care of you.
RECORD	para 41784	jl mih jMq aupwieAnu iqnw iB rojI dyie ] (955-10, rwmklI, mÚ 2) jal meh jant upaa-i-an tinaa bhe rojee day-ay. He created the creatures in water, and He gives them their nourishment.
DEFINE	para 41785	EQY htu n cleI nw ko ikrs kryie ] (955-10, rwmklI, mÚ 2) othai hat na chal-ee naa ko kiras karay-i. There are no stores open there, and no one farms there.
DEFINE	para 41786	saudw mUil n hoveI nw ko ley n dyie ] (955-11, rwmklI, mÚ 2) sa-udaa mool na hova-ee naa ko la-ay na day-ay. No business is ever transacted there, and no one buys or sells.
DEFINE	para 41787	jIAw kw Awhwru jIA Kwxw eyhu kryie ] (955-11, rwmklI, mÚ 2) jee-aa kaa aahaar jee-a khaanaa ayhu karay-i. Animals eat other animals; this is what the Lord has given them as food.
RECORD	para 41788	ivic aupwey swierw iqnw iB swr kryie ] (955-12, rwmklI, mÚ 2) vich upaa-ay saa-iraa tinaa bhe saar karay-i. He created them in the oceans, and He provides for them as well.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk icMqw mq krhu icMqw iqs hI hyie ]1] (955-12, rwmklI, mÚ 2) naanak chintaa mat karahu chintaa tis hee hay-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, don't be anxious; the Lord will take care of you. ||1||
RECORD	para 41790	mÚ 1 ] (955-13) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41791	nwnk iehu jIau mCulI JIvru iqRsnw kwlu ] (955-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak ih jee-o machhulee jheevar tarisnaa kaal. O Nanak, this soul is the fish, and death is the hungry fisherman.
DEFINE	para 41792	mnUAw AMDu n cyqeI pVY AicMqw jwlu ] (955-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) manoo-aa anDh na chayt-ee parhai achintaa jaal. The blind man does not even think of this. And suddenly, the net is cast.
DEFINE	para 41793	nwnk icqu Acyqu hY icMqw bDw jwie ] (955-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak chit achayt hai chintaa baDhaa jaa-ay. O Nanak, his consciousness is unconscious, and he departs, bound by anxiety.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	ndir kry jy AwpxI qw Awpy ley imlwie ]2] (955-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) nadar karay jay aapnee taa aapay la-ay milaa-ay. ||2||
WHEN	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	But if the Lord bestows His Glance of Grace, then He unites the soul with Himself. ||2||
RECORD	para 41795	pauVI ] (955-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41796	sy jn swcy sdw sdw ijnI hir rsu pIqw ] (955-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) say jan saachay sadaa sadaa jinee har ras peetaa. They are true, forever true, who drink in the sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	para 41797	gurmuiK scw min vsY scu saudw kIqw ] (955-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gurmukh sachaa man vasai sach sa-udaa keetaa. The True Lord abides in the mind of the Gurmukh; He strikes the true bargain.
DEFINE	para 41798	sBu ikCu Gr hI mwih hY vfBwgI lIqw ] (955-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabh kichh ghar hee maahi hai vadbhaagee leetaa. Everything is in the home of the self within; only the very fortunate obtain it.
DEFINE	para 41799	AMqir iqRsnw mir geI hir gux gwvIqw ] (955-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) antar tarisnaa mar ga-ee har gun gaaveetaa. The hunger within is conquered and overcome, singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v18	Awpy myil imlwieAnu Awpy dyie buJweI ]18] (955-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay mayl milaa-i-an aapay day-ay bujhaa-ee. ||18||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v18	He Himself unites in His Union; He Himself blesses them with understanding. ||18||
RECORD	para 41801	slok mÚ 1 ] (955-17) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41802	vyil ipM\wieAw kiq vuxwieAw ] (955-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) vayl pinjaa-i-aa kat gunaa-i-aa. The cotton is ginned, woven and spun;
DEFINE	para 41803	kit kuit kir KuMib cVwieAw ] (955-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kat kut kar khumb charhaa-i-aa. the cloth is laid out, washed and bleached white.
RECORD	para 41804	lohw vFy drjI pwVy sUeI Dwgw sIvY ] (955-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) lohaa vadhay darjee paarhay soo-ee Dhaagaa seevai. The tailor cuts it with his scissors, and sews it with his thread.
RECORD	para 41805	ieau piq pwtI isPqI sIpY nwnk jIvq jIvY ] (955-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) i-o pat paatee siftee seepai naanak jeevat jeevai. Thus, the torn and tattered honor is sewn up again, through the Lord's Praise, O Nanak, and one lives the true life.
DEFINE	para 41806	hoie purwxw kpVu pwtY sUeI Dwgw gMFY ] (955-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ho-ay puraanaa kaparh paatai soo-ee Dhaagaa gandhai. Becoming worn, the cloth is torn; with needle and thread it is sewn up again.
RECORD	para 41807	mwhu pKu ikhu clY nwhI GVI muhqu ikCu hMFY ] (955-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) maahu pakh kihu chalai naahee gharhee muhat kichh handhai. It will not last for a month, or even a week. It barely lasts for an hour, or even a moment.
DEFINE	para 41809	scu purwxw hovY nwhI sIqw kdy n pwtY ] (956-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sach puraanaa hovai naahee seetaa kaday na paatai. But the Truth does not grow old; and when it is stitched, it is never torn again.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk swihbu sco scw iqcru jwpI jwpY ]1] (956-1, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak saahib sacho sachaa tichar jaapee jaapai. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, the Lord and Master is the Truest of the True. While we meditate on Him, we see Him. ||1||
RECORD	para 41811	mÚ 1 ] (956-2) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41812	sc kI kwqI scu sBu swru ] (956-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sach kee kaatee sach sabh saar. The knife is Truth, and its steel is totally True.
DEFINE	para 41813	GwVq iqs kI Apr Apwr ] (956-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ghaarhat tis kee apar apaar. Its workmanship is incomparably beautiful.
DEFINE	para 41814	sbdy swx rKweI lwie ] (956-2, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sabday saan rakhaa-ee laa-ay. It is sharpened on the grindstone of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 41815	gux kI QykY ivic smwie ] (956-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) gun kee thaykai vich samaa-ay. It is placed in the scabbard of virtue.
DEFINE	para 41816	iqs dw kuTw hovY syKu ] (956-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) tis daa kuthaa hovai saykh. If the Shaykh is killed with that,
RECORD	para 41817	lohU lbu inkQw vyKu ] (956-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) lohoo lab nikthaa vaykh. then the blood of greed will spill out.
DEFINE	para 41818	hoie hlwlu lgY hik jwie ] (956-3, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ho-ay halaal lagai hak jaa-ay. One who is slaughtered in this ritualistic way, will be attached to the Lord.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk dir dIdwir smwie ]2] (956-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak dar deedaar samaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, at the Lord's door, he is absorbed into His Blessed Vision. ||2||
RECORD	para 41820	mÚ 1 ] (956-4) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41821	kmir ktwrw bMkuVw bMky kw Asvwru ] (956-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) kamar kataaraa ba Nkurhaa bankay kaa asvaar. A beautiful dagger hangs by your waist, and you ride such a beautiful horse.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	grbu n kIjY nwnkw mqu isir AwvY Bwru ]3] (956-4, rwmklI, mÚ 1) garab na keejai naankaa mat sir aavai bhaar. ||3||
ALLOW	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v3	But don't be too proud; O Nanak, you may fall head first to the ground. ||3||
RECORD	para 41823	pauVI ] (956-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 41824	so sqsMgiq sbid imlY jo gurmuiK clY ] (956-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) so satsangat sabad milai jo gurmukh chalai. They alone walk as Gurmukh, who receive the Shabad in the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation.
RECORD	para 41825	scu iDAwiein sy scy ijn hir Krcu Dnu plY ] (956-5, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sach Dhi-aa-in say sachay jin har kharach Dhan palai. Meditating on the True Lord, they become truthful; they carry in their robes the supplies of the Lord's wealth.
RECORD	para 41826	Bgq sohin gux gwvdy gurmiq AclY ] (956-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bhagat sohan gun gaavday gurmat achlai. The devotees look beautiful, singing the Praises of the Lord; following the Guru's Teachings, they become stable and unchanging.
RECORD	para 41827	rqn bIcwru min visAw gur kY sbid BlY ] (956-6, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ratan beechaar man vasi-aa gur kai sabad bhalai. They enshrine the jewel of contemplation within their minds, and the most sublime Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v19	Awpy myil imlwiedw Awpy dyie vifAweI ]19] (956-7, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay mayl milaa-idaa aapay day-ay vadi-aa-ee. ||19||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v19	He Himself unites in His Union; He Himself grants glorious greatness. ||19||
RECORD	para 41829	slok mÚ 3 ] (956-7) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41830	Awsw AMdir sBu ko koie inrwsw hoie ] (956-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) aasaa andar sabh ko ko-ay niraasaa ho-ay. Everyone is filled with hope; hardly anyone is free of hope.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk jo mir jIivAw sihlw AwieAw soie ]1] (956-8, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naanak jo mar jeevi-aa sahilaa aa-i-aa so-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, blessed is the birth of one, who remains dead while yet alive. ||1||
RECORD	para 41832	mÚ 3 ] (956-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41833	nw ikCu Awsw hiQ hY kyau inrwsw hoie ] (956-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) naa kichh aasaa hath hai kay-o niraasaa ho-ay. Nothing is in the hands of hope. How can one become free of hope?
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	ikAw kry eyh bpuVI jW Buolwey soie ]2] (956-9, rwmklI, mÚ 3) ki-aa karay ayh bapurhee jaa N bholaa-ay so-ay. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	What can this poor being do? The Lord Himself creates confusion. ||2||
RECORD	para 41835	pauVI ] (956-9) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41836	iDRgu jIvxu sMswr scy nwm ibnu ] (956-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) Dharig jeevan sansaar sachay naam bin. Cursed is the life in this world, without the True Name.
DEFINE	para 41837	pRBu dwqw dwqwr inhclu eyhu Dnu ] (956-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) parabh daataa daataar nihchal ayhu Dhan. God is the Great Giver of givers. His wealth is permanent and unchanging.
DEFINE	para 41838	swis swis AwrwDy inrmlu soie jnu ] (956-10, rwmklI, mÚ 3) saas saas aaraaDhay nirmal so-ay jan. That humble being is immaculate, who worships the Lord with each and every breath.
RECORD	para 41839	AMqrjwmI Agmu rsnw eyku Bnu ] (956-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) antarjaamee agam rasnaa ayk bhan. With your tongue, vibrate the One Inaccessible Lord, the Inner-knower, the Searcher of hearts.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v20	riv rihAw srbiq nwnku bil jweI ]20] (956-11, rwmklI, mÚ 3) rav rahi-aa sarbat naanak bal jaa-ee. ||20||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v20	He is all-pervading everywhere. Nanak is a sacrifice to Him. ||20||
RECORD	para 41841	sloku mÚ 1 ] (956-12) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 41842	srvr hMs Dury hI mylw KsmY eyvY Bwxw ] (956-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sarvar hans Dhuray hee maylaa khasmai ayvai bhaanaa. The union between the lake of the True Guru, and the swan of the soul, was pre- ordained from the very beginning, by the Pleasure of the Lord's Will.
DEFINE	para 41843	srvr AMdir hIrw moqI so hMsw kw Kwxw ] (956-12, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sarvar andar heeraa motee so hansaa kaa khaanaa. The diamonds are in this lake; they are the food of the swans.
ALLOW	para 41844	bgulw kwgu n rheI srvir jy hovY Aiq isAwxw ] (956-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) bagulaa kaag na rah-ee sarvar jay hovai at si-aanaa. The cranes and the ravens may be very wise, but they do not remain in this lake.
DEFINE	para 41845	Enw irjku n pieE EQY En@w horo Kwxw ] (956-13, rwmklI, mÚ 1) onaa rijak na pa-i-o othai on Haa horo khaanaa. They do not find their food there; their food is different.
DEFINE	para 41846	sic kmwxY sco pweIAY kUVY kUVw mwxw ] (956-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) sach kamaanai sacho paa-ee-ai koorhai koorhaa maanaa. Practicing Truth, the True Lord is found. False is the pride of the false.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk iqn kO siqguru imilAw ijnw Dury pYXw prvwxw ]1] (956-14, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak tin kou satgur mili-aa jinaa Dhuray paiyaa parvaanaa. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, they alone meet the True Guru, who are so pre-destined by the Lord's Command. ||1||
RECORD	para 41848	mÚ 1 ] (956-15) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41849	swihbu myrw aujlw jy ko iciq kryie ] (956-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) saahib mayraa ujlaa jay ko chit karay-i. My Lord and Master is immaculate, as are those who think of Him.
RECORD	para 41850	nwnk soeI syvIAY sdw sdw jo dyie ] (956-15, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak so-ee sayvee-ai sadaa sadaa jo day-ay. O Nanak, serve Him, who gives to you forever and ever.
DEFINE	para 41851	nwnk soeI syvIAY ijqu syivAY duKu jwie ] (956-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak so-ee sayvee-ai jit sayvi-ai dukh jaa-ay. O Nanak, serve Him; by serving Him, sorrow is dispelled.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	Avgux vM\in gux rvih min suKu vsY Awie ]2] (956-16, rwmklI, mÚ 1) avgun vanjan gun raveh man sukh vasai aa-ay. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v2	Faults and demerits vanish, and virtues take their place; peace comes to dwell in the mind. ||2||
RECORD	para 41853	pauVI ] (956-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41854	Awpy Awip vrqdw Awip qwVI lweIAnu ] (956-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay aap varatdaa aap taarhee laa-ee-an. He Himself is all-pervading; He Himself is absorbed in the profound state of Samaadhi.
DEFINE	para 41855	Awpy hI aupdysdw gurmuiK pqIAweIAnu ] (956-17, rwmklI, mÚ 1) aapay hee updaysdaa gurmukh patee-aa-ee-an. He Himself instructs; the Gurmukh is satisfied and fulfilled.
DEFINE	para 41856	ieik Awpy auJiV pwieAnu ieik BgqI lwieAnu ] (956-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) ik aapay ujharh paa-i-an ik bhagtee laa-i-an. Some, He causes to wander in the wilderness, while others are committed to His devotional worship.
RECORD	para 41857	ijsu Awip buJwey so buJsI Awpy nwie lweIAnu ] (956-18, rwmklI, mÚ 1) jis aap bujhaa-ay so bujhsee aapay naa-ay laa-ee-an. He alone understands, whom the Lord causes to understand; He Himself attaches mortals to His Name.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v21	nwnk nwmu iDAweIAY scI vifAweI ]21]1] suDu ] (956-19, rwmklI, mÚ 1) naanak naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai sachee vadi-aa-ee. ||21||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 3 v21	1|| suDh. O Nanak, meditating on the Naam, the Name of the Lord, true greatness is obtained. ||21||1|| Sudh||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 (957-1)
RECORD	para 41860	raamkalee kee vaar mehlaa 5 Vaar Of Raamkalee, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 41861	<> siqgur pRswid ] (957-1) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	para 41862	slok mÚ 5 ] (957-2) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 41863	jYsw siqguru suxIdw qYso hI mY fITu ] (957-2, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jaisaa satgur suneedaa taiso hee mai deeth. As I have heard of the True Guru, so I have seen Him.
DEFINE	para 41864	ivCuiVAw myly pRBU hir drgh kw bsITu ] (957-2, rwmklI, mÚ 5) vichhurhi-aa maylay parabhoo har dargeh kaa baseeth. He re-unites the separated ones with God; He is the Mediator at the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	para 41865	hir nwmo mMqRü idRVwiedw kty haumY rogu ] (957-3, rwmklI, mÚ 5) har naamo mantar darirhaa-idaa katay ha-umai rog. He implants the Mantra of the Lord's Name, and eradicates the illness of egotism.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	nwnk siqguru iqnw imlwieAw ijnw Dury pieAw sMjogu ]1] (957-3, rwmklI, mÚ 5) naanak satgur tinaa milaa-i-aa jinaa Dhuray pa-i-aa sanjog. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	O Nanak, he alone meets the True Guru, who has such union pre-ordained. ||1||
RECORD	para 41867	mÚ 5 ] (957-4) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41868	ieku sjxu siB sjxw ieku vYrI siB vwid ] (957-4, rwmklI, mÚ 5) ik sajan sabh sajnaa ik vairee sabh vaad. If the One Lord is my Friend, then all are my friends. If the One Lord is my enemy, then all fight with me.
DEFINE	para 41869	guir pUrY dyKwilAw ivxu nwvY sB bwid ] (957-4, rwmklI, mÚ 5) gur poorai daykhaali-aa vin naavai sabh baad. The Perfect Guru has shown me that, without the Name, everything is useless.
DEFINE	para 41870	swkq durjn BrimAw jo lgy dUjY swid ] (957-5, rwmklI, mÚ 5) saakat durjan bharmi-aa jo lagay doojai saad. The faithless cynics and the evil people wander in reincarnation; they are attached to other tastes.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	jn nwnik hir pRBu buiJAw gur siqgur kY prswid ]2] (957-5, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jan naanak har parabh bujhi-aa gur satgur kai parsaad. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	Servant Nanak has realized the Lord God, by the Grace of the Guru, the True Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 41872	pauVI ] (957-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 41873	QtxhwrY Qwtu Awpy hI QitAw ] (957-6, rwmklI, mÚ 5) thatanhaarai thaat aapay hee thati-aa. The Creator Lord created the Creation.
DEFINE	para 41874	Awpy pUrw swhu Awpy hI KitAw ] (957-6, rwmklI, mÚ 5) aapay pooraa saahu aapay hee khati-aa. He Himself is the perfect Banker; He Himself earns His profit.
DEFINE	para 41875	Awpy kir pwswru Awpy rMg ritAw ] (957-6, rwmklI, mÚ 5) aapay kar paasaar aapay rang rati-aa. He Himself made the expansive Universe; He Himself is imbued with joy.
RECORD	para 41876	kudriq kIm n pwie AlK bRhmitAw ] (957-7, rwmklI, mÚ 5) kudrat keem na paa-ay alakh barahmati-aa. The value of God's almighty creative power cannot be estimated.
DEFINE	para 41877	Agm AQwh byAMq prY pritAw ] (957-7, rwmklI, mÚ 5) agam athaah bay-ant parai parti-aa. He is inaccessible, unfathomable, endless, the farthest of the far.
DEFINE	para 41878	Awpy vf pwiqswhu Awip vjIritAw ] (957-8, rwmklI, mÚ 5) aapay vad paatisaahu aap vajeerti-aa. He Himself is the greatest Emperor; He Himself is His own Prime Minister.
RECORD	para 41879	koie n jwxY kIm kyvfu mitAw ] (957-8, rwmklI, mÚ 5) ko-ay na jaanai keem kayvad mati-aa. No one knows His worth, or the greatness of His resting place.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	scw swihbu Awip gurmuiK prgitAw ]1] (957-8, rwmklI, mÚ 5) sachaa saahib aap gurmukh pargati-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	He Himself is our True Lord and Master. He reveals Himself to the Gurmukh. ||1||
RECORD	para 41881	sloku mÚ 5 ] (957-9) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 41882	suix sjx pRIqm myirAw mY siqguru dyhu idKwil ] (957-9, rwmklI, mÚ 5) sun sajan pareetam mayri-aa mai satgur dayh dikhaal. Listen, O my beloved friend: please show me the True Guru.
RECORD	para 41883	hau iqsu dyvw mnu Awpxw inq ihrdY rKw smwil ] (957-9, rwmklI, mÚ 5) ha-o tis dayvaa man aapnaa nit hirdai rakhaa samaal. I dedicate my mind to Him; I keep Him continually enshrined within my heart.
DEFINE	para 41884	ieksu siqgur bwhrw iDRgu jIvxu sMswir ] (957-10, rwmklI, mÚ 5) ikas satgur baahraa Dharig jeevan sansaar. Without the One and Only True Guru, life in this world is cursed.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	jn nwnk siqguru iqnw imlwieEnu ijn sd hI vrqY nwil ]1] (957-10, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jan naanak satgur tinaa milaa-i-on jin sad hee vartai naal. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	O servant Nanak, they alone meet the True Guru, with whom He constantly abides. ||1||
RECORD	para 41886	mÚ 5 ] (957-11) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41887	myrY AMqir locw imlx kI ikau pwvw pRB qoih ] (957-11, rwmklI, mÚ 5) mayrai antar lochaa milan kee ki-o paavaa parabh tohi. Deep within me is the longing to meet You; how can I find You, God?
RECORD	para 41888	koeI AYsw sjxu loiV lhu jo myly pRIqmu moih ] (957-12, rwmklI, mÚ 5) ko-ee aisaa sajan lorh lahu jo maylay pareetam mohi. I will search for someone, some friend, who will unite me with my Beloved.
RECORD	para 41889	guir pUrY mylwieAw jq dyKw qq soie ] (957-12, rwmklI, mÚ 5) gur poorai maylaa-i-aa jat daykhaa tat so-ay. The Perfect Guru has united me with Him; wherever I look, there He is.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	jn nwnk so pRBu syivAw iqsu jyvfu Avru n koie ]2] (957-13, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jan naanak so parabh sayvi-aa tis jayvad avar na ko-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	Servant Nanak serves that God; there is no other as great as He is. ||2||
RECORD	para 41891	pauVI ] (957-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41892	dyvxhwru dwqwru ikqu muiK swlwhIAY ] (957-13, rwmklI, mÚ 5) dayvanhaar daataar kit mukh salaahee-ai. He is the Great Giver, the Generous Lord; with what mouth can I praise Him?
RECORD	para 41893	ijsu rKY ikrpw Dwir irjku smwhIAY ] (957-14, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jis rakhai kirpaa Dhaar rijak samaahee-ai. In His Mercy, He protects, preserves and sustains us.
DEFINE	para 41894	koie n iks hI vis sBnw iek Dr ] (957-14, rwmklI, mÚ 5) ko-ay na kis hee vas sabhnaa ik Dhar. No one is under anyone else's control; He is the One Support of all.
RECORD	para 41895	pwly bwlk vwig dy kY Awip kr ] (957-15, rwmklI, mÚ 5) paalay baalak vaag day kai aap kar. He cherishes all as His children, and reaches out with His hand.
RECORD	para 41896	krdw And ibnod ikCU n jwxIAY ] (957-15, rwmklI, mÚ 5) kardaa anad binod kichhoo na jaanee-ai. He stages His joyous plays, which no one understands at all.
RECORD	para 41897	srb Dwr smrQ hau iqsu kurbwxIAY ] (957-15, rwmklI, mÚ 5) sarab Dhaar samrath ha-o tis kurbaanee-ai. The all-powerful Lord gives His Support to all; I am a sacrifice to Him.
DEFINE	para 41898	gweIAY rwiq idnµqu gwvx joigAw ] (957-16, rwmklI, mÚ 5) gaa-ee-ai raat dinant gaavan jogi-aa. Night and day, sing the Praises of the One who is worthy of being praised.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	jo gur kI pYrI pwih iqnI hir rsu BoigAw ]2] (957-16, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jo gur kee pairee paahi tinee har ras bhogi-aa. ||2||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	Those who fall at the Guru's Feet, enjoy the sublime essence of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 41900	slok mÚ 5 ] (957-17) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 41901	BIVhu moklweI kIqIAnu sB rKy kutMbY nwil ] (957-17, rwmklI, mÚ 5) bheerhahu moklaa-ee keetee-an sabh rakhay kutambi naal. He has widened the narrow path for me, and preserved my integrity, along with that of my family.
RECORD	para 41902	kwrj Awip svwirAnu so pRB sdw sBwil ] (957-17, rwmklI, mÚ 5) kaaraj aap savaari-an so parabh sadaa sabhaal. He Himself has arranged and resolved my affairs. I dwell upon that God forever.
RECORD	para 41903	pRBu mwq ipqw kMiT lwiedw lhuVy bwlk pwil ] (957-18, rwmklI, mÚ 5) parabh maat pitaa kanth laa-idaa lahurhay baalak paal. God is my mother and father; He hugs me close in His embrace, and cherishes me, like His tiny baby.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	dieAwl hoey sB jIA jMqR hir nwnk ndir inhwl ]1] (957-18, rwmklI, mÚ 5) da-i-aal ho-ay sabh jee-a jantar har naanak nadar nihaal. ||1||
UPHOLD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	All beings and creatures have become kind and compassionate to me. O Nanak, the Lord has blessed me with His Glance of Grace. ||1||
RECORD	para 41906	mÚ 5 ] (958-1) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41907	ivxu quDu horu ij mMgxw isir duKw kY duK ] (958-1, rwmklI, mÚ 5) vin tuDh hor je mangnaa sir dukhaa kai dukh. To ask for any other than You, Lord, is the most miserable of miseries.
ALLOW	para 41908	dyih nwmu sMqoKIAw auqrY mn kI BuK ] (958-1, rwmklI, mÚ 5) deh naam santokhee-aa utrai man kee bhukh. Please bless me with Your Name, and make me content; may the hunger of my mind be satisfied.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	guir vxu iqxu hirAw kIiqAw nwnk ikAw mnuK ]2] (958-2, rwmklI, mÚ 5) gur van tin hari-aa keeti-aa naanak ki-aa manukh. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	The Guru has made the woods and meadows green again. O Nanak, is it any wonder that He blesses human beings as well? ||2||
RECORD	para 41910	pauVI ] (958-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
ALLOW	para 41911	so AYsw dwqwru mnhu n vIsrY ] (958-2, rwmklI, mÚ 5) so aisaa daataar manhu na veesrai. Such is that Great Giver; may I never forget Him from my mind.
RECORD	para 41912	GVI n muhqu csw iqsu ibnu nw srY ] (958-3, rwmklI, mÚ 5) gharhee na muhat chasaa tis bin naa sarai. I cannot survive without Him, for an instant, for a moment, for a second.
DEFINE	para 41913	AMqir bwhir sMig ikAw ko luik krY ] (958-3, rwmklI, mÚ 5) antar baahar sang ki-aa ko luk karai. Inwardly and outwardly, He is with us; how can we hide anything from Him?
RECORD	para 41914	ijsu piq rKY Awip so Bvjlu qrY ] (958-4, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jis pat rakhai aap so bhavjal tarai. One whose honor He Himself has preserved, crosses over the terrifying world-ocean.
DEFINE	para 41915	Bgqu igAwnI qpw ijsu ikrpw krY ] (958-4, rwmklI, mÚ 5) bhagat gi-aanee tapaa jis kirpaa karai. He alone is a devotee, a spiritual teacher, and a disciplined pratictioner of meditation, whom the Lord has so blessed.
DEFINE	para 41916	so pUrw prDwnu ijs no blu DrY ] (958-4, rwmklI, mÚ 5) so pooraa parDhaan jis no bal Dharai. He alone is perfect and renowned as supreme, whom the Lord has blessed with His power.
RECORD	para 41917	ijsih jrwey Awip soeI Ajru jrY ] (958-5, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jisahi jaraa-ay aap so-ee ajar jarai. He alone endures the unendurable, whom the Lord inspires to endure it.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v3	iqs hI imilAw scu mMqRü gur min DrY ]3] (958-5, rwmklI, mÚ 5) tis hee mili-aa sach mantar gur man Dharai. ||3||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v3	And he alone meets the True Lord, within whose mind the Guru's Mantra is implanted. ||3||
RECORD	para 41919	sloku mÚ 5 ] (958-6) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41920	DMnu su rwg surMgVy Awlwpq sB iqK jwie ] (958-6, rwmklI, mÚ 5) Dhan so raag surangrhay aalaapat sabh tikh jaa-ay. Blessed are those beautiful Ragas which, when chanted, quench all thirst.
DEFINE	para 41921	DMnu su jMq suhwvVy jo gurmuiK jpdy nwau ] (958-6, rwmklI, mÚ 5) Dhan so jant suhaavrhay jo gurmukh japday naa-o. Blessed are those beautiful people who, as Gurmukh, chant the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 41922	ijnI iek min ieku ArwiDAw iqn sd bilhwrY jwau ] (958-7, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jinee ik man ik araaDhi-aa tin sad balihaarai jaa-o. I am a sacrifice to those who single-mindedly worship and adore the One Lord.
DEFINE	para 41923	iqn kI DUiV hm bwCdy krmI plY pwie ] (958-7, rwmklI, mÚ 5) tin kee Dhoorh ham baachh-day karmee palai paa-ay. I yearn for the dust of their feet; by His Grace, it is obtained.
DEFINE	para 41924	jo rqy rMig goivd kY hau iqn bilhwrY jwau ] (958-8, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jo ratay rang govid kai ha-o tin balihaarai jaa-o. I am a sacrifice to those who are imbued with love for the Lord of the Universe.
ALLOW	para 41925	AwKw ibrQw jIA kI hir sjxu mylhu rwie ] (958-8, rwmklI, mÚ 5) aakhaa birthaa jee-a kee har sajan maylhu raa-ay. I tell them the state of my soul, and pray that I may be united with the Sovereign Lord King, my Friend.
RECORD	para 41926	guir pUrY mylwieAw jnm mrx duKu jwie ] (958-9, rwmklI, mÚ 5) gur poorai maylaa-i-aa janam maran dukh jaa-ay. The Perfect Guru has united me with Him, and the pains of birth and death have departed.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	jn nwnk pwieAw Agm rUpu Anq n kwhU jwie ]1] (958-9, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jan naanak paa-i-aa agam roop anat na kaahoo jaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	Servant Nanak has found the inaccessible, infinitely beautiful Lord, and he will not go anywhere else. ||1||
RECORD	para 41928	mÚ 5 ] (958-10) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41929	DMnu su vylw GVI DMnu Dnu mUrqu plu swru ] (958-10, rwmklI, mÚ 5) Dhan so vaylaa gharhee Dhan Dhan moorat pal saar. Blessed is that time, blessed is that hour, blessed is that second, excellent is that instant;
WHEN	para 41930	DMnu su idnsu sMjogVw ijqu ifTw gur drswru ] (958-10, rwmklI, mÚ 5) Dhan so dinas sanjogrhaa jit dithaa gur darsaar. blessed is that day, and that opportunity, when I gazed upon the Blessed Vision of the Guru's Darshan.
DEFINE	para 41931	mn kIAw ieCw pUrIAw hir pwieAw Agm Apwru ] (958-11, rwmklI, mÚ 5) man kee-aa ichhaa pooree-aa har paa-i-aa agam apaar. The mind's desires are fulfilled, when the inaccessible, unfathomable Lord is obtained.
DEFINE	para 41932	haumY qutw mohVw ieku scu nwmu AwDwru ] (958-11, rwmklI, mÚ 5) ha-umai tutaa mohrhaa ik sach naam aaDhaar. Egotism and emotional attachment are eradicated, and one leans only on the Support of the True Name.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	jnu nwnku lgw syv hir auDirAw sgl sMswru ]2] (958-12, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jan naanak lagaa sayv har uDhri-aa sagal sansaar. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	O servant Nanak, one who is committed to the Lord's service - the whole world is saved along with him. ||2||
RECORD	para 41934	pauVI ] (958-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41935	isPiq slwhxu Bgiq ivrly idqIAnu ] (958-12, rwmklI, mÚ 5) sifat salaahan bhagat virlay ditee-an. How rare are those who are blessed to praise the Lord, in devotional worship.
DEFINE	para 41936	saupy ijsu BMfwr iPir puC n lIqIAnu ] (958-13, rwmklI, mÚ 5) sa-upay jis bhandaar fir puchh na leetee-an. Those who are blessed with the Lord's treasures are not called to give their account again.
DEFINE	para 41937	ijs no lgw rMgu sy rMig riqAw ] (958-13, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jis no lagaa rang say rang rati-aa. Those who are imbued with His Love are absorbed in ecstasy.
DEFINE	para 41938	Enw ieko nwmu ADwru iekw aun BiqAw ] (958-14, rwmklI, mÚ 5) onaa iko naam aDhaar ikaa un bhati-aa. They take the Support of the One Name; the One Name is their only food.
RECORD	para 41939	Enw ipCY jgu BuMcY BogeI ] (958-14, rwmklI, mÚ 5) onaa pichhai jag bhunchai bhog-ee. For their sake, the world eats and enjoys.
RECORD	para 41940	Enw ipAwrw rbu Enwhw jogeI ] (958-14, rwmklI, mÚ 5) onaa pi-aaraa rab onaahaa jog-ee. Their Beloved Lord belongs to them alone.
RECORD	para 41941	ijsu imilAw guru Awie iqin pRBu jwixAw ] (958-15, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jis mili-aa gur aa-ay tin parabh jaani-aa. The Guru comes and meets them; they alone know God.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v4	hau bilhwrI iqn ij KsmY BwixAw ]4] (958-15, rwmklI, mÚ 5) ha-o balihaaree tin je khasmai bhaani-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v4	I am a sacrifice to those who are pleasing to their Lord and Master. ||4||
RECORD	para 41943	slok mÚ 5 ] (958-16) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41944	hir ieksY nwil mY dosqI hir ieksY nwil mY rMgu ] (958-16, rwmklI, mÚ 5) har iksai naal mai dostee har iksai naal mai rang. My friendship is with the One Lord alone; I am in love with the One Lord alone.
DEFINE	para 41945	hir ieko myrw sjxo hir ieksY nwil mY sMgu ] (958-16, rwmklI, mÚ 5) har iko mayraa sajno har iksai naal mai sang. The Lord is my only friend; my companionship is with the One Lord alone.
DEFINE	para 41946	hir ieksY nwil mY gosty muhu mYlw krY n BMgu ] (958-17, rwmklI, mÚ 5) har iksai naal mai gostay muhu mailaa karai na bhang. My conversation is with the One Lord alone; He never frowns, or turns His face away.
RECORD	para 41947	jwxY ibrQw jIA kI kdy n moVY rMgu ] (958-17, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jaanai birthaa jee-a kee kaday na morhai rang. He alone knows the state of my soul; He never ignores my love.
DEFINE	para 41948	hir ieko myrw mslqI BMnx GVn smrQu ] (958-18, rwmklI, mÚ 5) har iko mayraa maslatee bhannan gharhan samrath. He is my only counselor, all-powerful to destroy and create.
DEFINE	para 41949	hir ieko myrw dwqwru hY isir dwiqAw jg hQu ] (958-18, rwmklI, mÚ 5) har iko mayraa daataar hai sir daati-aa jag hath. The Lord is my only Giver. He places His hand upon the heads of the generous in the world.
DEFINE	para 41950	hir ieksY dI mY tyk hY jo isir sBnw smrQu ] (958-19, rwmklI, mÚ 5) har iksai dee mai tayk hai jo sir sabhnaa samrath. I take the Support of the One Lord alone; He is all-powerful, over the heads of all.
RECORD	para 41951	siqguir sMqu imlwieAw msqik Dir kY hQu ] (958-19, rwmklI, mÚ 5) satgur sant milaa-i-aa mastak Dhar kai hath. The Saint, the True Guru, has united me with the Lord. He placed His hand on my forehead.
RECORD	para 41953	vfw swihbu gurU imlwieAw ijin qwirAw sgl jgqu ] (959-1, rwmklI, mÚ 5) vadaa saahib guroo milaa-i-aa jin taari-aa sagal jagat. The Guru led me to meet the greatest Lord and Master; He saved the whole world.
DEFINE	para 41954	mn kIAw ieCw pUrIAw pwieAw Duir sMjog ] (959-1, rwmklI, mÚ 5) man kee-aa ichhaa pooree-aa paa-i-aa Dhur sanjog. The desires of the mind are fulfilled; I have attained my pre-destined Union with God.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	nwnk pwieAw scu nwmu sd hI Bogy Bog ]1] (959-2, rwmklI, mÚ 5) naanak paa-i-aa sach naam sad hee bhogay bhog. ||1||
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v1	Nanak has obtained the True Name; He enjoys the enjoyments forever. ||1||
RECORD	para 41956	mÚ 5 ] (959-2) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 41957	mnmuKw kyrI dosqI mwieAw kw snbMDu ] (959-2, rwmklI, mÚ 5) manmukhaa kayree dostee maa-i-aa kaa san-banDh. Friendship with the self-willed manmukhs is an alliance with Maya.
RECORD	para 41958	vyKidAw hI Bij jwin kdy n pwiein bMDu ] (959-3, rwmklI, mÚ 5) vaykh-di-aa hee bhaj jaan kaday na paa-in banDh. As we watch, they run away; they never stand firm.
RECORD	para 41959	ijcru pYnin Kwvn@y iqcru rKin gMFu ] (959-3, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jichar painan khaavn Hay tichar rakhan gandh. As long as they get food and clothing, they stick around.
WHEN	para 41960	ijqu idin ikCu n hoveI iqqu idin bolin gMDu ] (959-4, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jit din kichh na hova-ee tit din bolan ganDh. But on that day when they receive nothing, then they start to curse.
DEFINE	para 41961	jIA kI swr n jwxnI mnmuK AigAwnI AMDu ] (959-4, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jee-a kee saar na jaannee manmukh agi-aanee anDh. The self-willed manmukhs are ignorant and blind; they do not know the secrets of the soul.
DEFINE	para 41962	kUVw gMFu n cleI ickiV pQr bMDu ] (959-5, rwmklI, mÚ 5) koorhaa gandh na chal-ee chikarh pathar banDh. The false bond does not last; it is like stones joined with mud.
DEFINE	para 41963	AMDy Awpu n jwxnI PkVu iptin DMDu ] (959-5, rwmklI, mÚ 5) anDhay aap na jaannee fakarh pitan DhanDh. The blind do not understand themselves; they are engrossed in false worldly entanglements.
RECORD	para 41964	JUTY moih lptwieAw hau hau krq ibhMDu ] (959-6, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jhoothai mohi laptaa-i-aa ha-o ha-o karat bihanDh. Entangled in false attachments, they pass their lives in egotism and self-conceit.
UPHOLD	para 41965	ik®pw kry ijsu AwpxI Duir pUrw krmu kryie ] (959-6, rwmklI, mÚ 5) kirpaa karay jis aapnee Dhur pooraa karam karay-i. But that being, whom the Lord has blessed with His Mercy from the very beginning, does perfect deeds, and accumulates good karma.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	jn nwnk sy jn aubry jo siqgur srix pry ]2] (959-7, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jan naanak say jan ubray jo satgur saran paray. ||2||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v2	O servant Nanak, those humble beings alone are saved, who enter the Sanctuary of the True Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 41967	pauVI ] (959-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 41968	jo rqy dIdwr syeI scu hwku ] (959-7, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jo ratay deedaar say-ee sach haak. Those who are imbued with the Lord's Vision, speak the Truth.
RECORD	para 41969	ijnI jwqw Ksmu ikau lBY iqnw Kwku ] (959-7, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jinee jaataa khasam ki-o labhai tinaa khaak. How can I obtain the dust of those who realize their Lord and Master?
RECORD	para 41970	mnu mYlw vykwru hovY sMig pwku ] (959-8, rwmklI, mÚ 5) man mailaa vaykaar hovai sang paak. The mind, stained by corruption, becomes pure by associating with them.
DEFINE	para 41971	idsY scw mhlu KulY Brm qwku ] (959-8, rwmklI, mÚ 5) disai sachaa mahal khulai bharam taak. One sees the Mansion of the Lord's Presence, when the door of doubt is opened.
DEFINE	para 41972	ijsih idKwly mhlu iqsu n imlY Dwku ] (959-9, rwmklI, mÚ 5) jisahi dikhaalay mahal tis na milai Dhaak. That one, unto whom the Mansion of the Lord's Presence is revealed, is never pushed or shoved.
DEFINE	para 41973	mnu qnu hoie inhwlu ibMdk ndir Jwku ] (959-9, rwmklI, mÚ 5) man tan ho-ay nihaal bindak nadar jhaak. My mind and body are enraptured, when the Lord blesses me, even for an instant, with His Glance of Grace.
DEFINE	para 41974	nau iniD nwmu inDwnu gur kY sbid lwgu ] (959-9, rwmklI, mÚ 5) na-o niDh naam niDhaan gur kai sabad laag. The nine treasures, and the treasure of the Naam are obtained by commitment to the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v5	iqsY imlY sMq Kwku msqik ijsY Bwgu ]5] (959-10, rwmklI, mÚ 5) tisai milai sant khaak mastak jisai bhaag. ||5||
DEFINE	rwmklI kI vwr mhlw 5 v5	He alone is blessed with the dust of the feet of the Saints, upon whose forehead such pre-ordained desiny is inscribed. ||5||
RECORD	para 41976	slok mÚ 5 ] (959-10) salok mehlaa 5. Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 41977	hrxwKI kU scu vYxu suxweI jo qau kry auDwrxu ] (959-11, rwmklI, mÚ 5) harnaakhee koo sach vain sunaa-ee jo ta-o karay uDhaaran. O deer-eyed bride, I speak the Truth, which shall save you.
RECORD	para 41978	suMdr bcn qum suxhu CbIlI ipru qYfw mn swDwrxu ] (959-11, rwmklI, mÚ 5) sundar bachan tum sunhu chhabeelee pir taidaa man saaDhaaran. Listen to these beautiful words, O beauteous bride; your Beloved Lord is your mind's only support.
RECORD	para 41979	durjn syqI nyhu rcwieE dis ivKw mY kwrxu ] (959-12, rwmklI, mÚ 5) durjan saytee nayhu rachaa-i-o das vikhaa mai kaaran. You have fallen in love with an evil person; tell me - show me why!
RECORD	para 41980	aUxI nwhI JUxI nwhI nwhI iksY ivhUxI ] (959-12, rwmklI, mÚ 5) oonee naahee jhoonee naahee naahee kisai vihoonee. I lack nothing, and I am not sad or depressed; I have no deficiency at all.
