RECORD	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v4	gurmqI jgjIvnu min vsY siB kul auDwrxhwr ]4] (1009-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmatee jagjeevan man vasai sabh kul uDhaaranhaar. ||4||
WHEN	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v4	When he follows the Guru's Teachings, and enshrines the Lord, the Life of the World, within his mind, he redeems all his generations. ||4||
DEFINE	para 43986	scw vKru nwmu hY scw vwpwrw ] (1009-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) sachaa vakhar naam hai sachaa vaapaaraa. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is the true object, the true commodity.
DEFINE	para 43987	lwhw nwmu sMswir hY gurmqI vIcwrw ] (1009-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) laahaa naam sansaar hai gurmatee veechaaraa. The Naam is the only true profit in this world. Follow the Guru's Teachings, and contemplate it.
RECORD	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v5	dUjY Bwie kwr kmwvxI inq qotw sYswrw ]5] (1009-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) doojai bhaa-ay kaar kamaavnee nit totaa saisaaraa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v5	To work in the love of duality, brings constant loss in this world. ||5||
RECORD	para 43989	swcI sMgiq Qwnu scu scy Gr bwrw ] scw Bojnu Bwau scu scu nwmu ADwrw ] (1009-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachee sangat thaan sach sachay ghar baaraa. sachaa bhojan bhaa-o sach sach naam aDhaaraa. True is one's association, true is one's place, and true is one's hearth and home, when one has the support of the Naam.
RECORD	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v6	scI bwxI sMqoiKAw scw sbdu vIcwrw ]6] (1009-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) sachee banee santokhi-aa sachaa sabad veechaaraa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v6	Contemplating the True Word of the Guru's Bani, and the True Word of the Shabad, one becomes content. ||6||
REQUIRE	para 43991	rs Bogx pwiqswhIAw duK suK sMGwrw ] (1009-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) ras bhogan paatisaahee-aa dukh sukh sanghaaraa. Enjoying princely pleasures, one shall be destroyed in pain and pleasure.
RECORD	para 43992	motw nwau DrweIAY gil Aaugx Bwrw ] (1009-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) motaa naa-o Dharaa-ee-ai gal a-ugan bhaaraa. Adopting a name of greatness, one strings heavy sins around his neck.
RECORD	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v7	mwxs dwiq n hoveI qU dwqw swrw ]7] (1009-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) maanas daat na hova-ee too daataa saaraa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v7	Mankind cannot give gifts; You alone are the Giver of everything. ||7||
DEFINE	para 43994	Agm Agocru qU DxI Aivgqu Apwrw ] (1009-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) agam agochar too Dhanee avigat apaaraa. You are inaccessible and unfathomable; O Lord, You are imperishable and infinite.
RECORD	para 43995	gur sbdI dru joeIAY mukqy BMfwrw ] (1009-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur sabdee dar jo-ee-ai muktay bhandaaraa. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, seeking at the Lord's Door, one finds the treasure of liberation.
RECORD	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v8	nwnk mylu n cUkeI swcy vwpwrw ]8]1] (1009-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak mayl na chook-ee saachay vaapaaraa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU AstpdIAw mhlw 1 Gru 1 v8	1|| O Nanak, this union is not broken, if one deals in the merchandise of Truth. ||8||1||
DEFINE	para 43998	ibKu boihQw lwidAw dIAw smuMd mMJwir ] (1009-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) bikh bohithaa laadi-aa dee-aa samund manjhaar. The boat is loaded with sin and corruption, and launched into the sea.
RECORD	para 43999	kMDI idis n AwveI nw aurvwru n pwru ] (1009-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) kanDhee dis na aavee naa urvaar na paar. The shore cannot be seen on this side, nor on the shore beyond.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	vMJI hwiQ n KyvtU jlu swgru Asrwlu ]1] (1009-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) vanjhee haath na khayvtoo jal saagar asraal. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	There are no oars, nor any boatmen, to cross over the terrifying world-ocean. ||1||
DEFINE	para 44001	bwbw jgu PwQw mhw jwil ] (1009-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) baabaa jag faathaa mahaa jaal. O Baba, the world is caught in the great noose.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	gur prswdI aubry scw nwmu smwil ]1] rhwau ] (1009-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee ubray sachaa naam samaal. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. By Guru's Grace, they are saved, contemplating the True Name. ||1||Pause||
DEFINE	para 44003	siqgurU hY boihQw sbid lµGwvxhwru ] (1009-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) satguroo hai bohithaa sabad langhaavanhaar. The True Guru is the boat; the Word of the Shabad will carry them across.
DEFINE	para 44004	iqQY pvxu n pwvko nw jlu nw Awkwru ] (1009-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) tithai pavan na paavko naa jal naa aakaar. There is neither wind nor fire, neither water nor form there.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	iqQY scw sic nwie Bvjl qwrxhwru ]2] (1009-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) tithai sachaa sach naa-ay bhavjal taaranhaar. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	The True Name of the True Lord is there; it carries them across the terrifying world- ocean. ||2||
RECORD	para 44006	gurmuiK lµGy sy pwir pey scy isau ilv lwie ] (1009-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh langhay say paar pa-ay sachay si-o liv laa-ay. The Gurmukhs reach the shore beyond, lovingly focusing on the True Lord.
DEFINE	para 44007	Awvw gauxu invwirAw joqI joiq imlwie ] (1009-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) aavaa ga-on nivaari-aa jotee jot milaa-ay. Their comings and goings are ended, and their light merges into the Light.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	gurmqI shju aUpjY scy rhY smwie ]3] (1009-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmatee sahj oopjai sachay rahai samaa-ay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Following the Guru's Teachings, intuitive peace wells up within them, and they remain merged in the True Lord. ||3||
ALLOW	para 44009	spu ipVweI pweIAY ibKu AMqir min rosu ] (1009-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) sap pirhaa-ee paa-ee-ai bikh antar man ros. The snake may be locked in a basket, but it is still poisonous, and the anger within its mind remains.
DEFINE	para 44010	pUrib iliKAw pweIAY iks no dIjY dosu ] (1009-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) poorab likhi-aa paa-ee-ai kis no deejai dos. One obtains what is pre-ordained; why does he blame others?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	gurmuiK gwrVu jy suxy mMny nwau sMqosu ]4] (1009-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh gaararh jay sunay mannay naa-o santos. ||4||
WHEN	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	If one, as Gurmukh, hears and believes in the Name, the charm against poison, his mind becomes content. ||4||
DEFINE	para 44012	mwgrmCu PhweIAY kuMfI jwlu vqwie ] (1009-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) maagarmachh fahaa-ee-ai kundee jaal vataa-ay. The crocodile is caught by the hook and line;
RECORD	para 44013	durmiq PwQw PwhIAY iPir iPir pCoqwie ] (1009-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) durmat faathaa faa-ee-ai fir fir pachhotaa-ay. caught in the trap of evil-mindedness, he regrets and repents, again and again.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	jMmx mrxu n suJeI ikrqu n myitAw jwie ]5] (1009-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaman maran na sujh-ee kirat na mayti-aa jaa-ay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	He does not understand birth and death; the inscription of one's past actions cannot be erased. ||5||
RECORD	para 44015	haumY ibKu pwie jgqu aupwieAw sbdu vsY ibKu jwie ] (1009-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai bikh paa-ay jagat upaa-i-aa sabad vasai bikh jaa-ay. Injecting the poison of egotism, the world was created; with the Shabad enshrined within, the poison is eliminated.
RECORD	para 44016	jrw joih n skeI sic rhY ilv lwie ] (1009-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaraa johi na sak-ee sach rahai liv laa-ay. Old age cannot torment one who remains lovingly absorbed in the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	jIvn mukqu so AwKIAY ijsu ivchu haumY jwie ]6] (1009-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) jeevan mukat so aakhee-ai jis vichahu ha-umai jaa-ay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	He alone is called Jivan-Mikta, liberated while yet alive, from within whom egotism is eradicated. ||6||
RECORD	para 44019	DMDY Dwvq jgu bwiDAw nw bUJY vIcwru ] (1010-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) DhanDhai Dhaavat jag baaDhi-aa naa boojhai veechaar. The world is chasing after worldly affairs; caught and bound, it does not understand contemplative meditation.
RECORD	para 44020	jMmx mrxu ivswirAw mnmuK mugDu gvwru ] (1010-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaman maran visaari-aa manmukh mugaDh gavaar. The foolish, ignorant, self-willed manmukh has forgotten birth and death.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	guir rwKy sy aubry scw sbdu vIcwir ]7] (1010-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur raakhay say ubray sachaa sabad veechaar. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	Those whom the Guru has protected are saved, contemplating the True Word of the Shabad. ||7||
RECORD	para 44022	sUhtu ipMjir pRym kY bolY bolxhwru ] (1010-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) soohat pinjar paraym kai bolai bolanhaar. In the cage of divine love, the parrot, speaks.
RECORD	para 44023	scu cugY AMimRqu pIAY aufY q eykw vwr ] (1010-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach chugai amrit pee-ai udai ta aykaa vaar. It pecks at the Truth, and drinks in the Ambrosial Nectar; it flies away, only once.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	guir imilAY Ksmu pCwxIAY khu nwnk moK duAwru ]8]2] (1010-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur mili-ai khasam pachhaanee-ai kaho naanak mokh du-aar. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	2|| Meeting with the Guru, one recognizes his Lord and Master; says Nanak, he finds the gate of liberation. ||8||2||
RECORD	para 44026	sbid mrY qw mwir mru Bwgo iksu pih jwau ] (1010-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad marai taa maar mar bhaago kis peh jaa-o. One who dies in the Word of the Shabad conquers death; otherwise, where can you run?
DEFINE	para 44027	ijs kY fir BY BwgIAY AMimRqu qw ko nwau ] (1010-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis kai dar bhai bhaagee-ai amrit taa ko naa-o. Through the Fear of God, fear runs away; His Name is Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	mwrih rwKih eyku qU bIjau nwhI Qwau ]1] (1010-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) maareh raakhahi ayk too beeja-o naahee thaa-o. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	You alone kill and protect; except for You, there is no place at all. ||1||
RECORD	para 44029	bwbw mY kucIlu kwcau miqhIn ] (1010-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) baabaa mai kucheel kaacha-o matiheen. O Baba, I am filthy, shallow and totally without understanding.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	nwm ibnw ko kCu nhI guir pUrY pUrI miq kIn ]1] rhwau ] (1010-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam binaa ko kachh nahee gur poorai pooree mat keen. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Without the Naam, no one is anything; the Perfect Guru has made my intellect perfect. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 44031	Avgix suBr gux nhI ibnu gux ikau Gir jwau ] (1010-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) avgan subhar gun nahee bin gun ki-o ghar jaa-o. I am full of faults, and I have no virtue at all. Without virtues, how can I go home?
DEFINE	para 44032	shij sbid suKu aUpjY ibnu Bwgw Dnu nwih ] (1010-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) sahj sabad sukh oopjai bin bhaagaa Dhan naahi. Through the Word of the Shabad, intuitive peace wells up; without good destiny, the wealth is not obtained.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	ijn kY nwmu n min vsY sy bwDy dUK shwih ]2] (1010-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin kai naam na man vasai say baaDhay dookh sahaahi. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Those whose minds are not filled with the Naam are bound and gagged, and suffer in pain. ||2||
RECORD	para 44034	ijnI nwmu ivswirAw sy ikqu Awey sMswir ] (1010-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) jinee naam visaari-aa say kit aa-ay sansaar. Those who have forgotten the Naam - why have they even come into the world?
RECORD	para 44035	AwgY pwCY suKu nhI gwfy lwdy Cwru ] (1010-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) aagai paachhai sukh nahee gaaday laaday chhaar. Here and hereafter, they do not find any peace; they have loaded their carts with ashes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	ivCuiVAw mylw nhI dUKu Gxo jm duAwir ]3] (1010-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) vichhurhi-aa maylaa nahee dookh ghano jam du-aar. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Those who are separated, do not meet with the Lord; they suffer in terrible pain at Death's Door. ||3||
RECORD	para 44037	AgY ikAw jwxw nwih mY BUly qU smJwie ] (1010-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) agai ki-aa jaanaa naahi mai bhoolay too samjhaa-ay. I do not know what will happen in the world hereafter; I am so confused - please teach me, Lord!
RECORD	para 44038	BUly mwrgu jo dsy iqs kY lwgau pwie ] (1010-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhoolay maarag jo dasay tis kai laaga-o paa-ay. I am confused; I would fall at the feet of one who shows me the Way.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	gur ibnu dwqw ko nhI kImiq khxu n jwie ]4] (1010-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur bin daataa ko nahee keemat kahan na jaa-ay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	Without the Guru, there is no giver at all; His value cannot be described. ||4||
WHEN	para 44040	swjnu dyKw qw gil imlw swcu pTwieE lyKu ] (1010-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) saajan daykhaa taa gal milaa saach pathaa-i-o laykh. If I see my friend, then I will embrace Him; I have sent Him the letter of Truth.
RECORD	para 44041	muiK iDmwxY Dn KVI gurmuiK AwKI dyKu ] (1010-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) mukh Dhimaanai Dhan kharhee gurmukh aakhee daykh. His soul-bride stands waiting expectantly; as Gurmukh, I see Him with my eyes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	quDu BwvY qU min vsih ndrI krim ivsyKu ]5] (1010-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) tuDh bhaavai too man vaseh nadree karam visaykh. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	By the Pleasure of Your Will, You abide in my mind, and bless me with Your Glance of Grace. ||5||
DEFINE	para 44043	BUK ipAwso jy BvY ikAw iqsu mwgau dyie ] (1010-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhookh pi-aaso jay bhavai ki-aa tis maaga-o day-ay. One who is wandering hungry and thirsty - what can he give, and what can anyone ask from him?
RECORD	para 44044	bIjau sUJY ko nhI min qin pUrnu dyie ] (1010-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) beeja-o soojhai ko nahee man tan pooran day-ay. I cannot conceive of any other, who can bless my mind and body with perfection.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	ijin kIAw iqin dyiKAw Awip vfweI dyie ]6] (1010-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin kee-aa tin daykhi-aa aap vadaa-ee day-ay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	The One who created me takes care of me; He Himself blesses me with glory. ||6||
DEFINE	para 44046	ngrI nwieku nvqno bwlku lIl AnUpu ] (1010-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) nagree naa-ik navtano baalak leel anoop. In the body-village is my Lord and Master, whose body is ever-new, Innocent and child-like, incomparably playful.
DEFINE	para 44047	nwir n purKu n pMKxU swcau cquru srUpu ] (1010-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) naar na purakh na pankh-noo saacha-o chatur saroop. He is neither a woman, nor a man, nor a bird; the True Lord is so wise and beautiful.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	jo iqsu BwvY so QIAY qU dIpku qU DUpu ]7] (1010-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo tis bhaavai so thee-ai too deepak too Dhoop. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	Whatever pleases Him, happens; You are the lamp, and You are the incense. ||7||
RECORD	para 44049	gIq swd cwKy suxy bwd swd qin rogu ] (1010-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) geet saad chaakhay sunay baad saad tan rog. He hears the songs and tastes the flavors, but these flavors are useless and insipid, and bring only disease to the body.
RECORD	para 44050	scu BwvY swcau cvY CUtY sog ivjogu ] (1010-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach bhaavai saacha-o chavai chhootai sog vijog. One who loves the Truth and speaks the Truth, escapes from the sorrow of separation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	nwnk nwmu n vIsrY jo iqsu BwvY su hogu ]8]3] (1010-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak naam na veesrai jo tis bhaavai so hog. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	3|| Nanak does not forget the Naam; whatever happens is by the Lord's Will. ||8||3||
DEFINE	para 44053	swcI kwr kmwvxI hoir lwlc bwid ] (1010-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachee kaar kamaavnee hor laalach baad. Practice Truth - other greed and attachments are useless.
RECORD	para 44054	iehu mnu swcY moihAw ijhvw sic swid ] (1010-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) ih man saachai mohi-aa jihvaa sach saad. The True Lord has fascinated this mind, and my tongue enjoys the taste of Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	ibnu nwvY ko rsu nhI hoir clih ibKu lwid ]1] (1010-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin naavai ko ras nahee hor chaleh bikh laad. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	Without the Name, there is no juice; the others depart, loaded with poison. ||1||
RECORD	para 44056	AYsw lwlw myry lwl ko suix Ksm hmwry ] (1010-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) aisaa laalaa mayray laal ko sun khasam hamaaray. I am such a slave of Yours, O my Beloved Lord and Master.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	ijau Purmwvih iqau clw scu lwl ipAwry ]1] rhwau ] (1010-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) ji-o furmaaveh ti-o chalaa sach laal pi-aaray. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. I walk in harmony with Your Command, O my True, Sweet Beloved. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 44058	Anidnu lwly cwkrI goly isir mIrw ] (1010-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) an-din laalay chaakree golay sir meeraa. Night and day, the slave works for his overlord.
DEFINE	para 44059	gur bcnI mnu vyicAw sbid mnu DIrw ] (1010-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur bachnee man vaychi-aa sabad man Dheeraa. I have sold my mind for the Word of the Guru's Shabad; my mind is comforted and consoled by the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	gur pUry swbwis hY kwtY mn pIrw ]2] (1011-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur pooray saabaas hai kaatai man peeraa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	The Perfect Guru is honored and celebrated; He has taken away the pains of my mind. ||2||
RECORD	para 44062	lwlw golw DxI ko ikAw khau vifAweIAY ] (1011-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) laalaa golaa Dhanee ko ki-aa kaha-o vadi-aa-ee-ai. I am the servant and slave of my Master; what glorious greatness of His can I describe?
RECORD	para 44063	BwxY bKsy pUrw DxI scu kwr kmweIAY ] (1011-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhaanai bakhsay pooraa Dhanee sach kaar kamaa-ee-ai. The Perfect Master, by the Pleasure of His Will, forgives, and then one practices Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	ivCuiVAw kau myil ley gur kau bil jweIAY ]3] (1011-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) vichhurhi-aa ka-o mayl la-ay gur ka-o bal jaa-ee-ai. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	I am a sacrifice to my Guru, who re-unites the separated ones. ||3||
DEFINE	para 44065	lwly goly miq KrI gur kI miq nIkI ] (1011-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) laalay golay mat kharee gur kee mat neekee. The intellect of His servant and slave is noble and true; it is made so by the Guru's intellect.
DEFINE	para 44066	swcI suriq suhwvxI mnmuK miq PIkI ] (1011-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachee surat suhaavanee manmukh mat feekee. The intuition of those who are true is beautiful; the intellect of the self-willed manmukh is insipid.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	mnu qnu qyrw qU pRBU scu DIrk Dur kI ]4] (1011-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) man tan tayraa too parabhoo sach Dheerak Dhur kee. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	My mind and body belong to You, God; from the very beginning, Truth has been my only support. ||4||
RECORD	para 44068	swcY bYsxu auTxw scu Bojnu BwiKAw ] (1011-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachai baisan uth-naa sach bhojan bhaakhi-aa. In Truth I sit and stand; I eat and speak the Truth.
RECORD	para 44069	iciq scY ivqo scw swcw rsu cwiKAw ] (1011-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) chit sachai vito sachaa saachaa ras chaakhi-aa. With Truth in my consciousness, I gather the wealth of Truth, and drink in the sublime essence of Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	swcY Gir swcY rKy gur bcin suBwiKAw ]5] (1011-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachai ghar saachai rakhay gur bachan subhaakhi-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	In the home of Truth, the True Lord protects me; I speak the Words of the Guru's Teachings with love. ||5||
DEFINE	para 44071	mnmuK kau Awlsu Gxo PwQy EjwVI ] (1011-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh ka-o aalas ghano faathay ojaarhee. The self-willed manmukh is very lazy; he is trapped in the wilderness.
DEFINE	para 44072	PwQw cugY inq cogVI lig bMDu ivgwVI ] (1011-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) faathaa chugai nit chogrhee lag banDh vigaarhee. He is drawn to the bait, and continually pecking at it, he is trapped; his link to the Lord is ruined.
