RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. By Guru's Grace, I am saved, in the Sanctuary of the Lord. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 44086	lwly no isir kwr hY Duir Ksim PurmweI ] (1011-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) laalay no sir kaar hai Dhur khasam furmaa-ee. The slave has been given the most excellent task, by the Primal Command of the Master.
RECORD	para 44087	lwlY hukmu pCwixAw sdw rhY rjweI ] (1011-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) laalai hukam pachhaani-aa sadaa rahai rajaa-ee. The slave realizes the Hukam of His Command, and submits to His Will forever.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Awpy mIrw bKis ley vfI vifAweI ]2] (1011-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay meeraa bakhas la-ay vadee vadi-aa-ee. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	The Lord King Himself grants forgiveness; how glorious is His greatness! ||2||
DEFINE	para 44089	Awip scw sBu scu hY gur sbid buJweI ] (1011-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap sachaa sabh sach hai gur sabad bujhaa-ee. He Himself is True, and everything is True; this is revealed through the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 44090	qyrI syvw so kry ijs no lYih qU lweI ] (1011-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) tayree sayvaa so karay jis no laihi too laa-ee. He alone serves You, whom You have enjoined to do so.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	ibnu syvw iknY n pwieAw dUjY Brim KuAweI ]3] (1011-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin sayvaa kinai na paa-i-aa doojai bharam khu-aa-ee. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Without serving Him, no one finds Him; in duality and doubt, they are ruined. ||3||
RECORD	para 44092	so ikau mnhu ivswrIAY inq dyvY cVY svwieAw ] (1011-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) so ki-o manhu visaaree-ai nit dayvai charhai savaa-i-aa. How could we forget Him from our minds? The gifts which he bestows increase day by day.
RECORD	para 44093	jIau ipMfu sBu iqs dw swhu iqnY ivic pwieAw ] (1011-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) jee-o pind sabh tis daa saahu tinai vich paa-i-aa. Soul and body, all belong to Him; He infused the breath into us.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	jw ik®pw kry qw syvIAY syiv sic smwieAw ]4] (1011-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaa kirpaa karay taa sayvee-ai sayv sach samaa-i-aa. ||4||
WHEN	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	If he shows His Mercy, then we serve Him; serving Him, we merge in Truth. ||4||
DEFINE	para 44095	lwlw so jIvqu mrY mir ivchu Awpu gvwey ] (1011-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) laalaa so jeevat marai mar vichahu aap gavaa-ay. He alone is the Lord's slave, who remains dead while yet alive, and eradicates egotism from within.
DEFINE	para 44096	bMDn qUtih mukiq hoie iqRsnw Agin buJwey ] (1011-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) banDhan tooteh mukat ho-ay tarisnaa agan bujhaa-ay. His bonds are broken, the fire of his desire is quenched, and he is liberated.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	sB mih nwmu inDwnu hY gurmuiK ko pwey ]5] (1011-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabh meh naam niDhaan hai gurmukh ko paa-ay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	The treasure of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, is within all, but how rare are those who, as Gurmukh, obtain it. ||5||
DEFINE	para 44098	lwly ivic guxu ikCu nhI lwlw AvgixAwru ] (1011-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) laalay vich gun kichh nahee laalaa avgani-aar. Within the Lord's slave, there is no virtue at all; the Lord's slave is totally unworthy.
DEFINE	para 44099	quDu jyvfu dwqw ko nhI qU bKsxhwru ] (1011-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) tuDh jayvad daataa ko nahee too bakhsanhaar. There is no Giver as great as You, Lord; You alone are the Forgiver.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	qyrw hukmu lwlw mMny eyh krxI swru ]6] (1011-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) tayraa hukam laalaa mannay ayh karnee saar. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Your slave obeys the Hukam of Your Command; this is the most excellent action. ||6||
DEFINE	para 44101	guru swgru AMimRq sru jo ieCy so Plu pwey ] (1011-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur saagar amrit sar jo ichhay so fal paa-ay. The Guru is the pool of nectar in the world-ocean; whatever one desires, that fruit is obtained.
RECORD	para 44102	nwmu pdwrQu Amru hY ihrdY mMin vswey ] (1011-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam padaarath amar hai hirdai man vasaa-ay. The treasure of the Naam brings immortality; enshrine it in your heart and mind.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	gur syvw sdw suKu hY ijs no hukmu mnwey ]7] (1012-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur sayvaa sadaa sukh hai jis no hukam manaa-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	Serving the Guru, eternal peace is obtained, by those whom the Lord inspires to obey the Hukam of His Command. ||7||
