RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	His perishable body does not remember the Word of the Shabad; like a beast, he fills his belly. ||1||
DEFINE	para 44140	bwbw AYsI rvq rvY sMinAwsI ] (1012-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) baabaa aisee ravat ravai sani-aasee. O Baba, this is the way of life of the Sannyaasi, the renunciate.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	gur kY sbid eyk ilv lwgI qyrY nwim rqy iqRpqwsI ]1] rhwau ] (1012-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kai sabad ayk liv laagee tayrai naam ratay tariptaasee. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	rahaa-o. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, he is to enshrine love for the One Lord. Imbued with Your Name, Lord, he remains satisfied and fulfilled. ||1||Pause||
RECORD	para 44142	GolI gyrU rMgu cVwieAw vsqR ByK ByKwrI ] (1012-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) gholee gayroo rang charhaa-i-aa vastar bhaykh bhaykhaaree. He dyes his robes with saffron dye, and wearing these robes, he goes out begging.
RECORD	para 44143	kwpV Pwir bnweI iKMQw JolI mwieAwDwrI ] (1012-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaaparh faar banaa-ee khinthaa jholee maa-i-aaDhaaree. Tearing his robes, he makes a patched coat, and puts the money in his wallet.
RECORD	para 44144	Gir Gir mwgY jgu prboDY min AMDY piq hwrI ] (1012-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) ghar ghar maagai jag parboDhai man anDhai pat haaree. From house to house he goes begging, and tries to teach the world; but his mind is blind, and so he loses his honor.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Brim Bulwxw sbdu n cInY jUAY bwjI hwrI ]2] (1012-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) bharam bhulaanaa sabad na cheenai joo-ai baajee haaree. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	He is deluded by doubt, and does not remember the Word of the Shabad. He loses his life in the gamble. ||2||
DEFINE	para 44147	AMqir Agin n gur ibnu bUJY bwhir pUAr qwpY ] (1013-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar agan na gur bin boojhai baahar poo-ar taapai. Without the Guru, the fire within is not quenched; and outside, the fire still burns.
RECORD	para 44148	gur syvw ibnu Bgiq n hovI ikau kir cInis AwpY ] (1013-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur sayvaa bin bhagat na hovee ki-o kar cheenas aapai. Without serving the Guru, there is no devotional worship. How can anyone, by himself, know the Lord?
DEFINE	para 44149	inMdw kir kir nrk invwsI AMqir Awqm jwpY ] (1013-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) nindaa kar kar narak nivaasee antar aatam jaapai. Slandering others, one lives in hell; within him is hazy darkness.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	ATsiT qIrQ Brim ivgUcih ikau mlu DopY pwpY ]3] (1013-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) athsath tirath bharam vigoocheh ki-o mal Dhopai paapai. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Wandering to the eixty-eight sacred shrines of pilgrimage, he is ruined. How can the filth of sin be washed away? ||3||
RECORD	para 44151	CwxI Kwku ibBUq cVweI mwieAw kw mgu johY ] (1013-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) chhaanee khaak bibhoot charhaa-ee maa-i-aa kaa mag johai. He sifts through the dust, and applies ashes to his body, but he is searching for the path of Maya's wealth.
WHEN	para 44152	AMqir bwhir eyku n jwxY swcu khy qy CohY ] (1013-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar baahar ayk na jaanai saach kahay tay chhohai. Inwardly and outwardly, he does not know the One Lord; if someone tells him the Truth, he grows angry.
DEFINE	para 44153	pwTu pVY muiK JUTo bolY ingury kI miq EhY ] (1013-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) paath parhai mukh jhootho bolai niguray kee mat ohai. He reads the scriptures, but tells lies; such is the intellect of one who has no guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	nwmu n jpeI ikau suKu pwvY ibnu nwvY ikau sohY ]4] (1013-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam na jap-ee ki-o sukh paavai bin naavai ki-o sohai. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	Without chanting the Naam, how can he find peace? Without the Name, how can he look good? ||4||
RECORD	para 44155	mUMfu mufwie jtw isK bwDI moin rhY AiBmwnw ] (1013-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) moond mudaa-ay jataa sikh baaDhee mon rahai abhimaanaa. Some shave their heads, some keep their hair in matted tangles; some keep it in braids, while some keep silent, filled with egotistical pride.
RECORD	para 44156	mnUAw folY dh ids DwvY ibnu rq Awqm igAwnw ] (1013-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) manoo-aa dolai dah dis Dhaavai bin rat aatam gi-aanaa. Their minds waver and wander in ten directions, without loving devotion and enlightenment of the soul.
WHEN	para 44157	AMimRqu Coif mhw ibKu pIvY mwieAw kw dyvwnw ] (1013-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) amrit chhod mahaa bikh peevai maa-i-aa kaa dayvaanaa. They abandon the Ambrosial Nectar, and drink the deadly poison, driven mad by Maya.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	ikrqu n imteI hukmu n bUJY psUAw mwih smwnw ]5] (1013-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) kirat na mit-ee hukam na boojhai pasoo-aa maahi samaanaa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Past actions cannot be erased; without understanding the Hukam of the Lord's Command, they become beasts. ||5||
RECORD	para 44159	hwQ kmMflu kwpVIAw min iqRsnw aupjI BwrI ] (1013-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) haath kamandal kaaprhee-aa man tarisnaa upjee bhaaree. With bowl in hand, wearing his patched coat, great desires well up in his mind.
RECORD	para 44160	iesqRI qij kir kwim ivAwipAw icqu lwieAw pr nwrI ] (1013-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) istaree taj kar kaam vi-aapi-aa chit laa-i-aa par naaree. Abandoning his own wife, he is engrossed in sexual desire; his thoughts are on the wives of others.
