DEFINE	para 44402	ijqu ijqu lwvih iqqu iqqu lgnw ] (1019-16, mwrU, mÚ 5) jit jit laaveh tit tit lagnaa. Whatever He links us to, to that we are linked.
RECORD	para 44403	kir kir vyKY Apxy jcnw ] (1019-17, mwrU, mÚ 5) kar kar vaykhai apnay jachnaa. He acts, and does, and watches over His Creation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 Gru 8 AMjulIAw v8	nwnk ky pUrn suKdwqy qU dyih q nwmu smwlIAY ]8]1]7] (1019-17, mwrU, mÚ 5) naanak kay pooran sukh-daatay too deh ta naam samaalee-ai. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 5 Gru 8 AMjulIAw v8	You are the Giver of peace, the Perfect Lord of Nanak; as You grant Your blessings, I dwell upon Your Name. ||8||
RECORD	para 44406	ibrKY hyiT siB jMq iekTy ] (1019-18, mwrU, mÚ 5) birkhai hayth sabh jant ikthay. Beneath the tree, all beings have gathered.
DEFINE	para 44407	ieik qqy ieik bolin imTy ] (1019-18, mwrU, mÚ 5) ik tatay ik bolan mithay. Some are hot-headed, and some speak very sweetly.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v1	Asqu audoqu BieAw auiT cly ijau ijau AauD ivhwxIAw ]1] (1019-18, mwrU, mÚ 5) asat udot bha-i-aa uth chalay ji-o ji-o a-oDh vihaanee-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v1	Sunset has come, and they rise up and depart; their days have run their course and expired. ||1||
DEFINE	para 44409	pwp krydV srpr muTy ] (1019-19, mwrU, mÚ 5) paap karaydarh sarpar muthay. Those who committed sins are sure to be ruined.
RECORD	para 44410	AjrweIil PVy PiV kuTy ] (1019-19, mwrU, mÚ 5) ajraa-eel farhay farh kuthay. Azraa-eel, the Angel of Death, seizes and tortures them.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v2	dojik pwey isrjxhwrY lyKw mMgY bwxIAw ]2] (1020-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) dojak paa-ay sirjanhaarai laykhaa mangai baanee-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 5 v2	They are consigned to hell by the Creator Lord, and the Accountant calls them to give their account. ||2||
RECORD	para 44413	sMig n koeI BeIAw bybw ] (1020-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) sang na ko-ee bha-ee-aa baybaa. No brothers or sisters can go with them.
WHEN	para 44414	mwlu jobnu Dnu Coif v\ysw ] (1020-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) maal joban Dhan chhod vanjaysaa. Leaving behind their property, youth and wealth, they march off.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v3	krx krIm n jwqo krqw iql pIVy ijau GwxIAw ]3] (1020-2, mwrU, mÚ 5) karan kareem na jaato kartaa til peerhay ji-o ghaanee-aa. ||3||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 5 v3	They do not know the kind and compassionate Lord; they shall be crushed like sesame seeds in the oil-press. ||3||
RECORD	para 44416	Kuis Kuis lYdw vsqu prweI ] (1020-2, mwrU, mÚ 5) khus khus laidaa vasat paraa-ee. You happily, cheerfully steal the possessions of others,
DEFINE	para 44417	vyKY suxy qyrY nwil KudweI ] (1020-3, mwrU, mÚ 5) vaykhai sunay tayrai naal khudaa-ee. but the Lord God is with you, watching and listening.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v4	dunIAw lib pieAw Kwq AMdir AglI gl n jwxIAw ]4] (1020-3, mwrU, mÚ 5) dunee-aa lab pa-i-aa khaat andar aglee gal na jaanee-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v4	Through worldly greed, you have fallen into the pit; you know nothing of the future. ||4||
REQUIRE	para 44419	jim jim mrY mrY iPir jMmY ] (1020-4, mwrU, mÚ 5) jam jam marai marai fir jammai. You shall be born and born again, and die and die again, only to be reincarnated again.
REQUIRE	para 44420	bhuqu sjwie pieAw dyis lµmY ] (1020-4, mwrU, mÚ 5) bahut sajaa-ay pa-i-aa days lammai. You shall suffer terrible punishment, on your way to the land beyond.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v5	ijin kIqw iqsY n jwxI AMDw qw duKu shY prwxIAw ]5] (1020-4, mwrU, mÚ 5) jin keetaa tisai na jaanee anDhaa taa dukh sahai paraanee-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 5 v5	The mortal does not know the One who created him; he is blind, and so he shall suffer. ||5||
DEFINE	para 44422	Kwlk Qwvhu Bulw muTw ] (1020-5, mwrU, mÚ 5) khaalak thaavhu bhulaa muthaa. Forgetting the Creator Lord, he is ruined.
DEFINE	para 44423	dunIAw Kylu burw ruT quTw ] (1020-5, mwrU, mÚ 5) dunee-aa khayl buraa ruth tuthaa. The drama of the world is bad; it brings sadness and then happiness.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v6	isdku sbUrI sMqu n imilE vqY Awpx BwxIAw ]6] (1020-6, mwrU, mÚ 5) sidak sabooree sant na mili-o vatai aapan bhaanee-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v6	One who does not meet the Saint does not have faith or contentment; he wanders just as he pleases. ||6||
RECORD	para 44425	maulw Kyl kry siB Awpy ] ieik kFy ieik lhir ivAwpy ] (1020-6, mwrU, mÚ 5) ma-ulaa khayl karay sabh aapay. ik kadhay ik lahar vi-aapay. The Lord Himself stages all this drama. Some, he lifts up, and some he throws into the waves.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v7	ijau ncwey iqau iqau ncin isir isir ikrq ivhwxIAw ]7] (1020-7, mwrU, mÚ 5) ji-o nachaa-ay ti-o ti-o nachan sir sir kirat vihaanee-aa. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v7	As He makes them dance, so do they dance. Everyone lives their lives according to their past actions. ||7||
WHEN	para 44427	imhr kry qw Ksmu iDAweI ] (1020-8, mwrU, mÚ 5) mihar karay taa khasam Dhi-aa-ee. When the Lord and Master grants His Grace, then we meditate on Him.
DEFINE	para 44428	sMqw sMgiq nrik n pweI ] (1020-8, mwrU, mÚ 5) santaa sangat narak na paa-ee. In the Society of the Saints, one is not consigned to hell.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v8	AMimRq nwm dwnu nwnk kau gux gIqw inq vKwxIAw ]8]2]8]12]20] (1020-8, mwrU, mÚ 5) amrit naam daan naanak ka-o gun geetaa nit vakhaanee-aa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 5 v8	Please bless Nanak with the gift of the Ambrosial Naam, the Name of the Lord; he continually sings the songs of Your Glories. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 (1020-10)
RECORD	para 44430	maaroo solhay mehlaa 1 Maaroo, Solahas, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 44431	<> siqgur pRswid ] (1020-10) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
DEFINE	para 44432	swcw scu soeI Avru n koeI ] (1020-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachaa sach so-ee avar na ko-ee. The True Lord is True; there is no other at all.
REQUIRE	para 44433	ijin isrjI iqn hI Puin goeI ] (1020-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin sirjee tin hee fun go-ee. He who created, shall in the end destroy.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v1	ijau BwvY iqau rwKhu rhxw qum isau ikAw mukrweI hy ]1] (1020-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) ji-o bhaavai ti-o raakho rahnaa tum si-o ki-aa mukraa-ee hay. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v1	As it pleases You, so You keep me, and so I remain; what excuse could I offer to You? ||1||
RECORD	para 44435	Awip aupwey Awip Kpwey ] (1020-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap upaa-ay aap khapaa-ay. You Yourself create, and You Yourself destroy.
RECORD	para 44436	Awpy isir isir DMDY lwey ] (1020-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay sir sir DhanDhai laa-ay. You yourself link each and every person to their tasks.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v2	Awpy vIcwrI guxkwrI Awpy mwrig lweI hy ]2] (1020-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay veechaaree gunkaaree aapay maarag laa-ee hay. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v2	You contemplate Yourself, You Yourself make us worthy; You Yourself place us on the Path. ||2||
DEFINE	para 44438	Awpy dwnw Awpy bInw ] (1020-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay daanaa aapay beenaa. You Yourself are all-wise, You Yourself are all-knowing.
DEFINE	para 44439	Awpy Awpu aupwie pqInw ] (1020-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay aap upaa-ay pateenaa. You Yourself created the Universe, and You are pleased.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v3	Awpy pauxu pwxI bYsMqru Awpy myil imlweI hy ]3] (1020-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay pa-un paanee baisantar aapay mayl milaa-ee hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v3	You Yourself are the air, water and fire; You Yourself unite in Union. ||3||
DEFINE	para 44441	Awpy sis sUrw pUro pUrw ] (1020-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay sas sooraa pooro pooraa. You Yourself are the moon, the sun, the most perfect of the perfect.
DEFINE	para 44442	Awpy igAwin iDAwin guru sUrw ] (1020-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay gi-aan Dhi-aan gur sooraa. You Yourself are spiritual wisdom, meditation, and the Guru, the Warrior Hero.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v4	kwlu jwlu jmu joih n swkY swcy isau ilv lweI hy ]4] (1020-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaal jaal jam johi na saakai saachay si-o liv laa-ee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v4	The Messenger of Death, and his noose of death, cannot touch one, who is lovingly focused on You, O True Lord. ||4||
DEFINE	para 44444	Awpy purKu Awpy hI nwrI ] (1020-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay purakh aapay hee naaree. You Yourself are the male, and You Yourself are the female.
DEFINE	para 44445	Awpy pwsw Awpy swrI ] (1020-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay paasaa aapay saaree. You Yourself are the chess-board, and You Yourself are the chessman.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v5	Awpy ipV bwDI jgu KylY Awpy kImiq pweI hy ]5] (1020-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay pirh baaDhee jag khaylai aapay keemat paa-ee hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v5	You Yourself staged the drama in the arena of the world, and You Yourself evaluate the players. ||5||
DEFINE	para 44447	Awpy Bvru Pulu Plu qrvru ] (1020-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay bhavar ful fal tarvar. You Yourself are the bumble bee, the flower, the fruit and the tree.
DEFINE	para 44448	Awpy jlu Qlu swgru srvru ] (1020-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay jal thal saagar sarvar. You Yourself are the water, the desert, the ocean and the pool.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v6	Awpy mCu kCu krxIkru qyrw rUpu n lKxw jweI hy ]6] (1020-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay machh kachh karneekar tayraa roop na lakh-naa jaa-ee hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v6	You Yourself are the great fish, the tortoise, the Cause of causes; Your form cannot be known. ||6||
DEFINE	para 44450	Awpy idnsu Awpy hI rYxI ] (1020-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay dinas aapay hee rainee. You Yourself are the day, and You Yourself are the night.
DEFINE	para 44451	Awip pqIjY gur kI bYxI ] (1020-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap pateejai gur kee bainee. You Yourself are pleased by the Word of the Guru's Bani.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v7	Awid jugwid Anwhid Anidnu Git Git sbdu rjweI hy ]7] (1020-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) aad jugaad anaahad an-din ghat ghat sabad rajaa-ee hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v7	From the very beginning, and throughout the ages, the unstruck sound current resounds, night and day; in each and every heart, the Word of the Shabad, echoes Your Will. ||7||
DEFINE	para 44453	Awpy rqnu AnUpu Amolo ] (1020-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay ratan anoop amolo. You Yourself are the jewel, incomparably beautiful and priceless.
DEFINE	para 44454	Awpy prKy pUrw qolo ] (1020-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay parkhay pooraa tolo. You Yourself are the Assessor, the Perfect Weigher.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v8	Awpy iks hI kis bKsy Awpy dy lY BweI hy ]8] (1021-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay kis hee kas bakhsay aapay day lai bhaa-ee hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v8	You Yourself test and forgive. You Yourself give and take, O Siblings of Destiny. ||8||
DEFINE	para 44457	Awpy DnKu Awpy srbwxw ] (1021-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay Dhanakh aapay sarbaanaa. He Himself is the bow, and He Himself is the archer.
DEFINE	para 44458	Awpy suGVu srUpu isAwxw ] (1021-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay sugharh saroop si-aanaa. He Himself is all-wise, beautiful and all-knowing.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v9	khqw bkqw suxqw soeI Awpy bxq bxweI hy ]9] (1021-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) kahtaa baktaa suntaa so-ee aapay banat banaa-ee hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v9	He is the speaker, the orator and the listener. He Himself made what is made. ||9||
DEFINE	para 44460	pauxu gurU pwxI ipq jwqw ] (1021-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) pa-un guroo paanee pit jaataa. Air is the Guru, and water is known to be the father.
RECORD	para 44461	audr sMjogI DrqI mwqw ] (1021-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) udar sanjogee Dhartee maataa. The womb of the great mother earth gives birth to all.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v10	rYix idnsu duie dweI dwieAw jgu KylY KylweI hy ]10] (1021-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) rain dinas du-ay daa-ee daa-i-aa jag khaylai khaylaa-ee hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v10	Night and day are the two nurses, male and female; the world plays in this play. ||10||
DEFINE	para 44463	Awpy mCulI Awpy jwlw ] (1021-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay machhulee aapay jaalaa. You Yourself are the fish, and You Yourself are the net.
DEFINE	para 44464	Awpy gaU Awpy rKvwlw ] (1021-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay ga-oo aapay rakhvaalaa. You Yourself are the cows, and You yourself are their keeper.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v11	srb jIAw jig joiq qumwrI jYsI pRiB PurmweI hy ]11] (1021-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarab jee-aa jag jot tumaaree jaisee parabh furmaa-ee hay. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v11	Your Light fills all the beings of the world; they walk according to Your Command, O God. ||11||
DEFINE	para 44466	Awpy jogI Awpy BogI ] (1021-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay jogee aapay bhogee. You Yourself are the Yogi, and You Yourself are the enjoyer.
DEFINE	para 44467	Awpy rsIAw prm sMjogI ] (1021-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay rasee-aa param sanjogee. You Yourself are the reveller; You form the supreme Union.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v12	Awpy vybwxI inrMkwrI inrBau qwVI lweI hy ]12] (1021-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay vaybaanee nirankaaree nirbha-o taarhee laa-ee hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v12	You Yourself are speechless, formless and fearless, absorbed in the primal ecstasy of deep meditation. ||12||
DEFINE	para 44469	KwxI bwxI quJih smwxI ] (1021-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) khaanee banee tujheh samaanee. The sources of creation and speech are contained within You, Lord.
DEFINE	para 44470	jo dIsY sB Awvx jwxI ] (1021-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo deesai sabh aavan jaanee. All that is seen, is coming and going.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v13	syeI swh scy vwpwrI siqguir bUJ buJweI hy ]13] (1021-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) say-ee saah sachay vaapaaree satgur boojh bujhaa-ee hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v13	They are the true bankers and traders, whom the True Guru has inspired to understand. ||13||
DEFINE	para 44472	sbdu buJwey siqguru pUrw ] (1021-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad bujhaa-ay satgur pooraa. The Word of the Shabad is understood through the Perfect True Guru.
DEFINE	para 44473	srb klw swcy BrpUrw ] (1021-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarab kalaa saachay bharpooraa. The True Lord is overflowing with all powers.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v14	APirE vyprvwhu sdw qU nw iqsu iqlu n qmweI hy ]14] (1021-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) afri-o vayparvaahu sadaa too naa tis til na tamaa-ee hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v14	You are beyond our grasp, and forever independent. You do not have even an iota of greed. ||14||
DEFINE	para 44475	kwlu ibkwlu Bey dyvwny ] (1021-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaal bikaal bha-ay dayvaanay. Birth and death are meaningless, for those
RECORD	para 44476	sbdu shj rsu AMqir mwny ] (1021-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad sahj ras antar maanay. who enjoy the sublime celestial essence of the Shabad within their minds.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v15	Awpy mukiq iqRpiq vrdwqw Bgiq Bwie min BweI hy ]15] (1021-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay mukat taripat vardaataa bhagat bhaa-ay man bhaa-ee hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v15	He Himself is the Giver of liberation, satisfaction and blessings, to those devotees who love Him in their minds. ||15||
DEFINE	para 44478	Awip inrwlmu gur gm igAwnw ] (1021-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap niraalam gur gam gi-aanaa. He Himself is immaculate; by contact with the Guru, spiritual wisdom is obtained.
REQUIRE	para 44479	jo dIsY quJ mwih smwnw ] (1021-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo deesai tujh maahi samaanaa. Whatever is seen, shall merge into You.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v16	nwnku nIcu iBiKAw dir jwcY mY dIjY nwmu vfweI hy ]16]1] (1021-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak neech bhikhi-aa dar jaachai mai deejai naam vadaa-ee hay. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 1 v16	1|| Nanak, the lowly, begs for charity at Your Door; please, bless him with the glorious greatness of Your Name. ||16||1||
DEFINE	para 44482	Awpy DrqI Daulu AkwsM ] (1021-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay Dhartee Dha-ul akaasa N. He Himself is the earth, the mythical bull which supports it and the Akaashic ethers.
RECORD	para 44483	Awpy swcy gux prgwsM ] (1021-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay saachay gun pargaasa N. The True Lord Himself reveals His Glorious Virtues.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	jqI sqI sMqoKI Awpy Awpy kwr kmweI hy ]1] (1021-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) jatee satee santokhee aapay aapay kaar kamaa-ee hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	He Himself is celibate, chaste and contented; He Himself is the Doer of deeds. ||1||
RECORD	para 44485	ijsu krxw so kir kir vyKY ] (1021-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis karnaa so kar kar vaykhai. He who created the creation, beholds what He has created.
RECORD	para 44486	koie n mytY swcy lyKY ] (1021-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) ko-ay na maytai saachay laykhai. No one can erase the Inscription of the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Awpy kry krwey Awpy Awpy dy vifAweI hy ]2] (1021-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay karay karaa-ay aapay aapay day vadi-aa-ee hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	He Himself is the Doer, the Cause of causes; He Himself is the One who bestows glorious greatness. ||2||
RECORD	para 44488	pMc cor cMcl icqu cwlih ] (1021-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) panch chor chanchal chit chaaleh. The five thieves cause the fickle consciousness to waver.
RECORD	para 44489	pr Gr johih Gru nhI Bwlih ] (1021-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) par ghar joheh ghar nahee bhaaleh. It looks into the homes of others, but does not search its own home.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	kwieAw ngru FhY Fih FyrI ibnu sbdY piq jweI hy ]3] (1021-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa nagar dhahai dheh dhayree bin sabdai pat jaa-ee hay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	The body-village crumbles into dust; without the Word of the Shabad, one's honor is lost. ||3||
RECORD	para 44491	gur qy bUJY iqRBvxu sUJY ] (1021-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur tay boojhai taribhavan soojhai. One who realizes the Lord through the Guru, comprehends the three worlds.
RECORD	para 44492	mnsw mwir mnY isau lUJY ] (1021-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) mansaa maar manai si-o loojhai. He subdues his desires, and struggles with his mind.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	jo quDu syvih sy quD hI jyhy inrBau bwl sKweI hy ]4] (1021-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo tuDh sayveh say tuDh hee jayhay nirbha-o baal sakhaa-ee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	Those who serve You, become just like You; O Fearless Lord, You are their best friend from infancy. ||4||
DEFINE	para 44494	Awpy surgu mCu pieAwlw ] (1021-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay surag machh pa-i-aalaa. You Yourself are the heavenly realms, this world and the nether regions of the underworld.
DEFINE	para 44495	Awpy joiq srUpI bwlw ] (1021-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay jot saroopee baalaa. You Yourself are the embodiment of light, forever young.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	jtw ibkt ibkrwl srUpI rUpu n ryiKAw kweI hy ]5] (1021-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) jataa bikat bikraal saroopee roop na raykh-i-aa kaa-ee hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	With matted hair, and a horrible, dreadful form, still, You have no form or feature. ||5||
RECORD	para 44497	byd kqybI Bydu n jwqw ] (1021-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) bayd kataybee bhayd na jaataa. The Vedas and the Bible do not know the mystery of God.
RECORD	para 44498	nw iqsu mwq ipqw suq BRwqw ] (1021-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tis maat pitaa sut bharaataa. He has no mother, father, child or brother.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	sgly sYl aupwie smwey AlKu n lKxw jweI hy ]6] (1021-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) saglay sail upaa-ay samaa-ay alakh na lakh-naa jaa-ee hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	He created all the mountains, and levels them again; the Unseen Lord cannot be seen. ||6||
RECORD	para 44500	kir kir QwkI mIq Gnyry ] (1021-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) kar kar thaakee meet ghanayray. I have grown weary of making so many friends.
RECORD	para 44501	koie n kwtY Avgux myry ] (1021-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) ko-ay na kaatai avgun mayray. No one can rid me of my sins and mistakes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	suir nr nwQu swihbu sBnw isir Bwie imlY Bau jweI hy ]7] (1021-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) sur nar naath saahib sabhnaa sir bhaa-ay milai bha-o jaa-ee hay. ||7||
