DEFINE	para 44560	iqn kau qKiq imlI vifAweI ] (1023-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) tin ka-o takhat milee vadi-aa-ee. They alone are blessed with glorious greatness at the Lord's throne,
RECORD	para 44561	inrBau min visAw ilv lweI ] (1023-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirbha-o man vasi-aa liv laa-ee. who enshrine the fearless Lord in their minds, and lovingly center themselves on Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	KMfI bRhmMfI pwqwlI purIeI iqRBvx qwVI lweI hy ]10] (1023-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) khandee barahmandee paataalee puree-ee taribhavan taarhee laa-ee hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	In the galaxies and solar systems, nether regions, celestial realms and the three worlds, the Lord is in the primal void of deep absorption. ||10||
DEFINE	para 44563	swcI ngrI qKqu scwvw ] (1023-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachee nagree takhat sachaavaa. True is the village, and true is the throne,
RECORD	para 44564	gurmuiK swcu imlY suKu pwvw ] (1023-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh saach milai sukh paavaa. of those Gurmukhs who meet with the True Lord, and find peace.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	swcy swcY qKiq vfweI haumY gxq gvweI hy ]11] (1023-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachay saachai takhat vadaa-ee ha-umai ganat gavaa-ee hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	In Truth, seated upon the true throne, they are blessed with glorious greatness; their egotism is eradicated, along with the calculation of their account. ||11||
RECORD	para 44566	gxq gxIAY shsw jIAY ] (1023-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) ganat ganee-ai sahsaa jee-ai. Calculating its account, the soul becomes anxious.
RECORD	para 44567	ikau suKu pwvY dUAY qIAY ] (1023-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) ki-o sukh paavai doo-ai tee-ai. How can one find peace, through duality and the three gunas - the three qualities?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	inrmlu eyku inrMjnu dwqw gur pUry qy piq pweI hy ]12] (1023-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirmal ayk niranjan daataa gur pooray tay pat paa-ee hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	The One Lord is immaculate and formless, the Great Giver; through the Perfect Guru, honor is obtained. ||12||
DEFINE	para 44569	juig juig ivrlI gurmuiK jwqw ] (1023-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) jug jug virlee gurmukh jaataa. In each and every age, very rare are those who, as Gurmukh, realize the Lord.
DEFINE	para 44570	swcw riv rihAw mnu rwqw ] (1023-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachaa rav rahi-aa man raataa. Their minds are imbued with the True, all-pervading Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	iqs kI Et ghI suKu pwieAw min qin mYlu n kweI hy ]13] (1023-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) tis kee ot gahee sukh paa-i-aa man tan mail na kaa-ee hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	Seeking His Shelter, they find peace, and their minds and bodies are not stained with filth. ||13||
DEFINE	para 44572	jIB rswieix swcY rwqI ] (1023-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) jeebh rasaa-in saachai raatee. Their tongues are imbued with the True Lord, the source of nectar;
RECORD	para 44573	hir pRBu sMgI Bau n BrwqI ] (1023-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) har parabh sangee bha-o na bharaatee. abiding with the Lord God, they have no fear or doubt.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	sRvx sRoq rjy gurbwxI joqI joiq imlweI hy ]14] (1023-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarvan sarot rajay gurbaanee jotee jot milaa-ee hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Hearing the Word of the Guru's Bani, their ears are satisfied, and their light merges into the Light. ||14||
RECORD	para 44575	riK riK pYr Dry pau Drxw ] (1023-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) rakh rakh pair Dharay pa-o Dharnaa. Carefully, carefully, I place my feet upon the ground.
RECORD	para 44576	jq kq dyKau qyrI srxw ] (1023-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) jat kat daykh-a-u tayree sarnaa. Wherever I go, I behold Your Sanctuary.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	duKu suKu dyih qUhY min Bwvih quJ hI isau bix AweI hy ]15] (1023-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) dukh sukh deh toohai man bhaaveh tujh hee si-o ban aa-ee hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	Whether You grant me pain or pleasure, You are pleasing to my mind. I am in harmony with You. ||15||
DEFINE	para 44578	AMq kwil ko bylI nwhI ] (1023-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) ant kaal ko baylee naahee. No one is anyone's companion or helper at the very last moment;
RECORD	para 44579	gurmuiK jwqw quDu swlwhI ] (1023-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh jaataa tuDh saalaahee. as Gurmukh, I realize You and praise You.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	nwnk nwim rqy bYrwgI inj Gir qwVI lweI hy ]16]3] (1023-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak naam ratay bairaagee nij ghar taarhee laa-ee hay. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	3|| O Nanak, imbued with the Naam, I am detached; in the home of my own self deep within, I am absorbed in the primal void of deep meditation. ||16||3||
DEFINE	para 44582	Awid jugwdI Apr Apwry ] (1023-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) aad jugaadee apar apaaray. From the very beginning of time, and throughout the ages, You are infinite and incomparable.
DEFINE	para 44583	Awid inrMjn Ksm hmwry ] (1023-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aad niranjan khasam hamaaray. You are my primal, immaculate Lord and Master.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	swcy jog jugiq vIcwrI swcy qwVI lweI hy ]1] (1023-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachay jog jugat veechaaree saachay taarhee laa-ee hay. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	I contemplate the Way of Yoga, the Way of Union with the True Lord. I am truly absorbed in the primal void of deep meditation. ||1||
RECORD	para 44585	kyqiVAw jug DuMDUkwrY ] (1023-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) kayt-rhi-aa jug DhunDhookaarai. For so many ages, there was only pitch darkness;
RECORD	para 44586	qwVI lweI isrjxhwrY ] (1023-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) taarhee laa-ee sirjanhaarai. the Creator Lord was absorbed in the primal void.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	scu nwmu scI vifAweI swcY qKiq vfweI hy ]2] (1023-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach naam sachee vadi-aa-ee saachai takhat vadaa-ee hay. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	There was the True Name, the glorious greatness of the Truth, and the glory of His true throne. ||2||
RECORD	para 44588	sqjuig squ sMqoKu srIrw ] (1023-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) satjug sat santokh sareeraa. In the Golden Age of Truth, Truth and contentment filled the bodies.
RECORD	para 44589	siq siq vrqY gihr gMBIrw ] (1023-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) sat sat vartai gahir gambheeraa. Truth was pervasive, Truth, deep, profound and unfathomable.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	scw swihbu scu prKY swcY hukim clweI hy ]3] (1023-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) sachaa saahib sach parkhai saachai hukam chalaa-ee hay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	The True Lord appraises the mortals on the Touchstone of Truth, and issues His True Command. ||3||
DEFINE	para 44591	sq sMqoKI siqguru pUrw ] (1023-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) sat santokhee satgur pooraa. The Perfect True Guru is true and contented.
DEFINE	para 44592	gur kw sbdu mny so sUrw ] (1023-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kaa sabad manay so sooraa. He alone is a spiritual hero, who believes in the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	swcI drgh swcu invwsw mwnY hukmu rjweI hy ]4] (1023-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachee dargeh saach nivaasaa maanai hukam rajaa-ee hay. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	He alone obtains a true seat in the True Court of the Lord, who surrenders to the Command of the Commander. ||4||
RECORD	para 44594	sqjuig swcu khY sBu koeI ] (1023-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) satjug saach kahai sabh ko-ee. In the Golden Age of Truth, everyone spoke the Truth.
RECORD	para 44595	sic vrqY swcw soeI ] (1023-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach vartai saachaa so-ee. Truth was pervasive - the Lord was Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	min muiK swcu Brm Bau BMjnu gurmuiK swcu sKweI hy ]5] (1023-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) man mukh saach bharam bha-o bhanjan gurmukh saach sakhaa-ee hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	With Truth in their minds and mouths, mortals were rid of doubt and fear. Truth was the friend of the Gurmukhs. ||5||
RECORD	para 44597	qRyqY Drm klw iek cUkI ] (1023-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) taraytai Dharam kalaa ik chookee. In the Silver Age of Traytaa Yoga, one power of Dharma was lost.
RECORD	para 44598	qIin crx iek duibDw sUkI ] (1023-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) teen charan ik dubiDhaa sookee. Three feet remained; through duality, one was cut off.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	gurmuiK hovY su swcu vKwxY mnmuiK pcY AvweI hy ]6] (1023-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh hovai so saach vakhaanai manmukh pachai avaa-ee hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Those who were Gurmukh spoke the Truth, while the self-willed manmukhs wasted away in vain. ||6||
RECORD	para 44600	mnmuiK kdy n drgh sIJY ] (1023-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh kaday na dargeh seejhai. The manmukh never succeeds in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	para 44601	ibnu sbdY ikau AMqru rIJY ] (1023-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin sabdai ki-o antar reejhai. Without the Word of the Shabad, how can one be pleased within?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	bwDy Awvih bwDy jwvih soJI bUJ n kweI hy ]7] (1023-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) baaDhay aavahi baaDhay jaaveh sojhee boojh na kaa-ee hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	In bondage they come, and in bondage they go; they understand and comprehend nothing. ||7||
RECORD	para 44603	dieAw duAwpuir ADI hoeI ] (1023-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) da-i-aa du-aapur aDhee ho-ee. In the Brass Age of Dwaapur Yuga, compassion was cut in half.
RECORD	para 44605	gurmuiK ivrlw cInY koeI ] (1024-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh virlaa cheenai ko-ee. Only a few, as Gurmukh, remembered the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	duie pg Drmu Dry DrxIDr gurmuiK swcu iqQweI hy ]8] (1024-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) du-ay pag Dharam Dharay DharneeDhar gurmukh saach tithaa-ee hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	Dharmic faith, which upholds and supports the earth, had only two feet; Truth was revealed to the Gurmukhs. ||8||
UPHOLD	para 44607	rwjy Drmu krih prQwey ] (1024-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) raajay Dharam karahi parthaa-ay. The kings acted righteously only out of self-interest.
RECORD	para 44608	Awsw bMDy dwnu krwey ] (1024-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) aasaa banDhay daan karaa-ay. Tied to hopes of reward, they gave to charities.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	rwm nwm ibnu mukiq n hoeI Qwky krm kmweI hy ]9] (1024-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam bin mukat na ho-ee thaakay karam kamaa-ee hay. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	Without the Lord's Name, liberation did not come, although they grew weary of performing rituals. ||9||
RECORD	para 44610	krm Drm kir mukiq mMgwhI ] (1024-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) karam Dharam kar mukat mangaa-ee. Practicing religious rituals, they sought liberation,
RECORD	para 44611	mukiq pdwrQu sbid slwhI ] (1024-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) mukat padaarath sabad salaahee. but the treasure of liberation comes only by praising the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	ibnu gur sbdY mukiq n hoeI prpMcu kir BrmweI hy ]10] (1024-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur sabdai mukat na ho-ee parpanch kar bharmaa-ee hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	Without the Word of the Guru's Shabad, liberation is not obtained; practicing hypocrisy, they wander around confused. ||10||
RECORD	para 44613	mwieAw mmqw CofI n jweI ] (1024-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) maa-i-aa mamtaa chhodee na jaa-ee. Love and attachment to Maya cannot be abandoned.
RECORD	para 44614	sy CUty scu kwr kmweI ] (1024-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) say chhootay sach kaar kamaa-ee. They alone find release, who practice deeds of Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Aihinis Bgiq rqy vIcwrI Twkur isau bix AweI hy ]11] (1024-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) ahinis bhagat ratay veechaaree thaakur si-o ban aa-ee hay. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Day and night, the devotees remain imbued with contemplative meditation; they become just like their Lord and Master. ||11||
RECORD	para 44616	ieik jp qp kir kir qIrQ nwvih ] (1024-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik jap tap kar kar tirath naaveh. Some chant and practice intensive meditation, and take cleansing baths at sacred shrines of pilgrimage.
RECORD	para 44617	ijau quDu BwvY iqvY clwvih ] (1024-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) ji-o tuDh bhaavai tivai chalaaveh. They walk as You will them to walk.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	hiT ingRih ApqIju n BIjY ibnu hir gur ikin piq pweI hy ]12] (1024-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) hath nigrahi apteej na bheejai bin har gur kin pat paa-ee hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	By stubborn rituals of self-suppression, the Lord is not pleased. No one has ever obtained honor, without the Lord, without the Guru. ||12||
RECORD	para 44619	klI kwl mih iek kl rwKI ] (1024-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) kalee kaal meh ik kal raakhee. In the Iron Age, the Dark Age of Kali Yuga, only one power remains.
RECORD	para 44620	ibnu gur pUry iknY n BwKI ] (1024-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur pooray kinai na bhaakhee. Without the Perfect Guru, no one has even described it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	mnmuiK kUVu vrqY vrqwrw ibnu siqgur Brmu n jweI hy ]13] (1024-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh koorh vartai vartaaraa bin satgur bharam na jaa-ee hay. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	The self-willed manmukhs have staged the show of falsehood. Without the True Guru, doubt does not depart. ||13||
DEFINE	para 44622	siqguru vyprvwhu isrMdw ] (1024-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur vayparvaahu sirandaa. The True Guru is the Creator Lord, independent and carefree.
DEFINE	para 44623	nw jm kwix n CMdw bMdw ] (1024-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa jam kaan na chhandaa bandaa. He does not fear death, and He is not dependent on mortal men.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	jo iqsu syvy so AibnwsI nw iqsu kwlu sMqweI hy ]14] (1024-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo tis sayvay so abhinaasee naa tis kaal santaa-ee hay. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Whoever serves Him becomes immortal and imperishable, and will not be tortured by death. ||14||
RECORD	para 44625	gur mih Awpu riKAw krqwry ] (1024-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur meh aap rakhi-aa kartaaray. The Creator Lord has enshrined Himself within the Guru.
RECORD	para 44626	gurmuiK koit AsMK auDwry ] (1024-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh kot asa Nkh uDhaaray. The Gurmukh saves countless millions.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	srb jIAw jgjIvnu dwqw inrBau mYlu n kweI hy ]15] (1024-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarab jee-aa jagjeevan daataa nirbha-o mail na kaa-ee hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	The Life of the World is the Great Giver of all beings. The Fearless Lord has no filth at all. ||15||
RECORD	para 44628	sgly jwcih gur BMfwrI ] (1024-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) saglay jaacheh gur bhandaaree. Everyone begs from the Guru, God's Treasurer.
DEFINE	para 44629	Awip inrMjnu AlK ApwrI ] (1024-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap niranjan alakh apaaree. He Himself is the immaculate, unknowable, infinite Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	nwnku swcu khY pRB jwcY mY dIjY swcu rjweI hy ]16]4] (1024-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak saach kahai parabh jaachai mai deejai saach rajaa-ee hay. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	4|| Nanak speaks the Truth; he begs from God. Please bless me with the Truth, by Your Will. ||16||4||
DEFINE	para 44632	swcY myly sbid imlwey ] (1024-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachai maylay sabad milaa-ay. The True Lord unites with those who are united with the Word of the Shabad.
WHEN	para 44633	jw iqsu Bwxw shij smwey ] (1024-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaa tis bhaanaa sahj samaa-ay. When it pleases Him, we intuitively merge with Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	iqRBvx joiq DrI prmysir Avru n dUjw BweI hy ]1] (1024-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) taribhavan jot Dharee parmaysar avar na doojaa bhaa-ee hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	The Light of the Transcendent Lord pervades the three worlds; there is no other at all, O Siblings of Destiny. ||1||
RECORD	para 44635	ijs ky cwkr iqs kI syvw ] (1024-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis kay chaakar tis kee sayvaa. I am His servant; I serve Him.
DEFINE	para 44636	sbid pqIjY AlK AByvw ] (1024-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad pateejai alakh abhayvaa. He is unknowable and mysterious; He is pleased by the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Bgqw kw guxkwrI krqw bKis ley vifAweI hy ]2] (1024-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhagtaa kaa gunkaaree kartaa bakhas la-ay vadi-aa-ee hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	The Creator is the Benefactor of His devotees. He forgives them - such is His greatness. ||2||
RECORD	para 44638	dydy qoit n AwvY swcy ] (1024-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) dayday tot na aavai saachay. The True Lord gives and gives; His blessings never run short.
RECORD	para 44639	lY lY mukir paudy kwcy ] (1024-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) lai lai mukar pa-uday kaachay. The false ones receive, and then deny having received.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	mUlu n bUJih swic n rIJih dUjY Brim BulweI hy ]3] (1024-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) mool na boojheh saach na reejheh doojai bharam bhulaa-ee hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	They do not understand their origins, they are not pleased with the Truth, and so they wander in duality and doubt. ||3||
RECORD	para 44641	gurmuiK jwig rhy idn rwqI ] (1024-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh jaag rahay din raatee. The Gurmukhs remain awake and aware, day and night.
RECORD	para 44642	swcy kI ilv gurmiq jwqI ] (1024-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachay kee liv gurmat jaatee. Following the Guru's Teachings, they know the Love of the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	mnmuK soie rhy sy lUty gurmuiK swbqu BweI hy ]4] (1024-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh so-ay rahay say lootay gurmukh saabat bhaa-ee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	The self-willed manmukhs remain asleep, and are plundered. The Gurmukhs remain safe and sound, O Siblings of Destiny. ||4||
RECORD	para 44644	kUVy AwvY kUVy jwvY ] (1024-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) koorhay aavai koorhay jaavai. The false come, and the false go;
RECORD	para 44645	kUVy rwqI kUVu kmwvY ] (1024-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) koorhay raatee koorh kamaavai. imbued with falsehood, they practice only falsehood.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	sbid imly sy drgh pYDy gurmuiK suriq smweI hy ]5] (1024-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad milay say dargeh paiDhay gurmukh surat samaa-ee hay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Those who are imbued with the Shabad are robed in honor in the Court of the Lord; the Gurmukhs focus their consciousness on Him. ||5||
DEFINE	para 44647	kUiV muTI TgI TgvwVI ] (1024-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) koorh muthee thagee thagvaarhee. The false are cheated, and robbed by the robbers.
DEFINE	para 44648	ijau vwVI EjwiV aujwVI ] (1024-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) ji-o vaarhee ojaarh ujaarhee. The garden is laid waste, like the rough wilderness.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	nwm ibnw ikCu swid n lwgY hir ibsirAY duKu pweI hy ]6] (1024-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam binaa kichh saad na laagai har bisri-ai dukh paa-ee hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Without the Naam, the Name of the Lord, nothing tastes sweet; forgetting the Lord, they suffer in sorrow. ||6||
DEFINE	para 44650	Bojnu swcu imlY AwGweI ] (1024-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhojan saach milai aaghaa-ee. Receiving the food of Truth, one is satisfied.
DEFINE	para 44651	nwm rqnu swcI vifAweI ] (1024-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam ratan saachee vadi-aa-ee. True is the glorious greatness of the jewel of the Name.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	cInY Awpu pCwxY soeI joqI joiq imlweI hy ]7] (1024-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) cheenai aap pachhaanai so-ee jotee jot milaa-ee hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	One who understands his own self, realizes the Lord. His light merges into the Light. ||7||
RECORD	para 44654	nwvhu BulI cotw Kwey ] (1025-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) naavhu bhulee chotaa khaa-ay. Wandering from the Name, he endures beatings.
RECORD	para 44655	bhuqu isAwxp Brmu n jwey ] (1025-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) bahut si-aanap bharam na jaa-ay. Even great cleverness does not dispel doubt.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	pic pic muey Acyq n cyqih Ajgir Bwir ldweI hy ]8] (1025-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) pach pach mu-ay achayt na cheeteh ajgar bhaar ladaa-ee hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	The unconscious fool does not remain conscious of the Lord; he putrifies and rots away to death, carrying his heavy load of sin. ||8||
DEFINE	para 44657	ibnu bwd ibroDih koeI nwhI ] (1025-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin baad biroDheh ko-ee naahee. No one is free of conflict and strife.
RECORD	para 44658	mY dyKwilhu iqsu swlwhI ] (1025-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) mai daykhaalihu tis saalaahee. Show me anyone who is, and I will praise him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	mnu qnu Arip imlY jgjIvnu hir isau bxq bxweI hy ]9] (1025-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) man tan arap milai jagjeevan har si-o banat banaa-ee hay. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	Dedicating mind and body to God, one meets the Lord, the Life of the World, and becomes just like Him. ||9||
RECORD	para 44660	pRB kI giq imiq koie n pwvY ] (1025-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) parabh kee gat mit ko-ay na paavai. No one knows the state and extent of God.
RECORD	para 44661	jy ko vfw khwie vfweI KwvY ] (1025-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) jay ko vadaa kahaa-ay vadaa-ee khaavai. Whoever calls himself great, will be eaten by his greatness.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	swcy swihb qoit n dwqI sglI iqnih aupweI hy ]10] (1025-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachay saahib tot na daatee saglee tineh upaa-ee hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	There is no lack of gifts of our True Lord and Master. He created all. ||10||
DEFINE	para 44663	vfI vifAweI vyprvwhy ] (1025-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) vadee vadi-aa-ee vayparvaahay. Great is the glorious greatness of the independent Lord.
RECORD	para 44664	Awip aupwey dwnu smwhy ] (1025-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap upaa-ay daan samaahay. He Himself created, and gives sustanance to all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Awip dieAwlu dUir nhI dwqw imilAw shij rjweI hy ]11] (1025-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap da-i-aal door nahee daataa mili-aa sahj rajaa-ee hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	The Merciful Lord is not far away; the Great Giver spontaneously unites with Himself, by His Will. ||11||
DEFINE	para 44666	ieik sogI ieik roig ivAwpy ] (1025-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik sogee ik rog vi-aapay. Some are sad, and some are afflicted with disease.
RECORD	para 44667	jo ikCu kry su Awpy Awpy ] (1025-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo kichh karay so aapay aapay. Whatever God does, He does by Himself.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	Bgiq Bwau gur kI miq pUrI Anhid sbid lKweI hy ]12] (1025-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhagat bhaa-o gur kee mat pooree anhad sabad lakhaa-ee hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	Through loving devotion, and the Perfect Teachings of the Guru, the unstruck sound current of the Shabad is realized. ||12||
RECORD	para 44669	ieik nwgy BUKy Bvih Bvwey ] (1025-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik naagay bhookhay bhaveh bhavaa-ay. Some wander and roam around, hungry and naked.
RECORD	para 44670	ieik hTu kir mrih n kImiq pwey ] (1025-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik hath kar mareh na keemat paa-ay. Some act in stubbornness and die, but do not know the value of God.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	giq Aivgq kI swr n jwxY bUJY sbdu kmweI hy ]13] (1025-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) gat avigat kee saar na jaanai boojhai sabad kamaa-ee hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	They do not know the difference between good and bad; this is understood only through the practice of the Word of the Shabad. ||13||
RECORD	para 44672	ieik qIriQ nwvih AMnu n Kwvih ] (1025-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik tirath naaveh ann na khaaveh. Some bathe at sacred shrines and refuse to eat.
RECORD	para 44673	ieik Agin jlwvih dyh Kpwvih ] (1025-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik agan jalaaveh dayh khapaaveh. Some torment their bodies in burning fire.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	rwm nwm ibnu mukiq n hoeI ikqu ibiD pwir lµGweI hy ]14] (1025-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam bin mukat na ho-ee kit biDh paar langhaa-ee hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Without the Lord's Name, liberation is not obtained; how can anyone cross over? ||14||
RECORD	para 44675	gurmiq Cofih auJiV jweI ] (1025-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmat chhodeh ujharh jaa-ee. Abandoning the Guru's Teachings, some wander in the wilderness.
DEFINE	para 44676	mnmuiK rwmu n jpY AvweI ] (1025-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh raam na japai avaa-ee. The self-willed manmukhs are destitute; they do not meditate on the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	pic pic bUfih kUVu kmwvih kUiV kwlu bYrweI hy ]15] (1025-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) pach pach booDheh koorh kamaaveh koorh kaal bairaa-ee hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	They are ruined, destroyed and drowned from practicing falsehood; death is the enemy of the false. ||15||
ALLOW	para 44678	hukmy AwvY hukmy jwvY ] (1025-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) hukmay aavai hukmay jaavai. By the Hukam of the Lord's Command, they come, and by the Hukam of His Command, they go.
RECORD	para 44679	bUJY hukmu so swic smwvY ] (1025-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) boojhai hukam so saach samaavai. One who realizes His Hukam, merges in the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	nwnk swcu imlY min BwvY gurmuiK kwr kmweI hy ]16]5] (1025-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak saach milai man bhaavai gurmukh kaar kamaa-ee hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	5|| O Nanak, he merges in the True Lord, and his mind is pleased with the Lord. The Gurmukhs do His work. ||16||5||
DEFINE	para 44682	Awpy krqw purKu ibDwqw ] (1025-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay kartaa purakh biDhaataa. He Himself is the Creator Lord, the Architect of Destiny.
RECORD	para 44683	ijin Awpy Awip aupwie pCwqw ] (1025-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin aapay aap upaa-ay pachhaataa. He evaluates those whom He Himself has created.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	Awpy siqguru Awpy syvku Awpy isRsit aupweI hy ]1] (1025-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay satgur aapay sayvak aapay sarisat upaa-ee hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	He Himself is the True Guru, and He Himself is the servant; He Himself created the Universe. ||1||
DEFINE	para 44685	Awpy nyVY nwhI dUry ] (1025-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay nayrhai naahee dooray. He is near at hand, not far away.
DEFINE	para 44686	bUJih gurmuiK sy jn pUry ] (1025-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) boojheh gurmukh say jan pooray. The Gurmukhs understand Him; perfect are those humble beings.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	iqn kI sMgiq Aihinis lwhw gur sMgiq eyh vfweI hy ]2] (1025-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) tin kee sangat ahinis laahaa gur sangat ayh vadaa-ee hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Associating with them night and day is profitable. This is the glorious greatness of associating with the Guru. ||2||
DEFINE	para 44688	juig juig sMq Bly pRB qyry ] (1025-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) jug jug sant bhalay parabh tayray. Throughout the ages, Your Saints are holy and sublime, O God.
RECORD	para 44689	hir gux gwvih rsn rsyry ] (1025-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) har gun gaavahi rasan rasayray. They sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, savoring it with their tongues.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	ausqiq krih prhir duKu dwldu ijn nwhI icMq prweI hy ]3] (1025-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) ustat karahi parhar dukh daalad jin naahee chint paraa-ee hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	They chant His Praises, and their pain and poverty are taken away; they are not afraid of anyone else. ||3||
RECORD	para 44691	Eie jwgq rhih n sUqy dIsih ] (1025-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) o-ay jaagat raheh na sootay deeseh. They remain awake and aware, and do not appear to sleep.
RECORD	para 44692	sMgiq kul qwry swcu prIsih ] (1025-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) sangat kul taaray saach pareeseh. They serve up Truth, and so save their companions and relatives.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	kilml mYlu nwhI qy inrml Eie rhih Bgiq ilv lweI hy ]4] (1025-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) kalimal mail naahee tay nirmal o-ay raheh bhagat liv laa-ee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	They are not stained with the filth of sins; they are immaculate and pure, and remain absorbed in loving devotional worship. ||4||
RECORD	para 44694	bUJhu hir jn siqgur bwxI ] (1025-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) boojhhu har jan satgur banee. O humble servants of the Lord, understand the Word of the Guru's Bani.
REQUIRE	para 44695	eyhu jobnu swsu hY dyh purwxI ] (1025-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) ayhu joban saas hai dayh puraanee. This youth, breath and body shall pass away.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Awju kwil mir jweIAY pRwxI hir jpu jip irdY iDAweI hy ]5] (1025-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) aaj kaal mar jaa-ee-ai paraanee har jap jap ridai Dhi-aa-ee hay. ||5||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	O mortal, you shall die today or tomorrow; chant, and meditate on the Lord within your heart. ||5||
RECORD	para 44697	Cofhu pRwxI kUV kbwVw ] (1025-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) chhodahu paraanee koorh kabaarhaa. O mortal, abandon falsehood and your worthless ways.
RECORD	para 44698	kUVu mwry kwlu auCwhwVw ] (1025-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) koorh maaray kaal uchhaahaarhaa. Death viciously kills the false beings.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	swkq kUiV pcih min haumY duhu mwrig pcY pcweI hy ]6] (1025-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) saakat koorh pacheh man ha-umai duhu maarag pachai pachaa-ee hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	The faithless cynic is ruined through falsehood and his egotistical mind.On the path of duality, he rots away and decomposes. ||6||
RECORD	para 44701	Coifhu inMdw qwiq prweI ] (1026-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) chhodihu nindaa taat paraa-ee. Abandon slander and envy of others.
RECORD	para 44702	piV piV dJih swiq n AweI ] (1026-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) parh parh dajheh saat na aa-ee. Reading and studying, they burn, and do not find tranquility.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	imil sqsMgiq nwmu slwhhu Awqm rwmu sKweI hy ]7] (1026-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) mil satsangat naam salaahahu aatam raam sakhaa-ee hay. ||7||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	Joining the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation, praise the Naam, the Name of the Lord. The Lord, the Supreme Soul, shall be your helper and companion. ||7||
RECORD	para 44704	Cofhu kwm k®oDu buirAweI ] (1026-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) chhodahu kaam kroDh buri-aa-ee. Abandon sexual desire, anger and wickedness.
RECORD	para 44705	haumY DMDu Cofhu lµptweI ] (1026-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai DhanDh chhodahu lamptaa-ee. Abandon your involvement in egotistical affairs and conflicts.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	siqgur srix prhu qw aubrhu ieau qrIAY Bvjlu BweI hy ]8] (1026-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur saran parahu taa ubrahu i-o taree-ai bhavjal bhaa-ee hay. ||8||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	If you seek the Sanctuary of the True Guru, then you shall be saved. In this way you shall cross over the terrifying world-ocean, O Siblings of Destiny. ||8||
REQUIRE	para 44707	AwgY ibml ndI Agin ibKu Jylw ] (1026-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) aagai bimal nadee agan bikh jhaylaa. In the hereafter, you shall have to cross over the fiery river of poisonous flames.
REQUIRE	para 44708	iqQY Avru n koeI jIau iekylw ] (1026-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) tithai avar na ko-ee jee-o ikaylaa. No one else will be there; your soul shall be all alone.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	BV BV Agin swgru dy lhrI piV dJih mnmuK qweI hy ]9] (1026-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) bharh bharh agan saagar day lahree parh dajheh manmukh taa-ee hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	The ocean of fire spits out waves of searing flames; the self-willed manmukhs fall into it, and are roasted there. ||9||
RECORD	para 44710	gur pih mukiq dwnu dy BwxY ] (1026-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur peh mukat daan day bhaanai. Liberation comes from the Guru; He grants this blessing by the Pleasure of His Will.
RECORD	para 44711	ijin pwieAw soeI ibiD jwxY ] (1026-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin paa-i-aa so-ee biDh jaanai. He alone knows the way, who obtains it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	ijn pwieAw iqn pUChu BweI suKu siqgur syv kmweI hy ]10] (1026-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin paa-i-aa tin poochhahu bhaa-ee sukh satgur sayv kamaa-ee hay. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	So ask one who has obtained it, O Siblings of Destiny. Serve the True Guru, and find peace. ||10||
RECORD	para 44713	gur ibnu auriJ mrih bykwrw ] (1026-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur bin urajh mareh baykaaraa. Without the Guru, he dies entangled in sin and corruption.
RECORD	para 44714	jmu isir mwry kry KuAwrw ] (1026-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) jam sir maaray karay khu-aaraa. The Messenger of Death smashes his head and humiliates him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	bwDy mukiq nwhI nr inMdk fUbih inMd prweI hy ]11] (1026-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) baaDhay mukat naahee nar nindak doobeh nind paraa-ee hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	The slanderous person is not freed of his bonds; he is drowned, slandering others. ||11||
RECORD	para 44716	bolhu swcu pCwxhu AMdir ] (1026-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) bolhu saach pachhaanhu andar. So speak the Truth, and realize the Lord deep within.
DEFINE	para 44717	dUir nwhI dyKhu kir nµdir ] (1026-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) door naahee daykhhu kar nandar. He is not far away; look, and see Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	ibGnu nwhI gurmuiK qru qwrI ieau Bvjlu pwir lµGweI hy ]12] (1026-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) bighan naahee gurmukh tar taaree i-o bhavjal paar langhaa-ee hay. ||12||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	No obstacles shall block your way; become Gurmukh, and cross over to the other side. This is the way to cross over the terrifying world-ocean. ||12||
RECORD	para 44719	dyhI AMdir nwmu invwsI ] (1026-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) dayhee andar naam nivaasee. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, abides deep within the body.
DEFINE	para 44720	Awpy krqw hY AibnwsI ] (1026-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay kartaa hai abhinaasee. The Creator Lord is eternal and imperishable.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	nw jIau mrY n mwirAw jweI kir dyKY sbid rjweI hy ]13] (1026-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa jee-o marai na maari-aa jaa-ee kar daykhai sabad rajaa-ee hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	The soul does not die, and it cannot be killed; God creates and watches over all. Through the Word of the Shabad, His Will is manifest. ||13||
DEFINE	para 44722	Ehu inrmlu hY nwhI AMiDAwrw ] (1026-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) oh nirmal hai naahee anDhi-aaraa. He is immaculate, and has no darkness.
RECORD	para 44723	Ehu Awpy qKiq bhY sicAwrw ] (1026-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) oh aapay takhat bahai sachi-aaraa. The True Lord Himself sits upon His throne.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	swkq kUVy bMiD BvweIAih mir jnmih AweI jweI hy ]14] (1026-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) saakat koorhay banDh bhavaa-ee-ah mar janmeh aa-ee jaa-ee hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	The faithless cynics are bound and gagged, and forced to wander in reincarnation. They die, and are reborn, and continue coming and going. ||14||
DEFINE	para 44725	gur ky syvk siqgur ipAwry ] (1026-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kay sayvak satgur pi-aaray. The Guru's servants are the Beloveds of the True Guru.
RECORD	para 44726	Eie bYsih qKiq su sbdu vIcwry ] (1026-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) o-ay baiseh takhat so sabad veechaaray. Contemplating the Shabad, they sit upon His throne.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	qqu lhih AMqrgiq jwxih sqsMgiq swcu vfweI hy ]15] (1026-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) tat laheh antargat jaaneh satsangat saach vadaa-ee hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	They realize the essence of reality, and know the state of their inner being. This is the true glorious greatness of those who join the Sat Sangat. ||15||
RECORD	para 44728	Awip qrY jnu ipqrw qwry ] (1026-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap tarai jan pitraa taaray. He Himself saves His humble servant, and saves his ancestors as well.
DEFINE	para 44729	sMgiq mukiq su pwir auqwry ] (1026-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) sangat mukat so paar utaaray. His companions are liberated; He carries them across.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	nwnku iqs kw lwlw golw ijin gurmuiK hir ilv lweI hy ]16]6] (1026-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak tis kaa laalaa golaa jin gurmukh har liv laa-ee hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	6|| Nanak is the servant and slave of that Gurmukh who lovingly focuses his consciousness on the Lord. ||16||6||
RECORD	para 44732	kyqy jug vrqy gubwrY ] (1026-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaytay jug vartay gubaarai. For many ages, only darkness prevailed;
RECORD	para 44733	qwVI lweI Apr ApwrY ] (1026-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) taarhee laa-ee apar apaarai. the infinite, endless Lord was absorbed in the primal void.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	DuMDUkwir inrwlmu bYTw nw qid DMDu pswrw hy ]1] (1026-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) DhunDhookaar niraalam baithaa naa tad DhanDh pasaaraa hay. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	He sat alone and unaffected in absolute darkness; the world of conflict did not exist. ||1||
RECORD	para 44735	jug CqIh iqnY vrqwey ] (1026-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) jug chhateeh tinai vartaa-ay. Thirty-six ages passed like this.
RECORD	para 44736	ijau iqsu Bwxw iqvY clwey ] (1026-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) ji-o tis bhaanaa tivai chalaa-ay. He causes all to happen by the Pleasure of His Will.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	iqsih srIku n dIsY koeI Awpy Apr Apwrw hy ]2] (1026-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) tiseh sareek na deesai ko-ee aapay apar apaaraa hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	No rival of His can be seen. He Himself is infinite and endless. ||2||
DEFINE	para 44738	gupqy bUJhu jug cquAwry ] (1026-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) guptay boojhhu jug chatu-aaray. God is hidden throughout the four ages - understand this well.
DEFINE	para 44739	Git Git vrqY audr mJwry ] (1026-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) ghat ghat vartai udar majhaaray. He pervades each and every heart, and is contained within the belly.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	jugu jugu eykw eykI vrqY koeI bUJY gur vIcwrw hy ]3] (1026-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) jug jug aykaa aykee vartai ko-ee boojhai gur veechaaraa hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	The One and Only Lord prevails throughout the ages. How rare are those who contemplate the Guru, and understand this. ||3||
RECORD	para 44741	ibMdu rkqu imil ipMfu srIAw ] (1026-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) bind rakat mil pind saree-aa. From the union of the sperm and the egg, the body was formed.
DEFINE	para 44742	pauxu pwxI AgnI imil jIAw ] (1026-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) pa-un paanee agnee mil jee-aa. From the union of air, water and fire, the living being is made.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	Awpy coj kry rMg mhlI hor mwieAw moh pswrw hy ]4] (1026-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay choj karay rang mahlee hor maa-i-aa moh pasaaraa hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	He Himself plays joyfully in the mansion of the body; all the rest is just attachment to Maya's expanse. ||4||
RECORD	para 44744	grB kuMfl mih aurD iDAwnI ] (1026-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) garabh kundal meh uraDh Dhi-aanee. Within the mother's womb, upside-down, the mortal meditated on God.
RECORD	para 44745	Awpy jwxY AMqrjwmI ] (1026-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay jaanai antarjaamee. The Inner-knower, the Searcher of hearts, knows everything.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	swis swis scu nwmu smwly AMqir audr mJwrw hy ]5] (1026-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) saas saas sach naam samaalay antar udar majhaaraa hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	With each and every breath, he contemplated the True Name, deep within himself, within the womb. ||5||
RECORD	para 44748	cwir pdwrQ lY jig AwieAw ] (1027-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) chaar padaarath lai jag aa-i-aa. He came into the world to obtain the four great blessings.
RECORD	para 44749	isv skqI Gir vwsw pwieAw ] (1027-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) siv saktee ghar vaasaa paa-i-aa. He came to dwell in the home of the Shiva and Shakti, energy and matter.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	eyku ivswry qw ipV hwry AMDulY nwmu ivswrw hy ]6] (1027-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) ayk visaaray taa pirh haaray anDhulai naam visaaraa hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	But he forgot the One Lord, and he has lost the game. The blind person forgets the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||6||
RECORD	para 44751	bwlku mrY bwlk kI lIlw ] (1027-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) baalak marai baalak kee leelaa. The child dies in his childish games.
RECORD	para 44752	kih kih rovih bwlu rMgIlw ] (1027-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) kahi kahi roveh baal rangeelaa. They cry and mourn, saying that he was such a playful child.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	ijs kw sw so iqn hI lIAw BUlw rovxhwrw hy ]7] (1027-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis kaa saa so tin hee lee-aa bhoolaa rovanhaaraa hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	The Lord who owns him has taken him back. Those who weep and mourn are mistaken. ||7||
WHEN	para 44754	Bir jobin mir jwih ik kIjY ] (1027-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhar joban mar jaahi ke keejai. What can they do, if he dies in his youth?
DEFINE	para 44755	myrw myrw kir rovIjY ] (1027-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) mayraa mayraa kar roveejai. They cry out, "His is mine, he is mine!"
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	mwieAw kwrix roie ivgUcih iDRgu jIvxu sMswrw hy ]8] (1027-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) maa-i-aa kaaran ro-ay vigoocheh Dharig jeevan sansaaraa hay. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	They cry for the sake of Maya, and are ruined; their lives in this world are cursed. ||8||
RECORD	para 44757	kwlI hU Puin Dauly Awey ] (1027-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaalee hoo fun Dha-ulay aa-ay. Their black hair eventually turns grey.
RECORD	para 44758	ivxu nwvY gQu gieAw gvwey ] (1027-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) vin naavai gath ga-i-aa gavaa-ay. Without the Name, they lose their wealth, and then leave.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	durmiq AMDulw ibnis ibnwsY mUTy roie pUkwrw hy ]9] (1027-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) durmat anDhulaa binas binaasai moothay ro-ay pookaaraa hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	They are evil-minded and blind - they are totally ruined; they are plundered, and cry out in pain. ||9||
RECORD	para 44760	Awpu vIcwir n rovY koeI ] (1027-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap veechaar na rovai ko-ee. One who understands himself, does not cry.
WHEN	para 44761	siqguru imlY q soJI hoeI ] (1027-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur milai ta sojhee ho-ee. When he meets the True Guru, then he understands.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	ibnu gur bjr kpwt n KUlih sbid imlY insqwrw hy ]10] (1027-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur bajar kapaat na khooleh sabad milai nistaaraa hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	Without the Guru, the heavy, hard doors are not opened. Obtaining the Word of the Shabad, one is emancipated. ||10||
DEFINE	para 44763	ibriD BieAw qnu CIjY dyhI ] (1027-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) biraDh bha-i-aa tan chheejai dayhee. The body grows old, and is beaten out of shape.
RECORD	para 44764	rwmu n jpeI AMiq snyhI ] (1027-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam na jap-ee ant sanayhee. But he does not meditate on the Lord, His only friend, even at the end.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	nwmu ivswir clY muih kwlY drgh JUTu KuAwrw hy ]11] (1027-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam visaar chalai muhi kaalai dargeh jhooth khu-aaraa hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Forgetting the Naam, the Name of the Lord, he departs with his face blackened. The false are humiliated in the Court of the Lord. ||11||
RECORD	para 44766	nwmu ivswir clY kUiVAwro ] (1027-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam visaar chalai koorhi-aaro. Forgetting the Naam, the false ones depart.
RECORD	para 44767	Awvq jwq pVY isir Cwro ] (1027-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) aavat jaat parhai sir chhaaro. Coming and going, dust falls on their heads.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	swhurVY Gir vwsu n pwey pyeIAVY isir mwrw hy ]12] (1027-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) saahurrhai ghar vaas na paa-ay pay-ee-arhai sir maaraa hay. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	The soul-bride finds no home in her in-laws' home, the world hereafter; she suffers in agony in this world of her parents' home. ||12||
RECORD	para 44769	KwjY pYJY rlI krIjY ] (1027-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) khaajai paijhai ralee kareejai. She eats, dresses and plays joyfully,
RECORD	para 44770	ibnu AB BgqI bwid mrIjY ] (1027-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin abh bhagtee baad mareejai. but without loving devotional worship of the Lord, she dies uselessly.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	sr Apsr kI swr n jwxY jmu mwry ikAw cwrw hy ]13] (1027-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) sar apsar kee saar na jaanai jam maaray ki-aa chaaraa hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	One who does not distinguish between good and evil, is beaten by the Messenger of Death; how can anyone escape this? ||13||
RECORD	para 44772	privrqI nrivriq pCwxY ] (1027-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) parvirtee narvirat pachhaanai. One who realizes what he has to possess, and what he has to abandon,
RECORD	para 44773	gur kY sMig sbid Gru jwxY ] (1027-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kai sang sabad ghar jaanai. associating with the Guru, comes to know the Word of the Shabad, within the home of his own self.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	iks hI mMdw AwiK n clY sic Krw sicAwrw hy ]14] (1027-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) kis hee mandaa aakh na chalai sach kharaa sachi-aaraa hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Do not call anyone else bad; follow this way of life. Those who are true are judged to be genuine by the True Lord. ||14||
RECORD	para 44775	swc ibnw dir isJY n koeI ] (1027-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) saach binaa dar sijhai na ko-ee. Without Truth, no one succeeds in the Court of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 44776	swc sbid pYJY piq hoeI ] (1027-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) saach sabad paijhai pat ho-ee. Through the True Shabad, one is robed in honor.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	Awpy bKis ley iqsu BwvY haumY grbu invwrw hy ]15] (1027-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay bakhas la-ay tis bhaavai ha-umai garab nivaaraa hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	He forgives those with whom He is pleased; they silence their egotism and pride. ||15||
RECORD	para 44778	gur ikrpw qy hukmu pCwxY ] (1027-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kirpaa tay hukam pachhaanai. One who realizes the Hukam of God's Command, by the Grace of the Guru,
RECORD	para 44779	jugh jugMqr kI ibiD jwxY ] (1027-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) jugah jugantar kee biDh jaanai. comes to know the lifestyle of the ages.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	nwnk nwmu jphu qru qwrI scu qwry qwrxhwrw hy ]16]1]7] (1027-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak naam japahu tar taaree sach taaray taaranhaaraa hay. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	O Nanak, chant the Naam, and cross over to the other side. The True Lord will carry you across. ||16||
RECORD	para 44782	hir sw mIqu nwhI mY koeI ] (1027-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) har saa meet naahee mai ko-ee. I have no other friend like the Lord.
RECORD	para 44783	ijin qnu mnu dIAw suriq smoeI ] (1027-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin tan man dee-aa surat samo-ee. He gave me body and mind, and infused consciousness into my being.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	srb jIAw pRiqpwil smwly so AMqir dwnw bInw hy ]1] (1027-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarab jee-aa partipaal samaalay so antar daanaa beenaa hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	He cherishes and cares for all beings; He is deep within, the wise, all-knowing Lord. ||1||
DEFINE	para 44785	guru srvru hm hMs ipAwry ] (1027-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur sarvar ham hans pi-aaray. The Guru is the sacred pool, and I am His beloved swan.
DEFINE	para 44786	swgr mih rqn lwl bhu swry ] (1027-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) saagar meh ratan laal baho saaray. In the ocean, there are so many jewels and rubies.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	moqI mwxk hIrw hir jsu gwvq mnu qnu BInw hy ]2] (1027-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) motee maanak heeraa har jas gaavat man tan bheenaa hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	The Lord's Praises are pearls, gems and diamonds. Singing His Praises, my mind and body are drenched with His Love. ||2||
DEFINE	para 44788	hir Agm Agwhu AgwiD inrwlw ] (1027-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) har agam agaahu agaaDh niraalaa. The Lord is inaccessible, inscrutable, unfathomable and unattached.
DEFINE	para 44789	hir AMqu n pweIAY gur gopwlw ] (1027-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) har ant na paa-ee-ai gur gopaalaa. The Lord's limits cannot be found; the Guru is the Lord of the World.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	siqgur miq qwry qwrxhwrw myil ley rMig lInw hy ]3] (1027-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur mat taaray taaranhaaraa mayl la-ay rang leenaa hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Through the Teachings of the True Guru, the Lord carries us across to the other side. He unites in His Union those who are colored by His Love. ||3||
RECORD	para 44791	siqgur bwJhu mukiq iknyhI ] (1027-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur baajhahu mukat kinayhee. Without the True Guru, how can anyone be liberated?
RECORD	para 44792	Ehu Awid jugwdI rwm snyhI ] (1027-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) oh aad jugaadee raam sanayhee. He has been the Friend of the Lord, from the very beginning of time, and all throughout the ages.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	drgh mukiq kry kir ikrpw bKsy Avgux kInw hy ]4] (1027-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) dargeh mukat karay kar kirpaa bakhsay avgun keenaa hay. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	By His Grace, He grants liberation in His Court; He forgives them for their sins. ||4||
RECORD	para 44795	siqguru dwqw mukiq krwey ] (1028-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur daataa mukat karaa-ay. The True Guru, the Giver, grants liberation;
DEFINE	para 44796	siB rog gvwey AMimRq rsu pwey ] (1028-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabh rog gavaa-ay amrit ras paa-ay. all diseases are eradicated, and one is blessed with the Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	jmu jwgwiq nwhI kru lwgY ijsu Agin buJI Tru sInw hy ]5] (1028-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) jam jaagaat naahee kar laagai jis agan bujhee thar seenaa hay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Death, the tax collector, does not impose any tax on one whose inner fire has been put out, whose heart is cool and tranquil. ||5||
RECORD	para 44798	kwieAw hMs pRIiq bhu DwrI ] (1028-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa hans pareet baho Dhaaree. The body has developed a great love for the soul-swan.
DEFINE	para 44799	Ehu jogI purKu Eh suMdir nwrI ] (1028-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) oh jogee purakh oh sundar naaree. He is a Yogi, and she is a beautiful woman.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Aihinis BogY coj ibnodI auiT clqY mqw n kInw hy ]6] (1028-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) ahinis bhogai choj binodee uth chaltai mataa na keenaa hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Day and night, he enjoys her with delight, and then he arises and departs without consulting her. ||6||
RECORD	para 44801	isRsit aupwie rhy pRB CwjY ] (1028-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarisat upaa-ay rahay parabh chhaajai. Creating the Universe, God remains diffused throughout it.
RECORD	para 44802	paux pwxI bYsMqru gwjY ] (1028-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) pa-un paanee baisantar gaajai. In the wind, water and fire, He vibrates and resounds.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	mnUAw folY dUq sMgiq imil so pwey jo ikCu kInw hy ]7] (1028-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) manoo-aa dolai doot sangat mil so paa-ay jo kichh keenaa hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	The mind wavers, keeping company with evil passions; one obtains the rewards of his own actions. ||7||
RECORD	para 44804	nwmu ivswir doK duK shIAY ] (1028-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam visaar dokh dukh sahee-ai. Forgetting the Naam, one suffers the misery of his evil ways.
DEFINE	para 44805	hukmu BieAw clxw ikau rhIAY ] (1028-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) hukam bha-i-aa chalnaa ki-o rahee-ai. When the order to depart is issued, how can he remain here?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	nrk kUp mih goqy KwvY ijau jl qy bwhir mInw hy ]8] (1028-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) narak koop meh gotay khaavai ji-o jal tay baahar meenaa hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	He falls into the pit of hell, and suffers like a fish out of water. ||8||
RECORD	para 44807	caurwsIh nrk swkqu BogweIAY ] (1028-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) cha-oraaseeh narak saakat bhogaa-ee-ai. The faithless cynic has to endure 8.4 million hellish incarnations.
RECORD	para 44808	jYsw kIcY qYso pweIAY ] (1028-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaisaa keechai taiso paa-ee-ai. As he acts, so does he suffer.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	siqgur bwJhu mukiq n hoeI ikriq bwDw gRis dInw hy ]9] (1028-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur baajhahu mukat na ho-ee kirat baaDhaa garas deenaa hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	Without the True Guru, there is no liberation. Bound and gagged by his own actions, he is helpless. ||9||
DEFINE	para 44810	KMfy Dwr glI Aiq BIVI ] (1028-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) khanday Dhaar galee at bheerhee. This path is very narrow, like the sharp edge of a sword.
REQUIRE	para 44811	lyKw lIjY iql ijau pIVI ] (1028-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) laykhaa leejai til ji-o peerhee. When his account is read, he shall be crushed like the sesame seed in the mill.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	mwq ipqw klqR suq bylI nwhI ibnu hir rs mukiq n kInw hy ]10] (1028-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) maat pitaa kaltar sut baylee naahee bin har ras mukat na keenaa hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	Mother, father, spouse and child - none is anyone's friend in the end. Without the Lord's Love, no one is liberated. ||10||
ALLOW	para 44813	mIq sKy kyqy jg mwhI ] (1028-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) meet sakhay kaytay jag maahee. You may have many friends and companions in the world,
DEFINE	para 44814	ibnu gur prmysr koeI nwhI ] (1028-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur parmaysar ko-ee naahee. but without the Guru, the Transcendent Lord Incarnate, there is no one at all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	gur kI syvw mukiq prwieix Anidnu kIrqnu kInw hy ]11] (1028-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kee sayvaa mukat paraa-in an-din keertan keenaa hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Service to the Guru is the way to liberation. Night and day, sing the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises. ||11||
WHEN	para 44816	kUVu Coif swcy kau Dwvhu ] (1028-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) koorh chhod saachay ka-o Dhaavahu. Abandon falsehood, and pursue the Truth,
REQUIRE	para 44817	jo ieChu soeI Plu pwvhu ] (1028-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo ichhahu so-ee fal paavhu. and you shall obtain the fruits of your desires.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	swc vKr ky vwpwrI ivrly lY lwhw saudw kInw hy ]12] (1028-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) saach vakhar kay vaapaaree virlay lai laahaa sa-udaa keenaa hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	Very few are those who trade in the merchandise of Truth. Those who deal in it, obtain the true profit. ||12||
RECORD	para 44819	hir hir nwmu vKru lY clhu ] (1028-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) har har naam vakhar lai chalhu. Depart with the merchandise of the Name of the Lord, Har, Har,
REQUIRE	para 44820	drsnu pwvhu shij mhlhu ] (1028-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) darsan paavhu sahj mahlahu. and you shall intuitively obtain the Blessed Vision of His Darshan, in the Mansion of His Presence.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	gurmuiK Koij lhih jn pUry ieau smdrsI cInw hy ]13] (1028-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh khoj laheh jan pooray i-o samadrasee cheenaa hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	The Gurmukhs search for Him and find Him; they are the perfect humble beings. In this way, they see Him, who looks upon all alike. ||13||
DEFINE	para 44822	pRB byAMq gurmiq ko pwvih ] (1028-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) parabh bay-ant gurmat ko paavahi. God is endless; following the Guru's Teachings, some find Him.
RECORD	para 44823	gur kY sbid mn kau smJwvih ] (1028-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kai sabad man ka-o samjhaavahi. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, they instruct their minds.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	siqgur kI bwxI siq siq kir mwnhu ieau Awqm rwmY lInw hy ]14] (1028-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur kee banee sat sat kar maanhu i-o aatam raamai leenaa hay. ||14||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Accept as True, Perfectly True, the Word of the True Guru's Bani. In this way, you shall merge in the Lord, the Supreme Soul. ||14||
DEFINE	para 44825	nwrd swrd syvk qyry ] (1028-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) naarad saarad sayvak tayray. Naarad and Saraswati are Your servants.
DEFINE	para 44826	iqRBvix syvk vfhu vfyry ] (1028-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) taribhavan sayvak vadahu vadayray. Your servants are the greatest of the great, throughout the three worlds.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	sB qyrI kudriq qU isir isir dwqw sBu qyro kwrxu kInw hy ]15] (1028-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabh tayree kudrat too sir sir daataa sabh tayro kaaran keenaa hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	Your creative power permeates all; You are the Great Giver of all. You created the whole creation. ||15||
DEFINE	para 44828	ieik dir syvih drdu v\wey ] (1028-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik dar sayveh darad vanjaa-ay. Some serve at Your Door, and their sufferings are dispelled.
DEFINE	para 44829	Eie drgh pYDy siqgurU Cfwey ] (1028-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) o-ay dargeh paiDhay satguroo chhadaa-ay. They are robed with honor in the Court of the Lord, and emancipated by the True Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	haumY bMDn siqguir qoVy icqu cMclu clix n dInw hy ]16] (1028-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai banDhan satgur torhay chit chanchal chalan na deenaa hay. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	The True Guru breaks the bonds of egotism, and restrains the fickle consciousness. ||16||
RECORD	para 44831	siqgur imlhu cInhu ibiD sweI ] (1028-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur milhu cheenahu biDh saa-ee. Meet the True Guru, and search for the way,
ALLOW	para 44832	ijqu pRBu pwvhu gxq n kweI ] (1028-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) jit parabh paavhu ganat na kaa-ee. by which you may find God, and not have to answer for your account.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	haumY mwir krhu gur syvw jn nwnk hir rMig BInw hy ]17]2]8] (1028-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai maar karahu gur sayvaa jan naanak har rang bheenaa hay. ||17||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	Subdue your egotism, and serve the Guru; O servant Nanak, you shall be drenched with the Lord's Love. ||17||
DEFINE	para 44835	Asur sGwrx rwmu hmwrw ] (1028-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) asur saghaaran raam hamaaraa. My Lord is the Destroyer of demons.
DEFINE	para 44836	Git Git rmeIAw rwmu ipAwrw ] (1028-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) ghat ghat rama-ee-aa raam pi-aaraa. My Beloved Lord is pervading each and every heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	nwly AlKu n lKIAY mUly gurmuiK ilKu vIcwrw hy ]1] (1028-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) naalay alakh na lakhee-ai moolay gurmukh likh veechaaraa hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	The unseen Lord is always with us, but He is not seen at all. The Gurmukh contemplates the record. ||1||
RECORD	para 44838	gurmuiK swDU srix qumwrI ] (1028-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh saaDhoo saran tumaaree. The Holy Gurmukh seeks Your Sanctuary.
RECORD	para 44840	kir ikrpw pRiB pwir auqwrI ] (1029-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) kar kirpaa parabh paar utaaree. God grants His Grace, and carries him across to the other side.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Agin pwxI swgru Aiq ghrw guru siqguru pwir auqwrw hy ]2] (1029-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) agan paanee saagar at gahraa gur satgur paar utaaraa hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	The ocean is very deep, filled with fiery water; the Guru, the True Guru, carries us across to the other side. ||2||
RECORD	para 44842	mnmuK AMDuly soJI nwhI ] (1029-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh anDhulay sojhee naahee. The blind, self-willed manmukh does not understand.
RECORD	para 44843	Awvih jwih mrih mir jwhI ] (1029-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) aavahi jaahi mareh mar jaahee. He comes and goes in reincarnation, dying, and dying again.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	pUrib iliKAw lyKu n imteI jm dir AMDu KuAwrw hy ]3] (1029-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) poorab likhi-aa laykh na mit-ee jam dar anDh khu-aaraa hay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	The primal inscription of destiny cannot be erased. The spiritually blind suffer terribly at Death's door. ||3||
RECORD	para 44845	ieik Awvih jwvih Gir vwsu n pwvih ] (1029-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik aavahi jaaveh ghar vaas na paavahi. Some come and go, and do not find a home in their own heart.
RECORD	para 44846	ikrq ky bwDy pwp kmwvih ] (1029-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) kirat kay baaDhay paap kamaaveh. Bound by their past actions, they commit sins.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	AMDuly soJI bUJ n kweI loBu burw AhMkwrw hy ]4] (1029-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) anDhulay sojhee boojh na kaa-ee lobh buraa aha Nkaaraa hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	The blind ones have no understanding, no wisdom; they are trapped and ruined by greed and egotism. ||4||
DEFINE	para 44848	ipr ibnu ikAw iqsu Dn sIgwrw ] (1029-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) pir bin ki-aa tis Dhan seegaaraa. Without her Husband Lord, what good are the soul-bride's decorations?
DEFINE	para 44849	pr ipr rwqI Ksmu ivswrw ] (1029-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) par pir raatee khasam visaaraa. She has forgotten her Lord and Master, and is infatuated with another's husband.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	ijau bysuAw pUq bwpu ko khIAY iqau Pokt kwr ivkwrw hy ]5] (1029-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) ji-o baysu-aa poot baap ko kahee-ai ti-o fokat kaar vikaaraa hay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Just as no one knows who is the father of the prostitute's son, such are the worthless, useless deeds that are done. ||5||
RECORD	para 44851	pRyq ipMjr mih dUK Gnyry ] (1029-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) parayt pinjar meh dookh ghanayray. The ghost, in the body-cage, suffers all sorts of afflictions.
DEFINE	para 44852	nrik pcih AigAwn AMDyry ] (1029-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) narak pacheh agi-aan anDhayray. Those who are blind to spiritual wisdom, putrefy in hell.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Drm rwie kI bwkI lIjY ijin hir kw nwmu ivswrw hy ]6] (1029-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) Dharam raa-ay kee baakee leejai jin har kaa naam visaaraa hay. ||6||
