DEFINE	para 44878	kUkr sUkr khIAih kUiVAwrw ] (1029-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) kookar sookar kahee-ahi koorhi-aaraa. The false are called pigs and dogs.
RECORD	para 44879	Bauik mrih Bau Bau Bau hwrw ] (1029-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) bha-uk mareh bha-o bha-o bha-o haaraa. They bark themselves to death; they bark and bark and howl in fear.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	min qin JUTy kUVu kmwvih durmiq drgh hwrw hy ]15] (1029-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) man tan jhoothay koorh kamaaveh durmat dargeh haaraa hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	False in mind and body, they practice falsehood; through their evil-mindedness, they lose out in the Court of the Lord. ||15||
DEFINE	para 44881	siqguru imlY q mnUAw tykY ] (1029-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur milai ta manoo-aa taykai. Meeting the True Guru, the mind is stabilized.
DEFINE	para 44882	rwm nwmu dy srix prykY ] (1029-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam day saran paraykai. One who seeks His Sanctuary is blessed with the Lord's Name.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	hir Dnu nwmu Amolku dyvY hir jsu drgh ipAwrw hy ]16] (1029-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) har Dhan naam amolak dayvai har jas dargeh pi-aaraa hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	They are given the priceless wealth of the Lord's Name; singing His Praises, they are His beloveds in His court. ||16||
RECORD	para 44885	rwm nwmu swDU srxweI ] (1030-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam saaDhoo sarnaa-ee. In the Sanctuary of the Holy, chant the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 44886	siqgur bcnI giq imiq pweI ] (1030-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur bachnee gat mit paa-ee. Through the True Guru's Teachings, one comes to know His state and extent.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	nwnk hir jip hir mn myry hir myly mylxhwrw hy ]17]3]9] (1030-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak har jap har man mayray har maylay maylanhaaraa hay. ||17||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	Nanak: chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, O my mind; the Lord, the Uniter, shall unite you with Himself. ||17||
RECORD	para 44889	Gir rhu ry mn mugD ieAwny ] (1030-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) ghar rahu ray man mugaDh i-aanay. Remain in your own home, O my foolish and ignorant mind.
RECORD	para 44890	rwmu jphu AMqrgiq iDAwny ] (1030-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam japahu antargat Dhi-aanay. Meditate on the Lord - concentrate deep within your being and meditate on Him.
WHEN	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	lwlc Coif rchu AprMpir ieau pwvhu mukiq duAwrw hy ]1] (1030-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) laalach chhod rachahu aprampar i-o paavhu mukat du-aaraa hay. ||1||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	Renounce your greed, and merge with the infinite Lord. In this way, you shall find the door of liberation. ||1||
WHEN	para 44892	ijsu ibsirAY jmu johix lwgY ] (1030-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis bisri-ai jam johan laagai. If you forget Him, the Messenger of Death will catch sight of you.
RECORD	para 44893	siB suK jwih duKw Puin AwgY ] (1030-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabh sukh jaahi dukhaa fun aagai. All peace will be gone, and you will suffer in pain in the world hereafter.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	rwm nwmu jip gurmuiK jIAVy eyhu prm qqu vIcwrw hy ]2] (1030-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam jap gurmukh jee-arhay ayhu param tat veechaaraa hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Chant the Name of the Lord as Gurmukh, O my soul; this is the supreme essence of contemplation. ||2||
RECORD	para 44895	hir hir nwmu jphu rsu mITw ] (1030-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) har har naam japahu ras meethaa. Chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, the sweetest essence.
RECORD	para 44896	gurmuiK hir rsu AMqir fITw ] (1030-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh har ras antar deethaa. As Gurmukh, see the essence of the Lord deep within.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Aihinis rwm rhhu rMig rwqy eyhu jpu qpu sMjmu swrw hy ]3] (1030-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) ahinis raam rahhu rang raatay ayhu jap tap sanjam saaraa hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Day and night, remain imbued with the Lord's Love. This is the essence of all chanting, deep meditation and self-discipline. ||3||
RECORD	para 44898	rwm nwmu gur bcnI bolhu ] (1030-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam gur bachnee bolhu. Speak the Guru's Word, and the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 44899	sMq sBw mih iehu rsu tolhu ] (1030-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) sant sabhaa meh ih ras tolahu. In the Society of the Saints, search for this essence.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	gurmiq Koij lhhu Gru Apnw bhuiV n grB mJwrw hy ]4] (1030-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmat khoj lahhu ghar apnaa bahurh na garabh majhaaraa hay. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	Follow the Guru's Teachings - seek and find the home of your own self, and you shall never be consigned to the womb of reincarnation again. ||4||
RECORD	para 44901	scu qIriQ nwvhu hir gux gwvhu ] (1030-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach tirath naavhu har gun gaavhu. Bathe at the sacred shrine of Truth, and sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord.
RECORD	para 44902	qqu vIcwrhu hir ilv lwvhu ] (1030-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) tat veechaarahu har liv laavhu. Reflect upon the essence of reality, and lovingly focus your consciousness on the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	AMq kwil jmu joih n swkY hir bolhu rwmu ipAwrw hy ]5] (1030-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) ant kaal jam johi na saakai har bolhu raam pi-aaraa hay. ||5||
WHEN	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	At the very last moment, the Messenger of Death will not be able to touch you, if you chant the Name of the Beloved Lord. ||5||
DEFINE	para 44904	siqguru purKu dwqw vf dwxw ] (1030-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur purakh daataa vad daanaa. The True Guru, the Primal Being, the Great Giver, is all-knowing.
RECORD	para 44905	ijsu AMqir swcu su sbid smwxw ] (1030-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis antar saach so sabad samaanaa. Whoever has Truth within himself, merges in the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	ijs kau siqguru myil imlwey iqsu cUkw jm BY Bwrw hy ]6] (1030-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis ka-o satgur mayl milaa-ay tis chookaa jam bhai bhaaraa hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	One whom the True Guru unites in Union, is rid of the overpowering fear of death. ||6||
DEFINE	para 44907	pMc qqu imil kwieAw kInI ] (1030-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) panch tat mil kaa-i-aa keenee. The body is formed from the union of the five elements.
DEFINE	para 44908	iqs mih rwm rqnu lY cInI ] (1030-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) tis meh raam ratan lai cheenee. Know that the Lord's jewel is within it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	Awqm rwmu rwmu hY Awqm hir pweIAY sbid vIcwrw hy ]7] (1030-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) aatam raam raam hai aatam har paa-ee-ai sabad veechaaraa hay. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	The soul is the Lord, and the Lord is the soul; contemplating the Shabad, the Lord is found. ||7||
RECORD	para 44910	sq sMqoiK rhhu jn BweI ] (1030-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) sat santokh rahhu jan bhaa-ee. Abide in truth and contentment, O humble Siblings of Destiny.
RECORD	para 44911	iKmw ghhu siqgur srxweI ] (1030-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) khimaa gahhu satgur sarnaa-ee. Hold tight to compassion and the Sanctuary of the True Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	Awqmu cIin prwqmu cInhu gur sMgiq iehu insqwrw hy ]8] (1030-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aatam cheen paraatam cheenahu gur sangat ih nistaaraa hay. ||8||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	Know your soul, and know the Supreme Soul; associating with the Guru, you shall be emancipated. ||8||
DEFINE	para 44913	swkq kUV kpt mih tykw ] (1030-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) saakat koorh kapat meh taykaa. The faithless cynics are stuck in falsehood and deceit.
RECORD	para 44914	Aihinis inMdw krih Anykw ] (1030-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) ahinis nindaa karahi anaykaa. Day and night, they slander many others.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	ibnu ismrn Awvih Puin jwvih gRB jonI nrk mJwrw hy ]9] (1030-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin simran aavahi fun jaaveh garabh jonee narak majhaaraa hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	Without meditative remembrance, they come and then go, and are cast into the hellish womb of reincarnation. ||9||
DEFINE	para 44916	swkq jm kI kwix n cUkY ] (1030-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) saakat jam kee kaan na chookai. The faithless cynic is not rid of his fear of death.
DEFINE	para 44917	jm kw fMfu n kbhU mUkY ] (1030-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) jam kaa dand na kabhoo mookai. The Messenger of Death's club is never taken away.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	bwkI Drm rwie kI lIjY isir APirE Bwru APwrw hy ]10] (1030-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) baakee Dharam raa-ay kee leejai sir afri-o bhaar afaaraa hay. ||10||
UPHOLD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	He has to answer to the Righteous Judge of Dharma for the account of his actions; the egotistical being carries the unbearable load. ||10||
RECORD	para 44919	ibnu gur swkqu khhu ko qirAw ] (1030-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur saakat kahhu ko tari-aa. Tell me: without the Guru, what faithless cynic has been saved?
RECORD	para 44920	haumY krqw Bvjil pirAw ] (1030-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai kartaa bhavjal pari-aa. Acting egotistically, he falls into the terrifying world-ocean.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	ibnu gur pwru n pwvY koeI hir jpIAY pwir auqwrw hy ]11] (1030-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur paar na paavai ko-ee har japee-ai paar utaaraa hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Without the Guru, no one is saved; meditating on the Lord, they are carried across to the other side. ||11||
RECORD	para 44922	gur kI dwiq n mytY koeI ] (1030-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kee daat na maytai ko-ee. No one can erase the Guru's blessings.
RECORD	para 44923	ijsu bKsy iqsu qwry soeI ] (1030-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis bakhsay tis taaray so-ee. The Lord carries across those whom He forgives.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	jnm mrx duKu nyiV n AwvY min so pRBu Apr Apwrw hy ]12] (1030-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) janam maran dukh nayrh na aavai man so parabh apar apaaraa hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	The pains of birth and death do not even approach those whose minds are filled with God, the infinite and endless. ||12||
RECORD	para 44925	gur qy BUly Awvhu jwvhu ] (1030-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur tay bhoolay aavhu jaavhu. Those who forget the Guru come and go in reincarnation.
DEFINE	para 44926	jnim mrhu Puin pwp kmwvhu ] (1030-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) janam marahu fun paap kamaavahu. They are born, only to die again, and continue committing sins.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	swkq mUV Acyq n cyqih duKu lwgY qw rwmu pukwrw hy ]13] (1030-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) saakat moorh achayt na cheeteh dukh laagai taa raam pukaaraa hay. ||13||
WHEN	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	The unconscious, foolish, faithless cynic does not remember the Lord; but when he is stricken with pain, then he cries out for the Lord. ||13||
DEFINE	para 44928	suKu duKu purb jnm ky kIey ] (1030-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) sukh dukh purab janam kay kee-ay. Pleasure and pain are the consequences of the actions of past lives.
RECORD	para 44929	so jwxY ijin dwqY dIey ] (1030-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) so jaanai jin daatai dee-ay. The Giver, who blesses us with these - He alone knows.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	iks kau dosu dyih qU pRwxI shu Apxw kIAw krwrw hy ]14] (1030-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) kis ka-o dos deh too paraanee saho apnaa kee-aa karaaraa hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	So who can you blame, O mortal being? The hardships you suffer are from your own actions. ||14||
RECORD	para 44932	haumY mmqw krdw AwieAw ] (1031-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai mamtaa kardaa aa-i-aa. Practicing egotism and possessiveness, you have come into the world.
RECORD	para 44933	Awsw mnsw bMiD clwieAw ] (1031-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) aasaa mansaa banDh chalaa-i-aa. Hope and desire bind you and lead you on.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	myrI myrI krq ikAw ly cwly ibKu lwdy Cwr ibkwrw hy ]15] (1031-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) mayree mayree karat ki-aa lay chaalay bikh laaday chhaar bikaaraa hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	Indulging in egotism and self-conceit, what will you be able to carry with you, except the load of ashes from poison and corruption? ||15||
RECORD	para 44935	hir kI Bgiq krhu jn BweI ] (1031-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) har kee bhagat karahu jan bhaa-ee. Worship the Lord in devotion, O humble Siblings of Destiny.
RECORD	para 44936	AkQu kQhu mnu mnih smweI ] (1031-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) akath kathahu man maneh samaa-ee. Speak the Unspoken Speech, and the mind will merge back into the Mind.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	auiT clqw Twik rKhu Gir ApunY duKu kwty kwtxhwrw hy ]16] (1031-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) uth chaltaa thaak rakhahu ghar apunai dukh kaatay kaatanhaaraa hay. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	Restrain your restless mind within its own home, and the Lord, the Destroyer, shall destroy your pain. ||16||
RECORD	para 44938	hir gur pUry kI Et prwqI ] (1031-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) har gur pooray kee ot paraatee. I seek the support of the Perfect Guru, the Lord.
RECORD	para 44939	gurmuiK hir ilv gurmuiK jwqI ] (1031-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh har liv gurmukh jaatee. The Gurmukh loves the Lord; the Gurmukh realizes the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	nwnk rwm nwim miq aUqm hir bKsy pwir auqwrw hy ]17]4]10] (1031-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak raam naam mat ootam har bakhsay paar utaaraa hay. ||17||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	O Nanak, through the Lord's Name, the intellect is exalted; granting His forgiveness, the Lord carries him across to the other side. ||17||
RECORD	para 44942	srix pry gurdyv qumwrI ] (1031-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) saran paray gurdayv tumaaree. O Divine Guru, I have entered Your Sanctuary.
DEFINE	para 44943	qU smrQu dieAwlu murwrI ] (1031-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) too samrath da-i-aal muraaree. You are the Almighty Lord, the Merciful Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	qyry coj n jwxY koeI qU pUrw purKu ibDwqw hy ]1] (1031-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) tayray choj na jaanai ko-ee too pooraa purakh biDhaataa hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	No one knows Your wondrous plays; You are the perfect Architect of Destiny. ||1||
RECORD	para 44945	qU Awid jugwid krih pRiqpwlw ] (1031-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) too aad jugaad karahi partipaalaa. From the very beginning of time, and throughout the ages, You cherish and sustain Your beings.
DEFINE	para 44946	Git Git rUpu AnUpu dieAwlw ] (1031-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) ghat ghat roop anoop da-i-aalaa. You are in each and every heart, O Merciful Lord of incomparable beauty.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	ijau quDu BwvY iqvY clwvih sBu qyro kIAw kmwqw hy ]2] (1031-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) ji-o tuDh bhaavai tivai chalaaveh sabh tayro kee-aa kamaataa hay. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	As You will, You cause all to walk; everyone acts according to Your Command. ||2||
DEFINE	para 44948	AMqir joiq BlI jgjIvn ] (1031-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar jot bhalee jagjeevan. Deep within the nucleus of all, is the Light of the Life of the World.
RECORD	para 44949	siB Gt BogY hir rsu pIvn ] (1031-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabh ghat bhogai har ras peevan. The Lord enjoys the hearts of all, and drinks in their essence.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Awpy lyvY Awpy dyvY iqhu loeI jgq ipq dwqw hy ]3] (1031-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay layvai aapay dayvai tihu lo-ee jagat pit daataa hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	He Himself gives, and He himself takes; He is the generous father of the beings of the three worlds. ||3||
RECORD	para 44951	jgqu aupwie Kylu rcwieAw ] (1031-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) jagat upaa-ay khayl rachaa-i-aa. Creating the world, He has set His play into motion.
RECORD	para 44952	pvxY pwxI AgnI jIau pwieAw ] (1031-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) pavnai paanee agnee jee-o paa-i-aa. He placed the soul in the body of air, water and fire.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	dyhI ngrI nau drvwjy so dsvw gupqu rhwqw hy ]4] (1031-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) dayhee nagree na-o darvaajay so dasvaa gupat rahaataa hay. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	The body-village has nine gates; the Tenth Gate remains hidden. ||4||
DEFINE	para 44954	cwir ndI AgnI Asrwlw ] (1031-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) chaar nadee agnee asraalaa. There are four horrible rivers of fire.
DEFINE	para 44955	koeI gurmuiK bUJY sbid inrwlw ] (1031-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) ko-ee gurmukh boojhai sabad niraalaa. How rare is that Gurmukh who understands this, and through the Word of the Shabad, remains unattached.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	swkq durmiq fUbih dwJih guir rwKy hir ilv rwqw hy ]5] (1031-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) saakat durmat doobeh daajheh gur raakhay har liv raataa hay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	The faithless cynics are drowned and burnt through their evil-mindedness. The Guru saves those who are imbued with the Love of the Lord. ||5||
RECORD	para 44957	Apu qyju vwie ipRQmI Awkwsw ] (1031-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) ap tayj vaa-ay parithmee aakaasaa. Water, fire, air, earth and ether
RECORD	para 44958	iqn mih pMc qqu Gir vwsw ] (1031-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) tin meh panch tat ghar vaasaa. - in that house of the five elements, they dwell.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	siqgur sbid rhih rMig rwqw qij mwieAw haumY BRwqw hy ]6] (1031-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur sabad raheh rang raataa taj maa-i-aa ha-umai bharaataa hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Those who remain imbued with the Word of the True Guru's Shabad, renounce Maya, egotism and doubt. ||6||
DEFINE	para 44960	iehu mnu BIjY sbid pqIjY ] (1031-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) ih man bheejai sabad pateejai. This mind is drenched with the Shabad, and satisfied.
RECORD	para 44961	ibnu nwvY ikAw tyk itkIjY ] (1031-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin naavai ki-aa tayk tikeejai. Without the Name, what support can anyone have?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	AMqir coru muhY Gru mMdru iein swkiq dUqu n jwqw hy ]7] (1031-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar chor muhai ghar mandar in saakat doot na jaataa hay. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	The temple of the body is being plundered by the thieves within, but this faithless cynic does not even recognize these demons. ||7||
DEFINE	para 44963	duMdr dUq BUq BIhwly ] (1031-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) dundar doot bhoot bheehaalay. They are argumentative demons, terrifying goblins.
RECORD	para 44964	iKMcoqwix krih byqwly ] (1031-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) khinchotaan karahi baytaalay. These demons stir up conflict and strife.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	sbd suriq ibnu AwvY jwvY piq KoeI Awvq jwqw hy ]8] (1031-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad surat bin aavai jaavai pat kho-ee aavat jaataa hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	Without awareness of the Shabad, one comes and goes in reincarnation; he loses his honor in this coming and going. ||8||
DEFINE	para 44966	kUVu klru qnu BsmY FyrI ] (1031-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) koorh kalar tan bhasmai dhayree. The body of the false person is just a pile of barren dirt.
RECORD	para 44967	ibnu nwvY kYsI piq qyrI ] (1031-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin naavai kaisee pat tayree. Without the Name, what honor can you have?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	bwDy mukiq nwhI jug cwry jmkMkir kwil prwqw hy ]9] (1031-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) baaDhay mukat naahee jug chaaray jamkankar kaal paraataa hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	Bound and gagged throughout the four ages, there is no liberation; the Messenger of Death keeps such a person under his gaze. ||9||
DEFINE	para 44969	jm dir bwDy imlih sjweI ] (1031-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) jam dar baaDhay mileh sajaa-ee. At Death's door, he is tied up and punished;
RECORD	para 44970	iqsu AprwDI giq nhI kweI ] (1031-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) tis apraaDhee gat nahee kaa-ee. such a sinner does not obtain salvation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	krx plwv kry ibllwvY ijau kuMfI mInu prwqw hy ]10] (1031-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) karan palaav karay billaavai ji-o kundee meen paraataa hay. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	He cries out in pain, like the fish pierced by the hook. ||10||
DEFINE	para 44972	swkqu PwsI pVY iekylw ] (1031-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) saakat faasee parhai ikaylaa. The faithless cynic is caught in the noose all alone.
DEFINE	para 44973	jm vis kIAw AMDu duhylw ] (1031-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) jam vas kee-aa anDh duhaylaa. The miserable spiritually blind person is caught in the power of Death.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	rwm nwm ibnu mukiq n sUJY Awju kwil pic jwqw hy ]11] (1031-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam bin mukat na soojhai aaj kaal pach jaataa hay. ||11||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Without the Lord's Name, liberation is not known. He shall waste away, today or tomorrow. ||11||
DEFINE	para 44975	siqgur bwJu n bylI koeI ] (1031-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur baajh na baylee ko-ee. Other than the True Guru, no one is your friend.
DEFINE	para 44976	AYQY EQY rwKw pRBu soeI ] (1031-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) aithai othai raakhaa parabh so-ee. Here and hereafter, God is the Savior.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	rwm nwmu dyvY kir ikrpw ieau sllY sll imlwqw hy ]12] (1031-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam dayvai kar kirpaa i-o sallai salal milaataa hay. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	He grants His Grace, and bestows the Lord's Name. He merges with Him, like water with water. ||12||
RECORD	para 44979	BUly isK gurU smJwey ] (1032-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhoolay sikh guroo samjhaa-ay. The Guru instructs His wandering Sikhs;
WHEN	para 44980	auJiV jwdy mwrig pwey ] (1032-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) ujharh jaaday maarag paa-ay. if they go astray, He sets them on the right path.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	iqsu gur syiv sdw idnu rwqI duK BMjn sMig sKwqw hy ]13] (1032-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) tis gur sayv sadaa din raatee dukh bhanjan sang sakhaataa hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	So serve the Guru, forever, day and night; He is the Destroyer of pain - He is with you as your companion. ||13||
RECORD	para 44982	gur kI Bgiq krih ikAw pRwxI ] (1032-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kee bhagat karahi ki-aa paraanee. O mortal being, what devotional worship have you performed to the Guru?
RECORD	para 44983	bRhmY ieMidR mhyis n jwxI ] (1032-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) barahmai in-dar mahays na jaanee. Even Brahma, Indra and Shiva do not know it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	siqguru AlKu khhu ikau lKIAY ijsu bKsy iqsih pCwqw hy ]14] (1032-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur alakh kahhu ki-o lakhee-ai jis bakhsay tiseh pachhaataa hay. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Tell me, how can the unknowable True Guru be known? He alone attains this realization, whom the Lord forgives. ||14||
UPHOLD	para 44985	AMqir pRymu prwpiq drsnu ] (1032-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar paraym paraapat darsan. One who has love within, obtains the Blessed Vision of His Darshan.
RECORD	para 44986	gurbwxI isau pRIiq su prsnu ] (1032-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurbaanee si-o pareet so parsan. One who enshrines love for the Word of the Guru's Bani, meets with Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	Aihinis inrml joiq sbweI Git dIpku gurmuiK jwqw hy ]15] (1032-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) ahinis nirmal jot sabaa-ee ghat deepak gurmukh jaataa hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	Day and night, the Gurmukh sees the immaculate Divine Light everywhere; this lamp illuminates his heart. ||15||
DEFINE	para 44988	Bojn igAwnu mhw rsu mITw ] (1032-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhojan gi-aan mahaa ras meethaa. The food of spiritual wisdom is the supremely sweet essence.
UPHOLD	para 44989	ijin cwiKAw iqin drsnu fITw ] (1032-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin chaakhi-aa tin darsan deethaa. Whoever tastes it, sees the Blessed Vision of the Lord's Darshan.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	drsnu dyiK imly bYrwgI mnu mnsw mwir smwqw hy ]16] (1032-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) darsan daykh milay bairaagee man mansaa maar samaataa hay. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	Beholding His Darshan, the unattached one meets the Lord; subduing the mind's desires, he merges into the Lord. ||16||
DEFINE	para 44991	siqguru syvih sy prDwnw ] (1032-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur sayveh say parDhaanaa. Those who serve the True Guru are supreme and famous.
RECORD	para 44992	iqn Gt Gt AMqir bRhmu pCwnw ] (1032-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) tin ghat ghat antar barahm pachhaanaa. Deep within each and every heart, they recognize God.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	nwnk hir jsu hir jn kI sMgiq dIjY ijn siqguru hir pRBu jwqw hy ]17]5]11] (1032-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak har jas har jan kee sangat deejai jin satgur har parabh jaataa hay. ||17||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	Please bless Nanak with the Lord's Praises, and the Sangat, the Congregation of the Lord's humble servants; through the True Guru, they know their Lord God. ||17||
DEFINE	para 44995	swcy swihb isrjxhwry ] (1032-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachay saahib sirjanhaaray. The True Lord is the Creator of the Universe.
RECORD	para 44996	ijin Dr ck® Dry vIcwry ] (1032-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin Dhar chakar Dharay veechaaray. He established and contemplates the worldly sphere.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	Awpy krqw kir kir vyKY swcw vyprvwhw hy ]1] (1032-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay kartaa kar kar vaykhai saachaa vayparvaahaa hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	He Himself created the creation, and beholds it; He is True and independent. ||1||
RECORD	para 44998	vykI vykI jMq aupwey ] (1032-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) vaykee vaykee jant upaa-ay. He created the beings of different kinds.
RECORD	para 44999	duie pMdI duie rwh clwey ] (1032-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) du-ay pandee du-ay raah chalaa-ay. The two travellers have set out in two directions.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	gur pUry ivxu mukiq n hoeI scu nwmu jip lwhw hy ]2] (1032-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur pooray vin mukat na ho-ee sach naam jap laahaa hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Without the Perfect Guru, no one is liberated. Chanting the True Name, one profits. ||2||
RECORD	para 45001	pVih mnmuK pru ibiD nhI jwnw ] (1032-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) parheh manmukh par biDh nahee jaanaa. The self-willed manmukhs read and study, but they do not know the way.
RECORD	para 45002	nwmu n bUJih Brim Bulwnw ] (1032-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam na boojheh bharam bhulaanaa. They do not understand the Naam, the Name of the Lord; they wander, deluded by doubt.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	lY kY vFI dyin augwhI durmiq kw gil Pwhw hy ]3] (1032-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) lai kai vadhee dayn ugaahee durmat kaa gal faahaa hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	They take bribes, and give false testimony; the noose of evil-mindedness is around their necks. ||3||
RECORD	para 45004	isimRiq swsqR pVih purwxw ] (1032-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) simrit saastar parheh puraanaa. They read the Simritees, the Shaastras and the Puraanas;
RECORD	para 45005	vwdu vKwxih qqu n jwxw ] (1032-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) vaad vakaaneh tat na jaanaa. they argue and debate, but do not know the essence of reality.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	ivxu gur pUry qqu n pweIAY sc sUcy scu rwhw hy ]4] (1032-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) vin gur pooray tat na paa-ee-ai sach soochay sach raahaa hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	Without the Perfect Guru, the essence of reality is not obtained. The true and pure beings walk the Path of Truth. ||4||
RECORD	para 45007	sB swlwhy suix suix AwKY ] (1032-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabh saalaahay sun sun aakhai. All praise God and listen, and listen and speak.
DEFINE	para 45008	Awpy dwnw scu prwKY ] (1032-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay daanaa sach paraakhai. He Himself is wise, and He Himself judges the Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	ijn kau ndir kry pRBu ApnI gurmuiK sbdu slwhw hy ]5] (1032-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) jin ka-o nadar karay parabh apnee gurmukh sabad salaahaa hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Those whom God blesses with His Glance of Grace become Gurmukh, and praise the Word of the Shabad. ||5||
RECORD	para 45010	suix suix AwKY kyqI bwxI ] (1032-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) sun sun aakhai kaytee banee. Many listen and listen, and speak the Guru's Bani.
RECORD	para 45011	suix khIAY ko AMqu n jwxI ] (1032-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) sun kahee-ai ko ant na jaanee. Listening and speaking, no one knows His limits.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	jw kau AlKu lKwey Awpy AkQ kQw buiD qwhw hy ]6] (1032-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaa ka-o alakh lakhaa-ay aapay akath kathaa buDh taahaa hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	He alone is wise, unto whom the unseen Lord reveals Himself; he speaks the Unspoken Speech. ||6||
ALLOW	para 45013	jnmy kau vwjih vwDwey ] (1032-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) janmay ka-o vaajeh vaaDhaa-ay. At birth, the congratulations pour in;
RECORD	para 45014	soihlVy AigAwnI gwey ] (1032-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) sohilrhay agi-aanee gaa-ay. the ignorant sing songs of joy.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	jo jnmY iqsu srpr mrxw ikrqu pieAw isir swhw hy ]7] (1032-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo janmai tis sarpar marnaa kirat pa-i-aa sir saahaa hay. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	Whoever is born, is sure to die, according to the destiny of past deeds inscribed upon his head by the Sovereign Lord King. ||7||
RECORD	para 45016	sMjogu ivjogu myrY pRiB kIey ] (1032-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) sanjog vijog mayrai parabh kee-ay. Union and separation were created by my God.
RECORD	para 45017	isRsit aupwie duKw suK dIey ] (1032-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarisat upaa-ay dukhaa sukh dee-ay. Creating the Universe, He gave it pain and pleasure.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	duK suK hI qy Bey inrwly gurmuiK sIlu snwhw hy ]8] (1032-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) dukh sukh hee tay bha-ay niraalay gurmukh seel sanaahaa hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	The Gurmukhs remain unaffected by pain and pleasure; they wear the armor of humility. ||8||
DEFINE	para 45019	nIky swcy ky vwpwrI ] (1032-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) neekay saachay kay vaapaaree. The noble people are traders in Truth.
RECORD	para 45020	scu saudw lY gur vIcwrI ] (1032-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach sa-udaa lai gur veechaaree. They purchase the true merchandise, contemplating the Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	scw vKru ijsu Dnu plY sbid scY Emwhw hy ]9] (1032-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) sachaa vakhar jis Dhan palai sabad sachai omaahaa hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	One who has the wealth of the true commodity in his lap, is blessed with the rapture of the True Shabad. ||9||
RECORD	para 45022	kwcI saudI qotw AwvY ] (1032-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaachee sa-udee totaa aavai. The false dealings lead only to loss.
DEFINE	para 45023	gurmuiK vxju kry pRB BwvY ] (1032-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh vanaj karay parabh bhaavai. The trades of the Gurmukh are pleasing to God.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	pUMjI swbqu rwis slwmiq cUkw jm kw Pwhw hy ]10] (1032-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) poonjee saabat raas salaamat chookaa jam kaa faahaa hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	His stock is safe, and his capital is safe and sound. The noose of Death is cut away from around his neck. ||10||
RECORD	para 45026	sBu ko bolY Awpx BwxY ] (1033-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabh ko bolai aapan bhaanai. Everyone speaks as they please.
RECORD	para 45027	mnmuKu dUjY boil n jwxY ] (1033-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh doojai bol na jaanai. The self-willed manmukh, in duality, does not know how to speak.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	AMDuly kI miq AMDlI bolI Awie gieAw duKu qwhw hy ]11] (1033-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) anDhulay kee mat anDhlee bolee aa-ay ga-i-aa dukh taahaa hay. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	The blind person has a blind and deaf intellect; coming and going in reincarnation, he suffers in pain. ||11||
DEFINE	para 45029	duK mih jnmY duK mih mrxw ] (1033-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) dukh meh janmai dukh meh marnaa. In pain he is born, and in pain he dies.
DEFINE	para 45030	dUKu n imtY ibnu gur kI srxw ] (1033-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) dookh na mitai bin gur kee sarnaa. His pain is not relieved, without seeking the Sanctuary of the Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	dUKI aupjY dUKI ibnsY ikAw lY AwieAw ikAw lY jwhw hy ]12] (1033-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) dookhee upjai dookhee binsai ki-aa lai aa-i-aa ki-aa lai jaahaa hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	In pain he is created, and in pain he perishes. What has he brought with himself? And what will he take away? ||12||
DEFINE	para 45032	scI krxI gur kI isrkwrw ] (1033-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) sachee karnee gur kee sirkaaraa. True are the actions of those who are under the Guru's influence.
DEFINE	para 45033	Awvxu jwxu nhI jm Dwrw ] (1033-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) aavan jaan nahee jam Dhaaraa. They do not come and go in reincarnation, and they are not subject to the laws of Death.
WHEN	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	fwl Coif qqu mUlu prwqw min swcw Emwhw hy ]13] (1033-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) daal chhod tat mool paraataa man saachaa omaahaa hay. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	Whoever abandons the branches, and clings to the true root, enjoys true ecstasy within his mind. ||13||
RECORD	para 45035	hir ky log nhI jmu mwrY ] (1033-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) har kay log nahee jam maarai. Death cannot strike down the people of the Lord.
RECORD	para 45036	nw duKu dyKih pMiQ krwrY ] (1033-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa dukh daykheh panth karaarai. They do not see pain on the most difficult path.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	rwm nwmu Gt AMqir pUjw Avru n dUjw kwhw hy ]14] (1033-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam ghat antar poojaa avar na doojaa kaahaa hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Deep within the nucleus of their hearts, they worship and adore the Lord's Name; there is nothing else at all for them. ||14||
DEFINE	para 45038	EVu n kQnY isPiq sjweI ] (1033-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) orh na kathnai sifat sajaa-ee. There is no end to the Lord's sermon and Praise.
RECORD	para 45039	ijau quDu Bwvih rhih rjweI ] (1033-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) ji-o tuDh bhaaveh raheh rajaa-ee. As it pleases You, I remain under Your Will.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	drgh pYDy jwin suhyly hukim scy pwiqswhw hy ]15] (1033-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) dargeh paiDhay jaan suhaylay hukam sachay paatisaahaa hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	I am embellished with robes of honor in the Court of the Lord, by the Order of the True King. ||15||
RECORD	para 45041	ikAw khIAY gux kQih Gnyry ] (1033-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) ki-aa kahee-ai gun katheh ghanayray. How can I chant Your uncounted glories?
RECORD	para 45042	AMqu n pwvih vfy vfyry ] (1033-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) ant na paavahi vaday vadayray. Even the greatest of the great do not know Your limits.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	nwnk swcu imlY piq rwKhu qU isir swhw pwiqswhw hy ]16]6]12] (1033-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak saach milai pat raakho too sir saahaa paatisaahaa hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	Please bless Nanak with the Truth, and preserve his honor; You are the supreme emperor above the heads of kings. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI ] (1033-8)
RECORD	para 45044	maaroo mehlaa 1 dakh-nee. Maaroo, First Mehl, Dakhanee:
