RECORD	para 45063	pMKI pMc aufir nhI Dwvih ] (1033-16, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) pankhee panch udar nahee Dhaaveh. The five birds do not fly wild.
DEFINE	para 45064	sPilE ibrKu AMimRq Plu pwvih ] (1033-16, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) safli-o birakh amrit fal paavahi. The tree of life is fruitful, bearing the fruit of Ambrosial Nectar.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v7	gurmuiK shij rvY gux gwvY hir rsu cog cugwiedw ]7] (1033-16, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) gurmukh sahj ravai gun gaavai har ras chog chugaa-idaa. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v7	The Gurmukh intuitively sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord; he eats the food of the Lord's sublime essence. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45066	iJlimil iJlkY cMdu n qwrw ] (1033-17, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) jhilmil jhilkai chand na taaraa. The dazzling light glitters, although neither the moon nor the stars are shining;
RECORD	para 45067	sUrj ikrix n ibjuil gYxwrw ] (1033-17, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) sooraj kiran na bijul ghainaaraa. neither the sun's rays nor the lightning flashes across the sky.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v8	AkQI kQau ichnu nhI koeI pUir rihAw min Bwiedw ]8] (1033-18, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) akthee katha-o chihan nahee ko-ee poor rahi-aa man bhaa-idaa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v8	I describe the indescribable state, which has no sign, where the all-pervading Lord is still pleasing to the mind. ||8||
RECORD	para 45069	psrI ikrix joiq auijAwlw ] (1033-18, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) pasree kiran jot uji-aalaa. The rays of Divine Light have spread out their brilliant radiance.
RECORD	para 45070	kir kir dyKY Awip dieAwlw ] (1033-19, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) kar kar daykhai aap da-i-aalaa. Having created the creation, the Merciful Lord Himself gazes upon it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v9	Anhd rux Juxkwru sdw Duin inrBau kY Gir vwiedw ]9] (1033-19, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) anhad run jhunkaar sadaa Dhun nirbha-o kai ghar vaa-idaa. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v9	The sweet, melodious, unstruck sound current vibrates continuously in the home of the fearless Lord. ||9||
WHEN	para 45073	Anhdu vwjY BRmu Bau BwjY ] (1034-1, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) anhad vaajai bharam bha-o bhaajai. When the unstruck sound current resounds, doubt and fear run away.
DEFINE	para 45074	sgl ibAwip rihAw pRBu CwjY ] (1034-1, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) sagal bi-aap rahi-aa parabh chhaajai. God is all-pervading, giving shade to all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v10	sB qyrI qU gurmuiK jwqw dir sohY gux gwiedw ]10] (1034-1, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) sabh tayree too gurmukh jaataa dar sohai gun gaa-idaa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v10	All belong to You; to the Gurmukhs, You are known. Singing Your Praises, they look beautiful in Your Court. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45076	Awid inrMjnu inrmlu soeI ] (1034-2, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) aad niranjan nirmal so-ee. He is the Primal Lord, immaculate and pure.
RECORD	para 45077	Avru n jwxw dUjw koeI ] (1034-2, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) avar na jaanaa doojaa ko-ee. I know of no other at all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v11	eykMkwru vsY min BwvY haumY grbu gvwiedw ]11] (1034-3, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) aykankaar vasai man bhaavai ha-umai garab gavaa-idaa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v11	The One Universal Creator Lord dwells within, and is pleasing to the mind of those who banishe egotism and pride. ||11||
RECORD	para 45079	AMimRqu pIAw siqguir dIAw ] (1034-3, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) amrit pee-aa satgur dee-aa. I drink in the Ambrosial Nectar, given by the True Guru.
RECORD	para 45080	Avru n jwxw dUAw qIAw ] (1034-3, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) avar na jaanaa doo-aa tee-aa. I do not know any other second or third.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v12	eyko eyku su Apr prMpru priK KjwnY pwiedw ]12] (1034-4, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) ayko ayk so apar parampar parakh khajaanai paa-idaa. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v12	He is the One, Unique, Infinite and Endless Lord; He evaluates all beings and places some in His treasury. ||12||
DEFINE	para 45082	igAwnu iDAwnu scu gihr gMBIrw ] (1034-4, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) gi-aan Dhi-aan sach gahir gambheeraa. Spiritual wisdom and meditation on the True Lord are deep and profound.
RECORD	para 45083	koie n jwxY qyrw cIrw ] (1034-5, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) ko-ay na jaanai tayraa cheeraa. No one knows Your expanse.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v13	jyqI hY qyqI quDu jwcY krim imlY so pwiedw ]13] (1034-5, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) jaytee hai taytee tuDh jaachai karam milai so paa-idaa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v13	All that are, beg from You; You are attained only by Your Grace. ||13||
RECORD	para 45085	krmu Drmu scu hwiQ qumwrY ] (1034-5, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) karam Dharam sach haath tumaarai. You hold karma and Dharma in Your hands, O True Lord.
DEFINE	para 45086	vyprvwh AKut BMfwrY ] (1034-6, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) vayparvaah akhut bhandaarai. O Independent Lord, Your treasures are inexhaustible.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v14	qU dieAwlu ikrpwlu sdw pRBu Awpy myil imlwiedw ]14] (1034-6, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) too da-i-aal kirpaal sadaa parabh aapay mayl milaa-idaa. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v14	You are forever kind and compassionate, God. You unite in Your Union. ||14||
RECORD	para 45088	Awpy dyiK idKwvY Awpy ] (1034-7, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) aapay daykh dikhaavai aapay. You Yourself see, and cause Yourself to be seen.
RECORD	para 45089	Awpy Qwip auQwpy Awpy ] (1034-7, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) aapay thaap uthaapay aapay. You Yourself establish, and You Yourself disestablish.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v15	Awpy joiV ivCoVy krqw Awpy mwir jIvwiedw ]15] (1034-7, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) aapay jorh vichhorhay kartaa aapay maar jeevaa-idaa. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v15	The Creator Himself unites and separates; He Himself kills and rejuvenates. ||15||
DEFINE	para 45091	jyqI hY qyqI quDu AMdir ] (1034-8, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) jaytee hai taytee tuDh andar. As much as there is, is contained within You.
RECORD	para 45092	dyKih Awip bYis ibj mMdir ] (1034-8, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) daykheh aap bais bij mandar. You gaze upon Your creation, sitting within Your royal palace.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v16	nwnku swcu khY bynµqI hir drsin suKu pwiedw ]16]1]13] (1034-8, mwrU dKxI, mÚ 1) naanak saach kahai baynantee har darsan sukh paa-idaa. ||16||
UPHOLD	mwrU mhlw 1 dKxI v16	Nanak offers this true prayer; gazing upon the Blessed Vision of the Lord's Darshan, I have found peace. ||16||
WHEN	para 45095	drsnu pwvw jy quDu Bwvw ] (1034-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) darsan paavaa jay tuDh bhaavaa. If I am pleasing to You, Lord, then I obtain the Blessed Vision of Your Darshan.
RECORD	para 45096	Bwie Bgiq swcy gux gwvw ] (1034-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhaa-ay bhagat saachay gun gaavaa. In loving devotional worship, O True Lord, I sing Your Glorious Praises.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	quDu Bwxy qU Bwvih krqy Awpy rsn rswiedw ]1] (1034-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) tuDh bhaanay too bhaaveh kartay aapay rasan rasaa-idaa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	By Your Will, O Creator Lord, You have become pleasing to me, and so sweet to my tongue. ||1||
RECORD	para 45098	sohin Bgq pRBU drbwry ] (1034-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) sohan bhagat parabhoo darbaaray. The devotees look beautiful in the Darbaar, the Court of God.
DEFINE	para 45099	mukqu Bey hir dws qumwry ] (1034-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) mukat bha-ay har daas tumaaray. Your slaves, Lord, are liberated.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Awpu gvwie qyrY rMig rwqy Anidnu nwmu iDAwiedw ]2] (1034-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap gavaa-ay tayrai rang raatay an-din naam Dhi-aa-idaa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Eradicating self-conceit, they are attuned to Your Love; night and day, they meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 45101	eIsru bRhmw dyvI dyvw ] (1034-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) eesar barahmaa dayvee dayvaa. Shiva, Brahma, gods and goddesses,
RECORD	para 45102	ieMdR qpy muin qyrI syvw ] (1034-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) indar tapay mun tayree sayvaa. Indra, ascetics and silent sages serve You.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	jqI sqI kyqy bnvwsI AMqu n koeI pwiedw ]3] (1034-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) jatee satee kaytay banvaasee ant na ko-ee paa-idaa. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Celibates, givers of charity and the many forest-dwellers have not found the Lord's limits. ||3||
WHEN	para 45104	ivxu jwxwey koie n jwxY ] (1034-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) vin jaanaa-ay ko-ay na jaanai. No one knows You, unless You let them know You.
DEFINE	para 45105	jo ikCu kry su Awpx BwxY ] (1034-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo kichh karay so aapan bhaanai. Whatever is done, is by Your Will.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	lK caurwsIh jIA aupwey BwxY swh lvwiedw ]4] (1034-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) lakh cha-oraaseeh jee-a upaa-ay bhaanai saah lavaa-idaa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	You created the 8.4 million species of beings; by Your Will, they draw their breath. ||4||
DEFINE	para 45107	jo iqsu BwvY so inhcau hovY ] (1034-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo tis bhaavai so nihcha-o hovai. Whatever is pleasing to Your Will, undoubtedly comes to pass.
RECORD	para 45108	mnmuKu Awpu gxwey rovY ] (1034-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh aap ganaa-ay rovai. The self-willed manmukh shows off, and comes to grief.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	nwvhu Bulw Taur n pwey Awie jwie duKu pwiedw ]5] (1034-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) naavhu bhulaa tha-ur na paa-ay aa-ay jaa-ay dukh paa-idaa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Forgetting the Name, he finds no place of rest; coming and going in reincarnation, he suffers in pain. ||5||
DEFINE	para 45110	inrml kwieAw aUjl hMsw ] (1034-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirmal kaa-i-aa oojal hansaa. Pure is the body, and immaculate is the swan-soul;
DEFINE	para 45111	iqsu ivic nwmu inrMjn AMsw ] (1034-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) tis vich naam niranjan ansaa. within it is the immaculate essence of the Naam.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	sgly dUK AMimRqu kir pIvY bwhuiV dUKu n pwiedw ]6] (1034-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) saglay dookh amrit kar peevai baahurh dookh na paa-idaa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Such a being drinks in all his pains like Ambrosial Nectar; he never suffers sorrow again. ||6||
RECORD	para 45113	bhu swdhu dUKu prwpiq hovY ] (1034-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) baho saadahu dookh paraapat hovai. For his excessive indulgences, he receives only pain;
RECORD	para 45114	Boghu rog su AMiq ivgovY ] (1034-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhogahu rog so ant vigovai. from his enjoyments, he contracts diseases, and in the end, he wastes away.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	hrKhu sogu n imteI kbhU ivxu Bwxy Brmwiedw ]7] (1034-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) harkhahu sog na mit-ee kabhoo vin bhaanay bharmaa-idaa. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	His pleasure can never erase his pain; without accepting the Lord's Will, he wanders lost and confused. ||7||
UPHOLD	para 45116	igAwn ivhUxI BvY sbweI ] (1034-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) gi-aan vihoonee bhavai sabaa-ee. Without spiritual wisdom, they all just wander around.
DEFINE	para 45117	swcw riv rihAw ilv lweI ] (1034-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachaa rav rahi-aa liv laa-ee. The True Lord is pervading and permeating everywhere, lovingly engaged.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	inrBau sbdu gurU scu jwqw joqI joiq imlwiedw ]8] (1034-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirbha-o sabad guroo sach jaataa jotee jot milaa-idaa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	The Fearless Lord is known through the Shabad, the Word of the True Guru; one's light merges into the Light. ||8||
DEFINE	para 45119	Atlu Afolu Aqolu murwry ] (1034-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) atal adol atol muraaray. He is the eternal, unchanging, immeasurable Lord.
RECORD	para 45120	iKn mih Fwih Pyir auswry ] (1034-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) khin meh dhaahi fayr usaaray. In an instant, He destroys, ang then reconstructs.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	rUpu n ryiKAw imiq nhI kImiq sbid Byid pqIAwiedw ]9] (1034-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) roop na raykh-i-aa mit nahee keemat sabad bhayd patee-aa-idaa. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	He has no form or shape, no limit or value. Pierced by the Shabad, one is satisfied. ||9||
RECORD	para 45123	hm dwsn ky dws ipAwry ] (1035-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) ham daasan kay daas pi-aaray. I am the slave of Your slaves, O my Beloved.
RECORD	para 45124	swiDk swc Bly vIcwry ] (1035-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) saaDhik saach bhalay veechaaray. The seekers of Truth and goodness contemplate You.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	mMny nwau soeI ijix jwsI Awpy swcu idRVwiedw ]10] (1035-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) mannay naa-o so-ee jin jaasee aapay saach darirhaa-idaa. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	Whoever believes in the Name, wins; He Himself implants Truth within. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45126	plY swcu scy sicAwrw ] (1035-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) palai saach sachay sachi-aaraa. The Truest of the True has the Truth is His lap.
DEFINE	para 45127	swcy BwvY sbdu ipAwrw ] (1035-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachay bhaavai sabad pi-aaraa. The True Lord is pleased with those who love the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	iqRBvix swcu klw Dir QwpI swcy hI pqIAwiedw ]11] (1035-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) taribhavan saach kalaa Dhar thaapee saachay hee patee-aa-idaa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Exerting His power, the Lord has established Truth throughout the three worlds; with Truth He is pleased. ||11||
RECORD	para 45129	vfw vfw AwKY sBu koeI ] (1035-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) vadaa vadaa aakhai sabh ko-ee. Everyone calls Him the greatest of the great.
RECORD	para 45130	gur ibnu soJI iknY n hoeI ] (1035-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur bin sojhee kinai na ho-ee. Without the Guru, no one understands Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	swic imlY so swcy Bwey nw vICuiV duKu pwiedw ]12] (1035-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) saach milai so saachay bhaa-ay naa veechhurh dukh paa-idaa. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	The True Lord is pleased with those who merge in Truth; they are not separated again, and they do not suffer. ||12||
RECORD	para 45132	Durhu ivCuMny DwhI ruMny ] (1035-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) Dharahu vichhunay Dhaahee runnay. Separated from the Primal Lord, they loudly weep and wail.
WHEN	para 45133	mir mir jnmih muhliq puMny ] (1035-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) mar mar janmeh muhlat punnay. They die and die, only to be reborn, when their time has passed.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	ijsu bKsy iqsu dy vifAweI myil n pCoqwiedw ]13] (1035-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis bakhsay tis day vadi-aa-ee mayl na pachhotaa-idaa. ||13|| He blesses those whom He forgives with glorious greatness; united with Him, they do not regret or repent. ||13 |
DEFINE	para 45135	Awpy krqw Awpy Bugqw ] (1035-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay kartaa aapay bhugtaa. | He Himself is the Creator, and He Himself is the Enjoyer.
DEFINE	para 45136	Awpy iqRpqw Awpy mukqw ] (1035-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay tariptaa aapay muktaa. He Himself is satisfied, and He Himself is liberated.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Awpy mukiq dwnu mukqIsru mmqw mohu cukwiedw ]14] (1035-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay mukat daan mukteesar mamtaa moh chukaa-idaa. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	The Lord of liberation Himself grants liberation; He eradicates possessiveness and attachment. ||14||
RECORD	para 45138	dwnw kY isir dwnu vIcwrw ] (1035-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) daanaa kai sir daan veechaaraa. I consider Your gifts to be the most wonderful gifts.
DEFINE	para 45139	krx kwrx smrQu Apwrw ] (1035-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) karan kaaran samrath apaaraa. You are the Cause of causes, Almighty Infinite Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	kir kir vyKY kIqw Apxw krxI kwr krwiedw ]15] (1035-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) kar kar vaykhai keetaa apnaa karnee kaar karaa-idaa. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	Creating the creation, You gaze upon what You have created; You cause all to do their deeds. ||15||
DEFINE	para 45141	sy gux gwvih swcy Bwvih ] (1035-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) say gun gaavahi saachay bhaaveh. They alone sing Your Glorious Praises, who are pleasing to You, O True Lord.
RECORD	para 45142	quJ qy aupjih quJ mwih smwvih ] (1035-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) tujh tay upjahi tujh maahi samaaveh. They issue forth from You, and merge again into You.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	nwnku swcu khY bynµqI imil swcy suKu pwiedw ]16]2]14] (1035-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak saach kahai baynantee mil saachay sukh paa-idaa. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	Nanak offers this true prayer; meeting with the True Lord, peace is obtained. ||16||
RECORD	para 45145	Arbd nrbd DuMDUkwrw ] (1035-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) arbad narbad DhunDhookaaraa. For endless eons, there was only utter darkness.
RECORD	para 45146	Drix n ggnw hukmu Apwrw ] (1035-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) Dharan na gagnaa hukam apaaraa. There was no earth or sky; there was only the infinite Command of His Hukam.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	nw idnu rYin n cMdu n sUrju suMn smwiD lgwiedw ]1] (1035-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa din rain na chand na sooraj sunn samaaDh lagaa-idaa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	There was no day or night, no moon or sun; God sat in primal, profound Samaadhi. ||1||
RECORD	para 45148	KwxI n bwxI paux n pwxI ] (1035-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) khaanee na banee pa-un na paanee. There were no sources of creation or powers of speech, no air or water.
RECORD	para 45149	Epiq Kpiq n Awvx jwxI ] (1035-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) opat khapat na aavan jaanee. There was no creation or destruction, no coming or going.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	KMf pqwl spq nhI swgr ndI n nIru vhwiedw ]2] (1035-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) khand pataal sapat nahee saagar nadee na neer vahaa-idaa. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	There were no continents, nether regions, seven seas, rivers or flowing water. ||2||
RECORD	para 45151	nw qid surgu mCu pieAwlw ] (1035-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tad surag machh pa-i-aalaa. There were no heavenly realms, earth or nether regions of the underworld.
RECORD	para 45152	dojku iBsqu nhI KY kwlw ] (1035-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) dojak bhisat nahee khai kaalaa. There was no heaven or hell, no death or time.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	nrku surgu nhI jMmxu mrxw nw ko Awie n jwiedw ]3] (1035-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) narak surag nahee jaman marnaa naa ko aa-ay na jaa-idaa. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	There was no hell or heaven, no birth or death, no coming or going in reincarnation. ||3||
RECORD	para 45154	bRhmw ibsnu mhysu n koeI ] (1035-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) barahmaa bisan mahays na ko-ee. There was no Brahma, Vishnu or Shiva.
RECORD	para 45155	Avru n dIsY eyko soeI ] (1035-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) avar na deesai ayko so-ee. No one was seen, except the One Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	nwir purKu nhI jwiq n jnmw nw ko duKu suKu pwiedw ]4] (1035-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) naar purakh nahee jaat na janmaa naa ko dukh sukh paa-idaa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	There was no female or male, no social class or caste of birth; no one experienced pain or pleasure. ||4||
RECORD	para 45157	nw qid jqI sqI bnvwsI ] (1035-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tad jatee satee banvaasee. There were no people of celibacy or charity; no one lived in the forests.
RECORD	para 45158	nw qid isD swiDk suKvwsI ] (1035-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tad siDh saaDhik sukhvaasee. There were no Siddhas or seekers, no one living in peace.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	jogI jMgm ByKu n koeI nw ko nwQu khwiedw ]5] (1035-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) jogee jangam bhaykh na ko-ee naa ko naath kahaa-idaa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	There were no Yogis, no wandering pilgrims, no religious robes; no one called himself the master. ||5||
RECORD	para 45160	jp qp sMjm nw bRq pUjw ] (1035-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) jap tap sanjam naa barat poojaa. There was no chanting or meditation, no self-discipline, fasting or worship.
RECORD	para 45161	nw ko AwiK vKwxY dUjw ] (1035-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa ko aakh vakhaanai doojaa. No one spoke or talked in duality.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Awpy Awip aupwie ivgsY Awpy kImiq pwiedw ]6] (1035-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay aap upaa-ay vigsai aapay keemat paa-idaa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	He created Himself, and rejoiced; He evaluates Himself. ||6||
RECORD	para 45163	nw suic sMjmu qulsI mwlw ] (1035-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa such sanjam tulsee maalaa. There was no purification, no self-restraint, no malas of basil seeds.
RECORD	para 45164	gopI kwnu n gaU guoAwlw ] (1035-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) gopee kaan na ga-oo go-aalaa. There were no Gopis, no Krishna, no cows or cowherds.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	qMqu mMqu pwKMfu n koeI nw ko vMsu vjwiedw ]7] (1035-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) tant mant pakhand na ko-ee naa ko vans vajaa-idaa. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	There were no tantras, no mantras and no hypocrisy; no one played the flute. ||7||
RECORD	para 45166	krm Drm nhI mwieAw mwKI ] (1035-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) karam Dharam nahee maa-i-aa maakhee. There was no karma, no Dharma, no buzzing fly of Maya.
RECORD	para 45167	jwiq jnmu nhI dIsY AwKI ] (1035-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaat janam nahee deesai aakhee. Social class and birth were not seen with any eyes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	mmqw jwlu kwlu nhI mwQY nw ko iksY iDAwiedw ]8] (1035-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) mamtaa jaal kaal nahee maathai naa ko kisai Dhi-aa-idaa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	There was no noose of attachment, no death inscribed upon the forehead; no one meditated on anything. ||8||
RECORD	para 45169	inMdu ibMdu nhI jIau n ijMdo ] (1035-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) nind bind nahee jee-o na jindo. There was no slander, no seed, no soul and no life.
RECORD	para 45170	nw qid gorKu nw mwiCMdo ] (1035-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tad gorakh naa maachhindo. There was no Gorakh and no Maachhindra.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	nw qid igAwnu iDAwnu kul Epiq nw ko gxq gxwiedw ]9] (1035-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tad gi-aan Dhi-aan kul opat naa ko ganat ganaa-idaa. ||9||
UPHOLD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	There was no spiritual wisdom or meditation, no ancestry or creation, no reckoning of accounts. ||9||
RECORD	para 45173	vrn ByK nhI bRhmx KqRI ] (1036-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) varan bhaykh nahee barahman khatree. There were no castes or social classes, no religious robes, no Brahmin or Kh'shaatriya.
RECORD	para 45174	dyau n dyhurw gaU gwieqRI ] (1036-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) day-o na dayhuraa ga-oo gaa-itaree. There were no demi-gods or temples, no cows or Gaayatri prayer.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	hom jg nhI qIriQ nwvxu nw ko pUjw lwiedw ]10] (1036-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) hom jag nahee tirath naavan naa ko poojaa laa-idaa. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	There were no burnt offerings, no ceremonial feasts, no cleansing rituals at sacred shrines of pilgrimage; no one worshipped in adoration. ||10||
RECORD	para 45176	nw ko mulw nw ko kwjI ] (1036-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa ko mulaa naa ko kaajee. There was no Mullah, there was no Qazi.
RECORD	para 45177	nw ko syKu mswieku hwjI ] (1036-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa ko saykh masaa-ik haajee. There was no Shaykh, or pilgrims to Mecca.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	reIAiq rwau n haumY dunIAw nw ko khxu khwiedw ]11] (1036-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) ra-ee-at raa-o na ha-umai dunee-aa naa ko kahan kahaa-idaa. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	There was no king or subjects, and no worldly egotism; no one spoke of himself. ||11||
RECORD	para 45179	Bwau n BgqI nw isv skqI ] (1036-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhaa-o na bhagtee naa siv saktee. There was no love or devotion, no Shiva or Shakti - no energy or matter.
RECORD	para 45180	swjnu mIqu ibMdu nhI rkqI ] (1036-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) saajan meet bind nahee raktee. There were no friends or companions, no semen or blood.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	Awpy swhu Awpy vxjwrw swcy eyho Bwiedw ]12] (1036-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay saahu aapay vanjaaraa saachay ayho bhaa-idaa. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	He Himself is the banker, and He Himself is the merchant. Such is the Pleasure of the Will of the True Lord. ||12||
RECORD	para 45182	byd kqyb n isMimRiq swsq ] (1036-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) bayd katayb na simrit saasat. There were no Vedas, Korans or Bibles, no Simritees or Shaastras.
