RECORD	para 45278	isRsit aupwie kIAw pwswrw ] (1038-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarisat upaa-ay kee-aa paasaaraa. Creating the Universe, He made the expanse.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	dyv dwnv gx gMDrb swjy siB iliKAw krm kmwiedw ]12] (1038-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) dayv daanav gan ganDharab saajay sabh likhi-aa karam kamaa-idaa. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	He fashioned the demi-gods and demons, the heavenly heralds and celestial musicians; everyone acts according to their past karma. ||12||
RECORD	para 45280	gurmuiK smJY rogu n hoeI ] (1038-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmukh samjhai rog na ho-ee. The Gurmukh understands, and does not suffer the disease.
DEFINE	para 45281	ieh gur kI pauVI jwxY jnu koeI ] (1038-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) ih gur kee pa-orhee jaanai jan ko-ee. How rare are those who understand this ladder of the Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	jugh jugMqir mukiq prwiex so mukiq BieAw piq pwiedw ]13] (1038-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) jugah jugantar mukat paraa-in so mukat bha-i-aa pat paa-idaa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	Throughout the ages, they are dedicated to liberation, and so they become liberated; thus they are honored. ||13||
RECORD	para 45283	pMc qqu suMnhu prgwsw ] (1038-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) panch tat sunnahu pargaasaa. From the Primal Void, the five elements became manifest.
RECORD	para 45284	dyh sMjogI krm AiBAwsw ] (1038-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) dayh sanjogee karam abhi-aasaa. They joined to form the body, which engages in actions.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	burw Blw duie msqik lIKy pwpu puMnu bIjwiedw ]14] (1038-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) buraa bhalaa du-ay mastak leekhay paap punn beejaa-idaa. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Both bad and good are written on the forehead, the seeds of vice and virtue. ||14||
DEFINE	para 45286	aUqm siqgur purK inrwly ] (1038-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) ootam satgur purakh niraalay. The True Guru, the Primal Being, is sublime and detached.
DEFINE	para 45287	sbid rqy hir ris mqvwly ] (1038-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad ratay har ras matvaalay. Attuned to the Word of the Shabad, He is intoxicated with the sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	iriD buiD isiD igAwnu gurU qy pweIAY pUrY Bwig imlwiedw ]15] (1038-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) riDh buDh siDh gi-aan guroo tay paa-ee-ai poorai bhaag milaa-idaa. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	Riches, intellect, miraculous spiritual powers and spiritual wisdom are obtained from the Guru; through perfect destiny, they are received. ||15||
DEFINE	para 45289	iesu mn mwieAw kau nyhu Gnyrw ] (1038-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) is man maa-i-aa ka-o nayhu ghanayraa. This mind is so in love with Maya.
DEFINE	para 45290	koeI bUJhu igAwnI krhu inbyrw ] (1038-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) ko-ee boojhhu gi-aanee karahu nibayraa. Only a few are spiritually wise enough to understand and know this.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	Awsw mnsw haumY shsw nru loBI kUVu kmwiedw ]16] (1038-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) aasaa mansaa ha-umai sahsaa nar lobhee koorh kamaa-idaa. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v16	In hope and desire, egotism and skepticism, the greedy man acts falsely. ||16||
DEFINE	para 45292	siqgur qy pwey vIcwrw ] (1038-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur tay paa-ay veechaaraa. From the True Guru, contemplative meditation is obtained.
RECORD	para 45293	suMn smwiD scy Gr bwrw ] (1038-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) sunn samaaDh sachay ghar baaraa. And then, one dwells with the True Lord in His celestial home, the Primal State of Absorption in Deepest Samaadhi.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	nwnk inrml nwdu sbd Duin scu rwmY nwim smwiedw ]17]5]17] (1038-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak nirmal naad sabad Dhun sach raamai naam samaa-idaa. ||17||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v17	O Nanak, the immaculate sound current of the Naad, and the Music of the Shabad resound; one merges into the True Name of the Lord. ||17||
RECORD	para 45296	jh dyKw qh dIn dieAwlw ] (1038-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) jah daykhaa tah deen da-i-aalaa. Wherever I look, I see the Lord, merciful to the meek.
DEFINE	para 45297	Awie n jweI pRBu ikrpwlw ] (1038-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) aa-ay na jaa-ee parabh kirpaalaa. God is compassionate; He does not come or go in reincarnation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	jIAw AMdir jugiq smweI rihE inrwlmu rwieAw ]1] (1038-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) jee-aa andar jugat samaa-ee rahi-o niraalam raa-i-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	He pervades all beings in His mysterious way; the Sovereign Lord remains detached. ||1||
DEFINE	para 45299	jgu iqs kI CwieAw ijsu bwpu n mwieAw ] (1038-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) jag tis kee chhaa-i-aa jis baap na maa-i-aa. The world is a reflection of Him; He has no father or mother.
RECORD	para 45300	nw iqsu BYx n Brwau kmwieAw ] (1038-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tis bhain na bharaa-o kamaa-i-aa. He has not acquired any sister or brother.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	nw iqsu Epiq Kpiq kul jwqI Ehu Ajrwvru min BwieAw ]2] (1038-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tis opat khapat kul jaatee oh ajraavar man bhaa-i-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	There is no creation or destruction for Him; He has no ancestry or social status. The Ageless Lord is pleasing to my mind. ||2||
DEFINE	para 45302	qU Akwl purKu nwhI isir kwlw ] (1038-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) too akaal purakh naahee sir kaalaa. You are the Deathless Primal Being. Death does not hover over Your head.
DEFINE	para 45303	qU purKu AlyK AgMm inrwlw ] (1038-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) too purakh alaykh agamm niraalaa. You are the unseen inaccessible and detached Primal Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	sq sMqoiK sbid Aiq sIqlu shj Bwie ilv lwieAw ]3] (1038-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) sat santokh sabad at seetal sahj bhaa-ay liv laa-i-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	You are true and content; the Word of Your Shabad is cool and soothing. Through it, we are lovingly, intuitively attuned to You. ||3||
DEFINE	para 45305	qRY vrqwie cauQY Gir vwsw ] (1038-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) tarai vartaa-ay cha-uthai ghar vaasaa. The three qualities are pervasive; the Lord dwells in His home, the fourth state.
RECORD	para 45306	kwl ibkwl kIey iek gRwsw ] (1038-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaal bikaal kee-ay ik garasaa. He has made death and birth into a bite of food.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	inrml joiq srb jgjIvnu guir Anhd sbid idKwieAw ]4] (1038-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirmal jot sarab jagjeevan gur anhad sabad dikhaa-i-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	The immaculate Light is the Life of the whole world. The Guru reveals the unstruck melody of the Shabad. ||4||
DEFINE	para 45308	aUqm jn sMq Bly hir ipAwry ] (1038-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) ootam jan sant bhalay har pi-aaray. Sublime and good are those humble Saints, the Beloveds of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 45309	hir rs mwqy pwir auqwry ] (1038-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) har ras maatay paar utaaray. They are intoxicated with the sublime essence of the Lord, and are carried across to the other side.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	nwnk ryx sMq jn sMgiq hir gur prswdI pwieAw ]5] (1038-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak rayn sant jan sangat har gur parsaadee paa-i-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Nanak is the dust of the Society of the Saints; by Guru's Grace, he finds the Lord. ||5||
DEFINE	para 45311	qU AMqrjwmI jIA siB qyry ] (1038-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) too antarjaamee jee-a sabh tayray. You are the Inner-knower, the Searcher of hearts. All beings belong to You.
DEFINE	para 45313	qU dwqw hm syvk qyry ] (1039-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) too daataa ham sayvak tayray. You are the Great Giver; I am Your slave.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	AMimRq nwmu ik®pw kir dIjY guir igAwn rqnu dIpwieAw ]6] (1039-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) amrit naam kirpaa kar deejai gur gi-aan ratan deepaa-i-aa. ||6||
UPHOLD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	Please be merciful and bless me with Your Ambrosial Naam, and the jewel, the lamp of the Guru's spiritual wisdom. ||6||
RECORD	para 45315	pMc qqu imil iehu qnu kIAw ] (1039-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) panch tat mil ih tan kee-aa. From the union of the five elements, this body was made.
DEFINE	para 45316	Awqm rwm pwey suKu QIAw ] (1039-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) aatam raam paa-ay sukh thee-aa. Finding the Lord, the Supreme Soul, peace is established.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	krm krqUiq AMimRq Plu lwgw hir nwm rqnu min pwieAw ]7] (1039-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) karam kartoot amrit fal laagaa har naam ratan man paa-i-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	The good karma of past actions brings fruitful rewards, and man is blessed with the jewel of the Lord's Name. ||7||
RECORD	para 45318	nw iqsu BUK ipAws mnu mwinAw ] (1039-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa tis bhookh pi-aas man maani-aa. His mind does not feel any hunger or thirst.
RECORD	para 45319	srb inrMjnu Git Git jwinAw ] (1039-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarab niranjan ghat ghat jaani-aa. He knows the Immaculate Lord to be everywhere, in each and every heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	AMimRq ris rwqw kyvl bYrwgI gurmiq Bwie suBwieAw ]8] (1039-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) amrit ras raataa kayval bairaagee gurmat bhaa-ay subhaa-i-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	Imbued with the Lord's Ambrosial essence, he becomes a pure, detached renunciate; he is lovingly absorbed in the Guru's Teachings. ||8||
RECORD	para 45321	AiDAwqm krm kry idnu rwqI ] (1039-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) aDhi-aatam karam karay din raatee. Whoever does the deeds of the soul, day and night,
RECORD	para 45322	inrml joiq inrMqir jwqI ] (1039-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirmal jot nirantar jaatee. sees the immaculate Divine Light deep within.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	sbdu rswlu rsn ris rsnw byxu rswlu vjwieAw ]9] (1039-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad rasaal rasan ras rasnaa bayn rasaal vajaa-i-aa. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	Enraptured with the delightful essence of the Shabad, the source of nectar, my tongue plays the sweet music of the flute. ||9||
RECORD	para 45324	byxu rswl vjwvY soeI ] (1039-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) bayn rasaal vajaavai so-ee. He alone plays the sweet music of this flute,
RECORD	para 45325	jw kI iqRBvx soJI hoeI ] (1039-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaa kee taribhavan sojhee ho-ee. who knows the three worlds.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	nwnk bUJhu ieh ibiD gurmiq hir rwm nwim ilv lwieAw ]10] (1039-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak boojhhu ih biDh gurmat har raam naam liv laa-i-aa. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	O Nanak, know this, through the Guru's Teachings, and lovingly focus yourself on the Lord's Name. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45327	AYsy jn ivrly sMswry ] (1039-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) aisay jan virlay sansaaray. Rare are those beings in this world,
RECORD	para 45328	gur sbdu vIcwrih rhih inrwry ] (1039-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur sabad vichaareh raheh niraaray. who contemplate the Word of the Guru's Shabad, and remain detached.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Awip qrih sMgiq kul qwrih iqn sPl jnmu jig AwieAw ]11] (1039-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap tareh sangat kul taareh tin safal janam jag aa-i-aa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	They save themselves, and save all their associates and ancestors; fruitful is their birth and coming into this world. ||11||
RECORD	para 45330	Gru dru mMdru jwxY soeI ] (1039-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) ghar dar mandar jaanai so-ee. He alone knows the home of his own heart, and the door to the temple,
RECORD	para 45331	ijsu pUry gur qy soJI hoeI ] (1039-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis pooray gur tay sojhee ho-ee. who obtains perfect understanding from the Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	kwieAw gV mhl mhlI pRBu swcw scu swcw qKqu rcwieAw ]12] (1039-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaa-i-aa garh mahal mahlee parabh saachaa sach saachaa takhat rachaa-i-aa. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	In the body-fortress is the palace; God is the True Master of this Palace. The True Lord established His True Throne there. ||12||
DEFINE	para 45333	cqur ds hwt dIvy duie swKI ] (1039-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) chatur das haat deevay du-ay saakhee. The fourteen realms and the two lamps are the witnesses.
RECORD	para 45334	syvk pMc nwhI ibKu cwKI ] (1039-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) sayvak panch naahee bikh chaakhee. The Lord's servants, the self-elect, do not taste the poison of corruption.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	AMqir vsqu AnUp inrmolk guir imilAY hir Dnu pwieAw ]13] (1039-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar vasat anoop nirmolak gur mili-ai har Dhan paa-i-aa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	Deep within, is the priceless, incomparable commodity; meeting with the Guru, the wealth of the Lord is obtained. ||13||
DEFINE	para 45336	qKiq bhY qKqY kI lwiek ] (1039-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) takhat bahai takh-tai kee laa-ik. He alone sits on the throne, who is worthy of the throne.
RECORD	para 45337	pMc smwey gurmiq pwiek ] (1039-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) panch samaa-ay gurmat paa-ik. Following the Guru's Teachings, he subdues the five demons, and becomes the Lord's foot soldier.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Awid jugwdI hY BI hosI shsw Brmu cukwieAw ]14] (1039-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aad jugaadee hai bhee hosee sahsaa bharam chukaa-i-aa. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	He has existed from the very beginning of time and throughout the ages; He exists here and now, and will always exist. Meditating on Him, skepticism and doubt are dispelled. ||14||
DEFINE	para 45339	qKiq slwmu hovY idnu rwqI ] (1039-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) takhat salaam hovai din raatee. The Lord of the Throne is greeted and worshipped day and night.
RECORD	para 45340	iehu swcu vfweI gurmiq ilv jwqI ] (1039-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) ih saach vadaa-ee gurmat liv jaatee. This true glorious greatness comes to those who love the Guru's Teachings.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	nwnk rwmu jphu qru qwrI hir AMiq sKweI pwieAw ]15]1]18] (1039-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak raam japahu tar taaree har ant sakhaa-ee paa-i-aa. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	O Nanak, meditate on the Lord, and swim across the river; they find the Lord, their best friend, in the end. ||15||
RECORD	para 45343	hir Dnu sMchu ry jn BweI ] (1039-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) har Dhan sanchahu ray jan bhaa-ee. Gather in the wealth of the Lord, O humble Siblings of Destiny.
RECORD	para 45344	siqgur syiv rhhu srxweI ] (1039-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur sayv rahhu sarnaa-ee. Serve the True Guru, and remain in His Sanctuary.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	qskru coru n lwgY qw kau Duin aupjY sbid jgwieAw ]1] (1039-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) taskar chor na laagai taa ka-o Dhun upjai sabad jagaa-i-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	This wealth cannot be stolen; the celestial melody of the Shabad wells up and keeps us awake and aware. ||1||
DEFINE	para 45346	qU eykMkwru inrwlmu rwjw ] (1039-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) too aykankaar niraalam raajaa. You are the One Universal Creator, the Immaculate King.
RECORD	para 45347	qU Awip svwrih jn ky kwjw ] (1039-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) too aap savaareh jan kay kaajaa. You Yourself arrange and resolve the affairs of Your humble servant.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Amru Afolu Apwru Amolku hir AsiQr Qwin suhwieAw ]2] (1039-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) amar adol apaar amolak har asthir thaan suhaa-i-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	You are immortal, immovable, infinite and priceless; O Lord, Your place is beautiful and eternal. ||2||
RECORD	para 45349	dyhI ngrI aUqm Qwnw ] (1039-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) dayhee nagree ootam thaanaa. In the body-village, the most sublime place,
RECORD	para 45350	pMc lok vsih prDwnw ] (1039-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) panch lok vaseh parDhaanaa. the supremely noble people dwell.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	aUpir eykMkwru inrwlmu suMn smwiD lgwieAw ]3] (1039-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) oopar aykankaar niraalam sunn samaaDh lagaa-i-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Above them is the Immaculate Lord, the One Universal Creator; they are lovingly absorbed in the profound, primal state of Samaadhi. ||3||
DEFINE	para 45352	dyhI ngrI nau drvwjy ] (1039-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) dayhee nagree na-o darvaajay. There are nine gates to the body-village;
RECORD	para 45353	isir isir krxYhwrY swjy ] (1039-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) sir sir karnaihaarai saajay. the Creator Lord fashioned them for each and every person.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	dsvY purKu AqIqu inrwlw Awpy AlKu lKwieAw ]4] (1039-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) dasvai purakh ateet niraalaa aapay alakh lakhaa-i-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	Within the Tenth Gate, dwells the Primal Lord, detached and unequalled. The unknowable reveals Himself. ||4||
DEFINE	para 45355	purKu AlyKu scy dIvwnw ] (1039-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) purakh alaykh sachay deevaanaa. The Primal Lord cannot be held to account; True is His Celestial Court.
DEFINE	para 45356	hukim clwey scu nIswnw ] (1039-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) hukam chalaa-ay sach neesaanaa. The Hukam of His Command is in effect; True is His Insignia.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	nwnk Koij lhhu Gru Apnw hir Awqm rwm nwmu pwieAw ]5] (1039-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak khoj lahhu ghar apnaa har aatam raam naam paa-i-aa. ||5||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	O Nanak, search and examine your own home, and you shall find the Supreme Soul, and the Name of the Lord. ||5||
DEFINE	para 45359	srb inrMjn purKu sujwnw ] (1040-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarab niranjan purakh sujaanaa. The Primal Lord is everywhere, immaculate and all-knowing.
DEFINE	para 45360	Adlu kry gur igAwn smwnw ] (1040-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) adal karay gur gi-aan samaanaa. He administers justice, and is absorbed in the spiritual wisdom of the Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	kwmu k®oDu lY grdin mwry haumY loBu cukwieAw ]6] (1040-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaam kroDh lai gardan maaray ha-umai lobh chukaa-i-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	He seizes sexual desire and anger by their necks, and kills them; He eradicates egotism and greed. ||6||
RECORD	para 45362	scY Qwin vsY inrMkwrw ] (1040-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) sachai thaan vasai nirankaaraa. In the True Place, the Formless Lord abides.
RECORD	para 45363	Awip pCwxY sbdu vIcwrw ] (1040-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap pachhaanai sabad veechaaraa. Whoever understands his own self, contemplates the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	scY mhil invwsu inrMqir Awvx jwxu cukwieAw ]7] (1040-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) sachai mahal nivaas nirantar aavan jaan chukaa-i-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	He comes to abide deep within the True Mansion of His Presence, and his comings and goings are ended. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45365	nw mnu clY n pauxu aufwvY ] (1040-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa man chalai na pa-un udaavai. His mind does not waver, and he is not buffeted by the winds of desire.
RECORD	para 45366	jogI sbdu Anwhdu vwvY ] (1040-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) jogee sabad anaahad vaavai. Such a Yogi vibrates the unstruck sound current of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	pMc sbd Juxkwru inrwlmu pRiB Awpy vwie suxwieAw ]8] (1040-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) panch sabad jhunkaar niraalam parabh aapay vaa-ay sunaa-i-aa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	God Himself plays the pure music of the Panch Shabad, the five primal sounds to hear. ||8||
RECORD	para 45368	Bau bYrwgw shij smwqw ] (1040-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) bha-o bairaagaa sahj samaataa. In the Fear of God, in detachment, one intuitively merges into the Lord.
DEFINE	para 45369	haumY iqAwgI Anhid rwqw ] (1040-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai ti-aagee anhad raataa. Renouncing egotism, he is imbued with the unstruck sound current.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	AMjnu swir inrMjnu jwxY srb inrMjnu rwieAw ]9] (1040-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) anjan saar niranjan jaanai sarab niranjan raa-i-aa. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	With the ointment of enlightenment, the Immaculate Lord is known; the Immaculate Lord King is pervading everywhere. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45371	duK BY BMjnu pRBu AibnwsI ] (1040-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) dukh bhai bhanjan parabh abhinaasee. God is eternal and imperishable; He is the Destroyer of pain and fear.
RECORD	para 45372	rog kty kwtI jm PwsI ] (1040-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) rog katay kaatee jam faasee. He cures the disease, and cuts away the noose of death.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	nwnk hir pRBu so Bau BMjnu guir imilAY hir pRBu pwieAw ]10] (1040-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak har parabh so bha-o bhanjan gur mili-ai har parabh paa-i-aa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	O Nanak, the Lord God is the Destroyer of fear; meeting the Guru, the Lord God is found. ||10||
RECORD	para 45374	kwlY kvlu inrMjnu jwxY ] (1040-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaalai kaval niranjan jaanai. One who knows the Immaculate Lord chews up death.
RECORD	para 45375	bUJY krmu su sbdu pCwxY ] (1040-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) boojhai karam so sabad pachhaanai. One who understands karma, realizes the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Awpy jwxY Awip pCwxY sBu iqs kw coju sbwieAw ]11] (1040-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay jaanai aap pachhaanai sabh tis kaa choj sabaa-i-aa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	He Himself knows, and He Himself realizes. This whole world is all His play. ||11||
DEFINE	para 45377	Awpy swhu Awpy vxjwrw ] (1040-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay saahu aapay vanjaaraa. He Himself is the Banker, and He Himself is the Merchant.
RECORD	para 45378	Awpy prKy prKxhwrw ] (1040-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay parkhay parkhanhaaraa. The Appraiser Himself appraises.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	Awpy kis ksvtI lwey Awpy kImiq pwieAw ]12] (1040-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay kas kasvatee laa-ay aapay keemat paa-i-aa. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	He Himself tests upon His Touchstone, and He Himself estimates the value. ||12||
RECORD	para 45380	Awip dieAwil dieAw pRiB DwrI ] (1040-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap da-i-aal da-i-aa parabh Dhaaree. God Himself, the Merciful Lord, grants His Grace.
RECORD	para 45381	Git Git riv rihAw bnvwrI ] (1040-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) ghat ghat rav rahi-aa banvaaree. The Gardener pervades and permeates each and every heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	purKu AqIqu vsY inhkyvlu gur purKY purKu imlwieAw ]13] (1040-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) purakh ateet vasai nihkayval gur purkhai purakh milaa-i-aa. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	The pure, primal, detached Lord abides within all. The Guru, the Lord Incarnate, leads us to meet the Lord God. ||13||
DEFINE	para 45383	pRBu dwnw bInw grbu gvwey ] (1040-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) parabh daanaa beenaa garab gavaa-ay. God is wise and all-knowing; He purges men of their pride.
RECORD	para 45384	dUjw mytY eyku idKwey ] (1040-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) doojaa maytai ayk dikhaa-ay. Eradicating duality, the One Lord reveals Himself.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Awsw mwih inrwlmu jonI Akul inrMjnu gwieAw ]14] (1040-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) aasaa maahi niraalam jonee akul niranjan gaa-i-aa. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	Such a being remains unattached amidst hope, singing the Praise of the Immaculate Lord, who has no ancestry. ||14||
RECORD	para 45386	haumY myit sbid suKu hoeI ] (1040-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai mayt sabad sukh ho-ee. Eradicating egotism, he obtains the peace of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 45387	Awpu vIcwry igAwnI soeI ] (1040-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap veechaaray gi-aanee so-ee. He alone is spiritually wise, who contemplates his own self.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	nwnk hir jsu hir gux lwhw sqsMgiq scu Plu pwieAw ]15]2]19] (1040-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak har jas har gun laahaa satsangat sach fal paa-i-aa. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	O Nanak, singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, the true profit is obtained; in the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation, the fruit of Truth is obtained. ||15||
RECORD	para 45390	scu khhu scY Gir rhxw ] (1040-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach kahhu sachai ghar rahnaa. Speak the Truth, and remain in the home of Truth.
RECORD	para 45391	jIvq mrhu Bvjlu jgu qrxw ] (1040-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) jeevat marahu bhavjal jag tarnaa. Remain dead while yet alive, and cross over the terrifying world-ocean.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	guru boihQu guru byVI qulhw mn hir jip pwir lµGwieAw ]1] (1040-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur bohith gur bayrhee tulhaa man har jap paar langhaa-i-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	The Guru is the boat, the ship, the raft; meditating on the Lord in your mind, you shall be carried across to the other side. ||1||
RECORD	para 45393	haumY mmqw loB ibnwsnu ] (1040-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai mamtaa lobh binaasan. Eliminating egotism, possessiveness and greed,
DEFINE	para 45394	nau dr mukqy dsvY Awsnu ] (1040-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) na-o dar muktay dasvai aasan. one is liberated from the nine gates, and obtains a place in the Tenth Gate.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	aUpir prY prY AprMpru ijin Awpy Awpu aupwieAw ]2] (1040-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) oopar parai parai aprampar jin aapay aap upaa-i-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Lofty and high, the farthest of the far and infinite, He created Himself. ||2||
RECORD	para 45396	gurmiq lyvhu hir ilv qrIAY ] (1040-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmat layvhu har liv taree-ai. Receiving the Guru's Teachings, and lovingly attuned to the Lord, one crosses over.
RECORD	para 45397	Aklu gwie jm qy ikAw frIAY ] (1040-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) akal gaa-ay jam tay ki-aa daree-ai. Singing the Praises of the absolute Lord, why should anyone be afraid of death?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	jq jq dyKau qq qq qum hI Avru n duqIAw gwieAw ]3] (1040-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) jat jat daykh-a-u tat tat tum hee avar na dutee-aa gaa-i-aa. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Wherever I look, I see only You; I do not sing of any other at all. ||3||
DEFINE	para 45399	scu hir nwmu scu hY srxw ] (1040-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach har naam sach hai sarnaa. True is the Lord's Name, and True is His Sanctuary.
DEFINE	para 45400	scu gur sbdu ijqY lig qrxw ] (1040-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach gur sabad jitai lag tarnaa. True is the Word of the Guru's Shabad, grasping it, one is carries across.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	AkQu kQY dyKY AprMpru Puin griB n jonI jwieAw ]4] (1040-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) akath kathai daykhai aprampar fun garabh na jonee jaa-i-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	Speaking the Unspoken, one sees the Infinite Lord, and then, he does not have to enter the womb of reincarnation again. ||4||
RECORD	para 45402	sc ibnu squ sMqoKu n pwvY ] (1040-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach bin sat santokh na paavai. Without the Truth, no one finds sincerity or contentment.
DEFINE	para 45403	ibnu gur mukiq n AwvY jwvY ] (1040-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur mukat na aavai jaavai. Without the Guru, no one is liberated; coming and going in reincarnation continue.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	mUl mMqRü hir nwmu rswiexu khu nwnk pUrw pwieAw ]5] (1040-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) mool mantar har naam rasaa-in kaho naanak pooraa paa-i-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	Chanting the Mool Mantra, and the Name of the Lord, the source of nectar, says Nanak, I have found the Perfect Lord. ||5||
RECORD	para 45406	sc ibnu Bvjlu jwie n qirAw ] (1041-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) sach bin bhavjal jaa-ay na tari-aa. Without the Truth, the terrifying world-ocean cannot be crossed.
DEFINE	para 45407	eyhu smuMdu AQwhu mhw ibKu BirAw ] (1041-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) ayhu samund athaahu mahaa bikh bhari-aa. This ocean is vast and unfathomable; it is overflowing with the worst poison.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	rhY AqIqu gurmiq ly aUpir hir inrBau kY Gir pwieAw ]6] (1041-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) rahai ateet gurmat lay oopar har nirbha-o kai ghar paa-i-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	One who receives the Guru's Teachings, and remains aloof and detached, obtains a place in the home of the Fearless Lord. ||6||
DEFINE	para 45409	JUTI jg ihq kI cqurweI ] (1041-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) jhoothee jag hit kee chaturaa-ee. False is the cleverness of loving attachment to the world.
RECORD	para 45410	iblm n lwgY AwvY jweI ] (1041-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) bilam na laagai aavai jaa-ee. In no time at all, it comes and goes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	nwmu ivswir clih AiBmwnI aupjY ibnis KpwieAw ]7] (1041-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) naam visaar chaleh abhimaanee upjai binas khapaa-i-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	Forgetting the Naam, the Name of the Lord, the proud egotistical people depart; in creation and destruction they are wasted away. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45412	aupjih ibnsih bMDn bMDy ] (1041-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) upjahi binsahi banDhan banDhay. In creation and destruction, they are bound in bondage.
DEFINE	para 45413	haumY mwieAw ky gil PMDy ] (1041-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-umai maa-i-aa kay gal fanDhay. The noose of egotism and Maya is around their necks.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	ijsu rwm nwmu nwhI miq gurmiq so jm puir bMiD clwieAw ]8] (1041-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis raam naam naahee mat gurmat so jam pur banDh chalaa-i-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	Whoever does not accept the Guru's Teachings, and does not dwell upon the Lord's Name, is bound and bagged, and dragged into the City of Death. ||8||
RECORD	para 45415	gur ibnu moK mukiq ikau pweIAY ] (1041-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur bin mokh mukat ki-o paa-ee-ai. Without the Guru, how can anyone be emancipated or liberated?
RECORD	para 45416	ibnu gur rwm nwmu ikau iDAweIAY ] (1041-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur raam naam ki-o Dhi-aa-ee-ai. Without the Guru, how can anyone meditate on the Lord's Name?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	gurmiq lyhu qrhu Bv duqru mukiq Bey suKu pwieAw ]9] (1041-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmat layho tarahu bhav dutar mukat bha-ay sukh paa-i-aa. ||9||
