RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	O Nanak, the Gurmukh obtains the support of liberation; by perfect destiny, he meets the Lord. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45468	inrBau siqguru hY rKvwlw ] (1042-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirbha-o satgur hai rakhvaalaa. The Fearless True Guru is our Savior and Protector.
DEFINE	para 45469	Bgiq prwpiq gur gopwlw ] (1042-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhagat paraapat gur gopaalaa. Devotional worship is obtained through the Guru, the Lord of the world.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Duin Anµd Anwhdu vwjY gur sbid inrMjnu pwieAw ]11] (1042-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) Dhun anand anaahad vaajai gur sabad niranjan paa-i-aa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	The blissful music of the unstruck sound current vibrates and resounds; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Immaculate Lord is obtained. ||11||
DEFINE	para 45471	inrBau so isir nwhI lyKw ] (1042-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirbha-o so sir naahee laykhaa. He alone is fearless, who has no destiny written on His head.
DEFINE	para 45472	Awip AlyKu kudriq hY dyKw ] (1042-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap alaykh kudrat hai daykhaa. God Himself is unseen; He reveals Himself through His wondrous creative power.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	Awip AqIqu AjonI sMBau nwnk gurmiq so pwieAw ]12] (1042-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap ateet ajonee sambha-o naanak gurmat so paa-i-aa. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	He Himself is unattached, unborn and self-existent. O Nanak, through the Guru's Teachings, He is found. ||12||
RECORD	para 45474	AMqr kI giq siqguru jwxY ] (1042-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar kee gat satgur jaanai. The True Guru knows the state of one's inner being.
DEFINE	para 45475	so inrBau gur sbid pCwxY ] (1042-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) so nirbha-o gur sabad pachhaanai. He alone is fearless, who realizes the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	AMqru dyiK inrMqir bUJY Anq n mnu folwieAw ]13] (1042-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar daykh nirantar boojhai anat na man dolaa-i-aa. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	He looks within his own inner being, and realizes the Lord within all; his mind does not waver at all. ||13||
DEFINE	para 45477	inrBau so AB AMqir visAw ] (1042-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) nirbha-o so abh antar vasi-aa. He alone is fearless, within whose being the Lord abides.
DEFINE	para 45478	Aihinis nwim inrMjn risAw ] (1042-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) ahinis naam niranjan rasi-aa. Day and night, he is delighted with the Immaculate Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	nwnk hir jsu sMgiq pweIAY hir shjy shij imlwieAw ]14] (1042-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak har jas sangat paa-ee-ai har sehjay sahj milaa-i-aa. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	O Nanak, in the Sangat, the Holy Congregation, the Lord's Praise is obtained, and one easily, intuitively meets the Lord. ||14||
RECORD	para 45480	AMqir bwhir so pRBu jwxY ] (1042-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar baahar so parabh jaanai. One who knows God, within the self and beyond,
RECORD	para 45481	rhY Ailpqu clqy Gir AwxY ] (1042-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) rahai alipat chaltay ghar aanai. remains detached, and brings his wandering mind back to its home.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	aUpir Awid srb iqhu loeI scu nwnk AMimRq rsu pwieAw ]15]4]21] (1042-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) oopar aad sarab tihu lo-ee sach naanak amrit ras paa-i-aa. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	The True Primal Lord is over all the three worlds; O Nanak, His Ambrosial Nectar is obtained. ||15||
DEFINE	para 45484	kudriq krnYhwr Apwrw ] (1042-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) kudrat karnaihaar apaaraa. The Creator Lord is infinite; His creative power is wondrous.
RECORD	para 45485	kIqy kw nwhI ikhu cwrw ] (1042-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) keetay kaa naahee kihu chaaraa. Created beings have no power over Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	jIA aupwie irjku dy Awpy isir isir hukmu clwieAw ]1] (1042-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) jee-a upaa-ay rijak day aapay sir sir hukam chalaa-i-aa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v1	He formed the living beings, and He Himself sustains them; the Hukam of His Command controls each and every one. ||1||
RECORD	para 45487	hukmu clwie rihAw BrpUry ] (1042-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) hukam chalaa-ay rahi-aa bharpooray. The all-pervading Lord orchestrates all through His Hukam.
DEFINE	para 45488	iksu nyVY iksu AwKW dUry ] (1042-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) kis nayrhai kis aakhaaN dooray. Who is near, and who is far away?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	gupq pRgt hir Git Git dyKhu vrqY qwku sbwieAw ]2] (1042-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) gupat pargat har ghat ghat daykhhu vartai taak sabaa-i-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v2	Behold the Lord, both hidden and manifest, in each and every heart; the unique Lord is permeating all. ||2||
RECORD	para 45490	ijs kau myly suriq smwey ] (1042-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis ka-o maylay surat samaa-ay. One whom the Lord unites with Himself, merges in conscious awareness.
RECORD	para 45491	gur sbdI hir nwmu iDAwey ] (1042-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur sabdee har naam Dhi-aa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, meditate on the Lord's Name.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	Awnd rUp AnUp Agocr gur imilAY Brmu jwieAw ]3] (1042-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) aanad roop anoop agochar gur mili-ai bharam jaa-i-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v3	God is the embodiment of bliss, incomparably beautiful and unfathomable; meeting with the Guru, doubt is dispelled. ||3||
DEFINE	para 45493	mn qn Dn qy nwmu ipAwrw ] (1042-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) man tan Dhan tay naam pi-aaraa. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is more dear to me than my mind, body and wealth.
REQUIRE	para 45494	AMiq sKweI clxvwrw ] (1042-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) ant sakhaa-ee chalanvaaraa. In the end, when I must depart, it shall be my only help and support.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	moh pswr nhI sMig bylI ibnu hir gur ikin suKu pwieAw ]4] (1043-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) moh pasaar nahee sang baylee bin har gur kin sukh paa-i-aa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v4	In this world of love and attachment, no one is anyone else's friend or companion; without the Lord, without the Guru, who has ever found peace? ||4||
RECORD	para 45497	ijs kau ndir kry guru pUrw ] (1043-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis ka-o nadar karay gur pooraa. He, unto whom the Perfect Guru grants His Grace,
RECORD	para 45498	sbid imlwey gurmiq sUrw ] (1043-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabad milaa-ay gurmat sooraa. is merged in the Word of the Shabad, through the Teachings of the brave, heroic Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	nwnk gur ky crn sryvhu ijin BUlw mwrig pwieAw ]5] (1043-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak gur kay charan sarayvhu jin bhoolaa maarag paa-i-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v5	O Nanak, dwell upon, and serve at the Guru's feet; He places those who wander back on the Path. ||5||
DEFINE	para 45500	sMq jnW hir Dnu jsu ipAwrw ] (1043-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) sant janaa N har Dhan jas pi-aaraa. The wealth of the Lord's Praise is very dear to the humble Saints.
RECORD	para 45501	gurmiq pwieAw nwmu qumwrw ] (1043-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmat paa-i-aa naam tumaaraa. Through the Guru's Teachings, I have obtained Your Name, Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	jwicku syv kry dir hir kY hir drgh jsu gwieAw ]6] (1043-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) jaachik sayv karay dar har kai har dargeh jas gaa-i-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v6	The beggar serves at the Lord's door, and in the Court of the Lord, sings His Praises. ||6||
DEFINE	para 45503	siqguru imlY q mhil bulwey ] (1043-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur milai ta mahal bulaa-ay. When one meets the True Guru, he is called into the Mansion of the Lord's Presence.
DEFINE	para 45504	swcI drgh giq piq pwey ] (1043-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachee dargeh gat pat paa-ay. In the True Court, he is blessed with salvation and honor.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	swkq Taur nwhI hir mMdr jnm mrY duKu pwieAw ]7] (1043-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) saakat tha-ur naahee har mandar janam marai dukh paa-i-aa. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v7	The faithless cynic has no place of rest in the Lord's palace; he suffers the pains of birth and death. ||7||
RECORD	para 45506	syvhu siqgur smuMdu AQwhw ] (1043-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) sayvhu satgur samund athaahaa. So serve the True Guru, the unfathomable ocean,
REQUIRE	para 45507	pwvhu nwmu rqnu Dnu lwhw ] (1043-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) paavhu naam ratan Dhan laahaa. and you shall obtain the profit, the wealth, the jewel of the Naam.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	ibiKAw mlu jwie AMimRq sir nwvhu gur sr sMqoKu pwieAw ]8] (1043-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) bikhi-aa mal jaa-ay amrit sar naavhu gur sar santokh paa-i-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v8	The filth of corruption is washed away, by bathing in the pool of Ambrosial Nectar. In the Guru's pool, contentment is obtained. ||8||
RECORD	para 45509	siqgur syvhu sMk n kIjY ] (1043-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur sayvhu sank na keejai. So serve the Guru without hesitation.
RECORD	para 45510	Awsw mwih inrwsu rhIjY ] (1043-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) aasaa maahi niraas raheejai. And in the midst of hope, remain unmoved by hope.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	sMsw dUK ibnwsnu syvhu iPir bwhuiV rogu n lwieAw ]9] (1043-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) sansaa dookh binaasan sayvhu fir baahurh rog na laa-i-aa. ||9||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 1 v9	Serve the Eradicator of cynicism and suffering, and you shall never again be afflicted by the disease. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45512	swcy BwvY iqsu vfIAwey ] (1043-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) saachay bhaavai tis vadee-aa-ay. One who is pleasing to the True Lord is blessed with glorious greatness.
RECORD	para 45513	kaunu su dUjw iqsu smJwey ] (1043-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) ka-un so doojaa tis samjhaa-ay. Who else can teach him anything?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	hir gur mUriq eykw vrqY nwnk hir gur BwieAw ]10] (1043-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) har gur moorat aykaa vartai naanak har gur bhaa-i-aa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v10	The Lord and the Guru are pervading in one form. O Nanak, the Lord loves the Guru. ||10||
RECORD	para 45515	vwcih pusqk vyd purwnW ] (1043-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) vaacheh pustak vayd puraanaa N. Some read scriptures, the Vedas and the Puraanas.
RECORD	para 45516	iek bih sunih sunwvih kwnW ] (1043-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik bahi suneh sunaaveh kaanaa N. Some sit and listen, and read to others.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Ajgr kptu khhu ikau Kul@Y ibnu siqgur qqu n pwieAw ]11] (1043-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) ajgar kapat kahhu ki-o khul Hai bin satgur tat na paa-i-aa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v11	Tell me, how can the heavy, rigid doors be opened? Without the True Guru, the essence of reality is not realized. ||11||
RECORD	para 45518	krih ibBUiq lgwvih BsmY ] (1043-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) karahi bibhoot lagaaveh bhasmai. Some collect dust, and smear their bodies with ashes;
DEFINE	para 45519	AMqir k®oDu cMfwlu su haumY ] (1043-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar kroDh chandaal so ha-umai. but deep within them are the outcasts of anger and egotism.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	pwKMf kIny jogu n pweIAY ibnu siqgur AlKu n pwieAw ]12] (1043-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) pakhand keenay jog na paa-ee-ai bin satgur alakh na paa-i-aa. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v12	Practicing hypocrisy, Yoga is not obtained; without the True Guru, the unseen Lord is not found. ||12||
RECORD	para 45521	qIrQ vrq nym krih auidAwnw ] (1043-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) tirath varat naym karahi udi-aanaa. Some make vows to visit sacred shrines of pilgrimage, keep fasts and live in the forest.
UPHOLD	para 45522	jqu squ sMjmu kQih igAwnw ] (1043-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) jat sat sanjam katheh gi-aanaa. Some practice chastity, charity and self-discipline, and speak of spiritual wisdom.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	rwm nwm ibnu ikau suKu pweIAY ibnu siqgur Brmu n jwieAw ]13] (1043-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) raam naam bin ki-o sukh paa-ee-ai bin satgur bharam na jaa-i-aa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v13	But without the Lord's Name, how can anyone find peace? Without the True Guru, doubt is not dispelled. ||13||
RECORD	para 45524	inaulI krm BuieAMgm BwTI ] (1043-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) ni-ulee karam bhu-i-angam bhaathee. Inner cleansing techniques, channeling the energy to raise the Kundalini to the Tenth Gate,
RECORD	para 45525	ryck kuMBk pUrk mn hwTI ] (1043-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) raychak kumbhak poorak man haathee. inhaling, exhaling and holding the breath by the force of the mind -
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	pwKMf Drmu pRIiq nhI hir sau gur sbd mhw rsu pwieAw ]14] (1043-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) pakhand Dharam pareet nahee har sa-o gur sabad mahaa ras paa-i-aa. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v14	by empty hypocritical practices, Dharmic love for the Lord is not produced. Only through the Word of the Guru's Shabad is the sublime, supreme essence obtained. ||14||
RECORD	para 45527	kudriq dyiK rhy mnu mwinAw ] (1043-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) kudrat daykh rahay man maani-aa. Seeing the Lord's creative power, my mind remains satisfied.
DEFINE	para 45528	gur sbdI sBu bRhmu pCwinAw ] (1043-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur sabdee sabh barahm pachhaani-aa. Through the Guru's Shabad, I have realized that all is God.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	nwnk Awqm rwmu sbwieAw gur siqgur AlKu lKwieAw ]15]5]22] (1043-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak aatam raam sabaa-i-aa gur satgur alakh lakhaa-i-aa. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 1 v15	O Nanak, the Lord, the Supreme Soul, is in all. The Guru, the True Guru, has inspired me to see the unseen Lord. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 (1043-17)
RECORD	para 45530	maaroo solhay mehlaa 3 Maaroo, Solhay, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 45531	<> siqgur pRswid ] (1043-17) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	para 45532	hukmI shjy isRsit aupweI ] (1043-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) hukmee sehjay sarisat upaa-ee. By the Hukam of His Command, He effortlessly created the Universe.
RECORD	para 45533	kir kir vyKY ApxI vifAweI ] (1043-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) kar kar vaykhai apnee vadi-aa-ee. Creating the creation, He gazes upon His own greatness.
ALLOW	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v1	Awpy kry krwey Awpy hukmy rihAw smweI hy ]1] (1043-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay karay karaa-ay aapay hukmay rahi-aa samaa-ee hay. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v1	He Himself acts, and inspires all to act; in His Will, He pervades and permeates all. ||1||
DEFINE	para 45535	mwieAw mohu jgqu gubwrw ] (1043-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh jagat gubaaraa. The world is in the darkness of love and attachment to Maya.
DEFINE	para 45536	gurmuiK bUJY ko vIcwrw ] (1043-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh boojhai ko veechaaraa. How rare is that Gurmukh who contemplates, and understands.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v2	Awpy ndir kry so pwey Awpy myil imlweI hy ]2] (1043-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay nadar karay so paa-ay aapay mayl milaa-ee hay. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v2	He alone attains the Lord, unto whom He grants His Grace. He Himself unites in His Union. ||2||
RECORD	para 45539	Awpy myly dy vifAweI ] (1044-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay maylay day vadi-aa-ee. Uniting with Himself, He bestows glorious greatness.
RECORD	para 45540	gur prswdI kImiq pweI ] (1044-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee keemat paa-ee. By Guru's Grace, one comes to know the Lord's worth.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v3	mnmuiK bhuqu iPrY ibllwdI dUjY Bwie KuAweI hy ]3] (1044-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh bahut firai billaadee doojai bhaa-ay khu-aa-ee hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v3	The self-willed manmukh wanders everywhere, weeping and wailing; he is utterly ruined by the love of duality. ||3||
RECORD	para 45542	haumY mwieAw ivcy pweI ] (1044-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai maa-i-aa vichay paa-ee. Egotism was instilled into the illusion of Maya.
DEFINE	para 45543	mnmuK BUly piq gvweI ] (1044-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh bhoolay pat gavaa-ee. The self-willed manmukh is deluded, and loses his honor.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v4	gurmuiK hovY so nwie rwcY swcY rihAw smweI hy ]4] (1044-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so naa-ay raachai saachai rahi-aa samaa-ee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v4	But one who becomes Gurmukh is absorbed in the Name; he remains immersed in the True Lord. ||4||
DEFINE	para 45545	gur qy igAwnu nwm rqnu pwieAw ] (1044-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur tay gi-aan naam ratan paa-i-aa. Spiritual wisdom is obtained from the Guru, along with the jewel of the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 45546	mnsw mwir mn mwih smwieAw ] (1044-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) mansaa maar man maahi samaa-i-aa. Desires are subdued, and one remains immersed in the mind.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v5	Awpy Kyl kry siB krqw Awpy dyie buJweI hy ]5] (1044-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay khayl karay sabh kartaa aapay day-ay bujhaa-ee hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v5	The Creator Himself stages all His plays; He Himself bestows understanding. ||5||
RECORD	para 45548	siqguru syvy Awpu gvwey ] (1044-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay aap gavaa-ay. One who serves the True Guru eradicates self-conceit.
RECORD	para 45549	imil pRIqm sbid suKu pwey ] (1044-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) mil pareetam sabad sukh paa-ay. Meeting with his Beloved, he finds peace through the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v6	AMqir ipAwru BgqI rwqw shij mqy bix AweI hy ]6] (1044-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar pi-aar bhagtee raataa sahj matay ban aa-ee hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v6	Deep within his inner being, he is imbued with loving devotion; intuitively, he becomes one with the Lord. ||6||
DEFINE	para 45551	dUK invwrxu gur qy jwqw ] (1044-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) dookh nivaaran gur tay jaataa. The Destroyer of pain is known through the Guru.
RECORD	para 45552	Awip imilAw jgjIvnu dwqw ] (1044-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) aap mili-aa jagjeevan daataa. The Great Giver, the Life of the world, Himself has met me.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v7	ijs no lwey soeI bUJY Bau Brmu srIrhu jweI hy ]7] (1044-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis no laa-ay so-ee boojhai bha-o bharam sareerahu jaa-ee hay. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v7	He alone understands, whom the Lord joins with Himself. Fear and doubt are taken away from his body. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45554	Awpy gurmuiK Awpy dyvY ] (1044-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay gurmukh aapay dayvai. He Himself is the Gurmukh, and He Himself bestows His blessings.
RECORD	para 45555	scY sbid siqguru syvY ] (1044-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sabad satgur sayvai. Through the True Word of the Shabad, serve the True Guru.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v8	jrw jmu iqsu joih n swkY swcy isau bix AweI hy ]8] (1044-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) jaraa jam tis johi na saakai saachay si-o ban aa-ee hay. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v8	Old age and death cannot even touch one who is in harmony with the True Lord. ||8||
DEFINE	para 45557	iqRsnw Agin jlY sMswrw ] (1044-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) tarisnaa agan jalai sansaaraa. The world is burning up in the fire of desire.
DEFINE	para 45558	jil jil KpY bhuqu ivkwrw ] (1044-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) jal jal khapai bahut vikaaraa. It burns and burns, and is destroyed in all its corruption.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v9	mnmuKu Taur n pwey kbhU siqgur bUJ buJweI hy ]9] (1044-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh tha-ur na paa-ay kabhoo satgur boojh bujhaa-ee hay. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v9	The self-willed manmukh finds no place of rest anywhere. The True Guru has imparted this understanding. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45560	siqguru syvin sy vfBwgI ] (1044-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayvan say vadbhaagee. Those who serve the True Guru are very fortunate.
RECORD	para 45561	swcY nwim sdw ilv lwgI ] (1044-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) saachai naam sadaa liv laagee. They remain lovingly focused on the True Name forever.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v10	AMqir nwmu rivAw inhkyvlu iqRsnw sbid buJweI hy ]10] (1044-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar naam ravi-aa nihkayval tarisnaa sabad bujhaa-ee hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v10	The Immaculate Naam, the Name of the Lord, permeates the nucleus of their inner being; through the Shabad, their desires are quenched. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45563	scw sbdu scI hY bwxI ] (1044-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa sabad sachee hai banee. True is the Word of the Shabad, and True is the Bani of His Word.
DEFINE	para 45564	gurmuiK ivrlY iknY pCwxI ] (1044-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlai kinai pachhaanee. How rare is that Gurmukh who realizes this.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v11	scy sbid rqy bYrwgI Awvxu jwxu rhweI hy ]11] (1044-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachay sabad ratay bairaagee aavan jaan rahaa-ee hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v11	Those who are imbued with the True Shabad are detached. Their comings and goings in reincarnation are ended. ||11||
DEFINE	para 45566	sbdu buJY so mYlu cukwey ] (1044-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabad bujhai so mail chukaa-ay. One who realizes the Shabad is cleansed of impurities.
RECORD	para 45567	inrml nwmu vsY min Awey ] (1044-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) nirmal naam vasai man aa-ay. The Immaculate Naam abides within his mind.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v12	siqguru Apxw sd hI syvih haumY ivchu jweI hy ]12] (1044-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur apnaa sad hee sayveh ha-umai vichahu jaa-ee hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v12	He serves his True Guru forever, and egotism is eradicated from within. ||12||
WHEN	para 45569	gur qy bUJY qw dru sUJY ] (1044-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur tay boojhai taa dar soojhai. If one comes to understand, through the Guru, then he comes to know the Lord's Door.
RECORD	para 45570	nwm ivhUxw kiQ kiQ lUJY ] (1044-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) naam vihoonaa kath kath loojhai. But without the Naam, one babbles and argues in vain.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v13	siqgur syvy kI vifAweI iqRsnw BUK gvweI hy ]13] (1044-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay kee vadi-aa-ee tarisnaa bhookh gavaa-ee hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v13	The glory of serving the True Guru is that it eradicates hunger and thirst. ||13||
WHEN	para 45572	Awpy Awip imlY qw bUJY ] (1044-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay aap milai taa boojhai. When the Lord unites them with Himself, then they come to understand.
UPHOLD	para 45573	igAwn ivhUxw ikCU n sUJY ] (1044-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) gi-aan vihoonaa kichhoo na soojhai. Without spiritual wisdom, they understand nothing at all.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v14	gur kI dwiq sdw mn AMqir bwxI sbid vjweI hy ]14] (1044-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kee daat sadaa man antar banee sabad vajaa-ee hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v14	One whose mind is filled with the Guru's gift forever - his inner being resounds with the Shabad, and the Word of the Guru's Bani. ||14||
RECORD	para 45575	jo Duir iliKAw su krm kmwieAw ] (1044-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo Dhur likhi-aa so karam kamaa-i-aa. He acts according to his pre-ordained destiny.
RECORD	para 45576	koie n mytY Duir PurmwieAw ] (1044-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) ko-ay na maytai Dhur furmaa-i-aa. No one can erase the Command of the Primal Lord.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v15	sqsMgiq mih iqn hI vwsw ijn kau Duir iliK pweI hy ]15] (1044-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) satsangat meh tin hee vaasaa jin ka-o Dhur likh paa-ee hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v15	They alone dwell in the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation, who have such pre- ordained destiny. ||15||
RECORD	para 45578	ApxI ndir kry so pwey ] (1044-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) apnee nadar karay so paa-ay. He alone finds the Lord, unto whom He grants His Grace.
RECORD	para 45579	scY sbid qwVI icqu lwey ] (1044-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sabad taarhee chit laa-ay. He links his consciousness to the deep meditative state of the True Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v16	nwnk dwsu khY bynµqI BIiKAw nwmu dir pweI hy ]16]1] (1044-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak daas kahai baynantee bheekhi-aa naam dar paa-ee hay. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 3 v16	1|| Nanak, Your slave, offers this humble prayer; I stand at Your Door, begging for Your Name. ||16||1||
DEFINE	para 45582	eyko eyku vrqY sBu soeI ] (1044-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayko ayk vartai sabh so-ee. The One and only Lord is pervading and permeating everywhere.
DEFINE	para 45583	gurmuiK ivrlw bUJY koeI ] (1044-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlaa boojhai ko-ee. How rare is that person, who as Gurmukh, understands this.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	eyko riv rihAw sB AMqir iqsu ibnu Avru n koeI hy ]1] (1044-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayko rav rahi-aa sabh antar tis bin avar na ko-ee hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	The One Lord is permeating and pervading, deep within the nucleus of all. Without Him, there is no other at all. ||1||
RECORD	para 45585	lK caurwsIh jIA aupwey ] (1044-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) lakh cha-oraaseeh jee-a upaa-ay. He created the 8.4 millions species of beings.
RECORD	para 45587	igAwnI iDAwnI AwiK suxwey ] (1045-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) gi-aanee Dhi-aanee aakh sunaa-ay. The spiritual teachers and meditators proclaim this.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	sBnw irjku smwhy Awpy kImiq hor n hoeI hy ]2] (1045-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabhnaa rijak samaahay aapay keemat hor na ho-ee hay. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	He Himself nourishes all; no one else can estimate His value. ||2||
DEFINE	para 45589	mwieAw mohu AMDu AMDwrw ] (1045-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh anDh anDhaaraa. Love and attachment to Maya are utter darkness.
RECORD	para 45590	haumY myrw psirAw pwswrw ] (1045-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai mayraa pasri-aa paasaaraa. Egotism and possessiveness have spread throughout the expanse of the universe.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	Anidnu jlq rhY idnu rwqI gur ibnu sWiq n hoeI hy ]3] (1045-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din jalat rahai din raatee gur bin saa Nt na ho-ee hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	Night and day, they burn, day and night; without the Guru, there is no peace or tranquility. ||3||
RECORD	para 45592	Awpy joiV ivCoVy Awpy ] (1045-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay jorh vichhorhay aapay. He Himself unites, and He Himself separates.
RECORD	para 45593	Awpy Qwip auQwpy Awpy ] (1045-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay thaap uthaapay aapay. He Himself establishes, and He Himself disestablishes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	scw hukmu scw pwswrw horin hukmu n hoeI hy ]4] (1045-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa hukam sachaa paasaaraa horan hukam na ho-ee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	True is the Hukam of His Command, and True is the expanse of His universe. No one else can issue any Command. ||4||
DEFINE	para 45595	Awpy lwie ley so lwgY ] (1045-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay laa-ay la-ay so laagai. He alone is attached to the Lord, whom the Lord attaches to Himself.
RECORD	para 45596	gur prswdI jm kw Bau BwgY ] (1045-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee jam kaa bha-o bhaagai. By Guru's Grace, the fear of death runs away.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	AMqir sbdu sdw suKdwqw gurmuiK bUJY koeI hy ]5] (1045-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar sabad sadaa sukh-daata gurmukh boojhai ko-ee hay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	The Shabad, the Giver of peace, dwells forever deep within the nucleus of the self. One who is Gurmukh understands. ||5||
RECORD	para 45598	Awpy myly myil imlwey ] (1045-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay maylay mayl milaa-ay. God Himself unites those united in His Union.
DEFINE	para 45599	purib iliKAw so mytxw n jwey ] (1045-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) purab likhi-aa so maytnaa na jaa-ay. Whatever is pre-ordained by destiny, cannot be erased.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	Anidnu Bgiq kry idnu rwqI gurmuiK syvw hoeI hy ]6] (1045-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din bhagat karay din raatee gurmukh sayvaa ho-ee hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	Night and day, His devotees worship Him, day and night; one who becomes Gurmukh serves Him. ||6||
DEFINE	para 45601	siqguru syiv sdw suKu jwqw ] (1045-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayv sadaa sukh jaataa. Serving the True Guru, lasting peace is experienced.
RECORD	para 45602	Awpy Awie imilAw sBnw kw dwqw ] (1045-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay aa-ay mili-aa sabhnaa kaa daataa. He Himself, the Giver of all, has come and met me.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	haumY mwir iqRsnw Agin invwrI sbdu cIin suKu hoeI hy ]7] (1045-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai maar tarisnaa agan nivaaree sabad cheen sukh ho-ee hay. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	Subduing egotism, the fire of thirst has been extinguished; contemplating the Word of the Shabad, peace is found. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45604	kwieAw kutMbu mohu n bUJY ] (1045-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kutamb moh na boojhai. One who is attached to his body and family, does not understand.
RECORD	para 45605	gurmuiK hovY q AwKI sUJY ] (1045-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai ta aakhee soojhai. But one who becomes Gurmukh, sees the Lord with his eyes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Anidnu nwmu rvY idnu rwqI imil pRIqm suKu hoeI hy ]8] (1045-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din naam ravai din raatee mil pareetam sukh ho-ee hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Night and day, he chants the Naam, day and night; meeting with his Beloved, he finds peace. ||8||
RECORD	para 45607	mnmuK Dwqu dUjY hY lwgw ] (1045-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh Dhaat doojai hai laagaa. The self-willed manmukh wanders distracted, attached to duality.
RECORD	para 45608	jnmq kI n mUE AwBwgw ] (1045-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) janmat kee na moo-o aabhaagaa. That unfortunate wretch - why didn't he just die as soon as he was born?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Awvq jwq ibrQw jnmu gvwieAw ibnu gur mukiq n hoeI hy ]9] (1045-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) aavat jaat birthaa janam gavaa-i-aa bin gur mukat na ho-ee hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Coming and going, he wastes away his life in vain. Without the Guru, liberation is not obtained. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45610	kwieAw kusuD haumY mlu lweI ] (1045-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kusuDh ha-umai mal laa-ee. That body which is stained with the filth of egotism is false and impure.
ALLOW	para 45611	jy sau Dovih qw mYlu n jweI ] (1045-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) jay sa-o Dhoveh taa mail na jaa-ee. It may be washed a hundred times, but its filth is still not removed.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	sbid DopY qw hCI hovY iPir mYlI mUil n hoeI hy ]10] (1045-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabad Dhopai taa hachhee hovai fir mailee mool na ho-ee hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	But if it is washed with the Word of the Shabad, then it is truly cleansed, and it shall never be soiled again. ||10||
RECORD	para 45613	pMc dUq kwieAw sMGwrih ] (1045-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) panch doot kaa-i-aa sanghaareh. The five demons destroy the body.
RECORD	para 45614	mir mir jMmih sbdu n vIcwrih ] (1045-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) mar mar jameh sabad na vichaareh. He dies and dies again, only to be reincarnated; he does not contemplate the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	AMqir mwieAw moh gubwrw ijau supnY suiD n hoeI hy ]11] (1045-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar maa-i-aa moh gubaaraa ji-o supnai suDh na ho-ee hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	The darkness of emotional attachment to Maya is within his inner being; as if in a dream, he does not understand. ||11||
RECORD	para 45616	ieik pMcw mwir sbid hY lwgy ] (1045-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik panchaa maar sabad hai laagay. Some conquer the five demons, by being attached to the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 45617	siqguru Awie imilAw vfBwgy ] (1045-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur aa-ay mili-aa vadbhaagay. They are blessed and very fortunate; the True Guru comes to meet them.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	AMqir swcu rvih rMig rwqy shij smwvY soeI hy ]12] (1045-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar saach raveh rang raatay sahj samaavai so-ee hay. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Within the nucleus of their inner being, they dwell upon the Truth; attuned to the Lord's Love, they intuitively merge in Him. ||12||
DEFINE	para 45619	gur kI cwl gurU qy jwpY ] (1045-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kee chaal guroo tay jaapai. The Guru's Way is known through the Guru.
RECORD	para 45620	pUrw syvku sbid is\wpY ] (1045-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) pooraa sayvak sabad sinjaapai. His perfect servant attains realization through the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	sdw sbdu rvY Gt AMqir rsnw rsu cwKY scu soeI hy ]13] (1045-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) sadaa sabad ravai ghat antar rasnaa ras chaakhai sach so-ee hay. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	Deep within his heart, he dwells forever upon the Shabad; he tastes the sublime essence of the True Lord with his tongue. ||13||
DEFINE	para 45622	haumY mwry sbid invwry ] (1045-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai maaray sabad nivaaray. Egotism is conquered and subdued by the Shabad.
RECORD	para 45623	hir kw nwmu rKY auir Dwry ] (1045-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kaa naam rakhai ur Dhaaray. I have enshrined the Name of the Lord within my heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	eyksu ibnu hau horu n jwxw shjy hoie su hoeI hy ]14] (1045-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) aykas bin ha-o hor na jaanaa sehjay ho-ay so ho-ee hay. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Other than the One Lord, I know nothing at all. Whatever will be, will automatically be. ||14||
