DEFINE	para 45626	gurmuiK bUJY sic smwieAw ] (1045-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh boojhai sach samaa-i-aa. The Gurmukh understands, and is immersed in the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	scw syiv sbid sc rwqy haumY sbdy KoeI hy ]15] (1045-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa sayv sabad sach raatay ha-umai sabday kho-ee hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	He serves the True Lord, and is attuned to the True Shabad. The Shabad banishes egotism. ||15||
DEFINE	para 45628	Awpy guxdwqw bIcwrI ] (1045-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay gundaataa beechaaree. He Himself is the Giver of virtue, the Contemplative Lord.
DEFINE	para 45629	gurmuiK dyvih pkI swrI ] (1045-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh dayveh pakee saaree. The Gurmukh is given the winning dice.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwim smwvih swcY swcy qy piq hoeI hy ]16]2] (1045-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam samaaveh saachai saachay tay pat ho-ee hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	2|| O Nanak, immersed in the Naam, the Name of the Lord, one becomes true; from the True Lord, honor is obtained. ||16||2||
DEFINE	para 45632	jgjIvnu swcw eyko dwqw ] (1045-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) jagjeevan saachaa ayko daataa. One One True Lord is the Life of the World, the Great Giver.
DEFINE	para 45633	gur syvw qy sbid pCwqw ] (1045-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur sayvaa tay sabad pachhaataa. Serving the Guru, through the Word of the Shabad, He is realized.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	eyko Amru eykw piqswhI jugu jugu isir kwr bxweI hy ]1] (1046-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayko amar aykaa patisaahee jug jug sir kaar banaa-ee hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	There is only One Command, and there is only One Supreme King. In each and every age, He links each to their tasks. ||1||
DEFINE	para 45636	so jnu inrmlu ijin Awpu pCwqw ] (1046-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) so jan nirmal jin aap pachhaataa. That humble being is immaculate, who knows his own self.
RECORD	para 45637	Awpy Awie imilAw suKdwqw ] (1046-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay aa-ay mili-aa sukh-daata. The Lord, the Giver of peace, Himself comes and meets him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	rsnw sbid rqI gux gwvY dir swcY piq pweI hy ]2] (1046-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) rasnaa sabad ratee gun gaavai dar saachai pat paa-ee hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	His tongue is imbued with the Shabad, and he sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord; he is honored in the Court of the True Lord. ||2||
DEFINE	para 45639	gurmuiK nwim imlY vifAweI ] (1046-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh naam milai vadi-aa-ee. The Gurmukh is blessed with the glorious greatness of the Naam.
RECORD	para 45640	mnmuiK inMdik piq gvweI ] (1046-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh nindak pat gavaa-ee. The self-willed manmukh, the slanderer, loses his honor.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	nwim rqy prm hMs bYrwgI inj Gir qwVI lweI hy ]3] (1046-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) naam ratay param hans bairaagee nij ghar taarhee laa-ee hay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	Attuned to the Naam, the supreme soul-swans remain detached; in the home of the self, they remain absorbed in deep meditative trance. ||3||
DEFINE	para 45642	sbid mrY soeI jnu pUrw ] (1046-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabad marai so-ee jan pooraa. That humble being who dies in the Shabad is perfect.
RECORD	para 45643	siqguru AwiK suxwey sUrw ] (1046-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur aakh sunaa-ay sooraa. The brave, heroic True Guru chants and proclaims this.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	kwieAw AMdir AMimRq sru swcw mnu pIvY Bwie suBweI hy ]4] (1046-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa andar amrit sar saachaa man peevai bhaa-ay subhaa-ee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	Deep within the body is the true pool of Ambrosial Nectar; the mind drinks it in with loving devotion. ||4||
RECORD	para 45645	piV pMifqu Avrw smJwey ] (1046-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) parh pandit avraa samjhaa-ay. The Pandit, the religious scholar, reads and instructs others,
DEFINE	para 45646	Gr jlqy kI Kbir n pwey ] (1046-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) ghar jaltay kee khabar na paa-ay. but he does not realize that his own home is on fire.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	ibnu siqgur syvy nwmu n pweIAY piV Qwky sWiq n AweI hy ]5] (1046-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay naam na paa-ee-ai parh thaakay saa Nt na aa-ee hay. ||5||
FORBID	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	Without serving the True Guru, the Naam is not obtained. You can read until you are exhausted, but you shall not find peace and tranquility. ||5||
RECORD	para 45648	ieik Bsm lgwie iPrih ByKDwrI ] (1046-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik bhasam lagaa-ay fireh bhaykh-Dhaaree. Some smear their bodies with ashes, and wander around in religious disguises.
RECORD	para 45649	ibnu sbdY haumY ikin mwrI ] (1046-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin sabdai ha-umai kin maaree. Without the Word of the Shabad, who has ever subdued egotism?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	Anidnu jlq rhih idnu rwqI Brim ByiK BrmweI hy ]6] (1046-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din jalat raheh din raatee bharam bhaykh bharmaa-ee hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	Night and day, they continue burning, day and night; they are deluded and confused by their doubt and religious costumes. ||6||
RECORD	para 45651	ieik igRh kutMb mih sdw audwsI ] (1046-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik garih kutamb meh sadaa udaasee. Some, in the midst of their household and family, remain always unattached.
RECORD	para 45652	sbid muey hir nwim invwsI ] (1046-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabad mu-ay har naam nivaasee. They die in the Shabad, and dwell in the Lord's Name.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	Anidnu sdw rhih rMig rwqy BY Bwie Bgiq icqu lweI hy ]7] (1046-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din sadaa raheh rang raatay bhai bhaa-ay bhagat chit laa-ee hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	Night and day, they remain forever attuned to His Love; they focus their consciousness on loving devotion and the Fear of God. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45654	mnmuKu inMdw kir kir ivguqw ] (1046-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh nindaa kar kar vigutaa. The self-willed manmukh indulges in slander, and is ruined.
RECORD	para 45655	AMqir loBu BaukY ijsu kuqw ] (1046-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar lobh bha-ukai jis kutaa. The dog of greed barks within him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	jmkwlu iqsu kdy n CofY AMiq gieAw pCuqweI hy ]8] (1046-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) jamkaal tis kaday na chhodai ant ga-i-aa pachhutaa-ee hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	The Messenger of Death never leaves him, and in the end, he leaves, regretting and repenting. ||8||
DEFINE	para 45657	scY sbid scI piq hoeI ] (1046-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sabad sachee pat ho-ee. Through the True Word of the Shabad, true honor is obtained.
RECORD	para 45658	ibnu nwvY mukiq n pwvY koeI ] (1046-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin naavai mukat na paavai ko-ee. Without the Name, no one attains liberation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	ibnu siqgur ko nwau n pwey pRiB AYsI bxq bxweI hy ]9] (1046-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin satgur ko naa-o na paa-ay parabh aisee banat banaa-ee hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Without the True Guru, no one finds the Name. Such is the making which God has made. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45660	ieik isD swiDk bhuqu vIcwrI ] (1046-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik siDh saaDhik bahut veechaaree. Some are Siddhas and seekers, and great contemplators.
RECORD	para 45661	ieik Aihinis nwim rqy inrMkwrI ] (1046-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik ahinis naam ratay nirankaaree. Some remain imbued with the Naam, the Name of the Formless Lord, day and night.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	ijs no Awip imlwey so bUJY Bgiq Bwie Bau jweI hy ]10] (1046-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis no aap milaa-ay so boojhai bhagat bhaa-ay bha-o jaa-ee hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	He alone understands, whom the Lord unites with Himself; through loving devotional worship, fear is dispelled. ||10||
RECORD	para 45663	iesnwnu dwnu krih nhI bUJih ] (1046-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) isnaan daan karahi nahee boojheh. Some take cleansing baths and give donations to charities, but they do not understand.
RECORD	para 45664	ieik mnUAw mwir mnY isau lUJih ] (1046-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik manoo-aa maar manai si-o loojheh. Some struggle with their minds, and conquer and subdue their minds.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	swcY sbid rqy iek rMgI swcY sbid imlweI hy ]11] (1046-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) saachai sabad ratay ik rangee saachai sabad milaa-ee hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	Some are imbued with love for the True Word of the Shabad; they merge with the True Shabad. ||11||
RECORD	para 45666	Awpy isrjy dy vifAweI ] (1046-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay sirjay day vadi-aa-ee. He Himself creates and bestows glorious greatness.
RECORD	para 45667	Awpy BwxY dyie imlweI ] (1046-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay bhaanai day-ay milaa-ee. By the Pleasure of His Will, He bestows union.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Awpy ndir kry min visAw myrY pRiB ieau PurmweI hy ]12] (1046-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay nadar karay man vasi-aa mayrai parabh i-o furmaa-ee hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Bestowing His Grace, He comes to dwell in the mind; such is the Command ordained by my God. ||12||
DEFINE	para 45669	siqguru syvih sy jn swcy ] (1046-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayveh say jan saachay. Those humble beings who serve the True Guru are true.
RECORD	para 45670	mnmuK syiv n jwxin kwcy ] (1046-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh sayv na jaanan kaachay. The false, self-willed manmukhs do not know how to serve the Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	Awpy krqw kir kir vyKY ijau BwvY iqau lweI hy ]13] (1046-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kartaa kar kar vaykhai ji-o bhaavai ti-o laa-ee hay. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	The Creator Himself creates the creation and watches over it; he attaches all according to the Pleasure of His Will. ||13||
DEFINE	para 45672	juig juig swcw eyko dwqw ] (1046-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) jug jug saachaa ayko daataa. In each and every age, the True Lord is the one and only Giver.
RECORD	para 45673	pUrY Bwig gur sbdu pCwqw ] (1046-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorai bhaag gur sabad pachhaataa. Through perfect destiny, one realizes the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	sbid imly sy ivCuVy nwhI ndrI shij imlweI hy ]14] (1046-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabad milay say vichhurhay naahee nadree sahj milaa-ee hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Those who are immersed in the Shabad are not separated again. By His Grace, they are intuitively immersed in the Lord. ||14||
DEFINE	para 45675	haumY mwieAw mYlu kmwieAw ] (1046-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai maa-i-aa mail kamaa-i-aa. Acting in egotism, they are stained with the filth of Maya.
RECORD	para 45676	mir mir jMmih dUjw BwieAw ] (1046-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) mar mar jameh doojaa bhaa-i-aa. They die and die again, only to be reborn in the love of duality.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	ibnu siqgur syvy mukiq n hoeI min dyKhu ilv lweI hy ]15] (1046-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin satgur sayvay mukat na ho-ee man daykhhu liv laa-ee hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	Without serving the True Guru, no one finds liberation. O mind, tune into this, and see. ||15||
RECORD	para 45678	jo iqsu BwvY soeI krsI ] (1047-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo tis bhaavai so-ee karsee. He does whatever He pleases.
RECORD	para 45680	Awphu hoAw nw ikCu hosI ] (1047-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) aaphu ho-aa naa kichh hosee. No one has done, or can do anything by himself.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwmu imlY vifAweI dir swcY piq pweI hy ]16]3] (1047-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam milai vadi-aa-ee dar saachai pat paa-ee hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	3|| O Nanak, through the Name, one is blessed with glorious greatness, and obtains honor in the Court of the True Lord. ||16||3||
REQUIRE	para 45683	jo AwieAw so sBu ko jwsI ] (1047-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo aa-i-aa so sabh ko jaasee. All who come shall have to depart.
DEFINE	para 45684	dUjY Bwie bwDw jm PwsI ] (1047-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay baaDhaa jam faasee. In the love of duality, they are caught by the noose of the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	siqguir rwKy sy jn aubry swcy swic smweI hy ]1] (1047-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur raakhay say jan ubray saachay saach samaa-ee hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Those humble beings who are protected by the True Guru, are saved. They merge into the Truest of the True. ||1||
RECORD	para 45686	Awpy krqw kir kir vyKY ] (1047-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kartaa kar kar vaykhai. The Creator Himself creates the creation, and watches over it.
DEFINE	para 45687	ijs no ndir kry soeI jnu lyKY ] (1047-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis no nadar karay so-ee jan laykhai. Thay alone are acceptable, upon whom He bestows His Glance of Grace.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	gurmuiK igAwnu iqsu sBu ikCu sUJY AigAwnI AMDu kmweI hy ]2] (1047-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh gi-aan tis sabh kichh soojhai agi-aanee anDh kamaa-ee hay. ||2||
UPHOLD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	The Gurmukh attains spiritual wisdom, and understands everything. The ignorant ones act blindly. ||2||
DEFINE	para 45689	mnmuK shsw bUJ n pweI ] (1047-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh sahsaa boojh na paa-ee. The self-willed manmukh is cynical; he doesn't understand.
RECORD	para 45690	mir mir jMmY jnmu gvweI ] (1047-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) mar mar jammai janam gavaa-ee. He dies and dies again, only to be reborn, and loses his life uselessly again.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	gurmuiK nwim rqy suKu pwieAw shjy swic smweI hy ]3] (1047-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh naam ratay sukh paa-i-aa sehjay saach samaa-ee hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	The Gurmukh is imbued with the Naam, the Name of the Lord; he find peace, and is intuitively immersed in the True Lord. ||3||
RECORD	para 45692	DMDY Dwvq mnu BieAw mnUrw ] (1047-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) DhanDhai Dhaavat man bha-i-aa manooraa. Chasing after worldly affairs, the mind has become corroded and rusty.
DEFINE	para 45693	iPir hovY kMcnu BytY guru pUrw ] (1047-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) fir hovai kanchan bhaytai gur pooraa. But meeting with the Perfect Guru, it is transmuted into gold once again.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	Awpy bKis ley suKu pwey pUrY sbid imlweI hy ]4] (1047-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay bakhas la-ay sukh paa-ay poorai sabad milaa-ee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	When the Lord Himself grants forgiveness, then peace is obtained; through the Perfect Word of the Shabad, one is united with Him. ||4||
DEFINE	para 45695	durmiq JUTI burI buirAwir ] (1047-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) durmat jhoothee buree buri-aar. The false and evil-minded are the most wicked of the wicked.
DEFINE	para 45696	AaugixAwrI AaugixAwir ] (1047-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) a-ugani-aaree a-ugani-aar. They are the most unworthy of the unworthy.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	kcI miq PIkw muiK bolY durmiq nwmu n pweI hy ]5] (1047-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) kachee mat feekaa mukh bolai durmat naam na paa-ee hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	With false intellect, and insipid words of mouth, evil-minded, they do not obtain the Naam. ||5||
DEFINE	para 45698	AaugixAwrI kMq n BwvY ] (1047-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) a-ugani-aaree kant na bhaavai. The unworthy soul-bride is not pleasing to her Husband Lord.
DEFINE	para 45699	mn kI jUTI jUTu kmwvY ] (1047-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) man kee joothee jooth kamaavai. False-minded, her actions are false.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	ipr kw swau n jwxY mUriK ibnu gur bUJ n pweI hy ]6] (1047-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) pir kaa saa-o na jaanai moorakh bin gur boojh na paa-ee hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	The foolish person does not know the excellence of her Husband Lord. Without the Guru, she does not understand at all. ||6||
RECORD	para 45701	durmiq KotI Kotu kmwvY ] (1047-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) durmat khotee khot kamaavai. The evil-minded, wicked soul-bride practices wickedness.
DEFINE	para 45702	sIgwru kry ipr Ksm n BwvY ] (1047-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) seegaar karay pir khasam na bhaavai. She decorates herself, but her Husband Lord is not pleased.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	guxvMqI sdw ipru rwvY siqguir myil imlweI hy ]7] (1047-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) gunvantee sadaa pir raavai satgur mayl milaa-ee hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	The virtuous soul-bride enjoys and ravishes her Husband Lord forever; the True Guru unites her in His Union. ||7||
RECORD	para 45704	Awpy hukmu kry sBu vyKY ] (1047-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay hukam karay sabh vaykhai. God Himself issues the Hukam of His Command, and beholds all.
DEFINE	para 45705	ieknw bKis ley Duir lyKY ] (1047-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) iknaa bakhas la-ay Dhur laykhai. Some are forgiven, according to their pre-ordained destiny.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Anidnu nwim rqy scu pwieAw Awpy myil imlweI hy ]8] (1047-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din naam ratay sach paa-i-aa aapay mayl milaa-ee hay. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Night and day, they are imbued with the Naam, and they find the True Lord. He Himself unites them in His Union. ||8||
RECORD	para 45707	haumY Dwqu moh ris lweI ] (1047-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai Dhaat moh ras laa-ee. Egotism attaches them to the juice of emotional attachment, and makes them run around.
DEFINE	para 45708	gurmuiK ilv swcI shij smweI ] (1047-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh liv saachee sahj samaa-ee. The Gurmukh is intuitively immersed in the True Love of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Awpy mylY Awpy kir vyKY ibnu siqgur bUJ n pweI hy ]9] (1047-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay maylai aapay kar vaykhai bin satgur boojh na paa-ee hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	He Himself unites, He Himself acts, and beholds. Without the True Guru, understanding is not obtained. ||9||
RECORD	para 45710	ieik sbdu vIcwir sdw jn jwgy ] (1047-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik sabad veechaar sadaa jan jaagay. Some contemplate the Word of the Shabad; these humble beings remain always awake and aware.
DEFINE	para 45711	ieik mwieAw moih soie rhy ABwgy ] (1047-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik maa-i-aa mohi so-ay rahay abhaagay. Some are attached to the love of Maya; these unfortunate ones remain asleep.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	Awpy kry krwey Awpy horu krxw ikCU n jweI hy ]10] (1047-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay karay karaa-ay aapay hor karnaa kichhoo na jaa-ee hay. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	He Himself acts, and inspires all to act; no one else can do anything. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45713	kwlu mwir gur sbid invwry ] (1047-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaal maar gur sabad nivaaray. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, death is conquered and killed.
RECORD	para 45714	hir kw nwmu rKY aur Dwry ] (1047-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kaa naam rakhai ur Dhaaray. Keep the Name of the Lord enshrined within your heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	siqgur syvw qy suKu pwieAw hir kY nwim smweI hy ]11] (1047-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayvaa tay sukh paa-i-aa har kai naam samaa-ee hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	Serving the True Guru, peace is obtained, and one merges in the Name of the Lord. ||11||
RECORD	para 45716	dUjY Bwie iPrY dyvwnI ] (1047-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay firai dayvaanee. In the love of duality, the world wanders around insane.
RECORD	para 45717	mwieAw moih duK mwih smwnI ] (1047-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi dukh maahi samaanee. Immersed in love and attachment to Maya, it suffers in pain.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	bhuqy ByK krY nh pwey ibnu siqgur suKu n pweI hy ]12] (1047-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) bahutay bhaykh karai nah paa-ay bin satgur sukh na paa-ee hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Wearing all sorts of religious robes, He is not obtained. Without the True Guru, peace is not found. ||12||
DEFINE	para 45719	iks no khIAY jw Awip krwey ] (1047-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) kis no kahee-ai jaa aap karaa-ay. Who is to blame, when He Himself does everything?
DEFINE	para 45720	ijqu BwvY iqqu rwih clwey ] (1047-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) jit bhaavai tit raahi chalaa-ay. As He wills, so is the path we take.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	Awpy imhrvwnu suKdwqw ijau BwvY iqvY clweI hy ]13] (1047-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay miharvaan sukh-daata ji-o bhaavai tivai chalaa-ee hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	He Himself is the Merciful Giver of peace; as He wills, so do we follow. ||13||
DEFINE	para 45722	Awpy krqw Awpy Bugqw ] (1047-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kartaa aapay bhugtaa. He Himself is the Creator, and He Himself is the Enjoyer.
DEFINE	para 45723	Awpy sMjmu Awpy jugqw ] (1047-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay sanjam aapay jugtaa. He Himself is detached, and He Himself is attached.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Awpy inrmlu imhrvwnu mDusUdnu ijs dw hukmu n myitAw jweI hy ]14] (1047-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay nirmal miharvaan maDhusoodan jis daa hukam na mayti-aa jaa-ee hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	He Himself is immaculate, compassionate, the lover of nectar; the Hukam of His Command cannot be erased. ||14||
DEFINE	para 45725	sy vfBwgI ijnI eyko jwqw ] (1047-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) say vadbhaagee jinee ayko jaataa. Those who know the One Lord are very fortunate.
RECORD	para 45727	Git Git vis rihAw jgjIvnu dwqw ] (1048-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) ghat ghat vas rahi-aa jagjeevan daataa. He dwells in each and every heart, the Great Giver, the Life of the world.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	iek QY gupqu prgtu hY Awpy gurmuiK BRmu Bau jweI hy ]15] (1048-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik thai gupat pargat hai aapay gurmukh bharam bha-o jaa-ee hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	At the same time, He is both hidden and revealed. For the Gurmukh, doubt and fear are dispelled. ||15||
RECORD	para 45729	gurmuiK hir jIau eyko jwqw ] (1048-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh har jee-o ayko jaataa. The Gurmukh knows the One, the Dear Lord.
DEFINE	para 45730	AMqir nwmu sbid pCwqw ] (1048-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar naam sabad pachhaataa. Deep within the nucleus of his inner being, is the Naam, the Name of the Lord; he realizes the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	ijsu qU dyih soeI jnu pwey nwnk nwim vfweI hy ]16]4] (1048-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis too deh so-ee jan paa-ay naanak naam vadaa-ee hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	4|| He alone receives it, unto whom You give it. O Nanak, the Naam is glorious greatness. ||16||4||
RECORD	para 45733	scu swlwhI gihr gMBIrY ] (1048-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) sach saalaahee gahir gambheerai. I praise the true, profound and unfathomable Lord.
DEFINE	para 45734	sBu jgu hY iqs hI kY cIrY ] (1048-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabh jag hai tis hee kai cheerai. All the world is in His power.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	siB Gt BogvY sdw idnu rwqI Awpy sUK invwsI hy ]1] (1048-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabh ghat bhogvai sadaa din raatee aapay sookh nivaasee hay. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	He enjoys all hearts forever, day and night; He Himself dwells in peace. ||1||
DEFINE	para 45736	scw swihbu scI nweI ] (1048-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa saahib sachee naa-ee. True is the Lord and Master, and True is His Name.
RECORD	para 45737	gur prswdI mMin vsweI ] (1048-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee man vasaa-ee. By Guru's Grace, I enshrine Him in my mind.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	Awpy Awie visAw Gt AMqir qUtI jm kI PwsI hy ]2] (1048-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay aa-ay vasi-aa ghat antar tootee jam kee faasee hay. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	He Himself has come to dwell deep within the nucleus of my heart; the noose of death has been snapped. ||2||
RECORD	para 45739	iksu syvI qY iksu swlwhI ] (1048-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) kis sayvee tai kis saalaahee. Whom should I serve, and whom should I praise?
RECORD	para 45740	siqguru syvI sbid swlwhI ] (1048-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayvee sabad saalaahee. I serve the True Guru, and praise the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	scY sbid sdw miq aUqm AMqir kmlu pRgwsI hy ]3] (1048-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sabad sadaa mat ootam antar kamal pargaasee hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	Through the True Shabad, the intellect is exalted and ennobled forever, and the lotus deep within blossoms forth. ||3||
DEFINE	para 45742	dyhI kwcI kwgd imkdwrw ] (1048-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) dayhee kaachee kaagad mikdaaraa. The body is frail and perishable, like paper.
WHEN	para 45743	bUMd pvY ibnsY Fhq n lwgY bwrw ] (1048-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) boond pavai binsai dhahat na laagai baaraa. When the drop of water falls upon it, it crumbles and dissolves instantaneously.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	kMcn kwieAw gurmuiK bUJY ijsu AMqir nwmu invwsI hy ]4] (1048-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) kanchan kaa-i-aa gurmukh boojhai jis antar naam nivaasee hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	But the body of the Gurmukh, who understands, is like gold; the Naam, the Name of the Lord, dwells deep within. ||4||
DEFINE	para 45745	scw caukw suriq kI kwrw ] (1048-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa cha-ukaa surat kee kaaraa. Pure is that kitchen, which is enclosed by spiritual awareness.
DEFINE	para 45746	hir nwmu Bojnu scu AwDwrw ] (1048-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) har naam bhojan sach aaDhaaraa. The Lord's Name is my food, and Truth is my support.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	sdw iqRpiq pivqRü hY pwvnu ijqu Git hir nwmu invwsI hy ]5] (1048-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) sadaa taripat pavitar hai paavan jit ghat har naam nivaasee hay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	Forever satisfied, sanctified and pure is that person, within whose heart the Lord's Name abides. ||5||
DEFINE	para 45748	hau iqn bilhwrI jo swcY lwgy ] (1048-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-o tin balihaaree jo saachai laagay. I am a sacrifice to those who are attached to the Truth.
RECORD	para 45749	hir gux gwvih Anidnu jwgy ] (1048-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) har gun gaavahi an-din jaagay. They sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and remain awake and aware night and day.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	swcw sUKu sdw iqn AMqir rsnw hir ris rwsI hy ]6] (1048-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) saachaa sookh sadaa tin antar rasnaa har ras raasee hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	True peace fills them forever, and their tongues savor the sublime essence of the Lord. ||6||
RECORD	para 45751	hir nwmu cyqw Avru n pUjw ] (1048-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) har naam chaytaa avar na poojaa. I remember the Lord's Name, and no other at all.
RECORD	para 45752	eyko syvI Avru n dUjw ] (1048-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayko sayvee avar na doojaa. I serve the One Lord, and no other at all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	pUrY guir sBu scu idKwieAw scY nwim invwsI hy ]7] (1048-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorai gur sabh sach dikhaa-i-aa sachai naam nivaasee hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	The Perfect Guru has revealed the whole Truth to me; I dwell in the True Name. ||7||
RECORD	para 45754	BRim BRim jonI iPir iPir AwieAw ] (1048-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) bharam bharam jonee fir fir aa-i-aa. Wandering, wandering in reincarnation, again and again, he comes into the world.
DEFINE	para 45755	Awip BUlw jw Ksim BulwieAw ] (1048-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) aap bhoolaa jaa khasam bhulaa-i-aa. He is deluded and confused, when the Lord and Master confuses him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	hir jIau imlY qw gurmuiK bUJY cInY sbdu AibnwsI hy ]8] (1048-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) har jee-o milai taa gurmukh boojhai cheenai sabad abhinaasee hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	He meets with the Dear Lord, when, as Gurmukh, he understands; he remembers the Shabad, the Word of the immortal, eternal Lord God. ||8||
RECORD	para 45757	kwim k®oiD Bry hm AprwDI ] (1048-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaam kroDh bharay ham apraaDhee. I am a sinner, overflowing with sexual desire and anger.
RECORD	para 45758	ikAw muhu lY bolh nw hm gux n syvw swDI ] (1048-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) ki-aa muhu lai bolah naa ham gun na sayvaa saaDhee. With what mouth should I speak? I have no virtue, and I have rendered no service.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	fubdy pwQr myil lYhu qum Awpy swcu nwmu AibnwsI hy ]9] (1048-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) dubday paathar mayl laihu tum aapay saach naam abhinaasee hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	I am a sinking stone; please, Lord, unite me with Yourself. Your Name is eternal and imperishable. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45760	nw koeI kry n krxY jogw ] (1048-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) naa ko-ee karay na karnai jogaa. No one does anything; no one is able to do anything.
RECORD	para 45761	Awpy krih krwvih su hoiegw ] (1048-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay karahi karaaveh so ho-igaa. That alone happens, which the Lord Himself does, and causes to be done.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	Awpy bKis lYih suKu pwey sd hI nwim invwsI hy ]10] (1048-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay bakhas laihi sukh paa-ay sad hee naam nivaasee hay. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	Those whom He Himself forgives, find peace; they dwell forever in the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45763	iehu qnu DrqI sbdu bIij Apwrw ] (1048-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) ih tan Dhartee sabad beej apaaraa. This body is the earth, and the infinite Shabad is the seed.
RECORD	para 45764	hir swcy syqI vxju vwpwrw ] (1048-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) har saachay saytee vanaj vaapaaraa. Deal and trade with the True Name alone.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	scu Dnu jMimAw qoit n AwvY AMqir nwmu invwsI hy ]11] (1048-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) sach Dhan jammi-aa tot na aavai antar naam nivaasee hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	The True wealth increases; it is never exhausted, when the Naam dwells deep within. ||11||
RECORD	para 45766	hir jIau AvgixAwry no guxu kIjY ] (1048-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) har jee-o avgani-aaray no gun keejai. O Dear Lord, please bless me, the worthless sinner, with virtue.
RECORD	para 45767	Awpy bKis lYih nwmu dIjY ] (1048-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay bakhas laihi naam deejai. Forgive me, and bless me with Your Name.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	gurmuiK hovY so piq pwey iekqu nwim invwsI hy ]12] (1048-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so pat paa-ay ikat naam nivaasee hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	One who becomes Gurmukh, is honored; he dwells in the Name of the One Lord alone. ||12||
DEFINE	para 45769	AMqir hir Dnu smJ n hoeI ] (1048-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar har Dhan samajh na ho-ee. The wealth of the Lord is deep within one's inner being, but he does not realize it.
RECORD	para 45770	gur prswdI bUJY koeI ] (1048-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee boojhai ko-ee. By Guru's Grace, one comes to understand.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	gurmuiK hovY so Dnu pwey sd hI nwim invwsI hy ]13] (1048-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so Dhan paa-ay sad hee naam nivaasee hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	One who becomes Gurmukh is blessed with this wealth; he lives forever in the Naam. ||13||
RECORD	para 45772	Anl vwau Brim BulweI ] (1048-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) anal vaa-o bharam bhulaa-ee. Fire and wind lead him into delusions of doubt.
RECORD	para 45774	mwieAw moih suiD n kweI ] (1049-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi suDh na kaa-ee. In love and attachment to Maya, he has no understanding at all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	mnmuK AMDy ikCU n sUJY gurmiq nwmu pRgwsI hy ]14] (1049-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh anDhay kichhoo na soojhai gurmat naam pargaasee hay. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	The blind, self-willed manmukh sees nothing; through the Guru's Teachings, the Naam is gloriously revealed. ||14||
DEFINE	para 45776	mnmuK haumY mwieAw sUqy ] (1049-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh ha-umai maa-i-aa sootay. The manmukhs are asleep in egotism and Maya.
DEFINE	para 45777	Apxw Gru n smwlih AMiq ivgUqy ] (1049-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) apnaa ghar na samaaleh ant vigootay. They do not watch over their own homes, and are ruined in the end.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	pr inMdw krih bhu icMqw jwlY duKy duiK invwsI hy ]15] (1049-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) par nindaa karahi baho chintaa jaalai dukhay dukh nivaasee hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	They slander others, and burn in great anxiety; they dwell in pain and suffering. ||15||
RECORD	para 45779	Awpy krqY kwr krweI ] (1049-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kartai kaar karaa-ee. The Creator Himself has created the creation.
RECORD	para 45780	Awpy gurmuiK dyie buJweI ] (1049-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay gurmukh day-ay bujhaa-ee. He blesses the Gurmukh with understanding.
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwim rqy mnu inrmlu nwmy nwim invwsI hy ]16]5] (1049-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay man nirmal naamay naam nivaasee hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	5|| O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam - their minds become immaculate; they dwell in the Naam, and only the Naam. ||16||5||
DEFINE	para 45783	eyko syvI sdw iQru swcw ] (1049-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayko sayvee sadaa thir saachaa. I serve the One Lord, who is eternal, stable and True.
DEFINE	para 45784	dUjY lwgw sBu jgu kwcw ] (1049-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai laagaa sabh jag kaachaa. Attached to duality, the whole world is false.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	gurmqI sdw scu swlwhI swcy hI swic pqIjY hy ]1] (1049-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmatee sadaa sach saalaahee saachay hee saach pateejai hay. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Following the Guru's Teachings, I praise the True Lord forever, pleased with the Truest of the True. ||1||
DEFINE	para 45786	qyry gux bhuqy mY eyku n jwqw ] (1049-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) tayray gun bahutay mai ayk na jaataa. Your Glorious Virtues are so many, Lord; I do not know even one.
RECORD	para 45787	Awpy lwie ley jgjIvnu dwqw ] (1049-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay laa-ay la-ay jagjeevan daataa. The Life of the world, the Great Giver, attaches us to himself.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	Awpy bKsy dy vifAweI gurmiq iehu mnu BIjY hy ]2] (1049-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay bakhsay day vadi-aa-ee gurmat ih man bheejai hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	He Himself forgives, and bestows glorious greatness. Following the Guru's Teachings, this mind is delighted. ||2||
RECORD	para 45789	mwieAw lhir sbid invwrI ] (1049-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa lahar sabad nivaaree. The Word of the Shabad has subdued the waves of Maya.
RECORD	para 45790	iehu mnu inrmlu haumY mwrI ] (1049-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) ih man nirmal ha-umai maaree. Egotism has been conquered, and this mind has become immaculate.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	shjy gux gwvY rMig rwqw rsnw rwmu rvIjY hy ]3] (1049-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) sehjay gun gaavai rang raataa rasnaa raam raveejai hay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	I intuitively sing His Glorious Praises, imbued with the Lord's Love. My tongue chants and savors the Lord's Name. ||3||
RECORD	para 45792	myrI myrI krq ivhwxI ] (1049-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) mayree mayree karat vihaanee. Crying out, "Mine, mine!" he spends his life.
RECORD	para 45793	mnmuiK n bUJY iPrY ieAwxI ] (1049-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh na boojhai firai i-aanee. The self-willed manmukh does not understand; he wanders around in ignorance.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	jmkwlu GVI muhqu inhwly Anidnu Awrjw CIjY hy ]4] (1049-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) jamkaal gharhee muhat nihaalay an-din aarjaa chheejai hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	The Messenger of Death watches over him every moment, every instant; night and day, his life is wasting away. ||4||
RECORD	para 45795	AMqir loBu krY nhI bUJY ] (1049-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar lobh karai nahee boojhai. He practices greed within, and does not understand.
RECORD	para 45796	isr aUpir jmkwlu n sUJY ] (1049-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) sir oopar jamkaal na soojhai. He does not see the Messenger of Death hovering over his head.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	AYQY kmwxw su AgY AwieAw AMqkwil ikAw kIjY hy ]5] (1049-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) aithai kamaanaa so agai aa-i-aa antkaal ki-aa keejai hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	Whatever one does in this world, will come to face him in the hereafter; what can he do at that very last moment? ||5||
DEFINE	para 45798	jo sic lwgy iqn swcI soie ] (1049-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo sach laagay tin saachee so-ay. Those who are attached to the Truth are true.
RECORD	para 45799	dUjY lwgy mnmuiK roie ] (1049-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai laagay manmukh ro-ay. The self-willed manmukhs, attached to duality, weep and wail.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	duhw isirAw kw Ksmu hY Awpy Awpy gux mih BIjY hy ]6] (1049-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) duhaa siri-aa kaa khasam hai aapay aapay gun meh bheejai hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	He is the Lord and Master of both worlds; He Himself delights in virtue. ||6||
DEFINE	para 45801	gur kY sbid sdw jnu sohY ] (1049-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad sadaa jan sohai. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, His humble servant is exalted forever.
DEFINE	para 45802	nwm rswieix iehu mnu mohY ] (1049-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) naam rasaa-in ih man mohai. This mind is enticed by the Naam, the source of nectar.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	mwieAw moh mYlu pqMgu n lwgY gurmqI hir nwim BIjY hy ]7] (1049-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh mail patang na laagai gurmatee har naam bheejai hay. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	It is not stained at all by the dirt of attachment to Maya; through the Guru's Teachings, it is pleased and saturated with the Lord's Name. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45804	sBnw ivic vrqY ieku soeI ] (1049-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabhnaa vich vartai ik so-ee. The One Lord is contained within all.
DEFINE	para 45805	gur prswdI prgtu hoeI ] (1049-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee pargat ho-ee. By Guru's Grace, He is revealed.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	haumY mwir sdw suKu pwieAw nwie swcY AMimRqu pIjY hy ]8] (1049-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai maar sadaa sukh paa-i-aa naa-ay saachai amrit peejai hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	One who subdues his ego, finds lasting peace; he drinks in the Ambrosial Nectar of the True Name. ||8||
DEFINE	para 45807	iklibK dUK invwrxhwrw ] (1049-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) kilbikh dookh nivaaranhaaraa. God is the Destroyer of sin and pain.
RECORD	para 45808	gurmuiK syivAw sbid vIcwrw ] (1049-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sayvi-aa sabad veechaaraa. The Gurmukh serves Him, and contemplates the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	sBu ikCu Awpy Awip vrqY gurmuiK qnu mnu BIjY hy ]9] (1049-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabh kichh aapay aap vartai gurmukh tan man bheejai hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	He Himself is pervading everything. The Gurmukh's body and mind are saturated and pleased. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45810	mwieAw Agin jlY sMswry ] (1049-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa agan jalai sansaaray. The world is burning in the fire of Maya.
RECORD	para 45811	gurmuiK invwrY sbid vIcwry ] (1049-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh nivaarai sabad veechaaray. The Gurmukh extinguishes this fire, by contemplating the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	AMqir sWiq sdw suKu pwieAw gurmqI nwmu lIjY hy ]10] (1049-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar saaNt sadaa sukh paa-i-aa gurmatee naam leejai hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	Deep within are peace and tranquility, and lasting peace is obtained. Following the Guru's Teachings, one is blessed with the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45813	ieMdR ieMdRwsix bYTy jm kw Bau pwvih ] (1049-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) indar indaraasan baithay jam kaa bha-o paavahi. Even Indra, seated upon his throne, is caught in the fear of death.
RECORD	para 45814	jmu n CofY bhu krm kmwvih ] (1049-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) jam na chhodai baho karam kamaaveh. The Messenger of Death will not spare them, even though they try all sorts of things.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	siqguru BytY qw mukiq pweIAY hir hir rsnw pIjY hy ]11] (1049-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur bhaytai taa mukat paa-ee-ai har har rasnaa peejai hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	When one meets with the True Guru, one is liberated, drinking in and savoring the sublime essence of the Lord, Har, Har. ||11||
DEFINE	para 45816	mnmuiK AMqir Bgiq n hoeI ] (1049-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh antar bhagat na ho-ee. There is no devotion within the self-willed manmukh.
RECORD	para 45817	gurmuiK Bgiq sWiq suKu hoeI ] (1049-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh bhagat saa Nt sukh ho-ee. Through devotional worship, the Gurmukh obtains peace and tranquility.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	pivqR pwvn sdw hY bwxI gurmiq AMqru BIjY hy ]12] (1049-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) pavitar paavan sadaa hai banee gurmat antar bheejai hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Forever pure and sanctified is the Word of the Guru's Bani; following the Guru's Teachings, one's inner being is drenched in it. ||12||
RECORD	para 45819	bRhmw ibsnu mhysu vIcwrI ] (1049-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) barahmaa bisan mahays veechaaree. I have considered Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva.
DEFINE	para 45820	qRY gux bDk mukiq inrwrI ] (1049-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) tarai gun baDhak mukat niraaree. They are bound by the three qualities - the three gunas; they are far away from liberation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	gurmuiK igAwnu eyko hY jwqw Anidnu nwmu rvIjY hy ]13] (1050-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh gi-aan ayko hai jaataa an-din naam raveejai hay. ||13||
UPHOLD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	The Gurmukh knows the spiritual wisdom of the One Lord. Night and day, he chants the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||13||
ALLOW	para 45823	byd pVih hir nwmu n bUJih ] (1050-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) bayd parheh har naam na boojheh. He may read the Vedas, but he does not realize the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 45824	mwieAw kwrix piV piV lUJih ] (1050-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa kaaran parh parh loojheh. For the sake of Maya, he reads and recites and argues.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	AMqir mYlu AigAwnI AMDw ikau kir duqru qrIjY hy ]14] (1050-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar mail agi-aanee anDhaa ki-o kar dutar tareejai hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	The ignorant and blind person is filled with filth within. How can he cross over the impassable world-ocean? ||14||
RECORD	para 45826	byd bwd siB AwiK vKwxih ] (1050-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) bayd baad sabh aakh vakaaneh. He voices all the controversies of the Vedas,
DEFINE	para 45827	n AMqru BIjY n sbdu pCwxih ] (1050-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) na antar bheejai na sabad pachhaaneh. but his inner being is not saturated or satisfied, and he does not realize the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	puMnu pwpu sBu byid idRVwieAw gurmuiK AMimRqu pIjY hy ]15] (1050-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) punn paap sabh bayd drirh-aa-i-aa gurmukh amrit peejai hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	The Vedas tell all about virtue and vice, but only the Gurmukh drinks in the Ambrosial Nectar. ||15||
DEFINE	para 45829	Awpy swcw eyko soeI ] (1050-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay saachaa ayko so-ee. The One True Lord is all by Himself.
DEFINE	para 45830	iqsu ibnu dUjw Avru n koeI ] (1050-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) tis bin doojaa avar na ko-ee. There is no one else except Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwim rqy mnu swcw sco scu rvIjY hy ]16]6] (1050-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay man saachaa sacho sach raveejai hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	6|| O Nanak, true is the mind of one who is attuned to the Naam; he speaks Truth, and nothing but Truth. ||16||6||
RECORD	para 45833	scY scw qKqu rcwieAw ] (1050-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sachaa takhat rachaa-i-aa. The True Lord has established the Throne of Truth.
DEFINE	para 45834	inj Gir visAw iqQY mohu n mwieAw ] (1050-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) nij ghar vasi-aa tithai moh na maa-i-aa. He dwells in His own home deep within the self, where there is no emotional attachment to Maya.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	sd hI swcu visAw Gt AMqir gurmuiK krxI swrI hy ]1] (1050-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) sad hee saach vasi-aa ghat antar gurmukh karnee saaree hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	The True Lord dwells deep within the nucleus of the Gurmukh's heart forever; his actions are excellent. ||1||
DEFINE	para 45836	scw saudw scu vwpwrw ] (1050-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa sa-udaa sach vaapaaraa. True is his merchandise, and true is his trade.
DEFINE	para 45837	n iqQY Brmu n dUjw pswrw ] (1050-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) na tithai bharam na doojaa pasaaraa. There is no doubt within him, and no expanse of duality.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	scw Dnu KitAw kdy qoit n AwvY bUJY ko vIcwrI hy ]2] (1050-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa Dhan khati-aa kaday tot na aavai boojhai ko veechaaree hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	He has earned the true wealth, which is never exhausted. How few are those who contemplate this, and understand. ||2||
DEFINE	para 45839	scY lwey sy jn lwgy ] (1050-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai laa-ay say jan laagay. They alone are attached to the True Name, whom the Lord Himself attaches.
DEFINE	para 45840	AMqir sbdu msqik vfBwgy ] (1050-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar sabad mastak vadbhaagay. The Word of the Shabad is deep within the nucleus of the self; good fortune is recorded upon their foreheads.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	scY sbid sdw gux gwvih sbid rqy vIcwrI hy ]3] (1050-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sabad sadaa gun gaavahi sabad ratay veechaaree hay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	Through the True Word of the Shabad, they sing the True Praises of the Lord; they are attuned to contemplative meditation on the Shabad. ||3||
RECORD	para 45842	sco scw scu swlwhI ] (1050-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) sacho sachaa sach saalaahee. I praise the True Lord, the Truest of the True.
RECORD	para 45843	eyko vyKw dUjw nwhI ] (1050-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayko vaykhaa doojaa naahee. I see the One Lord, and no other.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	gurmiq aUco aUcI pauVI igAwin rqin haumY mwrI hy ]4] (1050-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmat oocho oochee pa-orhee gi-aan ratan ha-umai maaree hay. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	The Guru's Teachings are the ladder to reach the highest of the high. the jewel of spiritual wisdom conquers egotism. ||4||
DEFINE	para 45845	mwieAw mohu sbid jlwieAw ] (1050-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh sabad jalaa-i-aa. Emotional attachment to Maya is burnt away by the Word of the Shabad.
WHEN	para 45846	scu min visAw jw quDu BwieAw ] (1050-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) sach man vasi-aa jaa tuDh bhaa-i-aa. The True One comes to dwell in the mind, when it pleases You, O Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	scy kI sB scI krxI haumY iqKw invwrI hy ]5] (1050-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachay kee sabh sachee karnee ha-umai tikhaa nivaaree hay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	True are all the actions of the truthful; the thirst of egotism is subdued. ||5||
RECORD	para 45848	mwieAw mohu sBu Awpy kInw ] (1050-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh sabh aapay keenaa. All by Himself, God created emotional attachment to Maya.
DEFINE	para 45849	gurmuiK ivrlY ikn hI cInw ] (1050-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlai kin hee cheenaa. How rare are those who, as Gurmukh, realize the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	gurmuiK hovY su scu kmwvY swcI krxI swrI hy ]6] (1050-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so sach kamaavai saachee karnee saaree hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	One who becomes Gurmukh practices Truth; true and excellent are his actions. ||6||
DEFINE	para 45851	kwr kmweI jo myry pRB BweI ] (1050-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaar kamaa-ee jo mayray parabh bhaa-ee. He does those deeds which are pleasing to my God;
RECORD	para 45852	haumY iqRsnw sbid buJweI ] (1050-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai tarisnaa sabad bujhaa-ee. through the Shabad, he burns away egotism and the thirst of desire.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	gurmiq sd hI AMqru sIqlu haumY mwir invwrI hy ]7] (1050-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmat sad hee antar seetal ha-umai maar nivaaree hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	Following the Guru's Teachings, he remains forever cool and calm deep within; he conquers and subdues his ego. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45854	sic lgy iqn sBu ikCu BwvY ] (1050-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) sach lagay tin sabh kichh bhaavai. Those who are attached to the Truth are pleased with everything.
DEFINE	para 45855	scY sbdy sic suhwvY ] (1050-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sabday sach suhaavai. They are embellished with the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	AYQY swcy sy dir swcy ndrI ndir svwrI hy ]8] (1050-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) aithai saachay say dar saachay nadree nadar savaaree hay. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Those who are true in this world, are true in the Court of the Lord. The Merciful Lord adorns them with His Mercy. ||8||
DEFINE	para 45857	ibnu swcy jo dUjY lwieAw ] (1050-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin saachay jo doojai laa-i-aa. Those who are attached to duality, and not the Truth,
RECORD	para 45858	mwieAw moh duK sbwieAw ] (1050-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh dukh sabaa-i-aa. are trapped in emotional attachment to Maya; they totally suffer in pain.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	ibnu gur duKu suKu jwpY nwhI mwieAw moh duKu BwrI hy ]9] (1050-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin gur dukh sukh jaapai naahee maa-i-aa moh dukh bhaaree hay. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Without the Guru, they do not understand pain and pleasure; attached to Maya, they suffer in terrible pain. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45860	swcw sbdu ijnw min BwieAw ] (1050-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) saachaa sabad jinaa man bhaa-i-aa. Those whose minds are pleased with the True Word of the Shabad
RECORD	para 45861	pUrib iliKAw iqnI kmwieAw ] (1050-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorab likhi-aa tinee kamaa-i-aa. act according to pre-ordained destiny.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	sco syvih scu iDAwvih sic rqy vIcwrI hy ]10] (1050-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) sacho sayveh sach Dhi-aavahi sach ratay veechaaree hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	They serve the True Lord, and meditate on the True Lord; they are imbued with contemplative meditation on the True Lord. ||10||
RECORD	para 45863	gur kI syvw mITI lwgI ] (1050-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kee sayvaa meethee laagee. Service to the Guru seems sweet to them.
DEFINE	para 45864	Anidnu sUK shj smwDI ] (1050-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din sookh sahj samaaDhee. Night and day, they are intuitively immersed in celestial peace.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	hir hir kriqAw mnu inrmlu hoAw gur kI syv ipAwrI hy ]11] (1050-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) har har karti-aa man nirmal ho-aa gur kee sayv pi-aaree hay. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	Chanting the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, their minds become immaculate; they love to serve the Guru. ||11||
DEFINE	para 45866	sy jn suKIey siqguir scy lwey ] (1050-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) say jan sukhee-ay satgur sachay laa-ay. Those humble beings are at peace, whom the True Guru attaches to the Truth.
RECORD	para 45867	Awpy Bwxy Awip imlwey ] (1050-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay bhaanay aap milaa-ay. He Himself, in His Will, merges them into Himself.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	siqguir rwKy sy jn aubry hor mwieAw moh KuAwrI hy ]12] (1050-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur raakhay say jan ubray hor maa-i-aa moh khu-aaree hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Those humble beings, whom the True Guru protects, are saved. The rest are ruined through emotional attachment to Maya. ||12||
RECORD	para 45870	gurmuiK swcw sbid pCwqw ] (1051-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh saachaa sabad pachhaataa. The Gurmukh realizes the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 45871	nw iqsu kutMbu nw iqsu mwqw ] (1051-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) naa tis kutamb naa tis maataa. He has no family, and he has no mother.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	eyko eyku rivAw sB AMqir sBnw jIAw kw AwDwrI hy ]13] (1051-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayko ayk ravi-aa sabh antar sabhnaa jee-aa kaa aaDhaaree hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	The One and Only Lord is pervading and permeating deep within the nucleus of all. He is the Support of all beings. ||13||
RECORD	para 45873	haumY myrw dUjw BwieAw ] (1051-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai mayraa doojaa bhaa-i-aa. Egotism, possessiveness, and the love of duality
REQUIRE	para 45874	ikCu n clY Duir Ksim iliK pwieAw ] (1051-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) kichh na chalai Dhur khasam likh paa-i-aa. - none of these shall go along with you; such is the pre-ordained will of our Lord and Master.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	gur swcy qy swcu kmwvih swcY dUK invwrI hy ]14] (1051-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur saachay tay saach kamaaveh saachai dookh nivaaree hay. ||14||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Through the True Guru, practice Truth, and the True Lord shall take away your pains. ||14||
REQUIRE	para 45876	jw qU dyih sdw suKu pwey ] (1051-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) jaa too deh sadaa sukh paa-ay. If You so bless me, then I shall find lasting peace.
RECORD	para 45877	swcY sbdy swcu kmwey ] (1051-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) saachai sabday saach kamaa-ay. Through the True Word of the Shabad, I live the Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	AMdru swcw mnu qnu swcw Bgiq Bry BMfwrI hy ]15] (1051-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) andar saachaa man tan saachaa bhagat bharay bhandaaree hay. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	The True Lord is within me, and my mind and body have become True. I am blessed with the overflowing treasure of devotional worship. ||15||
RECORD	para 45879	Awpy vyKY hukim clwey ] (1051-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay vaykhai hukam chalaa-ay. He Himself watches, and issues His Command.
RECORD	para 45880	Apxw Bwxw Awip krwey ] (1051-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) apnaa bhaanaa aap karaa-ay. He Himself inspires us to obey His Will.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwim rqy bYrwgI mnu qnu rsnw nwim svwrI hy ]16]7] (1051-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay bairaagee man tan rasnaa naam savaaree hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	7|| O Nanak, only those who are attuned to the Naam are detached; their minds, bodies and tongues are embellished with the Naam. ||16||7||
RECORD	para 45883	Awpy Awpu aupwie aupMnw ] (1051-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay aap upaa-ay upannaa. He Himself created Himself, and came into being.
DEFINE	para 45884	sB mih vrqY eyku prCMnw ] (1051-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabh meh vartai ayk parchhannaa. The One Lord is pervading in all, remaining hidden.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	sBnw swr kry jgjIvnu ijin Apxw Awpu pCwqw hy ]1] (1051-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabhnaa saar karay jagjeevan jin apnaa aap pachhaataa hay. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	The Lord, the Life of the world, takes care of all. Whoever knows his own self, realizes God. ||1||
RECORD	para 45886	ijin bRhmw ibsnu mhysu aupwey ] (1051-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin barahmaa bisan mahays upaa-ay. He who created Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva,
RECORD	para 45887	isir isir DMDY Awpy lwey ] (1051-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) sir sir DhanDhai aapay laa-ay. links each and every being to its tasks.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	ijsu BwvY iqsu Awpy myly ijin gurmuiK eyko jwqw hy ]2] (1051-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis bhaavai tis aapay maylay jin gurmukh ayko jaataa hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	He merges into Himself, whoever is pleasing to His Will. The Gurmukh knows the One Lord. ||2||
DEFINE	para 45889	Awvw gauxu hY sMswrw ] (1051-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) aavaa ga-on hai sansaaraa. The world is coming and going in reincarnation.
RECORD	para 45890	mwieAw mohu bhu icqY ibkwrw ] (1051-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh baho chitai bikaaraa. Attached to Maya, it dwells on its many sins.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	iQru swcw swlwhI sd hI ijin gur kw sbdu pCwqw hy ]3] (1051-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) thir saachaa saalaahee sad hee jin gur kaa sabad pachhaataa hay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	One who realizes the Word of the Guru's Shabad, praises forever the eternal, unchanging True Lord. ||3||
DEFINE	para 45892	ieik mUil lgy EnI suKu pwieAw ] (1051-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik mool lagay onee sukh paa-i-aa. Some are attached to the root - they find peace.
DEFINE	para 45893	fwlI lwgy iqnI jnmu gvwieAw ] (1051-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) daalee laagay tinee janam gavaa-i-aa. But those who are attached to the branches, waste their lives away uselessly.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	AMimRq Pl iqn jn kau lwgy jo bolih AMimRq bwqw hy ]4] (1051-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) amrit fal tin jan ka-o laagay jo boleh amrit baataa hay. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	Those humble beings, who chant the Name of the Ambrosial Lord, produce the ambrosial fruit. ||4||
RECORD	para 45895	hm gux nwhI ikAw bolh bol ] (1051-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) ham gun naahee ki-aa bolah bol. I have no virtues; what words should I speak?
RECORD	para 45896	qU sBnw dyKih qolih qol ] (1051-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) too sabhnaa daykheh toleh tol. You see all, and weigh them on Your scale.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	ijau BwvY iqau rwKih rhxw gurmuiK eyko jwqw hy ]5] (1051-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) ji-o bhaavai ti-o raakhahi rahnaa gurmukh ayko jaataa hay. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	By Your will, You preserve me, and so do I remain. The Gurmukh knows the One Lord. ||5||
RECORD	para 45898	jw quDu Bwxw qw scI kwrY lwey ] (1051-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) jaa tuDh bhaanaa taa sachee kaarai laa-ay. According to Your Will, You link me to my true tasks.
WHEN	para 45899	Avgx Coif gux mwih smwey ] (1051-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) avgan chhod gun maahi samaa-ay. Renouncing vice, I am immersed in virtue.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	gux mih eyko inrmlu swcw gur kY sbid pCwqw hy ]6] (1051-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) gun meh ayko nirmal saachaa gur kai sabad pachhaataa hay. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	The One Immaculate True Lord abides in virtue; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, He is realized. ||6||
RECORD	para 45901	jh dyKw qh eyko soeI ] (1051-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) jah daykhaa tah ayko so-ee. Wherever I look, there I see Him.
DEFINE	para 45902	dUjI durmiq sbdy KoeI ] (1051-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojee durmat sabday kho-ee. Duality and evil-mindedness are destroyed through the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	eyksu mih pRBu eyku smwxw ApxY rMig sd rwqw hy ]7] (1051-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) aykas meh parabh ayk samaanaa apnai rang sad raataa hay. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	The One Lord God is immersed in His Oneness. He is attuned forever to His own delight. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45904	kwieAw kmlu hY kumlwxw ] (1051-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kamal hai kumlaanaa. The body-lotus is withering away,
RECORD	para 45905	mnmuKu sbdu n buJY ieAwxw ] (1051-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh sabad na bujhai i-aanaa. but the ignorant, self-willed manmukh does not understand the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	gur prswdI kwieAw Kojy pwey jgjIvnu dwqw hy ]8] (1051-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee kaa-i-aa khojay paa-ay jagjeevan daataa hay. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	By Guru's Grace, he searches his body, and finds the Great Giver, the Life of the world. ||8||
RECORD	para 45907	kot ghI ky pwp invwry ] (1051-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) kot gahee kay paap nivaaray. The Lord frees up the body-fortress, which was seized by sins,
WHEN	para 45908	sdw hir jIau rwKY aur Dwry ] (1051-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) sadaa har jee-o raakhai ur Dhaaray. when one keeps the Dear Lord enshrined forever in the heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	jo ieCy soeI Plu pwey ijau rMgu mjITY rwqw hy ]9] (1051-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo ichhay so-ee fal paa-ay ji-o rang majeethai raataa hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	The fruits of his desires are obtained, and he is dyed in the permanent color of the Lord's Love. ||9||
UPHOLD	para 45910	mnmuKu igAwnu kQy n hoeI ] (1051-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh gi-aan kathay na ho-ee. The self-willed manmukh speaks of spiritual wisdom, but does not understand.
RECORD	para 45911	iPir iPir AwvY Taur n koeI ] (1051-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) fir fir aavai tha-ur na ko-ee. Again and again, he comes into the world, but he finds no place of rest.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	gurmuiK igAwnu sdw swlwhy juig juig eyko jwqw hy ]10] (1051-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh gi-aan sadaa saalaahay jug jug ayko jaataa hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	The Gurmukh is spiritually wise, and praises the Lord forever. Throughout each and every age, the Gurmukh knows the One Lord. ||10||
RECORD	para 45913	mnmuKu kwr kry siB duK sbwey ] (1051-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh kaar karay sabh dukh sabaa-ay. All the deeds which the manmukh does bring pain - nothing but pain.
DEFINE	para 45914	AMqir sbdu nwhI ikau dir jwey ] (1051-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar sabad naahee ki-o dar jaa-ay. The Word of the Shabad is not within him; how can he go to the Court of the Lord?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	gurmuiK sbdu vsY min swcw sd syvy suKdwqw hy ]11] (1051-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sabad vasai man saachaa sad sayvay sukh-daata hay. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	The True Shabad dwells deep within the mind of the Gurmukh; he serves the Giver of peace forever. ||11||
RECORD	para 45917	jh dyKw qU sBnI QweI ] (1052-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) jah daykhaa too sabhnee thaa-ee. Wherever I look, I see You, everywhere.
DEFINE	para 45918	pUrY guir sB soJI pweI ] (1052-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorai gur sabh sojhee paa-ee. Through the Perfect Guru, all this is known.
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	nwmo nwmu iDAweIAY sdw sd iehu mnu nwmy rwqw hy ]12] (1052-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) naamo naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai sadaa sad ih man naamay raataa hay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	I meditate forever and ever on the Naam; this mind is imbued with the Naam. ||12||
ALLOW	para 45920	nwmy rwqw pivqu srIrw ] (1052-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) naamay raataa pavit sareeraa. Imbued with the Naam, the body is sanctified.
DEFINE	para 45921	ibnu nwvY fUib muey ibnu nIrw ] (1052-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin naavai doob mu-ay bin neeraa. Without the Naam, they are drowned and die without water.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	Awvih jwvih nwmu nhI bUJih ieknw gurmuiK sbdu pCwqw hy ]13] (1052-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) aavahi jaaveh naam nahee boojheh iknaa gurmukh sabad pachhaataa hay. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	They come and go, but do not understand the Naam. Some, as Gurmukh, realize the Word of the Shabad. ||13||
RECORD	para 45923	pUrY siqguir bUJ buJweI ] (1052-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorai satgur boojh bujhaa-ee. The Perfect True Guru has imparted this understanding.
RECORD	para 45924	ivxu nwvY mukiq iknY n pweI ] (1052-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) vin naavai mukat kinai na paa-ee. Without the Name, no one attains liberation.
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	nwmy nwim imlY vifAweI shij rhY rMig rwqw hy ]14] (1052-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) naamay naam milai vadi-aa-ee sahj rahai rang raataa hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Through the Naam, the Name of the Lord, one is blessed with glorious greatness; he remains intuitively attuned to the Lord's Love. ||14||
RECORD	para 45926	kwieAw ngru FhY Fih FyrI ] (1052-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa nagar dhahai dheh dhayree. The body-village crumbles and collapses into a pile of dust.
DEFINE	para 45927	ibnu sbdY cUkY nhI PyrI ] (1052-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin sabdai chookai nahee fayree. Without the Shabad, the cycle of reincarnation is not brought to an end.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	swcu slwhy swic smwvY ijin gurmuiK eyko jwqw hy ]15] (1052-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) saach salaahay saach samaavai jin gurmukh ayko jaataa hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	One who knows the One Lord, through the True Guru, praises the True Lord, and remains immersed in the True Lord. ||15||
WHEN	para 45929	ijs no ndir kry so pwey ] swcw sbdu vsY min Awey ] (1052-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis no nadar karay so paa-ay. saachaa sabad vasai man aa-ay. The True Word of the Shabad comes to dwell in the mind, when the Lord bestows His Glance of Grace.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwim rqy inrMkwrI dir swcY swcu pCwqw hy ]16]8] (1052-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay nirankaaree dar saachai saach pachhaataa hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	8|| O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam, the Name of the Formless Lord, realize the True Lord in His True Court. ||16||8||
RECORD	para 45931	mwrU solhy 3 ] (1052-7) maaroo solhay 3. Maaroo, Solhay, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 45932	Awpy krqw sBu ijsu krxw ] (1052-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kartaa sabh jis karnaa. O Creator, it is You Yourself who does all.
DEFINE	para 45933	jIA jMq siB qyrI srxw ] (1052-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) jee-a jant sabh tayree sarnaa. All beings and creatures are under Your Protection.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Awpy gupqu vrqY sB AMqir gur kY sbid pCwqw hy ]1] (1052-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay gupat vartai sabh antar gur kai sabad pachhaataa hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	You are hidden, and yet permeating within all; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, You are realized. ||1||
DEFINE	para 45935	hir ky Bgiq Bry BMfwrw ] (1052-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kay bhagat bharay bhandaaraa. Devotion to the Lord is a treasure overflowing.
RECORD	para 45936	Awpy bKsy sbid vIcwrw ] (1052-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay bakhsay sabad veechaaraa. He Himself blesses us with contemplative meditation on the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	jo quDu BwvY soeI krsih scy isau mnu rwqw hy ]2] (1052-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo tuDh bhaavai so-ee karseh sachay si-o man raataa hay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	You do whatever You please; my mind is attuned to the True Lord. ||2||
DEFINE	para 45938	Awpy hIrw rqnu Amolo ] (1052-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay heeraa ratan amolo. You Yourself are the priceless diamond and jewel.
RECORD	para 45939	Awpy ndrI qoly qolo ] (1052-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay nadree tolay tolo. In Your Mercy, You weigh with Your scale.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	jIA jMq siB srix qumwrI kir ikrpw Awip pCwqw hy ]3] (1052-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) jee-a jant sabh saran tumaaree kar kirpaa aap pachhaataa hay. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	All beings and creatures are under Your protection. One who is blessed by Your Grace realizes his own self. ||3||
RECORD	para 45941	ijs no ndir hovY Duir qyrI ] (1052-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis no nadar hovai Dhur tayree. One who receives Your Mercy, O Primal Lord,
DEFINE	para 45942	mrY n jMmY cUkY PyrI ] (1052-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) marai na jammai chookai fayree. does not die, and is not reborn; he is released from the cycle of reincarnation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	swcy gux gwvY idnu rwqI juig juig eyko jwqw hy ]4] (1052-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) saachay gun gaavai din raatee jug jug ayko jaataa hay. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	He sings the Glorious Praises of the True Lord, day and night, and, throughout the ages, he knows the One Lord. ||4||
RECORD	para 45944	mwieAw moih sBu jgqu aupwieAw ] (1052-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi sabh jagat upaa-i-aa. Emotional attachment to Maya wells up throughout the whole world,
RECORD	para 45945	bRhmw ibsnu dyv sbwieAw ] (1052-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) barahmaa bisan dayv sabaa-i-aa. from Brahma, Vishnu and all the demi-gods.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	jo quDu Bwxy sy nwim lwgy igAwn mqI pCwqw hy ]5] (1052-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo tuDh bhaanay say naam laagay gi-aan matee pachhaataa hay. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	Those who are pleasing to Your Will, are attached to the Naam; through spiritual wisdom and understanding, You are recognized. ||5||
DEFINE	para 45947	pwp puMn vrqY sMswrw ] (1052-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) paap punn vartai sansaaraa. The world is engrossed in vice and virtue.
DEFINE	para 45948	hrKu sogu sBu duKu hY Bwrw ] (1052-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) harakh sog sabh dukh hai bhaaraa. Happiness and misery are totally loaded with pain.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	gurmuiK hovY so suKu pwey ijin gurmuiK nwmu pCwqw hy ]6] (1052-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so sukh paa-ay jin gurmukh naam pachhaataa hay. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	One who becomes Gurmukh finds peace; such a Gurmukh recognizes the Naam. ||6||
RECORD	para 45950	ikrqu n koeI mytxhwrw ] (1052-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) kirat na ko-ee maytanhaaraa. No one can erase the record of one's actions.
RECORD	para 45951	gur kY sbdy moK duAwrw ] (1052-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabday mokh du-aaraa. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, one finds the door of salvation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	pUrib iliKAw so Plu pwieAw ijin Awpu mwir pCwqw hy ]7] (1052-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorab likhi-aa so fal paa-i-aa jin aap maar pachhaataa hay. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	One who conquers self-conceit and recognizes the Lord, obtains the fruits of his pre- destined rewards. ||7||
DEFINE	para 45953	mwieAw moih hir isau icqu n lwgY ] (1052-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi har si-o chit na laagai. Emotionally attached to Maya, one's consciousness is not attached to the Lord.
RECORD	para 45954	dUjY Bwie Gxw duKu AwgY ] (1052-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay ghanaa dukh aagai. In the love of duality, he will suffer terrible agony in the world hereafter.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	mnmuK Brim Buly ByKDwrI AMq kwil pCuqwqw hy ]8] (1052-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh bharam bhulay bhaykh-Dhaaree ant kaal pachhutaataa hay. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	The hypocritical, self-willed manmukhs are deluded by doubt; at the very last moment, they regret and repent. ||8||
RECORD	para 45956	hir kY BwxY hir gux gwey ] (1052-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kai bhaanai har gun gaa-ay. In accordance with the Lord's Will, he sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 45957	siB iklibK kwty dUK sbwey ] (1052-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabh kilbikh kaatay dookh sabaa-ay. He is rid of all sins, and all suffering.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	hir inrmlu inrml hY bwxI hir syqI mnu rwqw hy ]9] (1052-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) har nirmal nirmal hai banee har saytee man raataa hay. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	The Lord is immaculate, and immaculate is the Word of His Bani. My mind is imbued with the Lord. ||9||
DEFINE	para 45959	ijs no ndir kry so gux iniD pwey ] (1052-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis no nadar karay so gun niDh paa-ay. One who is blessed with the Lord's Glance of Grace, obtains the Lord, the treasure of virtue.
DEFINE	para 45960	haumY myrw Twik rhwey ] (1052-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai mayraa thaak rahaa-ay. Egotism and possessiveness are brought to an end.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	gux Avgx kw eyko dwqw gurmuiK ivrlI jwqw hy ]10] (1052-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gun avgan kaa ayko daataa gurmukh virlee jaataa hay. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	The One Lord is the only Giver of virtue and vice, merits and demerits; how rare are those who, as Gurmukh, understand this. ||10||
DEFINE	para 45962	myrw pRBu inrmlu Aiq Apwrw ] (1052-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) mayraa parabh nirmal at apaaraa. My God is immaculate, and utterly infinite.
RECORD	para 45963	Awpy mylY gur sbid vIcwrw ] (1052-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay maylai gur sabad veechaaraa. God unites with Himself, through contemplation of the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	Awpy bKsy scu idRVwey mnu qnu swcY rwqw hy ]11] (1053-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay bakhsay sach drirh-aa-ay man tan saachai raataa hay. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	He Himself forgives, and implants the Truth. The mind and body are then attuned to the True Lord. ||11||
DEFINE	para 45966	mnu qnu mYlw ivic joiq Apwrw ] (1053-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) man tan mailaa vich jot apaaraa. Within the polluted mind and body is the Light of the Infinite Lord.
RECORD	para 45967	gurmiq bUJY kir vIcwrw ] (1053-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmat boojhai kar veechaaraa. One who understands the Guru's Teachings, contemplates this.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	haumY mwir sdw mnu inrmlu rsnw syiv suKdwqw hy ]12] (1053-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai maar sadaa man nirmal rasnaa sayv sukh-daata hay. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Conquering egotism, the mind becomes immaculate forever; with his tongue, he serves the Lord, the Giver of peace. ||12||
DEFINE	para 45969	gV kwieAw AMdir bhu ht bwjwrw ] (1053-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) garh kaa-i-aa andar baho hat baajaaraa. In the fortress of the body there are many shops and bazaars;
DEFINE	para 45970	iqsu ivic nwmu hY Aiq Apwrw ] (1053-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) tis vich naam hai at apaaraa. within them is the Naam, the Name of the utterly infinite Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	gur kY sbid sdw dir sohY haumY mwir pCwqw hy ]13] (1053-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad sadaa dar sohai ha-umai maar pachhaataa hay. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	In His Court, one is embellished forever with the Word of the Guru's Shabad; he conquers egotism and realizes the Lord. ||13||
DEFINE	para 45972	rqnu Amolku Agm Apwrw ] (1053-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) ratan amolak agam apaaraa. The jewel is priceless, inaccessible and infinite.
RECORD	para 45973	kImiq kvxu kry vycwrw ] (1053-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) keemat kavan karay vaychaaraa. How can the poor wretch estimate its worth?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	gur kY sbdy qoil qolwey AMqir sbid pCwqw hy ]14] (1053-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabday tol tolaa-ay antar sabad pachhaataa hay. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, it is weighed, and so the Shabad is realized deep within. ||14||
RECORD	para 45975	isimRiq swsqR bhuqu ibsQwrw ] mwieAw mohu psirAw pwswrw ] (1053-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) simrit saastar bahut bisthaaraa. maa-i-aa moh pasri-aa paasaaraa. The great volumes of the Simritees and the Shaastras only extend the extension of attachment to Maya.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	mUrK pVih sbdu n bUJih gurmuiK ivrlY jwqw hy ]15] (1053-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) moorakh parheh sabad na boojheh gurmukh virlai jaataa hay. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	The fools read them, but do not understand the Word of the Shabad. How rare are those who, as Gurmukh, understand. ||15||
RECORD	para 45977	Awpy krqw kry krwey ] (1053-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kartaa karay karaa-ay. The Creator Himself acts, and causes all to act.
DEFINE	para 45978	scI bwxI scu idRVwey ] (1053-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachee banee sach drirh-aa-ay. Through the True Word of His Bani, Truth is implanted deep within.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwmu imlY vifAweI juig juig eyko jwqw hy ]16]9] (1053-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam milai vadi-aa-ee jug jug ayko jaataa hay. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	9|| O Nanak, through the Naam, one is blessed with glorious greatness, and throughout the ages, the One Lord is known. ||16||9||
RECORD	para 45981	so scu syivhu isrjxhwrw ] (1053-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) so sach sayvihu sirjanhaaraa. Serve the True Creator Lord.
DEFINE	para 45982	sbdy dUK invwrxhwrw ] (1053-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabday dookh nivaaranhaaraa. The Word of the Shabad is the Destroyer of pain.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Agmu Agocru kImiq nhI pweI Awpy Agm AQwhw hy ]1] (1053-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) agam agochar keemat nahee paa-ee aapay agam athaahaa hay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	He is inaccessible and unfathomable; He cannot be evaluated. He Himself is inaccessible and immeasurable. ||1||
RECORD	para 45984	Awpy scw scu vrqwey ] (1053-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay sachaa sach vartaa-ay. The True Lord Himself makes Truth pervasive.
RECORD	para 45985	ieik jn swcY Awpy lwey ] (1053-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik jan saachai aapay laa-ay. He attaches some humble beings to the Truth.
