RECORD	para 46237	gur kI swKI AMimRq BwKI ] (1058-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kee saakhee amrit bhaakhee. I speak the Ambrosial Teachings of the Guru.
RECORD	para 46238	scY sbdy scu suBwKI ] (1058-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sabday sach subhaakhee. I lovingly chant the Truth, through the True Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	sdw sic rMig rwqw mnu myrw scy sic smwiedw ]3] (1058-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) sadaa sach rang raataa man mayraa sachay sach samaa-idaa. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	My mind remains forever imbued with the Love of the True Lord. I am immersed in the Truest of the True. ||3||
DEFINE	para 46240	gurmuiK mnu inrmlu sq sir nwvY ] (1058-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh man nirmal sat sar naavai. Immaculate and pure is the mind of the Gurmukh, who bathes in the Pool of Truth.
RECORD	para 46241	mYlu n lwgY sic smwvY ] (1058-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) mail na laagai sach samaavai. No filth attaches to him; he merges in the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	sco scu kmwvY sd hI scI Bgiq idRVwiedw ]4] (1058-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) sacho sach kamaavai sad hee sachee bhagat darirhaa-idaa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	He truly practices Truth forever; true devotion is implanted within him. ||4||
DEFINE	para 46243	gurmuiK scu bYxI gurmuiK scu nYxI ] (1058-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sach bainee gurmukh sach nainee. True is the speech of the Gurmukh; true are the eyes of the Gurmukh.
RECORD	para 46244	gurmuiK scu kmwvY krxI ] (1058-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sach kamaavai karnee. The Gurmukh practices and lives the Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	sd hI scu khY idnu rwqI Avrw scu khwiedw ]5] (1058-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) sad hee sach kahai din raatee avraa sach kahaa-idaa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	He speaks the Truth forever, day and night, and inspires others to speak the Truth. ||5||
DEFINE	para 46246	gurmuiK scI aUqm bwxI ] (1058-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sachee ootam banee. True and exalted is the speech of the Gurmukh.
RECORD	para 46247	gurmuiK sco scu vKwxI ] (1058-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sacho sach vakhaanee. The Gurmukh speaks Truth, only Truth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	gurmuiK sd syvih sco scw gurmuiK sbdu suxwiedw ]6] (1058-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sad sayveh sacho sachaa gurmukh sabad sunaa-idaa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	The Gurmukh serves the Truest of the True forever; the Gurmukh proclaims the Word of the Shabad. ||6||
RECORD	para 46250	gurmuiK hovY su soJI pwey ] (1059-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so sojhee paa-ay. One who becomes Gurmukh understands.
RECORD	para 46251	haumY mwieAw Brmu gvwey ] (1059-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai maa-i-aa bharam gavaa-ay. He rids himself of egotism, Maya and doubt.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	gur kI pauVI aUqm aUcI dir scY hir gux gwiedw ]7] (1059-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kee pa-orhee ootam oochee dar sachai har gun gaa-idaa. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	He ascends the sublime, exalted ladder of the Guru, and he sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord at His True Door. ||7||
RECORD	para 46253	gurmuiK scu sMjmu krxI swru ] (1059-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sach sanjam karnee saar. The Gurmukh practices true self-control, and acts in excellence.
RECORD	para 46254	gurmuiK pwey moK duAwru ] (1059-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh paa-ay mokh du-aar. The Gurmukh obtains the gate of salvation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Bwie Bgiq sdw rMig rwqw Awpu gvwie smwiedw ]8] (1059-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) bhaa-ay bhagat sadaa rang raataa aap gavaa-ay samaa-idaa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Through loving devotion, he remains forever imbued with the Lord's Love; eradicating self-conceit, he merges in the Lord. ||8||
RECORD	para 46256	gurmuiK hovY mnu Koij suxwey ] (1059-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai man khoj sunaa-ay. One who becomes Gurmukh examines his own mind, and instructs others.
DEFINE	para 46257	scY nwim sdw ilv lwey ] (1059-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai naam sadaa liv laa-ay. He is lovingly attuned to the True Name forever.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	jo iqsu BwvY soeI krsI jo scy min Bwiedw ]9] (1059-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo tis bhaavai so-ee karsee jo sachay man bhaa-idaa. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	They act in harmony with the Mind of the True Lord. ||9||
RECORD	para 46259	jw iqsu BwvY siqgurU imlwey ] (1059-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) jaa tis bhaavai satguroo milaa-ay. As it pleases His Will, He unites us with the True Guru.
RECORD	para 46260	jw iqsu BwvY qw mMin vswey ] (1059-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) jaa tis bhaavai taa man vasaa-ay. As it pleases His Will, He comes to dwell within the mind.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	AwpxY BwxY sdw rMig rwqw BwxY mMin vswiedw ]10] (1059-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapnai bhaanai sadaa rang raataa bhaanai man vasaa-idaa. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	As it pleases His Will, He imbues us with His Love; as it pleases His Will, He comes to dwell in the mind. ||10||
DEFINE	para 46262	mnhiT krm kry so CIjY ] (1059-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) manhath karam karay so chheejai. Those who act stubborn-mindedly are destroyed.
RECORD	para 46263	bhuqy ByK kry nhI BIjY ] (1059-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) bahutay bhaykh karay nahee bheejai. Wearing all sorts of religious robes, they do not please the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	ibiKAw rwqy duKu kmwvih duKy duiK smwiedw ]11] (1059-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) bikhi-aa raatay dukh kamaaveh dukhay dukh samaa-idaa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	Tinged by corruption, they earn only pain; they are immersed in pain. ||11||
RECORD	para 46265	gurmuiK hovY su suKu kmwey ] (1059-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so sukh kamaa-ay. One who becomes Gurmukh earns peace.
RECORD	para 46266	mrx jIvx kI soJI pwey ] (1059-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) maran jeevan kee sojhee paa-ay. He comes to understand death and birth.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	mrxu jIvxu jo sm kir jwxY so myry pRB Bwiedw ]12] (1059-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) maran jeevan jo sam kar jaanai so mayray parabh bhaa-idaa. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	One who looks alike upon death and birth, is pleasing to my God. ||12||
DEFINE	para 46268	gurmuiK mrih su hih prvwxu ] (1059-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh mareh so heh parvaan. The Gurmukh, while remaining dead, is respected and approved.
DEFINE	para 46269	Awvx jwxw sbdu pCwxu ] (1059-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) aavan jaanaa sabad pachhaan. He realizes that coming and going are according to God's Will.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	mrY n jMmY nw duKu pwey mn hI mnih smwiedw ]13] (1059-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) marai na jammai naa dukh paa-ay man hee maneh samaa-idaa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	He does not die, he is not reborn, and he does not suffer in pain; his mind merges in the Mind of God. ||13||
DEFINE	para 46271	sy vfBwgI ijnI siqguru pwieAw ] (1059-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) say vadbhaagee jinee satgur paa-i-aa. Very fortunate are those who find the True Guru.
RECORD	para 46272	haumY ivchu mohu cukwieAw ] (1059-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai vichahu moh chukaa-i-aa. They eradicate egotism and attachment from within.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	mnu inrmlu iPir mYlu n lwgY dir scY soBw pwiedw ]14] (1059-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) man nirmal fir mail na laagai dar sachai sobhaa paa-idaa. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Their minds are immaculate, and they are never again stained with filth. They are honored at the Door of the True Court. ||14||
RECORD	para 46274	Awpy kry krwey Awpy ] (1059-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay karay karaa-ay aapay. He Himself acts, and inspires all to act.
RECORD	para 46275	Awpy vyKY Qwip auQwpy ] (1059-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay vaykhai thaap uthaapay. He Himself watches over all; He establishes and disestablishes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	gurmuiK syvw myry pRB BwvY scu suix lyKY pwiedw ]15] (1059-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sayvaa mayray parabh bhaavai sach sun laykhai paa-idaa. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	The service of the Gurmukh is pleasing to my God; one who listens to the Truth is approved. ||15||
RECORD	para 46277	gurmuiK sco scu kmwvY ] (1059-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sacho sach kamaavai. The Gurmukh practices Truth, and only Truth.
DEFINE	para 46278	gurmuiK inrmlu mYlu n lwvY ] (1059-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh nirmal mail na laavai. The Gurmukh is immaculate; no filth attaches to him.
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwim rqy vIcwrI nwmy nwim smwiedw ]16]1]15] (1059-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay veechaaree naamay naam samaa-idaa. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	O Nanak, those who contemplate the Naam are imbued with it. They merge in the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||16||
RECORD	para 46281	Awpy isRsit hukim sB swjI ] (1059-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay sarisat hukam sabh saajee. He Himself fashioned the Universe, through the Hukam of His Command.
RECORD	para 46282	Awpy Qwip auQwip invwjI ] (1059-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay thaap uthaap nivaajee. He Himself establishes and disestablishes, and embellishes with grace.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Awpy inAwau kry sBu swcw swcy swic imlwiedw ]1] (1059-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay ni-aa-o karay sabh saachaa saachay saach milaa-idaa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	The True Lord Himself administers all justice; through Truth, we merge in the True Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 46284	kwieAw kotu hY Awkwrw ] (1059-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kot hai aakaaraa. The body takes the form of a fortress.
RECORD	para 46285	mwieAw mohu psirAw pwswrw ] (1059-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh pasri-aa paasaaraa. Emotional attachment to Maya has expanded throughout its expanse.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	ibnu sbdY BsmY kI FyrI KyhU Kyh rlwiedw ]2] (1059-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin sabdai bhasmai kee dhayree khayhoo khayh ralaa-idaa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	Without the Word of the Shabad, the body is reduced to a pile of ashes; in the end, dust mingles with dust. ||2||
DEFINE	para 46287	kwieAw kMcn kotu Apwrw ] (1059-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kanchan kot apaaraa. The body is the infinite fortress of gold;
DEFINE	para 46288	ijsu ivic rivAw sbdu Apwrw ] (1059-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis vich ravi-aa sabad apaaraa. it is permeated by the Infinite Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	gurmuiK gwvY sdw gux swcy imil pRIqm suKu pwiedw ]3] (1059-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh gaavai sadaa gun saachay mil pareetam sukh paa-idaa. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	The Gurmukh sings the Glorious Praises of the True Lord forever; meeting his Beloved, he finds peace. ||3||
DEFINE	para 46290	kwieAw hir mMdru hir Awip svwry ] (1059-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa har mandar har aap savaaray. The body is the temple of the Lord; the Lord Himself embellishes it.
RECORD	para 46291	iqsu ivic hir jIau vsY murwry ] (1059-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) tis vich har jee-o vasai muraaray. The Dear Lord dwells within it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	gur kY sbid vxjin vwpwrI ndrI Awip imlwiedw ]4] (1059-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad vanjan vaapaaree nadree aap milaa-idaa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the merchants trade, and in His Grace, the Lord merges them with Himself. ||4||
DEFINE	para 46293	so sUcw ij kroDu invwry ] (1059-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) so soochaa je karoDh nivaaray. He alone is pure, who eradicates anger.
RECORD	para 46294	sbdy bUJY Awpu svwry ] (1059-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabday boojhai aap savaaray. He realizes the Shabad, and reforms himself.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	Awpy kry krwey krqw Awpy mMin vswiedw ]5] (1059-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay karay karaa-ay kartaa aapay man vasaa-idaa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	The Creator Himself acts, and inspires all to act; He Himself abides in the mind. ||5||
DEFINE	para 46296	inrml Bgiq hY inrwlI ] (1059-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) nirmal bhagat hai niraalee. Pure and unique is devotional worship.
DEFINE	para 46297	mnu qnu Dovih sbid vIcwrI ] (1059-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) man tan Dhoveh sabad veechaaree. The mind and body are washed clean, contemplating the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	Anidnu sdw rhY rMig rwqw kir ikrpw Bgiq krwiedw ]6] (1060-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din sadaa rahai rang raataa kar kirpaa bhagat karaa-idaa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	One who remains forever imbued with His Love, night and day - in His Mercy, the Lord inspires him to perform devotional worship service. ||6||
RECORD	para 46300	iesu mn mMdr mih mnUAw DwvY ] (1060-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) is man mandar meh manoo-aa Dhaavai. In this temple of the mind, the mind wanders around.
RECORD	para 46301	suKu plir iqAwig mhw duKu pwvY ] (1060-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) sukh palar ti-aag mahaa dukh paavai. Discarding joy like straw, it suffers in terrible pain.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	ibnu siqgur Byty Taur n pwvY Awpy Kylu krwiedw ]7] (1060-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin satgur bhaytay tha-ur na paavai aapay khayl karaa-idaa. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	Without meeting the True Guru, it finds no place of rest; He Himself has staged this play. ||7||
DEFINE	para 46303	Awip AprMpru Awip vIcwrI ] (1060-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aap aprampar aap veechaaree. He Himself is infinite; He contemplates Himself.
RECORD	para 46304	Awpy myly krxI swrI ] (1060-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay maylay karnee saaree. He Himself bestows Union through actions of excellence.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	ikAw ko kwr kry vycwrw Awpy bKis imlwiedw ]8] (1060-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) ki-aa ko kaar karay vaychaaraa aapay bakhas milaa-idaa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	What can the poor creatures do? Granting forgiveness, He unites them with Himself. ||8||
RECORD	para 46306	Awpy siqguru myly pUrw ] (1060-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay satgur maylay pooraa. The Perfect Lord Himself unites them with the True Guru.
RECORD	para 46307	scY sbid mhwbl sUrw ] (1060-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachai sabad mahaabal sooraa. Through the True Word of the Shabad, he makes them brave spiritual heroes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Awpy myly dy vifAweI scy isau icqu lwiedw ]9] (1060-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay maylay day vadi-aa-ee sachay si-o chit laa-idaa. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Uniting them with Himself, He bestows glorious greatness; He inspires them to focus their consciousness on the True Lord. ||9||
DEFINE	para 46309	Gr hI AMdir swcw soeI ] (1060-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) ghar hee andar saachaa so-ee. The True Lord is deep within the heart.
DEFINE	para 46310	gurmuiK ivrlw bUJY koeI ] (1060-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlaa boojhai ko-ee. How rare are those who, as Gurmukh, realize this.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	nwmu inDwnu visAw Gt AMqir rsnw nwmu iDAwiedw ]10] (1060-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) naam niDhaan vasi-aa ghat antar rasnaa naam Dhi-aa-idaa. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	The treasure of the Naam abides deep within their hearts; they meditate on the Naam with their tongues. ||10||
RECORD	para 46312	idsMqru BvY AMqru nhI Bwly ] (1060-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) disantar bhavai antar nahee bhaalay. He wanders through foreign lands, but does not look within himself.
DEFINE	para 46313	mwieAw moih bDw jmkwly ] (1060-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi baDhaa jamkaalay. Attached to Maya, he is bound and gagged by the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	jm kI PwsI kbhU n qUtY dUjY Bwie Brmwiedw ]11] (1060-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) jam kee faasee kabhoo na tootai doojai bhaa-ay bharmaa-idaa. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	The noose of death around his neck will never be untied; in the love of duality, he wanders in reincarnation. ||11||
DEFINE	para 46315	jpu qpu sMjmu horu koeI nwhI ] (1060-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) jap tap sanjam hor ko-ee naahee. There is no real chanting, meditation, penance or self-control,
RECORD	para 46316	jb lgu gur kw sbdu n kmwhI ] (1060-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) jab lag gur kaa sabad na kamaahee. as long as one does not live to the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	gur kY sbid imilAw scu pwieAw scy sic smwiedw ]12] (1060-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad mili-aa sach paa-i-aa sachay sach samaa-idaa. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Accepting the Word of the Guru's Shabad, one obtains Truth; through Truth, one merges in the True Lord. ||12||
DEFINE	para 46318	kwm kroDu sbl sMswrw ] (1060-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaam karoDh sabal sansaaraa. Sexual desire and anger are very powerful in the world.
RECORD	para 46319	bhu krm kmwvih sBu duK kw pswrw ] (1060-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) baho karam kamaaveh sabh dukh kaa pasaaraa. They lead to all sorts of actions, but these only add to all the pain.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	siqgur syvih sy suKu pwvih scY sbid imlwiedw ]13] (1060-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayveh say sukh paavahi sachai sabad milaa-idaa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	Those who serve the True Guru find peace; they are united with the True Shabad. ||13||
RECORD	para 46321	pauxu pwxI hY bYsMqru ] (1060-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) pa-un paanee hai baisantar. Air, water and fire make up the body.
RECORD	para 46322	mwieAw mohu vrqY sB AMqir ] (1060-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh vartai sabh antar. Emotional attachment to Maya rules deep within all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	ijin kIqy jw iqsY pCwxih mwieAw mohu cukwiedw ]14] (1060-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin keetay jaa tisai pachhaaneh maa-i-aa moh chukaa-idaa. ||14||
WHEN	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	When one realizes the One who created him, emotional attachment to Maya is dispelled. ||14||
DEFINE	para 46324	ieik mwieAw moih grib ivAwpy ] (1060-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik maa-i-aa mohi garab vi-aapay. Some are engrossed in emotional attachment to Maya and pride.
DEFINE	para 46325	haumY hoie rhy hY Awpy ] (1060-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai ho-ay rahay hai aapay. They are self-conceited and egotistical.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	jmkwlY kI Kbir n pweI AMiq gieAw pCuqwiedw ]15] (1060-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) jamkaalai kee khabar na paa-ee ant ga-i-aa pachhutaa-idaa. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	They never think about the Messenger of Death; in the end, they leave, regretting and repenting. ||15||
RECORD	para 46327	ijin aupwey so ibiD jwxY ] (1060-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin upaa-ay so biDh jaanai. He alone knows the Way, who created it.
DEFINE	para 46328	gurmuiK dyvY sbdu pCwxY ] (1060-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh dayvai sabad pachhaanai. The Gurmukh, who is blessed with the Shabad, realizes Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk dwsu khY bynµqI sic nwim icqu lwiedw ]16]2]16] (1060-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak daas kahai baynantee sach naam chit laa-idaa. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	Slave Nanak offers ths prayer; O Lord, let my consciousness be attached to the True Name. ||16||
RECORD	para 46331	Awid jugwid dieAwpiq dwqw ] (1060-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) aad jugaad da-i-aapat daataa. From the very beginning of time, and throughout the ages, the Merciful Lord has been the Great Giver.
DEFINE	para 46332	pUry gur kY sbid pCwqw ] (1060-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) pooray gur kai sabad pachhaataa. Through the Shabad, the Word of the Perfect Guru, He is realized.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	quDuno syvih sy quJih smwvih qU Awpy myil imlwiedw ]1] (1060-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) tuDhuno sayveh say tujheh samaaveh too aapay mayl milaa-idaa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Those who serve You are immersed in You. You unite them in Union with Yourself. ||1||
DEFINE	para 46334	Agm Agocru kImiq nhI pweI ] (1060-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) agam agochar keemat nahee paa-ee. You are inaccessible and unfathomable; Your limits cannot be found.
RECORD	para 46335	jIA jMq qyrI srxweI ] (1060-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) jee-a jant tayree sarnaa-ee. All beings and creatures seek Your Sanctuary.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	ijau quDu BwvY iqvY clwvih qU Awpy mwrig pwiedw ]2] (1060-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) ji-o tuDh bhaavai tivai chalaaveh too aapay maarag paa-idaa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	As is pleases Your Will, You guide us along; You Yourself place us on the Path. ||2||
REQUIRE	para 46337	hY BI swcw hosI soeI ] (1060-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) hai bhee saachaa hosee so-ee. The True Lord is, and shall always be.
DEFINE	para 46338	Awpy swjy Avru n koeI ] (1060-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay saajay avar na ko-ee. He Himself creates - there is no other at all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	sBnw swr kry suKdwqw Awpy irjku phucwiedw ]3] (1060-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabhnaa saar karay sukh-daata aapay rijak pahuchaa-idaa. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	The Giver of peace takes care of all; He Himself sustains them. ||3||
DEFINE	para 46340	Agm Agocru AlK Apwrw ] (1060-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) agam agochar alakh apaaraa. You are inaccessible, unfathomable, invisible and infinite;
RECORD	para 46341	koie n jwxY qyrw prvwrw ] (1060-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) ko-ay na jaanai tayraa parvaaraa. no one knows Your extent.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	Awpxw Awpu pCwxih Awpy gurmqI Awip buJwiedw ]4] (1060-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapnaa aap pachhaaneh aapay gurmatee aap bujhaa-idaa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	You Yourself realize Yourself. Through the Guru's Teachings, You reveal Yourself. ||4||
RECORD	para 46343	pwqwl purIAw loA Awkwrw ] iqsu ivic vrqY hukmu krwrw ] (1060-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) paataal puree-aa lo-a aakaaraa. tis vich vartai hukam karaaraa. Your Almighty Command prevails throughout the nether worlds, realms and worlds of form.
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	hukmy swjy hukmy Fwhy hukmy myil imlwiedw ]5] (1061-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) hukmay saajay hukmay dhaahay hukmay mayl milaa-idaa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	By the Hukam of Your Command, You create, and by Your Command, You destroy. By Your Command, You unite in Union. ||5||
RECORD	para 46346	hukmY bUJY su hukmu slwhy ] (1061-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) hukmai boojhai so hukam salaahay. One who realizes Your Command, praises Your Command.
DEFINE	para 46347	Agm Agocr vyprvwhy ] (1061-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) agam agochar vayparvaahay. You are Inaccessible, Unfathomable and Self-Sufficient.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	jyhI miq dyih so hovY qU Awpy sbid buJwiedw ]6] (1061-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) jayhee mat deh so hovai too aapay sabad bujhaa-idaa. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	As is the understanding You give, so do I become. You Yourself reveal the Shabad. ||6||
RECORD	para 46349	Anidnu Awrjw iCjdI jwey ] (1061-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din aarjaa chhijdee jaa-ay. Night and day, the days of our lives wear away.
RECORD	para 46350	rYix idnsu duie swKI Awey ] (1061-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) rain dinas du-ay saakhee aa-ay. Night and day both bear witness to this loss.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	mnmuKu AMDu n cyqY mUVw isr aUpir kwlu rUAwiedw ]7] (1061-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh anDh na chaytai moorhaa sir oopar kaal roo-aa-idaa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	The blind, foolish, self-willed manmukh is not aware of this; death is hovering over his head. ||7||
DEFINE	para 46352	mnu qnu sIqlu gur crxI lwgw ] (1061-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) man tan seetal gur charnee laagaa. The mind and body are cooled and soothed, holding tight to the Guru's Feet.
DEFINE	para 46353	AMqir Brmu gieAw Bau Bwgw ] (1061-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar bharam ga-i-aa bha-o bhaagaa. Doubt is eliminated from within, and fear runs away.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	sdw Anµdu scy gux gwvih scu bwxI bolwiedw ]8] (1061-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) sadaa anand sachay gun gaavahi sach banee bolaa-idaa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	One is in bliss forever, singing the Glorious Praises of the True Lord, and speaking the True Word of His Bani. ||8||
RECORD	para 46355	ijin qU jwqw krm ibDwqw ] (1061-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin too jaataa karam biDhaataa. One who knows You as the Architect of Karma,
RECORD	para 46356	pUrY Bwig gur sbid pCwqw ] (1061-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorai bhaag gur sabad pachhaataa. has the good fortune of perfect destiny, and recognizes the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	jiq piq scu scw scu soeI haumY mwir imlwiedw ]9] (1061-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) jat pat sach sachaa sach so-ee ha-umai maar milaa-idaa. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	The Lord, the Truest of the True, is his social class and honor. Conquering his ego, he is united with the Lord. ||9||
DEFINE	para 46358	mnu kToru dUjY Bwie lwgw ] (1061-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) man kathor doojai bhaa-ay laagaa. The stubborn and insensitive mind is attached to the love of duality.
ALLOW	para 46359	Brmy BUlw iPrY ABwgw ] (1061-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) bharmay bhoolaa firai abhaagaa. Deluded by doubt, the unfortunate wander around in confusion.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	krmu hovY qw siqguru syvy shjy hI suKu pwiedw ]10] (1061-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) karam hovai taa satgur sayvay sehjay hee sukh paa-idaa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	But if they are blessed by God's Grace, they serve the True Guru, and easily obtain peace. ||10||
RECORD	para 46361	lK caurwsIh Awip aupwey ] (1061-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) lakh cha-oraaseeh aap upaa-ay. He Himself created the 8.4 million species of beings.
DEFINE	para 46362	mwns jnim gur Bgiq idRVwey ] (1061-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) maanas janam gur bhagat drirh-aa-ay. Only in this human life, is devotional worship to the Guru implanted within.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	ibnu BgqI ibstw ivic vwsw ibstw ivic iPir pwiedw ]11] (1061-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin bhagtee bistaa vich vaasaa bistaa vich fir paa-idaa. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	Without devotion, one lives in manure; he falls into manure again and again. ||11||
DEFINE	para 46364	krmu hovY guru Bgiq idRVwey ] (1061-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) karam hovai gur bhagat drirh-aa-ay. If one is blessed with His Grace, devotional worship to the Guru is implanted within.
RECORD	para 46365	ivxu krmw ikau pwieAw jwey ] (1061-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) vin karmaa ki-o paa-i-aa jaa-ay. Without God's Grace, how can anyone find Him?
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Awpy kry krwey krqw ijau BwvY iqvY clwiedw ]12] (1061-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay karay karaa-ay kartaa ji-o bhaavai tivai chalaa-idaa. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	The Creator Himself acts, and inspires all to act; as He wills, he leads us on. ||12||
RECORD	para 46367	isimRiq swsq AMqu n jwxY ] (1061-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) simrit saasat ant na jaanai. The Simritees and the Shaastras do not know His limits.
RECORD	para 46368	mUrKu AMDw qqu n pCwxY ] (1061-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) moorakh anDhaa tat na pachhaanai. The blind fool does not recognize the essence of reality.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	Awpy kry krwey krqw Awpy Brim Bulwiedw ]13] (1061-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay karay karaa-ay kartaa aapay bharam bhulaa-idaa. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	The Creator Himself acts, and inspires all to act; He Himself deludes with doubt. ||13||
RECORD	para 46370	sBu ikCu Awpy Awip krwey ] (1061-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabh kichh aapay aap karaa-ay. He Himself causes everything to be done.
RECORD	para 46371	Awpy isir isir DMDY lwey ] (1061-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay sir sir DhanDhai laa-ay. He Himself joins each and every person to his tasks.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Awpy Qwip auQwpy vyKY gurmuiK Awip buJwiedw ]14] (1061-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay thaap uthaapay vaykhai gurmukh aap bujhaa-idaa. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	He Himself establishes and disestablishes, and watches over all; He reveals Himself to the Gurmukh. ||14||
DEFINE	para 46373	scw swihbu gihr gMBIrw ] (1061-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa saahib gahir gambheeraa. The True Lord and Master is profoundly deep and unfathomable.
DEFINE	para 46374	sdw slwhI qw mnu DIrw ] (1061-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) sadaa salaahee taa man Dheeraa. Praising Him forever, the mind is comforted and consoled.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	Agm Agocru kImiq nhI pweI gurmuiK mMin vswiedw ]15] (1061-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) agam agochar keemat nahee paa-ee gurmukh man vasaa-idaa. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	He is inaccessible and unfathomable; His value cannot be estimated. He dwells in the mind of the Gurmukh. ||15||
DEFINE	para 46376	Awip inrwlmu hor DMDY loeI ] (1061-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) aap niraalam hor DhanDhai lo-ee. He Himself is detached; all others are entangled in their affairs.
RECORD	para 46377	gur prswdI bUJY koeI ] (1061-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee boojhai ko-ee. By Guru's Grace, one comes to understand Him.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwmu vsY Gt AMqir gurmqI myil imlwiedw ]16]3]17] (1061-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam vasai ghat antar gurmatee mayl milaa-idaa. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	O Nanak, the Naam, the Name of the Lord, comes to dwell deep within the heart; through the Guru's Teachings, one is united in His Union. ||16||
RECORD	para 46380	jug CqIh kIE gubwrw ] (1061-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) jug chhateeh kee-o gubaaraa. For thirty-six ages, utter darkness prevailed.
RECORD	para 46381	qU Awpy jwxih isrjxhwrw ] (1061-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) too aapay jaaneh sirjanhaaraa. Only You Yourself know this, O Creator Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	hor ikAw ko khY ik AwiK vKwxY qU Awpy kImiq pwiedw ]1] (1061-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) hor ki-aa ko kahai ke aakh vakhaanai too aapay keemat paa-idaa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	What can anyone else say? What can anyone explain? Only You Yourself can estimate Your worth. ||1||
RECORD	para 46383	EAMkwir sB isRsit aupweI ] (1061-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) o-ankaar sabh sarisat upaa-ee. The One Universal Creator created the entire Universe.
DEFINE	para 46384	sBu Kylu qmwsw qyrI vifAweI ] (1061-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabh khayl tamaasaa tayree vadi-aa-ee. All the plays and dramas are to Your glory and greatness.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	Awpy vyk kry siB swcw Awpy BMin GVwiedw ]2] (1061-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay vayk karay sabh saachaa aapay bhann gharhaa-idaa. ||2||
