RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	By Guru's Grace, the Naam dwells deep within the heart, and one meditates upon the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||12||
RECORD	para 46517	nwvY no locY jyqI sB AweI ] (1064-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) naavai no lochai jaytee sabh aa-ee. Everyone who comes into the world, longs for the Name.
DEFINE	para 46518	nwau iqnw imlY Duir purib kmweI ] (1064-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) naa-o tinaa milai Dhur purab kamaa-ee. They alone are blessed with the Name, whose past actions were so ordained by the Primal Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	ijnI nwau pwieAw sy vfBwgI gur kY sbid imlwiedw ]13] (1064-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) jinee naa-o paa-i-aa say vadbhaagee gur kai sabad milaa-idaa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	Those who obtain the Name are very fortunate. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, they are united with God. ||13||
DEFINE	para 46520	kwieAw kotu Aiq Apwrw ] (1064-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kot at apaaraa. Utterly incomparable is the fortress of the body.
RECORD	para 46521	iqsu ivic bih pRBu kry vIcwrw ] (1064-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) tis vich bahi parabh karay veechaaraa. Within it, God sits in contemplation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	scw inAwau sco vwpwrw inhclu vwsw pwiedw ]14] (1064-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa ni-aa-o sacho vaapaaraa nihchal vaasaa paa-idaa. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	He administers true justice, and trades in Truth; through Him, one finds the eternal, unchanging dwelling. ||14||
DEFINE	para 46523	AMqr Gr bMky Qwnu suhwieAw ] (1064-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar ghar bankay thaan suhaa-i-aa. Deep within the inner self are glorious homes and beautiful places.
DEFINE	para 46524	gurmuiK ivrlY iknY Qwnu pwieAw ] (1064-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh virlai kinai thaan paa-i-aa. But rare is that person who, as Gurmukh, finds these places.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	iequ swiQ inbhY swlwhy scy hir scw mMin vswiedw ]15] (1064-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) it saath nibhai saalaahay sachay har sachaa man vasaa-idaa. ||15||
WHEN	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	If one stays in these places, and praises the True Lord, the True Lord comes to dwell in the mind. ||15||
RECORD	para 46526	myrY krqY iek bxq bxweI ] (1064-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) mayrai kartai ik banat banaa-ee. My Creator Lord has formed this formation.
RECORD	para 46527	iesu dyhI ivic sB vQu pweI ] (1064-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) is dayhee vich sabh vath paa-ee. He has placed everything within this body.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwmu vxjih rMig rwqy gurmuiK ko nwmu pwiedw ]16]6]20] (1064-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam vanjahi rang raatay gurmukh ko naam paa-idaa. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	O Nanak, those who deal in the Naam are imbued with His Love. The Gurmukh obtains the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||16||
RECORD	para 46530	kwieAw kMcnu sbdu vIcwrw ] (1064-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kanchan sabad veechaaraa. Contemplating the Word of the Shabad, the body becomes golden.
RECORD	para 46531	iqQY hir vsY ijs dw AMqu n pwrwvwrw ] (1064-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) tithai har vasai jis daa ant na paaraavaaraa. The Lord abides there; He has no end or limitation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Anidnu hir syivhu scI bwxI hir jIau sbid imlwiedw ]1] (1064-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din har sayvihu sachee banee har jee-o sabad milaa-idaa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Night and day, serve the Lord, and chant the True Word of the Guru's Bani. Through the Shabad, meet the Dear Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 46534	hir cyqih iqn bilhwrY jwau ] (1065-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) har cheeteh tin balihaarai jaa-o. I am a sacrifice to those who remember the Lord.
RECORD	para 46535	gur kY sbid iqn myil imlwau ] (1065-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad tin mayl milaa-o. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, I unite in Union with the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	iqn kI DUir lweI muiK msqik sqsMgiq bih gux gwiedw ]2] (1065-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) tin kee Dhoor laa-ee mukh mastak satsangat bahi gun gaa-idaa. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	I touch the dust of their feet to my face and forehead; sitting in the Society of the Saints, I sing His Glorious Praises. ||2||
RECORD	para 46537	hir ky gux gwvw jy hir pRB Bwvw ] (1065-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kay gun gaavaa jay har parabh bhaavaa. I sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, as I am pleasing to the Lord God.
RECORD	para 46538	AMqir hir nwmu sbid suhwvw ] (1065-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar har naam sabad suhaavaa. With the Lord's Name deep within my inner being, I am adorned with the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	gurbwxI chu kuMfI suxIAY swcY nwim smwiedw ]3] (1065-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurbaanee chahu kundee sunee-ai saachai naam samaa-idaa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	The Word of the Guru's Bani is heard throughout the four corners of the world; through it, we merge in the True Name. ||3||
RECORD	para 46540	so jnu swcw ij AMqru Bwly ] gur kY sbid hir ndir inhwly ] (1065-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) so jan saachaa je antar bhaalay. gur kai sabad har nadar nihaalay. That humble being, who searches within himself, through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, sees the Lord with his eyes.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	igAwn AMjnu pwey gur sbdI ndrI ndir imlwiedw ]4] (1065-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) gi-aan anjan paa-ay gur sabdee nadree nadar milaa-idaa. ||4||
UPHOLD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	Through the Guru's Shabad, he applies the ointment of spiritual wisdom to his eyes; the Gracious Lord, in His Grace, unites him with Himself. ||4||
RECORD	para 46542	vfY Bwig iehu srIru pwieAw ] (1065-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) vadai bhaag ih sareer paa-i-aa. By great good fortune, I obtained this body;
RECORD	para 46543	mwxs jnim sbid icqu lwieAw ] (1065-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) maanas janam sabad chit laa-i-aa. in this human life, I have focused my consciousness on the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	ibnu sbdY sBu AMD AMDyrw gurmuiK iksih buJwiedw ]5] (1065-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin sabdai sabh anDh anDhayraa gurmukh kiseh bujhaa-idaa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	Without the Shabad, everything is enveloped in utter darkness; only the Gurmukh understands. ||5||
RECORD	para 46545	ieik ikqu Awey jnmu gvwey ] (1065-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) ik kit aa-ay janam gavaa-ay. Some merely waste away their lives - why have they even come into the world?
DEFINE	para 46546	mnmuK lwgy dUjY Bwey ] (1065-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh laagay doojai bhaa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs are attached to the love of duality.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	eyh vylw iPir hwiQ n AwvY pig iKisAY pCuqwiedw ]6] (1065-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayh vaylaa fir haath na aavai pag khisi-ai pachhutaa-idaa. ||6||
FORBID	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	This opportunity shall not into their hands again; their foot slips, and they come to regret and repent. ||6||
DEFINE	para 46548	gur kY sbid pivqRü srIrw ] (1065-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad pavitar sareeraa. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the body is sanctified.
RECORD	para 46549	iqsu ivic vsY scu guxI ghIrw ] (1065-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) tis vich vasai sach gunee gaheeraa. The True Lord, the ocean of virtue, dwells within it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	sco scu vyKY sB QweI scu suix mMin vswiedw ]7] (1065-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) sacho sach vaykhai sabh thaa-ee sach sun man vasaa-idaa. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	One who sees the Truest of the True everywhere, hears the Truth, and enshrines it within his mind. ||7||
DEFINE	para 46551	haumY gxq gur sbid invwry ] (1065-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai ganat gur sabad nivaaray. Egotism and mental calculations are relieved through the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 46552	hir jIau ihrdY rKhu aur Dwry ] (1065-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) har jee-o hirdai rakhahu ur Dhaaray. Keep the Dear Lord close, and enshrine Him in your heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	gur kY sbid sdw swlwhy imil swcy suKu pwiedw ]8] (1065-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad sadaa saalaahay mil saachay sukh paa-idaa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	One who praises the Lord forever, through the Guru's Shabad, meets with the True Lord, and finds peace. ||8||
RECORD	para 46554	so cyqy ijsu Awip cyqwey ] (1065-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) so chaytay jis aap chaytaa-ay. He alone remembers the Lord, whom the Lord inspires to remember.
RECORD	para 46555	gur kY sbid vsY min Awey ] (1065-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad vasai man aa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, He comes to dwell in the mind.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Awpy vyKY Awpy bUJY AwpY Awpu smwiedw ]9] (1065-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay vaykhai aapay boojhai aapai aap samaa-idaa. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	He Himself sees, and He Himself understands; He merges all into Himself. ||9||
RECORD	para 46557	ijin mn ivic vQu pweI soeI jwxY ] (1065-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin man vich vath paa-ee so-ee jaanai. He alone knows, who has placed the object within his mind.
RECORD	para 46558	gur kY sbdy Awpu pCwxY ] (1065-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabday aap pachhaanai. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, he comes to understand himself.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	Awpu pCwxY soeI jnu inrmlu bwxI sbdu suxwiedw ]10] (1065-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) aap pachhaanai so-ee jan nirmal banee sabad sunaa-idaa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	That humble being who understands himself is immaculate. He proclaims the Guru's Bani, and the Word of the Shabad. ||10||
DEFINE	para 46560	eyh kwieAw pivqu hY srIru ] (1065-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayh kaa-i-aa pavit hai sareer. This body is sanctified and purified;
RECORD	para 46561	gur sbdI cyqY guxI ghIru ] (1065-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur sabdee chaytai gunee gaheer. through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, it contemplates the Lord, the ocean of virtue.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	Anidnu gux gwvY rMig rwqw gux kih guxI smwiedw ]11] (1065-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din gun gaavai rang raataa gun kahi gunee samaa-idaa. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	One who chants the Glorious Praises of the Lord night and day, and remains attuned to His Love, chants His Glorious Virtues, immersed in the Glorious Lord. ||11||
DEFINE	para 46563	eyhu srIru sB mUlu hY mwieAw ] (1065-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayhu sareer sabh mool hai maa-i-aa. This body is the source of all Maya;
DEFINE	para 46564	dUjY Bwie Brim BulwieAw ] (1065-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay bharam bhulaa-i-aa. in love with duality, it is deluded by doubt.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	hir n cyqY sdw duKu pwey ibnu hir cyqy duKu pwiedw ]12] (1065-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) har na chaytai sadaa dukh paa-ay bin har chaytay dukh paa-idaa. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	It does not remember the Lord, and suffers in eternal pain. Without remembering the Lord, it suffers in pain. ||12||
DEFINE	para 46566	ij siqguru syvy so prvwxu ] (1065-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) je satgur sayvay so parvaan. One who serves the True Guru is approved and respected.
DEFINE	para 46567	kwieAw hMsu inrmlu dir scY jwxu ] (1065-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa hans nirmal dar sachai jaan. His body and soul-swan are immaculate and pure; in the Court of the Lord, he is known to be true.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	hir syvy hir mMin vswey sohY hir gux gwiedw ]13] (1065-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) har sayvay har man vasaa-ay sohai har gun gaa-idaa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	He serves the Lord, and enshrines the Lord in his mind; he is exalted, singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||13||
RECORD	para 46569	ibnu Bwgw guru syivAw n jwie ] (1065-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin bhaagaa gur sayvi-aa na jaa-ay. Without good destiny, no one can serve the True Guru.
DEFINE	para 46570	mnmuK BUly muey ibllwie ] (1065-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh bhoolay mu-ay billaa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs are deluded, and die weeping and wailing.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	ijn kau ndir hovY gur kyrI hir jIau Awip imlwiedw ]14] (1065-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin ka-o nadar hovai gur kayree har jee-o aap milaa-idaa. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Those who are blessed by the Guru's Glance of Grace - the Dear Lord unites them with Himself. ||14||
DEFINE	para 46572	kwieAw kotu pky htnwly ] (1065-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa kot pakay hatnaalay. In the body fortress, are the solidly-constructed markets.
RECORD	para 46573	gurmuiK lyvY vsqu smwly ] (1065-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh layvai vasat samaalay. The Gurmukh purchases the object, and takes care of it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	hir kw nwmu iDAwie idnu rwqI aUqm pdvI pwiedw ]15] (1065-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kaa naam Dhi-aa-ay din raatee ootam padvee paa-idaa. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	Meditating on the Name of the Lord, day and night, he attains the sublime, exalted status. ||15||
DEFINE	para 46575	Awpy scw hY suKdwqw ] (1065-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay sachaa hai sukh-daata. The True Lord Himself is the Giver of peace.
DEFINE	para 46576	pUry gur kY sbid pCwqw ] (1065-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) pooray gur kai sabad pachhaataa. Through the Shabad of the Perfect Guru, He is realized.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwmu slwhy swcw pUrY Bwig ko pwiedw ]16]7]21] (1065-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam salaahay saachaa poorai bhaag ko paa-idaa. ||16||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	Nanak praises the Naam, the True Name of the Lord; through perfect destiny, He is found. ||16||
RECORD	para 46580	inrMkwir Awkwru aupwieAw ] (1066-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) nirankaar aakaar upaa-i-aa. The Formless Lord created the universe of form.
RECORD	para 46581	mwieAw mohu hukim bxwieAw ] (1066-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh hukam banaa-i-aa. By the Hukam of His Command, He created attachment to Maya.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	Awpy Kyl kry siB krqw suix swcw mMin vswiedw ]1] (1066-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay khayl karay sabh kartaa sun saachaa man vasaa-idaa. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	The Creator Himself stages all the plays; hearing of the True Lord, enshrine Him in your mind. ||1||
RECORD	para 46583	mwieAw mweI qRY gux prsUiq jmwieAw ] (1066-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa maa-ee tarai gun parsoot jamaa-i-aa. Maya, the mother, gave birth to the three gunas, the three qualities,
ALLOW	para 46584	cwry byd bRhmy no PurmwieAw ] (1066-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) chaaray bayd barahmay no furmaa-i-aa. and proclaimed the four Vedas to Brahma.
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	vrHy mwh vwr iQqI kir iesu jg mih soJI pwiedw ]2] (1066-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) var Hay maah vaar thitee kar is jag meh sojhee paa-idaa. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	Creating the years, months, days and dates, He infused intelligence into the world. ||2||
DEFINE	para 46586	gur syvw qy krxI swr ] (1066-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur sayvaa tay karnee saar. Service to the Guru is the most excellent action.
RECORD	para 46587	rwm nwmu rwKhu auir Dwr ] (1066-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) raam naam raakho ur Dhaar. Enshrine the Lord's Name within your heart.
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	gurbwxI vrqI jg AMqir iesu bwxI qy hir nwmu pwiedw ]3] (1066-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurbaanee vartee jag antar is banee tay har naam paa-idaa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	The Word of the Guru's Bani prevails throughout the world; through this Bani, the Lord's Name is obtained. ||3||
RECORD	para 46589	vydu pVY Anidnu vwd smwly ] (1066-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) vayd parhai an-din vaad samaalay. He reads the Vedas, but he starts arguments night and day.
DEFINE	para 46590	nwmu n cyqY bDw jmkwly ] (1066-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) naam na chaytai baDhaa jamkaalay. He does not remember the Naam, the Name of the Lord; he is bound and gagged by the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	dUjY Bwie sdw duKu pwey qRY gux Brim Bulwiedw ]4] (1066-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay sadaa dukh paa-ay tarai gun bharam bhulaa-idaa. ||4||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	In the love of duality, he suffers in pain forever; he is deluded by doubt, and confused by the three gunas. ||4||
DEFINE	para 46592	gurmuiK eyksu isau ilv lwey ] (1066-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh aykas si-o liv laa-ay. The Gurmukh is in love with the One Lord alone;
RECORD	para 46593	iqRibiD mnsw mnih smwey ] (1066-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) taribaDh mansaa maneh samaa-ay. he submerges in his mind the three-phased desire.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	swcY sbid sdw hY mukqw mwieAw mohu cukwiedw ]5] (1066-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) saachai sabad sadaa hai muktaa maa-i-aa moh chukaa-idaa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	Through the True Word of the Shabad, he is liberated forever; he renounces emotional attachment to Maya. ||5||
DEFINE	para 46595	jo Duir rwqy sy huix rwqy ] (1066-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo Dhur raatay say hun raatay. Those who are so pre-ordained to be imbued, are imbued with love for the Lord.
DEFINE	para 46596	gur prswdI shjy mwqy ] (1066-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee sehjay maatay. By Guru's Grace, they are intuitively intoxicated.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	siqguru syiv sdw pRBu pwieAw AwpY Awpu imlwiedw ]6] (1066-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayv sadaa parabh paa-i-aa aapai aap milaa-idaa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	Serving the True Guru forever, they find God; He Himself unites them with Himself. ||6||
DEFINE	para 46598	mwieAw moih Brim n pwey ] (1066-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi bharam na paa-ay. In attachment to Maya and doubt, the Lord is not found.
RECORD	para 46599	dUjY Bwie lgw duKu pwey ] (1066-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay lagaa dukh paa-ay. Attached to the love of duality, one suffers in pain.
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	sUhw rMgu idn QoVy hovY iesu jwdy iblm n lwiedw ]7] (1066-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) soohaa rang din thorhay hovai is jaaday bilam na laa-idaa. ||7||
