RECORD	para 46601	eyhu mnu BY Bwie rMgwey ] (1066-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayhu man bhai bhaa-ay rangaa-ay. So color this mind in the Fear and the Love of God.
RECORD	para 46602	iequ rMig swcy mwih smwey ] (1066-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) it rang saachay maahi samaa-ay. Dyed in this color, one merges in the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	pUrY Bwig ko iehu rMgu pwey gurmqI rMgu cVwiedw ]8] (1066-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorai bhaag ko ih rang paa-ay gurmatee rang charhaa-idaa. ||8||
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	By perfect destiny, some may obtain this color. Through the Guru's Teachings, this color is applied. ||8||
RECORD	para 46604	mnmuKu bhuqu kry AiBmwnu ] (1066-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh bahut karay abhimaan. The self-willed manmukhs take great pride in themselves.
DEFINE	para 46605	drgh kb hI n pwvY mwnu ] (1066-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) dargeh kab hee na paavai maan. In the Court of the Lord, they are never honored.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	dUjY lwgy jnmu gvwieAw ibnu bUJy duKu pwiedw ]9] (1066-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai laagay janam gavaa-i-aa bin boojhay dukh paa-idaa. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Attached to duality, they waste their lives; without understanding, they suffer in pain. ||9||
RECORD	para 46607	myrY pRiB AMdir Awpu lukwieAw ] (1066-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) mayrai parabh andar aap lukaa-i-aa. My God has hidden Himself deep within the self.
DEFINE	para 46608	gur prswdI hir imlY imlwieAw ] (1066-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee har milai milaa-i-aa. By Guru's Grace, one is united in the Lord's Union.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	scw pRBu scw vwpwrw nwmu Amolku pwiedw ]10] (1066-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa parabh sachaa vaapaaraa naam amolak paa-idaa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	God is True, and True is His trade, through which the priceless Naam is obtained. ||10||
RECORD	para 46610	iesu kwieAw kI kImiq iknY n pweI ] (1066-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) is kaa-i-aa kee keemat kinai na paa-ee. No one has found this body's value.
RECORD	para 46611	myrY Twkuir ieh bxq bxweI ] (1066-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) mayrai thaakur ih banat banaa-ee. My Lord and Master has worked His handiwork.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	gurmuiK hovY su kwieAw soDY Awpih Awpu imlwiedw ]11] (1066-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so kaa-i-aa soDhai aapeh aap milaa-idaa. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	One who becomes Gurmukh purifies his body, and then the Lord unites him with Himself. ||11||
RECORD	para 46613	kwieAw ivic qotw kwieAw ivic lwhw ] (1066-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa vich totaa kaa-i-aa vich laahaa. Within the body, one loses, and within the body, one wins.
RECORD	para 46614	gurmuiK Kojy vyprvwhw ] (1066-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh khojay vayparvaahaa. The Gurmukh seeks the self-sustaining Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	gurmuiK vxij sdw suKu pwey shjy shij imlwiedw ]12] (1066-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh vanaj sadaa sukh paa-ay sehjay sahj milaa-idaa. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	The Gurmukh trades, and finds peace forever; he intuitively merges in the Celestial Lord. ||12||
DEFINE	para 46616	scw mhlu scy BMfwrw ] (1066-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa mahal sachay bhandaaraa. True is the Lord's Mansion, and True is His treasure.
RECORD	para 46617	Awpy dyvY dyvxhwrw ] (1066-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay dayvai dayvanhaaraa. The Great Giver Himself gives.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	gurmuiK swlwhy suKdwqy min myly kImiq pwiedw ]13] (1066-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh saalaahay sukh-daatay man maylay keemat paa-idaa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	The Gurmukh praises the Giver of peace; his mind is united with the Lord, and he comes to know His worth. ||13||
DEFINE	para 46619	kwieAw ivic vsqu kImiq nhI pweI ] (1066-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa vich vasat keemat nahee paa-ee. Within the body is the object; its value cannot be estimated.
RECORD	para 46620	gurmuiK Awpy dy vifAweI ] (1066-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh aapay day vadi-aa-ee. He Himself grants glorious greatness to the Gurmukh.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	ijs dw htu soeI vQu jwxY gurmuiK dyie n pCoqwiedw ]14] (1066-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis daa hat so-ee vath jaanai gurmukh day-ay na pachhotaa-idaa. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	He alone knows this object, to whom this store belongs; the Gurmukh is blessed with it, and does not come to regret. ||14||
DEFINE	para 46622	hir jIau sB mih rihAw smweI ] (1066-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) har jee-o sabh meh rahi-aa samaa-ee. The Dear Lord is pervading and permeating all.
DEFINE	para 46623	gur prswdI pwieAw jweI ] (1066-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee paa-i-aa jaa-ee. By Guru's Grace, He is found.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	Awpy myil imlwey Awpy sbdy shij smwiedw ]15] (1066-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay mayl milaa-ay aapay sabday sahj samaa-idaa. ||15||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	He Himself unites in His Union; through the Word of the Shabad, one intuitively merges with Him. ||15||
RECORD	para 46626	Awpy scw sbid imlwey ] (1067-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay sachaa sabad milaa-ay. The True Lord Himself unites us in the Word of His Shabad.
DEFINE	para 46627	sbdy ivchu Brmu cukwey ] (1067-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabday vichahu bharam chukaa-ay. Within the Shabad, doubt is driven out.
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwim imlY vifAweI nwmy hI suKu pwiedw ]16]8]22] (1067-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam milai vadi-aa-ee naamay hee sukh paa-idaa. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	O Nanak, He blesses us with His Naam, and throgh the Naam, peace is found. ||16||
DEFINE	para 46630	Agm Agocr vyprvwhy ] (1067-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) agam agochar vayparvaahay. He is inaccessible, unfathomable and self-sustaining.
DEFINE	para 46631	Awpy imhrvwn Agm AQwhy ] (1067-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay miharvaan agam athaahay. He Himself is merciful, inaccessible and unlimited.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	ApiV koie n skY iqs no gur sbdI mylwieAw ]1] (1067-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aparh ko-ay na sakai tis no gur sabdee maylaa-i-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	No one can reach up to Him; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, He is met. ||1||
RECORD	para 46633	quDuno syvih jo quDu Bwvih ] (1067-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) tuDhuno sayveh jo tuDh bhaaveh. He alone serves You, who pleases You.
RECORD	para 46634	gur kY sbdy sic smwvih ] (1067-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabday sach samaaveh. Through the Guru's Shabad, he merges in the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	Anidnu gux rvih idnu rwqI rsnw hir rsu BwieAw ]2] (1067-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din gun raveh din raatee rasnaa har ras bhaa-i-aa. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	Night and day, he chants the Lord's Praises, day and night; his tongue savors and delights in the sublime essence of the Lord. ||2||
DEFINE	para 46636	sbid mrih sy mrxu svwrih ] (1067-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabad mareh say maran savaareh. Those who die in the Shabad - their death is exalted and glorified.
RECORD	para 46637	hir ky gux ihrdY aur Dwrih ] (1067-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kay gun hirdai ur Dhaareh. They enshrine the Lord's Glories in their hearts.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	jnmu sPlu hir crxI lwgy dUjw Bwau cukwieAw ]3] (1067-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) janam safal har charnee laagay doojaa bhaa-o chukaa-i-aa. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	Holding tight to the Guru's feet, their lives becomes prosperous, and they are rid of the love of duality. ||3||
RECORD	para 46639	hir jIau myly Awip imlwey ] (1067-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) har jee-o maylay aap milaa-ay. The Dear Lord unites them in Union with Himself.
DEFINE	para 46640	gur kY sbdy Awpu gvwey ] (1067-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabday aap gavaa-ay. Through the Guru's Shabad, self-conceit is dispelled.
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	Anidnu sdw hir BgqI rwqy iesu jg mih lwhw pwieAw ]4] (1067-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din sadaa har bhagtee raatay is jag meh laahaa paa-i-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	Those who remain attuned to devotional worship to the Lord, night and day, earn the profit in this world. ||4||
RECORD	para 46642	qyry gux khw mY khxu n jweI ] (1067-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) tayray gun kahaa mai kahan na jaa-ee. What Glorious Virtues of Yours should I describe? I cannot describe them.
RECORD	para 46643	AMqu n pwrw kImiq nhI pweI ] (1067-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) ant na paaraa keemat nahee paa-ee. You have no end or limitation. Your value cannot be estimated.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	Awpy dieAw kry suKdwqw gux mih guxI smwieAw ]5] (1067-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay da-i-aa karay sukh-daata gun meh gunee samaa-i-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	When the Giver of peace Himself bestows His Mercy, the virtuous are absorbed in virtue. ||5||
DEFINE	para 46645	iesu jg mih mohu hY pwswrw ] (1067-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) is jag meh moh hai paasaaraa. In this world, emotional attachment is spread all over.
DEFINE	para 46646	mnmuKu AigAwnI AMDu AMDwrw ] (1067-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh agi-aanee anDh anDhaaraa. The ignorant, self-willed manmukh is immersed in utter darkness.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	DMDY Dwvqu jnmu gvwieAw ibnu nwvY duKu pwieAw ]6] (1067-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) DhanDhai Dhaavat janam gavaa-i-aa bin naavai dukh paa-i-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	Chasing after worldly affairs, he wastes away his life in vain; without the Name, he suffers in pain. ||6||
WHEN	para 46648	krmu hovY qw siqguru pwey ] (1067-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) karam hovai taa satgur paa-ay. If God grants His Grace, then one finds the True Guru.
DEFINE	para 46649	haumY mYlu sbid jlwey ] (1067-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai mail sabad jalaa-ay. Through the Shabad, the filth of egotism is burned away.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	mnu inrmlu igAwnu rqnu cwnxu AigAwnu AMDyru gvwieAw ]7] (1067-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) man nirmal gi-aan ratan chaanan agi-aan anDhayr gavaa-i-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	The mind becomes immaculate, and the jewel of spiritual wisdom brings enlightenment; the darkness of spiritual ignorance is dispelled. ||7||
DEFINE	para 46651	qyry nwm Anyk kImiq nhI pweI ] (1067-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) tayray naam anayk keemat nahee paa-ee. Your Names are countless; Your value cannot be estimated.
RECORD	para 46652	scu nwmu hir ihrdY vsweI ] (1067-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) sach naam har hirdai vasaa-ee. I enshrine the Lord's True Name within my heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	kImiq kauxu kry pRB qyrI qU Awpy shij smwieAw ]8] (1067-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) keemat ka-un karay parabh tayree too aapay sahj samaa-i-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Who can estimate Your value, God? You are immersed and absorbed in Yourself. ||8||
DEFINE	para 46654	nwmu Amolku Agm Apwrw ] (1067-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) naam amolak agam apaaraa. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is priceless, inaccessible and infinite.
RECORD	para 46655	nw ko hoAw qolxhwrw ] (1067-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) naa ko ho-aa tolanhaaraa. No one can weigh it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Awpy qoly qoil qolwey gur sbdI myil qolwieAw ]9] (1067-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay tolay tol tolaa-ay gur sabdee mayl tolaa-i-aa. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	You Yourself weigh, and estimate all; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, You unite, when the weight is perfect. ||9||
RECORD	para 46657	syvk syvih krih Ardwis ] (1067-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) sayvak sayveh karahi ardaas. Your servant serves, and offers this prayer.
RECORD	para 46658	qU Awpy myil bhwlih pwis ] (1067-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) too aapay mayl bahaaleh paas. Please, let me sit near You, and unite me with Yourself.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	sBnw jIAw kw suKdwqw pUrY krim iDAwieAw ]10] (1067-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabhnaa jee-aa kaa sukh-daata poorai karam Dhi-aa-i-aa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	You are the Giver of peace to all beings; by perfect karma, we meditate on You. ||10||
RECORD	para 46660	jqu squ sMjmu ij scu kmwvY ] (1067-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) jat sat sanjam je sach kamaavai. Chastity, truth and self-control come by practicing and living the Truth.
RECORD	para 46661	iehu mnu inrmlu ij hir gux gwvY ] (1067-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) ih man nirmal je har gun gaavai. This mind becomes immaculate and pure, singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	iesu ibKu mih AMimRqu prwpiq hovY hir jIau myry BwieAw ]11] (1067-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) is bikh meh amrit paraapat hovai har jee-o mayray bhaa-i-aa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	In this world of poison, the Ambrosial Nectar is obtained, if it pleases my Dear Lord. ||11||
RECORD	para 46663	ijs no buJwey soeI bUJY ] (1067-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) jis no bujhaa-ay so-ee boojhai. He alone understands, whom God inspires to understand.
DEFINE	para 46664	hir gux gwvY AMdru sUJY ] (1067-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) har gun gaavai andar soojhai. Singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, one's inner being is awakened.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	haumY myrw Twik rhwey shjy hI scu pwieAw ]12] (1067-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai mayraa thaak rahaa-ay sehjay hee sach paa-i-aa. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	Egotism and possessiveness are silenced and subdued, and one intuitively finds the True Lord. ||12||
RECORD	para 46666	ibnu krmw hor iPrY GnyrI ] (1067-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin karmaa hor firai ghanayree. Without good karma, countless others wander around.
RECORD	para 46667	mir mir jMmY cukY n PyrI ] (1067-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) mar mar jammai chukai na fayree. They die, and die again, only to be reborn; they cannot escape the cycle of reincarnation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	ibKu kw rwqw ibKu kmwvY suKu n kbhU pwieAw ]13] (1067-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) bikh kaa raataa bikh kamaavai sukh na kabhoo paa-i-aa. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	Imbued with poison, they practice poison and corruption, and they never find peace. ||13||
RECORD	para 46669	bhuqy ByK kry ByKDwrI ] (1067-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) bahutay bhaykh karay bhaykh-Dhaaree. Many disguise themselves with religious robes.
RECORD	para 46670	ibnu sbdY haumY iknY n mwrI ] (1067-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin sabdai ha-umai kinai na maaree. Without the Shabad, no one has conquered egotism.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	jIvqu mrY qw mukiq pwey scY nwie smwieAw ]14] (1067-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) jeevat marai taa mukat paa-ay sachai naa-ay samaa-i-aa. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	One who remains dead while yet alive is liberated, and merges in the True Name. ||14||
DEFINE	para 46672	AigAwnu iqRsnw iesu qnih jlwey ] (1067-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) agi-aan tarisnaa is taneh jalaa-ay. Spiritual ignorance and desire burn this human body.
RECORD	para 46674	iqs dI bUJY ij gur sbdu kmwey ] (1068-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) tis dee boojhai je gur sabad kamaa-ay. He alone puts out this fire, who practices and lives the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	qnu mnu sIqlu k®oDu invwry haumY mwir smwieAw ]15] (1068-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) tan man seetal kroDh nivaaray ha-umai maar samaa-i-aa. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	His body and mind are cooled and soothed, and his anger is silenced; conquering egotism, he merges in the Lord. ||15||
DEFINE	para 46676	scw swihbu scI vifAweI ] (1068-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachaa saahib sachee vadi-aa-ee. True is the Lord and Master, and True is His glorious greatness.
RECORD	para 46677	gur prswdI ivrlY pweI ] (1068-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee virlai paa-ee. By Guru's Grace, a rare few attain this.
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnku eyk khY bynµqI nwmy nwim smwieAw ]16]1]23] (1068-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak ayk kahai baynantee naamay naam samaa-i-aa. ||16||
ALLOW	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	Nanak offers this one prayer: through the Naam, the Name of the Lord, may I merge in the Lord. ||16||
RECORD	para 46680	ndrI Bgqw lYhu imlwey ] (1068-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) nadree bhagtaa laihu milaa-ay. By Your Grace, please unite with Your devotees.
RECORD	para 46681	Bgq slwhin sdw ilv lwey ] (1068-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) bhagat salaahan sadaa liv laa-ay. Your devotees ever praise You, lovingly focusing on You.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	qau srxweI aubrih krqy Awpy myil imlwieAw ]1] (1068-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) ta-o sarnaa-ee ubrahi kartay aapay mayl milaa-i-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v1	In Your Sanctuary, they are saved, O Creator Lord; You unite them in Union with Yourself. ||1||
DEFINE	para 46683	pUrY sbid Bgiq suhweI ] (1068-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) poorai sabad bhagat suhaa-ee. Sublime and exalted is devotion to the Perfect Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 46684	AMqir suKu qyrY min BweI ] (1068-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar sukh tayrai man bhaa-ee. Peace prevails within; they are pleasing to Your Mind.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	mnu qnu scI BgqI rwqw scy isau icqu lwieAw ]2] (1068-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) man tan sachee bhagtee raataa sachay si-o chit laa-i-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v2	One whose mind and body are imbued with true devotion, focuses his consciousness on the True Lord. ||2||
DEFINE	para 46686	haumY ivic sd jlY srIrw ] (1068-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) ha-umai vich sad jalai sareeraa. In egotism, the body is forever burning.
WHEN	para 46687	krmu hovY Byty guru pUrw ] (1068-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) karam hovai bhaytay gur pooraa. When God grants His Grace, one meets the Perfect Guru.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	AMqir AigAwnu sbid buJwey siqgur qy suKu pwieAw ]3] (1068-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar agi-aan sabad bujhaa-ay satgur tay sukh paa-i-aa. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v3	The Shabad dispels the spiritual ignorance within, and through the True Guru, one finds peace. ||3||
RECORD	para 46689	mnmuKu AMDw AMDu kmwey ] (1068-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh anDhaa anDh kamaa-ay. The blind, self-willed manmukh acts blindly.
DEFINE	para 46690	bhu sMkt jonI Brmwey ] (1068-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) baho sankat jonee bharmaa-ay. He is in terrible trouble, and wanders in reincarnation.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	jm kw jyvVw kdy n kwtY AMqy bhu duKu pwieAw ]4] (1068-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) jam kaa jayvrhaa kaday na kaatai antay baho dukh paa-i-aa. ||4||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v4	He can never snap the noose of Death, and in the end, he suffers in horrible pain. ||4||
DEFINE	para 46692	Awvx jwxw sbid invwry ] (1068-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) aavan jaanaa sabad nivaaray. Through the Shabad, one's comings and goings in reincarnation are ended.
RECORD	para 46693	scu nwmu rKY aur Dwry ] (1068-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) sach naam rakhai ur Dhaaray. He keeps the True Name enshrined within his heart.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	gur kY sbid mrY mnu mwry haumY jwie smwieAw ]5] (1068-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad marai man maaray ha-umai jaa-ay samaa-i-aa. ||5||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v5	He dies in the Word of the Guru's Shabad, and conquers his mind; stilling his egotism, he merges in the Lord. ||5||
DEFINE	para 46695	Awvx jwxY prj ivgoeI ] (1068-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) aavan jaanai paraj vigo-ee. Coming and going, the people of the world are wasting away.
RECORD	para 46696	ibnu siqgur iQru koie n hoeI ] (1068-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin satgur thir ko-ay na ho-ee. Without the True Guru, no one finds permanence and stability.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	AMqir joiq sbid suKu visAw joqI joiq imlwieAw ]6] (1068-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar jot sabad sukh vasi-aa jotee jot milaa-i-aa. ||6||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v6	The Shabad shines its Light deep within the self, and one dwells in peace; one's light merges into the Light. ||6||
RECORD	para 46698	pMc dUq icqvih ivkwrw ] (1068-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) panch doot chitvahi vikaaraa. The five demons think of evil and corruption.
DEFINE	para 46699	mwieAw moh kw eyhu pswrw ] (1068-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh kaa ayhu pasaaraa. The expanse is the manifestation of emotional attachment to Maya.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	siqguru syvy qw mukqu hovY pMc dUq vis AwieAw ]7] (1068-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay taa mukat hovai panch doot vas aa-i-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v7	Serving the True Guru, one is liberated, and the five demons are put under his control. ||7||
DEFINE	para 46701	bwJu gurU hY mohu gubwrw ] (1068-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) baajh guroo hai moh gubaaraa. Without the Guru, there is only the darkness of attachment.
DEFINE	para 46702	iPir iPir fubY vwro vwrw ] (1068-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) fir fir dubai vaaro vaaraa. Over and over, time and time again, they are drowned.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	siqgur Byty scu idRVwey scu nwmu min BwieAw ]8] (1068-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur bhaytay sach drirh-aa-ay sach naam man bhaa-i-aa. ||8||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v8	Meeting the True Guru, Truth is implanted within, and the True Name becomes pleasing to the mind. ||8||
DEFINE	para 46704	swcw dru swcw drvwrw ] (1068-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) saachaa dar saachaa darvaaraa. True is His Door, and True is His Court, His Royal Darbaar.
RECORD	para 46705	scy syvih sbid ipAwrw ] (1068-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachay sayveh sabad pi-aaraa. The true ones serve Him, through the Beloved Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	scI Duin scy gux gwvw scy mwih smwieAw ]9] (1068-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachee Dhun sachay gun gaavaa sachay maahi samaa-i-aa. ||9||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v9	Singing the Glorious Praises of the True Lord, in the true melody, I am immersed and absorbed in Truth. ||9||
RECORD	para 46707	GrY AMdir ko Gru pwey ] (1068-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) gharai andar ko ghar paa-ay. Deep within the home of the self, one finds the home of the Lord.
RECORD	para 46708	gur kY sbdy shij suBwey ] (1068-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabday sahj subhaa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, one easily, intuitively finds it.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	EQY sogu ivjogu n ivAwpY shjy shij smwieAw ]10] (1068-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) othai sog vijog na vi-aapai sehjay sahj samaa-i-aa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v10	There, one is not afflicted with sorrow or separation; merge into the Celestial Lord with intuitive ease. ||10||
RECORD	para 46710	dUjY Bwie dustw kw vwsw ] (1068-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay dustaa kaa vaasaa. The evil people live in the love of duality.
RECORD	para 46711	Baudy iPrih bhu moh ipAwsw ] (1068-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) bha-uday fireh baho moh pi-aasaa. They wander around, totally attached and thirsty.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	kusMgiq bhih sdw duKu pwvih duKo duKu kmwieAw ]11] (1068-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) kusangat baheh sadaa dukh paavahi dukho dukh kamaa-i-aa. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v11	They sit in evil gatherings, and suffer in pain forever; they earn pain, nothing but pain. ||11||
DEFINE	para 46713	siqgur bwJhu sMgiq n hoeI ] (1068-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur baajhahu sangat na ho-ee. Without the True Guru, there is no Sangat, no Congregation.
RECORD	para 46714	ibnu sbdy pwru n pwey koeI ] (1068-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin sabday paar na paa-ay ko-ee. Without the Shabad, no one can cross over to the other side.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	shjy gux rvih idnu rwqI joqI joiq imlwieAw ]12] (1068-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) sehjay gun raveh din raatee jotee jot milaa-i-aa. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v12	One who intuitively chants God's Glorious Praises day and night - his light merges into the Light. ||12||
DEFINE	para 46716	kwieAw ibrKu pMKI ivic vwsw ] (1068-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa birakh pankhee vich vaasaa. The body is the tree; the bird of the soul dwells within it.
RECORD	para 46717	AMimRqu cugih gur sbid invwsw ] (1068-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) amrit chugeh gur sabad nivaasaa. It drinks in the Ambrosial Nectar, resting in the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	aufih n mUly n Awvih n jwhI inj Gir vwsw pwieAw ]13] (1068-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) udeh na moolay na aavahi na jaahee nij ghar vaasaa paa-i-aa. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v13	It never flies away, and it does not come or go; it dwells within the home of its own self. ||13||
RECORD	para 46719	kwieAw soDih sbdu vIcwrih ] (1068-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaa-i-aa soDheh sabad vichaareh. Purify the body, and contemplate the Shabad.
RECORD	para 46720	moh TgaurI Brmu invwrih ] (1068-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) moh thag-uree bharam nivaareh. Remove the poisonous drug of emotional attachment, and eradicate doubt.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	Awpy ik®pw kry suKdwqw Awpy myil imlwieAw ]14] (1068-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kirpaa karay sukh-daata aapay mayl milaa-i-aa. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v14	The Giver of peace Himself bestows His Mercy, and unites us in Union with Himself. ||14||
DEFINE	para 46723	sd hI nyVY dUir n jwxhu ] (1069-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) sad hee nayrhai door na jaanhu. He is always near at hand; He is never far away.
DEFINE	para 46724	gur kY sbid njIik pCwxhu ] (1069-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur kai sabad najeek pachhaanhu. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, realize that He is very near.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	ibgsY kmlu ikrix prgwsY prgtu kir dyKwieAw ]15] (1069-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) bigsai kamal kiran pargaasai pargat kar daykhaa-i-aa. ||15||
REQUIRE	mwrU mhlw 3 v15	Your heart-lotus shall blossom forth, and the ray of God's Divine Light shall illuminate your heart; He shall be revealed to You. ||15||
DEFINE	para 46726	Awpy krqw scw soeI ] (1069-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kartaa sachaa so-ee. The True Lord is Himself the Creator.
DEFINE	para 46727	Awpy mwir jIvwly Avru n koeI ] (1069-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay maar jeevaalay avar na ko-ee. He Himself kills, and gives life; there is no other at all.
RECORD	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	nwnk nwmu imlY vifAweI Awpu gvwie suKu pwieAw ]16]2]24] (1069-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam milai vadi-aa-ee aap gavaa-ay sukh paa-i-aa. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU mhlw 3 v16	O Nanak, through the Naam, the Name of the Lord, glorious greatness is obtained. Eradicating self-conceit, peace is found. ||16||
