DEFINE	para 47028	kljug mih kIrqnu prDwnw ] (1075-19, mwrU, mÚ 5) kaljug meh keertan parDhaanaa. In this Dark Age of Kali Yuga, the Kirtan of the Lord's Praises are most sublime and exalted.
RECORD	para 47029	gurmuiK jpIAY lwie iDAwnw ] (1075-19, mwrU, mÚ 5) gurmukh japee-ai laa-ay Dhi-aanaa. Become Gurmukh, chant and focus your meditation.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v6	Awip qrY sgly kul qwry hir drgh piq isau jwiedw ]6] (1076-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) aap tarai saglay kul taaray har dargeh pat si-o jaa-idaa. ||6||
REQUIRE	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v6	You shall save yourself, and save all your generations as well. You shall go to the Court of the Lord with honor. ||6||
RECORD	para 47032	KMf pqwl dIp siB loAw ] (1076-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) khand pataal deep sabh lo-aa. All the continents, nether worlds, islands and worlds
RECORD	para 47033	siB kwlY vis Awip pRiB kIAw ] (1076-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) sabh kaalai vas aap parabh kee-aa. - God Himself has made them all subject to death.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v7	inhclu eyku Awip AibnwsI so inhclu jo iqsih iDAwiedw ]7] (1076-2, mwrU, mÚ 5) nihchal ayk aap abhinaasee so nihchal jo tiseh Dhi-aa-idaa. ||7||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v7	The One Imperishable Lord Himself is unmoving and unchanging. Meditating on Him, one becomes unchanging. ||7||
RECORD	para 47035	hir kw syvku so hir jyhw ] (1076-3, mwrU, mÚ 5) har kaa sayvak so har jayhaa. The Lord's servant becomes like the Lord.
DEFINE	para 47036	Bydu n jwxhu mwxs dyhw ] (1076-3, mwrU, mÚ 5) bhayd na jaanhu maanas dayhaa. Do not think that, because of his human body, he is different.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v8	ijau jl qrMg auTih bhu BwqI iPir sllY sll smwiedw ]8] (1076-3, mwrU, mÚ 5) ji-o jal tarang utheh baho bhaatee fir sallai salal samaa-idaa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v8	The waves of the water rise up in various ways, and then the water merges again in water. ||8||
RECORD	para 47038	ieku jwicku mMgY dwnu duAwrY ] (1076-4, mwrU, mÚ 5) ik jaachik mangai daan du-aarai. A beggar begs for charity at His Door.
