RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v9	dyhu drsu ijqu mnu iqRpqwsY hir kIrqin mnu Thrwiedw ]9] (1076-5, mwrU, mÚ 5) dayh daras jit man tariptaasai har keertan man thehraa-idaa. ||9||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v9	Please bless me with the Blessed Vision of Your Darshan, to satisfy my mind, O Lord. Through the Kirtan of Your Praises, my mind is held steady. ||9||
DEFINE	para 47041	rUVo Twkuru ikqY vis n AwvY ] (1076-5, mwrU, mÚ 5) roorho thaakur kitai vas na aavai. The Beauteous Lord and Master is not controlled in any way.
RECORD	para 47042	hir so ikCu kry ij hir ikAw sMqw BwvY ] (1076-6, mwrU, mÚ 5) har so kichh karay je har ki-aa santaa bhaavai. The Lord does that which pleases the Saints of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v10	kIqw loVin soeI krwiein dir Pyru n koeI pwiedw ]10] (1076-6, mwrU, mÚ 5) keetaa lorhan so-ee karaa-in dar fayr na ko-ee paa-idaa. ||10||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v10	He does whatever they wish to be done; nothing blocks their way at His Door. ||10||
DEFINE	para 47044	ijQY AauGtu Awie bnqu hY pRwxI ] (1076-7, mwrU, mÚ 5) jithai a-ughat aa-ay banat hai paraanee. Wherever the mortal is confronted with difficulty,
RECORD	para 47045	iqQY hir iDAweIAY swirMgpwxI ] (1076-7, mwrU, mÚ 5) tithai har Dhi-aa-ee-ai saaringpaanee. there he should meditate on the Lord of the Universe.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v11	ijQY puqRü klqRü n bylI koeI iqQY hir Awip Cfwiedw ]11] (1076-8, mwrU, mÚ 5) jithai putar kalatar na baylee ko-ee tithai har aap chhadaa-idaa. ||11||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v11	Where there are no children, spouse or friends, there the Lord Himself comes to the rescue. ||11||
DEFINE	para 47047	vfw swihbu Agm AQwhw ] (1076-8, mwrU, mÚ 5) vadaa saahib agam athaahaa. The Great Lord and Master is inaccessible and unfathomable.
RECORD	para 47048	ikau imlIAY pRB vyprvwhw ] (1076-9, mwrU, mÚ 5) ki-o milee-ai parabh vayparvaahaa. How can anyone meet with God, the self-suficient One?
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v12	kwit islk ijsu mwrig pwey so ivic sMgiq vwsw pwiedw ]12] (1076-9, mwrU, mÚ 5) kaat silak jis maarag paa-ay so vich sangat vaasaa paa-idaa. ||12||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v12	Those who have had the noose cut away from around their necks, whom God has set back upon the Path, obtain a place in the Sangat, the Congregation. ||12||
DEFINE	para 47050	hukmu bUJY so syvku khIAY ] (1076-10, mwrU, mÚ 5) hukam boojhai so sayvak kahee-ai. One who realizes the Hukam of the Lord's Command is said to be His servant.
RECORD	para 47051	burw Blw duie smsir shIAY ] (1076-10, mwrU, mÚ 5) buraa bhalaa du-ay samsar sahee-ai. He endures both bad and good equally.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v13	haumY jwie q eyko bUJY so gurmuiK shij smwiedw ]13] (1076-10, mwrU, mÚ 5) ha-umai jaa-ay ta ayko boojhai so gurmukh sahj samaa-idaa. ||13||
DEFINE	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v13	When egotism is silenced, then one comes to know the One Lord. Such a Gurmukh intuitively merges in the Lord. ||13||
RECORD	para 47053	hir ky Bgq sdw suKvwsI ] (1076-11, mwrU, mÚ 5) har kay bhagat sadaa sukhvaasee. The devotees of the Lord dwell forever in peace.
RECORD	para 47054	bwl suBwie AqIq audwsI ] (1076-11, mwrU, mÚ 5) baal subhaa-ay ateet udaasee. With a child-like, innocent nature, they remain detached, turning away from the world.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v14	Aink rMg krih bhu BwqI ijau ipqw pUqu lwfwiedw ]14] (1076-12, mwrU, mÚ 5) anik rang karahi baho bhaatee ji-o pitaa poot laadaa-idaa. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v14	They enjoy various pleasures in many ways; God caresses them, like a father caressing his son. ||14||
DEFINE	para 47056	Agm Agocru kImiq nhI pweI ] (1076-12, mwrU, mÚ 5) agam agochar keemat nahee paa-ee. He is inaccessible and unfathomable; His value cannot be estimated.
WHEN	para 47057	qw imlIAY jw ley imlweI ] (1076-13, mwrU, mÚ 5) taa milee-ai jaa la-ay milaa-ee. We meet Him, only when He causes us to meet.
RECORD	mwrU solhy mhlw 5 v15	gurmuiK pRgtu BieAw iqn jn kau ijn Duir msqik lyKu ilKwiedw ]15] (1076-13, mwrU, mÚ 5) gurmukh pargat bha-i-aa tin jan ka-o jin Dhur mastak laykh likhaa-idaa. ||15||
