DEFINE	para 47598	gur kI bwxI inrmlI hir rsu pIAwieAw ] (1088-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) gur kee banee nirmalee har ras pee-aa-i-aa. The Word of the Guru's Bani is immaculate and pure; through it, one drinks in the sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	para 47599	hir rsu ijnI cwiKAw An rs Twik rhwieAw ] (1088-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) har ras jinee chaakhi-aa an ras thaak rahaa-i-aa. Those who taste the sublime essence of the Lord, forsake other flavors.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v5	hir rsu pI sdw iqRpiq Bey iPir iqRsnw BuK gvwieAw ]5] (1088-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) har ras pee sadaa taripat bha-ay fir tarisnaa bhukh gavaa-i-aa. ||5||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v5	Drinking in the sublime essence of the Lord, they remain satisfied forever; their hunger and thirst are quenched. ||5||
RECORD	para 47601	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1088-12) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47602	ipr KusIey Dn rwvIey Dn auir nwmu sIgwru ] (1088-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) pir khusee-ay Dhan raavee-ay Dhan ur naam seegaar. Her Husband Lord is pleased, and He enjoys His bride; the soul-bride adorns her heart with the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk Dn AwgY KVI soBwvMqI nwir ]1] (1088-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak Dhan aagai kharhee sobhaavantee naar. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, that bride who stands before Him, is the most noble and respected woman. ||1||
RECORD	para 47604	mÚ 1 ] (1088-13) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 47605	ssurY pyeIAY kMq kI kMqu AgMmu AQwhu ] (1088-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) sasurai pay-ee-ai kant kee kant agamm athaahu. In her father-in-law's home hereafter, and in her parents' home in this world, she belongs to her Husband Lord. Her Husband is inaccessible and unfathomable.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk DMnu suohwgxI jo Bwvih vyprvwh ]2] (1088-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak Dhan sohaaganee jo bhaaveh vayparvaah. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, she is the happy soul-bride, who is pleasing to her carefree, independent Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 47607	pauVI ] (1088-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47608	qKiq rwjw so bhY ij qKqY lwiek hoeI ] (1088-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) takhat raajaa so bahai je takh-tai laa-ik ho-ee. That king sits upon the throne, who is worthy of that throne.
DEFINE	para 47609	ijnI scu pCwixAw scu rwjy syeI ] (1088-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) jinee sach pachhaani-aa sach raajay say-ee. Those who realize the True Lord, they alone are the true kings.
DEFINE	para 47610	eyih BUpiq rwjy n AwKIAih dUjY Bwie duKu hoeI ] (1088-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) ayhi bhoopat raajay na aakhee-ahi doojai bhaa-ay dukh ho-ee. These mere earthly rulers are not called kings; in the love of duality, they suffer.
DEFINE	para 47611	kIqw ikAw swlwhIAY ijsu jwdy iblm n hoeI ] (1088-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) keetaa ki-aa salaahee-ai jis jaaday bilam na ho-ee. Why should someone praise someone else who is also created? They depart in no time at all.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v6	inhclu scw eyku hY gurmuiK bUJY su inhclu hoeI ]6] (1088-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) nihchal sachaa ayk hai gurmukh boojhai so nihchal ho-ee. ||6||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v6	The One True Lord is eternal and imperishable. One who, as Gurmukh, understands becomes eternal as well. ||6||
RECORD	para 47613	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1088-17) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47614	sBnw kw ipru eyku hY ipr ibnu KwlI nwih ] (1088-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabhnaa kaa pir ayk hai pir bin khaalee naahi. The One Lord is the Husband of all. No one is without the Husband Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk sy sohwgxI ij siqgur mwih smwih ]1] (1088-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak say sohaaganee je satgur maahi samaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, they are the pure soul-brides, who merge in the True Guru. ||1||
RECORD	para 47616	mÚ 3 ] (1088-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47617	mn ky AiDk qrMg ikau dir swihb CutIAY ] (1088-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) man kay aDhik tarang ki-o dar saahib chhutee-ai. The mind is churning with so many waves of desire. How can one be emancipated in the Court of the Lord?
RECORD	para 47618	jy rwcY sc rMig gUVY rMig Apwr kY ] (1088-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) jay raachai sach rang goorhai rang apaar kai. Be absorbed in the Lord's True Love, and imbued with the deep color of the Lord's Infinite Love.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk gur prswdI CutIAY jy icqu lgY sic ]2] (1088-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak gur parsaadee chhutee-ai jay chit lagai sach. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, by Guru's Grace, one is emancipated, if the consciousness is attached to the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 47620	pauVI ] (1088-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47621	hir kw nwmu Amolu hY ikau kImiq kIjY ] (1088-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kaa naam amol hai ki-o keemat keejai. The Name of the Lord is priceless. How can its value be estimated?
DEFINE	para 47623	Awpy isRsit sB swjIAnu Awpy vrqIjY ] (1089-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay sarisat sabh saajee-an aapay varteejai. He Himself created the entire universe, and He Himself is pervading it.
RECORD	para 47624	gurmuiK sdw slwhIAY scu kImiq kIjY ] (1089-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sadaa salaahee-ai sach keemat keejai. The Gurmukhs praise the Lord forever, and through the Truth, they assess Him.
RECORD	para 47625	gur sbdI kmlu ibgwisAw iev hir rsu pIjY ] (1089-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur sabdee kamal bigaasi-aa iv har ras peejai. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the heart-lotus blossoms forth, and in this way, one drinks in the sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v7	Awvx jwxw TwikAw suiK shij svIjY ]7] (1089-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) aavan jaanaa thaaki-aa sukh sahj saveejai. ||7||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v7	Coming and going in reincarnation ceases, and one sleeps in peace and poise. ||7||
RECORD	para 47627	sloku mÚ 1 ] (1089-3) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 47628	nw mYlw nw DuMDlw nw Bgvw nw kcu ] (1089-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) naa mailaa naa DhunDhlaa naa bhagvaa naa kach. Neither dirty, nor dull, nor saffron, nor any color that fades.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk lwlo lwlu hY scY rqw scu ]1] (1089-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak laalo laal hai sachai rataa sach. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, crimson - deep crimson is the color of one who is imbued with the True Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 47630	mÚ 3 ] (1089-4) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
WHEN	para 47631	shij vxspiq Pulu Plu Bvru vsY BY KMif ] (1089-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) sahj vanaspat ful fal bhavar vasai bhai khand. The bumble bee intuitively and fearlessly dwells among the vegetation, flowers and fruits.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk qrvru eyku hY eyko Pulu iBrMgu ]2] (1089-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak tarvar ayk hai ayko ful bhirang. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, there is only one tree, one flower, and one bumble bee. ||2||
RECORD	para 47633	pauVI ] (1089-5) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47634	jo jn lUJih mnY isau sy sUry prDwnw ] (1089-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo jan loojheh manai si-o say sooray parDhaanaa. Those humble beings who struggle with their minds are brave and distinguished heroes.
RECORD	para 47635	hir syqI sdw imil rhy ijnI Awpu pCwnw ] (1089-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) har saytee sadaa mil rahay jinee aap pachhaanaa. Those who realize their own selves, remain forever united with the Lord.
DEFINE	para 47636	igAwnIAw kw iehu mhqu hY mn mwih smwnw ] (1089-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) gi-aanee-aa kaa ih mahat hai man maahi samaanaa. This is the glory of the spiritual teachers, that they remain absorbed in their mind.
RECORD	para 47637	hir jIau kw mhlu pwieAw scu lwie iDAwnw ] (1089-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) har jee-o kaa mahal paa-i-aa sach laa-ay Dhi-aanaa. They attain the Mansion of the Lord's Presence, and focus their meditation on the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v8	ijn gur prswdI mnu jIiqAw jgu iqnih ijqwnw ]8] (1089-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin gur parsaadee man jeeti-aa jag tineh jitaanaa. ||8||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v8	Those who conquer their own minds, by Guru's Grace, conquer the world. ||8||
RECORD	para 47639	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1089-7) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
WHEN	para 47640	jogI hovw jig Bvw Gir Gir BIiKAw lyau ] (1089-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) jogee hovaa jag bhavaa ghar ghar bheekhi-aa lay-o. If I were to become a Yogi, and wander around the world, begging from door to door,
WHEN	para 47641	drgh lyKw mMgIAY iksu iksu auqru dyau ] (1089-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) dargeh laykhaa mangee-ai kis kis utar day-o. then, when I am summoned to the Court of the Lord, what answer could I give?
RECORD	para 47642	iBiKAw nwmu sMqoKu mVI sdw scu hY nwil ] (1089-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) bhikhi-aa naam santokh marhee sadaa sach hai naal. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is the charity I beg for; contentment is my temple. The True Lord is always with me.
DEFINE	para 47643	ByKI hwQ n lDIAw sB bDI jmkwil ] (1089-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) bhaykhee haath na laDhee-aa sabh baDhee jamkaal. Nothing is obtained by wearing religious robes; all will be seized by the Messenger of Death.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk glw JUTIAw scw nwmu smwil ]1] (1089-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak galaa jhoothee-aa sachaa naam samaal. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, talk is false; contemplate the True Name. ||1||
RECORD	para 47645	mÚ 3 ] (1089-10) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47646	ijqu dir lyKw mMgIAY so dru syivhu n koie ] (1089-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) jit dar laykhaa mangee-ai so dar sayvihu na ko-ay. Through that door, you will be called to account; do not serve at that door.
RECORD	para 47647	AYsw siqguru loiV lhu ijsu jyvfu Avru n koie ] (1089-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) aisaa satgur lorh lahu jis jayvad avar na ko-ay. Seek and find such a True Guru, who has no equal in His greatness.
DEFINE	para 47648	iqsu srxweI CUtIAY lyKw mMgY n koie ] (1089-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) tis sarnaa-ee chhootee-ai laykhaa mangai na ko-ay. In His Sanctuary, one is released, and no one calls him to account.
RECORD	para 47649	scu idRVwey scu idRVu scw Ehu sbdu dyie ] (1089-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) sach drirh-aa-ay sach darirh sachaa oh sabad day-ay. Truth is implanted within Him, and He implants Truth within others. He bestows the blessing of the True Shabad.
DEFINE	para 47650	ihrdY ijs dY scu hY qnu mnu BI scw hoie ] (1089-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) hirdai jis dai sach hai tan man bhee sachaa ho-ay. One who has Truth within his heart - his body and mind are also true.
WHEN	para 47651	nwnk scY hukim mMinAY scI vifAweI dyie ] (1089-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak sachai hukam mani-ai sachee vadi-aa-ee day-ay. O Nanak, if one submits to the Hukam, the Command of the True Lord God, he is blessed with true glory and greatness.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	scy mwih smwvsI ijs no ndir kryie ]2] (1089-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) sachay maahi samaavasee jis no nadar karay-i. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	He is immersed and merged in the True Lord, who blesses him with His Glance of Grace. ||2||
RECORD	para 47653	pauVI ] (1089-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47654	sUry eyih n AwKIAih AhMkwir mrih duKu pwvih ] (1089-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) sooray ayhi na aakhee-ahi aha Nkaar mareh dukh paavahi. They are not called heroes, who die of egotism, suffering in pain.
RECORD	para 47655	AMDy Awpu n pCwxnI dUjY pic jwvih ] (1089-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) anDhay aap na pachhaannee doojai pach jaaveh. The blind ones do not realize their own selves; in the love of duality, they rot.
RECORD	para 47656	Aiq kroD isau lUJdy AgY ipCY duKu pwvih ] (1089-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) at karoDh si-o loojh-day agai pichhai dukh paavahi. They struggle with great anger; here and hereafter, they suffer in pain.
DEFINE	para 47657	hir jIau AhMkwru n BwveI vyd kUik suxwvih ] (1089-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) har jee-o aha Nkaar na bhaav-ee vayd kook sunaaveh. The Dear Lord is not pleased by egotism; the Vedas proclaim this clearly.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v9	AhMkwir muey sy ivgqI gey mir jnmih iPir Awvih ]9] (1089-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) aha Nkaar mu-ay say vigtee ga-ay mar janmeh fir aavahi. ||9||
FORBID	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v9	Those who die of egotism, shall not find salvation. They die, and are reborn in reincarnation. ||9||
RECORD	para 47659	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1089-16) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47660	kwgau hoie n aUjlw lohy nwv n pwru ] (1089-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) kaaga-o ho-ay na oojlaa lohay naav na paar. The crow does not become white, and an iron boat does not float across.
DEFINE	para 47661	iprm pdwrQu mMin lY DMnu svwrxhwru ] (1089-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) piram padaarath man lai Dhan savaaranhaar. One who puts his faith in the treasure of his Beloved Lord is blessed; he exalts and embellishes others as well.
RECORD	para 47662	hukmu pCwxY aUjlw isir kwst lohw pwir ] (1089-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) hukam pachhaanai oojlaa sir kaasat lohaa paar. One who realizes the Hukam of God's Command - his face is radiant and bright; he floats across, like iron upon wood.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	iqRsnw CofY BY vsY nwnk krxI swru ]1] (1089-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) tarisnaa chhodai bhai vasai naanak karnee saar. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	Forsake thirst and desire, and abide in the Fear of God; O Nanak, these are the most excellent actions. ||1||
RECORD	para 47664	mÚ 3 ] (1089-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47665	mwrU mwrx jo gey mwir n skih gvwr ] (1089-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) maaroo maaran jo ga-ay maar na sakahi gavaar. The ignorant people who go to the desert to conquer their minds, are not able to conquer them.
REQUIRE	para 47666	nwnk jy iehu mwrIAY gur sbdI vIcwir ] (1089-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak jay ih maaree-ai gur sabdee veechaar. O Nanak, if this mind is to be conquered, one must contemplate the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
DEFINE	para 47667	eyhu mnu mwirAw nw mrY jy locY sBu koie ] (1089-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayhu man maari-aa naa marai jay lochai sabh ko-ay. This mind is not conquered by conquering it, even though everyone longs to do so.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk mn hI kau mnu mwrsI jy siqguru BytY soie ]2] (1089-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak man hee ka-o man maarsee jay satgur bhaytai so-ay. ||2||
WHEN	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, the mind itself conquers the mind, if one meets with the True Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 47670	pauVI ] (1090-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 47671	dovY qrPw aupweIEnu ivic skiq isv vwsw ] (1090-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) dovai tarfaa opaa-ee-on vich sakat siv vaasaa. He created both sides; Shiva dwells within Shakti (the soul dwells within the material universe).
RECORD	para 47672	skqI iknY n pwieE iPir jnim ibnwsw ] (1090-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) saktee kinai na paa-i-o fir janam binaasaa. Through the material universe of Shakti, no one has ever found the Lord; they continue to be born and die in reincarnation.
DEFINE	para 47673	guir syivAY swiq pweIAY jip sws igrwsw ] (1090-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur sayvi-ai saat paa-ee-ai jap saas giraasaa. Serving the Guru, peace is found, meditating on the Lord with every breath and morsel of food.
RECORD	para 47674	isimRiq swsq soiD dyKu aUqm hir dwsw ] (1090-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) simrit saasat soDh daykh ootam har daasaa. Searching and looking through the Simritees and the Shaastras, I have found that the most sublime person is the slave of the Lord.
ALLOW	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v10	nwnk nwm ibnw ko iQru nhI nwmy bil jwsw ]10] (1090-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam binaa ko thir nahee naamay bal jaasaa. ||10||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v10	O Nanak, without the Naam, nothing is permanent and stable; I am a sacrifice to the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||10||
RECORD	para 47676	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1090-3) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47677	hovw pMifqu joqkI vyd pVw muiK cwir ] (1090-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) hovaa pandit jotkee vayd parhaa mukh chaar. I might become a Pandit, a religious scholar, or an astrologer, and recite the four Vedas with my mouth;
UPHOLD	para 47678	nv KMf mDy pUjIAw ApxY cij vIcwir ] (1090-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) nav khand maDhay poojee-aa apnai chaj veechaar. I might be worshipped throughout the nine regions of the earth for my wisdom and thought;
RECORD	para 47679	mqu scw AKru Buil jwie caukY iBtY n koie ] (1090-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) mat sachaa akhar bhul jaa-ay cha-ukai bhitai na ko-ay. let me not forget the Word of Truth, that no one can touch my sacred cooking square.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	JUTy cauky nwnkw scw eyko soie ]1] (1090-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) jhoothay cha-ukay naankaa sachaa ayko so-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	Such cooking squares are false, O Nanak; only the One Lord is True. ||1||
RECORD	para 47681	mÚ 3 ] (1090-5) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47682	Awip aupwey kry Awip Awpy ndir kryie ] (1090-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) aap upaa-ay karay aap aapay nadar karay-i. He Himself creates and He Himself acts; He bestows His Glance of Grace.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	Awpy dy vifAweIAw khu nwnk scw soie ]2] (1090-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay day vadi-aa-ee-aa kaho naanak sachaa so-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	He Himself grants glorious greatness; says Nanak, He is the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 47684	pauVI ] (1090-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47685	kMtku kwlu eyku hY horu kMtku n sUJY ] (1090-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) kantak kaal ayk hai hor kantak na soojhai. Only death is painful; I cannot conceive of anything else as painful.
DEFINE	para 47686	APirE jg mih vrqdw pwpI isau lUJY ] (1090-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) afri-o jag meh varatdaa paapee si-o loojhai. It is unstoppable; it stalks and pervades the world, and fights with the sinners.
RECORD	para 47687	gur sbdI hir BydIAY hir jip hir bUJY ] (1090-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur sabdee har bhaydee-ai har jap har boojhai. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, one is immersed in the Lord. Meditating on the Lord, one comes to realize the Lord.
DEFINE	para 47688	so hir srxweI CutIAY jo mn isau jUJY ] (1090-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) so har sarnaa-ee chhutee-ai jo man si-o joojhai. He alone is emancipated in the Sanctuary of the Lord, who struggles with his own mind.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v11	min vIcwir hir jpu kry hir drgh sIJY ]11] (1090-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) man veechaar har jap karay har dargeh seejhai. ||11||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v11	One who contemplates and meditates on the Lord in his mind, succeeds in the Court of the Lord. ||11||
RECORD	para 47690	sloku mÚ 1 ] (1090-9) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47691	hukim rjweI swKqI drgh scu kbUlu ] (1090-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) hukam rajaa-ee saakh-tee dargeh sach kabool. Submit to the Will of the Lord Commander; in His Court, only Truth is accepted.
REQUIRE	para 47692	swihbu lyKw mMgsI dunIAw dyiK n BUlu ] (1090-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) saahib laykhaa mangsee dunee-aa daykh na bhool. Your Lord and Master shall call you to account; do not go astray on beholding the world.
DEFINE	para 47693	idl drvwnI jo kry drvysI idlu rwis ] (1090-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) dil darvaanee jo karay darvaysee dil raas. One who keeps watch over his heart, and keeps his heart pure, is a dervish, a saintly devotee.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	iesk muhbiq nwnkw lyKw krqy pwis ]1] (1090-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) isak muhabat naankaa laykhaa kartay paas. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	Love and affection, O Nanak, are in the accounts placed before the Creator. ||1||
RECORD	para 47695	mÚ 1 ] (1090-10) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47696	Algau joie mDUkVau swrMgpwix sbwie ] (1090-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) alga-o jo-ay maDhookarha-o sarangpaan sabaa-ay. One who is unattached like the bumble bee, sees the Lord of the world everywhere.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	hIrY hIrw byiDAw nwnk kMiT suBwie ]2] (1090-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) heerai heeraa bayDhi-aa naanak kanth subhaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	The diamond of his mind is pierced through with the Diamond of the Lord's Name; O Nanak, his neck is embellished with it. ||2||
RECORD	para 47698	pauVI ] (1090-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47699	mnmuK kwlu ivAwpdw moih mwieAw lwgy ] (1090-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) manmukh kaal vi-aapdaa mohi maa-i-aa laagay. The self-willed manmukhs are afflicted by death; they cling to Maya in emotional attachment.
DEFINE	para 47700	iKn mih mwir pCwVsI Bwie dUjY Twgy ] (1090-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) khin meh maar pachhaarhsee bhaa-ay doojai thaagay. In an instant, they are thrown to the ground and killed; in the love of duality, they are deluded.
FORBID	para 47701	iPir vylw hiQ n AwveI jm kw fMfu lwgy ] (1090-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) fir vaylaa hath na aavee jam kaa dand laagay. This opportunity shall not come into their hands again; they are beaten by the Messenger of Death with his stick.
RECORD	para 47702	iqn jm fMfu n lgeI jo hir ilv jwgy ] (1090-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) tin jam dand na lag-ee jo har liv jaagay. But Death's stick does not even strike those who remain awake and aware in the Love of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v12	sB qyrI quDu CfwvxI sB quDY lwgy ]12] (1090-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) sabh tayree tuDh chhadaavanee sabh tuDhai laagay. ||12||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v12	All are Yours, and cling to You; only You can save them. ||12||
RECORD	para 47704	sloku mÚ 1 ] (1090-14) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 47705	srby joie AgCmI dUKu Gnyro AwiQ ] (1090-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) sarbay jo-ay agachhmee dookh ghanayro aath. See the imperishable Lord everywhere; attachment to wealth brings only great pain.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	kwlru lwdis sru lwGxau lwBu n pUMjI swiQ ]1] (1090-14, mwrU, mÚ 1) kaalar laadas sar laaghana-o laabh na poonjee saath. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	Loaded with dust, you have to cross over the world-ocean; you are not carrying the profit and capital of the Name with you. ||1||
RECORD	para 47707	mÚ 1 ] (1090-15) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47708	pUMjI swcau nwmu qU AKutau drbu Apwru ] (1090-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) poonjee saacha-o naam too akhuta-o darab apaar. My capital is Your True Name, O Lord; this wealth is inexhaustible and infinite.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk vKru inrmlau DMnu swhu vwpwru ]2] (1090-15, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak vakhar nirmalo Dhan saahu vaapaar. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, this merchandise is immaculate; blessed is the banker who trades in it. ||2||
RECORD	para 47710	mÚ 1 ] (1090-16) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 47711	pUrb pRIiq iprwix lY motau Twkuru mwix ] (1090-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) poorab pareet piraan lai mota-o thaakur maan. Know and enjoy the primal, eternal Love of the Great Lord and Master.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v3	mwQY aUBY jmu mwrsI nwnk mylxu nwim ]3] (1090-16, mwrU, mÚ 1) maathai oobhai jam maarsee naanak maylan naam. ||3||
REQUIRE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v3	Blessed with the Naam, O Nanak, you shall strike down the Messenger of Death, and push his face to the ground. ||3||
RECORD	para 47713	pauVI ] (1090-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 47714	Awpy ipMfu svwirEnu ivic nv iniD nwmu ] (1090-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) aapay pind savaari-on vich nav niDh naam. He Himself has embellished the body, and placed the nine treasures of the Naam within it.
DEFINE	para 47715	ieik Awpy Brim BulwieAnu iqn inhPl kwmu ] (1090-17, mwrU, mÚ 1) ik aapay bharam bhulaa-i-an tin nihfal kaam. He confuses some in doubt; fruitless are their actions.
RECORD	para 47716	ieknI gurmuiK buiJAw hir Awqm rwmu ] (1090-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) iknee gurmukh bujhi-aa har aatam raam. Some, as Gurmukh, realize their Lord, the Supreme Soul.
DEFINE	para 47717	ieknI suix kY mMinAw hir aUqm kwmu ] (1090-18, mwrU, mÚ 1) iknee sun kai mani-aa har ootam kaam. Some listen to the Lord, and obey Him; sublime and exalted are their actions.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v13	AMqir hir rMgu aupijAw gwieAw hir gux nwmu ]13] (1090-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) antar har rang upji-aa gaa-i-aa har gun naam. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v13	Love for the Lord wells up deep within, singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord's Name. ||13||
RECORD	para 47719	sloku mÚ 1 ] (1090-19) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47721	Bolqix BY min vsY hykY pwDr hIfu ] (1091-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) bhogtan bhai man vasai haykai paaDhar heed. The Fear of God abides in the mind of the innocent; this is the straight path to the One Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	Aiq fwhpix duKu Gxo qIny Qwv BrIfu ]1] (1091-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) at daahpan dukh ghano teenay thaav bhareed. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	Jealousy and envy bring terrible pain, and one is cursed throughout the three worlds. ||1||
RECORD	para 47723	mÚ 1 ] (1091-1) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47724	mWdlu byid is bwjxo Gxo DVIAY joie ] (1091-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) maaNdal bayd se baajno ghano Dharhee-ai jo-ay. The drum of the Vedas vibrates, bringing dispute and divisiveness.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk nwmu smwil qU bIjau Avru n koie ]2] (1091-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak naam samaal too beeja-o avar na ko-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, contemplate the Naam, the Name of the Lord; there is none except Him. ||2||
RECORD	para 47726	mÚ 1 ] (1091-2) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47727	swgru guxI AQwhu ikin hwQwlw dyKIAY ] (1091-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) saagar gunee athaahu kin haathaalaa daykhee-ai. The world-ocean of the three qualities is unfathomably deep; how can its bottom be seen?
WHEN	para 47728	vfw vyprvwhu siqguru imlY q pwir pvw ] (1091-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) vadaa vayparvaahu satgur milai ta paar pavaa. If I meet with the great, self-sufficient True Guru, then I am carried across.
DEFINE	para 47729	mJ Bir duK bduK ] (1091-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) majh bhar dukh badukh. This ocean is filled up with pain and suffering.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v3	nwnk scy nwm ibnu iksY n lQI BuK ]3] (1091-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak sachay naam bin kisai na lathee bhukh. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v3	O Nanak, without the True Name, no one's hunger is appeased. ||3||
RECORD	para 47731	pauVI ] (1091-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 47732	ijnI AMdru BwilAw gur sbid suhwvY ] (1091-4, mwrU, mÚ 1) jinee andar bhaali-aa gur sabad suhaavai. Those who search their inner beings, through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, are exalted and adorned.
RECORD	para 47733	jo ieCin so pwiedy hir nwmu iDAwvY ] (1091-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) jo ichhan so paa-iday har naam Dhi-aavai. They obtain what they wish for, meditating on the Lord's Name.
UPHOLD	para 47734	ijs no ik®pw kry iqsu guru imlY so hir gux gwvY ] (1091-5, mwrU, mÚ 1) jis no kirpaa karay tis gur milai so har gun gaavai. One who is blessed by God's Grace, meets with the Guru; he sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 47735	Drm rwie iqn kw imqu hY jm mig n pwvY ] (1091-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) Dharam raa-ay tin kaa mit hai jam mag na paavai. The Righteous Judge of Dharma is his friend; he does not have to walk on the Path of Death.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v14	hir nwmu iDAwvih idnsu rwiq hir nwim smwvY ]14] (1091-6, mwrU, mÚ 1) har naam Dhi-aavahi dinas raat har naam samaavai. ||14||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v14	He meditates on the Lord's Name, day and night; he is absorbed and immersed in the Lord's Name. ||14||
RECORD	para 47737	sloku mÚ 1 ] (1091-7) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 47738	suxIAY eyku vKwxIAY surig imriq pieAwil ] (1091-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) sunee-ai ayk vakhaanee-ai surag mirat pa-i-aal. Listen to and speak the Name of the One Lord, who permeates the heavens, this world and the nether regions of the underworld.
REQUIRE	para 47739	hukmu n jweI myitAw jo iliKAw so nwil ] (1091-7, mwrU, mÚ 1) hukam na jaa-ee mayti-aa jo likhi-aa so naal. The Hukam of His Command cannot be erased; whatever He has written, shall go with the mortal.
RECORD	para 47740	kauxu mUAw kauxu mwrsI kauxu AwvY kauxu jwie ] (1091-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) ka-un moo-aa ka-un maarsee ka-un aavai ka-un jaa-ay. Who has died, and who kills? Who comes and who goes?
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	kauxu rhsI nwnkw iks kI suriq smwie ]1] (1091-8, mwrU, mÚ 1) ka-un rahsee naankaa kis kee surat samaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	Who is enraptured, O Nanak, and whose consciousness merges in the Lord? ||1||
RECORD	para 47742	mÚ 1 ] (1091-9) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 47743	hau muAw mY mwirAw pauxu vhY drIAwau ] (1091-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-o mu-aa mai maari-aa pa-un vahai daree-aa-o. In egotism, he dies; possessiveness kills him, and the breath flows out like a river.
DEFINE	para 47744	iqRsnw QkI nwnkw jw mnu rqw nwie ] (1091-9, mwrU, mÚ 1) tarisnaa thakee naankaa jaa man rataa naa-ay. Desire is exhausted, O Nanak, only when the mind is imbued with the Name.
DEFINE	para 47745	loiex rqy loiexI kMnI suriq smwie ] (1091-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) lo-in ratay lo-inee kannee surat samaa-ay. His eyes are imbued with the eyes of the Lord, and his ears ring with celestial consciousness.
RECORD	para 47746	jIB rswieix cUnVI rqI lwl lvwie ] (1091-10, mwrU, mÚ 1) jeebh rasaa-in choonrhee ratee laal lavaa-ay. His tongue drinks in the sweet nectar, dyed crimson by chanting the Name of the Beloved Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	AMdru musik JkoilAw kImiq khI n jwie ]2] (1091-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) andar musak jhakoli-aa keemat kahee na jaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	His inner being is drenched with the Lord's fragrance; his worth cannot be described. ||2||
RECORD	para 47748	pauVI ] (1091-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47749	iesu jug mih nwmu inDwnu hY nwmo nwil clY ] (1091-11, mwrU, mÚ 1) is jug meh naam niDhaan hai naamo naal chalai. In this age, the Naam, the Name of the Lord, is the treasure. Only the Naam goes along in the end.
ALLOW	para 47750	eyhu AKutu kdy n inKuteI Kwie Kricau plY ] (1091-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) ayhu akhut kaday na nikhuta-ee khaa-ay kharchi-o palai. It is inexhaustible; it is never empty, no matter how much one may eat, consume or spend.
RECORD	para 47751	hir jn nyiV n AwveI jmkMkr jmklY ] (1091-12, mwrU, mÚ 1) har jan nayrh na aavee jamkankar jamkalai. The Messenger of Death does not even approach the humble servant of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 47752	sy swh scy vxjwirAw ijn hir Dnu plY ] (1091-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) say saah sachay vanjaari-aa jin har Dhan palai. They alone are the true bankers and traders, who have the wealth of the Lord in their laps.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v15	hir ikrpw qy hir pweIAY jw Awip hir GlY ]15] (1091-13, mwrU, mÚ 1) har kirpaa tay har paa-ee-ai jaa aap har ghalai. ||15||
WHEN	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v15	By the Lord's Mercy, one finds the Lord, only when the Lord Himself sends for him. ||15||
RECORD	para 47754	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1091-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47755	mnmuK vwpwrY swr n jwxnI ibKu ivhwJih ibKu sMgRhih ibK isau Drih ipAwru ] (1091-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh vaapaarai saar na jaannee bikh vihaajheh bikh sangar-hahi bikh si-o Dhareh pi-aar. The self-willed manmukh does not appreciate the excellence of trading in Truth. He deals in poison, collects poison, and is in love with poison.
RECORD	para 47756	bwhrhu pMifq sdwiedy mnhu mUrK gwvwr ] (1091-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) baahrahu pandit sadaa-iday manhu moorakh gaavaar. Outwardly, they call themselves Pandits, religious scholars, but in their minds they are foolish and ignorant.
RECORD	para 47757	hir isau icqu n lwienI vwdI Drin ipAwru ] (1091-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) har si-o chit na laa-inee vaadee Dharan pi-aar. They do not focus their consciousness on the Lord; they love to engage in arguments.
RECORD	para 47758	vwdw kIAw krin khwxIAw kUVu boil krih Awhwru ] (1091-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) vaadaa kee-aa karan kahaanee-aa koorh bol karahi aahaar. They speak to cause arguments, and earn their living by telling lies.
RECORD	para 47759	jg mih rwm nwmu hir inrmlw horu mYlw sBu Awkwru ] (1091-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) jag meh raam naam har nirmalaa hor mailaa sabh aakaar. In this world, only the Lord's Name is immaculate and pure. All other objects of creation are polluted.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk nwmu n cyqnI hoie mYly mrih gvwr ]1] (1091-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam na chaytnee ho-ay mailay mareh gavaar. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, those who do not remember the Naam, the Name of the Lord, are polluted; they die in ignorance. ||1||
RECORD	para 47761	mÚ 3 ] (1091-17) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47762	duKu lgw ibnu syivAY hukmu mMny duKu jwie ] (1091-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) dukh lagaa bin sayvi-ai hukam mannay dukh jaa-ay. Without serving the Lord, he suffers in pain; accepting the Hukam of God's Command, pain is gone.
DEFINE	para 47763	Awpy dwqw suKY dw Awpy dyie sjwie ] (1091-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay daataa sukhai daa aapay day-ay sajaa-ay. He Himself is the Giver of peace; He Himself awards punishment.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk eyvY jwxIAY sBu ikCu iqsY rjwie ]2] (1091-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak ayvai jaanee-ai sabh kichh tisai rajaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, know this well; all that happens is according to His Will. ||2||
RECORD	para 47765	pauVI ] (1091-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47766	hir nwm ibnw jgqu hY inrDnu ibnu nwvY iqRpiq nwhI ] (1091-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) har naam binaa jagat hai nirDhan bin naavai taripat naahee. Without the Lord's Name, the world is poor. Without the Name, no one is satisfied.
DEFINE	para 47767	dUjY Brim BulwieAw haumY duKu pwhI ] (1091-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) doojai bharam bhulaa-i-aa ha-umai dukh paahee. He is deluded by duality and doubt. In egotism, he suffers in pain.
ALLOW	para 47769	ibnu krmw ikCU n pweIAY jy bhuqu locwhI ] (1092-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin karmaa kichhoo na paa-ee-ai jay bahut lochaahee. Without good karma, he does not obtain anything, no matter how much he may wish for it.
DEFINE	para 47770	AwvY jwie jMmY mrY gur sbid CutwhI ] (1092-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) aavai jaa-ay jammai marai gur sabad chhutaahee. Coming and going in reincarnation, and birth and death are ended, through the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v16	Awip krY iksu AwKIAY dUjw ko nwhI ]16] (1092-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) aap karai kis aakhee-ai doojaa ko naahee. ||16||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v16	He Himself acts, so unto whom should we complain? There is no other at all. ||16||
RECORD	para 47772	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1092-2) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47773	iesu jg mih sMqI Dnu KitAw ijnw siqguru imilAw pRBu Awie ] (1092-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) is jag meh santee Dhan khati-aa jinaa satgur mili-aa parabh aa-ay. In this world, the Saints earn the wealth; they come to meet God through the True Guru.
RECORD	para 47774	siqguir scu idRVwieAw iesu Dn kI kImiq khI n jwie ] (1092-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) satgur sach drirh-aa-i-aa is Dhan kee keemat kahee na jaa-ay. The True Guru implants the Truth within; the value of this wealth cannot be described.
DEFINE	para 47775	iequ Din pwieAY BuK lQI suKu visAw min Awie ] (1092-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) it Dhan paa-i-ai bhukh lathee sukh vasi-aa man aa-ay. Obtaining this wealth, hunger is relieved, and peace comes to dwell in the mind.
RECORD	para 47776	ijMn@w kau Duir iliKAw iqnI pwieAw Awie ] (1092-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin Haa ka-o Dhur likhi-aa tinee paa-i-aa aa-ay. Only those who have such pre-ordained destiny, come to receive this.
DEFINE	para 47777	mnmuKu jgqu inrDnu hY mwieAw no ibllwie ] (1092-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh jagat nirDhan hai maa-i-aa no billaa-ay. The world of the self-willed manmukh is poor, crying out for Maya.
DEFINE	para 47778	Anidnu iPrdw sdw rhY BuK n kdy jwie ] (1092-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) an-din firdaa sadaa rahai bhukh na kaday jaa-ay. Night and day, it wanders continually, and its hunger is never relieved.
RECORD	para 47779	sWiq n kdy AwveI nh suKu vsY min Awie ] (1092-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) saaNt na kaday aavee nah sukh vasai man aa-ay. It never finds calm tranquility, and peace never comes to dwell in its mind.
DEFINE	para 47780	sdw icMq icqvdw rhY shsw kdy n jwie ] (1092-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) sadaa chint chitvadaa rahai sahsaa kaday na jaa-ay. It is always plagued by anxiety, and its cynicism never departs.
WHEN	para 47781	nwnk ivxu siqgur miq BvI siqgur no imlY qw sbdu kmwie ] (1092-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak vin satgur mat bhavee satgur no milai taa sabad kamaa-ay. O Nanak, without the True Guru, the intellect is perverted; if one meets the True Guru, then one practices the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	sdw sdw suK mih rhY scy mwih smwie ]1] (1092-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa sukh meh rahai sachay maahi samaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	Forever and ever, he dwells in peace, and merges in the True Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 47783	mÚ 3 ] (1092-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47784	ijin aupweI mydnI soeI swr kryie ] (1092-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin upaa-ee maydnee so-ee saar karay-i. The One who created the world, takes care of it.
DEFINE	para 47785	eyko ismrhu Bwierhu iqsu ibnu Avru n koie ] (1092-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) ayko simrahu bhaa-irahu tis bin avar na ko-ay. Meditate in remembrance on the One Lord, O Siblings of Destiny; there is none other than Him.
REQUIRE	para 47786	Kwxw sbdu cMigAweIAw ijqu KwDY sdw iqRpiq hoie ] (1092-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) khaanaa sabad chang-aa-ee-aa jit khaaDhai sadaa taripat ho-ay. So eat the food of the Shabad and goodness; eating it, you shall remain satisfied forever.
RECORD	para 47787	pYnxu isPiq snwie hY sdw sdw Ehu aUjlw mYlw kdy n hoie ] (1092-9, mwrU, mÚ 3) painan sifat sanaa-ay hai sadaa sadaa oh oojlaa mailaa kaday na ho-ay. Dress yourself in the Praise of the Lord. Forever and ever, it is radiant and bright; it is never polluted.
RECORD	para 47788	shjy scu Dnu KitAw QoVw kdy n hoie ] (1092-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) sehjay sach Dhan khati-aa thorhaa kaday na ho-ay. I have intuitively earned the true wealth, which never decreases.
DEFINE	para 47789	dyhI no sbdu sIgwru hY ijqu sdw sdw suKu hoie ] (1092-10, mwrU, mÚ 3) dayhee no sabad seegaar hai jit sadaa sadaa sukh ho-ay. The body is adorned with the Shabad, and is at peace forever and ever.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk gurmuiK buJIAY ijs no Awip ivKwly soie ]2] (1092-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh bujhee-ai jis no aap vikhaalay so-ay. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukh realizes the Lord, who reveals Himself. ||2||
RECORD	para 47791	pauVI ] (1092-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47792	AMqir jpu qpu sMjmo gur sbdI jwpY ] (1092-11, mwrU, mÚ 3) antar jap tap sanjamo gur sabdee jaapai. Deep within the self are meditation and austere self-discipline, when one realizes the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
DEFINE	para 47793	hir hir nwmu iDAweIAY haumY AigAwnu gvwpY ] (1092-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) har har naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai ha-umai agi-aan gavaapai. Meditating on the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, egotism and ignorance are eliminated.
DEFINE	para 47794	AMdru AMimRiq BrpUru hY cwiKAw swdu jwpY ] (1092-12, mwrU, mÚ 3) andar amrit bharpoor hai chaakhi-aa saad jaapai. One's inner being is overflowing with Ambrosial Nectar; tasting it, the flavor is known.
DEFINE	para 47795	ijn cwiKAw sy inrBau Bey sy hir ris DRwpY ] (1092-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin chaakhi-aa say nirbha-o bha-ay say har ras Dharaapai. Those who taste it become fearless; they are satisfied with the sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v17	hir ikrpw Dwir pIAwieAw iPir kwlu n ivAwpY ]17] (1092-13, mwrU, mÚ 3) har kirpaa Dhaar pee-aa-i-aa fir kaal na vi-aapai. ||17||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v17	Those who drink it in, by the Grace of the Lord, are never again afflicted by death. ||17||
RECORD	para 47797	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1092-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47798	loku Avgxw kI bMn@Y gMTVI gux n ivhwJY koie ] (1092-14, mwrU, mÚ 3) lok avganaa kee ban Hai ganth-rhee gun na vihaajhai ko-ay. People tie up bundles of demerits; no one deals in virtue.
DEFINE	para 47799	gux kw gwhku nwnkw ivrlw koeI hoie ] (1092-15, mwrU, mÚ 3) gun kaa gaahak naankaa virlaa ko-ee ho-ay. Rare is that person, O Nanak, who purchases virtue.
