DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	By Guru's Grace, one is blessed with virtue, when the Lord bestows His Glance of Grace. ||1||
RECORD	para 47801	mÚ 3 ] (1092-16) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47802	gux Avgux smwin hih ij Awip kIqy krqwir ] (1092-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) gun avgun samaan heh je aap keetay kartaar. Merits and demerits are the same; they are both created by the Creator.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk hukim mMinAY suKu pweIAY gur sbdI vIcwir ]2] (1092-16, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak hukam mani-ai sukh paa-ee-ai gur sabdee veechaar. ||2||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, one who obeys the Hukam of the Lord's Command, finds peace, contemplating the Word of the Guru's Shabad. ||2||
RECORD	para 47804	pauVI ] (1092-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 47805	AMdir rwjw qKqu hY Awpy kry inAwau ] (1092-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) andar raajaa takhat hai aapay karay ni-aa-o. The King sits on the throne within the self; He Himself administers justice.
RECORD	para 47806	gur sbdI dru jwxIAY AMdir mhlu Asrwau ] (1092-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) gur sabdee dar jaanee-ai andar mahal asraa-o. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Lord's Court is known; within the self is the Sanctuary, the Mansion of the Lord's Presence.
RECORD	para 47807	Kry priK KjwnY pweIAin KoitAw nwhI Qwau ] (1092-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) kharay parakh khajaanai paa-ee-an khoti-aa naahee thaa-o. The coins are assayed, and the genuine coins are placed in His treasury, while the counterfeit ones find no place.
DEFINE	para 47808	sBu sco scu vrqdw sdw scu inAwau ] (1092-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabh sacho sach varatdaa sadaa sach ni-aa-o. The Truest of the True is all-pervading; His justice is forever True.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v18	AMimRq kw rsu AwieAw min visAw nwau ]18] (1092-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) amrit kaa ras aa-i-aa man vasi-aa naa-o. ||18||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v18	One comes to enjoy the Ambrosial essence, when the Name is enshrined in the mind. ||18||
RECORD	para 47810	slok mÚ 1 ] (1092-19) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47811	hau mY krI qW qU nwhI qU hovih hau nwih ] (1092-19, mwrU, mÚ 1) ha-o mai karee taa N too naahee too hoveh ha-o naahi. When one acts in egotism, then You are not there, Lord. Wherever You are, there is no ego.
DEFINE	para 47813	bUJhu igAwnI bUJxw eyh AkQ kQw mn mwih ] (1093-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) boojhhu gi-aanee boojh-naa ayh akath kathaa man maahi. O spiritual teachers, understand this: the Unspoken Speech is in the mind.
DEFINE	para 47814	ibnu gur qqu n pweIAY AlKu vsY sB mwih ] (1093-1, mwrU, mÚ 1) bin gur tat na paa-ee-ai alakh vasai sabh maahi. Without the Guru, the essence of reality is not found; the Invisible Lord dwells everywhere.
WHEN	para 47815	siqguru imlY q jwxIAY jW sbdu vsY mn mwih ] (1093-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) satgur milai ta jaanee-ai jaa N sabad vasai man maahi. One meets the True Guru, and then the Lord is known, when the Word of the Shabad comes to dwell in the mind.
WHEN	para 47816	Awpu gieAw BRmu Bau gieAw jnm mrn duK jwih ] (1093-2, mwrU, mÚ 1) aap ga-i-aa bharam bha-o ga-i-aa janam maran dukh jaahi. When self-conceit departs, doubt and fear also depart, and the pain of birth and death is removed.
DEFINE	para 47817	gurmiq AlKu lKweIAY aUqm miq qrwih ] (1093-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) gurmat alakh lakhaa-ee-ai ootam mat taraahi. Following the Guru's Teachings, the Unseen Lord is seen; the intellect is exalted, and one is carried across.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk sohM hMsw jpu jwphu iqRBvx iqsY smwih ]1] (1093-3, mwrU, mÚ 1) naanak soha N hansaa jap jaapahu taribhavan tisai samaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, chant the chant of 'Sohang hansaa' - 'He is me, and I am Him.' The three worlds are absorbed in Him. ||1||
RECORD	para 47819	mÚ 3 ] (1093-4) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 47820	mnu mwxku ijin priKAw gur sbdI vIcwir ] (1093-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) man maanak jin parkhi-aa gur sabdee veechaar. Some assay their mind-jewel, and contemplate the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
DEFINE	para 47821	sy jn ivrly jwxIAih kljug ivic sMswir ] (1093-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) say jan virlay jaanee-ahi kaljug vich sansaar. Only a few of those humble beings are known in this world, in this Dark Age of Kali Yuga.
WHEN	para 47822	AwpY no Awpu imil rihAw haumY duibDw mwir ] (1093-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapai no aap mil rahi-aa ha-umai dubiDhaa maar. One's self remains blended with the Lord's Self, when egotism and duality are conquered.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk nwim rqy duqru qry Baujlu ibKmu sMswru ]2] (1093-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay dutar taray bha-ojal bikham sansaar. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, those who are imbued with the Naam cross over the difficult, treacherous and terrifying world-ocean. ||2||
RECORD	para 47824	pauVI ] (1093-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47825	mnmuK AMdru n BwlnI muTy AhMmqy ] (1093-6, mwrU, mÚ 3) manmukh andar na bhaalnee muthay ahamtay. The self-willed manmukhs do not search within their own selves; they are deluded by their egotistical pride.
RECORD	para 47826	cwry kuMfW Biv Qky AMdir iqK qqy ] (1093-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) chaaray kundaa N bhav thakay andar tikh tatay. Wandering in the four directions, they grow weary, tormented by burning desire within.
RECORD	para 47827	isMimRiq swsq n soDnI mnmuK ivguqy ] (1093-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) simrit saasat na soDhnee manmukh vigutay. They do not study the Simritees and the Shaastras; the manmukhs waste away and are lost.
RECORD	para 47828	ibnu gur iknY n pwieE hir nwmu hir sqy ] (1093-7, mwrU, mÚ 3) bin gur kinai na paa-i-o har naam har satay. Without the Guru, no one finds the Naam, the Name of the True Lord.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v19	qqu igAwnu vIcwirAw hir jip hir gqy ]19] (1093-8, mwrU, mÚ 3) tat gi-aan veechaari-aa har jap har gatay. ||19||
UPHOLD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v19	One who contemplates the essence of spiritual wisdom and meditates on the Lord is saved. ||19||
RECORD	para 47830	slok mÚ 2 ] (1093-8) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 47831	Awpy jwxY kry Awip Awpy AwxY rwis ] (1093-9, mwrU, mÚ 2) aapay jaanai karay aap aapay aanai raas. He Himself knows, He Himself acts, and He Himself does it right.
