DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	You do not even think of that God; O Nanak, it is not in your karma. ||1||
RECORD	para 47845	mÚ 5 ] (1093-14) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
FORBID	para 47846	mwieAw swiQ n cleI ikAw lptwvih AMD ] (1093-14, mwrU, mÚ 5) maa-i-aa saath na chal-ee ki-aa laptaavahi anDh. Maya and its wealth shall not go along with you, so why do you cling to it - are you blind?
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	gur ky crx iDAwie qU qUtih mwieAw bMD ]2] (1093-14, mwrU, mÚ 5) gur kay charan Dhi-aa-ay too tooteh maa-i-aa banDh. ||2||
REQUIRE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	Meditate on the Guru's Feet, and the bonds of Maya shall be cut away from you. ||2||
RECORD	para 47848	pauVI ] (1093-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 47849	BwxY hukmu mnwieEnu BwxY suKu pwieAw ] (1093-15, mwrU, mÚ 5) bhaanai hukam manaa-i-on bhaanai sukh paa-i-aa. By the Pleasure of His Will, the Lord inspires us to obey the Hukam of His Command; by the Pleasure of His Will, we find peace.
RECORD	para 47850	BwxY siqguru myilEnu BwxY scu iDAwieAw ] (1093-15, mwrU, mÚ 5) bhaanai satgur mayli-on bhaanai sach Dhi-aa-i-aa. By the Pleasure of His Will, He leads us to meet the True Guru; by the Pleasure of His Will, we meditate on the Truth.
DEFINE	para 47851	Bwxy jyvf hor dwiq nwhI scu AwiK suxwieAw ] (1093-16, mwrU, mÚ 5) bhaanay jayvad hor daat naahee sach aakh sunaa-i-aa. There is no other gift as great as the Pleasure of His Will; this Truth is spoken and proclaimed.
RECORD	para 47852	ijn kau pUrib iliKAw iqn scu kmwieAw ] (1093-16, mwrU, mÚ 5) jin ka-o poorab likhi-aa tin sach kamaa-i-aa. Those who have such pre-ordained destiny, practice and live the Truth.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v21	nwnk iqsu srxwgqI ijin jgqu aupwieAw ]21] (1093-17, mwrU, mÚ 5) naanak tis sarnaagatee jin jagat upaa-i-aa. ||21||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v21	Nanak has entered His Sanctuary; He created the world. ||21||
RECORD	para 47854	slok mÚ 3 ] (1093-17) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
UPHOLD	para 47855	ijn kau AMdir igAwnu nhI BY kI nwhI ibMd ] (1093-17, mwrU, mÚ 3) jin ka-o andar gi-aan nahee bhai kee naahee bind. Those who do not have spiritual wisdom within, do not have even an iota of the Fear of God.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	nwnk muieAw kw ikAw mwrxw ij Awip mwry goivMd ]1] (1093-18, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak mu-i-aa kaa ki-aa maarnaa je aap maaray govind. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, why kill those who are already dead? The Lord of the Universe Himself has killed them. ||1||
RECORD	para 47857	mÚ 3 ] (1093-18) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 47858	mn kI pqRI vwcxI suKI hU suKu swru ] (1093-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) man kee patree vaachnee sukhee hoo sukh saar. To read the horoscope of the mind, is the most sublime joyful peace.
DEFINE	para 47859	so bRwhmxu Blw AwKIAY ij bUJY bRhmu bIcwru ] (1093-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) so baraahman bhalaa aakhee-ai je boojhai barahm beechaar. He alone is called a good Brahmin, who understands God in contemplative meditation.
RECORD	para 47860	hir swlwhy hir pVY gur kY sbid vIcwir ] (1093-19, mwrU, mÚ 3) har saalaahay har parhai gur kai sabad veechaar. He praises the Lord, and reads of the Lord, and contemplates the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 47862	AwieAw Ehu prvwxu hY ij kul kw kry auDwru ] (1094-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) aa-i-aa oh parvaan hai je kul kaa karay uDhaar. Celebrated and approved is the coming into the world of such a person, who saves all his generations as well.
RECORD	para 47863	AgY jwiq n puCIAY krxI sbdu hY swru ] (1094-1, mwrU, mÚ 3) agai jaat na puchhee-ai karnee sabad hai saar. Hereafter, no one is questioned about social status; excellent and sublime is the practice of the Word of the Shabad.
DEFINE	para 47864	horu kUVu pVxw kUVu kmwvxw ibiKAw nwil ipAwru ] (1094-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) hor koorh parh-naa koorh kamaavanaa bikhi-aa naal pi-aar. Other study is false, and other actions are false; such people are in love with poison.
RECORD	para 47865	AMdir suKu n hoveI mnmuK jnmu KuAwru ] (1094-2, mwrU, mÚ 3) andar sukh na hova-ee manmukh janam khu-aar. They do not find any peace within themselves; the self-willed manmukhs waste away their lives.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	nwnk nwim rqy sy aubry gur kY hyiq Apwir ]2] (1094-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay say ubray gur kai hayt apaar. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam are saved; they have infinite love for the Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 47867	pauVI ] (1094-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 47868	Awpy kir kir vyKdw Awpy sBu scw ] (1094-3, mwrU, mÚ 3) aapay kar kar vaykh-daa aapay sabh sachaa. He Himself creates the creation, and gazes upon it; He Himself is totally True.
RECORD	para 47869	jo hukmu n bUJY Ksm kw soeI nru kcw ] (1094-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) jo hukam na boojhai khasam kaa so-ee nar kachaa. One who does not understand the Hukam, the Command of his Lord and Master, is false.
RECORD	para 47870	ijqu BwvY iqqu lwiedw gurmuiK hir scw ] (1094-4, mwrU, mÚ 3) jit bhaavai tit laa-idaa gurmukh har sachaa. By the Pleasure of His Will, the True Lord joins the Gurmukh to Himself.
DEFINE	para 47871	sBnw kw swihbu eyku hY gur sbdI rcw ] (1094-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) sabhnaa kaa saahib ayk hai gur sabdee rachaa. He is the One Lord and Master of all; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, we are blended with Him.
DEFINE	para 47872	gurmuiK sdw slwhIAY siB iqs dy jcw ] (1094-5, mwrU, mÚ 3) gurmukh sadaa salaahee-ai sabh tis day jachaa. The Gurmukhs praise Him forever; all are beggars of Him.
