RECORD	para 48098	mÚ 5 ] (1098-17) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
WHEN	para 48099	iprIAw sMdVI BuK mU lwvx QI ivQrw ] (1098-17, mwrU, mÚ 5) piree-aa sand-rhee bhukh moo laavan thee vithraa. If my Beloved becomes hungry, I will become food, and place myself before Him.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v2	jwxu imTweI ieK byeI pIVy nw hutY ]2] (1098-18, mwrU, mÚ 5) jaan mithaa-ee ikh bay-ee peerhay naa hutai. ||2||
ALLOW	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v2	I may be crushed, again and again, but like sugarcane, I do not stop yielding sweet juice. ||2||
RECORD	para 48101	mÚ 5 ] (1098-18) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 48102	Tgw nIhu mqRoiV jwxu gMDRbw ngrI ] (1098-18, mwrU, mÚ 5) thagaa neehu matrorh jaan ganDharbaa nagree. Break off your love with the cheaters; realize that it is a mirage.
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v3	suK GtwaU fUie iesu pMDwxU Gr Gxy ]3] (1098-19, mwrU, mÚ 5) sukh ghataa-oo doo-ay is panDhaanoo ghar ghanay. ||3||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v3	Your pleasure lasts for only two moments; this traveller wanders through countless homes. ||3||
RECORD	para 48104	pauVI ] (1098-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 48105	Akl klw nh pweIAY pRBu AlK AlyKM ] (1098-19, mwrU, mÚ 5) akal kalaa nah paa-ee-ai parabh alakh alaykhaN. God is not found by intellectual devices; He is unknowable and unseen.
RECORD	para 48107	Ktu drsn BRmqy iPrih nh imlIAY ByKM ] (1099-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) khat darsan bharamtay fireh nah milee-ai bhaykhaN. The followers of the six orders wander and roam around wearing religious robes, but they do not meet God.
DEFINE	para 48108	vrq krih cMdRwiexw sy ikqY n lyKM ] (1099-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) varat karahi chandraa-inaa say kitai na laykhaN. They keep the lunar fasts, but they are of no account.
RECORD	para 48109	byd pVih sMpUrnw qqu swr n pyKM ] (1099-1, mwrU, mÚ 5) bayd parheh sampoornaa tat saar na paykhaN. Those who read the Vedas in their entirety, still do not see the sublime essence of reality.
RECORD	para 48110	iqlku kFih iesnwnu kir AMqir kwlyKM ] (1099-2, mwrU, mÚ 5) tilak kadheh isnaan kar antar kaalaykhaN. They apply ceremonial marks to their foreheads, and take cleansing baths, but they are blackened within.
DEFINE	para 48111	ByKI pRBU n lBeI ivxu scI isKM ] (1099-2, mwrU, mÚ 5) bhaykhee parabhoo na labh-ee vin sachee sikhaN. They wear religious robes, but without the True Teachings, God is not found.
DEFINE	para 48112	BUlw mwrig so pvY ijsu Duir msqik lyKM ] (1099-3, mwrU, mÚ 5) bhoolaa maarag so pavai jis Dhur mastak laykhaN. One who had strayed, finds the Path again, if such pre-ordained destiny is written on his forehead.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v13	iqin jnmu svwirAw Awpxw ijin guru AKI dyKM ]13] (1099-3, mwrU, mÚ 5) tin janam savaari-aa aapnaa jin gur akhee daykhaN. ||13||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v13	One who sees the Guru with his eyes, embellishes and exalts his human life. ||13||
RECORD	para 48114	fKxy mÚ 5 ] (1099-4) dakh-nay mehlaa 5. Dakhanay, Fifth Mehl:
WHEN	para 48115	so invwhU gif jo clwaU n QIAY ] (1099-4, mwrU, mÚ 5) so nivaahoo gad jo chalaa-oo na thee-ai. Focus on that which will not pass away.
WHEN	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v1	kwr kUVwvI Cif sMmlu scu DxI ]1] (1099-4, mwrU, mÚ 5) kaar koorhaavee chhad sammal sach Dhanee. ||1||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v1	Abandon your false actions, and meditate on the True Master. ||1||
RECORD	para 48117	mÚ 5 ] (1099-5) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 48118	hB smwxI joiq ijau jl GtwaU cMdRmw ] (1099-5, mwrU, mÚ 5) habh samaanee jot ji-o jal ghataa-oo chandarmaa. God's Light is permeating all, like the moon reflected in the water.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v2	prgtu QIAw Awip nwnk msqik iliKAw ]2] (1099-5, mwrU, mÚ 5) pargat thee-aa aap naanak mastak likhi-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v2	He Himself is revealed, O Nanak, to one who has such destiny inscribed upon his forehead. ||2||
RECORD	para 48120	mÚ 5 ] (1099-6) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 48121	muK suhwvy nwmu cau AwT phr gux gwau ] (1099-6, mwrU, mÚ 5) mukh suhaavay naam cha-o aath pahar gun gaa-o. One's face becomes beautiful, chanting the Naam, the Name of the Lord, and singing His Glorious Praises, twenty-four hours a day.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v3	nwnk drgh mMnIAih imlI inQwvy Qwau ]3] (1099-6, mwrU, mÚ 5) naanak dargeh manee-ah milee nithaavay thaa-o. ||3||
REQUIRE	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v3	O Nanak, in the Court of the Lord, you shall be accepted; even the homeless find a home there. ||3||
RECORD	para 48123	pauVI ] (1099-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 48124	bwhr ByiK n pweIAY pRBu AMqrjwmI ] (1099-7, mwrU, mÚ 5) baahar bhaykh na paa-ee-ai parabh antarjaamee. By wearing religious robes outwardly, God, the Inner-knower is not found.
RECORD	para 48125	ieksu hir jIau bwhrI sB iPrY inkwmI ] (1099-7, mwrU, mÚ 5) ikas har jee-o baahree sabh firai nikaamee. Without the One Dear Lord, all wander around aimlessly.
DEFINE	para 48126	mnu rqw kutMb isau inq grib iPrwmI ] (1099-8, mwrU, mÚ 5) man rataa kutamb si-o nit garab firaamee. Their minds are imbued with attachment to family, and so they continually wander around, puffed up with pride.
DEFINE	para 48127	iPrih gumwnI jg mih ikAw grbih dwmI ] (1099-8, mwrU, mÚ 5) fireh gumaanee jag meh ki-aa garbeh daamee. The arrogant wander around the world; why are they so proud of their wealth?
FORBID	para 48128	clidAw nwil n cleI iKn jwie iblwmI ] (1099-9, mwrU, mÚ 5) chaldi-aa naal na chal-ee khin jaa-ay bilaamee. Their wealth shall not go with them when they depart; in an instant, it is gone.
RECORD	para 48129	ibcrdy iPrih sMswr mih hir jI hukwmI ] (1099-9, mwrU, mÚ 5) bicharday fireh sansaar meh har jee hukaamee. They wander around in the world, according to the Hukam of the Lord's Command.
DEFINE	para 48130	krmu Kulw guru pwieAw hir imilAw suAwmI ] (1099-10, mwrU, mÚ 5) karam khulaa gur paa-i-aa har mili-aa su-aamee. When one's karma is activated, one finds the Guru, and through Him, the Lord and Master is found.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v14	jo jnu hir kw syvko hir iqs kI kwmI ]14] (1099-10, mwrU, mÚ 5) jo jan har kaa sayvko har tis kee kaamee. ||14||
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v14	That humble being, who serves the Lord, has his affairs resolved by the Lord. ||14||
RECORD	para 48132	fKxy mÚ 5 ] (1099-11) dakh-nay mehlaa 5. Dakhanay, Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 48133	muKhu Alwey hB mrxu pCwxMdo koie ] (1099-11, mwrU, mÚ 5) mukhahu alaa-ay habh maran pachhaanado ko-ay. All speak with their mouths, but rare are those one who realize death.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v1	nwnk iqnw Kwku ijnw XkInw ihk isau ]1] (1099-11, mwrU, mÚ 5) naanak tinaa khaak jinaa yakeenaa hik si-o. ||1||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v1	Nanak is the dust of the feet of those who have faith in the One Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 48135	mÚ 5 ] (1099-12) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 48136	jwxu vsMdo mMiJ pCwxU ko hykVo ] (1099-12, mwrU, mÚ 5) jaan vasando manjh pachhaanoo ko haykrho. Know that He dwells within all; rare are those who realize this.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v2	qY qin pVdw nwih nwnk jY guru ByitAw ]2] (1099-12, mwrU, mÚ 5) tai tan parh-daa naahi naanak jai gur bhayti-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v2	There is no obscuring veil on the body of that one, O Nanak, who meets the Guru. ||2||
RECORD	para 48138	mÚ 5 ] (1099-13) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 48139	mqVI kWFku Awh pwv DovMdo pIvsw ] (1099-13, mwrU, mÚ 5) mat-rhee kaaNdhak aah paav Dhovando peevsaa. I drink in the water which has washed the feet of those who share the Teachings.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v3	mU qin pRymu AQwh psx kU scw DxI ]3] (1099-13, mwrU, mÚ 5) moo tan paraym athaah pasan koo sachaa Dhanee. ||3||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v3	My body is filled with infinite love to see my True Master. ||3||
RECORD	para 48141	pauVI ] (1099-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 48142	inrBau nwmu ivswirAw nwil mwieAw rcw ] (1099-14, mwrU, mÚ 5) nirbha-o naam visaari-aa naal maa-i-aa rachaa. Forgetting the Naam, the Name of the Fearless Lord, he becomes attached to Maya.
RECORD	para 48143	AwvY jwie BvweIAY bhu jonI ncw ] (1099-14, mwrU, mÚ 5) aavai jaa-ay bhavaa-ee-ai baho jonee nachaa. He comes and goes, and wanders, dancing in countless incarnations.
DEFINE	para 48144	bcnu kry qY iKsik jwie boly sBu kcw ] (1099-14, mwrU, mÚ 5) bachan karay tai khisak jaa-ay bolay sabh kachaa. He gives his word, but then backs out. All that he says is false.
DEFINE	para 48145	AMdrhu QoQw kUiVAwru kUVI sB Kcw ] (1099-15, mwrU, mÚ 5) andrahu thothaa koorhi-aar koorhee sabh khachaa. The false person is hollow within; he is totally engrossed in falsehood.
RECORD	para 48146	vYru kry inrvYr nwil JUTy lwlcw ] (1099-15, mwrU, mÚ 5) vair karay nirvair naal jhoothay laalchaa. He tries to take vengeance upon the Lord, who bears no vengeance; such a person is trapped by falsehood and greed.
WHEN	para 48147	mwirAw scY pwiqswih vyiK Duir krmcw ] (1099-16, mwrU, mÚ 5) maari-aa sachai paatisaah vaykh Dhur karamchaa. The True King, the Primal Lord God, kills him when He sees what he has done.
RECORD	para 48148	jmdUqI hY hyirAw duK hI mih pcw ] (1099-16, mwrU, mÚ 5) jamdootee hai hayri-aa dukh hee meh pachaa. The Messenger of Death sees him, and he rots away in pain.
RECORD	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v15	hoAw qpwvsu Drm kw nwnk dir scw ]15] (1099-16, mwrU, mÚ 5) ho-aa tapaavas Dharam kaa naanak dar sachaa. ||15||
DEFINE	mwrU vwr mhlw 5 fKxy mÚ 5 v15	Even-handed justice is administered, O Nanak, in the Court of the True Lord. ||15||
RECORD	para 48150	fKxy mÚ 5 ] (1099-17) dakh-nay mehlaa 5. Dakhanay, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 48151	prBwqy pRB nwmu jip gur ky crx iDAwie ] (1099-17, mwrU, mÚ 5) parbhaatay parabh naam jap gur kay charan Dhi-aa-ay. In the early hours of the morning, chant the Name of God, and meditate on the Feet of the Guru.
