DEFINE	quKwrI CMq mhlw 1 bwrh mwhw v6	O Nanak, finding God in Baisakhi, the consciousness is filled with the Word of the Shabad, and the mind comes to believe. ||6||
DEFINE	para 48489	mwhu jyTu Blw pRIqmu ikau ibsrY ] (1108-6, quKwrI, mÚ 1) maahu jayth bhalaa pareetam ki-o bisrai. The month of Jayt'h is so sublime. How could I forget my Beloved?
RECORD	para 48490	Ql qwpih sr Bwr sw Dn ibnau krY ] (1108-7, quKwrI, mÚ 1) thal taapeh sar bhaar saa Dhan bin-o karai. The earth burns like a furnace, and the soul-bride offers her prayer.
RECORD	para 48491	Dn ibnau krydI gux swrydI gux swrI pRB Bwvw ] (1108-7, quKwrI, mÚ 1) Dhan bin-o karaydee gun saaraydee gun saaree parabh bhaavaa. The bride offers her prayer, and sings His Glorious Praises; singing His Praises, she becomes pleasing to God.
WHEN	para 48492	swcY mhil rhY bYrwgI Awvx dyih q Awvw ] (1108-8, quKwrI, mÚ 1) saachai mahal rahai bairaagee aavan deh ta aavaa. The Unattached Lord dwells in His true mansion. If He allows me, then I will come to Him.
DEFINE	para 48493	inmwxI inqwxI hir ibnu ikau pwvY suK mhlI ] (1108-8, quKwrI, mÚ 1) nimaanee nitaanee har bin ki-o paavai sukh mahlee. The bride is dishonored and powerless; how will she find peace without her Lord?
