DEFINE	para 48502	mY min qin shu BwvY ipr prdyis isDwey ] (1108-13, quKwrI, mÚ 1) mai man tan saho bhaavai pir pardays siDhaa-ay. My mind and body are pleased by my Lord, but my Beloved has gone away.
RECORD	para 48503	ipru Gir nhI AwvY mrIAY hwvY dwmin cmik frwey ] (1108-13, quKwrI, mÚ 1) pir ghar nahee aavai maree-ai haavai daaman chamak daraa-ay. My Beloved has not come home, and I am dying of the sorrow of separation. The lightning flashes, and I am scared.
DEFINE	para 48504	syj iekylI KrI duhylI mrxu BieAw duKu mwey ] (1108-14, quKwrI, mÚ 1) sayj ikaylee kharee duhaylee maran bha-i-aa dukh maa-ay. My bed is lonely, and I am suffering in agony. I am dying in pain, O my mother!
RECORD	para 48505	hir ibnu nId BUK khu kYsI kwpVu qin n suKwvey ] (1108-14, quKwrI, mÚ 1) har bin need bhookh kaho kaisee kaaparh tan na sukhaava-ay. Tell me - without the Lord, how can I sleep, or feel hungry? My clothes give no comfort to my body.
RECORD	quKwrI CMq mhlw 1 bwrh mwhw v9	nwnk sw sohwgix kMqI ipr kY AMik smwvey ]9] (1108-15, quKwrI, mÚ 1) naanak saa sohagan kantee pir kai ank samaav-ay. ||9||
DEFINE	quKwrI CMq mhlw 1 bwrh mwhw v9	O Nanak, she alone is a happy soul-bride, who merges in the Being of her Beloved Husband Lord. ||9||
DEFINE	para 48507	Bwdau Brim BulI Bir jobin pCuqwxI ] (1108-15, quKwrI, mÚ 1) bhaada-o bharam bhulee bhar joban pachhutaanee. In Bhaadon, the young woman is confused by doubt; later, she regrets and repents.
DEFINE	para 48508	jl Ql nIir Bry brs ruqy rMgu mwxI ] (1108-16, quKwrI, mÚ 1) jal thal neer bharay baras rutay rang maanee. The lakes and fields are overflowing with water; the rainy season has come - the time to celebrate!
RECORD	para 48509	brsY inis kwlI ikau suKu bwlI dwdr mor lvMqy ] (1108-16, quKwrI, mÚ 1) barsai nis kaalee ki-o sukh baalee daadar mor lavantay. In the dark of night it rains; how can the young bride find peace? The frogs and peacocks send out their noisy calls.
