ALLOW	para 54227	nv iCA Kt kw kry bIcwru ] (1237-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) nav chhi-a khat kaa karay beechaar. You may study the nine grammars, the six Shaastras and the six divions of the Vedas.
ALLOW	para 54228	inis idn aucrY Bwr ATwr ] (1237-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) nis din uchrai bhaar athaar. You may recite the Mahaabhaarata.
RECORD	para 54229	iqin BI AMqu n pwieAw qoih ] (1237-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) tin bhee ant na paa-i-aa tohi. Even these cannot find the limits of the Lord.
RECORD	para 54230	nwm ibhUx mukiq ikau hoie ] (1237-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) naam bihoon mukat ki-o ho-ay. Without the Naam, the Name of the Lord, how can anyone be liberated?
RECORD	para 54231	nwiB vsq bRhmY AMqu n jwixAw ] (1237-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) naabh vasat barahmai ant na jaani-aa. Brahma, in the lotus of the navel, does not know the limits of God.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v3	gurmuiK nwnk nwmu pCwixAw ]3] (1237-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) gurmukh naanak naam pachhaani-aa. ||3||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v3	The Gurmukh, O Nanak, realizes the Naam. ||3||
RECORD	para 54233	pauVI ] (1237-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54234	Awpy Awip inrMjnw ijin Awpu aupwieAw ] (1237-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) aapay aap niranjanaa jin aap upaa-i-aa. The Immaculate Lord Himself, by Himself, created Himself.
RECORD	para 54235	Awpy Kylu rcwieEnu sBu jgqu sbwieAw ] (1237-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) aapay khayl rachaa-i-on sabh jagat sabaa-i-aa. He Himself created the whole drama of all the world's play.
RECORD	para 54236	qRY gux Awip isrijAnu mwieAw mohu vDwieAw ] (1237-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) tarai gun aap sirji-an maa-i-aa moh vaDhaa-i-aa. He Himself formed the three gunas, the three qualities; He increased the attachment to Maya.
DEFINE	para 54237	gur prswdI aubry ijn Bwxw BwieAw ] (1237-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee ubray jin bhaanaa bhaa-i-aa. By Guru's Grace, they are saved - those who love the Will of God.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	nwnk scu vrqdw sB sic smwieAw ]1] (1237-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak sach varatdaa sabh sach samaa-i-aa. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, the True Lord is pervading everywhere; all are contained within the True Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 54241	Awip aupwey nwnkw Awpy rKY vyk ] (1238-1, swrMg, mÚ 2) aap upaa-ay naankaa aapay rakhai vayk. He Himself creates, O Nanak; He establishes the various creatures.
RECORD	para 54242	mMdw iks no AwKIAY jW sBnw swihbu eyku ] (1238-1, swrMg, mÚ 2) mandaa kis no aakhee-ai jaa N sabhnaa saahib ayk. How can anyone be called bad? We have only One Lord and Master.
DEFINE	para 54243	sBnw swihbu eyku hY vyKY DMDY lwie ] (1238-2, swrMg, mÚ 2) sabhnaa saahib ayk hai vaykhai DhanDhai laa-ay. There is One Lord and Master of all; He watches over all, and assigns all to their tasks.
DEFINE	para 54244	iksY QoVw iksY Aglw KwlI koeI nwih ] (1238-2, swrMg, mÚ 2) kisai thorhaa kisai aglaa khaalee ko-ee naahi. Some have less, and some have more; no one is allowed to leave empty.
RECORD	para 54245	Awvih nµgy jwih nµgy ivcy krih ivQwr ] (1238-3, swrMg, mÚ 2) aavahi nangay jaahi nangay vichay karahi vithaar. Naked we come, and naked we go; in between, we put on a show.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	nwnk hukmu n jwxIAY AgY kweI kwr ]1] (1238-3, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak hukam na jaanee-ai agai kaa-ee kaar. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	O Nanak, one who does not understand the Hukam of God's Command - what will he have to do in the world hereafter? ||1||
RECORD	para 54247	mhlw 1 ] (1238-4) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54248	ijnis Qwip jIAW kau ByjY ijnis Qwip lY jwvY ] (1238-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) jinas thaap jee-aa N ka-o bhayjai jinas thaap lai jaavai. He sends out the various created beings, and he calls back the various created beings again.
RECORD	para 54249	Awpy Qwip auQwpY Awpy eyqy vys krwvY ] (1238-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) aapay thaap uthaapai aapay aytay vays karaavai. He himself establishes, and He Himself disestablishes. He fashions them in various forms.
RECORD	para 54250	jyqy jIA iPrih AauDUqI Awpy iBiKAw pwvY ] (1238-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) jaytay jee-a fireh a-uDhootee aapay bhikhi-aa paavai. And all the human beings who wander around as beggars, He Himself gives in charity to them.
DEFINE	para 54251	lyKY bolxu lyKY clxu kwiequ kIcih dwvy ] (1238-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) laykhai bolan laykhai chalan kaa-it keecheh daavay. As it is recorded, the mortals speak, and as it is recorded, they walk. So why put on all this show?
DEFINE	para 54252	mUlu miq prvwxw eyho nwnku AwiK suxwey ] (1238-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) mool mat parvaanaa ayho naanak aakh sunaa-ay. This is the basis of intelligence; this is certified and approved. Nanak speaks and proclaims it.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	krxI aupir hoie qpwvsu jy ko khY khwey ]2] (1238-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) karnee upar ho-ay tapaavas jay ko kahai kahaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	By past actions, each being is judged; what else can anyone say? ||2||
RECORD	para 54254	pauVI ] (1238-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54255	gurmuiK clqu rcwieEnu gux prgtI AwieAw ] (1238-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) gurmukh chalat rachaa-i-on gun pargatee aa-i-aa. The Guru's Word makes the drama play itself out. Through virtue, this becomes evident.
DEFINE	para 54256	gurbwxI sd aucrY hir mMin vswieAw ] (1238-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) gurbaanee sad uchrai har man vasaa-i-aa. Whoever utters the Word of the Guru's Bani - the Lord is enshrined in his mind.
DEFINE	para 54257	skiq geI BRmu kitAw isv joiq jgwieAw ] (1238-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) sakat ga-ee bharam kati-aa siv jot jagaa-i-aa. Maya's power is gone, and doubt is eradicated; awaken to the Light of the Lord.
RECORD	para 54258	ijn kY poqY puMnu hY guru purKu imlwieAw ] (1238-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) jin kai potai punn hai gur purakh milaa-i-aa. Those who hold onto goodness as their treasure meet the Guru, the Primal Being.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	nwnk shjy imil rhy hir nwim smwieAw ]2] (1238-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak sehjay mil rahay har naam samaa-i-aa. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	O Nanak, they are intuitively absorbed and blended into the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 54261	swh cly vxjwirAw iliKAw dyvY nwil ] (1238-9, swrMg, mÚ 2) saah chalay vanjaari-aa likhi-aa dayvai naal. The merchants come from the Banker; He sends the account of their destiny with them.
RECORD	para 54262	ilKy aupir hukmu hoie leIAY vsqu sm@wil ] (1238-10, swrMg, mÚ 2) likhay upar hukam ho-ay la-ee-ai vasat sam Haal. On the basis of their accounts, He issues the Hukam of His Command, and they are left to take care of their merchandise.
RECORD	para 54263	vsqu leI vxjwreI vKru bDw pwie ] (1238-10, swrMg, mÚ 2) vasat la-ee vanjaara-ee vakhar baDhaa paa-ay. The merchants have purchased their merchandise and packed up their cargo.
RECORD	para 54264	kyeI lwhw lY cly ieik cly mUlu gvwie ] (1238-11, swrMg, mÚ 2) kay-ee laahaa lai chalay ik chalay mool gavaa-ay. Some depart after having earned a good profit, while others leave, having lost their investment altogether.
RECORD	para 54265	QoVw iknY n mMigE iksu khIAY swbwis ] (1238-11, swrMg, mÚ 2) thorhaa kinai na mangi-o kis kahee-ai saabaas. No one asks to have less; who should be celebrated?
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	ndir iqnw kau nwnkw ij swbqu lwey rwis ]1] (1238-12, swrMg, mÚ 2) nadar tinaa ka-o naankaa je saabat laa-ay raas. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	The Lord casts His Glance of Grace, O Nanak, upon those who have preserved their capital investment. ||1||
RECORD	para 54267	mhlw 1 ] (1238-12) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54268	juiV juiV ivCuVy ivCuiV juVy ] (1238-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) jurh jurh vichhurhay vichhurh jurhay. United, the united separate, and separated, they unite again.
RECORD	para 54269	jIiv jIiv muey muey jIvy ] (1238-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) jeev jeev mu-ay mu-ay jeevay. Living, the living die, and dying, they live again.
RECORD	para 54270	kyiqAw ky bwp kyiqAw ky byty kyqy gur cyly hUey ] (1238-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) kayti-aa kay baap kayti-aa kay baytay kaytay gur chaylay hoo-ay. They become the fathers of many, and the sons of many; they become the gurus of many, and the disciples.
REQUIRE	para 54271	AwgY pwCY gxq n AwvY ikAw jwqI ikAw huix hUey ] (1238-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) aagai paachhai ganat na aavai ki-aa jaatee ki-aa hun hoo-ay. No account can be made of the future or the past; who knows what shall be, or what was?
RECORD	para 54272	sBu krxw ikrqu kir ilKIAY kir kir krqw kry kry ] (1238-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabh karnaa kirat kar likee-ai kar kar kartaa karay karay. All the actions and events of the past are recorded; the Doer did, He does, and He will do.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	mnmuiK mrIAY gurmuiK qrIAY nwnk ndrI ndir kry ]2] (1238-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) manmukh maree-ai gurmukh taree-ai naanak nadree nadar karay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	The self-willed manmukh dies, while the Gurmukh is saved; O Nanak, the Gracious Lord bestows His Glance of Grace. ||2||
RECORD	para 54274	pauVI ] (1238-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54275	mnmuiK dUjw Brmu hY dUjY loBwieAw ] (1238-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) manmukh doojaa bharam hai doojai lobhaa-i-aa. The self-willed manmukh wanders in duality, lured and enticed by duality.
RECORD	para 54276	kUVu kptu kmwvdy kUVo AwlwieAw ] (1238-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) koorh kapat kamaavday koorho aalaa-i-aa. He practices falsehood and deception, telling lies.
DEFINE	para 54277	puqR klqRü mohu hyqu hY sBu duKu sbwieAw ] (1238-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) putar kalatar moh hayt hai sabh dukh sabaa-i-aa. Love and attachment to children and spouse is total misery and pain.
DEFINE	para 54278	jm dir bDy mwrIAih Brmih BrmwieAw ] (1238-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) jam dar baDhay maaree-ah bharmeh bharmaa-i-aa. He is gagged and bound at the door of the Messenger of Death; he dies, and wanders lost in reincarnation.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v3	mnmuiK jnmu gvwieAw nwnk hir BwieAw ]3] (1238-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) manmukh janam gavaa-i-aa naanak har bhaa-i-aa. ||3||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v3	The self-willed manmukh wastes his life; Nanak loves the Lord. ||3||
UPHOLD	para 54281	ijn vifAweI qyry nwm kI qy rqy mn mwih ] (1238-18, swrMg, mÚ 2) jin vadi-aa-ee tayray naam kee tay ratay man maahi. Those who are blessed with the glorious greatness of Your Name - their minds are imbued with Your Love.
DEFINE	para 54282	nwnk AMimRqu eyku hY dUjw AMimRqu nwih ] (1238-18, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak amrit ayk hai doojaa amrit naahi. O Nanak, there is only One Ambrosial Nectar; there is no other nectar at all.
DEFINE	para 54283	nwnk AMimRqu mnY mwih pweIAY gur prswid ] (1238-19, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak amrit manai maahi paa-ee-ai gur parsaad. O Nanak, the Ambrosial Nectar is obtained within the mind, by Guru's Grace.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	iqn@I pIqw rMg isau ijn@ kau iliKAw Awid ]1] (1238-19, swrMg, mÚ 2) tin Hee peetaa rang si-o jin H ka-o likhi-aa aad. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	They alone drink it in with love, who have such pre-ordained destiny. ||1||
RECORD	para 54286	mhlw 2 ] (1239-1) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 54287	kIqw ikAw swlwhIAY kry soie swlwih ] (1239-1, swrMg, mÚ 2) keetaa ki-aa salaahee-ai karay so-ay saalaahi. Why praise the created being? Praise the One who created all.
DEFINE	para 54288	nwnk eykI bwhrw dUjw dwqw nwih ] (1239-1, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak aykee baahraa doojaa daataa naahi. O Nanak, there is no other Giver, except the One Lord.
RECORD	para 54289	krqw so swlwhIAY ijin kIqw Awkwru ] (1239-2, swrMg, mÚ 2) kartaa so salaahee-ai jin keetaa aakaar. Praise the Creator Lord, who created the creation.
RECORD	para 54290	dwqw so swlwhIAY ij sBsY dy AwDwru ] (1239-2, swrMg, mÚ 2) daataa so salaahee-ai je sabhsai day aaDhaar. Praise the Great Giver, who gives sustenence to all.
DEFINE	para 54291	nwnk Awip sdIv hY pUrw ijsu BMfwru ] (1239-3, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak aap sadeev hai pooraa jis bhandaar. O Nanak, the treasure of the Eternal Lord is over-flowing.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	vfw kir swlwhIAY AMqu n pwrwvwru ]2] (1239-3, swrMg, mÚ 2) vadaa kar salaahee-ai ant na paaraavaar. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	Praise and honor the One, who has no end or limitation. ||2||
RECORD	para 54293	pauVI ] (1239-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54294	hir kw nwmu inDwnu hY syivAY suKu pweI ] (1239-4, swrMg, mÚ 2) har kaa naam niDhaan hai sayvi-ai sukh paa-ee. The Name of the Lord is a treasure. Serving it, peace is obtained.
ALLOW	para 54295	nwmu inrMjnu aucrW piq isau Gir jWeI ] (1239-4, swrMg, mÚ 2) naam niranjan uchraa N pat si-o ghar jaa N-ee. I chant the Name of the Immaculate Lord, so that I may go home with honor.
DEFINE	para 54296	gurmuiK bwxI nwmu hY nwmu irdY vsweI ] (1239-5, swrMg, mÚ 2) gurmukh banee naam hai naam ridai vasaa-ee. The Word of the Gurmukh is the Naam; I enshrine the Naam within my heart.
RECORD	para 54297	miq pMKyrU vis hoie siqgurU iDAweˆØI ] (1239-5, swrMg, mÚ 2) mat pankhayroo vas ho-ay satguroo Dhi-aa-eeN. The bird of the intellect comes under one's control, by meditating on the True Guru.
ALLOW	slok mhlw 2 v4	nwnk Awip dieAwlu hoie nwmy ilv lweI ]4] (1239-5, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak aap da-i-aal ho-ay naamay liv laa-ee. ||4||
WHEN	slok mhlw 2 v4	O Nanak, if the Lord becomes merciful, the mortal lovingly tunes in to the Naam. ||4||
RECORD	para 54300	iqsu isau kYsw bolxw ij Awpy jwxY jwxu ] (1239-6, swrMg, mÚ 2) tis si-o kaisaa bolnaa je aapay jaanai jaan. How can we speak of Him? Only He knows Himself.
DEFINE	para 54301	cIrI jw kI nw iPrY swihbu so prvwxu ] (1239-7, swrMg, mÚ 2) cheeree jaa kee naa firai saahib so parvaan. His decree cannot be challenged; He is our Supreme Lord and Master.
REQUIRE	para 54302	cIrI ijs kI clxw mIr mlk slwr ] (1239-7, swrMg, mÚ 2) cheeree jis kee chalnaa meer malak salaar. By His Decree, even kings, nobles and commanders must step down.
DEFINE	para 54303	jo iqsu BwvY nwnkw sweI BlI kwr ] (1239-7, swrMg, mÚ 2) jo tis bhaavai naankaa saa-ee bhalee kaar. Whatever is pleasing to His Will, O Nanak, is a good deed.
RECORD	para 54304	ijn@w cIrI clxw hiQ iqn@w ikCu nwih ] (1239-8, swrMg, mÚ 2) jin Haa cheeree chalnaa hath tin Haa kichh naahi. By His Decree, we walk; nothing rests in our hands.
REQUIRE	para 54305	swihb kw Purmwxu hoie auTI krlY pwih ] (1239-8, swrMg, mÚ 2) saahib kaa furmaan ho-ay uthee karlai paahi. When the Order comes from our Lord and Master, all must rise up and take to the road.
DEFINE	para 54306	jyhw cIrI iliKAw qyhw hukmu kmwih ] (1239-9, swrMg, mÚ 2) jayhaa cheeree likhi-aa tayhaa hukam kamaahi. As His Decree is issued, so is His Command obeyed.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v1	Gly Awvih nwnkw sdy auTI jwih ]1] (1239-9, swrMg, mÚ 2) ghalay aavahi naankaa saday uthee jaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v1	Those who are sent, come, O Nanak; when they are called back, they depart and go. ||1||
RECORD	para 54308	mhlw 2 ] (1239-10) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54309	isPiq ijnw kau bKsIAY syeI poqydwr ] (1239-10, swrMg, mÚ 2) sifat jinaa ka-o bakhsee-ai say-ee potaydaar. Those whom the Lord blesses with His Praises, are the true keepers of the treasure.
DEFINE	para 54310	kuMjI ijn kau idqIAw iqn@w imly BMfwr ] (1239-10, swrMg, mÚ 2) kunjee jin ka-o ditee-aa tin Haa milay bhandaar. Those who are blessed with the key - they alone receive the treasure.
DEFINE	para 54311	jh BMfwrI hU gux inklih qy kIAih prvwxu ] (1239-11, swrMg, mÚ 2) jah bhandaaree hoo gun niklahi tay kee-ah parvaan. That treasure, from which virtue wells up - that treasure is approved.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v2	ndir iqn@w kau nwnkw nwmu ijn@w nIswxu ]2] (1239-11, swrMg, mÚ 2) nadar tin Haa ka-o naankaa naam jin Haa neesaan. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v2	Those who are blessed by His Glance of Grace, O Nanak, bear the Insignia of the Naam. ||2||
RECORD	para 54313	pauVI ] (1239-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54314	nwmu inrMjnu inrmlw suixAY suKu hoeI ] (1239-12, swrMg, mÚ 2) naam niranjan nirmalaa suni-ai sukh ho-ee. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is immaculate and pure; hearing it, peace is obtained.
DEFINE	para 54315	suix suix mMin vsweIAY bUJY jnu koeI ] (1239-12, swrMg, mÚ 2) sun sun man vasaa-ee-ai boojhai jan ko-ee. Listening and hearing, It is enshrined in the mind; how rare is that humble being who realizes it.
REQUIRE	para 54316	bhidAw auTidAw n ivsrY swcw scu soeI ] (1239-13, swrMg, mÚ 2) bahdi-aa uth-di-aa na visrai saachaa sach so-ee. Sitting down and standing up, I shall never forget Him, the Truest of the true.
ALLOW	para 54317	Bgqw kau nwm ADwru hY nwmy suKu hoeI ] (1239-13, swrMg, mÚ 2) bhagtaa ka-o naam aDhaar hai naamay sukh ho-ee. His devotees have the Support of His Name; in His Name, they find peace.
RECORD	slok mhlw 2 v5	nwnk min qin riv rihAw gurmuiK hir soeI ]5] (1239-13, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak man tan rav rahi-aa gurmukh har so-ee. ||5||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 2 v5	O Nanak, He permeates and pervades mind and body; He is the Lord, the Guru's Word. ||5||
RECORD	para 54319	salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54320	nwnk qulIAih qol jy jIau ipCY pweIAY ] (1239-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak tulee-ah tol jay jee-o pichhai paa-ee-ai. O Nanak, the weight is weighed out, when the soul is placed on the scale.
DEFINE	para 54321	ieksu n pujih bol jy pUry pUrw kir imlY ] (1239-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) ikas na pujeh bol jay pooray pooraa kar milai. Nothing is equal to speaking of the One, who perfectly unites us with the Perfect Lord.
RECORD	para 54322	vfw AwKxu Bwrw qolu ] (1239-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) vadaa aakhan bhaaraa tol. To call Him glorious and great carries such a heavy weight.
DEFINE	para 54323	hor haulI mqI hauly bol ] (1239-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) hor ha-ulee matee ha-ulay bol. Other intellectualisms are lightweight; other words are lightweight as well.
RECORD	para 54324	DrqI pwxI prbq Bwru ] (1239-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) Dhartee paanee parbat bhaar. The weight of the earth, water and mountains
RECORD	para 54325	ikau kMfY qolY suinAwru ] (1239-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) ki-o kandai tolai suni-aar. - how can the goldsmith weigh it on the scale?
RECORD	para 54326	qolw mwsw rqk pwie ] (1239-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) tolaa maasaa ratak paa-ay. What weights can balance the scale?
DEFINE	para 54327	nwnk puiCAw dyie pujwie ] (1239-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak puchhi-aa day-ay pujaa-ay. O Nanak, when questioned, the answer is given.
DEFINE	para 54328	mUrK AMiDAw AMDI Dwqu ] (1239-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) moorakh anDhi-aa anDhee Dhaat. The blind fool is running around, leading the blind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	kih kih khxu khwiein Awpu ]1] (1239-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) kahi kahi kahan kahaa-in aap. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	The more they say, the more they expose themselves. ||1||
RECORD	para 54330	mhlw 1 ] (1239-17) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54331	AwKix AauKw sunix AauKw AwiK n jwpI AwiK ] (1239-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) aakhan a-ukhaa sunan a-ukhaa aakh na jaapee aakh. It is difficult to chant it; it is difficult to listen to it. It cannot be chanted with the mouth.
RECORD	para 54332	ieik AwiK AwKih sbdu BwKih ArD aurD idnu rwiq ] (1239-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) ik aakh aakhahi sabad bhaakhahi araDh uraDh din raat. Some speak with their mouths and chant the Word of the Shabad - the low and the high, day and night.
WHEN	para 54333	jy ikhu hoie q ikhu idsY jwpY rUpu n jwiq ] (1239-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) jay kihu ho-ay ta kihu disai jaapai roop na jaat. If He were something, then He would be visible. His form and state cannot be seen.
DEFINE	para 54334	siB kwrx krqw kry Gt AauGt Gt Qwip ] (1239-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabh kaaran kartaa karay ghat a-ughat ghat thaap. The Creator Lord does all deeds; He is established in the hearts of the high and the low.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	AwKix AauKw nwnkw AwiK n jwpY AwiK ]2] (1240-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) aakhan a-ukhaa naankaa aakh na jaapai aakh. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	It is so difficult to chant it, O Nanak; it cannot be chanted with the mouth. ||2||
RECORD	para 54337	pauVI ] (1240-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
ALLOW	para 54338	nwie suixAY mnu rhsIAY nwmy sWiq AweI ] (1240-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai man rehsee-ai naamay saa Nt aa-ee. Hearing the Name, the mind is delighted. The Name brings peace and tranquility.
DEFINE	para 54339	nwie suixAY mnu iqRpqIAY sB duK gvweI ] (1240-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai man taripat-ee-ai sabh dukh gavaa-ee. Hearing the Name, the mind is satisfied, and all pains are taken away.
ALLOW	para 54340	nwie suixAY nwau aUpjY nwmy vifAweI ] (1240-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai naa-o oopjai naamay vadi-aa-ee. Hearing the Name, one becomes famous; the Name brings glorious greatness.
ALLOW	para 54341	nwmy hI sB jwiq piq nwmy giq pweI ] (1240-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) naamay hee sabh jaat pat naamay gat paa-ee. The Name brings all honor and status; through the Name, salvation is obtained.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v6	gurmuiK nwmu iDAweIAY nwnk ilv lweI ]6] (1240-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) gurmukh naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai naanak liv laa-ee. ||6||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v6	The Gurmukh meditates on the Name; Nanak is lovingly attuned to the Name. ||6||
RECORD	para 54344	jUiT n rwgˆØI jUiT n vydˆØI ] (1240-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) jooth na raagee N jooth na vaydee N. Impurity does not come from music; impurity does not come from the Vedas.
RECORD	para 54345	jUiT n cMd sUrj kI BydI ] (1240-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) jooth na chand sooraj kee bhaydee. Impurity does not come from the phases of the sun and the moon.
RECORD	para 54346	jUiT n AMnI jUiT n nweI ] (1240-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) jooth na annee jooth na naa-ee. Impurity does not come from food; impurity does not come from ritual cleansing baths.
RECORD	para 54347	jUiT n mIhu virHAY sB QweI ] (1240-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) jooth na meehu var Hi-ai sabh thaa-ee. Impurity does not come from the rain, which falls everywhere.
RECORD	para 54348	jUiT n DrqI jUiT n pwxI ] (1240-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) jooth na Dhartee jooth na paanee. Impurity does not come from the earth; impurity does not come from the water.
DEFINE	para 54349	jUiT n pauxY mwih smwxI ] (1240-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) jooth na pa-unai maahi samaanee. Impurity does not come from the air which is diffused everywhere.
RECORD	para 54350	nwnk inguirAw guxu nwhI koie ] (1240-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak niguri-aa gun naahee ko-ay. O Nanak, the one who has no Guru, has no redeeming virtues at all.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	muih PyirAY muhu jUTw hoie ]1] (1240-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) muhi fayri-ai muhu joothaa ho-ay. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	Impurity comes from turning one's face away from God. ||1||
RECORD	para 54352	mhlw 1 ] (1240-6) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54353	nwnk culIAw sucIAw jy Bir jwxY koie ] (1240-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak chulee-aa suchee-aa jay bhar jaanai ko-ay. O Nanak, the mouth is truly cleansed by ritual cleansing, if you really know how to do it.
DEFINE	para 54354	surqy culI igAwn kI jogI kw jqu hoie ] (1240-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) surtay chulee gi-aan kee jogee kaa jat ho-ay. For the intuitively aware, cleansing is spiritual wisdom. For the Yogi, it is self-control.
DEFINE	para 54355	bRhmx culI sMqoK kI igrhI kw squ dwnu ] (1240-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) barahman chulee santokh kee girhee kaa sat daan. For the Brahmin, cleansing is contentment; for the householder, it is truth and charity.
DEFINE	para 54356	rwjy culI inAwv kI piVAw scu iDAwnu ] (1240-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) raajay chulee ni-aav kee parhi-aa sach Dhi-aan. For the king, cleansing is justice; for the scholar, it is true meditation.
DEFINE	para 54357	pwxI icqu n DopeI muiK pIqY iqK jwie ] (1240-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) paanee chit na Dhop-ee mukh peetai tikh jaa-ay. The consciousness is not washed with water; you drink it to quench your thirst.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	pwxI ipqw jgq kw iPir pwxI sBu Kwie ]2] (1240-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) paanee pitaa jagat kaa fir paanee sabh khaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	Water is the father of the world; in the end, water destroys it all. ||2||
RECORD	para 54359	pauVI ] (1240-9) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54360	nwie suixAY sB isiD hY iriD ipCY AwvY ] (1240-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai sabh siDh hai riDh pichhai aavai. Hearing the Name, all supernatural spiritual powers are obtained, and wealth follows along.
DEFINE	para 54361	nwie suixAY nau iniD imlY mn icMidAw pwvY ] (1240-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai na-o niDh milai man chindi-aa paavai. Hearing the Name, the nine treasures are received, and the mind's desires are obtained.
RECORD	para 54362	nwie suixAY sMqoKu hoie kvlw crn iDAwvY ] (1240-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai santokh ho-ay kavlaa charan Dhi-aavai. Hearing the Name, contentment comes, and Maya meditates at one's feet.
RECORD	para 54363	nwie suixAY shju aUpjY shjy suKu pwvY ] (1240-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai sahj oopjai sehjay sukh paavai. Hearing the Name, intuitive peace and poise wells up.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v7	gurmqI nwau pweIAY nwnk gux gwvY ]7] (1240-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) gurmatee naa-o paa-ee-ai naanak gun gaavai. ||7||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v7	Through the Guru's Teachings, the Name is obtained; O Nanak, sing His Glorious Praises. ||7||
DEFINE	para 54366	duK ivic jMmxu duiK mrxu duiK vrqxu sMswir ] (1240-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) dukh vich jaman dukh maran dukh vartan sansaar. In pain, we are born; in pain, we die. In pain, we deal with the world.
RECORD	para 54367	duKu duKu AgY AwKIAY piV@ piV@ krih pukwr ] (1240-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) dukh dukh agai aakhee-ai parh H parh H karahi pukaar. Hereafter, there is said to be pain, only pain; the more the mortals read, the more they cry out.
DEFINE	para 54368	duK kIAw pMfw Kul@IAw suKu n inkilE koie ] (1240-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) dukh kee-aa pandaa khulHee-aa sukh na nikli-o ko-ay. The packages of pain are untied, but peace does not emerge.
RECORD	para 54369	duK ivic jIau jlwieAw duKIAw cilAw roie ] (1240-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) dukh vich jee-o jalaa-i-aa dukhee-aa chali-aa ro-ay. In pain, the soul burns; in pain, it departs weeping and wailing.
RECORD	para 54370	nwnk isPqI riqAw mnu qnu hirAw hoie ] (1240-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak siftee rati-aa man tan hari-aa ho-ay. O Nanak, imbued with the Lord's Praise, the mind and body blossom forth, rejuvenated.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	duK kIAw AgI mwrIAih BI duKu dwrU hoie ]1] (1240-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) dukh kee-aa agee maaree-ah bhee dukh daaroo ho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	In the fire of pain, the mortals die; but pain is also the cure. ||1||
RECORD	para 54372	mhlw 1 ] (1240-15) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54373	nwnk dunIAw Bsu rMgu BsU hU Bsu Kyh ] (1240-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak dunee-aa bhas rang bhasoo hoo bhas khayh. O Nanak, worldly pleasures are nothing more than dust. They are the dust of the dust of ashes.
DEFINE	para 54374	Bso Bsu kmwvxI BI Bsu BrIAY dyh ] (1240-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) bhaso bhas kamaavnee bhee bhas bharee-ai dayh. The mortal earns only the dust of the dust; his body is covered with dust.
DEFINE	para 54375	jw jIau ivchu kFIAY BsU BirAw jwie ] (1240-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) jaa jee-o vichahu kadhee-ai bhasoo bhari-aa jaa-ay. When the soul is taken out of the body, it too is covered with dust.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	AgY lyKY mMigAY hor dsUxI pwie ]2] (1240-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) agai laykhai mangi-ai hor dasoonee paa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	And when one's account is called for in the world hereafter, he receives only ten times more dust. ||2||
RECORD	para 54377	pauVI ] (1240-17) pa-orhee. Pauree:
UPHOLD	para 54378	nwie suixAY suic sMjmo jmu nyiV n AwvY ] (1240-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai such sanjamo jam nayrh na aavai. Hearing the Name, one is blessed with purity and self-control, and the Messenger of Death will not draw near.
DEFINE	para 54379	nwie suixAY Git cwnxw Awn@yru gvwvY ] (1240-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai ghat chaannaa aan Hayr gavaavai. Hearing the Name, the heart is illumined, and darkness is dispelled.
RECORD	para 54380	nwie suixAY Awpu buJIAY lwhw nwau pwvY ] (1240-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai aap bujhee-ai laahaa naa-o paavai. Hearing the Name, one comes to understand his own self, and the profit of the Name is obtained.
DEFINE	para 54381	nwie suixAY pwp ktIAih inrml scu pwvY ] (1240-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay suni-ai paap katee-ah nirmal sach paavai. Hearing the Name, sins are eradicated, and one meets the Immaculate True Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v8	nwnk nwie suixAY muK aujly nwau gurmuiK iDAwvY ]8] (1240-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak naa-ay suni-ai mukh ujlay naa-o gurmukh Dhi-aavai. ||8||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v8	O Nanak, hearing the Name, one's face becomes radiant. As Gurmukh, meditate on the Name. ||8||
DEFINE	para 54384	Gir nwrwiexu sBw nwil ] (1240-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) ghar naaraa-in sabhaa naal. In your home, is the Lord God, along with all your other gods.
RECORD	para 54385	pUj kry rKY nwvwil ] (1241-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) pooj karay rakhai naavaal. You wash your stone gods and worship them.
RECORD	para 54387	kuMgU cMnxu Pul cVwey ] (1241-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) kungoo channan ful charhaa-ay. You offer saffron, sandalwood and flowers.
RECORD	para 54388	pYrI pY pY bhuqu mnwey ] (1241-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) pairee pai pai bahut manaa-ay. Falling at their feet, you try so hard to appease them.
RECORD	para 54389	mwxUAw mMig mMig pYn@Y Kwie ] (1241-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) maanoo-aa mang mang pain Hai khaa-ay. Begging, begging from other people, you get things to wear and eat.
RECORD	para 54390	AMDI kMmI AMD sjwie ] (1241-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) anDhee kammee anDh sajaa-ay. For your blind deeds, you will be blindly punished.
RECORD	para 54391	BuiKAw dyie n mridAw rKY ] (1241-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) bhukhi-aa day-ay na mardi-aa rakhai. Your idol does not feed the hungry, or save the dying.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	AMDw JgVw AMDI sQY ]1] (1241-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) anDhaa jhagrhaa anDhee sathai. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	The blind assembly argues in blindness. ||1||
RECORD	para 54393	mhlw 1 ] (1241-3) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54394	sBy surqI jog siB sBy byd purwx ] (1241-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay surtee jog sabh sabhay bayd puraan. All intuitive understanding, all Yoga, all the Vedas and Puraanas.
UPHOLD	para 54395	sBy krxy qp siB sBy gIq igAwn ] (1241-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay karnay tap sabh sabhay geet gi-aan. All actions, all penances, all songs and spiritual wisdom.
RECORD	para 54396	sBy buDI suiD siB siB qIrQ siB Qwn ] (1241-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay buDhee suDh sabh sabh tirath sabh thaan. All intellect, all enlightenment, all sacred shrines of pilgrimage.
RECORD	para 54397	siB pwiqswhIAw Amr siB siB KusIAw siB Kwn ] (1241-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabh paatisaahee-aa amar sabh sabh khusee-aa sabh khaan. All kingdoms, all royal commands, all joys and all delicacies.
RECORD	para 54398	sBy mwxs dyv siB sBy jog iDAwn ] (1241-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay maanas dayv sabh sabhay jog Dhi-aan. All mankind, all divinites, all Yoga and meditation.
RECORD	para 54399	sBy purIAw KMf siB sBy jIA jhwn ] (1241-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay puree-aa khand sabh sabhay jee-a jahaan. All worlds, all celestial realms; all the beings of the universe.
RECORD	para 54400	hukim clwey AwpxY krmI vhY klwm ] (1241-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) hukam chalaa-ay aapnai karmee vahai kalaam. According to His Hukam, He commands them. His Pen writes out the account of their actions.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk scw sic nwie scu sBw dIbwnu ]2] (1241-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak sachaa sach naa-ay sach sabhaa deebaan. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, True is the Lord, and True is His Name. True is His Congregation and His Court. ||2||
RECORD	para 54402	pauVI ] (1241-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
ALLOW	para 54403	nwie mMinAY suKu aUpjY nwmy giq hoeI ] (1241-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai sukh oopjai naamay gat ho-ee. With faith in the Name, peace wells up; the Name brings emancipation.
DEFINE	para 54404	nwie mMinAY piq pweIAY ihrdY hir soeI ] (1241-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai pat paa-ee-ai hirdai har so-ee. With faith in the Name, honor is obtained. The Lord is enshrined in the heart.
RECORD	para 54405	nwie mMinAY Bvjlu lµGIAY iPir ibGnu n hoeI ] (1241-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai bhavjal langhee-ai fir bighan na ho-ee. With faith in the Name, one crosses over the terrifying world-ocean, and no obstructions are ever again encountered.
ALLOW	para 54406	nwie mMinAY pMQu prgtw nwmy sB loeI ] (1241-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai panth pargataa naamay sabh lo-ee. With faith in the Name, the Path is revealed; through the Name, one is totally enlightened.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v9	nwnk siqguir imilAY nwau mMnIAY ijn dyvY soeI ]9] (1241-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak satgur mili-ai naa-o mannee-ai jin dayvai so-ee. ||9||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v9	O Nanak, meeting with the True Guru, one comes to have faith in the Name; he alone has faith, who is blessed with it. ||9||
RECORD	para 54408	slok mÚ 1 ] (1241-9) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54409	purIAw KMfw isir kry iek pYir iDAwey ] (1241-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) puree-aa khanda sir karay ik pair Dhi-aa-ay. The mortal walks on his head through the worlds and realms; he meditates, balaced on one foot.
RECORD	para 54410	pauxu mwir min jpu kry isru muMfI qlY dyie ] (1241-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) pa-un maar man jap karay sir mundee talai day-ay. Controlling the wind of the breath, he meditates within his mind, tucking his chin down into his chest.
RECORD	para 54411	iksu aupir Ehu itk itkY iks no joru kryie ] (1241-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) kis upar oh tik tikai kis no jor karay-i. What does he lean on? Where does he get his power?
DEFINE	para 54412	iks no khIAY nwnkw iks no krqw dyie ] (1241-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) kis no kahee-ai naankaa kis no kartaa day-ay. What can be said, O Nanak? Who is blessed by the Creator?
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	hukim rhwey AwpxY mUrKu Awpu gxyie ]1] (1241-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) hukam rahaa-ay aapnai moorakh aap ganay-ay. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	God keeps all under His Command, but the fool shows off himself. ||1||
RECORD	para 54414	mÚ 1 ] (1241-11) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54415	hY hY AwKW koit koit kotI hU koit koit ] (1241-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) hai hai aakhaa N kot kot kotee hoo kot kot. He is, He is - I say it millions upon millions, millions upon millions of times.
DEFINE	para 54416	AwKUM AwKW sdw sdw khix n AwvY qoit ] (1241-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) aakhooN aakhaaN sadaa sadaa kahan na aavai tot. With my mouth I say it, forever and ever; there is no end to this speech.
DEFINE	para 54417	nw hau QkW n TwkIAw eyvf rKih joiq ] (1241-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa ha-o thakaa N na thaakee-aa ayvad rakheh jot. I do not get tired, and I will not be stopped; this is how great my determination is.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk cisAhu cuK ibMd aupir AwKxu dosu ]2] (1241-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak chasi-ahu chukh bind upar aakhan dos. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, this is tiny and insignificant. To say that it is more, is wrong. ||2||
RECORD	para 54419	pauVI ] (1241-13) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54420	nwie mMinAY kulu auDrY sBu kutMbu sbwieAw ] (1241-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai kul uDhrai sabh kutamb sabaa-i-aa. With faith in the Name, all one's ancestors and family are saved.
DEFINE	para 54421	nwie mMinAY sMgiq auDrY ijn irdY vswieAw ] (1241-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai sangat uDhrai jin ridai vasaa-i-aa. With faith in the Name, one's associates are saved; enshrine it within your heart.
DEFINE	para 54422	nwie mMinAY suix auDry ijn rsn rswieAw ] (1241-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai sun uDhray jin rasan rasaa-i-aa. With faith in the Name, those who hear it are saved; let your tongue delight in it.
RECORD	para 54423	nwie mMinAY duK BuK geI ijn nwim icqu lwieAw ] (1241-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai dukh bhukh ga-ee jin naam chit laa-i-aa. With faith in the Name, pain and hunger are dispelled; let your consciousness be attached to the Name.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v10	nwnk nwmu iqnI swlwihAw ijn gurU imlwieAw ]10] (1241-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak naam tinee salaahi-aa jin guroo milaa-i-aa. ||10||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v10	O Nanak, they alone Praise the Name, who meet with the Guru. ||10||
RECORD	para 54425	slok mÚ 1 ] (1241-16) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54426	sBy rwqI siB idh siB iQqI siB vwr ] (1241-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay raatee sabh dih sabh thitee sabh vaar. All nights, all days, all dates, all days of the week;
RECORD	para 54427	sBy ruqI mwh siB siB DrqˆØI siB Bwr ] (1241-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay rutee maah sabh sabh Dhartee N sabh bhaar. All seasons, all months, all the earth and everything on it.
RECORD	para 54428	sBy pwxI paux siB siB AgnI pwqwl ] (1241-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay paanee pa-un sabh sabh agnee paataal. All waters, all winds, all fires and underworlds.
RECORD	para 54429	sBy purIAw KMf siB siB loA loA Awkwr ] (1241-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabhay puree-aa khand sabh sabh lo-a lo-a aakaar. All solar systems and galaxies, all worlds, people and forms.
RECORD	para 54430	hukmu n jwpI kyqVw kih n skIjY kwr ] (1241-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) hukam na jaapee kayt-rhaa kahi na sakeejai kaar. No one knows how great the Hukam of His Command is; no one can describe His actions.
ALLOW	para 54431	AwKih Qkih AwiK AwiK kir isPqˆØI vIcwr ] (1241-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) aakhahi thakeh aakh aakh kar siftee N veechaar. Mortals may utter, chant, recite and contemplate His Praises until they grow weary.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	iqRxu n pwieE bpuVI nwnku khY gvwr ]1] (1241-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) tarin na paa-i-o bapurhee naanak kahai gavaar. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	The poor fools, O Nanak, cannot find even a tiny bit of the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 54433	mÚ 1 ] (1241-19) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
WHEN	para 54434	AKˆØI prxY jy iPrW dyKW sBu Awkwru ] (1241-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) akhee N parnai jay firaa N daykhaaN sabh aakaar. If I were to walk around with my eyes wide open, gazing at all the created forms;
RECORD	para 54435	puCw igAwnI pMifqW puCw byd bIcwr ] (1241-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) puchhaa gi-aanee pandhitaaN puchhaa bayd beechaar. I could ask the spiritual teachers and religious scholars, and those who contemplate the Vedas;
RECORD	para 54437	puCw dyvW mwxsW joD krih Avqwr ] (1242-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) puchhaa dayvaaN maansaaN joDh karahi avtaar. I could ask the gods, mortal men, warriors and divine incarnations;
RECORD	para 54438	isD smwDI siB suxI jwie dyKW drbwru ] (1242-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) siDh samaaDhee sabh sunee jaa-ay daykhaaN darbaar. I could consult all the Siddhas in Samaadhi, and go to see the Lord's Court.
DEFINE	para 54439	AgY scw sic nwie inrBau BY ivxu swru ] (1242-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) agai sachaa sach naa-ay nirbha-o bhai vin saar. Hereafter, Truth is the Name of all; the Fearless Lord has no fear at all.
DEFINE	para 54440	hor kcI mqI kcu ipcu AMiDAw AMDu bIcwru ] (1242-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) hor kachee matee kach pich anDhi-aa anDh beechaar. False are other intellectualisms, false and shallow; blind are the contemplations of the blind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk krmI bMdgI ndir lµGwey pwir ]2] (1242-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak karmee bandagee nadar langhaa-ay paar. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, by the karma of good actions, the mortal comes to meditate on the Lord; by His Grace, we are carried across. ||2||
RECORD	para 54442	pauVI ] (1242-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54443	nwie mMinAY durmiq geI miq prgtI AwieAw ] (1242-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai durmat ga-ee mat pargatee aa-i-aa. With faith in the Name, evil-mindedness is eradicated, and the intellect is enlightened.
DEFINE	para 54444	nwau mMinAY haumY geI siB rog gvwieAw ] (1242-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-o mani-ai ha-umai ga-ee sabh rog gavaa-i-aa. With faith in the Name, egotism is eradicated, and all sickness is cured.
RECORD	para 54445	nwie mMinAY nwmu aUpjY shjy suKu pwieAw ] (1242-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai naam oopjai sehjay sukh paa-i-aa. Believing in the Name, The Name wells up, and intuitive peace and poise are obtained.
DEFINE	para 54446	nwie mMinAY sWiq aUpjY hir mMin vswieAw ] (1242-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai saa Nt oopjai har man vasaa-i-aa. Believing in the Name, tranquility and peace well up, and the Lord is enshrined in the mind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v11	nwnk nwmu rqMnu hY gurmuiK hir iDAwieAw ]11] (1242-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak naam ratann hai gurmukh har Dhi-aa-i-aa. ||11||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v11	O Nanak, the Name is a jewel; the Gurmukh meditates on the Lord. ||11||
RECORD	para 54448	slok mÚ 1 ] (1242-6) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
WHEN	para 54449	horu srIku hovY koeI qyrw iqsu AgY quDu AwKW ] (1242-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) hor sareek hovai ko-ee tayraa tis agai tuDh aakhaaN. If there were any other equal to You, O Lord, I would speak to them of You.
RECORD	para 54450	quDu AgY quDY swlwhI mY AMDy nwau sujwKw ] (1242-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) tuDh agai tuDhai saalaahee mai anDhay naa-o sujaakhaa. You, I praise You; I am blind, but through the Name, I am all-seeing.
DEFINE	para 54451	jyqw AwKxu swhI sbdI BwiKAw Bwie suBweI ] (1242-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) jaytaa aakhan saahee sabdee bhaakhi-aa bhaa-ay subhaa-ee. Whatever is spoken, is the Word of the Shabad. Chanting it with love, we are embellished.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk bhuqw eyho AwKxu sB qyrI vifAweI ]1] (1242-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak bahutaa ayho aakhan sabh tayree vadi-aa-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	Nanak, this is the greatest thing to say: all glorious greatness is Yours. ||1||
RECORD	para 54453	mÚ 1 ] (1242-8) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
ALLOW	para 54454	jW n isAw ikAw cwkrI jW jMmy ikAw kwr ] (1242-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) jaa N na si-aa ki-aa chaakree jaa N jammay ki-aa kaar. When there was nothing, what happened? What happens when one is born?
RECORD	para 54455	siB kwrx krqw kry dyKY vwro vwr ] (1242-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabh kaaran kartaa karay daykhai vaaro vaar. The Creator, the Doer, does all; He watches over all, again and again
RECORD	para 54456	jy cupY jy mMigAY dwiq kry dwqwru ] (1242-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) jay chupai jay mangi-ai daat karay daataar. . Whether we keep silent or beg out loud, the Great Giver blesses us with His gifts.
DEFINE	para 54457	ieku dwqw siB mMgqy iPir dyKih Awkwru ] (1242-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) ik daataa sabh mangtay fir daykheh aakaar. The One Lord is the Giver; we are all beggars. I have seen this throughout the Universe.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk eyvY jwxIAY jIvY dyvxhwru ]2] (1242-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak ayvai jaanee-ai jeevai dayvanhaar. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	Nanak knows this: the Great Giver lives forever. ||2||
RECORD	para 54459	pauVI ] (1242-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
ALLOW	para 54460	nwie mMinAY suriq aUpjY nwmy miq hoeI ] (1242-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai surat oopjai naamay mat ho-ee. With faith in the Name, intuitive awareness wells up; through the Name, intelligence comes.
ALLOW	para 54461	nwie mMinAY gux aucrY nwmy suiK soeI ] (1242-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai gun uchrai naamay sukh so-ee. With faith in the Name, chant the Glories of God; through the Name, peace is obtained.
DEFINE	para 54462	nwie mMinAY BRmu ktIAY iPir duKu n hoeI ] (1242-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai bharam katee-ai fir dukh na ho-ee. With faith in the Name, doubt is eradicated, and the mortal never suffers again.
REQUIRE	para 54463	nwie mMinAY swlwhIAY pwpW miq DoeI ] (1242-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) naa-ay mani-ai salaahee-ai paapaa N mat Dho-ee. With faith in the Name, sing His Praises, and your sinful intellect shall be washed clean.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v12	nwnk pUry gur qy nwau mMnIAY ijn dyvY soeI ]12] (1242-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak pooray gur tay naa-o mannee-ai jin dayvai so-ee. ||12||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v12	O Nanak, through the Perfect Guru, one comes to have faith in the Name; they alone receive it, unto whom He gives it. ||12||
RECORD	para 54465	slok mÚ 1 ] (1242-12) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54466	swsqR byd purwx pV@Mqw ] (1242-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) saastar bayd puraan parh HaNtaa. Some read the Shaastras, the Vedas and the Puraanas.
RECORD	para 54467	pUkwrMqw AjwxMqw ] (1242-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) pookaarantaa ajaanantaa. They recite them, out of ignorance.
WHEN	para 54468	jW bUJY qW sUJY soeI ] (1242-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) jaa N boojhai taaN soojhai so-ee. If they really understood them, they would realize the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnku AwKY kUk n hoeI ]1] (1242-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak aakhai kook na ho-ee. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	Nanak says, there is no need to shout so loud. ||1||
RECORD	para 54470	mÚ 1 ] (1242-14) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54471	jW hau qyrw qW sBu ikCu myrw hau nwhI qU hovih ] (1242-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) jaa N ha-o tayraa taaN sabh kichh mayraa ha-o naahee too hoveh. When I am Yours, then everything is mine. When I am not, You are.
RECORD	para 54472	Awpy skqw Awpy surqw skqI jgqu provih ] (1242-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) aapay saktaa aapay surtaa saktee jagat paroveh. You Yourself are All-powerful, and You Yourself are the Intuitive Knower. The whole world is strung on the Power of Your Shakti.
RECORD	para 54473	Awpy Byjy Awpy sdy rcnw ric ric vyKY ] (1242-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) aapay bhayjay aapay saday rachnaa rach rach vaykhai. You Yourself send out the mortal beings, and You Yourself call them back home. Having created the creation, You behold it.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk scw scI nWeI scu pvY Duir lyKY ]2] (1242-15, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak sachaa sachee naa N-ee sach pavai Dhur laykhai. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, True is the Name of the True Lord; through Truth, one is accepted by the Primal Lord God. ||2||
RECORD	para 54475	pauVI ] (1242-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54476	nwmu inrMjn AlKu hY ikau liKAw jweI ] (1242-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) naam niranjan alakh hai ki-o lakhi-aa jaa-ee. The Name of the Immaculate Lord is unknowable. How can it be known?
DEFINE	para 54477	nwmu inrMjn nwil hY ikau pweIAY BweI ] (1242-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) naam niranjan naal hai ki-o paa-ee-ai bhaa-ee. The Name of the Immaculate Lord is with the mortal being. How can it be obtained, O Siblings of Destiny?
DEFINE	para 54478	nwmu inrMjn vrqdw rivAw sB TWeI ] (1242-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) naam niranjan varatdaa ravi-aa sabh thaaN-ee. The Name of the Immaculate Lord is all-pervading and permeating everywhere.
DEFINE	para 54479	gur pUry qy pweIAY ihrdY dyie idKweI ] (1242-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) gur pooray tay paa-ee-ai hirdai day-ay dikhaa-ee. Through the Perfect Guru, it is obtained. It is revealed within the heart.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v13	nwnk ndrI krmu hoie gur imlIAY BweI ]13] (1242-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak nadree karam ho-ay gur milee-ai bhaa-ee. ||13||
WHEN	slok mhlw 1 v13	O Nanak, when the Merciful Lord grants His Grace, the mortal meets with the Guru, O Siblings of Desitny. ||13||
RECORD	para 54481	slok mÚ 1 ] (1242-18) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54482	kil hoeI kuqy muhI Kwju hoAw murdwru ] (1242-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) kal ho-ee kutay muhee khaaj ho-aa murdaar. In this Dark Age of Kali Yuga, people have faces like dogs; they eat rotting carcasses for food.
UPHOLD	para 54483	kUVu boil boil Baukxw cUkw Drmu bIcwru ] (1242-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) koorh bol bol bha-ukanaa chookaa Dharam beechaar. They bark and speak, telling only lies; all thought of righteousness has left them.
RECORD	para 54484	ijn jIvMidAw piq nhI muieAw mMdI soie ] (1242-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) jin jeevandi-aa pat nahee mu-i-aa mandee so-ay. Those who have no honor while alive, will have an evil reputation after they die.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	iliKAw hovY nwnkw krqw kry su hoie ]1] (1243-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) likhi-aa hovai naankaa kartaa karay so ho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	Whatever is predestined, happens, O Nanak; whatever the Creator does, comes to pass. ||1||
RECORD	para 54487	mÚ 1 ] (1243-1) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54488	rMnw hoeIAw boDIAw purs hoey seIAwd ] (1243-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) rannaa ho-ee-aa boDhee-aa puras ho-ay sa-ee-aad. Women have become advisors, and men have become hunters.
FORBID	para 54489	sIlu sMjmu suc BMnI Kwxw Kwju Ahwju ] (1243-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) seel sanjam such bhannee khaanaa khaaj ahaaj. Humility, self-control and purity have run away; people eat the uneatable, forbidden food.
RECORD	para 54490	srmu gieAw Gir AwpxY piq auiT clI nwil ] (1243-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) saram ga-i-aa ghar aapnai pat uth chalee naal. Modesty has left her home, and honor has gone away with her.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk scw eyku hY Aauru n scw Bwil ]2] (1243-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak sachaa ayk hai a-or na sachaa bhaal. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, there is only One True Lord; do not bother to search for any other as true. ||2||
RECORD	para 54492	pauVI ] (1243-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54493	bwhir Bsm lypn kry AMqir gubwrI ] (1243-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) baahar bhasam laypan karay antar gubaaree. You smear your outer body with ashes, but within, you are filled with darkness.
RECORD	para 54494	iKMQw JolI bhu ByK kry durmiq AhMkwrI ] (1243-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) khinthaa jholee baho bhaykh karay durmat aha Nkaaree. You wear the patched coat and all the right clothes and robes, but you are still egotistical and proud.
DEFINE	para 54495	swihb sbdu n aUcrY mwieAw moh pswrI ] (1243-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) saahib sabad na oochrai maa-i-aa moh pasaaree. You do not chant the Shabad, the Word of Your Lord and Master; you are attached to the expanse of Maya.
DEFINE	para 54496	AMqir lwlcu Brmu hY BrmY gwvwrI ] (1243-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) antar laalach bharam hai bharmai gaavaaree. Within, you are filled with greed and doubt; you wander around like a fool.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v14	nwnk nwmu n cyqeI jUAY bwjI hwrI ]14] (1243-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak naam na chayt-ee joo-ai baajee haaree. ||14||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v14	Says Nanak, you never even think of the Naam; you have lost the game of life in the gamble. ||14||
RECORD	para 54498	slok mÚ 1 ] (1243-5) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
ALLOW	para 54499	lK isau pRIiq hovY lK jIvxu ikAw KusIAw ikAw cwau ] (1243-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) lakh si-o pareet hovai lakh jeevan ki-aa khusee-aa ki-aa chaa-o. You may be in love with tens of thousands, and live for thousands of years; but what good are these pleasures and occupations?
REQUIRE	para 54500	ivCuiVAw ivsu hoie ivCoVw eyk GVI mih jwie ] (1243-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) vichhurhi-aa vis ho-ay vichhorhaa ayk gharhee meh jaa-ay. And when you must separate from them, that separation is like poison, but they will be gone in an instant.
ALLOW	para 54501	jy sau virHAw imTw KwjY BI iPir kauVw Kwie ] (1243-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) jay sa-o var Hi-aa mithaa khaajai bhee fir ka-urhaa khaa-ay. You may eat sweets for a hundred years, but eventually, you will have to eat the bitter as well.
RECORD	para 54502	imTw KwDw iciq n AwvY kauVqxu Dwie jwie ] (1243-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) mithaa khaaDhaa chit na aavai ka-urh-tan Dhaa-ay jaa-ay. Then, you will not remember eating the sweets; bitterness will permeate you.
DEFINE	para 54503	imTw kauVw dovY rog ] (1243-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) mithaa ka-urhaa dovai rog. The sweet and the bitter are both diseases.
RECORD	para 54504	nwnk AMiq ivguqy Bog ] (1243-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak ant vigutay bhog. O Nanak, eating them, you will come to ruin in the end.
DEFINE	para 54505	JiK JiK JKxw JgVw JwK ] (1243-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) jhakh jhakh jhakh-naa jhagrhaa jhaakh. It is useless to worry and struggle to death.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	JiK JiK jwih JKih iqn@ pwis ]1] (1243-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) jhakh jhakh jaahi jhakheh tin H paas. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	Entangled in worries and struggles, people exhaust themselves. ||1||
RECORD	para 54507	mÚ 1 ] (1243-9) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54508	kwpVu kwTu rMgwieAw rWig ] (1243-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) kaaparh kaath rangaa-i-aa raa Ng. They have fine clothes and furniture of various colors.
DEFINE	para 54509	Gr gc kIqy bwgy bwg ] (1243-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) ghar gach keetay baagay baag. Their houses are painted beautifully white.
RECORD	para 54510	swd shj kir mnu KylwieAw ] (1243-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) saad sahj kar man khaylaa-i-aa. In pleasure and poise, they play their mind games.
REQUIRE	para 54511	qY sh pwshu khxu khwieAw ] (1243-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) tai sah paashu kahan kahaa-i-aa. When they approach You, O Lord, they shall be spoken to.
DEFINE	para 54512	imTw kir kY kauVw KwieAw ] (1243-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) mithaa kar kai ka-urhaa khaa-i-aa. They think it is sweet, so they eat the bitter.
RECORD	para 54513	iqin kauVY qin rogu jmwieAw ] (1243-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) tin ka-urhai tan rog jamaa-i-aa. The bitter disease grows in the body.
RECORD	para 54514	jy iPir imTw pyVY pwie ] (1243-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) jay fir mithaa payrhai paa-ay. If, later on, they receive the sweet,
REQUIRE	para 54515	qau kauVqxu cUkis mwie ] (1243-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) ta-o ka-urh-tan chookas maa-ay. then their bitterness shall be gone, O mother.
DEFINE	para 54516	nwnk gurmuiK pwvY soie ] (1243-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh paavai so-ay. O Nanak, the Gurmukh is blessed to receive
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	ijs no pRwpiq iliKAw hoie ]2] (1243-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) jis no paraapat likhi-aa ho-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	what he is predestined to receive. ||2||
RECORD	para 54518	pauVI ] (1243-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
ALLOW	para 54519	ijn kY ihrdY mYlu kptu hY bwhru DovwieAw ] (1243-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) jin kai hirdai mail kapat hai baahar Dhovaa-i-aa. Those whose hearts are filled with the filth of deception, may wash themselves on the outside.
DEFINE	para 54520	kUVu kptu kmwvdy kUVu prgtI AwieAw ] (1243-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) koorh kapat kamaavday koorh pargatee aa-i-aa. They practice falsehood and deception, and their falsehood is revealed.
DEFINE	para 54521	AMdir hoie su inklY nh CpY CpwieAw ] (1243-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) andar ho-ay so niklai nah chhapai chhapaa-i-aa. That which is within them, comes out; it cannot be concealed by concealment.
DEFINE	para 54522	kUVY lwlic ligAw iPir jUnI pwieAw ] (1243-13, swrMg, mÚ 1) koorhai laalach lagi-aa fir joonee paa-i-aa. Attached to falsehood and greed, the mortal is consigned to reincarnation over and over again.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v15	nwnk jo bIjY so Kwvxw krqY iliK pwieAw ]15] (1243-14, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak jo beejai so khaavnaa kartai likh paa-i-aa. ||15||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 1 v15	O Nanak, whatever the mortal plants, he must eat. The Creator Lord has written our destiny. ||15||
RECORD	para 54524	slok mÚ 2 ] (1243-14) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
RECORD	para 54525	kQw khwxI bydˆØI AwxI pwpu puMnu bIcwru ] (1243-15, swrMg, mÚ 2) kathaa kahaanee baydee N aanee paap punn beechaar. The Vedas bring forth stories and legends, and thoughts of vice and virtue.
DEFINE	para 54526	dy dy lYxw lY lY dyxw nrik surig Avqwr ] (1243-15, swrMg, mÚ 2) day day lainaa lai lai daynaa narak surag avtaar. What is given, they receive, and what is received, they give. They are reincarnated in heaven and hell.
RECORD	para 54527	auqm miDm jwqIN ijnsI Brim BvY sMswru ] (1243-15, swrMg, mÚ 2) utam maDhim jaatee N jinsee bharam bhavai sansaar. High and low, social class and status - the world wanders lost in superstition.
UPHOLD	para 54528	AMimRq bwxI qqu vKwxI igAwn iDAwn ivic AweI ] (1243-16, swrMg, mÚ 2) amrit banee tat vakhaanee gi-aan Dhi-aan vich aa-ee. The Ambrosial Word of Gurbani proclaims the essence of reality. Spiritual wisdom and meditation are contained within it.
RECORD	para 54529	gurmuiK AwKI gurmuiK jwqI surqˆØI krim iDAweI ] (1243-17, swrMg, mÚ 2) gurmukh aakhee gurmukh jaatee surtee N karam Dhi-aa-ee. The Gurmukhs chant it, and the Gurmukhs realize it. Intuitively aware, they meditate on it.
RECORD	para 54530	hukmu swij hukmY ivic rKY hukmY AMdir vyKY ] (1243-17, swrMg, mÚ 2) hukam saaj hukmai vich rakhai hukmai andar vaykhai. By the Hukam of His Command, He formed the Universe, and in His Hukam, He keeps it. By His Hukam, He keeps it under His Gaze.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk Aghu haumY qutY qW ko ilKIAY lyKY ]1] (1243-18, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak agahu ha-umai tutai taaN ko likee-ai laykhai. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, if the mortal shatters his ego before he departs, as it is pre-ordained, then he is approved. ||1||
RECORD	para 54532	mÚ 1 ] (1243-18) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54533	bydu pukwry puMnu pwpu surg nrk kw bIau ] (1243-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) bayd pukaaray punn paap surag narak kaa bee-o. The Vedas proclaim that vice and virtue are the seeds of heaven and hell.
REQUIRE	para 54534	jo bIjY so augvY KWdw jwxY jIau ] (1243-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) jo beejai so ugvai khaa Ndaa jaanai jee-o. Whatever is planted, shall grow. The soul eats the fruits of its actions, and understands.
UPHOLD	para 54535	igAwnu slwhy vfw kir sco scw nwau ] (1243-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) gi-aan salaahay vadaa kar sacho sachaa naa-o. Whoever praises spiritual wisdom as great, becomes truthful in the True Name.
REQUIRE	para 54536	scu bIjY scu augvY drgh pweIAY Qwau ] (1243-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) sach beejai sach ugvai dargeh paa-ee-ai thaa-o. When Truth is planted, Truth grows. In the Court of the Lord, you shall find your place of honor.
DEFINE	para 54538	bydu vpwrI igAwnu rwis krmI plY hoie ] (1244-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) bayd vapaaree gi-aan raas karmee palai ho-ay. The Vedas are only merchants; spiritual wisdom is the capital; by His Grace, it is received.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk rwsI bwhrw lid n cilAw koie ]2] (1244-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak raasee baahraa lad na chali-aa ko-ay. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, without capital, no one has ever departed with profit. ||2||
RECORD	para 54540	pauVI ] (1244-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54541	inMmu ibrKu bhu sMcIAY AMimRq rsu pwieAw ] (1244-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) nimm birakh baho sanchee-ai amrit ras paa-i-aa. You can water a bitter neem tree with ambrosial nectar.
RECORD	para 54542	ibsIAru mMiqR ivswhIAY bhu dUDu pIAwieAw ] (1244-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) bisee-ar mantar visaahee-ai baho dooDh pee-aa-i-aa. You can feed a venomous snake lots of milk.
DEFINE	para 54543	mnmuKu AiBMnu n iBjeI pQru nwvwieAw ] (1244-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) manmukh abhinn na bhij-ee pathar navaa-i-aa. The self-willed manmukh is resistant; he cannot be softened. You might as well water a stone.
DEFINE	para 54544	ibKu mih AMimRqu isMcIAY ibKu kw Plu pwieAw ] (1244-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) bikh meh amrit sinchee-ai bikh kaa fal paa-i-aa. Irrigating a poisonous plant with ambrosial nectar, only poisonous fruit is obtained.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v16	nwnk sMgiq myil hir sB ibKu lih jwieAw ]16] (1244-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak sangat mayl har sabh bikh leh jaa-i-aa. ||16||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v16	O Lord, please unite Nanak with the Sangat, the Holy Congregation, so that he may be rid of all poison. ||16||
RECORD	para 54546	slok mÚ 1 ] (1244-4) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54547	mrix n mUrqu puiCAw puCI iQiq n vwru ] (1244-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) maran na moorat puchhi-aa puchhee thit na vaar. Death does not ask the time; it does not ask the date or the day of the week.
RECORD	para 54548	iekn@I lidAw ieik lid cly iekn@I bDy Bwr ] (1244-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) ikn Hee ladi-aa ik lad chalay ikn Hee baDhay bhaar. Some have packed up, and some who have packed up have gone.
DEFINE	para 54549	iekn@w hoeI swKqI iekn@w hoeI swr ] (1244-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) ikn Haa ho-ee saakh-tee iknHaa ho-ee saar. Some are severely punished, and some are taken care of.
REQUIRE	para 54550	lskr sxY dmwimAw Cuty bMk duAwr ] (1244-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) laskar sanai damaami-aa chhutay bank du-aar. They must leave their armies and drums, and their beautiful mansions.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk FyrI Cwru kI BI iPir hoeI Cwr ]1] (1244-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak dhayree chhaar kee bhee fir ho-ee chhaar. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, the pile of dust is once again reduced to dust. ||1||
RECORD	para 54552	mÚ 1 ] (1244-7) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
REQUIRE	para 54553	nwnk FyrI Fih peI imtI sMdw kotu ] (1244-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak dhayree dheh pa-ee mitee sandaa kot. O Nanak, the pile shall fall apart; the fortress of the body is made of dust.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	BIqir coru bhwilAw Kotu vy jIAw Kotu ]2] (1244-7, swrMg, mÚ 1) bheetar chor bahaali-aa khot vay jee-aa khot. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	The thief has settled within you; O soul, your life is false. ||2||
RECORD	para 54555	pauVI ] (1244-8) pa-orhee. Pauree:
REQUIRE	para 54556	ijn AMdir inMdw dustu hY nk vFy nk vFwieAw ] (1244-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) jin andar nindaa dusat hai nak vadhay nak vaDhaa-i-aa. Those who are filled with vicious slander, shall have their noses cut, and be shamed.
DEFINE	para 54557	mhw krUp duKIey sdw kwly muh mwieAw ] (1244-8, swrMg, mÚ 1) mahaa karoop dukhee-ay sadaa kaalay muh maa-i-aa. They are totally ugly, and always in pain. Their faces are blackened by Maya.
RECORD	para 54558	Blky auiT inq pr drbu ihrih hir nwmu curwieAw ] (1244-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) bhalkay uth nit par darab hireh har naam churaa-i-aa. They rise early in the morning, to cheat and steal from others; they hide from the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 54559	hir jIau iqn kI sMgiq mq krhu riK lyhu hir rwieAw ] (1244-9, swrMg, mÚ 1) har jee-o tin kee sangat mat karahu rakh layho har raa-i-aa. O Dear Lord, let me not even associate with them; save me from them, O my Sovereign Lord King.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v17	nwnk pieAY ikriq kmwvdy mnmuiK duKu pwieAw ]17] (1244-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak pa-i-ai kirat kamaavday manmukh dukh paa-i-aa. ||17||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v17	O Nanak, the self-willed manmukhs act according to their past deeds, producing nothing but pain. ||17||
RECORD	para 54561	slok mÚ 4 ] (1244-10) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 54562	sBu koeI hY Ksm kw Ksmhu sBu ko hoie ] (1244-11, swrMg, mÚ 4) sabh ko-ee hai khasam kaa khasmahu sabh ko ho-ay. Everyone belongs to our Lord and Master. Everyone came from Him.
DEFINE	para 54563	hukmu pCwxY Ksm kw qw scu pwvY koie ] (1244-11, swrMg, mÚ 4) hukam pachhaanai khasam kaa taa sach paavai ko-ay. Only by realizing the Hukam of His Command, is Truth obtained.
RECORD	para 54564	gurmuiK Awpu pCwxIAY burw n dIsY koie ] (1244-11, swrMg, mÚ 4) gurmukh aap pachhaanee-ai buraa na deesai ko-ay. The Gurmukh realizes his own self; no one appears evil to him.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk gurmuiK nwmu iDAweIAY sihlw AwieAw soie ]1] (1244-12, swrMg, mÚ 4) naanak gurmukh naam Dhi-aa-ee-ai sahilaa aa-i-aa so-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukh meditates on the Naam, the Name of the Lord. Fruitful is his coming into the world. ||1||
RECORD	para 54566	mÚ 4 ] (1244-13) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54567	sBnw dwqw Awip hY Awpy mylxhwru ] (1244-13, swrMg, mÚ 4) sabhnaa daataa aap hai aapay maylanhaar. He Himself is the Giver of all; He unites all with Himself.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk sbid imly n ivCuVih ijnw syivAw hir dwqwru ]2] (1244-13, swrMg, mÚ 4) naanak sabad milay na vichhurheh jinaa sayvi-aa har daataar. ||2||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, they are united with the Word of the Shabad; serving the Lord, the Great Giver, they shall never be separated from Him again. ||2||
RECORD	para 54569	pauVI ] (1244-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54570	gurmuiK ihrdY sWiq hY nwau augiv AwieAw ] (1244-14, swrMg, mÚ 4) gurmukh hirdai saa Nt hai naa-o ugav aa-i-aa. Peace and tranquility fill the heart of the Gurmukh; the Name wells up within them.
RECORD	para 54571	jp qp qIrQ sMjm kry myry pRB BwieAw ] (1244-14, swrMg, mÚ 4) jap tap tirath sanjam karay mayray parabh bhaa-i-aa. Chanting and meditation, penance and self-discipline, and bathing at sacred shrines of pilgrimage - the merits of these come by pleasing my God.
REQUIRE	para 54572	ihrdw suDu hir syvdy sohih gux gwieAw ] (1244-15, swrMg, mÚ 4) hirdaa suDh har sayvday soheh gun gaa-i-aa. So serve the Lord with a pure heart; singing His Glorious Praises, you shall be embellished and exalted.
DEFINE	para 54573	myry hir jIau eyvY Bwvdw gurmuiK qrwieAw ] (1244-15, swrMg, mÚ 4) mayray har jee-o ayvai bhaavdaa gurmukh taraa-i-aa. My Dear Lord is pleased by this; he carries the Gurmukh across.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v18	nwnk gurmuiK myilAnu hir dir sohwieAw ]18] (1244-16, swrMg, mÚ 4) naanak gurmukh mayli-an har dar sohaa-i-aa. ||18||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v18	O Nanak, the Gurmukh is merged with the Lord; he is embellished in His Court. ||18||
RECORD	para 54575	slok mÚ 1 ] (1244-16) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54576	DnvMqw iev hI khY AvrI Dn kau jwau ] (1244-16, swrMg, mÚ 1) Dhanvantaa iv hee kahai avree Dhan ka-o jaa-o. Thus speaks the wealthy man: I should go and get more wealth.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnku inrDnu iqqu idin ijqu idin ivsrY nwau ]1] (1244-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak nirDhan tit din jit din visrai naa-o. ||1||
WHEN	slok mhlw 1 v1	Nanak becomes poor on that day when he forgets the Lord's Name. ||1||
RECORD	para 54578	mÚ 1 ] (1244-17) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 54579	sUrju cVY ivjoig sBsY GtY Awrjw ] (1244-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) sooraj charhai vijog sabhsai ghatai aarjaa. The sun rises and sets, and the lives of all run out.
RECORD	para 54580	qnu mnu rqw Boig koeI hwrY ko ijxY ] (1244-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) tan man rataa bhog ko-ee haarai ko jinai. The mind and body experience pleasures; one loses, and another wins.
DEFINE	para 54581	sBu ko BirAw PUik AwKix khix n QMm@IAY ] (1244-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) sabh ko bhari-aa fook aakhan kahan na tham H-ee-ai. Everyone is puffed up with pride; even after they are spoken to, they do not stop.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk vyKY Awip PUk kFwey Fih pvY ]2] (1244-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak vaykhai aap fook kadhaa-ay dheh pavai. ||2||
WHEN	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, the Lord Himself sees all; when He takes the air out of the balloon, the body falls. ||2||
RECORD	para 54583	pauVI ] (1244-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54584	sqsMgiq nwmu inDwnu hY ijQhu hir pwieAw ] (1244-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) satsangat naam niDhaan hai jithahu har paa-i-aa. The treasure of the Name is in the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation. There, the Lord is found.
DEFINE	para 54586	gur prswdI Git cwnxw Awn@yru gvwieAw ] (1245-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) gur parsaadee ghat chaannaa aan Hayr gavaa-i-aa. By Guru's Grace, the heart is illumined, and darkness is dispelled.
DEFINE	para 54587	lohw pwris BytIAY kMcnu hoie AwieAw ] (1245-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) lohaa paaras bhaytee-ai kanchan ho-ay aa-i-aa. Iron is transformed into gold, when it touches the Philosopher's Stone.
RECORD	para 54588	nwnk siqguir imilAY nwau pweIAY imil nwmu iDAwieAw ] (1245-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak satgur mili-ai naa-o paa-ee-ai mil naam Dhi-aa-i-aa. O Nanak, meeting with the True Guru, the Name is obtained. Meeting Him, the mortal meditates on the Name.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v19	ijn@ kY poqY puMnu hY iqn@I drsnu pwieAw ]19] (1245-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) jin H kai potai punn hai tin Hee darsan paa-i-aa. ||19||
UPHOLD	slok mhlw 1 v19	Those who have virtue as their treasure, obtain the Blessed Vision of His Darshan. ||19||
RECORD	para 54590	slok mÚ 1 ] (1245-3) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54591	iDRgu iqnw kw jIivAw ij iliK iliK vycih nwau ] (1245-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) Dharig tinaa kaa jeevi-aa je likh likh vaycheh naa-o. Cursed are the lives of those who read and write the Lord's Name to sell it.
DEFINE	para 54592	KyqI ijn kI aujVY KlvwVy ikAw Qwau ] (1245-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) khaytee jin kee ujrhai khalvaarhay ki-aa thaa-o. Their crop is devastated - what harvest will they have?
FORBID	para 54593	scY srmY bwhry AgY lhih n dwid ] (1245-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) sachai sarmai baahray agai laheh na daad. Lacking truth and humility, they shall not be appreciated in the world hereafter.
DEFINE	para 54594	Akil eyh n AwKIAY Akil gvweIAY bwid ] (1245-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) akal ayh na aakhee-ai akal gavaa-ee-ai baad. Wisdom which leads to arguments is not called wisdom.
DEFINE	para 54595	AklI swihbu syvIAY AklI pweIAY mwnu ] (1245-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) aklee saahib sayvee-ai aklee paa-ee-ai maan. Wisdom leads us to serve our Lord and Master; through wisdom, honor is obtained.
UPHOLD	para 54596	AklI piV@ kY buJIAY AklI kIcY dwnu ] (1245-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) aklee parhH kai bujhee-ai aklee keechai daan. Wisdom does not come by reading textbooks; wisdom inspires us to give in charity.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnku AwKY rwhu eyhu hoir glW sYqwnu ]1] (1245-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak aakhai raahu ayhu hor galaa N saitaan. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	Says Nanak, this is the Path; other things lead to Satan. ||1||
RECORD	para 54598	mÚ 2 ] (1245-6) mehlaa 2. Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54599	jYsw krY khwvY qYsw AYsI bnI jrUriq ] (1245-6, swrMg, mÚ 2) jaisaa karai kahaavai taisaa aisee banee jaroorat. Mortals are known by their actions; this is the way it has to be.
RECORD	para 54600	hovih ilµ| iJM| nh hovih AYsI khIAY sUriq ] (1245-7, swrMg, mÚ 2) hoveh liny jhiny nah hoveh aisee kahee-ai soorat. They should show goodness, and not be deformed by their actions; this is how they are called beautiful.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	jo Esu ieCy so Plu pwey qW nwnk khIAY mUriq ]2] (1245-7, swrMg, mÚ 2) jo os ichhay so fal paa-ay taaN naanak kahee-ai moorat. ||2||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 1 v2	Whatever they desire, they shall receive; O Nanak, they become the very image of God. ||2||
RECORD	para 54602	pauVI ] (1245-8) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54603	siqguru AMimRq ibrKu hY AMimRq ris PilAw ] (1245-8, swrMg, mÚ 2) satgur amrit birakh hai amrit ras fali-aa. The True Guru is the tree of ambrosia. it bears the fruit of sweet nectar.
DEFINE	para 54604	ijsu prwpiq so lhY gur sbdI imilAw ] (1245-8, swrMg, mÚ 2) jis paraapat so lahai gur sabdee mili-aa. He alone receives it, who is so pre-destined, through the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
DEFINE	para 54605	siqgur kY BwxY jo clY hir syqI rilAw ] (1245-9, swrMg, mÚ 2) satgur kai bhaanai jo chalai har saytee rali-aa. One who walks in harmony with the Will of the True Guru, is blended with the Lord.
DEFINE	para 54606	jmkwlu joih n skeI Git cwnxu bilAw ] (1245-9, swrMg, mÚ 2) jamkaal johi na sak-ee ghat chaanan bali-aa. The Messenger of Death cannot even see him; his heart is illumined with God's Light.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v20	nwnk bKis imlwieAnu iPir griB n gilAw ]20] (1245-10, swrMg, mÚ 2) naanak bakhas milaa-i-an fir garabh na gali-aa. ||20||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v20	O Nanak, God forgives him, and blends him with Himself; he does not rot away in the womb of reincarnation ever again. ||20||
RECORD	para 54608	slok mÚ 1 ] (1245-10) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
UPHOLD	para 54609	scu vrqu sMqoKu qIrQu igAwnu iDAwnu iesnwnu ] (1245-10, swrMg, mÚ 1) sach varat santokh tirath gi-aan Dhi-aan isnaan. Those who have truth as their fast, contentment as their sacred shrine of pilgrimage, spiritual wisdom and meditation as their cleansing bath,
RECORD	para 54610	dieAw dyvqw iKmw jpmwlI qy mwxs prDwn ] (1245-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) da-i-aa dayvtaa khimaa japmaalee tay maanas parDhaan. kindness as their deity, and forgiveness as their chanting beads - they are the most excellent people.
RECORD	para 54611	jugiq DoqI suriq caukw iqlku krxI hoie ] (1245-11, swrMg, mÚ 1) jugat Dhotee surat cha-ukaa tilak karnee ho-ay. Those who take the Way as their loincloth, and intuitive awareness their ritualistically purified enclosure, with good deeds their ceremonial forehead mark,
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	Bwau Bojnu nwnkw ivrlw q koeI koie ]1] (1245-12, swrMg, mÚ 1) bhaa-o bhojan naankaa virlaa ta ko-ee ko-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	and love their food - O Nanak, they are very rare. ||1||
RECORD	para 54613	mhlw 3 ] (1245-12) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54614	naumI nymu scu jy krY ] (1245-12, swrMg, mÚ 3) na-umee naym sach jay karai. On the ninth day of the month, make a vow to speak the Truth,
REQUIRE	para 54615	kwm k®oDu iqRsnw aucrY ] (1245-13, swrMg, mÚ 3) kaam kroDh tarisnaa uchrai. and your sexual desire, anger and desire shall be eaten up.
RECORD	para 54616	dsmI dsy duAwr jy TwkY eykwdsI eyku kir jwxY ] (1245-13, swrMg, mÚ 3) dasmee dasay du-aar jay thaakai aykaadasee ayk kar jaanai. On the tenth day, regulate your ten doors; on the eleventh day, know that the Lord is One.
RECORD	para 54617	duAwdsI pMc vsgiq kir rwKY qau nwnk mnu mwnY ] (1245-13, swrMg, mÚ 3) du-aadasee panch vasgat kar raakhai ta-o naanak man maanai. On the twelfth day, the five thieves are subdued, and then, O Nanak, the mind is pleased and appeased.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	AYsw vrqu rhIjY pwfy hor bhuqu isK ikAw dIjY ]2] (1245-14, swrMg, mÚ 3) aisaa varat raheejai paaday hor bahut sikh ki-aa deejai. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	Observe such a fast as this, O Pandit, O religious scholar; of what use are all the other teachings? ||2||
RECORD	para 54619	pauVI ] (1245-15) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54620	BUpiq rwjy rMg rwie sMcih ibKu mwieAw ] (1245-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) bhoopat raajay rang raa-ay sa Ncheh bikh maa-i-aa. Kings, rulers and monarchs enjoy pleasures and gather the poison of Maya.
RECORD	para 54621	kir kir hyqu vDwiedy pr drbu curwieAw ] (1245-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) kar kar hayt vaDhaa-iday par darab churaa-i-aa. In love with it, they collect more and more, stealing the wealth of others.
DEFINE	para 54622	puqR klqR n ivshih bhu pRIiq lgwieAw ] (1245-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) putar kaltar na vishahi baho pareet lagaa-i-aa. They do not trust their own children or spouses; they are totally attached to the love of Maya.
RECORD	para 54623	vyKidAw hI mwieAw Duih geI pCuqih pCuqwieAw ] (1245-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) vaykh-di-aa hee maa-i-aa Dhuhi ga-ee pachhuteh pachhutaa-i-aa. But even as they look on, Maya cheats them, and they come to regret and repent.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v21	jm dir bDy mwrIAih nwnk hir BwieAw ]21] (1245-17, swrMg, mÚ 3) jam dar baDhay maaree-ah naanak har bhaa-i-aa. ||21||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v21	Bound and gagged at Death's door, they are beaten and punished; O Nanak, it pleases the Will of the Lord. ||21||
RECORD	para 54625	slok mÚ 1 ] (1245-17) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
UPHOLD	para 54626	igAwn ivhUxw gwvY gIq ] (1245-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) gi-aan vihoonaa gaavai geet. The one who lacks spiritual wisdom sings religious songs.
RECORD	para 54627	BuKy mulW Gry msIiq ] (1245-17, swrMg, mÚ 1) bhukhay mulaa N gharay maseet. The hungry Mullah turns his home into a mosque.
RECORD	para 54628	mKtU hoie kY kMn pVwey ] (1245-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) makhtoo ho-ay kai kann parhaa-ay. The lazy unemployed has his ears pierced to look like a Yogi.
RECORD	para 54629	Pkru kry horu jwiq gvwey ] (1245-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) fakar karay hor jaat gavaa-ay. Someone else becomes a pan-handler, and loses his social status.
RECORD	para 54630	guru pIru sdwey mMgx jwie ] (1245-18, swrMg, mÚ 1) gur peer sadaa-ay mangan jaa-ay. One who calls himself a guru or a spiritual teacher, while he goes around begging
RECORD	para 54631	qw kY mUil n lgIAY pwie ] (1245-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) taa kai mool na lagee-ai paa-ay. - don't ever touch his feet.
RECORD	para 54632	Gwil Kwie ikCu hQhu dyie ] (1245-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) ghaal khaa-ay kichh hathahu day-ay. One who works for what he eats, and gives some of what he has
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk rwhu pCwxih syie ]1] (1245-19, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak raahu pachhaaneh say-ay. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	- O Nanak, he knows the Path. ||1||
RECORD	para 54634	mÚ 1 ] (1246-1) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
WHEN	para 54636	mnhu ij AMDy kUp kihAw ibrdu n jwxn@I ] (1246-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) manhu je anDhay koop kahi-aa birad na jaanan Hee. Those mortals whose minds are like deep dark pits do not understand the purpose of life, even when it is explained to them.
DEFINE	para 54637	min AMDY aUNDY kvil idsin@ Kry krUp ] (1246-1, swrMg, mÚ 1) man anDhai oo NDhai kaval disniH kharay karoop. Their minds are blind, and their heart-lotuses are upside-down; they look totally ugly.
DEFINE	para 54638	ieik kih jwxih kihAw buJih qy nr suGV srUp ] (1246-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) ik kahi jaaneh kahi-aa bujheh tay nar sugharh saroop. Some know how to speak, and understand what they are told. They are wise and beautiful.
RECORD	para 54639	ieknw nwd n byd n gIA rsu rs ks n jwxMiq ] (1246-2, swrMg, mÚ 1) iknaa naad na bayd na gee-a ras ras kas na jaanant. Some do not understand about the Sound-current of the Naad or the Vedas, music, virtue or vice.
UPHOLD	para 54640	ieknw suiD n buiD n Akil sr AKr kw Byau n lhMiq ] (1246-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) iknaa suDh na buDh na akal sar akhar kaa bhay-o na laahant. Some are not blessed with understanding, intelligence, or sublime intellect; they do not grasp the mystery of God's Word.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk sy nr Asil Kr ij ibnu gux grbu krMiq ]2] (1246-3, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak say nar asal khar je bin gun garab karant. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, they are donkeys; they are very proud of themselves, but they have no virtues at all. ||2||
RECORD	para 54642	pauVI ] (1246-4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54643	gurmuiK sB pivqu hY Dnu sMpY mwieAw ] (1246-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) gurmukh sabh pavit hai Dhan sampai maa-i-aa. To the Gurmukh, everything is sacred: wealth, property, Maya.
RECORD	para 54644	hir AriQ jo Krcdy dyNdy suKu pwieAw ] (1246-4, swrMg, mÚ 1) har arath jo kharchaday day Nday sukh paa-i-aa. Those who spend the wealth of the Lord find peace through giving.
REQUIRE	para 54645	jo hir nwmu iDAwiedy iqn qoit n AwieAw ] (1246-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) jo har naam Dhi-aa-iday tin tot na aa-i-aa. Those who meditate on the Lord's Name shall never be deprived.
RECORD	para 54646	gurmuKW ndrI Awvdw mwieAw suit pwieAw ] (1246-5, swrMg, mÚ 1) gurmukhaa N nadree aavdaa maa-i-aa sut paa-i-aa. The Gurmukhs come to see the Lord, and leave behind the things of Maya.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v22	nwnk BgqW horu iciq n AwveI hir nwim smwieAw ]22] (1246-6, swrMg, mÚ 1) naanak bhagtaaN hor chit na aavee har naam samaa-i-aa. ||22||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v22	O Nanak, the devotees do not think of anything else; they are absorbed in the Name of the Lord. ||22||
RECORD	para 54648	slok mÚ 4 ] (1246-6) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54649	siqguru syvin sy vfBwgI ] (1246-7, swrMg, mÚ 4) satgur sayvan say vadbhaagee. Those who serve the True Guru are very fortunate.
DEFINE	para 54650	scY sbid ijn@w eyk ilv lwgI ] (1246-7, swrMg, mÚ 4) sachai sabad jin Haa ayk liv laagee. They are lovingly attuned to the True Shabad, the Word of the One God.
DEFINE	para 54651	igrh kutMb mih shij smwDI ] (1246-7, swrMg, mÚ 4) girah kutamb meh sahj samaaDhee. In their own household and family, they are in natural Samaadhi.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk nwim rqy sy scy bYrwgI ]1] (1246-8, swrMg, mÚ 4) naanak naam ratay say sachay bairaagee. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, those who are attuned to the Naam are truly detached from the world. ||1||
RECORD	para 54653	mÚ 4 ] (1246-8) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54654	gxqY syv n hoveI kIqw Qwie n pwie ] (1246-8, swrMg, mÚ 4) gantai sayv na hova-ee keetaa thaa-ay na paa-ay. Calculated service is not service at all, and what is done is not approved.
DEFINE	para 54655	sbdY swdu n AwieE sic n lgo Bwau ] (1246-8, swrMg, mÚ 4) sabdai saad na aa-i-o sach na lago bhaa-o. The flavor of the Shabad, the Word of God, is not tasted if the mortal is not in love with the True Lord God.
RECORD	para 54656	siqguru ipAwrw n lgeI mnhiT AwvY jwie ] (1246-9, swrMg, mÚ 4) satgur pi-aaraa na lag-ee manhath aavai jaa-ay. The stubborn-minded person does not even like the True Guru; he comes and goes in reincarnation.
RECORD	para 54657	jy iek ivK Agwhw Bry qW ds ivKW ipCwhw jwie ] (1246-9, swrMg, mÚ 4) jay ik vikh agaahaa bharay taaN das vikhaaN pichhaahaa jaa-ay. He takes one step forward, and ten steps back.
WHEN	para 54658	siqgur kI syvw cwkrI jy clih siqgur Bwie ] (1246-10, swrMg, mÚ 4) satgur kee sayvaa chaakree jay chaleh satgur bhaa-ay. The mortal works to serve the True Guru, if he walks in harmony with the True Guru's Will.
RECORD	para 54659	Awpu gvwie siqgurU no imlY shjy rhY smwie ] (1246-10, swrMg, mÚ 4) aap gavaa-ay satguroo no milai sehjay rahai samaa-ay. He loses his self-conceit, and meets the True Guru; he remains intuitively absorbed in the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk iqn@w nwmu n vIsrY scy myil imlwie ]2] (1246-11, swrMg, mÚ 4) naanak tin Haa naam na veesrai sachay mayl milaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, they never forget the Naam, the Name of the Lord; they are united in Union with the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 54661	pauVI ] (1246-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54662	Kwn mlUk khwiedy ko rhxu n pweI ] (1246-12, swrMg, mÚ 4) khaan malook kahaa-iday ko rahan na paa-ee. They call themselves emperors and rulers, but none of them will be allowed to stay.
RECORD	para 54663	gV@ mMdr gc gIrIAw ikCu swiQ n jweI ] (1246-12, swrMg, mÚ 4) garhH mandar gach geeree-aa kichh saath na jaa-ee. Their sturdy forts and mansions - none of them will go along with them.
DEFINE	para 54664	soien swKiq paux vyg iDRgu iDRgu cqurweI ] (1246-12, swrMg, mÚ 4) so-in saakhat pa-un vayg Dharig Dharig chaturaa-ee. Their gold and horses, fast as the wind, are cursed, and cursed are their clever tricks.
RECORD	para 54665	CqIh AMimRq prkwr krih bhu mYlu vDweI ] (1246-13, swrMg, mÚ 4) chhateeh amrit parkaar karahi baho mail vaDhaa-ee. Eating the thirty-six delicacies, they become bloated with pollution.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v23	nwnk jo dyvY iqsih n jwxn@I mnmuiK duKu pweI ]23] (1246-13, swrMg, mÚ 4) naanak jo dayvai tiseh na jaanan Hee manmukh dukh paa-ee. ||23||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v23	O Nanak, the self-willed manmukh does not know the One who gives, and so he suffers in pain. ||23||
RECORD	para 54667	slok mÚ 3 ] (1246-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54668	piV@ piV@ pMifq muonI Qky dysMqr Biv Qky ByKDwrI ] (1246-14, swrMg, mÚ 3) parhH parh H pandit monee thakay daysantar bhav thakay bhaykh-Dhaaree. The Pandits, the religious scholars and the silent sages read and recite until they get tired. They wander through foreign lands in their religious robes, until they are exhausted.
RECORD	para 54669	dUjY Bwie nwau kdy n pwiein duKu lwgw Aiq BwrI ] (1246-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay naa-o kaday na paa-in dukh laagaa at bhaaree. In love with duality, they never receive the Name. Held in the grasp of pain, they suffer terribly.
RECORD	para 54670	mUrK AMDy qRY gux syvih mwieAw kY ibauhwrI ] (1246-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) moorakh anDhay tarai gun sayveh maa-i-aa kai bi-uhaaree. The blind fools serve the three gunas, the three dispositions; they deal only with Maya.
RECORD	para 54671	AMdir kptu audru Brx kY qweI pwT pVih gwvwrI ] (1246-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) andar kapat udar bharan kai taa-ee paath parheh gaavaaree. With deception in their hearts, the fools read sacred texts to fill their bellies.
RECORD	para 54672	siqguru syvy so suKu pwey ijn haumY ivchu mwrI ] (1246-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay so sukh paa-ay jin ha-umai vichahu maaree. One who serves the True Guru finds peace; he eradicates egotism from within.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk pVxw gunxw ieku nwau hY bUJY ko bIcwrI ]1] (1246-17, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak parh-naa gunnaa ik naa-o hai boojhai ko beechaaree. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, there is One Name to chant and dwell on; how rare are those who reflect on this and understand. ||1||
RECORD	para 54674	mÚ 3 ] (1246-17) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54675	nWgy Awvxw nWgy jwxw hir hukmu pwieAw ikAw kIjY ] (1246-17, swrMg, mÚ 3) naa Ngay aavnaa naa Ngay jaanaa har hukam paa-i-aa ki-aa keejai. Naked we come, and naked we go. This is by the Lord's Command; what else can we do?
REQUIRE	para 54676	ijs kI vsqu soeI lY jwiegw rosu iksY isau kIjY ] (1246-18, swrMg, mÚ 3) jis kee vasat so-ee lai jaa-igaa ros kisai si-o keejai. The object belongs to Him; He shall take it away; with whom should one be angry.
RECORD	para 54677	gurmuiK hovY su Bwxw mMny shjy hir rsu pIjY ] (1246-19, swrMg, mÚ 3) gurmukh hovai so bhaanaa mannay sehjay har ras peejai. One who becomes Gurmukh accepts God's Will; he intuitively drinks in the Lord's sublime essence.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk suKdwqw sdw slwihhu rsnw rwmu rvIjY ]2] (1246-19, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak sukh-daata sadaa salaahihu rasnaa raam raveejai. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, praise the Giver of peace forever; with your tongue, savor the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 54680	pauVI ] (1247-1) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54681	giV@ kwieAw sIgwr bhu BWiq bxweI ] (1247-1, swrMg, mÚ 3) garheh kaa-i-aa seegaar baho bhaaNt banaa-ee. The fortress of the body has been decorated and adorned in so many ways.
RECORD	para 54682	rMg prMg kqIiPAw pihrih Dr mweI ] (1247-1, swrMg, mÚ 3) rang parang kateefi-aa pahirahi Dhar maa-ee. The wealthy wear beautiful silk robes of various colors.
RECORD	para 54683	lwl supyd dulIicAw bhu sBw bxweI ] (1247-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) laal supayd duleechi-aa baho sabhaa banaa-ee. They hold elegant and beautiful courts, on red and white carpets.
DEFINE	para 54684	duKu Kwxw duKu Bogxw grbY grbweI ] (1247-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) dukh khaanaa dukh bhognaa garbai garbaa-ee. But they eat in pain, and in pain they seek pleasure; they are very proud of their pride.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v24	nwnk nwmu n cyiqE AMiq ley CfweI ]24] (1247-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak naam na chayti-o ant la-ay chhadaa-ee. ||24||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 1 v24	O Nanak, the mortal does not even think of the Name, which shall deliver him in the end. ||24||
RECORD	para 54686	slok mÚ 3 ] (1247-3) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54687	shjy suiK suqI sbid smwie ] (1247-3, swrMg, mÚ 3) sehjay sukh sutee sabad samaa-ay. She sleeps in intuitive peace and poise, absorbed in the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 54688	Awpy pRiB myil leI gil lwie ] (1247-3, swrMg, mÚ 3) aapay parabh mayl la-ee gal laa-ay. God hugs her close in His Embrace, and merges her into Himself.
DEFINE	para 54689	duibDw cUkI shij suBwie ] (1247-4, swrMg, mÚ 3) dubiDhaa chookee sahj subhaa-ay. Duality is eradicated with intuitive ease.
RECORD	para 54690	AMqir nwmu visAw min Awie ] (1247-4, swrMg, mÚ 3) antar naam vasi-aa man aa-ay. The Naam comes to abide in her mind.
RECORD	para 54691	sy kMiT lwey ij BMin GVwie ] (1247-4, swrMg, mÚ 3) say kanth laa-ay je bhann gharhaa-ay. He hugs close in His Embrace those who shatter and reform their beings.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk jo Duir imly sy huix Awix imlwie ]1] (1247-5, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak jo Dhur milay say hun aan milaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, those who are predestined to meet Him, come and meet Him now. ||1||
RECORD	para 54693	mÚ 3 ] (1247-5) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
WHEN	para 54694	ijn@I nwmu ivswirAw ikAw jpu jwpih hoir ] (1247-5, swrMg, mÚ 3) jin Hee naam visaari-aa ki-aa jap jaapeh hor. Those who forget the Naam, the Name of the Lord - so what if they chant other chants?
DEFINE	para 54695	ibstw AMdir kIt sy muTy DMDY coir ] (1247-6, swrMg, mÚ 3) bistaa andar keet say muthay DhanDhai chor. They are maggots in manure, plundered by the thief of worldly entanglements.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk nwmu n vIsrY JUTy lwlc hoir ]2] (1247-6, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak naam na veesrai jhoothay laalach hor. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, never forget the Naam; greed for anything else is false. ||2||
RECORD	para 54697	pauVI ] (1247-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54698	nwmu slwhin nwmu mMin AsiQru jig soeI ] (1247-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) naam salaahan naam man asthir jag so-ee. Those who praise the Naam, and believe in the Naam, are eternally stable in this world.
RECORD	para 54699	ihrdY hir hir icqvY dUjw nhI koeI ] (1247-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) hirdai har har chitvai doojaa nahee ko-ee. Within their hearts, they dwell on the Lord, and nothing else at all.
RECORD	para 54700	roim roim hir aucrY iKnu iKnu hir soeI ] (1247-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) rom rom har uchrai khin khin har so-ee. With each and every hair, they chant the Lord's Name, each and every instant, the Lord.
DEFINE	para 54701	gurmuiK jnmu skwrQw inrmlu mlu KoeI ] (1247-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) gurmukh janam sakaarthaa nirmal mal kho-ee. The birth of the Gurmukh is fruitful and certified; pure and unstained, his filth is washed away.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v25	nwnk jIvdw purKu iDAwieAw Amrw pdu hoeI ]25] (1247-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak jeevdaa purakh Dhi-aa-i-aa amraa pad ho-ee. ||25||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v25	O Nanak, meditating on the Lord of eternal life, the status of immortality is obtained. ||25||
RECORD	para 54703	sloku mÚ 3 ] (1247-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54704	ijnI nwmu ivswirAw bhu krm kmwvih hoir ] (1247-9, swrMg, mÚ 3) jinee naam visaari-aa baho karam kamaaveh hor. Those who forget the Naam and do other things,
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk jm puir bDy mwrIAih ijau sMn@I aupir cor ]1] (1247-10, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak jam pur baDhay maaree-ah ji-o san Hee upar chor. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, will be bound and gagged and beaten in the City of Death, like the thief caught red-handed. ||1||
RECORD	para 54706	mÚ 5 ] (1247-10) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54707	Driq suhwvVI Awkwsu suhMdw jpMidAw hir nwau ] (1247-10, swrMg, mÚ 5) Dharat suhaavarhee aakaas suhandaa japandi-aa har naa-o. The earth is beauteous, and the sky is lovely, chanting the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk nwm ivhUixAw iqn@ qn Kwvih kwau ]2] (1247-11, swrMg, mÚ 5) naanak naam vihooni-aa tin H tan khaaveh kaa-o. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, those who lack the Naam - their carcasses are eaten by the crows. ||2||
RECORD	para 54709	pauVI ] (1247-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54710	nwmu slwhin Bwau kir inj mhlI vwsw ] (1247-12, swrMg, mÚ 5) naam salaahan bhaa-o kar nij mahlee vaasaa. Those who lovingly praise the Naam, and dwell in the mansion of the self deep within,
REQUIRE	para 54711	Eie bwhuiV join n AwvnI iPir hoih n ibnwsw ] (1247-12, swrMg, mÚ 5) o-ay baahurh jon na aavnee fir hohi na binaasaa. do not enter into reincarnation ever again; they shall never be destroyed.
RECORD	para 54712	hir syqI rMig riv rhy sB sws igrwsw ] (1247-13, swrMg, mÚ 5) har saytee rang rav rahay sabh saas giraasaa. They remain immersed and absorbed in the love of the Lord, with every breath and morsel of food.
DEFINE	para 54713	hir kw rMgu kdy n auqrY gurmuiK prgwsw ] (1247-13, swrMg, mÚ 5) har kaa rang kaday na utrai gurmukh pargaasaa. The color of the Lord's Love never fades away; the Gurmukhs are enlightened.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v26	Eie ikrpw kir kY myilAnu nwnk hir pwsw ]26] (1247-13, swrMg, mÚ 5) o-ay kirpaa kar kai mayli-an naanak har paasaa. ||26||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v26	Granting His Grace, He unites them with Himself; O Nanak, the Lord keeps them by His side. ||26||
RECORD	para 54715	slok mÚ 3 ] (1247-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54716	ijcru iehu mnu lhrI ivic hY haumY bhuqu AhMkwru ] (1247-14, swrMg, mÚ 3) jichar ih man lahree vich hai ha-umai bahut aha Nkaar. As long as his mind is disturbed by waves, he is caught in ego and egotistical pride.
RECORD	para 54717	sbdY swdu n AwveI nwim n lgY ipAwru ] (1247-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) sabdai saad na aavee naam na lagai pi-aar. He does not find the taste of the Shabad, and he does not embrace love for the Name.
DEFINE	para 54718	syvw Qwie n pveI iqs kI Kip Kip hoie KuAwru ] (1247-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) sayvaa thaa-ay na pav-ee tis kee khap khap ho-ay khu-aar. His service is not accepted; worrying and worrying, he wastes away in misery.
DEFINE	para 54719	nwnk syvku soeI AwKIAY jo isru Dry auqwir ] (1247-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak sayvak so-ee aakhee-ai jo sir Dharay utaar. O Nanak, he alone is called a selfless servant, who cuts off his head, and offers it to the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	siqgur kw Bwxw mMin ley sbdu rKY aur Dwir ]1] (1247-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) satgur kaa bhaanaa man la-ay sabad rakhai ur Dhaar. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	He accepts the Will of the True Guru, and enshrines the Shabad within his heart. ||1||
RECORD	para 54721	mÚ 3 ] (1247-17) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54722	so jpu qpu syvw cwkrI jo KsmY BwvY ] (1247-17, swrMg, mÚ 3) so jap tap sayvaa chaakree jo khasmai bhaavai. That is chanting and meditation, work and selfless service, which is pleasing to our Lord and Master.
RECORD	para 54723	Awpy bKsy myil ley Awpqu gvwvY ] (1247-17, swrMg, mÚ 3) aapay bakhsay mayl la-ay aapat gavaavai. The Lord Himself forgives, and takes away self-conceit, and unites the mortals with Himself.
DEFINE	para 54724	imilAw kdy n vICuVY joqI joiq imlwvY ] (1247-18, swrMg, mÚ 3) mili-aa kaday na veechhurhai jotee jot milaavai. United with the Lord, the mortal is never separated again; his light merges into the Light.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk gur prswdI so buJsI ijsu Awip buJwvY ]2] (1247-18, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak gur parsaadee so bujhsee jis aap bujhaavai. ||2||
WHEN	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, by Guru's Grace, the mortal understands, when the Lord allows him to understand. ||2||
RECORD	para 54726	pauVI ] (1247-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54727	sBu ko lyKy ivic hY mnmuKu AhMkwrI ] (1247-19, swrMg, mÚ 3) sabh ko laykhay vich hai manmukh aha Nkaaree. All are held accountable, even the egotistical self-willed manmukhs.
REQUIRE	para 54728	hir nwmu kdy n cyqeI jmkwlu isir mwrI ] (1247-19, swrMg, mÚ 3) har naam kaday na chayt-ee jamkaal sir maaree. They never even think of the Name of the Lord; the Messenger of Death shall hit them on their heads.
DEFINE	para 54730	pwp ibkwr mnUr siB ldy bhu BwrI ] (1248-1, swrMg, mÚ 3) paap bikaar manoor sabh laday baho bhaaree. Their sin and corruption are like rusty slag; they carry such a heavy load.
DEFINE	para 54731	mwrgu ibKmu frwvxw ikau qrIAY qwrI ] (1248-1, swrMg, mÚ 3) maarag bikham daraavanaa ki-o taree-ai taaree. The path is treacherous and terrifying; how can they cross over to the other side?
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v27	nwnk guir rwKy sy aubry hir nwim auDwrI ]27] (1248-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak gur raakhay say ubray har naam uDhaaree. ||27||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v27	O Nanak, those whom the Guru protects are saved. They are saved in the Name of the Lord. ||27||
RECORD	para 54733	slok mÚ 3 ] (1248-2) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54734	ivxu siqgur syvy suKu nhI mir jMmih vwro vwr ] (1248-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) vin satgur sayvay sukh nahee mar jameh vaaro vaar. Without serving the True Guru, no one finds peace; mortals die and are reborn, over and over again.
RECORD	para 54735	moh TgaulI pweIAnu bhu dUjY Bwie ivkwr ] (1248-3, swrMg, mÚ 3) moh thag-ulee paa-ee-an baho doojai bhaa-ay vikaar. They have been given the drug of emotional attachment; in love with duality, they are totally corrupt.
DEFINE	para 54736	ieik gur prswdI aubry iqsu jn kau krih siB nmskwr ] (1248-3, swrMg, mÚ 3) ik gur parsaadee ubray tis jan ka-o karahi sabh namaskaar. Some are saved, by Guru's Grace. Everyone humbly bows before such humble beings.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk Anidnu nwmu iDAwie qU AMqir ijqu pwvih moK duAwr ]1] (1248-4, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak an-din naam Dhi-aa-ay too antar jit paavahi mokh du-aar. ||1||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, meditate on the Naam, deep within yourself, day and night. You shall find the Door of Salvation. ||1||
RECORD	para 54738	mÚ 3 ] (1248-5) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54739	mwieAw moih ivswirAw scu mrxw hir nwmu ] (1248-5, swrMg, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi visaari-aa sach marnaa har naam. Emotionally attached to Maya, the mortal forgets truth, death and the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 54740	DMDw kriqAw jnmu gieAw AMdir duKu shwmu ] (1248-5, swrMg, mÚ 3) DhanDhaa karti-aa janam ga-i-aa andar dukh sahaam. Engaged in worldly affairs, his life wastes away; deep within himself, he suffers in pain.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk siqguru syiv suKu pwieAw ijn@ pUrib iliKAw krwmu ]2] (1248-6, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak satgur sayv sukh paa-i-aa jin H poorab likhi-aa karaam. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, those who have the karma of such pre-ordained destiny, serve the True Guru and find peace. ||2||
RECORD	para 54742	pauVI ] (1248-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
REQUIRE	para 54743	lyKw pVIAY hir nwmu iPir lyKu n hoeI ] (1248-6, swrMg, mÚ 3) laykhaa parhee-ai har naam fir laykh na ho-ee. Read the account of the Name of the Lord, and you shall never again be called to account.
RECORD	para 54744	puiC n skY koie hir dir sd FoeI ] (1248-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) puchh na sakai ko-ay har dar sad dho-ee. No one will question you, and you will always be safe in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	para 54745	jmkwlu imlY dy Byt syvku inq hoeI ] (1248-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) jamkaal milai day bhayt sayvak nit ho-ee. The Messenger of Death will meet you, and be your constant servant.
REQUIRE	para 54746	pUry gur qy mhlu pwieAw piq prgtu loeI ] (1248-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) pooray gur tay mahal paa-i-aa pat pargat lo-ee. Through the Perfect Guru, you shall find the Mansion of the Lord's Presence. You shall be famous throughout the world.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v28	nwnk Anhd DunI dir vjdy imilAw hir soeI ]28] (1248-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak anhad Dhunee dar vajday mili-aa har so-ee. ||28||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v28	O Nanak, the unstruck celestial melody vibrates at your door; come and merge with the Lord. ||28||
RECORD	para 54748	slok mÚ 3 ] (1248-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54749	gur kw kihAw jy kry suKI hU suKu swru ] (1248-9, swrMg, mÚ 3) gur kaa kahi-aa jay karay sukhee hoo sukh saar. Whoever follows the Guru's Teachings, attains the most sublime peace of all peace.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	gur kI krxI Bau ktIAY nwnk pwvih pwru ]1] (1248-9, swrMg, mÚ 3) gur kee karnee bha-o katee-ai naanak paavahi paar. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	Acting in accordance with the Guru, his fear is cut away; O Nanak, he is carried across. ||1||
RECORD	para 54751	mÚ 3 ] (1248-10) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54752	scu purwxw nw QIAY nwmu n mYlw hoie ] (1248-10, swrMg, mÚ 3) sach puraanaa naa thee-ai naam na mailaa ho-ay. The True Lord does not grow old; His Naam is never dirtied.
FORBID	para 54753	gur kY BwxY jy clY bhuiV n Awvxu hoie ] (1248-10, swrMg, mÚ 3) gur kai bhaanai jay chalai bahurh na aavan ho-ay. Whoever walks in harmony with the Guru's Will, shall not be reborn again.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk nwim ivswirAY Awvx jwxw doie ]2] (1248-11, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak naam visaari-ai aavan jaanaa do-ay. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, those who forget the Naam, come and go in reincarnation. ||2||
RECORD	para 54755	pauVI ] (1248-11) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54756	mMgq jnu jwcY dwnu hir dyhu suBwie ] (1248-11, swrMg, mÚ 3) mangat jan jaachai daan har dayh subhaa-ay. I am a beggar; I ask this blessing of You: O Lord, please embellish me with Your Love.
UPHOLD	para 54757	hir drsn kI ipAws hY drsin iqRpqwie ] (1248-12, swrMg, mÚ 3) har darsan kee pi-aas hai darsan tariptaa-ai. I am so thirsty for the Blessed Vision of the Lord's Darshan; His Darshan brings me satisfaction.
RECORD	para 54758	iKnu plu GVI n jIvaU ibnu dyKy mrW mwie ] (1248-12, swrMg, mÚ 3) khin pal gharhee na jeev-oo bin daykhay maraa N maa-ay. I cannot live for a moment, for even an instant, without seeing Him, O my mother.
DEFINE	para 54759	siqguir nwil idKwilAw riv rihAw sB Qwie ] (1248-13, swrMg, mÚ 3) satgur naal dikhaali-aa rav rahi-aa sabh thaa-ay. The Guru has shown me that the Lord is always with me; He is permeating and pervading all places.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v29	suiqAw Awip auTwil dyie nwnk ilv lwie ]29] (1248-13, swrMg, mÚ 3) suti-aa aap uthaal day-ay naanak liv laa-ay. ||29||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v29	He Himself wakes the sleepers, O Nanak, and lovingly attunes them to Himself. ||29||
RECORD	para 54761	slok mÚ 3 ] (1248-14) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54762	mnmuK boil n jwxn@I Enw AMdir kwmu k®oDu AhMkwru ] (1248-14, swrMg, mÚ 3) manmukh bol na jaanan Hee onaa andar kaam kroDh aha Nkaar. The self-willed manmukhs do not even know how to speak. They are filled with sexual desire, anger and egotism.
RECORD	para 54763	Qwau kuQwau n jwxnI sdw icqvih ibkwr ] (1248-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) thaa-o kuthaa-o na jaannee sadaa chitvahi bikaar. They do not know the difference between good and bad; they constantly think of corruption.
DEFINE	para 54764	drgh lyKw mMgIAY EQY hoih kUiVAwr ] (1248-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) dargeh laykhaa mangee-ai othai hohi koorhi-aar. In the Lord's Court, they are called to account, and they are judged to be false.
RECORD	para 54765	Awpy isRsit aupweIAnu Awip kry bIcwru ] (1248-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) aapay sarisat upaa-ee-an aap karay beechaar. He Himself creates the Universe. He Himself contemplates it.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk iks no AwKIAY sBu vrqY Awip sicAwru ]1] (1248-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak kis no aakhee-ai sabh vartai aap sachiaar. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, whom should we tell? The True Lord is permeating and pervading all. ||1||
RECORD	para 54767	mÚ 3 ] (1248-17) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54768	hir gurmuiK iqn@I ArwiDAw ijn@ krim prwpiq hoie ] (1248-17, swrMg, mÚ 3) har gurmukh tin Hee araaDhi-aa jin H karam paraapat ho-ay. The Gurmukhs worship and adore the Lord; they receive the good karma of their actions.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk hau bilhwrI iqn@ kau ijn@ hir min visAw soie ]2] (1248-17, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak ha-o balihaaree tin H ka-o jin H har man vasi-aa so-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, I am a sacrifice to those whose minds are filled with the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 54770	pauVI ] (1248-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 54771	Aws kry sBu loku bhu jIvxu jwixAw ] (1248-18, swrMg, mÚ 3) aas karay sabh lok baho jeevan jaani-aa. All people cherish hope, that they will live long lives.
RECORD	para 54772	inq jIvx kau icqu gV@ mMfp svwirAw ] (1248-18, swrMg, mÚ 3) nit jeevan ka-o chit garh H mandap savaari-aa. They wish to live forever; they adorn and embellish their forts and mansions.
RECORD	para 54773	vlvMc kir aupwv mwieAw ihir AwixAw ] (1248-19, swrMg, mÚ 3) valvanch kar upaav maa-i-aa hir aani-aa. By various frauds and deceptions, they steal the wealth of others.
RECORD	para 54774	jmkwlu inhwly sws Awv GtY byqwilAw ] (1248-19, swrMg, mÚ 3) jamkaal nihaalay saas aav ghatai baytaali-aa. But the Messenger of Death keeps his gaze on their breath, and the life of those goblins decreases day by day.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v30	nwnk gur srxweI aubry hir gur rKvwilAw ]30] (1249-1, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak gur sarnaa-ee ubray har gur rakhvaali-aa. ||30||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v30	Nanak has come to the Sanctuary of the Guru, and is saved. The Guru, the Lord, is his Protector. ||30||
RECORD	para 54777	slok mÚ 3 ] (1249-1) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54778	piV piV pMifq vwdu vKwxdy mwieAw moh suAwie ] (1249-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) parh parh pandit vaad vkhaanday maa-i-aa moh su-aa-ay. Reading and writing, the Pandits engage in debates and disputes; they are attached to the flavors of Maya.
REQUIRE	para 54779	dUjY Bwie nwmu ivswirAw mn mUrK imlY sjwie ] (1249-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) doojai bhaa-ay naam visaari-aa man moorakh milai sajaa-ay. In the love of duality, they forget the Naam. Those foolish mortals shall receive their punishment.
RECORD	para 54780	ijin@ kIqy iqsY n syvn@I dydw irjku smwie ] (1249-3, swrMg, mÚ 3) jiniH keetay tisai na sayvn Hee daydaa rijak samaa-ay. They do not serve the One who created them, who gives sustenance to all.
RECORD	para 54781	jm kw Pwhw glhu n ktIAY iPir iPir Awvih jwie ] (1249-3, swrMg, mÚ 3) jam kaa faahaa galhu na katee-ai fir fir aavahi jaa-ay. The noose of Death around their necks is not cut off; they come and go in reincarnation, over and over again.
RECORD	para 54782	ijn kau pUrib iliKAw siqguru imilAw iqn Awie ] (1249-4, swrMg, mÚ 3) jin ka-o poorab likhi-aa satgur mili-aa tin aa-ay. The True Guru comes and meets those who have such pre-ordained destiny.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	Anidnu nwmu iDAwiedy nwnk sic smwie ]1] (1249-4, swrMg, mÚ 3) an-din naam Dhi-aa-iday naanak sach samaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	Night and day, they meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; O Nanak, they merge into the True Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 54784	mÚ 3 ] (1249-5) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54785	scu vxjih scu syvdy ij gurmuiK pYrI pwih ] (1249-5, swrMg, mÚ 3) sach vanjahi sach sayvday je gurmukh pairee paahi. Those Gurmukhs who fall at His Feet deal with the True Lord and serve the True Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk gur kY BwxY jy clih shjy sic smwih ]2] (1249-5, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak gur kai bhaanai jay chaleh sehjay sach samaahi. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, those who walk in harmony with the Guru's Will are intuitively absorbed in the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 54787	pauVI ] (1249-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54788	Awsw ivic Aiq duKu Gxw mnmuiK icqu lwieAw ] (1249-6, swrMg, mÚ 3) aasaa vich at dukh ghanaa manmukh chit laa-i-aa. In hope, there is very great pain; the self-willed manmukh focuses his consciousness on it.
RECORD	para 54789	gurmuiK Bey inrws prm suKu pwieAw ] (1249-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) gurmukh bha-ay niraas param sukh paa-i-aa. The Gurmukhs become desireless, and attain supreme peace.
DEFINE	para 54790	ivcy igrh audws Ailpq ilv lwieAw ] (1249-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) vichay girah udaas alipat liv laa-i-aa. In the midst of their household, they remain detached; they are lovingly attuned to the Detached Lord.
DEFINE	para 54791	Enw sogu ivjogu n ivAwpeI hir Bwxw BwieAw ] (1249-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) onaa sog vijog na vi-aapa-ee har bhaanaa bhaa-i-aa. Sorrow and separation do not cling to them at all. They are pleased with the Lord's Will.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v31	nwnk hir syqI sdw riv rhy Duir ley imlwieAw ]31] (1249-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak har saytee sadaa rav rahay Dhur la-ay milaa-i-aa. ||31||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v31	O Nanak, they remain forever immersed in the Primal Lord, who blends them with Himself. ||31||
RECORD	para 54793	slok mÚ 3 ] (1249-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54794	prweI Amwx ikau rKIAY idqI hI suKu hoie ] (1249-9, swrMg, mÚ 3) paraa-ee amaan ki-o rakhee-ai ditee hee sukh ho-ay. Why keep what is held in trust for another? Giving it back, peace is found.
RECORD	para 54795	gur kw sbdu gur QY itkY hor QY prgtu n hoie ] (1249-9, swrMg, mÚ 3) gur kaa sabad gur thai tikai hor thai pargat na ho-ay. The Word of the Guru's Shabad rests in the Guru; it does not appear through anyone else.
RECORD	para 54796	AMn@y vis mwxku pieAw Gir Gir vycx jwie ] (1249-10, swrMg, mÚ 3) aNn Hay vas maanak pa-i-aa ghar ghar vaychan jaa-ay. The blind man finds a jewel, and goes from house to house selling it.
RECORD	para 54797	Enw prK n AwveI AFu n plY pwie ] (1249-10, swrMg, mÚ 3) onaa parakh na aavee adh na palai paa-ay. But they cannot appraise it, and they do not offer him even half a shell for it.
WHEN	para 54798	jy Awip prK n AwveI qW pwrKIAw Qwvhu lieEu prKwie ] (1249-11, swrMg, mÚ 3) jay aap parakh na aavee taaN paarkhee-aa thaavhu la-i-o parkhaa-ay. If he cannot appraise it himself, then he should have it appraised by an appraiser.
WHEN	para 54799	jy Esu nwil icqu lwey qW vQu lhY nau iniD plY pwie ] (1249-11, swrMg, mÚ 3) jay os naal chit laa-ay taaN vath lahai na-o niDh palai paa-ay. If he focuses his consciousness, then he obtains the true object, and he is blessed with the nine treasures.
RECORD	para 54800	Gir hodY Din jgu BuKw muAw ibnu siqgur soJI n hoie ] (1249-12, swrMg, mÚ 3) ghar hodai Dhan jag bhukhaa mu-aa bin satgur sojhee na ho-ay. The wealth is within the house, while the world is dying of hunger. Without the True Guru, no one has a clue.
WHEN	para 54801	sbdu sIqlu min qin vsY iqQY sogu ivjogu n koie ] (1249-12, swrMg, mÚ 3) sabad seetal man tan vasai tithai sog vijog na ko-ay. When the cooling and soothing Shabad comes to dwell in the mind and body, there is no sorrow or separation there.
DEFINE	para 54802	vsqu prweI Awip grbu kry mUrKu Awpu gxwey ] (1249-13, swrMg, mÚ 3) vasat paraa-ee aap garab karay moorakh aap ganaa-ay. The object belongs to someone else, but the fool is proud of it, and shows his shallow nature.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk ibnu bUJy iknY n pwieE iPir iPir AwvY jwey ]1] (1249-13, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak bin boojhay kinai na paa-i-o fir fir aavai jaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, without understanding, no one obtains it; they come and go in reincarnation, over and over again. ||1||
RECORD	para 54804	mÚ 3 ] (1249-14) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54805	min Andu BieAw imilAw hir pRIqmu srsy sjx sMq ipAwry ] (1249-14, swrMg, mÚ 3) man anad bha-i-aa mili-aa har pareetam sarsay sajan sant pi-aaray. My mind is in ecstasy; I have met my Beloved Lord. My beloved friends, the Saints, are delighted.
REQUIRE	para 54806	jo Duir imly n ivCuVih kbhU ij Awip myly krqwry ] (1249-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) jo Dhur milay na vichhurheh kabhoo je aap maylay kartaaray. Those who are united with the Primal Lord shall never be separated again. The Creator has united them with Himself.
RECORD	para 54807	AMqir sbdu rivAw guru pwieAw sgly dUK invwry ] (1249-15, swrMg, mÚ 3) antar sabad ravi-aa gur paa-i-aa saglay dookh nivaaray. The Shabad permeates my inner being, and I have found the Guru; all my sorrows are dispelled.
RECORD	para 54808	hir suKdwqw sdw slwhI AMqir rKW aur Dwry ] (1249-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) har sukh-daata sadaa salaahee antar rakhaaN ur Dhaaray. I praise forever the Lord, the Giver of peace; I keep Him enshrined deep within my heart.
RECORD	para 54809	mnmuKu iqn kI bKIlI ik kry ij scY sbid svwry ] (1249-16, swrMg, mÚ 3) manmukh tin kee bakheelee ke karay je sachai sabad savaaray. How can the self-willed manmukh gossip about those who are embellished and exalted in the True Word of the Shabad?
RECORD	para 54810	Enw dI Awip piq rKsI myrw ipAwrw srxwgiq pey gur duAwry ] (1249-17, swrMg, mÚ 3) onaa dee aap pat rakhsee mayraa pi-aaraa sarnaagat pa-ay gur du-aaray. My Beloved Himself preserves the honor of those who have come to the Guru's Door seeking Sanctuary.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk gurmuiK sy suhyly Bey muK aUjl drbwry ]2] (1249-18, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh say suhaylay bha-ay mukh oojal darbaaray. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are filled with joy; their faces are radiant in the Court of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 54812	pauVI ] (1249-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54813	iesqrI purKY bhu pRIiq imil mohu vDwieAw ] (1249-18, swrMg, mÚ 3) istaree purkhai baho pareet mil moh vaDhaa-i-aa. The husband and wife are very much in love; joining together, their love increases.
DEFINE	para 54814	puqRü klqRü inq vyKY ivgsY moih mwieAw ] (1249-19, swrMg, mÚ 3) putar kalatar nit vaykhai vigsai mohi maa-i-aa. Gazing on his children and his wife, the man is pleased and attached to Maya.
RECORD	para 54815	dyis prdyis Dnu corwie Awix muih pwieAw ] (1249-19, swrMg, mÚ 3) days pardays Dhan choraa-ay aan muhi paa-i-aa. Stealing the wealth of his own country and other lands, he brings it home and feeds them.
RECORD	para 54817	AMiq hovY vYr ivroDu ko skY n CfwieAw ] (1250-1, swrMg, mÚ 3) ant hovai vair viroDh ko sakai na chhadaa-i-aa. In the end, hatred and conflict well up, and no one can save him.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v32	nwnk ivxu nwvY iDRgu mohu ijqu lig duKu pwieAw ]32] (1250-1, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak vin naavai Dharig moh jit lag dukh paa-i-aa. ||32||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v32	O Nanak, without the Name, those loving attachments are cursed; engrossed in them, he suffers in pain. ||32||
RECORD	para 54819	slok mÚ 3 ] (1250-2) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 54820	gurmuiK AMimRqu nwmu hY ijqu KwDY sB BuK jwie ] (1250-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) gurmukh amrit naam hai jit khaaDhai sabh bhukh jaa-ay. The Guru's Word is the Ambrosial Nectar of the Naam. Eating it, all hunger departs.
DEFINE	para 54821	iqRsnw mUil n hoveI nwmu vsY min Awie ] (1250-2, swrMg, mÚ 3) tarisnaa mool na hova-ee naam vasai man aa-ay. There is no thirst or desire at all, when the Naam comes to dwell in the mind.
RECORD	para 54822	ibnu nwvY ij horu Kwxw iqqu rogu lgY qin Dwie ] (1250-3, swrMg, mÚ 3) bin naavai je hor khaanaa tit rog lagai tan Dhaa-ay. Eating anything other than the Name, disease runs to afflict the body.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk rs ks sbdu slwhxw Awpy ley imlwie ]1] (1250-3, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak ras kas sabad salaahnaa aapay la-ay milaa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, whoever takes the Praise of the Shabad as his spices and flavors - the Lord unites him in His Union. ||1||
RECORD	para 54824	mÚ 3 ] (1250-4) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54825	jIAw AMdir jIau sbdu hY ijqu sh mylwvw hoie ] (1250-4, swrMg, mÚ 3) jee-aa andar jee-o sabad hai jit sah maylaavaa ho-ay. The life within all living beings is the Word of the Shabad. Through it, we meet our Husband Lord.
DEFINE	para 54826	ibnu sbdY jig Awn@yru hY sbdy prgtu hoie ] (1250-5, swrMg, mÚ 3) bin sabdai jag aan Hayr hai sabday pargat ho-ay. Without the Shabad, the world is in darkness. Through the Shabad, it is enlightened.
RECORD	para 54827	pMifq monI piV piV Qky ByK Qky qnu Doie ] (1250-5, swrMg, mÚ 3) pandit monee parh parh thakay bhaykh thakay tan Dho-ay. The Pandits, the religious scholars, and the silent sages read and write until they are weary. The religious fanatics are tired of washing their bodies.
RECORD	para 54828	ibnu sbdY iknY n pwieE duKIey cly roie ] (1250-6, swrMg, mÚ 3) bin sabdai kinai na paa-i-o dukhee-ay chalay ro-ay. Without the Shabad, no one attains the Lord; the miserable depart weeping and wailing.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	nwnk ndrI pweIAY krim prwpiq hoie ]2] (1250-6, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak nadree paa-ee-ai karam paraapat ho-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v2	O Nanak, by His Glance of Grace, the Merciful Lord is attained. ||2||
RECORD	para 54830	pauVI ] (1250-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 54831	iesqRI purKY Aiq nyhu bih mMdu pkwieAw ] (1250-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) istaree purkhai at nayhu bahi mand pakaa-i-aa. The husband and wife are very much in love; sitting together, they make evil plans.
REQUIRE	para 54832	idsdw sBu ikCu clsI myry pRB BwieAw ] (1250-7, swrMg, mÚ 3) disdaa sabh kichh chalsee mayray parabh bhaa-i-aa. All that is seen shall pass away. This is the Will of my God.
ALLOW	para 54833	ikau rhIAY iQru jig ko kFhu aupwieAw ] (1250-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) ki-o rahee-ai thir jag ko kadhahu upaa-i-aa. How can anyone remain in this world forever? Some may try to devise a plan.
RECORD	para 54834	gur pUry kI cwkrI iQru kMDu sbwieAw ] (1250-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) gur pooray kee chaakree thir kanDh sabaa-i-aa. Working for the Perfect Guru, the wall becomes permanent and stable.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v33	nwnk bKis imlwieAnu hir nwim smwieAw ]33] (1250-8, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak bakhas milaa-i-an har naam samaa-i-aa. ||33||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 1 v33	O Nanak, the Lord forgives them, and merges them into Himself; they are absorbed in the Lord's Name. ||33||
RECORD	para 54836	slok mÚ 3 ] (1250-9) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 54837	mwieAw moih ivswirAw gur kw Bau hyqu Apwru ] (1250-9, swrMg, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi visaari-aa gur kaa bha-o hayt apaar. Attached to Maya, the mortal forgets the Fear of God and Guru, and love for the Infinite Lord.
UPHOLD	para 54838	loiB lhir suiD miq geI sic n lgY ipAwru ] (1250-10, swrMg, mÚ 3) lobh lahar suDh mat ga-ee sach na lagai pi-aar. The waves of greed take away his wisdom and understanding, and he does not embrace love for the True Lord.
RECORD	para 54839	gurmuiK ijnw sbdu min vsY drgh moK duAwru ] (1250-10, swrMg, mÚ 3) gurmukh jinaa sabad man vasai dargeh mokh du-aar. The Word of the Shabad abides in the mind of the Gurmukhs, who find the Gate of Salvation.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	nwnk Awpy myil ley Awpy bKsxhwru ]1] (1250-11, swrMg, mÚ 3) naanak aapay mayl la-ay aapay bakhsanhaar. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v1	O Nanak, the Lord Himself forgives them, and unites them in Union with Himself. ||1||
RECORD	para 54841	mÚ 4 ] (1250-11) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 54842	nwnk ijsu ibnu GVI n jIvxw ivsry srY n ibMd ] (1250-11, swrMg, mÚ 4) naanak jis bin gharhee na jeevnaa visray sarai na bind. O Nanak, without Him, we could not live for a moment. Forgetting Him, we could not succeed for an instant.
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	iqsu isau ikau mn rUsIAY ijsih hmwrI icMd ]2] (1250-12, swrMg, mÚ 4) tis si-o ki-o man roosee-ai jisahi hamaaree chind. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 1 v2	O mortal, how can you be angry with the One who cares for you? ||2||
RECORD	para 54844	mÚ 4 ] (1250-12) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
