RECORD	para 56242	ieik Bsm cV@wvih AMig mYlu n DovhI ] (1284-19, mlwr, mÚ 3) ik bhasam charh Haavahi ang mail na Dhovhee. Some rub ashes on their bodies, and never wash off their dirt.
RECORD	para 56243	ieik jtw ibkt ibkrwl kulu Gru KovhI ] (1284-19, mlwr, mÚ 3) ik jataa bikat bikraal kul ghar khovhee. Some look hideous, with their uncut hair matted and dishevelled. They bring dishonor to their family and ancestry.
RECORD	para 56245	ieik ngn iPrih idnu rwiq nˆØId n sovhI ] (1285-1, mlwr, mÚ 3) ik nagan fireh din raat nee Nd na sovhee. Some wander naked day and night and never sleep.
RECORD	para 56246	ieik Agin jlwvih AMgu Awpu ivgovhI ] (1285-1, mlwr, mÚ 3) ik agan jalaaveh ang aap vigovahee. Some burn their limbs in fire, damaging and ruining themselves.
DEFINE	para 56247	ivxu nwvY qnu Cwru ikAw kih rovhI ] (1285-2, mlwr, mÚ 3) vin naavai tan chhaar ki-aa kahi rovhee. Without the Name, the body is reduced to ashes; what good is it to speak and cry then?
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v15	sohin Ksm duAwir ij siqguru syvhI ]15] (1285-2, mlwr, mÚ 3) sohan khasam du-aar je satgur sayvhee. ||15||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v15	Those who serve the True Guru, are embellished and exalted in the Court of their Lord and Master. ||15||
RECORD	para 56249	slok mÚ 3 ] (1285-3) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 56250	bwbIhw AMimRq vylY boilAw qW dir suxI pukwr ] (1285-3, mlwr, mÚ 3) baabeehaa amrit vaylai boli-aa taaN dar sunee pukaar. The rainbird chirps in the ambrosial hours of the morning before the dawn; its prayers are heard in the Court of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 56251	myGY no Purmwnu hoAw vrshu ikrpw Dwir ] (1285-3, mlwr, mÚ 3) mayghai no furmaan ho-aa varsahu kirpaa Dhaar. The order is issued to the clouds, to let the rains of mercy shower down.
RECORD	para 56252	hau iqn kY bilhwrxY ijnI scu riKAw auir Dwir ] (1285-4, mlwr, mÚ 3) ha-o tin kai balihaarnai jinee sach rakhi-aa ur Dhaar. I am a sacrifice to those who enshrine the True Lord within their hearts.
ALLOW	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk nwmy sB hrIAwvlI gur kY sbid vIcwir ]1] (1285-4, mlwr, mÚ 3) naanak naamay sabh haree-aavalee gur kai sabad veechaar. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, through the Name, all are rejuvenated, contemplating the Word of the Guru's Shabad. ||1||
RECORD	para 56254	mÚ 3 ] (1285-5) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
ALLOW	para 56255	bwbIhw iev qyrI iqKw n auqrY jy sau krih pukwr ] (1285-5, mlwr, mÚ 3) baabeehaa iv tayree tikhaa na utrai jay sa-o karahi pukaar. O rainbird, this is not the way to quench your thirst, even though you may cry out a hundred times.
DEFINE	para 56256	ndrI siqguru pweIAY ndrI aupjY ipAwru ] (1285-6, mlwr, mÚ 3) nadree satgur paa-ee-ai nadree upjai pi-aar. By God's Grace, the True Guru is found; by His Grace, love wells up.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk swihbu min vsY ivchu jwih ivkwr ]2] (1285-6, mlwr, mÚ 3) naanak saahib man vasai vichahu jaahi vikaar. ||2||
WHEN	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, when the Lord and Master abides in the mind, corruption and evil leave from within. ||2||
RECORD	para 56258	pauVI ] (1285-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 56259	ieik jYnI auJV pwie Durhu KuAwieAw ] (1285-7, mlwr, mÚ 3) ik jainee ujharh paa-ay Dharahu khu-aa-i-aa. Some are Jains, wasting their time in the wilderness; by their pre-ordained destiny, they are ruined.
DEFINE	para 56260	iqn muiK nwhI nwmu n qIriQ n@wieAw ] (1285-7, mlwr, mÚ 3) tin mukh naahee naam na tirath n Haa-i-aa. The Naam, the Name of the Lord, is not on their lips; they do not bathe at sacred shrines of pilgrimage.
RECORD	para 56261	hQI isr Kohwie n Bdu krwieAw ] (1285-8, mlwr, mÚ 3) hathee sir khohaa-ay na bhad karaa-i-aa. They pull out their hair with their hands, instead of shaving.
RECORD	para 56262	kuicl rhih idn rwiq sbdu n BwieAw ] (1285-8, mlwr, mÚ 3) kuchil raheh din raat sabad na bhaa-i-aa. They remain unclean day and night; they do not love the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	para 56263	iqn jwiq n piq n krmu jnmu gvwieAw ] (1285-8, mlwr, mÚ 3) tin jaat na pat na karam janam gavaa-i-aa. They have no status, no honor, and no good karma. They waste away their lives in vain.
DEFINE	para 56264	min jUTY vyjwiq jUTw KwieAw ] (1285-9, mlwr, mÚ 3) man joothai vayjaat joothaa khaa-i-aa. Their minds are false and impure; that which they eat is impure and defiled.
RECORD	para 56265	ibnu sbdY Awcwru n ikn hI pwieAw ] (1285-9, mlwr, mÚ 3) bin sabdai aachaar na kin hee paa-i-aa. Without the Shabad, no one achieves a lifestyle of good conduct.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v16	gurmuiK EAMkwir sic smwieAw ]16] (1285-10, mlwr, mÚ 3) gurmukh o-ankaar sach samaa-i-aa. ||16||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v16	The Gurmukh is absorbed in the True Lord God, the Universal Creator. ||16||
RECORD	para 56267	slok mÚ 3 ] (1285-10) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 56268	swvix srsI kwmxI gur sbdI vIcwir ] (1285-10, mlwr, mÚ 3) saavan sarsee kaamnee gur sabdee veechaar. In the month of Saawan, the bride is happy, contemplating the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk sdw suhwgxI gur kY hyiq Apwir ]1] (1285-11, mlwr, mÚ 3) naanak sadaa suhaaganee gur kai hayt apaar. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, she is a happy soul-bride forever; her love for the Guru is unlimited. ||1||
RECORD	para 56270	mÚ 3 ] (1285-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 56271	swvix dJY gux bwhrI ijsu dUjY Bwie ipAwru ] (1285-11, mlwr, mÚ 3) saavan dajhai gun baahree jis doojai bhaa-ay pi-aar. In Saawan, she who has no virtue is burned, in attachment and love of duality.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk ipr kI swr n jwxeI sBu sIgwru KuAwru ]2] (1285-12, mlwr, mÚ 3) naanak pir kee saar na jaan-ee sabh seegaar khu-aar. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, she does not appreciate the value of her Husband Lord; all her decorations are worthless. ||2||
RECORD	para 56273	pauVI ] (1285-12) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 56274	scw AlK AByau hiT n pqIjeI ] (1285-12, mlwr, mÚ 3) sachaa alakh abhay-o hath na pateeja-ee. The True, Unseen, Mysterious Lord is not won over by stubbornness.
DEFINE	para 56275	ieik gwvih rwg prIAw rwig n BIjeI ] (1285-13, mlwr, mÚ 3) ik gaavahi raag paree-aa raag na bheej-ee. Some sing according to traditional ragas, but the Lord is not pleased by these ragas.
RECORD	para 56276	ieik nic nic pUrih qwl Bgiq n kIjeI ] (1285-13, mlwr, mÚ 3) ik nach nach pooreh taal bhagat na keej-ee. Some dance and dance and keep the beat, but they do not worship Him with devotion.
RECORD	para 56277	ieik AMnu n Kwih mUrK iqnw ikAw kIjeI ] (1285-14, mlwr, mÚ 3) ik ann na khaahi moorakh tinaa ki-aa keej-ee. Some refuse to eat; what can be done with these fools?
RECORD	para 56278	iqRsnw hoeI bhuqu ikvY n DIjeI ] (1285-14, mlwr, mÚ 3) tarisnaa ho-ee bahut kivai na Dheej-ee. Thirst and desire have greatly increased; nothing brings satisfaction.
DEFINE	para 56279	krm vDih kY loA Kip mrIjeI ] (1285-14, mlwr, mÚ 3) karam vaDheh kai lo-a khap mareeja-ee. Some are tied down by rituals; they hassle themselves to death.
RECORD	para 56280	lwhw nwmu sMswir AMimRqu pIjeI ] (1285-15, mlwr, mÚ 3) laahaa naam sansaar amrit peej-ee. In this world, profit comes by drinking in the Ambrosial Nectar of the Naam.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v17	hir BgqI Asnyih gurmuiK GIjeI ]17] (1285-15, mlwr, mÚ 3) har bhagtee asnayhi gurmukh gheej-ee. ||17||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v17	The Gurmukhs gather in loving devotional worship of the Lord. ||17||
RECORD	para 56282	slok mÚ 3 ] (1285-16) salok mehlaa 3. Shalok, Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 56283	gurmuiK mlwr rwgu jo krih iqn mnu qnu sIqlu hoie ] (1285-16, mlwr, mÚ 3) gurmukh malaar raag jo karahi tin man tan seetal ho-ay. Those Gurmukhs who sing in the Raga of Malaar - their minds and bodies become cool and calm.
RECORD	para 56284	gur sbdI eyku pCwixAw eyko scw soie ] (1285-16, mlwr, mÚ 3) gur sabdee ayk pachhaani-aa ayko sachaa so-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, they realize the One, the One True Lord.
DEFINE	para 56285	mnu qnu scw scu min scy scI soie ] (1285-17, mlwr, mÚ 3) man tan sachaa sach man sachay sachee so-ay. Their minds and bodies are true; they obey the True Lord, and they are known as true.
DEFINE	para 56286	AMdir scI Bgiq hY shjy hI piq hoie ] (1285-17, mlwr, mÚ 3) andar sachee bhagat hai sehjay hee pat ho-ay. True devotional worship is deep within them; they are automatically blessed with honor.
RECORD	para 56287	kiljug mih Gor AMDwru hY mnmuK rwhu n koie ] (1285-18, mlwr, mÚ 3) kalijug meh ghor anDhaar hai manmukh raahu na ko-ay. In this Dark Age of Kali Yuga, there is utter darkness; the self-willed manmukh cannot find the way.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	sy vfBwgI nwnkw ijn gurmuiK prgtu hoie ]1] (1285-18, mlwr, mÚ 3) say vadbhaagee naankaa jin gurmukh pargat ho-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, very blessed are those Gurmukhs, unto whom the Lord is revealed. ||1||
RECORD	para 56289	mÚ 3 ] (1285-19) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 56290	ieMdu vrsY kir dieAw lokW min aupjY cwau ] (1285-19, mlwr, mÚ 3) ind varsai kar da-i-aa lokaa N man upjai chaa-o. The clouds rain down mercifully, and joy wells up in the minds of the people.
RECORD	para 56291	ijs kY hukim ieMdu vrsdw iqs kY sd bilhwrY jWau ] (1285-19, mlwr, mÚ 3) jis kai hukam ind varasdaa tis kai sad balihaarai jaa N-o. I am forever a sacrifice to the One, by whose Command the clouds burst forth with rain.
RECORD	para 56293	gurmuiK sbdu sm@wlIAY scy ky gux gwau ] (1286-1, mlwr, mÚ 3) gurmukh sabad sam Haalee-ai sachay kay gun gaa-o. The Gurmukhs dwell on the Word of the Shabad. They sing the Glorious Praises of the True Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk nwim rqy jn inrmly shjy sic smwau ]2] (1286-1, mlwr, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay jan nirmalay sehjay sach samaa-o. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, those humble beings who are imbued with the Naam are pure and immaculate. They are intuitively merged in the True Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 56295	pauVI ] (1286-2) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 56296	pUrw siqguru syiv pUrw pwieAw ] (1286-2, mlwr, mÚ 3) pooraa satgur sayv pooraa paa-i-aa. Serving the Perfect True Guru, I have found the Perfect Lord.
RECORD	para 56297	pUrY krim iDAwie pUrw sbdu mMin vswieAw ] (1286-2, mlwr, mÚ 3) poorai karam Dhi-aa-ay pooraa sabad man vasaa-i-aa. Meditating on the Perfect Lord, by perfect karma, I have enshrined the Shabad within my mind.
UPHOLD	para 56298	pUrY igAwin iDAwin mYlu cukwieAw ] (1286-3, mlwr, mÚ 3) poorai gi-aan Dhi-aan mail chukaa-i-aa. Through perfect spiritual wisdom and meditation, my filth has been washed away.
DEFINE	para 56299	hir sir qIriQ jwix mnUAw nwieAw ] (1286-3, mlwr, mÚ 3) har sar tirath jaan manoo-aa naa-i-aa. The Lord is my sacred shrine of pilgrimage and pool of purification; I wash my mind in Him.
DEFINE	para 56300	sbid mrY mnu mwir DMnu jxydI mwieAw ] (1286-4, mlwr, mÚ 3) sabad marai man maar Dhan janaydee maa-i-aa. One who dies in the Shabad and conquers his mind - blessed is the mother who gave birth to him.
DEFINE	para 56301	dir scY sicAwru scw AwieAw ] (1286-4, mlwr, mÚ 3) dar sachai sachiaar sachaa aa-i-aa. He is true in the Court of the Lord, and his coming into this world is judged to be true.
DEFINE	para 56302	puiC n skY koie jW KsmY BwieAw ] (1286-4, mlwr, mÚ 3) puchh na sakai ko-ay jaa N khasmai bhaa-i-aa. No one can challenge that person, with whom our Lord and Master is pleased.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v18	nwnk scu slwih iliKAw pwieAw ]18] (1286-5, mlwr, mÚ 3) naanak sach salaahi likhi-aa paa-i-aa. ||18||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v18	O Nanak, praising the True Lord, his pre-ordained destiny is activated. ||18||
RECORD	para 56304	slok mÚ 1 ] (1286-5) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 56305	kulhW dyNdy bwvly lYNdy vfy inlj ] (1286-5, mlwr, mÚ 1) kulhaa N day Nday baavlay lai Nday vaday nilaj. Those who give out ceremonial hats of recognition are fools; those who receive them have no shame.
RECORD	para 56306	cUhw Kf n mwveI iqkil bMn@Y Cj ] (1286-6, mlwr, mÚ 1) choohaa khad na maav-ee tikal ban Hai chhaj. The mouse cannot enter its hole with a basket tied around its waist.
REQUIRE	para 56307	dyin@ duAweI sy mrih ijn kau dyin is jwih ] (1286-6, mlwr, mÚ 1) dayniH du-aa-ee say mareh jin ka-o dayn se jaahi. Those who give out blessings shall die, and those that they bless shall also depart.
REQUIRE	para 56308	nwnk hukmu n jwpeI ikQY jwie smwih ] (1286-7, mlwr, mÚ 1) naanak hukam na jaap-ee kithai jaa-ay samaahi. O Nanak, no one knows the Lord's Command, by which all must depart.
DEFINE	para 56309	Psil AhwVI eyku nwmu swvxI scu nwau ] (1286-7, mlwr, mÚ 1) fasal ahaarhee ayk naam saavnee sach naa-o. The spring harvest is the Name of the One Lord; the harvest of autumn is the True Name.
WHEN	para 56310	mY mhdUdu ilKwieAw KsmY kY dir jwie ] (1286-8, mlwr, mÚ 1) mai mehdood likhaa-i-aa khasmai kai dar jaa-ay. I receive a letter of pardon from my Lord and Master, when I reach His Court.
DEFINE	para 56311	dunIAw ky dr kyqVy kyqy Awvih jWih ] (1286-8, mlwr, mÚ 1) dunee-aa kay dar kayt-rhay kaytay aavahi jaa Nhi. There are so many courts of the world, and so many who come and go there.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	kyqy mMgih mMgqy kyqy mMig mMig jwih ]1] (1286-8, mlwr, mÚ 1) kaytay mangeh mangtay kaytay mang mang jaahi. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	There are so many beggars begging; so many beg and beg until death. ||1||
RECORD	para 56313	mÚ 1 ] (1286-9) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 56314	sau mxu hsqI iGau guVu KwvY pMij sY dwxw Kwie ] (1286-9, mlwr, mÚ 1) sa-o man hastee ghi-o gurh khaavai panj sai daanaa khaa-ay. The elephant eats a hundred pounds of ghee and molasses, and five hundred pounds of corn.
WHEN	para 56315	fkY PUkY Kyh aufwvY swih gieAY pCuqwie ] (1286-10, mlwr, mÚ 1) dakai fookai khayh udaavai saahi ga-i-ai pachhutaa-ay. He belches and grunts and scatters dust, and when the breath leaves his body, he regrets it.
RECORD	para 56316	AMDI PUik mueI dyvwnI ] (1286-10, mlwr, mÚ 1) anDhee fook mu-ee dayvaanee. The blind and arrogant die insane.
RECORD	para 56317	Ksim imtI iPir BwnI ] (1286-10, mlwr, mÚ 1) khasam mitee fir bhaanee. Submitting to the Lord, one become pleasing to Him.
RECORD	para 56318	ADu gulHw icVI kw cugxu gYix cVI ibllwie ] (1286-11, mlwr, mÚ 1) aDh gul Haa chirhee kaa chugan gain charhee billaa-ay. The sparrow eats only half a grain, then it flies through the sky and chirps.
DEFINE	para 56319	KsmY BwvY Ehw cMgI ij kry Kudwie Kudwie ] (1286-11, mlwr, mÚ 1) khasmai bhaavai ohaa changee je karay khudaa-ay khudaa-ay. The good sparrow is pleasing to her Lord and Master, if she chirps the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 56320	skqw sIhu mwry sY imirAw sB ipCY pY Kwie ] (1286-12, mlwr, mÚ 1) saktaa seehu maaray sai miri-aa sabh pichhai pai khaa-ay. The powerful tiger kills hundreds of deer, and all sorts of other animals eat what it leaves.
REQUIRE	para 56321	hoie sqwxw GurY n mwvY swih gieAY pCuqwie ] (1286-12, mlwr, mÚ 1) ho-ay sataanaa ghurai na maavai saahi ga-i-ai pachhutaa-ay. It becomes very strong, and cannot be contained in its den, but when it must go, it regrets.
DEFINE	para 56322	AMDw iks no buik suxwvY ] (1286-13, mlwr, mÚ 1) anDhaa kis no buk sunaavai. So who is impressed by the roar of the blind beast?
DEFINE	para 56323	KsmY mUil n BwvY ] (1286-13, mlwr, mÚ 1) khasmai mool na bhaavai. He is not pleasing at all to his Lord and Master.
RECORD	para 56324	Ak isau pRIiq kry Ak iqfw Ak fwlI bih Kwie ] (1286-13, mlwr, mÚ 1) ak si-o pareet karay ak tidaa ak daalee bahi khaa-ay. The insect loves the milkweed plant; perched on its branch, it eats it.
WHEN	para 56325	KsmY BwvY Eho cMgw ij kry Kudwie Kudwie ] (1286-14, mlwr, mÚ 1) khasmai bhaavai oho changa je karay khudaa-ay khudaa-ay. It becomes good and pleasing to its Lord and Master, if it chirps the Name of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 56326	nwnk dunIAw cwir idhwVy suiK kIqY duKu hoeI ] (1286-14, mlwr, mÚ 1) naanak dunee-aa chaar dihaarhay sukh keetai dukh ho-ee. O Nanak, the world lasts for only a few days; indulging in pleasures, pain is produced.
DEFINE	para 56327	glw vwly hYin Gxyry Cif n skY koeI ] (1286-15, mlwr, mÚ 1) galaa vaalay hain ghanayray chhad na sakai ko-ee. There are many who boast and brag, but none of them can remain detached from the world.
RECORD	para 56328	mKˆØI imTY mrxw ] (1286-15, mlwr, mÚ 1) makhee N mithai marnaa. The fly dies for the sake of sweets.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	ijn qU rKih iqn nyiV n AwvY iqn Bau swgru qrxw ]2] (1286-15, mlwr, mÚ 1) jin too rakheh tin nayrh na aavai tin bha-o saagar tarnaa. ||2||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Lord, death does not even approach those whom You protect. You carry them across the terrifying world-ocean. ||2||
RECORD	para 56330	pauVI ] (1286-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 56331	Agm Agocru qU DxI scw AlK Apwru ] (1286-16, mlwr, mÚ 1) agam agochar too Dhanee sachaa alakh apaar. You are Inaccessible and Unfathomable, O Invisible and Infinite True Lord Master.
DEFINE	para 56332	qU dwqw siB mMgqy ieko dyvxhwru ] (1286-16, mlwr, mÚ 1) too daataa sabh mangtay iko dayvanhaar. You are the Giver, all are beggars of You. You alone are the Great Giver.
RECORD	para 56333	ijnI syivAw iqnI suKu pwieAw gurmqI vIcwru ] (1286-17, mlwr, mÚ 1) jinee sayvi-aa tinee sukh paa-i-aa gurmatee veechaar. Those who serve You find peace, reflecting on the Guru's Teachings.
DEFINE	para 56334	ieknw no quDu eyvY Bwvdw mwieAw nwil ipAwru ] (1286-17, mlwr, mÚ 1) iknaa no tuDh ayvai bhaavdaa maa-i-aa naal pi-aar. Some, according to Your Will, are in love with Maya.
RECORD	para 56335	gur kY sbid slwhIAY AMqir pRym ipAwru ] (1286-18, mlwr, mÚ 1) gur kai sabad salaahee-ai antar paraym pi-aar. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, praise the Lord with love and affection within.
DEFINE	para 56336	ivxu pRIqI Bgiq n hoveI ivxu siqgur n lgY ipAwru ] (1286-18, mlwr, mÚ 1) vin pareetee bhagat na hova-ee vin satgur na lagai pi-aar. Without love, there is no devotion. Without the True Guru, love is not enshrined.
DEFINE	para 56337	qU pRBu siB quDu syvdy iek FwFI kry pukwr ] (1286-19, mlwr, mÚ 1) too parabh sabh tuDh sayvday ik dhaadhee karay pukaar. You are the Lord God; everyone serves You. This is the prayer of Your humble minstrel.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v19	dyih dwnu sMqoKIAw scw nwmu imlY AwDwru ]19] (1286-19, mlwr, mÚ 1) deh daan santokhee-aa sachaa naam milai aaDhaar. ||19||
ALLOW	slok mhlw 3 v19	Please bless me with the gift of contentment, that I may receive the True Name as my Support. ||19||
RECORD	para 56340	slok mÚ 1 ] (1287-1) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
RECORD	para 56341	rwqI kwlu GtY idin kwlu ] (1287-1, mlwr, mÚ 1) raatee kaal ghatai din kaal. Through the night the time ticks away; through the day the time ticks away.
RECORD	para 56342	iCjY kwieAw hoie prwlu ] (1287-1, mlwr, mÚ 1) chhijai kaa-i-aa ho-ay paraal. The body wears away and turns to straw.
DEFINE	para 56343	vrqix vriqAw srb jMjwlu ] (1287-2, mlwr, mÚ 1) vartan varti-aa sarab janjaal. All are involved and entangled in worldly entanglements.
RECORD	para 56344	BuilAw cuik gieAw qp qwlu ] (1287-2, mlwr, mÚ 1) bhuli-aa chuk ga-i-aa tap taal. The mortal has mistakenly renounced the way of service.
DEFINE	para 56345	AMDw JiK JiK pieAw Jyir ] (1287-2, mlwr, mÚ 1) anDhaa jhakh jhakh pa-i-aa jhayr. The blind fool is caught in conflict, bothered and bewildered.
RECORD	para 56346	ipCY rovih ilAwvih Pyir ] (1287-3, mlwr, mÚ 1) pichhai roveh li-aaveh fayr. Those who weep after someone has died - can they bring him back to life?
RECORD	para 56347	ibnu bUJy ikCu sUJY nwhI ] (1287-3, mlwr, mÚ 1) bin boojhay kichh soojhai naahee. Without realization, nothing can be understood.
REQUIRE	para 56348	moieAw roNih roNdy mir jWhˆØI ] (1287-3, mlwr, mÚ 1) mo-i-aa roNhi roNday mar jaa Nhee N. The weepers who weep for the dead shall themselves die as well.
DEFINE	para 56349	nwnk KsmY eyvY BwvY ] (1287-4, mlwr, mÚ 1) naanak khasmai ayvai bhaavai. O Nanak, this is the Will of our Lord and Master.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	syeI muey ijin iciq n AwvY ]1] (1287-4, mlwr, mÚ 1) say-ee mu-ay jin chit na aavai. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	Those who do not remember the Lord, are dead. ||1||
RECORD	para 56351	mÚ 1 ] (1287-4) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 56352	muAw ipAwru pRIiq mueI muAw vYru vwdI ] (1287-4, mlwr, mÚ 1) mu-aa pi-aar pareet mu-ee mu-aa vair vaadee. Love dies, and affection dies; hatred and strife die.
RECORD	para 56353	vMnu gieAw rUpu ivxisAw duKI dyh rulI ] (1287-5, mlwr, mÚ 1) vann ga-i-aa roop vinsi-aa dukhee dayh rulee. The color fades, and beauty vanishes; the body suffers and collapses.
DEFINE	para 56354	ikQhu AwieAw kh gieAw ikhu n sIE ikhu sI ] (1287-5, mlwr, mÚ 1) kithhu aa-i-aa kah ga-i-aa kihu na see-o kihu see. Where did he come from? Where is he going? Did he exist or not?
RECORD	para 56355	min muiK glw goeIAw kIqw cwau rlI ] (1287-6, mlwr, mÚ 1) man mukh galaa go-ee-aa keetaa chaa-o ralee. The self-willed manmukh made empty boasts, indulging in parties and pleasures.
