DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, without the True Name, his honor is torn away, from head to foot. ||2||
RECORD	para 56357	pauVI ] (1287-7) pa-orhee. Pauree:
REQUIRE	para 56358	AMimRq nwmu sdw suKdwqw AMqy hoie sKweI ] (1287-7, mlwr, mÚ 1) amrit naam sadaa sukh-daata antay ho-ay sakhaa-ee. The Ambrosial Naam, the Name of the Lord, is forever the Giver of peace. It shall be your Help and Support in the end.
DEFINE	para 56359	bwJu gurU jgqu baurwnw nwvY swr n pweI ] (1287-7, mlwr, mÚ 1) baajh guroo jagat ba-uraanaa naavai saar na paa-ee. Without the Guru, the world is insane. It does not appreciate the worth of the Name.
DEFINE	para 56360	siqguru syvih sy prvwxu ijn@ joqI joiq imlweI ] (1287-8, mlwr, mÚ 1) satgur sayveh say parvaan jin H jotee jot milaa-ee. Those who serve the True Guru are accepted and approved. Their light merges into the Light.
RECORD	para 56361	so swihbu so syvku qyhw ijsu Bwxw mMin vsweI ] (1287-8, mlwr, mÚ 1) so saahib so sayvak tayhaa jis bhaanaa man vasaa-ee. That servant who enshrines the Lord's Will within his mind, becomes just like his Lord and Master.
RECORD	para 56362	AwpxY BwxY khu ikin suKu pwieAw AMDw AMDu kmweI ] (1287-9, mlwr, mÚ 1) aapnai bhaanai kaho kin sukh paa-i-aa anDhaa anDh kamaa-ee. Tell me, who has ever found peace by following his own will? The blind act in blindness.
RECORD	para 56363	ibiKAw kdy hI rjY nwhI mUrK BuK n jweI ] (1287-9, mlwr, mÚ 1) bikhi-aa kaday hee rajai naahee moorakh bhukh na jaa-ee. No one is ever satisfied and fulfilled by evil and corruption. The hunger of the fool is not satisfied.
DEFINE	para 56364	dUjY sBu ko lig ivguqw ibnu siqgur bUJ n pweI ] (1287-10, mlwr, mÚ 1) doojai sabh ko lag vigutaa bin satgur boojh na paa-ee. Attached to duality, all are ruined; without the True Guru, there is no understanding.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v20	siqguru syvy so suKu pwey ijs no ikrpw kry rjweI ]20] (1287-10, mlwr, mÚ 1) satgur sayvay so sukh paa-ay jis no kirpaa karay rajaa-ee. ||20||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v20	Those who serve the True Guru find peace; they are blessed with Grace by the Will of the Lord. ||20||
RECORD	para 56366	slok mÚ 1 ] (1287-11) salok mehlaa 1. Shalok, First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 56367	srmu Drmu duie nwnkw jy Dnu plY pwie ] (1287-11, mlwr, mÚ 1) saram Dharam du-ay naankaa jay Dhan palai paa-ay. Modesty and righteousness both, O Nanak, are qualities of those who are blessed with true wealth.
RECORD	para 56368	so Dnu imqRü n kWFIAY ijqu isir cotW Kwie ] (1287-11, mlwr, mÚ 1) so Dhan mitar na kaa Ndhee-ai jit sir chotaaN khaa-ay. Do not refer to that wealth as your friend, which leads you to get your head beaten.
DEFINE	para 56369	ijn kY plY Dnu vsY iqn kw nwau PkIr ] (1287-12, mlwr, mÚ 1) jin kai palai Dhan vasai tin kaa naa-o fakeer. Those who possess only this worldly wealth are known as paupers.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	ijn@ kY ihrdY qU vsih qy nr guxI ghIr ]1] (1287-12, mlwr, mÚ 1) jin H kai hirdai too vaseh tay nar gunee gaheer. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	But those, within whose hearts You dwell, O Lord - those people are oceans of virtue. ||1||
RECORD	para 56371	mÚ 1 ] (1287-13) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 56372	duKI dunI shyVIAY jwie q lgih duK ] (1287-13, mlwr, mÚ 1) dukhee dunee sahayrhee-ai jaa-ay ta lageh dukh. Worldly possessions are obtained by pain and suffering; when they are gone, they leave pain and suffering.
DEFINE	para 56373	nwnk scy nwm ibnu iksY n lQI BuK ] (1287-13, mlwr, mÚ 1) naanak sachay naam bin kisai na lathee bhukh. O Nanak, without the True Name, hunger is never satisfied.
WHEN	para 56374	rUpI BuK n auqrY jW dyKW qW BuK ] (1287-14, mlwr, mÚ 1) roopee bhukh na utrai jaa N daykhaaN taaN bhukh. Beauty does not satisfy hunger; when the man sees beauty, he hungers even more.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	jyqy rs srIr ky qyqy lgih duK ]2] (1287-14, mlwr, mÚ 1) jaytay ras sareer kay taytay lageh dukh. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	As many as are the pleasures of the body, so many are the pains which afflict it. ||2||
RECORD	para 56376	mÚ 1 ] (1287-14) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
RECORD	para 56377	AMDI kMmI AMDu mnu min AMDY qnu AMDu ] (1287-14, mlwr, mÚ 1) anDhee kammee anDh man man anDhai tan anDh. Acting blindly, the mind becomes blind. The blind mind makes the body blind.
RECORD	para 56378	ickiV lwieAY ikAw QIAY jW qutY pQr bMDu ] (1287-15, mlwr, mÚ 1) chikarh laa-i-ai ki-aa thee-ai jaa N tutai pathar banDh. Why make a dam with mud and plaster? Even a dam made of stones gives way.
DEFINE	para 56379	bMDu qutw byVI nhI nw qulhw nw hwQ ] (1287-15, mlwr, mÚ 1) banDh tutaa bayrhee nahee naa tulhaa naa haath. The dam has burst. There is no boat. There is no raft. The water's depth is unfathomable.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v3	nwnk scy nwm ivxu kyqy fuby swQ ]3] (1287-16, mlwr, mÚ 1) naanak sachay naam vin kaytay dubay saath. ||3||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v3	O Nanak, without the True Name, many multitudes have drowned. ||3||
RECORD	para 56381	mÚ 1 ] (1287-16) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
