RECORD	para 56383	lK lskr lK vwjy nyjy lKI GoVI pwiqswh ] (1287-17, mlwr, mÚ 1) lakh laskar lakh vaajay nayjay lakhee ghorhee paatisaah. Thousands of armies, thousands of marching bands and spearmen; the emperor of thousands of horsemen.
REQUIRE	para 56384	ijQY swieru lµGxw Agin pwxI Asgwh ] (1287-17, mlwr, mÚ 1) jithai saa-ir langh-naa agan paanee asgaah. The unfathomable ocean of fire and water must be crossed.
RECORD	para 56385	kMDI idis n AwveI DwhI pvY khwh ] (1287-18, mlwr, mÚ 1) kanDhee dis na aavee Dhaahee pavai kahaah. The other shore cannot be seen; only the roar of pitiful cries can be heard.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v4	nwnk EQY jwxIAih swh kyeI pwiqswh ]4] (1287-18, mlwr, mÚ 1) naanak othai jaanee-ahi saah kay-ee paatisaah. ||4||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 3 v4	O Nanak, there, it shall be known, whether anyone is a king or an emperor. ||4||
RECORD	para 56387	pauVI ] (1287-19) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 56388	ieknw glIN jMjIr bMid rbwxIAY ] (1287-19, mlwr, mÚ 1) iknaa galee N janjeer band rabaanee-ai. Some have chains around their necks, in bondage to the Lord.
DEFINE	para 56389	bDy Cutih sic scu pCwxIAY ] (1287-19, mlwr, mÚ 1) baDhay chhuteh sach sach pachhaanee-ai. They are released from bondage, realizing the True Lord as True.
DEFINE	para 56391	iliKAw plY pwie so scu jwxIAY ] (1288-1, mlwr, mÚ 1) likhi-aa palai paa-ay so sach jaanee-ai. One whose pre-ordained destiny is activated, comes to know the True Lord.
DEFINE	para 56392	hukmI hoie inbyVu gieAw jwxIAY ] (1288-1, mlwr, mÚ 1) hukmee ho-ay nibayrh ga-i-aa jaanee-ai. By God's Command, it is ordained. When the mortal goes, he knows.
RECORD	para 56393	Baujl qwrxhwru sbid pCwxIAY ] (1288-1, mlwr, mÚ 1) bha-ojal taaranhaar sabad pachhaanee-ai. Realize the Word of the Shabad, and cross over the terrifying world-ocean.
DEFINE	para 56394	cor jwr jUAwr pIVy GwxIAY ] (1288-2, mlwr, mÚ 1) chor jaar joo-aar peerhay ghaanee-ai. Thieves, adulterers and gamblers are pressed like seeds in the mill.
DEFINE	para 56395	inMdk lwieqbwr imly hV@vwxIAY ] (1288-2, mlwr, mÚ 1) nindak laa-itbaar milay harh Hvaanee-ai. Slanderers and gossipers are hand-cuffed.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v21	gurmuiK sic smwie su drgh jwxIAY ]21] (1288-2, mlwr, mÚ 1) gurmukh sach samaa-ay so dargeh jaanee-ai. ||21||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v21	The Gurmukh is absorbed in the True Lord, and is famous in the Court of the Lord. ||21||
RECORD	para 56397	slok mÚ 2 ] (1288-3) salok mehlaa 2. Shalok, Second Mehl:
DEFINE	para 56398	nwau PkIrY pwiqswhu mUrK pMifqu nwau ] (1288-3, mlwr, mÚ 2) naa-o fakeerai paatisaahu moorakh pandit naa-o. The beggar is known as an emperor, and the fool is known as a religious scholar.
DEFINE	para 56399	AMDy kw nwau pwrKU eyvY kry guAwau ] (1288-3, mlwr, mÚ 2) anDhay kaa naa-o paarkhoo ayvai karay gu-aa-o. The blind man is known as a seer; this is how people talk.
DEFINE	para 56400	ieliq kw nwau cauDrI kUVI pUry Qwau ] (1288-4, mlwr, mÚ 2) ilat kaa naa-o cha-uDhree koorhee pooray thaa-o. The trouble-maker is called a leader, and the liar is seated with honor.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v1	nwnk gurmuiK jwxIAY kil kw eyhu inAwau ]1] (1288-4, mlwr, mÚ 2) naanak gurmukh jaanee-ai kal kaa ayhu ni-aa-o. ||1||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs know that this is justice in the Dark Age of Kali Yuga. ||1||
RECORD	para 56402	mÚ 1 ] (1288-5) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 56403	hrxW bwjW qY iskdwrW eyn@w piV@Aw nwau ] (1288-5, mlwr, mÚ 1) harnaa N baajaa N tai sikdaaraaN ayn Haa parh H-aa naa-o. Deer, falcons and government officials are known to be trained and clever.
DEFINE	para 56404	PWDI lgI jwiq Phwiein AgY nwhI Qwau ] (1288-5, mlwr, mÚ 1) faaNDhee lagee jaat fahaa-in agai naahee thaa-o. When the trap is set, they trap their own kind; hereafter they will find no place of rest.
DEFINE	para 56405	so piVAw so pMifqu bInw ijn@I kmwxw nwau ] (1288-6, mlwr, mÚ 1) so parhi-aa so pandit beenaa jin Hee kamaanaa naa-o. He alone is learned and wise, and he alone is a scholar, who practices the Name.
RECORD	para 56406	pihlo dy jV AMdir jMmY qw aupir hovY CWau ] (1288-6, mlwr, mÚ 1) pahilo day jarh andar jammai taa upar hovai chhaaN-o. First, the tree puts down its roots, and then it spreads out its shade above.
DEFINE	para 56407	rwjy sIh mukdm kuqy ] (1288-7, mlwr, mÚ 1) raajay seeh mukdam kutay. The kings are tigers, and their officials are dogs;
RECORD	para 56408	jwie jgwiein@ bYTy suqy ] (1288-7, mlwr, mÚ 1) jaa-ay jagaa-ini H baithay sutay. they go out and awaken the sleeping people to harass them.
RECORD	para 56409	cwkr nhdw pwiein@ Gwau ] (1288-7, mlwr, mÚ 1) chaakar nahdaa paa-ini H ghaa-o. The public servants inflict wounds with their nails.
DEFINE	para 56410	rqu ipqu kuiqho cit jwhu ] (1288-8, mlwr, mÚ 1) rat pit kutiho chat jaahu. The dogs lick up the blood that is spilled.
