DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v1	It is good to be silent, O Nanak; without the Name, one's mouth spews forth only filth. ||1||
RECORD	para 56427	mÚ 1 ] (1288-14) mehlaa 1. First Mehl:
DEFINE	para 56428	rwju mwlu rUpu jwiq jobnu pMjy Tg ] (1288-14, mlwr, mÚ 1) raaj maal roop jaat joban panjay thag. Royal power, wealth, beauty, social status and youth are the five thieves.
RECORD	para 56429	eynI TgIN jgu TigAw iknY n rKI lj ] (1288-15, mlwr, mÚ 1) aynee thageeN jag thagi-aa kinai na rakhee laj. These thieves have plundered the world; no one's honor has been spared.
DEFINE	para 56430	eynw Tgin@ Tg sy ij gur kI pYrI pwih ] (1288-15, mlwr, mÚ 1) aynaa thagniH thag say je gur kee pairee paahi. But these thieves themselves are robbed, by those who fall at the Guru's Feet.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v2	nwnk krmw bwhry hoir kyqy muTy jwih ]2] (1288-16, mlwr, mÚ 1) naanak karmaa baahray hor kaytay muthay jaahi. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v2	O Nanak, the multitudes who do not have good karma are plundered. ||2||
RECORD	para 56432	pauVI ] (1288-16) pa-orhee. Pauree:
DEFINE	para 56433	piVAw lyKydwru lyKw mMgIAY ] (1288-16, mlwr, mÚ 1) parhi-aa laykhaydaar laykhaa mangee-ai. The learned and educated are called to account for their actions.
DEFINE	para 56434	ivxu nwvY kUiVAwru AauKw qMgIAY ] (1288-17, mlwr, mÚ 1) vin naavai koorhi-aar a-ukhaa tangee-ai. Without the Name, they are judged false; they become miserable and suffer hardship.
