RECORD	para 57430	hir Awpy iBiKAw pwiedw sB issit aupweI jIA jMq ] (1315-8, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har aapay bhikhi-aa paa-idaa sabh sisat upaa-ee jee-a jant. The Lord Himself gives in charity to the whole world, and all the beings and creatures which He created.
RECORD	para 57431	hir dyvhu dwnu dieAwl pRB hir mWgih hir jn sMq ] (1315-9, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har dayvhu daan da-i-aal parabh har maa Ngeh har jan sant. O Merciful Lord God, please bless me with Your Bountiful Gifts; the humble Saints of the Lord beg for them.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	jn nwnk ky pRB Awie imlu hm gwvh hir gux CMq ]1] (1315-10, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jan naanak kay parabh aa-ay mil ham gaavah har gun chhant. ||1||
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	O God of servant Nanak, please come and meet me; I sing the Songs of the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 57433	mÚ 4 ] (1315-10) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 57434	hir pRBu sjxu nwmu hir mY min qin nwmu srIir ] (1315-10, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har parabh sajan naam har mai man tan naam sareer. The Name of the Lord God is my Best Friend. My mind and body are drenched with the Naam.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	siB Awsw gurmuiK pUrIAw jn nwnk suix hir DIr ]2] (1315-11, kwnVw, mÚ 4) sabh aasaa gurmukh pooree-aa jan naanak sun har Dheer. ||2||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	All the hopes of the Gurmukh are fulfilled; servant Nanak is comforted, hearing the Naam, the Name of the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 57436	pauVI ] (1315-12, kwnVw, mÚ 4) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 57437	hir aUqmu hirAw nwmu hY hir purKu inrMjnu maulw ] (1315-12, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har ootam hari-aa naam hai har purakh niranjan ma-ulaa. The Lord's Sublime Name is energizing and rejuvenating. The Immaculate Lord, the Primal Being, blossoms forth.
RECORD	para 57438	jo jpdy hir hir idnsu rwiq iqn syvy crn inq kaulw ] (1315-12, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jo japday har har dinas raat tin sayvay charan nit ka-ulaa. Maya serves at the feet of those who chant and meditate on the Lord, Har, Har, day and night.
RECORD	para 57439	inq swir smwl@y sB jIA jMq hir vsY inkit sB jaulw ] (1315-13, kwnVw, mÚ 4) nit saar samaal Hay sabh jee-a jant har vasai nikat sabh ja-ulaa. The Lord always looks after and cares for all His beings and creatures; He is with all, near and far.
RECORD	para 57440	so bUJY ijsu Awip buJwiesI ijsu siqguru purKu pRBu saulw ] (1315-13, kwnVw, mÚ 4) so boojhai jis aap bujhaa-isee jis satgur purakh parabh sa-ulaa. Those whom the Lord inspires to understand, understand; the True Guru, God, the Primal Being, is pleased with them.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v6	siB gwvhu gux goivMd hry goivMd hry goivMd hry gux gwvq guxI smaulw ]6] (1315-14, kwnVw, mÚ 4) sabh gaavhu gun govind haray govind haray govind haray gun gaavat gunee sama- ulaa. ||6||
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v6	Let everyone sing the Praise of the Lord of the Universe, the Lord, the Lord of the Universe, the Lord, the Lord of the Universe; singing the Praise of the Lord, one is absorbed in His Glorious Virtues. ||6||
RECORD	para 57442	slok mÚ 4 ] (1315-15) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 57443	suiqAw hir pRBu cyiq min hir shij smwiD smwie ] (1315-15, kwnVw, mÚ 4) suti-aa har parabh chayt man har sahj samaaDh samaa-ay. O mind, even in sleep, remember the Lord God; let yourself be intuitively absorbed into the Celestial State of Samaadhi.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	jn nwnk hir hir cwau min guru quTw myly mwie ]1] (1315-16, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jan naanak har har chaa-o man gur tuthaa maylay maa-ay. ||1||
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	Servant Nanak's mind longs for the Lord, Har, Har. As the Guru pleases, he is absorbed into the Lord, O mother. ||1||
RECORD	para 57445	mÚ 4 ] (1315-16) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 57446	hir ieksu syqI iprhVI hir ieko myrY iciq ] (1315-16, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har ikas saytee pirharhee har iko mayrai chit. I am in love with the One and Only Lord; the One Lord fills my consciousness.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	jn nwnk ieku ADwru hir pRB ieks qy giq piq ]2] (1315-17, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jan naanak ik aDhaar har parabh ikas tay gat pat. ||2||
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	Servant Nanak takes the Support of the One Lord God; through the One, he obtains honor and salvation. ||2||
RECORD	para 57448	pauVI ] (1315-18) pa-orhee. Pauree:
UPHOLD	para 57449	pMcy sbd vjy miq gurmiq vfBwgI Anhdu vijAw ] (1315-18, kwnVw, mÚ 4) panchay sabad vajay mat gurmat vadbhaagee anhad vaji-aa. The Panch Shabad, the Five Primal Sounds, vibrate with the Wisdom of the Guru's Teachings; by great good fortune, the Unstruck Melody resonates and resounds.
RECORD	para 57450	Awnd mUlu rwmu sBu dyiKAw gur sbdI goivdu gijAw ] (1315-18, kwnVw, mÚ 4) aanad mool raam sabh daykhi-aa gur sabdee govid gaji-aa. I see the Lord, the Source of Bliss, everywhere; through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Lord of the Universe is revealed.
UPHOLD	para 57451	Awid jugwid vysu hir eyko miq gurmiq hir pRBu BijAw ] (1315-19, kwnVw, mÚ 4) aad jugaad vays har ayko mat gurmat har parabh bhaji-aa. From the primal beginning, and throughout the ages, the Lord has One Form. Through the Wisdom of the Guru's Teachings, I vibrate and meditate on the Lord God.
RECORD	para 57452	hir dyvhu dwnu dieAwl pRB jn rwKhu hir pRB lijAw ] (1315-19, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har dayvhu daan da-i-aal parabh jan raakho har parabh laji-aa. O Merciful Lord God, please bless me with Your Bounty; O Lord God, please preserve and protect the honor of Your humble servant.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v7	siB DMnu khhu guru siqgurU guru siqgurU ijqu imil hir pVdw kijAw ]7] (1316-1, kwnVw, mÚ 4) sabh Dhan kahhu gur satguroo gur satguroo jit mil har parh-daa kaji-aa. ||7||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v7	Let everyone proclaim: Blessed is the Guru, the True Guru, the Guru, the True Guru; meeting Him, the Lord covers their faults and deficiencies. ||7||
RECORD	para 57455	sloku mÚ 4 ] (1316-2) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 57456	Bgiq srovru auClY suBr Bry vhMin ] (1316-2, kwnVw, mÚ 4) bhagat sarovar uchhlai subhar bharay vahann. The sacred pool of devotional worship is filled to the brim and overflowing in torrents.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	ijnw siqguru mMinAw jn nwnk vf Bwg lhMin ]1] (1316-2, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jinaa satgur mani-aa jan naanak vad bhaag lahann. ||1||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	Those who obey the True Guru, O servant Nanak, are very fortunate - they find it. ||1||
RECORD	para 57458	mÚ 4 ] (1316-3) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 57459	hir hir nwm AsMK hir hir ky gun kQnu n jwih ] (1316-3, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har har naam asa Nkh har har kay gun kathan na jaahi. The Names of the Lord, Har, Har, are countless. The Glorious Virtues of the Lord, Har, Har, cannot be described.
RECORD	para 57460	hir hir Agmu AgwiD hir jn ikqu ibiD imlih imlwih ] (1316-4, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har har agam agaaDh har jan kit biDh mileh milaahi. The Lord, Har, Har, is Inaccessible and Unfathomable; how can the humble servants of the Lord be united in His Union?
RECORD	para 57461	hir hir jsu jpq jpMq jn ieku iqlu nhI kImiq pwie ] (1316-4, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har har jas japat japant jan ik til nahee keemat paa-ay. Those humble beings meditate and chant the Praises of the Lord, Har, Har, but they do not attain even a tiny bit of His Worth.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	jn nwnk hir Agm pRB hir myil lYhu liV lwie ]2] (1316-5, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jan naanak har agam parabh har mayl laihu larh laa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	O servant Nanak, the Lord God is Inaccessible; the Lord has attached me to His Robe, and united me in His Union. ||2||
RECORD	para 57463	pauVI ] (1316-6) pa-orhee. Pauree:
UPHOLD	para 57464	hir Agmu Agocru Agmu hir ikau kir hir drsnu ipKw ] (1316-6, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har agam agochar agam har ki-o kar har darsan pikhaa. The Lord is Inaccessible and Unfathomable. How will I see the Blessed Vision of the Lord's Darshan?
WHEN	para 57465	ikCu vKru hoie su vrnIAY iqsu rUpu n irKw ] (1316-6, kwnVw, mÚ 4) kichh vakhar ho-ay so varnee-ai tis roop na rikhaa. If He were a material object, then I could describe Him, but He has no form or feature.
WHEN	para 57466	ijsu buJwey Awip buJwie dyie soeI jnu idKw ] (1316-7, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jis bujhaa-ay aap bujhaa-ay day-ay so-ee jan dikhaa. Understanding comes only when the Lord Himself gives understanding; only such a humble being sees it.
RECORD	para 57467	sqsMgiq siqgur ctswl hY ijqu hir gux isKw ] (1316-7, kwnVw, mÚ 4) satsangat satgur chatsaal hai jit har gun sikhaa. The Sat Sangat, the True Congregation of the True Guru, is the school of the soul, where the Glorious Virtues of the Lord are studied.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v8	Dnu DMnu su rsnw DMnu kr DMnu su pwDw siqgurU ijqu imil hir lyKw ilKw ]8] (1316-8, kwnVw, mÚ 4) Dhan Dhan so rasnaa Dhan kar Dhan so paaDhaa satguroo jit mil har laykhaa likhaa. ||8||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v8	Blessed, blessed is the tongue, blessed is the hand, and blessed is the Teacher, the True Guru; meeting Him, the Account of the Lord is written. ||8||
RECORD	para 57469	slok mÚ 4 ] (1316-9) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 57470	hir hir nwmu AMimRqu hY hir jpIAY siqgur Bwie ] (1316-9, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har har naam amrit hai har japee-ai satgur bhaa-ay. The Name of the Lord, Har, Har, is Ambrosial Nectar. Meditate on the Lord, with love for the True Guru.
RECORD	para 57471	hir hir nwmu pivqu hY hir jpq sunq duKu jwie ] (1316-9, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har har naam pavit hai har japat sunat dukh jaa-ay. The Name of the Lord, Har, Har is Sacred and Pure. Chanting it and listening to it, pain is taken away.
RECORD	para 57472	hir nwmu iqnI AwrwiDAw ijn msqik iliKAw Duir pwie ] (1316-10, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har naam tinee aaraaDhi-aa jin mastak likhi-aa Dhur paa-ay. They alone worship and adore the Lord's Name, upon whose foreheads such pre- ordained destiny is written.
RECORD	para 57473	hir drgh jn pYnweIAin ijn hir min visAw Awie ] (1316-11, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har dargeh jan painaa-ee-an jin har man vasi-aa aa-ay. Those humble beings are honored in the Court of the Lord; the Lord comes to abide in their minds.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	jn nwnk qy muK aujly ijn hir suixAw min Bwie ]1] (1316-11, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jan naanak tay mukh ujlay jin har suni-aa man bhaa-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	O servant Nanak, their faces are radiant. They listen to the Lord; their minds are filled with love. ||1||
RECORD	para 57475	mÚ 4 ] (1316-12) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 57476	hir hir nwmu inDwnu hY gurmuiK pwieAw jwie ] (1316-12, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har har naam niDhaan hai gurmukh paa-i-aa jaa-ay. The Name of the Lord, Har, Har, is the greatest treasure. The Gurmukhs obtain it.
RECORD	para 57477	ijn Duir msqik iliKAw iqn siqguru imilAw Awie ] (1316-12, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jin Dhur mastak likhi-aa tin satgur mili-aa aa-ay. The True Guru comes to meet those who have such pre-ordained destiny written upon their foreheads.
DEFINE	para 57478	qnu mnu sIqlu hoieAw sWiq vsI min Awie ] (1316-13, kwnVw, mÚ 4) tan man seetal ho-i-aa saa Nt vasee man aa-ay. Their bodies and minds are cooled and soothed; peace and tranquility come to dwell in their minds.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	nwnk hir hir cauidAw sBu dwldu duKu lih jwie ]2] (1316-14, kwnVw, mÚ 4) naanak har har cha-udi-aa sabh daalad dukh leh jaa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	O Nanak, chanting the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, all poverty and pain is dispelled. ||2||
RECORD	para 57480	pauVI ] (1316-14) pa-orhee. Pauree:
RECORD	para 57481	hau vwirAw iqn kau sdw sdw ijnw siqguru myrw ipAwrw dyiKAw ] (1316-14, kwnVw, mÚ 4) ha-o vaari-aa tin ka-o sadaa sadaa jinaa satgur mayraa pi-aaraa daykhi-aa. I am a sacrifice, forever and ever, to those who have seen my Beloved True Guru.
RECORD	para 57482	iqn kau imilAw myrw siqgurU ijn kau Duir msqik lyiKAw ] (1316-15, kwnVw, mÚ 4) tin ka-o mili-aa mayraa satguroo jin ka-o Dhur mastak laykhi-aa. They alone meet my True Guru, who have such pre-ordaind destiny written upon their foreheads.
RECORD	para 57483	hir Agmu iDAwieAw gurmqI iqsu rUpu nhI pRB ryiKAw ] (1316-16, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har agam Dhi-aa-i-aa gurmatee tis roop nahee parabh raykh-i-aa. I meditate on the Inaccessible Lord, according to the Guru's Teachings; God has no form or feature.
RECORD	para 57484	gur bcin iDAwieAw ijnw Agmu hir qy Twkur syvk ril eyikAw ] (1316-16, kwnVw, mÚ 4) gur bachan Dhi-aa-i-aa jinaa agam har tay thaakur sayvak ral ayki-aa. Those who follow the Guru's Teachings and meditate on the Inaccessible Lord, merge with their Lord and Master and become one with Him.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v9	siB khhu muKhu nr nrhry nr nrhry nr nrhry hir lwhw hir Bgiq ivsyiKAw ]9] (1316-17, kwnVw, mÚ 4) sabh kahhu mukhahu nar narharay nar narharay nar narharay har laahaa har bhagat vasaykhi-aa. ||9||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v9	Let everyone proclaim out loud, the Name of the Lord, the Lord, the Lord; the profit of devotional worship of the Lord is blessed and sublime. ||9||
RECORD	para 57486	slok mÚ 4 ] (1316-18) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 57487	rwm nwmu rmu riv rhy rmu rwmo rwmu rmIiq ] (1316-18, kwnVw, mÚ 4) raam naam ram rav rahay ram raamo raam rameet. The Lord's Name is permeating and pervading all. Repeat the Name of the Lord, Raam, Raam.
RECORD	para 57488	Git Git Awqm rwmu hY pRiB Kylu kIE rMig rIiq ] (1316-19, kwnVw, mÚ 4) ghat ghat aatam raam hai parabh khayl kee-o rang reet. The Lord is in the home of each and every soul. God created this play with its various colors and forms.
RECORD	para 57489	hir inkit vsY jgjIvnw prgwsu kIE gur mIiq ] (1316-19, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har nikat vasai jagjeevanaa pargaas kee-o gur meet. The Lord, the Life of the World, dwells near at hand. The Guru, my Friend, has made this clear.
RECORD	para 57491	hir suAwmI hir pRBu iqn imly ijn iliKAw Duir hir pRIiq ] (1317-1, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har su-aamee har parabh tin milay jin likhi-aa Dhur har pareet. They alone meet the Lord, the Lord God, their Lord and Master, whose love for the Lord is pre-ordained.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	jn nwnk nwmu iDAwieAw gur bcin jipE min cIiq ]1] (1317-1, kwnVw, mÚ 4) jan naanak naam Dhi-aa-i-aa gur bachan japi-o man cheet. ||1||
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	Servant Nanak meditates on the Naam, the Name of the Lord; through the Word of the Guru's Teachings, chant it consciously with your mind. ||1||
RECORD	para 57493	mÚ 4 ] (1317-2) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 57494	hir pRBu sjxu loiV lhu Bwig vsY vfBwig ] (1317-2, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har parabh sajan lorh lahu bhaag vasai vadbhaag. Seek the Lord God, your Best Friend; by great good fortune, He comes to dwell with the very fortunate ones.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	guir pUrY dyKwilAw nwnk hir ilv lwig ]2] (1317-3, kwnVw, mÚ 4) gur poorai daykhaali-aa naanak har liv laag. ||2||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	Through the Perfect Guru, He is revealed, O Nanak, and one is lovingly attuned to the Lord. ||2||
RECORD	para 57496	pauVI ] (1317-3) pa-orhee. Pauree:
WHEN	para 57497	Dnu Dnu suhwvI sPl GVI ijqu hir syvw min BwxI ] (1317-3, kwnVw, mÚ 4) Dhan Dhan suhaavee safal gharhee jit har sayvaa man bhaanee. Blessed, blessed, beauteous and fruitful is that moment, when service to the Lord becomes pleasing to the mind.
RECORD	para 57498	hir kQw suxwvhu myry gurisKhu myry hir pRB AkQ khwxI ] (1317-4, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har kathaa sunavhu mayray gursikhahu mayray har parabh akath kahaanee. So proclaim the story of the Lord, O my GurSikhs; speak the Unspoken Speech of my Lord God.
RECORD	para 57499	ikau pweIAY ikau dyKIAY myrw hir pRBu suGVu sujwxI ] (1317-4, kwnVw, mÚ 4) ki-o paa-ee-ai ki-o daykhee-ai mayraa har parabh sugharh sujaanee. How can I attain Him? How can I see Him? My Lord God is All-knowing and All-seeing.
RECORD	para 57500	hir myil idKwey Awip hir gur bcnI nwim smwxI ] (1317-5, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har mayl dikhaa-ay aap har gur bachnee naam samaanee. Through the Word of the Guru's Teachings, the Lord reveals Himself; we merge in absorption in the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v10	iqn ivthu nwnku vwirAw jo jpdy hir inrbwxI ]10] (1317-5, kwnVw, mÚ 4) tin vitahu naanak vaari-aa jo japday har nirbaanee. ||10||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v10	Nanak is a sacrifice unto those who meditate on the Lord of Nirvaanaa. ||10||
RECORD	para 57502	slok mÚ 4 ] (1317-6) salok mehlaa 4. Shalok, Fourth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 57503	hir pRB rqy loiexw igAwn AMjnu guru dyie ] (1317-6, kwnVw, mÚ 4) har parabh ratay lo-inaa gi-aan anjan gur day-ay. One's eyes are anointed by the Lord God, when the Guru bestows the ointment of spiritual wisdom.
RECORD	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	mY pRBu sjxu pwieAw jn nwnk shij imlyie ]1] (1317-7, kwnVw, mÚ 4) mai parabh sajan paa-i-aa jan naanak sahj milay-ay. ||1||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v1	I have found God, my Best Friend; servant Nanak is intuitively absorbed into the Lord. ||1||
RECORD	para 57505	mÚ 4 ] (1317-7) mehlaa 4. Fourth Mehl:
RECORD	para 57506	gurmuiK AMqir sWiq hY min qin nwim smwie ] (1317-7, kwnVw, mÚ 4) gurmukh antar saa Nt hai man tan naam samaa-ay. The Gurmukh is filled with peace and tranquility deep within. His mind and body are absorbed in the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 57507	nwmu icqvY nwmo pVY nwim rhY ilv lwie ] (1317-8, kwnVw, mÚ 4) naam chitvai naamo parhai naam rahai liv laa-ay. He thinks of the Naam, and reads the Naam; he remains lovingly attuned to the Naam.
DEFINE	para 57508	nwmu pdwrQu pweIAY icMqw geI iblwie ] (1317-8, kwnVw, mÚ 4) naam padaarath paa-ee-ai chintaa ga-ee bilaa-ay. He obtains the Treasure of the Naam, and is rid of anxiety.
RECORD	para 57509	siqguir imilAY nwmu aUpjY iqRsnw BuK sB jwie ] (1317-9, kwnVw, mÚ 4) satgur mili-ai naam oopjai tarisnaa bhukh sabh jaa-ay. Meeting with the True Guru, the Naam wells up, and all hunger and thirst depart.
ALLOW	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	nwnk nwmy riqAw nwmo plY pwie ]2] (1317-9, kwnVw, mÚ 4) naanak naamay rati-aa naamo palai paa-ay. ||2||
DEFINE	kwnVy kI vwr mhlw 4 mUsy kI vwr kI DunI v2	O Nanak, one who is imbued with the Naam, gathers the Naam in his lap. ||2||
RECORD	para 57511	pauVI ] (1317-10) pa-orhee. Pauree:
