DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v2	bilhwrI ies jwiq kau ijh jipE isrjnhwru ]2] (1364-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) balihaaree is jaat ka-o jih japi-o sirjanhaar. ||2||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v2	I am a sacrifice to this social class, in which I chant and meditate on the Creator. ||2||
RECORD	para 59430	kbIr fgmg ikAw krih khw fulwvih jIau ] (1364-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer dagmag ki-aa karahi kahaa dulaaveh jee-o. Kabeer, why do you stumble? Why does your soul waver?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v3	srb sUK ko nwieko rwm nwm rsu pIau ]3] (1364-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) sarab sookh ko naa-iko raam naam ras pee-o. ||3||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v3	He is the Lord of all comforts and peace; drink in the Sublime Essence of the Lord's Name. ||3||
RECORD	para 59432	kbIr kMcn ky kuMfl bny aUpir lwl jVwau ] (1364-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kanchan kay kundal banay oopar laal jarhaa-o. Kabeer, earrings made of gold and studded with jewels,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v4	dIsih dwDy kwn ijau ijn@ min nwhI nwau ]4] (1364-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) deeseh daaDhay kaan ji-o jin H man naahee naa-o. ||4||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v4	look like burnt twigs, if the Name is not in the mind. ||4||
DEFINE	para 59434	kbIr AYsw eyku AwDu jo jIvq imrqku hoie ] (1364-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aisaa ayk aaDh jo jeevat mirtak ho-ay. Kabeer, rare is such a person, who remains dead while yet alive.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v5	inrBY hoie kY gun rvY jq pyKau qq soie ]5] (1364-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) nirbhai ho-ay kai gun ravai jat paykha-o tat so-ay. ||5||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v5	Singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, he is fearless. Wherever I look, the Lord is there. ||5||
REQUIRE	para 59436	kbIr jw idn hau mUAw pwCY BieAw Anµdu ] (1364-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jaa din ha-o moo-aa paachhai bha-i-aa anand. Kabeer, on the day when I die, afterwards there shall be bliss.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v6	moih imilE pRBu Awpnw sMgI Bjih guoibMdu ]6] (1364-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) mohi mili-o parabh aapnaa sangee bhajeh gobind. ||6||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v6	I shall meet with my Lord God. Those with me shall meditate and vibrate on the Lord of the Universe. ||6||
DEFINE	para 59438	kbIr sB qy hm bury hm qij Blo sBu koie ] (1364-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sabh tay ham buray ham taj bhalo sabh ko-ay. Kabeer, I am the worst of all. Everyone else is good.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v7	ijin AYsw kir bUiJAw mIqu hmwrw soie ]7] (1364-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jin aisaa kar boojhi-aa meet hamaaraa so-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v7	Whoever understands this is a friend of mine. ||7||
RECORD	para 59440	kbIr AweI muJih pih Aink kry kir Bys ] (1364-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aa-ee mujheh peh anik karay kar bhays. Kabeer, she came to me in various forms and disguises.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v8	hm rwKy gur Awpny auin kIno Awdysu ]8] (1364-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ham raakhay gur aapnay un keeno aadays. ||8||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v8	My Guru saved me, and now she bows humbly to me. ||8||
REQUIRE	para 59442	kbIr soeI mwrIAY ijh mUAY suKu hoie ] (1364-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer so-ee maaree-ai jih moo-ai sukh ho-ay. Kabeer, kill only that, which, when killed, shall bring peace.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v9	Blo Blo sBu ko khY buro n mwnY koie ]9] (1364-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) bhalo bhalo sabh ko kahai buro na maanai ko-ay. ||9||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v9	Everyone shall call you good, very good, and no one shall think you are bad. ||9||
DEFINE	para 59444	kbIr rwqI hovih kwrIAw kwry aUBy jMq ] (1364-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer raatee hoveh kaaree-aa kaaray oobhay jant. Kabeer, the night is dark, and men go about doing their dark deeds.
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v10	lY Pwhy auiT Dwvqy is jwin mwry BgvMq ]10] (1365-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) lai faahay uth Dhaavtay se jaan maaray bhagvant. ||10||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v10	They take the noose and run around; but rest assured that God shall destroy them. ||10||
DEFINE	para 59447	kbIr cMdn kw ibrvw Blw byiV@E Fwk plws ] (1365-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer chandan kaa birvaa bhalaa bayrheha-o dhaak palaas. Kabeer, the sandalwood tree is good, even though it is surrounded by weeds.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v11	Eie BI cMdnu hoie rhy bsy ju cMdn pwis ]11] (1365-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) o-ay bhee chandan ho-ay rahay basay jo chandan paas. ||11||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v11	Those who dwell near the sandalwood tree, become just like the sandalwood tree. ||11||
DEFINE	para 59449	kbIr bWsu bfweI bUifAw ieau mq fUbhu koie ] (1365-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer baa Ns badaa-ee boodi-aa i-o mat doobahu ko-ay. Kabeer, the bamboo is drowned in its egotistical pride. No one should drown like this.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v12	cMdn kY inkty bsY bWsu sugMDu n hoie ]12] (1365-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) chandan kai niktay basai baa Ns suganDh na ho-ay. ||12||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v12	Bamboo also dwells near the sandalwood tree, but it does not take up its fragrance. ||12||
FORBID	para 59451	kbIr dInu gvwieAw dunI isau dunI n cwlI swiQ ] (1365-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer deen gavaa-i-aa dunee si-o dunee na chaalee saath. Kabeer, the mortal loses his faith, for the sake of the world, but the world shall not go along with him in the end.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v13	pwie kuhwVw mwirAw gwPil ApunY hwiQ ]13] (1365-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paa-ay kuhaarhaa maari-aa gaafal apunai haath. ||13||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v13	The idiot strikes his own foot with the axe by his own hand. ||13||
RECORD	para 59453	kbIr jh jh hau iPirE kauqk TwE Twie ] (1365-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jah jah ha-o firi-o ka-utak thaa-o thaa-ay. Kabeer, wherever I go, I see wonders everywhere.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v14	iek rwm snyhI bwhrw aUjru myrY BWie ]14] (1365-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ik raam sanayhee baahraa oojar mayrai bhaa N-ay. ||14||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v14	But without the devotees of the One Lord, it is all wilderness to me. ||14||
UPHOLD	para 59455	kbIr sMqn kI JuMgIAw BlI BiT kusqI gwau ] (1365-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer santan kee jhungee-aa bhalee bhath kustee gaa-o. Kabeer, the dwelling of the Saints is good; the dwelling of the unrighteous burns like an oven.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v15	Awig lgau iqh Daulhr ijh nwhI hir ko nwau ]15] (1365-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aag laga-o tih Dha-ulhar jih naahee har ko naa-o. ||15||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v15	Those mansions in which the Lord's Name is not chanted might just as well burn down. ||15||
DEFINE	para 59457	kbIr sMq mUey ikAw roeIAY jo Apuny igRih jwie ] (1365-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sant moo-ay ki-aa ro-ee-ai jo apunay garihi jaa-ay. Kabeer, why cry at the death of a Saint? He is just going back to his home.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v16	rovhu swkq bwpury ju hwtY hwt ibkwie ]16] (1365-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) rovhu saakat baapuray jo haatai haat bikaa-ay. ||16||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v16	Cry for the wretched, faithless cynic, who is sold from store to store. ||16||
DEFINE	para 59459	kbIr swkqu AYsw hY jYsI lsn kI Kwin ] (1365-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saakat aisaa hai jaisee lasan kee khaan. Kabeer, the faithless cynic is like a piece of garlic.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v17	kony bYTy KweIAY prgt hoie indwin ]17] (1365-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) konay baithay khaa-ee-ai pargat ho-ay nidaan. ||17||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v17	Even if you eat it sitting in a corner, it becomes obvious to everyone. ||17||
DEFINE	para 59461	kbIr mwieAw folnI pvnu Jkolnhwru ] (1365-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maa-i-aa dolnee pavan jhakolanhaar. Kabeer, Maya is the butter-churn, and the breath is the churning-stick.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v18	sMqhu mwKnu KwieAw CwiC pIAY sMswru ]18] (1365-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) santahu maakhan khaa-i-aa chhaachh pee-ai sansaar. ||18||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v18	The Saints eat the butter, while the world drinks the whey. ||18||
DEFINE	para 59463	kbIr mwieAw folnI pvnu vhY ihv Dwr ] (1365-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maa-i-aa dolnee pavan vahai hiv Dhaar. Kabeer, Maya is the butter-churn; the breath flows like ice water.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v19	ijin ibloieAw iqin KwieAw Avr iblovnhwr ]19] (1365-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jin bilo-i-aa tin khaa-i-aa avar bilovanhaar. ||19||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v19	Whoever does the churning eats the butter; the others are just churning-sticks. ||19||
DEFINE	para 59465	kbIr mwieAw cortI muis muis lwvY hwit ] (1365-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maa-i-aa chortee mus mus laavai haat. Kabeer, Maya is the thief, which breaks in and plunders the store.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v20	eyku kbIrw nw musY ijin kInI bwrh bwt ]20] (1365-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ayk kabeeraa naa musai jin keenee baarah baat. ||20||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v20	Only Kabeer is not plundered; he has cut her into twelve pieces. ||20||
RECORD	para 59467	kbIr sUKu n eyNh juig krih ju bhuqY mIq ] (1365-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sookh na ay Nh jug karahi jo bahutai meet. Kabeer, peace does not come in this world by making lots of friends.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v21	jo icqu rwKih eyk isau qy suKu pwvih nIq ]21] (1365-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jo chit raakhahi ayk si-o tay sukh paavahi neet. ||21||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v21	Those who keep their consciousness focused on the One Lord shall find eternal peace. ||21||
DEFINE	para 59469	kbIr ijsu mrny qy jgu frY myry min Awnµdu ] (1365-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jis marnay tay jag darai mayray man aanand. Kabeer, the world is afraid of death - that death fills my mind with bliss.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v22	mrny hI qy pweIAY pUrnu prmwnµdu ]22] (1365-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) marnay hee tay paa-ee-ai pooran parmaanand. ||22||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v22	It is only by death that perfect, supreme bliss is obtained. ||22||
DEFINE	para 59471	rwm pdwrQu pwie kY kbIrw gWiT n Kol@ ] (1365-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raam padaarath paa-ay kai kabeeraa gaa Nth na kholH. The Treasure of the Lord is obtained, O Kabeer, but do not undo its knot.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v23	nhI ptxu nhI pwrKU nhI gwhku nhI molu ]23] (1365-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) nahee patan nahee paarkhoo nahee gaahak nahee mol. ||23||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v23	There is no market to sell it, no appraiser, no customer, and no price. ||23||
DEFINE	para 59473	kbIr qw isau pRIiq kir jw ko Twkuru rwmu ] (1365-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer taa si-o pareet kar jaa ko thaakur raam. Kabeer, be in love with only that one, whose Master is the Lord.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v24	pMifq rwjy BUpqI Awvih kauny kwm ]24] (1365-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) pandit raajay bhooptee aavahi ka-unay kaam. ||24||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v24	The Pandits, the religious scholars, kings and landlords - what good is love for them? ||24||
DEFINE	para 59475	kbIr pRIiq iek isau kIey Awn duibDw jwie ] (1365-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer pareet ik si-o kee-ay aan dubiDhaa jaa-ay. Kabeer, when you are in love with the One Lord, duality and alienation depart.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v25	BwvY lWby kys kru BwvY Grir mufwie ]25] (1365-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) bhaavai laa Nbay kays kar bhaavai gharar mudaa-ay. ||25||
ALLOW	cauboly mhlw 5 v25	You may have long hair, or you may shave your head bald. ||25||
DEFINE	para 59477	kbIr jgu kwjl kI koTrI AMD pry iqs mwih ] (1365-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jag kaajal kee kothree anDh paray tis maahi. Kabeer, the world is a room filled with black soot; the blind fall into its trap.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v26	hau bilhwrI iqn kau pYis ju nIkis jwih ]26] (1365-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ha-o balihaaree tin ka-o pais jo neekas jaahi. ||26||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v26	I am a sacrifice to those who are thrown in, and still escape. ||26||
REQUIRE	para 59479	kbIr iehu qnu jwiegw skhu q lyhu bhoir ] (1365-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ih tan jaa-igaa sakahu ta layho bahor. Kabeer, this body shall perish; save it, if you can.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v27	nWgy pwvhu qy gey ijn ky lwK kroir ]27] (1365-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) naa Ngay paavhu tay ga-ay jin kay laakh karor. ||27||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v27	Even those who have tens of thousands and millions, must depart bare-footed in the end. ||27||
REQUIRE	para 59481	kbIr iehu qnu jwiegw kvnY mwrig lwie ] (1365-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ih tan jaa-igaa kavnai maarag laa-ay. Kabeer, this body shall perish; place it on the path.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v28	kY sMgiq kir swD kI kY hir ky gun gwie ]28] (1365-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kai sangat kar saaDh kee kai har kay gun gaa-ay. ||28||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v28	Either join the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, or sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||28||
RECORD	para 59483	kbIr mrqw mrqw jgu mUAw mir BI n jwinAw koie ] (1365-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer martaa martaa jag moo-aa mar bhee na jaani-aa ko-ay. Kabeer, dying, dying, the whole world has to die, and yet, none know how to die.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v29	AYsy mrny jo mrY bhuir n mrnw hoie ]29] (1366-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aisay marnay jo marai bahur na marnaa ho-ay. ||29||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v29	Let those who die, die such a death, that they shall never have to die again. ||29||
RECORD	para 59486	kbIr mwns jnmu dulµBu hY hoie n bwrY bwr ] (1366-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maanas janam dulambh hai ho-ay na baarai baar. Kabeer, it is so difficult to obtain this human body; it does not just come over and over again.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v30	ijau bn Pl pwky Buie igrih bhuir n lwgih fwr ]30] (1366-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ji-o ban fal paakay bhu-ay gireh bahur na laageh daar. ||30||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v30	It is like the ripe fruit on the tree; when it falls to the ground, it cannot be re-attached to the branch. ||30||
DEFINE	para 59488	kbIrw quhI kbIru qU qyro nwau kbIru ] (1366-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeeraa tuhee kabeer too tayro naa-o kabeer. Kabeer, you are Kabeer; your name means great.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v31	rwm rqnu qb pweIAY jau pihly qjih srIru ]31] (1366-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raam ratan tab paa-ee-ai ja-o pahilay tajeh sareer. ||31||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v31	O Lord, You are Kabeer. The Jewel of the Lord is obtained, when the mortal first gives up his body. ||31||
RECORD	para 59490	kbIr JMKu n JMKIAY qumro kihE n hoie ] (1366-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jhankh na jhankhee-ai tumro kahi-o na ho-ay. Kabeer, do not struggle in stubborn pride; nothing happens just because you say so.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v32	krm krIm ju kir rhy myit n swkY koie ]32] (1366-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) karam kareem jo kar rahay mayt na saakai ko-ay. ||32||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v32	No one can erase the actions of the Merciful Lord. ||32||
DEFINE	para 59492	kbIr ksautI rwm kI JUTw itkY n koie ] (1366-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kasa-utee raam kee jhoothaa tikai na ko-ay. Kabeer, no one who is false can withstand the Touchstone of the Lord.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v33	rwm ksautI so shY jo mir jIvw hoie ]33] (1366-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raam kasa-utee so sahai jo mar jeevaa ho-ay. ||33||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v33	He alone can pass the test of the Lord's Touchstone, who remains dead while yet alive. ||33||
RECORD	para 59494	kbIr aUjl pihrih kwpry pwn supwrI Kwih ] (1366-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer oojal pahirahi kaapray paan supaaree khaahi. Kabeer, some wear gaudy robes, and chew betel leaves and betel nuts.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v34	eyks hir ky nwm ibnu bwDy jm puir jWih ]34] (1366-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aykas har kay naam bin baaDhay jam pur jaa Nhi. ||34||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v34	Without the Name of the One Lord, they are bound and gagged and taken to the City of Death. ||34||
DEFINE	para 59496	kbIr byVw jrjrw PUty CyNk hjwr ] (1366-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer bayrhaa jarjaraa footay chhay Nk hajaar. Kabeer, the boat is old, and it has thousands of holes.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v35	hrUey hrUey iqir gey fUby ijn isr Bwr ]35] (1366-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) haroo-ay haroo-ay tir ga-ay doobay jin sir bhaar. ||35||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v35	Those who are light get across, while those who carry the weight of their sins on their heads are drowned. ||35||
RECORD	para 59498	kbIr hwf jry ijau lwkrI kys jry ijau Gwsu ] (1366-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer haad jaray ji-o laakree kays jaray ji-o ghaas. Kabeer, the bones burn like wood, and the hair burns like straw.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v36	iehu jgu jrqw dyiK kY BieE kbIru audwsu ]36] (1366-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ih jag jartaa daykh kai bha-i-o kabeer udaas. ||36||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v36	Seeing the world burning like this, Kabeer has become sad. ||36||
RECORD	para 59500	kbIr grbu n kIjIAY cwm lpyty hwf ] (1366-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer garab na keejee-ai chaam lapaytay haad. Kabeer, do not be so proud of your bones wrapped up in skin.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v37	hYvr aUpir CqR qr qy Puin DrnI gwf ]37] (1366-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) haivar oopar chhatar tar tay fun Dharnee gaad. ||37||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v37	Those who were on their horses and under their canopies, were eventually buried under the ground. ||37||
RECORD	para 59502	kbIr grbu n kIjIAY aUcw dyiK Avwsu ] (1366-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer garab na keejee-ai oochaa daykh avaas. Kabeer, do not be so proud of your tall mansions.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v38	Awju kwil@ Buie lytxw aUpir jwmY Gwsu ]38] (1366-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aaj kaali H bhu-ay laytnaa oopar jaamai ghaas. ||38||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v38	Today or tomorrow, you shall lie beneath the ground, and the grass shall grow above you. ||38||
RECORD	para 59504	kbIr grbu n kIjIAY rMku n hsIAY koie ] (1366-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer garab na keejee-ai rank na hasee-ai ko-ay. Kabeer, do not be so proud, and do not laugh at the poor.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v39	Ajhu su nwau smuMdR mih ikAw jwnau ikAw hoie ]39] (1366-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ajahu so naa-o samundar meh ki-aa jaan-o ki-aa ho-ay. ||39||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v39	Your boat is still out at sea; who knows what will happen? ||39||
RECORD	para 59506	kbIr grbu n kIjIAY dyhI dyiK surMg ] (1366-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer garab na keejee-ai dayhee daykh surang. Kabeer, do not be so proud, looking at your beautiful body.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v40	Awju kwil@ qij jwhugy ijau kWcurI BuXMg ]40] (1366-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aaj kaali H taj jaahugay ji-o kaa Nchuree bhuyang. ||40||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v40	Today or tomorrow, you will have to leave it behind, like the snake shedding its skin. ||40||
REQUIRE	para 59508	kbIr lUtnw hY q lUit lY rwm nwm hY lUit ] (1366-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer lootnaa hai ta loot lai raam naam hai loot. Kabeer, if you must rob and plunder, then plunder the plunder of the Lord's Name.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v41	iPir pwCY pCuqwhugy pRwn jwihMgy CUit ]41] (1366-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) fir paachhai pachhutaahugay paraan jaahingay chhoot. ||41||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v41	Otherwise, in the world hereafter, you will regret and repent, when the breath of life leaves the body. ||41||
DEFINE	para 59510	kbIr AYsw koeI n jnimE ApnY Gir lwvY Awig ] (1366-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aisaa ko-ee na janmi-o apnai ghar laavai aag. Kabeer, there is no one born, who burns his own home,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v42	pWcau lirkw jwir kY rhY rwm ilv lwig ]42] (1366-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paa Ncha-o larikaa jaar kai rahai raam liv laag. ||42||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v42	and burning his five sons, remains lovingly attuned to the Lord. ||42||
DEFINE	para 59512	ko hY lirkw byceI lirkI bycY koie ] (1366-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ko hai larikaa baych-ee larikee baychai ko-ay. Kabeer, how rare are those who sell their son and sell their daughter
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v43	swJw krY kbIr isau hir sMig bnju kryie ]43] (1366-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) saajhaa karai kabeer si-o har sang banaj karay-i. ||43||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v43	and, entering into partnership with Kabeer, deal with the Lord. ||43||
RECORD	para 59514	kbIr ieh cyqwvnI mq shsw rih jwie ] (1366-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ih chaytaavnee mat sahsaa reh jaa-ay. Kabeer, let me remind you of this. Do not be skeptical or cynical.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v44	pwCY Bog ju Bogvy iqn ko guVu lY Kwih ]44] (1366-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paachhai bhog jo bhogvay tin ko gurh lai khaahi. ||44||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v44	Those pleasures which you enjoyed so much in the past - now you must eat their fruits. ||44||
RECORD	para 59516	kbIr mY jwinE piVbo Blo piVby isau Bl jogu ] (1366-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer mai jaani-o parhibo bhalo parhibay si-o bhal jog. Kabeer, at first, I thought learning was good; then I thought Yoga was better.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v45	Bgiq n Cwfau rwm kI BwvY inMdau logu ]45] (1366-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) bhagat na chhaada-o raam kee bhaavai ninda-o log. ||45||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v45	I shall never abandon devotional worship of the Lord, even though people may slander me. ||45||
UPHOLD	para 59518	kbIr logu ik inMdY bpuVw ijh min nwhI igAwnu ] (1366-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer log ke nindai bapurhaa jih man naahee gi-aan. Kabeer, how can the wretched people slander me? They have no wisdom or intelligence.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v46	rwm kbIrw riv rhy Avr qjy sB kwm ]46] (1366-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raam kabeeraa rav rahay avar tajay sabh kaam. ||46||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v46	Kabeer continues to dwell upon the Lord's Name; I have abandoned all other affairs. ||46||
RECORD	para 59520	kbIr prdysI kY GwGrY chu idis lwgI Awig ] (1366-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer pardaysee kai ghaaghrai chahu dis laagee aag. Kabeer, the robe of the stranger-soul has caught fire on all four sides.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v47	iKMQw jil koielw BeI qwgy AWc n lwg ]47] (1366-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) khinthaa jal ko-ilaa bha-ee taagay aa Nch na laag. ||47||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v47	The cloth of the body has been burnt and reduced to charcoal, but the fire did not touch the thread of the soul. ||47||
RECORD	para 59522	kbIr iKMQw jil koielw BeI Kwpru PUt mPUt ] (1366-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer khinthaa jal ko-ilaa bha-ee khaapar foot mafoot. Kabeer, the cloth has been burnt and reduced to charcoal, and the begging bowl is shattered into pieces.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v48	jogI bpuVw KyilE Awsin rhI ibBUiq ]48] (1366-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jogee bapurhaa khayli-o aasan rahee bibhoot. ||48||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v48	The poor Yogi has played out his game; only ashes remain on his seat. ||48||
DEFINE	para 59525	kbIr QorY jil mwCulI JIvir myilE jwlu ] (1367-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer thorai jal maachhulee jheevar mayli-o jaal. Kabeer, the fish is in the shallow water; the fisherman has cast his net.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v49	ieh toGnY n CUtsih iPir kir smuMdu sm@wil ]49] (1367-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ih toghnai na chhootsahi fir kar samund sam Haal. ||49||
FORBID	cauboly mhlw 5 v49	You shall not escape this little pool; think about returning to the ocean. ||49||
DEFINE	para 59527	kbIr smuMdu n CofIAY jau Aiq Kwro hoie ] (1367-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer samund na chhodee-ai ja-o at khaaro ho-ay. Kabeer, do not leave the ocean, even if it is very salty.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v50	poKir poKir FUFqy Blo n kihhY koie ]50] (1367-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) pokhar pokhar dhoodh-tay bhalo na kahihai ko-ay. ||50||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v50	If you poke around searching from puddle to puddle, no one will call you smart. ||50||
DEFINE	para 59529	kbIr ingusWeyN bih gey QWGI nwhI koie ] (1367-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer nigusaa N-ay N bahi ga-ay thaa Nghee naahee ko-ay. Kabeer, those who have no guru are washed away. No one can help them.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v51	dIn grIbI AwpunI krqy hoie su hoie ]51] (1367-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) deen gareebee aapunee kartay ho-ay so ho-ay. ||51||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v51	Be meek and humble; whatever happens is what the Creator Lord does. ||51||
RECORD	para 59531	kbIr bYsnau kI kUkir BlI swkq kI burI mwie ] (1367-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer baisna-o kee kookar bhalee saakat kee buree maa-ay. Kabeer, even the dog of a devotee is good, while the mother of the faithless cynic is bad.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v52	Eh inq sunY hir nwm jsu auh pwp ibswhn jwie ]52] (1367-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) oh nit sunai har naam jas uh paap bisaahan jaa-ay. ||52||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v52	The dog hears the Praises of the Lord's Name, while the other is engaged in sin. ||52||
DEFINE	para 59533	kbIr hrnw dUblw iehu hrIAwrw qwlu ] (1367-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer harnaa dooblaa ih haree-aaraa taal. Kabeer, the deer is weak, and the pool is lush with green vegetation.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v53	lwK AhyrI eyku jIau kyqw bMcau kwlu ]53] (1367-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) laakh ahayree ayk jee-o kaytaa bancha-o kaal. ||53||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v53	Thousands of hunters are chasing after the soul; how long can it escape death? ||53||
RECORD	para 59535	kbIr gMgw qIr ju Gru krih pIvih inrml nIru ] (1367-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer gangaa teer jo ghar karahi peeveh nirmal neer. Kabeer, some make their homes on the banks of the Ganges, and drink pure water.
ALLOW	cauboly mhlw 5 v54	ibnu hir Bgiq n mukiq hoie ieau kih rmy kbIr ]54] (1367-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) bin har bhagat na mukat ho-ay i-o kahi ramay kabeer. ||54||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v54	Without devotional worship of the Lord, they are not liberated. Kabeer proclaims this. ||54||
RECORD	para 59537	kbIr mnu inrmlu BieAw jYsw gMgw nIru ] (1367-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer man nirmal bha-i-aa jaisaa gangaa neer. Kabeer, my mind has become immaculate, like the waters of the Ganges.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v55	pwCY lwgo hir iPrY khq kbIr kbIr ]55] (1367-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paachhai laago har firai kahat kabeer kabeer. ||55||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v55	The Lord follows after me, calling, "Kabeer! Kabeer!"||55||
DEFINE	para 59539	kbIr hrdI pIArI cUMnW aUjl Bwie ] (1367-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer hardee pee-aree chooNnaa N oojal bhaa-ay. Kabeer, tumeric is yelow, and lime is white.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v56	rwm snyhI qau imlY donau brn gvwie ]56] (1367-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raam sanayhee ta-o milai don-o baran gavaa-ay. ||56||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v56	You shall meet the Beloved Lord, only when both colors are lost. ||56||
RECORD	para 59541	kbIr hrdI pIrqnu hrY cUn ichnu n rhwie ] (1367-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer hardee peertan harai choon chihan na rahaa-ay. Kabeer, tumeric has lost its yellow color, and no trace of lime's whiteness remains.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v57	bilhwrI ieh pRIiq kau ijh jwiq brnu kulu jwie ]57] (1367-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) balihaaree ih pareet ka-o jih jaat baran kul jaa-ay. ||57||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v57	I am a sacrifice to this love, by which social class and status, color and ancestry are taken away. ||57||
DEFINE	para 59543	kbIr mukiq duAwrw sMkurw rweI dseyN Bwie ] (1367-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer mukat du-aaraa sankuraa raa-ee das-ayN bhaa-ay. Kabeer, the door of liberation is very narrow, less than the width of a mustard seed.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v58	mnu qau mYglu hoie rihE inkso ikau kY jwie ]58] (1367-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) man ta-o maigal ho-ay rahi-o nikso ki-o kai jaa-ay. ||58||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v58	Your mind is larger than an elephant; how will it pass through? ||58||
WHEN	para 59545	kbIr AYsw siqguru jy imlY quTw kry pswau ] (1367-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aisaa satgur jay milai tuthaa karay pasaa-o. Kabeer, if I meet such a True Guru, who mercifully blesses me with the gift,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v59	mukiq duAwrw moklw shjy Awvau jwau ]59] (1367-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) mukat du-aaraa moklaa sehjay aava-o jaa-o. ||59||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v59	then the door of liberation will open wide for me, and I will easily pass through. ||59||
RECORD	para 59547	kbIr nw muoih Cwin n CwprI nw muoih Gru nhI gwau ] (1367-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer naa mohi chhaan na chhaapree naa mohi ghar nahee gaa-o. Kabeer, I have no hut or hovel, no house or village.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v60	mq hir pUCY kaunu hY myry jwiq n nwau ]60] (1367-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) mat har poochhai ka-un hai mayray jaat na naa-o. ||60||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v60	I hope that the Lord will not ask who I am. I have no social status or name. ||60||
RECORD	para 59549	kbIr muih mrny kw cwau hY mrau q hir kY duAwr ] (1367-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer muhi marnay kaa chaa-o hai mara-o ta har kai du-aar. Kabeer, I long to die; let me die at the Lord's Door.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v61	mq hir pUCY kaunu hY prw hmwrY bwr ]61] (1367-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) mat har poochhai ka-un hai paraa hamaarai baar. ||61||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v61	I hope that the Lord does not ask, "Who is this, lying at my door?"||61||
FORBID	para 59551	kbIr nw hm kIAw n krihgy nw kir skY srIru ] (1367-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer naa ham kee-aa na karhigay naa kar sakai sareer. Kabeer, I have not done anything; I shall not do anything; my body cannot do anything.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v62	ikAw jwnau ikCu hir kIAw BieE kbIru kbIru ]62] (1367-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ki-aa jaan-o kichh har kee-aa bha-i-o kabeer kabeer. ||62||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v62	I do not know what the Lord has done, but the call has gone out: "Kabeer, Kabeer."||62||
WHEN	para 59553	kbIr supnY hU brVwie kY ijh muiK inksY rwmu ] (1367-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer supnai hoo barrhaa-ay kai jih mukh niksai raam. Kabeer, if someone utters the Name of the Lord even in dreams,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v63	qw ky pg kI pwnhI myry qn ko cwmu ]63] (1367-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) taa kay pag kee paanhee mayray tan ko chaam. ||63||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v63	I would make my skin into shoes for his feet. ||63||
DEFINE	para 59555	kbIr mwtI ky hm pUqry mwnsu rwiKEu nwau ] (1367-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maatee kay ham pootray maanas raakhi-o naa-o. Kabeer, we are puppets of clay, but we take the name of mankind.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v64	cwir idvs ky pwhuny bf bf rUMDih Twau ]64] (1367-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) chaar divas kay paahunay bad bad roo NDheh thaa-o. ||64||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v64	We are guests here for only a few days, but we take up so much space. ||64||
RECORD	para 59557	kbIr mihdI kir GwilAw Awpu pIswie pIswie ] (1367-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer mahidee kar ghaali-aa aap peesaa-ay peesaa-ay. Kabeer, I have made myself into henna, and I grind myself into powder.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v65	qY sh bwq n pUCIAY kbhu n lweI pwie ]65] (1367-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) tai sah baat na poochhee-ai kabahu na laa-ee paa-ay. ||65||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v65	But You, O my Husband Lord, have not asked about me; You have never applied me to Your Feet. ||65||
RECORD	para 59559	kbIr ijh dir Awvq jwiqAhu htkY nwhI koie ] (1367-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jih dar aavat jaati-ahu hatkai naahee ko-ay. Kabeer, that door, through which people never stop coming and going
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v66	so dru kYsy CofIAY jo dru AYsw hoie ]66] (1367-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) so dar kaisay chhodee-ai jo dar aisaa ho-ay. ||66||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v66	- how can I leave such a door as that? ||66||
RECORD	para 59561	kbIr fUbw Qw pY aubirE gun kI lhir Jbik ] (1367-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer doobaa thaa pai ubri-o gun kee lahar jhabak. Kabeer, I was drowning, but the waves of virtue saved me in an instant.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v67	jb dyiKE byVw jrjrw qb auqir pirE hau Prik ]67] (1368-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jab daykhi-o bayrhaa jarjaraa tab utar pari-o ha-o farak. ||67||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v67	When I saw that my boat was rotten, then I immediately got out. ||67||
RECORD	para 59564	kbIr pwpI Bgiq n BwveI hir pUjw n suhwie ] (1368-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer paapee bhagat na bhaav-ee har poojaa na suhaa-ay. Kabeer, the sinner does not like devotion to the Lord; he does not appreciate worship.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v68	mwKI cMdnu prhrY jh ibgMD qh jwie ]68] (1368-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) maakhee chandan parharai jah biganDh tah jaa-ay. ||68||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v68	The fly abandons the sandalwood tree, and goes after the rotten smell. ||68||
DEFINE	para 59566	kbIr bYdu mUAw rogI mUAw mUAw sBu sMswru ] (1368-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer baid moo-aa rogee moo-aa moo-aa sabh sansaar. Kabeer, the physician is dead, and the patient is dead; the whole world is dead.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v69	eyku kbIrw nw mUAw ijh nwhI rovnhwru ]69] (1368-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ayk kabeeraa naa moo-aa jih naahee rovanhaar. ||69||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v69	Only Kabeer is not dead; there is no one to mourn for him. ||69||
DEFINE	para 59568	kbIr rwmu n iDAwieE motI lwgI Koir ] (1368-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer raam na Dhi-aa-i-o motee laagee khor. Kabeer, I have not meditated on the Lord; such is the bad habit I have developed.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v70	kwieAw hWfI kwT kI nw Eh crHY bhoir ]70] (1368-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kaa-i-aa haa Ndee kaath kee naa oh char Hai bahor. ||70||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v70	The body is a wooden pot; it cannot be put back on the fire. ||70||
RECORD	para 59570	kbIr AYsI hoie prI mn ko Bwvqu kInu ] (1368-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aisee ho-ay paree man ko bhaavat keen. Kabeer, it came to pass, that I did whatever I pleased.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v71	mrny qy ikAw frpnw jb hwiQ isDaurw lIn ]71] (1368-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) marnay tay ki-aa darapnaa jab haath siDha-uraa leen. ||71||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v71	Why should I be afraid of death? I have invited death for myself. ||71||
RECORD	para 59572	kbIr rs ko gWfo cUsIAY gun kau mrIAY roie ] (1368-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ras ko gaa Ndo choosee-ai gun ka-o maree-ai ro-ay. Kabeer, the mortals suck at the sugar cane, for the sake of the sweet juice. They should work just as hard for virtue.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v72	AvgunIAwry mwnsY Blo n kihhY koie ]72] (1368-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) avgunee-aaray maansai bhalo na kahihai ko-ay. ||72||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v72	The person who lacks virtue - no one calls him good. ||72||
DEFINE	para 59574	kbIr gwgir jl BrI Awju kwil@ jYhY PUit ] (1368-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer gaagar jal bharee aaj kaali H jaihai foot. Kabeer, the pitcher is full of water; it will break, today or tomorrow.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v73	guru ju n cyqih Awpno AD mwiJ lIjihgy lUit ]73] (1368-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) gur jo na cheeteh aapno aDh maajh leejhigay loot. ||73||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v73	Those who do not remember their Guru, shall be plundered on the way. ||73||
DEFINE	para 59576	kbIr kUkru rwm ko muqIAw myro nwau ] (1368-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kookar raam ko mutee-aa mayro naa-o. Kabeer, I am the Lord's dog; Moti is my name.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v74	gly hmwry jyvrI jh iKMcY qh jwau ]74] (1368-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) galay hamaaray jayvree jah khinchai tah jaa-o. ||74||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v74	There is a chain around my neck; wherever I am pulled, I go. ||74||
RECORD	para 59578	kbIr jpnI kwT kI ikAw idKlwvih loie ] (1368-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer japnee kaath kee ki-aa dikhlaavahi lo-ay. Kabeer, why do you show other people your rosary beads?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v75	ihrdY rwmu n cyqhI ieh jpnI ikAw hoie ]75] (1368-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) hirdai raam na chaythee ih japnee ki-aa ho-ay. ||75||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v75	You do not remember the Lord in your heart, so what use is this rosary to you? ||75||
RECORD	para 59580	kbIr ibrhu BuXMgmu min bsY mMqu n mwnY koie ] (1368-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer birahu bhuyangam man basai mant na maanai ko-ay. Kabeer, the snake of separation from the Lord abides within my mind; it does not respond to any mantra.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v76	rwm ibEgI nw jIAY jIAY q baurw hoie ]76] (1368-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raam bi-ogee naa jee-ai jee-ai ta ba-uraa ho-ay. ||76||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v76	One who is separated from the Lord does not live; if he does live, he goes insane. ||76||
RECORD	para 59582	kbIr pwrs cMdnY iqn@ hY eyk sugMD ] (1368-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer paaras chandnai tin H hai ayk suganDh. Kabeer, the philosopher's stone and sandalwood oil have the same good quality.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v77	iqh imil qyaU aUqm Bey loh kwT inrgMD ]77] (1368-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) tih mil tay-oo ootam bha-ay loh kaath nirganDh. ||77||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v77	Whatever comes into contact with them is uplifted. Iron is transformed into gold, and ordinary wood becomes fragrant. ||77||
DEFINE	para 59584	kbIr jm kw TyNgw burw hY Ehu nhI sihAw jwie ] (1368-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jam kaa thay Ngaa buraa hai oh nahee sahi-aa jaa-ay. Kabeer, Death's club is terrible; it cannot be endured.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v78	eyku ju swDU muoih imilE iqin@ lIAw AMcil lwie ]78] (1368-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ayk jo saaDhoo mohi mili-o tiniH lee-aa anchal laa-ay. ||78||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v78	I have met with the holy man; he has attached me to the hem of his robe. ||78||
DEFINE	para 59586	kbIr bYdu khY hau hI Blw dwrU myrY vis ] (1368-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer baid kahai ha-o hee bhalaa daaroo mayrai vas. Kabeer, the physician says that he alone is good, and all the medicine is under his control.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v79	ieh qau bsqu gupwl kI jb BwvY lyie Kis ]79] (1368-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ih ta-o basat gupaal kee jab bhaavai lay-ay khas. ||79||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v79	But these things belong to the Lord; He takes them away whenever He wishes. ||79||
RECORD	para 59588	kbIr naubiq AwpnI idn ds lyhu bjwie ] (1368-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer na-ubat aapnee din das layho bajaa-ay. Kabeer, take your drum and beat it for ten days.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v80	ndI nwv sMjog ijau bhuir n imlhY Awie ]80] (1368-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) nadee naav sanjog ji-o bahur na milhai aa-ay. ||80||
FORBID	cauboly mhlw 5 v80	Life is like people meeting on a boat on a river; they shall not meet again. ||80||
WHEN	para 59590	kbIr swq smuMdih msu krau klm krau bnrwie ] (1368-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saat samundeh mas kara-o kalam kara-o banraa-ay. Kabeer, if I could change the seven seas into ink and make all the vegetation my pen,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v81	bsuDw kwgdu jau krau hir jsu ilKnu n jwie ]81] (1368-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) basuDhaa kaagad ja-o kara-o har jas likhan na jaa-ay. ||81||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v81	and the earth my paper, even then, I could not write the Praises of the Lord. ||81||
RECORD	para 59592	kbIr jwiq julwhw ikAw krY ihrdY bsy gupwl ] (1368-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jaat julaahaa ki-aa karai hirdai basay gupaal. Kabeer, what can my lowly status as a weaver do to me? The Lord dwells in my heart.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v82	kbIr rmeIAw kMiT imlu cUkih srb jMjwl ]82] (1368-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer rama-ee-aa kanth mil chookeh sarab janjaal. ||82||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v82	Kabeer, the Lord hugs me close in His Embrace; I have forsaken all my entanglements. ||82||
RECORD	para 59594	kbIr AYsw ko nhI mMdru dyie jrwie ] (1368-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aisaa ko nahee mandar day-ay jaraa-ay. Kabeer, will anyone set fire to his home
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v83	pWcau lirky mwir kY rhY rwm ilau lwie ]83] (1368-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paa Ncha-o larikay maar kai rahai raam li-o laa-ay. ||83||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v83	and kill his five sons (the five thieves) to remain lovingly attached to the Lord? ||83||
RECORD	para 59596	kbIr AYsw ko nhI iehu qnu dyvY PUik ] (1368-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aisaa ko nahee ih tan dayvai fook. Kabeer, will anyone burn his own body?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v84	AMDw logu n jwneI rihE kbIrw kUik ]84] (1368-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) anDhaa log na jaan-ee rahi-o kabeeraa kook. ||84||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v84	The people are blind - they do not know, although Kabeer continues to shout at them. ||84||
RECORD	para 59598	kbIr sqI pukwrY ich cVI sunu ho bIr mswn ] (1368-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer satee pukaarai chih charhee sun ho beer masaan. Kabeer, the widow mounts the funeral pyre and cries out, "Listen, O brother funeral pyre.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v85	logu sbwieAw cil gieE hm qum kwmu indwn ]85] (1368-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) log sabaa-i-aa chal ga-i-o ham tum kaam nidaan. ||85||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v85	All people must depart in the end; it is only you and I."||85||
WHEN	para 59601	kbIr mnu pMKI BieE auif auif dh ids jwie ] (1369-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer man pankhee bha-i-o ud ud dah dis jaa-ay. Kabeer, the mind has become a bird; it soars and flies in the ten directions.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v86	jo jYsI sMgiq imlY so qYso Plu Kwie ]86] (1369-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jo jaisee sangat milai so taiso fal khaa-ay. ||86||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v86	According to the company it keeps, so are the fruits it eats. ||86||
RECORD	para 59603	kbIr jw kau Kojqy pwieE soeI Tauru ] (1369-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jaa ka-o khojtay paa-i-o so-ee tha-ur. Kabeer, you have found that place which you were seeking.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v87	soeI iPir kY qU BieAw jw kau khqw Aauru ]87] (1369-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) so-ee fir kai too bha-i-aa jaa ka-o kahtaa a-or. ||87||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v87	You have become that which you thought was separate from yourself. ||87||
RECORD	para 59605	kbIr mwrI mrau kusMg kI kyly inkit ju byir ] (1369-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maaree mara-o kusang kee kaylay nikat jo bayr. Kabeer, I have been ruined and destroyed by bad company, like the banana plant near the thorn bush.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v88	auh JUlY auh cIrIAY swkq sMgu n hyir ]88] (1369-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) uh jhoolai uh cheeree-ai saakat sang na hayr. ||88||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v88	The thorn bush waves in the wind, and pierces the banana plant; see this, and do not associate with the faithless cynics. ||88||
RECORD	para 59607	kbIr Bwr prweI isir crY cilE cwhY bwt ] (1369-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer bhaar paraa-ee sir charai chali-o chaahai baat. Kabeer, the mortal wants to walk on the path, carrying the load of others' sins on his head.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v89	Apny Bwrih nw frY AwgY AauGt Gwt ]89] (1369-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) apnay bhaareh naa darai aagai a-ughat ghaat. ||89||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v89	He is not afraid of his own load of sins; the road ahead shall be difficult and treacherous. ||89||
DEFINE	para 59609	kbIr bn kI dwDI lwkrI TwFI krY pukwr ] (1369-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ban kee daaDhee laakree thaadhee karai pukaar. Kabeer, the forest is burning; the tree standing in it is crying out,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v90	miq bis prau luhwr ky jwrY dUjI bwr ]90] (1369-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) mat bas para-o luhaar kay jaarai doojee baar. ||90||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v90	"Do not let me fall into the hands of the blacksmith, who would burn me a second time."||90||
WHEN	para 59611	kbIr eyk mrMqy duie mUey doie mrMqh cwir ] (1369-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ayk marantay du-ay moo-ay do-ay marantah chaar. Kabeer, when one died, two were dead. When two died, four were dead.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v91	cwir mrMqh Ch mUey cwir purK duie nwir ]91] (1369-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) chaar marantah chhah moo-ay chaar purakh du-ay naar. ||91||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v91	When four died, six were dead, four males and two females. ||91||
RECORD	para 59613	kbIr dyiK dyiK jgu FUMiFAw khUM n pwieAw Tauru ] (1369-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer daykh daykh jag dhooNdhi-aa kahoo-a N na paa-i-aa tha-ur. Kabeer, I have seen and observed, and searched all over the world, but I have found no place of rest anywhere.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v92	ijin hir kw nwmu n cyiqE khw Bulwny Aaur ]92] (1369-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jin har kaa naam na chayti-o kahaa bhulaanay a-or. ||92||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v92	Those who do not remember the Lord's Name - why do they delude themselves in other pursuits? ||92||
RECORD	para 59615	kbIr sMgiq krIAY swD kI AMiq krY inrbwhu ] (1369-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sangat karee-ai saaDh kee ant karai birbaahu. Kabeer, associate with the Holy people, who will take you to Nirvaanaa in the end.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v93	swkq sMgu n kIjIAY jw qy hoie ibnwhu ]93] (1369-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) saakat sang na keejee-ai jaa tay ho-ay binaahu. ||93||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v93	Do not associate with the faithless cynics; they would bring you to ruin. ||93||
DEFINE	para 59617	kbIr jg mih cyiqE jwin kY jg mih rihE smwie ] (1369-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jag meh chayti-o jaan kai jag meh rahi-o samaa-ay. Kabeer, I contemplate the Lord in the world; I know that He is permeating the world.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v94	ijn hir kw nwmu n cyiqE bwdih jnmyN Awie ]94] (1369-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jin har kaa naam na chayti-o baadeh janmay N aa-ay. ||94||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v94	Those who do not contemplate the Name of the Lord - their birth into this world is useless. ||94||
RECORD	para 59619	kbIr Awsw krIAY rwm kI AvrY Aws inrws ] (1369-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aasaa karee-ai raam kee avrai aas niraas. Kabeer, place your hopes in the Lord; other hopes lead to despair.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v95	nrik prih qy mwneI jo hir nwm audws ]95] (1369-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) narak pareh tay maan-ee jo har naam udaas. ||95||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v95	Those who dissociate themselves from the Lord's Name - when they fall into hell, then they will appreciate its value. ||95||
RECORD	para 59621	kbIr isK swKw bhuqy kIey kyso kIE n mIqu ] (1369-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sikh saakhaa bahutay kee-ay kayso kee-o na meet. Kabeer has made many students and disciples, but he has not made God his friend.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v96	cwly Qy hir imln kau bIcY AtikE cIqu ]96] (1369-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) chaalay thay har milan ka-o beechai atki-o cheet. ||96||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v96	He set out on a journey to meet the Lord, but his consciousness failed him half-way. ||96||
WHEN	para 59623	kbIr kwrnu bpurw ikAw krY jau rwmu n krY shwie ] (1369-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kaaran bapuraa ki-aa karai ja-o raam na karai sahaa-ay. Kabeer, what can the poor creature do, if the Lord does not give him assistance?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v97	ijh ijh fwlI pgu Drau soeI muir muir jwie ]97] (1369-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jih jih daalee pag Dhara-o so-ee mur mur jaa-ay. ||97||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v97	Whatever branch he steps on breaks and collapses. ||97||
RECORD	para 59625	kbIr Avrh kau aupdysqy muK mY pir hY ryqu ] (1369-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer avrah ka-o updaystay mukh mai par hai rayt. Kabeer, those who only preach to others - sand falls into their mouths.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v98	rwis ibrwnI rwKqy KwXw Gr kw Kyqu ]98] (1369-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raas biraanee raakh-tay khaa-yaa ghar kaa khayt. ||98||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v98	They keep their eyes on the property of others, while their own farm is being eaten up. ||98||
WHEN	para 59627	kbIr swDU kI sMgiq rhau jau kI BUsI Kwau ] (1369-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saaDhoo kee sangat raha-o ja-o kee bhoosee khaa-o. Kabeer, I will remain in the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, even if I have only coarse bread to eat.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v99	honhwru so hoiehY swkq sMig n jwau ]99] (1369-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) honhaar so ho-ihai saakat sang na jaa-o. ||99||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v99	Whatever will be, will be. I will not associate with the faithless cynics. ||99||
RECORD	para 59629	kbIr sMgiq swD kI idn idn dUnw hyqu ] (1369-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sangat saaDh kee din din doonaa hayt. Kabeer, in the Saadh Sangat, love for the Lord doubles day by day.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v100	swkq kwrI kWbrI Doey hoie n syqu ]100] (1369-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) saakat kaaree kaaNbree Dho-ay ho-ay na sayt. ||100||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v100	The faithless cynic is like a black blanket, which does not become white by being washed. ||100||
RECORD	para 59631	kbIr mnu mUMifAw nhI kys muMfwey kWie ] (1369-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer man moo Ndi-aa nahee kays mundaa-ay kaa N-ay. Kabeer, you have not shaved your mind, so why do you shave your head?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v101	jo ikCu kIAw so mn kIAw mUMfw mUMfu AjWie ]101] (1369-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jo kichh kee-aa so man kee-aa moo Ndaa moond ajaa N-ay. ||101||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v101	Whatever is done, is done by the mind; it is useless to shave your head. ||101||
REQUIRE	para 59633	kbIr rwmu n CofIAY qnu Dnu jwie q jwau ] (1369-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer raam na chhodee-ai tan Dhan jaa-ay ta jaa-o. Kabeer, do not abandon the Lord; your body and wealth shall go, so let them go.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v102	crn kml icqu byiDAw rwmih nwim smwau ]102] (1369-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) charan kamal chit bayDhi-aa raameh naam samaa-o. ||102||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v102	My consciousness is pierced by the Lord's Lotus Feet; I am absorbed in the Name of the Lord. ||102||
DEFINE	para 59635	kbIr jo hm jMqu bjwvqy tUit geIN sB qwr ] (1369-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jo ham jant bajaavtay toot ga-ee N sabh taar. Kabeer, all the strings of the instrument I played are broken.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v103	jMqu ibcwrw ikAw krY cly bjwvnhwr ]103] (1369-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jant bichaaraa ki-aa karai chalay bajaavanhaar. ||103||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v103	What can the poor instrument do, when the player has departed as well. ||103||
RECORD	para 59637	kbIr mwie mUMfau iqh gurU kI jw qy Brmu n jwie ] (1369-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maa-ay moonda-o tih guroo kee jaa tay bharam na jaa-ay. Kabeer, shave the mother of that guru, who does not take away one's doubt.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v104	Awp fuby chu byd mih cyly dIey bhwie ]104] (1370-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aap dubay chahu bayd meh chaylay dee-ay bahaa-ay. ||104||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v104	He himself is drowning in the four Vedas; he drowns his disciples as well. ||104||
RECORD	para 59640	kbIr jyqy pwp kIey rwKy qlY durwie ] (1370-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jaytay paap kee-ay raakhay talai duraa-ay. Kabeer, whatever sins the mortal has committed, he tries to keep hidden under cover.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v105	prgt Bey indwn sB jb pUCy Drm rwie ]105] (1370-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) pargat bha-ay nidaan sabh jab poochhay Dharam raa-ay. ||105||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v105	But in the end, they shall all be revealed, when the Righteous Judge of Dharma investigates. ||105||
WHEN	para 59642	kbIr hir kw ismrnu Cwif kY pwilE bhuqu kutMbu ] (1370-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer har kaa simran chhaad kai paali-o bahut kutamb. Kabeer, you have given up meditating on the Lord, and you have raised a large family.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v106	DMDw krqw rih gieAw BweI rihAw n bMDu ]106] (1370-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) DhanDhaa kartaa reh ga-i-aa bhaa-ee rahi-aa na banDh. ||106||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v106	You continue to involve yourself in worldly affairs, but none of your brothers and relatives remain. ||106||
WHEN	para 59644	kbIr hir kw ismrnu Cwif kY rwiq jgwvn jwie ] (1370-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer har kaa simran chhaad kai raat jagaavan jaa-ay. Kabeer, those who give up meditation on the Lord, and get up at night to wake the spirits of the dead,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v107	srpin hoie kY AauqrY jwey Apuny Kwie ]107] (1370-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) sarpan ho-ay kai a-utarai jaa-ay apunay khaa-ay. ||107||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v107	shall be reincarnated as snakes, and eat their own offspring. ||107||
WHEN	para 59646	kbIr hir kw ismrnu Cwif kY AhoeI rwKY nwir ] (1370-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer har kaa simran chhaad kai aho-ee raakhai naar. Kabeer, the woman who gives up meditation on the Lord, and observes the ritual fast of Ahoi,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v108	gdhI hoie kY AauqrY Bwru shY mn cwir ]108] (1370-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) gadhee ho-ay kai a-utarai bhaar sahai man chaar. ||108||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v108	shall be reincarnated as a donkey, to carry heavy burdens. ||108||
DEFINE	para 59648	kbIr cqurweI Aiq GnI hir jip ihrdY mwih ] (1370-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer chaturaa-ee at ghanee har jap hirdai maahi. Kabeer, it is the most clever wisdom, to chant and meditate on the Lord in the heart.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v109	sUrI aUpir Kylnw igrY q Twhr nwih ]109] (1370-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) sooree oopar khaylnaa girai ta thaahar naahi. ||109||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v109	It is like playing on a pig; if you fall off, you will find no place of rest. ||109||
DEFINE	para 59650	kbIr suoeI muKu DMin hY jw muiK khIAY rwmu ] (1370-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer so-ee mukh Dhan hai jaa mukh kahee-ai raam. Kabeer, blessed is that mouth, which utters the Lord's Name.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v110	dyhI iks kI bwpurI pivqRü hoiego gRwmu ]110] (1370-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) dayhee kis kee baapuree pavitar ho-igo garaam. ||110||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v110	It purifies the body, and the whole village as well. ||110||
DEFINE	para 59652	kbIr soeI kul BlI jw kul hir ko dwsu ] (1370-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer so-ee kul bhalee jaa kul har ko daas. Kabeer, that family is good, in which the Lord's slave is born.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v111	ijh kul dwsu n aUpjY so kul Fwku plwsu ]111] (1370-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jih kul daas na oopjai so kul dhaak palaas. ||111||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v111	But that family in which the Lord's slave is not born is as useless as weeds. ||111||
RECORD	para 59654	kbIr hY gie bwhn sGn Gn lwK Djw Phrwih ] (1370-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer hai ga-ay baahan saghan ghan laakh Dhajaa fahraahi. Kabeer, some have lots of horses, elephants and carriages, and thousands of banners waving.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v112	ieAw suK qy iBK´w BlI jau hir ismrq idn jwih ]112] (1370-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) i-aa sukh tay bhikh-yaa bhalee ja-o har simrat din jaahi. ||112||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v112	But begging is better than these comforts, if one spends his days meditating in remembrance on the Lord. ||112||
RECORD	para 59656	kbIr sBu jgu hau iPirE mWdlu kMD cFwie ] (1370-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sabh jag ha-o firi-o maa Ndal kanDh chadhaa-ay. Kabeer, I have wandered all over the world, carrying the drum on my shoulder.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v113	koeI kwhU ko nhI sB dyKI Toik bjwie ]113] (1370-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ko-ee kaahoo ko nahee sabh daykhee thok bajaa-ay. ||113||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v113	No one belongs to anyone else; I have looked and carefully studied it. ||113||
DEFINE	para 59658	mwrig moqI bIQry AMDw inkisE Awie ] (1370-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) maarag motee beethray anDhaa niksi-o aa-ay. The pearls are scattered on the road; the blind man comes along.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v114	joiq ibnw jgdIs kI jgqu aulµGy jwie ]114] (1370-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jot binaa jagdees kee jagat ulanghay jaa-ay. ||114||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v114	Without the Light of the Lord of the Universe, the world just passes them by. ||114||
DEFINE	para 59660	bUfw bMsu kbIr kw aupijE pUqu kmwlu ] (1370-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) boodaa bans kabeer kaa upji-o poot kamaal. My family is drowned, O Kabeer, since the birth of my son Kamaal.
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v115	hir kw ismrnu Cwif kY Gir ly AwXw mwlu ]115] (1370-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) har kaa simran chhaad kai ghar lay aa-yaa maal. ||115||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v115	He has given up meditating on the Lord, in order to bring home wealth. ||115||
RECORD	para 59662	kbIr swDU kau imlny jweIAY swiQ n lIjY koie ] (1370-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saaDhoo ka-o milnay jaa-ee-ai saath na leejai ko-ay. Kabeer, go out to meet the holy man; do not take anyone else with you.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v116	pwCY pwau n dIjIAY AwgY hoie su hoie ]116] (1370-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paachhai paa-o na deejee-ai aagai ho-ay so ho-ay. ||116||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v116	Do not turn back - keep on going. Whatever will be, will be. ||116||
RECORD	para 59664	kbIr jgu bwiDE ijh jyvrI iqh mq bMDhu kbIr ] (1370-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jag baaDhi-o jih jayvree tih mat banDhhu kabeer. Kabeer, do not bind yourself with that chain, which binds the whole world.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v117	jYhih Awtw lon ijau son smwin srIru ]117] (1370-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jaiheh aataa lon ji-o son samaan sareer. ||117||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v117	As the salt is lost in the flour, so shall your golden body be lost. ||117||
DEFINE	para 59666	kbIr hMsu auifE qnu gwifE soJweI sYnwh ] (1370-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer hans udi-o tan gaadi-o sojhaa-ee sainaah. Kabeer, the soul-swan is flying away, and the body is being buried, and still he makes gestures.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v118	AjhU jIau n CofeI rMkweI nYnwh ]118] (1370-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ajhoo jee-o na chhod-ee rankaa-ee nainaah. ||118||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v118	Even then, the mortal does not give up the cruel look in his eyes. ||118||
RECORD	para 59668	kbIr nYn inhwrau quJ kau sRvn sunau quA nwau ] (1370-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer nain nihaara-o tujh ka-o sarvan sun-o tu-a naa-o. Kabeer: with my eyes, I see You, Lord; with my ears, I hear Your Name.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v119	bYn aucrau quA nwm jI crn kml ird Twau ]119] (1370-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) bain uchara-o tu-a naam jee charan kamal rid thaa-o. ||119||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v119	With my tongue I chant Your Name; I enshrine Your Lotus Feet within my heart. ||119||
RECORD	para 59670	kbIr surg nrk qy mY rihE siqgur ky prswid ] (1370-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer surag narak tay mai rahi-o satgur kay parsaad. Kabeer, I have been spared from heaven and hell, by the Grace of the True Guru.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v120	crn kml kI mauj mih rhau AMiq Aru Awid ]120] (1370-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) charan kamal kee ma-uj meh raha-o ant ar aad. ||120||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v120	From beginning to end, I abide in the joy of the Lord's Lotus Feet. ||120||
RECORD	para 59672	kbIr crn kml kI mauj ko kih kYsy aunmwn ] (1370-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer charan kamal kee ma-uj ko kahi kaisay unmaan. Kabeer, how can I even describe the extent of the joy of the Lord's Lotus Feet?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v121	kihby kau soBw nhI dyKw hI prvwnu ]121] (1370-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kahibay ka-o sobhaa nahee daykhaa hee parvaan. ||121||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v121	I cannot describe its sublime glory; it has to be seen to be appreciated. ||121||
RECORD	para 59674	kbIr dyiK kY ikh khau khy n ko pqIAwie ] (1370-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer daykh kai kih kaha-o kahay na ko patee-aa-ay. Kabeer, how can I describe what I have seen? No one will believe my words.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v122	hir jYsw qYsw auhI rhau hriK gun gwie ]122] (1370-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) har jaisaa taisaa uhee raha-o harakh gun gaa-ay. ||122||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v122	The Lord is just as He is. I dwell in delight, singing His Glorious Praises. ||122||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v123	kbIr cugY icqwrY BI cugY cuig cuig icqwry ] jYsy bcrih kUMj mn mwieAw mmqw ry ]123] (1371-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer chugai chitaarai bhee chugai chug chug chitaaray. jaisay bachrahi koo Nj man maa-i-aa mamtaa ray. ||123||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v123	Kabeer, the flamingo pecks and feeds, and remembers her chicks. She pecks and pecks and feeds, and remembers them always. Her chicks are very dear to her, just like the love of wealth and Maya is dear to the mortal's mind. ||123||
DEFINE	para 59678	kbIr AMbr Gnhru CwieAw briK Bry sr qwl ] (1371-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ambar ghanhar chhaa-i-aa barakh bharay sar taal. Kabeer, the sky is overcast and cloudy; the ponds and lakes are overflowing with water.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v124	cwiqRk ijau qrsq rhY iqn ko kaunu hvwlu ]124] (1371-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) chaatrik ji-o tarsat rahai tin ko ka-un havaal. ||124||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v124	Like the rainbird, some remain thirsty - what is their condition? ||124||
RECORD	para 59680	kbIr ckeI jau inis bICurY Awie imlY prBwiq ] (1371-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer chak-ee ja-o nis beechhurai aa-ay milai parbhaat. Kabeer, the chakvi duck is separated from her love through the night, but in the morning, she meets him again.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v125	jo nr ibCury rwm isau nw idn imly n rwiq ]125] (1371-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jo nar bichhuray raam si-o naa din milay na raat. ||125||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v125	Those who are separated from the Lord do not meet Him in the day, or in the night. ||125||
RECORD	para 59682	kbIr rYnwier ibCoirAw rhu ry sMK mJUir ] (1371-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer rainaa-ir bichhori-aa rahu ray sankh majhoor. Kabeer: O conch shell, remain in the ocean.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v126	dyvl dyvl DwhVI dysih augvq sUr ]126] (1371-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) dayval dayval Dhaahrhee dayseh ugvat soor. ||126||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v126	If you are separated from it, you shall scream at sunrise from temple to temple. ||126||
DEFINE	para 59684	kbIr sUqw ikAw krih jwgu roie BY duK ] (1371-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sootaa ki-aa karahi jaag ro-ay bhai dukh. Kabeer, what are you doing sleeping? Wake up and cry in fear and pain.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v127	jw kw bwsw gor mih so ikau sovY suK ]127] (1371-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jaa kaa baasaa gor meh so ki-o sovai sukh. ||127||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v127	Those who live in the grave - how can they sleep in peace? ||127||
DEFINE	para 59686	kbIr sUqw ikAw krih auiT ik n jpih murwir ] (1371-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sootaa ki-aa karahi uth ke na jaapeh muraar. Kabeer, what are you doing sleeping? Why not rise up and meditate on the Lord?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v128	iek idn sovnu hoiego lWby gof pswir ]128] (1371-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ik din sovan ho-igo laa Nbay god pasaar. ||128||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v128	One day you shall sleep with your legs outstretched. ||128||
DEFINE	para 59688	kbIr sUqw ikAw krih bYTw rhu Aru jwgu ] (1371-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sootaa ki-aa karahi baithaa rahu ar jaag. Kabeer, what are you doing sleeping? Wake up, and sit up.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v129	jw ky sMg qy bICurw qw hI ky sMig lwgu ]129] (1371-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jaa kay sang tay beechhuraa taa hee kay sang laag. ||129||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v129	Attach yourself to the One, from whom you have been separated. ||129||
RECORD	para 59690	kbIr sMq kI gYl n CofIAY mwrig lwgw jwau ] (1371-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sant kee gail na chhodee-ai maarag laagaa jaa-o. Kabeer, do not leave the Society of the Saints; walk upon this Path.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v130	pyKq hI puMnIq hoie Bytq jpIAY nwau ]130] (1371-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paykhat hee punneet ho-ay bhaytat japee-ai naa-o. ||130||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v130	See them, and be sanctified; meet them, and chant the Name. ||130||
RECORD	para 59692	kbIr swkq sMgu n kIjIAY dUrih jweIAY Bwig ] (1371-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saakat sang na keejee-ai dooreh jaa-ee-ai bhaag. Kabeer, do not associate with the faithless cynics; run far away from them.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v131	bwsnu kwro prsIAY qau kCu lwgY dwgu ]131] (1371-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) baasan kaaro parsee-ai ta-o kachh laagai daag. ||131||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v131	If you touch a vessel stained with soot, some of the soot will stick to you. ||131||
RECORD	para 59694	kbIrw rwmu n cyiqE jrw phUMicE Awie ] (1371-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeeraa raam na chayti-o jaraa pahoo Nchi-o aa-ay. Kabeer, you have not contemplated the Lord, and now old age has overtaken you.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v132	lwgI mMidr duAwr qy Ab ikAw kwiFAw jwie ]132] (1371-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) laagee mandir du-aar tay ab ki-aa kaadhi-aa jaa-ay. ||132||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v132	Now that the door of your mansion is on fire, what can you take out? ||132||
RECORD	para 59696	kbIr kwrnu so BieE jo kIno krqwir ] (1371-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kaaran so bha-i-o jo keeno kartaar. Kabeer, the Creator does whatever He pleases.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v133	iqsu ibnu dUsru ko nhI eykY isrjnhwru ]133] (1371-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) tis bin doosar ko nahee aykai sirjanhaar. ||133||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v133	There is none other than Him; He alone is the Creator of all. ||133||
DEFINE	para 59698	kbIr Pl lwgy Plin pwkin lwgy AWb ] (1371-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer fal laagay falan paakan laagay aa Nb. Kabeer, the fruit trees are bearing fruit, and the mangoes are becoming ripe.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v134	jwie phUcih Ksm kau jau bIic n KwhI kWb ]134] (1371-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jaa-ay pahoocheh khasam ka-o ja-o beech na khaahee kaaNb. ||134||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v134	They will reach the owner, only if the crows do not eat them first. ||134||
RECORD	para 59700	kbIr Twkuru pUjih moil ly mnhiT qIrQ jwih ] (1371-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer thaakur poojeh mol lay manhath tirath jaahi. Kabeer, some buy idols and worship them; in their stubborn-mindedness, they make pilgrimages to sacred shrines.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v135	dyKw dyKI sÍWgu Dir BUly Btkw Kwih ]135] (1371-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) daykhaa daykhee savaaNg Dhar bhoolay bhatkaa khaahi. ||135||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v135	They look at one another, and wear religious robes, but they are deluded and lost. ||135||
RECORD	para 59702	kbIr pwhnu prmysuru kIAw pUjY sBu sMswru ] (1371-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer paahan parmaysur kee-aa poojai sabh sansaar. Kabeer, someone sets up a stone idol and all the world worships it as the Lord.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v136	ies Brvwsy jo rhy bUfy kwlI Dwr ]136] (1371-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) is bharvaasay jo rahay booday kaalee Dhaar. ||136||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v136	Those who hold to this belief will be drowned in the river of darkness. ||136||
DEFINE	para 59704	kbIr kwgd kI EbrI msu ky krm kpwt ] (1371-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kaagad kee obree mas kay karam kapaat. Kabeer, the paper is the prison, and the ink of rituals are the bars on the windows.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v137	pwhn borI iprQmI pMifq pwVI bwt ]137] (1371-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paahan boree pirathmee pandit paarhee baat. ||137||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v137	The stone idols have drowned the world, and the Pandits, the religious scholars, have plundered it on the way. ||137||
RECORD	para 59706	kbIr kwil krMqw Abih kru Ab krqw suie qwl ] (1371-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kaal karantaa abeh kar ab kartaa su-ay taal. Kabeer, that which you have to do tomorrow - do it today instead; and that which you have to do now - do it immediately!
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v138	pwCY kCU n hoiegw jau isr pir AwvY kwlu ]138] (1371-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paachhai kachhoo na ho-igaa ja-o sir par aavai kaal. ||138||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v138	Later on, you will not be able to do anything, when death hangs over your head. ||138||
DEFINE	para 59708	kbIr AYsw jMqu ieku dyiKAw jYsI DoeI lwK ] (1371-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aisaa jant ik daykhi-aa jaisee Dho-ee laakh. Kabeer, I have seen a person, who is as shiny as washed wax.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v139	dIsY cMclu bhu gunw miq hInw nwpwk ]139] (1371-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) deesai chanchal baho gunaa mat heenaa naapaak. ||139||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v139	He seems very clever and very virtuous, but in reality, he is without understanding, and corrupt. ||139||
FORBID	para 59710	kbIr myrI buiD kau jmu n krY iqskwr ] (1371-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer mayree buDh ka-o jam na karai tiskaar. Kabeer, the Messenger of Death shall not compromise my understanding.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v140	ijin iehu jmUAw isrijAw su jipAw privdgwr ]140] (1371-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jin ih jamoo-aa sirji-aa so japi-aa parvidagaar. ||140||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v140	I have meditated on the Lord, the Cherisher, who created this Messenger of Death. ||140||
DEFINE	para 59712	kbIru ksqUrI BieAw Bvr Bey sB dws ] (1371-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kastooree bha-i-aa bhavar bha-ay sabh daas. Kabeer, the Lord is like musk; all His slaves are like bumble bees.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v141	ijau ijau Bgiq kbIr kI iqau iqau rwm invws ]141] (1372-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ji-o ji-o bhagat kabeer kee ti-o ti-o raam nivaas. ||141||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v141	The more Kabeer worships Him, the more the Lord abides within his mind. ||141||
RECORD	para 59715	kbIr ghgic pirE kutMb kY kWTY rih gieE rwmu ] (1372-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer gahgach pari-o kutamb kai kaa Nthai reh ga-i-o raam. Kabeer, the mortal has fallen into the grip of family life, and the Lord has been set aside.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v142	Awie pry Drm rwie ky bIcih DUmw Dwm ]142] (1372-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aa-ay paray Dharam raa-ay kay beecheh Dhoomaa Dhaam. ||142||
UPHOLD	cauboly mhlw 5 v142	The messengers of the Righteous Judge of Dharma descend upon the mortal, in the midst of all his pomp and ceremony. ||142||
DEFINE	para 59717	kbIr swkq qy sUkr Blw rwKY AwCw gwau ] (1372-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saakat tay sookar bhalaa raakhai aachhaa gaa-o. Kabeer, even a pig is better than the faithless cynic; at least the pig keeps the village clean.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v143	auhu swkqu bpurw mir gieAw koie n lYhY nwau ]143] (1372-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) uho saakat bapuraa mar ga-i-aa ko-ay na laihai naa-o. ||143||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v143	When the wretched, faithless cynic dies, no one even mentions his name. ||143||
RECORD	para 59719	kbIr kaufI kaufI joir kY jory lwK kroir ] (1372-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ka-udee ka-udee jor kai joray laakh karor. Kabeer, the mortal gathers wealth, shell by shell, accumulating thousands and millions.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v144	clqI bwr n kCu imilE leI lµgotI qoir ]144] (1372-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) chaltee baar na kachh mili-o la-ee langotee tor. ||144||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v144	But when the time of his departure comes, he takes nothing at all with him. He is even stripped of his loin-cloth. ||144||
DEFINE	para 59721	kbIr bYsno hUAw q ikAw BieAw mwlw mylIN cwir ] (1372-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer baisno hoo-aa ta ki-aa bha-i-aa maalaa maylee N chaar. Kabeer, what good is it to become a devotee of Vishnu, and wear four malas?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v145	bwhir kMcnu bwrhw BIqir BrI BMgwr ]145] (1372-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) baahar kanchan baarhaa bheetar bharee bhangaar. ||145||
ALLOW	cauboly mhlw 5 v145	On the outside, he may look like pure gold, but on the inside, he is stuffed with dust. ||145||
RECORD	para 59723	kbIr roVw hoie rhu bwt kw qij mn kw AiBmwnu ] (1372-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer rorhaa ho-ay rahu baat kaa taj man kaa abhimaan. Kabeer, let yourself be a pebble on the path; abandon your egotistical pride.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v146	AYsw koeI dwsu hoie qwih imlY Bgvwnu ]146] (1372-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aisaa ko-ee daas ho-ay taahi milai bhagvaan. ||146||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v146	Such a humble slave shall meet the Lord God. ||146||
RECORD	para 59725	kbIr roVw hUAw q ikAw BieAw pMQI kau duKu dyie ] (1372-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer rorhaa hoo-aa ta ki-aa bha-i-aa panthee ka-o dukh day-ay. Kabeer, what good would it be, to be a pebble? It would only hurt the traveller on the path.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v147	AYsw qyrw dwsu hY ijau DrnI mih Kyh ]147] (1372-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) aisaa tayraa daas hai ji-o Dharnee meh khayh. ||147||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v147	Your slave, O Lord, is like the dust of the earth. ||147||
WHEN	para 59727	kbIr Kyh hUeI qau ikAw BieAw jau auif lwgY AMg ] (1372-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer khayh hoo-ee ta-o ki-aa bha-i-aa ja-o ud laagai ang. Kabeer, what then, if one could become dust? It is blown up by the wind, and sticks to the body.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v148	hir jnu AYsw cwhIAY ijau pwnI srbMg ]148] (1372-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) har jan aisaa chaahee-ai ji-o paanee sarbang. ||148||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v148	The humble servant of the Lord should be like water, which cleans everything. ||148||
WHEN	para 59729	kbIr pwnI hUAw q ikAw BieAw sIrw qwqw hoie ] (1372-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer paanee hoo-aa ta ki-aa bha-i-aa seeraa taataa ho-ay. Kabeer, what then, if one could become water? It becomes cold, then hot.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v149	hir jnu AYsw cwhIAY jYsw hir hI hoie ]149] (1372-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) har jan aisaa chaahee-ai jaisaa har hee ho-ay. ||149||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v149	The humble servant of the Lord should be just like the Lord. ||149||
RECORD	para 59731	aUc Bvn knkwmnI isKir Djw Phrwie ] (1372-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ooch bhavan kankaamnee sikhar Dhajaa fehraa-ay. The banners wave above the lofty mansions, filled with gold and beautiful women.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v150	qw qy BlI mDUkrI sMqsMig gun gwie ]150] (1372-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) taa tay bhalee maDhookree satsang gun gaa-ay. ||150||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v150	But better than these is dry bread, if one sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord in the Society of the Saints. ||150||
DEFINE	para 59733	kbIr pwtn qy aUjru Blw rwm Bgq ijh Twie ] (1372-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer paatan tay oojar bhalaa raam bhagat jih thaa-ay. Kabeer, the wilderness is better than a city, if the Lord's devotees live there.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v151	rwm snyhI bwhrw jm puru myry BWie ]151] (1372-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raam sanayhee baahraa jam pur mayray bhaa N-ay. ||151||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v151	Without my Beloved Lord, it is like the City of Death for me. ||151||
RECORD	para 59735	kbIr gMg jmun ky AMqry shj suMn ky Gwt ] (1372-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer gang jamun kay antray sahj sunn kay ghaat. Kabeer, between the Ganges and Jamunaa Rivers, on the shore of Celestial Silence,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v152	qhw kbIrY mtu kIAw Kojq muin jn bwt ]152] (1372-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) tahaa kabeerai mat kee-aa khojat mun jan baat. ||152||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v152	there, Kabeer has made his home. The silent sages and the humble servants of the Lord search for the way to get there. ||152||
WHEN	para 59737	kbIr jYsI aupjI pyf qy jau qYsI inbhY EiV ] (1372-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jaisee upjee payd tay ja-o taisee nibhai orh. Kabeer, if the mortal continues to love the Lord in the end, as he pledged in the beginning,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v153	hIrw iks kw bwpurw pujih n rqn kroiV ]153] (1372-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) heeraa kis kaa baapuraa pujeh na ratan karorh. ||153||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v153	no poor diamond, not even millions of jewels, can equal him. ||153||
RECORD	para 59739	kbIrw eyku AcMBau dyiKE hIrw hwt ibkwie ] (1372-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeeraa ayk achambha-o daykhi-o heeraa haat bikaa-ay. Kabeer, I saw a strange and wonderful thing. A jewel was being sold in a store.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v154	bnjnhwry bwhrw kaufI bdlY jwie ]154] (1372-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) banjanhaaray baahraa ka-udee badlai jaa-ay. ||154||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v154	Because there was no buyer, it was going in exchange for a shell. ||154||
UPHOLD	para 59741	kbIrw jhw igAwnu qh Drmu hY jhw JUTu qh pwpu ] (1372-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeeraa jahaa gi-aan tah Dharam hai jahaa jhooth tah paap. Kabeer, where there is spiritual wisdom, there is righteousness and Dharma. Where there is falsehood, there is sin.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v155	jhw loBu qh kwlu hY jhw iKmw qh Awip ]155] (1372-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jahaa lobh tah kaal hai jahaa khimaa tah aap. ||155||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v155	Where there is greed, there is death. Where there is forgiveness, there is God Himself. ||155||
WHEN	para 59743	kbIr mwieAw qjI q ikAw BieAw jau mwnu qijAw nhI jwie ] (1372-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maa-i-aa tajee ta ki-aa bha-i-aa ja-o maan taji-aa nahee jaa-ay. Kabeer, what good is it to give up Maya, if the mortal does not give up his pride?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v156	mwn munI muinvr gly mwnu sBY kau Kwie ]156] (1372-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) maan munee munivar galay maan sabhai ka-o khaa-ay. ||156||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v156	Even the silent sages and seers are destroyed by pride; pride eats up everything. ||156||
RECORD	para 59745	kbIr swcw siqguru mY imilAw sbdu ju bwihAw eyku ] (1372-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saachaa satgur mai mili-aa sabad jo baahi-aa ayk. Kabeer, the True Guru has met me; He aimed the Arrow of the Shabad at me.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v157	lwgq hI Buie imil gieAw pirAw klyjy Cyku ]157] (1372-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) laagat hee bhu-ay mil ga-i-aa pari-aa kalayjay chhayk. ||157||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v157	As soon as it struck me, I fell to the ground with a hole in my heart. ||157||
DEFINE	para 59747	kbIr swcw siqguru ikAw krY jau isKw mih cUk ] (1372-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saachaa satgur ki-aa karai ja-o sikhaa meh chook. Kabeer, what can the True Guru do, when His Sikhs are at fault?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v158	AMDy eyk n lwgeI ijau bWsu bjweIAY PUk ]158] (1372-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) anDhay ayk na laag-ee ji-o baa Ns bajaa-ee-ai fook. ||158||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v158	The blind do not take in any of His Teachings; it is as useless as blowing into bamboo. ||158||
RECORD	para 59749	kbIr hY gY bwhn sGn Gn CqRpqI kI nwir ] (1372-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer hai gai baahan saghan ghan chhatarpatee kee naar. Kabeer, the wife of the king has all sorts of horses, elephants and carriages.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v159	qwsu ptMqr n pujY hir jn kI pinhwir ]159] (1373-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) taas patantar na pujai har jan kee panihaar. ||159||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v159	But she is not equal to the water-carrier of the Lord's humble servant. ||159||
RECORD	para 59752	kbIr inRp nwrI ikau inMdIAY ikau hir cyrI kau mwnu ] (1373-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer nrip naaree ki-o nindee-ai ki-o har chayree ka-o maan. Kabeer, why do you slander the wife of the king? Why do you honor the slave of the Lord?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v160	Eh mWg svwrY ibKY kau Eh ismrY hir nwmu ]160] (1373-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) oh maa Ng savaarai bikhai ka-o oh simrai har naam. ||160||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v160	Because one combs her hair for corruption, while the other remembers the Name of the Lord. ||160||
RECORD	para 59754	kbIr QUnI pweI iQiq BeI siqgur bMDI DIr ] (1373-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer thoonee paa-ee thit bha-ee satgur banDhee Dheer. Kabeer, with the Support of the Lord's Pillar, I have become steady and stable.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v161	kbIr hIrw bnijAw mwn srovr qIr ]161] (1373-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer heeraa banji-aa maan sarovar teer. ||161||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v161	The True Guru has given me courage. Kabeer, I have purchased the diamond, on the banks of the Mansarovar Lake. ||161||
RECORD	para 59756	kbIr hir hIrw jn jauhrI ly kY mWfY hwt ] (1373-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer har heeraa jan ja-uharee lay kai maa Ndai haat. Kabeer, the Lord is the Diamond, and the Lord's humble servant is the jeweller who has set up his shop.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v162	jb hI pweIAih pwrKU qb hIrn kI swt ]162] (1373-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jab hee paa-ee-ah paarkhoo tab heeran kee saat. ||162||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v162	As soon as an appraiser is found, the price of the jewel is set. ||162||
WHEN	para 59758	kbIr kwm pry hir ismrIAY AYsw ismrhu inq ] (1373-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kaam paray har simree-ai aisaa simrahu nit. Kabeer, you remember the Lord in meditation, only when the need arises. You should remember Him all the time.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v163	Amrw pur bwsw krhu hir gieAw bhorY ibq ]163] (1373-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) amraa pur baasaa karahu har ga-i-aa bahorai bit. ||163||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v163	You shall dwell in the city of immortality, and the Lord shall restore the wealth you lost. ||163||
DEFINE	para 59760	kbIr syvw kau duie Bly eyku sMqu ieku rwmu ] (1373-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sayvaa ka-o du-ay bhalay ayk sant ik raam. Kabeer, it is good to perform selfless service for two - the Saints and the Lord.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v164	rwmu ju dwqw mukiq ko sMqu jpwvY nwmu ]164] (1373-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raam jo daataa mukat ko sant japaavai naam. ||164||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v164	The Lord is the Giver of liberation, and the Saint inspires us to chant the Naam. ||164||
RECORD	para 59762	kbIr ijh mwrig pMifq gey pwCY prI bhIr ] (1373-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jih maarag pandit ga-ay paachhai paree baheer. Kabeer, the crowds follow the path which the Pandits, the religious scholars, have taken.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v165	iek AvGt GwtI rwm kI iqh ciV rihE kbIr ]165] (1373-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ik avghat ghaatee raam kee tih charh rahi-o kabeer. ||165||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v165	There is a difficult and treacherous cliff on that path to the Lord; Kabeer is climbing that cliff. ||165||
RECORD	para 59764	kbIr dunIAw ky doKy mUAw cwlq kul kI kwin ] (1373-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer dunee-aa kay dokhay moo-aa chaalat kul kee kaan. Kabeer, the mortal dies of his worldly troubles and pain, after worrying about his family.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v166	qb kulu iks kw lwjsI jb ly Drih mswin ]166] (1373-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) tab kul kis kaa laajsee jab lay Dhareh masaan. ||166||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v166	Whose family is dishonored, when he is placed on the funeral pyre? ||166||
REQUIRE	para 59766	kbIr fUbihgo ry bwpury bhu logn kI kwin ] (1373-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer doob-higo ray baapuray baho logan kee kaan. Kabeer, you shall drown, you wretched being, from worrying about what other people think.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v167	pwrosI ky jo hUAw qU Apny BI jwnu ]167] (1373-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paarosee kay jo hoo-aa too apnay bhee jaan. ||167||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v167	You know that whatever happens to your neighbors, will also happen to you. ||167||
DEFINE	para 59768	kbIr BlI mDUkrI nwnw ibiD ko nwju ] (1373-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer bhalee maDhookree naanaa biDh ko naaj. Kabeer, even dry bread, made of various grains, is good.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v168	dwvw kwhU ko nhI bfw dysu bf rwju ]168] (1373-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) daavaa kaahoo ko nahee badaa days bad raaj. ||168||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v168	No one brags about it, throughout the vast country and great empire. ||168||
REQUIRE	para 59770	kbIr dwvY dwJnu hoqu hY inrdwvY rhY insMk ] (1373-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer daavai daajhan hot hai nirdaavai rahai nisank. Kabeer, those who brag, shall burn. Those who do not brag remain carefree.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v169	jo jnu inrdwvY rhY so gnY ieMdR so rMk ]169] (1373-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jo jan nirdaavai rahai so ganai indar so rank. ||169||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v169	That humble being who does not brag, looks upon the gods and the poor alike. ||169||
DEFINE	para 59772	kbIr pwil smuhw srvru Brw pI n skY koeI nIru ] (1373-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer paal samuhaa sarvar bharaa pee na sakai ko-ee neer. Kabeer, the pool is filled to overflowing, but no one can drink the water from it.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v170	Bwg bfy qY pwieE qUM Bir Bir pIau kbIr ]170] (1373-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) bhaag baday tai paa-i-o tooN bhar bhar pee-o kabeer. ||170||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v170	By great good fortune, you have found it; drink it in handfuls, O Kabeer. ||170||
REQUIRE	para 59774	kbIr prBwqy qwry iKsih iqau iehu iKsY srIru ] (1373-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer parbhaatay taaray khiseh ti-o ih khisai sareer. Kabeer, just as the stars disappear at dawn, so shall this body disappear.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v171	ey duie AKr nw iKsih so gih rihE kbIru ]171] (1373-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ay du-ay akhar naa khiseh so geh rahi-o kabeer. ||171||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v171	Only the letters of God's Name do not disappear; Kabeer holds these tight. ||171||
DEFINE	para 59776	kbIr koTI kwT kI dh idis lwgI Awig ] (1373-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kothee kaath kee dah dis laagee aag. Kabeer, the wooden house is burning on all sides.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v172	pMifq pMifq jil mUey mUrK aubry Bwig ]172] (1373-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) pandit pandit jal moo-ay moorakh ubray bhaag. ||172||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v172	The Pandits, the religious scholars, have been burnt to death, while the illiterate ones run to safety. ||172||
RECORD	para 59778	kbIr sMsw dUir kru kwgd dyh ibhwie ] (1373-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sansaa door kar kaagad dayh bihaa-ay. Kabeer, give up your skepticism; let your papers float away.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v173	bwvn AKr soiD kY hir crnI icqu lwie ]173] (1373-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) baavan akhar soDh kai har charnee chit laa-ay. ||173||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v173	Find the essence of the letters of the alphabet, and focus your consciousness on the Lord. ||173||
RECORD	para 59780	kbIr sMqu n CwfY sMqeI jau koitk imlih AsMq ] (1373-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sant na chhaadai sant-ee ja-o kotik mileh asant. Kabeer, the Saint does not forsake his Saintly nature, even though he meets with millions of evil-doers.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v174	milAwgru BuXMgm byiFE q sIqlqw n qjMq ]174] (1373-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) mali-aagar bhuyangam baydhi-o ta seetaltaa na tajant. ||174||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v174	Even when sandalwood is surrounded by snakes, it does not give up its cooling fragrance. ||174||
DEFINE	para 59782	kbIr mnu sIqlu BieAw pwieAw bRhm igAwnu ] (1373-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer man seetal bha-i-aa paa-i-aa barahm gi-aan. Kabeer, my mind is cooled and soothed; I have become God-conscious.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v175	ijin juAwlw jgu jwirAw su jn ky audk smwin ]175] (1373-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jin ju-aalaa jag jaari-aa so jan kay udak samaan. ||175||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v175	The fire which has burnt the world is like water to the Lord's humble servant. ||175||
RECORD	para 59784	kbIr swrI isrjnhwr kI jwnY nwhI koie ] (1373-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saaree sirjanhaar kee jaanai naahee ko-ay. Kabeer, no one knows the Play of the Creator Lord.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v176	kY jwnY Awpn DnI kY dwsu dIvwnI hoie ]176] (1373-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kai jaanai aapan Dhanee kai daas deevaanee ho-ay. ||176||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v176	Only the Lord Himself and the slaves at His Court understand it. ||176||
RECORD	para 59786	kbIr BlI BeI jo Bau pirAw idsw geˆØI sB BUil ] (1373-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer bhalee bha-ee jo bha-o pari-aa disaa ga-ee N sabh bhool. Kabeer, it is good that I feel the Fear of God; I have forgotten everything else.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v177	Erw gir pwnI BieAw jwie imilE Fil kUil ]177] (1374-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) oraa gar paanee bha-i-aa jaa-ay mili-o dhal kool. ||177||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v177	The hail-stone has melted into water, and flowed into the ocean. ||177||
DEFINE	para 59789	kbIrw DUir skyil kY purIAw bWDI dyh ] (1374-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeeraa Dhoor sakayl kai puree-aa baa NDhee dayh. Kabeer, the body is a pile of dust, collected and packed together.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v178	idvs cwir ko pyKnw AMiq Kyh kI Kyh ]178] (1374-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) divas chaar ko paykhnaa ant khayh kee khayh. ||178||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v178	It is a show which lasts for only a few days, and then dust returns to dust. ||178||
DEFINE	para 59791	kbIr sUrj cWd kY audY BeI sB dyh ] (1374-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer sooraj chaa Nd kai udai bha-ee sabh dayh. Kabeer, bodies are like the rising and setting of the sun and the moon.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v179	gur goibMd ky ibnu imly plit BeI sB Kyh ]179] (1374-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) gur gobind kay bin milay palat bha-ee sabh khayh. ||179||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v179	Without meeting the Guru, the Lord of the Universe, they are all reduced to dust again. ||179||
DEFINE	para 59793	jh AnBau qh BY nhI jh Bau qh hir nwih ] (1374-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jah anbha-o tah bhai nahee jah bha-o tah har naahi. Where the Fearless Lord is, there is no fear; where there is fear, the Lord is not there.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v180	kihE kbIr ibcwir kY sMq sunhu mn mwih ]180] (1374-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kahi-o kabeer bichaar kai sant sunhu man maahi. ||180||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v180	Kabeer speaks after careful consideration; hear this, O Saints, in your minds. ||180||
RECORD	para 59795	kbIr ijnhu ikCU jwinAw nhI iqn suK nId ibhwie ] (1374-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jinahu kichhoo jaani-aa nahee tin sukh need bihaa-ay. Kabeer, those who do not know anything, pass their lives in peaceful sleep.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v181	hmhu ju bUJw bUJnw pUrI prI blwie ]181] (1374-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) hamhu jo boojhaa boojhnaa pooree paree balaa-ay. ||181||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v181	But I have understood the riddle; I am faced with all sorts of troubles. ||181||
DEFINE	para 59797	kbIr mwry bhuqu pukwirAw pIr pukwrY Aaur ] (1374-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer maaray bahut pukaari-aa peer pukaarai a-or. Kabeer, those who are beaten cry a lot; but the cries of the pain of separation are different.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v182	lwgI cot mrMm kI rihE kbIrw Taur ]182] (1374-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) laagee chot maramm kee rahi-o kabeeraa tha-ur. ||182||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v182	Struck by the Mystery of God, Kabeer remains silent. ||182||
DEFINE	para 59799	kbIr cot suhylI syl kI lwgq lyie ausws ] (1374-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer chot suhaylee sayl kee laagat lay-ay usaas. Kabeer, the stroke of a lance is easy to bear; it takes away the breath.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v183	cot shwrY sbd kI qwsu gurU mY dws ]183] (1374-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) chot sahaarai sabad kee taas guroo mai daas. ||183||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v183	But one who endures the stroke of the Word of the Shabad is the Guru, and I am his slave. ||183||
RECORD	para 59801	kbIr mulW munwry ikAw cFih sWeI n bhrw hoie ] (1374-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer mulaa N munaaray ki-aa chadheh saa N-ee na bahraa ho-ay. Kabeer: O Mullah, why do you climb to the top of the minaret? The Lord is not hard of hearing.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v184	jw kwrin qUM bWg dyih idl hI BIqir joie ]184] (1374-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jaa kaaran too N baa Ng deh dil hee bheetar jo-ay. ||184||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v184	Look within your own heart for the One, for whose sake you shout your prayers. ||184||
DEFINE	para 59803	syK sbUrI bwhrw ikAw hj kwby jwie ] (1374-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) saykh sabooree baahraa ki-aa haj kaabay jaa-ay. Why does the Shaykh bother to go on pilgrimage to Mecca, if he is not content with himself?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v185	kbIr jw kI idl swbiq nhI qw kau khW Kudwie ]185] (1374-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jaa kee dil saabat nahee taa ka-o kahaa N khudaa-ay. ||185||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v185	Kabeer, one whose heart is not healthy and whole - how can he attain his Lord? ||185||
RECORD	para 59805	kbIr Alh kI kir bMdgI ijh ismrq duKu jwie ] (1374-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer alah kee kar bandagee jih simrat dukh jaa-ay. Kabeer, worship the Lord Allah; meditating in remembrance on Him, troubles and pains depart.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v186	idl mih sWeI prgtY buJY blµqI nWie ]186] (1374-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) dil meh saa N-ee pargatai bujhai balantee naaN-ay. ||186||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v186	The Lord shall be revealed within your own heart, and the burning fire within shall be extinguished by His Name. ||186||
DEFINE	para 59807	kbIr jorI kIey julmu hY khqw nwau hlwlu ] (1374-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer joree kee-ay julam hai kahtaa naa-o halaal. Kabeer, to use force is tyranny, even if you call it legal.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v187	dPqir lyKw mWgIAY qb hoiego kaunu hvwlu ]187] (1374-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) daftar laykhaa maa Ngee-ai tab ho-igo ka-un havaal. ||187||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v187	When your account is called for in the Court of the Lord, what will your condition be then? ||187||
DEFINE	para 59809	kbIr KUbu Kwnw KIcrI jw mih AMimRqu lonu ] (1374-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer khoob khaanaa kheechree jaa meh amrit lon. Kabeer, the dinner of beans and rice is excellent, if it is flavored with salt.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v188	hyrw rotI kwrny glw ktwvY kaunu ]188] (1374-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) hayraa rotee kaarnay galaa kataavai ka-un. ||188||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v188	Who would cut his throat, to have meat with his bread? ||188||
WHEN	para 59811	kbIr guru lwgw qb jwnIAY imtY mohu qn qwp ] (1374-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer gur laagaa tab jaanee-ai mitai moh tan taap. Kabeer, one is known to have been touched by the Guru, only when his emotional attachment and physical illnesses are eradicated.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v189	hrK sog dwJY nhI qb hir Awpih Awip ]189] (1374-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) harakh sog daajhai nahee tab har aapeh aap. ||189||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v189	He is not burned by pleasure or pain, and so he becomes the Lord Himself. ||189||
RECORD	para 59813	kbIr rwm khn mih Bydu hY qw mih eyku ibcwru ] (1374-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer raam kahan meh bhayd hai taa meh ayk bichaar. Kabeer, it does make a difference, how you chant the Lord's Name, 'Raam'. This is something to consider.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v190	soeI rwmu sBY khih soeI kauqkhwr ]190] (1374-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) so-ee raam sabhai kaheh so-ee ka-utakhaar. ||190||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v190	Everyone uses the same word for the son of Dasrath and the Wondrous Lord. ||190||
REQUIRE	para 59815	kbIr rwmY rwm khu kihby mwih ibbyk ] (1374-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer raamai raam kaho kahibay maahi bibayk. Kabeer, use the word 'Raam', only to speak of the All-pervading Lord. You must make that distinction.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v191	eyku Anykih imil gieAw eyk smwnw eyk ]191] (1374-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ayk anaykeh mil ga-i-aa ayk samaanaa ayk. ||191||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v191	One 'Raam' is pervading everywhere, while the other is contained only in himself. ||191||
DEFINE	para 59817	kbIr jw Gr swD n syvIAih hir kI syvw nwih ] (1374-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jaa ghar saaDh na sayvee-ah har kee sayvaa naahi. Kabeer, those houses in which neither the Holy nor the Lord are served
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v192	qy Gr mrht swrKy BUq bsih iqn mwih ]192] (1374-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) tay ghar marhat saarkhay bhoot baseh tin maahi. ||192||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v192	- those houses are like cremation grounds; demons dwell within them. ||192||
RECORD	para 59819	kbIr gUMgw hUAw bwvrw bhrw hUAw kwn ] (1374-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer goongaa hoo-aa baavraa bahraa hoo-aa kaan. Kabeer, I have become mute, insane and deaf.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v193	pwvhu qy ipMgul BieAw mwirAw siqgur bwn ]193] (1374-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paavhu tay pingul bha-i-aa maari-aa satgur baan. ||193||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v193	I am crippled - the True Guru has pierced me with His Arrow. ||193||
ALLOW	para 59821	kbIr siqgur sUrmy bwihAw bwnu ju eyku ] (1374-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer satgur soormay baahi-aa baan jo ayk. Kabeer, the True Guru, the Spiritual Warrior, has shot me with His Arrow.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v194	lwgq hI Buie igir pirAw prw kryjy Cyku ]194] (1374-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) laagat hee bhu-ay gir pari-aa paraa karayjay chhayk. ||194||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v194	As soon as it struck me, I fell to the ground, with a hole in my heart. ||194||
RECORD	para 59823	kbIr inrml bUMd Akws kI pir geI BUim ibkwr ] (1374-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer nirmal boond akaas kee par ga-ee bhoom bikaar. Kabeer, the pure drop of water falls from the sky, onto the dirty ground.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v195	ibnu sMgiq ieau mWneI hoie geI BT Cwr ]195] (1375-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) bin sangat i-o maa Nn-ee ho-ay ga-ee bhath chhaar. ||195||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v195	You must acknowledge this, that without the Sangat, the Holy Congregation, it turns into burnt ashes. ||195||
RECORD	para 59826	kbIr inrml bUMd Akws kI lInI BUim imlwie ] (1375-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer nirmal boond akaas kee leenee bhoom milaa-ay. Kabeer, the pure drop of water falls from the sky, and mixes with the dust.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v196	Aink isAwny pic gey nw inrvwrI jwie ]196] (1375-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) anik si-aanay pach ga-ay naa nirvaaree jaa-ay. ||196||
ALLOW	cauboly mhlw 5 v196	Millions of clever people may try, but they will fail - it cannot be made separate again. ||196||
RECORD	para 59828	kbIr hj kwby hau jwie Qw AwgY imilAw Kudwie ] (1375-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer haj kaabay ha-o jaa-ay thaa aagai mili-aa khudaa-ay. Kabeer, I was going on a pilgrimage to Mecca, and God met me on the way.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v197	sWeI muJ isau lir pirAw quJY ikin@ PurmweI gwie ]197] (1375-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) saaN-ee mujh si-o lar pari-aa tujhai kini H furmaa-ee gaa-ay. ||197||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v197	He scolded me and asked, "Who told you that I am only there?"||197||
RECORD	para 59830	kbIr hj kwbY hoie hoie gieAw kyqI bwr kbIr ] (1375-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer haj kaabai ho-ay ho-ay ga-i-aa kaytee baar kabeer. Kabeer, I went to Mecca - how many times, Kabeer?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v198	sWeI muJ mih ikAw Kqw muKhu n bolY pIr ]198] (1375-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) saaN-ee mujh meh ki-aa khataa mukhahu na bolai peer. ||198||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v198	O Lord, what is the problem with me? You have not spoken to me with Your Mouth. ||198||
RECORD	para 59832	kbIr jIA ju mwrih joru kir khqy hih ju hlwlu ] (1375-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jee-a jo maareh jor kar kahtay heh jo halaal. Kabeer, they oppress living beings and kill them, and call it proper.
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v199	dPqru deI jb kwiF hY hoiegw kaunu hvwlu ]199] (1375-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) daftar da-ee jab kaadh hai ho-igaa ka-un havaal. ||199||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v199	When the Lord calls for their account, what will their condition be? ||199||
REQUIRE	para 59834	kbIr joru kIAw so julmu hY lyie jbwbu Kudwie ] (1375-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jor kee-aa so julam hai lay-ay jabaab khudaa-ay. Kabeer, it is tyranny to use force; the Lord shall call you to account.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v200	dPqir lyKw nIksY mwr muhY muih Kwie ]200] (1375-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) daftar laykhaa neeksai maar muhai muhi khaa-ay. ||200||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v200	When your account is called for, your face and mouth shall be beaten. ||200||
DEFINE	para 59836	kbIr lyKw dynw suhylw jau idl sUcI hoie ] (1375-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer laykhaa daynaa suhaylaa ja-o dil soochee ho-ay. Kabeer, it is easy to render your account, if your heart is pure.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v201	ausu swcy dIbwn mih plw n pkrY koie ]201] (1375-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) us saachay deebaan meh palaa na pakrai ko-ay. ||201||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v201	In the True Court of the Lord, no one will seize you. ||201||
DEFINE	para 59838	kbIr DrqI Aru Awkws mih duie qUM brI AbD ] (1375-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer Dhartee ar aakaas meh du-ay tooN baree abaDh. Kabeer: O duality, you are mighty and powerful in the earth and the sky.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v202	Kt drsn sMsy pry Aru caurwsIh isD ]202] (1375-8, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) khat darsan sansay paray ar cha-oraaseeh siDh. ||202||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v202	The six Shaastras and the eighty-four Siddhas are entrenched in skepticism. ||202||
DEFINE	para 59840	kbIr myrw muJ mih ikCu nhI jo ikCu hY so qyrw ] (1375-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer mayraa mujh meh kichh nahee jo kichh hai so tayraa. Kabeer, nothing is mine within myself. Whatever there is, is Yours, O Lord.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v203	qyrw quJ kau saupqy ikAw lwgY myrw ]203] (1375-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) tayraa tujh ka-o sa-upatay ki-aa laagai mayraa. ||203||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v203	If I surrender to You what is already Yours, what does it cost me? ||203||
RECORD	para 59842	kbIr qUM qUM krqw qU hUAw muJ mih rhw n hUM ] (1375-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer tooN tooN kartaa too hoo-aa mujh meh rahaa na hoo N. Kabeer, repeating, "You, You", I have become like You. Nothing of me remains in myself.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v204	jb Awpw pr kw imit gieAw jq dyKau qq qU ]204] (1375-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jab aapaa par kaa mit ga-i-aa jat daykh-a-u tat too. ||204||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v204	When the difference between myself and others is removed, then wherever I look, I see only You. ||204||
RECORD	para 59844	kbIr ibkwrh icqvqy JUTy krqy Aws ] (1375-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer bikaareh chitvatay jhoothay kartay aas. Kabeer, those who think of evil and entertain false hopes
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v205	mnorQu koie n pUirE cwly aUiT inrws ]205] (1375-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) manorath ko-ay na poori-o chaalay ooth niraas. ||205||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v205	- none of their desires shall be fulfilled; they shall depart in despair. ||205||
DEFINE	para 59846	kbIr hir kw ismrnu jo krY so suKIAw sMswir ] (1375-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer har kaa simran jo karai so sukhee-aa sansaar. Kabeer, whoever meditates in remembrance on the Lord, he alone is happy in this world.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v206	ieq auq kqih n foleI ijs rwKY isrjnhwr ]206] (1375-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) it ut kateh na dol-ee jis raakhai sirjanhaar. ||206||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v206	One who is protected and saved by the Creator Lord, shall never waver, here or hereafter. ||206||
RECORD	para 59848	kbIr GwxI pIVqy siqgur lIey Cfwie ] (1375-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ghaanee peerh-tay satgur lee-ay chhadaa-ay. Kabeer, I was being crushed like sesame seeds in the oil-press, but the True Guru saved me.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v207	prw pUrblI BwvnI prgtu hoeI Awie ]207] (1375-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paraa poorablee bhaavnee pargat ho-ee aa-ay. ||207||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v207	My pre-ordained primal destiny has now been revealed. ||207||
RECORD	para 59850	kbIr twlY tolY idnu gieAw ibAwju bFMqau jwie ] (1375-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer taalai tolai din ga-i-aa bi-aaj badhanta-o jaa-ay. Kabeer, my days have passed, and I have postponed my payments; the interest on my account continues to increase.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v208	nw hir BijE n Kqu PitE kwlu phUMco Awie ]208] (1375-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) naa har bhaji-o na khat fati-o kaal pahoo Ncho aa-ay. ||208||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v208	I have not meditated on the Lord and my account is still pending, and now, the moment of my death has come! ||208||
RECORD	para 59852	mhlw 5 ] (1375-15) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 59853	kbIr kUkru Bauknw krMg ipCY auiT Dwie ] (1375-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kookar bha-ukanaa karang pichhai uth Dhaa-ay. Kabeer, the mortal is a barking dog, chasing after a carcass.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v209	krmI siqguru pwieAw ijin hau lIAw Cfwie ]209] (1375-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) karmee satgur paa-i-aa jin ha-o lee-aa chhadaa-ay. ||209||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v209	By the Grace of good karma, I have found the True Guru, who has saved me. ||209||
RECORD	para 59855	mhlw 5 ] (1375-16) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 59856	kbIr DrqI swD kI qskr bYsih gwih ] (1375-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer Dhartee saaDh kee taskar baiseh gaahi. Kabeer, the earth belongs to the Holy, but it is being occupied by thieves.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v210	DrqI Bwir n ibAwpeI aun kau lwhU lwih ]210] (1375-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) Dhartee bhaar na bi-aapa-ee un ka-o laahoo laahi. ||210||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v210	They are not a burden to the earth; they receive its blessings. ||210||
RECORD	para 59858	mhlw 5 ] (1375-17) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 59859	kbIr cwvl kwrny quK kau muhlI lwie ] (1375-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer chaaval kaarnay tukh ka-o muhlee laa-ay. Kabeer, the rice is beaten with a mallet to get rid of the husk.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v211	sMig kusMgI bYsqy qb pUCY Drm rwie ]211] (1375-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) sang kusangee baistay tab poochhai Dharam raa-ay. ||211||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v211	When people sit in evil company, the Righteous Judge of Dharma calls them to account. ||211||
RECORD	para 59861	nwmw mwieAw moihAw khY iqlocnu mIq ] (1375-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) naamaa maa-i-aa mohi-aa kahai tilochan meet. Trilochan says, O Naam Dayv, Maya has enticed you, my friend.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v212	kwhy CIphu CwielY rwm n lwvhu cIqu ]212] (1375-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kaahay chheepahu chhaa-ilai raam na laavhu cheet. ||212||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v212	Why are you printing designs on these sheets, and not focusing your consciousness on the Lord? ||212||
RECORD	para 59863	nwmw khY iqlocnw muK qy rwmu sMm@wil ] (1375-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) naamaa kahai tilochanaa mukh tay raam sam Haal. Naam Dayv answers, O Trilochan, chant the Lord's Name with your mouth.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v213	hwQ pwau kir kwmu sBu cIqu inrMjn nwil ]213] (1376-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) haath paa-o kar kaam sabh cheet niranjan naal. ||213||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v213	With your hands and feet, do all your work, but let your consciousness remain with the Immaculate Lord. ||213||
RECORD	para 59866	mhlw 5 ] (1376-1) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 59867	kbIrw hmrw ko nhI hm iks hU ky nwih ] (1376-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeeraa hamraa ko nahee ham kis hoo kay naahi. Kabeer, no one belongs to me, and I belong to no one else.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v214	ijin iehu rcnu rcwieAw iqs hI mwih smwih ]214] (1376-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) jin ih rachan rachaa-i-aa tis hee maahi samaahi. ||214||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v214	The One who created the creation - into Him I shall be absorbed. ||214||
RECORD	para 59869	kbIr kIciV Awtw igir pirAw ikCU n AwieE hwQ ] (1376-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer keecharh aataa gir pari-aa kichhoo na aa-i-o haath. Kabeer, the flour has fallen into the mud; nothing has come into my hands.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v215	pIsq pIsq cwibAw soeI inbihAw swQ ]215] (1376-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) peesat peesat chaabi-aa so-ee nibhi-aa saath. ||215||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v215	That which was eaten while it was being ground - that alone is of any use. ||215||
RECORD	para 59871	kbIr mnu jwnY sB bwq jwnq hI Aaugnu krY ] (1376-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer man jaanai sabh baat jaanat hee a-ugan karai. Kabeer, the mortal knows everything, and knowing, he still makes mistakes.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v216	kwhy kI kuslwq hwiQ dIpu kUey prY ]216] (1376-4, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kaahay kee kuslaat haath deep koo-ay parai. ||216||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v216	What good is a lamp in one's hand, if he falls into the well? ||216||
RECORD	para 59873	kbIr lwgI pRIiq sujwn isau brjY logu Ajwnu ] (1376-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer laagee pareet sujaan si-o barjai log ajaan. Kabeer, I am in love with the All-knowing Lord; the ignorant ones try to hold me back.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v217	qw isau tUtI ikau bnY jw ky jIA prwn ]217] (1376-5, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) taa si-o tootee ki-o banai jaa kay jee-a paraan. ||217||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v217	How could I ever break with the One, who owns our soul and breath of life. ||217||
RECORD	para 59875	kbIr koTy mMfp hyqu kir kwhy mrhu svwir ] (1376-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kothay mandap hayt kar kaahay marahu savaar. Kabeer, why kill yourself for your love of decorations of your home and mansion?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v218	kwrju swFy qIin hQ GnI q pauny cwir ]218] (1376-6, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kaaraj saadhay teen hath ghanee ta pa-unay chaar. ||218||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v218	In the end, only six feet, or a little more, shall be your lot. ||218||
RECORD	para 59877	kbIr jo mY icqvau nw krY ikAw myry icqvy hoie ] (1376-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer jo mai chitva-o naa karai ki-aa mayray chitvay ho-ay. Kabeer, whatever I wish for does not happen. What can I accomplish by merely thinking?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v219	Apnw icqivAw hir krY jo myry iciq n hoie ]219] (1376-7, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) apnaa chitvi-aa har karai jo mayray chit na ho-ay. ||219||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v219	The Lord does whatever He wishes; it is not up to me at all. ||219||
RECORD	para 59879	mÚ 3 ] (1376-8) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 59880	icMqw iB Awip krwiesI AicMqu iB Awpy dyie ] (1376-8, slok, mÚ 3) chintaa bhe aap karaa-isee achint bhe aapay day-ay. God Himself makes the mortals anxious, and He Himself takes the anxiety away.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v220	nwnk so swlwhIAY ij sBnw swr kryie ]220] (1376-9, slok, mÚ 3) naanak so salaahee-ai je sabhnaa saar karay-i. ||220||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v220	O Nanak, praise the One, who takes care of all. ||220||
RECORD	para 59882	mÚ 5 ] (1376-9) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 59883	kbIr rwmu n cyiqE iPirAw lwlc mwih ] (1376-9, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer raam na chayti-o firi-aa laalach maahi. Kabeer, the mortal does not remember the Lord; he wanders around, engrossed in greed.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v221	pwp krMqw mir gieAw AauD punI iKn mwih ]221] (1376-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) paap karantaa mar ga-i-aa a-oDh punee khin maahi. ||221||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v221	Committing sins, he dies, and his life ends in an instant. ||221||
DEFINE	para 59885	kbIr kwieAw kwcI kwrvI kyvl kwcI Dwqu ] (1376-10, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kaa-i-aa kaachee kaarvee kayval kaachee Dhaat. Kabeer, the body is like a clay vessel or a brittle metal pot.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v222	swbqu rKih q rwm Bju nwih q ibnTI bwq ]222] (1376-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) saabat rakheh ta raam bhaj naahi ta binthee baat. ||222||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v222	If you wish to keep it safe and sound, then vibrate and meditate on the Lord; otherwise, the thing shall break. ||222||
RECORD	para 59887	kbIr kyso kyso kUkIAY n soeIAY Aswr ] (1376-11, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kayso kayso kookee-ai na so-ee-ai asaar. Kabeer, chant the Name of the Beautifully-haired Lord; do not sleep unaware.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v223	rwiq idvs ky kUkny kbhU ky sunY pukwr ]223] (1376-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) raat divas kay kooknay kabhoo kay sunai pukaar. ||223||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v223	Chanting His Name night and day, the Lord will eventually hear your call. ||223||
DEFINE	para 59889	kbIr kwieAw kjlI bnu BieAw mnu kuMcru mX mMqu ] (1376-12, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer kaa-i-aa kajlee ban bha-i-aa man kunchar ma-y mant. Kabeer, the body is a banana forest, and the mind is an intoxicated elephant.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v224	AMksu g´wnu rqnu hY Kyvtu ibrlw sMqu ]224] (1376-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ankas ga-yaan ratan hai khayvat birlaa sant. ||224||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v224	The jewel of spiritual wisdom is the prod, and the rare Saint is the rider. ||224||
RECORD	para 59891	kbIr rwm rqnu muKu koQrI pwrK AwgY Koil ] (1376-13, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer raam ratan mukh kothree paarakh aagai khol. Kabeer, the Lord's Name is the jewel, and the mouth is the purse; open this purse to the Appraiser.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v225	koeI Awie imlYgo gwhkI lygo mhgy moil ]225] (1376-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) ko-ee aa-ay milaigo gaahkee laygo mahgay mol. ||225||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v225	If a buyer can be found, it will go for a high price. ||225||
RECORD	para 59893	kbIr rwm nwmu jwinE nhI pwilE ktku kutMbu ] (1376-14, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer raam naam jaani-o nahee paali-o katak kutamb. Kabeer, the mortal does not know the Lord's Name, but he has raised a very large family.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v226	DMDy hI mih mir gieE bwhir BeI n bMb ]226] (1376-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) DhanDhay hee meh mar ga-i-o baahar bha-ee na bamb. ||226||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v226	He dies in the midst of his worldly affairs, and then he is not heard in the external world. ||226||
DEFINE	para 59895	kbIr AwKI kyry mwtuky plu plu geI ibhwie ] (1376-15, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aakhee kayray maatukay pal pal ga-ee bihaa-ay. Kabeer, in the blink of an eye, moment by moment, life is passing by.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v227	mnu jMjwlu n CofeI jm dIAw dmwmw Awie ]227] (1376-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) man janjaal na chhod-ee jam dee-aa damaamaa aa-ay. ||227||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v227	The mortal does not give up his worldly entanglements; the Messenger of Death walks in and beats the drum. ||227||
DEFINE	para 59897	kbIr qrvr rUpI rwmu hY Pl rUpI bYrwgu ] (1376-16, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer tarvar roopee raam hai fal roopee bairaag. Kabeer, the Lord is the tree, and disillusionment with the world is the fruit.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v228	CwieAw rUpI swDu hY ijin qijAw bwdu ibbwdu ]228] (1376-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) chhaa-i-aa roopee saaDh hai jin taji-aa baad bibaad. ||228||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v228	The Holy man, who has abandoned useless arguments, is the shade of the tree. ||228||
REQUIRE	para 59899	kbIr AYsw bIju boie bwrh mws Plµq ] (1376-17, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer aisaa beej bo-ay baarah maas falant. Kabeer, plant the seeds of such a plant, which shall bear fruit throughout the twelve months,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v229	sIql CwieAw gihr Pl pMKI kyl krMq ]229] (1376-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) seetal chhaa-i-aa gahir fal pankhee kayl karant. ||229||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v229	with cooling shade and abundant fruit, upon which birds joyously play. ||229||
DEFINE	para 59901	kbIr dwqw qrvru dXw Plu aupkwrI jIvMq ] (1376-18, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer daataa tarvar da-yaa fal upkaaree jeevant. Kabeer, the Great Giver is the tree, which blesses all with the fruit of compassion.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v230	pMKI cly idswvrI ibrKw suPl Plµq ]230] (1376-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) pankhee chalay disaavaree birkhaa sufal falant. ||230||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v230	When the birds migrate to other lands, O Tree, you bear the fruits. ||230||
WHEN	para 59903	kbIr swDU sMgu prwpqI iliKAw hoie illwt ] (1376-19, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer saaDhoo sang paraapatee likhi-aa ho-ay lilaat. Kabeer, the mortal finds the Saadh Sangat, the Company of the Holy, if he has such destiny written upon his forehead.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v231	mukiq pdwrQu pweIAY Twk n AvGt Gwt ]231] (1377-1, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) mukat padaarath paa-ee-ai thaak na avghat ghaat. ||231||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v231	He obtains the treasure of liberation, and the difficult road to the Lord is not blocked. ||231||
DEFINE	para 59906	kbIr eyk GVI AwDI GrI AwDI hUM qy AwD ] (1377-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer ayk gharhee aaDhee gharee aaDhee hooN tay aaDh. Kabeer, whether is is for an hour, half an hour, or half of that,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v232	Bgqn syqI gosty jo kIny so lwB ]232] (1377-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) bhagtan saytee gostay jo keenay so laabh. ||232||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v232	whatever it is, it is worthwhile to speak with the Holy. ||232||
RECORD	para 59908	kbIr BWg mwCulI surw pwin jo jo pRwnI KWih ] (1377-2, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) kabeer bhaa Ng maachhulee suraa paan jo jo paraanee khaaNhi. Kabeer, those mortals who consume marijuana, fish and wine
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v233	qIrQ brq nym kIey qy sBY rswqil jWih ]233] (1377-3, slok, Bgq kbIr jI) tirath barat naym kee-ay tay sabhai rasaatal jaa Nhi. ||233||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v233	- no matter what pilgrimages, fasts and rituals they follow, they will all go to hell. ||233||
