RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v26	gihlw rUhu n jwxeI isru BI imtI Kwie ]26] (1379-5, slok, syK PrId jI) gahilaa roohu na jaan-ee sir bhee mitee khaa-ay. ||26||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v26	My thoughtless self did not realize that one day, dust will consume my head as well. ||26||
RECORD	para 59996	PrIdw skr KMfu invwq guVu mwiKEu mWJw duDu ] (1379-6, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa sakar khand nivaat gurh maakhi-o maa Njhaa duDh. Fareed: sugar cane, candy, sugar, molasses, honey and buffalo's milk
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v27	sBy vsqU imTIAW rb n pujin quDu ]27] (1379-6, slok, syK PrId jI) sabhay vastoo mithee-aaN rab na pujan tuDh. ||27||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v27	- all these things are sweet, but they are not equal to You. ||27||
DEFINE	para 59998	PrIdw rotI myrI kwT kI lwvxu myrI BuK ] (1379-7, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa rotee mayree kaath kee laavan mayree bhukh. Fareed, my bread is made of wood, and hunger is my appetizer.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v28	ijnw KwDI copVI Gxy shingy duK ]28] (1379-7, slok, syK PrId jI) jinaa khaaDhee choprhee ghanay sehnigay dukh. ||28||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v28	Those who eat buttered bread, will suffer in terrible pain. ||28||
RECORD	para 60000	ruKI suKI Kwie kY TMFw pwxI pIau ] (1379-8, slok, syK PrId jI) rukhee sukhee khaa-ay kai thandhaa paanee pee-o. Eat dry bread, and drink cold water.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v29	PrIdw dyiK prweI copVI nw qrswey jIau ]29] (1379-8, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa daykh paraa-ee choprhee naa tarsaa-ay jee-o. ||29||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v29	Fareed, if you see someone else's buttered bread, do not envy him for it. ||29||
DEFINE	para 60002	Aju n suqI kMq isau AMgu muVy muiV jwie ] (1379-9, slok, syK PrId jI) aj na sutee kant si-o ang murhay murh jaa-ay. This night, I did not sleep with my Husband Lord, and now my body is suffering in pain.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v30	jwie puChu fohwgxI qum ikau rYix ivhwie ]30] (1379-9, slok, syK PrId jI) jaa-ay puchhahu dohaaganee tum ki-o rain vihaa-ay. ||30||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v30	Go and ask the deserted bride, how she passes her night. ||30||
RECORD	para 60004	swhurY FoeI nw lhY pyeIAY nwhI Qwau ] (1379-10, slok, syK PrId jI) saahurai dho-ee naa lahai pay-ee-ai naahee thaa-o. She finds no place of rest in her father-in-law's home, and no place in her parents' home either.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v31	ipru vwqVI n puCeI Dn sohwgix nwau ]31] (1379-10, slok, syK PrId jI) pir vaat-rhee na puchh-ee Dhan sohagan naa-o. ||31||
UPHOLD	cauboly mhlw 5 v31	Her Husband Lord does not care for her; what sort of a blessed, happy soul-bride is she? ||31||
RECORD	para 60006	swhurY pyeIAY kMq kI kMqu AgMmu AQwhu ] (1379-11, slok, syK PrId jI) saahurai pay-ee-ai kant kee kant agamm athaahu. In her father-in-law's home hereafter, and in her parents' home in this world, she belongs to her Husband Lord. Her Husband is Inaccessible and Unfathomable.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v32	nwnk so sohwgxI ju BwvY byprvwh ]32] (1379-11, slok, syK PrId jI) naanak so sohaaganee jo bhaavai bayparvaah. ||32||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v32	O Nanak, she is the happy soul-bride, who is pleasing to her Carefree Lord. ||32||
RECORD	para 60008	nwqI DoqI sMbhI suqI Awie nicMdu ] (1379-11, slok, syK PrId jI) naatee Dhotee sambhee sutee aa-ay nachind. Bathing, washing and decorating herself, she comes and sleeps without anxiety.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v33	PrIdw rhI su byVI ihM|u dI geI kQUrI gMDu ]33] (1379-12, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa rahee so bayrhee hiny dee ga-ee kathooree ganDh. ||33||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v33	Fareed, she still smells like asafoetida; the fragrance of musk is gone. ||33||
RECORD	para 60010	jobn jWdy nw frW jy sh pRIiq n jwie ] (1379-12, slok, syK PrId jI) joban jaa Nday naa daraa N jay sah pareet na jaa-ay. I am not afraid of losing my youth, as long as I do not lose the Love of my Husband Lord.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v34	PrIdw ikqˆØI jobn pRIiq ibnu suik gey kumlwie ]34] (1379-13, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa kitee N joban pareet bin suk ga-ay kumlaa-ay. ||34||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v34	Fareed, so many youths, without His Love, have dried up and withered away. ||34||
RECORD	para 60012	PrIdw icMq Ktolw vwxu duKu ibrih ivCwvx lyPu ] (1379-13, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa chint khatolaa vaan dukh bireh vichhaavan layf. Fareed, anxiety is my bed, pain is my mattress, and the pain of separation is my blanket and quilt.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v35	eyhu hmwrw jIvxw qU swihb scy vyKu ]35] (1379-14, slok, syK PrId jI) ayhu hamaaraa jeevnaa too saahib sachay vaykh. ||35||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v35	Behold, this is my life, O my True Lord and Master. ||35||
DEFINE	para 60014	ibrhw ibrhw AwKIAY ibrhw qU sulqwnu ] (1379-14, slok, syK PrId jI) birhaa birhaa aakhee-ai birhaa too sultaan. Many talk of the pain and suffering of separation; O pain, you are the ruler of all.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v36	PrIdw ijqu qin ibrhu n aUpjY so qnu jwxu mswnu ]36] (1379-15, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa jit tan birahu na oopjai so tan jaan masaan. ||36||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v36	Fareed, that body, within which love of the Lord does not well up - look upon that body as a cremation ground. ||36||
DEFINE	para 60016	PrIdw ey ivsu gMdlw DrIAW KMfu ilvwiV ] (1379-15, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa ay vis gandlaa Dharee-aaN khand livaarh. Fareed, these are poisonous sprouts coated with sugar.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v37	ieik rwhydy rih gey ieik rwDI gey aujwiV ]37] (1379-16, slok, syK PrId jI) ik raahayday reh ga-ay ik raaDhee ga-ay ujaarh. ||37||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v37	Some die planting them, and some are ruined, harvesting and enjoying them. ||37||
WHEN	para 60018	PrIdw cwir gvwieAw hMiF kY cwir gvwieAw sMim ] (1379-16, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa chaar gavaa-i-aa handh kai chaar gavaa-i-aa samm. Fareed, the hours of the day are lost wandering around, and the hours of the night are lost in sleep.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v38	lyKw rbu mMgysIAw qU AWho kyrHy kMim ]38] (1379-17, slok, syK PrId jI) laykhaa rab mangaysee-aa too aa Nho kayr Hay kamm. ||38||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v38	God will call for your account, and ask you why you came into this world. ||38||
RECORD	para 60020	PrIdw dir drvwjY jwie kY ikau ifTo GVIAwlu ] (1379-17, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa dar darvaajai jaa-ay kai ki-o ditho gharhee-aal. Fareed, you have gone to the Lord's Door. Have you seen the gong there?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v39	eyhu indosW mwrIAY hm dosW dw ikAw hwlu ]39] (1379-18, slok, syK PrId jI) ayhu nidosaa N maaree-ai ham dosaaN daa ki-aa haal. ||39||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v39	This blameless object is being beaten - imagine what is in store for us sinners! ||39||
DEFINE	para 60022	GVIey GVIey mwrIAY phrI lhY sjwie ] (1379-19, slok, syK PrId jI) gharhee-ay gharhee-ay maaree-ai pahree lahai sajaa-ay. Each and every hour, it is beaten; it is punished every day.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v40	so hyVw GVIAwl ijau fuKI rYix ivhwie ]40] (1379-19, slok, syK PrId jI) so hayrhaa gharhee-aal ji-o dukhee rain vihaa-ay. ||40||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v40	This beautiful body is like the gong; it passes the night in pain. ||40||
RECORD	para 60025	buFw hoAw syK PrIdu kMbix lgI dyh ] (1380-1, slok, syK PrId jI) budhaa ho-aa saykh fareed kamban lagee dayh. Shaykh Fareed has grown old, and his body has begun to tremble.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v41	jy sau vir@Aw jIvxw BI qnu hosI Kyh ]41] (1380-1, slok, syK PrId jI) jay sa-o vareh-aa jeevnaa bhee tan hosee khayh. ||41||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v41	Even if he could live for hundreds of years, his body will eventually turn to dust. ||41||
RECORD	para 60027	PrIdw bwir prwieAY bYsxw sWeI muJY n dyih ] (1380-1, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa baar paraa-i-ai baisnaa saa N-ee mujhai na deh. Fareed begs, O Lord, do not make me sit at another's door.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v42	jy qU eyvY rKsI jIau srIrhu lyih ]42] (1380-2, slok, syK PrId jI) jay too ayvai rakhsee jee-o sareerahu layhi. ||42||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v42	If this is the way you are going to keep me, then go ahead and take the life out of my body. ||42||
