RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v47	The shaykhs and their disciples have all departed, each in his own turn. ||47||
DEFINE	para 60039	PrIdw duhu dIvI blµidAw mlku bihTw Awie ] (1380-7, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa duhu deevee balandi-aa malak bahithaa aa-ay. Fareed, the two lamps are lit, but death has come anyway.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v48	gVu lIqw Gtu luitAw dIvVy gieAw buJwie ]48] (1380-8, slok, syK PrId jI) garh leetaa ghat luti-aa deevrhay ga-i-aa bujhaa-ay. ||48||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v48	It has captured the fortress of the body, and plundered the home of the heart; it extinguishes the lamps and departs. ||48||
RECORD	para 60041	PrIdw vyKu kpwhY ij QIAw ij isir QIAw iqlwh ] (1380-8, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa vaykh kapaahai je thee-aa je sir thee-aa tilaah. Fareed, look at what has happened to the cotton and the sesame seed,
RECORD	para 60042	kmwdY Aru kwgdY kuMny koieilAwh ] (1380-9, slok, syK PrId jI) kamaadai ar kaagdai kunnay ko-ili-aah. the sugar cane and paper, the clay pots and the charcoal.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v49	mMdy Aml kryidAw eyh sjwie iqnwh ]49] (1380-9, slok, syK PrId jI) manday amal karaydi-aa ayh sajaa-ay tinaah. ||49||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v49	This is the punishment for those who do evil deeds. ||49||
RECORD	para 60044	PrIdw kMin muslw sUPu gil idil kwqI guVu vwiq ] (1380-10, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa kann muslaa soof gal dil kaatee gurh vaat. Fareed, you wear your prayer shawl on your shoulders and the robes of a Sufi; your words are sweet, but there is a dagger in your heart.
