DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v50	Outwardly, you look bright, but your heart is dark as night. ||50||
WHEN	para 60046	PrIdw rqI rqu n inklY jy qnu cIrY koie ] (1380-11, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa ratee rat na niklai jay tan cheerai ko-ay. Fareed, not even a drop of blood would issue forth, if someone cut my body.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v51	jo qn rqy rb isau iqn qin rqu n hoie ]51] (1380-11, slok, syK PrId jI) jo tan ratay rab si-o tin tan rat na ho-ay. ||51||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v51	Those bodies which are imbued with the Lord - those bodies contain no blood. ||51||
RECORD	para 60048	mÚ 3 ] (1380-12) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
DEFINE	para 60049	iehu qnu sBo rqu hY rqu ibnu qMnu n hoie ] (1380-12, slok, mÚ 3) ih tan sabho rat hai rat bin tann na ho-ay. This body is all blood; without blood, this body could not exist.
DEFINE	para 60050	jo sh rqy Awpxy iqqu qin loBu rqu n hoie ] (1380-12, slok, mÚ 3) jo sah ratay aapnay tit tan lobh rat na ho-ay. Those who are imbued with their Lord, do not have the blood of greed in their bodies.
WHEN	para 60051	BY pieAY qnu KIxu hoie loBu rqu ivchu jwie ] (1380-13, slok, mÚ 3) bhai pa-i-ai tan kheen ho-ay lobh rat vichahu jaa-ay. When the Fear of God fills the body, it becomes thin; the blood of greed departs from within.
RECORD	para 60052	ijau bYsMqir Dwqu suDu hoie iqau hir kw Bau durmiq mYlu gvwie ] (1380-13, slok, mÚ 3) ji-o baisantar Dhaat suDh ho-ay ti-o har kaa bha-o durmat mail gavaa-ay. Just as metal is purified by fire, the Fear of God removes the filthy residues of evil- mindedness.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v52	nwnk qy jn sohxy ij rqy hir rMgu lwie ]52] (1380-14, slok, mÚ 3) naanak tay jan sohnay je ratay har rang laa-ay. ||52||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v52	O Nanak, those humble beings are beautiful, who are imbued with the Lord's Love. ||52||
DEFINE	para 60054	PrIdw soeI srvru FUiF lhu ijQhu lBI vQu ] (1380-14, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa so-ee sarvar dhoodh lahu jithahu labhee vath. Fareed, seek that sacred pool, in which the genuine article is found.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v53	CpiV FUFY ikAw hovY ickiV fubY hQu ]53] (1380-15, slok, syK PrId jI) chhaparh dhoodhai ki-aa hovai chikarh dubai hath. ||53||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v53	Why do you bother to search in the pond? Your hand will only sink into the mud. ||53||
DEFINE	para 60056	PrIdw nµFI kMqu n rwivE vfI QI mueIAwsu ] (1380-15, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa nandhee kant na raavi-o vadee thee mu-ee-aas. Fareed, when she is young, she does not enjoy her Husband. When she grows up, she dies.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v54	Dn kUkyNdI gor myN qY sh nw imlIAwsu ]54] (1380-16, slok, syK PrId jI) Dhan kookay Ndee gor mayN tai sah naa milee-aas. ||54||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v54	Lying in the grave, the soul-bride cries, "I did not meet You, my Lord."||54||
RECORD	para 60058	PrIdw isru pilAw dwVI plI muCW BI plIAW ] (1380-16, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa sir pali-aa daarhee palee muchhaaN bhee palee-aaN. Fareed, your hair has turned grey, your beard has turned grey, and your moustache has turned grey.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v55	ry mn gihly bwvly mwxih ikAw rlIAW ]55] (1380-17, slok, syK PrId jI) ray man gahilay baavlay maaneh ki-aa ralee-aa N. ||55||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v55	O my thoughtless and insane mind, why are you indulging in pleasures? ||55||
RECORD	para 60060	PrIdw koTy Dukxu kyqVw ipr nIdVI invwir ] (1380-17, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa kothay Dhukan kayt-rhaa pir need-rhee nivaar. Fareed, how long can you run on the rooftop? You are asleep to your Husband Lord - give it up!
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v56	jo idh lDy gwxvy gey ivlwiV ivlwiV ]56] (1380-18, slok, syK PrId jI) jo dih laDhay gaanvay ga-ay vilaarh vilaarh. ||56||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v56	The days which were allotted to you are numbered, and they are passing, passing away. ||56||
RECORD	para 60062	PrIdw koTy mMfp mwVIAw eyqu n lwey icqu ] (1380-18, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa kothay mandap maarhee-aa ayt na laa-ay chit. Fareed, houses, mansions and balconies - do not attach your consciousness to these.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v57	imtI peI AqolvI koie n hosI imqu ]57] (1380-19, slok, syK PrId jI) mitee pa-ee atolavee ko-ay na hosee mit. ||57||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v57	When these collapse into heaps of dust, none of them will be your friend. ||57||
RECORD	para 60064	PrIdw mMfp mwlu n lwie mrg sqwxI iciq Dir ] (1380-19, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa mandap maal na laa-ay marag sataanee chit Dhar. Fareed, do not focus on mansions and wealth; center your consciousness on death, your powerful enemy.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v58	sweI jwie sm@wil ijQY hI qau vM\xw ]58] (1381-1, slok, syK PrId jI) saa-ee jaa-ay sam Haal jithai hee ta-o vanjnaa. ||58||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v58	Remember that place where you must go. ||58||
RECORD	para 60067	PrIdw ijn@I kMmI nwih gux qy kMmVy ivswir ] (1381-1, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa jin Hee kammee naahi gun tay kammrhay visaar. Fareed, those deeds which do not bring merit - forget about those deeds.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v59	mqu srimMdw QIvhI sWeI dY drbwir ]59] (1381-2, slok, syK PrId jI) mat sarmindaa theevhee saaN-ee dai darbaar. ||59||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v59	Otherwise, you shall be put to shame, in the Court of the Lord. ||59||
RECORD	para 60069	PrIdw swihb dI kir cwkrI idl dI lwih BrWid ] (1381-2, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa saahib dee kar chaakree dil dee laahi bharaaNd. Fareed, work for your Lord and Master; dispel the doubts of your heart.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v60	drvysW no loVIAY ruKW dI jIrWid ]60] (1381-3, slok, syK PrId jI) darvaysaaN no lorhee-ai rukhaaN dee jeeraaNd. ||60||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v60	The dervishes, the humble devotees, have the patient endurance of trees. ||60||
DEFINE	para 60071	PrIdw kwly mYfy kpVy kwlw mYfw vysu ] (1381-3, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa kaalay maiday kaprhay kaalaa maidaa vays. Fareed, my clothes are black, and my outfit is black.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v61	gunhI BirAw mY iPrw loku khY drvysu ]61] (1381-4, slok, syK PrId jI) gunhee bhari-aa mai firaa lok kahai darvays. ||61||
