DEFINE	para 60073	qqI qoie n plvY jy jil tubI dyie ] (1381-4, slok, syK PrId jI) tatee to-ay na palvai jay jal tubee day-ay. The crop which is burnt will not bloom, even if it is soaked in water.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v62	PrIdw jo fohwgix rb dI JUrydI JUryie ]62] (1381-5, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa jo dohaagan rab dee jhooraydee jooray-ay. ||62||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v62	Fareed, she who is forsaken by her Husband Lord, grieves and laments. ||62||
DEFINE	para 60075	jW kuAwrI qw cwau vIvwhI qW mwmly ] (1381-5, slok, syK PrId jI) jaa N ku-aaree taa chaa-o veevaahee taaN maamlay. When she is a virgin, she is full of desire; but when she is married, then her troubles begin.
