RECORD	para 60155	PrIdw drIAwvY kMn@Y bgulw bYTw kyl kry ] (1383-4, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa daree-aavai kan Hai bagulaa baithaa kayl karay. Fareed, the crane perches on the river bank, playing joyfully.
DEFINE	para 60156	kyl krydy hMJ no AicMqy bwj pey ] (1383-4, slok, syK PrId jI) kayl karayday hanjh no achintay baaj pa-ay. While it is playing, a hawk suddenly pounces on it.
DEFINE	para 60157	bwj pey iqsu rb dy kylW ivsrIAW ] (1383-4, slok, syK PrId jI) baaj pa-ay tis rab day kaylaa N visree-aa N. When the Hawk of God attacks, playful sport is forgotten.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v99	jo min iciq n cyqy sin so gwlI rb kIAW ]99] (1383-5, slok, syK PrId jI) jo man chit na chaytay san so gaalee rab kee-aa N. ||99||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v99	God does what is not expected or even considered. ||99||
DEFINE	para 60159	swFy qRY mx dyhurI clY pwxI AMin ] (1383-5, slok, syK PrId jI) saadhay tarai man dayhuree chalai paanee ann. The body is nourished by water and grain.
RECORD	para 60160	AwieE bMdw dunI ivic viq AwsUxI bMin@ ] (1383-6, slok, syK PrId jI) aa-i-o bandaa dunee vich vat aasoonee baneh. The mortal comes into the world with high hopes.
WHEN	para 60161	mlkl mauq jW AwvsI sB drvwjy BMin ] (1383-6, slok, syK PrId jI) malkal ma-ut jaa N aavsee sabh darvaajay bhann. But when the Messenger of Death comes, it breaks down all the doors.
RECORD	para 60162	iqn@w ipAwirAw BweIAW AgY idqw bMin@ ] (1383-7, slok, syK PrId jI) tin Haa pi-aari-aa bhaa-ee-aaN agai ditaa baneh. It binds and gags the mortal, before the eyes of his beloved brothers.
DEFINE	para 60163	vyKhu bMdw cilAw chu jixAw dY kMin@ ] (1383-7, slok, syK PrId jI) vaykhhu bandaa chali-aa chahu jani-aa dai ka NniH. Behold, the mortal being is going away, carried on the shoulders of four men.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v100	PrIdw Aml ij kIqy dunI ivic drgh Awey kMim ]100] (1383-8, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa amal je keetay dunee vich dargeh aa-ay kamm. ||100||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v100	Fareed, only those good deeds done in the world will be of any use in the Court of the Lord. ||100||
RECORD	para 60165	PrIdw hau bilhwrI iqn@ pMKIAw jMgil ijMn@w vwsu ] (1383-8, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa ha-o balihaaree tin H pankhee-aa jangal jin Haa vaas. Fareed, I am a sacrifice to those birds which live in the jungle.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v101	kkru cugin Qil vsin rb n Cofin pwsu ]101] (1383-9, slok, syK PrId jI) kakar chugan thal vasan rab na chhodan paas. ||101||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v101	They peck at the roots and live on the ground, but they do not leave the Lord's side. ||101||
RECORD	para 60167	PrIdw ruiq iPrI vxu kMibAw pq JVy JiV pwih ] (1383-9, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa rut firee van kambi-aa pat jharhay jharh paahi. Fareed, the seasons change, the woods shake and the leaves drop from the trees.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v102	cwry kuMfw FUMFIAW rhxu ikQwaU nwih ]102] (1383-10, slok, syK PrId jI) chaaray kundaa dhoo Ndhee-aaN rahan kithaa-oo naahi. ||102||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v102	I have searched in the four directions, but I have not found any resting place anywhere. ||102||
RECORD	para 60169	PrIdw pwiV ptolw Dj krI kMblVI pihryau ] (1383-10, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa paarh patolaa Dhaj karee kamblarhee pahiray-o. Fareed, I have torn my clothes to tatters; now I wear only a rough blanket.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v103	ijn@I vysI shu imlY syeI vys kryau ]103] (1383-11, slok, syK PrId jI) jin Hee vaysee saho milai say-ee vays karay-o. ||103||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v103	I wear only those clothes which will lead me to meet my Lord. ||103||
RECORD	para 60171	mÚ 3 ] (1383-11) mehlaa 3. Third Mehl:
RECORD	para 60172	kwie ptolw pwVqI kMblVI pihryie ] (1383-11, slok, mÚ 3) kaa-ay patolaa paarh-tee kamblarhee pahiray-ay. Why do you tear apart your fine clothes, and take to wearing a rough blanket?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v104	nwnk Gr hI bYiTAw shu imlY jy nIAiq rwis kryie ]104] (1383-12, slok, mÚ 3) naanak ghar hee baithi-aa saho milai jay nee-at raas karay-i. ||104||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v104	O Nanak, even sitting in your own home, you can meet the Lord, if your mind is in the right place. ||104||
RECORD	para 60174	mÚ 5 ] (1383-13) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 60175	PrIdw grbu ijn@w vifAweIAw Din jobin Awgwh ] (1383-13, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa garab jin Haa vadi-aa-ee-aa Dhan joban aagaah. Fareed, those who are very proud of their greatness, wealth and youth,
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v105	KwlI cly DxI isau itby ijau mIhwhu ]105] (1383-13, slok, syK PrId jI) khaalee chalay Dhanee si-o tibay ji-o meehahu. ||105||
REQUIRE	cauboly mhlw 5 v105	shall return empty-handed from their Lord, like sandhills after the rain. ||105||
DEFINE	para 60177	PrIdw iqnw muK frwvxy ijnw ivswirEnu nwau ] (1383-14, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa tinaa mukh daraavanay jinaa visaari-on naa-o. Fareed, the faces of those who forget the Lord's Name are dreadful.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v106	AYQY duK GxyirAw AgY Taur n Twau ]106] (1383-14, slok, syK PrId jI) aithai dukh ghanayri-aa agai tha-ur na thaa-o. ||106||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v106	They suffer terrible pain here, and hereafter they find no place of rest or refuge. ||106||
DEFINE	para 60179	PrIdw ipCl rwiq n jwigEih jIvdVo muieEih ] (1383-15, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa pichhal raat na jaagi-ohi jeevad-rho mu-i-ohi. Fareed, if you do not awaken in the early hours before dawn, you are dead while yet alive.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v107	jy qY rbu ivswirAw q rib n ivsirEih ]107] (1383-15, slok, syK PrId jI) jay tai rab visaari-aa ta rab na visari-ohi. ||107||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v107	Although you have forgotten God, God has not forgotten you. ||107||
RECORD	para 60181	mÚ 5 ] (1383-16) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 60182	PrIdw kMqu rMgwvlw vfw vymuhqwju ] (1383-16, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa kant rangvaalaa vadaa vaymuhtaaj. Fareed, my Husband Lord is full of joy; He is Great and Self-sufficient.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v108	Alh syqI riqAw eyhu scwvW swju ]108] (1383-16, slok, syK PrId jI) alah saytee rati-aa ayhu sachaavaa N saaj. ||108||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v108	To be imbued with the Lord God - this is the most beautiful decoration. ||108||
RECORD	para 60184	mÚ 5 ] (1383-17) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 60185	PrIdw duKu suKu ieku kir idl qy lwih ivkwru ] (1383-17, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa dukh sukh ik kar dil tay laahi vikaar. Fareed, look upon pleasure and pain as the same; eradicate corruption from your heart.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v109	Alh BwvY so Blw qW lBI drbwru ]109] (1383-17, slok, syK PrId jI) alah bhaavai so bhalaa taaN labhee darbaar. ||109||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v109	Whatever pleases the Lord God is good; understand this, and you will reach His Court. ||109||
RECORD	para 60187	mÚ 5 ] (1383-18) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 60188	PrIdw dunI vjweI vjdI qUM BI vjih nwil ] (1383-18, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa dunee vajaa-ee vajdee tooN bhee vajeh naal. Fareed, the world dances as it dances, and you dance with it as well.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v110	soeI jIau n vjdw ijsu Alhu krdw swr ]110] (1383-18, slok, syK PrId jI) so-ee jee-o na vajdaa jis alhu kardaa saar. ||110||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v110	That soul alone does not dance with it, who is under the care of the Lord God. ||110||
RECORD	para 60190	mÚ 5 ] (1383-19) mehlaa 5. Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 60191	PrIdw idlu rqw iesu dunI isau dunI n ikqY kMim ] (1383-19, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa dil rataa is dunee si-o dunee na kitai kamm. Fareed, the heart is imbued with this world, but the world is of no use to it at all.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v111	imsl PkIrW gwKVI su pweIAY pUr krMim ]111] (1384-1, slok, syK PrId jI) misal fakeeraa N gaakh-rhee so paa-ee-ai poor karamm. ||111||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v111	It is so difficult to be like the fakeers - the Holy Saints; it is only achieved by perfect karma. ||111||
RECORD	para 60194	pihlY phrY PulVw Plu BI pCw rwiq ] (1384-1, slok, syK PrId jI) pahilai pahrai fulrhaa fal bhee pachhaa raat. The first watch of the night brings flowers, and the later watches of the night bring fruit.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v112	jo jwgMin@ lhMin sy sweI kMno dwiq ]112] (1384-2, slok, syK PrId jI) jo jaaga NniH lahann say saa-ee kanno daat. ||112||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v112	Those who remain awake and aware, receive the gifts from the Lord. ||112||
DEFINE	para 60196	dwqI swihb sMdIAw ikAw clY iqsu nwil ] (1384-2, slok, syK PrId jI) daatee saahib sandee-aa ki-aa chalai tis naal. The gifts are from our Lord and Master; who can force Him to bestow them?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v113	ieik jwgMdy nw lhin@ iekn@w suiqAw dyie auTwil ]113] (1384-2, slok, syK PrId jI) ik jaaganday naa lahni H ikn Haa suti-aa day-ay uthaal. ||113||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v113	Some are awake, and do not receive them, while He awakens others from sleep to bless them. ||113||
REQUIRE	para 60198	FUFydIey suhwg kU qau qin kweI kor ] (1384-3, slok, syK PrId jI) dhoodhaydee-ay suhaag koo ta-o tan kaa-ee kor. You search for your Husband Lord; you must have some fault in your body.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v114	ijn@w nwau suhwgxI iqn@w Jwk n hor ]114] (1384-4, slok, syK PrId jI) jin Haa naa-o suhaaganee tin Haa jhaak na hor. ||114||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v114	Those who are known as happy soul-brides, do not look to others. ||114||
RECORD	para 60200	sbr mMJ kmwx ey sbru kw nIhxo ] (1384-4, slok, syK PrId jI) sabar manjh kamaan ay sabar kaa neehno. Within yourself, make patience the bow, and make patience the bowstring.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v115	sbr sMdw bwxu Kwlku Kqw n krI ]115] (1384-4, slok, syK PrId jI) sabar sandaa baan khaalak khataa na karee. ||115||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v115	Make patience the arrow, the Creator will not let you miss the target. ||115||
DEFINE	para 60202	sbr AMdir swbrI qnu eyvY jwlyin@ ] (1384-5, slok, syK PrId jI) sabar andar saabree tan ayvai jaalayni H. Those who are patient abide in patience; in this way, they burn their bodies.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v116	hoin njIik Kudwie dY Byqu n iksY dyin ]116] (1384-5, slok, syK PrId jI) hon najeek khudaa-ay dai bhayt na kisai dayn. ||116||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v116	They are close to the Lord, but they do not reveal their secret to anyone. ||116||
RECORD	para 60204	sbru eyhu suAwau jy qUM bMdw idVu krih ] (1384-6, slok, syK PrId jI) sabar ayhu su-aa-o jay too N bandaa dirh karahi. Let patience be your purpose in life; implant this within your being.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v117	viD QIvih drIAwau tuit n QIvih vwhVw ]117] (1384-6, slok, syK PrId jI) vaDh theeveh daree-aa-o tut na theeveh vaahrhaa. ||117||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v117	In this way, you will grow into a great river; you will not break off into a tiny stream. ||117||
DEFINE	para 60206	PrIdw drvysI gwKVI copVI prIiq ] (1384-7, slok, syK PrId jI) fareedaa darvaysee gaakh-rhee choprhee pareet. Fareed, it is difficult to be a dervish - a Holy Saint; it is easier to love bread when it is buttered.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v118	iekin iknY cwlIAY drvyswvI rIiq ]118] (1384-7, slok, syK PrId jI) ikan kinai chaalee-ai darvaysaavee reet. ||118||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v118	Only a rare few follow the way of the Saints. ||118||
DEFINE	para 60208	qnu qpY qnUr ijau bwlxu hf blµin@ ] (1384-8, slok, syK PrId jI) tan tapai tanoor ji-o baalan had bala NniH. My body is cooking like an oven; my bones are burning like firewood.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v119	pYrI QkW isir julW jy mUM iprI imlµin@ ]119] (1384-8, slok, syK PrId jI) pairee thakaaN sir julaa N jay moo N piree mila NniH. ||119||
