DEFINE	para 60212	hau FUFydI sjxw sjxu mYfy nwil ] (1384-10, slok, syK PrId jI) ha-o dhoodhaydee sajnaa sajan maiday naal. I search for my Friend, but my Friend is already with me.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v121	nwnk AlKu n lKIAY gurmuiK dyie idKwil ]121] (1384-10, slok, syK PrId jI) naanak alakh na lakhee-ai gurmukh day-ay dikhaal. ||121||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v121	O Nanak, the Unseen Lord cannot be seen; He is revealed only to the Gurmukh. ||121||
RECORD	para 60214	hMsw dyiK qrMidAw bgw AwieAw cwau ] (1384-11, slok, syK PrId jI) hansaa daykh tarandi-aa bagaa aa-i-aa chaa-o. Seeing the swans swimming, the cranes became excited.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v122	fuib muey bg bpuVy isru qil aupir pwau ]122] (1384-11, slok, syK PrId jI) dub mu-ay bag bapurhay sir tal upar paa-o. ||122||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v122	The poor cranes were drowned to death, with their heads below the water and their feet sticking out above. ||122||
RECORD	para 60216	mY jwixAw vf hMsu hY qW mY kIqw sMgu ] (1384-12, slok, syK PrId jI) mai jaani-aa vad hans hai taaN mai keetaa sang. I knew him as a great swan, so I associated with him.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v123	jy jwxw bgu bpuVw jnim n ByVI AMgu ]123] (1384-12, slok, syK PrId jI) jay jaanaa bag bapurhaa janam na bhayrhee ang. ||123||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v123	If I had known that he was a only wretched crane, I would never in my life have crossed paths with him. ||123||
DEFINE	para 60218	ikAw hMsu ikAw bgulw jw kau ndir Dry ] (1384-13, slok, syK PrId jI) ki-aa hans ki-aa bagulaa jaa ka-o nadar Dharay. Who is a swan, and who is a crane, if God blesses him with His Glance of Grace?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v124	jy iqsu BwvY nwnkw kwghu hMsu kry ]124] (1384-13, slok, syK PrId jI) jay tis bhaavai naankaa kaagahu hans karay. ||124||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v124	If it pleases Him, O Nanak, He changes a crow into a swan. ||124||
DEFINE	para 60220	srvr pMKI hykVo PwhIvwl pcws ] (1384-14, slok, syK PrId jI) sarvar pankhee haykrho faaheevaal pachaas. There is only one bird in the lake, but there are fifty trappers.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v125	iehu qnu lhrI gfu iQAw scy qyrI Aws ]125] (1384-14, slok, syK PrId jI) ih tan lahree gad thi-aa sachay tayree aas. ||125||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v125	This body is caught in the waves of desire. O my True Lord, You are my only hope! ||125||
DEFINE	para 60222	kvxu su AKru kvxu guxu kvxu su mxIAw mMqu ] (1384-14, slok, syK PrId jI) kavan so akhar kavan gun kavan so manee-aa mant. What is that word, what is that virtue, and what is that magic mantra?
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v126	kvxu su vyso hau krI ijqu vis AwvY kMqu ]126] (1384-15, slok, syK PrId jI) kavan so vayso ha-o karee jit vas aavai kant. ||126||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v126	What are those clothes, which I can wear to captivate my Husband Lord? ||126||
DEFINE	para 60224	invxu su AKru Kvxu guxu ijhbw mxIAw mMqu ] (1384-15, slok, syK PrId jI) nivan so akhar khavan gun jihbaa manee-aa mant. Humility is the word, forgiveness is the virtue, and sweet speech is the magic mantra.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v127	ey qRY BYxy vys kir qW vis AwvI kMqu ]127] (1384-16, slok, syK PrId jI) ay tarai bhainay vays kar taaN vas aavee kant. ||127||
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v127	Wear these three robes, O sister, and you will captivate your Husband Lord. ||127||
DEFINE	para 60226	miq hodI hoie ieAwxw ] (1384-16, slok, syK PrId jI) mat hodee ho-ay i-aanaa. If you are wise, be simple;
DEFINE	para 60227	qwx hody hoie inqwxw ] (1384-17, slok, syK PrId jI) taan hoday ho-ay nitaanaa. if you are powerful, be weak;
DEFINE	para 60228	Axhody Awpu vMfwey ] (1384-17, slok, syK PrId jI) anhoday aap vandaa-ay. and when there is nothing to share, then share with others.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v128	ko AYsw Bgqu sdwey ]128] (1384-17, slok, syK PrId jI) ko aisaa bhagat sadaa-ay. ||128||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v128	How rare is one who is known as such a devotee. ||128||
RECORD	para 60230	ieku iPkw n gwlwie sBnw mY scw DxI ] (1384-17, slok, syK PrId jI) ik fikaa na gaalaa-ay sabhnaa mai sachaa Dhanee. Do not utter even a single harsh word; your True Lord and Master abides in all.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v129	ihAwau n kYhI Twih mwxk sB Amolvy ]129] (1384-18, slok, syK PrId jI) hi-aa-o na kaihee thaahi maanak sabh amolvay. ||129||
DEFINE	cauboly mhlw 5 v129	Do not break anyone's heart; these are all priceless jewels. ||129||
DEFINE	para 60232	sBnw mn mwixk Twhxu mUil mcWgvw ] (1384-18, slok, syK PrId jI) sabhnaa man maanik thaahan mool machaa Ngvaa. The minds of all are like precious jewels; to harm them is not good at all.
RECORD	cauboly mhlw 5 v130	jy qau iprIAw dI isk ihAwau n Twhy khI dw ]130] (1384-19, slok, syK PrId jI) jay ta-o piree-aa dee sik hi-aa-o na thaahay kahee daa. ||130||
WHEN	cauboly mhlw 5 v130	If you desire your Beloved, then do not break anyone's heart. ||130||
RECORD	para 60235	<> siq nwmu krqw purKu inrBau inrvYru Akwl mUriq AjUnI sYBM gur pRswid ] (1385-1) ik-oNkaar sat naam kartaa purakh nirbha-o nirvair akaal moorat ajoonee saibhaN gur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. Truth Is The Name. Creative Being Personified. No Fear. No Hatred. Image Of The Undying. Beyond Birth. Self-Existent. By Guru's Grace:
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 ] (1385-3)
RECORD	para 60236	sava-yay saree mukhbaak-y mehlaa 5. Swaiyas From The Mouth Of The Great Fifth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 60237	Awid purK krqwr krx kwrx sB Awpy ] (1385-4, svXy, mÚ 5) aad purakh kartaar karan kaaran sabh aapay. O Primal Lord God, You Yourself are the Creator, the Cause of all causes.
DEFINE	para 60238	srb rihE BrpUir sgl Gt rihE ibAwpy ] (1385-4, svXy, mÚ 5) sarab rahi-o bharpoor sagal ghat rahi-o bi-aapay. You are All-pervading everywhere, totally filling all hearts.
RECORD	para 60239	b´wpqu dyKIAY jgiq jwnY kaunu qyrI giq srb kI rK´w krY Awpy hir piq ] (1385-5, svXy, mÚ 5) ba-yaapat daykhee-ai jagat jaanai ka-un tayree gat sarab kee rakh-yaa karai aapay har pat. You are seen pervading the world; who can know Your State? You protect all; You are our Lord and Master.
RECORD	para 60240	AibnwsI Aibgq Awpy Awip auqpiq ] (1385-5, svXy, mÚ 5) abhinaasee abigat aapay aap utpat. O my Imperishable and Formless Lord, You formed Yourself.
DEFINE	para 60241	eykY qUhI eykY An nwhI qum Biq ] (1385-6, svXy, mÚ 5) aykai toohee aykai an naahee tum bhat. You are the One and Only; no one else is like You.
RECORD	para 60242	hir AMqu nwhI pwrwvwru kaunu hY krY bIcwru jgq ipqw hY sRb pRwn ko ADwru ] (1385-6, svXy, mÚ 5) har ant naahee paaraavaar ka-un hai karai beechaar jagat pitaa hai sarab paraan ko aDhaar. O Lord, You have no end or limitation. Who can contemplate You? You are the Father of the world, the Support of all life.
RECORD	para 60243	jnu nwnku Bgqu dir quil bRhm smsir eyk jIh ikAw bKwnY ] (1385-7, svXy, mÚ 5) jan naanak bhagat dar tul barahm samsar ayk jeeh ki-aa bakhaanai. Your devotees are at Your Door, O God - they are just like You. How can servant Nanak describe them with only one tongue?
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v1	hW ik bil bil bil bil sd bilhwir ]1] (1385-8, svXy, mÚ 5) haa N ke bal bal bal bal sad balihaar. ||1||
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v1	I am a sacrifice, a sacrifice, a sacrifice, a sacrifice, forever a sacrifice to them. ||1||
RECORD	para 60245	AMimRq pRvwh sir Aqul BMfwr Bir prY hI qy prY Apr Apwr pir ] (1385-8, svXy, mÚ 5) amrit parvaah sar atul bhandaar bhar parai hee tay parai apar apaar par. Streams of Ambrosial Nectar flow; Your Treasures are unweighable and overflowing in abundance. You are the Farthest of the far, Infinite and Incomparably Beautiful.
RECORD	para 60246	Awpuno Bwvnu kir mMiqR n dUsro Dir Epiq prlO eykY inmK qu Gir ] (1385-9, svXy, mÚ 5) aapuno bhaavan kar mantar na doosro Dhar opat parloua aykai nimakh to ghar. You do whatever You please; You do not take advice from anyone else. In Your Home, creation and destruction happen in an instant.
RECORD	para 60247	Awn nwhI smsir aujIAwro inrmir koit prwCq jwih nwm lIey hir hir ] (1385-10, svXy, mÚ 5) aan naahee samsar ujee-aaro nirmar kot paraachhat jaahi naam lee-ay har har. No one else is equal to You; Your Light is Immaculate and Pure. Millions of sins are washed away, chanting Your Name, Har, Har.
RECORD	para 60248	jnu nwnku Bgqu dir quil bRhm smsir eyk jIh ikAw bKwnY ] (1385-11, svXy, mÚ 5) jan naanak bhagat dar tul barahm samsar ayk jeeh ki-aa bakhaanai. Your devotees are at Your Door, God - they are just like You. How can servant Nanak describe them with only one tongue?
