RECORD	para 61146	audosIA Gry hI vuTI kuiVeˆØI rMnI DMmI ] (1412-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) udosee-a gharay hee vuthee kurhi-eeN rannee Dhammee. Prosperity dwells in his home, with the sounds of girls and women.
RECORD	para 61147	sqI rMnI Gry isAwpw rovin kUVI kMmI ] (1412-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) satee rannee gharay si-aapaa rovan koorhee kammee. All the women of his home shout and cry over useless things.
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v29	jo lyvY so dyvY nwhI Kty dMm shMmI ]29] (1412-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) jo layvai so dayvai naahee khatay damm sahamee. ||29||
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v29	Whatever he takes, he does not give back. Seeking to earn more and more, he is troubled and uneasy. ||29||
RECORD	para 61149	pbr qUM hrIAwvlw kvlw kMcn vMin ] (1412-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) pabar tooN haree-aavlaa kavlaa kanchan vann. O lotus, your leaves were green, and your blossoms were gold.
RECORD	para 61150	kY doKVY siVEih kwlI hoeIAw dyhurI nwnk mY qin BMgu ] (1412-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) kai dokh-rhai sarhi-ohi kaalee ho-ee-aa dayhuree naanak mai tan bhang. What pain has burnt you, and made your body black? O Nanak, my body is battered.
RECORD	para 61151	jwxw pwxI nw lhW jY syqI myrw sMgu ] (1412-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) jaanaa paanee naa lahaa N jai saytee mayraa sang. I have not received that water which I love.
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v30	ijqu ifTY qnu prPuVY cVY cvgix vMnu ]30] (1412-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) jit dithai tan parfurhai charhai chavgan vann. ||30||
UPHOLD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v30	Seeing it, my body blossomed forth, and I was blessed with a deep and beautiful color. ||30||
RECORD	para 61153	rij n koeI jIivAw phuic n cilAw koie ] (1412-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) raj na ko-ee jeevi-aa pahuch na chali-aa ko-ay. No one lives long enough to accomplish all he wishes.
DEFINE	para 61154	igAwnI jIvY sdw sdw surqI hI piq hoie ] (1412-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) gi-aanee jeevai sadaa sadaa surtee hee pat ho-ay. Only the spiritually wise live forever; they are honored for their intuitive awareness.
RECORD	para 61155	srPY srPY sdw sdw eyvY geI ivhwie ] (1412-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) sarfai sarfai sadaa sadaa ayvai ga-ee vihaa-ay. Bit by bit, life passes away, even though the mortal tries to hold it back.
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v31	nwnk iks no AwKIAY ivxu puiCAw hI lY jwie ]31] (1412-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) naanak kis no aakhee-ai vin puchhi-aa hee lai jaa-ay. ||31||
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v31	O Nanak, unto whom should we complain? Death takes one's life away without anyone's consent. ||31||
WHEN	para 61157	dosu n dyAhu rwie no miq clY jW buFw hovY ] (1412-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) dos na day-ahu raa-ay no mat chalai jaa N budhaa hovai. Do not blame the Sovereign Lord; when someone grows old, his intellect leaves him.
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v32	glW kry GxyrIAw qW AMn@y pvxw KwqI tovY ]32] (1412-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) galaa N karay ghanayree-aa taaN ann Hay pavnaa khaatee tovai. ||32||
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v32	The blind man talks and babbles, and then falls into the ditch. ||32||
RECORD	para 61159	pUry kw kIAw sB ikCu pUrw Git viD ikCu nwhI ] (1412-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) pooray kaa kee-aa sabh kichh pooraa ghat vaDh kichh naahee. All that the Perfect Lord does is perfect; there is not too little, or too much.
RECORD	svXy sRI muKbwk´ mhlw 5 v33	nwnk gurmuiK AYsw jwxY pUry mWih smWhI ]33] (1412-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 1) naanak gurmukh aisaa jaanai pooray maa Nhi samaa Nhee. ||33||
