WHEN	para 61170	bRhmx kYlI Gwqu kM\kw AxcwrI kw Dwnu ] (1413-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) barahman kailee ghaat kanjkaa anchaaree kaa Dhaan. If a Brahmin kills a cow or a female infant, and accepts the offerings of an evil person,
UPHOLD	para 61171	iPtk iPtkw koVu bdIAw sdw sdw AiBmwnu ] (1413-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) fitak fitkaa korh badee-aa sadaa sadaa abhimaan. he is cursed with the leprosy of curses and criticism; he is forever and ever filled with egotistical pride.
DEFINE	para 61172	pwih eyqy jwih vIsir nwnkw ieku nwmu ] (1413-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) paahi aytay jaahi veesar naankaa ik naam. One who forgets the Naam, O Nanak, is covered by countless sins.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v4	sB buDI jwlIAih ieku rhY qqu igAwnu ]4] (1413-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sabh buDhee jaalee-ah ik rahai tat gi-aan. ||4||
UPHOLD	slok mhlw 3 v4	Let all wisdom be burnt away, except for the essence of spiritual wisdom. ||4||
RECORD	para 61174	mwQY jo Duir iliKAw su myit n skY koie ] (1413-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) maathai jo Dhur likhi-aa so mayt na sakai ko-ay. No one can erase that primal destiny written upon one's forehead.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v5	nwnk jo iliKAw so vrqdw so bUJY ijs no ndir hoie ]5] (1413-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak jo likhi-aa so varatdaa so boojhai jis no nadar ho-ay. ||5||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v5	O Nanak, whatever is written there, comes to pass. He alone understands, who is blessed by God's Grace. ||5||
RECORD	para 61176	ijnI nwmu ivswirAw kUVY lwlic lig ] (1413-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jinee naam visaari-aa koorhai laalach lag. Those who forget the Naam, the Name of the Lord, and become attached to greed and fraud,
RECORD	para 61177	DMDw mwieAw mohxI AMqir iqsnw Aig ] (1413-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) DhanDhaa maa-i-aa mohnee antar tisnaa ag. are engrossed in the entanglements of Maya the enticer, with the fire of desire within them.
RECORD	para 61178	ijn@w vyil n qUMbVI mwieAw Tgy Tig ] (1413-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jin Haa vayl na toombrhee maa-i-aa thagay thag. Those who, like the pumpkin vine, are too stubborn climb the trellis, are cheated by Maya the cheater.
RECORD	para 61179	mnmuiK bMin@ clweIAih nw imlhI vig sig ] (1413-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh baneh chalaa-ee-ah naa milhee vag sag. The self-willed manmukhs are bound and gagged and led away; the dogs do not join the herd of cows.
RECORD	para 61180	Awip Bulwey BulIAY Awpy myil imlwie ] (1413-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) aap bhulaa-ay bhulee-ai aapay mayl milaa-ay. The Lord Himself misleads the misguided ones, and He Himself unites them in His Union.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v6	nwnk gurmuiK CutIAY jy clY siqgur Bwie ]6] (1413-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh chhutee-ai jay chalai satgur bhaa-ay. ||6||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v6	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are saved; they walk in harmony with the Will of the True Guru. ||6||
RECORD	para 61182	swlwhI swlwhxw BI scw swlwih ] (1413-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) saalaahee salaahnaa bhee sachaa saalaahi. I praise the Praiseworthy Lord, and sing the Praises of the True Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v7	nwnk scw eyku dru bIBw prhir Awih ]7] (1413-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak sachaa ayk dar beebhaa parhar aahi. ||7||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v7	O Nanak, the One Lord alone is True; stay away from all other doors. ||7||
RECORD	para 61184	nwnk jh jh mY iPrau qh qh swcw soie ] (1413-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak jah jah mai fira-o tah tah saachaa so-ay. O Nanak, wherever I go, I find the True Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v8	jh dyKw qh eyku hY gurmuiK prgtu hoie ]8] (1413-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jah daykhaa tah ayk hai gurmukh pargat ho-ay. ||8||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v8	Wherever I look, I see the One Lord. He reveals Himself to the Gurmukh. ||8||
DEFINE	para 61186	dUK ivswrxu sbdu hY jy mMin vswey koie ] (1413-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) dookh visaaran sabad hai jay man vasaa-ay ko-ay. The Word of the Shabad is the Dispeller of sorrow, if one enshrines it in the mind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v9	gur ikrpw qy min vsY krm prwpiq hoie ]9] (1413-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur kirpaa tay man vasai karam paraapat ho-ay. ||9||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v9	By Guru's Grace, it dwells in the mind; by God's Mercy, it is obtained. ||9||
RECORD	para 61188	nwnk hau hau krqy Kip muey KUhix lK AsMK ] (1413-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak ha-o ha-o kartay khap mu-ay khoohan lakh asa Nkh. O Nanak, acting in egotism, countless thousands have wasted away to death.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v10	siqgur imly su aubry swcY sbid AlµK ]10] (1413-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur milay so ubray saachai sabad alankh. ||10||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v10	Those who meet with the True Guru are saved, through the Shabad, the True Word of the Inscrutable Lord. ||10||
RECORD	para 61190	ijnw siqguru iek min syivAw iqn jn lwgau pwie ] (1413-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jinaa satgur ik man sayvi-aa tin jan laaga-o paa-ay. Those who serve the True Guru single-mindedly - I fall at the feet of those humble beings.
RECORD	para 61191	gur sbdI hir min vsY mwieAw kI BuK jwie ] (1413-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur sabdee har man vasai maa-i-aa kee bhukh jaa-ay. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, the Lord abides in the mind, and the hunger for Maya departs.
DEFINE	para 61192	sy jn inrml aUjly ij gurmuiK nwim smwie ] (1413-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) say jan nirmal oojlay je gurmukh naam samaa-ay. Immaculate and pure are those humble beings, who, as Gurmukh, merge in the Naam.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v11	nwnk hoir piqswhIAw kUVIAw nwim rqy pwiqswh ]11] (1413-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak hor patisaahee-aa koorhee-aa naam ratay paatisaah. ||11||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v11	O Nanak, other empires are false; they alone are true emperors, who are imbued with the Naam. ||11||
RECORD	para 61194	ijau purKY Gir BgqI nwir hY Aiq locY BgqI Bwie ] (1413-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ji-o purkhai ghar bhagtee naar hai at lochai bhagtee bhaa-ay. The devoted wife in her husband's home has a great longing to perform loving devotional service to him;
RECORD	para 61195	bhu rs swlxy svwrdI Kt rs mITy pwie ] (1413-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) baho ras saalnay savaardee khat ras meethay paa-ay. she prepares and offers to him all sorts of sweet delicacies and dishes of all flavors.
RECORD	para 61196	iqau bwxI Bgq slwhdy hir nwmY icqu lwie ] (1413-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ti-o banee bhagat salaahday har naamai chit laa-ay. In the same way, the devotees praise the Word of the Guru's Bani, and focus their consciousness on the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 61197	mnu qnu Dnu AwgY rwiKAw isru vyicAw gur AwgY jwie ] (1413-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) man tan Dhan aagai raakhi-aa sir vaychi-aa gur aagai jaa-ay. They place mind, body and wealth in offering before the Guru, and sell their heads to Him.
RECORD	para 61198	BY BgqI Bgq bhu locdy pRB locw pUir imlwie ] (1413-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bhai bhagtee bhagat baho lochday parabh lochaa poor milaa-ay. In the Fear of God, His devotees yearn for His devotional worship; God fulfills their desires, and merges them with Himself.
DEFINE	para 61200	hir pRBu vyprvwhu hY ikqu KwDY iqpqwie ] (1414-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har parabh vayparvaahu hai kit khaaDhai tiptaa-ay. My Lord God is Self-existent and Independent. What does He need to eat to be satisfied?
RECORD	para 61201	siqgur kY BwxY jo clY iqpqwsY hir gux gwie ] (1414-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur kai bhaanai jo chalai tiptaasai har gun gaa-ay. Whoever walks in harmony with the Will of the True Guru, and sings the Glorious Praises of the Lord, is pleasing to Him.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v12	Dnu Dnu kljuig nwnkw ij cly siqgur Bwie ]12] (1414-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) Dhan Dhan kaljug naankaa je chalay satgur bhaa-ay. ||12||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v12	Blessed, blessed are they, in this Dark Age of Kali Yuga, O Nanak, who walk in harmony with the Will of the True Guru. ||12||
RECORD	para 61203	siqgurU n syivE sbdu n riKE aur Dwir ] (1414-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satguroo na sayvi-o sabad na rakhi-o ur Dhaar. Those who do not serve the True Guru, and do not keep the Shabad enshrined in their hearts
DEFINE	para 61204	iDgu iqnw kw jIivAw ikqu Awey sMswir ] (1414-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) Dhig tinaa kaa jeevi-aa kit aa-ay sansaar. - cursed are their lives. Why did they even come into the world?
WHEN	para 61205	gurmqI Bau min pvY qW hir ris lgY ipAwir ] (1414-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmatee bha-o man pavai taaN har ras lagai pi-aar. If one follows the Guru's Teachings, and keeps the Fear of God in his mind, then he is lovingly attuned to the sublime essence of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v13	nwau imlY Duir iliKAw jn nwnk pwir auqwir ]13] (1414-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naa-o milai Dhur likhi-aa jan naanak paar utaar. ||13||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v13	By his primal destiny, he obtains the Name; O Nanak, he is carried across. ||13||
RECORD	para 61207	mwieAw moih jgu BrimAw Gru musY Kbir n hoie ] (1414-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi jag bharmi-aa ghar musai khabar na ho-ay. The world wanders lost in emotional attachment to Maya; it does not realize that its own home is being plundered.
RECORD	para 61208	kwm k®oiD mnu ihir lieAw mnmuK AMDw loie ] (1414-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) kaam kroDh man hir la-i-aa manmukh anDhaa lo-ay. The self-willed manmukh is blind in the world; his mind is lured away by sexual desire and anger.
UPHOLD	para 61209	igAwn KVg pMc dUq sMGwry gurmiq jwgY soie ] (1414-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gi-aan kharhag panch doot sanghaaray gurmat jaagai so-ay. With the sword of spiritual wisdom, kill the five demons. Remain awake and aware to the Guru's Teachings.
DEFINE	para 61210	nwm rqnu prgwisAw mnu qnu inrmlu hoie ] (1414-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naam ratan pargaasi-aa man tan nirmal ho-ay. The Jewel of the Naam is revealed, and the mind and body are purified.
RECORD	para 61211	nwmhIn nkty iPrih ibnu nwvY bih roie ] (1414-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naamheen naktay fireh bin naavai bahi ro-ay. Those who lack the Naam wander around lost, with their noses cut off; without the Name, they sit and cry.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v14	nwnk jo Duir krqY iliKAw su myit n skY koie ]14] (1414-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak jo Dhur kartai likhi-aa so mayt na sakai ko-ay. ||14||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v14	O Nanak, no one can erase that which is pre-ordained by the Creator Lord. ||14||
RECORD	para 61213	gurmuKw hir Dnu KitAw gur kY sbid vIcwir ] (1414-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukhaa har Dhan khati-aa gur kai sabad veechaar. The Gurmukhs earn the wealth of the Lord, contemplating the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
DEFINE	para 61214	nwmu pdwrQu pwieAw Aqut Bry BMfwr ] (1414-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naam padaarath paa-i-aa atut bharay bhandaar. They receive the wealth of the Naam; their treasures are overflowing.
RECORD	para 61215	hir gux bwxI aucrih AMqu n pwrwvwru ] (1414-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har gun banee uchrahi ant na paaraavaar. Through the Word of the Guru's Bani, they utter the Glorious Praises of the Lord, whose end and limitations cannot be found.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v15	nwnk sB kwrx krqw krY vyKY isrjnhwru ]15] (1414-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak sabh kaaran kartaa karai vaykhai sirjanhaar. ||15||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v15	O Nanak, the Creator is the Doer of all; the Creator Lord beholds all. ||15||
RECORD	para 61217	gurmuiK AMqir shju hY mnu ciVAw dsvY Awkwis ] (1414-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukh antar sahj hai man charhi-aa dasvai aakaas. Within the Gurmukh is intuitive peace and poise; his mind ascends to the Tenth Plane of the Akaashic Ethers.
RECORD	para 61218	iqQY aUNG n BuK hY hir AMimRq nwmu suK vwsu ] (1414-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tithai ooNgh na bhukh hai har amrit naam sukh vaas. No one is sleepy or hungry there; they dwell in the peace of the Ambrosial Name of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v16	nwnk duKu suKu ivAwpq nhI ijQY Awqm rwm pRgwsu ]16] (1414-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak dukh sukh vi-aapat nahee jithai aatam raam pargaas. ||16||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v16	O Nanak, pain and pleasure do not afflict anyone, where the Light of the Lord, the Supreme Soul, illuminates. ||16||
RECORD	para 61220	kwm k®oD kw colVw sB gil Awey pwie ] (1414-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) kaam kroDh kaa cholrhaa sabh gal aa-ay paa-ay. All have come, wearing the robes of sexual desire and anger.
ALLOW	para 61221	ieik aupjih ieik ibnis jWih hukmy AwvY jwie ] (1414-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ik upjahi ik binas jaa Nhi hukmay aavai jaa-ay. Some are born, and some pass away. They come and go according to the Hukam of the Lord's Command.
RECORD	para 61222	jMmxu mrxu n cukeI rMgu lgw dUjY Bwie ] (1414-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jaman maran na chuk-ee rang lagaa doojai bhaa-ay. Their comings and goings in reincarnation do not end; they are imbued with the love of duality.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v17	bMDin bMiD BvweIAnu krxw kCU n jwie ]17] (1414-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) banDhan banDh bhavaa-ee-an karnaa kachhoo na jaa-ay. ||17||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v17	Bound in bondage, they are made to wander, and they cannot do anything about it. ||17||
RECORD	para 61224	ijn kau ikrpw DwrIAnu iqnw siqguru imilAw Awie ] (1414-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jin ka-o kirpaa Dhaaree-an tinaa satgur mili-aa aa-ay. Those, upon whom the Lord showers His Mercy, come and meet the True Guru.
RECORD	para 61225	siqguir imly aultI BeI mir jIivAw shij suBwie ] (1414-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur milay ultee bha-ee mar jeevi-aa sahj subhaa-ay. Meeting with the True Guru, they turn away from the world; they remain dead while still alive, with intuitive peace and poise.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v18	nwnk BgqI riqAw hir hir nwim smwie ]18] (1414-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak bhagtee rati-aa har har naam samaa-ay. ||18||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v18	O Nanak, the devotees are imbued with the Lord; they are absorbed in the Name of the Lord. ||18||
DEFINE	para 61227	mnmuK cMcl miq hY AMqir bhuqu cqurweI ] (1414-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh chanchal mat hai antar bahut chaturaa-ee. The intellect of the self-willed manmukh is fickle; he is very tricky and clever within.
RECORD	para 61228	kIqw kriqAw ibrQw gieAw ieku iqlu Qwie n pweI ] (1414-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) keetaa karti-aa birthaa ga-i-aa ik til thaa-ay na paa-ee. Whatever he has done, and all that he does, is useless. Not even an iota of it is acceptable.
UPHOLD	para 61229	puMn dwnu jo bIjdy sB Drm rwie kY jweI ] (1414-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) punn daan jo beejday sabh Dharam raa-ay kai jaa-ee. The charity and generosity he pretends to give will be judged by the Righteous Judge of Dharma.
RECORD	para 61230	ibnu siqgurU jmkwlu n CofeI dUjY Bwie KuAweI ] (1414-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bin satguroo jamkaal na chhod-ee doojai bhaa-ay khu-aa-ee. Without the True Guru, the Messenger of Death does not leave the mortal alone; he is ruined by the love of duality.
RECORD	para 61231	jobnu jWdw ndir n AwveI jru phucY mir jweI ] (1414-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) joban jaa Ndaa nadar na aavee jar pahuchai mar jaa-ee. Youth slips away imperceptibly, old age comes, and then he dies.
RECORD	para 61232	puqu klqu mohu hyqu hY AMiq bylI ko n sKweI ] (1414-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) put kalat moh hayt hai ant baylee ko na sakhaa-ee. The mortal is caught in love and emotional attachment to children and spouse, but none of them will be his helper and support in the end.
RECORD	para 61233	siqguru syvy so suKu pwey nwau vsY min AweI ] (1414-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur sayvay so sukh paa-ay naa-o vasai man aa-ee. Whoever serves the True Guru finds peace; the Name comes to abide in the mind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v19	nwnk sy vfy vfBwgI ij gurmuiK nwim smweI ]19] (1414-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak say vaday vadbhaagee je gurmukh naam samaa-ee. ||19||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v19	O Nanak, great and very fortunate are those who, as Gurmukh, are absorbed in the Naam. ||19||
RECORD	para 61235	mnmuK nwmu n cyqnI ibnu nwvY duK roie ] (1414-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh naam na chaytnee bin naavai dukh ro-ay. The self-willed manmukhs do not even think of the Name; without the Name, they cry in pain.
RECORD	para 61237	Awqmw rwmu n pUjnI dUjY ikau suKu hoie ] (1415-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) aatmaa raam na poojnee doojai ki-o sukh ho-ay. They do not worship the Lord, the Supreme Soul; how can they find peace in duality?
RECORD	para 61238	haumY AMqir mYlu hY sbid n kwFih Doie ] (1415-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ha-umai antar mail hai sabad na kaadheh Dho-ay. They are filled with the filth of egotism; they do not wash it away with the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v20	nwnk ibnu nwvY mYilAw muey jnmu pdwrQu Koie ]20] (1415-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak bin naavai maili-aa mu-ay janam padaarath kho-ay. ||20||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v20	O Nanak, without the Name, they die in their filth; they waste the priceless opportunity of this human life. ||20||
DEFINE	para 61240	mnmuK boly AMDuly iqsu mih AgnI kw vwsu ] (1415-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh bolay anDhulay tis meh agnee kaa vaas. The self-willed manmukhs are deaf and blind; they are filled with the fire of desire.
RECORD	para 61241	bwxI suriq n buJnI sbid n krih pRgwsu ] (1415-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) banee surat na bujhnee sabad na karahi pargaas. They have no intuitive understanding of the Guru's Bani; they are not illumined with the Shabad.
RECORD	para 61242	Enw AwpxI AMdir suiD nhI gur bcin n krih ivswsu ] (1415-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) onaa aapnee andar suDh nahee gur bachan na karahi visaas. They do not know their own inner being, and they have no faith in the Guru's Word.
RECORD	para 61243	igAwnIAw AMdir gur sbdu hY inq hir ilv sdw ivgwsu ] (1415-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gi-aanee-aa andar gur sabad hai nit har liv sadaa vigaas. The Word of the Guru's Shabad is within the being of the spiritually wise ones. They always blossom in His love.
RECORD	para 61244	hir igAwnIAw kI rKdw hau sd bilhwrI qwsu ] (1415-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har gi-aanee-aa kee rakh-daa ha-o sad balihaaree taas. The Lord saves the honor of the spiritually wise ones.I am forever a sacrifice to them.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v21	gurmuiK jo hir syvdy jn nwnku qw kw dwsu ]21] (1415-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukh jo har sayvday jan naanak taa kaa daas. ||21||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v21	Servant Nanak is the slave of those Gurmukhs who serve the Lord. ||21||
RECORD	para 61246	mwieAw BuieAMgmu srpu hY jgu GyirAw ibKu mwie ] (1415-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa bhu-i-angam sarap hai jag ghayri-aa bikh maa-ay. The poisonous snake, the serpent of Maya, has surrounded the world with its coils, O mother!
RECORD	para 61247	ibKu kw mwrxu hir nwmu hY gur gruV sbdu muiK pwie ] (1415-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bikh kaa maaran har naam hai gur garurh sabad mukh paa-ay. The antidote to this poisonous venom is the Name of the Lord; the Guru places the magic spell of the Shabad into the mouth.
DEFINE	para 61248	ijn kau pUrib iliKAw iqn siqguru imilAw Awie ] (1415-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jin ka-o poorab likhi-aa tin satgur mili-aa aa-ay. Those who are blessed with such pre-ordained destiny come and meet the True Guru.
RECORD	para 61249	imil siqgur inrmlu hoieAw ibKu haumY gieAw iblwie ] (1415-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) mil satgur nirmal ho-i-aa bikh ha-umai ga-i-aa bilaa-ay. Meeting with the True Guru, they become immaculate, and the poison of egotism is eradicated.
RECORD	para 61250	gurmuKw ky muK aujly hir drgh soBw pwie ] (1415-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukhaa kay mukh ujlay har dargeh sobhaa paa-ay. Radiant and bright are the faces of the Gurmukhs; they are honored in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v22	jn nwnku sdw kurbwxu iqn jo cwlih siqgur Bwie ]22] (1415-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jan naanak sadaa kurbaan tin jo chaaleh satgur bhaa-ay. ||22||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v22	Servant Nanak is forever a sacrifice to those who walk in harmony with the Will of the True Guru. ||22||
RECORD	para 61252	siqgur purKu inrvYru hY inq ihrdY hir ilv lwie ] (1415-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur purakh nirvair hai nit hirdai har liv laa-ay. The True Guru, the Primal Being, has no hatred or vengeance. His heart is constantly attuned to the Lord.
RECORD	para 61253	inrvYrY nwil vYru rcwiedw ApxY Gir lUkI lwie ] (1415-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) nirvairai naal vair rachaa-idaa apnai ghar lookee laa-ay. Whoever directs hatred against the Guru, who has no hatred at all, only sets his own home on fire.
RECORD	para 61254	AMqir k®oDu AhMkwru hY Anidnu jlY sdw duKu pwie ] (1415-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) antar kroDh aha Nkaar hai an-din jalai sadaa dukh paa-ay. Anger and egotism are within him night and day; he burns, and suffers constant pain.
RECORD	para 61255	kUVu boil boil inq Baukdy ibKu KwDy dUjY Bwie ] (1415-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) koorh bol bol nit bha-ukday bikh khaaDhay doojai bhaa-ay. They babble and tell lies, and keep on barking, eating the poison of the love of duality.
RECORD	para 61256	ibKu mwieAw kwrix Brmdy iPir Gir Gir piq gvwie ] (1415-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bikh maa-i-aa kaaran bharamday fir ghar ghar pat gavaa-ay. For the sake of the poison of Maya, they wander from house to house, and lose their honor.
DEFINE	para 61257	bysuAw kyry pUq ijau ipqw nwmu iqsu jwie ] (1415-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) baysu-aa kayray poot ji-o pitaa naam tis jaa-ay. They are like the son of a prostitute, who does not know the name of his father.
RECORD	para 61258	hir hir nwmu n cyqnI krqY Awip KuAwie ] (1415-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har har naam na chaytnee kartai aap khu-aa-ay. They do not remember the Name of the Lord, Har, Har; the Creator Himself brings them to ruin.
RECORD	para 61259	hir gurmuiK ikrpw DwrIAnu jn ivCuVy Awip imlwie ] (1415-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har gurmukh kirpaa Dhaaree-an jan vichhurhay aap milaa-ay. The Lord showers His Mercy upon the Gurmukhs, and reunites the separated ones with Himself.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v23	jn nwnku iqsu bilhwrxY jo siqgur lwgy pwie ]23] (1415-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jan naanak tis balihaarnai jo satgur laagay paa-ay. ||23||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v23	Servant Nanak is a sacrifice to those who fall at the Feet of the True Guru. ||23||
REQUIRE	para 61261	nwim lgy sy aUbry ibnu nwvY jm puir jWih ] (1415-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naam lagay say oobray bin naavai jam pur jaa Nhi. Those who are attached to the Naam, the Name of the Lord, are saved; without the Name, they must go to the City of Death.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v24	nwnk ibnu nwvY suKu nhI Awie gey pCuqwih ]24] (1415-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak bin naavai sukh nahee aa-ay ga-ay pachhutaahi. ||24||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v24	O Nanak, without the Name, they find no peace; they come and go in reincarnation with regrets. ||24||
WHEN	para 61263	icMqw Dwvq rih gey qW min BieAw Anµdu ] (1415-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) chintaa Dhaavat reh ga-ay taaN man bha-i-aa anand. When anxiety and wanderings come to an end, the mind becomes happy.
RECORD	para 61264	gur pRswdI buJIAY sw Dn suqI inicMd ] (1415-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee bujhee-ai saa Dhan sutee nichind. By Guru's Grace, the soul-bride understands, and then she sleeps without worry.
RECORD	para 61265	ijn kau pUrib iliKAw iqn@w ByitAw gur goivMdu ] (1415-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jin ka-o poorab likhi-aa tin Haa bhayti-aa gur govind. Those who have such pre-ordained destiny meet with the Guru, the Lord of the Universe.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v25	nwnk shjy imil rhy hir pwieAw prmwnµdu ]25] (1415-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak sehjay mil rahay har paa-i-aa parmaanand. ||25||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v25	O Nanak, they merge intuitively into the Lord, the Embodiment of Supreme Bliss. ||25||
RECORD	para 61267	siqguru syvin Awpxw gur sbdI vIcwir ] (1415-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur sayvan aapnaa gur sabdee veechaar. Those who serve their True Guru, who contemplate the Word of the Guru's Shabad,
RECORD	para 61268	siqgur kw Bwxw mMin lYin hir nwmu rKih aur Dwir ] (1415-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur kaa bhaanaa man lain har naam rakheh ur Dhaar. who honor and obey the Will of the True Guru, who keep the Lord's Name enshrined within their hearts,
DEFINE	para 61269	AYQY EQY mMnIAin hir nwim lgy vwpwir ] (1415-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) aithai othai mannee-an har naam lagay vaapaar. are honored, here and hereafter; they are dedicated to the business of the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 61270	gurmuiK sbid is\wpdy iqqu swcY drbwir ] (1415-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukh sabad sinjaapadai tit saachai darbaar. Through the Word of the Shabad, the Gurmukhs gain recognition in that Court of the True Lord.
RECORD	para 61271	scw saudw Krcu scu AMqir iprmu ipAwru ] (1415-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sachaa sa-udaa kharach sach antar piram pi-aar. The True Name is their merchandise, the True Name is their expenditure; the Love of their Beloved fills their inner beings.
RECORD	para 61272	jmkwlu nyiV n AwveI Awip bKsy krqwir ] (1415-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jamkaal nayrh na aavee aap bakhsay kartaar. The Messenger of Death does not even approach them; the Creator Lord Himself forgives them.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v26	nwnk nwm rqy sy DnvMq hYin inrDnu horu sMswru ]26] (1416-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak naam ratay say Dhanvant hain nirDhan hor sansaar. ||26||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v26	O Nanak, they alone are wealthy, who are imbued with the Naam; the rest of the world is poor. ||26||
RECORD	para 61275	jn kI tyk hir nwmu hir ibnu nwvY Tvr n Twau ] (1416-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jan kee tayk har naam har bin naavai thavar na thaa-o. The Lord's Name is the Support of the Lord's humble servants. Without the Lord's Name, the there is no other place, no place of rest.
RECORD	para 61276	gurmqI nwau min vsY shjy shij smwau ] (1416-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmatee naa-o man vasai sehjay sahj samaa-o. Following the Guru's Teachings, the Name abides in the mind, and one is intuitively, automatically absorbed in the Lord.
RECORD	para 61277	vfBwgI nwmu iDAwieAw Aihinis lwgw Bwau ] (1416-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) vadbhaagee naam Dhi-aa-i-aa ahinis laagaa bhaa-o. Those with great good fortune meditate on the Naam; night and day, they embrace love for the Name.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v27	jn nwnku mMgY DUiV iqn hau sd kurbwxY jwau ]27] (1416-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jan naanak mangai Dhoorh tin ha-o sad kurbaanai jaa-o. ||27||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v27	Servant Nanak begs for the dust of their feet; I am forever a sacrifice to them. ||27||
RECORD	para 61279	lK caurwsIh mydnI iqsnw jlqI kry pukwr ] (1416-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) lakh cha-oraaseeh maydnee tisnaa jaltee karay pukaar. The 8.4 million species of beings burn in desire and cry in pain.
FORBID	para 61280	iehu mohu mwieAw sBu psirAw nwil clY n AMqI vwr ] (1416-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ih moh maa-i-aa sabh pasri-aa naal chalai na antee vaar. All this show of emotional attachment to Maya shall not go with you at that very last instant.
RECORD	para 61281	ibnu hir sWiq n AwveI iksu AwgY krI pukwr ] (1416-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bin har saa Nt na aavee kis aagai karee pukaar. Without the Lord, peace and tranquility do not come; unto whom should we go and complain?
RECORD	para 61282	vfBwgI siqguru pwieAw bUiJAw bRhmu ibcwru ] (1416-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) vadbhaagee satgur paa-i-aa boojhi-aa barahm bichaar. By great good fortune, one meets the True Guru, and comes to understand the contemplation of God.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v28	iqsnw Agin sB buiJ geI jn nwnk hir auir Dwir ]28] (1416-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tisnaa agan sabh bujh ga-ee jan naanak har ur Dhaar. ||28||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v28	The fire of desire is totally extinguished, O servant Nanak, enshrining the Lord within the heart. ||28||
DEFINE	para 61284	AsI Kqy bhuqu kmwvdy AMqu n pwrwvwru ] (1416-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) asee khatay bahut kamaavday ant na paaraavaar. I make so many mistakes, there is no end or limit to them.
RECORD	para 61285	hir ikrpw kir kY bKis lYhu hau pwpI vf gunhgwru ] (1416-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har kirpaa kar kai bakhas laihu ha-o paapee vad gunahgaar. O Lord, please be merciful and forgive me; I am a sinner, a great offender.
WHEN	para 61286	hir jIau lyKY vwr n AwveI qUM bKis imlwvxhwru ] (1416-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har jee-o laykhai vaar na aavee tooN bakhas milaavanhaar. O Dear Lord, if You made an account of my mistakes, my turn to be forgiven would not even come. Please forgive me, and unite me with Yourself.
RECORD	para 61287	gur quTY hir pRBu myilAw sB iklivK kit ivkwr ] (1416-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur tuthai har parabh mayli-aa sabh kilvikh kat vikaar. The Guru, in His Pleasure, has united me with the Lord God; He has cut away all my sinful mistakes.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v29	ijnw hir hir nwmu iDAwieAw jn nwnk iqn@ jYkwru ]29] (1416-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jinaa har har naam Dhi-aa-i-aa jan naanak tin H jaikaar. ||29||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v29	Servant Nanak celebrates the victory of those who meditate on the Name of the Lord, Har, Har. ||29||
RECORD	para 61289	ivCuiV ivCuiV jo imly siqgur ky BY Bwie ] (1416-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) vichhurh vichhurh jo milay satgur kay bhai bhaa-ay. Those who have been separated and alienated from the Lord are united with Him again, through the Fear and the Love of the True Guru.
RECORD	para 61290	jnm mrx inhclu Bey gurmuiK nwmu iDAwie ] (1416-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) janam maran nihchal bha-ay gurmukh naam Dhi-aa-ay. They escape the cycle of birth and death, and, as Gurmukh, they meditate on the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	para 61291	gur swDU sMgiq imlY hIry rqn lBMin@ ] (1416-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur saaDhoo sangat milai heeray ratan labhaNniH. Joining the Saadh Sangat, the Guru's Congregation, the diamonds and jewels are obtained.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v30	nwnk lwlu Amolkw gurmuiK Koij lhMin@ ]30] (1416-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak laal amolkaa gurmukh khoj laha NniH. ||30||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v30	O Nanak, the jewel is priceless; the Gurmukhs seek and find it. ||30||
UPHOLD	para 61293	mnmuK nwmu n cyiqE iDgu jIvxu iDgu vwsu ] (1416-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh naam na chayti-o Dhig jeevan Dhig vaas. The self-willed manmukhs do not even think of the Naam. Cursed are their lives, and cursed are their homes.
RECORD	para 61294	ijs dw idqw Kwxw pYnxw so min n visE guxqwsu ] (1416-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jis daa ditaa khaanaa painnaa so man na vasi-o guntaas. That Lord who gives them so much to eat and wear - they do not enshrine that Lord, the Treasure of Virtue, in their minds.
DEFINE	para 61295	iehu mnu sbid n ByidE ikau hovY Gr vwsu ] (1416-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ih man sabad na baydi-o ki-o hovai ghar vaas. This mind is not pierced by the Word of the Shabad; how can it come to dwell in its true home?
RECORD	para 61296	mnmuKIAw dohwgxI Awvx jwix mueIAwsu ] (1416-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukhee-aa duhaaganee aavan jaan mu-ee-aas. The self-willed manmukhs are like discarded brides, ruined by coming and going in the cycle of reincarnation.
RECORD	para 61297	gurmuiK nwmu suhwgu hY msqik mxI iliKAwsu ] (1416-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukh naam suhaag hai mastak manee likhi-aas. The Gurmukhs are embellished and exalted by the Naam, the Name of the Lord; the jewel of destiny is engraved upon their foreheads.
RECORD	para 61298	hir hir nwmu auir DwirAw hir ihrdY kml pRgwsu ] (1416-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har har naam ur Dhaari-aa har hirdai kamal pargaas. They enshrine the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, within their hearts; the Lord illumines their heart-lotus.
RECORD	para 61299	siqguru syvin Awpxw hau sd bilhwrI qwsu ] (1416-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur sayvan aapnaa ha-o sad balihaaree taas. I am forever a sacrifice to those who serve their True Guru.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v31	nwnk iqn muK aujly ijn AMqir nwmu pRgwsu ]31] (1416-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak tin mukh ujlay jin antar naam pargaas. ||31||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v31	O Nanak, radiant and bright are the faces of those whose inner beings are illuminated with the Light of the Naam. ||31||
RECORD	para 61301	sbid mrY soeI jnu isJY ibnu sbdY mukiq n hoeI ] (1416-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sabad marai so-ee jan sijhai bin sabdai mukat na ho-ee. Those who die in the Word of the Shabad are saved. Without the Shabad, no one is liberated.
RECORD	para 61302	ByK krih bhu krm ivguqy Bwie dUjY prj ivgoeI ] (1416-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bhaykh karahi baho karam vigutay bhaa-ay doojai paraj vigo-ee. They wear religious robes and perform all sorts of rituals, but they are ruined; in the love of duality, their world is ruined.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v32	nwnk ibnu siqgur nwau n pweIAY jy sau locY koeI ]32] (1416-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak bin satgur naa-o na paa-ee-ai jay sa-o lochai ko-ee. ||32||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v32	O Nanak, without the True Guru, the Name is not obtained, even though one may long for it hundreds of times. ||32||
DEFINE	para 61304	hir kw nwau Aiq vf aUcw aUcI hU aUcw hoeI ] (1416-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har kaa naa-o at vad oochaa oochee hoo oochaa ho-ee. The Name of the Lord is utterly great, lofty and high, the highest of the high.
ALLOW	para 61305	ApiV koie n skeI jy sau locY koeI ] (1416-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) aparh ko-ay na sak-ee jay sa-o lochai ko-ee. No one can climb up to it, even though one may long for it, hundreds of times.
RECORD	para 61306	muiK sMjm hCw n hoveI kir ByK BvY sB koeI ] (1416-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) mukh sanjam hachhaa na hova-ee kar bhaykh bhavai sabh ko-ee. Speaking about self-discipline, no one become pure; everyone walks around wearing religious robes.
UPHOLD	para 61307	gur kI pauVI jwie cVY krim prwpiq hoeI ] (1416-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur kee pa-orhee jaa-ay charhai karam paraapat ho-ee. Those blessed by the karma of good deeds go and climb the ladder of the Guru.
RECORD	para 61308	AMqir Awie vsY gur sbdu vIcwrY koie ] (1416-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) antar aa-ay vasai gur sabad veechaarai ko-ay. The Lord comes and dwells within that one who contemplates the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v33	nwnk sbid mrY mnu mwnIAY swcy swcI soie ]33] (1417-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak sabad marai man maanee-ai saachay saachee so-ay. ||33||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v33	O Nanak, when someone dies in the Word of the Shabad, the mind is pleased and appeased. True is the reputation of those who are true. ||33||
RECORD	para 61311	mwieAw mohu duKu swgru hY ibKu duqru qirAw n jwie ] (1417-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh dukh saagar hai bikh dutar tari-aa na jaa-ay. Emotional attachment to Maya is a treacherous ocean of pain and poison, which cannot be crossed.
RECORD	para 61312	myrw myrw krdy pic muey haumY krq ivhwie ] (1417-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) mayraa mayraa karday pach mu-ay ha-umai karat vihaa-ay. Screaming, "Mine, mine!", they rot and die; they pass their lives in egotism.
RECORD	para 61313	mnmuKw aurvwru n pwru hY AD ivic rhy lptwie ] (1417-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukhaa urvaar na paar hai aDh vich rahay laptaa-ay. The self-willed manmukhs are in limbo, neither on this side, nor the other; they are stuck in the middle.
DEFINE	para 61314	jo Duir iliKAw su kmwvxw krxw kCU n jwie ] (1417-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jo Dhur likhi-aa so kamaavanaa karnaa kachhoo na jaa-ay. They act as they are pre-destined; they cannot do anything else.
UPHOLD	para 61315	gurmqI igAwnu rqnu min vsY sBu dyiKAw bRhmu suBwie ] (1417-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmatee gi-aan ratan man vasai sabh daykhi-aa barahm subhaa-ay. Following the Guru's Teachings, the jewel of spiritual wisdom abides in the mind, and then God is easily seen in all.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v34	nwnk siqguir boihQY vfBwgI cVY qy Baujil pwir lµGwie ]34] (1417-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak satgur bohithai vadbhaagee charhai tay bha-ojal paar langhaa-ay. ||34||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v34	O Nanak, the very fortunate ones embark on the Boat of the True Guru; they are carried across the terrifying world-ocean. ||34||
RECORD	para 61317	ibnu siqgur dwqw ko nhI jo hir nwmu dyie AwDwru ] (1417-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bin satgur daataa ko nahee jo har naam day-ay aaDhaar. Without the True Guru, there is no giver who can bestow the Support of the Lord's Name.
RECORD	para 61318	gur ikrpw qy nwau min vsY sdw rhY auir Dwir ] (1417-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur kirpaa tay naa-o man vasai sadaa rahai ur Dhaar. By Guru's Grace, the Name comes to dwell in the mind; keep it enshrined in your heart.
RECORD	para 61319	iqsnw buJY iqpiq hoie hir kY nwie ipAwir ] (1417-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tisnaa bujhai tipat ho-ay har kai naa-ay pi-aar. The fire of desire is extinguished, and one finds satisfaction, through the Love of the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v35	nwnk gurmuiK pweIAY hir ApnI ikrpw Dwir ]35] (1417-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh paa-ee-ai har apnee kirpaa Dhaar. ||35||
WHEN	slok mhlw 3 v35	O Nanak, the Gurmukh finds the Lord, when He showers His Mercy. ||35||
DEFINE	para 61321	ibnu sbdY jgqu brilAw khxw kCU n jwie ] (1417-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bin sabdai jagat barli-aa kahnaa kachhoo na jaa-ay. Without the Shabad, the world is so insane, that it cannot even be described.
RECORD	para 61322	hir rKy sy aubry sbid rhy ilv lwie ] (1417-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har rakhay say ubray sabad rahay liv laa-ay. Those who are protected by the Lord are saved; they remain lovingly attuned to the Word of the Shabad.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v36	nwnk krqw sB ikCu jwxdw ijin rKI bxq bxwie ]36] (1417-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak kartaa sabh kichh jaandaa jin rakhee banat banaa-ay. ||36||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v36	O Nanak, the Creator who made this making knows everything. ||36||
RECORD	para 61324	hom jg siB qIrQw piV@ pMifq Qky purwx ] (1417-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) hom jag sabh teerthaa parhH pandit thakay puraan. The Pandits, the religious scholars, have grown weary of making fire-offerings and sacrifices, making pilgrimages to all the sacred shrines, and reading the Puraanas.
RECORD	para 61325	ibKu mwieAw mohu n imteI ivic haumY Awvxu jwxu ] (1417-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bikh maa-i-aa moh na mit-ee vich ha-umai aavan jaan. But they cannot get rid of the poison of emotional attachment to Maya; they continue to come and go in egotism.
RECORD	para 61326	siqgur imilAY mlu auqrI hir jipAw purKu sujwxu ] (1417-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur mili-ai mal utree har japi-aa purakh sujaan. Meeting with the True Guru, one's filth is washed off, meditating on the Lord, the Primal Being, the All-knowing One.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v37	ijnw hir hir pRBu syivAw jn nwnku sd kurbwxu ]37] (1417-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jinaa har har parabh sayvi-aa jan naanak sad kurbaan. ||37||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v37	Servant Nanak is forever a sacrifice to those who serve their Lord God. ||37||
RECORD	para 61328	mwieAw mohu bhu icqvdy bhu Awsw loBu ivkwr ] (1417-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh baho chitvaday baho aasaa lobh vikaar. Mortals give great thought to Maya and emotional attachment; they harbor great hopes, in greed and corruption.
RECORD	para 61329	mnmuiK AsiQru nw QIAY mir ibnis jwie iKn vwr ] (1417-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh asthir naa thee-ai mar binas jaa-ay khin vaar. The self-willed manmukhs do not become steady and stable; they die and are gone in an instant.
UPHOLD	para 61330	vf Bwgu hovY siqguru imlY haumY qjY ivkwr ] (1417-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) vad bhaag hovai satgur milai ha-umai tajai vikaar. Only those who are blessed with great good fortune meet the True Guru, and leave behind their egotism and corruption.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v38	hir nwmw jip suKu pwieAw jn nwnk sbdu vIcwr ]38] (1417-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har naamaa jap sukh paa-i-aa jan naanak sabad veechaar. ||38||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v38	Chanting the Name of the Lord, they find peace; servant Nanak contemplates the Word of the Shabad. ||38||
RECORD	para 61332	ibnu siqgur Bgiq n hoveI nwim n lgY ipAwru ] (1417-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bin satgur bhagat na hova-ee naam na lagai pi-aar. Without the True Guru, there is no devotional worship, and no love of the Naam, the Name of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v39	jn nwnk nwmu ArwiDAw gur kY hyiq ipAwir ]39] (1417-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jan naanak naam araaDhi-aa gur kai hayt pi-aar. ||39||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v39	Servant Nanak worships and adores the Naam, with love and affection for the Guru. ||39||
WHEN	para 61334	loBI kw vyswhu n kIjY jy kw pwir vswie ] (1417-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) lobhee kaa vaysaahu na keejai jay kaa paar vasaa-ay. Do not trust greedy people, if you can avoid doing so.
RECORD	para 61335	AMiq kwil iqQY DuhY ijQY hQu n pwie ] (1417-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ant kaal tithai Dhuhai jithai hath na paa-ay. At the very last moment, they will deceive you there, where no one will be able to lend a helping hand.
RECORD	para 61336	mnmuK syqI sMgu kry muih kwlK dwgu lgwie ] (1417-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh saytee sang karay muhi kaalakh daag lagaa-ay. Whoever associates with the self-willed manmukhs, will have his face blackened and dirtied.
DEFINE	para 61337	muh kwly iqn@ loBIAW jwsin jnmu gvwie ] (1417-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) muh kaalay tin H lobhee-aaN jaasan janam gavaa-ay. Black are the faces of those greedy people; they lose their lives, and leave in disgrace.
ALLOW	para 61338	sqsMgiq hir myil pRB hir nwmu vsY min Awie ] (1417-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satsangat har mayl parabh har naam vasai man aa-ay. O Lord, let me join the Sat Sangat, the True Congregation; may the Name of the Lord God abide in my mind.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v40	jnm mrn kI mlu auqrY jn nwnk hir gun gwie ]40] (1417-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) janam maran kee mal utrai jan naanak har gun gaa-ay. ||40||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v40	The filth and pollution of birth and death is washed away, O servant Nanak, singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord. ||40||
DEFINE	para 61340	Duir hir pRiB krqY iliKAw su mytxw n jwie ] (1417-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) Dhur har parabh kartai likhi-aa so maytnaa na jaa-ay. Whatever is pre-destined by the Lord God Creator, cannot be erased.
DEFINE	para 61341	jIau ipMfu sBu iqs dw pRiqpwil kry hir rwie ] (1417-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jee-o pind sabh tis daa partipaal karay har raa-ay. Body and soul are all His. The Sovereign Lord King cherishes all.
REQUIRE	para 61342	cugl inMdk BuKy ruil muey eynw hQu n ikQwaU pwie ] (1417-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) chugal nindak bhukhay rul mu-ay aynaa hath na kithaa-oo paa-ay. The gossipers and slanderers shall remain hungry and die, rolling in the dust; their hands cannot reach anywhere.
RECORD	para 61343	bwhir pwKMf sB krm krih min ihrdY kptu kmwie ] (1417-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) baahar pakhand sabh karam karahi man hirdai kapat kamaa-ay. Outwardly, they do all the proper deeds, but they are hypocrites; in their minds and hearts, they practice deception and fraud.
REQUIRE	para 61344	Kyiq srIir jo bIjIAY so AMiq KloAw Awie ] (1417-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) khayt sareer jo beejee-ai so ant khalo-aa aa-ay. Whatever is planted in the farm of the body, shall come and stand before them in the end.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v41	nwnk kI pRB bynqI hir BwvY bKis imlwie ]41] (1418-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak kee parabh bayntee har bhaavai bakhas milaa-ay. ||41||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v41	Nanak offers this prayer: O Lord God, please forgive me, and unite me with Yourself. ||41||
RECORD	para 61347	mn Awvx jwxu n suJeI nw suJY drbwru ] (1418-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) man aavan jaan na sujh-ee naa sujhai darbaar. The mortal being does not understand the comings and goings of reincarnation; he does not see the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	para 61348	mwieAw moih plyitAw AMqir AigAwnu gubwru ] (1418-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa mohi palayti-aa antar agi-aan gubaar. He is wrapped up in emotional attachment and Maya, and within his being is the darkness of ignorance.
DEFINE	para 61349	qb nru suqw jwigAw isir fMfu lgw bhu Bwru ] (1418-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tab nar sutaa jaagi-aa sir dand lagaa baho bhaar. The sleeping person wakes, only when he is hit on the head by a heavy club.
RECORD	para 61350	gurmuKW krW aupir hir cyiqAw sy pwiein moK duAwru ] (1418-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukhaa N karaa N upar har chayti-aa say paa-in mokh du-aar. The Gurmukhs dwell upon the Lord; they find the door of salvation.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v42	nwnk Awip Eih auDry sB kutMb qry prvwr ]42] (1418-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak aap ohi uDhray sabh kutamb taray parvaar. ||42||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v42	O Nanak, they themselves are saved, and all their relatives are carried across as well. ||42||
DEFINE	para 61352	sbid mrY so muAw jwpY ] (1418-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sabad marai so mu-aa jaapai. Whoever dies in the Word of the Shabad, is known to be truly dead.
DEFINE	para 61353	gur prswdI hir ris DRwpY ] (1418-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur parsaadee har ras Dharaapai. By Guru's Grace, the mortal is satisfied by the sublime essence of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 61354	hir drgih gur sbid is\wpY ] (1418-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har dargahi gur sabad sinjaapai. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, he is recognized in the Court of the Lord.
DEFINE	para 61355	ibnu sbdY muAw hY sBu koie ] (1418-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bin sabdai mu-aa hai sabh ko-ay. Without the Shabad, everyone is dead.
DEFINE	para 61356	mnmuKu muAw Apunw jnmu Koie ] (1418-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh mu-aa apunaa janam kho-ay. The self-willed manmukh dies; his life is wasted.
REQUIRE	para 61357	hir nwmu n cyqih AMiq duKu roie ] (1418-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har naam na cheeteh ant dukh ro-ay. Those who do not remember the Name of the Lord, shall cry in pain in the end.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v43	nwnk krqw kry su hoie ]43] (1418-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak kartaa karay so ho-ay. ||43||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v43	O Nanak, whatever the Creator Lord does, comes to pass. ||43||
UPHOLD	para 61359	gurmuiK buFy kdy nwhI ijn@w AMqir suriq igAwnu ] (1418-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukh budhay kaday naahee jin Haa antar surat gi-aan. The Gurmukhs never grow old; within them is intuitive understanding and spiritual wisdom.
RECORD	para 61360	sdw sdw hir gux rvih AMqir shj iDAwnu ] (1418-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sadaa sadaa har gun raveh antar sahj Dhi-aan. They chant the Praises of the Lord, forever and ever; deep within, they intuitively meditate on the Lord.
RECORD	para 61361	Eie sdw Anµid ibbyk rhih duiK suiK eyk smwin ] (1418-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) o-ay sadaa anand bibayk raheh dukh sukh ayk samaan. They dwell forever in blissful knowledge of the Lord; they look upon pain and pleasure as one and the same.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v44	iqnw ndrI ieko AwieAw sBu Awqm rwmu pCwnu ]44] (1418-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tinaa nadree iko aa-i-aa sabh aatam raam pachhaan. ||44||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v44	They see the One Lord in all, and realize the Lord, the Supreme Soul of all. ||44||
RECORD	para 61363	mnmuKu bwlku ibriD smwin hY ijn@w AMqir hir suriq nwhI ] (1418-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh baalak biraDh samaan hai jin Haa antar har surat naahee. The self-willed manmukhs are like stupid children; they do not keep the Lord in their thoughts.
REQUIRE	para 61364	ivic haumY krm kmwvdy sB Drm rwie kY jWhI ] (1418-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) vich ha-umai karam kamaavday sabh Dharam raa-ay kai jaa Nhee. They do all their deeds in egotism, and they must answer to the Righteous Judge of Dharma.
RECORD	para 61365	gurmuiK hCy inrmly gur kY sbid suBwie ] (1418-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukh hachhay nirmalay gur kai sabad subhaa-ay. The Gurmukhs are good and immaculately pure; they are embellished and exalted with the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 61366	Enw mYlu pqMgu n lgeI ij clin siqgur Bwie ] (1418-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) onaa mail patang na lag-ee je chalan satgur bhaa-ay. Not even a tiny bit of filth sticks to them; they walk in harmony with the Will of the True Guru.
DEFINE	para 61367	mnmuK jUiT n auqrY jy sau Dovx pwie ] (1418-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh jooth na utrai jay sa-o Dhovan paa-ay. The filth of the manmukhs is not washed away, even if they wash hundreds of times.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v45	nwnk gurmuiK myilAnu gur kY AMik smwie ]45] (1418-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh mayli-an gur kai ank samaa-ay. ||45||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v45	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are united with the Lord; they merge into the Guru's Being. ||45||
RECORD	para 61369	burw kry su kyhw isJY ] (1418-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) buraa karay so kayhaa sijhai. How can someone do bad things, and still live with himself?
RECORD	para 61370	AwpxY roih Awpy hI dJY ] (1418-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) aapnai rohi aapay hee dajhai. By his own anger, he only burns himself.
RECORD	para 61371	mnmuiK kmlw rgVY luJY ] (1418-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh kamlaa ragrhai lujhai. The self-willed manmukh drives himself crazy with worries and stubborn struggles.
RECORD	para 61372	gurmuiK hoie iqsu sB ikCu suJY ] (1418-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukh ho-ay tis sabh kichh sujhai. But those who become Gurmukh understand everything.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v46	nwnk gurmuiK mn isau luJY ]46] (1418-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh man si-o lujhai. ||46||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v46	O Nanak, the Gurmukh struggles with his own mind. ||46||
RECORD	para 61374	ijnw siqguru purKu n syivE sbid n kIqo vIcwru ] (1418-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jinaa satgur purakh na sayvi-o sabad na keeto veechaar. Those who do not serve the True Guru, the Primal Being, and do not reflect upon the Word of the Shabad
DEFINE	para 61375	Eie mwxs jUin n AwKIAin psU For gwvwr ] (1418-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) o-ay maanas joon na aakhee-an pasoo dhor gaavaar. - do not call them human beings; they are just animals and stupid beasts.
UPHOLD	para 61376	Enw AMqir igAwnu n iDAwnu hY hir sau pRIiq n ipAwru ] (1418-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) onaa antar gi-aan na Dhi-aan hai har sa-o pareet na pi-aar. They have no spiritual wisdom or meditation within their beings; they are not in love with the Lord.
RECORD	para 61377	mnmuK muey ivkwr mih mir jMmih vwro vwr ] (1418-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh mu-ay vikaar meh mar jameh vaaro vaar. The self-willed manmukhs die in evil and corruption; they die and are reborn, again and again.
RECORD	para 61378	jIvidAw no imlY su jIvdy hir jgjIvn aur Dwir ] (1418-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jeevdi-aa no milai so jeevday har jagjeevan ur Dhaar. They alone live, who join with the living; enshrine the Lord, the Lord of Life, within your heart.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v47	nwnk gurmuiK sohxy iqqu scY drbwir ]47] (1418-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh sohnay tit sachai darbaar. ||47||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v47	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs look beautiful in that Court of the True Lord. ||47||
RECORD	para 61380	hir mMdru hir swijAw hir vsY ijsu nwil ] (1418-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har mandar har saaji-aa har vasai jis naal. The Lord built the Harimandir, the Temple of the Lord; the Lord dwells within it.
RECORD	para 61381	gurmqI hir pwieAw mwieAw moh prjwil ] (1418-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmatee har paa-i-aa maa-i-aa moh parjaal. Following the Guru's Teachings, I have found the Lord; my emotional attachment to Maya has been burnt away.
RECORD	para 61382	hir mMdir vsqu Anyk hY nv iniD nwmu smwil ] (1418-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har mandar vasat anayk hai nav niDh naam samaal. Countless things are in the Harimandir, the Temple of the Lord; contemplate the Naam, and the nine treasures will be yours.
UPHOLD	para 61383	Dnu BgvMqI nwnkw ijnw gurmuiK lDw hir Bwil ] (1418-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) Dhan bhagvantee naankaa jinaa gurmukh laDhaa har bhaal. Blessed is that happy soul-bride, O Nanak, who, as Gurmukh, seeks and finds the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v48	vfBwgI gV mMdru KoijAw hir ihrdY pwieAw nwil ]48] (1418-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) vadbhaagee garh mandar khoji-aa har hirdai paa-i-aa naal. ||48||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v48	By great good fortune, one searches the temple of the body-fortress, and finds the Lord within the heart. ||48||
RECORD	para 61385	mnmuK dh idis iPir rhy Aiq iqsnw loB ivkwr ] (1418-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) manmukh dah dis fir rahay at tisnaa lobh vikaar. The self-willed manmukhs wander lost in the ten directions, led by intense desire, greed and corruption.
RECORD	para 61387	mwieAw mohu n cukeI mir jMmih vwro vwr ] (1419-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) maa-i-aa moh na chuk-ee mar jameh vaaro vaar. Their attachment to Maya does not cease; they die, only to be reborn, over and over again.
DEFINE	para 61388	siqguru syiv suKu pwieAw Aiq iqsnw qij ivkwr ] (1419-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur sayv sukh paa-i-aa at tisnaa taj vikaar. Serving the True Guru, peace is found; intense desire and corruption are discarded.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v49	jnm mrn kw duKu gieAw jn nwnk sbdu bIcwir ]49] (1419-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) janam maran kaa dukh ga-i-aa jan naanak sabad beechaar. ||49||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v49	The pains of death and birth are taken away; servant Nanak reflects upon the Word of the Shabad. ||49||
REQUIRE	para 61390	hir hir nwmu iDAwie mn hir drgh pwvih mwnu ] (1419-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har har naam Dhi-aa-ay man har dargeh paavahi maan. Meditate on the Name of the Lord, Har, Har, O mortal being, and you shall be honored in the Court of the Lord.
REQUIRE	para 61391	iklivK pwp siB ktIAih haumY cukY gumwnu ] (1419-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) kilvikh paap sabh katee-ah ha-umai chukai gumaan. All your sins and terrible mistakes shall be taken away, and you shall be rid of your pride and egotism.
RECORD	para 61392	gurmuiK kmlu ivgisAw sBu Awqm bRhmu pCwnu ] (1419-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gurmukh kamal vigsi-aa sabh aatam barahm pachhaan. The heart-lotus of the Gurmukh blossoms forth, realizing God, the Soul of all.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v50	hir hir ikrpw Dwir pRB jn nwnk jip hir nwmu ]50] (1419-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har har kirpaa Dhaar parabh jan naanak jap har naam. ||50||
ALLOW	slok mhlw 3 v50	O Lord God, please shower Your Mercy upon servant Nanak, that he may chant the Name of the Lord. ||50||
RECORD	para 61394	DnwsrI DnvMqI jwxIAY BweI jW siqgur kI kwr kmwie ] (1419-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) Dhanaasree Dhanvantee jaanee-ai bhaa-ee jaaN satgur kee kaar kamaa-ay. In Dhanaasaree, the soul-bride is known to be wealthy, O Siblings of Destiny, when she works for the True Guru.
RECORD	para 61395	qnu mnu saupy jIA sau BweI ley hukim iPrwau ] (1419-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tan man sa-upay jee-a sa-o bhaa-ee la-ay hukam firaa-o. She surrenders her body, mind and soul, O Siblings of Destiny, and lives according to the Hukam of His Command.
RECORD	para 61396	jh bYswvih bYsh BweI jh Byjih qh jwau ] (1419-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jah baisaaveh baisah bhaa-ee jah bhayjeh tah jaa-o. I sit where He wishes me to sit, O Siblings of Destiny; wherever He sends me, I go.
RECORD	para 61397	eyvfu Dnu horu ko nhI BweI jyvfu scw nwau ] (1419-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ayvad Dhan hor ko nahee bhaa-ee jayvad sachaa naa-o. There is no other wealth as great, O Siblings of Destiny; such is the greatness of the True Name.
REQUIRE	para 61398	sdw scy ky gux gwvW BweI sdw scy kY sMig rhwau ] (1419-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sadaa sachay kay gun gaavaa N bhaa-ee sadaa sachay kai sang rahaa-o. I sing forever the Glorious Praises of the True Lord; I shall remain with the True One forever.
RECORD	para 61399	pYnxu gux cMigAweIAw BweI AwpxI piq ky swd Awpy Kwie ] (1419-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) painan gun chang-aa-ee-aa bhaa-ee aapnee pat kay saad aapay khaa-ay. So wear the clothes of His Glorious Virtues and goodness, O Siblings of Destiny; eat and enjoy the flavor of your own honor.
UPHOLD	para 61400	iqs kw ikAw swlwhIAY BweI drsn kau bil jwie ] (1419-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tis kaa ki-aa salaahee-ai bhaa-ee darsan ka-o bal jaa-ay. How can I praise Him, O Siblings of Destiny? I am a sacrifice to the Blessed Vision of His Darshan.
WHEN	para 61401	siqgur ivic vfIAw vifAweIAw BweI krim imlY qW pwie ] (1419-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) satgur vich vadee-aa vadi-aa-ee-aa bhaa-ee karam milai taaN paa-ay. Great is the Glorious Greatness of the True Guru, O Siblings of Destiny; if one is blessed with good karma, He is found.
RECORD	para 61402	ieik hukmu mMin n jwxnI BweI dUjY Bwie iPrwie ] (1419-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ik hukam man na jaannee bhaa-ee doojai bhaa-ay firaa-ay. Some do not know how to submit to the Hukam of His Command, O Siblings of Destiny; they wander around lost in the love of duality.
RECORD	para 61403	sMgiq FoeI nw imlY BweI bYsix imlY n Qwau ] (1419-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sangat dho-ee naa milai bhaa-ee baisan milai na thaa-o. They find no place of rest in the Sangat, O Siblings of Destiny; they find no place to sit.
RECORD	para 61404	nwnk hukmu iqnw mnwiesI BweI ijnw Dury kmwieAw nwau ] (1419-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak hukam tinaa manaa-isee bhaa-ee jinaa Dhuray kamaa-i-aa naa-o. Nanak: they alone submit to His Command, O Siblings of Destiny, who are pre- destined to live the Name.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v51	iqn@ ivthu hau vwirAw BweI iqn kau sd bilhwrY jwau ]51] (1419-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tin H vitahu ha-o vaari-aa bhaa-ee tin ka-o sad balihaarai jaa-o. ||51||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v51	I am a sacrifice to them, O Siblings of Destiny, I am forever a sacrifice to them. ||51||
DEFINE	para 61406	sy dwVIAW scIAw ij gur crnI lgMin@ ] (1419-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) say daarhee-aaN sachee-aa je gur charnee laga NniH. Those beards are true, which brush the feet of the True Guru.
RECORD	para 61407	Anidnu syvin guru Awpxw Anidnu Anid rhMin@ ] (1419-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) an-din sayvan gur aapnaa an-din anad raha NniH. Those who serve their Guru night and day, live in bliss, night and day.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v52	nwnk sy muh sohxy scY dir idsMin@ ]52] (1419-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak say muh sohnay sachai dar disaNniH. ||52||
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v52	O Nanak, their faces appear beautiful in the Court of the True Lord. ||52||
RECORD	para 61409	muK scy scu dwVIAw scu bolih scu kmwih ] (1419-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) mukh sachay sach daarhee-aa sach boleh sach kamaahi. True are the faces and true are the beards, of those who speak the Truth and live the Truth.
DEFINE	para 61410	scw sbdu min visAw siqgur mWih smWih ] (1419-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sachaa sabad man vasi-aa satgur maa Nhi samaa Nhi. The True Word of the Shabad abides in their minds; they are absorbed in the True Guru.
DEFINE	para 61411	scI rwsI scu Dnu auqm pdvI pWih ] (1419-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sachee raasee sach Dhan utam padvee paaNhi. True is their capital, and true is their wealth; they are blessed with the ultimate status.
RECORD	para 61412	scu suxih scu mMin lYin scI kwr kmwih ] (1419-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sach suneh sach man lain sachee kaar kamaahi. They hear the Truth, they believe in the Truth; they act and work in the Truth.
DEFINE	para 61413	scI drgh bYsxw scy mwih smwih ] (1419-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sachee dargeh baisnaa sachay maahi samaahi. They are given a place in the Court of the True Lord; they are absorbed in the True Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v53	nwnk ivxu siqgur scu n pweIAY mnmuK BUly jWih ]53] (1419-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak vin satgur sach na paa-ee-ai manmukh bhoolay jaa Nhi. ||53||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v53	O Nanak, without the True Guru, the True Lord is not found. The self-willed manmukhs leave, wandering around lost. ||53||
RECORD	para 61415	bwbIhw ipRau ipRau kry jliniD pRym ipAwir ] (1419-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) baabeehaa pari-o pari-o karay jalniDh paraym pi-aar. The rainbird cries, "Pri-o! Pri-o! Beloved! Beloved!" She is in love with the treasure, the water.
RECORD	para 61416	gur imly sIql jlu pwieAw siB dUK invwrxhwru ] (1419-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) gur milay seetal jal paa-i-aa sabh dookh nivaaranhaar. Meeting with the Guru, the cooling, soothing water is obtained, and all pain is taken away.
RECORD	para 61417	iqs cukY shju aUpjY cukY kUk pukwr ] (1419-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) tis chukai sahj oopjai chukai kook pukaar. My thirst has been quenched, and intuitive peace and poise have welled up; my cries and screams of anguish are past.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v54	nwnk gurmuiK sWiq hoie nwmu rKhu auir Dwir ]54] (1419-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak gurmukh saa Nt ho-ay naam rakhahu ur Dhaar. ||54||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v54	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are peaceful and tranquil; they enshrine the Naam, the Name of the Lord, within their hearts. ||54||
RECORD	para 61419	bwbIhw qUM scu cau scy sau ilv lwie ] (1419-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) baabeehaa too N sach cha-o sachay sa-o liv laa-ay. O rainbird, chirp the True Name, and let yourself be attuned to the True Lord.
REQUIRE	para 61420	boilAw qyrw Qwie pvY gurmuiK hoie Alwie ] (1419-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) boli-aa tayraa thaa-ay pavai gurmukh ho-ay alaa-ay. Your word shall be accepted and approved, if you speak as Gurmukh.
REQUIRE	para 61421	sbdu cIin iqK auqrY mMin lY rjwie ] (1419-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sabad cheen tikh utrai man lai rajaa-ay. Remember the Shabad, and your thirst shall be relieved; surrender to the Will of the Lord.
RECORD	para 61423	cwry kuMfw Joik vrsdw bUMd pvY shij suBwie ] (1420-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) chaaray kundaa jhok varasdaa boond pavai sahj subhaa-ay. The clouds are heavy, hanging low, and the rain is pouring down on all sides; the rain-drop is received, with natural ease.
DEFINE	para 61424	jl hI qy sB aUpjY ibnu jl ipAws n jwie ] (1420-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jal hee tay sabh oopjai bin jal pi-aas na jaa-ay. From water, everything is produced; without water, thirst is not quenched.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v55	nwnk hir jlu ijin pIAw iqsu BUK n lwgY Awie ]55] (1420-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak har jal jin pee-aa tis bhookh na laagai aa-ay. ||55||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 3 v55	O Nanak, whoever drinks in the Water of the Lord, shall never feel hunger again. ||55||
RECORD	para 61426	bwbIhw qUM shij boil scY sbid suBwie ] (1420-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) baabeehaa too N sahj bol sachai sabad subhaa-ay. O rainbird, speak the Shabad, the True Word of God, with natural peace and poise.
DEFINE	para 61427	sBu ikCu qyrY nwil hY siqguir dIAw idKwie ] (1420-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) sabh kichh tayrai naal hai satgur dee-aa dikhaa-ay. Everything is with you; the True Guru will show you this.
REQUIRE	para 61428	Awpu pCwxih pRIqmu imlY vuTw Chbr lwie ] (1420-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) aap pachhaaneh pareetam milai vuthaa chhahbar laa-ay. So understand your own self, and meet your Beloved; His Grace shall rain down in torrents.
RECORD	para 61429	iJim iJim AMimRqu vrsdw iqsnw BuK sB jwie ] (1420-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) jhim jhim amrit varasdaa tisnaa bhukh sabh jaa-ay. Drop by drop, the Ambrosial Nectar rains down softly and gently; thirst and hunger are completely gone.
REQUIRE	para 61430	kUk pukwr n hoveI joqI joiq imlwie ] (1420-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) kook pukaar na hova-ee jotee jot milaa-ay. Your cries and screams of anguish have ceased; your light shall merge into the Light.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v56	nwnk suiK svin@ sohwgxI scY nwim smwie ]56] (1420-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak sukh savni H sohaaganee sachai naam samaa-ay. ||56||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v56	O Nanak, the happy soul-brides sleep in peace; they are absorbed in the True Name. ||56||
RECORD	para 61432	Durhu Ksim ByijAw scY hukim pTwie ] (1420-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) Dharahu khasam bhayji-aa sachai hukam pathaa-ay. The Primal Lord and Master has sent out the True Hukam of His Command.
RECORD	para 61433	ieMdu vrsY dieAw kir gUV@I Chbr lwie ] (1420-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) ind varsai da-i-aa kar goorh Hee chhahbar laa-ay. Indra mercifully sends forth the rain, which falls in torrents.
WHEN	para 61434	bwbIhy qin min suKu hoie jW qqu bUMd muih pwie ] (1420-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) baabeehay tan man sukh ho-ay jaa N tat boond muhi paa-ay. The body and mind of the rainbird are happy. only when the rain-drop falls into its mouth.
DEFINE	para 61435	Anu Dnu bhuqw aupjY DrqI soBw pwie ] (1420-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) an Dhan bahutaa upjai Dhartee sobhaa paa-ay. The corn grows high, wealth increases, and the earth is embellished with beauty.
RECORD	para 61436	Anidnu loku Bgiq kry gur kY sbid smwie ] (1420-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) an-din lok bhagat karay gur kai sabad samaa-ay. Night and day, people worship the Lord with devotion, and are absorbed in the Word of the Guru's Shabad.
RECORD	para 61437	Awpy scw bKis ley kir ikrpw krY rjwie ] (1420-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) aapay sachaa bakhas la-ay kar kirpaa karai rajaa-ay. The True Lord Himself forgives them, and showering them with His Mercy, He leads them to walk in His Will.
RECORD	para 61438	hir gux gwvhu kwmxI scY sbid smwie ] (1420-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) har gun gaavhu kaamnee sachai sabad samaa-ay. O brides, sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and be absorbed in the True Word of His Shabad.
RECORD	para 61439	BY kw shju sIgwru kirhu sic rhhu ilv lwie ] (1420-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) bhai kaa sahj seegaar karihu sach rahhu liv laa-ay. Let the Fear of God be your decoration, and remain lovingly attuned to the True Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 3 v57	nwnk nwmo min vsY hir drgh ley Cfwie ]57] (1420-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) naanak naamo man vasai har dargeh la-ay chhadaa-ay. ||57||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 3 v57	O Nanak, the Naam abides in the mind, and the mortal is saved in the Court of the Lord. ||57||
WHEN	para 61441	bwbIhw sglI DrqI jy iPrih aUif cVih Awkwis ] (1420-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 3) baabeehaa saglee Dhartee jay fireh ood charheh aakaas. The rainbird wanders all over the earth, soaring high through the skies.
