DEFINE	para 61521	ij gurmuiK kry sweI Bgiq hovY ] (1422-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) je gurmukh karay saa-ee bhagat hovai. Whatever the Gurmukh does, is devotional worship.
RECORD	para 61522	gurmuiK hovY su kry vIcwru ] (1422-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gurmukh hovai so karay veechaar. Whoever becomes Gurmukh contemplates the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v14	gurmuiK nwnk pwvY pwru ]14] (1422-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gurmukh naanak paavai paar. ||14||
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v14	The Gurmukh, O Nanak, crosses over to the other shore. ||14||
RECORD	para 61524	ijnw AMdir nwmu inDwnu hY gurbwxI vIcwir ] (1422-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) jinaa andar naam niDhaan hai gurbaanee veechaar. Those who have the Naam within, contemplate the Word of the Guru's Bani.
DEFINE	para 61525	iqn ky muK sd aujly iqqu scY drbwir ] (1422-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) tin kay mukh sad ujlay tit sachai darbaar. Their faces are always radiant in the Court of the True Lord.
RECORD	para 61526	iqn bhidAw auTidAw kdy n ivsrY ij Awip bKsy krqwir ] (1422-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) tin bahdi-aa uth-di-aa kaday na visrai je aap bakhsay kartaar. Sitting down and standing up, they never forget the Creator, who forgives them.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v15	nwnk gurmuiK imly n ivCuVih ij myly isrjxhwir ]15] (1422-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak gurmukh milay na vichhurheh je maylay sirjanhaar. ||15||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 4 v15	O Nanak, the Gurmukhs are united with the Lord. Those united by the Creator Lord, shall never be separated again. ||15||
RECORD	para 61528	gur pIrW kI cwkrI mhW krVI suK swru ] (1422-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gur peeraa N kee chaakree mahaaN karrhee sukh saar. To work for the Guru, or a spiritual teacher, is terribly difficult, but it brings the most excellent peace.
RECORD	para 61529	ndir kry ijsu AwpxI iqsu lwey hyq ipAwru ] (1422-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) nadar karay jis aapnee tis laa-ay hayt pi-aar. The Lord casts His Glance of Grace, and inspires love and affection.
RECORD	para 61530	siqgur kI syvY ligAw Baujlu qrY sMswru ] (1422-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) satgur kee sayvai lagi-aa bha-ojal tarai sansaar. Joined to the service of the True Guru, the mortal being crosses over the terrifying world-ocean.
RECORD	para 61531	mn icMidAw Plu pwiesI AMqir ibbyk bIcwru ] (1422-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) man chindi-aa fal paa-isee antar bibayk beechaar. The fruits of the mind's desires are obtained, with clear contemplation and discriminating understanding within.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v16	nwnk siqguir imilAY pRBu pweIAY sBu dUK invwrxhwru ]16] (1422-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak satgur mili-ai parabh paa-ee-ai sabh dookh nivaaranhaar. ||16||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 4 v16	O Nanak, meeting the True Guru, God is found; He is the Eradicator of all sorrow. ||16||
ALLOW	para 61533	mnmuK syvw jo kry dUjY Bwie icqu lwie ] (1422-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) manmukh sayvaa jo karay doojai bhaa-ay chit laa-ay. The self-willed manmukh may perform service, but his consciousness is attached to the love of duality.
RECORD	para 61534	puqu klqu kutMbu hY mwieAw mohu vDwie ] (1422-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) put kalat kutamb hai maa-i-aa moh vaDhaa-ay. Through Maya, his emotional attachment to children, spouse and relatives increases.
REQUIRE	para 61535	drgih lyKw mMgIAY koeI AMiq n skI Cfwie ] (1422-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) dargahi laykhaa mangee-ai ko-ee ant na sakee chhadaa-ay. He shall be called to account in the Court of the Lord, and in the end, no one will be able to save him.
DEFINE	para 61537	ibnu nwvY sBu duKu hY duKdweI moh mwie ] (1423-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) bin naavai sabh dukh hai dukh-daa-ee moh maa-ay. Without the Lord's Name, all is pain. Attachment to Maya is agonizingly painful.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v17	nwnk gurmuiK ndrI AwieAw moh mwieAw ivCuiV sB jwie ]17] (1423-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak gurmukh nadree aa-i-aa moh maa-i-aa vichhurh sabh jaa-ay. ||17||
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v17	O Nanak, the Gurmukh comes to see, that attachment to Maya separates all from the Lord. ||17||
ALLOW	para 61539	gurmuiK hukmu mMny sh kyrw hukmy hI suKu pwey ] (1423-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gurmukh hukam mannay sah kayraa hukmay hee sukh paa-ay. The Gurmukh obeys the Order of her Husband Lord God; through the Hukam of His Command, she finds peace.
ALLOW	para 61540	hukmo syvy hukmu ArwDy hukmy smY smwey ] (1423-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) hukmo sayvay hukam araaDhay hukmay samai samaa-ay. In His Will, she serves; in His Will, she worship and adores Him.
RECORD	para 61541	hukmu vrqu nymu suc sMjmu mn icMidAw Plu pwey ] (1423-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) hukam varat naym such sanjam man chindi-aa fal paa-ay. In His Will, she merges in absorption. His Will is her fast, vow, purity and self- discipline; through it, she obtains the fruits of her mind's desires.
RECORD	para 61542	sdw suhwgix ij hukmY buJY siqguru syvY ilv lwey ] (1423-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) sadaa suhaagan je hukmai bujhai satgur sayvai liv laa-ay. She is always and forever the happy, pure soul-bride, who realizes His Will; she serves the True Guru, inspired by loving absorption.
ALLOW	slok mhlw 4 v18	nwnk ik®pw kry ijn aUpir iqnw hukmy ley imlwey ]18] (1423-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak kirpaa karay jin oopar tinaa hukmay la-ay milaa-ay. ||18||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 4 v18	O Nanak, those upon whom the Lord showers His Mercy, are merged and immersed in His Will. ||18||
RECORD	para 61544	mnmuiK hukmu n buJy bpuVI inq haumY krm kmwie ] (1423-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) manmukh hukam na bujhay bapurhee nit ha-umai karam kamaa-ay. The wretched, self-willed manmukhs do not realize His Will; they continually act in ego.
WHEN	para 61545	vrq nymu suc sMjmu pUjw pwKMif Brmu n jwie ] (1423-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) varat naym such sanjam poojaa pakhand bharam na jaa-ay. By ritualistic fasts, vows, purities, self-disciplines and worship ceremonies, they still cannot get rid of their hypocrisy and doubt.
RECORD	para 61546	AMqrhu kusuDu mwieAw moih byDy ijau hsqI Cwru aufwey ] (1423-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) antrahu kusuDh maa-i-aa mohi bayDhay ji-o hastee chhaar udaa-ay. Inwardly, they are impure, pierced through by attachment to Maya; they are like elephants, who throw dirt all over themselves right after their bath.
RECORD	para 61547	ijin aupwey iqsY n cyqih ibnu cyqy ikau suKu pwey ] (1423-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) jin upaa-ay tisai na cheeteh bin chaytay ki-o sukh paa-ay. They do not even think of the One who created them. Without thinking of Him, they cannot find peace.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v19	nwnk prpMcu kIAw Duir krqY pUrib iliKAw kmwey ]19] (1423-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak parpanch kee-aa Dhur kartai poorab likhi-aa kamaa-ay. ||19||
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v19	O Nanak, the Primal Creator has made the drama of the Universe; all act as they are pre-ordained. ||19||
RECORD	para 61549	gurmuiK prqIiq BeI mnu mwinAw Anidnu syvw krq smwie ] (1423-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gurmukh parteet bha-ee man maani-aa an-din sayvaa karat samaa-ay. The Gurmukh has faith; his mind is contented and satisfied. Night and day, he serves the Lord, absorbed in Him.
UPHOLD	para 61550	AMqir siqguru gurU sB pUjy siqgur kw drsu dyKY sB Awie ] (1423-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) antar satgur guroo sabh poojay satgur kaa daras daykhai sabh aa-ay. The Guru, the True Guru, is within; all worship and adore Him. Everyone comes to see the Blessed Vision of His Darshan.
RECORD	para 61551	mMnIAY siqgur prm bIcwrI ijqu imilAY iqsnw BuK sB jwie ] (1423-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) mannee-ai satgur param beechaaree jit mili-ai tisnaa bhukh sabh jaa-ay. So believe in the True Guru, the supreme sublime Contemplator. Meeting with Him, hunger and thirst are completely relieved.
RECORD	para 61552	hau sdw sdw bilhwrI gur Apuny jo pRBu scw dyie imlwie ] (1423-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) ha-o sadaa sadaa balihaaree gur apunay jo parabh sachaa day-ay milaa-ay. I am forever a sacrifice to my Guru, who leads me to meet the True Lord God.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v20	nwnk krmu pwieAw iqn scw jo gur crxI lgy Awie ]20] (1423-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak karam paa-i-aa tin sachaa jo gur charnee lagay aa-ay. ||20||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 4 v20	O Nanak, those who come and fall at the Feet of the Guru are blessed with the karma of Truth. ||20||
DEFINE	para 61554	ijn iprIAw sau nyhu sy sjx mY nwil ] (1423-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) jin piree-aa sa-o nayhu say sajan mai naal. That Beloved, with whom I am in love, that Friend of mine is with me.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v21	AMqir bwhir hau iPrW BI ihrdY rKw smwil ]21] (1423-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) antar baahar ha-o firaa N bhee hirdai rakhaa samaal. ||21||
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v21	I wander around inside and outside, but I always keep Him enshrined within my heart. ||21||
RECORD	para 61556	ijnw iek min iek iciq iDAwieAw siqgur sau icqu lwie ] (1423-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) jinaa ik man ik chit Dhi-aa-i-aa satgur sa-o chit laa-ay. Those who meditate on the Lord single-mindedly, with one-pointed concentration, link their consciousness to the True Guru.
RECORD	para 61557	iqn kI duK BuK haumY vfw rogu gieAw inrdoK Bey ilv lwie ] (1423-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) tin kee dukh bhukh ha-umai vadaa rog ga-i-aa nirdokh bha-ay liv laa-ay. They are rid of pain, hunger, and the great illness of egotism; lovingly attuned to the Lord, they become free of pain.
RECORD	para 61558	gux gwvih gux aucrih gux mih svY smwie ] (1423-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gun gaavahi gun uchrahi gun meh savai samaa-ay. They sing His Praises, and chant His Praises; in His Glorious Praises, they sleep in absorption.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v22	nwnk gur pUry qy pwieAw shij imilAw pRBu Awie ]22] (1423-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak gur pooray tay paa-i-aa sahj mili-aa parabh aa-ay. ||22||
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v22	O Nanak, through the Perfect Guru, they come to meet God with intuitive peace and poise. ||22||
RECORD	para 61560	mnmuiK mwieAw mohu hY nwim n lgY ipAwru ] (1423-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) manmukh maa-i-aa moh hai naam na lagai pi-aar. The self-willed manmukhs are emotionally attached to Maya; they are not in love with the Naam.
RECORD	para 61561	kUVu kmwvY kUVu sMGrY kUiV krY Awhwru ] (1423-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) koorh kamaavai koorh sanghrai koorh karai aahaar. They practice falsehood, gather falsehood, and eat the food of falsehood.
RECORD	para 61562	ibKu mwieAw Dnu sMic mrih AMiq hoie sBu Cwru ] (1423-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) bikh maa-i-aa Dhan sanch mareh ant ho-ay sabh chhaar. Gathering the poisonous wealth and property of Maya, they die; in the end, they are all reduced to ashes.
RECORD	para 61563	krm Drm suic sMjmu krih AMqir loBu ivkwr ] (1423-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) karam Dharam such sanjam karahi antar lobh vikaar. They perform religious rituals of purity and self-discipline, but they are filled with greed, evil and corruption.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v23	nwnk mnmuiK ij kmwvY su Qwie n pvY drgh hoie KuAwru ]23] (1423-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak manmukh je kamaavai so thaa-ay na pavai dargeh ho-ay khu-aar. ||23||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 4 v23	O Nanak, the actions of the self-willed manmukhs are not accepted; in the Court of the Lord, they are miserable. ||23||
RECORD	para 61565	sBnw rwgW ivic so Blw BweI ijqu visAw min Awie ] (1423-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) sabhnaa raagaa N vich so bhalaa bhaa-ee jit vasi-aa man aa-ay. Among all Ragas, that one is sublime, O Siblings of Destiny, by which the Lord comes to abide in the mind.
RECORD	para 61566	rwgu nwdu sBu scu hY kImiq khI n jwie ] (1423-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) raag naad sabh sach hai keemat kahee na jaa-ay. Those Ragas which are in the Sound-current of the Naad are totally true; their value cannot be expressed.
RECORD	para 61567	rwgY nwdY bwhrw ienI hukmu n bUiJAw jwie ] (1423-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) raagai naadai baahraa inee hukam na boojhi-aa jaa-ay. Those Ragas which are not in the Sound-current of the Naad - by these, the Lord's Will cannot be understood.
RECORD	para 61568	nwnk hukmY bUJY iqnw rwis hoie siqgur qy soJI pwie ] (1423-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak hukmai boojhai tinaa raas ho-ay satgur tay sojhee paa-ay. O Nanak, they alone are right, who understand the Will of the True Guru.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v24	sBu ikCu iqs qy hoieAw ijau iqsY dI rjwie ]24] (1423-19, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) sabh kichh tis tay ho-i-aa ji-o tisai dee rajaa-ay. ||24||
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v24	Everything happens as He wills. ||24||
DEFINE	para 61571	siqgur ivic AMimRq nwmu hY AMimRqu khY khwie ] (1424-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) satgur vich amrit naam hai amrit kahai kahaa-ay. The Ambrosial Nectar of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, is within the True Guru.
RECORD	para 61572	gurmqI nwmu inrmluo inrml nwmu iDAwie ] (1424-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gurmatee naam nirmalo nirmal naam Dhi-aa-ay. Following the Guru's Teachings, one meditates on the Immaculate Naam, the Pure and Holy Naam.
RECORD	para 61573	AMimRq bwxI qqu hY gurmuiK vsY min Awie ] (1424-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) amrit banee tat hai gurmukh vasai man aa-ay. The Ambrosial Word of His Bani is the true essence. It comes to abide in the mind of the Gurmukh.
RECORD	para 61574	ihrdY kmlu prgwisAw joqI joiq imlwie ] (1424-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) hirdai kamal pargaasi-aa jotee jot milaa-ay. The heart-lotus blossoms forth, and one's light merges in the Light.
RECORD	para 61575	nwnk siqguru iqn kau myilEnu ijn Duir msqik Bwgu ilKwie ]25] (1424-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v25	4) naanak satgur tin ka-o mayli-on jin Dhur mastak bhaag likhaa-ay. ||25||
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v25	O Nanak, they alone meet with the True Guru, who have such pre-ordained destiny inscribed upon their foreheads. ||25||
DEFINE	para 61577	AMdir iqsnw Aig hY mnmuK BuK n jwie ] (1424-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) andar tisnaa ag hai manmukh bhukh na jaa-ay. Within the self-willed manmukhs is the fire of desire; their hunger does not depart.
RECORD	para 61578	mohu kutMbu sBu kUVu hY kUiV rihAw lptwie ] (1424-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) moh kutamb sabh koorh hai koorh rahi-aa laptaa-ay. Emotional attachments to relatives are totally false; they remain engrossed in falsehood.
DEFINE	para 61579	Anidnu icMqw icMqvY icMqw bDw jwie ] (1424-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) an-din chintaa chintvai chintaa baDhaa jaa-ay. Night and day, they are troubled by anxiety; bound to anxiety, they depart.
RECORD	para 61580	jMmxu mrxu n cukeI haumY krm kmwie ] (1424-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) jaman maran na chuk-ee ha-umai karam kamaa-ay. Their comings and goings in reincarnation never end; they do their deeds in egotism.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v26	gur srxweI aubrY nwnk ley Cfwie ]26] (1424-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gur sarnaa-ee ubrai naanak la-ay chhadaa-ay. ||26||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 4 v26	But in the Guru's Sanctuary, they are saved, O Nanak, and set free. ||26||
RECORD	para 61582	siqgur purKu hir iDAwiedw sqsMgiq siqgur Bwie ] (1424-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) satgur purakh har Dhi-aa-idaa satsangat satgur bhaa-ay. The True Guru meditates on the Lord, the Primal Being. The Sat Sangat, the True Congregation, loves the True Guru.
RECORD	para 61583	sqsMgiq siqgur syvdy hir myly guru mylwie ] (1424-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) satsangat satgur sayvday har maylay gur maylaa-ay. Those who join the Sat Sangat, and serve the True Guru - the Guru unites them in the Lord's Union.
RECORD	para 61584	eyhu Baujlu jgqu sMswru hY guru boihQu nwim qrwie ] (1424-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) ayhu bha-ojal jagat sansaar hai gur bohith naam taraa-ay. This world, this universe, is a terrifying ocean. On the Boat of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, the Guru carries us across.
RECORD	para 61585	gurisKI Bwxw mMinAw guru pUrw pwir lµGwie ] (1424-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gursikhee bhaanaa mani-aa gur pooraa paar langhaa-ay. The Sikhs of the Guru accept and obey the Lord's Will; the Perfect Guru carries them across.
RECORD	para 61586	gurisKW kI hir DUiV dyih hm pwpI BI giq pWih ] (1424-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gursikhaa N kee har Dhoorh deh ham paapee bhee gat paa Nhi. O Lord, please bless me with the dust of the feet of the Guru's Sikhs. I am a sinner - please save me.
RECORD	para 61587	Duir msqik hir pRB iliKAw gur nwnk imilAw Awie ] (1424-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) Dhur mastak har parabh likhi-aa gur naanak mili-aa aa-ay. Those who have such pre-ordained destiny written upon their foreheads by the Lord God, come to meet Guru Nanak.
RECORD	para 61588	jmkMkr mwir ibdwirAnu hir drgh ley Cfwie ] (1424-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) jamkankar maar bidaari-an har dargeh la-ay chhadaa-ay. The Messenger of Death is beaten and driven away; we are saved in the Court of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v27	gurisKw no swbwis hY hir quTw myil imlwie ]27] (1424-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gursikhaa no saabaas hai har tuthaa mayl milaa-ay. ||27||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 4 v27	Blessed and celebrated are the Sikhs of the Guru; in His Pleasure, the Lord unites them in His Union. ||27||
RECORD	para 61590	guir pUrY hir nwmu idVwieAw ijin ivchu Brmu cukwieAw ] (1424-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gur poorai har naam dirhaa-i-aa jin vichahu bharam chukaa-i-aa. The Perfect Guru has implanted the Lord's Name within me; it has dispelled my doubts from within.
RECORD	para 61591	rwm nwmu hir kIriq gwie kir cwnxu mgu dyKwieAw ] (1424-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) raam naam har keerat gaa-ay kar chaanan mag daykhaa-i-aa. Singing the Kirtan of the Praises of the Lord's Name, the Lord's path is illuminated and shown to His Sikhs.
RECORD	para 61592	haumY mwir eyk ilv lwgI AMqir nwmu vswieAw ] (1424-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) ha-umai maar ayk liv laagee antar naam vasaa-i-aa. Conquering my egotism, I remain lovingly attuned to the One Lord; the Naam, the Name of the Lord, dwells within me.
RECORD	para 61593	gurmqI jmu joih n skY scY nwie smwieAw ] (1424-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gurmatee jam johi na sakai sachai naa-ay samaa-i-aa. I follow the Guru's Teachings, and so the Messenger of Death cannot even see me; I am immersed in the True Name.
RECORD	para 61594	sBu Awpy Awip vrqY krqw jo BwvY so nwie lwieAw ] (1424-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) sabh aapay aap vartai kartaa jo bhaavai so naa-ay laa-i-aa. The Creator Himself is All-pervading; as He pleases, He links us to His Name.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v28	jn nwnku nwau ley qW jIvY ibnu nwvY iKnu mir jwieAw ]28] (1424-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) jan naanak naa-o la-ay taa N jeevai bin naavai khin mar jaa-i-aa. ||28||
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v28	Servant Nanak lives, chanting the Name. Without the Name, he dies in an instant. ||28||
RECORD	para 61596	mn AMqir haumY rogu BRim BUly haumY swkq durjnw ] (1424-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) man antar ha-umai rog bharam bhoolay ha-umai saakat durjanaa. Within the minds of the faithless cynics is the disease of egotism; these evil people wander around lost, deluded by doubt.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v29	nwnk rogu gvwie imil siqgur swDU sjxw ]29] (1424-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) naanak rog gavaa-ay mil satgur saaDhoo sajnaa. ||29||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 4 v29	O Nanak, this disease is eradicated only by meeting with the True Guru, the Holy Friend. ||29||
RECORD	para 61598	gurmqI hir hir boly ] (1424-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gurmatee har har bolay. Following the Guru's Teachings, chant the Name of the Lord, Har, Har.
RECORD	para 61599	hir pRyim ksweI idnsu rwiq hir rqI hir rMig coly ] (1424-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) har paraym kasaa-ee dinas raat har ratee har rang cholay. Attracted by the Lord's Love, day and night, the body-robe is imbued with the Lord's Love.
RECORD	para 61600	hir jYsw purKu n lBeI sBu dyiKAw jgqu mY toly ] (1424-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) har jaisaa purakh na labh-ee sabh daykhi-aa jagat mai tolay. I have not found any being like the Lord, although I have searched and looked all over the world.
RECORD	para 61601	gur siqguir nwmu idVwieAw mnu Anq n kwhU foly ] (1424-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) gur satgur naam dirhaa-i-aa man anat na kaahoo dolay. The Guru, the True Guru, has implanted the Naam within; now, my mind does not waver or wander anywhere else.
RECORD	slok mhlw 4 v30	jn nwnku hir kw dwsu hY gur siqgur ky gul goly ]30] (1424-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 4) jan naanak har kaa daas hai gur satgur kay gul golay. ||30||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 4 v30	Servant Nanak is the slave of the Lord, the slave of the slaves of the Guru, the True Guru. ||30||
RECORD	para 61604	salok mehlaa 5 Shalok, Fifth Mehl:
RECORD	para 61605	<> siqgur pRswid ] (1425-1) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	para 61606	rqy syeI ij muKu n moVMin@ ijn@I is\wqw sweI ] (1425-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) ratay say-ee je mukh na morhaNniH jin Hee sinjaataa saa-ee. They alone are imbued with the Lord, who do not turn their faces away from Him - they realize Him.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v1	JiV JiV pvdy kcy ibrhI ijn@w kwir n AweI ]1] (1425-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jharh jharh pavday kachay birhee jin Haa kaar na aa-ee. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v1	The false, immature lovers do not know the way of love, and so they fall. ||1||
RECORD	para 61608	DxI ivhUxw pwt ptMbr BwhI syqI jwly ] (1425-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) Dhanee vihoonaa paat patambar bhaahee saytee jaalay. Without my Master, I will burn my silk and satin clothes in the fire.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v2	DUVI ivic lufMdVI sohW nwnk qY sh nwly ]2] (1425-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) Dhoorhee vich ludand-rhee sohaaN naanak tai sah naalay. ||2||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v2	Even rolling in the dust, I look beautiful, O Nanak, if my Husband Lord is with me. ||2||
RECORD	para 61610	gur kY sbid ArwDIAY nwim rMig bYrwgu ] (1425-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) gur kai sabad araaDhee-ai naam rang bairaag. Through the Word of the Guru's Shabad, I worship and adore the Naam, with love and balanced detachment.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v3	jIqy pMc bYrweIAw nwnk sPl mwrU iehu rwgu ]3] (1425-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jeetay panch bairaa-ee-aa naanak safal maaroo ih raag. ||3||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v3	When the five enemies are overcome, O Nanak, this musical measure of Raga Maaroo becomes frtuiful. ||3||
WHEN	para 61612	jW mUM ieku q lK qau ijqI ipnxy dir ikqVy ] (1425-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jaa N moo N ik ta lakh ta-o jitee pinnay dar kit-rhay. When I have the One Lord, I have tens of thousands. Otherwise, people like me beg from door to door.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v4	bwmxu ibrQw gieE jnµmu ijin kIqo so ivsry ]4] (1425-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) baaman birthaa ga-i-o jannam jin keeto so visray. ||4||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v4	O Brahmin, your life has passed away uselessly; you have forgotten the One who created you. ||4||
RECORD	para 61614	soriT so rsu pIjIAY kbhU n PIkw hoie ] (1425-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) sorath so ras peejee-ai kabhoo na feekaa ho-ay. In Raga Sorat'h, drink in this sublime essence, which never loses its taste.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v5	nwnk rwm nwm gun gweIAih drgh inrml soie ]5] (1425-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak raam naam gun gaa-ee-ah dargeh nirmal so-ay. ||5||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v5	O Nanak, singing the Glorious Praises of the Lord's Name, one's reputation is immaculate in the Court of the Lord. ||5||
RECORD	para 61616	jo pRiB rKy Awip iqn koie n mwreI ] (1425-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jo parabh rakhay aap tin ko-ay na maar-ee. No one can kill those whom God Himself protects.
DEFINE	para 61617	AMdir nwmu inDwnu sdw gux swreI ] (1425-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) andar naam niDhaan sadaa gun saar-ee. The treasure of the Naam, the Name of the Lord, is within them. They cherish His Glorious Virtues forever.
RECORD	para 61618	eykw tyk AgMm min qin pRBu DwreI ] (1425-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) aykaa tayk agamm man tan parabh Dhaar-ee. They take the Support of the One, the Inaccessible Lord; they enshrine God in their mind and body.
DEFINE	para 61619	lgw rMgu Apwru ko n auqwreI ] (1425-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) lagaa rang apaar ko na utaara-ee. They are imbued with the Love of the Infinite Lord, and no one can wipe it away.
RECORD	para 61620	gurmuiK hir gux gwie shij suKu swreI ] (1425-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) gurmukh har gun gaa-ay sahj sukh saar-ee. The Gurmukhs sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord; they obtain the most excellent celestial peace and poise.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v6	nwnk nwmu inDwnu irdY auir hwreI ]6] (1425-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak naam niDhaan ridai ur haar-ee. ||6||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v6	O Nanak, they enshrine the treasure of the Naam in their hearts. ||6||
RECORD	para 61622	kry su cMgw mwin duXI gxq lwih ] (1425-9, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) karay so changa maan duyee ganat laahi. Whatever God does, accept that as good; leave behind all other judgements.
REQUIRE	para 61623	ApxI ndir inhwil Awpy lYhu lwie ] (1425-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) apnee nadar nihaal aapay laihu laa-ay. He shall cast His Glance of Grace, and attach you to Himself.
RECORD	para 61624	jn dyhu mqI aupdysu ivchu Brmu jwie ] (1425-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jan dayh matee updays vichahu bharam jaa-ay. Instruct yourself with the Teachings, and doubt will depart from within.
DEFINE	para 61625	jo Duir iliKAw lyKu soeI sB kmwie ] (1425-10, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jo Dhur likhi-aa laykh so-ee sabh kamaa-ay. Everyone does that which is pre-ordained by destiny.
DEFINE	para 61626	sBu kCu iqs dY vis dUjI nwih jwie ] (1425-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) sabh kachh tis dai vas doojee naahi jaa-ay. Everything is under His control; there is no other place at all.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v7	nwnk suK And Bey pRB kI mMin rjwie ]7] (1425-11, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak sukh anad bha-ay parabh kee man rajaa-ay. ||7||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v7	Nanak is in peace and bliss, accepting the Will of God. ||7||
DEFINE	para 61628	guru pUrw ijn ismirAw syeI Bey inhwl ] (1425-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) gur pooraa jin simri-aa say-ee bha-ay nihaal. Those who meditate in remembrance on the Perfect Guru, are exalted and uplifted.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v8	nwnk nwmu ArwDxw kwrju AwvY rwis ]8] (1425-12, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak naam araaDhanaa kaaraj aavai raas. ||8||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v8	O Nanak, dwelling on the Naam, the Name of the Lord, all affairs are resolved. ||8||
RECORD	para 61630	pwpI krm kmwvdy krdy hwey hwie ] (1425-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) paapee karam kamaavday karday haa-ay haa-ay. The sinners act, and generate bad karma, and then they weep and wail.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v9	nwnk ijau mQin mwDwxIAw iqau mQy DRm rwie ]9] (1425-13, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak ji-o mathan maaDhaanee-aa ti-o mathay Dharam raa-ay. ||9||
UPHOLD	slok mhlw 5 v9	O Nanak, just as the churning stick churns the butter, so does the Righteous Judge of Dharma churn them. ||9||
DEFINE	para 61632	nwmu iDAwiein swjnw jnm pdwrQu jIiq ] (1425-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naam Dhi-aa-in saajnaa janam padaarath jeet. Meditating on the Naam, O friend, the treasure of life is won.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v10	nwnk Drm AYsy cvih kIqo Bvnu punIq ]10] (1425-14, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak Dharam aisay chaveh keeto bhavan puneet. ||10||
UPHOLD	slok mhlw 5 v10	O Nanak, speaking in Righteousness, one's world becomes sanctified. ||10||
RECORD	para 61634	KuBVI kuQwie imTI glix kumMqRIAw ] (1425-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) khubh-rhee kuthaa-ay mithee galan kumantaree-aa. I am stuck in an evil place, trusting the sweet words of an evil advisor.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v11	nwnk syeI aubry ijnw Bwgu mQwih ]11] (1425-15, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak say-ee ubray jinaa bhaag mathaahi. ||11||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v11	O Nanak, they alone are saved, who have such good destiny inscribed upon their foreheads. ||11||
DEFINE	para 61636	suqVy suKI svMin@ jo rqy sh AwpxY ] (1425-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) sut-rhay sukhee savaNniH jo ratay sah aapnai. They alone sleep and dream in peace, who are imbued with the Love of their Husband Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v12	pRym ivCohw DxI sau ATy phr lvMin@ ]12] (1425-16, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) paraym vichhohaa Dhanee sa-o athay pahar lava NniH. ||12||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v12	Those who have been separated from the Love of their Master, scream and cry twenty-four hours a day. ||12||
DEFINE	para 61638	suqVy AsMK mwieAw JUTI kwrxy ] (1425-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) sut-rhay asaNkh maa-i-aa jhoothee kaarnay. Millions are asleep, in the false illusion of Maya.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v13	nwnk sy jwgMin@ ij rsnw nwmu aucwrxy ]13] (1425-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak say jaaga NniH je rasnaa naam uchaarnay. ||13||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v13	O Nanak, they alone are awake and aware, who chant the Naam with their tongues. ||13||
DEFINE	para 61640	imRg iqsnw pyiK Bulxy vuTy ngr gMDRb ] (1425-17, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) marig tisnaa paykh bhulnay vuthay nagar ganDharab. Seeing the mirage, the optical illusion, the people are confused and deluded.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v14	ijnI scu ArwiDAw nwnk min qin Pb ]14] (1425-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jinee sach araaDhi-aa naanak man tan fab. ||14||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v14	Those who worship and adore the True Lord, O Nanak, their minds and bodies are beautiful. ||14||
DEFINE	para 61642	piqq auDwrx pwrbRhmu sMmRQ purKu Apwru ] (1425-18, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) patit uDhaaran paarbarahm samrath purakh apaar. The All-powerful Supreme Lord God, the Infinite Primal Being, is the Saving Grace of sinners.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v15	ijsih auDwry nwnkw so ismry isrjxhwru ]15] (1426-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jisahi uDhaaray naankaa so simray sirjanhaar. ||15||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v15	Those whom He saves, meditate in remembrance on the Creator Lord. ||15||
WHEN	para 61645	dUjI Coif kuvwtVI ieks sau icqu lwie ] (1426-1, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) doojee chhod kuvaatarhee ikas sa-o chit laa-ay. Forsake duality and the ways of evil; focus your consciousness on the One Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v16	dUjY BwvˆØI nwnkw vhix luV@MdVI jwie ]16] (1426-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) doojai bhaaveeN naankaa vahan lurh HaNdarhee jaa-ay. ||16||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v16	In the love of duality, O Nanak, the mortals are being washed downstream. ||16||
RECORD	para 61647	iqhtVy bwjwr saudw krin vxjwirAw ] (1426-2, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) tihtarhay baajaar sa-udaa karan vanjaari-aa. In the markets and bazaars of the three qualities, the merchants make their deals.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v17	scu vKru ijnI lidAw sy scVy pwswr ]17] (1426-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) sach vakhar jinee ladi-aa say sachrhay paasaar. ||17||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v17	Those who load the true merchandise are the true traders. ||17||
DEFINE	para 61649	pMQw pRym n jwxeI BUlI iPrY gvwir ] (1426-3, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) panthaa paraym na jaan-ee bhoolee firai gavaar. Those who do not know the way of love are foolish; they wander lost and confused.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v18	nwnk hir ibsrwie kY paudy nrik AMD´wr ]18] (1426-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) naanak har bisraa-ay kai pa-uday narak anDh-yaar. ||18||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v18	O Nanak, forgetting the Lord, they fall into the deep, dark pit of hell. ||18||
RECORD	para 61651	mwieAw mnhu n vIsrY mWgY dMmW dMm ] (1426-4, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) maa-i-aa manhu na veesrai maa Ngai dammaa N damm. In his mind, the mortal does not forget Maya; he begs for more and more wealth.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v19	so pRBu iciq n AwveI nwnk nhI krMim ]19] (1426-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) so parabh chit na aavee naanak nahee karamm. ||19||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v19	That God does not even come into his consciousness; O Nanak, it is not in his karma. ||19||
DEFINE	para 61653	iqcru mUil n QuVˆØIdo ijcru Awip ik®pwlu ] (1426-5, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) tichar mool na thurhee Ndo jichar aap kirpaal. The mortal does not run out of capital, as long as the Lord Himself is merciful.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v20	sbdu AKutu bwbw nwnkw Kwih Kric Dnu mwlu ]20] (1426-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) sabad akhut baabaa naankaa khaahi kharach Dhan maal. ||20||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v20	The Word of the Shabad is Guru Nanak's inexhaustible treasure; this wealth and capital never runs out, no matter how much it is spent and consumed. ||20||
WHEN	para 61655	KMB ivkWdVy jy lhW iGMnw swvI qoil ] (1426-6, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) khanbh vikaa Nd-rhay jay lahaa N ghinnaa saavee tol. If I could find wings for sale, I would buy them with an equal weight of my flesh.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v21	qMin jVWeI AwpxY lhW su sjxu toil ]21] (1426-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) tann jarhaaN-ee aapnai lahaa N so sajan tol. ||21||
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v21	I would attach them to my body, and seek out and find my Friend. ||21||
DEFINE	para 61657	sjxu scw pwiqswhu isir swhW dY swhu ] (1426-7, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) sajan sachaa paatisaahu sir saahaa N dai saahu. My Friend is the True Supreme King, the King over the heads of kings.
RECORD	slok mhlw 5 v22	ijsu pwis bihiTAw sohIAY sBnW dw vyswhu ]22] (1426-8, slok vwrW qy vDIk, mÚ 5) jis paas bahithi-aa sohee-ai sabhnaa N daa vaysaahu. ||22||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 5 v22	Sitting by His side, we are exalted and beautified; He is the Support of all. ||22||
RECORD	para 61659	<> siqgur pRswid ] (1426-9) ik-oNkaar satgur parsaad. One Universal Creator God. By The Grace Of The True Guru:
RECORD	para 61660	salok mehlaa 9. Shalok, Ninth Mehl:
DEFINE	para 61661	gun goibMd gwieE nhI jnmu AkwrQ kInu ] (1426-10, slok, mÚ 9) gun gobind gaa-i-o nahee janam akaarath keen. If you do not sing the Praises of the Lord, your life is rendered useless.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v1	khu nwnk hir Bju mnw ijh ibiD jl kau mInu ]1] (1426-10, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak har bhaj manaa jih biDh jal ka-o meen. ||1||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v1	Says Nanak, meditate, vibrate upon the Lord; immerse your mind in Him, like the fish in the water. ||1||
DEFINE	para 61663	ibiKAn isau kwhy ricE inmK n hoih audwsu ] (1426-11, slok, mÚ 9) bikhi-an si-o kaahay rachi-o nimakh na hohi udaas. Why are you engrossed in sin and corruption? You are not detached, even for a moment!
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v2	khu nwnk Bju hir mnw prY n jm kI Pws ]2] (1426-11, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak bhaj har manaa parai na jam kee faas. ||2||
FORBID	slok mhlw 9 v2	Says Nanak, meditate, vibrate upon the Lord, and you shall not be caught in the noose of death. ||2||
RECORD	para 61665	qrnwpo ieau hI gieE lIE jrw qnu jIiq ] (1426-12, slok, mÚ 9) tarnaapo i-o hee ga-i-o lee-o jaraa tan jeet. Your youth has passed away like this, and old age has overtaken your body.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v3	khu nwnk Bju hir mnw AauD jwqu hY bIiq ]3] (1426-12, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak bhaj har manaa a-oDh jaat hai beet. ||3||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v3	Says Nanak, meditate, vibrate upon the Lord; your life is fleeting away! ||3||
DEFINE	para 61667	ibriD BieE sUJY nhI kwlu phUicE Awin ] (1426-13, slok, mÚ 9) biraDh bha-i-o soojhai nahee kaal pahoochi-o aan. You have become old, and you do not understand that death is overtaking you.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v4	khu nwnk nr bwvry ikau n BjY Bgvwnu ]4] (1426-13, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak nar baavray ki-o na bhajai bhagvaan. ||4||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v4	Says Nanak, you are insane! Why do you not remember and meditate on God? ||4||
RECORD	para 61669	Dnu dwrw sMpiq sgl ijin ApunI kir mwin ] (1426-14, slok, mÚ 9) Dhan daaraa sampat sagal jin apunee kar maan. Your wealth, spouse, and all the possessions which you claim as your own
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v5	ien mY kCu sMgI nhI nwnk swcI jwin ]5] (1426-14, slok, mÚ 9) in mai kachh sangee nahee naanak saachee jaan. ||5||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 9 v5	- none of these shall go along with you in the end. O Nanak, know this as true. ||5||
DEFINE	para 61671	piqq auDwrn BY hrn hir AnwQ ky nwQ ] (1426-15, slok, mÚ 9) patit uDhaaran bhai haran har anaath kay naath. He is the Saving Grace of sinners, the Destroyer of fear, the Master of the masterless.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v6	khu nwnk iqh jwnIAY sdw bsqu qum swiQ ]6] (1426-15, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak tih jaanee-ai sadaa basat tum saath. ||6||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v6	Says Nanak, realize and know Him, who is always with you. ||6||
DEFINE	para 61673	qnu Dnu ijh qo kau dIE qW isau nyhu n kIn ] (1426-16, slok, mÚ 9) tan Dhan jih to ka-o dee-o taaN si-o nayhu na keen. He has given you your body and wealth, but you are not in love with Him.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v7	khu nwnk nr bwvry Ab ikau folq dIn ]7] (1426-16, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak nar baavray ab ki-o dolat deen. ||7||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v7	Says Nanak, you are insane! Why do you now shake and tremble so helplessly? ||7||
RECORD	para 61675	qnu Dnu sMpY suK dIE Aru ijh nIky Dwm ] (1426-17, slok, mÚ 9) tan Dhan sampai sukh dee-o ar jih neekay Dhaam. He has given you your body, wealth, property, peace and beautiful mansions.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v8	khu nwnk sunu ry mnw ismrq kwih n rwmu ]8] (1426-17, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa simrat kaahi na raam. ||8||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v8	Says Nanak, listen, mind: why don't you remember the Lord in meditation? ||8||
DEFINE	para 61677	sB suK dwqw rwmu hY dUsr nwihn koie ] (1426-18, slok, mÚ 9) sabh sukh daataa raam hai doosar naahin ko-ay. The Lord is the Giver of all peace and comfort. There is no other at all.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v9	khu nwnk suin ry mnw iqh ismrq giq hoie ]9] (1426-18, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa tih simrat gat ho-ay. ||9||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v9	Says Nanak, listen, mind: meditating in remembrance on Him, salvation is attained. ||9||
DEFINE	para 61680	ijh ismrq giq pweIAY iqh Bju ry qY mIq ] (1427-1, slok, mÚ 9) jih simrat gat paa-ee-ai tih bhaj ray tai meet. Remembering Him in meditation, salvation is attained; vibrate and meditate on Him, O my friend.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v10	khu nwnk sunu ry mnw AauD Gtq hY nIq ]10] (1427-1, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa a-oDh ghatat hai neet. ||10||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v10	Says Nanak, listen, mind: your life is passing away! ||10||
DEFINE	para 61682	pWc qq ko qnu ricE jwnhu cqur sujwn ] (1427-2, slok, mÚ 9) paa Nch tat ko tan rachi-o jaanhu chatur sujaan. Your body is made up of the five elements; you are clever and wise - know this well.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v11	ijh qy aupijE nwnkw lIn qwih mY mwnu ]11] (1427-2, slok, mÚ 9) jih tay upji-o naankaa leen taahi mai maan. ||11||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 9 v11	Believe it - you shall merge once again into the One, O Nanak, from whom you originated. ||11||
RECORD	para 61684	Gt Gt mY hir jU bsY sMqn kihE pukwir ] (1427-3, slok, mÚ 9) ghat ghat mai har joo basai santan kahi-o pukaar. The Dear Lord abides in each and every heart; the Saints proclaim this as true.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v12	khu nwnk iqh Bju mnw Bau iniD auqrih pwir ]12] (1427-3, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak tih bhaj manaa bha-o niDh utreh paar. ||12||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 9 v12	Says Nanak, meditate and vibrate upon Him, and you shall cross over the terrifying world-ocean. ||12||
DEFINE	para 61686	suKu duKu ijh prsY nhI loBu mohu AiBmwnu ] (1427-4, slok, mÚ 9) sukh dukh jih parsai nahee lobh moh abhimaan. One who is not touched by pleasure or pain, greed, emotional attachment and egotistical pride
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v13	khu nwnk sunu ry mnw so mUriq Bgvwn ]13] (1427-4, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa so moorat bhagvaan. ||13||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v13	- says Nanak, listen, mind: he is the very image of God. ||13||
DEFINE	para 61688	ausqiq inMidAw nwih ijih kMcn loh smwin ] (1427-5, slok, mÚ 9) ustat nindi-aa naahi jihi kanchan loh samaan. One who is beyond praise and slander, who looks upon gold and iron alike
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v14	khu nwnk suin ry mnw mukiq qwih qY jwin ]14] (1427-5, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa mukat taahi tai jaan. ||14||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v14	- says Nanak, listen, mind: know that such a person is liberated. ||14||
DEFINE	para 61690	hrKu sogu jw kY nhI bYrI mIq smwin ] (1427-6, slok, mÚ 9) harakh sog jaa kai nahee bairee meet samaan. One who is not affected by pleasure or pain, who looks upon friend and enemy alike
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v15	khu nwnk suin ry mnw mukiq qwih qY jwin ]15] (1427-6, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa mukat taahi tai jaan. ||15||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v15	- says Nanak, listen, mind: know that such a person is liberated. ||15||
DEFINE	para 61692	BY kwhU kau dyq nih nih BY mwnq Awn ] (1427-7, slok, mÚ 9) bhai kaahoo ka-o dayt neh neh bhai maanat aan. One who does not frighten anyone, and who is not afraid of anyone else
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v16	khu nwnk suin ry mnw igAwnI qwih bKwin ]16] (1427-7, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa gi-aanee taahi bakhaan. ||16||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v16	- says Nanak, listen, mind: call him spiritually wise. ||16||
RECORD	para 61694	ijih ibiKAw sglI qjI lIE ByK bYrwg ] (1427-8, slok, mÚ 9) jihi bikhi-aa saglee tajee lee-o bhaykh bairaag. One who has forsaken all sin and corruption, who wears the robes of neutral detachment
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v17	khu nwnk sunu ry mnw iqh nr mwQY Bwgu ]17] (1427-8, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa tih nar maathai bhaag. ||17||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v17	- says Nanak, listen, mind: good destiny is written on his forehead. ||17||
DEFINE	para 61696	ijih mwieAw mmqw qjI sB qy BieE audwsu ] (1427-9, slok, mÚ 9) jihi maa-i-aa mamtaa tajee sabh tay bha-i-o udaas. One who renounces Maya and possessiveness and is detached from everything
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v18	khu nwnk sunu ry mnw iqh Git bRhm invwsu ]18] (1427-9, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa tih ghat barahm nivaas. ||18||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v18	- says Nanak, listen, mind: God abides in his heart. ||18||
RECORD	para 61698	ijih pRwnI haumY qjI krqw rwmu pCwin ] (1427-10, slok, mÚ 9) jihi paraanee ha-umai tajee kartaa raam pachhaan. That mortal, who forsakes egotism, and realizes the Creator Lord
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v19	khu nwnk vhu mukiq nru ieh mn swcI mwnu ]19] (1427-10, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak vahu mukat nar ih man saachee maan. ||19||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v19	- says Nanak, that person is liberated; O mind, know this as true. ||19||
RECORD	para 61700	BY nwsn durmiq hrn kil mY hir ko nwmu ] (1427-11, slok, mÚ 9) bhai naasan durmat haran kal mai har ko naam. In this Dark Age of Kali Yuga, the Name of the Lord is the Destroyer of fear, the Eradicator of evil-mindedness.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v20	inis idnu jo nwnk BjY sPl hoih iqh kwm ]20] (1427-11, slok, mÚ 9) nis din jo naanak bhajai safal hohi tih kaam. ||20||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v20	Night and day, O Nanak, whoever vibrates and meditates on the Lord's Name, sees all of his works brought to fruition. ||20||
RECORD	para 61702	ijhbw gun goibMd Bjhu krn sunhu hir nwmu ] (1427-12, slok, mÚ 9) jihbaa gun gobind bhajahu karan sunhu har naam. Vibrate with your tongue the Glorious Praises of the Lord of the Universe; with your ears, hear the Lord's Name.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v21	khu nwnk suin ry mnw prih n jm kY Dwm ]21] (1427-12, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa pareh na jam kai Dhaam. ||21||
FORBID	slok mhlw 9 v21	Says Nanak, listen, man: you shall not have to go to the house of Death. ||21||
RECORD	para 61704	jo pRwnI mmqw qjY loB moh AhMkwr ] (1427-13, slok, mÚ 9) jo paraanee mamtaa tajai lobh moh aha Nkaar. That mortal who renounces possessiveness, greed, emotional attachment and egotism
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v22	khu nwnk Awpn qrY Aaurn lyq auDwr ]22] (1427-13, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak aapan tarai a-uran layt uDhaar. ||22||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v22	- says Nanak, he himself is saved, and he saves many others as well. ||22||
REQUIRE	para 61706	ijau supnw Aru pyKnw AYsy jg kau jwin ] (1427-14, slok, mÚ 9) ji-o supnaa ar paykhnaa aisay jag ka-o jaan. Like a dream and a show, so is this world, you must know.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v23	ien mY kCu swco nhI nwnk ibnu Bgvwn ]23] (1427-14, slok, mÚ 9) in mai kachh saacho nahee naanak bin bhagvaan. ||23||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v23	None of this is true, O Nanak, without God. ||23||
RECORD	para 61708	inis idnu mwieAw kwrny pRwnI folq nIq ] (1427-15, slok, mÚ 9) nis din maa-i-aa kaarnay paraanee dolat neet. Night and day, for the sake of Maya, the mortal wanders constantly.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v24	kotn mY nwnk koaU nwrwienu ijh cIiq ]24] (1427-15, slok, mÚ 9) kotan mai naanak ko-oo naaraa-in jih cheet. ||24||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v24	Among millions, O Nanak, there is scarcely anyone, who keeps the Lord in his consciousness. ||24||
RECORD	para 61710	jYsy jl qy budbudw aupjY ibnsY nIq ] (1427-16, slok, mÚ 9) jaisay jal tay budbudaa upjai binsai neet. As the bubbles in the water well up and disappear again,
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v25	jg rcnw qYsy rcI khu nwnk suin mIq ]25] (1427-16, slok, mÚ 9) jag rachnaa taisay rachee kaho naanak sun meet. ||25||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v25	so is the universe created; says Nanak, listen, O my friend! ||25||
DEFINE	para 61712	pRwnI kCU n cyqeI mid mwieAw kY AMDu ] (1427-16, slok, mÚ 9) paraanee kachhoo na chayt-ee mad maa-i-aa kai anDh. The mortal does not remember the Lord, even for a moment; he is blinded by the wine of Maya.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v26	khu nwnk ibnu hir Bjn prq qwih jm PMD ]26] (1427-17, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak bin har bhajan parat taahi jam fanDh. ||26||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v26	Says Nanak, without meditating on the Lord, he is caught by the noose of Death. ||26||
WHEN	para 61714	jau suK kau cwhY sdw srin rwm kI lyh ] (1427-17, slok, mÚ 9) ja-o sukh ka-o chaahai sadaa saran raam kee layh. If you yearn for eternal peace, then seek the Sanctuary of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v27	khu nwnk suin ry mnw durlB mwnuK dyh ]27] (1427-18, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa durlabh maanukh dayh. ||27||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v27	Says Nanak, listen, mind: this human body is difficult to obtain. ||27||
RECORD	para 61716	mwieAw kwrin DwvhI mUrK log Ajwn ] (1427-18, slok, mÚ 9) maa-i-aa kaaran Dhaavhee moorakh log ajaan. For the sake of Maya, the fools and ignorant people run all around.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v28	khu nwnk ibnu hir Bjn ibrQw jnmu isrwn ]28] (1427-19, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak bin har bhajan birthaa janam siraan. ||28||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v28	Says Nanak, without meditating on the Lord, life passes away uselessly. ||28||
RECORD	para 61718	jo pRwnI inis idnu BjY rUp rwm iqh jwnu ] (1427-19, slok, mÚ 9) jo paraanee nis din bhajai roop raam tih jaan. That mortal who meditates and vibrates upon the Lord night and day - know him to be the embodiment of the Lord.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v29	hir jn hir AMqru nhI nwnk swcI mwnu ]29] (1428-1, slok, mÚ 9) har jan har antar nahee naanak saachee maan. ||29||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v29	There is no difference between the Lord and the humble servant of the Lord; O Nanak, know this as true. ||29||
DEFINE	para 61721	mnu mwieAw mY PiD rihE ibsirE goibMd nwmu ] (1428-1, slok, mÚ 9) man maa-i-aa mai faDh rahi-o bisri-o gobind naam. The mortal is entangled in Maya; he has forgotten the Name of the Lord of the Universe.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v30	khu nwnk ibnu hir Bjn jIvn kauny kwm ]30] (1428-2, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak bin har bhajan jeevan ka-unay kaam. ||30||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v30	Says Nanak, without meditating on the Lord, what is the use of this human life? ||30||
DEFINE	para 61723	pRwnI rwmu n cyqeI mid mwieAw kY AMDu ] (1428-2, slok, mÚ 9) paraanee raam na chayt-ee mad maa-i-aa kai anDh. The mortal does not think of the Lord; he is blinded by the wine of Maya.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v31	khu nwnk hir Bjn ibnu prq qwih jm PMD ]31] (1428-3, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak har bhajan bin parat taahi jam fanDh. ||31||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v31	Says Nanak, without meditating on the Lord, he is caught in the noose of Death. ||31||
DEFINE	para 61725	suK mY bhu sMgI Bey duK mY sMig n koie ] (1428-3, slok, mÚ 9) sukh mai baho sangee bha-ay dukh mai sang na ko-ay. In good times, there are many companions around, but in bad times, there is no one at all.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v32	khu nwnk hir Bju mnw AMiq shweI hoie ]32] (1428-4, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak har bhaj manaa ant sahaa-ee ho-ay. ||32||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 9 v32	Says Nanak, vibrate, and meditate on the Lord; He shall be your only Help and Support in the end. ||32||
RECORD	para 61727	jnm jnm Brmq iPirE imitE n jm ko qRwsu ] (1428-4, slok, mÚ 9) janam janam bharmat firi-o miti-o na jam ko taraas. Mortals wander lost and confused through countless lifetimes; their fear of death is never removed.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v33	khu nwnk hir Bju mnw inrBY pwvih bwsu ]33] (1428-5, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak har bhaj manaa nirbhai paavahi baas. ||33||
REQUIRE	slok mhlw 9 v33	Says Nanak, vibrate and meditate on the Lord, and you shall dwell in the Fearless Lord. ||33||
RECORD	para 61729	jqn bhuqu mY kir rihE imitE n mn ko mwnu ] (1428-5, slok, mÚ 9) jatan bahut mai kar rahi-o miti-o na man ko maan. I have tried so many things, but the pride of my mind has not been dispelled.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v34	durmiq isau nwnk PiDE rwiK lyhu Bgvwn ]34] (1428-6, slok, mÚ 9) durmat si-o naanak faDhi-o raakh layho bhagvaan. ||34||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v34	I am engrossed in evil-mindedness, Nanak. O God, please save me! ||34||
RECORD	para 61731	bwl juAwnI Aru ibriD Puin qIin AvsQw jwin ] (1428-7, slok, mÚ 9) baal ju-aanee ar biraDh fun teen avasthaa jaan. Childhood, youth and old age - know these as the three stages of life.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v35	khu nwnk hir Bjn ibnu ibrQw sB hI mwnu ]35] (1428-7, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak har bhajan bin birthaa sabh hee maan. ||35||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v35	Says Nanak, without meditating on the Lord, everything is useless; you must appreciate this. ||35||
DEFINE	para 61733	krxo huqo su nw kIE pirE loB kY PMD ] (1428-8, slok, mÚ 9) karno huto so naa kee-o pari-o lobh kai fanDh. You have not done what you should have done; you are entangled in the web of greed.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v36	nwnk simE rim gieE Ab ikau rovq AMD ]36] (1428-8, slok, mÚ 9) naanak sami-o ram ga-i-o ab ki-o rovat anDh. ||36||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v36	Nanak, your time is past and gone; why are you crying now, you blind fool? ||36||
DEFINE	para 61735	mnu mwieAw mY rim rihE inksq nwihn mIq ] (1428-9, slok, mÚ 9) man maa-i-aa mai ram rahi-o niksat naahin meet. The mind is absorbed in Maya - it cannot escape it, my friend.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v37	nwnk mUriq icqR ijau Cwifq nwihn BIiq ]37] (1428-9, slok, mÚ 9) naanak moorat chitar ji-o chhaadit naahin bheet. ||37||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v37	Nanak, it is like a picture painted on the wall - it cannot leave it. ||37||
RECORD	para 61737	nr cwhq kCu Aaur AaurY kI AaurY BeI ] (1428-10, slok, mÚ 9) nar chaahat kachh a-or a-urai kee a-urai bha-ee. The man wishes for something, but something different happens.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v38	icqvq rihE Tgaur nwnk PwsI gil prI ]38] (1428-10, slok, mÚ 9) chitvat rahi-o thaga-ur naanak faasee gal paree. ||38||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v38	He plots to deceive others, O Nanak, but he places the noose around his own neck instead. ||38||
RECORD	para 61739	jqn bhuq suK ky kIey duK ko kIE n koie ] (1428-11, slok, mÚ 9) jatan bahut sukh kay kee-ay dukh ko kee-o na ko-ay. People make all sorts of efforts to find peace and pleasure, but no one tries to earn pain.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v39	khu nwnk suin ry mnw hir BwvY so hoie ]39] (1428-11, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak sun ray manaa har bhaavai so ho-ay. ||39||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v39	Says Nanak, listen, mind: whatever pleases God comes to pass. ||39||
DEFINE	para 61741	jgqu iBKwrI iPrqu hY sB ko dwqw rwmu ] (1428-12, slok, mÚ 9) jagat bhikhaaree firat hai sabh ko daataa raam. The world wanders around begging, but the Lord is the Giver of all.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v40	khu nwnk mn ismru iqh pUrn hovih kwm ]40] (1428-12, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak man simar tih pooran hoveh kaam. ||40||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v40	Says Nanak, meditate in remembrance on Him, and all your works will be successful. ||40||
REQUIRE	para 61743	JUTY mwnu khw krY jgu supny ijau jwnu ] (1428-13, slok, mÚ 9) jhoothai maan kahaa karai jag supnay ji-o jaan. Why do you take such false pride in yourself? You must know that the world is just a dream.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v41	ien mY kCu qyro nhI nwnk kihE bKwin ]41] (1428-13, slok, mÚ 9) in mai kachh tayro nahee naanak kahi-o bakhaan. ||41||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v41	None of this is yours; Nanak proclaims this truth. ||41||
REQUIRE	para 61745	grbu krqu hY dyh ko ibnsY iCn mY mIq ] (1428-13, slok, mÚ 9) garab karat hai dayh ko binsai chhin mai meet. You are so proud of your body; it shall perish in an instant, my friend.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v42	ijih pRwnI hir jsu kihE nwnk iqih jgu jIiq ]42] (1428-14, slok, mÚ 9) jihi paraanee har jas kahi-o naanak tihi jag jeet. ||42||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v42	That mortal who chants the Praises of the Lord, O Nanak, conquers the world. ||42||
DEFINE	para 61747	ijh Git ismrnu rwm ko so nru mukqw jwnu ] (1428-14, slok, mÚ 9) jih ghat simran raam ko so nar muktaa jaan. That person, who meditates in remembrance on the Lord in his heart, is liberated - know this well.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v43	iqih nr hir AMqru nhI nwnk swcI mwnu ]43] (1428-15, slok, mÚ 9) tihi nar har antar nahee naanak saachee maan. ||43||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v43	There is no difference between that person and the Lord: O Nanak, accept this as the Truth. ||43||
RECORD	para 61749	eyk Bgiq Bgvwn ijh pRwnI kY nwih min ] (1428-15, slok, mÚ 9) ayk bhagat bhagvaan jih paraanee kai naahi man. That person, who does not feel devotion to God in his mind
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v44	jYsy sUkr suAwn nwnk mwno qwih qnu ]44] (1428-16, slok, mÚ 9) jaisay sookar su-aan naanak maano taahi tan. ||44||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v44	- O Nanak, know that his body is like that of a pig, or a dog. ||44||
RECORD	para 61751	suAwmI ko igRhu ijau sdw suAwn qjq nhI inq ] (1428-16, slok, mÚ 9) su-aamee ko garihu ji-o sadaa su-aan tajat nahee nit. A dog never abandons the home of his master.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v45	nwnk ieh ibiD hir Bjau iek min huie iek iciq ]45] (1428-17, slok, mÚ 9) naanak ih biDh har bhaja-o ik man hu-ay ik chit. ||45||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v45	O Nanak, in just the same way, vibrate, and meditate on the Lord, single-mindedly, with one-pointed consciousness. ||45||
RECORD	para 61753	qIrQ brq Aru dwn kir mn mY DrY gumwnu ] (1428-18, slok, mÚ 9) tirath barat ar daan kar man mai Dharai gumaan. Those who make pilgrimages to sacred shrines, observe ritualistic fasts and make donations to charity while still taking pride in their minds
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v46	nwnk inhPl jwq iqh ijau kuMcr iesnwnu ]46] (1428-18, slok, mÚ 9) naanak nihfal jaat tih ji-o kunchar isnaan. ||46||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v46	- O Nanak, their actions are useless, like the elephant, who takes a bath, and then rolls in the dust. ||46||
RECORD	para 61755	isru kMipE pg fgmgy nYn joiq qy hIn ] (1428-18, slok, mÚ 9) sir kampi-o pag dagmagay nain jot tay heen. The head shakes, the feet stagger, and the eyes become dull and weak.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v47	khu nwnk ieh ibiD BeI qaU n hir ris lIn ]47] (1428-18, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak ih biDh bha-ee ta-oo na har ras leen. ||47||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v47	Says Nanak, this is your condition. And even now, you have not savored the sublime essence of the Lord. ||47||
RECORD	para 61758	inj kir dyiKE jgqu mY ko kwhU ko nwih ] (1429-1, slok, mÚ 9) nij kar daykhi-o jagat mai ko kaahoo ko naahi. I had looked upon the world as my own, but no one belongs to anyone else.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v48	nwnk iQru hir Bgiq hY iqh rwKo mn mwih ]48] (1429-1, slok, mÚ 9) naanak thir har bhagat hai tih raakho man maahi. ||48||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v48	O Nanak, only devotional worship of the Lord is permanent; enshrine this in your mind. ||48||
DEFINE	para 61760	jg rcnw sB JUT hY jwin lyhu ry mIq ] (1429-2, slok, mÚ 9) jag rachnaa sabh jhooth hai jaan layho ray meet. The world and its affairs are totally false; know this well, my friend.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v49	kih nwnk iQru nw rhY ijau bwlU kI BIiq ]49] (1429-2, slok, mÚ 9) kahi naanak thir naa rahai ji-o baaloo kee bheet. ||49||
FORBID	slok mhlw 9 v49	Says Nanak, it is like a wall of sand; it shall not endure. ||49||
RECORD	para 61762	rwmu gieE rwvnu gieE jw kau bhu prvwru ] (1429-3, slok, mÚ 9) raam ga-i-o raavan ga-i-o jaa ka-o baho parvaar. Raam Chand passed away, as did Raawan, even though he had lots of relatives.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v50	khu nwnk iQru kCu nhI supny ijau sMswru ]50] (1429-3, slok, mÚ 9) kaho naanak thir kachh nahee supnay ji-o sansaar. ||50||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v50	Says Nanak, nothing lasts forever; the world is like a dream. ||50||
WHEN	para 61764	icMqw qw kI kIjIAY jo AnhonI hoie ] (1429-4, slok, mÚ 9) chintaa taa kee keejee-ai jo anhonee ho-ay. People become anxious, when something unexpected happens.
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v51	iehu mwrgu sMswr ko nwnk iQru nhI koie ]51] (1429-4, slok, mÚ 9) ih maarag sansaar ko naanak thir nahee ko-ay. ||51||
DEFINE	slok mhlw 9 v51	This is the way of the world, O Nanak; nothing is stable or permanent. ||51||
REQUIRE	para 61766	jo aupijE so ibnis hY pro Awju kY kwil ] (1429-4, slok, mÚ 9) jo upji-o so binas hai paro aaj kai kaal. Whatever has been created shall be destroyed; everyone shall perish, today or tomorrow.
WHEN	slok mhlw 9 v52	nwnk hir gun gwie ly Cwif sgl jMjwl ]52] (1429-5, slok, mÚ 9) naanak har gun gaa-ay lay chhaad sagal janjaal. ||52||
RECORD	slok mhlw 9 v52	O Nanak, sing the Glorious Praises of the Lord, and give up all other entanglements. ||52||
RECORD	para 61768	dohrw ] (1429-5) dohraa. Dohraa:
