RECORD	para 40	Scale matters. A “biome” is a broad system; an “ecoregion” is a geographically distinct ecological unit; a “plant association” is much more local; a “landform” is physical shape; and “land cover” is what occupies the surface right now. They are related but not interchangeable.
RECORD	para 41	Suggested reading path for terrain generation: Sections 1-4 explain drivers; Sections 6-12 supply categories; Sections 13-16 convert the concepts into geographical and classification rules.
