ALLOW	para 308	Islands can create sharp elevation belts, cloud forests, windward/lee patterns, and endemism over small distances. Volcanic islands may have young porous substrates, geothermal zones, lava fields, and strong soil-age gradients. Oceanic isolation and local history can make their species assemblages unlike those of continental regions with similar climate.
WHEN	para 310	Similar climate envelopes do not create identical biomes everywhere. The Cape fynbos, Californian chaparral, central Chilean matorral, Mediterranean maquis and southwestern Australian kwongan share some climate and plant-functional traits, but their species histories, soils and fire regimes differ. Use the climatic/terrain label to describe physical conditions; use ecoregion or floristic information when species identity matters. [15]
