RECORD	Processes that shift local vegetation	Processes that shift local vegetation
RECORD	DRIVER ECOLOGICAL EFFECT VARIABLES TO TRACK	DRIVER ECOLOGICAL EFFECT VARIABLES TO TRACK
RECORD	para 406	Fire Can favor grasses and fire-adapted shrubs or pines; repeated fire can prevent tree recruitment; too-frequent fire can also degrade adapted communities. Fire return interval, fuel continuity, seasonality, severity.
RECORD	Herbivory / grazing Changes grass biomass, tree recruitment, shrub cover, soil c	Herbivory / grazing Changes grass biomass, tree recruitment, shrub cover, soil compaction and erosion. Wildlife or livestock intensity, browsing pressure, movement corridors.
RECORD	Floods and channel	Floods and channel migration Create patches of different ages, scour surfaces, deposit sediment, reconnect wetlands. Flood recurrence, channel migration, levees, oxbows and terraces.
RECORD	Avalanche / wind / landslide Repeated disturbance can maintain open corridors in	Avalanche / wind / landslide Repeated disturbance can maintain open corridors in forested mountain landscapes. Slope, snow loading, exposure, geology, storm climatology.
RECORD	Soil development and	Soil development and succession Vegetation and microbial activity alter organic matter, nutrient cycles and soil structure over time. Substrate age, weathering, erosion, parent material.
RECORD	para 411	Climate shifts Move suitable temperature/moisture envelopes; alter fire, pests, snowpack and drought. Trend + variability, extreme events, dispersal limits, land-use barriers.
